{"columns":["comment_id","issue_key","issue_project_key","comment_author_email","comment_author_name","comment_body","comment_created_at_ts"],"row_count":10000,"rows":[["3792607","WD-22500","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","please check now","2026-01-07T11:03:10.265Z"],["3792611","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","Please reach out directly to me if there are any questions about DriverX part, or any issues on our side.","2026-01-07T11:03:40.795Z"],["3792615","PFI-830459","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Manually captured the payment in Fondy portal. \n\nWaiting for a double approval for the capture. \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/PFI/queues/custom/379/PFI-830459|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/PFI/queues/custom/379/PFI-830459]","2026-01-07T11:05:19.245Z"],["3792617","LSS-61194","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Thank you very much, [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85]!","2026-01-07T11:05:27.081Z"],["3792620","DSR-3561","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-07T11:06:08.739Z"],["3792621","DELIVERY-1759","DELIVERY","raj.parekh@bolt.eu","Raj Parekh","I cannot edit the description but we have to set courier_settings.earnings_schedule.distances = [1,3,5,6,8]","2026-01-07T11:06:22.790Z"],["3792623","PFI-830164","PFI","mary.adjakonor@bolt-outsource.eu","Mary Adjakonor","Hello Marten,\n\nThank you for your feedback.\n\nRegards,\n\nMary","2026-01-07T11:06:40.379Z"],["3792625","WD-22497","WD","dagmar.olesk@bolt.eu","Dagmar Olesk","[~accountid:712020:f07ce685-1b60-4571-98ae-08c611861c25] Hey!\n\nCan you notify here once the journals are approved? \n\nThen [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] can put the validation back on 🙂 \n\n\n\nThanks!","2026-01-07T11:07:32.488Z"],["3792626","FRAUDOPS-1107","FRAUDOPS","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Impact:\n~1.8K EUR overcharge amount recalculated per month\n~200 recalculations per month\n35 less CS tickets per month","2026-01-07T11:07:39.541Z"],["3792629","LSS-61210","LSS","marc.naether@bolt.eu","Marc Naether","[^uea_555899_Bolt Support Services NL B.V._202601071157484_niet_ondertekend.pdf] _(172 kB)_","2026-01-07T11:08:06.234Z"],["3792630","SRED-926","SRED","mehran.eftekhari@bolt.eu","Shahriar Eftekhari","Got error upgrading aws-ebs-csi-driver. Had to remove deployment and daemonSet, then apply worked fine.","2026-01-07T11:08:46.398Z"],["3792633","PAW-14684","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-07T11:09:41.545Z"],["3792635","PAW-14687","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-review-and-approval-system, pint-product-identity-and-communication-management, pint-capability-itgc\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-07T11:10:19.508Z"],["3792637","PFI-830483","PFI","mia.hartova@bolt.eu","Mia Hartová","!Výstřižek.PNG|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T11:10:52.439Z"],["3792639","LSS-61174","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] please help with finding the doc in inbox and sign by Ahto ","2026-01-07T11:11:36.241Z"],["3792640","LSS-60694","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","[^AIM_Group_Code_of_Ethics_Rev._1.pdf]\n\nHi Irene! The code of Ethics has now been provided by the partner - could you please review? I’ll do the same and share any concerns here. ","2026-01-07T11:11:48.431Z"],["3792641","LSS-61168","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:712020:e1ac2fb7-37ff-4b97-826c-d884246d8177] did we had any previous cases in which a customer was not refund in a similar situation? I just wanted to make sure how this is usually handled. ","2026-01-07T11:11:52.172Z"],["3792642","HS-28689","HS","veronika.gainetdinova@bolt.eu","Veronika Gainetdinova","!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.05.58.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T11:12:02.925Z"],["3792644","LSS-61140","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Great! Thanks a lot [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] , I don’t have any red flag either. \n\nSuper for the courtesy translation, this is a very good idea!\n\nPlease put in the loop (cc) also Aurélien.\n\nGood to go for me if fine for Privacy.\n\nThank you!\n\nELISABETTA ","2026-01-07T11:12:56.764Z"],["3792645","LSS-61050","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:712020:979961a6-5216-4ee0-aa85-a7302993f5e6] Do I understand correctly that our standard NDA template can’t be used? Thank you ","2026-01-07T11:13:16.715Z"],["3792647","LSS-59015","LSS","joao.ramos@bolt.eu","João Nuno Ferreira Ramos","Gladly [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] .\n\n\n1st ticket:[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/635454205|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/635454205]\n\nOn this interaction, she states that her phone had a broken camera and she did the verification in another one, in a different place, while driving: \n\n*_Eu não fiz fraude nenhuma eu vivo do lado do gaia eu abri o telemóvel e_*\n\n*_pediu a identificação, esse mesmo tlml que é o tlml com que eu trabalho tem_*\n\n*_a câmara partida, então fechei a seção e abri no meu outro tlml que é um_*\n\n*_iPhone eu trabalho com um xiomi_*\n\n\n\n2nd ticket: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/649351641|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/649351641]\n\n\nIn this one, the second justification sent via ticket, she states that she was at a funeral for a friend and inadvertently opened up her camera for a selfie check, which contradicts her later statement. In this same ticket she comes up with a new version, blaming our app for the latency of the selfie check, stating that she tried to do the verification on one point, but our system only allowed her to do in another point:\n\n*_Reconheço que cometi um erro, ao permitir que outra pessoa fizesse a verificação da selfie. Na altura, estava num funeral e, devido a uma situação pessoal, uma amiga ficou com o meu telemóvel. Sem ter consciência da importância do procedimento de segurança, ela tirou uma selfie com a minha conta. Entendo que esta ação viola as políticas de segurança da Bolt, e lamento profundamente o sucedido._*\n\n\nn this same ticket she comes up with a new version, blaming our app for the latency of the selfie check, stating that she tried to do the verification on one point, but our system only allowed her to do in another point:\n\n\n*_A segunda razão para o bloqueio, a alegação de que iniciei uma viagem num local diferente de onde a aplicação foi aberta, é o resultado de um erro técnico do sistema de GPS da vossa aplicação. Abri a aplicação ainda no Porto, mas, devido ao tempo de latência do sistema e ao movimento constante, a minha localização só foi atualizada para Gaia depois de eu já ter atravessado a Ponte da Arrábida. Não houve nenhuma tentativa de iniciar a viagem em locais diferentes, mas sim uma falha na atualização em tempo real da minha localização, levando ao bloqueio da conta._*\n\nAdding up, she went to our physical hub with someone to accompany her as well. She threatened both of the workers over there; one of them had to close the door of her room because she was afraid the driver would harm her. Not even the security was able to remove her from the premises. We had to call the police to remove her from there, and even though she stayed for at least 30 minutes, surveilling the hub door.  \n\nLast but not least, you can see that all of her statements are false as her selfie check is not from a friend, not taken at a funeral, not even at a car.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 11.12.42.png|width=1226,height=632,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 11.12.42.png\"!\n\n\n\n","2026-01-07T11:13:28.068Z"],["3792648","SRED-1001","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done","2026-01-07T11:13:28.392Z"],["3792651","PAR-3839","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","For now I can force the currency check for those types\n\n{{[ClientType.BUSINESS]}}\n\n{{[ClientType.FOOD_COURIER]}} \n\n{{[ClientType.FOOD_PROVIDER]}}\n\n{{[ClientType.RIDE_HAILING_DRIVER]}}\n\n{{[ClientType.RIDE_HAILING_FLEET]}}\n\n{{[ClientType.CAR_SHARING_FLEET]}}\n\n{{[ClientType.DELIVERY_PROVIDER_COMPANY]}} \nBut for other types, it needs to integration with the vertical  as we don't do it now","2026-01-07T11:15:34.225Z"],["3792652","LSS-58166","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:85a31a38-edb2-4253-b037-fa5bcad14728] !\nYes, I will send the [FA global template|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1igrgRwUHHPbrUqIA3HfqllnJmYoZmJ-8AQeoyW6MVJM/edit?tab=t.0] to F&F and ask for their views (and which of the KPIs they believe we can adopt safely). \nI will let you know as soon as we have an answer. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-07T11:16:12.328Z"],["3792653","LSS-60657","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:712020:0637b36b-27c8-4bd8-8670-62a8e1156004], do we have any updates?","2026-01-07T11:16:14.652Z"],["3792657","RS-1936","RS","aviv.geron@bolt.eu","Aviv Geron","Hi João,\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket and for sharing the additional background.\n\nAfter careful consideration and discussion with Legal and Compliance, we’re not able to approve this request at this time. While we appreciate that the role involved is considered low risk, the trip does not currently demonstrate a sufficiently clear or business-critical purpose, and the overall expense and nature of the hospitality make it difficult to support under our ABAC (Anti Bribery Anti Corruption) policy principles.\n\nThat said, if there is additional business context that hasn’t yet been captured and would be helpful to consider, the Risk and Compliance Team would be happy to discuss this directly with you and your manager.\n\nPlease let us know if you have any questions, and thank you for your understanding.\n\nBest,\nAviv","2026-01-07T11:17:47.390Z"],["3792658","LSS-59325","LSS","david.leung@bolt.eu","David Thepathat Leung","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd],\nMay I follow up on the MOU?\n\n[^MEMORANDUM OF UNDERSTANDING - Bolt - 20260102 (1).docx]\n\n","2026-01-07T11:18:27.207Z"],["3792659","RS-1936","RS","aviv.geron@bolt.eu","Aviv Geron","Hi João,\r\n\r\nThank you for submitting the ticket and for sharing the additional background.\r\n\r\nAfter careful consideration and discussion with Legal and Compliance, we’re not able to approve this request at this time. While we appreciate that the role involved is considered low risk, the trip does not currently demonstrate a sufficiently clear or business-critical purpose, and the overall expense and nature of the hospitality make it difficult to support under our ABAC (Anti Bribery Anti Corruption) policy principles.\r\n\r\nThat said, if there is additional business context that hasn’t yet been captured and would be helpful to consider, the Risk and Compliance Team would be happy to discuss this directly with you and your manager.\r\n\r\nPlease let us know if you have any questions, and thank you for your understanding.\r\n\r\nBest,\r\nAviv","2026-01-07T11:18:40.270Z"],["3792660","PFI-830453","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe refund has failed as it was rejected by MB Way. \nWe have started an email thread with MB Way to get more information about why the refund failed. However, we cannot guarantee a quick response from them. \n\nIf you would like to give a quick solution to the customer then you could issue a Bolt balance refund instead. \n\nAlternatively you could ask the user to reach out to their bank to see why the refund has failed. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-07T11:19:19.751Z"],["3792663","LSS-61087","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] \n\nWe offer such alternative version of the solicitation clause. Please share with the supplier. It’s well balanced and mutual, so should work for the other party. \n\n_During the term of this Agreement and for 12 months thereafter, neither party shall, directly or indirectly, solicit for employment or engagement any senior employee or key personnel of the other party who was directly involved in the provision or receipt of services under this Agreement, without the prior written consent of the other party. This clause shall not apply to (i) general recruitment not directed at such employees, (ii) hiring resulting from unsolicited applications, or (iii) engaging personnel responding to public advertisements or non-targeted recruitment efforts._\n\n\n\nIf all agreed please ask them to add this clause and send the agreement to [+ahto.kink@bolt.eu+|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu] and cc [+signing@bolt.eu+|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] (we will not be able to find the request without putting this email in cc)","2026-01-07T11:20:32.731Z"],["3792664","DO-5769","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","I created and shared the credentials with Akos.","2026-01-07T11:20:34.439Z"],["3792667","WD-22491","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","changes made","2026-01-07T11:20:46.281Z"],["3792668","SRED-1004","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done","2026-01-07T11:20:54.410Z"],["3792669","PFI-828958","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nPlease note this is a reuse booking case. This payment was used for another order. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2298267662/3?orderTryId=2936520542|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2298267662/3?orderTryId=2936520542]\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3947703797|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3947703797]\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-07T11:21:13.256Z"],["3792670","LSS-61197","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:0b5de1fd-6c52-410d-afb2-757ecf5f9da4] !\n\nI believe we can present the following response (please LMK if something I wrote is wrong or not accurate):\n\n“_Dear xxxxxxx,_\n\n_In regards to the commission reduction you are entitled two, following your agreement with BOLT, we would like to point out that the said agreement states that:_\n\n* _“Bolt shall give a reduction in commission of 10%, not in conjunction with any other offer, capped at Eur 4,500 per BYD E6 unit”; and_\n* _“This benefit will flow to owners in the form of less commissions withheld by BOLT, at the rate of 10% of revenue per month, until the Eur 4,500 cap per unit is reached.”_\n\n_Based on the above, the incentive is intended to deliver a total commission reduction of 10% for eligible BYD e6 units, and it is not stackable with other commission-related offers._\n\n_In Malta there is already a standard 6% branding bonus. To ensure the overall benefit matches the agreement’s 10% total (and remains “not in conjunction with any other offer”), we apply it as:_\n\n* _6% branding bonus (existing), plus_\n* _an additional 4% under the BYD e6 incentive,_\n_so that the combined benefit equals 10%, until the €4,500 cap per unit is reached._\n\n_This is why it may appear split into two components in statements, but the total reduction aligns with the agreement wording._\n\n_If you share the specific vehicle/unit(s) and the statement period(s) you are disputing, we will gladly re-check the calculations against the vehicle registration date and the €4,500 cap and confirm whether any adjustment is required._\n\n_Best regards,”._\n\n\n\nThank you!","2026-01-07T11:21:15.987Z"],["3792671","SRED-791","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done. All checked and some unused redises removed.","2026-01-07T11:21:21.108Z"],["3792672","PFI-828949","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team is unfortunately not able to assist with pricing, discount or promo code related questions. \nPricing is decided by the vertical and the customer payments team does not have any impact on it. \nCould you please raise a ticket with the verticals technical support team instead. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2]\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-07T11:21:42.830Z"],["3792674","DO-5763","DO","ester.georgieva@bolt.eu","Ester Georgieva","[https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/46319|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/46319]\n\nThis is the one","2026-01-07T11:22:36.023Z"],["3792681","WEBSD-1455","WEBSD","tom.gander@bolt.eu","Tom Gander","*QR Code + Link*\n\n!5w7bpkm3_qr_code.png|width=286,alt=\"5w7bpkm3_qr_code.png\"!\n\n{{https://bolt.onelink.me/sbJ2/5w7bpkm3}}","2026-01-07T11:23:56.409Z"],["3792682","LSS-61087","LSS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Thank you, sent to supplier for consideration. ","2026-01-07T11:23:57.912Z"],["3792683","PAW-14685","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-07T11:24:00.226Z"],["3792684","DO-5763","DO","ester.georgieva@bolt.eu","Ester Georgieva","I need to add filters, etc","2026-01-07T11:24:17.302Z"],["3792687","LSS-60553","LSS","wiktoria.lis@bolt.eu","Wiktoria Lis","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] \ndo I understand correctly that we must share the signed PDF with the contractor ourselves? Via email? My concern is if the Mahmoud’s signature will be valid once the contractor uploads it to their system to sign the notice?\n\nThanks for your input!","2026-01-07T11:24:25.035Z"],["3792691","PFI-828898","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI have checked all of the cases that you have highlighted. There are no refund issued to the customer because we did not charge the user. All of the cases are pre-authorization related. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-07T11:25:16.553Z"],["3792695","SRED-647","SRED","artem.timchenko@bolt.eu","Artem Timchenko","Since ZT is dead. We’ll create different tickets for NetBird based on required work.","2026-01-07T11:27:08.510Z"],["3792696","SRED-646","SRED","artem.timchenko@bolt.eu","Artem Timchenko","Since ZT is dead. We’ll create different tickets for NetBird based on required work.","2026-01-07T11:27:19.412Z"],["3792698","SRED-645","SRED","artem.timchenko@bolt.eu","Artem Timchenko","Since ZT is dead. We’ll create different tickets for NetBird based on required work.","2026-01-07T11:27:26.685Z"],["3792699","SRED-629","SRED","artem.timchenko@bolt.eu","Artem Timchenko","Since ZT is dead. We’ll create different tickets for NetBird based on required work.","2026-01-07T11:27:42.428Z"],["3792701","HS-28650","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hi [~accountid:712020:8b648e21-acb5-4024-87b2-2f76f00cfcc2] \n\nThe document has been sent for a signature. Once signed we will send a scanned version to your email and a hard copy to your home address.\n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-07T11:28:17.998Z"],["3792708","LSS-58375","LSS","david.vysoky@bolt.eu","Dávid Vysoký","Here is the court documentation which mentioned the police assessed sum.\n\n[^priloha_1613658523_1_V000010.PDF]\n[^priloha_1613658523_0_Kotyzová_274_2a.PDF]\n\n","2026-01-07T11:29:14.761Z"],["3792712","LSS-51628","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:5067a0c1-57d4-43be-82ef-d8f1c03140a2] hey can you please let me know if there are any updates here?\n\ncc [~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] ","2026-01-07T11:30:14.470Z"],["3792716","LSS-54291","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:5067a0c1-57d4-43be-82ef-d8f1c03140a2] [~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] hey can you please let me know if there are any updates here?","2026-01-07T11:30:32.283Z"],["3792719","WD-22462","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello access granted. Please note that account certification sets are not yet done for PL004","2026-01-07T11:30:54.781Z"],["3792722","LSS-56382","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:639b104bf134138b5a515e5b] hey do you have any updates here?","2026-01-07T11:31:14.703Z"],["3792725","WD-22463","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello, access granted to Workday Sandbox","2026-01-07T11:31:19.659Z"],["3792728","LSS-61211","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^PoA_Zenoriah_KRS.pdf] _(104 kB)_\n\n[^Zenoriah_BOOK OF SHARES.pdf] _(133 kB)_\n\n[^Zenoriah_consent for appointment to the management board + address Ahto Kink.pdf] _(107 kB)_\n\n[^Zenoriah_LIST OF PERSONS AUTHORIZED TO APPOINT THE MANAGEMENT BOARD.pdf] _(110 kB)_\n\n[^Zenoriah_LIST OF SHAREHOLDERS.pdf] _(122 kB)_\n\n[^Zenoriah_notice of purchase of shares.pdf] _(113 kB)_\n\n[^Zenoriah_resolution on address.pdf] _(99 kB)_\n\n[^Zenoriah_statement on shareholders address.pdf] _(102 kB)_","2026-01-07T11:31:35.707Z"],["3792729","LSS-59952","LSS","mario.morais@bolt.eu","Mário Morais","[~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] I agree","2026-01-07T11:31:49.211Z"],["3792730","LSS-57077","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:5067a0c1-57d4-43be-82ef-d8f1c03140a2] hey do you have any updates here?\n\ncc [~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] ","2026-01-07T11:31:51.466Z"],["3792733","LSS-59633","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:edc5b324-043b-4263-83ea-09673acdfe71] hey, will you be able to check the outstanding comments? Thanks!","2026-01-07T11:32:19.337Z"],["3792735","LSS-60943","LSS","neeraj.bhatia@bolt.eu","Neeraj Bhatia","Thanks [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] have shared this with flydubai. Will get back to you with their opinion.","2026-01-07T11:33:17.161Z"],["3792737","WEB-9839","WEB","elina.heno@bolt.eu","Elina Liina Heno","Hey [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] \n\nI made the changes based on the content document.\n\nThe link to the Figma design is [here|https://www.figma.com/design/EA6o5cVzolpDBewnCZ3BOd/Bolt-Web-3.0-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Supply?node-id=1479-18729&t=DXtsq7HexnawZukL-1]\n\nThe link to Drive folder with media is [here|https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Hevo-G-cn2t0DB-YLteEmps8uSOFphjS&usp=drive_fs]\n\nThe link to the prototype is [here|https://www.figma.com/proto/EA6o5cVzolpDBewnCZ3BOd/Bolt-Web-3.0-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Supply?page-id=1440%3A34221&node-id=1510-15491&viewport=1256%2C713%2C0.15&t=8AJc9CT0QHtyjRNr-1&scaling=scale-down&content-scaling=fixed&starting-point-node-id=1510%3A15491]","2026-01-07T11:33:20.996Z"],["3792747","LSS-57542","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team,\n[~accountid:712020:d3fd53e6-f124-4770-a577-b09d6688566f] I have reviewed the updated LOI and accepted appropriate additions. \nThere are a few questions regarding Stella's suggested changes, so please review those. Once clarified, we’ll be able to proceed with signatures.\nThanks!\n","2026-01-07T11:35:06.304Z"],["3792748","PFI-830157","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:6329554614c6b4b2210a39be] \n\nWe have received a confirmation from Paystack the refund has been issued. User will be refunded within 72 hours. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-07T11:35:13.845Z"],["3792749","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Hi DB Owners of {{taxify_commerce_ledger_live}}, I see that this schema has very heavy cron queries on {{TI-LEDGER}} :tidb: cluster.\nI have a suggestion to add a better index that can help with query performance. Details in :thread: below.\ncc: *@user-U04GUHQ4CDN* *@user-U010WFSLQCD* *@user-U02BZ8AUBT2* *@user-U0655CKQU5A*","2026-01-07T11:35:26.093Z"],["3792750","DBRE-8678","DBRE",null,"Slack","[Leandro Morgado|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f5b4e070e396800690aa153] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0875S9HGAF/p1767785302672039?thread_ts=1767785302.672039&cid=C0875S9HGAF|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0875S9HGAF/p1767785302672039?thread_ts=1767785302.672039&cid=C0875S9HGAF|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-07T11:35:27.045Z"],["3792751","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Query ID is: {{43303cdead7a7fca0b378e7a4d8a49f60b6f8dcfbf51f639b7a2f743838d4818}}","2026-01-07T11:35:27.712Z"],["3792752","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","[example|http://ti-ledger-pd-2.sqldb:2379/dashboard/#/slow_query/detail?digest=43303cdead7a7fca0b378e7a4d8a49f60b6f8dcfbf51f639b7a2f743838d4818&connection_id=3697809094&timestamp=1767784117.5509] and impact / RU usage\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7NF6AYHX/screencapture-ti-ledger-pd-2-sqldb-2379-dashboard-2026-01-07-11_26_19.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7NF6AYHX/screencapture-ti-ledger-pd-2-sqldb-2379-dashboard-2026-01-07-11_26_19.png|smart-link]\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A77G9Q9PY/screenshot_2026-01-07_at_11.27.02.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A77G9Q9PY/screenshot_2026-01-07_at_11.27.02.png|smart-link]\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7NF8L4JV/screenshot_2026-01-07_at_11.26.41.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7NF8L4JV/screenshot_2026-01-07_at_11.26.41.png|smart-link]","2026-01-07T11:35:28.298Z"],["3792753","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Problem is {{ledger_storage_layer_id}} column only has a single 1 value and index starts with this:\n\n{noformat}             |   PRIMARY KEY (`id`) /*T![clustered_index] CLUSTERED */,                                                                                                                                                 |\n|              |   KEY `idx_ledger_entry_account_id_id` (`ledger_storage_layer_id`,`account_id`,`id`),                                                                                                                    |\n|              |   KEY `idx_ledger_entry_acc_id_business_ts` (`ledger_storage_layer_id`,`account_id`,`business_event_timestamp_utc`),                                                                                     |\n|              |   KEY `idx_ledger_entry_posting_id` (`ledger_storage_layer_id`,`posting_id`),                                                                                                                            |\n|              |   UNIQUE KEY `udx_le_idempotency_key_index` (`ledger_storage_layer_id`,`account_id`,`posting_entity_id`,`posting_entity_namespace`,`entry_type`,`entry_sub_type`,`correction_id`,`correction_namespace`) |\n\nroot@ti-ledger-dba.sqldb:taxify_commerce_ledger_live>select count(ledger_storage_layer_id), ledger_storage_layer_id from ledger_entry group by ledger_storage_layer_id;\n+--------------------------------+-------------------------+\n| count(ledger_storage_layer_id) | ledger_storage_layer_id |\n|--------------------------------+-------------------------|\n| 545809532                      | 1                       |\n+--------------------------------+-------------------------+\n1 row in set\nTime: 11.397s{noformat}","2026-01-07T11:35:28.834Z"],["3792754","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","WHERE clause is\n\n{noformat}WHERE\n  ledger_storage_layer_id = 1\n  AND account_id = 1000000090001\n  AND id < 1005426232041\n  AND id > 1000000000881;{noformat}","2026-01-07T11:35:29.367Z"],["3792755","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado",":info: Suggestion is to search by {{account_id}} first, not by {{ledger_storage_layer_id}}\nFor that add indexes that start with  {{account_id}} , options to try:\n• add single index on account_id\n• add composite indexes\n    ◦ (account_id, ledger_storage_layer_id, id) -> if you expect to have more distinct values of ledger_storage_layer_id\n    ◦ (account_id, id) -> if ledger_storage_layer_id is expected to stay at single value = 1","2026-01-07T11:35:29.910Z"],["3792756","CCM-22260","CCM","miroslava.solarova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Solárová","Thanks for the reply! Okay, that makes sense. I have enrolled Polina in the full CEE ride-hailing onboarding. \n\nHave a lovely rest of your day! \n\nMirka 🙂 ","2026-01-07T11:35:52.904Z"],["3792758","LSS-61197","LSS","natalia.fronczuk@bolt.eu","Natalia Frończuk","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac], thanks a lot for your assistance - everything looks correct. I have sent out the formed replied to the Fleet Owner.","2026-01-07T11:36:21.358Z"],["3792762","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","BTW, reason for this is that account_id has much more distinct values than single unique ledger_storage_layer_id=1\n\n{noformat}root@ti-ledger-dba.sqldb:taxify_commerce_ledger_live>select count(account_id), account_id  from ledger_entry group by account_id;\n+-------------------+---------------+\n| count(account_id) | account_id    |\n|-------------------+---------------|\n| 4249089           | 1000000030020 |\n| 119136            | 1000000060022 |\n| 646878            | 1000000120014 |\n| 26241             | 1000000090019 |\n| 20                | 1000000180000 |\n...\n| 54381             | 1000000120036 |\n| 4077              | 1000000150034 |\n+-------------------+---------------+\n371 rows in set\nTime: 11.995s{noformat}","2026-01-07T11:37:51.160Z"],["3792764","LSS-58423","LSS","karl.laspina@bolt.eu","Karl Laspina","I fear we may frustrate the rider if we give them 16 €3 promo codes. [~accountid:712020:1e9398f2-efcd-4dcd-8ece-28e6f8578e37] are we able to issue a more standard promo code?","2026-01-07T11:37:58.346Z"],["3792770","PFI-830157","PFI","mary.adjakonor@bolt-outsource.eu","Mary Adjakonor","Hello [~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24] \n\nI appreciate your feedback.\n\nHave a nice day\n\nMary","2026-01-07T11:39:01.226Z"],["3792771","PFI-830494","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-07T11:39:08.894Z"],["3792772","LSS-61198","LSS","onyekachi.nwokocha@bolt-outsource.eu","Onyekachi Nwokocha","[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] All incident report and communications with the driver partner can be found in these beehive tickets: [Ticket 1|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/699863436], [Ticket 2|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/715412639]","2026-01-07T11:39:10.329Z"],["3792773","WFM-9878","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hello [~accountid:712020:a4969d25-8e58-49a1-a0b4-179bb77e9ff8] ,\n\nThank you for reaching out and correcting the emails.\n\nWe are now on the issue, meanwhile note that [+diogo.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:diogo.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu], [+miguel.oliveira@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:miguel.oliveira@bolt-outsource.eu],  [+joao.maia@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:joao.maia@bolt-outsource.eu],  [joao.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:joao.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu], [+raquel.lulendo@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:raquel.lulendo@bolt-outsource.eu], [+eduardo.lopes@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:eduardo.lopes@bolt-outsource.eu] \n\nall have *CS-Safety* role which allows them to unmatch the rider and driver.","2026-01-07T11:39:39.600Z"],["3792777","LSS-60694","LSS","irene.cobian@bolt.eu","Irene Cobian Martin","Hi [~accountid:62a88aabd0132d0068800eba] ! It doesn’t look problematic at first glance but this seems to be their own code of conduct for their employees no?","2026-01-07T11:40:40.060Z"],["3792778","FRAUD-4225","FRAUD","ivan.honchar@bolt.eu","Ivan Honchar","UPD\n\nIn scope of New Year Eve preparation we set 40mCPU container size for many services. So far, it works well.\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FRAUD-5689|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FRAUD-5689|smart-link] \n\n[https://unicorn-builder.platform.boltint.net/builder-ui/service-info-list?filter={\"limit\"%3A50%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"codeowner\"%3A\"fraud\"%2C\"state\"%3A\"active\"}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://unicorn-builder.platform.boltint.net/builder-ui/service-info-list?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A50%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22codeowner%22%3A%22fraud%22%2C%22state%22%3A%22active%22%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-07T11:40:43.301Z"],["3792780","ITI-1161","ITI","marko.toomla@bolt.eu","Marko Toomla","[Webhook - New Hire|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/settings/automation#/rule/019b983c-9493-74a2-bfb6-0d9f41d42979/a0e0b992-662c-4c99-8e54-0a291036aa46]","2026-01-07T11:41:04.952Z"],["3792783","WD-22496","WD","roberts.mitrevics@bolt.eu","Roberts Mitrevičs","Hey Lil,\n\nStill don't see this app in my Okta","2026-01-07T11:41:32.591Z"],["3792785","WD-22489","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Existing delegation request thats pending needs to be cancelled before creating a new request","2026-01-07T11:42:09.756Z"],["3792786","LSS-56313","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Current status: we are in the process of obtaining the access to Nicchiano’s bank account at mBank; however this is handled by finance and from the legal side everything is done ","2026-01-07T11:42:18.132Z"],["3792790","PFI-830453","PFI","austin.fagbolagun@bolt-outsource.eu","Austin Fagbolagun","Hi Marten,\n\nThank you for the swift response. \n\nThe user has been informed about the current development and has been advised to contact their bank about the issue. Please, do notify us of any new developments about this issue.\n\nCheers,\nAustin","2026-01-07T11:42:52.686Z"],["3792791","WD-22496","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","You will need to request IT to add this in Okta, but from our side we have granted access","2026-01-07T11:43:18.217Z"],["3792792","WD-22500","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","You will need to request IT to add this in Okta, but from our side we have granted access","2026-01-07T11:43:33.572Z"],["3792795","WFM-9878","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541589|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541589]","2026-01-07T11:44:20.819Z"],["3792797","LSS-59952","LSS","sofia.carto@bolt.eu","Sofia Cartó","Thank you [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] and [~accountid:712020:ab95f96b-73f1-4bb8-a5fd-5178ef3f1339] \n\n[~accountid:712020:46da73ea-bcbb-4b69-8e3e-ac27402d61bc], i believe you are the owner of the  e-mail [documentacao@bolt.eu|mailto:documentacao@bolt.eu] can you please reply to the e-mail received on that address  and keep me CC? thanks!","2026-01-07T11:44:33.615Z"],["3792798","PFI-830438","PFI","vadim.kozjakov@bolt.eu","Vadim Kozjakov","Hey [~accountid:712020:fc661671-1d51-4372-9578-b46465bd51ac] thanks for the manual. Seems like other error. “To execute”\n\n!Snímek obrazovky 2026-01-07 v 12.43.48.png|width=795,height=483,alt=\"Snímek obrazovky 2026-01-07 v 12.43.48.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-07T11:44:35.208Z"],["3792799","WD-22496","WD","roberts.mitrevics@bolt.eu","Roberts Mitrevičs","Also, this is what I see when trying to signup from the email I received. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 13.42.02.png|width=473,height=507,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 13.42.02.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-07T11:44:52.767Z"],["3792801","DBRE-8678","DBRE","kristjan.vedler@bolt.eu","Kristjan Vedler","the thing with the storage layer id is its supposed to basically become partitioning key in the future (included in every index) - theoretically its more of a sharding key shared across multiple tables, but these \"shards\" are fully configurable in AP and the data between the layers should never be mixed and matched, they live in their own separate financial worlds\n\nto be honest, we want to deprecate this entire cron anyway and go to a different snapshotting logic\n\nso I think it is fine to move account_id to the start of the index for now and to add the new account_id index as well\n\nbut maybe its even better to shut down this cron overall, wdyt [@konstantin.peshekhonov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63a2bfff48b367d78a14db98]","2026-01-07T11:45:15.655Z"],["3792803","DBRE-8678","DBRE","kristjan.vedler@bolt.eu","Kristjan Vedler","its creating unnecessary pressure for a feature that is not used yet and will be rewritten","2026-01-07T11:45:27.494Z"],["3792806","PFI-830438","PFI","vadim.kozjakov@bolt.eu","Vadim Kozjakov","My bad, probably it is the row under the one I reffer, so sum is too small, right?","2026-01-07T11:46:06.805Z"],["3792808","PAW-14688","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-07T11:46:18.597Z"],["3792809","DRX-27981","DRX","taxifyqa@bolt.eu","QA Testing","PR comment for QA:\nPlease verify that Western Sahara country option isn't available on login via phone and add/edit trusted contact screen. In addition, please point out other places where Western Sahara country option is visible","2026-01-07T11:46:37.738Z"],["3792813","LSS-59952","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Resposta - [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1M6Nf9Spcq0GHDmTgCDwODoWKRBZTAkDS-qSwSw-utaQ/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1M6Nf9Spcq0GHDmTgCDwODoWKRBZTAkDS-qSwSw-utaQ/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nAnexos - [^documentos.pdf] ","2026-01-07T11:47:34.538Z"],["3792816","LSS-60538","LSS","klara.kuzebska@bolt.eu","Klara Olejniczak","Thank you, answer sent.","2026-01-07T11:48:10.421Z"],["3792820","HS-28690","HS","pedro.sousa@bolt.eu","Pedro Sousa","!image (16).png|thumbnail!\n\n!image (17).png|thumbnail!\n\n!image (18).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T11:49:15.831Z"],["3792823","RCE-327","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767786662201909]*{color}:\nThank you for removing incorrect `extends` in out test!\n{quote}","2026-01-07T11:51:15.984Z"],["3792824","HS-28692","HS","anas.irshad@bolt.eu","Anas Irshad","!IMG_5547.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T11:51:19.252Z"],["3792827","LSS-58367","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] ,\n\nThanks. May you please advise why it is preferable to use the local entity in this case?\n\nCould we instead use Bolt Operations, given that the spend is allocated to the Performance Marketing cost centre?\n\nThanks in advance for the clarifying 🙏 ","2026-01-07T11:51:37.754Z"],["3792828","RCE-327","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767786688200819]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-327 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T11:51:39.486Z"],["3792829","BD-1972","BD","rafael.barros@bolt.eu","Rafael Adson Barbosa Barros","After the migration to billing-document, some of the tasks no longer had a processor to handle them.\n\nSince these are very old tasks (newest one January of 2025, most of them in 2024,2023, I set them to ignore for now.\n\n{noformat}[2026-01-07 12:50:06] taxify_delivery_invoicing> update task\n                                                 set state='ignore', ignore_reason='There is no longer a processor for these tasks'\n                                                 where state='to_execute'\n                                                 and entity_type='order_refund_invoice'\n[2026-01-07 12:50:06] 179 rows affected in 94 ms{noformat}","2026-01-07T11:51:42.076Z"],["3792831","BD-1972","BD","rafael.barros@bolt.eu","Rafael Adson Barbosa Barros","Stale tasks csv (collected from Databricks):\n\n[^stale_tasks.csv]\n\n","2026-01-07T11:52:28.160Z"],["3792832","DBRE-8678","DBRE","konstantin.peshekhonov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Peshekhonov","Would we even loose something if we kill it? Also is it related to errors we saw earlier?","2026-01-07T11:52:57.711Z"],["3792835","MLC-795","MLC","karl.maasen@bolt.eu","Karl Maasen","[~accountid:712020:d30129ff-7d6f-4bbd-82d3-3c1cbd5e1d77] I see that you changed the Due Date for this - do you think it would make more sense to close this task and create a new task for ‘26. This way there’s a clear understanding of which tickets were handled in '25 vs '26. Otherwise, the list of related tickets will get longer and longer with comments going further and further down.","2026-01-07T11:53:48.002Z"],["3792837","DBRE-8592","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}root@ti-manager:~/tidb/gamma# tiup cluster display gamma | grep tikv | awk '{print $1, $6}'\ngamma-kv-1.sqldb:20160 Up\ngamma-kv-10.sqldb:20160 Up\ngamma-kv-11.sqldb:20160 Up\ngamma-kv-12.sqldb:20160 Up\ngamma-kv-13.sqldb:20160 Tombstone\ngamma-kv-14.sqldb:20160 Tombstone\ngamma-kv-15.sqldb:20160 Tombstone\ngamma-kv-2.sqldb:20160 Up\ngamma-kv-3.sqldb:20160 Up\ngamma-kv-4.sqldb:20160 Up\ngamma-kv-5.sqldb:20160 Up\ngamma-kv-6.sqldb:20160 Up\ngamma-kv-7.sqldb:20160 Up\ngamma-kv-8.sqldb:20160 Up\ngamma-kv-9.sqldb:20160 Up{noformat}\n\n{noformat}There are some nodes can be pruned:\n\tNodes: [gamma-kv-13.sqldb:20160 gamma-kv-14.sqldb:20160 gamma-kv-15.sqldb:20160]\n\tYou can destroy them with the command: `tiup cluster prune gamma`{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~/tidb/gamma# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u gamma-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 21535992 | grep \"region_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u gamma-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 21535992\n    \"region_count\": 0,\n\nroot@ti-manager:~/tidb/gamma# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u gamma-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 21535993 | grep \"region_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u gamma-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 21535993\n    \"region_count\": 0,\n\nroot@ti-manager:~/tidb/gamma# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u gamma-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 21535994 | grep \"region_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u gamma-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 21535994\n    \"region_count\": 0,{noformat}","2026-01-07T11:54:25.088Z"],["3792838","LSS-59991","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f],\n\nWould you be available to discuss this later this afternoon? Your insight on competition law would be very helpful!💚 \n\nThank you!","2026-01-07T11:54:48.067Z"],["3792840","MLC-795","MLC","shubham.sureka@bolt.eu","Shubham Sureka","[~accountid:614b06ac47a8b5006f86d538] Works, the only caveat was the old ones will still be active, so then we move them to the new one so that we can close this task.","2026-01-07T11:54:55.460Z"],["3792841","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Then perhaps just add a new index for now on account_id as temporary mitigation measure?","2026-01-07T11:54:57.093Z"],["3792843","FDBT-4738","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-07T11:55:55.027Z"],["3792844","DSR-3563","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-07T11:56:06.736Z"],["3792846","CRC-2321","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Waiting for Pay After the Ride Flow - Expected first real life test around JAN 8-10","2026-01-07T11:56:31.168Z"],["3792847","DBRE-8592","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","Returning original values:\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~/tidb/gamma# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u gamma-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store limit all 15\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u gamma-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store limit all 15\nSuccess! Set store limit successfully.\n\nroot@ti-manager:~/tidb/gamma# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u gamma-pd-2.sqldb:2379 scheduler add balance-region-scheduler\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u gamma-pd-2.sqldb:2379 scheduler add balance-region-scheduler\nSuccess! The scheduler is created.{noformat}\n\n\n\nPruning the cluster:\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~/tidb/gamma# tiup cluster prune gamma\n...\nWill destroy these nodes: [gamma-kv-13.sqldb:20160 gamma-kv-14.sqldb:20160 gamma-kv-15.sqldb:20160]\nDo you confirm this action? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nStart destroy Tombstone nodes: [gamma-kv-13.sqldb:20160 gamma-kv-14.sqldb:20160 gamma-kv-15.sqldb:20160] ...\n...\n+ [ Serial ] - RemoveTomestoneNodesInPD\nDestroy success{noformat}\n\n\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~/tidb/gamma# tiup cluster display gamma | grep tikv | awk '{print $1, $2}'\ngamma-kv-1.sqldb:20160 tikv\ngamma-kv-10.sqldb:20160 tikv\ngamma-kv-11.sqldb:20160 tikv\ngamma-kv-12.sqldb:20160 tikv\ngamma-kv-2.sqldb:20160 tikv\ngamma-kv-3.sqldb:20160 tikv\ngamma-kv-4.sqldb:20160 tikv\ngamma-kv-5.sqldb:20160 tikv\ngamma-kv-6.sqldb:20160 tikv\ngamma-kv-7.sqldb:20160 tikv\ngamma-kv-8.sqldb:20160 tikv\ngamma-kv-9.sqldb:20160 tikv{noformat}","2026-01-07T11:57:01.965Z"],["3792848","CRC-2308","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Confirmed as queued task at ProcessOut for February 2026.","2026-01-07T11:57:17.681Z"],["3792849","WD-20427","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:712020:2261816b-1a2b-4b75-b1dc-d5fce431ad15] Bulgaria Daily Allowance EUR is completed. Although when i tested it seemed that employee was still reimbursed in EUR. [~accountid:623ace37b75ca80070562c04] could you please overview and update payment elections for Bulgarian employees?","2026-01-07T11:57:30.606Z"],["3792853","PFI-830503","PFI","ittipat.sithiputi@bolt-outsource.eu","Ittipat Sithiputi","!image-20260107-115750.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260107-115806.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T11:58:27.554Z"],["3792857","WFM-9877","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey [~accountid:712020:a4969d25-8e58-49a1-a0b4-179bb77e9ff8] ,\n\nThank you for reaching out. Yes, we got it, actually one of the agents *Luis Gonçalves (ID: 622375)* didn’t have even unmatching permission.\n\nOnly [joao.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:joao.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu] required role for invoice editing.\n\nWe have raised the necessary access requests and they are pending approval. Kindly raise another request if needed, according to template rules.\n\nHave a nice day,\n\nKamran","2026-01-07T11:58:40.747Z"],["3792860","LSS-61053","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d753c43a-57b4-4847-a216-8e6323364ca3] - This appears to be a phone recycling case, where the reporting user got access to another user’s Bolt [account|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/35149909/overview] via their new phone number +995557141532 which was initially associated with the account through another user.\n\nPlease proceed as follows:\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nIf there is an outstanding debt from the *original account owner* on the account \n{panel}\n\nPlease reach out to the fraud team, explain the situation, and ask them if the debt can be forgiven in order to archive the account. \n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nMessage the user who reported logging in the account with the recycled phone number:\n{panel}\n\nDear {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add user’s name]*{color},\n\nThank you for your patience while we investigated your case.\n\nThe Bolt account you are currently using was originally registered by another individual with the phone number ending with {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add 4 last digits of the phone number]*{color} that has since been reassigned to you by your mobile operator. Please note that, in accordance with our policies, we will now archive this account.\n\nOnce this account is archived, you will be able to create a new account using your phone number. To continue using our services, we kindly request that you create a new account. This will give you a secure and personalized experience, without any of the previous account owner’s data linked to it.\n\nTo help protect your account going forward, please ensure that:\n\n* Your phone number linked to the account is up to date;\n* Your email address linked to the account is verified; and\n* You enable multi-factor authentication by clicking to _“My account > Log in and security > Turn on Two-Step Verification”_.\n\nIf you have any questions or need assistance during the process, please contact our Support Team.\n\nBest regards,\n\nBolt Customer Support\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nMessage the original account owner at [magdajikia99@gmail.com|mailto:magdajikia99@gmail.com]:\n{panel}\n\nDear {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add user’s name]*{color},\n\nWe hope this message finds you well. \n\nOur records show that your Bolt account associated with the phone number ending with {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add 4 last digits of the phone number]*{color} was recently accessed by another user. This happened because your account was still linked to that phone number, which has since been reassigned by your mobile operator. This can sometimes occur when operators recycle numbers that are no longer in use. Bolt users may log into their account via their phone number. If a user does not enable two-factor authentication (‘2FA’) in the Bolt App nor updates their phone number in the Bolt App after changing it, and their old phone number is later reassigned by the mobile provider to a new customer, that new customer may inadvertently gain access to the existing Bolt account linked to it. This situation may occur if the new customer attempts to register a new account or requests a one-time password (‘OTP’) to a phone number previously owned by an account holder.\n\nPlease note that, in accordance with our terms and conditions available at: [Terms and Conditions|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/] , you must inform us of any update in your contact details, including phone number changes, at the earliest opportunity. This ensures the continued security of your Bolt account and prevents similar situations from occurring. If you’d like to continue using Bolt, please create a new account using your current phone number.\n\nTo protect your data and ensure proper access control, the account in question will now be permanently archived. Once archived, neither you nor the new number owner will be able to access its details, data, or history.\n\nTo help keep your new account secure going forward, please ensure that:\n\n* Your phone number linked to the account is up to date;\n* Your email address linked to the account is verified; and\n* You enable multi-factor authentication via_“My account > Log in and security > Turn on Two-Step Verification”_;\n* You never share your passkey, or OTP codes received via SMS with anyone.\n\nIf you notice any suspicious activity in your account in the future, or receive an email about a new device login, please contact our Customer Support Team immediately.\n\nBest regards,\n\nBolt\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n+*Archive*+ *the disputed* [*account*|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/35149909/overview] \n{panel}\n\nPlease *archive* the account (do not _delete_ or _schedule for deletion_ ⚠️). If you do not have the necessary access rights to *archive* (in contrast to _delete_) an account, please escalate this case to the CSPC team. This is important for audit trails.","2026-01-07T12:00:21.440Z"],["3792861","MVRT-1446","MVRT","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","[~accountid:6131fd9fdae0a20071ad22a3] clear, thanks! Let’s sync next week, then. All send-out dates can be adjusted easily from our side 🙌 We’ll keep you updated on the progress too.","2026-01-07T12:00:24.507Z"],["3792862","FTO-3","FTO","rostislav.popov@bolt.eu","Rostislav Popov","Latest update:\n+*Łukasz Wołodkiewicz*+  \n\n\nHey everyone!\nWe’ll be getting additional resources on the team in mid-January, so I expect us to move into the design doc phase by the end of the month and then proceed with implementation in February.I'll update here once we have a project lead assigned","2026-01-07T12:00:46.268Z"],["3792863","WFM-9877","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571618|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571618]","2026-01-07T12:01:06.050Z"],["3792865","FDBT-4739","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-07T12:01:24.605Z"],["3792867","GRWA-1466","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","[Slack post|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08UX5MD6AH/p1767735398516059?thread_ts=1767704261.500249&cid=C08UX5MD6AH] ","2026-01-07T12:01:53.248Z"],["3792873","PRF-1746","PRF","teele.vallimae@bolt.eu","Teele Vallimäe","Hey, so we don’t run any courier ads in Google at the moment but i will remember this ticket in the future if we have to launch something for couriers with visuals.","2026-01-07T12:04:01.541Z"],["3792875","CRC-2323","CRC","ahmad.eldefrawy@bolt.eu","Ahmad ElDefrawy","Implementation done from Billing Busiess side in 2025Q4","2026-01-07T12:04:32.672Z"],["3792877","PFI-830438","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nright, sum is too small","2026-01-07T12:04:42.318Z"],["3792879","DBRE-8592","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.05.08.png|width=621,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.05.08.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.04.27.png|width=621,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.04.27.png\"!","2026-01-07T12:05:25.529Z"],["3792880","HS-28659","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi again Refilwe, the letter should be with you now. Please let me know if you need anything else. For now I’ll close the ticket. ","2026-01-07T12:05:34.973Z"],["3792883","SCM-1001","SCM","zuzanna.antoniewska@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Izabela Antoniewska","Reply from Lev “[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] thank you for the detailed input and for outlining the operational considerations. Given that several of the questions touch on policy, legal requirements, operational feasibility and process design, we will consolidate feedback from each responsible teams, including ODPO and Risk & Compliance, to ensure we have a coordinated and aligned response.\n\nAs pointed out earlier, this requires the assessment of local legal requirements (especially retention periods). Which markets should we focus on first?\n\nWe will follow up with the coordinated answers as soon as the internal review is completed.” \n\nI shared the list of countries based on GMV and added that we need all markets to be checked, and to not focus on Italy, Croatia, Czech, GE, AZ (as we are leaving these markets)","2026-01-07T12:06:28.521Z"],["3792884","WAVE-179","WAVE","aleksandra.shulman@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Shulman","[~accountid:5d7b698997d8980d8ead4b01] please notice that in current Kalep implementation there is a mistake in SELECTED Chip:\nfor Action, Danger, Promo the color of content (text + icons) should be not content.primary-inverted but static.content.key-light. It’s already fixed in Figma, so you can reference it","2026-01-07T12:06:42.443Z"],["3792886","LSS-58375","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Thank you [~accountid:5e0f07ab9a4b780d990e9fb9] were we able to collect the amount of the damage through the debt collection parter/insurer? \n\nAlso, is the amount of the damage from the prosector letter correct?  ","2026-01-07T12:06:55.826Z"],["3792887","LSS-59711","LSS","zuzanna.antoniewska@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Izabela Antoniewska","Hi, \nWhen we can expect review of the processes? ","2026-01-07T12:07:07.712Z"],["3792889","CRC-2365","CRC","ahmad.eldefrawy@bolt.eu","Ahmad ElDefrawy","Archiving as duplicate of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CRC-2362|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CRC-2362|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T12:07:20.971Z"],["3792890","LSS-61212","LSS","nariman.abbasov@bolt.eu","Nariman Abbasov","[^Bolt for Baku ACM.pdf] _(4.67 MB)_","2026-01-07T12:07:53.742Z"],["3792895","HS-28670","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Sitang, thank you for the request. I have sent the letter for signing. Once it’s signed it should come to your personal email. Regarding travel insurance, please log a ticket here -[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/39|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/39|smart-link]. ","2026-01-07T12:08:42.191Z"],["3792896","PFA-557","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","Main Docs: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1l2xoffoxwwpbm7K59Jzrys2fGBGdjKEfzgC1MSQLjFA/edit?gid=1799423704#gid=1799423704|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1l2xoffoxwwpbm7K59Jzrys2fGBGdjKEfzgC1MSQLjFA/edit?gid=1799423704#gid=1799423704|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T12:08:45.660Z"],["3792897","CEBF-1803","CEBF","pavlo.savenko@bolt.eu","Pavlo Savenko","\n\n[https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.lightning.force.com/lightning/r/Opportunity/006dt000007VMZhAAO/view?ws=%2Flightning%2Fr%2FOpportunity%2F006dt000007JoLFAA0%2Fview%23%2F|https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.lightning.force.com/lightning/r/Opportunity/006dt000007VMZhAAO/view?ws=%2Flightning%2Fr%2FOpportunity%2F006dt000007JoLFAA0%2Fview%23%2F|smart-card]\n\n!image-20260107-120838.png|width=654,alt=\"image-20260107-120838.png\"!","2026-01-07T12:08:53.491Z"],["3792898","DBRE-8593","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.06.45.png|width=621,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.06.45.png\"!\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u ti-fraud-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 3563914 | grep \"leader_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u ti-fraud-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 3563914\n    \"leader_count\": 20,\n\nroot@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u ti-fraud-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 3563915 | grep \"leader_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u ti-fraud-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 3563915\n    \"leader_count\": 99,\n\nroot@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u ti-fraud-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 3563916 | grep \"leader_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u ti-fraud-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 3563916\n    \"leader_count\": 210,{noformat}","2026-01-07T12:08:55.317Z"],["3792900","INT-777","INT","adil.ansar@bolt.eu","Mohammad Adil Ansar","# Currently we block all the active enrollments (if the provider test is created with correct ocnfiguration for the market)\n# Do we not want to ban bolt funded campaigns? Because currently we just disable all campaigns on provider.\n# What information do we want to show on provider portal and in the email? Currently we can show that provider will be banned because they increased their prices and {{all}} the campaigns will be banned till {{x_date}}","2026-01-07T12:09:19.549Z"],["3792904","FX-3180","FX","emiwodew.gizaw@bolt.eu","Emiwodew Nigussie Gizaw","As discussed [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02EWCR0A6R/p1767692555042759?thread_ts=1765557189.575699&cid=C02EWCR0A6R] this is not needed anymore","2026-01-07T12:10:07.309Z"],["3792908","BDB-1494","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:628e5c9d8026a10068b1e457] [~accountid:63189c4056010c40d4481ce2] \nI see a thumbs-up emoji on the previous comment. Does that mean I can proceed with printing the files? 😁  Thank you ","2026-01-07T12:11:01.218Z"],["3792911","DSR-3565","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-07T12:11:18.544Z"],["3792912","SREC-355","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","* Destroyed VNG Cloud resources\n* Removed related SSM secrets\n* Removed related SG rules\n* Removed related AWS Firewall rules\n* Removed IPAM entry\n* Removed SSH key from 1password","2026-01-07T12:11:35.504Z"],["3792913","RS-1936","RS","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hi [~accountid:712020:b0d06119-b7c8-4491-85a9-a5cb1e609b96] \n\nThank you again for the explanation and for taking the time to review this.\n\nYou mentioned that if there is additional business context that hasn’t yet been captured, the Risk and Compliance team would be open to discussing this further with me and my manager, and I wanted to follow up on that point for clarity.\n\nIn this case, the invitation relates to a hosted partner event intended for relationship maintenance, *extended to multiple partner companies*, with no ongoing negotiations, commercial decision-making sessions attached. From my reading of the policy, relationship-maintenance hospitality is recognised in principle, and I appreciate that the value and nature of the hospitality were key considerations in the assesment. To ensure I’m applying the policy correctly going forward, it would be very helpful to understand *what type of additional business context or structure* would typically be required for an event of this nature to be supportable from an ABAC perspective, particularly where relationship maintenance is the primary objective.\n\nIf helpful, I’m of course open to discussing this together with my manager.","2026-01-07T12:11:46.461Z"],["3792915","PFI-830514","PFI","justas.gaizauskas@bolt.eu","Justas Gaižauskas","[^ES1526-172 (2).pdf]","2026-01-07T12:12:01.506Z"],["3792916","PFI-830514","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-07T12:12:03.824Z"],["3792919","DRX-26853","DRX","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","Tested the task on DI.126.0 (194094834) on iOS 26.1\n\nVerified the complete flow of the Dashcam through settings:\n\n* User is able to add vehicles in the dashcam listing\n* User is able to remove dashcam from the “Dashcams” listing screen\n* “Add dashcam” label is hidden when all the vehicles are added in the list\n* Snack bars are populating: When a dashcam is removed, when a dashcam is added, when user taps on Next button without selecting any vehicle from the “select a vehicle” screen & when user taps on “Done” button without selecting any dashcam details from the list\n* View is not distorted in RTL\n* All the elements are visible in Dark theme mode\n\nAttaching the screen recording for reference:\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-07-2026 13-53-53_1.MP4]\n\n\n\n*RTL flow in Dark Theme mode:*\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-07-2026 14-03-49_1.MP4]\n\nVerified","2026-01-07T12:12:15.132Z"],["3792920","DRX-26853","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Ticket is tested by [~accountId:628dd714269a9a0068f2a783].","2026-01-07T12:12:28.325Z"],["3792921","DRX-26848","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26853 has been resolved","2026-01-07T12:12:28.791Z"],["3792922","PFI-830516","PFI","inorca.rudolph@bolt.eu","Inorca Rudolph","[^PDF document.pdf]","2026-01-07T12:13:27.179Z"],["3792923","LSS-58375","LSS","david.vysoky@bolt.eu","Dávid Vysoký","No, the debt collector couldn’t as the debt was charged to the user persona L.Zidek (stolen documents). \nHere is the original invoice: \n\n[^CZ Bolt Drive customer C-CZ001-25-000066 2025-01-31 (1) (47ba21f7-608f-41c7-860c-bf9deba94876).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T12:14:03.446Z"],["3792925","RDXENG-4511","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","*Tested with user* {{111484422}} *and unable to reproduce* (/) \n\n||*Device name*||Google Pixel 8a||\n|OS Version|16|\n|Client build|CA.192.0 RC|\n|Comment|physical|\n\n!capture-20260107-121145.png|width=210,alt=\"capture-20260107-121145.png\"!","2026-01-07T12:14:11.211Z"],["3792927","BR-4084","BR","triinu.tasa@bolt.eu","Triinu Tasa","To hide interest rate and due date: dynamic config {{RIDE_HAILING_PARTNER_AGGREGATED_HIDE_INTEREST_INFO_COUNTRY_LIST}}","2026-01-07T12:15:55.458Z"],["3792929","PFI-830335","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi [~accountid:712020:291ca72f-3929-4484-9fab-a29203ceb5ea],\n\nI am unfortunately not certain, as their story does not match our logs.\n\nAs internal information, please look at the screenshot below:\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.12.30.png|width=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.12.30.png\"!\n\nFrom the picture it is visible that they have attempted to make an order via some kind of discount. Not sure if maybe they have a discount applied unknowingly.\nThere is also a chance that they have created a new user which has new user discount applied immediately, however, we can see that they have multiple users and that this user is not in fact new.\nMost likely this user is trying to abuse our systems.\n\nIf they insist on saying that they are not using discounts and such, then advise them that due to irregular activities they are not able to make further orders.\n\nMarten","2026-01-07T12:16:11.824Z"],["3792931","DBRE-8593","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster scale-in ti-fraud -N ti-fraud-kv1-15.sqldb:20160\nThis operation will delete the ti-fraud-kv1-15.sqldb:20160 nodes in `ti-fraud` and all their data.\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nThe component `[tikv]` will become tombstone, maybe exists in several minutes or hours, after that you can use the prune command to clean it\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nScale-in nodes...\n...\nScaled cluster `ti-fraud` in successfully{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster scale-in ti-fraud -N ti-fraud-kv1-14.sqldb:20160\nThis operation will delete the ti-fraud-kv1-14.sqldb:20160 nodes in `ti-fraud` and all their data.\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nThe component `[tikv]` will become tombstone, maybe exists in several minutes or hours, after that you can use the prune command to clean it\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nScale-in nodes...\n...\nScaled cluster `ti-fraud` in successfully{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster scale-in ti-fraud -N ti-fraud-kv1-13.sqldb:20160\nThis operation will delete the ti-fraud-kv1-13.sqldb:20160 nodes in `ti-fraud` and all their data.\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nThe component `[tikv]` will become tombstone, maybe exists in several minutes or hours, after that you can use the prune command to clean it\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nScale-in nodes...\n...\nScaled cluster `ti-fraud` in successfully{noformat}","2026-01-07T12:16:31.265Z"],["3792934","LSS-57150","LSS","roman.igaz@bolt.eu","Roman Igaz","Hey [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f], can we proceed with the repayment schedule for Eliáš Mitra?","2026-01-07T12:16:49.454Z"],["3792935","CCM-22263","CCM","karina.kligina@bolt.eu","Karina Kligina","!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 13.26.56.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T12:16:50.615Z"],["3792936","LSS-56824","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] ! Rejected ticket, that duplicated this one.\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached (dokobit version). \n\nEpuap will be ready at first Ahto’s convenience.\n\n[^Pelnomocnictwo-pocztowe BOLT RIDES (2) (1).pdf] [^Pelnomocnictwo-pocztowe BOLT SERVICES PL (1) (1).pdf]  ","2026-01-07T12:17:03.978Z"],["3792937","SREC-357","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Done in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREC-355|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREC-355|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T12:17:05.060Z"],["3792939","SREDESK-7369","SREDESK","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","Assigned to [~accountid:61419ea255bbfb007620b7dd]  as follow-up from her on-call week, preemptively added into current sprint.","2026-01-07T12:17:09.195Z"],["3792940","LSS-61085","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:62a3287576c0360069f59b72] thank you Daniel - can you please let me know if any specific further input is needed from my side or from the Operations team ([~accountid:61d80a617c6f9800706f8ef2])?","2026-01-07T12:17:23.631Z"],["3792941","PFA-557","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","*Progress Update* [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1H5Gks_qJxOkDiU45iwGgqCe9HKWI-_X7_pHAo1S16Hs/edit?gid=1799423704#gid=1799423704|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1H5Gks_qJxOkDiU45iwGgqCe9HKWI-_X7_pHAo1S16Hs/edit?gid=1799423704#gid=1799423704]","2026-01-07T12:17:37.350Z"],["3792946","DBRE-8593","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster display ti-fraud | grep tikv | awk '{print $1, $6}'\nti-fraud-kv1-1.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-fraud-kv1-10.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-fraud-kv1-11.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-fraud-kv1-12.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-fraud-kv1-13.sqldb:20160 Pending Offline\nti-fraud-kv1-14.sqldb:20160 Pending Offline\nti-fraud-kv1-15.sqldb:20160 Pending Offline\nti-fraud-kv1-2.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-fraud-kv1-3.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-fraud-kv1-4.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-fraud-kv1-5.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-fraud-kv1-6.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-fraud-kv1-7.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-fraud-kv1-8.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-fraud-kv1-9.sqldb:20160 Up{noformat}","2026-01-07T12:18:11.601Z"],["3792947","PFI-830476","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello,\n\nNo need for a duplicate ticket, answer has been provided in the previous one and this one will be cancelled.\n\nMarten","2026-01-07T12:18:28.025Z"],["3792951","PFI-830168","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Please reach out to privacy team via BH for this. ","2026-01-07T12:18:57.615Z"],["3792952","LSS-61082","LSS","maarja.nommets@bolt.eu","Maarja Nõmmets","Hello! Confirming I am looking into it! Is it important to have a specific supplier category (related to facility management services, for example) or any service/product will be accepted?\ncc [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] ","2026-01-07T12:18:58.813Z"],["3792953","PFI-830168","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-07T12:19:05.127Z"],["3792955","PFA-558","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","Analysis Result : [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CD/pages/7318077607/2025+12+-+Identify+discrepancy+between+Routine+Dashboard+and+Experiment+Result|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CD/pages/7318077607/2025+12+-+Identify+discrepancy+between+Routine+Dashboard+and+Experiment+Result|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T12:19:10.164Z"],["3792956","PFI-830513","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:1d3994f3-6a46-4495-8e2e-33c428f6b555],\n\n\nWhile this is out of scope for the Fraud team, I will be sharing 2 KB articles regarding this situation that I found.\n\n[I have an unrecognised charge|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360013746119?country=global&language=en]\n[I noticed suspicious activity on my account|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/70724?country=global&language=en]\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-07T12:19:22.345Z"],["3792957","HS-28680","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","New amendment sent for signing. ","2026-01-07T12:19:22.640Z"],["3792960","PFA-558","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","EM was aligned (/) ","2026-01-07T12:19:28.723Z"],["3792962","CLIENTAPP-38761","CLIENTAPP","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","UI tests execution has been completed. Test cycle created: \"https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/CLIENTAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin%3Acom.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/testPlayer/CLIENTAPP-R2990\"","2026-01-07T12:19:50.138Z"],["3792966","FX-3563","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767788432313439]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3563] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T12:20:44.358Z"],["3792967","LSS-61174","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] [~accountid:712020:10c3f4ef-f975-47a3-8af8-927b01cd9521] ! The document has been signed by Ahto. \n\nThe signature from Ulla Helm is pending.","2026-01-07T12:20:47.016Z"],["3792968","WFM-9766","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Handover to Gosia and Rux ","2026-01-07T12:21:02.264Z"],["3792972","FX-3563","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767788477180909]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3563 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T12:21:30.184Z"],["3792973","LSS-59952","LSS","rita.silva@bolt.eu","Rita Santos Silva","[~accountid:5b7bea09d08e47445d6fd01e] can you access the [documentacao@bolt.eu|mailto:documentacao@bolt.eu] email and reply what is necessary please? As [~accountid:712020:011a9eb3-77af-4c62-bb26-e6c10e6097ec] and [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] mention!\n\nThank you","2026-01-07T12:21:31.723Z"],["3792974","WD-22421","WD","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Hi Valerie,\n\nPlease try submitting the expense now. I implemented a workaround to resolve the error, but we still need to investigate the root cause with our colleagues in Finance tech.\n\nThank you and apologies for all the back and forth.\n\nkind regards,\n\nOana","2026-01-07T12:21:43.688Z"],["3792976","WD-22374","WD","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Hi Irene,\n\nPlease try submitting the expense now. I implemented a workaround to resolve the error, but we still need to investigate the root cause with our colleagues in Finance tech.\n\nThank you and apologies for all the back and forth.","2026-01-07T12:22:08.035Z"],["3792977","FX-3563","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Halavan [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767788555082739]*{color}:\n{code}-200\n+1000{code}\nIncrease batch size of order aggregations to 1000. With current limitation of 800 drivers this should reduce concurrency to 1 (as there will be only one single batch to process).\nI’d like to monitor and see if there are any issues with a single batch execution and then increase driver ids limitation from current 800 to 1000.\ncc <@U079RS54W7N>\n{quote}","2026-01-07T12:22:47.670Z"],["3792978","PFA-559","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","WIP : [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/29378?2nd+Time+Range=2025%2F12%2F29+to+2026%2F01%2F05&1st+Time+Range=2025%2F12%2F22+to+2025%2F12%2F29&Case+State=-draft%2C-duplicate&Specific+Issue+Key+-+Country+Level+Filter=&Overall+-+Issue+Key=-NULL&Is+Partner+market+(Yes+%2F+No)=No|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/29378?2nd+Time+Range=2025%2F12%2F29+to+2026%2F01%2F05&1st+Time+Range=2025%2F12%2F22+to+2025%2F12%2F29&Case+State=-draft%2C-duplicate&Specific+Issue+Key+-+Country+Level+Filter=&Overall+-+Issue+Key=-NULL&Is+Partner+market+%28Yes+%2F+No%29=No]","2026-01-07T12:22:55.262Z"],["3792979","PFA-543","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","Will be pick up after Unassignment Reason complete","2026-01-07T12:23:22.915Z"],["3792980","LSS-60650","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] \nThe business explained that we need a new NDA because _“we are discussing payouts from Estonia Bolt Ops OU to Ukraine, we thought we need a separate NDA, as the existing agreement with Mono is for the localised setup. We proposed our standard one, and they responded with their template.”_\n\nI honestly do not see the need of a new NDA when we have an ongoing relation with the bank, but if they insist I am ok signing a new one. The NDA here is in Ukranian only. Would you mind helping me out and giving it a quick look? \n\nI’ll just let the business know they can just move on without a new NDA but if the bank insist then we can simply sign this new one. \n\nThank you in advance! ","2026-01-07T12:23:26.733Z"],["3792981","SCM-790","SCM","omar.masum@bolt.eu","Omar Faruk Masum","As Majority task timeline updated in *“Reminder”* tab SP Procurement Dashboard file. Now we can closed this ticket, in future time to time I will update this tab data in Dashboard. ","2026-01-07T12:23:27.726Z"],["3792983","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767788600239139]*{color}:\nOk, how do we proceed here <@U04FV4Z0GQ4> <@U09430SS0J3> I am now in a situation where I cannot proceed with balance transfeers from old Viggo legacy Console into Bolt Admin, no possibility to also payback equipment deposit to Bolt FOs that are exiting the platform after the launch of Bolt due to lack of visibility in the Fleet Portal, this is starting to become a snowball.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T12:23:34.068Z"],["3792986","INS-899","INS","volha.anishchanka@bolt.eu","Volha Anishchanka","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/folder/7262634355?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiODY4ZmI4ODU5NTZhNDVmOTkxNTY0ZWM1Njk5NTg0ZDciLCJwIjoiYyJ9|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/folder/7262634355?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiODY4ZmI4ODU5NTZhNDVmOTkxNTY0ZWM1Njk5NTg0ZDciLCJwIjoiYyJ9|smart-link] \nWill be updated as the release per project goes. Warehouse Ops will be updated after agreeing with users on how to approach it","2026-01-07T12:24:31.337Z"],["3792987","WFM-9838","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Messaged the role owners to approve ","2026-01-07T12:24:44.223Z"],["3792988","LSS-60650","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:712020:e970ee87-f3c5-4314-827e-503375f99daf] As we have an ongoing relation with this bank, I do not see the need of a new NDA, you should simply let them know this and move on with your discussions. However, in case the bank insists, I have asked Anna to kindly take a quick look to the NDA they shared, as it is only in Ukrainian. ","2026-01-07T12:24:51.458Z"],["3792990","DPX-3550","DPX","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","I tried to extract some data to understand if such “duplicate” requests actually can be a thing, 20 examples from the example data set [^147b141a-db9f-46af-aa65-800a97f58b56_2025-11-09_11-52-24 (1).csv] \n\n# *Region 353 (Gap: 3m 47s)*\n\n* {{{\"status\":\"Activate\",\"regionId\":353,\"alarmType\":\"ARTILLERY\",\"createdAt\":\"2025-11-01T11:43:37Z\"} 2025-11-01 11:43:46}}\n* {{{\"status\":\"Activate\",\"regionId\