tivate\",\"regionId\":99,\"alarmType\":\"AIR\",\"createdAt\":\"2025-11-07T22:59:24.2365514Z\"} 2025-11-07 22:59:54}}","2026-01-07T12:25:20.580Z"],["3792993","PFI-830532","PFI","roselyne.ndiga@bolt-outsource.eu","Roselyne Ndiga","[^7109361_PMT_DOMESTIC.pdf]","2026-01-07T12:25:38.772Z"],["3792994","LSS-59379","LSS","sonia.caetano@bolt.eu","Sónia Caetano","Hi Giullia, we don’t. I sent you the Authorisation Letter template, will that be sufficient? \n\nThanks,\n\nSonia","2026-01-07T12:25:38.768Z"],["3792995","PFI-830532","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-07T12:25:40.965Z"],["3792996","LSS-60367","LSS","indrek.eelmets@bolt.eu","Indrek Eelmets","Hello [~accountid:712020:1018a6cf-f63b-4dae-a04a-743bfd3b7900], please review the draft [response|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1f2g-tDsOxk0zQhLF8s0vfo6b_o9bFL18MMEr_mZsDcc/edit?tab=t.0].  ","2026-01-07T12:25:41.677Z"],["3792997","WFM-9879","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Hello [~accountid:5fc09e33aca10c00698efb1c] , agent assigned to queue 11 REG_Ireland_Driver Registrations. Let me know if you need further help here.","2026-01-07T12:25:58.802Z"],["3793000","RNTL-30262","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","thanks *@user-UK9K30SQ2*!\n\nWhile you are away, perhaps *@user-UCL1L70BU* can check this. Technically there should be no reason for deploying inside the warehouse but this was the case with the vehicle on [27th of Oct when it was automatically deployed and then actually deployed again on 28th of Oct|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/rentals-micromobility/vehicles/list/edit/germany/590503?tab=tasks_events&filter=%7B%22limit%22:25,%22offset%22:0,%22filter%22:%7B%22start_ts%22:1759299089,%22end_ts%22:1761808289,%22task_states%22:%5B%22opened%22,%22in_progress%22%5D%7D%7D&tz=Europe/Tallinn]. This is potentially messing up our data.","2026-01-07T12:27:41.354Z"],["3793001","RNTL-30262","RNTL",null,"Slack","[Dmitry Zamaleev|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d773c785a4d810d2c4de81c] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C030MJW96CA/p1767683913240269?thread_ts=1761309533.884879&cid=C030MJW96CA|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C030MJW96CA/p1767683913240269?thread_ts=1761309533.884879&cid=C030MJW96CA|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-07T12:27:42.460Z"],["3793002","SCM-790","SCM","zuzanna.antoniewska@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Izabela Antoniewska","[~accountid:712020:16f9a1bd-630a-44fc-acfd-57a270c13c42] What is the process and timelines for each country? Did you set up buffers?","2026-01-07T12:27:50.388Z"],["3793005","LEG-1182","LEG","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","9.11.2025: Under the main thicket it is seen that stakeholders are discussing whether to add sth under this MVRA ticket or not. Currently no update.","2026-01-07T12:28:17.754Z"],["3793008","RIDE-159","RIDE","katarina.saage@bolt.eu","Katarina Elisabeth Saage","{panel:bgColor=#ffebe6}\n*The market has been deprioritised & removed from the Rides launch pipeline.*\n{panel}\n\n{quote}After we approved the business case in March 2024, the following factors have led to a change in our launch decision:\n\n* The regulatory process has remained unclear, with ongoing challenges at multiple stages\n* The competitive landscape has shifted, with the local player GSM increasing investment and benefiting from recent changes to electric vehicle regulations that impact the original business case\n* From a central perspective, we are applying a higher bar to new market investments where efficiency is uncertain and long-term investment security is less clear. \n\nVietnam launch plans are removed for now, and unless the market/policy meaningfully changes, will remain a no-go country for Bolt.{quote}","2026-01-07T12:28:35.258Z"],["3793010","PFA-560","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","WIP : 90% Identified / expected, 10% left is under deep dive - under supervision Eng team\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yQ-0P5lsLMIJ3TJeKEVuVh0UK7oSdWA5N9E_Wz_vCdU/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yQ-0P5lsLMIJ3TJeKEVuVh0UK7oSdWA5N9E_Wz_vCdU/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T12:28:59.237Z"],["3793011","WFM-9880","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","checking validity of request with Team Lead","2026-01-07T12:29:15.721Z"],["3793012","PFI-830535","PFI","dominika.wozniak@bolt-outsource.eu","Dominika Woźniak","[^transaction-statement.pdf (1).pdf]","2026-01-07T12:29:26.121Z"],["3793014","LEG-993","LEG","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Marking this as Done as Commerce Legal support for Bolt + expansions should be provided through the project when needed. ","2026-01-07T12:29:48.616Z"],["3793015","MARTECH3-1396","MARTECH3","gergo.zavecz@bolt.eu","Gergõ Závecz","* The {{Reactivation}} metric has been added to {{mart_models_spark.mart_rider_ads_metrics}} as requested in this [ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MARTECH3-1362].\n* A [folder|https://bolt-datascience.cloud.databricks.com/browse/folders/2487055656115461?o=3829506390716583] for reactivation sensitivity analysis has been created, the relevant notebooks have been kept and adjusted/rewritten.\n* The orchestrator notebook running the {{causalimpact}} models has been started today to find the model parameters which fit our FPR standards. Currently it has been started for five markets (France, Poland, Romania, South Africa, Thailand).","2026-01-07T12:29:52.522Z"],["3793018","PFI-830438","PFI","vadim.kozjakov@bolt.eu","Vadim Kozjakov","In CZ this monthly invoice is important regarding the reverse charge. Subjects are obligated to pay VAT on our commission. Since the document is not generated, do you know how the FO should proceed? ","2026-01-07T12:30:25.470Z"],["3793020","PFI-823156","PFI","yurii.bilynskyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Yurii Bilynskyi","Repeat one more pls . Hi team! The driver is asking if it is possibly to cancel this payout so that it can be included in the next payout. Can we do it?","2026-01-07T12:30:51.389Z"],["3793025","DBRE-8678","DBRE","kristjan.vedler@bolt.eu","Kristjan Vedler","{quote}Would we even loose something if we kill it{quote}\n\nI have a feeling that nope","2026-01-07T12:32:10.584Z"],["3793027","PFI-830516","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThank you for escalating! \nI have reached out to our accounting team to see if they are able to locate and refund the payment. \nWill let you know when we have any updates. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-07T12:32:20.313Z"],["3793028","DBRE-8678","DBRE","kristjan.vedler@bolt.eu","Kristjan Vedler","{quote}Also is it related to errors we saw earlier{quote}\n\nnope, those were invoicing-balance","2026-01-07T12:32:24.832Z"],["3793029","PFI-830516","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/G7BT51XJ4/p1767789086282829|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/G7BT51XJ4/p1767789086282829]","2026-01-07T12:32:35.426Z"],["3793030","LSS-60650","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] hey, I translated the NDA in DeepL, please see the English version attached. \n\nFrom my side, I have 2 comments re the legal issues with the draft:\n\n# The term is set to 10 years.\n# Each person handling the information from our side would need to be indicated in the annex and sign another annex with the confirmation to protect the confidential information - this is an excessive administrative burden and is never done for NDAs.\n\nPlease check the draft in case you have more comments.\n\n[^3_2__dogovir_pro_konfidenciynist_18_07_2025 en-US.doc]\n\n","2026-01-07T12:32:42.223Z"],["3793031","LSS-61087","LSS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Sodali accepted our amended Solicitation clause and also clarified that the total cost remains 90k with 6% admin fees included, with clarification reflected in the MSA text: \n\n_Also, see 10. b) below where the 6% admin and research fee is already incorporated in the EUR90,000 total._\n\n \n\n# *_Project Fees, Expenses, and Summary by Service_*   \n\n_a. Subject to the terms herein, Consultant will perform all Services and provide all Deliverables under this SOW for a fixed fee (the “_*_Fee_*_”) as outlined below._ \n\n_b. An amount equal to 6% of the Fee has been incorporated into the summary of Fees by Service below, for administration, technology, and research and data services._   \n\nSigning ticket raised here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61214|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61214|smart-link] \n\nThank you for your support! 🙏 ","2026-01-07T12:32:46.879Z"],["3793034","GRWA-1462","GRWA","taron.davtyan@bolt.eu","Taron Davtyan","Results are collected in [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LIWo0XY148m2Hbuxh9OV14QT8PfOvVkBvUAOVe0OO-Y/edit?gid=1734412213#gid=1734412213|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LIWo0XY148m2Hbuxh9OV14QT8PfOvVkBvUAOVe0OO-Y/edit?gid=1734412213#gid=1734412213|smart-link] tab - *WIP Results [Dec Batch]*\n\nIt is scheduled to be updated every day in the morning.","2026-01-07T12:33:33.692Z"],["3793035","LSS-59952","LSS","joao.ramos@bolt.eu","João Nuno Ferreira Ramos","Reply sent, with the attachment as well.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.30.36.png|width=1438,height=646,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.30.36.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.30.23.png|width=1440,height=589,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.30.23.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-07T12:33:45.153Z"],["3793038","LSS-59689","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, attaching here the scanned original. Documents will be sent with the other NDA.\n\n[^NDA_Bolt Operations OÜ_Petrol Contract LLC_27.11.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T12:34:18.158Z"],["3793039","HS-28580","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-07T12:34:33.712Z"],["3793041","PFI-830547","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-07T12:34:46.165Z"],["3793043","DBRE-8678","DBRE","konstantin.peshekhonov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Peshekhonov","but the same cluster still","2026-01-07T12:34:54.310Z"],["3793044","MLC-3817","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","[~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff] typically we’d also reach out to IT team here that we have an email address set up for ride receipts in the launch country. I imagine we already have this for Italy as we have micromobility there, but shared access to [this ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-303911] with you so you have a template of what to request.\n\nRide receipt localisations are in [this sheet|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1bJBrUJh3QFzrthHlR0W_PT0k9-2HytBHE0ZcGbgpREA/edit?gid=226343535#gid=226343535]. They’ve already been done by Mirko (previous GM for Italy) but I see he marked a couple rows with ?, so you can reach out to the local team to confirm what translations should be there (following our call about localisations tomorrow, since I imagine we’ll discuss there who the POC will be for translations)","2026-01-07T12:35:06.367Z"],["3793046","LSS-61082","LSS","alina.eversone@bolt.eu","Alina Eversone","[~accountid:712020:714baa0e-ddd0-4776-8064-c5a5d3ae37aa] requested reference for  *Bolt Operations UK Ltd*. (thank you)\nShe will upload it as soon as we will get reply.","2026-01-07T12:35:17.626Z"],["3793047","DBRE-8678","DBRE","konstantin.peshekhonov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Peshekhonov","if nothing will be lost as of now and we plan to redo this cron, let’s stop it","2026-01-07T12:35:20.376Z"],["3793048","DBRE-8678","DBRE","konstantin.peshekhonov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Peshekhonov","just monitor that captures are okay after it","2026-01-07T12:35:27.327Z"],["3793049","MLC-3813","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","[Localisation ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-99789]","2026-01-07T12:35:51.233Z"],["3793051","CMO-12963","CMO","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","06.01 update shared with working group - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C096QFSNMD0/p1767709073993849|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C096QFSNMD0/p1767709073993849|smart-link] \n\n\n\n*Deck Localisation Wrap Up; Review Phase Initiation*Hi team! Sharing an update on the deck localisation progress.*Initial BPO Input - Done*\n\n\n*BPO Timeline.* Yesterday was the deadline for BPOs to adjust the decks. The majority of BPOs have marked their decks as ready for review. CNX is still working on 2 decks, which are expected to be finalised tomorrow.\n\n\n*BPO Effort.* Based on a preliminary spot check, markets took different approaches:\n\n* Some fully translated the decks\n* Some added only language-specific phrases\n* Some decks appear largely unchanged\n\nIn the next phase, we’ll review whether the adjustments are appropriate and identify any additional changes needed.*Next Stage - In-house Review*\n\n\n*Owner assignment.* In the deck trackers for each supplier, I’ve added:\n\n* A column identifying the Training Specialist owning each market\n* Additional status options\n* A new in-house comments column for feedback and notes\n\n*Training Specialist Comms.* Tomorrow, I’ll remind Training Specialists about the review phase kickoff and share detailed instructions. The goal of this phase is for Training Specialists to conduct a cosmetic review + partner with local TLs for a language-specific review. Comms are planned for tomorrow, as many team members are still on leave today.\n\n\n*TL Comms.* In parallel, I will also make a post about this initiative in [cs-trainers-leads-updates|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/GP3KLC83Z] channel (where we share training updates with TLs). The goal is to:\n\n* inform the leads that we will host this workshop for all in-house agents\n* set the expectation that their Training Specialist may reach out for help with the language-specific review.","2026-01-07T12:36:21.156Z"],["3793053","LSS-61140","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd], please allow me to loop you in this ticket. \n\nAs part of our engagement within the _Dialogue Social_, the ARPE (Authority for Social Relations on Employment Platforms) is requesting that we send anonymised data regarding the number of active drivers using our platform during the years 2024 and 2025. Their request is available for you to review in the attached letter which has been translated to English to facilitate your review. \n\nElisabetta and I have reviewed the Convention that the ARPE wants Bolt to sign in order to provide a framework for this transfer of data. We have also translated this document for you. We have made some minor amends and have no further issues to raise. We are waiting for [~accountid:712020:cf457436-e17c-4575-8d48-f2b9135ccc82] to respond to some of our questions in the document regarding the parties who will have access to this data and our right to review the final report drafted by the ARPE before publication.\n\nENG translations: \n\n* [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yTeWcRVVzsQRGE4eOQaL9zXvxrGf_XQG/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yTeWcRVVzsQRGE4eOQaL9zXvxrGf_XQG/edit|smart-link] (Letter received from ARPE)\n* [https://docs.google.com/document/d/17weaN04H9vH_Kp2kZ7-k__2pDnZZn-DL/edit#heading=h.30j0zll|https://docs.google.com/document/d/17weaN04H9vH_Kp2kZ7-k__2pDnZZn-DL/edit#heading=h.30j0zll|smart-link] (Convention governing the transfer of data)\n\nPlease could you review and let us know if you have any issues to raise regarding signing the convention and sending the requested data?\n\n[~accountid:712020:cf457436-e17c-4575-8d48-f2b9135ccc82] pending Privacy’s review, please could you review our comments in the document?\n\nThank you ! \n\ncc. [~accountid:5be58278903b2054a70c21b9] ","2026-01-07T12:36:56.453Z"],["3793055","CMO-12963","CMO","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","07.01- comms sent to IN training specialists and IH leads to kick off the review process\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C095AFVCXEJ/p1767785927710889|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C095AFVCXEJ/p1767785927710889|smart-link] \n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GP3KLC83Z/p1767786523678859|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GP3KLC83Z/p1767786523678859|smart-link] \ndetailed instructions - [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1AOU6d3BsAMKhV94pUjIdM0Y-rkZhAcfSR-BIpYnzmfU/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1AOU6d3BsAMKhV94pUjIdM0Y-rkZhAcfSR-BIpYnzmfU/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T12:37:37.268Z"],["3793057","RNTL-30266","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","based on [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tShyDj6qCeLqpuXi8VGgyMCrvqUqgyP68Aa81D6_qs4/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.8eaxfysd53oz|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tShyDj6qCeLqpuXi8VGgyMCrvqUqgyP68Aa81D6_qs4/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.8eaxfysd53oz|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T12:38:05.112Z"],["3793060","CSXRD-260","CSXRD","aleksandra.menio@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Menio","* Articles updated\n* Announcement sent\n\n\n\nNext step: Will analyze next 5 articles related to the compensations. ","2026-01-07T12:38:08.055Z"],["3793063","LSS-61118","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached. Delivery will be organised ASAP.\n\n[^PoA_Bolt Services PL Sp. z o.o._Piotr Garbacz_07.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T12:38:55.331Z"],["3793064","RNTL-30266","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","also fix the ambiguous UX of 3 feedback dashboard filter (include cancelled rides yes/no)\n\n\n\n* [+Arvind Jayashankar+|mailto:arvind.jayashankar@bolt.eu] - Can you clarify what the ‘yes’ and ‘no’ check boxes mean exactly as the wording is a bit confusing. When only ‘no’ is selected on board 3, boards 1 and 3 match. We’re assuming ‘no’ checked excludes short and canceled rides. We get different results when both ‘yes’ and ‘no’ are checked, and when only ‘yes’ is checked.\n** No ✔️- short and canceled rides excluded\n** No ✔️+ Yes ✔️- means what?\n** Yes ✔️ - means what?","2026-01-07T12:38:56.114Z"],["3793065","DRAG101-455","DRAG101","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","All the tests that have been done and are on going can be found from this page: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RNTL/pages/7118520382/D3+-Testing|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RNTL/pages/7118520382/D3+-Testing|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T12:38:59.326Z"],["3793066","RNTL-30266","RNTL","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:5d773c785a4d810d2c4de81c] let’s also clarify how measure “[Percent of Rides with Negative Feedback|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/rental/order_order?qid=VxwTgEjSekaEUiIYSxZtiO&origin_space=5890&toggle=fil,vis]” field is calculated. Does it look at all rides, rides which were not cancelled or something else?","2026-01-07T12:39:22.047Z"],["3793069","LSS-58825","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Finalised agreement\n\n[^Lease Office 34 Silkstone House.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T12:39:51.735Z"],["3793070","MLC-3814","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","[~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff] list of growth comms (canvases/campaigns) that need to be localised:\n\n# Basic to Bolt\n# Basic to Women for Women\n# Bolt to Premium\n# Bolt to Comfort\n# Reactivating Premium Users\n# Reactivating Comfort Users\n# Bolt to XL\n# Notify about nearby cities\n# Popular Destinations\n# Airport Fares\n# Weekend to Weekday\n# Weekday to Weekend\n# Pushing to 8th ride\n# Pushing to 10th ride\n# Frequency - Urban commute\n# Frequency - Social events\n# Frequency - Errands\n\nYou can reach out to the local team to confirm which ones are actually relevant to the market before you submit the localisation request (once you’ve mapped out the Crowdin links for them to review).","2026-01-07T12:40:00.201Z"],["3793071","PFI-829509","PFI","roman.igaz@bolt.eu","Roman Igaz","Hey [~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56], adding to what [~accountid:712020:891b9409-10db-4442-9b0c-57416d584827] has raised above - earlier in 2025 we were not displaying the VAT rate on the food invoices for the customers. This had been changed somewhere around October 2025. Do you happen to know why? \nIf we do not display the VAT on the food invoice we sent to the eater, we have no issue. ","2026-01-07T12:40:00.515Z"],["3793073","MLC-3815","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","[~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff] list of churn comms (canvases) that need to be set up:\n\n# We Miss You\n# We Miss You Loyal Riders\n# User Campaign Received Percentage, Churning","2026-01-07T12:40:53.478Z"],["3793074","HS-28659","HS","refilwe@bolt.eu","Refilwe Masanabo","Hello Berit. Thank you! Just one request with the travel dates, please. Can we indicate travel dates as: 16 Feb - 20 Feb. My return flight is on the 20th. These are the same dates on the invitation letter. Thanks.","2026-01-07T12:41:17.710Z"],["3793077","LSS-61125","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached. Delivery will be organised ASAP.\n\n[^PoA_Bolt Teknoloji Anonim Sirketi_Talip Bozkurt_07.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T12:42:34.840Z"],["3793078","HS-28685","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","waiting for PQ","2026-01-07T12:42:39.039Z"],["3793079","PFI-816808","PFI","peter.vrba@bolt-outsource.eu","Peter Vrba","Hi, any news please?\n\n","2026-01-07T12:42:40.299Z"],["3793081","RNTL-29746","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","Jan 9 → Jan 13-14\n\n[~accountid:712020:e77ef51b-4584-479b-bc00-b172e7475d2e] ","2026-01-07T12:42:53.951Z"],["3793083","PFI-830557","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-07T12:43:05.109Z"],["3793084","PFI-830557","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:5d8df399c7d4e30dc2836580] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-07T12:43:06.567Z"],["3793085","LSS-60240","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","I updated the ENG part in the bilingual version in this document: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1arg1hmveJDrFoEc-ZJETpuhwwScij5srnOemnsc0y8Q/edit?tab=t.2hq8cux4ou02|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1arg1hmveJDrFoEc-ZJETpuhwwScij5srnOemnsc0y8Q/edit?tab=t.2hq8cux4ou02|smart-link] \n\nPlease match the Thai translation accordingly. Once done, please let me know and I’ll get these uploaded to our web.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-07T12:43:23.673Z"],["3793086","DRX-27973","DRX","ajinkya.deshmukh@bolt.eu","Ajinkya Suhas Deshmukh","Tested Driver Coach banner on DA and DI.\n\n!DriverCoach.mp4|width=320,alt=\"DriverCoach.mp4\"!","2026-01-07T12:43:37.855Z"],["3793088","DLVR-291","DLVR","marleen.parmakson@bolt.eu","Marleen Parmakson","Hi [~accountid:70121:ee1db84d-628e-425d-8dbf-b29d08232b2a] Are there any commercial terms included in the contract (discounts, bonuses, other special terms) that would require Finance reporting review?","2026-01-07T12:44:23.347Z"],["3793089","PFI-829032","PFI","lilian.thomas@bolt-outsource.eu","Lilian Thomas","The driver’s issue isn’t related to a payout, but to a campaign bonus deduction from their balance. Please advise which request type should be selected.","2026-01-07T12:44:32.033Z"],["3793090","WFM-9843","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541592|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541592]","2026-01-07T12:44:54.468Z"],["3793093","WFM-9843","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Hey [~accountid:5d6cc1f8dc6e480dbc01e946] Request has been submitted and is pending approval, we will confirm once approved.","2026-01-07T12:45:16.381Z"],["3793094","GRWA-1461","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","[Slack post|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08UX5MD6AH/p1767732950373889?thread_ts=1767687273.845439&cid=C08UX5MD6AH]","2026-01-07T12:45:20.142Z"],["3793096","WD-22477","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","[~accountid:712020:04a4dca9-f17a-4d4d-9882-7b195bc04f23] - please can you approve for me to extend?","2026-01-07T12:45:39.779Z"],["3793097","LSS-60367","LSS","gabriela.patrichi@bolt.eu","Gabriela Patrichi","Thank you!!","2026-01-07T12:45:43.527Z"],["3793098","MLC-3765","MLC","lorrayne.oliveira@bolt.eu","Lorrayne Corais","* Automated communications are now live for Malmö (SE), Kaunas (LT), Bratislava (SK) and Klaipeda (LT). (/) ","2026-01-07T12:46:03.370Z"],["3793099","SCM-841","SCM","omar.masum@bolt.eu","Omar Faruk Masum","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1IyuqRFU2vO38xlgOHG-kK-tXEEUcok7ddv4zcC-PUi0/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1IyuqRFU2vO38xlgOHG-kK-tXEEUcok7ddv4zcC-PUi0/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] \n- Monthly Average forecast usage done - _Tab: Dashboard Network Level_. Also separated EU and NON-EU counties data in different tab\n- Monthly Seasonality % change data also bring in this file under _Tab: Seasonality %_\n- 8 Weeks consumption data bring to SP Procurement Dashboard for better overview: _Column AI_ alone with all time average consumption data in _Column AH_\n\n","2026-01-07T12:47:14.305Z"],["3793101","LSS-59427","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thank you[~accountid:5d0c7ac70f1d390c4db46fed]! It is however, still unclear to me if the EUR 600k includes the food order value or only the delivery fees? ","2026-01-07T12:47:46.223Z"],["3793103","LSS-57150","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:5fbf9493f8b0120069af2a45] yes sure. Thank you ","2026-01-07T12:47:49.981Z"],["3793105","SCM-1074","SCM","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","Preload 10Nm can be added only when the handle of the clamp is in closed position. Otherwise the clamp will be stucked and the locking/unlocking function do not work anymore and it is very easy to brake the handle.\n\n|!5f16931bc03591ad4d224bbd4a88fb0a-20260107-124750.jpg|width=459,alt=\"5f16931bc03591ad4d224bbd4a88fb0a-20260107-124750.jpg\"!|!f627a4ece8189897b17a144178e8b788-20260107-124756.jpg|width=260,alt=\"f627a4ece8189897b17a144178e8b788-20260107-124756.jpg\"!|\n\nSimulation data:\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"8571b93e-05c8-4491-a0d8-3bb1a8f70ec8\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"50N\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"100N\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"150N\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"150N\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" reinforced solution 2006.01.09\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"volume: 22.9 cm3\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"weight: 61.8 g\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"YCX 3D model\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"volume: 32.67 cm3\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"weight: 88g\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"YCX has followed BOLT design but added 1.5mm extra wall thickness to the handle outer surfaces\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":323,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260108-122538.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260108-122538.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1283,\"width\":1849}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Max stress: 46.6 MPa\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":323,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260108-122438.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260108-122438.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1282,\"width\":1746}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Max stress: 93.3 MPa\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":323,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260108-122640.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260108-122640.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1278,\"width\":1751}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Max stress: 139.9 MPa\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"SimScale\"}]},{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":323,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260109-130324.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260109-130324.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1599,\"width\":2195}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Max stress: 80.3 MPa\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"SolidWorks\"}]},{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":262,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260109-140401.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260109-140401.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1352,\"width\":2480}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Max stress: 81.8 MPa\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":216,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260112-111914.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260112-111914.png\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-1711628516\",\"height\":1069,\"width\":1385}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Max stress: 54 MPa\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Max stress on handlebar: 39 MPa\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":324,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260108-121846.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260108-121846.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1282,\"width\":1754}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Deformation: 0.46 mm\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":324,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260108-122801.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260108-122801.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1279,\"width\":1746}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Deformation: 0.93 mm\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":324,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260108-122722.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260108-122722.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1282,\"width\":1748}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Deformation: 1.39 mm\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":323,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260109-130035.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260109-130035.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1595,\"width\":2181}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Deformation: 0.8 mm\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":262,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260109-140454.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260109-140454.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1354,\"width\":2380}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Deformation: 0.82 mm\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":216,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260112-112041.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260112-112041.png\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-1711628516\",\"height\":1066,\"width\":1379}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Deformation: 0.32 mm\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":323,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260108-123251.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260108-123251.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1114,\"width\":1680}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":323,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260108-123158.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260108-123158.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1125,\"width\":1473}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":323,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260108-123332.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260108-123332.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1125,\"width\":1467}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":332,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260109-130241.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260109-130241.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1457,\"width\":1927}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":262,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260109-140638.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260109-140638.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1671,\"width\":2499}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Over 28 MPa\"}]},{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":262,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260109-140732.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260109-140732.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1619,\"width\":2467}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Over 70 MPa\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":216,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260112-112321.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260112-112321.png\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-1711628516\",\"height\":1130,\"width\":1605}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Over 30 MPa\"}]},{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":216,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260112-112221.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260112-112221.png\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-1711628516\",\"height\":1129,\"width\":1610}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Over 40 MPa\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n\n\nHandle production method: ADC12 material, after die casting, polishing, water grinding, painting\n\n\n\nADC12 die casting and Al6061 comparison:\n\n!image-20260108-121159.png|width=694,alt=\"image-20260108-121159.png\"!\n\n!image-20260108-121250.png|width=706,alt=\"image-20260108-121250.png\"!","2026-01-07T12:48:20.193Z"],["3793106","LSS-61126","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed PoA attached. Delivery will be organised ASAP.\n\n[^PoA_Bolt Services CZ s.r.o._SPZ SERVIS s.r.o._07.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T12:48:20.177Z"],["3793107","RDXENG-4466","RDXENG","juri.noga@bolt.eu","Juri Noga","Waiting for design decision.","2026-01-07T12:48:34.342Z"],["3793108","SREC-355","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Deleted Ansible code","2026-01-07T12:48:53.127Z"],["3793112","HS-28696","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","Hey Nika,\n\nI just sent you the PIT-2 form to fill and sign to your personal email. Once filled and signed, I will share this with our Payroll team.\n\nKind regards,\n\nKristin - People Ops","2026-01-07T12:49:54.103Z"],["3793117","LSS-57150","LSS","roman.igaz@bolt.eu","Roman Igaz","[~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f], great. Could you please prepare the agreement to be signed with Eliáš Mitra with the repayment schedule you mentioned in one of the replies above?","2026-01-07T12:51:04.645Z"],["3793120","DLVR-291","DLVR","nikolai.zenevitsh@bolt.eu","Nikolai Zenevitsh","Nope, not in this one! Just some local terms on marketing and dynamic commission\n\n_This comment was left via Slack._","2026-01-07T12:51:49.840Z"],["3793122","PFI-830569","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^comprobante_2419468085.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-07T12:52:01.682Z"],["3793125","CLIENTAPP-38759","CLIENTAPP","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","Tested the ticket on CA.192.0 (4000) on Pixel 8a - Android 16 & Pixel 4a - Android 13\n\nVerified that user is able to see both buttons on the “Trusted contacts” screen when there is no contact added in the list\n\nAttaching the screenshot for reference:\n\n!Screenshot_20260107-144210.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260107-144210.png\"!\n\n\n\nFixed","2026-01-07T12:54:55.498Z"],["3793127","WFM-9843","WFM","jalal.safarli@bolt.eu","Jalal Safarli","Thank you [~accountid:5b31360d7b8c14625a47e4f5] 🙏 ","2026-01-07T12:56:03.002Z"],["3793128","PC-4468","PC","kevin.kanarbik@bolt.eu","Kevin Kanarbik","Status update!\n\nThe proposed solution of just using {{payment_attempt_id}} instead of {{payment_action_id}} as {{reference}} in the [SF Refund request|https://docs.silverflow.com/apidocs/latest/index.html#tag/Charge-Actions/operation/refund] will FAIL because this reference in SF’s vault will later be used when processing this async refund command in {{ChargesActionNotificationService.getPaymentAttemptIdAndActionMetadata()}}\nThere it will need the {{payment_action_id}} to be used as an event that is eventually used by {{PaymentAttemptEntity.getPaymentActionById()}} where it will fail if the ID is incorrect aka if it is {{payment_attempt_id}} instead. What to do?\n\nOne idea would be to change the reference to contain also the action ID for this `{{getPaymentAttemptIdAndActionMetadata}}` but this would defeat the original purpose of the rewrite → put something as reference for Silverflow that doesn’t change like action ID changes after every retry.\n\nDiscussed with [~accountid:60717fb3edc14f0076ca5a3e] and we came up with this solution: {{ChargesActionNotificationService}}’s uses two SF explicit objects - {{SilverflowCharge}}which comes from[ this API |https://docs.silverflow.com/apidocs/latest/index.html#tag/Create-Recurring/operation/createChargeMit] and {{SilverflowChargeAction}} which comes from[ here|https://docs.silverflow.com/apidocs/latest/index.html#tag/Charge-Actions/operation/getAction]. {{SilverflowCharge}}has a field called {{transactionReference}} that we POST in {{SilverflowExternalAPi.createUnreferencedMitCharge}} and we put {{paymentAttemptId}} as {{transactionReference}}. As stated before, currently {{paymentActionId}} is used as {{reference}} currently as the {{SilverflowChargeAction}}\n\nThus the proposed solution is to switch these ID-s between each other: {{paymentAttemptId}} will be in {{SilverflowChargeAction.reference}} and {{paymentActionId}} will be in {{SilverflowCharge.transactionReference}} These IDs are used only in this refund flow in specific places so the rewrite will be small.\n\nThe only issue will be with the migration and deployment since we’re talking about async MQ processes - of an event is posted to the queue with the old {{paymentActionId}} reference and we deploy and the new deployed solution will expect a different event with {{paymentAttemptId}} as reference then we’ll get errors so we need to think about migration. One idea would be to stop the queue during deployment.\n\n[~accountid:61de8e0e7c6f980070b38d2b] please review this and we can sync about this possible change.\n","2026-01-07T12:56:27.167Z"],["3793132","WEBSD-1442","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf]  👋 \n\nI hope you ar e doing great.\n\nI cannot work with this structure you have in these documents because there is a table hidden and makes our editor to add a big table.\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.55.37.png|width=632,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.55.37.png\"!\n\n\n\nPlease remove the table and if you manage to add the numbered list manually is even better to do a quick copy and paste.\n\nPlease let me know your comments \n\nRegards,","2026-01-07T12:57:30.969Z"],["3793135","LSS-59427","LSS","lukas.kulertas@bolt.eu","Lukas Kulertas","[~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] total order value (food+delivery)","2026-01-07T12:57:58.740Z"],["3793136","RNTL-30272","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","Hey team!\nCould we get data on scooter battery cycle counts?\nThe SQL I made currently shows the battery cycle count, the BMS serial, the last scooter IoT ID the battery was in, the scooter model, and the timestamp when the data was created.\n\nQuery:\n\n{noformat}WITH ranked AS (\n  SELECT\n    device_id,\n    created,\n\n    get_json_object(message_json, '$.scooter.bmsSerial') AS bms_serial,\n\n    get_json_object(message_json, '$.scooter.scooterType') AS scooter_model,\n\n    CAST(\n      get_json_object(message_json, '$.scooter.batteryInfo.boltBattery.cycleCount')\n      AS INT\n    ) AS cycle_count,\n\n    row_number() OVER (\n      PARTITION BY get_json_object(message_json, '$.scooter.bmsSerial')\n      ORDER BY created DESC\n    ) AS rn\n  FROM ng_rental_spark.rental_iot_mngmt_global_scoot\n  WHERE created_date = date_format(current_date(), 'yyyy-MM-dd')\n    AND message_json LIKE '{\"configuration\":%'\n    AND message_json LIKE '%\"cycleCount\"%'\n)\n\nSELECT\n  cycle_count,\n  bms_serial,\n  device_id AS last_scooter_id,\n  scooter_model,\n  created\nFROM ranked\nWHERE rn = 1\n  AND bms_serial IS NOT NULL;{noformat}","2026-01-07T12:58:17.097Z"],["3793137","RNTL-30272","RNTL",null,"Slack","[Dmitry Zamaleev|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d773c785a4d810d2c4de81c] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C030MJW96CA/p1767605797964779?thread_ts=1767605797.964779&cid=C030MJW96CA|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C030MJW96CA/p1767605797964779?thread_ts=1767605797.964779&cid=C030MJW96CA|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-07T12:58:18.305Z"],["3793138","RNTL-30272","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","[@norman.tamm|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:8d272f38-d046-4ad2-a5b3-a47b219e9fa1] hey, you want us to validate the sql or to run it against db?","2026-01-07T12:58:18.696Z"],["3793139","RNTL-30272","RNTL","norman.tamm@bolt.eu","Norman Tamm","Hey, sorry I should have been more clear. I would like to have this data available in Looker Explore.","2026-01-07T12:58:19.439Z"],["3793140","RNTL-30272","RNTL","norman.tamm@bolt.eu","Norman Tamm","We would like to get the battery cycle count in to this dimension:\n\n[https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/rental/rental_battery_report_battery_state?qid=Nf9EadBEaPzNQjsmZIsVlX|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/rental/rental_battery_report_battery_state?qid=Nf9EadBEaPzNQjsmZIsVlX]","2026-01-07T12:58:20.264Z"],["3793142","CEBF-1759","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","[~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] I found a [https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.my.salesforce-setup.com/lightning/setup/ObjectManager/Opportunity/ValidationRules/03dTs0000000WeDIAU/view|https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.my.salesforce-setup.com/lightning/setup/ObjectManager/Opportunity/ValidationRules/03dTs0000000WeDIAU/view]\n\n\n{noformat}IF(AND( $User.Alias != 'aauto', $User.Alias != 'admin', $User.Alias != 'guest', $User.ProfileId != '00e7Q000002x35r'),\nAND(\nAND(ISPICKVAL(StageName, 'Won'), RecordType.DeveloperName == 'Sales_Opportunity'),\nAND(Account.Country__c != 'Ukraine',Account.Country__c != 'Azerbaijan',Account.Country__c != 'Ghana',Account.Country__c != 'Kenya'),\nISBLANK(Account.Link_to_registration_certificate__c)), false){noformat}\n\nI can move logic by Country from the hardcode to the [https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.my.salesforce-setup.com/lightning/setup/CustomMetadata/page?address=%2Fm08%3Fsetupid%3DCustomMetadata|https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.my.salesforce-setup.com/lightning/setup/CustomMetadata/page?address=%2Fm08%3Fsetupid%3DCustomMetadata]\n\nWhat do you think?","2026-01-07T12:59:34.659Z"],["3793146","SREP-145","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","Contact with DAP team, got input, made a schemas with common overview how’s it communicates: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/7361691788/SREP+DAP+eks+communications+schemas|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/7361691788/SREP+DAP+eks+communications+schemas|smart-link]  ","2026-01-07T12:59:49.356Z"],["3793149","PFA-559","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","Try to explore in Looker MCP","2026-01-07T12:59:59.686Z"],["3793155","SREP-1044","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* Control plane updated \n* kube-proxy updated\n* All nodes reprovisioned \n\n!image-20260107-130057.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260107-130057.png\"!\n\nNo issues so far ","2026-01-07T13:01:36.515Z"],["3793156","PFI-830570","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-07T13:01:40.145Z"],["3793159","LSS-59427","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thank you [~accountid:5d0c7ac70f1d390c4db46fed] ! ","2026-01-07T13:02:27.095Z"],["3793160","SREP-1046","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* Control plane updated\n* kube-proxy updated\n* All nodes reprovisioned\n\n!image-20260107-130208.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260107-130208.png\"!\n\nNo issues so far ","2026-01-07T13:02:29.821Z"],["3793161","PFI-830576","PFI","mariam.omogoye@bolt-outsource.eu","Mariam Omogoye","!{0D35CAE2-2DE8-4532-95ED-48C62D1AA59E}-20260107-125920.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T13:02:31.226Z"],["3793162","WD-22487","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Hi Matthew, this is because your job change has not been fully concluded in WD, please refer to your manager","2026-01-07T13:02:38.511Z"],["3793163","DSR-3351","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC, we can answer the following:\n\n{quote}Dear [name],\n\nThank you for your data subject request, which was received by us on *[date].*\n\nFollowing a review of our records, we can confirm that a limited set of your personal data — specifically your name, email address, and phone number — was shared with our partner, Eternis.\n\nThis transfer was carried out strictly based on your explicit consent, which was requested via clear in-app messaging that outlined the purpose of the transfer (to enable Eternis to provide you with promotional offers).\n\nYou were presented with this consent request on two separate occasions (25 April 2025 and 13 May 2025), and on each occasion, you affirmatively confirmed your consent.\n\nThe consent serves as the legal basis for the processing under Article 6(1)(a) of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). As per GDPR requirements, you were informed of the data transfer and its purposes in advance via the consent prompts. \n\nFor information on how we process relevant personal data, we refer you to our Privacy Policy at [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|smart-link] , which includes further information about:\n\n* The categories of personal data we process;\n* The purposes for which we process personal data;\n* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom the personal data has been or will be disclosed;\n* The criteria we use to determine how long to retain personal data;\n* The sources of personal data received from other parties;\n* Your rights in relation to your personal data;\n* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making/profiling of personal data; and\n* Details of any transfer of your personal data to third countries or international organisations and the safeguards used for any such transfers.\n\n*Your rights* \n\nIn addition to your right to access any personal data we hold about you, you have the right to request us to rectify, erase your personal data, restrict the processing of your personal data or to object to such processing. Any such requests that are received will be considered in conjunction with the applicable provisions of relevant data protection laws. \n\nIf you are dissatisfied with this response to your request or in relation to any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve them. You also have the right to complain directly to your data protection/supervisory authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek a judicial remedy.\n\nIf you have any additional questions, please contact our Customer Support Team by replying to this email.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nBolt{quote}","2026-01-07T13:02:58.224Z"],["3793165","PFI-830577","PFI","vadim.kozjakov@bolt.eu","Vadim Kozjakov","[^1002319-CZ1125-33406.pdf]\n\n[^1002319-CZ1125-33611.pdf]","2026-01-07T13:03:09.862Z"],["3793166","SREP-1047","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* Control plane updated\n* kube-proxy updated\n* All nodes reprovisioned\n\n!image-20260107-130307.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260107-130307.png\"!\n\n\n\nNo issues so far","2026-01-07T13:03:11.035Z"],["3793167","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Thanks for handling this :pray:","2026-01-07T13:03:10.769Z"],["3793169","PFI-830577","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-07T13:03:11.920Z"],["3793171","WD-20519","WD","janeli.niinemaa@bolt.eu","Janeli Niinemaa","Hey! Sorry for the delay! Can we please move forward with adding the error message that for learning and development activity, Talent (HQ) cost center should be used? And then route the approval to *Michał Lindenberg* as said above. \n\n\n\nWe will also update the expense items list in Confluence too. ","2026-01-07T13:03:40.083Z"],["3793173","MLC-3765","MLC","lorrayne.oliveira@bolt.eu","Lorrayne Corais","* Automated communications are live for Warsaw, Bucharest, Rzeszow, Bialystok, Poznan, Bydgoszcz and Porto. (/) \n\n* Still waiting the localisation for UA.  :loading: ","2026-01-07T13:04:22.585Z"],["3793174","SREP-1043","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* Control plane updated\n* kube-proxy updated\n* All nodes reprovisioned\n\n!image-20260107-130419.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260107-130419.png\"!\n\nNo issues so far","2026-01-07T13:04:24.183Z"],["3793175","DPX-3550","DPX","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","Verified that now there is a cooldown period (depending on the [configuration value|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/dynamic-config/entity/edit/ZHAtdWtyYWluZS1haXItYWxlcnQvb3JkZXJfZmFpbHVyZV9kZWxheV9zZWNvbmRz/:shard]) which prevents creating false expectations to the user.","2026-01-07T13:04:29.044Z"],["3793176","PFI-829471","PFI","laura.loaiza@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Muñoz","New case: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719397707|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719397707]\n\nBusiness profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/354116?tab=business_company|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/354116?tab=business_company]","2026-01-07T13:04:39.298Z"],["3793181","PFI-830171","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi,\n\nEC has been disabled for the driver.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-07T13:06:54.387Z"],["3793182","LSS-60602","LSS","martyna.puksmyte@bolt.eu","Martyna Pukšmytė","Hi Elīna,\n\nThank you for the detailed explanation and guidance.\n\nI would like to inform you that we have already resolved the situation. The case was assessed and the response to the user was prepared, so no further Legal involvement is required at this stage.\n\nThank you again for your support and helpful recommendations.","2026-01-07T13:06:55.306Z"],["3793184","PFI-830437","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi,\n\nEC has been enabled for the driver.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-07T13:07:13.253Z"],["3793185","PFI-829471","PFI","laura.loaiza@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Muñoz","New case: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719171628|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719171628]\n\nBusiness profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/263902?tab=business_company|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/263902?tab=business_company]","2026-01-07T13:07:26.451Z"],["3793187","RDXENG-4271","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","*Tested on CA.192.0 and OK* (/) ","2026-01-07T13:08:36.009Z"],["3793191","LSS-61151","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nAs this is a business-critical tool, we are ok to keep the auto-renewal in place. This does not prevent us from negotiating the terms, am I right?\n\nIf so, let’s proceed with the signature.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-07T13:09:30.040Z"],["3793192","WEBSD-1452","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi! 👋 \n\nThere are 2 options here:\n\n1.- We can add some link in some part of the text but you need to point out where (Chinese and English) and then they will be able to see the pdf for that certificate once they click the link.\n\n2.- I can create a separate link (It will be added in the list of the files) under [https://bolt.eu/en-tw/legal/?category=other|https://bolt.eu/en-tw/legal/?category=other|smart-link]  and they will be able to see the image as pdf but I will need the titles (Name of the links) for Chinese and English.\n\nPlease let me know your comments. \n\nRegards,","2026-01-07T13:09:31.890Z"],["3793201","LSS-56686","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] , hey! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^PoA_Portugal1.pdf] \n\nI will share the tracking number soon.","2026-01-07T13:10:32.503Z"],["3793202","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Closing as DB owners will remove this cron.","2026-01-07T13:10:37.416Z"],["3793205","PFI-830581","PFI","andre.trahhov@bolt-outsource.eu","Andre Trahhov","[^Kviitung_RD311875850.pdf]","2026-01-07T13:10:56.704Z"],["3793206","SREDESK-7384","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Order-eu alter has started at 2026-01-07 15:00 EET","2026-01-07T13:11:05.024Z"],["3793207","WD-22465","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","Hi [~accountid:712020:b73d65c1-8791-4157-9850-c426365a190b] \n\nThe 5 personal days were added for you. \nRegarding annual leave - The Estonian *Annual Leave is 20 WORKING days* meaning you have the correct amount.\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BILP/pages/1596654634/Estonia#Holidays-and-Time-Off-%F0%9F%8C%B4|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BILP/pages/1596654634/Estonia#Holidays-and-Time-Off-%F0%9F%8C%B4|smart-link] \nHope this was helpful.\nKind regards,\n\nDarja ","2026-01-07T13:11:05.227Z"],["3793218","PFI-830582","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^Pago Bolt mes de diciembre B00TU4QGT.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-07T13:13:11.471Z"],["3793219","MKP-9753","MKP","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","Some suggestion for matching system : [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7241499344/DRAFT+Auto+acceptance+for+price+confirmation+FOO+custom+pricing+Upsell|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7241499344/DRAFT+Auto+acceptance+for+price+confirmation+FOO+custom+pricing+Upsell|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T13:13:19.174Z"],["3793220","L10N-26330","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26329](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26329)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-07T13:13:20.957Z"],["3793221","L10N-26335","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26329](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26329)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-07T13:13:22.273Z"],["3793222","L10N-26333","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation