s that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26329](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26329)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-07T13:13:27.834Z"],["3793230","INT-777","INT","alexander.tsyba@bolt.eu","Alexander Tsyba","[~accountid:63d0ecc2f386bda5dcab9d6e] for 1. - don’t understand what you want to say with it?\n2. No we don’t. I thought we are not doing that. Only cost-shared and fully merchant funded\n3. The only difference is in pausing now, so message can either say that campaigns will be blocked, or current are blocked, so perhaps we can list active campaigns that are paused.","2026-01-07T13:13:58.425Z"],["3793231","BB-2268","BB","ahmad.eldefrawy@bolt.eu","Ahmad ElDefrawy","Create new Epic and move this and [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BB-2267|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BB-2267|smart-link] along with an RFC document ticket","2026-01-07T13:14:05.197Z"],["3793232","SREC-359","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Doesn’t seem like this can be done in the UI. I’ve created a support ticket.","2026-01-07T13:14:05.565Z"],["3793233","LSS-60602","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thank you very much for the update [~accountid:712020:d1f60be9-f6ea-4a65-975f-93235797e04e]! Kindly follow my below recommendation for future cases 🙂 ","2026-01-07T13:14:36.872Z"],["3793235","LSS-60694","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi [~accountid:712020:7a9c1391-243a-422e-806d-72d75be13638] at first glance it does look like an internal code for their employees, however, it is drafted with wide application and expressly also extends to commercial partners, so it applies to us as well (though, most likely not in its entirety). The relevant wording is:\n\n{quote}“This Code of Ethics applies to all AIM Group operators … consultants, suppliers, commercial partners and all those who … act on behalf of the Company.”{quote}\n\nThis structure indeed is quite standard, the main point to be aware of is that a breach of the Code of Ethics gives them a contractual right to terminate the agreement.\n\nIf you’re comfortable proceeding on that basis, the only remaining item is the contracting details. Since the document is in PDF format (and editing it via GDoc would disrupt the formatting), you can provide the company details directly.\n\nAs confirmed by yourself earlier, the contracting entity will be:\n\n*Bolt Operations OÜ*\nVAT: *EE102090374*\nAddress: *Vana-Lõuna tn 15, Kesklinna linnaosa, 10134 Tallinn, Harju maakond*\nInvoice contact info: I’m not so sure what’s the standard operating procedure - I was able to find that the following email applies for invoices to Bolt Ops OU [invoices.ops@bolt.eu|mailto:invoices.bfy@bolt.eu] however if you prefer to receive invoices to your personal work email then please use that. \n\nThank you! \n","2026-01-07T13:15:18.203Z"],["3793236","SREDO-395","SREDO","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","Duplicate of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDO-394|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDO-394|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T13:15:34.004Z"],["3793238","RF-63","RF","siddhant.saxena@bolt.eu","Siddhant Saxena","CS Notebook : [https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/4137099874156693?o=3598988355446810|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/4137099874156693?o=3598988355446810]","2026-01-07T13:16:01.505Z"],["3793239","DSR-3567","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-07T13:16:05.372Z"],["3793240","CRC-2288","CRC","shubashini.chandran@bolt.eu","Shuba Chandran","*Payments Expansion update*\n\n# *Acquiring: Dlocal*\n## Contract awaiting to be signed on Partners end. \n# *Debt Collection: Dlocal* \n## Dlocal is using local collection agent called Wafacash\n## In parallel, Partner Payouts team will enable card payments for debt with our existing infrastructure. \n# *Payouts:* \n## If we use Chari bank accounts for driver payouts, will need to confirm with partner on the agreed file format. ","2026-01-07T13:16:34.406Z"],["3793241","DBRE-8595","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","Keep the old instances until [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7384|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7384|smart-link]  is resolved: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1767791559415069?thread_ts=1767778665.045829&cid=GFGTF111A|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1767791559415069?thread_ts=1767778665.045829&cid=GFGTF111A].\n\nUPD: ok to destroy; destroyed.","2026-01-07T13:16:36.674Z"],["3793242","PFI-830584","PFI","alijan.dias@bolt.eu","Alijan Keval","!37f4ed84-2431-49f7-afae-b3ed33253859.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!image (2).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T13:17:14.424Z"],["3793243","BP-13349","BP","sebastian.kurpios@bolt.eu","Sebastian Kurpios","[~accountid:712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] FYI Final version from live env:\n\n* BOLT\n\n*business_portal_company_user_added*\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.03.22.png|width=914,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.03.22.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.03.37.png|width=438,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.03.37.png\"!\n\n\n\n*business_portal_company_existing_user_added*\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.04.12.png|width=437,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.04.12.png\"!\n\n\n\n* HOPP\n*business_portal_company_user_added*\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.04.58.png|width=914,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.04.58.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.05.12.png|width=421,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.05.12.png\"!\n\n*business_portal_company_existing_user_added*\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.05.23.png|width=433,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 14.05.23.png\"!","2026-01-07T13:17:46.910Z"],["3793244","RDXENG-4265","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","*Tested in CI.217.0 and OK* (/) ","2026-01-07T13:18:13.486Z"],["3793247","LSS-61041","LSS","adam.sokolowski@bolt.eu","Adam Sokołowski","hi [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] I just returned from a PTO\nI believe we should submit the claim - the company was a contract with us to deliver rides for 3 or 4 years and if they do not meet the KPIs to pay us back the invested amount.\n\n[~accountid:712020:228a835c-834d-4ca5-b7c2-ebedb4eb0356] do you have the contract signed with this fleet to review if there is a clause where we can instantly request the repayment in case they break the contract? ","2026-01-07T13:19:58.977Z"],["3793255","PFI-809450","PFI","nariman.abbasov@bolt.eu","Nariman Abbasov","this payout was bounced back to balance","2026-01-07T13:20:51.436Z"],["3793256","LSS-61171","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you [~accountid:712020:66939b2f-e5c1-42e2-8cbe-244458fd12f9], I have reached out to [~accountid:712020:8bcb68bd-f8da-4da1-8320-2536f6bb0c0c] who has been able to redirect me to a contact at Forvis Mazars. \n\nThis ticket can be closed, thanks","2026-01-07T13:20:57.220Z"],["3793259","HS-28663","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hi Giulia! I believe you should reach eligibility for 26 days annual leave in about two months. We have all the documentation needed, so nothing needed from you for now! The additional days will be added to your Workday account from the beginning of March.\n\nLet me know if you have any additional questions or concerns!","2026-01-07T13:21:13.594Z"],["3793260","PFI-830591","PFI","lina.kkolou@bolt.eu","Lina Kkolou","!Screenshot_2026-01-05-09-35-53-517_com.revolut.revolut.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T13:21:21.863Z"],["3793261","PFI-830555","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:93f92945-2c23-4781-9680-b6dd154892d8],\n\nThank you for bringing this into our attention.\nWe have suspended the user and their devices/payment methods.\nSeems like they were performing fraud via a Post-Paid business.\n\nAs this was performed via Post-Paid business and a market as strict as PT then the Fraud team does not have the jurisdiction to immediately block the business profile.\nIf possible, then I would recommend looking over this business: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/803477?tab=business_company|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/803477?tab=business_company] and confirming if we want them active on our platform. They have not yet passed the 1 month billing cycle, however, they have already generated almost up to -7000€ from 19th of December.\nIf possible, then please re-evaluate the business profile.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-07T13:21:30.906Z"],["3793263","LSS-61118","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Excellent, thank you!","2026-01-07T13:21:48.085Z"],["3793264","CRC-2178","CRC","shubashini.chandran@bolt.eu","Shuba Chandran","+*Payments Expansion Update*+\n\n*Customer Payments*\n\n* Network International to be ready Mid March.\n* Existing [+Checkout.com+|http://checkout.com/] connectivity as backup- it is really.\n\n*Partner Payments*\n\n* Partner Payments: [~accountid:5d50390ec6b9320d9ea58352] to help remind partner on the UAA form for Abu Dhabi bank accounts.\n*# Bank accounts are opened, but Bolt is not authorised to use these bank accounts.","2026-01-07T13:21:51.087Z"],["3793266","PAW-14680","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-admin-panel-automations, pint-product-workflow-and-automation-platform, pint-capability-process-automation\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-07T13:22:12.469Z"],["3793267","LSS-61208","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:33a1a5e8-52cb-4605-9ef3-0b89d57fe7b8] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^E-US Skarbowy Nicchiano (1).pdf] ","2026-01-07T13:22:44.855Z"],["3793268","CRC-1961","CRC","shubashini.chandran@bolt.eu","Shuba Chandran","Market deprioritised indefinitely. \n\nWill proceed to Payment Partners to Dlocal & Deutche Bank. ","2026-01-07T13:23:00.141Z"],["3793269","SREDESK-7384","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Order-zaf alter has started at 2026-01-07 15:23 EET","2026-01-07T13:23:10.776Z"],["3793270","CCM-22263","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey Karina 👋 \n\nThe test has been reset. ☀️ \n\nAll the best,\nIrena","2026-01-07T13:23:27.330Z"],["3793271","LSS-61151","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] then we can proceed with signing. Should we sign first and share pdf with Rootly or they will send signing request to us ? ","2026-01-07T13:23:30.409Z"],["3793272","LSS-56686","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432],\n\nCould you please put the shipment of the PoA on hold for the moment? I still need to provide you with a form in order to complete the registration.\n\nMany thanks!","2026-01-07T13:23:34.191Z"],["3793274","DSR-2999","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Status update:\n\n* Prepared an answer letter. We will re-send the full PDE from our end as well. IMO the Rider is seeking information about a specific ride they had an issue with (see note below) - in the answer letter, I have invited them to clarify what they are seeking so that we can investigate it clearly (thus promoting a collaborative approach)\n* [Checking|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06GYAPEM60/p1767791754584389] with engineers whether we can fix the way cancelled rides are displayed in PDE :loading: ","2026-01-07T13:23:57.850Z"],["3793282","SCM-790","SCM","omar.masum@bolt.eu","Omar Faruk Masum","[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] Each county references to the Non-EU below 4 countries- \n\n* United States of America\n* Ukraine\n* Kazakhstan\n* United Kingdom\n\nOrder will be created in half yearly with 1 month consumption + 6months buffer.\n\nInformation updated in “Reminder” tab","2026-01-07T13:26:01.861Z"],["3793283","LSS-56824","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] [~accountid:712020:590a0677-fdbb-4c13-9916-d32af1588d3e] , Please find the signed document(s) attached (via Profil zaufany)\n\n[^Pelnomocnictwo-pocztowe BOLT RIDES (3) (1).pdf]\n\n [^Pelnomocnictwo-pocztowe BOLT SERVICES PL (2) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-07T13:26:03.227Z"],["3793284","FIN2-937","FIN2","marleen.parmakson@bolt.eu","Marleen Parmakson","We have reviewed the draft agreement and concluded that from IFRS and reporting perspective, the draft agreement does not give rise to any new recognition, measurement, or disclosure requirements. Memo is documented [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hBM6d5hsJcjjQmOHfHS3eA5Rdjhq7iofehgkLH0vzZ4/edit?tab=t.0].","2026-01-07T13:26:27.641Z"],["3793285","LSS-56686","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Alright!","2026-01-07T13:26:44.019Z"],["3793286","PAW-16569","PAW",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the bug!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-07T13:27:25.327Z"],["3793287","WFM-9776","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Hey [~accountid:712020:d92e20dc-92b8-47fd-920c-26e5630a941a], \r\n\r\nThe queues have been added. How about Cyril? ","2026-01-07T13:27:32.136Z"],["3793289","CEBF-1759","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","[~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] are you sure we need to populate MT1 and MT2 to Close Lost the Opp?\n[https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.my.salesforce-setup.com/lightning/setup/ObjectManager/Opportunity/ValidationRules/03ddt0000008V8HAAU/view|https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.my.salesforce-setup.com/lightning/setup/ObjectManager/Opportunity/ValidationRules/03ddt0000008V8HAAU/view]","2026-01-07T13:27:43.362Z"],["3793292","WFM-9830","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","No problem. \nHave a great day, [~accountid:712020:920c01df-fbe5-497b-a992-6fd9b26d50eb].","2026-01-07T13:28:17.367Z"],["3793295","L10N-26349","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26346](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26346)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-07T13:28:51.229Z"],["3793296","L10N-26348","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi