 one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26346](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26346)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-07T13:29:04.172Z"],["3793305","DSR-3351","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Nice! Thank you! Answer has been sent to the driver ✅","2026-01-07T13:29:10.989Z"],["3793306","LSS-58865","LSS","jack.cook@bolt.eu","Jack Cook","[^AI_PJ_NDA_Employee_Ground_Transportation (1) (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T13:29:18.993Z"],["3793310","LSS-60824","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","Will be signed by: It will be Kobi Eisenberg, CEO, [kobi@autofleet.io|mailto:kobi@autofleet.io]\nPlease add for signing [~accountid:62a88aabd0132d0068800eba] ","2026-01-07T13:30:10.830Z"],["3793311","PFI-830584","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hello, \r\n\r\nWe have ongoing projects to validate the beneficiary name partially, however it's still under developement and adjustments with our banking partner. The transaction was fully processed by our side but apparently the beneficiary bank didn't claim it yet exactly due to the name mismatching. You can handle so far as internal fraud perhaps or request some clarification from the outsourced agent to idenfity the best way for compensation. \r\n\r\nUnfortunately we are not able to cancel or recall the payout, once the funds are already under the beneficiary's bank domain and the recall process demands certain amount of documentation to be filled and time. \r\n\r\nPlease address it properly internally and do let us know if some assistance related to the transaction would be requested. ","2026-01-07T13:30:18.582Z"],["3793313","PFI-830592","PFI","jelena.griciva@bolt-outsource.eu","Jelena Griciva","!20260107_111059.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T13:30:36.204Z"],["3793314","LSS-59991","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","FYI \n\n* Bolt Food’s market share in Cyprus is *below 15%*, and we are currently the *third player* in the market, behind *Wolt* and *Foody*.\n* Below are the communications exchanged by the Ops team with the Evolution team:\n\n_\"Thank you for your follow-up and for your ongoing interest in collaborating with Bolt Food.I understand your position regarding the importance of securing API access before proceeding with development. However, as previously mentioned, our team currently lacks the capacity for the technical support this integration requires. This includes more than just sharing the API, as it also involves setting up a dedicated testing environment, providing daily support, responding to technical queries, and conducting test calls.That being said, our integrations team can formally assess your solution for potential future collaboration. Please complete_ [_this_|https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd9nv-83pF7UEDTS9QQ4GDrYU0Uzjt_7YIKwOpl-7Q9qT4s0Q/viewform] _form.\"_\n*_----_*\n_\"As mentioned, your request is now with our central integrations team. This team prioritizes and oversees all integration projects, including those in Cyprus, based on criteria such as the number of integrated providers.I am happy to revisit this collaboration once you have a fully tested product with potential or existing Bolt Food partners successfully integrated and onboarded.\"_\n*_---_*_\"I understand your perspective, but I believe we are not fully aligned on the process. As mentioned previously, our decision to prioritize any new integration is based on criteria, such as a demonstrable business case supported by a number of existing or potential clients contributing a meaningful share of the market’s GMV. This is all I can disclose at this_ [http://stage.To|http://stage.To|smart-link]  _assess your product's potential further, please provide the three points I requested in my last email:_\n\n* _The list of potentially interested restaurants._\n* _A breakdown of the cost structure beyond the note that it is based on order volume._\n* _The demo.\"_\n\n*_---_*\n_\"As I said, to prioritise this, a business case is important. This means we need more than a list of interested customers. Also, this list includes restaurants already integrated with a POS system or via a third party; therefore, I don't see why they would choose your_ [_solution.In_|http://solution.In] _any case, I understand your product's concept and requirements, but I cannot push for it internally until we have something more solid. We cannot proceed with the integration now, but we can revisit it later on.\"_\n_---_\n_\"As stated previously, we will not pursue a collaboration at this stage, our position has not changed.Nonetheless, we acknowledge the potential of your solution, and we are open to reconsidering it in the future once your product and client base have developed further.For now, I kindly ask that follow-up emails and calls to me or my colleagues be paused. We expect that this decision is respected.\"_","2026-01-07T13:30:39.024Z"],["3793315","PFI-830592","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-07T13:30:39.181Z"],["3793317","SREDESK-7384","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Order-nig alter has started at 2026-01-07 15:30 EET","2026-01-07T13:31:05.599Z"],["3793318","LSS-60939","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:614ae82ed747e80075f8baa5] !\n\nThere was an issue with Laimonas’ signature. The thing is, he is no longer a director and cannot sign retrospectively, so the counsel offered a solution: to put the name of the new director and add the following statement:\n\n_“This Amendment is entered into on [signing date in January] and shall be effective as of 5 September 2025.”_\n\nWill that work?","2026-01-07T13:31:13.121Z"],["3793319","HS-28617","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Hey Dean!\n\nVitality has confirmed Your membership and Your membership number is 1285925036.\n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin","2026-01-07T13:31:43.698Z"],["3793322","HS-28663","HS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Noted, thanks a lot!","2026-01-07T13:32:56.412Z"],["3793323","LSS-60808","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nMay we please proceed with signing the amendment?\n\nApologies for the follow-up—Mapbox has been checking in daily.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-07T13:33:13.952Z"],["3793326","PFI-808893","PFI","jakub.pekar@bolt-outsource.eu","Jakub Pekar","Hello, it seems that the driver did not receive the amount back. I also checked his payout and it seems that the driver only received his regular earnings.","2026-01-07T13:33:56.102Z"],["3793329","INT-777","INT","artem.borisov@bolt.eu","Artem Borisov","[~accountid:62a9857bd0132d0068809cdd], from the code, I can see no filtering, and it feels like we are “pausing” all the ongoing campaigns as well. In more technical details, we mark those enrollments as banned, and when the ban period ends, we restore the enrollment to its active state. The duration of the lock is defined by the provider profile {{price_increase_ineligibility_end_date}} field.\n\nAs for the topic of mass enabling, we would be better off migrating the test-based price inflation to ca ron-based approach:\n\n# Add remote config value to control feature availability\n# Migrate the logic from the test-based API to cron\n\nOverall, with testing, the effort is ~1.5 MW","2026-01-07T13:35:09.484Z"],["3793330","CEBF-1759","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","Also, we have {{checkContactInformation}} method in the {{AccountValidations}} class. This method checks fields not in bulk.","2026-01-07T13:35:27.435Z"],["3793331","PFI-808893","PFI","jakub.pekar@bolt-outsource.eu","Jakub Pekar","[Payouts|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts?tz=Europe%2FPrague&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1764543600%2C%22show_empty_rejection_code%22%3Afalse%2C%22show_total%22%3Afalse%2C%22external_client_id%22%3A7472273%7D%7D]","2026-01-07T13:35:45.166Z"],["3793338","INT-777","INT","alexander.tsyba@bolt.eu","Alexander Tsyba","[~accountid:5d288c50590c9c0c25f7a0e5] [~accountid:63d0ecc2f386bda5dcab9d6e] that’s very strange as we’ve 1) never heard any complaints which otherwise would be all the time, for pausing ongoing campaigns; 2) we see cases of menu price inflation after campaign start and prices are discounted by that campaign. Shall we double check that’s it’s really working like that?","2026-01-07T13:37:23.781Z"],["3793341","PRIV-485","PRIV","edik.davtian@bolt.eu","Edik Davtian","Hello! just to align on the timing of the Privacy support.\n\n\n\nIs it something we can review on the next week? I would like to align on expectations & we want to have v1 of our draft ready sooner - so we can try & learn from it. \n\n\n\nThanks in advance!","2026-01-07T13:38:12.108Z"],["3793342","PFI-824868","PFI","pakrampar.silrapasangchai@bolt.eu","Pakrampar Silrapasangchai","Hey [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] ,\n\n[~accountid:712020:7b0eaf7d-a9e3-4e7c-8642-85758502063d]  has attached proof of payment from their bank. Please investigate and match the payment accordingly.","2026-01-07T13:38:50.705Z"],["3793344","LSS-61125","LSS","freek.engel@bolt.eu","Freek van den Engel","Thank you! Once sent plz share the tracking ID","2026-01-07T13:39:35.872Z"],["3793345","SREDESK-7384","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Order-was alter has started at 2026-01-07 15:39 EET","2026-01-07T13:39:55.159Z"],["3793346","PFI-830598","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-07T13:40:00.324Z"],["3793347","PFI-829428","PFI","pakrampar.silrapasangchai@bolt.eu","Pakrampar Silrapasangchai","Hey [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] ,\n\n[~accountid:712020:8bf42e01-1aca-45ba-8ceb-0b23822aeb53]  has attached proof of payment from their bank. Please investigate and match the payment accordingly.","2026-01-07T13:40:14.050Z"],["3793349","BD-1972","BD","rafael.barros@bolt.eu","Rafael Adson Barbosa Barros","Conversation in slack about what to do with these tasks: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01TV59SHR8/p1767789428851729|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01TV59SHR8/p1767789428851729|smart-link] \n\nConclusion: we are not going to send these emails anymore, only if providers request it.","2026-01-07T13:40:52.977Z"],["3793352","BD-1972","BD","rafael.barros@bolt.eu","Rafael Adson Barbosa Barros","Ignoring provider tasks sql:\n\n{code:sql}update task\nset state='ignore', ignore_reason='Old emails should no longer be sent to providers'\nwhere id IN (\n2783150510, 2796681159, 2840257607, 2774508932, 2772821295,\n       2817820363, 2817603558, 2766460755, 2767459172, 2767153146,\n       2766022566, 2765852916, 2834992809, 2824333477, 2789054842,\n  