       2221455084, 2222320545, 2221584632, 2221558451, 2221338496,\n       2221336711, 2669555894, 2205979105, 2206840758, 2206130633,\n       2206415366, 2206080973, 2205960949, 2253423927, 2253642336,\n       2253334005, 2253319489, 2253864498, 2254460771, 2237004679,\n       2236999501, 2173354846, 2174131925, 2173358121, 2038928580,\n       2526846241, 2525839041, 2718041018, 2223257925, 2131037275,\n       2370387596, 2371968400, 2157910470, 2159187501, 2158040996,\n       2159045776, 2157920559, 2191162243, 2191356574, 2353009827,\n       2352841526, 2353033844, 2353198790, 2353119745, 2353537646,\n       2353455307, 2352749668, 2353820658, 2353152475, 2118744162,\n       2089254862, 2099089376, 2111918449, 2111031289, 2111080250,\n       2162502198, 2177619300, 2288450176, 2288801256, 2288874363,\n       2034203510, 2034712052, 2034045994, 2107288682, 2146628331,\n       2176269484, 2175289095, 2101120850, 2101130874, 2239668818,\n       2142840206, 2142505064, 2086299213, 2354912653, 2355916025,\n       2356131075, 2354685221, 2354808340, 2354955086, 2355546741,\n       2355646130, 2355316295\n) and state='to_execute';{code}","2026-01-07T13:43:26.309Z"],["3793359","L10N-26375","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26346](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26346)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-07T13:43:40.531Z"],["3793360","L10N-26374","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26346](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26346)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-07T13:43:41.146Z"],["3793361","L10N-26378","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26346](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26346)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-07T13:43:42.561Z"],["3793362","L10N-26379","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26346](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26346)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-07T13:43:43.103Z"],["3793363","MAB-219","MAB","zhanna.azizova@bolt.eu","Zhanna Azizova","[~accountid:712020:cc5e7269-1cb5-4771-92a0-efc0befbe5f9] works! Thanks a lot!","2026-01-07T13:43:52.961Z"],["3793367","PFI-829712","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo,\n\nchanges have been scheduled for 08.01.","2026-01-07T13:44:22.915Z"],["3793370","WD-22503","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","Hi Adam,\n\nAccording to WD, your parental leave will start in June, which pauses your monthly accrual. While there is an estimated return date, accrual only resumes once your actual return date is confirmed. I suggest checking with your People Partner to clarify.\n\nKind regards,\n\nOli ","2026-01-07T13:45:10.942Z"],["3793371","GEORM-428","GEORM","kenneth.tenny@bolt.eu","Kenneth Tenny","First draft: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yhedF2-M08l6RSJN8biBst7m4YS4d0fzL2T__hG43HA/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yhedF2-M08l6RSJN8biBst7m4YS4d0fzL2T__hG43HA/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T13:45:22.062Z"],["3793373","MLC-3765","MLC","helina.nommik@bolt.eu","Helina Nõmmik","[~accountid:712020:a68bad68-4d18-4aca-aaf7-10e00df84534] , some additional cities were added to the pilot. \n\n# Berlin \n# Hamburg \n# Frankfurt \n# Dusseldorf\n# Essen \n# Mannheim \n# Münster \n# Kiel \n# Stuttgart \n# Zurich\n# Augsburg \n# Bremen\n# Halle (Saale)\n\nLet’s prep the setups in Braze. ☺️ ","2026-01-07T13:45:27.038Z"],["3793385","LSS-61219","LSS","sandra.loewe@bolt.eu","Sandra Löwe","[^Extension - Nova Mobility  - Bolt Cooperation Agreement - Germany.docx (1).pdf] _(521 kB)_","2026-01-07T13:46:49.089Z"],["3793392","LSS-61104","LSS","luke.grima@bolt.eu","Luke Grima","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] \n\nI looked into the Beehive tickets opened by this rider, seems that she has opened 9 tickets within the last 4 months (screenshot attached)\n\nFurthermore, she has in more than one ticket said that this is the last time she’s using Bolt, and that she expects large reimbursement. \n\n!image-20260107-131312.png|width=596,height=207,alt=\"image-20260107-131312.png\"!\n\n!image-20260107-131158.png|width=625,height=180,alt=\"image-20260107-131158.png\"!\n\n!image-20260107-131229.png|width=588,height=128,alt=\"image-20260107-131229.png\"!\n\n!image-20260107-115630.png|width=1382,height=756,alt=\"image-20260107-115630.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n* Trip ID + driver ID for 23 Dec 2025 (Valletta → Żejtun, ~10:54) and confirmation of whether this is the same driver as the earlier incident(s)\n\nTrip ID: *2312039077* [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2312039077/324?orderTryId=2960545927]\nDriver ID: *5636454* [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/5636454?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n\nHowever, the driver here does not seem to be the same as the videos.\n\n\n* Trip ID(s)/driver ID(s) for the earlier incident mentioned in MCCAA email (17 Oct 2025) + any other relevant safety tickets linked to the complainant.\n\nI was checking the beehive tickets, and the last one they opened on vaping was for 10th October not on the 17th, link [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/664047309]\n\nTripID: *#2203601717* [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2203601717/324?orderTryId=2777173077]\nDriverID *3820560* [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/3820560?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n\nThe driver in this case is different potentially the one in the video.\n\n\n\n* Current enforcement decision for the driver(s): warning/suspension/removal.\n\nDriver 1 - October complaint - No suspensions for the driver, it seems no actions were taken against the driver\n\nDriver 2 - December complaint - No linked driver cases, it seems no actions were taken against the driver \n\n\n\n* Any internal guidance used by Support in those cases (so we can confirm what has been corrected going forward).\n\nThis was the KB article that was attached [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/public/360000440614]\n\n”_If you were involved in an accident or became a victim of violent behaviour, let us know via the Bolt safety toolkit by clicking on the green shield icon on the map._\n\n_If you have been involved in an accident, immediately notify the police and paramedics if necessary._\n\n_We assure you that we treat such incidents with the utmost priority._”\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] [~accountid:6273b7d8e51c620070bea596] ","2026-01-07T13:49:00.138Z"],["3793393","LSS-61041","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[~accountid:712020:552b5d62-f64b-4147-b52a-d5178d160c21] thank you for stepping in! Much appreciated.\nThis is the signed cooperation agreement:\n[^Cooperation agreement_Bolt Operations OÜ_Tur Taxi AS_17.09.25 (1).pdf] \n\nAs far as my analysis of the agreement goes, the contract does not clearly state that they are obliged to refund the money in the event that insolvency proceedings are initiated or if Bolt terminates the agreement. From their side, they have not terminated the agreement (the refund obligation is explicitly provided for only in the case where the Contractor terminates the agreement themselves).\n\nIn any event, since insolvency proceedings have been initiated, we cannot directly demand immediate payment of the full amount. We must participate in the insolvency proceedings together with the other creditors and submit a claim to be included in the general list of creditors.\n\n*In order to prepare such a claim, I need the information that was previously provided in the ticket comments.*\n\n*Could you please provide this information again today?*\n\nThank you.","2026-01-07T13:49:01.376Z"],["3793394","PFI-830604","PFI","emily.onyango@bolt.eu","Emily Onyango","!Screenshot 2026-01-07 4.48.55 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T13:49:31.239Z"],["3793395","SREDESK-7384","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Confirm rest of cluster has the target columns\n\n{noformat}➜  ~ mysql --defaults-file=~/mysql/slave-ukr.cnf -D taxify_company -e\"show create table order_try_driver\\G\" | grep operating_model\n  `operating_model` enum('agency','principal') DEFAULT NULL,\n➜  ~ mysql --defaults-file=~/mysql/slave-weu.cnf -D taxify_company -e\"show create table order_try_driver\\G\" | grep operating_model\n  `operating_model` enum('agency','principal') DEFAULT NULL,\n➜  ~ mysql --defaults-file=~/mysql/slave-gb.cnf -D taxify_company -e\"show create table order_try_driver\\G\" | grep operating_model\n  `operating_model` enum('agency','principal') DEFAULT NULL,\n➜  ~ mysql --defaults-file=~/mysql/slave-afr.cnf -D taxify_company -e\"show create table order_try_driver\\G\" | grep operating_model\n  `operating_model` enum('agency','principal') DEFAULT NULL,\n➜  ~ mysql --defaults-file=~/mysql/slave-na.cnf -D taxify_company -e\"show create table order_try_driver\\G\" | grep operating_model\n  `operating_model` enum('agency','principal') DEFAULT NULL,\n➜  ~ mysql --defaults-file=~/mysql/slave-au.cnf -D taxify_company -e\"show create table order_try_driver\\G\" | grep operating_model\n  `operating_model` enum('agency','principal') DEFAULT NULL,\n➜  ~ mysql --defaults-file=~/mysql/slave-kz.cnf -D taxify_company -e\"show create table order_try_driver\\G\" | grep operating_model\n  `operating_model` enum('agency','principal') DEFAULT NULL,\n➜  ~ mysql --defaults-file=~/mysql/slave-ru.cnf -D taxify_company -e\"show create table order_try_driver\\G\" | grep operating_model\n  `operating_model` enum('agency','principal') DEFAULT NULL,{noformat}","2026-01-07T13:49:44.065Z"],["3793396","LSS-60882","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","Thanks [~accountid:5e0f07ab9a4b780d990e9fb9] for all the information provided! \n\nI understand that if you would follow the standard procedure, this case would be referred straight to the debt collector, correct? If so, what are your doubts in this case? Is it because of the value, the disputed circumstances of the case or something else?","2026-01-07T13:49:58.898Z"],["3793399","LSS-61105","LSS","ramone.edwards@bolt.eu","Ramone Edwards","h4. Hey [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] [~accountid:5dde532fcdc2d20d05377446] please see below \n\n\n\nh4. *1. Verify Suspension History*\n\n* Confirm if the driver is licensed in London and/or operates in London?\n** _The driver is licensed by Wolverhampton council, he has not undertaken any trips in London_\n* Confirm the exact dates and reasons for both suspensions:\n** _12–15 November 2025 – vehicle year issue - CONFIRMED_ \n** _23rd November 2025 to present - The color information for your vehicle on the DVLA website is incorrect - CONFIRMED_\n* Clarify which data sources were used (e.g. MOT checker, DVLA, PHV licence).\n** _All cars documents are checked when approving vehicles. In this instance the driver should not have been blocked as the source for information is taken from the MOT website._ \n* Confirm if any manual override or reinstatement occurred, and why.\n** _The driver was reinstated on 15th November 2025 and the block was put back on, on 23rd November 2025_ _to today_\n\nh4. *2. Review Submitted Evidence*\n\n* Locate and review documents submitted by the driver, including:\n** V5C logbook\n** DVLA vehicle data\nPHV licence(s), current and previous\n* Do these match the data Bolt is relying on? _Yes_\n* Do we have valid reasons for suspending him? _We usually do not suspend drivers for colour mismatches so not valid reason found, the reason in unknown but seems to point to human error._ \n\nh4. *3. Check Internal Handling*\n\n* Review all relevant ticket threads and case notes:\n** _The driver was was informed of the reason for the suspension and what he needed to do to resolve the issue. Please see attached PDF by CS._\n\nh4. *4. Assess Risk and Resolution Options*\n\n* Can the account be reinstated, if documents are compliant?\n** _Checked with compliance team and the driver can be reinstated_ \n* Did any procedural issues or delays contribute to the current situation?\n** _Looks like the driver shouldn’t have been blocked for the mismatch colour  as seen in the slack thread, tickets were raised by CS but these were not actioned correctly._ \n*** Ticket [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/31/UKOPS-43310]\n\n\n\n[^Beehive ticket.pdf]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 13.37.31.png|width=741,height=702,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 13.37.31.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-07T13:50:19.356Z"],["3793404","WD-22503","WD","adam.cherry@bolt.eu","Adam Cherry","Hi Oli, \n\nThanks for confirming — makes sense. So, between now and when my parental leave begins on 12 June, I’ll accrue 3 more annual leave days. Is this correct?\n\nThanks,\nAdam","2026-01-07T13:51:03.086Z"],["3793406","DSR-3569","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-07T13:51:06.198Z"],["3793407","LSS-61109","LSS","raphael.perna@bolt.eu","Raphaël Samy Perna","Thank you [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nI have *shared the representative’s details (full name and email address) directly as a comment in the document*, so that the e-signature process can be initiated.\n\nRegarding the signature, I confirm that *an electronic signature is preferred*: it should be fully acceptable for the fleet manager and will enable faster processing of the case.\nIf needed, we can of course switch to *a handwritten signature with the PDF attached*.\n\nCould you please confirm whether *the document can now be considered reviewed and ready to be sent*?\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything further to proceed.\n\nThank you again,","2026-01-07T13:51:08.758Z"],["3793409","LSS-60931","LSS","dmytro.yermolenko@bolt.eu","Dmytro Yermolenko","[~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] Hi! The sign-ready version is below:\n\n[^VIK-156784-1225_Cash payment_Bolt_SRV.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T13:51:28.880Z"],["3793411","WD-22488","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","we have adjusted ZAF study leave to be able to capture half day now.","2026-01-07T13:51:46.291Z"],["3793412","DSR-2981","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC, many thanks for gathering the data and doing the necessary investigative work here!\n\nI have reviewed the response letter and the responsive data (+added suspension notes). It is outside of Privacy/CSPC’s scope to review suspension decisions, so we will share the requested data and monitor the ticket. Should the Driver follow-up (which he likely will), T2/Ops can then make the decision themselves (/) ","2026-01-07T13:51:48.434Z"],["3793413","PFI-829471","PFI","laura.loaiza@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Muñoz","New case: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719205243|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719205243]\n\nBusiness profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/337350?tab=business_company|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/337350?tab=business_company]","2026-01-07T13:51:55.837Z"],["3793414","LSS-61099","LSS","olesja.timofejeva@bolt.eu","Olesja Timofejeva","Hey! Thank you so much for the letters provided. \nIs there any update on Alex’s signature?","2026-01-07T13:51:58.286Z"],["3793416","PFI-830608","PFI","lukas.dusek@bolt-outsource.eu","Lukas Dusek","!IMG_2997.png|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_2998.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T13:52:20.588Z"],["3793419","LSS-59671","LSS","karolina.wiater@bolt.eu","Karolina Wiater","Hi, do we have any update?","2026-01-07T13:53:01.551Z"],["3793421","LSS-52572","LSS","tomasz.symonowicz@bolt.eu","Tomasz Symonowicz","hey [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] as we have changed our entity in Poland, we are required to fill in the online questionnaire again, this time for Bolt Poland, could you please support us in this process, so they are no mistakes? : ) it’s quite urgent and really important to get this done ASAP;\n\nhere is the new link: [https://forms-r1.bvdinfo.com/EQuestionnaire/Edit?formId=3328140&context=wp9adVoztCO52GuBl%2banePCk5ksTP7wbocHVPfKTQb%2bDLt1nWCVb0bPZKZm4RjatPF6pQBSywnSEC5woxQrvCg%3d%3d|https://forms-r1.bvdinfo.com/EQuestionnaire/Edit?formId=3328140&context=wp9adVoztCO52GuBl%2banePCk5ksTP7wbocHVPfKTQb%2bDLt1nWCVb0bPZKZm4RjatPF6pQBSywnSEC5woxQrvCg%3d%3d|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T13:53:30.265Z"],["3793423","PFI-830589","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","requesting double approval \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1767794009279?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1767794009279?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-07T13:53:41.984Z"],["3793426","LSS-57242","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nThanks for this! Before circulating it to the business, I suggest we clarify or explore a few additional aspects that could impact the viability of the proposed options:\n\n# Do we have any written exchanges (emails, visit notes) where the landlord addressed the ERP classification or public access suitability? Even informal assurances could support a negotiation strategy around misrepresentation or incomplete disclosure. WDYT?\n# Was the insurance policy ever formally put in place for this site? If so, we should check:\n#* Does it cover business interruption or regulatory barriers?\n#* Are delays due to ERP works potentially claimable?\nClarifying this could influence our negotiation leverage or help reduce financial exposure.\n# Do we have any indication that the premises could attract another tenant not subject to ERP rules (e.g. back office, storage, non-public access use)? If not, we may want to downplay this as a viable option and focus on negotiation. \n# Do we have a broker view or any precedent (maybe Devon knows) on what level of indemnity might be acceptable for early exit in similar Paris-area commercial leases? If market conditions favour tenants, the landlord might accept less than the full term value.\n# Unless we have clear evidence of Bolt relying on the broker’s advice re ERP compliance, I suggest we flag this only as a potential avenue pending further review of documentation.\n\nCan you check please the above before moving on with the Business? \n\nThanks a lot,\nElisabetta","2026-01-07T13:53:58.043Z"],["3793430","PFI-809177","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Apologies for delay. This is the internal bug related to price charged being higher than final price for the order, there will be automatic refunds for such refunds and is being looked at by engineering, but it’s not yet done","2026-01-07T13:54:41.874Z"],["3793431","MLC-2253","MLC","dovainis.kaleda@bolt.eu","Dovainis Kalėda","Interesting one in terms of exploration. Idea in itself is not bad, but the way how we are building Messaging Platform, how growth operates with incentive enrolments and the role that lifecycle plays in it doesn’t add up to a standalone separate incentive enrolment mechanism at least now. For those reasons this was parked.","2026-01-07T13:54:55.763Z"],["3793432","PFI-830609","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-07T13:54:56.610Z"],["3793433","PFI-830609","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:5b8517da332df52a5d9460cc] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-07T13:54:58.539Z"],["3793435","LSS-59991","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:b467cd93-0037-45b9-9f33-992ba5f38b42],\n\nThanks for reaching out again with this update. \n\nIn order to understand the cause of discontent of the legal vendor (represented now by the consultancy company), I kindly ask you to clarify:\n\n# Is is true that Bolt allows “Capitan Spect” to connect via API to Bolt? (it is not mentioned in the email).\n# Does Bolt allow connection via API to other vendors, or only to Capitan Spect?\n# What are the requisites that would need to be fulfilled by the potential legal vendor to be granted access to the Bolt Food App? \n\nMany thanks!\n\nAngela \n\n","2026-01-07T13:55:09.238Z"],["3793436","FIN2-886","FIN2","marleen.parmakson@bolt.eu","Marleen Parmakson","*IFRS analysis summary – OK Incure agreement is* [*here*|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1K_kGev-7yDgupmUf1vnk6m4ry6rlQEhgxrP7XfT-7H4/edit?tab=t.0]\n\nAn IFRS 9 analysis has been performed for the signed OK Incure debt-collection agreement. The contract represents an agency / contingent recovery arrangement, not a sale of receivables, as Bolt retains ownership and all credit risk.\n\n*Accounting treatment:*\n\n* *Upon transfer to Incure:* No derecognition; courier receivables remain recognised at amortised cost.\n* *When cash is received:* Recognise cash received and derecognise the collected portion of the receivable.\n* *Incure’s commission:* Recognise as an operating expense (debt-collection costs / bad-debt expense) at the time of recovery.","2026-01-07T13:55:40.421Z"],["3793437","PFI-830608","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nHere is the payment\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4008183109|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4008183109]\n\nThe initial price was 27.20 EUR, but was increased by 8.90 EUR. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-07T13:55:51.421Z"],["3793441","LSS-59845","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] [~accountid:5d7b698997d8980d8ead4b01] i checked the msa \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/19MN79tbPIKtWd151uCy50EiaojI1D6jn/edit#heading=h.1ksv4uv|https://docs.google.com/document/d/19MN79tbPIKtWd151uCy50EiaojI1D6jn/edit#heading=h.1ksv4uv|smart-link]  \n\n* Please reply to my questions \n* Let me know if infosec approved supplier, we added a link to our Infosec code \n* how much we are paying per year ? It affects our liability limit  \n* please share here Order form for the review, we can exclude automatic renewal there as already agreed by Senrty in Slack \n\n[~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] I found this link what data is shared with Sentry [https://docs.sentry.io/organization/data-storage-location/#what-types-of-data-are-stored-where|https://docs.sentry.io/organization/data-storage-location/#what-types-of-data-are-stored-where|smart-link] , we can also try to exclude data protection breaches from the liability cap in liability section if needed or offer a separate cap for data protection. Sentry seems ready to compromise.  ","2026-01-07T13:56:14.496Z"],["3793442","MLC-2633","MLC","dovainis.kaleda@bolt.eu","Dovainis Kalėda","Parked while Storytelling is fully rolled out and once the HTML issues that followed are fixed and confirmed. Will be picked up either very late in Q1 of 2026 or start of Q2. Approach and information outlined is relevant.","2026-01-07T13:56:14.917Z"],["3793445","LSS-60882","LSS","david.vysoky@bolt.eu","Dávid Vysoký","Yes, the standard procedure will be followed, debt will be handed over to debt collector.\n\nDoubt in this specific case are:\n\n# as mentioned _“User did the pre-ride check and reported a scratch and mess in the vehicle properly. In this scenario, if the tire blowout was genuinely due to pre-existing operational wear or a prior fault (not the User’s fault), the User is protected from liability under T&Cs 4.1.5. The User shall examine the Motor Vehicle’s interior and exterior to ensure that the Motor Vehicle does not have clearly visible damages and shall undertake to check if all fittings and accessories of the Motor Vehicle such as the ignition key (if any), Fuel Card/Charging Card (as defined below) and the Motor Vehicle documents and manuals are in the Motor Vehicle.) and the 9.4. The User is not liable for any failures of the Motor Vehicle caused by previous use, operation or normal wear and tear, if the User immediately notifies Bolt through one of the available contact channels and complies with the instructions given by Bolt.”_\n# When I shared this reasoning, CS *messaged to user that he won’t be fined*. After reviewing the case again, he was fined with liability cap 25000 czk.\n\n","2026-01-07T13:56:35.844Z"],["3793448","BR-4072","BR","triinu.tasa@bolt.eu","Triinu Tasa","{quote}Once you are back from holiday, perhaps you can clarify whether these queries only come for finished specific orders.{quote}\n\nIn p99 of cases, yes - we don't mind returning null for the rest\n\n{quote}Also, we would need to know whether you can provide us with order_id and city_id as input{quote}\n\nYes, no problem with that","2026-01-07T13:57:18.664Z"],["3793450","LSS-60931","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Hey team, please add wet ink signature of Ahto Kink on the below doc and the stamp of Bolt Operations OU and send us the scan, thank you!\n\n[^VIK-156784-1225_Cash payment_Bolt_SRV (6aca4227-a1fe-4d8e-bdc3-756517377b52).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T13:57:30.303Z"],["3793456","LEG-1001","LEG","marleen.parmakson@bolt.eu","Marleen Parmakson","Hi [~accountid:712020:b1a3aa39-56a5-492b-9453-5372da990388] I documented IFRS analyis of debt collection topic and OK Incure agreement in this [ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FIN2-886] . With this contract we derecignise only the collected part once we receive the cash and record Incure’s commission as an operating expense (“Debt-collection costs” / “Bad-debt expense”) at the time of recovery.","2026-01-07T13:58:14.295Z"],["3793459","PFI-830589","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team has refunded the customers payment and corrected the state in Admin. \nPlease note 2C2P does not allow refunds on the same day. We are aware of the issue and will try to find a solution for the future with the help of payment engineers. \n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-07T13:58:33.381Z"],["3793460","HS-28702","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-07T13:58:43.716Z"],["3793462","PAW-14691","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-07T13:59:21.450Z"],["3793465","PFI-830459","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe payment had gotten stuck with Fondy. \nCustomer payments team has managed to capture to payment and correct the payment state in admin. \nThe debt has been cleared. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-07T14:00:13.861Z"],["3793466","MLC-3240","MLC","dovainis.kaleda@bolt.eu","Dovainis Kalėda","To be picked up as project in 2026 Q2. Real value, somewhat of a low hanging given all the data we currently have.\n\n*Prerequisite:* full Deliverability dashboard handling soft and hard bounces with a granularity level on dedicated IP addresses;\n\nRider team Invalid Email Address validation experiment in 2026 Q1.","2026-01-07T14:00:31.323Z"],["3793469","PFI-828885","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Payment has been refunded in the Tingg portal. \nRequesting double approval to change the payment state. \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1767794488205?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1767794488205?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-07T14:01:47.467Z"],["3793470","LSS-61221","LSS","mercynorah.nyiti@bolt.eu","Mercynorah Nyiti","[^DECEMBER 2025 SERVICE ACCEPTANCE-BOLT RIDES-BOLT TANZANIA.pdf] _(191 kB)_\n\n[^NOVEMBER 2025 SERVICE ACCEPTANCE-BOLT RIDES-BOLT TANZANIA.pdf] _(194 kB)_","2026-01-07T14:01:58.103Z"],["3793471","PFI-830614","PFI","jan.dohnal@bolt-outsource.eu","Jan Dohnal","!image-20260107-140207.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T14:02:12.966Z"],["3793474","LSS-59211","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","[~accountid:712020:a9500cde-28bc-4a8e-95d6-7818a2252cf8] please check over the SOW part for Luminor - ad terms + fees part. I combined Banca Transilvania and Mastercard examples. Ideally I would sync with you for 10 min today or tomorrow. Otherwise we go back and forth with the doc for too long [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Se9OBNebTg1TZCa_yfNtvON_0WBypMiJidFEDWoAsYs/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Se9OBNebTg1TZCa_yfNtvON_0WBypMiJidFEDWoAsYs/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nLiisa","2026-01-07T14:02:32.594Z"],["3793476","DBRE-8586","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Fixing schema drift\n* [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/schema-change/pipelines/191703|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/schema-change/pipelines/191703]\n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7384|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7384|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T14:02:42.284Z"],["3793479","MLC-2504","MLC","dovainis.kaleda@bolt.eu","Dovainis Kalėda","Aiming to launch the EXP around 2nd week of January.\n\nSetups on Eater side are all done.\n\nCurrently only the user query is needed from MarTech Analysts for the 3 selected markets.","2026-01-07T14:03:06.735Z"],["3793482","MLC-1885","MLC","dovainis.kaleda@bolt.eu","Dovainis Kalėda","License is purchased. Trademark is under investigation at EUIPO. To follow suite with IP team. Move further once there’s updates that we can actually implement it live.","2026-01-07T14:04:04.136Z"],["3793483","PFI-830617","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-07T14:04:16.882Z"],["3793484","BDB-1500","BDB","liisi.tamra@bolt.eu","Liisi Tamra","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c], did you notice my suggestions? [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79]  took the copy from the media plan, so I assume it wasn’t updated there? Currently, the templates use phrases like “Bolt out,” which we can’t use.","2026-01-07T14:04:19.557Z"],["3793485","LSS-59454","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","[~accountid:712020:0051a059-9c34-4c65-96bf-ddd219dfda7c] as already explained, from my experience, financial institutions are reluctant to give any in blanco signatures, irrespectively of the content of the document. However, if we have a good relationship with LHV, it could be an exception, especially if you explain that this is required by the police in Czechia. Also, asking them will not hurt, in the worst case scenario they say no. If they decline, we will think about other solution. So from my perspective, you may go ahead, talk to LHV and share with them the document you prepared.\n\nBtw, who is Kooperativa and Renomia? I don’t think they were mentioned before.","2026-01-07T14:04:42.442Z"],["3793488","WFM-9882","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Hello [~accountid:61515e3c64ff010071e17133], \r\n\r\nPlaymode was activated. \r\nHave a great day! ","2026-01-07T14:05:20.639Z"],["3793489","LSS-60650","LSS","maksims.kostenko@bolt.eu","Maksims Kostenko","Hi [~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] \nI’m aware about the ongoing partnership, but I don’t which entity has signed the NDA / Agreement with Mono. My thoughts are following: \n1) If it’s signed by the local “Bolt Food“ entity then we need a separate one\n2) If it’s signed by “Bolt Operations OU” then we should be already covered. \nI rely on your and Anna opinion here. If the second is true and we can continue without the NDA it would be great and convenient for us. ","2026-01-07T14:05:35.164Z"],["3793491","DSR-3571","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-07T14:06:17.536Z"],["3793497","PFI-829509","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Thanks for the info - I’ve raised this with tax to get their input and followed up. Without it, we will not be able to do anything. \nI will look into what you’ve provided further and get back to you with any findings and tax input.\n","2026-01-07T14:07:30.304Z"],["3793498","MLC-1887","MLC","dovainis.kaleda@bolt.eu","Dovainis Kalėda","Trademark is under investigation at EUIPO. To follow up again with IP team. Move further once there’s updates that we can actually implement it live.\n*Current blocker:* trademark status being under investigation.","2026-01-07T14:07:30.446Z"],["3793502","PRODSEC-681","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Will update to latest 4.X before upgrading to 5.X. Cloudflare recommends to wait before going to 5.X since it is still in development. Last 4.X version is 4 months older which is already improvement from 2 years old version.","2026-01-07T14:08:42.614Z"],["3793505","LSS-60768","LSS","wiktoria.lis@bolt.eu","Wiktoria Lis","[~accountid:712020:b1700666-82b2-4a86-82f7-550a84f716c8]could you please resend the document to Eternis? They’re claiming they didn’t receive anything","2026-01-07T14:09:19.884Z"],["3793506","LSS-61126","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Thank you [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] !","2026-01-07T14:09:42.079Z"],["3793509","PRODSEC-577","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Working notebook to get IPQS and store in Databrics DBFS. Missing step to upload and retrieve from S3 since that requires adding S3 to Databrics connection. Submitted ticket for it [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/data-platform-authorisation/authorisation/requests/660024|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/data-platform-authorisation/authorisation/requests/660024]\n\nCurrently script is able to retrieve from DBFS and then use database to analyze IPs","2026-01-07T14:10:48.820Z"],["3793511","PAW-16569","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-product-resource-provisioning, pint-capability-self-service-infrastructure\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-07T14:11:14.481Z"],["3793513","PRODSEC-577","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Will need to separate download notebook to use it in scheduled form","2026-01-07T14:11:19.812Z"],["3793518","HS-28595","HS","maximilian.linek@bolt.eu","Maximilian Linek","[^arbeitsnachweis_arbeitnehmer_2022_03.pdf]\n\nAttached the template. The information of my son is: Enno Serafin Linek, born 21.11.2019\n\nCan you please return this to me and I will send it to the Jugendamt with all the other documents that they requested.","2026-01-07T14:12:58.747Z"],["3793519","L10N-26338","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-07T14:13:13.938Z"],["3793520","L10N-26335","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-07T14:13:13.969Z"],["3793521","L10N-26345","L10N",null,"Automation for Ji