Thank you for the report, <@sudipto.das>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-328] `Mass unblock driver selfie verification users in SA` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:16:27.872Z"],["3793542","DSR-3009","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC, please also add the _Block_ plug-in to the responsive data. Once this is done, the data and answer letter can be shared with the driver 🙂 ","2026-01-07T14:16:47.449Z"],["3793543","CEBF-1759","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","[~accountid:712020:fc274657-f7b5-4366-9f2d-5ec68865cf48] I leave some validation rules to decide what I have to do with them later\n\n\n* [https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.my.salesforce-setup.com/lightning/setup/ObjectManager/Opportunity/ValidationRules/03dTs0000000VWrIAM/view|https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.my.salesforce-setup.com/lightning/setup/ObjectManager/Opportunity/ValidationRules/03dTs0000000VWrIAM/view]\n* [https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.my.salesforce-setup.com/lightning/setup/ObjectManager/Opportunity/ValidationRules/03dTs0000000WeDIAU/view|https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.my.salesforce-setup.com/lightning/setup/ObjectManager/Opportunity/ValidationRules/03dTs0000000WeDIAU/view]\n\nMay be you find others","2026-01-07T14:18:06.909Z"],["3793545","WAVE-225","WAVE","raido@bolt.eu","Raido Kuli","If we want just UI Platform team's repos then no need to scrape - [https://docs.github.com/en/rest/teams/teams?apiVersion=2022-11-28#list-team-repositories|https://docs.github.com/en/rest/teams/teams?apiVersion=2022-11-28#list-team-repositories] - there's API to return list of all repos UI Platform currently has access to.\n\nIf we want to add ourselves to all \"web\" related repos, then yes we need pull the repos list and parse a bit more data.","2026-01-07T14:19:05.818Z"],["3793546","WAVE-225","WAVE",null,"Slack","[Raido Kuli|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/557058:2ccf5293-0c3a-4db8-9ee1-dfe72f75cfb4] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08SG8THU2J/p1767779714451879?thread_ts=1767778407.063529&cid=C08SG8THU2J|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08SG8THU2J/p1767779714451879?thread_ts=1767778407.063529&cid=C08SG8THU2J|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-07T14:19:07.195Z"],["3793547","DSR-3571","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","All data download without communications plugins [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/personal-data-export/exports/1326972?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]\nRider invoices download [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-bulk-invoice-download/item/1740001/view]\nResponse letter in the [folder|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1X4rhwH4D0OLAiw9Zk5DBiVSWxQKl0dww]\nAcceptance rate added\nAverage rating added\nBeehive calls :loading: ","2026-01-07T14:19:58.742Z"],["3793549","PIF-3256","PIF","dmitrii.shilonosov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Shilonosov","related: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04T8LF7Y4D/p1767795380803689|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04T8LF7Y4D/p1767795380803689|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T14:20:19.325Z"],["3793550","DSR-3575","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-07T14:21:07.044Z"],["3793551","DSR-3573","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-07T14:21:07.101Z"],["3793553","EBIKE1-237","EBIKE1","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","Checked the new frames and brake fixation with correct washer in LY and it was all good now\n\n\n\nDouble check when the new assembling starts {{2026-01-26}} ","2026-01-07T14:21:48.106Z"],["3793554","LSS-61050","LSS","dieulinh.tran@bolt.eu","Diệu Linh Tran","The supplier would like their NDA to be signed as well. This means there would be two NDAs in place: one based on our standard NDA template and one based on theirs.\n\nWould there be any concerns or considerations regarding signing both agreements? The supplier is asking to have both NDAs executed - are we okay with this?","2026-01-07T14:21:50.285Z"],["3793555","LSS-60621","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Thank you [~accountid:712020:70d80a66-553d-4db2-b50f-6bdb7d3bd7a1]! Not sure I completely understand this one, apologies! Am I correct the process would be as follows:\n\n* business customer needs a ride\n* business customer reaches out to GS to request a ride\n* GS forwards the request to Bolt\n* Bolt is arranging the ride for the business customer via Ride Booker\n\nAt which step of this process would business customer be introduced our Business T&Cs?","2026-01-07T14:22:15.820Z"],["3793556","DRX-28001","DRX","ajinkya.deshmukh@bolt.eu","Ajinkya Suhas Deshmukh","Tested on DI.127.0 (194280211) Firebase build on iPhone 11 iOS:26\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-07-2026 16-11-52_1.MP4]","2026-01-07T14:22:55.993Z"],["3793558","EBIKE1-178","EBIKE1","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] do we have to update the 3D cabling based on the final set up ? \n\nQuite a lot of stuff was changed","2026-01-07T14:23:28.284Z"],["3793559","LSS-61219","LSS","sandra.loewe@bolt.eu","Sandra Löwe","Extra Info: 2 Signatures have to be collected - 1 for the main contract, 1 for the appendix. Thank you!","2026-01-07T14:23:49.628Z"],["3793560","CEBF-1815","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","[~accountid:712020:fc274657-f7b5-4366-9f2d-5ec68865cf48] values erased after the saving","2026-01-07T14:23:54.556Z"],["3793561","CSXPC-233","CSXPC","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","KB article updated and changes announced to agents","2026-01-07T14:24:03.802Z"],["3793565","LSS-58530","LSS","elena.skoutaridou@bolt.eu","Elena Skoutaridou","Hey [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] thank you for this. Can we also include this paragraph? It will be needed for the old office and the new office in the next months\n\nTo represent the Company before the Electricity Authority of Cyprus (EAC), the Water Board and any water supply authority, as well as internet and telecommunications service providers, including but not limited to submitting applications, signing and filing forms and declarations, requesting, receiving and providing information and documents, arranging connections, disconnections, reconnections, installations, transfers or changes of services, and generally performing any acts necessary in relation to electricity, water and internet/telecommunications services for the Company.","2026-01-07T14:24:50.172Z"],["3793566","PFI-830555","PFI","guilherme.oliveira@bolt.eu","Guilherme Oliveira","Thanks [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] do you mean this is a Bolt Business customer? ","2026-01-07T14:25:05.375Z"],["3793567","BEE-3619","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Hey, it's done :white_check_mark:","2026-01-07T14:25:12.617Z"],["3793569","WEBSD-1459","WEBSD","maria.montoya@bolt.eu","Maria Paula Montoya","!Capture d’écran 2026-01-07 à 15.20.54.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Capture d’écran 2026-01-07 à 15.22.40.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T14:26:08.986Z"],["3793570","EBIKE1-6","EBIKE1","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","[~accountid:5eb363355862510b794e3507] please ask MinTa to prepare a new frame for the pedaling test to check the strength of the controller bracket. \n\nIt is important because MinTa has problems with the welding and there is a risk that the bracket might interfere with the battery. If the frame do not brake during the test we can cut the bracket smaller and eliminate the risk.","2026-01-07T14:26:10.445Z"],["3793572","HS-28533","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","Thank you, please let me know what type of signature we will be proceeding with, once you have the confirmation from Fidan. \r\n","2026-01-07T14:26:34.603Z"],["3793573","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767795937940059]*{color}:\nHi, Sudipto! Do they all need to get another attempt to do the verification, or is the goal to disable driver verifications in SA?\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:26:37.758Z"],["3793574","RS-1911","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:31cea34c-cf90-4827-8bcd-428a9ac6e80d] ,\n\nThank you for raising a ticket. CTM is updated:done: ","2026-01-07T14:26:39.538Z"],["3793575","LSS-60982","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9], here’s a summary of the case: The passenger filed a mediation request after ordering a scheduled ride for November 10, 2025. When the ride arrived, it was a shared account situation; the driver and vehicle did not match the app's details. Consequently, the passenger refused the ride and cancelled it in the app, and received a €15 cancellation fee refund from CS.\n\nAt the time of her ride request, a promotional campaign promised €120 compensation if Bolt could not fulfil the scheduled ride. Customer Service did not compensate her because the situation did not meet the offer's criteria.\n\nGiven the shared account issue and the lack of mediator details when requested, I recommend confirming Customer Service's decision but also offering a €120 commercial gesture to resolve the request.\n\nDraft letter here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XcOaUaGWH9qtBPFa3eiQy9OPQhf9lOpZ/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XcOaUaGWH9qtBPFa3eiQy9OPQhf9lOpZ/edit]\n\nWhat do you think? We need to respond to the passenger by tomorrow regarding the mediation request.\n\nThank you in advance for your review.","2026-01-07T14:26:52.967Z"],["3793576","PFI-830532","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Please escalate through the correct channels - the KB link you have provided has the correct link. Billing is not able to support with Partner Payments topics. ","2026-01-07T14:27:04.578Z"],["3793577","PFI-830532","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team!  🍔\n\n- Provider/Courier payment didn't reflect in their balance: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/503\n- Provider/Courier didn't receive payout: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/319\n- Eater had issues with the payment: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/316\n- Early cashout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/556\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/317\n- App and backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/76\n- Balance and Invoices issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/318\n- Invoice Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-07T14:27:10.025Z"],["3793579","PIF-3256","PIF","dmitrii.shilonosov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Shilonosov","one of the solutions is to order messages in message sender cron by last_updated ascending and retry attempt descending, so the new messages would go first. unfortunately that doesn’t solve the ddos attack issue observed by the link below","2026-01-07T14:28:10.833Z"],["3793580","LSS-60621","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","In terms of the contract, I went over your comments and have nothing against them. The only outstanding questions are now:\n\n* T&C acceptance point raised below by me,\n* Privacy-related question raised by [~accountid:712020:70d80a66-553d-4db2-b50f-6bdb7d3bd7a1] ","2026-01-07T14:28:11.734Z"],["3793581","RNTL-29677","RNTL","ping.li@bolt.eu","Ping Sheng Li","[~accountid:61b06988d5986c006a9a8fda] v2 table has been created","2026-01-07T14:28:14.833Z"],["3793582","PFI-830630","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^COMPROB, DE PAGO - GASTOS DE MOVILIDAD CIUDAD MODELO B01UGNT8T.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-07T14:28:18.472Z"],["3793583","EBIKE1-87","EBIKE1","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","I have raised up the issue in YCX chat in WeChat and waiting supplier feedback","2026-01-07T14:28:33.716Z"],["3793585","PFI-830555","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi [~accountid:712020:93f92945-2c23-4781-9680-b6dd154892d8],\n\nNot exactly.\nThe business that I linked is a Post-Paid business, therefore, as per my understanding they give out vouchers to other people.\nI would recommend reaching out to for example [afonso.freitasecosta@bolt.eu|mailto:afonso.freitasecosta@bolt.eu] as they are the one who converted them from Credit-Card to Post-Paid, perhaps they can do another check.\n\nMarten","2026-01-07T14:28:59.661Z"],["3793586","RDXENG-4244","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","(x) *Tested on CI.218.0 and “Who is riding?” is triggered for user.*\n\n[^actual.MP4]\n\nLogs → [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TECH-149723|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TECH-149723|smart-link] \n\nReference to Android comment → [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDXENG-4241?focusedCommentId=3783555|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDXENG-4241?focusedCommentId=3783555|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T14:29:14.868Z"],["3793587","FX-3564","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767796146311849]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3564] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:29:25.698Z"],["3793588","FX-3565","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767796159137499]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3565] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:29:31.038Z"],["3793590","LSS-59454","LSS","magdalena.kment@bolt.eu","Magdalena Kment","[~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] Thank you. Kooperativa has been our insurer since the beginning for the vehicles MTPL insurance and also the cross-border assistance insurance, and Renomia has been our broker since the beginning. ","2026-01-07T14:29:32.648Z"],["3793591","PFI-829900","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Not as VAT compensation - compensation if there are issues with reporting further on. The problem is that we do not have tooling to reissue such invoices 😞 ","2026-01-07T14:29:34.419Z"],["3793593","PFI-829216","PFI","darina.vozgrina@bolt-outsource.eu","Darina Vozgrina","Hi,\n\nThere has been an update regarding the courier's debt. The courier decided not to wait and has already paid the debt to the correct account (the Pärnu account). The debt is now settled, and the city has been updated.\n\nThe courier is now requesting a refund for the initial incorrect payment back to his original payment method.\n\nThank you in advance!\n\n!Screenshot_20260107_160251_Bolt Courier.jpg|width=1080,height=1618,alt=\"Screenshot_20260107_160251_Bolt Courier.jpg\"!\n\n","2026-01-07T14:29:44.497Z"],["3793594","WD-22486","WD","karolina.krysiak@bolt.eu","Karolina Krysiak","I approve ","2026-01-07T14:29:51.258Z"],["3793595","RDXENG-4503","RDXENG","zhanna.shapoval@bolt.eu","Zhanna Shapoval","Was solved by reporter. ","2026-01-07T14:30:12.709Z"],["3793596","PFI-814073","PFI","lauma.sile@bolt.eu","Lauma Sīle","Perfect, thanks so much! ","2026-01-07T14:30:28.285Z"],["3793597","EBIKE1-380","EBIKE1","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","I have asked Suzan to get alternative crank arm samples for testing\n\nAlso we will get alternative crank arms from our current supplier for testing\n\n\n\nAfter all the samples have arrived to LY we can do new tests and then make a decision how to proceed.","2026-01-07T14:30:28.551Z"],["3793601","LSS-61222","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-07T14:31:07.431Z"],["3793602","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767796259003219]*{color}:\n• To give them another selfie check attempt, we can use \"Batch schedule identifications\" tools and need a list of driver IDs to unblock.\n• To disable verifications in SA we need to also change the verification config. Note that this will disable selfie checks for all SA drivers, not only specific ones.\n<@U04RDTQ5AJC>, let me know what is the goal here.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:31:14.452Z"],["3793603","PAW-14692","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-07T14:31:38.412Z"],["3793604","EBIKE1-390","EBIKE1","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","I have asked Suzan to get alternative crank arm samples for testing\n\nAlso we will get alternative crank arms from our current supplier for testing\n\n \n\nAfter all the samples have arrived to LY we can do new tests and then make a decision how to proceed.","2026-01-07T14:31:42.976Z"],["3793605","RDS-850","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] technically anonymous, yes. But consider:\n\n* Driver takes a low number of rides in a given week (say 20)\n* Only one ride has a tense encounter with a rider\n* Driver notices their score drops significantly the following week\n\nIn a case like this, it’s not hard for drivers to connect the dots and figure out which rider gave them the low rating. If a driver remembers where they dropped off that rider, it’s possible for them to seek retribution. Unlikely, but possible.\n\nOur current feedback UI says “Your feedback is anonymous”, but based on user research from [~accountid:712020:2f29b932-0bdf-4a3e-aa45-0ccbb584a767] we thought about adding an (i) icon to explain further and encourage more honest reviews:\n\n!image-20260107-142741.png|width=1300,height=742,alt=\"image-20260107-142741.png\"!","2026-01-07T14:31:48.393Z"],["3793606","RS-1939","RS","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[^SKonica_Min26010708560.pdf.pdf] _(455 kB)_","2026-01-07T14:31:58.671Z"],["3793607","WD-22486","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Access granted!","2026-01-07T14:32:12.068Z"],["3793609","RDXENG-3312","RDXENG","pedro.araujo@bolt.eu","Pedro Araújo","We would like to make this consistent with iOS","2026-01-07T14:32:47.316Z"],["3793610","PFI-830555","PFI","guilherme.oliveira@bolt.eu","Guilherme Oliveira","[~accountid:5fa511639e35e50068b366f0] we are facing a possible fraud situation and it seems to be linked to a business customer, could you and the team check the above? \n\ncc: [~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] ","2026-01-07T14:32:51.809Z"],["3793611","FX-3564","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767796366953239]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3564 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:33:00.321Z"],["3793612","FX-3565","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767796377967409]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3565 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:33:11.659Z"],["3793613","DSR-3351","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] driver response:\n\n{quote}I did not give my consent, please show me in a photo when I gave my consent on 25 April 2025 and 13 May 2025.{quote}","2026-01-07T14:33:16.352Z"],["3793615","WD-22487","WD","matthew.stokell@bolt.eu","Matthew Stokell","Thank you, I will communicate with my manager.\n\nHowever what about my team whose days are not accurate?","2026-01-07T14:33:37.394Z"],["3793617","RDXENG-4244","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","Tested with following flag setups:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 16.32.38-20260107-143244.png|width=329,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 16.32.38-20260107-143244.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 16.32.48-20260107-143254.png|width=330,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 16.32.48-20260107-143254.png\"!","2026-01-07T14:34:00.884Z"],["3793618","CSDT-843","CSDT","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","A new Looker report will be created instead of building a GSheet file - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CSDT-901|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CSDT-901|smart-link].","2026-01-07T14:34:20.685Z"],["3793620","CSDT-844","CSDT","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","A new Looker report will be created instead of building a GSheet file - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CSDT-901|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CSDT-901|smart-link].","2026-01-07T14:34:36.449Z"],["3793621","RDS-1118","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] Ahh yes, you told me about this already. Yes, lets make this easy, in the app.","2026-01-07T14:34:37.875Z"],["3793623","LSS-61225","LSS","kaur.kalmu@bolt.eu","Kaur Kalmu","[^20-2.12125-6 25.11.2025 Raamleping.asice] _(1.08 MB)_","2026-01-07T14:34:53.324Z"],["3793624","CSDA-212","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","A new Looker report will be created instead of building a GSheet file - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CSDT-901|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CSDT-901|smart-link].","2026-01-07T14:35:04.721Z"],["3793626","DSR-3123","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi team, we can answer the following:\n\n{quote}Thank you for your request.\n\nWe can confirm that the individual named above was registered on the Bolt platform as a self-employed driver (independent contractor) and as such was not employed by Bolt. Bolt does not engage drivers under contracts of employment and does not act as their employer.\n\nBased on our records, the individual had an active driver account on the Bolt platform between *[start date]* and *[end date]*.\n\nBeyond confirming the period during which the individual accessed the Bolt platform as an independent service provider, we are unable to provide further information. In particular:\n\n* We cannot confirm a “position”, as drivers do not hold roles or positions within Bolt.\n* We cannot comment on reasons for leaving, reliability, honesty, timekeeping, health record, relationships with colleagues, or suitability for employment, as these are employment-related or character assessments and Bolt is not the individual’s employer.\n* We do not provide character references for drivers.\n\nWe trust this clarification is helpful for your screening purposes.\n\nSincerely,\n\nBolt{quote}","2026-01-07T14:36:10.012Z"],["3793628","RDS-1108","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] if there are no net business impacts, I absolutely agree! Better UX overall, no question. \n\nBut when I proposed this before, I remember being told it’s not possible — though I don’t remember the precise explanation (it was in a meeting so I don’t have a written record). Fully support challenging this again. ","2026-01-07T14:36:40.635Z"],["3793629","DSR-3123","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}\n*Internal note - rationale:*\n\n* Drivers are *not employees* of Bolt; they are independent contractors using the Bolt platform.\n* Providing answers to questions on reliability, honesty, conduct, health, or re-employment would:\n** Create a *false impression of an employment relationship*.\n** Risk providing a *character reference*, which we are not in a position to give and should avoid.\n* We can safely confirm only:\n** That the individual had a driver account.\n** The dates during which the account was active.\n* This approach aligns with data minimisation and reduces legal and misrepresentation risk while still supporting third-party screening where the driver has provided authorisation.\n{panel}","2026-01-07T14:36:58.993Z"],["3793630","LSS-61199","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","[~accountid:712020:f8f2551b-99ed-4847-a4b5-9d8bc4dbdfa8] please refer to Flank’s answer on Slack - I tagged you under the relevant post. For similar requests in future, please use Flank. Thank you!","2026-01-07T14:37:09.177Z"],["3793631","RDS-1232","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:9db8be0f-eb61-4ebc-bac7-a9563c14e4b0] is this something you are also interested in?","2026-01-07T14:37:32.646Z"],["3793633","LSS-57150","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:5fbf9493f8b0120069af2a45] here is the agreement: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PjvTw2qY2jVMUasLqCLg40AQyTcAl18E/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PjvTw2qY2jVMUasLqCLg40AQyTcAl18E/edit|smart-link]  please complete the table with the repayment schedule. Thank you! ","2026-01-07T14:37:35.939Z"],["3793635","PFI-814507","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! I’ve followed up with engineering to have them look into this. Will keep you updated.","2026-01-07T14:38:03.527Z"],["3793637","WD-22374","WD","irene.nguyen@bolt.eu","Irene Nguyen","Thank you Oana","2026-01-07T14:38:07.067Z"],["3793638","LSS-60982","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","merci [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] all good, I would just prefer deleting a para. to avoid providing too much detaisl.\n\nthanks\n\nEli ","2026-01-07T14:38:10.967Z"],["3793639","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Shreya Bhandari [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767796687171249]*{color}:\n<@URVM3U4RF> if we do the second, does it mean all will be unblocked as well?\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:38:23.105Z"],["3793640","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Shreya Bhandari [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767796693336499]*{color}:\nWe have an ongoing test\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:38:26.391Z"],["3793641","PFI-830635","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 11.33.47 AM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T14:38:40.595Z"],["3793642","LSS-61126","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Shipment tracking code: [https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=1224487600&submit=1|https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=1224487600&submit=1|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T14:38:57.431Z"],["3793643","WD-22421","WD","valerie.doan@bolt.eu","Valerie Doan","Hi Oana,\n\nIt went through!\n\nThank you for your assistance in resolving and the follow up.\n\nValerie","2026-01-07T14:39:05.359Z"],["3793645","PFI-829756","PFI","erik.andersson@bolt-outsource.eu","Erik Johnatan Andersson","Payments still not marked as paid in company profile. Please advice.","2026-01-07T14:40:14.624Z"],["3793646","DSR-3351","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Thanks [~accountid:6001a723d364960139286c95] - Radu is OOO today (bank holiday), we can follow-up with him tomorrow :loading: ","2026-01-07T14:40:36.084Z"],["3793647","LSS-60630","LSS","oluwatosin.ogunsanwo@bolt.eu","Oluwatosin Ogunsanwo","Hello [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] \n\nThanks for the reply. I’ve tried to complete the assessment form using the information available on Confluence, but I wasn’t able to answer some of the questions as there are no corresponding answers provided there.\n\nCould you please help review and provide answers to the outstanding questions?\n\nFor reference, the unanswered items are highlighted in red and located in column E [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1w7CDmbtYbCSjK5f1schDBDApPXXREBw-ieanzUBQXAU/edit?gid=0#gid=0].\n\nKindly note that this is a T0 account, and they are eager to go live. Please help prioritise.\n\nThanks in advance!","2026-01-07T14:41:04.843Z"],["3793648","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767796879057099]*{color}:\nIf they already failed verification and blocked with \"identity verification failed\", then no, they will also need to be unblocked as well, even if new verifications are disabled.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:41:32.464Z"],["3793651","LSS-61226","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","Creating a personal ticket to track progress on MSA creation for Procurement","2026-01-07T14:42:27.733Z"],["3793652","LSS-60183","LSS","andres.jogi@bolt.eu","Andres Jõgi","(hopefully) Final fix pushed to live today (at 15:23 UTC+2). I will observe the logs for 1-2 days if no new presigned (and sensitive) URLs appear during this time we can consider the vulnerability remediated.\n\n\n!image-20260107-144207.png|width=1654,height=232,alt=\"image-20260107-144207.png\"!\n\n(NB timestamps for log events in UTC time)","2026-01-07T14:42:29.519Z"],["3793654","RNTL-30251","RNTL","rehan.qadir@bolt.eu","Rehan Qadir","Here is the PR:\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159990|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159990|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T14:42:48.387Z"],["3793655","RDXENG-4439","RDXENG","pedro.araujo@bolt.eu","Pedro Araújo","Will close the task as it is for mobile and will be done as part of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/9233454?selectedIssue=RDS-1208&issueViewLayout=sidebar&issueViewSection=overview|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/9233454?selectedIssue=RDS-1208&issueViewLayout=sidebar&issueViewSection=overview|smart-link]","2026-01-07T14:42:48.488Z"],["3793658","LSS-60660","LSS","natalie.kolinova@bolt-outsource.eu","Natalie Kolínova","[~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] is there any other chance how to contact CSPC tier? Cause the ticket is closed already 😕 \nAnd I found info from Slack channel *dev-user-auth-support*, when phone number was removed:\n_“I can remove the phone number, but the user 122661268 will loose access to this account. The user will be able to access this account logging in with the Google account linked to the Bolt account_”. ","2026-01-07T14:43:07.165Z"],["3793660","LSS-61109","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85],  please could you send the attached PDF for e-signature to the following contact: \n\nName : Benbrahim Mohammed Amine\n\nEmail : [+Prestigedrive591@gmail.com+|mailto:Prestigedrive591@gmail.com]\n\n\n\nwith in cc. [raphael.perna@bolt.eu|mailto:raphael.perna@bolt.eu]\n\n[^Bolt - Paris Fleet Drive Lux_Plan de paiement échelonné (a29f70e9-5980-4ccb-b2bd-4450c351788c).pdf] \n\nThank you !\n\nHi [~accountid:712020:af076e83-bb33-4eb6-8634-6e435217c5e4], thank you, the instalment plan will be sent via e-signature and you will be added in cc in order to have visibility on the status of the signature process. The review of the email has been finalised, please feel free to send it to the fleet owner when you are ready. \n\nThank you !\n\n","2026-01-07T14:43:45.985Z"],["3793661","LSS-60660","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:d94524c3-94e8-4fa9-95f2-5afd20cbd32c] - in which case, please ask on *dev-user-auth-support*  🙂 ","2026-01-07T14:44:00.837Z"],["3793664","C3HW-98","C3HW","endrik.salak@bolt.eu","Endrik Salak","The IOT BOMs need to be finished before the production package can be provided for prototype ordering.","2026-01-07T14:45:17.080Z"],["3793665","LSS-60931","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Scan_UA_monobank.pdf] ","2026-01-07T14:45:20.055Z"],["3793666","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767797114428219]*{color}:\nBut disabling selfie checks will prevent more drivers with pending selfie checks from getting blocked.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:45:27.266Z"],["3793669","LSS-61227","LSS","taras.stomin@bolt.eu","Taras Stomin","[^Dohovr na pryiom platezhv BOLT FOOD final (1).pdf] _(949 kB)_","2026-01-07T14:45:51.235Z"],["3793670","LSS-61227","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nTaras Stomin has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-07T14:45:52.837Z"],["3793671","LSS-61227","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-07T14:46:09.322Z"],["3793673","UXROPS-73","UXROPS","akram.yacob@bolt.eu","Akram Yacob","In 2025, the adoption of dogfooding programs \n\n* was about 71 out of 266\n* be a driver: 6 out of 33 were product people\n* be a courier: 15 to 20 out of 24 were product people\n* be an agent: 50 out of 60 were product people \n* but these names are not unique, so we need the lists from all of them. to see how many unique product people did dogfooding\n* Plus since the above people who did them already, they are unlikely to do this again,\n* so we need to get 71+ 14 (20% increase in 2026) = 85 people (about 20% of total product people) need to do dogfooding in 2026\n\nfyi [~accountid:5f4388069aa9650046ece0f7] ","2026-01-07T14:46:52.654Z"],["3793674","INT-759","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","[~accountid:712020:6f095333-c438-429c-9660-a9de5d845fe7] and [~accountid:63184a4556010c40d44804e6] collaborating task","2026-01-07T14:47:06.373Z"],["3793675","LSS-61227","LSS","taras.stomin@bolt.eu","Taras Stomin","[^Комерційна пропозиція Bolt Food.pptx]\n[^ДОГОВІР_ПРО_ПРИЙМАННЯ_ПЛАТЕЖІВ_розрахунок_за_актами.docx]\n\n","2026-01-07T14:47:20.968Z"],["3793676","HS-28706","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Task sent back on Workday","2026-01-07T14:47:41.927Z"],["3793679","PFI-830639","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-07T14:48:32.551Z"],["3793680","RDS-1245","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] I thin k we have very similar plans for individual drivers / some features already live. Is this leveraging the same to allow fleet owners to better manage or a net new solution?","2026-01-07T14:48:33.942Z"],["3793681","PFI-830639","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:712020:92672895-e990-4451-9f97-baec95337272, 610279973900e60070a3495c] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-07T14:48:34.165Z"],["3793682","LSS-61227","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Hey [~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] - please advise whether this can be reassigned to you as this requires a review of the funds acceptance agreement with Universal Bank. ","2026-01-07T14:49:41.911Z"],["3793683","PFI-830640","PFI","damilola.ojo@bolt-outsource.eu","Damilola Ojo","!incorrect commission.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T14:49:54.873Z"],["3793684","LSS-61218","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","\n\nRecording comments from Slack [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C040NCWV75H/p1767790670902769?thread_ts=1767787290.655269&cid=C040NCWV75H].\n\n----\n\nHi @catarina.faria - I am not aware of the origin of this clause, but in any case it’s doesn’t reflect any global processes. There is currently no live global process for collecting cleaning or damage fees from riders, although a process for cleaning fees is in development.\n\nAt present, drivers may be compensated (by Bolt) for cleaning fees that are reported to Bolt via the app after a trip. Depending on the circumstances, Customer Support may request supporting evidence such as photos or cleaning receipts. Teams would like to begin collecting cleaning fees from riders in Q1 or Q2 this year. There is wording dealing with this in the global terms template for passengers.\n\nAcross all markets, there is no desirable reason for Bolt to be involved in claims relating to damage. That should sit between the fleet and its insurers, or directly between the fleet and the customer.\n\nIn your case, Bolt’s obligations to the fleet owner would be set out in the Malta service provider terms. Those terms do not impose any obligation on Bolt to collect sums relating to damage. Clause 15.14.2 also excludes Bolt’s liability for damage, except where caused by Bolt’s negligence or similar fault.\n\nIf the fleet owner has not yet requested any compensation or action from Bolt (the ticket isn't clear on this) then I would not suggest offering any action referred to in the passenger terms.","2026-01-07T14:50:18.597Z"],["3793685","RDS-1291","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] We base this on the VIN as the unique identifier then? Any potential for abuse? E.g. are any of these reapplications ever blocked by Ops?","2026-01-07T14:50:29.853Z"],["3793686","CSDA-212","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hey hey! Sorry for the delay from my side 🙏 \n\nAs also shared via Slack DMs, the plan and the timeline are the following:\n\nHere is the plan we have regarding WBR & MBR dashboards; the plan was also shared in one of the channels with CS OPS and CS EXP managers:\n\n{quote}The current plan from our team's side is to move all weekly & monthly reporting from google sheets to Looker. Earlier last year we've gathered the [*list*|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1o_5dwbbN3QCpjA-hjbKgjku72vIU36tr8E1iAhOOlyA/edit?gid=0#gid=0] of metrics that would be needed for that. We will use those metrics to create a master weekly/monthly dashboard that can be used for all verticals.\n*Scope*: same reports & metrics as in current weekly/monthly files, but with additional time intervals, such as daily or quarterly\nThose dashboards will aim to replace Google Sheets and answer same questions. That way it should make it easier to prepare for MBRs etc.A lot of the metrics from the list above are already available, some are yet to be built. However, we are ready to create a first usable version of this already. Therefore, our current timeline is to:\n\n* Prepare and discuss a *draft of the master dashboard* within the team *this and early next week*\n* Prepare and share the *first usable version* of the dashboard *next week* to the CS organization. The goal will be to get the first version out asap and iterate based on user feedback\n\nIn order for the above to work, dashboard should be usable by all verticals.{quote}\n\nAnd here is more about why it was decided to move along with Looker migration instead - [slack post|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C091MSW59SL/p1765972167637189].\n\nSo next week there will be a first version of the dashboard shared. The format will be similar to the format of the reports we currently have in GSheets, and the list of metrics will be almost the same (some metrics are not yet available in the new models).\n\nPlease let me know if you have any further questions or comments 🙏 ","2026-01-07T14:50:30.051Z"],["3793687","LSS-58166","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","+*Update - 09.01.2026*+\n\nF&F already responded with a fee quote and timeline and I gave our Ok.\n\nWe should have a response by next week.\n\n\n\n+*Update - 07.01.2026*+\n\nSent email to F&F:\n\n_“Hi F&F Team,_\n\n_I hope you are well._\n\n_The Bolt Food team wants to introduce courier-level access restrictions (i.e., suspending/blocking individual couriers linked to a fleet) where couriers show very low acceptance rates (e.g., below 50%), due to a small number of couriers repeatedly accepting but not progressing orders (or otherwise abusing the system). Today, our Malta fleet agreements generally contain fleet-level KPIs (e.g., acceptance/completion rate ≥ 90%) but do not clearly provide for courier-level enforcement._\n\n_We are mindful of Malta’s framework for digital platform delivery workers, including S.L. 452.127, and the associated reclassification risk. We understand that courier-level performance enforcement can be a factor in a reclassification argument, but we also believe that maybe this initiative can be framed as platform integrity/abuse prevention rather than performance management._ \n\n_Our approach and advise to the Bolt Food team was that we believe this is primarily a business decidion since, while the risk is not negligible, it is also true that Malta is currently not amongst the riskiest jurisdicionts when it comes to reclassification (for now), especially if this is applied exclusively to fleet couriers._\n\n_However, we would appreciate your view on this as well: is courier-level blocking for low acceptance rate an absolute “red line” in Malta, or do you consider there is a defensible / lower-risk way to implement it (e.g., framed as platform integrity/abuse prevention; applied only to fleets; based on objective misuse indicators; with safeguards)?_\n\n_We would also appreciate your review and advice on the Fleet Agreement template attached, since the team intends to roll it out in Malta for Fleets. Kindly let us know if you think we can adopt it and/or if you recommend any changes._\n\n_Before initiating your assessment, could you kindly share:_\n\n* _Your fee estimate / quote for this review (including any proposed drafting amendments), and_\n* _Your estimated timeline for delivering feedback._\n\n_Let us know if you have any doubts and/or need additional information._\n\n_Kind regards,”_","2026-01-07T14:50:31.690Z"],["3793688","EBIKE1-397","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] [~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e] I checked and we can use EB1 clamp, just with out the handle. So we can call this task done","2026-01-07T14:50:56.413Z"],["3793689","LSS-59454","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","Thanks for explaining [~accountid:712020:0051a059-9c34-4c65-96bf-ddd219dfda7c]! Please keep me updated once you have answer from LHV. Thank you!","2026-01-07T14:51:25.457Z"],["3793690","EBIKE1-379","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","We can use EB1 seat clamp, without handle","2026-01-07T14:51:38.694Z"],["3793691","HS-28714","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Juan! Thank you for being vigilant and letting us know. I can see from the MinuDoc system that they are still importing some information. Once everything has loaded from their side, you’ll receive an email from them - it might take a week or so. If you haven’t received an invite from them soon, then let us know again and I’ll look into it.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-07T14:51:57.074Z"],["3793692","DSR-3569","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Profile was deleted 5 Dec 2025 ([BH request|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/695540727])\nAll data export without communications plugins [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/personal-data-export/exports/1357027?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]\n[Failed verification|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity-trust/verifications/329aad4b-6cd9-487e-8f36-71d136f9efda?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FStockholm], faces don’t match. User explanation, wife made the picture as a joke.\n\n[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] Can you please advise how to approach this request? Driver is requesting _Immediate reinstatement of my driver account_ however he already requested account deletion that was actioned. \nBecause the account is deleted should we still ask verification-support whether the verification can be rescheduled? Or should we  just find out if diver suspension can be lifted and new account created?\n","2026-01-07T14:51:58.701Z"],["3793693","CSDT-901","CSDT","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Looker dashboard draft - [DRAFT - WMB / MBR Global|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/29407?Time+Grain=Month&Client+Type=All+Client&Geography+Grain=Global&Market+Type+Grain=All+Market&Calendar+%28UTC%29+Date=6+month+ago+for+6+month&Market+Type=&Geography+Value=&Vertical+Value=]","2026-01-07T14:52:04.389Z"],["3793694","PAW-14622","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @sergey-seleznev\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159679\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-07 14:52:35 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-07T14:52:35.855Z"],["3793695","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Benjamin Walch [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767797600232449]*{color}:\n<@U09D62DKH9P> - Is it possible to get a rough timeline on when you would have the capacity to look into this? That would allow us to assess if we (Local Ops DK) can wait or need to find a workaround.\n\ncc <@U090E7WNXUG>\n{quote}","2026-01-07T14:53:35.195Z"],["3793697","WD-22487","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","thanks.\n\nyou can share the employee names and the info around what they have vs what should be","2026-01-07T14:54:01.667Z"],["3793699","DO-5767","DO","kostiantyn.tsykulenko@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Tsykulenko","please specify the schemas SP needs access to, including the new one you want to use for writing. Also please create a separate ticket for Looker as it’s handled by a different team.","2026-01-07T14:54:41.469Z"],["3793700","PFI-820114","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","{quote}In the past, when we had similar scenarios, invoices were fixed and reissued{quote}\n\nCould you please provide an example tickets, so I’ll check accordingly ","2026-01-07T14:54:50.616Z"],["3793701","PFI-830642","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^transferencia-25121594820.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-07T14:54:54.447Z"],["3793705","LSS-61151","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nGot confirmation from Rootly that we can sign and send to them.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-07T14:55:43.908Z"],["3793706","LSS-60982","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:dbc22d70-1983-4414-80b3-27f087787ae4] thank you for your quick support on this short deadline. After reviewing the facts you shared of the situation, we are aligned with CS that the conditions of the offer were not met and that the 120 € compensation was not due. However, given the shared account situation, that the rider could not get another ride and that the details of the mediator were not shared with the rider, it would be our recommendation to settle the case by providing a commercial gesture of 120 € in order to avoid any further escalation. \n\nPlease find attached the letter we have drafted in this sense. \n\nCould you confirm that you can indeed proceed with the compensation of 120 € to this rider (as a manual comp, not a Scheduled Ride guarantee) ? \n\nIf you have no objection to this position and you confirm that the compensation is possible, please could you proceed and confirm once this has been done? \n\nThank you ! 🙏 \n\n\n\n[^2025.01.07 Réponse médiation BOLLE.docx.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T14:55:55.887Z"],["3793708","HS-28054","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","WD task submitted for recruitment - he has NC signed, waiting for the resignation letter","2026-01-07T14:55:58.376Z"],["3793709","RDS-1235","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] I really like the ‘firstly bring campaigns to life’ approach to this one.","2026-01-07T14:56:13.020Z"],["3793712","CAMLE-9578","CAMLE","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","was discussed during metrics review meeting and one suggestion related to {{/getCampaignsForHomeScreen}} timeouts is that we should call {{rider-conditional-campaign}} not from {{campaign-internal}} but from the top level service call itself in the chain.\n\nCC: [~accountid:6305dd67cf3340e8737f8f66] [~accountid:712020:33f5377e-b994-4440-a1e7-1f39311a68a5] [~accountid:712020:b8094c97-c94f-4f57-ace0-b8f45753b3d6] ","2026-01-07T14:56:29.503Z"],["3793714","LSS-60971","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2cddb26-abb1-4f93-a8d1-b7cc3f21bfa3] , thanks for escalating. Could you please clarify with the user whether they recently changed their phone number, and whether they have shared their OTP or password with anyone?","2026-01-07T14:56:32.220Z"],["3793715","ROPSC-347","ROPSC","riin@bolt.eu","Riin Kotsalainen","Update post 07.01 \n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C045B2ATEN4/p1767781969342229?thread_ts=1767351306.614889&cid=C045B2ATEN4|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C045B2ATEN4/p1767781969342229?thread_ts=1767351306.614889&cid=C045B2ATEN4|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T14:56:35.838Z"],["3793717","HWMISC-768","HWMISC","rasad.nadzafov@bolt.eu","Räšad Nadžafov","Reinstated to “In Progress” due to 1 additional task:\n- Create a master tracking file to view all network Cobra decomm’s in one place","2026-01-07T14:57:28.650Z"],["3793720","HS-28668","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-07T14:58:48.187Z"],["3793722","LSS-60122","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","Hi [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7], \n\nPlease find below comments from the landlord. [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qh9N1RvHxtT_xv01OZ-G4j-KZ2XBjth0/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qh9N1RvHxtT_xv01OZ-G4j-KZ2XBjth0/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T14:59:43.275Z"],["3793723","DRX-26219","DRX","ajinkya.deshmukh@bolt.eu","Ajinkya Suhas Deshmukh","Tested on DI.127.0 (194280211) Firebase build on iPhone 11 iOS:26. \n\nVisually there was no difference.\n\n!IMG_1774.PNG|width=188,alt=\"IMG_1774.PNG\"!\n\n!IMG_1773.PNG|width=190,alt=\"IMG_1773.PNG\"!","2026-01-07T14:59:53.283Z"],["3793724","DRX-27872","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26219 has been resolved","2026-01-07T14:59:58.386Z"],["3793726","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","[^192259-E568706-04E---Demande-recevable.pdf] _(85 kB)_","2026-01-07T15:00:52.811Z"],["3793727","LSS-61228","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-07T15:01:35.187Z"],["3793729","RDS-1362","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] Just for sense of scale: how often do we onboard a new larg-ish fleet?","2026-01-07T15:01:49.815Z"],["3793731","SREDESK-7384","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Order-nig alter is completed at 2026-01-07 17:20 EET","2026-01-07T15:02:30.270Z"],["3793735","LSS-60963","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:7837f0a4-cc9c-48c7-9fe9-71cece7a1020] - This appears to be a phone recycling case, where a new user got access to the reporting user’s Bolt [account|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/186699691/overview] via their old phone number +420771200106.\n\nPlease proceed as follows:\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n# Message the reporting user at [bereshivan0@gmail.com|mailto:bereshivan0@gmail.com]:\n{panel}\n\nDear {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add user’s name]*{color},\n\nThank you for your patience while we investigated your case.\n\nOur records show that your Bolt account associated with the phone number ending with +420*****0106 was recently accessed by another user. This happened because your old account was still linked to that phone number, which has since been reassigned by your mobile operator. This can sometimes occur when operators recycle numbers that are no longer in use. Bolt users may log into their account via their phone number. If a user does not enable two-factor authentication (‘2FA’) in the Bolt App nor updates their phone number in the Bolt App after changing it, and their old phone number is later reassigned by the mobile provider to a new customer, that new customer may inadvertently gain access to the existing Bolt account linked to it. This situation may occur if the new customer attempts to register a new account or requests a one-time password (‘OTP’) to a phone number previously owned by an account holder.\n\nPlease note that, in accordance with our terms and conditions available at: [Terms and Conditions|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/] , you must inform us of any update in your contact details, including phone number changes, at the earliest opportunity. This ensures the continued security of your Bolt account and prevents similar situations from occurring. If you’d like to continue using Bolt, please create a new account using your current phone number.\n\nTo protect your data and ensure proper access control, the account in question will now be permanently archived. Once archived, neither you nor the new number owner will be able to access its details, data, or history.\n\nTo help keep your new{color:#bf2600} {color}account secure going forward, please ensure that:\n\n* Your phone number linked to the account is up to date;\n* Your email address linked to the account is verified; and\n* You enable multi-factor authentication via_“My account > Log in and security > Turn on Two-Step Verification”_;\n* You never share your passkey, or OTP codes received via SMS with anyone.\n\nIf you notice any suspicious activity in your account in the future, or receive an email about a new device login, please contact our Customer Support Team immediately.\n\nBest regards,\n\nBolt Customer Support\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n*2.* +*Archive*+ *the disputed* [*account*|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/186699691/overview] \n{panel}\n\nPlease *archive* the account (do not _delete_ / _schedule for deletion_ ⚠️). If you do not have the necessary access rights to *archive* (in contrast to _delete_) an account, please escalate this case to the CSPC team. This is important for audit trails.","2026-01-07T15:03:58.949Z"],["3793736","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767798238642759]*{color}:\nThis is going to need bigger investigation + potentially back end + front end changes, so i think you should try to find a workaround if you need this urgently\n{quote}","2026-01-07T15:04:12.038Z"],["3793739","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","*@user-U01CRA5CR7D*\nHey!\nWe are bidding for Eindhoven tender (good subsidy in the range of €800k/yearly for 3y).\nOriginally the cargo bike requirement was going to be fulfilled by partner (Baqme). Unfortunately they pulled out.\nWe still want to bid independently but we got stuck as Dolly does not manufacture the old model no longer and we need a gradual deployment of 50 cargo bikes (5 in the first 12 months, 50 after that).\nWe clearly do not want to start another retail bike transformation.\nI think the most logic solution is to adapt EB1 to be able to carry 2 children in the back like the below image.\nCan we study such a solution? What requirements would you need (Seat size, passenger mass…etc)?","2026-01-07T15:04:45.643Z"],["3793740","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1",null,"Slack","[Klemet-Gustav Tamm|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02CQUFUKQC/p1767787598143679?thread_ts=1767787598.143679&cid=C02CQUFUKQC|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02CQUFUKQC/p1767787598143679?thread_ts=1767787598.143679&cid=C02CQUFUKQC|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-07T15:04:46.933Z"],["3793741","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","Hey!\n\nVery interesting, I think it should be doable and we can probably build something based on what we developed for the cruiser.\n1. What are the requirements for the cargo bikes by the city if any?\n2. What's the ETA?","2026-01-07T15:04:47.296Z"],["3793742","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","guglielmo.fontanarava@bolt.eu","Guglielmo Fontana-Rava Andreae","1. Very broad: _A two- or three-wheeled cargo bike with pedal assistance, no wider than one meter, equipped with an electric motor, and designed for a maximum speed of no more than 25 km/h; the cargo bike is suitable and equipped for transporting both goods and children._\n2. The official tender requirement is: Minimum 30 e-bakfietsen within 12 months (i.e. spring 2027) Min 50 within 3 years. We’re still trying to negotiating this down, but that’s the requirement as it stands now.","2026-01-07T15:04:48.092Z"],["3793744","PAW-14689","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159988\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-07 15:05:12 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-07T15:05:12.932Z"],["3793746","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[@guglielmo.fontanarava|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63abfbf7159df2c252e762e5] :point_up: I created a Jira RM item for that, feel free to add details there if any","2026-01-07T15:06:29.820Z"],["3793747","RDXENG-3712","RDXENG","pavel.panarad@bolt.eu","Pavel Panarad","* {{Category Addon Deselected}} sends when switching to another addon. It doesn’t happen on iOS – which is right? [~accountid:557058:a4479a6f-2844-4924-9d31-5fa074226e03] [~accountid:60420d6730320b00696dab69] ","2026-01-07T15:06:36.757Z"],["3793753","LSS-60982","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d15dd8c0d64020c403ae98c], in Maël stead, please could you help send the attached letter of response to the passenger Chantal BOLLE please? ","2026-01-07T15:09:19.338Z"],["3793755","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[@guglielmo.fontanarava|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63abfbf7159df2c252e762e5] - the ETA is still a bit unclear, what is the soonest we need to have a sample and deployable units?","2026-01-07T15:09:32.498Z"],["3793757","LSS-60122","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:46ca1bd4-650e-4217-b42f-78a9deb502a3] please see below the revised version and check my comment to clause 4.1, thanks!\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qh9N1RvHxtT_xv01OZ-G4j-KZ2XBjth0/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qh9N1RvHxtT_xv01OZ-G4j-KZ2XBjth0/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T15:10:39.266Z"],["3793760","PAW-14693","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-07T15:11:55.711Z"],["3793761","LSS-61151","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","Hi legal ops \n\nPlease support with signing by Ahto [^bolt.eu (taxify) x Rootly Renewal Agreement 01062026 (1) (142f0f7d-13d8-49d1-bca7-40ce286d2f8a).pdf] ","2026-01-07T15:12:07.305Z"],["3793763","GRWA-1470","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","It was happening due to issues in google sheets, all good now.\nhere is the detailed [thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07H09AR6HL/p1767789615976379]. ","2026-01-07T15:12:52.161Z"],["3793764","WD-21984","WD","aneta.kopka@bolt.eu","Aneta Kopka","Hi Enelys, I have never used these supplier groups dimensions","2026-01-07T15:12:53.715Z"],["3793766","PFI-830647","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-07T15:14:00.487Z"],["3793771","LSS-61226","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","* In 2025 together with DLA Piper we developed to use in the new CLM Zycus \n** MSA for goods & services (not for SaaS) \n*** [+Bolt - Master Supply Agreement (Goods) (V2 - 07NOV25)(208874803.1).docx+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1AqkDA1a0bfgX_egML1nmlwasJfpz3VRa/edit]\n*** [+Bolt - Master Services Agreement (V2 - 07NOV25)(208874922.1).docx+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rNvCFW39p1JFU3f979Q_HZOv6pc1MKlP/edit]\n** T&Cs for PO [+Bolt_PO_T_and_C November 2025.docx+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kx-XDen-tl0BSP30tQ94X86brhTYD5Xj/edit#heading=h.amfg9uvvvp1n]\n\n\n\nAll docs to be finalised ","2026-01-07T15:16:14.053Z"],["3793773","PAW-15268","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Severity: 7\n• Reproducibility: 6\n• Priority: N/A\n• Accept: 1\n• Suggested improvements: Sufficient for triage","2026-01-07T15:16:54.293Z"],["3793775","LSS-61188","LSS","luke.grima@bolt.eu","Luke Grima","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac], thanks for the above!\n\nWill reply as you have suggested, and will let you know should they come back with any further feedback.\n\nThanks!\n\n","2026-01-07T15:17:33.942Z"],["3793777","LSS-60650","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Thank you so much [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] this is super. I went over the ENG version, I have no concerns overall but in addition to your observations:\n\n#  it seems (but might be a translation issue: that in clause 1.3.2. we should ask to change from _\"not known to the Disclosing Party\"_ to _\"not known to the Receiving Party\"_ because the Receiving Party cannot reasonably be expected to know what the Disclosing Party knows about third-party obligations. \n# There are two clauses 1.2. \n\n\nHey [~accountid:712020:e970ee87-f3c5-4314-827e-503375f99daf] we better sign a new one then. Please ask the bank if they can: \n1. Explain what is the need for the term to set to be 10 years? \n\nWe propose: _“This Agreement automatically will terminate upon the earlier of (i) termination of all written agreements between the parties or their Affiliates regarding the Relationship, or (ii) if no agreements are executed, termination of discussions between the parties or their Affiliates regarding the Relationship or delivery of written notice terminating this Agreement;_ +_provided_+_,_ +_however_+_, that (i) each party’s obligations with respect to the other party’s Confidential Information will survive for three (3) years following termination”._ We can agree on those sections/clauses which will survive indefinitely in accordance with common practice. \n\n# _Each person handling the information from our side would need to be indicated in the annex and sign another annex with the confirmation to protect the confidential information_ - We this is an excessive administrative burden and is never done for NDAs. We request this to be removed. \n#  it seems (but might be a translation issue: that in clause 1.3.2. we should ask to change from _\"not known to the Disclosing Party\"_ to _\"not known to the Receiving Party\"_ because the Receiving Party cannot reasonably be expected to know what the Disclosing Party knows about third-party obligations. \n# There are two clauses 1.2. please fix numbering in the document. \n# We need to sign the NDA in English as well, not only in Ukrainian. We are sharing a translation made in-house for your review. We kindly ask you to out it together before signing. \n\n\nFeel free to cc me in the email. Dont forget to attach the NDA in ENG. ","2026-01-07T15:18:18.254Z"],["3793778","LSS-61105","LSS","vivien.antoniou@bolt.eu","Vivien Antoniou","for visibility - there is an issue with the beehive ticket being assigned to safety team and therefore am unable to send the driver an email. I’ve addressed the issue with the assigned person and will update the ticket asap ","2026-01-07T15:18:35.859Z"],["3793779","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Shreya Bhandari [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767799126341599]*{color}:\n<@URVM3U4RF> if I stop the test, the feature becomes default as per our discussion last time.\nWe want to re-start but with only 30% instead of 50% which means we need help unblocking these 50% who are enrolled in the current test\n{quote}","2026-01-07T15:18:59.575Z"],["3793780","LSS-50913","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team, \nDo we have any updates? \nI see that related MVRA ticket was closed.\n\nThanks. ","2026-01-07T15:19:20.320Z"],["3793781","LSS-61105","LSS","vivien.antoniou@bolt.eu","Vivien Antoniou","Hi [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] the driver is registered under Wolverhampton council. ","2026-01-07T15:19:24.089Z"],["3793783","L10N-25323","L10N","marina.santacreu@bolt.eu","Marina Santacreu","Cancelling as source language is not EN.","2026-01-07T15:19:45.643Z"],["3793784","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","{quote}+Details shared by the mediator+: \n\n///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\n\nMadame, Monsieur le Médiateur,\n\nJe vous saisis conformément aux articles L.612-1 et suivants du Code de la consommation, dans le cadre d'un litige m'opposant à la société Bolt, relatif à une surfacturation injustifiée et à un refus de remboursement, malgré la reconnaissance explicite par Bolt d'un dysfonctionnement technique de sa plateforme.\n\n* Rappel chronologique des faits:\n\nLe 23 décembre 2025 à 23h17, j'ai effectué une course via l'application Bolt, au départ de l'aéroport Paris?Charles de Gaulle (CDG) à destination de mon domicile situé 20, avenue du Pays de Galie, 78860 Saint-Nom-la-Bretèche.\n\nAu moment du lancement de la course, le montant estimé affiché dans l'application était de 37,10 Euro.\nÀ l'issue de la course, ce montant a été unilatéralement porté à 59,60 Euro, sans justification valable.\n\nLe chauffeur qui avait accepté la course au tarif initial, m'a alors exigé un paiement de 60 Euro en espèces, exigence présentée comme émanant du service Bolt lui-même. J'ai réglé cette somme afin d'éviter tout conflit sur place.\n\n* Dysfonctionnement reconnu par Bolt\n\nÀ la suite de cette course, j'ai immédiatement formulé une réclamation auprès du service client Bolt.\n\nDans leurs réponses, les services Bolt ont reconnu l'existence d'un dysfonctionnement technique de leur plateforme, lequel a entraîné une surfacturation lors de cette course.\n\nToutefois, malgré cette reconnaissance, Bolt a refusé de procéder à tout remboursement, au motif que le paiement aurait été effectué en espèces.\n\n# Suppression des échanges et éléments de preuve\n\nJe précise par ailleurs que l'intégralité des échanges relatifs à ma réclamation a été supprimée par les services Bolt, ne laissant aucune trace accessible via mon compte client.\n\nHeureusement, j'ai conservé des captures d'écran des échanges, des montants affichés, ainsi que des éléments attestant :du montant initial annoncé,\n\ndu montant final surfacturé,\n\nde la reconnaissance du dysfonctionnement par Bolt.\n\nCes éléments sont tenus à votre disposition et pourront être joints à la procédure.{quote}","2026-01-07T15:19:58.163Z"],["3793786","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","guglielmo.fontanarava@bolt.eu","Guglielmo Fontana-Rava Andreae","I will check exact timeline for you!","2026-01-07T15:20:14.686Z"],["3793787","LSS-60122","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:46ca1bd4-650e-4217-b42f-78a9deb502a3] thanks for the reply - to avoid back and forth with the draft, please communicate the need to have the unilateral termination right back to the landlord and let me know what the final decision is.","2026-01-07T15:20:37.620Z"],["3793788","HS-27589","HS","julien.elghoul@bolt.eu","Julien El Ghoul","Hello [~accountid:712020:58704fb5-3b31-40a0-896f-1d862e6e1fd9],\n\nCould you please tell me why I had 7.01 days of RTT (i.e., 7) and only 6.23 were carried over to my December pay slip? \nThere may have been some confusion because I was promoted at the end of the year and switched from hourly pay to daily pay. But I shouldn't lose the RTT days I had accumulated before when I was on hourly pay.\n\nIf you could assist me with this please,\nBest ","2026-01-07T15:20:45.142Z"],["3793795","HS-28704","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-07T15:26:00.798Z"],["3793796","PFI-830658","PFI","dmytro.skrebnytskyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Dmytro Skrebnytskyi","[^Виписка за рахунком20260107_165931_877.pdf]","2026-01-07T15:27:19.726Z"],["3793797","HS-28524","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Employee cancelled.","2026-01-07T15:27:36.170Z"],["3793798","RDXENG-3712","RDXENG","oleg.voitenko@bolt.eu","Oleg Voitenko","[~accountid:5c66c5ba58edf75c2b8e458b] I would prefer to avoid multiple events being sent at the same time but do not have strong opinion.","2026-01-07T15:30:04.864Z"],["3793800","EBIKE1-399","EBIKE1","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","I test fitted the last cables (IOT to basket) and everything fits well and all wire lengths are good (/) \n\n!image-20260107-152342.png|width=643,alt=\"image-20260107-152342.png\"!\n\n!image-20260107-153055.png|width=624,alt=\"image-20260107-153055.png\"!","2026-01-07T15:31:30.987Z"],["3793802","FX-3572","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767799917715389]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3572] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T15:32:12.140Z"],["3793803","FX-3572","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Halavan [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767799920386979]*{color}:\nReducing back to 1000 as I see some requests started to time out on p99\n{quote}","2026-01-07T15:32:13.902Z"],["3793804","WFM-9872","WFM","francisco.silva@bolt-outsource.eu","Francisco Moreira Da Silva","Hi [~accountid:5ee36bc3283ae50ab5999c9e] thank you!\n\nAfter reviewing it seems that keeps not appearing any queue as per below.\n\n\n\nCould you please help?\n\n!image-20260107-153159.png|width=1104,height=690,alt=\"image-20260107-153159.png\"!\n\n\n","2026-01-07T15:32:16.688Z"],["3793806","PFI-829471","PFI","laura.loaiza@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Muñoz","New case: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719334667|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719334667]\n\nbusiness profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/264713?tab=business_company|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/264713?tab=business_company]","2026-01-07T15:32:52.912Z"],["3793807","LSS-50913","LSS","edik.davtian@bolt.eu","Edik Davtian","Hi [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] \n\nHappy New Year! \n\n\n\njust to update, we had the MVRA meeting earlier today & I shared with Legal that - agreement is on RIMI’s side to approve & proceed with signing. Therefore, we do not expect anything else in the current stage to come to legal as of now. \n\n\n\nStatus:\n\n*  agreement should be approved by RIMI’s procurement to be proceeded for signing. The process started on 05.01 & will take a week approximately. \n* Then we expect it to go to Marketa & be signed by Dokobit (as RIMI preferred).\n* It means that once signed - we would need to share the agreement here in the ticket for Archiving purposes, if I remember correctly\n\n\n\nOn the separate note, If we would need an Addendum for expansion of RIMI - I will just make a separate ticket as we expect in Q1 to work on the pilot.\n\n\n\nLet me know if there is anything else. ","2026-01-07T15:33:12.001Z"],["3793809","CRC-1490","CRC","ahmad.eldefrawy@bolt.eu","Ahmad ElDefrawy","Note: nothing to do for BB side after scoping, the rest is on Business team to pick up . We may close this one for now","2026-01-07T15:34:31.222Z"],["3793813","LSS-61212","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Bolt for Baku ACM_07.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T15:36:38.593Z"],["3793815","DO-5772","DO","hassan.farooq@bolt.eu","Hassan Farooq","Hi *group-S05FGH5B82W*,\nQ: I need a new user group under already existing user attribute in Looker. Do I need to reach out to IT or is this something your team maintains? Some examples [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/FIN/pages/4377117377/FP+A+Looker+accesses+overview#Overview] for reference.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 13.53.39.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T15:36:49.615Z"],["3793816","PFI-830663","PFI","juliet.imeze@bolt-outsource.eu","Juliet Imeze","[^TRANSACTION 2.pdf]","2026-01-07T15:38:14.578Z"],["3793817","LSS-57189","LSS","benjamin.walch@bolt.eu","Benjamin Walch","Hi Thomas - Will ping you on slack.\n\nCheers","2026-01-07T15:38:29.195Z"],["3793819","LSS-61230","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","[^New Vendor Request Forms 2025.xlsx] _(50 kB)_","2026-01-07T15:39:27.424Z"],["3793821","RDS-1245","RDS","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] correct - leveraging anything existing/planned for drivers and exposing to fleets","2026-01-07T15:40:52.883Z"],["3793822","WFM-9766","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601569|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601569]","2026-01-07T15:41:35.033Z"],["3793823","LSS-60939","LSS","alejandro.sanz@bolt.eu","Alejandro Sanz","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] , Fine for me.\n\nWould you include the sentence in the agreement directly? (I don’t know when it will be signed from LT perspective). In any case, please note that the sentence should be:\n\n_“This Amendment is entered into on [signing date in January] and shall be effective as of_ *_1 September 2025_*_.”_\n\nMaybe we can put this in the current Appendix A? How do you see it?\n\nThanks!","2026-01-07T15:42:17.848Z"],["3793825","WFM-9885","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","[Hello, it's done[ DE_Ukraine_for Blend_Temp|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/queues/edit/3210001?tab=overview&agent_tab=auto_inbox]","2026-01-07T15:42:29.152Z"],["3793827","WFM-9766","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Hey [~accountid:637b7db2f48fbd9b62d4c450] Aligned with Process team and the permission has been added to Outsource CS - Rides role. Currently its pending approval form permission owner. We will confirm once its  been applied. \n\n\n\nThank you for highlighting this issue.","2026-01-07T15:42:45.530Z"],["3793828","WFM-9886","WFM","francisco.silva@bolt-outsource.eu","Francisco Moreira Da Silva","!Captura de ecrã 2026-01-07 154242.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T15:43:45.660Z"],["3793829","RDS-1291","RDS","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] No, we do not use VIN today as we do not hold this for our cars, light reading investigation [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QN92HVQjozWJzeceChPCrJ7iLcCsrso8rP-0jzO7yTI/edit?tab=t.ajs2u6ed0pji] I did last year into whether we can/should move to this. \n\nyes, reapplications are flagged to ops and blocked - the key thing here is identifying this upfront when the fleet goes to actually register this vehicle, detecting it’s a duplicate, detecting if it’s already blocked etc. and making sure we have single thread of data for this vehicle versus whatever the fleet has typed in. ","2026-01-07T15:43:49.927Z"],["3793831","WDFT-3605","WDFT","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi, as per latest message from Carmen. \nAP team is the process owner here, we thought our researched approach would be a better choice but now we completely understand the business need. \nI would like to kindly ask [~accountid:641ae2031273131f2ae2333a] and [~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82] to sign off on the proposed process:\n\n- Credit Note Due Date that is set in Telema, will be used as input data point for all Workday Supplier Adjustments Invoice Due Date field. \n\nNext steps:\n\n* Confirmation of the new process by AP Manager and Head of ERP Platform\n* Confirmation that new process is possible to implement in the integration by [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] \n* Transfering the ticket to [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] ","2026-01-07T15:45:11.963Z"],["3793832","LSS-61231","LSS","asher.zerbib@bolt.eu","Asher Zerbib","[^Bolt NDA (Non-disclosure agreement)_rev. 05.01.2026 (3).docx] _(29 kB)_","2026-01-07T15:45:26.982Z"],["3793834","LSS-61231","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-07T15:46:08.174Z"],["3793837","PFI-830676","PFI","lorrita.uzoma@bolt-outsource.eu","Lorrita Uzoma","!1000471899.jpg.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T15:47:57.686Z"],["3793838","LSS-55393","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","[~accountid:712020:0db6c6e6-af60-46ff-ba53-133f0ab23c9b] could you please confirm if you have any valid PoA for employement-related actions for Romanian market ([~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95] mentioned to me once that she had probably prepared sth like this but need to confirm with you before we sign my template for RO)?\n\nThe PoAs for rest of the CEE countries are listed below - +*let’s arrange a wet ink for all of them + a stamp for UA and AZ.*+ Thank you!\n\nRO - TBC with [~accountid:712020:0db6c6e6-af60-46ff-ba53-133f0ab23c9b] as said above\n\n[^(RO) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026.docx (7f3a3a9a-f18f-4ea5-999e-aeb2326ce4a3).pdf]\n[^(CZ) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026.docx (2708e67a-0d54-4280-8d83-d132f102e219).pdf]\n[^(BG) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026.docx (b0cda3b1-bc96-42c6-95d7-1fdc08de1412).pdf]\n[^(TH) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026.docx (ffad14a2-0bdc-45ed-9f3b-474ff53d61fe).pdf]\n[^(SL) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026.docx (d34969ec-7a4d-44f9-8ce5-bb26470bf35f).pdf]\n[^(SK) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026.docx (f938a940-2128-4b39-9903-483611637b1e).pdf]\n[^(PL) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026 - Senago.docx.pdf]\n[^(PL) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026 - Nicchiano.docx.pdf]\n[^(PL) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026 - Bolt Services PL.docx.pdf]\n[^(PL) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026 - Bolt Rides PL.docx.pdf]\n[^(PL) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026 - Bolt Poland.docx.pdf]\n[^(AZ) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026 - wet ink + stamp.docx.pdf]\n[^(UA) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026 - LLC Bolt Operations - Ukraine + stamp.docx.pdf]\n[^(UA) PoA HR - A. Lipson 2026 - LLC TY Services Ukraine + stamp.docx.pdf]\n\n*the signing representative of Bolt: as indicated in each PoA* \n\nmany thanks 😀 ","2026-01-07T15:48:47.548Z"],["3793839","LSS-47399","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hello [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] , if you have time, could you please assist here with drafting the sample cooperation agreement with branding partners in EE?🙏\nWe don't have a tailored global template, but the following could be used: \n\n# [Romanian template |https://docs.google.com/document/d/14QmqxCRzofvMs5zO37j2nlMKrPgT7L51cP0awuwPz7g/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.scgmr3d9y5mm]\n# Global services agreement template (adjust where needed), include branding SLAs in the SLA section. [^Services_agreement_and_SOW_consultant_excl.non-compete_[TEMPLATE]_2023.docx] I could not find it on confluence, therefore attached below. \n\nPlease clarify the commercial terms with the business first - the branding process, standards to follow (I see guidelines are attached, thus those should be integrated into the agreement, keeping our right to amend them at our discretion), fees/discounts, duration of cooperation, termination, payments, invoicing, delivery timelines, warranty, etc. Thank you! ","2026-01-07T15:49:05.074Z"],["3793842","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sudipto Das [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767800972869279]*{color}:\n<@URVM3U4RF> The goal here is to reduce the thr\n{quote}","2026-01-07T15:49:45.959Z"],["3793846","LSS-61233","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","* *Background*:\n** We are trying to optimise driver-rider matching. In the past, we have used historical driver performance (DQO) to reorder/filter drivers with poor historical performance. However, we have not previously looked at recent driver activity.\n** Business is proposing looking at recent driver activity (in the last 15-60 minutes) to predict driver acceptance probability, and reorder the queue based on that probability.\n*** This was already shadow tested in London in Dec 2025.\n** Probability will be calculated using simple LightGBM classifier (appears to leverage machine learning) which will look at:\n*** (i) Order features (price, duration, distance, location).\n*** (ii) Match features (ETA, pickup distance, optionality).\n*** (iii) Last 15 minutes driver activity (number of order tries, and responses).\n*** (iv) Last 60 minutes driver activity (number of order tries, and responses).\n*** (v) City streaming features (55-83).\n**** These seem to be new. Calculated on driver level.\n** In terms of how this translates regarding reordering, it is similar to DQO.\n*** ETA is adjusted. This affects their place in the queue.\n* *Thoughts*:\n** Purpose = Matching drivers and rider effectively; Legal basis = legitimate interest.\n*** This would require a LIA -> I cannot find one. Check with Gab.\n** The main ‘risk’ element here is trip allocation, which is a sensitive topic.\n*** Risk of exclusion / significant effects, which would trigger A22 -> We can argue that A22 is not triggered here. Indeed, the ‘impact’ is just placement in the queue; drivers are not prevented from taking trips altogether. However, we need an idea of impact on earnings (e.g., 25%+ drop).\n*** This does amount to profiling, which would require DPIA -> We would need to update the DPIA.\n**** [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VE_4GMF6-QqjC-F57j2reX4OCWjUORP1/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VE_4GMF6-QqjC-F57j2reX4OCWjUORP1/edit]\n** In addition, AI element in the process.\n*** This will require logging in the AI sheet. Could fall into high-risk, potentially -> I can do this.\n*** System should be designed in a robust way, and we should make sure we are only using strictly necessary data categories.\n*** We would ideally need a more detailed document breaking down how the algorithm actually works, for accountability purposes and to prove it is fair/non-discriminatory.\n** In terms of transparency, escalated risk due to ICO inquiry.\n*** Driver PN -> We do mention looking at historical activity. We can argue (if pushed) that it is covered, although obviously could be better. I need to know more about the new categories / streaming features.\n*** No need for a driver app UI update - we just need something that refers to driver behaviour.\n* *Conclusion*:\n** Questions:\n*** -When next week are we launching the test? How long will it be run for? When would be the full rollout?-\n*** -Other than streaming features, are any of these data categories new? Or are we just doing the same thing in a tighter timeframe.-\n*** -I cannot access the streaming features definition via the internal hyperlink - can some summarise was categories of driver data are being processed, and how this is being calculated?-\n*** -Gab - Is there a general LIA on trip allocation features that I can contribute to?-\n** We can run a test in London, provided that it is limited. \n*** As part of the test, it would be helpful to understand impact on driver earnings.\n** When the feature itself is rolled out:\n*** This should be because the test proved that driver earnings not substantially affected.\n*** We should ensure the system is designed robustly, uses the minimum data necessary, and has better internal docs.\n*** Main risk here is transparency. Depending on new categories, we have typically taken a risk-based approach, but there will still be risk here. \n** Privacy team action items:\n*** Draft / update a LIA.\n*** Draft / update a DPIA.\n*** Log this in the AI sheet.","2026-01-07T15:51:19.372Z"],["3793847","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","The troubleshooting confirms that the production version is correct, meeting the minimum wall thickness of 1.2mm under the clip.\n\nThe issue arises from a loose clip and silicone holder.\n\n*Solutions:*\n\n# We can tighten the clip by modifying the mold, increasing the wall thickness shown below more than 1.2mm, which involves milling material from it.\n!image-20260107-153542.png|width=226,alt=\"image-20260107-153542.png\"!\n# Adding *glue between the clip and holder* will prevent the holder from rotating. We can still replace the silicone holder if it breaks in the future. This will create a plastic-to-plastic glue joint since the slot in the holder is not covered with rubber. You can apply the glue while assembling the holder to the bracket, which keeps the holder and clip aligned. They may misalign if glued separately. [~accountid:60b9e4f58cf91900699878ec] \n\n!image-20260107-160210.png|width=220,alt=\"image-20260107-160210.png\"!\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"8c097f9e-e8c3-44d4-85a6-f0074dce19c9\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":8},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Troubleshooting\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"3D model\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"D3 scooter\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"D2 scooter\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Off-the shelf\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Loose clip and silicone holder.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"There is a \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"gap \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"that could be eliminated for a tighter fix.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"If these features were securely fixed, the silicone holder would be properly fixed.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The clip does not hold it tightly enough, causing the features below to misalign.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"1.2\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"1.24\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"1.25\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"1.69\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"d575f73d8ba071bbd8db1047ce3988fa.mp4\",\"alt\":\"d575f73d8ba071bbd8db1047ce3988fa.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1280,\"width\":720}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":122,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260107-153829.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260107-153829.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":684,\"width\":684}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":122,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260107-153933.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260107-153933.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":104,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260107-154506.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260107-154506.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":226,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260107-153542.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260107-153542.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1280,\"width\":1280}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":306,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"71f6941106895a2d2fc70ddedf2a6b87-20260107-153506.jpg\",\"alt\":\"71f6941106895a2d2fc70ddedf2a6b87-20260107-153506.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":177,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"490928d0938f3aeb04ba7feeac599fa9-20260107-153604.jpg\",\"alt\":\"490928d0938f3aeb04ba7feeac599fa9-20260107-153604.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":177,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"e96789763d2858ac8945c146f5516b07-20260107-153554.jpg\",\"alt\":\"e96789763d2858ac8945c146f5516b07-20260107-153554.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-07T15:52:52.606Z"],["3793848","LSS-61142","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Template that will be used and has been renewed and sent for signing.\n\n[^PoA_Svajūnas Aliukonis (Bolt Drive, LT-LV-EE)_2026.docx]\n\n","2026-01-07T15:53:29.405Z"],["3793851","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","guglielmo.fontanarava@bolt.eu","Guglielmo Fontana-Rava Andreae","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] [~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] \n\n\n* *When is the bid due and what details do we need by that time?* -> 16 January. Actually for the bid I think we don't need much more, but this is for [@giulio.delbalzo|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U07A3J6DKGW] to confirm\n* *Do we need a demo at some point during the bid/process?* No\n* *When is award?* -> 30 January\n* *When is deployment? (i will take this date +12m for the actual deployment of the cargo solution)* -> 20 February","2026-01-07T15:54:39.628Z"],["3793852","PFI-830682","PFI","anna.korniienko@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Korniienko","[^report_07-01-2026_17-45-15.pdf]","2026-01-07T15:55:09.234Z"],["3793853","LSS-52572","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hey, [~accountid:712020:0b391d02-6c8a-4494-99fd-3d2ff0d7ef37] ! I will have it done by EOW. :loading: ","2026-01-07T15:55:32.243Z"],["3793854","DO-5772","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","Hmmm, I have never seen this before, and based on the confluence page, it seems that FP&A is managing such groups.\n\n{quote}FP&A is able to configure for each group their specific data access.{quote}\n\nMaybe you can reach out to them?\nPlease let me know if they could help you.","2026-01-07T15:55:44.764Z"],["3793856","LSS-61234","LSS","jack.cook@bolt.eu","Jack Cook","Also if you could please provide a rough timeline to complete this work that would be much appreciated! thank","2026-01-07T15:56:30.916Z"],["3793860","RDS-1362","RDS","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] Depends what we determine as largish…. like if you’re a fleet of 20 drivers and 30 cars, filing in 50 forms to get live with us is already brutal and you’re not going to jump to it immediately (i.e straight away resulting in days offline). \n\nLooking at last 90 days of fleets created, based on driver registrations completed, we have 50% of the drivers sitting with fleets > 50 drivers. \n\n||*Size (# drivers)*||*Number of new fleets*||*% of fleets*||*Number of drivers*||*% of drivers*||\n|<10|1,420|80%|4,516|21%|\n|10-50|296|17%|6,053|29%|\n|50-100|39|2%|2,634|13%|\n|100-500|19|1%|3,995|19%|\n|1,000+|1|0%|3,817|18%|\n|*TOTAL*|*1,775*| | | |","2026-01-07T15:57:42.565Z"],["3793862","PFI-807434","PFI","dominika.kusz@bolt-outsource.eu","Dominika Kusz","any news?","2026-01-07T15:58:01.321Z"],["3793864","LSS-61235","LSS","jenny.jensen@bolt.eu","Jenny Jensen","[^Branding Agreement_ Hekam AB .docx.pdf] _(235 kB)_","2026-01-07T15:59:25.804Z"],["3793867","SRED-981","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done. Tested, looks good, examples:\n\n{noformat}$ inv ssm.scp -p redis -h route-prediction-global1.prelive.redis.boltint.net -s ~/Downloads/configless.csv -d /tmp\n{\n    \"RequestId\": \"1fa97721-7c46-4f1d-b5be-bf72a7a530f5\",\n    \"Success\": true\n}\nconfigless.csv\n\n$ inv ssm.scp -p redis -h route-prediction-global1.prelive.redis.boltint.net -s /tmp/configless.csv -d . -r from          \n{\n    \"RequestId\": \"fb5e16a5-2fa6-4bdd-9982-c1dda3fc92af\",\n    \"Success\": true\n}\nconfigless.csv                                                                                                  {noformat}","2026-01-07T16:01:25.655Z"],["3793869","PFI-830683","PFI","tung.lok@bolt.eu","Zip Lok","[^Rahalise nõude arestimisest Bolt Operations OÜ-le - MKD SOFIA QUALITY SRL.pdf]","2026-01-07T16:01:42.291Z"],["3793870","LSS-60181","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:618d2fe286c210006aa6241e] [~accountid:61fba8d88d9e3c00688fac2e] - please find the signed doc attached 🙂 \n\n[^ABCD Partners OÜ Provision of Service Agreement (Bolt Drive Services)_ET -2.docx.asice]\n\n","2026-01-07T16:01:59.681Z"],["3793872","MVRT-1443","MVRT","marina.santacreu@bolt.eu","Marina Santacreu","Hi [~accountid:6131fd9fdae0a20071ad22a3]!\n\nDo you happen to have the link for the new e-bike launch blog post in English, so that I start working on the localisation into Spanish? I don’t see any mention of it in the [toolkit|https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1qH2_6EgyicudGaHOv1mLxUqeJHrQqte_Etfjjdkua_o/edit?slide=id.g30dd3bd9a62_0_1173#slide=id.g30dd3bd9a62_0_1173] and I can’t seem to find it anywhere. Thank you! 🙏 ","2026-01-07T16:03:05.104Z"],["3793874","LSS-60181","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/339610?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/339610?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T16:03:34.626Z"],["3793875","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767801851320439]*{color}:\nThe issue with reducing the distribution from 50% to 30% is that targeting in will not allow to keep enrollments. In other words, other drivers will selected for the treatment group. Because of that, to hit the expected percentage all drivers need to be unblocked.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:04:30.702Z"],["3793876","LSS-57405","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, attaching also here the document that they have sent. Is this correct now and what was agreed on?[^Malta International Airport - License and Service Agreement (d9c71c5c-8831-4423-98c1-32d87aa02c2d).pdf] ","2026-01-07T16:04:46.755Z"],["3793877","LSS-57290","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:5e3d86bd22a6390c9c0ebc42] the below program terms were sent to the advisor to prepare separate drafts for different fleets; will let you know when we receive them.\n\n[^2 - Умови Програми.xlsx]\n[^1 - Умови Програми.xlsx]\n\n","2026-01-07T16:05:18.551Z"],["3793880","WD-22505","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","you can now your iban, please updated in WD directly","2026-01-07T16:05:38.541Z"],["3793883","BEE-3626","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","Hey team!\nOne thing that I would like to follow up and ask for permission to update our list of metrics, the feature to drill down to specific cases in queue that was recently developed by you guys made CS teams really amazed and thankful and they have requested a similar ability to view cases with reopen state in live section. Is it okay to update our list of metrics with the request for number of cases reopened more than 3 time (if reopen counter only accounts for manual case handling) ?","2026-01-07T16:06:26.500Z"],["3793885","BEE-3626","BEE",null,"Slack","[Stanislau Binko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:9687d9a4-446e-4c1f-9bf8-68017b3676b1] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QVGBP73R/p1767795399696319?thread_ts=1767795399.696319&cid=C08QVGBP73R|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QVGBP73R/p1767795399696319?thread_ts=1767795399.696319&cid=C08QVGBP73R|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-07T16:06:27.411Z"],["3793886","BEE-3626","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","{quote}3 times as you wrote)? or like e.g. also \"Pending\"/\"On-Hold\" (but without \"Solved\"/\"Closed\" as otherwise it's not very much \"Live data\")?{quote}\n\nhi :wave: small question on this request meanwhile:\n\nwould you want to see cases that are currently \"Open\" (well and reopened ","2026-01-07T16:06:27.795Z"],["3793888","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sudipto Das [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767802004140689]*{color}:\nExactly, and hence the ask to do it cleanly as bulk vs manual over a looooong time for 110k.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:06:56.895Z"],["3793889","PFI-830043","PFI","iyanu.afolabi@bolt-outsource.eu","Iyanu Afolabi","Courier reference number - C005VTQ0T","2026-01-07T16:07:26.606Z"],["3793892","RCE-329","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767802140329009]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@andrii.pustovoit>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-329] `Review pull request 160018 on GitHub` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:09:11.631Z"],["3793895","RDS-1362","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] That is already massive. Thanks!","2026-01-07T16:11:02.655Z"],["3793898","RDS-1291","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] So the license plate is the UID?","2026-01-07T16:12:27.349Z"],["3793900","WD-22418","WD","george.matu@bolt.eu","George Matu","hey Max, sorry for the delay, I was OOO during the winter break. \n\nFrom what I see now, your 15, 16 and 19 Dec visits are correctly captured. (this issue appears sometimes because there is a delay of the Mac address in JAMF), but we are doing weekly corrections to solve for this issue.\n\nAlso, for your remote work request, most likely the request/ approval was done a bit later vs the start date. We are doing a monthly data re-upload and correction for such cases (late submissions/ approvals) and your entire period from the request will now be counted as OOO days. Tomorrow the data should also be refreshed in One Model, so let me know in case something would still be missing. \n\nthanks,","2026-01-07T16:12:47.105Z"],["3793901","LSS-61237","LSS","madara.abeliteorola@bolt.eu","Madara Abelite-Orola","[^20260106_1 police Bolt atbilde.docx.pdf] _(82 kB)_","2026-01-07T16:12:48.489Z"],["3793902","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","as there's 12 months until cargo bikes have to be deployed, we can decide whether to proceed with development after 30th of Jan, correct?","2026-01-07T16:12:56.992Z"],["3793904","PAW-13706","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-local-setup, pint-product-local-development-experience, pint-capability-devx\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-07T16:13:13.990Z"],["3793905","LSS-60982","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hi again, I had the time to finish this case. The letter is sent (with a little loupé, it forgot to attach it at first 😑 ) and the rider has been refunded for an amount of 120€.\n\nI will reply in this ticket if the rider send any response. 👋 \n\n----\n\n*For reference*\n[Beehive case|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/718154179] (email with the letter and refund information)\n*Details of the refunds*\n\n* [full refund €12.50|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3845453204] - [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1467762072/18?orderTryId=2687584725]\n* [full refund €13.20|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3844866559] - [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1467653975/18]\n* [full refund €19.00|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3844552636] - [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1467581470/18?orderTryId=2686872921]\n* [full refund €26.10|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3824517325] - [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1463642981/18?orderTryId=2668035783]\n* [full refund €30.60|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3818794118] - [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1462589867/18?orderTryId=2663669731]\n* [partial refund €18.60 of €25.90|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3814108964] - [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1461580979/18?orderTryId=2659205369] \n\nTotal 120€ refunded\n\n\n","2026-01-07T16:13:35.875Z"],["3793906","PAW-14701","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-07T16:13:48.690Z"],["3793907","LSS-58423","LSS","alexia.lia@bolt.eu","Alexia Lia","Hey! What we can do is actually give the user an allocation of trips through the code, as, if we give one code with €50 they will only be entitled to one trip.\n\nI would suggest we give the user a code with 5 trips (100% free). At the moment ASP is around €10.80 so doable. [~accountid:712020:0b5de1fd-6c52-410d-afb2-757ecf5f9da4] please can we do the code? 🙏 ","2026-01-07T16:14:49.063Z"],["3793908","LSS-61225","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Riigihanke raamleping_Toidu tellimine ja kohaletoimetamine infoühiskonna teenuse vahendusel_Bolt Operations OÜ_Politse- ja Piirivalveamet_07.01.26.asice]\n\n","2026-01-07T16:14:58.856Z"],["3793910","PFI-824581","PFI","richard.ndaa@bolt-outsource.eu","Richard Ndaa","[~accountid:5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b] the driver is still inquiring about the proof of payment.I am also unable to access the proof of payment.  Please assist.","2026-01-07T16:15:13.811Z"],["3793916","LSS-60982","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you [~accountid:712020:dbc22d70-1983-4414-80b3-27f087787ae4] for your confirmation and your help !","2026-01-07T16:18:08.700Z"],["3793917","CRC-2360","CRC","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:29d8b602-d17f-40cd-9cae-5653bc2c54b7] I believe with the use of the app all users of the driver app will have to agree to the TnCs.\n\n[~accountid:6215e9f4347c690072f6f91d] correct?","2026-01-07T16:18:25.051Z"],["3793922","RDS-1291","RDS","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] today licence plate which is HIGHLY flawed (especialliy in places like CH where licence plate follows the driver, not the car) - hence this guy first being specced - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDS-1302|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDS-1302|smart-link] ","2026-01-07T16:19:40.943Z"],["3793923","PFI-830692","PFI","valdas.jocas@bolt-outsource.eu","Valdas Jocas","!46677271-6152-4a7e-b677-78c0d9ab81be.png|thumbnail!\n\n!bcfda8c9-f96d-4039-a070-28d164e14a32.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T16:19:51.114Z"],["3793924","LSS-61099","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, unfortunately Alex hasn’t provided his signature.","2026-01-07T16:20:24.757Z"],["3793926","LSS-57405","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] , \nI believe this is the correct document / version.\nThank you!","2026-01-07T16:21:06.772Z"],["3793927","LSS-43450","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! signed and archived from our side.\n\n[^Licence agreement - Antwerp Distribution_Bolt Operations OÜ_STAD ANTWERPEN_06.11.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T16:21:18.633Z"],["3793928","SREDESK-7384","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Order-eu alter is completed at 2026-01-07 18:21 EET","2026-01-07T16:21:30.424Z"],["3793932","PFI-830693","PFI","aminat.tijani@bolt-outsource.eu","Aminat Tijani","!absa.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T16:22:40.561Z"],["3793933","LSS-61147","LSS","chirag.yadav@bolt.eu","Chirag Yadav","Sharing the docs I got from Attio today\n\nCustomer agreement - [https://attio.com/legal/terms-and-conditions|https://attio.com/legal/terms-and-conditions|smart-link] \n\nDPA attached\n\n[^Attio DPA with SCCs - October 2025 (2).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T16:22:42.578Z"],["3793934","SREDESK-7384","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Order-zaf alter is completedd at 2026-01-07 18:22 EET","2026-01-07T16:22:50.132Z"],["3793935","LSS-57112","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Bolt Business. Special Terms_Bolt Operations OÜ_Evolution Madrid SLU_07.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T16:23:54.329Z"],["3793936","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767803059959069]*{color}:\nOk, so considering that everyone needs to be unblocked, proposal is:\n• Add feature flag disabling feature in SA.\n• Stop the currently running test.\n• Unblocking. For that I need a list of driver that I do not have a good way to obtain (Presto is gone, and we are outside working hours so I probably will not get DB access approved). SA has almost 900k drivers, seems like, so exporting it via Looker might be a bit of an issue as well. So it will take time.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:24:35.418Z"],["3793937","PFI-830694","PFI","kongpop.nakla@bolt-outsource.eu","Kongpop Nakla","!JPEG_1767801649765_5649920577732908966.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!JPEG_1767802066545_4312583130720558925.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T16:24:36.658Z"],["3793938","LSS-60985","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","Hi [~accountid:712020:b63472c3-a177-45a8-b81f-2269d17e33ac] I reviewed and revised, please have a look if the changes fit your needs!","2026-01-07T16:24:46.588Z"],["3793940","LSS-60674","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hey, [~accountid:712020:5cf40694-0837-4f72-b92a-c4936529065f]! I have completed the review of the comments and suggestions from Aladin both in Special and General Terms. I have added my comments for them directly to the document. In addition to that I started preparing this summary for them, which you can continue to prepare if you wish so: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gCl5erQqFDvfmE_kSO3PAORkJGxxu_KB4nBfTTdNztw/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gCl5erQqFDvfmE_kSO3PAORkJGxxu_KB4nBfTTdNztw/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link], otherwise we can skip this.\n\nHere are the commented General Terms: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dJIwxQM3MZBaDbAZaMLLTjoDJGAUA31x/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dJIwxQM3MZBaDbAZaMLLTjoDJGAUA31x/edit|smart-link] \n\nHere is the draft of the Special Terms incorporating changes to which we agree: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ttJWp85IXqke23Ex1Vp9pALCLnDMO6Kg/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ttJWp85IXqke23Ex1Vp9pALCLnDMO6Kg/edit|smart-link].\n\nNext steps:\n\n* Before sending any documents to Aladin please review these clauses and comments I left for you in the documents (they start with “Internal:”. I need your decision/some action from you in relation to the clauses that are subject to business decision listed below:\n** *General Terms*\n*** 4.1 - The original wording is used to prevent Partners from delaying integration.\n*** 4.4 - this wording is needed to ensure that Bolt's losses due to Partner's delay are compensated, if any.\n*** 5.7 - please explain the Partner how refunds and complaints work. We can offer them customised refunds policy if needed (example here).\n*** 6.1 - this clause enables Bolt to amend Agency Fee unilaterally, but we can agree that it may only be changed if both parties agree in writing. The change proposed by the Partner means that Bolt will not be able to change the Agency Fee without Partner's consent.\n*** 6.5 - the Partner is confused about Minimum Order Value concept. I have added the explanation in the comment to 6.5, but I know that sometimes in case of ROD we don't pay Small Order Fee to Partners. Let me know if we don't plan to pay this to the Partner, in which case we can say that this concept and related clauses don't apply to Aladin.\n*** 7.2 - Normally we will only have Agency Fee and it is automatically deducted from payouts. We have this wording in case there will be any other outstanding amounts. So this is more a precaution.\n*** 7.6 - The clause should stay if there will be cash payments, or we can agree to remove it if there will be no cash payments.\n*** 7.8 - the late interest rate is subject to business decision.\n*** Schedule 1, clause 1.1 \n** *Special Terms*\n*** 3 - this is not aligned with our normal operations and we may not be able to accommodate this.\n*** 4\n*** 9 - relates to 6.1 of the General Terms\n*** 11 and 12\n*** 13 - will they determine the delivery fee? I.e. will they have a fixed fee or our algorithm will be calculating the fee?\n* Once you let me know of your decisions / provide all information I will finalise the draft of Special Terms and General Terms and you can send it out to Aladin.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions.","2026-01-07T16:24:51.389Z"],["3793941","LSS-61239","LSS","tyler.ison@bolt.eu","Tyler Hamilton Ison","[^Bolt Services US, Inc._Business_ICMEngagementLetter100015_48165_9.Pdf] _(282 kB)_","2026-01-07T16:25:19.990Z"],["3793945","LSS-61238","LSS","aivo.toots@bolt.eu","Aivo Toots","Could not add files on ticket creation, so adding now.\n\n[^Sertifitseerimise üldtingimused.pdf]\n[^Bolt Technology OÜ ISO-IEC 27001 Certification contract.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T16:26:07.106Z"],["3793949","PFI-814791","PFI","ana.cordoba@bolt.eu","Ana de Córdoba","Hi team, this ticket has been closed but we don’t know if the company has been removed or not from the supply netting ( please mantain the demand netting) \nLet us know if there is anything missing, thanks","2026-01-07T16:26:55.452Z"],["3793950","PFI-814791","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-07T16:26:58.857Z"],["3793951","LSS-60754","LSS","lucca.carney@bolt.eu","Lucca Carney","Thanks for this [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] it has been very helpful\n\nWe’ve since been talking to third parties who offer those accounting tools - before we start working with them is there any due diligence you would like to do, or would like us to do?\n\nSummary of who we’ve spoken to so far, and what we want to do with them linked in this doc: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zCGl6O-bpj88upGA2b0GyW5w9CZHjjrn5mnGwJu0cPo/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zCGl6O-bpj88upGA2b0GyW5w9CZHjjrn5mnGwJu0cPo/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]  \n\n\n\nIs there anything we can do to lightly lock drivers in once VAT registered? E.g. do X rides with Bolt a month and we will subsidise your accounting bill\n\n\n\nThanks!","2026-01-07T16:27:50.999Z"],["3793953","LSS-55393","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Are original documents also needed or just scan would be sufficient? Please let me know, thanks!","2026-01-07T16:28:05.035Z"],["3793954","TAXP-1467","TAXP","alejandro.sanz@bolt.eu","Alejandro Sanz","It was determined that it was not necessary to submit the CbC report in Tunisia. Further details in the FY2024 TP Doc tracker","2026-01-07T16:28:43.228Z"],["3793956","PFI-830695","PFI","jan.dohnal@bolt-outsource.eu","Jan Dohnal","!image-20260107-162910.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T16:29:31.295Z"],["3793957","PFI-830695","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-07T16:29:33.427Z"],["3793959","WEBSD-1442","WEBSD","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:9e668ce4-0877-43c6-bae9-52f1ecbc753f] please find below non formatted version. \n\n[^Bolt E-vehicles - ENG - non formatted .docx]\n\n","2026-01-07T16:30:09.760Z"],["3793960","DRX-28010","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Aleksandr Leontev, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-07T16:30:54.633Z"],["3793962","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767803428753289]*{color}:\nPlease approve feature flag: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/featureflags/edit/14840]\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:31:27.890Z"],["3793963","FX-3557","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767803471481239]*{color}:\nHow would it be possible to know exactly what are duplicates through this bug?\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:31:37.222Z"],["3793964","FX-3557","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767803513337219]*{color}:\nMaybe makes sense for <@U08RKV2V0JJ> to find those vehicles that are possibly made like this and are not in use and provide the ids for us to block them or something :shrug:\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:32:06.902Z"],["3793965","PFI-819356","PFI","ana.rosa@bolt.eu","Ana Rosa","Hello team,\n\nDid you have the chance to look into this request?\n\nThank you","2026-01-07T16:33:05.844Z"],["3793966","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767803576050329]*{color}:\nOk, it does not seem too bad - driver search lists 9701 suspended SA driver with failed selfie checks.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:33:14.183Z"],["3793970","LSS-59921","LSS","teresa.yeh@bolt.eu","Teresa Yeh","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] Though KKday hasn’t gotten back with signed contracts yet, I believe they don’t have further questions about our English-version only contracts. Hence, we can close the ticket. Thank you for your help!","2026-01-07T16:34:42.544Z"],["3793971","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sudipto Das [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767803677574489]*{color}:\nLet me set a short sync with Shreya tomorrow to clarify and move ahead :pray::skin-tone-3:\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:34:49.583Z"],["3793972","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767803694513259]*{color}:\nOh, so we do not need to stop the rollout right now?\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:35:07.255Z"],["3793973","SAI-1232","SAI","anton.belski@bolt.eu","Anton Belski","shadow testing is done. too many requests are marked as violation (14%)\n\nneed to revisit guardrail prompts and routines prompts as well","2026-01-07T16:35:11.533Z"],["3793974","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767803714411939]*{color}:\nIn that case please ignore the feature flag.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:35:26.655Z"],["3793975","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sudipto Das [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767803721876549]*{color}:\nNo! Not right away. Ignored :slightly_smiling_face:\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:35:35.872Z"],["3793976","SAI-1233","SAI","anton.belski@bolt.eu","Anton Belski","results\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09NMLL5FCH/p1765792582658729|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09NMLL5FCH/p1765792582658729]","2026-01-07T16:35:50.078Z"],["3793977","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767803750637399]*{color}:\nAll good, no worries. I'll leave it pending so we can proceed tomorrow. :+1:\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:36:03.787Z"],["3793978","WEBSD-1460","WEBSD","louis.humbert@bolt.eu","Louis Humbert","!Capture d’écran 2026-01-07 à 17.34.25.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T16:36:28.378Z"],["3793980","PFI-830381","PFI","umenwanne.isika@bolt-outsource.eu","Umenwanne Isika","Payment Link: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75933303?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Africa%2FLagos|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75933303?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Africa%2FLagos]","2026-01-07T16:39:48.819Z"],["3793986","FX-3557","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767804208039559]*{color}:\nNot sure we need data analytics here, I'll take a look at the data, should be pretty easy to see those in the same fleet where make model and license plate is the same and I’m guessing all but one has zero activity….\n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:43:57.928Z"],["3793987","PAW-14592","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159593\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-07 16:46:13 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-07T16:46:13.601Z"],["3793988","FX-3557","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767804444712799]*{color}:\nCan you check one case and also check the created by of the duplicates? Maybe we can identify by that too if it's a system user or null or something \n{quote}","2026-01-07T16:47:37.081Z"],["3793992","LSS-60213","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:6215e9f4347c690072f6f91d] \n\n*Contractual assessment – clawback feasibility (RentaCab)*\n\nThe contract does not provide for a generic repayment of the full €440,000 “downpayment”, and Clause 11.2 (full repayment upon contractor termination) does not apply, as the Contractor did not terminate.\n\nHowever, Bolt does have a contractual basis to recover amounts already paid via contractual penalties and set-off, specifically:\n\n* *Clause 3.5*: For each month a car failed to meet the 150h KPI, the Contractor owes Bolt €183.33 per car per month as a contractual penalty. These penalties accrue automatically and create a liquid debt owed to Bolt.\n\n* *Clause 3.7*: Where KPIs are not met during a KPI Year or where the Agreement is terminated before the end of the Term (regardless of which party terminates), the Contractor owes Bolt a KPI Penalty equal to ¼ of the Fee per affected car, per KPI Year.\n\n* *Clauses 5.10–5.11*: Bolt has an express contractual right to set off any amounts owed by the Contractor (including KPI penalties) against Fees and Branding Bonuses payable to the Contractor.\n\nAccordingly, Bolt can lawfully:\n\n* calculate accrued monthly KPI penalties (Clause 3.5),\n* apply KPI Year penalties triggered by termination (Clause 3.7),\n* set off those amounts against Fees and Branding Bonuses already paid or payable.\n\n*Important*: The claim should be framed as net contractual penalties and set-off, not as repayment of a “guaranteed downpayment”. To be defensible, the amount we want to claim must be supported by a penalty ledger (missed months, cars affected, KPI Years crossed). Please calculate this on basis of the above logic.","2026-01-07T16:50:30.877Z"],["3793993","LSS-58375","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^260107_BOL_Návrh na náhradu škody.docx]\n\n[~accountid:5e0f07ab9a4b780d990e9fb9] please find attached the motion to be submitted today. Thank you! ","2026-01-07T16:51:01.198Z"],["3793995","TAXP-1467","TAXP","alejandro.sanz@bolt.eu","Alejandro Sanz","[~accountid:61b9ad7c2900b00071da0b68] Thanks for the comment 🙏 . I meant Tunisia. Updated 🙂 ","2026-01-07T16:52:55.448Z"],["3793997","BEE-3626","BEE",null,"Slack","Thanks Stas! Yes we would be focusing on all live states Open, and Pending / On-Hold and exclude Solved / Closed to keep the metric actionable in real time. The reopen counter should reflect *manual case handling only*, so the signal remains meaningful as currently I suppose Alfred has 3 times \"no\" policy","2026-01-07T16:54:55.056Z"],["3793999","PFI-830695","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Adjustments, Compensations*\n* If driver was compensated a while ago in some CS ticket - and this compensation is still not added to driver's balance -> please raise it with Local operations.\n\n*Why?* \nWhen Compensation is created in CS ticket -> it gets added to a csv file. Then local ops take it once a month and submit it into Manual Adjustment tool. They might submit it late, or submitting csv file gets delayed.\n\n\n*Campaign Bonus*\n* If driver did not recevei a bonus for a campaign -> please raise it with campaign team.\n\n*Why?*\nBilling team does not handle campaign setups. So we do not know when, why, how drivers should receive bonuses.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-07T17:00:40.175Z"],["3794000","PFI-830598","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-07T17:00:40.986Z"],["3794001","PFI-830592","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-07T17:00:41.646Z"],["3794002","LSS-59952","LSS","joao.ramos@bolt.eu","João Nuno Ferreira Ramos","Hey! \n\nReopening this as the police came back with the following email (sent to my personal inbox):\n\n\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"default\",\"localId\":\"e473259a-6e67-42f8-9784-f4a738e8efff\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"layout\":\"center\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"external\",\"url\":\"https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0?ui=2&ik=16ed32dc33&attid=0.5&permmsgid=msg-f:1853670832136200876&th=19b98fccf7fb22ac&view=fimg&fur=ip&permmsgid=msg-f:1853670832136200876&sz=s0-l75-ft&attbid=ANGjdJ9sjRVh6-oOGY0OQTq-N3LCWqxGeCwpocD3WZbfKa_zux6Pd5iik1CrJbCMxfkABJjTppCkZF6Izl09cSX-ZZvUFKTCUJv-_I60PSfz-EEBbg09f3FgnuLddyM&disp=emb&zw\"}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"POLÍCIA\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"SEGURANÇA PÚBLICA                    \"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"COMANDO METROPOLITANO DE LISBOA\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"DIVISÃO POLICIAL AMADORA\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Esquadra de Trânsito da Amadora\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" \"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Assunto:\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Pedido de Informação / Colaboração - Veículo 82-ZT-16\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n \n\nEx.mos(as) Srs.(as)\n\n \n\nBom dia Sr. João Ramos…\n\n \n\nRelativamente ao assunto em epígrafe, encarrega-me o Exmo. Senhor Comandante da Esquadra de Trânsito da Amadora - Comando Metropolitano de Lisboa, de informar V.Ex.ª que, os documentos enviados, não são os referidos no titulo em assunto, mas sim do veículo 05-ZX-99.\n\n \n\nPossivelmente, e por lapso da minha parte, mencionei a matricula errada…\n\n \n\nAssim, questiono a possibilidade de nos remeter a informação acerca do veículo 82-ZT-16, os documentos apresentados aquando da inscrição do mesmo na plataforma BOLT, nomeadamente:\n\n1-    seguros RC e AP;\n\n2-    DUA (Documento Único Automóvel);\n\n3-    Contrato de comodato, e qual a empresa Operadora TVDE, nos períodos abaixo identificados;\n\n4-    Licença de Operador;\n\n5-    Identificação do condutor associado ao veículo/empresa.\n\nData Inicial dos dados Requisitados: 08H00 - 2025-03-31\n\nData Final dos Dados Requisitados: 08H00 - 2025-12-10\n\n \n\nCom os melhores cumprimentos,\n\n \n\n  _“Presente pela Proximidade, Próxima na Segurança!” – Estratégia PSP 2025-2027_\n\n[~accountid:712020:011a9eb3-77af-4c62-bb26-e6c10e6097ec] [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] [~accountid:712020:d77c5e6c-f92f-4d79-955d-9f88e6d0a883] \n\n","2026-01-07T17:03:03.710Z"],["3794004","LSS-56855","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:f1fcbe05-e4af-4cd0-b974-656802946f17] please find the new version of the agreement drafted in accordance with your instructions. \n\n[^7.125. .Hrvatsko narodno kazalište ZG_ugovor o suradnj-Bolt_2025 (2) (1) (2) (1).docx]\n\nRegarding your question:\n\nFrom a tax and VAT perspective, the label of the contract is not decisive. What matters is the substance of the transaction. If:\n\n* HNK supplies identifiable promotional/marketing services,\n* HNK issues an invoice for those services, and\n* Bolt provides consideration (even if settled in kind),\n\nthen this is a taxable supply of services, regardless of whether the contract is called a sponsorship, marketing, or cooperation agreement.\n\nSo no, you do not need to explicitly define it as a “sponsorship agreement” for the taxable exchange to be valid.\n\nh3. ","2026-01-07T17:06:14.339Z"],["3794005","SREDESK-7384","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Order-was alter is completed at 2026-01-07 19:07 EET","2026-01-07T17:07:37.297Z"],["3794006","WD-22512","WD","demetri.manias@bolt.eu","Demetri Manias","!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 12.04.54 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T17:08:21.142Z"],["3794009","SREDESK-7384","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Done","2026-01-07T17:09:53.494Z"],["3794011","LSS-55901","LSS","migle.zuvelyte@bolt.eu","Miglė Žuvelytė","Hi everyone,\n\nAMES will come back with questions or suggestions after their final review later this week.\n\nIn parallel, we’d like to start aligning internally on the practical execution of the offer, especially from a budget-control and risk-mitigation perspective. We would need your’s [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] help here.\n\nWhile we’ve already discussed the positions we want to avoid, we believe it’s important to introduce clear and transparent usage rules in the driver-facing communication, so we don’t end up overspending in cases where drivers do not meaningfully participate in the courses (e.g. attend only one lesson, discontinue early, or leave the platform shortly after).\n\nOur main objective is to ensure that the benefit supports drivers who genuinely complete the language course and provide the official NŠA exam certificate upon completion.\n\nA few constraints to keep in mind:\n\n* The course structure and pricing scheme from the schools cannot be modified, as this is already agreed.\n* We will be covering costs based on actual voucher usage, month by month.\n\nGiven this, we’d like Legal’s advice on what kind of eligibility conditions and safeguard mechanisms could be applied for drivers enrolling in the 4-month language courses.\n\nSome initial approaches we’ve been considering (one of the following could be applied):\n\n# Clearly communicating that if a driver does not complete the course and does not submit the NŠA certificate to us, the costs covered by Bolt for unused or incomplete participation could be deducted from the driver’s balance.\n# Defining consequences for cases where a driver uses the offer but discontinues the course and/or also stops driving on the platform (e.g. balance adjustment or being removed from the platform).\n# Linking coverage of the course costs to continued activity on the platform until a defined date (e.g. end of year), with the possibility of deducting costs from the balance if this condition is not met.\n\nOur intention is not to apply penalties, but to:\n\n* Protect the allocated budget\n* Avoid misuse of the benefit\n* Ensure fairness toward drivers who genuinely commit to completing the course\n\nWe would really appreciate Legal’s guidance on:\n\n* Which of these approaches (or alternatives) would be feasible and compliant\n* Whether and under what conditions deductions from driver balances could be applied\n* How these rules should be framed and communicated clearly and fairly to drivers\n\nThank you very much for looking into this and helping us shape a balanced approach.\n\ncc: [~accountid:5acb064d56d6c72b45183935] ","2026-01-07T17:10:02.434Z"],["3794013","PFI-830703","PFI","wisdom.salaou@bolt-outsource.eu","Wisdom Delphine Salaou","!IMG_0416.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T17:12:22.920Z"],["3794016","DBRE-8590","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 17.14.52.png|width=607,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 17.14.52.png\"!\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569245 | grep \"leader_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569245\n    \"leader_count\": 857,\n\nroot@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569246 | grep \"leader_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569246\n    \"leader_count\": 544,\n\nroot@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569247 | grep \"leader_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569247\n    \"leader_count\": 637,{noformat}","2026-01-07T17:15:14.250Z"],["3794017","DSR-3577","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-07T17:16:06.010Z"],["3794018","DBRE-8590","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster scale-in internal -N internal-kv1-15.sqldb:20160\nThis operation will delete the internal-kv1-15.sqldb:20160 nodes in `internal` and all their data.\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nThe component `[tikv]` will become tombstone, maybe exists in several minutes or hours, after that you can use the prune command to clean it\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nScale-in nodes...\n...\nScaled cluster `internal` in successfully{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster scale-in internal -N internal-kv1-14.sqldb:20160\nThis operation will delete the internal-kv1-14.sqldb:20160 nodes in `internal` and all their data.\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nThe component `[tikv]` will become tombstone, maybe exists in several minutes or hours, after that you can use the prune command to clean it\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nScale-in nodes...\n...\nScaled cluster `internal` in successfully{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster scale-in internal -N internal-kv1-13.sqldb:20160\nThis operation will delete the internal-kv1-13.sqldb:20160 nodes in `internal` and all their data.\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nThe component `[tikv]` will become tombstone, maybe exists in several minutes or hours, after that you can use the prune command to clean it\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nScale-in nodes...\n...\nScaled cluster `internal` in successfully{noformat}","2026-01-07T17:19:16.253Z"],["3794020","DBRE-8590","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster display internal | grep tikv | awk '{print $1, $6}'\ninternal-kv1-1.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-10.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-11.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-12.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-13.sqldb:20160 Pending Offline\ninternal-kv1-14.sqldb:20160 Pending Offline\ninternal-kv1-15.sqldb:20160 Pending Offline\ninternal-kv1-2.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-3.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-4.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-5.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-6.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-7.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-8.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-9.sqldb:20160 Up{noformat}","2026-01-07T17:19:57.910Z"],["3794021","LSS-60784","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached!\n\n[^1st addendum to the agreement for provision of access to Bolt Business platform_Bolt Operations OÜ_Airtel Tanzania Public Limited Company_16.12.24.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T17:20:11.246Z"],["3794023","LSS-61142","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed PoA attached.\n\n[^PoA_Svajūnas Aliukonis (Bolt Drive, LT-LV-EE)_2026.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T17:22:06.728Z"],["3794024","DBRE-8591","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 17.22.10.png|width=607,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 17.22.10.png\"!\n\n\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008779 | grep \"leader_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008779\n    \"leader_count\": 739,\n\nroot@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008780 | grep \"leader_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008780\n    \"leader_count\": 829,\n\nroot@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008781 | grep \"leader_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008781\n    \"leader_count\": 1044,{noformat}","2026-01-07T17:22:26.870Z"],["3794025","LSS-61201","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed documents attached. Documents will be archived to Legisway as well!\n\n[^PoA - shareholders meeting_Bolt Services PL Sp. z o.o._Anna Jeleń_Aleksandra Sotomska_07.01.26.pdf]\n[^Consent for appointment to the management board + address_Bolt Rides PL Sp. z o.o._07.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T17:23:55.101Z"],["3794026","WFM-9843","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Only 1 permission pending reached out to *Lynda* in dm ","2026-01-07T17:24:16.114Z"],["3794027","WFM-9840","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Access granted ","2026-01-07T17:24:42.013Z"],["3794028","LSS-61211","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed documents attached. Documents will be properly archived to Legisway as well.\n\n[^Zenoriah_statement on shareholders address (9e1ae8b3-f99b-4f9e-b52a-f47b71596c81).pdf]\n[^Zenoriah_resolution on address (25aa9ff1-bdf8-48a4-882c-1a8e90d991d5).pdf]\n[^Zenoriah_notice of purchase of shares (767c2c25-8b1a-4169-ad93-0c8abbc537b5).pdf]\n[^Zenoriah_LIST OF SHAREHOLDERS (05e68861-353d-4a26-a386-70aa39e2517b).pdf]\n[^Zenoriah_LIST OF PERSONS AUTHORIZED TO APPOINT THE MANAGEMENT BOARD (1ad2db1c-762a-4c8e-b6b5-8907a55cd94a).pdf]\n[^Zenoriah_consent for appointment to the management board + address Ahto Kink (7174a7c6-af54-45de-ac67-6481007553be).pdf]\n[^Zenoriah_BOOK OF SHARES (4bc45e76-a818-47bc-8443-8dc51b968cb6).pdf]\n[^PoA_Zenoriah_KRS (f57c725a-c9a8-4e6c-9b1c-dd6f440b2227).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-07T17:24:46.711Z"],["3794029","WFM-9777","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Closing ticket as no response in 5 days. If access still relevant please resubmit with all details shared + email of an agent who has the same access","2026-01-07T17:25:46.687Z"],["3794030","DBRE-8591","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster scale-in ti-iot -N ti-iot-kv-12.sqldb:20160\nThis operation will delete the ti-iot-kv-12.sqldb:20160 nodes in `ti-iot` and all their data.\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nThe component `[tikv]` will become tombstone, maybe exists in several minutes or hours, after that you can use the prune command to clean it\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nScale-in nodes...\n...\nScaled cluster `ti-iot` in successfully{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster scale-in ti-iot -N ti-iot-kv-11.sqldb:20160\nThis operation will delete the ti-iot-kv-11.sqldb:20160 nodes in `ti-iot` and all their data.\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nThe component `[tikv]` will become tombstone, maybe exists in several minutes or hours, after that you can use the prune command to clean it\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nScale-in nodes...\n...\nScaled cluster `ti-iot` in successfully{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster scale-in ti-iot -N ti-iot-kv-10.sqldb:20160\nThis operation will delete the ti-iot-kv-10.sqldb:20160 nodes in `ti-iot` and all their data.\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nThe component `[tikv]` will become tombstone, maybe exists in several minutes or hours, after that you can use the prune command to clean it\nDo you want to continue? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nScale-in nodes...\n...\nScaled cluster `ti-iot` in successfully{noformat}","2026-01-07T17:27:15.079Z"],["3794031","DBRE-8591","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster display ti-iot | grep tikv | awk '{print $1, $6}'\nti-iot-kv-1.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-10.sqldb:20160 Pending Offline\nti-iot-kv-11.sqldb:20160 Pending Offline\nti-iot-kv-12.sqldb:20160 Pending Offline\nti-iot-kv-2.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-3.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-4.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-5.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-6.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-7.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-8.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-9.sqldb:20160 Up{noformat}","2026-01-07T17:27:41.724Z"],["3794032","WFM-9846","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","[~accountid:712020:ecec6e8c-aedd-4f4a-be6d-1b5a31d92686] Request was partially approved and applied. This means that 1 permission was *not* approved, see screenshot attached. All other permissions are now part of the role. Please align with permission owners and if approved resubmit a ticket for the permission to be added to *CS - Safety Incident Manager*\n\n\n\nI will close this ticket. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 11.26.05.png|width=921,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 11.26.05.png\"!","2026-01-07T17:28:30.790Z"],["3794034","WFM-9853","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Access granted ","2026-01-07T17:28:58.369Z"],["3794035","WFM-9857","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Access granted ","2026-01-07T17:29:15.114Z"],["3794036","WFM-9862","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Access granted ","2026-01-07T17:29:32.541Z"],["3794037","LSS-57659","LSS","luis.gonzaga@bolt.eu","Luís Gonzaga","[~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] hey!\n\nFinal feedback from the client attached! Waiting for yours.\n\n[^Universal Cover SA final 07_01 CF.docx]\n\n\n\nThank you,","2026-01-07T17:29:48.825Z"],["3794038","WFM-9865","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Access granted ","2026-01-07T17:29:56.365Z"],["3794039","WFM-9844","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541599|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541599]","2026-01-07T17:31:01.847Z"],["3794040","WFM-9844","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Access requested, pending approval ","2026-01-07T17:31:19.461Z"],["3794041","WFM-9838","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Access granted ","2026-01-07T17:31:42.480Z"],["3794042","WFM-9709","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","[~accountid:5f80303a25fbdf0068910efb] unfortunately not yet. we are still waiting for all permission owners to return. ","2026-01-07T17:32:35.941Z"],["3794043","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","This driver has 2 accounts [standard|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/4325244?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] and [flex|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8249003?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] and the flex account is not exist in our system\n\n[@saiful.islam|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/60528926695c3900706cc79e] When was this flex account created?","2026-01-07T17:33:08.640Z"],["3794044","WFM-9709","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Anshul requested to be role owner for the 2 fleet roles but at of 07.01 still not in effective. ","2026-01-07T17:33:20.234Z"],["3794046","TAXP-2099","TAXP","alejandro.sanz@bolt.eu","Alejandro Sanz","IC agreement sent for signature collection [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-60939?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6IjM0ZWEyNGE4ZmVlM2Q2MGRiMjcyMzQ4N2E3ZDY5NjIxMGVmOTNjMzUyOGRlMTgwMDY2OTdiZWZlNDJjNDVlNWQiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiMjMyMzIiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IkxTUy02MDkzOSJ9LCJleHAiOjE3NzAwMjU4ODAsImlhdCI6MTc2NzYwNjY4MH0.GCxmgd5wWTwHvHhXYrdRiIBt_dxKqI79I9qP3gG8Q-Y] in December 2025. Still pending having the agreement signed by all parties.","2026-01-07T17:34:20.777Z"],["3794047","PFI-830695","PFI","jan.dohnal@bolt-outsource.eu","Jan Dohnal","Hey team, I was specifically asking if you could tell me the reason of the deuction. Could you please look into it?","2026-01-07T17:36:27.485Z"],["3794049","PAR-3841","PAR",null,"Slack","19 Nov 2025, 18:26:42 see [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8249003?tab=changeLogs&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A100%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_time%22%3A1757372400%7D%7D]\nFlex profiles are created automatically after drivers sign t&cs in-app. Their standard profile details get copied over","2026-01-07T17:46:26.076Z"],["3794050","FX-3557","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767807970961989]*{color}:\nmaybe this one?\n\nLinked files:\n* [Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 19.44.07.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A7R7R8TMF/screenshot_2026-01-07_at_19.44.07.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-07T17:46:26.717Z"],["3794051","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","It seems something didn't work, [@alexander.fokau|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6083d099cbff1b0070445fea] could you please check why we didn't receive client account created event for this driver  ?","2026-01-07T17:51:29.436Z"],["3794052","PFI-830598","PFI","grzegorz.zabrzecki@bolt-outsource.eu","Grzegorz Zabrzecki","Hey, this automated answer does not answer our issue. The generated invoice is not suitable for billing, as it is stated in the invoice. The rider needs an invoice that is suitable for billing.","2026-01-07T17:55:10.150Z"],["3794054","PFI-830719","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^BOLT SERVICE PAGO B00PQH30T.pdf]","2026-01-07T18:00:30.753Z"],["3794059","PFI-830547","PFI","catarina.silva@bolt.eu","Catarina Caneira da Silva","Another client asking about the invoice: [mafalda.almeida@openbook.pt|mailto:mafalda.almeida@openbook.pt]","2026-01-07T18:00:55.941Z"],["3794061","WD-22418","WD","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","[~accountid:6321ed3ced8abffd7ffcea40], both Monday and Tuesday are missing for me, despite being in the office both days for 9-ish hours.","2026-01-07T18:01:07.695Z"],["3794062","WD-22418","WD","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","I mean this week, Jan 5 & Jan 6.","2026-01-07T18:01:20.636Z"],["3794064","PFI-830721","PFI","aleksandrs.muhins@bolt-outsource.eu","Aleksandrs Muhins","!20260107_111059.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T18:09:02.470Z"],["3794065","PFI-830722","PFI","jane.dike@bolt-outsource.eu","Jane Dike","[^receit_0000006272_.pdf]","2026-01-07T18:09:45.924Z"],["3794067","PFI-830695","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nwe do not know the exact reason for deduction. seems to be some campaign bonus\n\nsince you provided this screenshot - this is as much as we can provide as well:\n\n!image-20260107-162910 (5f866b77-6694-4046-85d3-36067770c47b).png|width=250,alt=\"image-20260107-162910.png\"!","2026-01-07T18:11:53.500Z"],["3794068","RF-76","RF","afua.tutuwaa@bolt.eu","Afua Tutuwaa-Ampofo","Expanded reconciliation to include bolt plus, commission submissions,  and branding spends","2026-01-07T18:14:45.830Z"],["3794069","SREDESK-7378","SREDESK","kourosh.tafreshi@bolt.eu","Kourosh Tafreshi","Sent and On-boarded successfully.","2026-01-07T18:25:29.806Z"],["3794070","LSS-60372","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:763c8a8f-ead8-40d2-bc44-d2be1f5306ad] what’s the status of the CS ticket? Have you followed the instructions below? Please ensure user has their phone number up to date and log user account out of all devices.","2026-01-07T18:25:30.914Z"],["3794073","LSS-61241","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-07T18:31:08.428Z"],["3794078","HS-28718","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Kerubo, thank you for the request. I have sent the letter for signing. Once it’s signed the letter should come to your personal email. ","2026-01-07T18:50:54.097Z"],["3794079","GCAP-278","GCAP","hana.rotinsulu@bolt.eu","Hana Rotinsulu","Fixed, this is due to column rearrangement in sources","2026-01-07T18:51:31.384Z"],["3794087","WD-22296","WD","david.thienel@bolt.eu","David Thienel","In the past, I have seen this divided into 3 different tiers, similar to the “high cost/low cost” solution. If you wanted to only utilize 2 tiers I would keep the “low cost” option at the higher end of the range. With how large the country is, the cost average gets diluted with the smaller cities (which is a very like likelihood for travel destinations). ","2026-01-07T19:14:50.350Z"],["3794091","PFI-826508","PFI","yurii.kotsaba@bolt-outsource.eu","Yurii Kotsaba","Hi! Cashout is still pending and driver is very unhappy. How can we help the driver?","2026-01-07T19:31:29.683Z"],["3794092","RCE-330","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767815347354329]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@maksim.shashkov>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-330] `Migrate tfl datadownloader cron to dynamiccronconfig` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T19:49:20.723Z"],["3794093","RCE-329","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767815842222959]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-329 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-07T19:58:17.267Z"],["3794095","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767816153301319]*{color}:\n&gt; the ask to do it cleanly as bulk vs manual over a looooong time for 110k\nAdmin tooling is the way to go here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/scheduled-blockings/driverBatchScheduledBlockings]\n{quote}","2026-01-07T20:02:48.487Z"],["3794097","PFI-828532","PFI","chinonyerem.ogueri@bolt-outsource.eu","Chinonyerem Ogueri","Hello Team,\n\nPlease be reminded that we’re waiting for feedback. user is complaining about an unrecognized charge 163 kr charge on the 11th of November, 2025. Please review and assist further.","2026-01-07T20:10:46.251Z"],["3794098","RCE-330","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767816931544029]*{color}:\nTrying out [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08BGG4696J/p1767816182386299] @ [https://jenkins.boltint.net/job/PL/job/autocode-baca-autocode/140/]\n\nLinked messages:\n[January 7th, 2026 12:03 PM] dmitrii.shilonosov: :robot_face: *BACA Coding Pipeline is ready for testing!*\nPINT is building an AI coding assistant. It reads your JIRA ticket and writes code for you. We need your help to test it.\n\n*What it does now:*\n1. You give it a JIRA ticket\n2. AI reads the ticket and writes code\n3. It creates a branch and opens a PR\n4. It writes a PR description from the ticket\n\n*Coming next:*\n:soon: Run component tests automatically\n:soon: Auto-pick tickets labelled “ready for agent”\n:soon: Guide the agent via PR comments after it starts\n\n*How to use it:*\n1. Go to Jenkins -> [autocode-baca-autocode|https://jenkins.boltint.net/job/PL/job/autocode-baca-autocode/]\n2. Click “Build with Parameters”\n3. Enter your JIRA ticket ID (e.g. `PAW-12345`)\n4. Click “Build”\n5. Wait ~10 min\n6. Check the PR it creates\n\n*What is supported:*\n:white_check_mark: `bolt-server` repository only\n:white_check_mark: Any JIRA ticket\n:white_check_mark: TypeScript code\n:white_check_mark: You get a PR with AI-generated description\n\n*Tips:*\n:bulb: Write clear tickets — the agent only knows what is in the ticket\n:bulb: Small tasks work better than big ones\n:bulb: Tickets from the “plan” feature of coding agents (Cursor, Claude Code) work well\n:bulb: Check “Build Artifacts” in Jenkins for the work log — it shows what the agent did\n:bulb: The code may not compile — review before merging\n\n*Feedback?*\nTell us in <#C0A74FRM7TM|> — what worked, what failed, what you want next.\n\n:rocket: Thanks for testing!\n{quote}","2026-01-07T20:15:44.384Z"],["3794099","RCE-330","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767816953411889]*{color}:\nDecent draft outcome: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160048]\n\nLinked messages:\n#160048 [BACA] RCE-330: [Duty] Migrate tfl datadownloader cron to dynamiccronconfig\n{quote}","2026-01-07T20:16:06.689Z"],["3794103","PFI-830745","PFI","oluwabunmi.vivian@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwabunmi Vivian","!Moses 2.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T20:41:55.728Z"],["3794105","PFI-830746","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 5.44.01 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T20:45:48.065Z"],["3794106","PFI-830748","PFI","lamine.diop@bolt-outsource.eu","Lamine Diop","!image0.png.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T20:48:05.580Z"],["3794109","PFI-830570","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-07T21:00:35.311Z"],["3794113","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","[@ahmed.farghaly|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63fc5f040a4a47fb8d20cf92] are you asking about Flex driver?\nPayments to Flex drivers should go via their company, the client is company, not the driver","2026-01-07T21:10:56.565Z"],["3794114","PFI-826862","PFI","rauf.fetelizada@bolt-outsource.eu","Rauf Feteli̇zada","Here is 8 december payout link: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/230463673?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Asia%2FBaku|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/230463673?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Asia%2FBaku] ","2026-01-07T21:13:43.399Z"],["3794115","PFI-826864","PFI","rauf.fetelizada@bolt-outsource.eu","Rauf Feteli̇zada","Here is 22 december payout link: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/230463673?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Asia%2FBaku|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/230463673?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Asia%2FBaku]","2026-01-07T21:14:09.252Z"],["3794116","RDS-1173","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] possible scenario is this:\n\n* A driver is at the destination dropping off a rider.\n* At the end of every ride, drivers need to do three things: 1) swipe “End ride”, 2) review the price details and tap “Confirm”, and 3) rate the rider and tap “Confirm”.\n* During this time, new order requests can still be coming in. These are called B2B (back-to-back) orders because these orders are arriving before the current order has ended. Each new order request completely takes over the entire screen and must be accepted or declined (or the driver can wait 15 seconds, at which time it’s auto-declined). It basically blocks the entire app and demands attention.\n* Drivers can reject these orders, which immediately dismisses the order and kills the 15-sec timer. The order is gone for good, and it brings the driver back to the current ride’s UI. But before the driver can interact with the current order’s UI, _another_ order comes in and again takes over the screen. And again. And again. \n\nThis is exactly what’s happening in the video. If you watch closely, the driver is trying to first swipe the red “End ride” button at the bottom of the screen. But they can’t because order requests keep taking over the screen. The driver continually taps “Decline” on these incoming orders (black button in the top right), but there’s still not enough time between requests to even swipe the “End ride” button. Toward the end of the video, they finally manage to swipe “End ride”, but then can’t tap “Confirm price” because of new incoming requests continually taking over the screen.\n\nSo the driver’s goal here is to simply end the ride. But the new orders are arriving so quickly that even this most basic app navigation is completely impossible. \n\nAdding a cooldown means that, once “Decline” is pressed, a full 3 seconds would elapse before the next order comes in. This should give drivers enough time to handle basic tasks like ending a ride or going offline. \n\nBut right now, orders are arriving so fast that it’s completely paralysing. I cannot even imagine how frustrating this must be. I get irritated just watching the video. \n\n(To be clear, this behaviour only applies in super high-demand areas — this isn’t a typical everyday experience for most drivers. But it is still worth addressing.)","2026-01-07T21:20:36.075Z"],["3794117","PFI-830756","PFI","pedro.ferreira@bolt-outsource.eu","Pedro Ferreira","!campaign.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T21:23:42.561Z"],["3794118","PFI-830758","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-07T21:32:09.356Z"],["3794120","LSS-61089","LSS","kenechukwu.ibeneme@bolt-outsource.eu","Kenechukwu Ibeneme","Thank you, Alon. Looking forward to your feedback.","2026-01-07T21:37:10.760Z"],["3794122","PFI-826190","PFI","florina.braga@bolt-outsource.eu","Florina Nicoleta Braga","It wasn't that the payment wasn't received, but why there were discrepancies between the two reports.","2026-01-07T21:42:40.210Z"],["3794123","PFI-829576","PFI","oluwabunmi.vivian@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwabunmi Vivian","*Bank name: Palmpay*\n\n*Account name: Jessica Adaobi Akujekwe* \n\n*Account number: 8124504347*","2026-01-07T22:00:05.419Z"],["3794124","PFI-830768","PFI","sanita.tesa@bolt-outsource.eu","Sanita Teša","!Screenshot_2026-01-06-17-13-36-836_lv.swedbank.mobile.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T22:42:20.121Z"],["3794128","PFI-828481","PFI","agne.ciplyte@bolt-outsource.eu","Agnė Ciplytė","Courier confirmed that all payouts are received now.","2026-01-07T23:13:52.115Z"],["3794129","PFI-830773","PFI","harrison.iyere@bolt-outsource.eu","Harrison Iyere","!IMG_0788.png|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_0790.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T23:14:57.563Z"],["3794130","PFI-828481","PFI","agne.ciplyte@bolt-outsource.eu","Agnė Ciplytė","Courier confirmed that all payouts are received now.","2026-01-07T23:15:00.827Z"],["3794133","PFI-823611","PFI","ernests.suskevics@bolt-outsource.eu","Ernests Suskevics","Agent \n\n","2026-01-07T23:19:55.626Z"],["3794134","PFI-830774","PFI","harrison.iyere@bolt-outsource.eu","Harrison Iyere","!1002468247.jpg.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!1002499754.jpg.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!dd198a91-39db-447c-9637-b38b661b7556-1_all_39119.jpg.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!dd198a91-39db-447c-9637-b38b661b7556-1_all_39120.jpg.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-07T23:27:32.336Z"],["3794135","PFI-830695","PFI","adam.dubjel@bolt-outsource.eu","Adam Dubjel","Hello team, so is there any lead from your side on who should know why was the campaign actually not paid out in full? Because this should be the same [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/supply-campaign/campaigns/542983?periodId=4286591|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/supply-campaign/campaigns/542983?periodId=4286591] and it was paid out in full 🙂.\n\n!image-20260107-233622.png|width=1779,height=514,alt=\"image-20260107-233622.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-07T23:36:26.146Z"],["3794136","PFI-823611","PFI","ernests.suskevics@bolt-outsource.eu","Ernests Suskevics","agent ","2026-01-07T23:46:33.872Z"],["3794137","PFI-806995","PFI","aleksandra.glowacka@bolt-outsource.eu","Aleksandra Glowacka","Hi! Okay, thank you! We are waiting for further information.","2026-01-07T23:51:22.024Z"],["3794138","WFM-9776","WFM","jin.ngo@bolt-outsource.eu","Jin Wei Ngo","Sorry for the missing information : \n\nFor Cyril, may assign (primary) to queue below : \n\n* RH_Malaysia_Safety_Significant\n* RH_Malaysia_T1_Low/Moderate\n* RH_Malaysia_Safety_High\n\nRegards, \nJin Wei","2026-01-08T00:08:43.385Z"],["3794139","WFM-9776","WFM","jin.ngo@bolt-outsource.eu","Jin Wei Ngo","Correction : \nCyril had been added into the safety queue mentioned just now. \n\nSo no further assistance needed for now. \n\nThanks. ","2026-01-08T00:09:36.372Z"],["3794141","RCE-331","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767831688770999]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@test_ci_notifier>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-331] `Create daily test stability report for 2026/01/07` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T00:21:41.335Z"],["3794143","WFM-9776","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello! \r\nSince no further assistance is needed now we will be closing this ticket.\r\n\r\nBest regards!\r\n","2026-01-08T00:32:07.868Z"],["3794144","PFI-830777","PFI","chondan.tepparak@bolt-outsource.eu","Chondan Tepparak","!IMG_0817.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!image.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T00:52:18.096Z"],["3794145","PFI-826494","PFI","kodjo.eklu@bolt-outsource.eu","Kodjo Agbetowofa Eklu","Hello Team, any update please ?","2026-01-08T01:06:16.097Z"],["3794146","PFI-826496","PFI","kodjo.eklu@bolt-outsource.eu","Kodjo Agbetowofa Eklu","Hello Team, any update please ?","2026-01-08T01:06:22.220Z"],["3794148","PFI-829025","PFI","bohdan.kazymyr@bolt-outsource.eu","Bohdan Kazymyr","any updates?","2026-01-08T01:27:01.277Z"],["3794152","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","xiangxue.hu@bolt.eu","Xiangxue Hu","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076]  All done, and the pre-assembly is finished as well.  ","2026-01-08T02:13:25.055Z"],["3794153","DRAG101-444","DRAG101","xiangxue.hu@bolt.eu","Xiangxue Hu","[~accountid:5e46575fc8ec310c955b0d4a] After production finished, it will take 8days to make the pattern, ETA:  {{2026-01-26}} ","2026-01-08T02:23:47.092Z"],["3794155","SCM-523","SCM","zixi.chen@bolt.eu","Zixi Chen","[~accountid:712020:199c869c-84be-4d6f-9d2d-2a504d806ff1]  FYI:\n\nRegarding all the faulty (K1/C1/D1) controllers reported so far, Genfo responded as follows:\n\n{quote}We need Bolt to provide the SN code, the fault reporting details, or send any NG controllers back to our company for actual testing and judgment to determine the conclusion: whether it is an issue with the electronic control itself, then the compensation will be provided.{quote}","2026-01-08T02:54:35.406Z"],["3794156","SCM-463","SCM","zixi.chen@bolt.eu","Zixi Chen","[~accountid:712020:199c869c-84be-4d6f-9d2d-2a504d806ff1] FYI:\n\nRegarding all the faulty (K1/C1/D1) controllers reported so far, Genfo responded as follows:\n\n{quote}We need Bolt to provide the SN code, the fault reporting details, or send any NG controllers back to our company for actual testing and judgment to determine the conclusion: whether it is an issue with the electronic control itself, then the compensation will be provided.{quote}","2026-01-08T02:55:10.792Z"],["3794157","SREDO-397","SREDO","tashik.moin@bolt.eu","Tashik Moin","found out they are trying to push more metrics than the push gateway 1000 limit which is hardcoded and cannot be changed. We already informed them and they are ok with this if there are issues with metrics.","2026-01-08T02:56:32.949Z"],["3794158","SCM-1018","SCM","xiangxue.hu@bolt.eu","Xiangxue Hu","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] Yes, the latest one after modification","2026-01-08T02:58:18.520Z"],["3794159","FDBT-4731","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_bank_payments fails on 2026-01-07 02:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task pl_task failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 377307703523284, 'task_key': 'pl_task'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_bank_payments/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-07T02%3A30%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=partner_payments_payment_cost.partner_payments_payment_cost&base_date=2026-01-07T02%3A30%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-08T03:11:32.705Z"],["3794160","WFM-9759","WFM","nurasyikin.jamil@bolt.eu","Asyikin Jamil","Noted on this, thanks for clarifying [~accountid:6294d703e76a9c00705d0785] ! I will raise another one.","2026-01-08T03:19:56.909Z"],["3794163","SCM-1018","SCM","xiangxue.hu@bolt.eu","Xiangxue Hu","We did IP test again,  now it already passed 47hours by now\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/NoAUtwE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/NoAUtwE|smart-link] Here is the test report [~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] ","2026-01-08T04:00:55.272Z"],["3794164","PFI-830790","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","\n\n[^M2309128.TXT] _(0.9 kB)_","2026-01-08T04:01:09.430Z"],["3794166","LSS-61242","LSS","jutisate.thanakulrutsami@bolt.eu","Jutisate Thanakulrutsami","[^Fleet Link Draft _ TH 25-26.docx] _(712 kB)_","2026-01-08T04:08:36.821Z"],["3794167","LSS-61242","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-08T04:16:13.539Z"],["3794169","PFI-830796","PFI","pakrampar.silrapasangchai@bolt.eu","Pakrampar Silrapasangchai","[^16.BOLT SUPPORT SERVICES (THAILAND) LIMITED._Bolt Business Nov (Transport Nov 2025) (1).pdf]","2026-01-08T04:29:26.927Z"],["3794170","PFI-830797","PFI","favour.chijioke@bolt-outsource.eu","Favour Chijioke","!image-20260108-044525.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T04:45:54.140Z"],["3794173","FDBT-4747","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-08T05:10:36.682Z"],["3794174","FDBT-4742","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-08T05:10:42.649Z"],["3794175","FDBT-4741","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-08T05:10:53.609Z"],["3794176","PFI-830801","PFI","chatrawee.saenwerm@bolt-outsource.eu","Chatrawee Saenwerm","!image-20260108-051008.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260108-051015.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T05:11:16.512Z"],["3794178","PFI-830803","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T05:31:26.820Z"],["3794179","DBRE-8679","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","h3. Resolution\n\n_Root Cause:_\nThe MySQL Prelive job was failing because EC2/EBS AWS API calls were being delegated to r.db.boltint.net \\(Rundeck server\\) without proper AWS credentials or network access.\n\n_Fix Applied:_\n\\- Changed delegate\\_to from r.db.boltint.net to localhost for the EC2 facts gathering block in common*base\\_init\\-tasks.yaml\n\\- Added delegate\\_to: localhost for EBS snapshot creation and status check tasks in tasks*main\\_\\_snapshot\\_backup.yaml\n\\- Added connection: local to ensure proper local execution\n\n_Verification:_\n\\- Successful run: [https://r.db.boltint.net/execution/show/138751#output|https://r.db.boltint.net/execution/show/138751#output]\n\n_PR:_ [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify\\-ansible/pull/5544|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5544]\n\n","2026-01-08T05:35:03.589Z"],["3794197","FDBT-4703","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-08T06:09:58.975Z"],["3794200","PFI-830807","PFI","nonthacha.bunkaew@bolt-outsource.eu","Nonthacha Bunkaew","!1767745322911.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_20260108_125036.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260108-061135.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T06:12:35.441Z"],["3794201","PFI-829900","PFI","juozas.masteika@bolt.eu","Juozas Masteika","Sorry, but I have only more questions 😅 \n\n\n# *Scope of Compensation*\n\nCould you please define exactly what Bolt will compensate? Does this cover the full VAT amount that was incorrectly charged, or does it only cover specific financial penalties (e.g., fines) incurred after a tax filing is rejected? Also, could you confirm if we should advise non-VAT drivers to first attempt to recover the VAT from the STI directly?\n\n# *Required Documentation*\n\nTo ensure our SOP is unambiguous, what specific supporting documents must the driver provide to prove a financial loss? Specifically, is an official 'Rejection Letter' or 'Notice of Assessment' from the STI mandatory to trigger a payout?\n\n# *Escalation Workflow*\n\nWhat is the designated internal workflow once a driver provides the necessary proof? Should CS open a new SD ticket for the Billing team for each individual case, or is there a different escalation channel?\n\n# *Authorized Communication*\n\nAre we authorized to provide a formal written guarantee to these drivers now? If so, do we have a pre-approved template or statement confirming Bolt’s commitment to compensate them if the STI rejects their invoices? If a guarantee is not permitted, what is the approved holding statement we should provide to the drivers?\n\n*As well I’m suggesting this kind of communication regarding such issues-what do you think?-* \n\n\"Hello [Driver Name],\n\nWe are writing to inform you that we have identified an error regarding the VAT applied to your recent invoices.\n\nDue to technical system limitations, we are currently unable to cancel or reissue these invoices. We recommend submitting them for your tax declaration in their current state.\n\nWe want to assure you that Bolt takes full responsibility for this situation. If the State Tax Inspectorate (STI) rejects these invoices or if you incur any direct financial losses due to this error, please inform us and provide the relevant supporting documentation. In such cases, Bolt commits to compensating you for the losses incurred.\n\nWe apologize for any inconvenience caused and thank you for your patience.\"\n\nh3.  \n\n","2026-01-08T06:14:43.197Z"],["3794202","PFI-807765","PFI","felicia.oprea@bolt-outsource.eu","Felicia Ștefania Oprea","Hello, \n\nAny updates on this return? \n\nThank you","2026-01-08T06:15:21.929Z"],["3794203","PFI-829951","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","სალამი, გთხოვთ უკუკავშირს.  \n\n   \n\nSincerely, \n\n________________________________________ \n\nთეკლე გოი/ Tekle goi \n\nCard Manager \n\nCustomer Support Department \n\nTel: +(995 32) 2 27 27 27 \n\n[{color:#0563C1}www.tbcbank.ge{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge] \n\n  \n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!{color:#0093D3}{color}","2026-01-08T06:17:05.984Z"],["3794204","PFI-829951","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Hello \n\n  \n\nPlease get back with an answer{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}  \n\n  \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n   \n\n პატივისცემით \n\n +Best Regards+ \n\n  \n\n{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#595959} -{color} {color:#595959}მირა წოწორია / Miranda{color} {color:#595959}Mira{color} {color:#595959} tsotsoria{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Customer Journey Expert{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Payments Development Tribe{color}{color:#595959}{color} \n\n[{color:#595959}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#595959}{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge/]{color:#595959}{color}{color:#595959}{color}\n !image001.png|thumbnail!{color:#595959}{color}","2026-01-08T06:21:27.581Z"],["3794209","HS-28670","HS","sitang.wasuthit@bolt.eu","Sitang Wasuthit","Hi Berit, thank you for you prompt support as always! Will proceed an insurance request as your suggestion. ","2026-01-08T06:28:51.972Z"],["3794215","PFI-814498","PFI","radka.remenikova@bolt-outsource.eu","Radka Remenikova","hey team, any update please? \n\n","2026-01-08T06:33:20.612Z"],["3794216","HS-27589","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Hey [~accountid:61f3e7cd632452006b8c120b] !\n\n[~accountid:6390559a2acfad92d7b59f11] assist Julien in his question. \n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin","2026-01-08T06:34:01.962Z"],["3794218","DSR-3579","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-08T06:36:12.971Z"],["3794220","HS-28670","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Amazing. The letter should be with you now. Let me know if you need anything else. In the meantime I’ll close the ticket. ","2026-01-08T06:37:15.301Z"],["3794221","HS-28659","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Refilwe, new letter with new dates should be in your email. Have a great rest of the day. ","2026-01-08T06:38:31.112Z"],["3794223","DSR-3467","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","First PDE failed,\nNew PDE without comms, started [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/personal-data-export/exports/800083?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]","2026-01-08T06:40:50.801Z"],["3794226","WFM-9887","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","The agent has Beehive CS Agent, Outsource CS - Rides and CS - Safety roles, needs access to Malta","2026-01-08T06:42:01.392Z"],["3794228","PFI-830814","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","\n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T06:45:50.990Z"],["3794233","WFM-9883","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","asked [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0969DN7RL1/p1767855251138629]","2026-01-08T06:54:40.828Z"],["3794234","WDFT-3605","WDFT","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska","Agreed from my side.","2026-01-08T06:56:04.966Z"],["3794235","RNTL-29425","RNTL","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:5d773c785a4d810d2c4de81c] can you please put a new ETA for fixing what we discussed yesterday- to exclude the deployments done by cron in the WH?","2026-01-08T06:56:56.641Z"],["3794236","WFM-9844","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Hey [~accountid:6092932c000224006a9fb0e4] request approved, role assigned!","2026-01-08T06:56:57.731Z"],["3794242","LSS-59920","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Wojciech Bodal,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-08T07:00:29.325Z"],["3794243","LSS-59775","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Marc Naether,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-08T07:00:29.601Z"],["3794244","LSS-60080","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Mbali Paula Mkize,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-08T07:00:30.054Z"],["3794245","LSS-59862","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Liisa Puu,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-08T07:00:31.789Z"],["3794246","LSS-57056","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Britta Hääl,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-08T07:00:34.971Z"],["3794248","PFI-828386","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Huseyn Huseynli̇,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-08T07:00:35.185Z"],["3794249","PFI-819306","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Cezar-Mihai Voicu,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira