\"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 424, in wrapper\n    return func(self, *args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/operators/aws/ecr_docker_operator.py\", line 139, in execute\n    self.runtime_strategy.wait_until_done(self.container_id)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/docker/batch/aws_batch_container_runtime_strategy.py\", line 215, in wait_until_done\n    raise AirflowException(f\"Batch job status is {current_job.status}, failing downstream task\")\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Batch job status is FAILED, failing downstream task\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_data_integration_workiva_workday_report_for_cash_flow/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-07T05%3A13%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=workiva_workday_report_for_cash_flow_post_generate_files_task&base_date=2026-01-07T05%3A13%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-08T08:10:42.810Z"],["3794512","WD-22415","WD","loredana.panait@bolt.eu","Loredana Panait","Hi [~accountid:62b1977ddcafd965c5ddc33e] , \n\nBolt Operations Ukraine and TY Services Ukraine Payroll primary reports should have happened on 2nd of January. As per your above confirmation, the reports should be now visible in WD, but this is not applicable for any of the two countries. Please check as soon as possible and confirm.\n\nThank you, \n\nLoredana","2026-01-08T08:12:12.351Z"],["3794513","CMO-12987","CMO","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","IH assigned 07.01\n\nOS assigned 08.01\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04LWD26QNM/p1767859835793789|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04LWD26QNM/p1767859835793789|smart-link] \n\nNext step - 26.01 check progress","2026-01-08T08:12:33.763Z"],["3794516","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:5e46575fc8ec310c955b0d4a] Good report. I agree that let’s modify the mold to increase the interference. \n\nMeanwhile, we can try to find glue to fix the current batch. During the upfitting, they can add glue between the snap and phone holder bracket. ","2026-01-08T08:12:42.272Z"],["3794517","DSR-2981","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","I have sent the response and data to the user ","2026-01-08T08:13:28.510Z"],["3794518","PFI-830784","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nYou can provide the user the ARN: 533041606119 to locate the payment. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-08T08:13:39.846Z"],["3794519","DO-5772","DO","hassan.farooq@bolt.eu","Hassan Farooq","I manage user groups for FP&A :sweat_smile:. I was asking in order to request new user group do I need to ask you guys or IT team?","2026-01-08T08:13:43.203Z"],["3794522","LSS-56585","LSS","emmanuel.lewis@bolt.eu","Emmanuel Lewis","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1], just following up again.","2026-01-08T08:15:15.533Z"],["3794525","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] Next time, please let us know if the proposed copy doesn’t work, and we’ll propose an alternative. All copy must be approved by the copywriter.","2026-01-08T08:15:33.774Z"],["3794527","LSS-59991","LSS","sofia.vasilakopoulou@bolt.eu","Sofia Vasilakopoulou","Hey [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f].\n\n# Yes, CaptainSpec is a local third party integrator. They were granted with API access a while back but I don’t recall that they ever had the same requirement with Evolution e.g. to be integrated with all platforms at the same time.\n# Yes Bolt is integrated with other third party integrators on a local/global level.\n# Integration requests are being handled by the integrations teams. [Here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BF/pages/2941981173/Integrations+Overview#How-do-we-prioritise-integrations?-%F0%9F%93%8A] you can read how the team prioritises new integrations requests.\n\nBelow is the response I received from the integrations team for Evolution. As this vendor is not of a strategic importance based on our assessment locally, we did not pursue this with the integrations team.\n\n“We don’t accept all integrators to our platform. We typically decline integrators who have zero or only one restaurant, as supporting a new integration requires significant time and effort from the Technical Support team — including creating a test setup, providing daily support, answering technical questions, and conducting test calls.\nThe article I shared earlier explains how we prioritize integrations. At the moment, we already have several large integrators in our backlog waiting to join, so unfortunately, we can’t prioritize smaller ones over them.\nPlease share the Google form with this integrator and ask them to fill it out. Once submitted, we’ll review the request and decide whether we can add them to the backlog.\nIf you believe this integrator is strategically important for us and should be prioritized, please support the request with relevant data or numbers to help us assess its impact.”\n\n\n\nLet me know if you need any clarifications on the above.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-08T08:15:54.873Z"],["3794532","RS-1924","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] ,\n\nWith this authority, maybe it’s worth adding a note to the authority market info sheet. Since there has been some agreement between Bolt and the Cybercrime Police Service, for future requests, we don’t need to be very strict regarding the proportionality. Please see Sorina’s response for more details","2026-01-08T08:16:45.596Z"],["3794533","FDBT-4689","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_data_integration_workiva_tb_revenue_note fails on 2026-01-07 05:18:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 771, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **exe