//taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26401)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T08:43:36.006Z"],["3794678","L10N-26436","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26401](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26401)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T08:43:37.649Z"],["3794679","L10N-26435","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26401](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26401)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T08:43:37.982Z"],["3794682","LSS-60741","LSS","alexia.lia@bolt.eu","Alexia Lia","Hello again!\n\nI have a couple of questions on the above (black), as well as any clarifications needed (purple): \n[~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] \n\n# *Branding & Sticker Application:*\n## *Taxis*: Branding can be done, in colour with out normal branding criteria, as long as the normal TAXI signs are not disrupted, am I correct to assume so? \n## *NCC:* NCC Vehicles can be any colour of vehicle? Therefore shall we adopt white branding in order to create a more smooth design not to have a lot of colours.\n# *Supplier & Driver Considerations:*\n## {color:#403294}Are there any restrictions when it comes to choosing a supplier for the branding work? - What I meant here, is there any pre-established suppliers who brand vehicles already established with Bolt, or shall I take the liberty of researching for a supplier that we can use in Milan in order to Brand the vehicles once the process is ready?{color} \n## Also ideally we do Branding with Tiering, according to achieved KPIs, is this possible? - Agreed with the Driver behaviour that caught, what I am thinking is more about having different % of branding kickback according to the number of FR or any other acceptable criteria, in order to minimise spend and have better focus of spend. \n## We may need a service agreement template for the supplier who will brand the vehicles, and the fleets? - I need to fine tune some elements, I will get back to you once done if that’s ok. with regards to your question: Ideally both in Italian and English. \n\n[~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] here are my answers for you: \n\n* What specific KPIs are we looking at to determine driver eligibility for branded cars? - {color:#403294}Since this was a preliminary discussion I have not finalised the eligibility criteria for Branded Vehicles. However as we mentioned above, we shall try to steer clear of driver behaviour and stick more to vehicle criteria.{color}\n* What sort of data privacy disclaimer are you expecting here? Are you aware of any previous similar arrangements with branding partners that I could take a look at? I am particularly keen to understand if we typically ask for the driver’s consent to share their data as part of the disclaimer (under similar branding setups). -{color:#403294} I am not aware of any to be honest with you, however I wanted to make sure that since we’re launching in Italy, everything is done in accordance to the regulations of the country, If nothing is needed since this will be through consent of the drivers as they would want to brand, there wouldn’t be the need for anything in particular. {color}\n* Who is the supplier, and how do these arrangements usually work in practice? In particular: (i) Has the supplier specified which categories of driver data they need from Bolt, or has this been determined by Bolt?; and (ii) Are we sharing driver personal data with the supplier for strict purposes that we have set, or will the supplier be keeping/re-using the data for any of its own purposes? - {color:#403294}This is very preliminary, we do not have a supplier yet, in fact I need confirmation from above to start researching suppliers. Therefore I have no answer for ( i ) as of yet, and with regards to point ( ii ) he should not utilise the information for anything else than the branding of the vehicles. {color}\n\nLet me know your thoughts, if you need more clarity please let me know, and I will update you accordingly. \n","2026-01-08T08:43:59.474Z"],["3794683","LSS-52369","LSS","kristiina.klemm@bolt.eu","Kristiina Klemm","[~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] Thanks for the latest comments! Redlined draft has been sent back to Zellis this morning and we will have meeting to discuss on Monday 12th of January.","2026-01-08T08:44:11.493Z"],["3794684","LSS-60824","LSS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Hi Legal Ops, could you please get the NDA signed? Counterparty’s info shared by Eimantas on Jan 7. Thank you!\n\n[^BOLT Operations NDA (Mutual) (Arnon-12.24.2025) - rev Bolt (1).docx]\n\n","2026-01-08T08:44:13.409Z"],["3794688","LSS-41351","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] Thanks for sharing. I will review it and if any questions then post them here or will arrange a short sync. \n\nLiisa","2026-01-08T08:44:21.854Z"],["3794691","RS-1935","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] can I close this ticket?","2026-01-08T08:45:13.815Z"],["3794692","WD-22466","WD","dagmar.olesk@bolt.eu","Dagmar Olesk","[~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82]  Hey! We haven’t received any response since Monday. This is quite critical already. Can you please assign this task to someone else? 🙏 \n\n1. Change Accounting Managers for those countries\n2. Use the same split to assign new account certification approvers\n\n\n\nThank you!","2026-01-08T08:45:32.461Z"],["3794693","MKP-6168","MKP","albert.tumanov@bolt.eu","Albert Tumanov","Not sure why it was rejected.\n\nWe still have the code and TODO\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/rides/marketplace/search_worker/main/service/OrderMatchingService.ts#L677|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/rides/marketplace/search_worker/main/service/OrderMatchingService.ts#L677] ","2026-01-08T08:45:46.445Z"],["3794694","WD-22466","WD","dagmar.olesk@bolt.eu","Dagmar Olesk","cc: [~accountid:624d3e6a45ece00069cdb4e5] [~accountid:638476d83e79f12e572272f3] [~accountid:62ea2a72da8620d53392aa71] ","2026-01-08T08:45:50.967Z"],["3794696","DELIVERY-91","DELIVERY","bertalan.vad@bolt.eu","Bertalan Vad","26W02: M1 finished last week (without the city change), M2 continues this week, I expect to finish the hard part this week.","2026-01-08T08:46:47.098Z"],["3794697","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] The below is the rate\n\n# For the Bajaji TZS 2,000\n# For the car(*Also rename it to Basic)* TZS 3,000","2026-01-08T08:46:47.595Z"],["3794700","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] I didn’t see that you changed the copy for the Motion. \n[~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c] Do you think it’s okay to use “Skip the queue and ride” across all visuals, or do we need some variation to drive better engagement?\n\n[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] Also, if you’re planning to use SW copy, please include it in the media plan before I start designing. SW copy can be shorter or longer than ENG, and it can affect composition decisions, so it’s important that we have the copy in the language you plan to use for the creatives. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-08T08:47:29.640Z"],["3794705","LSS-60768","LSS","wiktoria.lis@bolt.eu","Wiktoria Lis","[~accountid:712020:b1700666-82b2-4a86-82f7-550a84f716c8] apparently, Kamil doesn’t receive our emails - do you know what the issue might be? email address is correct, I double checked","2026-01-08T08:49:04.126Z"],["3794707","DO-5772","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","The Group {{fpa_group_headcount}} does not yet exist. Let's create it first.\n\nCan you tell me the members that you want to have in the group {{fpa_group_headcount}} ?","2026-01-08T08:49:12.271Z"],["3794708","SCM-1116","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","eb1-launch-barcelona Slack channel: [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0A3R8M6DC4|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0A3R8M6DC4|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T08:49:24.684Z"],["3794711","SCM-1018","SCM","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:60b9e4f58cf91900699878ec] Thanks a lot. Looking good. I will also check one more time if the gasket diameter is acceptable, then we can confirm the solution. ","2026-01-08T08:49:35.006Z"],["3794712","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] Thank you! Should we use UI across all the visuals?","2026-01-08T08:49:35.414Z"],["3794713","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","[@alexander.fokau|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6083d099cbff1b0070445fea] We should have received a webhook notification when this Flex account was created, but it seems that didn’t happen. As a result, the account is missing in our system, which is why early cashout cannot be created","2026-01-08T08:50:14.076Z"],["3794714","MLC-3765","MLC","lorrayne.oliveira@bolt.eu","Lorrayne Corais","* [Canvas|https://dashboard-02.braze.eu/engagement/canvas/695f6622e8f8600063a434e0/660bb12b05810f0061db0f3c?locale=en&step=build&version=flow&isEditing=true] has been created for DE cities (Berlin, Hamburg, Frankfurt, Düsseldorf, Essen, Mannheim, Münster, Kiel, Stuttgart, Augsburg, Halle (Saale) \n*Note*: Confirmed with local team that Bremen market is closed. \n\n* [Canvas|https://dashboard-02.braze.eu/engagement/canvas/695f6e460f54b80072ef58c4/660bb12b05810f0061db0f3c?locale=en&step=build&version=flow&isEditing=true] has been created for CH (Zurich). \n","2026-01-08T08:50:35.810Z"],["3794717","C2-455","C2","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","RE Female Connector pins, I measured a few with a feeler gauge and there was ~0.15mm deviation between the positive terminal pin width and negative terminal width, and it was always the negative terminal side which was slightly wider. With that being said, all measurements of the large pins were in spec (0.90 mm ↔︎ 1.2 mm), while large connector pins are measured at 1.4 mm, meaning that they will have an interference fit (pingist) which is expected. [~accountid:5e4a421e691b8a0c95c2cdec] will look into why the same pin is slightly wider on the opposite side, shouldn’t be any deviation between the two of them, even if they’re both in spec according to drawing..\n\n!image-20260108-084743.png|width=1030,alt=\"image-20260108-084743.png\"!\n\n\n\nBut still - LOPS should not measure any C3 battery pins according to old SOP as it does not apply according to the current documentation and will result in false reports.","2026-01-08T08:51:27.285Z"],["3794718","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Yes please","2026-01-08T08:51:27.359Z"],["3794720","DO-5772","DO","hassan.farooq@bolt.eu","Hassan Farooq","Let’s add [~accountid:712020:b75759f0-ea50-4319-bfe5-48b28f4cab21] for now.","2026-01-08T08:51:39.690Z"],["3794721","PFI-830875","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T08:51:44.322Z"],["3794724","LSS-60741","LSS","alexia.lia@bolt.eu","Alexia Lia","[~accountid:5f2cfe232aa2500028d741b9]  if you have some points from your end please feel free to chip in 🙏  Would appreciate your input a lot","2026-01-08T08:51:51.562Z"],["3794725","WD-22415","WD","loredana.panait@bolt.eu","Loredana Panait","Hi Yuvraj, \n\nFor both Ukraine entities We need to have the excel file, the Payroll primary report (please see example of the report available for Canada this month).\nAlso, we need to have Ukraine set up with tonight cut off date, so we need bot reports available at 8th of January, 23.00 GMT+1.\n\nPlease confirm.\n\nThank you, \n\nLoredana\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 10.45.03.png|width=1240,height=261,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 10.45.03.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-08T08:51:52.400Z"],["3794726","PFI-830876","PFI","mwanamu.hemed@bolt-outsource.eu","Mwanamu Hemed","!IMG_0707.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T08:51:56.073Z"],["3794728","PFI-830876","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-08T08:51:58.786Z"],["3794729","WD-22415","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:623ace37b75ca80070562c04] , good day and happy new year! The exception happened on the Ukraine primary payroll data file as the pay periods for 2026 for Ukraine entities were not created and is missing.\n\n\n\n Can you please create these periods for the both entities?\n\n!image-20260108-085200.png|width=657,alt=\"image-20260108-085200.png\"!\n\ncc: [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] ","2026-01-08T08:52:08.657Z"],["3794734","WD-22466","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:6131df23b1894f00718e9faa] I will start working on it now","2026-01-08T08:54:07.702Z"],["3794735","LSS-61248","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nLilijana Zaiceva has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-08T08:54:20.929Z"],["3794736","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] If glue is placed between the clips and holder, it will still allow the holder to rotate. Glue should also be added between the bracket and silicone holder. But it makes hard to replace holders in the future. [~accountid:60b9e4f58cf91900699878ec] \n\n!image-20260108-085306.png|width=640,alt=\"image-20260108-085306.png\"!","2026-01-08T08:54:25.580Z"],["3794739","RCE-332","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767862531710809]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@joel.palgi>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-332] `Revamp documents view for fleet registration` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T08:55:46.051Z"],["3794743","WEBSD-1432","WEBSD","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:9e668ce4-0877-43c6-bae9-52f1ecbc753f] thanks for your assistance to date - I note that the link to the .PDF file on “here” is missing from “_You can download an offline version of these Platform Terms for your records and future reference_ +_here_+.” at the beginning of the T&Cs\n\nPlease can you rectify this. Thanks ","2026-01-08T08:56:07.839Z"],["3794744","FDBT-4745","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-08T08:56:14.792Z"],["3794745","PTWS-2098","PTWS","mihut.arsene@bolt.eu","Mihuț-Andrei Arsene","Hi Oana,\n\nI’ve done the following changes to this, which are available in WD Sandbox:\n\n# Removed the eligibility rule of the Severance OTPs. They can now be selected in the LOV even before the Termination BP is completed. \n# Because of the change made at point 1, I was able to move the People Partner Request OTP step immediately after the initiation step. \n\nPlease take a look and let me know if this approach works better.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-08T08:56:23.591Z"],["3794750","TA-166","TA","jorick.polderman@bolt.eu","Jorick Thijs Polderman","(copy pasted from earlier update):\n\n\n* Our meeting with Rewards should be scheduled for January (exact date TBD). This session will provide more guidance on how we communicate salary information with candidates. We’re also working on documentation and a step-by-step guide, developed in collaboration with Rewards. In the meantime, please remember that the Pay Transparency Directive goes live in Poland on December 24th. Make sure we remain compliant. For a refresher on the required actions, please review the [+Bolt Brief+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/REC/pages/6908739601/Bolt+Brief+TA+-+November+2025#Process].\n\nWaiting on timeline for communication roll out from Rewards.","2026-01-08T08:56:59.402Z"],["3794753","LSS-60076","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nThank you. I have shared this with Certinal and will keep you updated.\n\nThank you.","2026-01-08T08:57:27.750Z"],["3794754","RDXENG-4558","RDXENG","denis.komissarov@bolt.eu","Denis Komissarov","After investigation: \n1. It happens on Android 15+ OS versions only\n2. It could be related to the complex Home tile layout (multiple containers with wrap_content width)\nDuring duty I couldn’t find the real cause within 2 hours, so deeper investigation is needed","2026-01-08T08:57:42.996Z"],["3794756","CSDA-281","CSDA","polina.fateeva@bolt.eu","Polina Fateeva","Hi [~accountid:5bdc567ddabb7e15b08738ec] , getting back on the above - here’s the response I got. \n\nFor convenience, I will tag you in the thread as well, in case there are some details missing 🙏 ","2026-01-08T08:58:07.592Z"],["3794757","L10N-26440","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26438](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26438)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T08:58:17.386Z"],["3794758","L10N-26441","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content 