ched. Do you think this role should also be attached to the {{fpa_group_headcount}}  group?","2026-01-08T08:58:56.844Z"],["3794776","DO-5772","DO","hassan.farooq@bolt.eu","Hassan Farooq","Yes, {{FP&A Developer}} should have access to all {{fpa_*}} groups.","2026-01-08T09:00:08.884Z"],["3794779","TA-285","TA","jorick.polderman@bolt.eu","Jorick Thijs Polderman","This will not move forward due to the limitations that are in place right now. It would only work well if we had our ATS setup with a BI connector and not through the API.","2026-01-08T09:01:31.829Z"],["3794785","DO-5772","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","Sorry, I was wrong.\nThis is the correct table\n\n{noformat}Group\nfpa_delvoper         FP&A Developer\nfpa_group            FP&A Power User\nfpa_vertical_all     <no role>\nfpa_...              FP&A Power User\n\nfpa_group_headcount  ???{noformat}","2026-01-08T09:04:10.712Z"],["3794787","LSS-61125","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Shipment tracking code: [https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=2550046483&submit=1|https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=2550046483&submit=1|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T09:04:55.456Z"],["3794789","LSS-61118","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Shipment tracking code: [https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=9058925120&submit=1|https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=9058925120&submit=1|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T09:05:26.475Z"],["3794790","TA-158","TA","jorick.polderman@bolt.eu","Jorick Thijs Polderman","* [Kick off meeting notes|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ci-YTfethp2jfRUsmS8W7TdiQsWp1HMTQfNBJnsypgo/edit?usp=meet_tnfm_email&urp=gmail_link] {{2026-01-08}}","2026-01-08T09:05:36.300Z"],["3794791","DO-5772","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","So, all the other groups have {{FP&A Power User}}\n\nSo the question is, does the new group {{fpa_group_headcount}} need to have the role:\n\n {{FP&A Power User}}  or {{FP&A Developer}}  or {{<no role>}}  or {{<a new role>}}","2026-01-08T09:05:50.350Z"],["3794792","SREC-275","SREC","seyedmohammadreza.hosseini@bolt.eu","Mo Hosseini","i have updated the event bridge rule, according to aws docs , we are now covered , cloudtrail , event bridge , event rule , lambda , sns all in us-east-1 deployed , and i latest change to the rule will trigger the pipeline to send us alert ","2026-01-08T09:06:02.661Z"],["3794795","TA-104","TA","jorick.polderman@bolt.eu","Jorick Thijs Polderman","[~accountid:5d553573f386720da657efe5] whats the latest with this one so I can put it in the update?","2026-01-08T09:06:41.796Z"],["3794796","LSS-58567","LSS","alexia.lia@bolt.eu","Alexia Lia","Thank you [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] will await your reply, would be great if you can nudge them a bit 🙏 ","2026-01-08T09:06:52.666Z"],["3794798","DO-5772","DO","hassan.farooq@bolt.eu","Hassan Farooq","There are more groups. Could you please list the roles for those too?","2026-01-08T09:07:00.790Z"],["3794799","TA-11","TA","jorick.polderman@bolt.eu","Jorick Thijs Polderman","[~accountid:712020:91c046ef-60e7-46b4-9bd9-4bdc45d13e7d] could you add some updates here as well, or are they in the channel?","2026-01-08T09:07:33.998Z"],["3794800","DO-5772","DO","hassan.farooq@bolt.eu","Hassan Farooq","some groups are {{fpa_group_ops}} {{fpa_group_ir}} {{fpa_group_cs}}","2026-01-08T09:07:35.542Z"],["3794803","PFI-830882","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T09:08:40.166Z"],["3794804","PAW-14698","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @troskoff\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17064\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-08 09:08:44 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-08T09:08:45.219Z"],["3794809","PFI-830570","PFI","igor.bassov@bolt.eu","Igor Bassov","There is no relation to rider invoices. As I was saying, the matter is about the commission invoices which driver receives every month for the past month. The invoices are missing correct information like company’s name, VAT number etc. Driver is stuck now with the accounting process of their company because the current invoices are incorrect.","2026-01-08T09:09:57.211Z"],["3794810","DO-5772","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","Yes, you are right, there were 3 more on the next page:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 10.08.45.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T09:10:31.752Z"],["3794811","LSS-58914","LSS","alexia.lia@bolt.eu","Alexia Lia","Hello team was this closed off? [~accountid:5d63777a64bfb10c11a242fc] [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] [~accountid:60bf496ea01e11006ac62a66] ","2026-01-08T09:10:37.936Z"],["3794812","LSS-58423","LSS","kristina.pugaca@bolt.eu","Kristina Pugaca","[~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] Can you please let me know if I can include this promo code in my reply to the authorities?\n","2026-01-08T09:10:40.650Z"],["3794813","LSS-61238","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:44e59489-5db2-4488-8537-588bccee709b]  can we please request agreement in English for the legal review ?\n\nPlease let us know if we share any personal data with supplier, if yes we need to enter into DPA, as well ","2026-01-08T09:10:44.767Z"],["3794815","BP-13166","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:712020:8973d5d2-02e2-4150-b678-3f91914bf467] I moved my design task to another epic so we can mark this as Done","2026-01-08T09:11:04.178Z"],["3794816","LSS-59711","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2], I will come back to you next week with an update on the timelines.","2026-01-08T09:11:05.564Z"],["3794817","DSR-3467","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","The driver requests all personal data but is also terminated and requests account reinstating and:\n\n{quote}If you are unable to follow up with this request, I will be escalating this matter to ACAS for unfair dismissal.{quote}\n\n* SD ticket to UK Case managers [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/31/UKOPS-45608?created=true]. \n* Infobip ticket with the termination [here|https://portal.infobip.com/conversations/my-work?conversationId=4347037a-1555-4300-bef7-cd1c5982eb3f].\n* We have already provided the driver an answer in this [Jira Ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DSR-2177].\n\n[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] we provided the driver a response regarding their suspension in the last ticket but we didn’t provide them *ALL* of their personal data as they didn’t request it before. Should we just provide them all of their personal data and cancel the UK Case Managers ticket or should we still wait for their input also?\n\nDriver also sent us a formal complaint - attached. [^Bolt_Formal_Complaint_Zain_Hussain_Dated.pdf.pdf]  ","2026-01-08T09:11:30.750Z"],["3794818","PFI-830883","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T09:11:33.906Z"],["3794819","BP-13166","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","[~accountid:712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] Done - thank you!","2026-01-08T09:11:49.524Z"],["3794821","WD-22425","WD","george.matu@bolt.eu","George Matu","Hi Dominika, as the sick leaves in Poland are not automatically added to Workday, the system does not know (yet) that you were on sick leave in November. Once those days will show in WD they will also show in One Model soon after. We do monthly re-uploads for correcting for such cases. \n\nThanks,","2026-01-08T09:12:29.118Z"],["3794822","FX-3577","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767863541593529]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@meruzhan.kerobyan>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3577] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T09:12:33.901Z"],["3794823","FX-3578","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767863541592729]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@meruzhan.kerobyan>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3578] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T09:12:34.176Z"],["3794824","LSS-61109","LSS","raphael.perna@bolt.eu","Raphaël Samy Perna","Hello everyone,\n\nThank you all very much for your efficiency and responsiveness in handling this case. It is greatly appreciated.\n\n[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] , could you please notify me once the electronic signature request has been sent? This will allow me to closely follow the status on my end.\n\nThank you again [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] , and have a great day ! ","2026-01-08T09:12:41.446Z"],["3794825","PFI-823249","PFI","patrycja.kowalczyk@bolt.eu","Patrycja Kowalczyk","Hi there, \n\nWould you be able to help?\n\nThank you","2026-01-08T09:12:55.450Z"],["3794826","FX-3578","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767863577024219]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3578 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T09:13:09.170Z"],["3794827","FX-3577","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767863578440969]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3577 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T09:13:10.879Z"],["3794829","LSS-61082","LSS","laura.newton@bolt.eu","Laura Newton","Hi [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5], please see updated reference. \n\n\n[^Bolt Operations UK Limited - Reference Letter.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T09:13:24.761Z"],["3794830","PFI-819866","PFI","szymon.barabasz@bolt.eu","Szymon Barabasz","Hi everyone, this is urgent. Could you please accelerate it? Thank you!\n\n","2026-01-08T09:13:30.702Z"],["3794833","LSS-61105","LSS","vivien.antoniou@bolt.eu","Vivien Antoniou","placeholder has been sent to the driver, as requested ","2026-01-08T09:14:34.535Z"],["3794835","DO-5772","DO","hassan.farooq@bolt.eu","Hassan Farooq","For {{fpa_group_headcount}}, it should be {{FP&A Power User}}","2026-01-08T09:15:09.225Z"],["3794839","LSS-53811","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (08.01.26)*+\n\n* PDPS closed proceedings on 11 November 2025, deferring to the prosecutor’s Office.\n* Prosecutor’s Office confirmed closure on 30 December 2025. \n* Overall matter therefore appears to be closed.","2026-01-08T09:15:45.983Z"],["3794843","ESL-1434","ESL","radu.androne@bolt.eu","Radu Androne","Marking this as closed - with resolution in slack thread. ","2026-01-08T09:16:50.780Z"],["3794849","PFI-808686","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nWe have received an update from the Billing team. \n\nUnfortuantely, currently there's no invoice issued due to the internal bug. Engineering team is working to fix it, but it will take some time.\nThank you for understanding!\n\nI will assign this ticket to the Billing queue for future updates. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-08T09:18:18.764Z"],["3794851","WD-22418","WD","george.matu@bolt.eu","George Matu","Thanks for checking. These days not appearing (yet) in One Model should be also caused by the delay of the Mac address sync with JAMF. In most of the cases, within 1-2 weeks we are able to catch back the right MAC address and add it to the corresponding employee. (similar to your missing office visits in December); \n\nWe know about the issue, but still don’t have a technical solution to avoid it. For this reason, we have even put a disclaimer in the Personal dashboard, saying that: \n\n_There is a known lag in data for 1-2 weeks for some employees, we are working on building a real time integration. Note that if you see some errors in the last 2 weeks, these will self correct and do not impact long term attendance stats;_\n\nThank you for your understanding and for keeping a close eye on the data. It really helps us. In the meantime, I see your December data should now be fully corrected. ","2026-01-08T09:18:27.545Z"],["3794855","WFM-9895","WFM","aurelija.jovani@bolt-outsource.eu","Aurelija Jovani","!support volumes error.webp|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T09:19:35.700Z"],["3794857","PAW-14714","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T09:19:44.211Z"],["3794858","PAW-14713","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T09:19:46.916Z"],["3794860","LSS-61124","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] we recently evaluated Qminder. \n\n*We request to add to new order similar wording as we did for the previous order.* \n\nThe Parties have agreed to amend the Terms and accept them in the following wording. \n\nSection 13 (Audit) - Fully excluded.\n\n\n\nAfter this we’re ok to move to signing. If all agreed please  ask them to send the agreement to [+ahto.kink@bolt.eu+|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu] and cc [+signing@bolt.eu+|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] (we will not be able to find the request without putting this email in cc)","2026-01-08T09:20:59.428Z"],["3794861","PFI-830881","PFI","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hi! Email was changed from [+medrivesas@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesas@gmail.com] (original one) to [+medrivesass@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesass@gmail.com] (alleged fraudster) on the 28 Dec 2025, 14:42:36 UTC+02:00, it can be found on the [fleet change logs|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/74814?tab=change-log&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D], from the IP 103.151.40.239, by the fleet manager [70795|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-manager/managers/edit/70795]. There is a lot of language updates and different IPs on the [fleet manager change log|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-manager/managers/edit/70795?tab=change_log], so this account could be compromised. Also, I think that external Fleet Owner information are also compomised, as fraudster provided 2 times verified a KBis, which can be obtained with a digital ID.","2026-01-08T09:21:04.002Z"],["3794864","DO-5765","DO","kristo.sarnets@bolt.eu","Kristo Sarnets","Would you happen to have an ETA estimate, when do you think this could get done? \n\nThank you.","2026-01-08T09:21:52.718Z"],["3794866","RS-1939","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:603cb85ec58c720071175949] ,\n\nYes, this looks like a court order. \n\n* Court heading: _Magistrates Court… held at Pinetown Court_ \n* Magistrate signature + court stamp/date on the subpoena page","2026-01-08T09:22:21.947Z"],["3794867","PAW-14750","PAW",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the bug!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-08T09:22:31.592Z"],["3794868","PRF-83","PRF","konul.hasanova@bolt.eu","Konul Hasanova","[~accountid:5c61221fdb49e4016460f3c1] I think we can close this as expansion team [removed|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06RVM2D0SY/p1767607699646869] Vietnam from the launch roadmap.","2026-01-08T09:22:35.295Z"],["3794869","LSS-54620","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] any updates here ?","2026-01-08T09:22:47.354Z"],["3794870","PAW-14750","PAW","mateusz.olszewski@bolt.eu","Mateusz Olszewski","Related slack thread - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1767784086380229|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1767784086380229|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T09:22:52.229Z"],["3794876","LSS-56593","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:a9500cde-28bc-4a8e-95d6-7818a2252cf8] should we close this ticket or there will be any updates ?","2026-01-08T09:23:31.397Z"],["3794880","LSS-60946","LSS","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","Hey [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] \n\nUpdate:\n\n* The info from the user auth team suggests that the new device that signed in on 05/12 was using the same Apple account as the original device and this allowed access to the Bolt app without additional authentication\n\nShould we communicate this to the user and advise them which device this was (make + model) in case it’s a family member or something? ","2026-01-08T09:23:51.770Z"],["3794881","LSS-61048","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:5c2f512d36647b5b91017d0c] just heads up that we’re on it and will proceed with the review ","2026-01-08T09:24:25.191Z"],["3794882","SRED-984","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Snapshot of the data created. Clsuter removed","2026-01-08T09:24:46.857Z"],["3794884","PAW-14709","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @xenJ\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/pull/3074\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-08 09:25:04 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-08T09:25:05.557Z"],["3794885","PAW-14708","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @xenJ\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/pull/3074\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-08 09:25:13 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-08T09:25:13.238Z"],["3794886","LSS-60973","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","Hi [~accountid:63e354e3010d35637974a02c] Just heads up that we received your request an will proceed with the review","2026-01-08T09:25:21.212Z"],["3794887","PRF-162","PRF","konul.hasanova@bolt.eu","Konul Hasanova","I’ll come up with the wrap up by the end of Feb. Because that’s when we’ll be able to finalise all the markets and new channel efforts(TH&ZA are ongoing). Until that time, keeping this epic in progress.","2026-01-08T09:25:21.657Z"],["3794888","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Shreya Bhandari [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767864324474199]*{color}:\n<@URVM3U4RF> where is the FF?\n{quote}","2026-01-08T09:25:37.599Z"],["3794889","DBRE-8586","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Master switch proxysql mishavior fix support\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNKLBL33P/p1767861082743129|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNKLBL33P/p1767861082743129]\n* ENG-RIDER-EU-1-live-proxysql-1.sqldb\n* {noformat}mysql> select * from mysql_servers where hostname like 'gb%';\n+--------------+---------------+------+-----------+--------------+--------+-------------+-----------------+---------------------+---------+----------------+--------------------+\n| hostgroup_id | hostname      | port | gtid_port | status       | weight | compression | max_connections | max_replication_lag | use_ssl | max_latency_ms | comment            |\n+--------------+---------------+------+-----------+--------------+--------+-------------+-----------------+---------------------+---------+----------------+--------------------+\n| 21           | gb-db-4.sqldb | 3306 | 0         | OFFLINE_HARD | 1      | 0           | 1000            | 7200                | 0       | 0              | 1767796555.1666067 |\n| 22           | gb-db-4.sqldb | 3306 | 0         | OFFLINE_HARD | 1      | 0           | 1000            | 7200                | 0       | 0              | 1767796555.1666067 |\n| 22           | gb-db-1.sqldb | 3306 | 0         | ONLINE       | 1      | 0           | 1000            | 7200                | 0       | 0              | 1767858143.874788  |\n| 22           | gb-db-2.sqldb | 3306 | 0         | ONLINE       | 1      | 0           | 1000            | 7200                | 0       | 0              | 1767858143.874788  |\n| 22           | gb-db-3.sqldb | 3306 | 0         | ONLINE       | 1      | 0           | 1000            | 7200                | 0       | 0              | 1767858143.874788  |\n| 22           | gb-db-5.sqldb | 3306 | 0         | ONLINE       | 1      | 0           | 1000            | 7200                | 0       | 0              | 1767858143.874788  |\n| 22           | gb-db-6.sqldb | 3306 | 0         | ONLINE       | 1      | 0           | 1000            | 7200                | 0       | 0              | 1767858143.874788  |\n+--------------+---------------+------+-----------+--------------+--------+-------------+-----------------+---------------------+---------+----------------+--------------------+\n7 rows in set (0.00 sec){noformat}","2026-01-08T09:25:40.827Z"],["3794890","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sudipto Das [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767864338801279]*{color}:\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/featureflags/edit/14840]\n{quote}","2026-01-08T09:25:50.718Z"],["3794891","CSXRD-313","CSXRD","polina.fateeva@bolt.eu","Polina Fateeva","Points of uncertainty clarified with OPS, announced to CS-OPS and documented in KB. Closing action item as no additional actions are needed at this stage.","2026-01-08T09:25:55.388Z"],["3794892","LSS-57452","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] have we signed this agreement ? can we close the ticket ?","2026-01-08T09:26:13.292Z"],["3794893","SRED-1045","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Downscaled","2026-01-08T09:26:31.026Z"],["3794894","SRED-1046","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Downscaled","2026-01-08T09:26:38.700Z"],["3794896","PFI-830895","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","[^76001507.pdf (3).pdf]","2026-01-08T09:27:19.223Z"],["3794897","LSS-59915","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","Hi [~accountid:712020:4afbd60d-276d-4d8c-8d4c-5669fd772468] [~accountid:712020:985a985c-b403-41bd-b116-abbf44b22175] we will close this ticket but please add here docs when they are signed ","2026-01-08T09:27:23.384Z"],["3794898","RDXENG-4379","RDXENG","sergei.emelianov@bolt.eu","Sergey Emeliyanov","Testing not required","2026-01-08T09:27:24.300Z"],["3794899","RDXENG-4380","RDXENG","sergei.emelianov@bolt.eu","Sergey Emeliyanov","Testing not required","2026-01-08T09:27:28.790Z"],["3794900","RDXENG-4383","RDXENG","sergei.emelianov@bolt.eu","Sergey Emeliyanov","Testing not required","2026-01-08T09:27:39.208Z"],["3794901","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Thanks! I can confirm I no longer see the heavy queries that were consuming 400K+ RUs.","2026-01-08T09:27:58.520Z"],["3794902","PFI-830881","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello,\n\nI'll need to advise that our team does not deal with internal fraud cases. in Bolt’s context *the fraud team* deals with payment issues such as credit cards.\n\nAs far as I am aware, then if an account is compromised, then it should be escalated to the Privacy team.\nIn case you suspect Internal fraud, then it should be reported to the internal audit team for further confirmation and review.\n\nRegarding the Change logs and its working, then we do not have the authority over its systems, it would be better to ask this specific question from the tech team.\n\nPlease escalate this to the Privacy team, or to the internal audit team in case of internal fraud.\n\nIf there are any other questions or if I misunderstood anything, then let me know ASAP by tagging me within this ticket.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-08T09:28:10.446Z"],["3794905","LSS-61134","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f],\n\nPlease find below the files containing both the *marked-up version* and the *clean version* provided by TransPerfect.\n\nMany thanks!\n\n* [Markup Version|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lOwk4k9xWwXa485vBCN4R7WmzlxILxK_/edit]\n* [Clean Version|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OyGrp915g3wK12hn5o5iytJwE25TUbQe/edit]\n\n ","2026-01-08T09:28:47.440Z"],["3794907","PRF-416","PRF","konul.hasanova@bolt.eu","Konul Hasanova","Based on the local’s input we decided to keep minimum ads budget which is 50/day on Meta just to keep raising awareness. Acquisition is not working properly (targeting and lead quality issues) when we try online ads. [Context|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08SD4YQ2AE/p1764089775203879?thread_ts=1763554270.509629&cid=C08SD4YQ2AE]. Closing this as we won’t have any ads activities in the region.","2026-01-08T09:29:08.313Z"],["3794909","DO-5772","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","OK, the group is now with the correct role in your user attribute\n\nDoes it now look like you intended?\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 10.27.16.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T09:29:27.827Z"],["3794910","LSS-54937","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:63e354e3010d35637974a02c] we will close the ticket, since review was already provided earlier. But please feel free to reach out in slack and reopen the ticket if needed. ","2026-01-08T09:29:35.495Z"],["3794913","PFI-830883","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\nIf you need a _report_, please refer to FleetX (DriverX). If your request concerns an _invoice_, follow these steps:\n\nPlease try:\n* Open the *Client page in Admin*: [link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D].\n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ - The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see another _error_ → provide us a link.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the {{Partner Invoices}}) tab\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-08T09:30:22.411Z"],["3794914","DO-5772","DO","hassan.farooq@bolt.eu","Hassan Farooq","I just hope it works now how I want it to be :sweat_smile:. Thank you.","2026-01-08T09:31:23.405Z"],["3794915","LSS-38940","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:5cbf158a6fbf5a10040d1d63] we will close the ticket for now as the review was already done but please feel free to reach out in slack if we need to reopen the ticket  ","2026-01-08T09:31:27.672Z"],["3794916","LSS-57405","LSS","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","Hi @Catarina Faria & @Kirsika Liiva,\nI can see that they’ve sent the updated version with the incorrect deposit value again, let me me flag again. Thanks!","2026-01-08T09:31:47.458Z"],["3794917","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] According to the media plan, there are three different promo codes. Does this mean that the assets will be placed in different cities, or is there another reason for having multiple promo codes? Thank you!","2026-01-08T09:32:08.921Z"],["3794919","LSS-51178","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] closing the ticket but please feel free to reach out in slack if we need to reopen ","2026-01-08T09:32:30.526Z"],["3794920","BSKT-4468","BSKT","paul.gordan@bolt.eu","Paul Gordan","Description was a bit confusing. Here is a better description (from slack dm):\n\nTask context:\nIf the split amount (BB + other payment) received from the user is different from the amount received from commerce gateway we immediately cancel the payment capture and don’t create the order.\nThis is normal as if user saw that he has to pay 10E card + 5E BB and on the we receive 11E card + 4E BB then we want to cancel the authorization request as the user didn’t agree with this split when placing the order.*That was the original logic without your changes*.Your changes are needed because for Kenya, we receive a different split due to some rounding issues (see the linked thread where I discussed with payment team). When they receive a request to capture an amount from user BB that’s not rounded, [they will fix the issue in a cron|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1761557221569449?thread_ts=1761206614.038539&cid=CNV6QPRFT] that runs every minute. If the user retries after 1 minute, the BB amount will be fixed on theirs side and the call will [pass.In|http://pass.In] the mean time, [we receive a lot of errors like this one|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02TWDM1QF9/p1761152052735339] so with [@tudor.maxim|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U01AAA9U6UU], we decided to just fix the error thrown. So most likely you should have just checked with the logic that you did and throw a warning instead of error in case we have a missmatch in Kenya. Please don’t mark the split as valid.","2026-01-08T09:32:36.686Z"],["3794921","HS-28718","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi again Kerubo, the letter is now signed and should be in your personal email. Please let me know if you need anything else. For now I’ll close the ticket. ","2026-01-08T09:32:44.288Z"],["3794922","FDBT-4754","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-08T09:32:44.984Z"],["3794925","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Shreya Bhandari [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767864798099219]*{color}:\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/edit/14140] : to be disabled in 10 minutes\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/edit/14690] —  to go :green: at 2pm (EE time)\n<@U04RDTQ5AJC> to check and approve\n\nWe will have a gap of about 2.5 hours\n{quote}","2026-01-08T09:33:31.538Z"],["3794928","LSS-60741","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:1e9398f2-efcd-4dcd-8ece-28e6f8578e37] ,\n\nhere my answers in bold and blue:\n\n# *Branding & Sticker Application:*\n## *Taxis*: Branding can be done, in colour with out normal branding criteria, as long as the normal TAXI signs are not disrupted, am I correct to assume so? {color:#008da6}*Correct.  Additional branding is possible, including coloured elements, provided that:*{color}\n##* {color:#008da6}*it does not interfere with or obscure mandatory taxi signs or identifiers; and*{color}\n##* {color:#008da6}*it does not alter the recognisability of the vehicle as a taxi.*{color}\n## {color:#008da6}*In practice, this means branding must be clearly secondary, non-intrusive, and not resemble taxi-specific graphics or colour schemes used by the municipality.*{color}\n## *NCC:* NCC Vehicles can be any colour of vehicle? Therefore shall we adopt white branding in order to create a more smooth design not to have a lot of colours. {color:#008da6}*Yes, NCC vehicles can be any colour. The only mandatory elements are: i) the “NCC” plate and; ii) the “noleggio/rental” signage (windshield + rear window). There is no general prohibition on additional branding, as long as it does not create confusion with taxis. From a legal perspective, adopting white or neutral-colour branding for NCC vehicles is not required, but it is a prudent design choice if the goal is visual consistency and to minimise any risk of perceived taxi-confusion — especially in mixed fleets.*{color}\n# *Supplier & Driver Considerations:*\n## {color:#403294}Are there any restrictions when it comes to choosing a supplier for the branding work? - What I meant here, is there any pre-established suppliers who brand vehicles already established with Bolt, or shall I take the liberty of researching for a supplier that we can use in Milan in order to Brand the vehicles once the process is ready? {color}{color:#008da6}*You are free to research and select a local supplier in Milan, provided that: i) branding complies with the vehicle rules above; and ii) appropriate contractual and data protection arrangements are put in place. From Legal/Privacy’s side, once a supplier is identified, we will need: i) a service agreement, ii) and a data processing arrangement, as already flagged by Privacy.*{color}\n## Also ideally we do Branding with Tiering, according to achieved KPIs, is this possible? - Agreed with the Driver behaviour that caught, what I am thinking is more about having different % of branding kickback according to the number of FR or any other acceptable criteria, in order to minimise spend and have better focus of spend. {color:#008da6}*What you are now describing — i.e. different branding kickback percentages linked to objective, non-behavioural metrics (e.g. number of completed trips / FRs as a volume indicator, or other neutral thresholds) — is feasible and less problematic, provided that:*{color}\n##* {color:#008da6}*the criteria are framed as commercial eligibility thresholds, not performance management;*{color}\n##* {color:#008da6}*there is no implication of minimum working time, exclusivity, or continuity;*{color}\n##* {color:#008da6}*branding remains optional and does not become a de facto condition to access work on the platform.*{color}\n# We may need a service agreement template for the supplier who will brand the vehicles, and the fleets? - {color:#008da6}*I need to fine tune some elements, I will get back to you once done if that’s ok. with regards to your question: Ideally both in Italian and English. Yes, we need one, I’m reviewing a fleet agreement including the “branding part “ for Giovanni, I’ll share here a version once ready.*{color}\n\nLet me know if you have further questions. \n\nThank you.\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-08T09:33:46.874Z"],["3794929","AIOT-588","AIOT","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","Hey folks, we recently had a case in DC where the rider slipped and fell and tried to sue us. But looking at the [footage|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U04LC3PAE5B/F0A2TSSSB4H/footage.mp4] paired with the telemetry gave us full confidence that it was not our fault so we refused liability. There's a little bubble on the corner and I was wondering if there's something simple we can implement on the lens cover like a hydrophobic spray? There are a couple of products used for car windshields like the one below, and I read that some photographers use the same thing for action cams, gopros with good results. Something to consider?","2026-01-08T09:33:52.617Z"],["3794930","AIOT-588","AIOT",null,"Slack","[Klemet-Gustav Tamm|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04EVS3V128/p1767606696615229?thread_ts=1767606696.615229&cid=C04EVS3V128|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04EVS3V128/p1767606696615229?thread_ts=1767606696.615229&cid=C04EVS3V128|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-08T09:33:53.513Z"],["3794931","AIOT-588","AIOT","arvind.jayashankar@bolt.eu","Arvind Jayashankar","*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A6WQYM10U/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A6WQYM10U/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-08T09:33:54.184Z"],["3794932","AIOT-588","AIOT","yong.lin@bolt.eu","Yong Lin","*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A6LV10611/img_0124.jpg|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A6LV10611/img_0124.jpg|smart-link]","2026-01-08T09:33:55.082Z"],["3794933","AIOT-588","AIOT","arvind.jayashankar@bolt.eu","Arvind Jayashankar","Masamitsu sounds wayyyy cooler than rain-x. Haha.\n\n{quote}Masamitsu (正光, etc.) is a common Japanese masculine given name meaning \"true light\" or \"real brightness,\" embodying authenticity, and is shared by various notable figures like historical daimyō, modern athletes (e.g., Masamitsu Ichiguchi), artists (Masamitsu Ota), and even a brand of security/lighting products.{quote}","2026-01-08T09:33:55.612Z"],["3794937","HS-28718","HS","kerubo.ombati@bolt.eu","Kerubo Ombati","receipt confirmed. Thanks","2026-01-08T09:34:58.270Z"],["3794939","LSS-58914","LSS","kristina.pugaca@bolt.eu","Kristina Pugaca","[~accountid:712020:1e9398f2-efcd-4dcd-8ece-28e6f8578e37] yes, this ticket was closed. We provided all the replies and they did not requested any new data. the last messages were about training ","2026-01-08T09:35:38.223Z"],["3794940","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767864952910609]*{color}:\nHi <@U09D62DKH9P> <@U04FV4Z0GQ4> we have been talking about the visibility problem and it has now become urgent that we can offboard FOs and pay back any remaining deposit they might have, and in order to solve that problem we are proposing to generate a manual credit note, please see attachment and let us know if we are good to proceed with this solution.\n\nLinked files:\n* [260108 Template_ Credit note deposit offboarding.pdf|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A71MA46LX/260108_template__credit_note_deposit_offboarding.pdf]\n{quote}","2026-01-08T09:36:07.082Z"],["3794942","PRF-691","PRF","konul.hasanova@bolt.eu","Konul Hasanova","I’ll come up with the wrap up by the end of Feb. Because that’s when we’ll be able to finalise all the markets and new channel efforts(TH&ZA are ongoing). Until that time, keeping this epic in progress. Confluence that will be updated is [+here+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/6217073351/New+channel+tests+for+driver+acquisition]. ","2026-01-08T09:36:56.247Z"],["3794944","BDB-1500","BDB","liisi.tamra@bolt.eu","Liisi Tamra","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] afaik, we’re using 3 different discount codes, meaning the placements are in three different cities or locations, correct? [~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] \n\nIf that’s the case, using the same copy across all three should be fine. Engagement will differ by location anyway.","2026-01-08T09:37:27.756Z"],["3794948","DBRE-8674","DBRE","akhmad.islami@bolt.eu","Akhmad Mukhson Islami","https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CH2LCDA69/p1767859113039429?thread_ts=1767778427.737099&cid=CH2LCDA69","2026-01-08T09:37:57.063Z"],["3794951","DSR-3069","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","Contacted recruiter Catalina Dinu re confirmation (8 Jan). ","2026-01-08T09:38:24.945Z"],["3794952","LSS-59915","LSS","alex.bucse@bolt.eu","Alex Bucșe","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] / [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] - I think it was signed, but I saw an e-mail from EY with their signature on it but they signed as .asice (I think that is the Estonian thingy) and asked that we sign the same. (I do not understand why that is needed) [~accountid:712020:4afbd60d-276d-4d8c-8d4c-5669fd772468] will confirm/reply here","2026-01-08T09:38:27.843Z"],["3794955","CEBF-1740","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Task is completed\n\n!2026-01-08_11-38-16.mp4|width=650,alt=\"2026-01-08_11-38-16.mp4\"!","2026-01-08T09:38:55.070Z"],["3794957","CEBF-1816","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","bug is fixed","2026-01-08T09:39:17.035Z"],["3794958","DRX-27780","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","❌ Tested on DA.126.0 (1502) Firebase build on Samsung A12, OS:13\n\nThe issue is still reproducible:\n\n!Recording_20260108_113432.mp4|width=320,alt=\"Recording_20260108_113432.mp4\"!","2026-01-08T09:39:37.002Z"],["3794959","DSR-3135","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","Contacted recruiter Sylwia Korcok, confirmed candidate data can be erased (8 Jan)","2026-01-08T09:39:50.511Z"],["3794963","LEG-1138","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Had a chat with [~accountid:712020:a0124a71-9df9-4683-aa0c-9dea10fcc90e] about this project on 7 January 2026. Francisco to share the document with Central Support Functions by 16 January 2026, and then the Legal work is to kick off.","2026-01-08T09:40:36.212Z"],["3794970","PAW-14713","PAW","tomasz.traczyk@bolt.eu","Tomasz Traczyk","Redirected to {{#dev-data-platform-support}}.","2026-01-08T09:41:23.760Z"],["3794973","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767865280923629]*{color}:\n<@U090E7WNXUG> I don't think this is mine to review, this needs to go through finance team\n{quote}","2026-01-08T09:41:34.083Z"],["3794974","PFI-830836","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:864e9529-05d3-4dad-8199-64bd1d3b9de9],\n\nWe have suspended all the related users.\nWe would recommend that Niniko blocks their card and proceeds with acquiring a new one, we do not know how of course, but it seems like the card was compromised.\nKeeping the card safe is the user’s own responsibility, therefore, please do not provide them with any compensation.\n\nThank you for escalating this.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-08T09:41:48.901Z"],["3794975","RS-1932","RS","innaaime.kalju@bolt.eu","Inna Aime Kalju","i will inform police","2026-01-08T09:41:59.254Z"],["3794976","DO-5773","DO","yichia.wu@bolt.eu","Yi-Chia Wu","Hello {{dbt-taskforce}}, could you approve this PR on deleting rows? Thank you [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15235|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15235]","2026-01-08T09:42:31.145Z"],["3794977","DO-5773","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","I will run it :wink:","2026-01-08T09:42:32.081Z"],["3794979","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767865354883979]*{color}:\nYes, that's why I also tagged Kerli as well :slightly_smiling_face:\n{quote}","2026-01-08T09:42:48.982Z"],["3794980","L10N-26457","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking 