comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26455](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26455)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T09:43:44.903Z"],["3794991","PFI-830897","PFI","kamile.dovainyte@bolt-outsource.eu","Kamilė Dovainytė","!invoice.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T09:43:49.433Z"],["3794993","PFI-830898","PFI","oluwaferanmi.arogundade@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwaferanmi Arogundade","!Screenshot_20260108_112707_Capitec.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T09:44:13.015Z"],["3794995","LSS-61250","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nBirgit Tohvrel has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-08T09:45:17.450Z"],["3794996","PFI-830704","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:68c5b922-c6c9-4f6c-9095-19083e5e9ce2],\n\nNo, this driver will not be unblocked.\nIt is visible that a rider account was created, and the rider took all of their trips with the aforementioned driver. This was done during campaign in order to get benefits. Due to the abusive behavior, the driver will not be unblocked.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-08T09:45:28.684Z"],["3794997","WFM-9893","WFM","mihaela.pahontu@bolt-outsource.eu","Mihaela Pahontu","closed request, I made another one with the correct template.","2026-01-08T09:46:01.449Z"],["3794999","WD-21984","WD","enelys.kalmus@bolt.eu","Enelys Kalmus","Alrighty 🙂 \n\nThen agreed that we will not add these supplier groups to the supplier card anymore. \n\nThanks! [~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82] ","2026-01-08T09:46:10.967Z"],["3795001","WD-22466","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:6131df23b1894f00718e9faa] [~accountid:624d3e6a45ece00069cdb4e5] [~accountid:638476d83e79f12e572272f3] [~accountid:62ea2a72da8620d53392aa71] all roles are updated, please let me know if you experience any issues","2026-01-08T09:46:20.984Z"],["3795002","HS-28505","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","waiting for JD from manager","2026-01-08T09:46:27.986Z"],["3795006","LSS-61251","LSS","reimo.arm@bolt.eu","Reimo Ärm","[^Bolt_IO_Jan2026 (1).docx] _(12 kB)_","2026-01-08T09:46:33.025Z"],["3795009","DLSP-1586","DLSP","habib.fikri@bolt.eu","Fikri Sundayana","Done in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLSP-1585|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLSP-1585|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T09:46:42.307Z"],["3795012","LSS-61252","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^EE20260109-001 Resa motors - Bolt Drive EE.docx.pdf] _(388 kB)_","2026-01-08T09:47:09.205Z"],["3795017","LSS-61250","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ubloYG8DUmVmATqMr7gsOhkpK4FFrCBi/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ubloYG8DUmVmATqMr7gsOhkpK4FFrCBi/edit|smart-link] \n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HnEDD480dDeet75eXYas91uXGxt_2f60/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HnEDD480dDeet75eXYas91uXGxt_2f60/edit|smart-link] \n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/11pqAcaAdHjZv1RQPMHl3nDFy6ddfHhPQ/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11pqAcaAdHjZv1RQPMHl3nDFy6ddfHhPQ/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T09:47:53.252Z"],["3795018","LSS-61253","LSS","szymon.barabasz@bolt.eu","Szymon Barabasz","[^SKM_C55826010720030.pdf] _(162 kB)_","2026-01-08T09:48:07.265Z"],["3795020","LSS-60939","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:614ae82ed747e80075f8baa5] , hey! \n\nI think if [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] as a responsible Legal Counsel suggested me this statement, we may include it like this.\n\nPlease see the updated agreement attached.\n\n[^Bolt Drive Sublease Master Agreement amendment_Bolt Technology (3).docx]  \n\nAfter your approval I will proceed with collecting signatures.","2026-01-08T09:48:20.238Z"],["3795022","LSS-61109","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:af076e83-bb33-4eb6-8634-6e435217c5e4] - Document was sent out yesterday for signing.","2026-01-08T09:48:31.611Z"],["3795024","DO-5773","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","Your rows were deleted successfully.\nI will approve and merge your PR :wink:","2026-01-08T09:48:42.900Z"],["3795027","DSR-3009","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","The driver has replied the following “Thank you for your message and for the details provided. I confirm that it was indeed me during that ride, and not another driver as the passenger states. The information mentioned by the latter does not correspond to reality and unfortunately reflects bad faith. I remain, of course, available for any further clarification if necessary. Furthermore, I strongly wish to be able to resume my activity with Bolt under the best conditions. Thank you in advance for the attention given to my situation.”\n\nHi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], as I don’t see any other privacy matter that we need to actually reply I closed the case. Let me know if you have any other opinion on this, otherwise we can change the status to “Done”. Thanks 🙏 ","2026-01-08T09:49:21.840Z"],["3795028","LSS-61058","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Hi [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] - could you please send me a link to Strapi and I will check if I still have access? It currently does not appear among my Okta apps - if my access has been revoked, I will make sure it is restored ASAP 🙂 ","2026-01-08T09:49:23.327Z"],["3795029","PFI-830825","PFI","elijah.ojeamien@bolt-outsource.eu","Elijah Ojeamien","The client said their bank asked them to check in with us. Any advice?","2026-01-08T09:49:35.605Z"],["3795031","PFI-819885","PFI","ashmi.zameer@bolt.eu","Ashmi Zameer","Thank you Nikolay. ","2026-01-08T09:49:45.755Z"],["3795032","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Kerli Uibo [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767865775362449]*{color}:\nHi\nCan you elaborate a little the plan with this credit notes, <@U090E7WNXUG>?\nThis is the doc, but how you are thinking about the money movement?\nThrough Admin or somehow outside?\n\n\nMy comment to the few thread replies above:\nUntil we do not have the possibility to use these manual adjustments type (which are not invoiced), there is possibility to use types, which are invoicable, meaning any adjustments done, will be reflected on the monthly invoice as a row. Which you know, is creating a lot of mess, but those at least would be visible on the portal.\n But for this we need tax approval as a \"one time thing\" because the invoices are affected. Also we need to use a separate subtypes, to be able to book these still separately from any other manual adjustments, which go to PnL.\ncc:<@U06217N0RJ5> <@U08RWJ9TRAA>\n{quote}","2026-01-08T09:49:49.005Z"],["3795035","WFM-9883","WFM","daiga.buligo@bolt.eu","Daiga Buligo","Please, also remove the same access from [~accountid:5f6cafc8d33d76007759cbf4] ","2026-01-08T09:50:01.837Z"],["3795036","LSS-61058","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","it is not in Okta - here’s the link [https://cms.bolt.eu/admin/auth/login|https://cms.bolt.eu/admin/auth/login]\n\nPlease contact IT / Web to get access if you don’t have it 🙏 ","2026-01-08T09:50:27.202Z"],["3795039","SREP-1038","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* Control plane upgraded \n* Kube-proxy bumped \n* Nodes recreated, no issues so far: \n* !image-20260108-095130.png|width=754,alt=\"image-20260108-095130.png\"!","2026-01-08T09:51:47.059Z"],["3795042","PFI-830902","PFI","victoria.akinfenwa@bolt-outsource.eu","Victoria Akinfenwa","!image-20260108-095201.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T09:52:20.824Z"],["3795044","LSS-61254","LSS","onyinye.osuagwu@bolt.eu","Onyinyechukwu Osuagwu","[^MDS- Vendor Personal Data Consent Form 2021 (1).pdf] _(310 kB)_","2026-01-08T09:53:22.024Z"],["3795046","RS-1935","RS","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","I would say so as [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] mentioned that a ticket was already raised","2026-01-08T09:53:28.074Z"],["3795051","HS-28458","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Reminder sent.","2026-01-08T09:54:05.269Z"],["3795052","LSS-60122","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","[~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] Please see attached landlord response. As explained in Slack, these steps are fine for us to take when ending the lease, however the the termination right without any relevant cause has to stay for Bolt. Could you please support with wording this? \n\n!image-20260108-095302.png|width=2060,height=950,alt=\"image-20260108-095302.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-08T09:54:16.901Z"],["3795055","RDXENG-4523","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","(/) *Tested and unable to reproduce.*\n\n||*Device name*||iPhone 15||\n|OS Version|26.0.1|\n|Client build|CI.217.0 (194279035)|\n|Comment|physical|","2026-01-08T09:54:27.781Z"],["3795058","PFI-829598","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:75cc9b72-db8b-4dff-9671-3ed8fde897df],\n\nUpdate on the case.\n\nThis driver has most likely indulged in fraudulent activities, however, before we can confirm this 100% we need to wait for the business profiles next billing cycle in order to be 100% certain.\nThis unfortunately will take time, however, after the cycle we can tell if the business and the drivers were associated with a fraudulent scheme.\nWe will update you once again when we have more information.\n\nMarten","2026-01-08T09:55:17.196Z"],["3795062","WFM-9311","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","hello! Access was approved","2026-01-08T09:56:20.820Z"],["3795063","LSS-61151","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ! No need to collect Counterparty’s signature?","2026-01-08T09:56:26.115Z"],["3795064","DSR-3585","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-08T09:56:32.751Z"],["3795065","DSR-3009","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] - if still possible, I suggest de-escalating to T2/Ops before fully closing the case. They can decide whether they want to engage with the driver on his follow-up. \n\nI agree that there’s no further input needed from us here. Could you please add a link to the BH where the driver answered (not included in your comment currently) for record-keeping? ","2026-01-08T09:56:38.987Z"],["3795067","LSS-61109","LSS","raphael.perna@bolt.eu","Raphaël Samy Perna","Thanks !\n\n","2026-01-08T09:57:01.710Z"],["3795070","WD-22504","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:63f742e4e8216251ae4e4ef6] since your company is different now, please follow instructions here in order to submit access for this case [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/FIN/pages/5220860448/Creating+Expense+Reports+in+Multiple+Countries|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/FIN/pages/5220860448/Creating+Expense+Reports+in+Multiple+Countries|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T09:57:33.041Z"],["3795072","LSS-61151","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] corect, only Ahto’s ","2026-01-08T09:57:58.099Z"],["3795073","PRF-516","PRF","konul.hasanova@bolt.eu","Konul Hasanova","In Q1 we’ll test reach frequency with multicell cls","2026-01-08T09:58:30.498Z"],["3795075","L10N-26486","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26455](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26455)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T09:58:40.412Z"],["3795076","L10N-26489","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26455](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26455)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T09:58:42.912Z"],["3795077","PFI-820831","PFI","aida.nikunlassi@bolt-outsource.eu","Aida Nikunlassi","No answer in FAQ, could you check this?","2026-01-08T09:58:51.183Z"],["3795079","WFM-9881","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541612|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541612]","2026-01-08T09:59:14.672Z"],["3795080","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Yes they are all in different parts in the city. ","2026-01-08T09:59:25.023Z"],["3795081","RDXENG-4445","RDXENG","pavel.panarad@bolt.eu","Pavel Panarad","[~accountid:557058:a4479a6f-2844-4924-9d31-5fa074226e03] something is still happening on swipe up 😃 \n\n!Screen_recording_20260108_115739.mp4|width=320,alt=\"Screen_recording_20260108_115739.mp4\"!","2026-01-08T09:59:40.735Z"],["3795082","LSS-61214","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Please_Docusign_Sodali_Bolt_MSASOW_07_Jan_2.pdf] ","2026-01-08T09:59:42.468Z"],["3795085","PRF-502","PRF","konul.hasanova@bolt.eu","Konul Hasanova","Always on CLS applied in CZ&FR but martech expectation of the data interpretation by Meta was not met. Therefore, we’ll postpone this experiment until we have built some automation on our side. ","2026-01-08T10:00:31.116Z"],["3795086","DRX-27946","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.126.0 (1502) Firebase build on Samsung A12, OS:13\n\nEarnings Island expanded and collapsed are logged as separate events:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.58.37.png|width=659,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.58.37.png\"!","2026-01-08T10:00:43.759Z"],["3795091","DRX-27635","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27946 has been resolved","2026-01-08T10:01:12.231Z"],["3795092","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Plus we want to be able to valuate the specific venues","2026-01-08T10:01:12.584Z"],["3795096","HS-28731","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello [~accountid:618d11745fe6c70069e888a3] \n\nCan you please raise this ticket with our Tech team as they can help to sort out issues with accesses and credits.\n\n\n\nKind regards,","2026-01-08T10:01:54.467Z"],["3795099","WD-22516","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi Carla!\n\nI have already create this tax code to address this request [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22318?search_id=5fbfbcf2-f1ea-4f92-8646-17c70135964d|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22318?search_id=5fbfbcf2-f1ea-4f92-8646-17c70135964d|smart-link] \n\n!image-20260108-100224.png|width=1441,alt=\"image-20260108-100224.png\"!\n\n\n\nAre you asking for some different code ? ","2026-01-08T10:02:56.101Z"],["3795100","LSS-61256","LSS","lilijana.zaiceva@bolt.eu","Lilijana Zaiceva","[^Bolt Inbank confirmation (Nataliya Rodevich).pdf] _(103 kB)_","2026-01-08T10:03:20.336Z"],["3795102","LSS-61211","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Thank you [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] !","2026-01-08T10:03:23.149Z"],["3795103","LSS-60908","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] - I won’t manage to look into this, this week.\n\nCan you please look on Monday?\n\nThank you.","2026-01-08T10:03:45.956Z"],["3795104","PFI-830905","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T10:03:51.528Z"],["3795107","DSR-3135","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","Confirmed Monika can delete user’s data; [~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60] to approve draft email to DS: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zT8RlWzC_rHdxI9GOW3UGL-TwNcGrk2pJOd35qrNaKY/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zT8RlWzC_rHdxI9GOW3UGL-TwNcGrk2pJOd35qrNaKY/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T10:04:27.849Z"],["3795109","FX-3581","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767866709727829]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@chantel.rowe>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3581] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T10:05:22.474Z"],["3795112","PFI-820068","PFI","akisa.mathenge@bolt.eu","Akisa Mathenge","Hello [~accountid:62026399c4e2c9006ae5fb59] I’ve called the rider and claims that he has not received the refund. Do you mind sending the MPESA code or any proof that the refund was made?","2026-01-08T10:05:53.426Z"],["3795113","LSS-61250","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] forwarding this to you as it is new supplier of equity platform (Carta replacement).","2026-01-08T10:05:56.426Z"],["3795115","RS-1936","RS","aviv.geron@bolt.eu","Aviv Geron","Hi [~accountid:712020:1a99e337-a650-4a85-a8ed-f0825a04e850] (CC [~accountid:5d3ff51eb7f3ac0da80c815c] )\n\nThank you for sharing the additional context. Relationship-maintenance hospitality is recognised in principle under our ABAC framework; however, approval also depends on proportionality and the presence of a clear and specific business justification. In this case, the request was difficult to support due to the high overall expense and the absence of a defined business agenda or demonstrated necessity beyond general relationship maintenance.\n\nFor future requests, hospitality is more likely to be supportable where there is a clear business objective, a structured agenda, modest and proportionate hospitality, and a clear rationale for travel or premium events. We are very happy to discuss how the policy is applied in practice and to work through examples together with you and your manager. For completeness, the decision on this request remains unchanged.\n\nBest,\n\nAviv","2026-01-08T10:06:19.299Z"],["3795116","LSS-57592","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","* External email [legacyadria@gmail.com|mailto:legacyadria@gmail.com] that sent the complaint above is the same email registered with driver profile [Mario Macan|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8431109?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] - not clear how “the driver Mario Macan has misused my personal information” checks out in this case unless someone accessed the account and drove under the person’s name. However from the description, it doesn’t seem like this is the case.\n* Fleet [MARKOMAR TRANS j.d.o.o|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/56667?tab=profile]. doesn’t have any drivers registered, but has 199 vehicles registered.\n* Car ZG368KD mentioned is only in a [fleet|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/157278?tab=profile] where the fleet owner is driver Mario Macan\n* Driver profile moved to Fleet [MARKOMAR TRANS j.d.o.o|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/56667?tab=profile] on 4 Sept 2025, 10:05:34 (UTC+03:00). \n\n➡️ Checking with Local Ops if they can clarify whether anything looks off from the change logs","2026-01-08T10:06:22.200Z"],["3795119","WFM-9881","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! all approved, wish you a great day!","2026-01-08T10:07:00.634Z"],["3795121","LSS-61201","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Thank you [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] !","2026-01-08T10:07:22.909Z"],["3795122","LSS-61206","LSS","prateek.gauba@bolt.eu","Prateek Gauba","We will be storing it together, so Bolt and Hopp data will be stored in the same place, however the data will not have any personal information except for internal state logic, and the user_id which is owned by the identity team.","2026-01-08T10:07:35.591Z"],["3795128","PAW-14716","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T10:08:36.814Z"],["3795129","PAW-14715","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T10:08:39.145Z"],["3795130","LSS-60908","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey, I'm offline and I will return on January 12th. If absolutely critical and can't wait my return, please contact Alon Alkalay.\n\nThank you for your patience and understanding.","2026-01-08T10:09:06.395Z"],["3795135","WFM-9845","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hi, was it solved?","2026-01-08T10:10:13.719Z"],["3795136","BP-8169","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Rejected in order to consolidate the epic’s tickets under [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|smart-link], [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|smart-link] and [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T10:10:24.383Z"],["3795137","BP-8168","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Rejected in order to consolidate the epic’s tickets under [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|smart-link], [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|smart-link] and [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T10:10:27.501Z"],["3795138","BP-8167","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Rejected in order to consolidate the epic’s tickets under [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|smart-link], [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|smart-link] and [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T10:10:29.424Z"],["3795139","LSS-61140","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] - adding [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] to support from privacy","2026-01-08T10:10:30.345Z"],["3795140","BP-8166","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Rejected in order to consolidate the epic’s tickets under [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|smart-link], [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|smart-link] and [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T10:10:31.622Z"],["3795141","BP-8165","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Rejected in order to consolidate the epic’s tickets under [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|smart-link], [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|smart-link] and [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T10:10:34.348Z"],["3795142","BP-8161","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Rejected in order to consolidate the epic’s tickets under [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|smart-link], [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|smart-link] and [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T10:10:36.140Z"],["3795143","BP-8158","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Rejected in order to consolidate the epic’s tickets under [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8155|smart-link], [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8156|smart-link] and [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-8157|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T10:10:37.968Z"],["3795144","DRX-27792","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.126.0 (1502) Firebase build on Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\n!Screenshot_20260108-103132.png|width=170,alt=\"Screenshot_20260108-103132.png\"!","2026-01-08T10:10:57.927Z"],["3795145","LSS-60707","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hello, [~accountid:712020:6cd5c50c-08f0-4f10-98a4-ab7a39fef5d3] ! \n\n# *Re 1 (termination period)*:  \n\n{color:#36b37e}*Answer from Legal:*{color} Yes, we can shorten the period of 30 days of termination notice up to 15 days. 7 days seem to be too short for both parties. Please bear in mind that any change of T&C comes into force after 15-day from the notification of the drivers. *So, I think that the most probable effective date of this amendment would be around February 1st*.\n\n# *Re 2 (incentive period)*: \n\n_Is the 3 month period a more or less arbitrary time just for the sake of the T&Cs? What does it mean in practice?_\n\n_The actual incentive timeline for campaigns and branding payouts is different. Should we change this section to reflect that?_\n\n_When a new car gets branded, they need to provide proof - uploading a  picture in the driver profile. If the vehicle is to be included in next week’s bonus campaign (starting Monday 00:00), the deadline for photo submission is Friday 11:59 AM. ->_ *_the incentive doesn’t commence on the first day that Bolt receives a proof._*\n\n_If a vehicle successfully completes this initial process, there is a second level of in-app verification during the first week of an active incentive. If a vehicle passes that, the incentive gets renewed for 30 days (unless it gets terminated by us) and needs to re-verify within a window of 7 days before the 30 day period ends. As long as the car keeps passing verification, this process keeps repeating indefinitely_\n\n{color:#36b37e}*Question from Legal*{color}: How does the verification level look like in practice? What is it? Is there any difference between first verification and re-verification? I don't get the 7-day-period window.\n\n# *Re requirement related to incentives*: \n\n_The specific conditions for incentives are currently posted_ [_here_|https://bolt.eu/cs-cz/blog/polepy-bolt-jsou-tady/]_. Can we add something like “communicated to you via email … or posted on the Bolt website or blog”?_ \n\n{color:#36b37e}*Answer from Legal:* {color}Yes, provided that these requirements are clearly and easily available on the website (it should not be hidden or sth).\n\n# *Re reaffixing services costs*\n\n_2.4.1. Where this is the case, the attachment or reaffixing services costs shall be made known to you before the Branding Materials are provided and can be subject to change during the term of this Agreement. By agreeing to the attachment of the Branding Materials to the Designated Vehicle(s), you agree to pay these costs. If you do not agree to such costs, you should not attach or allow the attachment of the Branding Materials to the Designated Vehicles._\n\n_We generally don’t inform the drivers about the specific sum required to repair a sticker as this varies between different cities/partner companies. The driver should only get instructed about the cost by the specific partner wrapping company. Does this require any updates to the 2.4.1. Section?_\n\n{color:#36b37e}*Question from Legal:* {color}Basically, yes, we can change it as you wish. But as you said “We GENERALLY don’t inform” and the provision states “Where this is the case”, so are there any cases when Bolt informs about the costs in advance or never does? If there is any situation when we do inform the drivers (fleets) about the costs, this provision should be rephrased so that it would be clearly stated when we do inform about the costs. \n\nI am looking forward to your feedback so I can be working on the update this week 😉\n\nBest,\n\nJola","2026-01-08T10:11:18.762Z"],["3795146","LSS-61257","LSS","reinis.levanovics@bolt.eu","Reinis Levanovičs","[^Pavēste.15550011055525-2.SIA Bolt Services LV.3.pdf]\n\nHii team 🌻 \nI didn’t allow me to upload request, so adding it in comments 🤗 ","2026-01-08T10:11:20.099Z"],["3795147","WFM-9883","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Hey [~accountid:5df3830d41fd8d0e35073cbd], thank you for your report, we updated permissions that are a part of the roles that agents have, so now the page you mentioned shouldn't be visible","2026-01-08T10:11:19.630Z"],["3795149","PAW-14750","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-product-data-management, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-08T10:11:26.544Z"],["3795152","LSS-61258","LSS","sylwia.wiktorowska@bolt.eu","Sylwia Wiktorowska","[^POA2026.pdf] _(105 kB)_","2026-01-08T10:11:58.451Z"],["3795153","DRX-27953","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: - nothing to test","2026-01-08T10:12:40.426Z"],["3795154","SREDESK-7387","SREDESK","mehran.eftekhari@bolt.eu","Shahriar Eftekhari","provisioning mq redises in k8s...","2026-01-08T10:12:55.449Z"],["3795157","LSS-61257","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi there, thanks for reaching out to the Privacy team!\n\nPlease note that *Law Enforcement Requests (LERs)* should be raised via the *Risk Service Desk*, not the Privacy Service Desk.\n\n➡️ [Click here to submit your LER to the Risk team|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/36/group/3303/create/4818]\n\n\n\nIf you have any questions in the meantime, feel free to reach out to the *Risk team* directly. This ticket will be closed.\n\nThanks for your attention and cooperation!","2026-01-08T10:13:35.646Z"],["3795159","LSS-61082","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Hi [~accountid:712020:135ca6fc-06c4-46bb-ae27-f67c40f280cf] I think a supplier of facility management services would be ideal, thanks.","2026-01-08T10:13:48.398Z"],["3795178","LSS-55393","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Thanks, [~accountid:712020:0db6c6e6-af60-46ff-ba53-133f0ab23c9b] 1 so, [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] please proceed with signing of all the files uploaded except the Romanian one. \n\nThank you 😀 ","2026-01-08T10:17:09.896Z"],["3795179","WFM-9884","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! Do agents need classic backlog or playmode ?","2026-01-08T10:17:17.651Z"],["3795180","FDBT-4748","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-08T10:17:35.788Z"],["3795181","WFM-9884","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601579|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601579] TL","2026-01-08T10:18:05.930Z"],["3795184","PFI-830911","PFI","patrik.kupco@bolt.eu","Patrik Kupčo","!Screenshot_20260108-110037.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T10:18:22.808Z"],["3795186","LSS-61048","LSS","karina.kochanovskaya@bolt.eu","Karina Kochanovskaya","thanks! ","2026-01-08T10:18:30.733Z"],["3795190","LSS-54143","LSS","etienne.lamysmith@bolt.eu","Etienne Lamy-Smith","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] thanks for the extra info. \n\nAligned on holding fire until we know more about the regulation/coopérative situation. \n(Will post about this in fr-fleet-employment for visibility)","2026-01-08T10:19:10.305Z"],["3795193","LSS-60888","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (08.01.26)*+\n\n* Specific KPIs that will be used to measure eligibility have not yet been confirmed. However, the aim will be to steer clear of driver behaviour and instead look at vehicle criteria.\n** *Thoughts*: Fine. Lowers the risk profile, so LIA/DPIA/A22 very unlikely to apply. \n* Alexia is not aware of what disclaimers we use here. Alexia also seems to have misinterpreted my Q to mean that consent is the legal basis here.\n** *Thoughts*: Although vehicle data is mentioned in the PN, the context is not quite specific enough, and so a disclaimer would still be helpful.  should also flag that we want to try and avoid relying on consent unless necessary here.\n* We do not yet know who the supplier is. However, we would only be sharing personal data with them for the strict purpose of car branding.\n** *Thoughts*: We should push for a DPA to cover this.\n\n*NEXT STEPS*:\n\n* Wait for confirmations re KPIs / supplier.\n* Once confirmed, draft a disclaimer and a DPA. Emphasis that LI is the best legal basis.","2026-01-08T10:19:34.717Z"],["3795194","TAXP-1317","TAXP","carmen.diaz@bolt.eu","Carmen Díaz-Carrasco","[~accountid:61b9ad7c2900b00071da0b68] is it ok if I update this due date?","2026-01-08T10:19:43.158Z"],["3795195","CSXPC-257","CSXPC","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","New process being drafted here: \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pbgChTVf4bU_nFoByFHZzXdzrYSLqBYKw1fprI_CU18/edit?tab=t.5xp98zbrlkzn|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pbgChTVf4bU_nFoByFHZzXdzrYSLqBYKw1fprI_CU18/edit?tab=t.5xp98zbrlkzn]\n\nManaged to draft how to action reports of illegal content and made a start on appeals. Think it would be best to combine these into one for better clarity. \n\nMeeting with Liisa today to cover any missing steps / information. ","2026-01-08T10:19:44.316Z"],["3795201","TAXP-1317","TAXP","tiiu.albin@bolt.eu","Tiiu Albin","[~accountid:608e5558f0db1300698c69d4] of course! TP is not critical as no red flags were raised during the FY24 review. ","2026-01-08T10:22:12.540Z"],["3795203","LSS-57592","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hey [~accountid:712020:1dfd242d-ab75-4618-8ae1-db899ee9b04c] - happy new year! \nI am following-up this ticket - unfortunately it slipped my radar due to an increased workload in the past months and I am only catching up to it now. I apologise for this.\n\nI did a bit of research on my own with the available data, and I've reached a point where I could benefits from your insights. What I've established so far is that:\n\n* The external email [legacyadria@gmail.com|mailto:legacyadria@gmail.com] used to share the complaint via BH is the same email registered with driver profile [Mario Macan|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8431109?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] - which makes it unclear how “the driver Mario Macan has misused my personal information” checks out in this case, unless someone accessed the account and drove under the person’s name. However from the description, it doesn’t seem like this is the case.\n* Fleet [+MARKOMAR TRANS j.d.o.o+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/56667?tab=profile]. doesn’t have any drivers registered, but has 199 vehicles registered.\n* Car ZG368KD mentioned is only in a [+fleet+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/157278?tab=profile] where the fleet owner is driver Mario Macan\n* Driver profile moved to Fleet [+MARKOMAR TRANS j.d.o.o+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/56667?tab=profile] on 4 Sept 2025, 10:05:34 (UTC+03:00). There were also a number of changes to the profile (e.g. email) around that time period).\n\nAs I am not very familiar with drivers' change log and how to interpret it, I was wondering if you could support - when you have a moment - on this front? Essentially, I would like to know if you can establish whether the change requests (e.g., fleet change, email change, etc) were made by the legitimate account owner or if there's any evidence that it may have been done by someone else (for example, via a different device). Thanks in advance!","2026-01-08T10:22:18.900Z"],["3795204","WD-22483","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[+WD-20427+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-20427]","2026-01-08T10:22:19.857Z"],["3795209","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","[@ahmed.farghaly|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63fc5f040a4a47fb8d20cf92] could you please point me to the subscriber code, so that I can track it down to the publisher and debug?","2026-01-08T10:23:41.450Z"],["3795210","CNT-321","CNT","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:6163ec849cdb930072d02e8e] and [~accountid:712020:bca00e26-f5bd-4a5b-9a82-68a8ff2fc37e] \n\nAt the end of last year, we launched several page variants that are currently being A/B tested via paid ads in selected regions:\n\nA = [https://bolt.eu/en/business/|https://bolt.eu/en/business/|smart-link] \n\nB = [https://bolt.eu/en/business/bolt-for-business/|https://bolt.eu/en/business/bolt-for-business/|smart-link] \n\nC = [https://bolt.eu/en/business/join-bolt/|https://bolt.eu/en/business/join-bolt/|smart-link] \n\nSince the test is still ongoing, I suggest we move this ticket to blocked or backlog until we can apply the learnings from the test to the next version of the page. Thanks!","2026-01-08T10:23:45.047Z"],["3795211","PAW-14710","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/pull/3074\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-08 10:23:54 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-08T10:23:55.021Z"],["3795214","HS-28588","HS","klaudia.skorlutowska@bolt.eu","Klaudia Skorłutowska","Thank you Kristin for claraficition. Please find attached document then 🙂  For next 2 points - I have entered 0PLN, because to be honest still not sure to understand it correctly 🙈  submitted the data as they’re correct. \n\n\n\n[^RMUA.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T10:25:12.876Z"],["3795215","WFM-9884","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","requested playmode for now [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541614|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541614]","2026-01-08T10:25:19.451Z"],["3795217","WD-22495","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hi, country requirement removed","2026-01-08T10:25:48.581Z"],["3795220","WFM-9889","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","cs - safety role needed","2026-01-08T10:26:10.172Z"],["3795221","HS-25553","HS","oleh.mykhash@bolt.eu","Oleh Mykhash","[~accountid:6012c28dc8c36c00697646b9] [~accountid:62e0e5a62fe585febb3bd6b4] \nKind reminder since I still didn’t get any notification about the payments.","2026-01-08T10:26:15.723Z"],["3795225","HS-25553","HS","oleh.mykhash@bolt.eu","Oleh Mykhash","Sorry, typo, was about to ping [~accountid:712020:950de065-187c-4170-babd-e5aa814bdb19] ","2026-01-08T10:26:55.630Z"],["3795228","WFM-9892","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! For new tools access, please raise request to IT ","2026-01-08T10:27:12.269Z"],["3795232","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767868073667879]*{color}:\nHi Kerli,\n\nThe plan in the case above would be to proceed with compensation subtype  and due to it not being transparent/visible for FOs in FOP we would create these manual credit notes so that they get the visibility they need.\n\nBut it seems like you have a better solution from what I can see, can you help us confirm if we have the possibility to proceed with the invoiceable subtypes and how to proceed from here <@U04FV4Z0GQ4>?\n\nFurthermore, when you say a 'one time thing' I believe you are referring to the balance transfer, right? But how do we approach the other compensations we need to do in which are done more sporadically such as equipment deposit would that also fall under 'one time thing' ?\n{quote}","2026-01-08T10:28:10.134Z"],["3795233","WD-22471","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hi, access granted to run integration","2026-01-08T10:28:14.093Z"],["3795236","LSS-60741","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:1e9398f2-efcd-4dcd-8ece-28e6f8578e37] - noted regarding the outstanding items on this which still need to be confirmed. Subject to those confirmations, my thoughts are as follows from the privacy side:\n\n* *KPIs*: I agree that we should stick to vehicle criteria rather than driver behaviour 💡  as this is much lower risk from a privacy POV. Please let me know once the specific KPIs are confirmed so that I can check them for good measure.\n* *Disclaimer*: To be clear, I am not necessarily recommending that we rely on consent here (I am merely asking if this is an approach that we have taken before). In either case, I would still recommend some short disclaimer language 💡 since this kind of processing/data sharing is not explicitly covered in our privacy notice, and so technically there is residual transparency risk here. Once this matter is more progressed, let me know and I would be happy to prepare a disclaimer to be shared with the relevant drivers.\n* *Data sharing*: Based on the information provided to date, it sounds as though we should include some data processing provisions in the service agreement that we enter into with the supplier 💡  Once the draft is up and running, let me know and I would be happy to prepare these.\n\n{color:#4c9aff}*In short* {color}- We will likely need a disclaimer and some additions to the agreement from the privacy side - I will prepare these once we have more visibility of the supplier / data sharing 🙂 ","2026-01-08T10:28:29.263Z"],["3795237","PFI-830915","PFI","ifeoluwa.adeola@bolt-outsource.eu","Ifeoluwa Adeola","[^Finca Microfinance Bank Limited.pdf]","2026-01-08T10:28:29.553Z"],["3795239","SUPX-2253","SUPX","michal.rapinczuk@bolt.eu","Michał Rapińczuk","*Agreed requirements:*\n\n* reduce the threshold for {{solved}} and {{pending}} cases to 48 hrs\n* keep the reminder set up for 24 hrs for {{solved}} cases\n* (future) introduce {{pending}} cases reminder (as it requires new translations and hence would introduce delay)\n* reducing thresholds further should be discussed (and possibly supported via admin panel)\n* keep the quiet hours implementation behind a feature flag (disabled for now)\n* potentially exclude emails (focusing on authorities as these should be excluded), safety is already not included","2026-01-08T10:28:56.529Z"],["3795240","LSS-53508","LSS","weronika.ners@bolt.eu","Weronika Ners","Hey! Can we send out the copies to Estonia to be signed?","2026-01-08T10:29:20.246Z"],["3795243","DO-5719","DO","asma.muzaffar@bolt.eu","Asma Muzaffar","{{ng_public_spark.user_user}}\n\n","2026-01-08T10:31:04.717Z"],["3795244","LSS-60050","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","[^SKM_C251i26010711290.pdf]\n[^2. Umowa najmu Angel Retail sp. z o.o. 1 sp.k. Bolt 29_12_2025 - zmiany najemcy RP -rev Bolt v2.docx (2) (1) (50958625-caa5-4924-8e48-24537b5e992d) (3a493cf6-f0c4-49d0-9d92-36d56529ef68).pdf]\n[^Zawiadomienia o przelewie Alior AR1 (1)-kopia.pdf]\n\nHi, Im sending both signed agreements, and also signed notice of assignment. \n","2026-01-08T10:31:16.691Z"],["3795249","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","We are subscribed to  {{DriverReliableEventSubscriberMqApi}}","2026-01-08T10:31:59.159Z"],["3795250","LSS-57452","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nYes, everything has been confirmed on AWS.\n\nThank you!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.30.54.png|width=1377,height=551,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.30.54.png\"!\n\n[^offer-otjmsos7hiuq6 (3).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T10:32:22.072Z"],["3795251","PFI-830881","PFI","raphael.perna@bolt.eu","Raphaël Samy Perna","Thanks for the heads-up, I’ve escalated the ticket to the Privacy team. You can close this one.","2026-01-08T10:32:38.615Z"],["3795252","WFM-9897","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541615|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541615]","2026-01-08T10:32:49.366Z"],["3795254","CEBF-1570","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","BulkOpportunityLosingController - 90%","2026-01-08T10:32:55.218Z"],["3795258","WFM-9897","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! backlog mode was activated, also request the team lead role to be used for training, waiting for approval ","2026-01-08T10:33:54.928Z"],["3795260","TA-11","TA","paulo.morna@bolt.eu","Paulo Morna","Updatxe from People Tech (December 18th):\n\nHello Everyone,\n\nThis past week has been quite productive so I’m happy to share with you the following updates:\n:progress_bar: Status: On track\n\nCustom Fields: we now have 8 custom fields that will pull in information automatically (Hiring Manager’s Name; Hiring Manager’s Business Title; Working Hours; Employment Type) +\n(NEW) Annual Gross Salary\n(NEW) Contract Length – for fixed-term contracts\n(NEW) Probation Period - created tables for 46 countries to pull the probation period, depending on the contract type (Regular/Fixed Term). For the other 6 countries, there is not probation period setup in Workday.\nStock Grant Amount and the Annualized Stock Grant Value.\n         :how: does it work  - check the thread's comments\n\n# Templates:\nCreated WC (White-collar) and BC (Blue-collar) templates for the following 9 countries: Croatia, Cyprus, Czech Republic, Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France, Romania, United Kingdom. Rest of 44 countries templates are WIP.\nFor each of these templates, the Personal Questionnaire takes the user to the correct country-specific personal information form.\nThe Benefits (WC/BC) are hardcoded in the templates. Where the benefits are not available (e.g BC Cyprus), I’ve left the section blank.\n\n:black_right_pointing_double_triangle_with_vertical_bar: Next steps:\nThoroughly test the Stock Grant Amount and the Annualized Stock Grant Value automation to ensure the calculations are 100% correct\nContinue to develop the WC/BC Offer templates for the rest of the 44 countries\nAnalyze the feasibility of going live in January/February with 5-15 pilot countries, but only after the 2026 stock calculator & final stock one pagers are finalized by the Equity Team.\n\n:documents:Attached you can find the latest WIP template and an example of the offer letter that was generated based on the template.","2026-01-08T10:34:16.070Z"],["3795261","WD-22415","WD","steve.white@bolt.eu","Steve White","[~accountid:62b1977ddcafd965c5ddc33e] my people are on it!  [~accountid:6271326a2db3080070241cfa] FYI","2026-01-08T10:34:42.741Z"],["3795263","WFM-9899","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","please request Beehive Rides *CS* Agent role, not ops","2026-01-08T10:35:03.239Z"],["3795264","HS-25553","HS","aleksandra.kusiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Kusiak","Hi Oleh, \n\nPlease be advised that we as the Payroll Team are unable to confirm, as we are not involved in the enrollment process directly, but we only process the PPK contribution payments. \nFor PPK queries I can advise to contact PPK:\n[https://www.mojeppk.pl/faq.html#type=pracownik&theme=all|https://www.mojeppk.pl/faq.html#type=pracownik&theme=all|smart-link] \n\nFor enrollment [~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0] could you please check on your side with the provider and advise Oleh?\n\nKind regards,\nAleksandra ","2026-01-08T10:35:26.214Z"],["3795266","SREDESK-7345","SREDESK","yehor.naumenko@bolt.eu","Yehor Naumenko","Decreased TTL to 100 days.\nNext step is 30 days.","2026-01-08T10:35:40.763Z"],["3795268","HS-28363","HS","maria-denisa.laslau@bolt.eu","Denisa Laslău","Hello\\!\n\nAre there any updates on this one?\nThe people partner was on holiday when I raised the ticket and mentioned she'll do the changes between Christmas and New Year.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-08T10:35:47.622Z"],["3795269","PFI-802926","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Thank youu\n\n--\n\nI have a question regarding the Hopp logo. [~accountid:712020:bba87790-3d07-4531-9af3-f5df86d0d56a], are there any plans to include the logo on Hopp Plus invoices?\n\nCurrently, there is no logo on RH or BB invoices. Based on that, I’d suggest following the same approach for subscription invoices as well and keeping them without a logo for consistency across other verticals.\n\nBut in case a logo is required, could you please provide it?","2026-01-08T10:36:24.690Z"],["3795271","LSS-61058","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] - I have submitted the update which should be published over the course of today. I will confirm once this has gone through 🙂 ","2026-01-08T10:36:31.910Z"],["3795273","BP-13382","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Tested in feature preview branch [+Bolt | Business+|https://business.prelive.bolt.eu/feature-BP-13167-use-semantic-colors/#/company/25870]  (/)\n\n||*Route*||*After [light mode]*||*After [dark mode]*||\n|/create|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.25.52.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.25.52.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.25.58.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.25.58.png\"!|\n|/company/:company/get-started|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.27.09.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.27.09.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.27.20.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.27.20.png\"!|\n|/reset-password/:code|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.36.29.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.36.29.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.35.54.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.35.54.png\"!|","2026-01-08T10:37:02.375Z"],["3795274","LSS-60660","LSS","natalie.kolinova@bolt-outsource.eu","Natalie Kolínova","Hello [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] , I have got answers from *dev-user-auth-support*, Slack channel:\n\n“From what I see the account of the user 122661268 still doesn’t have a phone number set back up and since I removed the phone number, nobody logged this account back in. There were no neither Ride Hailing nor Food orders made since Dec 18th when the user with the device id {{9D6E769B-3CB3-4134-8696-0F4E99EE6EEF}} was logged out. Only the user who setup Google social account in May 2022 may have access to this account and setup a new phone number there. The user who setup Google social account is quite likely the original user who created this account who hasn’t been active since Sep 2025.”\n\nSo, it looks like that account is safe and only original user who can have access to Google social account can log in this account.\n\n","2026-01-08T10:37:00.255Z"],["3795277","LSS-59915","LSS","kristiina.klemm@bolt.eu","Kristiina Klemm","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] please find attached docusigned contract by EY attached, could you please add Ahto’s signature also in docusign format?\n\n[^Agreement for the services provided_Bolt Operations OÜ_Ernst & Young Baltic AS_18.12.25.asice]\n\n","2026-01-08T10:37:54.542Z"],["3795278","WFM-9894","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Hey [~accountid:712020:207c95ff-c39e-492c-9c31-f804f0b6bb8a], as you are requesting reactive comms, the character limit is 150 characters while your message is 527, please review the text! \r\nWe also need a title as well as the translation into English. ","2026-01-08T10:37:59.789Z"],["3795279","BEE-3626","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko",":wave: small update so far: we discussed this story within team on grooming today and estimated it around 2 days of work\n\nit's hard to tell yet when it goes into work in terms of priorities etc, I'll post any updates as soon as we have them, also if you have any additional comments around that please let us know as well :pray:\n\nalso there is one related question we'd want to clarify:\n\nduring last hackathon we had [@piotr.musiol|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6017bc27a41ea5006a86f73b] implemented related feature showing number of \"reopens\" in casesview like on screenshot below - and well huge difference between that data point and what you were describing above is about counting or not counting reopens during Alfred part of things\n\nquestion is: do you think the difference between these two things - the way how we count for your metric request (without Alfred) and the way currently in UI (with Alfred) - could be confusing for someone? if yes - what would you prefer to do about it?\n\nsome of the possible options would be:\n1. ignore and do nothing - counting for metric and that label on UI would currently be just two separate things, like as is now (also we'd not have any places where we display that \"reopen\" count used in metric, so it's probably not going to be super noticeable)\n2. unify so that _both do not count_ (i.e. do not include) Alfred part - this adds a bit more work (can be handled as separate piece of delivery, so it's like option 1 above and then some extra follow-up work to unify whenever we prioritize that)\n3. unify so that _both do count_ (i.e. include into reopens number) also Alfred part - well, if I got your comments right this seems undesirable, and also coincidentally this happens to be the most complex technically option (i.e. if you choose this one - estimate of 2 days above no longer holds, and we'd need to reconsider approach within team entirely from scratch and give new estimates) \nwdyt? :pray:\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7E1HBFD3/screenshot_2026-01-08_at_11.26.52.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7E1HBFD3/screenshot_2026-01-08_at_11.26.52.png|smart-link]","2026-01-08T10:38:16.998Z"],["3795282","PFI-826390","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo,\n\nInvoice issuer is ready → [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing/invoiceIssuer/edit/1710004?tab=generalInfo|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing/invoiceIssuer/edit/1710004?tab=generalInfo]\n\n[~accountid:712020:876960aa-09c5-44ff-9c52-2cb24c637062] are there any plans regarding fiscalization for BB as well, considering it’s a fiscal market? ","2026-01-08T10:38:44.823Z"],["3795284","PFI-829471","PFI","laura.loaiza@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Muñoz","New case: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719678263|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719678263]\n\nBusiness profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/238211?tab=business_company|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/238211?tab=business_company]","2026-01-08T10:39:31.242Z"],["3795285","CSXPC-292","CSXPC","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","Web SD here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WEB-9805|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WEB-9805]","2026-01-08T10:40:02.375Z"],["3795288","LSS-61151","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Complete_with_Docusign_bolteu_(taxify)_x_Ro (1).pdf]\n\nPlease share signed document with the Counterparty’s signature for archiving purposes.","2026-01-08T10:40:51.005Z"],["3795289","LSS-61254","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - Kindly review the form as mentioned in the ticket to ensure that us filling it in would not expose us to any data protection or breach risks. Thank You! ","2026-01-08T10:41:05.044Z"],["3795290","EBIKE1-318","EBIKE1","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","It turned out that IOT does not support FOTA for hublock yet and it needs to be addressed by IOT team.\n\n\n\nTesting of the new Lofandi firmware can be done by {{2026-01-16}} ","2026-01-08T10:41:31.029Z"],["3795296","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","It`s being discussed currently with Rockbros, the silicone phone holder supplier, if they have any fixed phone orientation specific plastic clips.\n\nIn the picture below, you can see slots on the holder side (red) and higher notches (blue) on the clip side. If the notches on the clip were longer, they would reach the slots and secure the holder, preventing rotation.\n\n!3afbd6417374b3d93d437edae2c15593-20260108-103947.png|width=567,alt=\"3afbd6417374b3d93d437edae2c15593-20260108-103947.png\"!","2026-01-08T10:42:57.704Z"],["3795297","PFI-829960","PFI","ernestas.jurasius@bolt-outsource.eu","Ernestas Jurasius","Hello Nikolay, \n\nThe invoice that needs to be reissued is only related to order [#2254284956|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2254284956/9?orderTryId=2861451524]*.* This is the order invoice in admin: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5727806580|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5727806580?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]. \n\nAlso attaching the PDF file if relevant. \n\nThank you!\n\n[^invoice.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T10:43:22.663Z"],["3795299","LSS-60200","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:ae4fba9f-a97d-41eb-8fd7-bec2a5bc17d0] ,This ticket was initially raised with the marketing team and has only just been reassigned to us. We are reviewing it now and will get back to you as soon as possible.","2026-01-08T10:43:37.086Z"],["3795300","HS-28738","HS","richmond.lartey@bolt.eu","Richmond Sammy Lartey","!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 9.58.58 AM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T10:43:44.125Z"],["3795301","LSS-61174","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] [~accountid:712020:10c3f4ef-f975-47a3-8af8-927b01cd9521] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached. \n\n[^Document_for_your_Signature (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T10:44:23.515Z"],["3795302","CAMLE-7407","CAMLE","evgeniy.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Evgeniy Kuznetsov","Rejected by mobile devs","2026-01-08T10:44:26.052Z"],["3795303","PFI-820831","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Hi [~accountid:712020:a6603df2-60ae-46e4-bd8b-5b0da4563f9d] [~accountid:712020:e738da1c-d789-4e95-bd6a-9c1959a0ccd1] \n\nI see the invoice pdf in admin\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.43.35.png|width=919,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.43.35.png\"!","2026-01-08T10:44:32.561Z"],["3795305","PFI-830647","PFI","jose.vietto@bolt.eu","Jose Ignacio Gutierrez Vietto","Hello [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] \n\nHope you are doing well.\n\nAs is said, there didn't use the accounts from April and May….so i don't actually understand where those payments come from.\n\n\n\nCould you please clarify the periods?\n\n\n\nThanks","2026-01-08T10:44:44.207Z"],["3795306","PFI-830647","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-08T10:44:47.878Z"],["3795309","PRIV-503","PRIV","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Privacy provided a [recommendation|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09S7DSG3D1/p1767162789228669] to the Franchise & Commerce Teams to go with Scenario 2 in this setup:\n\n{quote}Scenario 2 (the Data-Transfer Model), is the most preferable.\n\n* It maintains the separation of roles between YourTrip and the regulated financial entity, Chari. Under this model, YourTrip remains a *pure data controller/transferor* for the initial data collection for the Bolt Platform and the transfer of that data,  avoiding the status of a regulated financial intermediary or agent.\n* This demarcation minimizes YourTrip's regulatory exposure, simplifies compliance with Moroccan data protection law (Law 09-08), and prevents scope creep of data processing responsibilities beyond the established Partnership Agreement and DSA.\n* This setup allows YourTrip's communications to drivers to be treated as non-promotional, *informational and operational* rather than regulated financial marketing, which is a cleaner and less burdensome compliance position.{quote}","2026-01-08T10:45:24.335Z"],["3795310","PRIV-520","PRIV","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Privacy provided a [+recommendation+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09S7DSG3D1/p1767162789228669] to the Franchise & Commerce Teams to go with Scenario 2 in this setup:\n\n{quote}Scenario 2 (the Data-Transfer Model), is the most preferable.\n\n* It maintains the separation of roles between YourTrip and the regulated financial entity, Chari. Under this model, YourTrip remains a *pure data controller/transferor* for the initial data collection for the Bolt Platform and the transfer of that data,  avoiding the status of a regulated financial intermediary or agent.\n* This demarcation minimizes YourTrip's regulatory exposure, simplifies compliance with Moroccan data protection law (Law 09-08), and prevents scope creep of data processing responsibilities beyond the established Partnership Agreement and DSA.\n* This setup allows YourTrip's communications to drivers to be treated as non-promotional, *informational and operational* rather than regulated financial marketing, which is a cleaner and less burdensome compliance position.{quote}\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n*Next steps*: ensure we have a proper consent flow for data-sharing with YourTrip and onward sharing to Chari Bank.\n{panel}","2026-01-08T10:45:38.595Z"],["3795312","LSS-58081","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Following up on this [~accountid:5d1b218591943f0d2ac52db0] . Can you please share a separate SoW for the capacity building courses. It will really help us speed things up. ","2026-01-08T10:46:17.088Z"],["3795313","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c] Yes, then that’s cool","2026-01-08T10:47:15.316Z"],["3795314","LSS-61261","LSS","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","[^ZO_3_2026_Bolt.docx] _(259 kB)_","2026-01-08T10:47:32.879Z"],["3795316","PFI-808451","PFI","adam.sokolowski@bolt.eu","Adam Sokołowski","hi [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] can you share an update on this please?\ncc: [~accountid:712020:d3fd53e6-f124-4770-a577-b09d6688566f] for visibility","2026-01-08T10:48:21.330Z"],["3795317","SREC-359","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","!image-20260108-104818.png|width=654,alt=\"image-20260108-104818.png\"!\n\nAccount will be deleted in 3 days.","2026-01-08T10:48:28.274Z"],["3795319","CSDT-947","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","PR merged. Will make a separate task for the final Looker sync after all scorecard metrics are done. ","2026-01-08T10:48:55.025Z"],["3795321","WD-22497","WD","merje.maripuu@bolt.eu","Merje Maripuu","done","2026-01-08T10:49:29.802Z"],["3795322","WD-22478","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","Hi [~accountid:712020:ba573a40-4536-4a67-b84d-7156c8a2f5ec] \n\nWe’ve updated the time tracking.\nPlease feel free to check and let me know if something else is needed.\n\nKind regards,\n\nDarja \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.47.31.png|width=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.47.31.png\"!","2026-01-08T10:49:31.093Z"],["3795323","CSDT-946","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","PR merged. Will make a separate task for the final Looker sync after all scorecard metrics are done. ","2026-01-08T10:49:33.427Z"],["3795325","LSS-60050","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hi, [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ! the landlord signed off the lease agreement and I ant to be 100% sure that this agreement was signed with a qualified e-signature by them. As I gave no access to Adobe, could you please verify and let me know? \n\nThis is the file [^2. Umowa najmu Angel Retail sp. z o.o. 1 sp.k. Bolt 29_12_2025 - zmiany najemcy RP -rev Bolt v2.docx (2) (1) (50958625-caa5-4924-8e48-24537b5e992d) (07b83743-b67e-4caa-865b-cb8fd17e5e55).pdf] \n\nAdditionally, could you please proceed with signing of the file on notification of agreement’s assignment - Ahto Kink’s signature is needed (SpotDraft is sufficient). \n\nThis is the file [^Zawiadomienia o przelewie Alior AR1 (1)-kopia (782ed5c1-0fd1-4c24-845b-df8c624b7542).pdf] \n\nThank you! 😉 \n\nBest, Jola","2026-01-08T10:49:49.538Z"],["3795326","SREC-358","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","I don’t see any payment methods added in the VNG Cloud UI. Let’s consider this done as we are already deleting the account.","2026-01-08T10:50:00.068Z"],["3795327","CSDA-278","CSDA","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Hey! Since there was no follow up to this task since 15.12, I will close it. Please feel free to reach out in the same task if the question is still relevant. ","2026-01-08T10:50:17.772Z"],["3795329","BP-13364","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Tested in feature preview branch [+Bolt | Business+|https://business.prelive.bolt.eu/feature-BP-13167-use-semantic-colors/#/company/25870]  (/)\n\n||*Route*||*After [light mode]*||*After [dark mode]*||\n|/company/:company|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.41.15.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.41.15.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.41.32.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.41.32.png\"!|\n|/company/:company/whats-new|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.50.08.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.50.08.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.50.38.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.50.38.png\"!|\n|/company/:company/how-to-pay|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.45.53.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.45.53.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.46.58.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.46.58.png\"!|","2026-01-08T10:51:20.729Z"],["3795331","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","alrighty, Aydin and the team are on it","2026-01-08T10:51:56.139Z"],["3795333","LSS-61238","LSS","aivo.toots@bolt.eu","Aivo Toots","Hello [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] !\n\nThe contract project was already in English, now adding the other document in English.\nAbout the personal data - I will come back to it soon.\n\n\n\n\n\n[^Certification Terms and Conditions.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T10:52:29.033Z"],["3795334","SUPX-2301","SUPX","michal.rapinczuk@bolt.eu","Michał Rapińczuk","Let’s follow up offline on implementation details","2026-01-08T10:52:43.016Z"],["3795336","LSS-61256","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8] ! May you please clarify who needs to sign? \n\nBoth Ahto and Nataliya?","2026-01-08T10:52:52.198Z"],["3795337","CSDA-256","CSDA","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Hi, Nargiz. Keeping you posted on this topic: we do not yet have agent level data available in new explores, but are picking up this topic in January. Will keep you informed on the updates. ","2026-01-08T10:52:53.147Z"],["3795338","PFI-830647","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Based on my initial message, regarding the payment reversals, contact the Payments Team. The company used services before and got some bank transfer made/wrongfully allocated, etc (Payments Team can advise). Afterwards, the payments were reversed and caused a debt, which was then captured. \n\nThe Balance movements, can be seen in the Start/End Balances.","2026-01-08T10:52:56.058Z"],["3795339","PFI-829471","PFI","laura.loaiza@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Muñoz","New case: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719533647|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719533647] \n\nBusiness profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/377861?tab=business_company|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/377861?tab=business_company]","2026-01-08T10:53:03.782Z"],["3795341","LSS-61256","LSS","lilijana.zaiceva@bolt.eu","Lilijana Zaiceva","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] just Ahto is enough","2026-01-08T10:53:56.794Z"],["3795342","PFI-830927","PFI","chiamaka.madujibeya@bolt-outsource.eu","Chiamaka Madujibeya","!image-20260108-105256.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T10:54:34.630Z"],["3795343","PFI-826390","PFI","tyler.ison@bolt.eu","Tyler Hamilton Ison","Hi [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] - no, fiscalisation applies only to B2C; BB should be all B2B transactions, outside of scope, and there are not currently e-invoicing requirements for B2B transactions in Moldova","2026-01-08T10:55:18.955Z"],["3795344","WFM-9895","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Hello [~accountid:712020:3a3742eb-3298-4df7-a8af-c0fd7279bf95], \r\n\r\nWhat countries should Jacob have access to? Please name them.","2026-01-08T10:55:24.972Z"],["3795346","PFI-830883","PFI","agne.majauskaiteshah@bolt-outsource.eu","Agnė Majauskaiteshah","Could you please review again, further help needed. The invoice cannot be found. ","2026-01-08T10:55:52.041Z"],["3795348","LSS-60050","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] , assigning this one to me, thank you!","2026-01-08T10:55:58.359Z"],["3795349","SUPX-2297","SUPX","michal.rapinczuk@bolt.eu","Michał Rapińczuk","Change led by safety keyword detection issues in Thailand and China.\n\nAlso, let’s consider adding alerts.","2026-01-08T10:56:03.649Z"],["3795351","PFI-830929","PFI","hans-kristjan.volmerson@bolt-outsource.eu","Hans-Kristjan Volmerson","!537ccf5e-b245-456a-8ce2-c1e09a854d39.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T10:56:40.835Z"],["3795353","LSS-51178","LSS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey! My bad - please find the signed agreement attached with our requested edits accepted. I realise I must have not made a ticket for signing - counterparty initiated via DocuSign and Legal Ops provided the signed copy over Slack.\n\n[^WRLD US Gift Agreement 2025 – Bolt – 20250613.docx.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T10:56:58.133Z"],["3795354","PFI-830930","PFI","mariel.caniza@bolt-outsource.eu","Mariel Ortega Cañiza","!WhatsApp Image 2026-01-05 at 08.03.14.jpeg.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T10:57:01.381Z"],["3795355","PFI-830931","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-08T10:57:29.791Z"],["3795356","EBIKE1-420","EBIKE1","aare.palm@bolt.eu","Aare Palm","From log it seems what main battery connection was bad, both data and power\n\n[https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/rentals-micromobility/vehicles/iot/view/10125?tab=logs&filter={\"limit\"%3A0%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"lines\"%3A1000%2C\"from_ts\"%3A1766758200%2C\"to_ts\"%3A1766768400}}|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/rentals-micromobility/vehicles/iot/view/10125?tab=logs&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A0%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22lines%22%3A1000%2C%22from_ts%22%3A1766758200%2C%22to_ts%22%3A1766768400%7D%7D]\n\n# PowerON commands fail in this case if there is no communication.\n## logging of this must be improved, added to ticket [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/G3IOT-1199|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/G3IOT-1199|smart-link] \n# Note that next open bat also fails {{rnd:Z72Gw6RM}} with error message: “{{hatchlock operation failed: communication fail}}“. This also indicates that there was no power in system.","2026-01-08T10:57:31.404Z"],["3795357","PFI-830931","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:712020:c9719acb-78c4-4bbc-b93d-e656e1839010] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-08T10:57:31.743Z"],["3795358","WFM-9846","WFM","alberto.vilasboas@bolt.eu","Alberto Vilas Boas","Helo Jose.\n\nI’m sorry to re-open this ticket. After reviewing the permissions the agents should not have access to these ones:\n\n*Emergency call config edit* ([emergency_call_config_edit|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-user/permissions/edit/1243])\n*Trip anomaly config: edit* ([trip_anomaly_config_edit|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-user/permissions/edit/301390])\n\nCan you please remove these accesses?\n\nThanks in advance!","2026-01-08T10:58:00.083Z"],["3795359","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Can we have an example of how it should look? I can’t see the image that you shared, as I don’t have access.  ","2026-01-08T10:58:05.387Z"],["3795364","WD-21984","WD","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska","Thank you so much.\n\n[~accountid:63fca2bdf00d095406f1fda7] could you please exclude extra not needed groups from the request file 🙏 ","2026-01-08T11:00:48.772Z"],["3795366","SUPX-2223","SUPX","michal.rapinczuk@bolt.eu","Michał Rapińczuk","[~accountid:712020:05337a38-da5a-4860-91ed-01ab7b7b6cca] to follow up with Beehive on the future of avatars in Beehive and possible support with implementation","2026-01-08T11:01:31.786Z"],["3795371","WFM-9888","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Hey [~accountid:61f7bc87aab3620070f324ce] please confirm that the role is needed for the agent, after that I’ll proceed with the request, thank you!","2026-01-08T11:02:48.665Z"],["3795379","RDS-1355","RDS","rishi.kar@bolt.eu","Rishi Raj Kar","[~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c]  would like to clarify the solution a bit. DriverX is a notification while RiderX is a snackbar, correct?\nDo you also envision updates to the active order screen? Also do we have templated text message in chat for these cases? ","2026-01-08T11:05:29.858Z"],["3795382","RS-1940","RS","vivien.antoniou@bolt.eu","Vivien Antoniou","[^Notice to Produce - Bolt - TFL KT71DWO.pdf] _(356 kB)_","2026-01-08T11:05:38.641Z"],["3795384","BDB-1500","BDB","liisi.tamra@bolt.eu","Liisi Tamra","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] I now got a new info from [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79]  that all three placements are in the same city, but at different venues. Just to make sure, are they at venues or train stations?\n","2026-01-08T11:06:22.638Z"],["3795389","SFLEET-140","SFLEET","charles.franca@bolt.eu","Charles França","[~accountid:712020:a1e1cc21-901c-43ed-b15e-7737d865bb5c] It looks awesome. Can we announce it already?","2026-01-08T11:07:44.793Z"],["3795391","LSS-57659","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:5ff3118b44065f013f974ef7]. \n\nCoverflex accepted our proposition for the 250k liability cap. So, on that part, everything is closed.\n\nThey just made an alteration regarding the rebate fee during and after the exclusivity period. Could you confirm if this is what was agreed?\n\n* 5% rebate on total monthly consumption exceeding 95k during the exclusivity period (that lasts until 31 March 2026, unless extended by the parties)\n* 4% rebate on total monthly consumption exceeding 95k after/outside the exclusivity period. (Meaning, after 31 March, if the exclusivity period is not extended, the applicable rate for 95k consumption will be 4% and if Coverflex breaches the exclusivity period, we will suspend the application of the 5% rate and apply 4%).","2026-01-08T11:07:54.904Z"],["3795395","PFI-830825","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:712020:517918d6-6e1c-4550-a162-bb39438a3c37] \n\nUnfortunately, there isn’t any proof that we are able to provide. \nOnce again confirming that the pre-authorization has been released from Bolt once the payment was captured. \n\n","2026-01-08T11:08:31.127Z"],["3795396","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","guglielmo.fontanarava@bolt.eu","Guglielmo Fontana-Rava Andreae","!image-20260108-110545.png|width=964,alt=\"image-20260108-110545.png\"!\n\n[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] something like this. Actually this same bike is a 24”. Its called Veloe, you can check the website ([https://veloe.eu/|https://veloe.eu/|smart-link] ).\nThe main concept is a rack with a flat seat, footrests and a cage. \nLater I can send you dimensions of this solution.","2026-01-08T11:08:37.362Z"],["3795398","PFI-813336","PFI","joseph.kamange@bolt-outsource.eu","Joseph Kamange","Please assist as payment is yet to be resolved. ","2026-01-08T11:09:16.972Z"],["3795400","RENT-205","RENT","guillermo.salceda@bolt.eu","Guillermo Salceda Pacheco","Hi [~accountid:712020:248d279a-85db-4438-8af9-d236e6e661d5] and [~accountid:6328384efedc6169aed38521], good afternoon.\n\nAccording to the information provided in the RFC attached and the explanation provided by Ping in yesterday’s meeting, this project does not seem to trigger any tax implications to be addressed by the tax team, as long as the invoice for the ride is issued as usual once it is finished. Anyway, if you think that we should take a look at any other tax-related question, please let us know.\n\nFor the time being, there’s no need to add any working hours for tax advice, but if you think we should add some hours, pls let us know as well.\n\nThanks, and have a nice day.\n\nc.c. [~accountid:62615f256cb53d006a6a3fe1] ","2026-01-08T11:10:03.446Z"],["3795403","PAW-14644","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-njsc-db, pint-product-backend-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-08T11:10:37.563Z"],["3795404","LSS-57659","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WOdGe61xIJgmZ9tzlPw-OU5WvQJdvcbZ/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WOdGe61xIJgmZ9tzlPw-OU5WvQJdvcbZ/edit|smart-link]","2026-01-08T11:10:38.207Z"],["3795405","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","guglielmo.fontanarava@bolt.eu","Guglielmo Fontana-Rava Andreae","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] This was the render you disnt have access to.\n\n\n!image-20260108-111026.png|width=720,alt=\"image-20260108-111026.png\"!","2026-01-08T11:10:50.537Z"],["3795408","SFLEET-199","SFLEET","charles.franca@bolt.eu","Charles França","[~accountid:712020:a1e1cc21-901c-43ed-b15e-7737d865bb5c] Great. This is a new version of the existing report. The only thing about it is the field Related Fleets? When it comes to the existing reports, what do I have to do to ensure that, when viewing KPI results of all fleets in a given list (including related fleets), I’ll be able to KPI results that encompass all covered fleets?","2026-01-08T11:11:07.501Z"],["3795409","PFI-830912","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:07cd480c-e6da-42c2-88d2-b601f4c40438],\n\nThis is the order in question: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1086557161/18?orderTryId=1399418103|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1086557161/18?orderTryId=1399418103]\nFrom what we can see, is that €29.80 was captured, however €9.3 is still unpaid.\nThis trip also most likely happened, as the duration of this order is 20+ minutes and the user has also left a 4/5 star rating to the driver.\nUser needs to settle this debt before deleting their profile.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-08T11:11:19.403Z"],["3795410","FRAUD-5735","FRAUD","jazib.sawar@bolt.eu","Jazib Sawar","Hi team, did rides or rides-pricing team communicated/aligned with us that they will stop calling {{ridehailing_driver_cancel_order_check}} checkpoint and implement [this rule|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/ridehailing_driver_cancel_order_check/DRIVER_CANCEL_ORDER_SKIP_DRIVER_FAR_AWAY?tab=script&scriptTab=script_view] logic on their end?\n\nThey have already merged this [PR|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159751/files] where they hardcoded the logic for Taiwan. This doesn't look right to me.\n\ncc: *group-S04D3AXC8QZ*","2026-01-08T11:11:38.077Z"],["3795411","FRAUD-5735","FRAUD",null,"Slack","[Jazib Sawar|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:6765abfb-c8e8-45e1-903e-e8b034dedaa8] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02PPBVUL56/p1767779651916959?thread_ts=1767779651.916959&cid=C02PPBVUL56|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02PPBVUL56/p1767779651916959?thread_ts=1767779651.916959&cid=C02PPBVUL56|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-08T11:11:38.982Z"],["3795412","LSS-61251","LSS","lisette.suik@bolt.eu","Lisette Suik","hei [~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2] -  seems like an Ads topic, re-assigned to you! ","2026-01-08T11:11:39.689Z"],["3795413","FRAUD-5735","FRAUD","jazib.sawar@bolt.eu","Jazib Sawar","Another issue, [@andre.tamm|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:e5386bed-3f86-4ef8-8665-6b54b5104b9d] posted the screenshot of the rule logic in the [PR|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159751]. He doesn't have permission to view or edit the rule. Did we share the rule logic with them?\n\nHowever, we’ve given edit permissions to {{RiderX QA}} role, which means they can view and edit all ride-hailing checkpoint rules. Is this intentional?\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7MV36SJV/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7MV36SJV/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-08T11:11:39.738Z"],["3795414","FRAUD-5735","FRAUD","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","Heya, yes, we did have a discussion on it and shared the logic. It was decided this is more their domain than ours but let me double-check where the conversations stopped...","2026-01-08T11:11:40.597Z"],["3795415","FRAUD-5735","FRAUD","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","Okay, so he discussion we had was here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0198U3PE8J/p1763033833741729?thread_ts=1762781163.530919&cid=C0198U3PE8J|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0198U3PE8J/p1763033833741729?thread_ts=1762781163.530919&cid=C0198U3PE8J|smart-link]\n\nBut we had no clarification on the timelines etc. [@guilherme.franciulli|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ce7b2073f4d610fdf029c16] Did you happen to talk with them meanwhile? Am I missing a portion of the convo? :smile:\n\n[@jazib.sawar|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:6765abfb-c8e8-45e1-903e-e8b034dedaa8] Kudos for noticing! :flower4u: Question, did they stop calling the checkpoint altogether? Like checkpoint is not working anymore?","2026-01-08T11:11:41.375Z"],["3795416","FRAUD-5735","FRAUD","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","there's this other [thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0198U3PE8J/p1765784151385129?thread_ts=1765440855.076959&cid=C0198U3PE8J], which is more recent. but other than that, nothing else. think it was already agreed on the call we had with him. but yea, wouldn't hurt for them to send us a heads-up that was implemented.","2026-01-08T11:11:42.105Z"],["3795417","FRAUD-5735","FRAUD","jazib.sawar@bolt.eu","Jazib Sawar","{quote}<@U0528F1FG7K{quote}\n\n> Kudos for noticing! :flower4u: Question, did they stop calling the checkpoint altogether? Like checkpoint is not working anymore?\nNot yet. There is another PR for review where they will stop calling fraud","2026-01-08T11:11:42.773Z"],["3795418","FRAUD-5735","FRAUD","jazib.sawar@bolt.eu","Jazib Sawar","[@guilherme.franciulli|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ce7b2073f4d610fdf029c16] [@lise.vaher|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5cefa65be2e3ec0fc196de31] I'm going to approve their PR and after deployment, they will stop calling {{ridehailing_driver_cancel_order_check}} checkpoint.\n\nAny concerns? I'll create separate adhoc task to delete this checkpoint from our codebase :killitwithfire:","2026-01-08T11:11:43.493Z"],["3795419","FRAUD-5735","FRAUD","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","No concerns on my side, we can proceed :+1:","2026-01-08T11:11:44.051Z"],["3795420","FRAUD-5735","FRAUD",null,"Slack","[Jazib Sawar|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:6765abfb-c8e8-45e1-903e-e8b034dedaa8] unsynced this conversation thread from the Slack thread - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02PPBVUL56/p1767779651916959|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02PPBVUL56/p1767779651916959|smart-link]. Future replies will no longer sync or update across Slack and Jira.","2026-01-08T11:11:57.388Z"],["3795422","WFM-9894","WFM","mihaela.pahontu@bolt-outsource.eu","Mihaela Pahontu","Title: Vreme nefavorabila","2026-01-08T11:12:19.079Z"],["3795424","SFLEET-196","SFLEET","charles.franca@bolt.eu","Charles França","[~accountid:712020:a1e1cc21-901c-43ed-b15e-7737d865bb5c] Does it mean that, for all metrics, when a period ends (week, month, quarter, etc), we’ll “freeze” their results so they won’t change in the future?","2026-01-08T11:12:57.104Z"],["3795425","WFM-9889","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571633|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571633]","2026-01-08T11:12:59.906Z"],["3795426","PFI-808451","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1767869808850709?thread_ts=1762264495.696189&cid=C02C2SY0MHT|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1767869808850709?thread_ts=1762264495.696189&cid=C02C2SY0MHT]","2026-01-08T11:13:03.251Z"],["3795427","LSS-61241","LSS","joao.ramos@bolt.eu","João Nuno Ferreira Ramos","Hey! \n\nThe driver was warned several times regarding safety issues, until his termination.\n\nYou can check the attached emails.\n\nBoth driver and fo were informed.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.09.47.png|width=926,height=520,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.09.47.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.10.36.png|width=953,height=567,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.10.36.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.10.18.png|width=575,height=552,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.10.18.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.10.29.png|width=903,height=569,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.10.29.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.10.12.png|width=846,height=661,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.10.12.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-08T11:13:11.779Z"],["3795429","WFM-9894","WFM","mihaela.pahontu@bolt-outsource.eu","Mihaela Pahontu","* Din cauza condițiilor meteo nefavorabile, pot apărea întârzieri la livrarea comenzilor. Vă mulțumim pentru înțelegere!                                                                                                                  english- Due to unfavorable weather conditions, delivery of orders may be delayed. Thank you for your understanding.       \n\n","2026-01-08T11:13:22.918Z"],["3795430","LSS-61236","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! I have viewed all the contract types and made sure that Bolt Poland has been added to all. Furthermore I have updated Bolt Business Special Terms template and replaced Bolt Rides PL with Bolt Poland PL. Please let me know if anything else is needed from our side. ","2026-01-08T11:13:38.498Z"],["3795431","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:63abfbf7159df2c252e762e5] Alright, if you have dimensions that would be nice. ","2026-01-08T11:13:44.749Z"],["3795432","L10N-26501","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26492](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26492)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T11:13:48.342Z"],["3795433","L10N-26496","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26492](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26492)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T11:13:50.021Z"],["3795434","L10N-26499","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26492](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26492)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T11:13:50.676Z"],["3795435","L10N-26506","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All li