enshot 2026-01-08 at 13.09.17.png|width=657,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.09.17.png\"!\n\n!Screen Recording 2026-01-08 at 13.13.34.mov|width=657,alt=\"Screen Recording 2026-01-08 at 13.13.34.mov\"!","2026-01-08T11:14:35.549Z"],["3795451","WFM-9900","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601582","2026-01-08T11:14:36.933Z"],["3795452","L10N-26525","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26492](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26492)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T11:14:41.575Z"],["3795453","LSS-59690","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Documents have been prepared for delivery and shipped, shipment tracking code attached: [https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=2551794206&submit=1|https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=2551794206&submit=1|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T11:14:42.077Z"],["3795455","WFM-9894","WFM","mihaela.pahontu@bolt-outsource.eu","Mihaela Pahontu","end of date can be EOD today, as the weather seems good starting tomorrow, tx\n\n","2026-01-08T11:15:01.165Z"],["3795456","PFI-823507","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi,\n\nif it was a bonus for campaign - please raise with campaign team.\n\nif it was a compensation/manual adjustment - please raise with local ops.\n\nask these teams what is the status of bonus/compensation in their systems.","2026-01-08T11:15:13.282Z"],["3795459","PFI-823507","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-08T11:15:45.810Z"],["3795464","LSS-61264","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-08T11:16:42.796Z"],["3795466","WFM-9896","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571634","2026-01-08T11:17:16.612Z"],["3795467","PFI-830906","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:92de8b35-6a42-4290-a24d-a4656c69eaa7],\n\nAs this is an on-going issue with this given user, then we will be permanently blocking them from the platform.\nIt also seems that they are clever enough to use the cash payment methods to dodge the cancellation fee.\nAdditionally, the user does not have a verified e-mail, so whatever the general intentions of this user are, they are most likely fraudulent.\nThis user will no longer will be able to make requests on our platform.\nThank you for escalating this user.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-08T11:17:43.996Z"],["3795468","PFI-820827","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","it was for this order:\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2284621781/350?orderTryId=2913265280|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2284621781/350?orderTryId=2913265280]\n\nit was detected as a fraud","2026-01-08T11:17:55.567Z"],["3795469","CMO-12988","CMO","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","07.01 - preliminary format check\n08.01\nMessage posted to IH TLs - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C090LLBEEBC/p1767870859305129|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C090LLBEEBC/p1767870859305129|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T11:18:07.690Z"],["3795473","DSR-3069","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","Draft response for [~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60] approval: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_h6op5WhobVsZwt3PURy_y-9N0zZYGRXL7Dorx0NclM/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_h6op5WhobVsZwt3PURy_y-9N0zZYGRXL7Dorx0NclM/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T11:18:30.172Z"],["3795475","MICRO-29","MICRO","tom.evans@bolt.eu","Tom Evans","[~accountid:712020:248d279a-85db-4438-8af9-d236e6e661d5] we are pushing to have the map view (phase II) developed by Berlin launch, not just compass that we currently have. We want to collect feedback as well as do user research to help guide phase III and improve phase II","2026-01-08T11:19:07.767Z"],["3795477","CSDA-284","CSDA","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Hi, Jose! Please find the data for November [*here*|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LNL1ErGIHB8of3O1nf6apQXWw1vR7pgud6GozBGm15I/edit?gid=0#gid=0]. The list contains all support cases raised by authority user persona, but which haven’t reached cs_privacy_compliance tier. Let me know if you have any further questions! ","2026-01-08T11:19:27.491Z"],["3795478","DRX-27934","DRX","kirill.chuyanov@bolt.eu","Kirill Chuyanov","QA: The changes affect only the Home screen - when a driver is offline and when online and waiting for orders\n Main features to test:\n\n* All buttons on the home screen work - nothing extra appreas, nothing overlaps\n* Matching to the destination works as before - the banner indicates that only orders towards the destination will be matched.\n* Working time works as before","2026-01-08T11:19:32.390Z"],["3795479","MLC-2769","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*26W2 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** Handed the launch over to Nida.\n** Katarina Saage opened a [ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-58813] to privacy team to check any restrictions on engaging with users at launch (existing micromobility users + users with Italian phone numbers in other countries). Wrote an update there to clarify questions on the country code/targeting logic & calculated the [segment|https://dashboard-02.braze.eu/engagement/segmenter/695d0d3bc9747cb849b346e4/660bb12b05810f0061db0f3c?locale=en] of users with Italian phone numbers who aren’t in Italy (128k). However I mentioned that we haven’t sent launch comms to users outside of the launch country in the past and this would need further discussion within the team before we proceed. Handed over to Nida to discuss with Cristina by EOW. \n* *Next steps:*\n** Setting up the comms (Nida to fill in any future progress)","2026-01-08T11:19:33.701Z"],["3795480","WFM-9899","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","[~accountid:61268a40129802006ae93f05] the agent already has a Beehive CS Agent role, CS - Rides - OPS Pilot (360158) is related to an Ops project of some sort according to the role description","2026-01-08T11:19:40.433Z"],["3795481","PRF-1249","PRF","beste.dulger@bolt.eu","Beste Dülger","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/5wEotAE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/5wEotAE|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T11:19:46.230Z"],["3795483","DRX-27973","DRX","ajinkya.deshmukh@bolt.eu","Ajinkya Suhas Deshmukh","Tested UK Partner Benefits Banner on DI and DA - \n\nAlso checked the banner disappears after enrolment.\n\n!UKPartnerBenefitsR.mp4|width=320,alt=\"UKPartnerBenefitsR.mp4\"!","2026-01-08T11:19:51.314Z"],["3795484","PFI-830939","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T11:19:52.115Z"],["3795488","DSR-3587","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-08T11:21:07.680Z"],["3795489","DSR-3009","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], yes it’s possible I’ll de-escalate the case. \n\nYou’re right, this is the [ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719534395]. Thanks!","2026-01-08T11:21:46.542Z"],["3795492","PFI-830940","PFI","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.19.34.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T11:22:51.181Z"],["3795493","MTE-1160","MTE","anton.hmelnitski@bolt.eu","Anton Hmelnitski","Let’s add this to Canvas service only","2026-01-08T11:22:51.887Z"],["3795494","PFI-830940","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T11:22:53.390Z"],["3795496","PFI-826351","PFI","darja.rojenko@bolt-outsource.eu","Darja Rojenko","issue resolved ","2026-01-08T11:23:07.768Z"],["3795497","PFI-813982","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey\nsounds okay.","2026-01-08T11:23:19.533Z"],["3795498","LSS-60050","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] !\n\nAdobe says that \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.56.37.png|width=417,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.56.37.png\"!\n\nSo I would recommend to sign via Dokobit from the Counterparty’s side too.\n\nAs for the file: I have sent it to Ahto for signing: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/339840|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/339840|smart-link]  ","2026-01-08T11:23:21.551Z"],["3795500","LSS-61168","LSS","nikola.spoustova@bolt.eu","Nikola Spoustová","Hello @Giulia Zanotto,\n\nWe don’t have a previous case we could share as an example at the moment—at least not one we’ve saved with an ID. Additionally, it’s not possible to search for historical cases in Beehive, so locating a suitable example wouldn’t be feasible anyway.\n\nWhether a courier should strictly follow customer notes is an ongoing topic. We’ve discussed this multiple times with our OPS team and confirmed that the correct approach is to recommend that couriers follow customer notes, but we cannot enforce this. Doing so would risk bordering on co-employment, which is not permitted in the CZ market. According to our T&Cs, couriers are obligated to deliver the order to the specified address, meaning delivery to the building entrance is sufficient—they are not required to deliver to, for example, the 13th floor, and we cannot mandate this.\n\nIn this specific case, the customer did not come downstairs. Based on the FAQ _“_[_The customer is not here_|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/public/453769098799]_,”_ the courier acted correctly by disposing of the order, as it contained age-restricted items.\n\nUnfortunately, there is no explicit KB article or formal statement covering this scenario. However, based on guidance from our OPS team and our T&Cs, this approach should be considered compliant and appropriate.","2026-01-08T11:23:45.805Z"],["3795503","WFM-9890","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571635\r\n\r\nrequesting Business role ","2026-01-08T11:24:09.405Z"],["3795508","RDS-1291","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] This also means [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDS-1302|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDS-1302|smart-link] is a prerequisite?","2026-01-08T11:24:56.679Z"],["3795510","WFM-9896","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Hey [~accountid:712020:a4969d25-8e58-49a1-a0b4-179bb77e9ff8], access granted, should be working now!","2026-01-08T11:25:33.548Z"],["3795511","EBIKE1-372","EBIKE1","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","I will close this task for now, the reflector is chosen and test fitted successfully (/) ","2026-01-08T11:25:45.217Z"],["3795513","WFM-9889","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Hey [~accountid:712020:a4969d25-8e58-49a1-a0b4-179bb77e9ff8], the appropriate role was added!","2026-01-08T11:26:30.179Z"],["3795514","LSS-61156","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hey, [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432]! The resolution and consent are now ready, the Google Doc files linked before were updated and I also attach the .pdf versions. As discussed before the signing will happen on 19th of January in Tallinn. Please scan the signed documents once they are ready and add them to this ticket. Also, please retain the original documents and obtain copies of passports and an extract regarding Bolt Holdings to be ready to send out to Georgia. All documents need to be certified and have an apostille to be used in Georgia.\n\n\n\n[^2026.01 ENG_Consent and Power of Attorney of the Director_Bolt Services GE.pdf]\n[^2026.01 ENG_Resolution_Bolt Holdings OÜ.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T11:26:34.168Z"],["3795515","FDBT-4757","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-08T11:26:48.802Z"],["3795516","LSS-60553","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:7ebf1982-dd36-43fb-a386-42b4b1ee6b59] !\n\nYes, that’s correct – we can share the signed PDF with the contractor directly (e.g. via email).\n\nMahmoud’s signature will remain valid even if the contractor later uploads the same PDF into their system to countersign the notice. This is a common practice, and the order of signatures or the upload itself does not invalidate an already applied signature.\n\nSo from our side, everything is fine.","2026-01-08T11:26:56.668Z"],["3795517","WFM-9900","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Hey [~accountid:712020:a4969d25-8e58-49a1-a0b4-179bb77e9ff8], the appropriate role was granted!","2026-01-08T11:27:18.989Z"],["3795518","PFI-735118","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, apologies for delay. The priority on the ticket has been increased and escalated further with engineering team.\n\nI will provide a further update as soon as we have a root cause and resolution for the bug.","2026-01-08T11:27:29.022Z"],["3795519","WD-22502","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi! Custom validation is updated : Prepaid Withholding tax (BS) is added as allowed spend category for acc 1306","2026-01-08T11:27:44.256Z"],["3795524","LSS-59913","LSS","jake.murphy@bolt.eu","Jake Murphy","Hi - So turns out Mimica can’t support Mac (wish they told me earlier!) but they are releasing this in March and have offered the Free PoC in April so keen to explore in Q2\n\nI’ve downloaded their trust centre docs and info needed to review - Mimica have also offered to have a call with their InfoSec team later in the quarter to field any open questions we have before green lighting any PoC in Q2\n\n\n[^Trust Center Resources.zip]\n\n","2026-01-08T11:28:14.480Z"],["3795526","MTE-1298","MTE","anton.hmelnitski@bolt.eu","Anton Hmelnitski","Just a note – we should also resolve correct user profiles for each domain","2026-01-08T11:28:19.477Z"],["3795531","RDS-1173","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] Thanks! [~accountid:712020:d2a0e53f-83a4-4e81-aebd-74db6f57d6fa] for the situation described by Dash here: I assume this impacts the drivers AR, having to cancel incoming orders to finish the current ride?","2026-01-08T11:29:11.194Z"],["3795532","PFI-830912","PFI","ibrahima.diop@bolt-outsource.eu","Ibrahima Diop","Hello Marten,\n\nThank your for the quick reply. \n\nI unfortunately do not have access to that order as it seems to be related to a country other than the one I support.\n\nThank you for the information. \n\nBest regards,\nIbrahim","2026-01-08T11:29:18.818Z"],["3795533","WFM-9894","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Thank you [~accountid:712020:207c95ff-c39e-492c-9c31-f804f0b6bb8a] , please provide the English text as well as it’s needed for the comms","2026-01-08T11:29:25.969Z"],["3795535","WD-22459","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Hi there, please can you check if you are able to enter your time now","2026-01-08T11:29:52.335Z"],["3795536","LSS-61156","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] ! \n\nThank you, received.\n\nI’ll forward everything to the notary. Please note that the signing will take place on *20 January at 9:50* (not on the 19th), so I guess we need to change the date in the documents.\n\nOnce the documents are signed, I’ll scan them and add the copies to this ticket. We’ll also retain the originals and make sure that the certified copies, passports, and the extract regarding Bolt Holdings are prepared for apostille and submission to Georgia.\n\nBest,\nAleksandra","2026-01-08T11:30:07.824Z"],["3795537","WD-22480","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Hi there, please can you check if you are able to enter your time now","2026-01-08T11:30:08.817Z"],["3795538","DSR-3490","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","* PDE export (*excluding* *_Communications_*) started [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/personal-data-export/exports/1206850?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]\n* Contacted Sweden SIS regarding the validity of the suspension. Second report under same group of category - block applied is correct\n* Driver offers off-platform journey report [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/699622188] - redacted tickets [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/18FCAoC4NsjET5iOcudiFM8tEAo1MMZYk]\n* Response letter [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/18UY_4WhggXKtK3eEmFhgzTgOtjqxb0GNjIOxxdvCBr4/edit?tab=t.0]\n* Average rating, acceptance rate added in the folder [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/15I_tlKrlZL0n76s5_B0d5Vn1APxpknuk]. Fleet driver, no call recordings.","2026-01-08T11:30:21.482Z"],["3795539","WD-22474","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","the ticket was solved via Slack DM","2026-01-08T11:30:49.841Z"],["3795542","PFI-830086","PFI","angela.gray@bolt.eu","Angela Gray","Hi Team, Thanks for the information. I have been able to download all invoices from the start date in 2022.  Please close 🙏 ","2026-01-08T11:31:27.521Z"],["3795543","DAEN-1249","DAEN","ielizaveta.rotgauz@bolt.eu","Liza Rotgauz","From [~accountid:5cefc04f0927e30f265e0d1f] \n\n\nI’ve checked the added metrics to the {{dbt_pedro_paiva_spark.mart_universal_test_segment_city_month_utc_rides}}, and have some comments:\n\n* rides_universal_test_count_active_users_utc - this is probably sum from control and treatment? please remove this since we do not care in additive totals from test+control, and this might frankly confuse even the users of the mart. Do the same for:\n** rides_universal_test_rides_per_active_user_utc\n** rides_universal_test_rides_per_enrolled_user_utc\n* please add normalised versions for the following (but also keep current, non-normalised):\n** rides_universal_test_count_active_users_control_utc\n** rides_universal_test_count_active_users_treatment_utc\n* Add fnished ride count metrics following the guideline above:\n** only treatment and contro separatelyl, no sum\n** normalised as well\n** total of 4 new metrics","2026-01-08T11:31:29.298Z"],["3795544","WFM-9897","WFM","michael.wanjiku@bolt-outsource.eu","Michael Wanjiku","Hello [~accountid:61268a40129802006ae93f05] \n\nThank you for the response and assistance as well. I, however, still have my view as shown in the attached image…\nCould you kindly advise me on the way forward?\n\n!image-20260108-113122.png|width=527,height=536,alt=\"image-20260108-113122.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-08T11:31:38.491Z"],["3795546","LSS-54833","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:2f68ebec-bff7-4acf-a855-0eeaf1c88737] ! [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] supports with this agreement as it’s Bolt Business related project ","2026-01-08T11:32:08.933Z"],["3795549","PFI-809183","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nbased on these records: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records?recordFilter={\"handling_timestamp_from\"%3A1761951600%2C\"handling_timestamp_to\"%3A1762038000%2C\"use_handling_timestamp\"%3Atrue%2C\"from_agent_type\"%3A\"driver\"%2C\"from_agent_id\"%3A5496278%2C\"agent_filter_operator\"%3A\"OR\"%2C\"to_agent_type\"%3A\"driver\"%2C\"to_agent_id\"%3A5496278%2C\"type\"%3Anull%2C\"order_id\"%3A2234193075}&page={\"limit\"%3A100%2C\"offset\"%3A0}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records?recordFilter=%7B%22handling_timestamp_from%22%3A1761951600%2C%22handling_timestamp_to%22%3A1762038000%2C%22use_handling_timestamp%22%3Atrue%2C%22from_agent_type%22%3A%22driver%22%2C%22from_agent_id%22%3A5496278%2C%22agent_filter_operator%22%3A%22OR%22%2C%22to_agent_type%22%3A%22driver%22%2C%22to_agent_id%22%3A5496278%2C%22type%22%3Anull%2C%22order_id%22%3A2234193075%7D&page=%7B%22limit%22%3A100%2C%22offset%22%3A0%7D]\n\nI see that we compensated the full amount and did not charge the commission for this ride. So net for this ride is 0, not -23.33\n\nIf user sees -23.33 - this is not correct. Billing team does not control this view - we provide data for this view.","2026-01-08T11:32:33.350Z"],["3795550","WFM-9884","WFM","ana.radmilo@bolt.eu","Ana Radmilo","Hi!\n\nYou can add them playmode, even though I can see that the in-house agents have this role: Rides - Driver Reg Processing via BH - Agent, Play + Backlog.","2026-01-08T11:32:36.620Z"],["3795553","PFI-820827","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-08T11:33:07.047Z"],["3795554","LSS-57383","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","EU payments license channel  - Lisanna Lomp discusses how to update CS processes to get license. \n\nLisanna’s question: since she is creating anw internal processes for CS then can she include AW requirements already there. ","2026-01-08T11:33:17.335Z"],["3795555","PFI-820831","PFI","aida.nikunlassi@bolt-outsource.eu","Aida Nikunlassi","Yes but the riders invoices aren’t coming to their email address although it is correct in their Admin. How are we fixing that issue?","2026-01-08T11:33:18.643Z"],["3795557","LSS-60600","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:b75759f0-ea50-4319-bfe5-48b28f4cab21] - happy new year! Yes, approving the pilot based on my requirements mentioned below:\n\n{quote}# _The dataset is limited to the currently proposed_ *_basic employee demographics_* _only;_\n# _The data is_ *_pseudonymised_*_, meaning the Data Platform team cannot technically link Workday Worker IDs to directly identifying attributes (e.g. name, surname, email); and_\n# _Access remains_ *_restricted to the People Analytics and Data Platform teams_* _as described._Thank you.{quote}\n\nPlease let me know once the Pilot is up and running — towards the end of January we can pick up a discussion to review the setup, access controls, permissions, monitoring and any other ‘privacy-enhancing-technologies’ for a future ‘Live’ setup. ","2026-01-08T11:33:47.952Z"],["3795558","CCM-22261","CCM","david.tomes@bolt.eu","David Tomeš","Hi Irena,\n\nthanks. This has been fixed, we’re ready.\n\nDavid","2026-01-08T11:33:49.026Z"],["3795559","LSS-61254","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] this seems to be more your field - please assist. Thanks ","2026-01-08T11:33:50.296Z"],["3795562","PFI-820831","PFI","aida.nikunlassi@bolt-outsource.eu","Aida Nikunlassi","And also what is happening with the payment/why it showed as cancelled?","2026-01-08T11:34:31.652Z"],["3795563","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","One is outside a shopping mall\nOne is at a train station\nOne is at a bus station","2026-01-08T11:34:49.446Z"],["3795564","WD-22517","WD","peggy.dano@bolt.eu","Peggy Stefany Dano","[^202501-202505 P9.zip]\n\n[^2026 KE P9 Jan-May.xlsx]","2026-01-08T11:35:05.579Z"],["3795569","FX-3557","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767872135505939]*{color}:\nIll try to find all the vehicles that we can clean up. As we never delete rows in DB itself, I guess we will do a delete from admin, BUT this means they are still visible in fleet portal for example as deactivated vehicle\n{quote}","2026-01-08T11:35:50.341Z"],["3795570","LSS-54833","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:2f68ebec-bff7-4acf-a855-0eeaf1c88737]! Yes, no problem - I’ll review this in the course of next week! ","2026-01-08T11:35:52.436Z"],["3795572","PFI-830912","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi,\n\nDetails of the order:\nCity: Paris, France\nCategory: Bolt - Paris - CDG\nPayment method: Googlepay\n\nFinal price of the trip: 39.10€\n€29.80 was captured.\n€9.3 is still unpaid.\nSeems to have been an airport trip.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.35.07.png|width=502,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.35.07.png\"!\n\nDo let me know if any other information is required.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-08T11:36:05.085Z"],["3795574","LSS-61254","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:60fa95ef411fae0070ad24fe] the Privacy team member who can assist with this is out of office and will revert on his return next week. ","2026-01-08T11:36:19.049Z"],["3795577","LSS-61265","LSS","aleksejs.batenko@bolt.eu","Aleksejs Batenko","[^Amserv 2026 Q1 cars returns.docx] _(297 kB)_","2026-01-08T11:37:36.295Z"],["3795579","SREDESK-7387","SREDESK","mehran.eftekhari@bolt.eu","Shahriar Eftekhari","https://monitor.boltint.net/d/000000038/redis3a-overview?orgId=1&var-alias=driverx-mqtt-broker-mq-africa&var-role=master&var-instance=All&var-job=All&var-datasource=P6BB142EF7CA4BDF6&var-cmd=All&from=now-3h&to=now\r\n\r\nhttps://monitor.boltint.net/d/000000038/redis3a-overview?orgId=1&var-alias=driverx-mqtt-broker-mq-europe&var-role=master&var-instance=All&var-job=All&var-datasource=P6BB142EF7CA4BDF6&var-cmd=All&from=now-3h&to=now\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://monitor.boltint.net/d/000000038/redis3a-overview?orgId=1&var-alias=driverx-mqtt-broker-mq-westasia&var-role=master&var-instance=All&var-job=All&var-datasource=P6BB142EF7CA4BDF6&var-cmd=All&from=now-3h&to=now\r\n\r\n\r\n3 new mq redises are up and running.","2026-01-08T11:37:54.783Z"],["3795580","DSR-2999","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:6001a723d364960139286c95], could you please send the [answer letter|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1X2PMm-3SmoKPJNNuvBjycrvqbMMubwPazdBDAe_UrqI/edit?usp=drive_link] and the PDE to the user?","2026-01-08T11:38:01.622Z"],["3795585","PFI-830703","PFI","wisdom.salaou@bolt-outsource.eu","Wisdom Delphine Salaou","Hello  the proof of payment was sent to the driver, and he contacted his bank, which provided him  proof of non-receipt of funds\n\ncan you please check","2026-01-08T11:39:43.857Z"],["3795588","LSS-61155","LSS","aleksejs.batenko@bolt.eu","Aleksejs Batenko","Hello, \n\nAny update on this agreement, please? ","2026-01-08T11:40:38.799Z"],["3795589","WFM-9898","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, queue assigned","2026-01-08T11:40:45.389Z"],["3795590","LSS-61266","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^TEMPLATE Fleet European Frame Agreement - UPDATED SEPT25.docx] _(60 kB)_","2026-01-08T11:41:08.802Z"],["3795592","RDS-1177","RDS","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","archiving and keeping clone, see linked ticket","2026-01-08T11:41:32.389Z"],["3795593","AIOT-588","AIOT","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[https://eshop.wuerth.ee/Universal-waterproofing-spray-IMPREGSPR-UNIVERSAL-400ML/0893[…]CsFu0000zV81Ha5G;sid=gTqHRo2O8xa_RuTRFpwLTX2E72XBbOPRxxB-htqN|https://eshop.wuerth.ee/Universal-waterproofing-spray-IMPREGSPR-UNIVERSAL-400ML/0893032100.sku/en/US/EUR/;pgid=JDzqY8ShT7_343FUCu.lCsFu0000zV81Ha5G;sid=gTqHRo2O8xa_RuTRFpwLTX2E72XBbOPRxxB-htqN]\n\nI can try this one. If it works, it would be easy to get it locally.","2026-01-08T11:41:36.058Z"],["3795594","LSS-54291","LSS","viktor.skalivskyi@bolt.eu","Viktor Skalivskyi","Hi! \nI will be meeting with them on Monday 12/01. I have passed on all your comments regarding their concerns. I will get back to you on Monday with an update.\n\n[~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] [~accountid:712020:d6cadc67-55ba-4993-9498-9fb9531798c5] ","2026-01-08T11:41:59.144Z"],["3795595","LSS-60462","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/339852|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/339852|smart-link]  ","2026-01-08T11:42:27.619Z"],["3795596","HS-28689","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hi [~accountid:6102799bc51f3a0069a7b43a] !\n\nThe best solution would be to agree with your line manager that you either leave after half a day or start later, and use that half day to rest. Unfortunately, I believe Workday does not currently allow requesting half-day leave (you can try, as there may have been changes, but I’m not certain this is possible). In that case, you can contact our tech team to inform them that you have used a half day, and they should be able to adjust your balance accordingly.\n\nIf you need any clarification or further assistance on this topic, please feel free to reach out to me on Slack.\n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-08T11:42:53.258Z"],["3795597","HS-28738","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Richmond, I have added [~accountid:6271326a2db3080070241cfa] here. She should be able to help. ","2026-01-08T11:42:57.691Z"],["3795598","LSS-61009","LSS","teodor.rachev@bolt.eu","Teodor Rachev","Hey [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2]! Please, once possible, can you provide a legal review (if you think it is needed) of the Letter for Road Safety + amendments.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bcD8mRlBmOBl9zpLaytkA0vzFZIW029R/edit#heading=h.gjdgxs|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bcD8mRlBmOBl9zpLaytkA0vzFZIW029R/edit#heading=h.gjdgxs|smart-link] \n\n\n\nWe are currently in a hurry to provide feedback with comments and proposals from operators' perspective. Currently, there is no differentiation with private scooters. The letter is based on the draft regulation- EN version attached by Sorina. \nThank you! \nTeodor ","2026-01-08T11:43:08.178Z"],["3795604","LSS-59866","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Fleet Agreement - Aceleragora_encrypted_ (1).pdf] ","2026-01-08T11:45:16.150Z"],["3795605","LSS-61268","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter ABB (Bolt Services AZ LLC).docx] _(2.79 MB)_","2026-01-08T11:45:28.701Z"],["3795607","FX-3557","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767872737497309]*{color}:\n'we never delete' - as in we can't? or we won't?\n{quote}","2026-01-08T11:45:50.958Z"],["3795609","DRAG-695","DRAG","norman.tamm@bolt.eu","Norman Tamm","h1. Dekasyl MS-2 passed the IPx7 and modified IPx7 tests.\n\nh2. Gluing process\n\nBefore gluing, both the inside of the blowmold and the top plastic were cleaned with Dinitrol 582. After cleaning, the BMS wire opening and the humidity vent hole were sealed with tape. Water-reactive tape was applied to the inside of the blowmold.\n\nThe glue was applied as shown in the picture. Since Dekasyl MS-2 is a high-viscosity glue, it did not flow easily. After application, the glue was smoothed using a finger to ensure that all crevices were fully filled.\n\nThe glue cured for 48 h. After 24 h, the glue had settled but remained slightly sticky when touched. I suggest that after 24 h the blowmold can be transported, but should not be deployed to the field until the full 48 h has passed.\n\n!20260108_122406.jpg|width=181,alt=\"20260108_122406.jpg\"!\n\nh2. IPx7 test\n\nThe glued blowmold was submerged in water so that the uppermost surface of the blowmold was 1 m below the water surface for 30 min.\n\nAfter 30 min, the blowmold was removed form the water and opened. No water or moisture was inside the blowmold, and the water reactive tape had not reacted.\n\nh2. IPx7 modified test\n\nThe modified IPx7 test was conducted under the same conditions as the IPx7 test, with the exception that the blowmold remained submerged for 24 h instead of 30 min.\n\nAfter 24 h, the blowmold was removed form the water and opened. No water or moisture was inside the blowmold, and the water reactive tape had not reacted\n\nh2. Conclusion\n\nDekasyl MS-2 passed the IPx7 and modified IPx7 tests. \nBefore passing the test the test failed several times due to issues in the gluing process. It is critical to ensure that the glue forms a continuous seal with no gaps or voids, and that the gluing procedure is followed precisely.\n\nIt should also be noted that under normal repair conditions, the humidity vent hole will not be glued and BMS wires will be present.","2026-01-08T11:46:08.928Z"],["3795611","PFI-826032","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","!c25358d3a5ad4bf9acd640b8b07083b5e07ff3d9becdc8454ee4e2652fa750c5.png|width=1185,height=190!\n\ni see that in balance history it is just 1 refund for 33 pln. it might have been a temp bug. now should be fixed.\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/balanceHistory?balanceHistoryFilterSearch={\"external_id\"%3A7563149%2C\"type\"%3A\"Driver\"%2C\"month\"%3A{\"month\"%3A10%2C\"year\"%3A2025}%2C\"viewType\"%3A\"monthly\"%2C\"week\"%3A{\"start\"%3A1768168800000%2C\"end\"%3A1768773599999}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/balanceHistory?balanceHistoryFilterSearch=%7B%22external_id%22%3A7563149%2C%22type%22%3A%22Driver%22%2C%22month%22%3A%7B%22month%22%3A10%2C%22year%22%3A2025%7D%2C%22viewType%22%3A%22monthly%22%2C%22week%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1768168800000%2C%22end%22%3A1768773599999%7D%7D]","2026-01-08T11:47:15.663Z"],["3795614","LSS-60050","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","edited:\n\nthanks, [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ! Does it mean that the problem is on the counterparty’s side or ours? The Adobe says that _it is not included in our list of trusted certificate._ this suggests that we don’t have a full list even if this is a qualified signature?\n\n[~accountid:61debf39e67ea2006b3a1cb5] please ask them if they can explain why we cannot verify their signature as it should have been signed off with qualified e-signature. If they have any problem with the signature they can sign it by Dokobit (also qualified e-signature) -we would send them a relevant link for signing via Dokobit. This is urgent. \n\nThanks!","2026-01-08T11:47:42.781Z"],["3795615","LSS-59668","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:26fa69f3-15e6-46ce-91ea-ece8964d0490] !\n\nSince there has been no activity on this ticket for 30 days, I will need to close it soon.\n\nThe contract will still be available for signing – you can simply reopen the ticket at any time.","2026-01-08T11:47:48.596Z"],["3795617","WEBSD-1313","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:4305a8c1-0495-4265-b6e0-ae34aff86b22] 👋 \n\nI added the localised images related to *Road Tax Renewal Guide* ✅ \n\n\n\nI have a question related to *Scenarios section*.\n\nIs this a new section so we can remove 2 type of cancellation?\n\nPlease let me know so I can consider otherwise all should be done and added from my part.","2026-01-08T11:48:00.638Z"],["3795619","LSS-61269","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter Papaya Global Ltd (Bolt Services LT UAB).docx] _(2.79 MB)_","2026-01-08T11:48:36.839Z"],["3795622","EBIKE1-196","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin"," Sate-lite has improved and made samples. The test is ongoing. Waiting for test results.\n\nIEC60529\nTest method: put the samples into water. The distance between the very bottom samples and water surface is at least 1m; The distance between the very top samples and water surface is at least 0.15m.\nTest standard: no water inside the light. After testing and being placed for an hour, the part can worknormally,y and led and other electronic components are fine.\n\n!7371ea61fe7ce3f1fbabf60d9297e54a-20260108-114717.png|width=742,alt=\"7371ea61fe7ce3f1fbabf60d9297e54a-20260108-114717.png\"!","2026-01-08T11:49:01.481Z"],["3795623","DSR-2999","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","Response and PDE sent out. ","2026-01-08T11:49:03.659Z"],["3795624","LSS-61270","LSS","stephanie.oreoluwa@bolt.eu","Stephanie Oreoluwa","[^20260108 VEHICLE-HAILING SERVICE PARTNERSHIP AGREEMENT-BOLT APP SUPPORT NIGERIA LIMITED.docx] _(60 kB)_","2026-01-08T11:49:09.266Z"],["3795627","HS-28595","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello!\n\nThe letter has been sent for a signature and once signed you will receive it to your personal email.\n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-08T11:50:59.073Z"],["3795629","LSS-59980","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:e240cb3e-a6f6-45ad-a60e-b19cc96e6af7] , hei!\n\nSince there has been no activity on this ticket for 30 days, I will need to close it soon.\n\nThe contract will still be available for signing – you can simply reopen the ticket at any time.","2026-01-08T11:51:21.201Z"],["3795630","LSS-59971","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:e240cb3e-a6f6-45ad-a60e-b19cc96e6af7] , hei!\n\nSince there has been no activity on this ticket for 30 days, I will need to close it soon.\n\nThe contract will still be available for signing – you can simply reopen the ticket at any time.","2026-01-08T11:51:48.598Z"],["3795633","LSS-61271","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter FNB (Bolt Services (ZA) Pty Ltd).docx] _(2.79 MB)_","2026-01-08T11:52:10.845Z"],["3795634","LSS-59978","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:e240cb3e-a6f6-45ad-a60e-b19cc96e6af7] , hei!\n\nSince there has been no activity on this ticket for 30 days, I will need to close it soon.\n\nThe contract will still be available for signing – you can simply reopen the ticket at any time.","2026-01-08T11:52:11.125Z"],["3795636","WD-22515","WD","mihut.arsene@bolt.eu","Mihuț-Andrei Arsene","Hey Kerilin,\n\nThis is to confirm that the entity has been adjusted for these contigent workers, as per your request. \n\nPlease feel free to reach out for any questions or concerns!\n\nMany thanks,\n\nMihut","2026-01-08T11:52:24.120Z"],["3795637","LSS-61058","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] - The address for the Belgian entity has now been updated ([LINK|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-controller-list/?category=rides]). Please double-check that you are happy with this. Otherwise, I will close the ticket 🙂 ","2026-01-08T11:52:31.278Z"],["3795639","PFI-830423","PFI","sasha.maletskaya@bolt.eu","Aliaksandra Maletskaya","Hi, his bank account was closed. He couldn’t receive payout  ","2026-01-08T11:52:39.387Z"],["3795643","PFI-816798","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi [~accountid:712020:7626ae07-ea91-4d23-8c4c-96510e3c6778]  \n\nTo be more compliant with tax rules, we do not reissue the rider invoices.\n\nPlease ask the user to make sure that their Personal Profile and/or Work profile have correct information. And make sure they pick the right Billing profile before the ride. \n\nIt is as essential as picking the right payment method before the ride.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,\n\nNikolay Roll  ","2026-01-08T11:53:02.061Z"],["3795646","RDXENG-3814","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","(/) *Tested on CI.217.0.* ","2026-01-08T11:53:51.798Z"],["3795647","FX-3557","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767873255345909]*{color}:\ni think its possible, but a hard suggestion as deleted data can never be recovered. Also for example if i deleted car row in the table, another service/logic might actually depend on that car row to exist and causes errors. So thats why deleting rows is rather not recommended. With the case of vehicles table i would think its also pretty widely used and might cause issues...\n{quote}","2026-01-08T11:54:29.591Z"],["3795650","LSS-61272","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter Airwallex (Bolt Services CA Inc.).docx] _(2.79 MB)_","2026-01-08T11:55:01.383Z"],["3795652","LSS-60050","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] , As far as I understand, the Adobe warning relates to our trust list configuration, not to the validity of the signature itself.\n\nA qualified signature can still be legally valid even if Adobe cannot verify it automatically. However, this type of signature does not align with our internal policy.","2026-01-08T11:55:37.807Z"],["3795654","ADS-48","ADS","dane.david@bolt.eu","Dane David","Hmm, I’m not sure if there’s an epic where I can group this. At some point we need to be able to add matching rule that will display ads content only to people within X km of a provider/store.\n\nIs there an epic for ad-hocs?","2026-01-08T11:55:50.146Z"],["3795655","PFI-817505","PFI","grace.anyumba@bolt-outsource.eu","Grace Anyumba","Hello, the rider is following up on the issue. Any updates ?","2026-01-08T11:55:53.825Z"],["3795657","PFI-830953","PFI","ronny.gikundi@bolt-outsource.eu","Ronny Gikundi","!IMG-20260106-WA0020.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T11:56:23.855Z"],["3795658","PFI-830944","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0],\n\nI have looked at the profile and I can not find any debt related to this account?\nI will be attaching 2 different screenshots of information that is currently visible.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.53.03.png|width=381,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.53.03.png\"!\n\nPicture above shows the reason why the account can not be deleted. Archive is also locked behind “Pending personal data export”.\n\nRegarding debt, then it does not seem like this user would have any debt that would restrict them from the deletion. Kindly see the picture below.\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.55.09.png|width=413,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.55.09.png\"!\n\nAdditionally, in our logs we do not see any rejection from the Fraud side, therefore we would advise that the problems mentioned above are resolved first, afterwards there should be no problems with the deletion/archival.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-08T11:56:27.126Z"],["3795659","BSKT-4581","BSKT","isham.faizal@bolt.eu","Isham Faizal","Using BSKT-4525","2026-01-08T11:56:26.377Z"],["3795662","LSS-51884","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:712020:f5c52198-9bb5-40b8-865d-70e96f6ccf5a] please find the requested analysis on how to exit the contract [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/121woy7U5xr-rzLhZoKJS3r71g_USwhBtFpbGO153I_0/edit?usp=sharing] and what are the steps to follow. I understand we are going for the wind down alternative, so I made the analysis based on this assumption. \n\nIn summary, these are the steps we need to follow: \n\n# Send termination notice (template is [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eESQwG3imJMOK1jx1_EMwQV7g5ZN2YnR41XMuf6u0sw/edit?usp=sharing]): for this we need to align on the amount to be paid and date of notification. Here we also need to state election +NOT to receive Transition Services+ \n# Pay Early Termination Damages (within 1 month of termination)\n# Work in good faith with Marqeta (no specific requirements defined)\n# Continue paying all fees (same terms as before, for up to 6 months)\n# Pay all wind-down costs and expenses (no specific amount defined or details on how it is calculated)\n# Request data deletion or return (within 30 days of end of Services)\n# Complete wind-down within 6 months maximum\n\n*Note* that the agreement with Marqeta does not specify: \n\n* How to coordinate wind-down activities\n* Specific wind-down milestones\n* Cardholder communication requirements\n* Data extraction procedures (beyond final data deletion/return)\n\n\n\ncc [~accountid:5bdbfc9b359ddf204e8c7e02] ","2026-01-08T11:56:55.160Z"],["3795663","LSS-61273","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter Papaya Global Ltd (Bolt Services PL Sp. z.o.o.).docx] _(2.79 MB)_","2026-01-08T11:57:25.519Z"],["3795664","PFI-826933","PFI","ruben.nogueira@bolt.eu","Rúben Nogueira","Hey [~accountid:5adef5687dd1e556227b7b2a]! (and [~accountid:619df382b43d5b006a0196e7] for your knowledge).\n\nHave you been noticing a decrease on these kind of registrations? Is there anything from the top of the funnel you can act on to prevent these clients from activating the account? Just want to make sure they stop harming our supply + impacting our sales pipelines.\n\nThank you.","2026-01-08T11:57:48.519Z"],["3795666","WFM-9894","WFM","mihaela.pahontu@bolt-outsource.eu","Mihaela Pahontu","You have it in the message I sent above, the romanian text and the english one.","2026-01-08T11:58:42.821Z"],["3795668","WFM-9894","WFM","mihaela.pahontu@bolt-outsource.eu","Mihaela Pahontu","!image-20260108-115854.png|width=730,height=189,alt=\"image-20260108-115854.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-08T11:58:58.674Z"],["3795670","FPD-1408","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","PR with the architecture implementation to run backtesting accuracy is now created and ready to review: [https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/787|https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/787|smart-link] \n\nAlongside it, the document with an overview on the backtesting accuracy logic and architecture has been updated to reflect the latest additions: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7280361616/IBM+Backtesting+Accuracy+Logic+and+Architecture|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7280361616/IBM+Backtesting+Accuracy+Logic+and+Architecture|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T11:59:13.846Z"],["3795672","MLC-185","MLC","shubhi.agrawal@bolt.eu","Shubhi Agrawal","Week 1 update\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* progress 92%\n* *Blockers:* None\n* *Status update:* \n** Vertical banners are rolled out to 50% of actual users :green_circle:  \n** On Monday 12th Jan the banners are getting rolled to 100% of users\n** Created the mixpanel dashboard for tracking of banners shown to Story funnel, Link 🔗 [here|https://mixpanel.com/project/1165336/view/32804/app/boards#id=10878375]\n** Control groups [discussion thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNH34A2BY/p1767602656291839]: \n*** For generic use cases -  which are targeting all users Martech asked to use the [+A/B Experimentation platform+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/new](i need to clarify the results and MDE, etc to be put in the setup  as the setups are different\n*** For segmented use cases-  we need to confirm whether using the Test platform as suggested is feasible, and whether the number of events triggered will be manageable for six use cases segmented across all countries\n*** Meeting with Ameer on Friday to discuss about next steps of adding control groups\n\n* *Next steps:*\n** Adding control groupS\n** Launching experiments for Airports and loyal churn banner\n** Preparing next 3 generic use cases","2026-01-08T11:59:39.212Z"],["3795673","LSS-58375","LSS","david.vysoky@bolt.eu","Dávid Vysoký","I have attended the court hearing.\nThe court ruling was in our favor, and the court awarded the full amount of damages. The defense attorney reserved the 8-day period following the judgment to consider a potential appeal. During the trial, the attorney for the convicted party only contested the amounts determined by the expert witness in the indictment (which was in total over one milion CZK).\n\nMatěj Krupa was informed and will be awaiting the court ruling once we receive it and requested a PoA for potential appeal.","2026-01-08T11:59:42.568Z"],["3795674","CSP-441","CSP","laimdota.vilistere@bolt.eu","Laimdota Vilistere","Any update on this? Should we include other product teams? \n\nThis initiative is in the CEE region 2026 Roadmap and OPS is expecting from us the delivery. \n\nWould be amazing to start implementation in Q2. Can we include this initiative in the Product roadmap?","2026-01-08T11:59:45.259Z"],["3795675","BDB-1500","BDB","liisi.tamra@bolt.eu","Liisi Tamra","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] ok, in that case let’s maybe test with different copy:\n\nTrain station: *Arrive by train. Leave with a ride.*\nBus station: *From platform to pickup*\nShopping mall: *Skip the queue and ride*\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] ","2026-01-08T12:00:06.854Z"],["3795676","LSS-61274","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter Jyske Bank A-S (Bolt Rides DK ApS).docx] _(2.79 MB)_","2026-01-08T12:00:11.540Z"],["3795678","LSS-57405","LSS","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","Hi [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] \nThe correct version was sent via contractbook to Ahto which i’m also attaching here for reference.\n\n[^Malta International Airport - License and Service Agreement 0801.pdf]\n\nthank you!","2026-01-08T12:00:22.256Z"],["3795682","PFI-687915","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.01.45.png|width=264,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.01.45.png\"!","2026-01-08T12:01:52.880Z"],["3795683","MLC-3584","MLC","shubhi.agrawal@bolt.eu","Shubhi Agrawal","Week 1 Update\n\n\n\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* 5%\n* *Blockers:* Storytelling template to roll out completely\n* *Status update:* \n** We will be picking this once Storytelling template is rolled out, probably End of Q1 or Q2\n\n* *Next steps*\n** None as of now","2026-01-08T12:01:52.662Z"],["3795684","PFI-830954","PFI","fatima.omran@bolt.eu","Fatima Amin Omran","[^b1kqz9cs2cf95064-f62b-40a0-a491-495b77094b6c.pdf]","2026-01-08T12:02:04.365Z"],["3795685","PFI-687915","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-08T12:02:17.928Z"],["3795688","BPPA-61","BPPA","yuliia.hakkinen@bolt.eu","Yuliia Häkkinen","[https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/1517483638694175?o=2472566184436351#command/6341914115808916|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/1517483638694175?o=2472566184436351#command/6341914115808916] \n\nNotebook used for getting to know the data. Will follow up with a team on the questions that I had on the way. ","2026-01-08T12:02:50.019Z"],["3795689","PFI-759356","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.02.50.png|width=255,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.02.50.png\"!","2026-01-08T12:02:58.408Z"],["3795692","LSS-61275","LSS","girts.tretjakovs@bolt.eu","Ģirts Tretjakovs","[^Nr. 7G-7754.docx.pdf] _(86 kB)_","2026-01-08T12:03:29.375Z"],["3795693","LSS-61275","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nĢirts Tretjakovs has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-08T12:03:31.402Z"],["3795695","PTWS-2073","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","hello,\n\nplease Separate *veteran status* so it exists as its own field and section — it should be available in Workday as a standalone field.\n\n\nthanks","2026-01-08T12:03:38.062Z"],["3795697","HS-28717","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Updated JD was sent out. ","2026-01-08T12:03:57.998Z"],["3795699","LSS-61259","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:af076e83-bb33-4eb6-8634-6e435217c5e4] , thanks a lot for escalating this case! I am looking into the FO’s claims with InfoSec to establish what happened here. I’ll get back to you ASAP 😊 ","2026-01-08T12:03:59.422Z"],["3795700","CCM-22261","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hi David,\n\nOnboarding has been enrolled. 🙌 \n\nAll the best 🌷 ,\nIrena","2026-01-08T12:04:08.131Z"],["3795701","PFI-830956","PFI","bielinskyi.roman@bolt-outsource.eu","Bielinskyi Roman","[^report_08-01-2026_13-04-19.pdf]","2026-01-08T12:04:09.232Z"],["3795702","DELIVERY-690","DELIVERY","fedor.novikov@bolt.eu","Fedor Novikov","26W01:\nWe are testing out replacements on 2 providers","2026-01-08T12:04:10.031Z"],["3795706","LSS-61259","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","* Checking with InfoSec here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04MYS31C0L/p1767873732513969|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04MYS31C0L/p1767873732513969|smart-link] \n* Disputed payout: [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/232472558?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-08T12:04:16.594Z"],["3795709","HWMISC-733","HWMISC","norman.tamm@bolt.eu","Norman Tamm","Me and [~accountid:712020:ef569842-27e0-4a96-b3b1-ee47d8709209] investigated the battery with E524 and we could not figure out the exact root cause, but the issue was BMS related.\n\nIn this specific case the E524 battery was not dangerous, but this may not apply for all E524 batteries.\n\nWe have decided to collect additional battery samples with E524 and send their BMSes to TechSum for further investigation.\n\nMoving this task to {color:#00B8D9}*[ ON HOLD ]*{color}  until we have received the E524 batteries","2026-01-08T12:05:21.799Z"],["3795710","PFI-830957","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T12:05:28.986Z"],["3795712","SREDESK-7386","SREDESK","mehran.eftekhari@bolt.eu","Shahriar Eftekhari","https://monitor.boltint.net/d/000000038/redis3a-overview?orgId=1&var-alias=driverx-mqtt-broker-africa&var-role=master&var-instance=All&var-job=All&var-datasource=P6BB142EF7CA4BDF6&var-cmd=All&from=now-30m&to=now\r\n\r\nhttps://monitor.boltint.net/d/000000038/redis3a-overview?orgId=1&var-alias=driverx-mqtt-broker-europe&var-role=master&var-instance=All&var-job=All&var-datasource=P6BB142EF7CA4BDF6&var-cmd=All&from=now-30m&to=now\r\n\r\nhttps://monitor.boltint.net/d/000000038/redis3a-overview?orgId=1&var-alias=driverx-mqtt-broker-westasia&var-role=master&var-instance=All&var-job=All&var-datasource=P6BB142EF7CA4BDF6&var-cmd=All&from=now-30m&to=now\r\n\r\n\r\n3 new redises up and running.","2026-01-08T12:05:39.938Z"],["3795715","WD-22430","WD","mihut.arsene@bolt.eu","Mihuț-Andrei Arsene","Hi Miina,\n\nUnfortunately, the Home Email usually cannot be displayed on the People search card, only on:\n\n* Contact Information\n* Worker Profile → Personal Details\n* Custom reports\n\nThis is an intentional *PII protection* decision by Workday and this way we maintain the cleanest WD-compliant setup. \n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions!\n\nMany thanks,\n\nMihut","2026-01-08T12:06:42.588Z"],["3795716","PFI-830958","PFI","chakkrit.panchorn@bolt-outsource.eu","Chakkrit Panchorn","!image-20260108-120321.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260108-120343.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T12:06:50.839Z"],["3795718","PFI-809183","PFI","milena.prazynska@bolt-outsource.eu","Milena Prazynska","so what we should do or tell the driver? should we do another sd for technical support because of wrong information in the app or just tell the driver that we did not charge any commission for this ride?","2026-01-08T12:07:16.610Z"],["3795719","PFI-830959","PFI","chakkrit.panchorn@bolt-outsource.eu","Chakkrit Panchorn","!Slip_500.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260108-120527.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T12:07:18.889Z"],["3795720","HS-28651","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hi [~accountid:60069928e2a1350069629f4b] \n\nThank you for the update. Her contract process has been paused until further notice from you or mobility team 🙂 \n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-08T12:08:18.364Z"],["3795721","PFI-792273","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo, reviewing the backlog\n\nCorrect, commission invoices are issued monthly. However, the branding bonus has been set up on the Campaign team’s side, and afaik, it doesn’t require any manual adjustments from the local team, no?\n\nI’d advise checking with the Campaign team in case any procedures have changed recently.","2026-01-08T12:08:46.190Z"],["3795722","PFI-821398","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","if by header they mean this part:\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-08 at 14.07.36@2x.png|width=345,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-08 at 14.07.36@2x.png\"!\n\nthen before they might have ordered Bolt Business → in such case Bolt is the seller.\n\nBut in this order - ride was personal → in this case seller is the driver.\n\n\n\nfor tip amount - need to investigate further.","2026-01-08T12:08:46.867Z"],["3795723","DELIVERY-1706","DELIVERY","fedor.novikov@bolt.eu","Fedor Novikov","26W01:\nWe have base implementation. \nWe are working under different type of prices.","2026-01-08T12:08:49.949Z"],["3795724","PFI-821398","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! \n\nLooks like this issue needs input from our developers. The issue has been flagged to them & they are investigating. We will keep you posted with any updates! \n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-08T12:08:53.334Z"],["3795726","LSS-61156","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432]! All clear. I attach the updated documents.\n\n[^2026.01 ENG_Resolution_Bolt Holdings OÜ 20.01.26).pdf]\n[^2026.01 ENG_Consent and Power of Attorney of the Director_Bolt Services GE (20.01.26).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T12:09:26.790Z"],["3795727","PFI-830960","PFI","lawrancetshepo.motsepe@bolt.eu","Lawrance Tshepo Motsepe","!Lwazi_POP.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T12:09:31.113Z"],["3795729","DRAG-695","DRAG","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Thanks a lot [~accountid:712020:8d272f38-d046-4ad2-a5b3-a47b219e9fa1] . Nice and detailed report with good suggestions. ","2026-01-08T12:10:06.609Z"],["3795731","PFI-830961","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T12:10:32.714Z"],["3795732","WD-22497","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","The validation is back ","2026-01-08T12:10:44.888Z"],["3795735","WD-22480","WD","andreicosmin.stan@bolt.eu","Andrei-Cosmin Stan","hi! \nIssue solved. Everyone can now report their hours in WD for 2026. \nThank you! ","2026-01-08T12:11:45.103Z"],["3795736","DO-5763","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","I found the reason.\n\nYou can see that Look through the {{delivery}} role. This role does not allow you to access the Explore.\n\nBut you also have the {{delivery_curated}} role. This gives you Explore rights to a limited set of well-tested, curated Looks and their Explorers.\n\nUnfortunately, we cannot give you access to the Explores of the non-curated Looks. Their Explores can only be done by power users.\n\nHere is a comment from the Analytics Engineer for the delivery vertical Bram:\n\n{quote}* Curated delivery model: widespread access, anyone can explore, high-quality data and explores should be built in a robust way so users cannot get wrong output.\n* Delivery model: limited access, only Looker power users can explore, lower quality requirements, more for experimental purposes.{quote}\n\nSo, unless you get the Power User role, you would not be able to access the Explores of non-curated delivery Looks. I’m sorry.","2026-01-08T12:11:51.959Z"],["3795737","DO-5767","DO","pedro.paiva@bolt.eu","Pedro Paiva","{{looker_meta}} would be the one to create\nthere’s no read access needed for the SP at the moment\n\n\n\nfor the looker credentials, which team should I ask for? from the #dap-and-ae-discussion I got the understanding it would be this ticket indeed…","2026-01-08T12:11:56.092Z"],["3795738","HS-28691","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Sent for signing.","2026-01-08T12:12:39.224Z"],["3795739","LSS-56585","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:5b7d5435b57ed25933f64464] thanks for your patience. \n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1u88-5ZkpTZ0Iq4woW7enDBkajRjgntS_/edit?pli=1|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1u88-5ZkpTZ0Iq4woW7enDBkajRjgntS_/edit?pli=1|smart-link]  this version of the MOU can be downloaded and shared with the partner. ","2026-01-08T12:12:44.771Z"],["3795742","L10N-26530","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26529](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26529)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T12:13:22.665Z"],["3795743","L10N-26534","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26529](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26529)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T12:13:23.856Z"],["3795744","L10N-26537","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the par