anks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T12:13:40.370Z"],["3795755","PFI-830963","PFI","elijah.ojeamien@bolt-outsource.eu","Elijah Ojeamien","[^LT1525-35090 (1).pdf]","2026-01-08T12:13:51.947Z"],["3795756","DPX-3551","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","Released under the Feature Flag.\n\nTo enable the feature, create an FF with similar content, when translations are ready, and the content is uploaded to Contentful\n\n{{guides_2026_01_release}} – enables new translations for old links and shows new links for new guides\n\n{{hide_sunmi_v3_guide}} – hides the Sunmi V3 link, since [~accountid:621f66f84160640069c66ff4]  shared that it might be ready later (in Feb)\n\n!image-20260108-121158.png|width=1323,alt=\"image-20260108-121158.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\nWaiting for translations:\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-100550?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-100550?created=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T12:13:53.883Z"],["3795757","PFI-830963","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T12:13:54.367Z"],["3795759","PAW-14720","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T12:14:09.222Z"],["3795760","BPPA-56","BPPA","yuliia.hakkinen@bolt.eu","Yuliia Häkkinen","We split the list of metrics: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1bsPzMRW4UYL2xsNPoPA4PO2LUsQxFKMkO8apyNs44yc/edit?gid=696847920#gid=696847920|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1bsPzMRW4UYL2xsNPoPA4PO2LUsQxFKMkO8apyNs44yc/edit?gid=696847920#gid=696847920|smart-link]  \n\nAgreed to have the first check on 08.01. Meeting notes: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KsjFkKsXDWA_IEM_pjKpiP_RmTgXl8IWWgVbOYCCKls/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KsjFkKsXDWA_IEM_pjKpiP_RmTgXl8IWWgVbOYCCKls/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T12:14:20.078Z"],["3795761","LSS-61277","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter Black Rock (Bolt Holdings OU).docx] _(2.79 MB)_\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter Goldman Sachs (Bolt Holdings OU).docx] _(2.79 MB)_\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter Standard Chartered Bank Ghana PLC (Bolt Holdings OU (Ghana branch)).docx] _(2.79 MB)_\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter Standard Chartered Bank Ghana PLC (Bolt Holdings OU).docx] _(2.79 MB)_\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter Bank of Georgia Group PLC (Bolt Operations OU).docx] _(2.79 MB)_\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter Citigroup Inc (Bolt Operations OU).docx] _(2.79 MB)_\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter PayPal (Bolt Operations OU).docx] _(2.79 MB)_\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter PawaPay (Bolt Operations OU).docx] _(2.79 MB)_\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter BNP Paribas S.A., Bankfilial Sverige  (Bolt Technology OU).docx] _(2.79 MB)_","2026-01-08T12:14:31.449Z"],["3795762","PFI-806303","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo, reviewing the backlog\n\nNo access to provided links, but taking into account the only invoice in admin with a total of 395.88->  is the accurate one, which also match with balance calculation for August.","2026-01-08T12:14:40.833Z"],["3795766","FX-3582","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767874528218629]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3582] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T12:15:40.971Z"],["3795767","WFM-9827","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","hello! roles were approved","2026-01-08T12:15:42.653Z"],["3795768","FDBT-4749","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-08T12:15:47.962Z"],["3795769","LSS-59833","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] , hey! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^PoA_Bolt Poland_E.Ożańska.docx_encrypted_.pdf] \n\n[^PoA_Bolt Poland_A.Lipson.docx_encrypted_.pdf] ","2026-01-08T12:16:03.449Z"],["3795770","LSS-61275","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-08T12:16:11.079Z"],["3795771","EBIKE1-420","EBIKE1","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[~accountid:5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] \n\n{quote}Note that next open bat also fails {{rnd:Z72Gw6RM}} with error message: “{{hatchlock operation failed: communication fail}}“. This also indicates that there was no power in system.{quote}\n\nTrue, but only if there are no communication errors and bus voltage by IOT as well. Alone, it could mean that there is a disturbance in CAN communication to the lock, right?\n\nAny idea why this did not qualify as E1?","2026-01-08T12:16:32.283Z"],["3795773","PFI-809250","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Closing the ticket, changes went live on 01.01 (16%) \n\nThank you","2026-01-08T12:17:06.169Z"],["3795774","IDC-164","IDC","artem.borisov@bolt.eu","Artem Borisov","We need to update the data structure. Also, there's no cache anymore","2026-01-08T12:17:08.011Z"],["3795775","FDBT-4750","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-08T12:17:17.994Z"],["3795776","LSS-57383","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2] yes it would be good if Lisanna includes AWX requirements. Do you need any assitance from me? ","2026-01-08T12:17:21.878Z"],["3795777","LSS-61259","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","From BH linked ticket:\n\n* Email was changed from [+medrivesas@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesas@gmail.com] (original one) to [+medrivesass@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesass@gmail.com] (alleged fraudster) on the 28 Dec 2025, 14:42:36 UTC+02:00, it can be found on the [+fleet change logs+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/74814?tab=change-log&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D], \n* from the IP 103.151.40.239, by the fleet manager [+70795+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-manager/managers/edit/70795]. \n* There is a lot of language updates and different IPs on the [+fleet manager change log+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-manager/managers/edit/70795?tab=change_log], so this account could be compromised. \n* Also, I think that external Fleet Owner information are also compomised, as fraudster provided 2 times verified a KBis, which can be obtained with a digital ID.\n\nOther relevant thread: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01HSEEAYSK/p1767713570717579|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01HSEEAYSK/p1767713570717579|smart-link] \n\n➡️ My suspicion is that the FO email was breached outside of Bolt, and that the malicious actor was able to gain access to the Fleet Portal that way. Waiting for InfoSec confirmation","2026-01-08T12:17:41.870Z"],["3795778","PAW-14584","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-configless-other, pint-product-resource-provisioning, pint-capability-self-service-infrastructure\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-08T12:17:46.785Z"],["3795779","LSS-57405","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, this has now been signed, but they also sent the extra charge form. Does this need to be signed as well? If yes then they have set it up with the phone number that doesn’t belong to Ahto.\n\n[^Malta International Airport - License and Service Agreement (d0d08340-8bd3-4a7b-be11-567053f30759).pdf]\n[^Malta International Airport - Extra Charge Form (63aea4de-8227-4bb8-9585-fc5739c14209).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T12:17:59.691Z"],["3795780","LSS-61159","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] - as it’s an AI tool - believe your team is better suited to pick up but if you need us to - let me know!","2026-01-08T12:18:03.703Z"],["3795781","PFI-812007","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","pending for now, more discussion in *bb-resellermodel-mt*","2026-01-08T12:18:04.546Z"],["3795782","RCE-332","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767874674615349]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-332 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T12:18:07.938Z"],["3795783","RCE-330","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767874679735489]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-330 is already in the state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T12:18:12.211Z"],["3795784","FDBT-4751","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-08T12:18:23.603Z"],["3795785","PFI-830519","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:92de8b35-6a42-4290-a24d-a4656c69eaa7],\n\nWe have looked over the orders and the users.\nWhile the users are extremely suspicious, then we can not exactly assign blame on the driver nor factually prove fraudulent behavior.\n\nKindly manually compensate the driver for the loss of their earnings.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-08T12:18:30.293Z"],["3795786","RCE-330","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767874706397819]*{color}:\nDeployed without issues for now. Good PR. :+1:\n{quote}","2026-01-08T12:18:38.564Z"],["3795788","DRAG-636","DRAG","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] is there a timeline for final validation? Do you need me to set up some vehicles for it?","2026-01-08T12:18:47.061Z"],["3795789","WFM-9894","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Hey [~accountid:712020:207c95ff-c39e-492c-9c31-f804f0b6bb8a] the comms are up until 08.01.2026 EOD","2026-01-08T12:18:50.154Z"],["3795791","LSS-61273","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter Papaya Global Ltd (Bolt Services PL Sp. z.o.o.).pdf] ","2026-01-08T12:19:18.826Z"],["3795796","PLUS-17","PLUS","evgeniy.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Evgeniy Kuznetsov","[~accountid:6282884a222d36006fb57e3e] were you planning to do it on Webview or Server side?","2026-01-08T12:19:32.112Z"],["3795797","PFI-813243","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Correct, you can proceed with replicating the same account and onboarding it with the relevant BFC.","2026-01-08T12:19:47.351Z"],["3795798","RS-1940","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hi [~accountid:60c7025b5c64b10071aef787] , we can comply with the request! If you have a specific concern, please do let me know🙏 \n","2026-01-08T12:19:51.767Z"],["3795799","LSS-61274","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter Jyske Bank A-S (Bolt Rides DK ApS).pdf] ","2026-01-08T12:19:54.409Z"],["3795802","PFI-830968","PFI","marta.yakymchuk@bolt.eu","Marta Yakymchuk","!IMG_5727.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_5728.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T12:20:14.242Z"],["3795803","FRAUDOPS-1108","FRAUDOPS","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","\n\n# actual price >= 200 EUR _OR (actual price >= 100 and (user_age <= 2))_ AND price increase > 1x\n# incremental price/distance increase - *90 less CS tickets monthly.* No recent indication of said fraud, but basic overcharges. ~270 recalculations monthly\n## actual price 5-10, price 1.9x, distance 1.9x\n## actual price 10-20, price 1.85x, distance 1.85x\n## etc…","2026-01-08T12:21:00.946Z"],["3795806","HS-28738","HS","richmond.lartey@bolt.eu","Richmond Sammy Lartey","Thanks for the feedback [~accountid:712020:4888de6c-ac03-4e7d-85c8-91ac19352650] ","2026-01-08T12:21:28.425Z"],["3795808","WFM-9888","WFM","ramin.karimov@bolt.eu","Ramin Karimov","Hey, I confirm(/) ","2026-01-08T12:21:42.116Z"],["3795809","PFI-830970","PFI","liisa-ingrid.kerson@bolt.eu","Liisa-Ingrid Kerson","[^EE1425-143282 (3).pdf]\n\n[^EE1425-146364.pdf]","2026-01-08T12:21:42.409Z"],["3795810","CSDT-945","CSDT","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","presentation slides (not used) - [https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1FrFcRuofkTNDG0HHwgDfGCv77_ByAp5FwVSXP7bBv5w/edit?slide=id.g3b5729e9754_0_13#slide=id.g3b5729e9754_0_13|https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1FrFcRuofkTNDG0HHwgDfGCv77_ByAp5FwVSXP7bBv5w/edit?slide=id.g3b5729e9754_0_13#slide=id.g3b5729e9754_0_13|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T12:21:57.865Z"],["3795811","HS-28715","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hi Maria, \n\nfrom your current records, I could identify the following: \n\n* Education (from diploma): 8 years\n\nEmployment periods\n\n# 15.09.2024 – 14.03.2025 → 181 days\n# 17.07.2023 – 30.12.2023 → 167 days\n# 07.07.2025 – 08.01.2026 (today) → 186 days\n\nFrom this, it seems you will reach eligibility in July 2026. Please let me know in case I’m missing something!\n","2026-01-08T12:22:00.053Z"],["3795812","DELIVERY-1238","DELIVERY","fedor.novikov@bolt.eu","Fedor Novikov","26W01:\nWe enabled configs including Discovery side.\nAuchan enabled. We are observing.","2026-01-08T12:22:00.711Z"],["3795816","BPPA-64","BPPA","yuliia.hakkinen@bolt.eu","Yuliia Häkkinen","Current docs and AS-IS on experimentation in the team: \n\n*A/B testing in Bolt Plus*\n\n*The moset recent example:* \n\n* Contextual Upsell: [+Page: 2025 Q2: Bolt Plus Upsell+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/6426656927/2025+Q2+Bolt+Plus+Upsell] [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JKNMLKRrZsoY4p37nRatj7waLr-zoP67nm3IudiN62I/edit?search_id=c3bfa12f-a59e-4ab4-94af-8e82285d59e1&tab=t.0#heading=h.7uay29u6ixel|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JKNMLKRrZsoY4p37nRatj7waLr-zoP67nm3IudiN62I/edit?search_id=c3bfa12f-a59e-4ab4-94af-8e82285d59e1&tab=t.0#heading=h.7uay29u6ixel|smart-link] \n* Proposal prepared by [~accountid:712020:84675a23-dfee-46a3-b3c2-8903b8ed4f60] : [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ty6tNu5WShpOuv6qM000rMLXUDfMfcd5U0zhkjy4reU/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.6rn6e0jj8xs2|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ty6tNu5WShpOuv6qM000rMLXUDfMfcd5U0zhkjy4reU/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.6rn6e0jj8xs2|smart-link] \n* Guru set the experiment: [+https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/edit/14277+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/edit/14277]\n\nMetrics: \n\n* A random metric is used currently in the scorecard; the actual metrics and guardrails are recalculated later. \n\nMixpanel: \n\n* Added events by ENG on request from Analytics, which weren’t in scope initially. \n\n\n\n*To be done:* \n\n* We need to have an agreed flow with Product and Engineering, including the experiment design and launch phase, during the planning. \n* We need to be able to launch experiments for Bolt Plus via the experimentation platform, using the correct metrics to leverage the scorecard and design (sample size, duration calculations) to reduce the time spent manually designing experiments. ","2026-01-08T12:22:20.380Z"],["3795818","HS-28738","HS","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Hi Richmond, what is the new hires employment date?","2026-01-08T12:22:29.719Z"],["3795819","WFM-9897","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.21.49.png|width=210,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.21.49.png\"!\n\nhey [~accountid:62060b8beaf9e20070759575] - can you check the right corner down if you see this Tootle inbox type button? ","2026-01-08T12:22:33.466Z"],["3795820","PFI-830972","PFI","sheraton.donbosco@bolt.eu","Sheraton Donbosco","!image (4).png|thumbnail!\n\n!image (6).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T12:22:54.105Z"],["3795821","PFI-830972","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T12:22:56.049Z"],["3795826","PFI-830555","PFI","afonso.freitasecosta@bolt.eu","Afonso Freitas e Costa","Hi [~accountid:712020:93f92945-2c23-4781-9680-b6dd154892d8],\n\nWhat triggered your assumption for fraud?\n\n[~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] this is a postpaid company with a contract signed. Please don’t suspend any users until we have conclusions.\n\nThanks.","2026-01-08T12:23:38.861Z"],["3795827","WD-22517","WD","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","Hello [~accountid:60ab52d6411c2200681a75e4] \n\nCan you please confirm deadline for delivery date of these documents to the employees?","2026-01-08T12:23:54.996Z"],["3795829","GRWA-1475","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","[+PR+|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15191] to remove the table. \n\nNow the table {{feature_models_spark.feature_rides_campaign_bulkgroup_user_performance}} is removed from dbt.","2026-01-08T12:23:56.928Z"],["3795831","HS-28738","HS","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","i see the employee started on 05 Jan, the payment will be captured WD in our next payment run which is in the first week of feb","2026-01-08T12:24:28.659Z"],["3795834","DELIVERY-1699","DELIVERY","fedor.novikov@bolt.eu","Fedor Novikov","26W01:\nWe improved the event loop lag, also we started making observability improvement for menu publishing.","2026-01-08T12:24:42.291Z"],["3795835","PFI-830974","PFI","joan.egbujoh@bolt-outsource.eu","Joan Egbujoh","[^3-Month statement (1).pdf]","2026-01-08T12:24:46.991Z"],["3795837","HS-28705","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hi [~accountid:712020:8070775c-28a4-4d71-a1f7-d3c0f06715a0] , you’re right, I have updated your annual leave entitlement in Workday, you should be able to see the change already.\nThanks for flagging this!\n\n\n\nAll the best","2026-01-08T12:25:13.033Z"],["3795838","PAW-14719","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @tomekt-bolt\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160100\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-08 12:25:27 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-08T12:25:28.241Z"],["3795843","PFI-830972","PFI","sheraton.donbosco@bolt.eu","Sheraton Donbosco","Update of payout statement* ","2026-01-08T12:27:05.366Z"],["3795846","LSS-61156","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] , just to make sure: is that document considered as a  A copy of the extract from the commercial register regarding Bolt Holdings OÜ?\n\n[^Registration Card_Bolt Holdings OÜ_Taxify Shareholder SPV OÜ_08.01.2026.pdf] \n\nThank you!","2026-01-08T12:27:43.814Z"],["3795848","LSS-61215","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*BACKGROUND*+\n\n* ARPE (Authority for Social Relations on Employment Platforms) collects and aggregates: (i) the number of private hire vehicle drivers active on mobility platforms in 2024 and 2025; and (ii) the number of workers employed by fleets in the same years.\n** This is for the purpose of monitoring changes in private hire driver numbers between 2024 and 2025, in order to promote social dialogue.\n** Although this is a public interest task, the APRE insists on entering into agreements with each organisation it requests this data from.\n* PP has asked us to review a DSA between Bolt and Bolt and ARPE (Authority for Social Relations on Employment Platforms) ([LINK|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T3Ti5hjEhwtC0sI-Xg3Dquan20quYtX0/edit])\n** According to PP, the DSA governs the sharing of “_anonymised data of the number of active drivers on our platform as required by the Dialogue Social_”.\n* In spite of a typo on the main ticket, it appears this information must be sent by 12 January (next Monday) :melting_face: \n** Regional Legal has already reviewed and provided their comments.\n\n+*ANALYSIS*+\n\n* Based on my review of the documents, it appears that +*we are sharing some personal data here*+ in spite of PP’s description (although this needs to be confirmed, due to the hashing element).\n** According to the letter from the APRE ([LINK|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yTeWcRVVzsQRGE4eOQaL9zXvxrGf_XQG/edit]), the datapoints being requested are as follows:\n*** (1) “_A file containing a list of_ *_unique keys for each active driver_* _(regardless of their affiliation status) corresponding to the private hire vehicle licence number_ *_hashed using the SHA256 algorithm_*_, for the period from 1 January 2024 to 31 December 2024. An identical file will be produced for the period from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2025._”\n*** (2) “_A file containing the list of_ *_unique keys per active driver_* _registered between 1 January 2024 and 31 December 2024 corresponding to the private hire vehicle licence number_ *_hashed by the SHA256 algorithm_*_. Driver registration will be assessed based on the status of the information as at 31 December 2024. An identical file will be produced for the period from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2025, taking into account the situation with regard to affiliation as at 31 December 2025_.”\n** According to the agreement ([LINK|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T3Ti5hjEhwtC0sI-Xg3Dquan20quYtX0/edit]), the ‘Protected Data’ is +*_pseudonymised_*+, not anonymised (it is shared in an encrypted and hashed form).\n*** i.e., Clause 6.1 lists the datapoints: (i) VTC card number; and (ii) confirmation of attachment to a fleet. The data will then be hashed with a hash key (that is not disclosed to APRE), and is then shared with APRE, as part of the exchange process. The APRE will then aggregate this data at the sector level.\n* However, although this is the data of a high volume of French drivers, it is pseudonymised private hire licence numbers / fleet confirmations only (which cannot be identified without an encryption key). As such, the data sharing is {color:#36b37e}*low risk*{color}.\n** Unfortunately, the timing on this is extremely tight, and so pushing for a full suite of data sharing provisions is neither necessary nor practical in this case.\n* My comments on the agreement are therefore as follows:\n** Agreement is in the EU (Estonia → France) → {color:#36b37e}*Fine*{color}.\n** Recital D states that Bolt does not consider the Protected Data as personal data → {color:#ff5630}*This is not accurate*{color} ⚠️ \n*** I have deleted this provision. Indeed, the rest of the agreement deals with GDPR obligations, so it would be absurd to agree to this.\n** Legal basis for sharing is listed as legitimate interest → {color:#36b37e}*Fine*{color}. This is accurate.\n** Parties are defined as independent controllers, who must comply with the GDPR → {color:#36b37e}*Fine*{color}. This is accurate.\n** The data shall be stored securely by APRE and deleted after one month → {color:#36b37e}*Fine*{color}. Lowers the risk profile.\n** Agreement remains in force until 28 February 2026 → {color:#36b37e}*Fine*{color}. Lowers the risk profile.\n*** Agreement can also be terminated early by either party, in which case APRE must delete the data. This is also good.\n** The only provisions missing that I would prefer to see are as follows ⚠️ However, given the risk profile, if the sharing is crucial then we can proceed without:\n*** {color:#ff991f}*Personal data breach*{color} notification / mitigation obligation → I have included this for good measure (Clause 10.2).\n*** {color:#ff991f}*Pro-Bolt indemnity*{color} → I have included this for good measure (Clause 12.5).\n\n+*NEXT STEPS*+\n\n* QUESTIONS:\n** Confirm: (i) datapoints in the agreement; and (ii) that we are fine with hashing the data on our side using the sha-256 algorithm (since the agreement says we must do this).\n* ADVICE:\n** Flag that the timing is too tight - this should not be the standard.\n** Flag that: (a) we must remove the provision saying that we do not consider any personal data to be involve; and (b) we should push for the PDB/indemnity changes, but if there is no time and we will be doing this sharing regardless then the latter can be dropped.","2026-01-08T12:27:46.129Z"],["3795849","DELIVERY-1705","DELIVERY","fedor.novikov@bolt.eu","Fedor Novikov","26W01:\nWe made a tool for updating stores and regions from the providers list.","2026-01-08T12:27:52.040Z"],["3795850","LSS-59700","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Need to log in Cognito","2026-01-08T12:28:22.417Z"],["3795852","L10N-26561","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26529](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26529)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T12:28:31.056Z"],["3795853","L10N-26562","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26529](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26529)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T12:28:31.659Z"],["3795854","L10N-26564","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26529](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26529)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T12:28:40.191Z"],["3795856","DPX-3546","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","Release instructions: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPX-3551?focusedCommentId=3795756|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPX-3551?focusedCommentId=3795756] \n\nCan release after translations are ready (Blocked until then):\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-100550?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-100550?created=true|smart-link]","2026-01-08T12:28:50.330Z"],["3795858","WFM-9846","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571644|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571644]","2026-01-08T12:29:14.768Z"],["3795859","HS-28730","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","requested the document from Mazars","2026-01-08T12:29:24.118Z"],["3795860","LSS-61270","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - Please assist with reviewing the agreement. Thanks!","2026-01-08T12:30:19.346Z"],["3795861","LSS-61217","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hi Mo,\n\nPlease find the details for the Taiwan entity below:\n\n* *Tax Registration Number:* 030518188 (Unified Business Number)\n* *House Tax Registration Number:* Not applicable, as the company does not own real estate in Taiwan.\n\nPlease let me know if you need any supporting documents.\n\nSincerely,\nAleksandra","2026-01-08T12:30:24.427Z"],["3795862","WFM-9903","WFM","shivam.pal@bolt-outsource.eu","Shivam Pal","above user is part of Teleperformance Global RTA Team","2026-01-08T12:30:30.510Z"],["3795864","LSS-61238","LSS","aivo.toots@bolt.eu","Aivo Toots","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] I asked about personal data protection from BV. They said the topic is covered in “Certification Terms and Conditions” under chapter 8. Also, if this is not enough, they are ready to improve / update.","2026-01-08T12:31:16.009Z"],["3795866","LSS-56917","LSS","davis.baltvilks@bolt.eu","Dāvis Baltvilks","[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] are there any updates?","2026-01-08T12:31:26.386Z"],["3795869","LSS-61278","LSS","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","[^Bolt Holdings CA nr301-fill-13e (1).pdf] _(206 kB)_","2026-01-08T12:31:44.531Z"],["3795870","LSS-61279","LSS","manuel.maldonadofelices@bolt.eu","Manuel Maldonado Felices","[^Interfunerarias_Signed.pdf] _(2.32 MB)_","2026-01-08T12:31:53.055Z"],["3795871","LSS-61269","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter Papaya Global Ltd (Bolt Services LT UAB).pdf] ","2026-01-08T12:32:13.339Z"],["3795872","DO-5774","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","Hey Moustafa,\n\nI don’t see a link to the Airflow DAG, but probably you mean this one:\n[https://airflow-common.data.boltint.net/dags/dbt_micromobility_vehicle_stats_daily/grid?search=dbt_micromobility_vehicle_stats_daily|https://airflow-common.data.boltint.net/dags/dbt_micromobility_vehicle_stats_daily/grid?search=dbt_micromobility_vehicle_stats_daily]\n\nThe DAG is truned of still. When you turn it on, it should start running.","2026-01-08T12:32:21.109Z"],["3795874","LSS-61279","LSS","manuel.maldonadofelices@bolt.eu","Manuel Maldonado Felices","Hey,\n\nTwo contracts are included in the same PDF; please sign both pages.","2026-01-08T12:32:37.159Z"],["3795875","DPX-3552","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4763058803/Updating+Merchant+Guidelines+Contentful#Creating-a-new-content-type-(for-a-new-type-of-guides)|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4763058803/Updating+Merchant+Guidelines+Contentful#Creating-a-new-content-type-(for-a-new-type-of-guides)|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T12:33:02.491Z"],["3795878","SRED-1048","SRED","asko.tamm@bolt.eu","Asko Tamm","* user-verification-properties\n* user-profile-auditing\n* chat-archive\n* beehive\n\nThose clusters are the candidates for further migrations in Q1.","2026-01-08T12:33:43.826Z"],["3795880","PAW-14726","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T12:34:01.517Z"],["3795883","SUPX-2302","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","Will be fixed by SUPX-2253 ","2026-01-08T12:34:11.967Z"],["3795884","LSS-61156","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432], the document attached by you would not be sufficient. The document needs to look like the one I attached. You can see how all the documents need to look like by checking this folder that contains documents from the previous change that we did last year: [https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1ul75YkCM_EydCNH5MrHnwT8UZIueuSFa|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1ul75YkCM_EydCNH5MrHnwT8UZIueuSFa|smart-link] .\n\n[^Business registry extract Bolt Holdings OÜ_20.11.24.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T12:34:26.264Z"],["3795885","PAW-14725","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T12:35:02.560Z"],["3795886","PAW-14724","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T12:35:05.796Z"],["3795887","LSS-61156","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] !😊 ","2026-01-08T12:35:28.804Z"],["3795890","MVRT-1450","MVRT","tiffany.irianto@bolt.eu","Tiffany Ainnurrahmi Irianto","Hi [~accountid:5e5cc920bbb5110c9a68f9f3] sorry about this one i think the action items was removed or something. There is a request for additional creative for this campaign.\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else\n\nThank you","2026-01-08T12:36:31.518Z"],["3795891","HS-28640","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hi, the visa letter has been prepared and will be printed and signed by your regional People Partner Fidan, you will receive it from her!","2026-01-08T12:36:35.462Z"],["3795893","LSS-61280","LSS","davis.baltvilks@bolt.eu","Dāvis Baltvilks","[^Apspriedes_veidlapa.docx] _(24 kB)_\n\n[^2_pielikums_Tehniska_specifikacija_un_tehniskais_piedavajums.docx] _(27 kB)_\n\n[^1_pielikums_Kvalifikacijas_prasibas.docx] _(20 kB)_\n\n[^Apspriedes_veidlapa (1).docx] _(24 kB)_","2026-01-08T12:36:46.040Z"],["3795896","LSS-61261","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] - I assume this is okay to be signed? The terms seem to be the same ones as for the main agreement, just the sums are different.","2026-01-08T12:38:05.112Z"],["3795897","HS-25553","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:7339525d-fb60-466f-8abf-16088e41a658], \n\nI confirm that you were enrolled in the PPK program in November. I checked the platform and your account is active. I also advise you to contact them directly: [https://www.mojeppk.pl/faq.html#type=pracownik&theme=all|https://www.mojeppk.pl/faq.html#type=pracownik&theme=all|smart-link] \n\n(CC: [~accountid:712020:950de065-187c-4170-babd-e5aa814bdb19])\n\nBest regards, \n\nKerilin ","2026-01-08T12:38:05.393Z"],["3795899","SREC-364","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Overall plan as of right now:\n\n* Modularise the whole setup and move the resources - currently we have duplicated all of the live code to prelive. This can cause them to drift apart and all updates will be need to be made in both places. Modularising it will make this migration and future maintenance easier.\n* Add health checks to the MIGs (managed instance groups) - currently they are only attached to the load balancer, however this doesn’t guarantee a smooth rollout by itself. Having health checks to the MIGs will guarantee that the instances aren’t considered as ready by GCE until the service responds.\n* Use Container Optimised OS with cloud-init to run the containers on the instances, as described here [https://docs.cloud.google.com/container-optimized-os/docs/how-to/create-configure-instance#use-cloud-init|https://docs.cloud.google.com/container-optimized-os/docs/how-to/create-configure-instance#use-cloud-init|smart-link]\n** Roll out the changes in prelive first and validate\n** Roll out the changes in live after that\n* After the migration has been performed, update SFTPGo, as we are probably quite a few versions behind by now.","2026-01-08T12:38:26.591Z"],["3795901","DBRE-8589","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","EC2 type [i4i.12xlarge|https://instances.vantage.sh/aws/ec2/i4i.12xlarge] replaced by [i4i.8xlarge|https://instances.vantage.sh/aws/ec2/i4i.8xlarge]","2026-01-08T12:38:32.106Z"],["3795902","WD-22505","WD","shady.elwaziry@bolt.eu","Shady El Waziry","Thanks Olivier, I have updated it in the WD, please take a look to verify.\n\nThanks,","2026-01-08T12:38:33.303Z"],["3795905","PFI-830883","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","could you send a link please?","2026-01-08T12:39:19.079Z"],["3795906","HS-28580","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","[^Naoise Sorahan Cunningham Employment Confirmation Letter 08.01.2026.pdf]\n\nHi, uploading the letter here. [~accountid:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb] - could you please print and sign this document? Thank you! ","2026-01-08T12:39:24.508Z"],["3795908","LSS-60050","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","ok, [~accountid:61debf39e67ea2006b3a1cb5] please hold on. I am verifying it in another way 😉 let you know asap.","2026-01-08T12:40:00.654Z"],["3795910","AIOT-509","AIOT","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","agreed with [~accountid:712020:4b03e27a-3746-4bbe-b026-a11ab5e65aaf] to do this by {{2026-01-16}} ","2026-01-08T12:40:53.030Z"],["3795911","PFI-829576","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nWe have received a confirmation from Paystack the refund has been issued. \nUser should receive their funds within 72 hours. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-08T12:41:07.492Z"],["3795913","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c] Copy adjujsted cc: [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] ","2026-01-08T12:41:53.031Z"],["3795914","WEBSD-1443","WEBSD","emma.sjoo@bolt.eu","Emma Sjöö","Hey, is it possible to get these numbers today? ","2026-01-08T12:41:53.219Z"],["3795918","PFI-830903","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-08T12:43:40.057Z"],["3795919","LSS-61281","LSS","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","[^Bolt Holdings_Iceland rsk5.42.pdf] _(379 kB)_","2026-01-08T12:44:22.810Z"],["3795920","PFI-830974","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 57.00 ZAR on 11/12/2025, 14:29:36UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 11th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-08T12:44:50.478Z"],["3795922","MLC-2622","MLC","shubhi.agrawal@bolt.eu","Shubhi Agrawal","* *Status / Milestone:* 94%\n* *Blockers:* none\n* *Status update:* \n** Created a new template using DND editor, and then converted to HTML, fixing translations now\n** Go live: EOW/ Next mid- week\n* *Next steps*\n** Setting canvas live","2026-01-08T12:45:43.152Z"],["3795924","LSS-61280","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-08T12:46:10.132Z"],["3795925","LSS-61279","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-08T12:46:10.184Z"],["3795929","CSDA-256","CSDA","nargiz.abdullayeva@bolt.eu","Nargiz Karimova","Hi Boris!\n\nThanks a lot for keeping updated🙏 ","2026-01-08T12:47:49.037Z"],["3795930","DBRE-7144","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","* Added prometheus metrics + code cleanup\n* Running a few cycles to generate metrics for testing purposes\n\nTODO:\n\n* Add Grafana Panel\n* Improve deployment (ansible)\n* Add alerting\n* Write docs","2026-01-08T12:48:13.062Z"],["3795931","SUPX-2193","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","We discussed it with Hugo and decided that the order details should be available even for failed authorization (given that they were available for the user to open the flow in the first place), so there is no harm in displaying this button. No action needed.","2026-01-08T12:48:53.000Z"],["3795934","PFI-813982","PFI","alexandra.pakkonen@bolt.eu","Alexandra Pakkonen","Hey, thank you!","2026-01-08T12:49:37.816Z"],["3795936","LSS-61261","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Yes it’s fine, thank you [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] !","2026-01-08T12:49:52.138Z"],["3795938","MKP-9774","MKP","daniil.popov@bolt.eu","Daniil Popov","That's exactly I want to do here. To expose strategy to the request.","2026-01-08T12:50:13.501Z"],["3795939","MKP-9774","MKP",null,"Slack","[Daniil Popov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f4905b29aa9650046196c33] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04SLV3GT5K/p1767876487513889?thread_ts=1767795333.403909&cid=C04SLV3GT5K|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04SLV3GT5K/p1767876487513889?thread_ts=1767795333.403909&cid=C04SLV3GT5K|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-08T12:50:14.724Z"],["3795940","LSS-61280","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hello [~accountid:712020:ef6a9562-f9aa-4bb5-a4d5-2b18cc77085b]! \nThank you. Technical specification shall be reviewed by the Bolt Business and Rides Business team, not by legal. Legal is not in a position to assess our ability to perform tender requirements from the technical perspective. Thus, please engage with [~accountid:712020:95922f19-94a5-49f1-b3c6-43a9c9ddd746] . \n\n[~accountid:5d0c7ac70f1d390c4db46fed] FYI ","2026-01-08T12:50:46.080Z"],["3795941","MLC-3471","MLC","shubhi.agrawal@bolt.eu","Shubhi Agrawal","* *Status / Milestone:* 90%\n* *Blockers:* none\n* *Status update:* \n** Assets are ready with localisation,\n** The feature is not live yet, waiting for the live date from [Product|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09D09ULB9R/p1767611253693059?thread_ts=1767609564.821389&cid=C09D09ULB9R].\n** Need to confirm with Cristina - Since majority(81%) of users are from France and 5% from unknown, i am thinking to launch one canvas with all languages as CB is french card and we dont need to check countrywise performance for adhoc comm.\n* *Next steps*\n** Setting up comms  as per live date","2026-01-08T12:50:49.381Z"],["3795943","MLC-2742","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*26W2 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* None.\n* *Status update:*\n** Updated the DND test based on previous feedback and sent a new round of tests out.\n** Braze link to the latest template - [here|https://dashboard-02.braze.eu/engagement/templates_and_media/email_templates/660bb12b05810f0061db0f3c/695f9e90cceec20778eca700].\n* *Next steps:*\n** Pending feedback on the latest version of the DND template.","2026-01-08T12:51:23.252Z"],["3795946","SREC-364","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Created subtasks on the epic to mirror the current plan. Considering this task done.","2026-01-08T12:52:57.950Z"],["3795948","LSS-61280","LSS","marcis.bakis@bolt.eu","Mārcis Baķis","Thank you [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774], I’ll look into this 🙏 ","2026-01-08T12:53:14.695Z"],["3795954","LSS-60939","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Approved. ","2026-01-08T12:54:29.339Z"],["3795957","PFI-830985","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T12:55:38.588Z"],["3795961","PFI-830555","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:5fa511639e35e50068b366f0],\n\nThis [user|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/294817481] is fraudulent and therefore we have immediately blocked them. The user has followed the regular fraudulent patterns that we have seen before.\nExamples on ridehailing vertical: [Order1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1500787633/816?orderTryId=2856694180] ; [Order2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1501920899/816?orderTryId=2861600582] ; [Order3|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1502612294/816?orderTryId=2865590472] ; [Order4|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1503156789/816?orderTryId=2868621559]\nBy looking at the orders from [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A50%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_timestamp%22%3A1765197258%2C%22end_timestamp%22%3A1767909599.999%2C%22all_order_try_states%22%3Atrue%2C%22user_id%22%3A294817481%7D%7D], you can also see how the user has back2back expensive trips with the same driver.\n\nExamples from delivery vertical: [Order1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280660763?cityId=386&showUserTz=false] ; [Order2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280667301?cityId=386&showUserTz=false] ; [Order3|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280670982?cityId=386&showUserTz=false] ; [Order4|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280677592?cityId=386&showUserTz=false].\nMultiple attempts to get high value technology items from the stores\n\nThe user has not made any regular orders.\n\nAdditionally, the very same user is connected/related to this [user|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/282070529] whom has added a lot of different US credit cards and trying each of them out, however, all payments failed.\nOur systems asked the user to 3DS verify themselves, but failed every single time. This gives us enough grounds to believe that the users mentioned above are fraudulent, considering their connections and behavior patterns.\n\nDecision regarding the Post-Paid business will be left with you, however, please do note that the very same business is already at -8650€\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-08T12:56:27.405Z"],["3795963","BP-13383","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Tested in feature preview branch [+Bolt | Business+|https://business.prelive.bolt.eu/feature-BP-13167-use-semantic-colors/#/company/25870]  (/)\n\n||*Route*||*After [light mode]*||*After [dark mode]*||\n|verify-admin-email-change/:verification_hash|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.20.37.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.20.37.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.20.50.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.20.50.png\"!|\n|/accept-invite|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.48.34.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.48.34.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.50.56.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.50.56.png\"!|\n|/accept-invite/verify|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.53.18.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.53.18.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.53.06.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.53.06.png\"!|\n|/accept-invite/success|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.55.31.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.55.31.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.55.50.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.55.50.png\"!|\n|-/trip-control-approval-request-| | |\n|/tpa/:token|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.10.53.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.10.53.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.09.46.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.09.46.png\"!|\n|/tpa/:token/approved|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.11.37.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.11.37.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.12.04.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.12.04.png\"!|\n|/tpa/:token/rejected|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.14.16.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.14.16.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.14.42.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.14.42.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.14.05.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.14.05.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.15.04.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.15.04.png\"!|\n|/tpa/:token/error|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.38.20.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.38.20.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.38.32.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.38.32.png\"!|\n|-/documentation-| | |\n|/documentation/api|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.53.44.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.53.44.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.53.56.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.53.56.png\"!|\n|/documentation/api/coupons|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.50.40.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.50.40.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.52.20.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.52.20.png\"!|\n|/page-not-found/error page|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.08.01.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.08.01.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.08.13.png|width=199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 13.08.13.png\"!|","2026-01-08T12:57:11.909Z"],["3795964","WEBSD-1449","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:03b9dd47-a13b-4694-b2eb-fcd7e49b9c60] 👋 \n\nI started to work with the page but I would like to comment few things.\n\n1.- We cannot create tables (Current components) so you need to provide images for the tables and you need to localised them so they can be displayed in the languages you need.\n\n2.- There are few small changes I made to make the content fit with our current layout.\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.52.25.png|width=632,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.52.25.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.52.48.png|width=632,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.52.48.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.53.08.png|width=632,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 14.53.08.png\"!\n\n\n*Note: I believe such events maybe should be under blog but for now I will make the pa*ge 🙌 \n\nPlease let me know about the tables so I can add them. We can start with English for all but waiting for your comments.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-08T12:57:06.436Z"],["3795966","PFI-830966","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have checked the payment and I could not find any records of the refund being issued to the customer. Could you please try to issue the refund again? \n\nLet me know how it goes. If you are not able to issue the refund then the customer payments team could assist with issuing the refund from the Adyen portal. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-08T12:57:14.561Z"],["3795968","LSS-61281","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:8bcb68bd-f8da-4da1-8320-2536f6bb0c0c] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^1Bolt Holdings_Iceland rsk5.42 .pdf] ","2026-01-08T12:57:43.290Z"],["3795971","BB-2271","BB","ahmad.eldefrawy@bolt.eu","Ahmad ElDefrawy","I found the values hardcoded in [+IndirectTaxesHelper+|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/31a158dbd4d59c446387777e1913ce0e92579e4f/common/billing/helper/IndirectTaxesHelper.ts#L1] and used by [+VATCalculator+|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/31a158dbd4d59c446387777e1913ce0e92579e4f/common/billing/helper/VATCalculator.ts#L158] helper on the platform side, we will need to check our VAT calculations and test it with fiscalization","2026-01-08T12:57:53.049Z"],["3795973","PFI-830985","PFI","cristina.marcova@bolt-outsource.eu","Cristina Marcova","Invoice link\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"public_id\"%3A\"RO1525-46126\"}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22public_id%22%3A%22RO1525-46126%22%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-08T12:58:24.305Z"],["3795975","RS-1936","RS","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hello team, \n\nThank you for your assistance and guidance on it. \n\nThe invitation came with very short notice, and the vendor was already moving forward with logistics. I fully understand and respect the outcome. pawaPay is one of our payment service providers in African markets, and their communication style around partners tends to be quite informal. In this case, that made it harder for me to proactively gather a structured agenda or clearer business framing upfront. Would elements like a clearer agenda, defined business objectives, cost-sharing, or limiting attendance to non-entertainment parts materially assist on reviewing the assessment? Happy to take this as a learning point and also align on best practice\n\n*Just to add some concrete context I’ve since received from pawaPay*:\n\n*There are business-focused sessions planned on Wednesday morning (14 Jan, until ~13:00) covering introductions and high-level business reviews similar to a QBR-style discussion (current performance, operational feedback topics),* before the hosted event later in the day.\n\nFor proportionality context only, the estimated hospitality value for this trip (€700–1,200) represents *approximately 0.03%–0.06% of the annual fees we paid associated with this partnership.* \n\nSharing this to ensure the business agenda and proportionality elements are fully visible, and to understand whether this additional structure materially affects the assessment.\n\n*Accordingly to the information I got from pawaPay, this is the agenda expected:*\n\n^*Tuesday, 13 January*^\n\n* ^Arrival of participants^\n* ^Informal introductions^\n\nh3. ^*Wednesday, 14 January — Business Session*^\n\n^*09:00 – 13:00 | Partner Business Review Session*^\n\n^Structured working session with pawaPay representatives and partner attendees, covering:^\n\n* ^Overview of the current pawaPay operational setup^\n* ^Review of existing payment flows and performance in active markets^\n* ^Operational feedback and issue resolution discussion (what is working well / recurring challenges)^\n* ^Alignment on service quality expectations and communication processes^\n* ^Exchange of feedback on day-to-day collaboration and support models^\n\n^_(Session format comparable to a high-level QBR-style discussion.)_^\n\n^*13:00 – 20:00*^\n\n* ^Transition to venue^\n* ^Hosted attendance at stadium venue (hospitality provided by pawaPay)^\n\nh3. ^*Thursday, 15 January*^ \n\n* ^Optional city activities organised for the remaining attendees^\n* ^Group lunch and dinner for participants still in town^\n\nh3. ^*Friday, 16 January*^\n\n* ^Hotel check-out and departures^\n\n","2026-01-08T12:58:33.761Z"],["3795977","LSS-61282","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[^260108_ Bolt PoA_aze.docx] _(19 kB)_","2026-01-08T12:59:51.506Z"],["3795978","LSS-61082","LSS","maarja.nommets@bolt.eu","Maarja Nõmmets","Hello [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] !\n\n[~accountid:712020:714baa0e-ddd0-4776-8064-c5a5d3ae37aa] and [~accountid:712020:46ca1bd4-650e-4217-b42f-78a9deb502a3] have received a reference from a local supplier.  Please find below.\n\n\n\n[^Trade Reference - Bolt Operations UK Ltd.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T12:59:53.438Z"],["3795979","HS-27589","HS","keidi.helm@bolt.eu","Keidi Helm","Hi\n\nThe available amount for RTT monetization was 6.23. In November payslip you can see the accrued balance of 9.61, In December you accrue additional 0.67, in total 10.28. Pris/taken days 4.05 resulting in the balance of 6.23. \n\nKind regards\nKeidi","2026-01-08T13:00:08.883Z"],["3795980","PFI-813837","PFI","marius.poroseci@bolt-outsource.eu","Marius Poroseci","any updates?","2026-01-08T13:00:37.677Z"],["3795981","RISK2-3182","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","shared with LogicGate in slack [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09RH0NTS8J/p1767020641863229].\n\ndoc we shared: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1TwBh1qo4dSizzWukY9AK3omxeZRIRLXw3eoNAToUcR4/edit?gid=154974468#gid=154974468|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1TwBh1qo4dSizzWukY9AK3omxeZRIRLXw3eoNAToUcR4/edit?gid=154974468#gid=154974468|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T13:01:28.113Z"],["3795982","PAW-14727","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T13:01:36.812Z"],["3795983","PFI-830956","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nWe have confirmed the payment state with Fondy. The payment had gotten stuck due to technical issues. \nThe customer payments team has issued a refund and correct the payment state in Admin. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-08T13:02:47.694Z"],["3795985","LSS-47893","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] please help us to find the doc from Xapads, it was sent to Ahto. We will ask to send it again this week. ","2026-01-08T13:03:23.023Z"],["3795987","WD-22518","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi!\n\nThe mapping is created.","2026-01-08T13:03:57.949Z"],["3795988","MLC-1666","MLC","shubhi.agrawal@bolt.eu","Shubhi Agrawal","* *Status / Milestone:* in progress 83%\n* *Blockers:* none \n* *Status update:*\n** I had a discussion with Shreya regarding the “No Cars Available” use case. We discussed sending a generic push notification (e.g., “Try other categories”) to users who encounter no availability in a specific category.\n** I raised a concern about whether other categories might also face supply constraints, in which case such a notification could be ineffective. She mentioned that this typically does not happen, except in newly launched markets. I’ve requested data to validate this assumption.\n** Once we receive the data, we can analyze it and proceed with sending generic push notifications. In parallel, we can also request a “Supply Available” event to trigger more targeted communications \n* *Next Steps*\n** Analyse and evaluate data for no cars available event","2026-01-08T13:04:09.459Z"],["3795991","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","guglielmo.fontanarava@bolt.eu","Guglielmo Fontana-Rava Andreae","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] please check this folder [https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1YOBqkZ4BdUugaXPWlhruLETeuyAWXIdc|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1YOBqkZ4BdUugaXPWlhruLETeuyAWXIdc|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T13:04:52.914Z"],["3795993","RISK2-3181","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","this sheet to be shared with SMEs: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/10GApZEcu4ekV5VAxC57QCN0hV3VsnznfZ5ix7Z9_8Ts/edit?gid=706133237#gid=706133237|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/10GApZEcu4ekV5VAxC57QCN0hV3VsnznfZ5ix7Z9_8Ts/edit?gid=706133237#gid=706133237|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T13:05:20.128Z"],["3795996","LSS-61270","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:dbef963c-e707-4042-8024-5afb4c08aa16] please load a ticket for contract review on Legal Service Desk here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/1310/create/735|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/1310/create/735|smart-link] \n\nUnder *Please specify what support is needed.** ➡️ select Contract Negotiation - Supplier Agreement \n\nThanks ","2026-01-08T13:05:40.580Z"],["3795997","FX-3399","FX","katharina.skolimowski@bolt.eu","Katharina Skolimowski","Should the activity items (finished ride, rejected ride etc) be connected to the vehicle, or just some time slots when the vehicle was used?","2026-01-08T13:06:09.809Z"],["3796002","FX-3276","FX","anastasia.kaivel@bolt.eu","Anastasia Kaivel","Hi! What’s the progress on this one, and is there any input needed from the operations team side?","2026-01-08T13:07:12.282Z"],["3796003","RISK2-3194","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","Shared with LogicGate on 29.12 [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09RH0NTS8J/p1767020641863229]:\n\n* {{Avoid}} *->* We were thinking that instead of prompting an action, we prompt a description field and potentially have it go to our review dashboard.\n** [@Bobby|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U03UQEYULF4] do you have any recommendations here? We don’t want to create too many actions for people for every choice they make.\n** [@Bobby|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U03UQEYULF4] also, if a user chooses {{Avoid}}, do these risks automatically go to the {{Inactive Risks Register}}?\n* {{Reduce}} -> User needs to input a Control in LogicGate. [@Sujith|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U03UQBS230B] currently this asks for an Action not a Control. Should it be changed?\n* {{Transfer}} -> We were thinking of just having a description box here and no action.\n* {{Accept}} -> We were thinking of just having a description box here and no action and having a dashboard that has a table report for Accepted, Transferred, Reduced and Avoided risks respectively.","2026-01-08T13:07:23.530Z"],["3796010","HS-28725","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:f46637ae-bde8-4da4-b9dd-de99fa5298b5], the confirmation letter is sent for signing. Once it’s signed, you will recieve it on your personal e-mail. Let us know if there is anything else we can help you with. Closing this ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-08T13:09:02.882Z"],["3796012","HS-28078","HS","bohdana.kalytchuk@bolt.eu","Bohdana Kalytchuk","Hi [~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0] \nAs far as I know it wasn’t Anton who requested it. Can you please check where this request came from?","2026-01-08T13:09:52.936Z"],["3796013","SREC-367","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","COS version might be out of date as well, update to the latest stable version if needed.","2026-01-08T13:10:22.040Z"],["3796014","LSS-61105","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Thanks [~accountid:5f17f7301084620015f4972a] for coming back to me.  It’ll be next week before I can consider the driver’s claims for lost earnings.  However, if there is no valid reason for the driver’s account being suspended and this been wholly our error, can he be reinstated asap please?  If his claims for lost earnings plus interest are valid, these will continue to increase for as long as he is suspended.  Thanks. \n\ncc. [~accountid:5dde532fcdc2d20d05377446] [~accountid:60c7025b5c64b10071aef787] ","2026-01-08T13:10:36.151Z"],["3796015","PFI-806303","PFI","augustas.baublys@bolt-outsource.eu","Augustas Baublys","Thank you for your reply. However, some solution must be found now, because the driver receives two different invoices for the same period, so how should he choose which one is correct, because in this case, the driver will have to write to us every time and we will have to forward it to you.","2026-01-08T13:10:42.173Z"],["3796016","DSR-3157","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","* Awaiting update regarding safety block. *Hopefully early next week*\n* Redacted rider and driver tickets prepared [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/18n8B-FW88q4mYROkT2YFQg520FDK9aQo] (_Rider report - 1_ has a call summary. Do we keep this?)\n* Response [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/18n8B-FW88q4mYROkT2YFQg520FDK9aQo]\n* All driver personal data including call recordings, average rating, acceptance rate, invoices added [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/1ylv7CD7GMnDsnQAvUDVoDhWUpSHEn6KR]. Invoice exports ([1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-bulk-invoice-download/item/1680007/view],[2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-bulk-invoice-download/item/1380022/view],[3|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-bulk-invoice-download/item/1470032/view],[4|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-bulk-invoice-download/item/1380023/view])","2026-01-08T13:10:49.762Z"],["3796018","EBIKE1-420","EBIKE1","aare.palm@bolt.eu","Aare Palm","[~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390] \n\n{quote}Alone, it could mean that there is a disturbance in CAN communication to the lock, right?{quote}\n\nTrue, it could me that. But this behavior just backed up my assumption. My diagnosis is made based on indirect symptoms. And there are two symptoms that back my hypothesis,","2026-01-08T13:10:50.881Z"],["3796019","RISK2-2640","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","22.12. iRisk questionnaire shared with Kadi (Sustainability) for feedback.\n\n05.01. iRisk questionnaire shared with Maarja (Procurement) and Paula (Legal Operations).\n\n08.01. Agreed during S2P call that Maarja can send it out to SMEs for populating. Call notes [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1f2f8dyKItZ_KH78EWRd99MUKmAx0yxiJYQIRkHVOGv0/edit?tab=t.0].\n\nAgreement made to support Procurement as needed, if anything needs to be clarified with the guidance.","2026-01-08T13:11:07.095Z"],["3796021","LSS-60650","LSS","maksims.kostenko@bolt.eu","Maksims Kostenko","Hey [~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] and [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] \nThank you for the comments and review. I have wrote Mono back with all the comments and eng version and added both of you to cc. \nLet me know if something else needed from me, otherwise I will let you know once we have an answer. \n","2026-01-08T13:11:40.112Z"],["3796024","PFI-806303","PFI","augustas.baublys@bolt-outsource.eu","Augustas Baublys","Attaching the invoices which were received by driver for the same period of time.\n\n[^LT1125-53250.pdf (abf31a31-78b8-46ba-9961-ff6765ae389b).pdf]\n[^LT1125-56200 (1).pdf (b801c05a-b334-4e61-b897-9a9948d161d8).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T13:12:01.996Z"],["3796025","EBIKE1-420","EBIKE1","aare.palm@bolt.eu","Aare Palm","[~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390] \n\n{quote}Any idea why this did not qualify as E1?{quote}\n\nWorks as expected. If hatchlock is opened then no communication issues are reported. Because it is undefined if battery is expected to be inserted or not.","2026-01-08T13:12:01.105Z"],["3796028","LSS-53508","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hello, [~accountid:5c010fa68ce9b546efc49454]! Yes, please arrange with Anna Sala / Karolina Jędrzejczak from Workspace a shipping of the original docs (two counterparties) to Tallin Office to be signed, each by Ahto. One signed counterparty should be kept at Bolt and the other one to be sent back to the City of Gdańsk.  \n\nI am opening a ticket for signing to Legal Ops.","2026-01-08T13:12:10.795Z"],["3796030","RISK2-3185","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","Access Matrix to be reviewed: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1m_R3ozky9DaIkCemNVMbM91XhAiKMPR7/edit?gid=1342593391#gid=1342593391|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1m_R3ozky9DaIkCemNVMbM91XhAiKMPR7/edit?gid=1342593391#gid=1342593391|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T13:12:43.856Z"],["3796031","PLUS-17","PLUS","daniil.aksim@bolt.eu","Dan Aksim","[~accountid:61386b180016a700697b9436] server side","2026-01-08T13:12:45.037Z"],["3796033","HS-28078","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:53e3735f-5982-4573-b427-e00ef719a47e], \n\nI am sorry, I think we need to forward it to [response@veroscreening.com|mailto:response@veroscreening.com]. Can you scan the signed version of the document and add it [here|https://bolt.box.com/s/zd2qk8etbukcgla8i0djtpbwmuggqfr6] so that I could send it to them? \n\nBest regards, \n\nKerilin ","2026-01-08T13:13:16.007Z"],["3796034","L10N-26517","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.381Z"],["3796035","L10N-26527","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.403Z"],["3796036","L10N-26516","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.455Z"],["3796037","L10N-26522","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.516Z"],["3796038","L10N-26520","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.536Z"],["3796039","L10N-26523","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.521Z"],["3796040","L10N-26524","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.536Z"],["3796041","L10N-26515","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.623Z"],["3796042","L10N-26513","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.648Z"],["3796043","L10N-26514","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.702Z"],["3796044","L10N-26528","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.709Z"],["3796045","L10N-26526","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.873Z"],["3796046","L10N-26518","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.885Z"],["3796047","L10N-26519","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.990Z"],["3796048","L10N-26525","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:27.981Z"],["3796049","L10N-26521","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:28.021Z"],["3796050","L10N-26507","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.076Z"],["3796051","L10N-26501","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.142Z"],["3796052","L10N-26500","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.147Z"],["3796053","L10N-26505","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.208Z"],["3796054","L10N-26502","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.224Z"],["3796055","L10N-26496","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.375Z"],["3796056","L10N-26493","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.404Z"],["3796057","L10N-26503","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.417Z"],["3796058","L10N-26497","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.472Z"],["3796059","L10N-26512","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.551Z"],["3796060","L10N-26494","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.545Z"],["3796061","L10N-26511","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.598Z"],["3796062","L10N-26509","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.606Z"],["3796063","L10N-26510","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.719Z"],["3796064","L10N-26499","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:33.808Z"],["3796065","L10N-26495","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:34.072Z"],["3796066","L10N-26508","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:34.350Z"],["3796067","L10N-26498","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:35.729Z"],["3796068","L10N-26504","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:36.477Z"],["3796069","L10N-26506","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:13:37.049Z"],["3796070","LSS-60257","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Hi [~accountid:62ff8d58b582d07a14a96588] Is there anything else you need on this?  If not, I will close the ticket. \n\nThanks","2026-01-08T13:13:38.779Z"],["3796071","WFM-9888","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601594","2026-01-08T13:14:01.488Z"],["3796076","EBIKE1-420","EBIKE1","aare.palm@bolt.eu","Aare Palm","[~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390] Superb analysis, well done 🙂 ","2026-01-08T13:14:17.289Z"],["3796077","LSS-53508","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","[~accountid:5c010fa68ce9b546efc49454] do you know the address of the City where we should send back the signed agreement? ","2026-01-08T13:14:27.052Z"],["3796078","FX-3276","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","[~accountid:618538f7bcb57400681fb581]I linked another dev ticket a comment below, it is in progress","2026-01-08T13:14:34.570Z"],["3796079","MLC-186","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 2*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:* Dropping email Open Rates\n* *Status update:*\n** *Data collections:* collecting data on optimised HTML\n*** *Conclusion:* the optimised storytelling template continues to perform well at higher volumes, with stable open rates.\n*** [+Data+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P7lI3QszzlC88QY1_Dgjzuz5xYflUxKkrRBvF0aSb4E/edit?gid=558325371#gid=558325371]\n** *Updating stakeholders:* Shared a status update in the #temp-email-template-issues Slack channel.\n*** *Pending:* ETA from the Web team on updating the HTML builder tool → this will unblock the whole department from rolling out the template.\n*** *Next step:* Updating the LCM department in #auto-comms-support (department-level Slack channel)\n** *Replicating storytelling template in drag-and-drop*\n*** Running an additional test (owned by [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327]) on 8 December\n*** *Main feedback from last time:* paddings\n*** *Next step:* Working on integrating the newest light green footer with DND. Currently, the formatting breaks → troubleshooting and testing.\n* *Next steps:*\n** *Mapping the next steps for storytelling rollout:*\n*** Fixing already existing templates + next communications to work on.\n** *Replicating storytelling templates in drag-and-drop*\n*** If the last test goes well, share an update with the whole department. There’s also interest from other teams to start using this.","2026-01-08T13:14:40.106Z"],["3796081","LSS-61285","LSS","bianca.alvesdeandrade@bolt.eu","Bianca Alves de Andrade","[^Branding Contract - Bolt Club Fleet BSH Fahrdienst GmbH.pdf] _(168 kB)_","2026-01-08T13:14:55.777Z"],["3796082","PFI-829288","PFI","illia.drobzhev@bolt-outsource.eu","Illia   Drobzhev","Hello, team.\n\nAre there any updates regarding this request?","2026-01-08T13:14:56.711Z"],["3796083","PFI-830935","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 69.40 EUR on 21/11/2025, 14:34:06UTC\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 72700925325156041343755  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 21st of November until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Proof of Refund 21-11-2025.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-08T13:15:12.336Z"],["3796084","PFI-830997","PFI","martin.brzek@bolt.eu","Martin Brzek","!Snímek obrazovky 2026-01-08 v 14.15.06.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T13:15:15.905Z"],["3796085","PFI-806303","PFI","daumantas.butvila@bolt-outsource.eu","Daumantas Butvila","Not needed, driver was registered in two accounts, so both invoices are correct and should be used","2026-01-08T13:15:24.174Z"],["3796086","PFI-806303","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-08T13:15:28.037Z"],["3796087","MLC-3755","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*26W2 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** Finalized all new subject lines with the content team.\n** Submitted localisation tickets for new subject lines (linked in ticket description).\n* *Next steps:*\n** Set up the A/B tests. ETA to launch next week.","2026-01-08T13:15:28.189Z"],["3796088","PFI-829673","PFI","sera.teng@bolt.eu","Sera Teng","Hi, \n\nwould you know why this commission is taken from the weekly payout so late? the FOP doesn't even update accordingly and so the FO thinks there has been a mistake with the payout. Is it possible for this deduction to take place with more time before crediting?\n\n","2026-01-08T13:15:35.839Z"],["3796089","LSS-59991","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] !\n\nI prepared the following response to Sofia and Alexandros. Could you please take a look at it and let me know if you consider it is fit to send it today? Please feel free to do any changes and suggestions! Many thanks!\n\n///// \n\nHello Sofia and Alexandros,\n\nMany thanks for your response regarding CapitanSpec and the integration requests that we use at Bolt.\n\nIn relation to this matter, we have the following comments:\n\n# We continue to agree that it is a business decision to grant or deny a vendor the possibility to integrate to Bolt via API. There is no law that we know of, obliging Bolt to grant access to everyone that requests it.\n# Bolt Food is not a dominant player in the Cyprus market, and therefore has no reinforced obligation to grant access to its system.\n# Given that Bolt has granted access to various third party integrators (CaptainSpec being only one of them), Bolt would not be favouring any particular provider with the aim of restricting competition in the market, or to impede the entry of new players (such as Evolution) to the market.\n# In connection with Trojan Economics’ email, even if they are mentioning that they will file a complaint against Bolt before the Competition Authority, we do not see any major risk if they finally proceed with the complaint, for the reasons mentioned above. \n# A possible future scenario could be a requirement from the Competition Authority asking Bolt to provide explanations on their decision-making process for accepting new vendors. If this arises, we believe that we are in a good position to answer an eventual requirement by the Competition Authority.\n\n\n\nIn light of the above, we suggest that you reply to the email sent by Trojan Economics, in an amicable and open manner. Below you will find a suggestion of the wording for the response. Please feel free to adapt the wording, according to your context.\n\n“Dear Panayiotis,\n\nMany thanks for your message, which we have shared with our internal legal department.\n\nAligned with their analysis and in connection with your questions, please be advised:\n\n# As we have already informed your clients, we are open to integrate new vendors and aggregators to Bolt Food via API, who will need to:\n\n* Meet the requirements listed in Bolt’s [developer portal|https://developer.bolt.eu/] which is of public access and can be consulted at any time.\n* Fill in the following form (see [here|https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSez67FYBsYWLieW7DcC03hMkZSUnaN0EQZY9LdTkpVpJ8SkJg/viewform]) \n* In addition to the above, Bolt analyses each request on a case-by-case basis to understand whether there are any particular technical needs for the onboarding, and if the potential vendor is attractive from a business perspective. In all cases, Bolt reserves the right to accept or deny the requests.\n\n\n\n# In the case of your clients Christos Hirodontis and Rodionas Papadopoulos, please note that:\n\n* We have received their request to integrate via API. \n* After analysis from our integrations team, we concluded that we do not yet envisage their integration to Bolt Food, as their business is still in a very early stage, and it would require significant time and effort from the Technical Support team — including creating a test setup, providing daily support, answering technical questions, and conducting test calls.\n* We have repeatedly communicated our reasons to your clients, and we look forward to reviewing their case once their business is in a more developed stage.\n* As expressed above, according to our business metrics and perspectives, we reserve the right to accept or reject requests from third parties.\n\n\n\n# Finally, from an antitrust perspective, Bolt Food:\n\n* Does not hold a dominant position in the market\n* Does not develop a public service or an essential facility\n* Is not obligated by law to grant indiscriminate access to its services to third parties\n* Has business autonomy and liberty to decide whether to engage or not with third parties. \n\n\n\nWe trust that this information is sufficient to clarify our position, and that it will avoid any further discontent with your clients.\n\n\n\nKind regards,”","2026-01-08T13:15:41.414Z"],["3796091","LSS-54620","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nI have sent another message to confirm receipt. \n\nThanks.","2026-01-08T13:15:58.653Z"],["3796092","MLC-3612","MLC","nida.altug@bolt.eu","Nida Altuğ","h3. *Week 2*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* done\n* *Blockers:*\n* *Status update:*\n** Will share the reach data and results to benchmark for decision making next year.","2026-01-08T13:16:10.085Z"],["3796096","CSXPC-292","CSXPC","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","Turns out each request type also has subcategories that the user needs to choose. These should also reflect in the Beehive ticket with supportCaseCreate comment.\n\nInfo about subcategories is available on page 5 + 6 of this doc: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/12hlliH9OupKeeKMkI6XkC6cZwiOtw5Htp49IwPSujLs/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/12hlliH9OupKeeKMkI6XkC6cZwiOtw5Htp49IwPSujLs/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-08T13:16:35.785Z"],["3796097","PAW-14722","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17071\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-08 13:16:41 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-08T13:16:42.416Z"],["3796099","WEBSD-1434","WEBSD","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","Additional info: \n\nTurns out each request type on the webform also has subcategories that the user needs to choose. These should also reflect in the Beehive ticket with supportCaseCreate comment.\n\nInfo about subcategories is available on page 5 + 6 of this doc: [+https://docs.google.com/document/d/12hlliH9OupKeeKMkI6XkC6cZwiOtw5Htp49IwPSujLs/edit?tab=t.0+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/12hlliH9OupKeeKMkI6XkC6cZwiOtw5Htp49IwPSujLs/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-08T13:17:36.572Z"],["3796100","FX-3399","FX","felicia.vincentio@bolt.eu","Karissa Vincentio","How common it is for drivers to drive more than one vehicle during the day?\n\n* 1 - 1,1% daily proportion, or\n* 4,5 - 5,3% weekly (proportion of one driver drives more than 1 vehicle per week)","2026-01-08T13:17:46.617Z"],["3796103","PFI-830874","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for RON 182.20 on Dec 16, 2025, 21:25:42 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 74987505350003651707085 to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 16th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_RS4VHFCWS6S7NKZ3_KG9M3DDQ7ZJSRBG6.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-08T13:18:33.230Z"],["3796105","MLC-2609","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 2*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:* None\n* *Status update:*\n** *Home_city_ID rollout:* Identity team is working on rolling out the city ID (WIP)\n*** *Followed up on the current status:* The Identity team had to pause the backfill for existing Riders during the holiday season because of the high traffic during that period. They need a couple of days to finalise it.\n*** [Slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0669RP1EMS/p1767706310641039]\n* *Next steps:*\n** *Data validation:* Once the full rollout has been completed, pick up data validation topic with MarTech.\n** *Context:* In Q4, I got in touch with MarTech to discuss how we can validate that everything’s in order on our side as well, once the home city ID has been updated.\n*** No response at that time, but also, it wasn’t urgent then → will follow up \n*** [+Slack thread+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNH34A2BY/p1765549837953819]","2026-01-08T13:18:50.625Z"],["3796107","FX-3276","FX","anastasia.kaivel@bolt.eu","Anastasia Kaivel","Right, I mean, is there any approximate ETA so we can roughly consider it while planning vehicle separation in the UK? ","2026-01-08T13:19:07.637Z"],["3796109","SREDESK-7385","SREDESK","andrus.viik@bolt.eu","Andrus Viik","Please find AWS app here https://bolt.okta.com\r\nas you are a member of a different team you have a separate group `FinanceAnalytics` but same permissions as DWH team has at dataeng account.\r\n ","2026-01-08T13:19:27.927Z"],["3796110","LSS-60122","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:46ca1bd4-650e-4217-b42f-78a9deb502a3] hey, in such a case we won’t have the option to decide on the termination unilaterally in any case, but I propose to amend the lease to say that *they can't refuse to sign the termination documents* if we ask for termination. Can you please discuss this with the landlord?","2026-01-08T13:19:33.778Z"],["3796111","SREDESK-7391","SREDESK","kourosh.tafreshi@bolt.eu","Kourosh Tafreshi","Sent 2 keys in DMs.","2026-01-08T13:20:01.609Z"],["3796112","HS-28747","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi! Assigning this ticket to you as it’s about a referral bonus :heart_hands: ","2026-01-08T13:20:09.149Z"],["3796115","HS-28651","HS","aleksandra.makarova@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Makarova","Hey [~accountid:712020:dc4824f4-a6bc-41f2-af89-59d155dc0cc8] ! \n\nWe need to update a new start date for March 16th 2026 instead. Gloria is receiving the new Blue Card on 13.01.26, confirmed with [~accountid:619df381744c4d0069b3deed] that once she receives we should send her contract by 16.01.26. Would it be possible to prepare everything. Once she has submits her new visa we would like to proceed further asap. Would you be able to make sure we are on time?\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 15.19.18.png|width=868,height=328,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 15.19.18.png\"!\n\nKind regards,\n\nAleksandra Makarova","2026-01-08T13:20:37.719Z"],["3796116","PFI-819772","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Payout already allocated","2026-01-08T13:21:02.391Z"],["3796119","MLC-3297","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 2*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:* None\n* *Status update:*\n** *Campaign end date:* {{2026-01-11}}\n*** After that, all banners will disappear from the app.\n*** Currently live: map view banner + vertical banners\n** *Data collection*\n*** Planned for week 3.\n*** Sub-task created: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-3794|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-3794|smart-link] \n** *Rewind 2025 Retrospective*\n*** Call between LCM, Brand and MarTech to discuss what went well and what can be improved next time.\n*** Happening on {{2026-01-09}}\n* *Next steps:*\n** Collecting data and sharing the results with stakeholders + within LCM.\n*** [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-3794|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-3794|smart-link]","2026-01-08T13:22:42.275Z"],["3796124","LSS-60050","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","I have verified the signatures through the [governmental website|https://www.gov.pl/web/gov/podpisz-dokument-elektronicznie-wykorzystaj-podpis-zaufany] and it turns out that the signature of the counterparty is valid but the ours is not valid (in PL: “*_status: nieważny_*”)… I don’t know what is going on with it. Afaik Dokobit signatures are qualified e-signatures. Could you please [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] confirm that our Dokobit signature put on this agreement is valid?\n\n!image-20260108-132233.png|width=899,alt=\"image-20260108-132233.png\"!","2026-01-08T13:23:07.936Z"],["3796125","BD-1970","BD","ave.tarend@bolt.eu","Ave Tarend","Reports are now confirmed by courier team to work correctly: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08T2Q5KASH/p1767878089156219?thread_ts=1767598680.227809&cid=C08T2Q5KASH|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08T2Q5KASH/p1767878089156219?thread_ts=1767598680.227809&cid=C08T2Q5KASH|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T13:23:09.554Z"],["3796132","MICRO-298","MICRO","ping.li@bolt.eu","Ping Sheng Li","[~accountid:712020:248d279a-85db-4438-8af9-d236e6e661d5] Okay in that case this is low prio. But we can keep this in mind if we have pressure from cities that this Allow pause in no parking areas is too liberal so we limit it to certain users. ","2026-01-08T13:24:33.689Z"],["3796134","DBRE-8586","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Alter automation issues:\n* missing master\n* gh-ost process killed during alters\n* missing prelive: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1767875192153139|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1767875192153139|smart-link] \n* Lost control on cut-over status: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1767877459920349|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1767877459920349|smart-link] \n* Multiple gh-ost processes running on the same cluster: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1767877459920349|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1767877459920349|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T13:24:50.495Z"],["3796136","PFI-831000","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customers' order was cancelled before we managed to capture the payment. Since the there was no payment we are not able to refund them. \nThe customer might mean the authorization has not been released instead. \n\nI have checked the case and can confirm everything looks line on Bolts end. The authorization has been released. \nYou can advise the customer to confirm with their bank if the authorized funds have been released. The customers bank is able to locate the funds with the authorization date and amount. \n\nPlease also refer to this KB article \n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-08T13:26:03.161Z"],["3796137","PAW-14728","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T13:26:45.435Z"],["3796140","HS-28738","HS","richmond.lartey@bolt.eu","Richmond Sammy Lartey","Thanks for the feedback team","2026-01-08T13:27:09.736Z"],["3796145","PFA-496","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","Completed until SSF","2026-01-08T13:28:01.196Z"],["3796146","WFM-9895","WFM","aurelija.jovani@bolt-outsource.eu","Aurelija Jovani","Lithuania, Latvia, Estonia, Croatia, Sweden, Norway, Finland, Netherlands, Denmark","2026-01-08T13:28:01.704Z"],["3796147","LSS-61259","LSS","raphael.perna@bolt.eu","Raphaël Samy Perna","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]. Please do not hesitate to reach out if you have any questions, and I look forward to your update.","2026-01-08T13:28:02.795Z"],["3796148","PFI-831007","PFI","daniel.tirca@bolt.eu","Daniel-Cosmin Tîrcă","[^op bolt pt nov 2026.pdf]","2026-01-08T13:28:05.747Z"],["3796149","L10N-26567","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26566](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26566)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T13:28:20.532Z"],["3796150","L10N-26569","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26566](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26566)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T13:28:20.967Z"],["3796151","L10N-26573","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26566](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26566)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T13:28:25.614Z"],["3796153","L10N-26572","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\