"L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:55.498Z"],["3796187","L10N-26505","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:55.663Z"],["3796188","L10N-26502","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:56.882Z"],["3796189","L10N-26501","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:57.281Z"],["3796190","L10N-26500","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:57.441Z"],["3796191","L10N-26499","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:57.447Z"],["3796192","L10N-26495","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:57.488Z"],["3796193","L10N-26493","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:57.696Z"],["3796194","L10N-26496","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:57.955Z"],["3796195","L10N-26494","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:58.018Z"],["3796196","L10N-26497","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:58.293Z"],["3796197","L10N-26498","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:28:58.356Z"],["3796198","SREDESK-7389","SREDESK","andrus.viik@bolt.eu","Andrus Viik","is there any existing project we can reuse {{itgc-google-audit}} doesnot exist","2026-01-08T13:29:00.705Z"],["3796200","PFI-830745","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nThe refund has failed. Our partner does not store refund details. We can ask our partner to issue the refund again, however we need the customers refund details. \nCould you please ask the customer to provide the following.\n\n*Bank name:* \n*Account name:* \n*Account number:*\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-08T13:29:12.272Z"],["3796202","WD-22485","WD","janeli.niinemaa@bolt.eu","Janeli Niinemaa","Hey, So I have done the first check for the expenses and these are the 3 categories that I   would like to be mass cancelled:\n * Expenses by prior workers in progress up to 31.08.2025 and all drafts\n\n* Drafts in amount 0 up to 31.08.2025\n* And all remaining old expenses in progress or in draft status up to 2024 end\n\nI have also added the excel files with all such expenses. \n\n[^Pior worker up to 2025.xlsx]\n[^Old items up tp 2024 end.xlsx]\n[^Drafts in 0 amount up to 31-08-25.xlsx]\n\n","2026-01-08T13:29:33.383Z"],["3796203","MLC-3683","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 2*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:*\n* *Status update:*\n** *Sending out an ad-hoc to dormant users in FR*\n*** *Campaign results:*\n**** Total sends: 385,784\n**** Open rate: 19.06%\n**** Conversion rate: 0.27%\n*** Kudos to [~accountid:712020:5ee0b1d5-3b9b-4a48-826c-fce4ef2d1492] for taking ownership of this during the holiday season!\n* *Next steps:*\n** *Planning the next steps for Q1:* Aligning on the experiment we planned for Q1.\n** *Updating Jira:* Updating this Jira epic with more context around the project.","2026-01-08T13:29:44.805Z"],["3796204","HS-28613","HS","ingrid.valgejarv@bolt.eu","Ingrid Valgejärv","Had a meeting with Confido team too.","2026-01-08T13:29:53.842Z"],["3796205","PFI-830997","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:f2dff8f9-836f-4a9a-8a1b-99464efc239f],\n\nThese 3 orders are highly suspicious.\nThey are back2back trips with bonuses included, and the trips have taken less then 1 minute to complete (extremely short distances). These are also cash orders, therefore the driver does not lose anything here besides the bonuses.\nIf the driver does not have any similar precedents, then this time do manually compensate them for the loss of bonus earnings, however, also leave a comment about this on their profile. Next time if something similar happens we will most likely remove their cash payment option.\n\nBest,\nMarten\n","2026-01-08T13:30:01.356Z"],["3796207","WFM-9905","WFM","gaurav.singh@bolt-outsource.eu","Gaurav Singh","!image-20260108-132843.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T13:30:17.024Z"],["3796208","LSS-61157","LSS","mikk.vachtmeister@bolt.eu","Mikk Vachtmeister","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] , any updates about this one?","2026-01-08T13:30:46.792Z"],["3796209","PAW-14470","PAW","mihai.casandra@bolt.eu","Mihai Casandra","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/12Mx_zmePEjTuWXiGvYUfwmwlee1sKMJuUksWdm_ypyk/edit|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/12Mx_zmePEjTuWXiGvYUfwmwlee1sKMJuUksWdm_ypyk/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T13:31:06.981Z"],["3796210","PFI-830735","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-08T13:31:14.200Z"],["3796212","PFI-830731","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-08T13:31:30.364Z"],["3796214","PFI-830713","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 366.00 ZAR on 04/12/2025, 07:19:14UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 1st of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-08T13:32:27.274Z"],["3796215","FRAUDOPS-1108","FRAUDOPS","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","likely ~93% TP rate - weekly\n\nlikely ~96% TP with higher multipliers, 5 less triggers, 2 less CS tickets avoided - weekly. Sticking with 2, 1.9, 1.85, 1.75, 1.65, 1.6","2026-01-08T13:32:28.838Z"],["3796216","WD-22415","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Thanks [~accountid:623ace37b75ca80070562c04] , the Canada pay periods needs to be updated too:\n\n!image-20260108-133111.png|width=713,alt=\"image-20260108-133111.png\"!\n\n\nat the moment its only once a month. Evgenia wrote to us today\n\n!image-20260108-133203.png|width=713,alt=\"image-20260108-133203.png\"!\n\nThank you!!\n\ncc: [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] ","2026-01-08T13:32:29.804Z"],["3796218","PFI-830744","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:4e933f7c-b064-4b4d-aa81-af221a3d370c],\n\nThe user’s current payment method is currently not available at this time.\nPlease advise them to use another payment method in the meantime.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-08T13:33:17.390Z"],["3796220","MLC-3830","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*26W2 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** Received context for the initiative. \n* *Next steps:*\n** Prepare comms setups for the local teams to use.\n** Share an update in the channel with ETAs.","2026-01-08T13:33:24.693Z"],["3796221","PFI-822230","PFI","barbora.trstenicova@bolt-outsource.eu","Barbora Trsteničová","Please, any update? ","2026-01-08T13:33:25.063Z"],["3796223","PFI-830701","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 69.00 ZAR on 04/12/2025, 16:01:37UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 2nd of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-08T13:34:07.431Z"],["3796225","LSS-61124","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nThank you. I have asked them to make this adjustment.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-08T13:34:26.285Z"],["3796227","LSS-59991","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f],\n\nThank you very much for handling this. I’m fully aligned with your response -please feel free to share it with Alexandros and Sofia.\n\nTHANK YOU SO MUCH!💚 ","2026-01-08T13:35:02.162Z"],["3796231","PFI-830696","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 229.96 ZAR on 22/11/2025, 11:20:56UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 21st of November until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-08T13:35:43.243Z"],["3796234","LSS-61182","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:cc9fc6f2-33e3-41d1-a4e5-1587e9f47322],\n\nThanks for your request. Given this potential agreement requires potential repayments to drivers, we are adding FinReg to this ticket.\n\n[~accountid:712020:29d8b602-d17f-40cd-9cae-5653bc2c54b7] [~accountid:624469dd45ece00069c967bd] : as an initial step in this request, could you kindly advise if you see this agreement works as it is conceived, and that it does not have any risks from a financial regulation perspective? \n\nMany thanks!\n\nAngela ","2026-01-08T13:36:42.324Z"],["3796236","PFI-829456","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","please raise with partner payment.","2026-01-08T13:37:33.344Z"],["3796237","PFI-829456","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-08T13:37:39.286Z"],["3796239","LSS-61157","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:10c3f4ef-f975-47a3-8af8-927b01cd9521] signature is ok, we will ask Legal Ops to sign from our side ","2026-01-08T13:38:15.174Z"],["3796241","WFM-9906","WFM","aurelija.jovani@bolt-outsource.eu","Aurelija Jovani","EDIT:\nAlso [margarita.jakovleva@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:margarita.jakovleva@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n","2026-01-08T13:38:48.992Z"],["3796242","PFI-831009","PFI","norbert.kato@bolt.eu","Norbert Kato","!Képernyőfotó 2025-11-25 - 12.47.04.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Képernyőfotó 2025-11-25 - 12.47.45.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Képernyőfotó 2025-11-25 - 12.56.03.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T13:38:54.127Z"],["3796243","PFI-831009","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T13:38:56.123Z"],["3796246","PFI-830692","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:4d97afd5-d8a8-4dea-9263-8e4189aeecc3],\n\nThis simply means that the aforementioned cards needs more trips done with it.\nPlease note that we do not want to give out information on how many trips exactly the user needs done, therefore, simply advise them to use that specific card for a couple of weeks or so and then try again.\nAs internal information, I can confirm that currently they are restricted simply because of the amount of trips, however, please do not forward this information on to the user.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-08T13:39:53.292Z"],["3796247","PFI-828695","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","please raise with partner payment team.","2026-01-08T13:39:56.901Z"],["3796248","PFI-828695","PFI",null,"Automation f