r all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26566](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26566)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T13:43:46.530Z"],["3796298","L10N-26608","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26566](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26566)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T13:43:48.265Z"],["3796299","DSR-3241","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","* PDE started [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/personal-data-export/exports/1267111?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] (*except communications plugin*)\n* Contacted French SIS in Slack - *block maintained*\n* Response [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TGBTneeHCKvNCFVl7gvQY3lvF0AuEy2JLLfywXg5JHY/edit?tab=t.0]\n* Redacted driver and rider ticket [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/127JoIX4rc3bj8TfizE4y56Dh-A7Ruf11]\n* No call recordings, fleet driver and average rating doc created [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/19BgQVk8I2i4Op5zmBmyPJDMCarREX6Ov]","2026-01-08T13:43:57.398Z"],["3796301","BEE-3602","BEE","michal.bielecki@bolt.eu","Michał Bielecki","Assigning this to myself to do the research if we want to expose more tiers there (it’s backend driven).","2026-01-08T13:44:18.603Z"],["3796302","WFM-9906","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Country permission: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571647","2026-01-08T13:44:31.491Z"],["3796303","PFI-830883","PFI","agne.majauskaiteshah@bolt-outsource.eu","Agnė Majauskaiteshah","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"created_from\"%3A1764540000%2C\"created_to\"%3A1767218399%2C\"is_source_of_truth\"%3Atrue%2C\"to_agent_type\"%3A\"ride_hailing_driver\"%2C\"to_agent_id\"%3A7841212%2C\"system_type\"%3A\"ride_hailing\"%2C\"invoice_type\"%3A\"ride_hailing_bolt_partner_aggregated\"}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22created_from%22%3A1764540000%2C%22created_to%22%3A1767218399%2C%22is_source_of_truth%22%3Atrue%2C%22to_agent_type%22%3A%22ride_hailing_driver%22%2C%22to_agent_id%22%3A7841212%2C%22system_type%22%3A%22ride_hailing%22%2C%22invoice_type%22%3A%22ride_hailing_bolt_partner_aggregated%22%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-08T13:44:41.996Z"],["3796306","PAW-14729","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @udankobolt\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160119\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-08 13:45:00 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-08T13:45:00.428Z"],["3796308","WFM-9906","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Country permission: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571648|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571648]","2026-01-08T13:45:31.888Z"],["3796311","SREDESK-7390","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","The schema is create in Prelive/Ti-incentives cluster","2026-01-08T13:47:21.870Z"],["3796312","PAW-14731","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T13:47:36.461Z"],["3796313","LSS-61140","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks all - This is quite a tight timeline indeed. \n\nI have taken a look from the privacy side and wanted to first confirm the following (?) \n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n{color:#4c9aff}*QUESTIONS*{color}\n\n# Are the only datapoints we are sharing about French drivers here: (i) their VTC numbers; and (ii) confirmation of whether they are attached to a fleet or not?\n# We will be hashing these datapoints on the Bolt side, using a sha-256 algorithm, before sharing them with the APRE (given that this is required in the agreement)?\n{panel}\n\nIf the above is correct, then technically we are sending *_pseudonymised_* (rather than anonymised) data to the APRE. The reason that this difference is important is that pseudonymised data still counts as personal data under the GDPR (which triggers data protection obligations wen sharing it) - As such, although the data sharing here is overall low risk (and is something we can do), it is not non-existent.\n\nI have therefore suggested the following amendments to the agreement ([+*LINK*+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T3Ti5hjEhwtC0sI-Xg3Dquan20quYtX0/edit]):\n\n* *Removed Recital (D) / Edited Clause 3.2* → Previously, these clauses said that we agree that the data is not personal data. For the reason set out above, this is not accurate. As such, we should not be agreeing to this - doing so would actually undermine the applicability of most of the obligations in the agreement. I would be surprised if the APRE pushes back on this.\n* *Inserted Clauses 10.2* *& 12.5* → In the (unlikely) event that the APRE suffers a data breach that concerns the data we are sharing with them, the affected drivers would most likely come after Bolt rather than the APRE. We should therefore try and include some provisions which protect Bolt in such circumstances, by: (i) requiring the APRE to notify us of these incidents; and (ii) give Bolt financial recourse if anything goes wrong. I have included explanatory comments in the document explaining this.\n\nI would recommend the next steps from the privacy side:\n\n{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}\n{color:#6554c0}*NEXT STEPS*{color}\n\n# Put these edits to the APRE, with the explanatory comments provided in the document, and see if they will accept them. \n# If the APRE pushes back, then (noting that we will be sharing the data on Monday and so are subject to a very strict timeline) we can take a risk-based approach and: (i) *permit the removal of Clauses 10.2 & 12.5* (as overall the data sharing is low risk and the agreement only lasts for one month); but nevertheless (ii) we should *still push for removing Recital (D) / editing Clause 3.2*, because as discussed these are not accurate and should not be accepted.\n{panel}\n\nI otherwise have no additional comments, but let me know if you have any questions 🙂 ","2026-01-08T13:48:08.948Z"],["3796315","WFM-9907","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Country permission: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541634","2026-01-08T13:48:10.163Z"],["3796316","LSS-60349","LSS","ban.beidas@bolt.eu","Ban Beidas","Hi [~accountid:61693adbbfa2c1006b54680d] ! I will take a look at these and get back to you early next week!","2026-01-08T13:48:19.109Z"],["3796317","LSS-61215","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Advice provided n the parent ticket ✅ ","2026-01-08T13:48:27.592Z"],["3796318","MLC-3472","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*26W2 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** TBC tomorrow, but no major updates this week\n* *Next steps:*\n** Start prepping results overview, ETA Monday","2026-01-08T13:48:38.735Z"],["3796319","WFM-9907","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Hey [~accountid:61515e3c64ff010071e17133], \r\n\r\nAgents received access now. Give the system 20 minutes to sync. \r\n\r\nHave a great day!","2026-01-08T13:48:55.573Z"],["3796320","RDXENG-4304","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","(/) *Tested on CI.217.0 and OK.*\n\n{{addCard}} containing {{\"preferred_scheme\" : \"no_preference\"}}.","2026-01-08T13:49:24.370Z"],["3796321","WFM-9906","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Hey [~accountid:712020:3a3742eb-3298-4df7-a8af-c0fd7279bf95], \r\n\r\nAccess granted. Give the system 20 minutes to sync. \r\n\r\nHave a good day!","2026-01-08T13:49:24.855Z"],["3796323","PFI-831018","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T13:49:28.518Z"],["3796324","MLC-3300","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*26W2 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** In-app stories will end this week (on the 11th).\n** Retrospective meeting tomorrow.\n* *Next steps:*\n** Compile campaign stats next week.","2026-01-08T13:49:42.127Z"],["3796329","WEB-8509","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] \n\nCould you please review the feedback in the [file|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1tjwRMPfWRLlKW49QO2ihdb_5p0IW1WVTEXntxe2v86Y/edit?usp=sharing]. \n\nPlease let me know if there’s anything I can help with 🙏 \n\nNext steps:\n\n* Sharing the final prototype with stakeholders (no further feedback is expected at this stage)\n* Design handover to Engineering","2026-01-08T13:51:02.588Z"],["3796331","RDXENG-4305","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","(/) *Tested on CA.192.0 and OK.*\n\n{{addCard}} containing {{\"preferred_scheme\" : \"no_preference\"}}.","2026-01-08T13:51:39.549Z"],["3796334","GRWA-1315","GRWA","getter.poru@bolt.eu","Getter Põru","Will be done in product team in Q1 '26","2026-01-08T13:53:00.698Z"],["3796337","LSS-61288","LSS","stephanie.oreoluwa@bolt.eu","Stephanie Oreoluwa","[^20260108 VEHICLE-HAILING SERVICE PARTNERSHIP AGREEMENT-BOLT APP SUPPORT NIGERIA LIMITED (1).docx] _(60 kB)_","2026-01-08T13:53:31.658Z"],["3796341","MLC-3423","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 2*\n\n* *Context of the project/initiative:* Multiple initiatives to support the expansion and growth of the Bolt Plus membership.\n* *Status / Milestone:*\n* *Blockers:* None.\n* *Status update:*\n* *Uplift validation: Experiment on Plus-ready modals*\n** [+Confluence page+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7018905601/2025-11+Bolt+Plus+Plus-ready+modal+experiment]\n** *Status:* {color:#36B37E}*[ EXPERIMENT RUNNING ]*{color}\n** *Tentative ETA for results:* January 2026, but it also depends on the enrolments\n** *Monitoring the enrolments*: more time is needed to draw conclusions.\n** *Updating the Confluence page:* ensuring everything’s up to date (WIP); including got in touch from MarTech so they’d ensure the same from their side.\n* *Acquisition flow improvements*\n** Received copies back from the proofreader.\n** *Implementation:* 26Q1\n*** *Reason behind stalling:* Initially, writing the content was blocked by the Content team + LCM is having issues with the newest template.\n** *Next step:*\n*** Setting up the comms templates once the HTML builder tool is updated.\n*** Requesting localisations.\n* *Hopp Plus launch*\n** *Technical preparations:* Got in touch with the Bolt Plus Engineering team to pass the necessary events and Custom Attributes with the correct brand value to the Hopp workspace in Braze.\n*** [Slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09FF7S5JV9/p1767697226236519]\n** *Hopp Plus logo:* Getting in touch with the Brand team on {{2026-01-09}} to get a logo for our emails.\n* *2026 planning*\n** Call with Spencer and Food LCM to review the potential items for Q1 2026.\n* *Bolt Plus – Market Scale Launch Plan*\n** *Context:* Vertical Marketing is preparing a document for the Product team to provide context on the amount of heads-up time Marketing would need to launch a set of markets. Product team is thinking about how we can potentially speed up and decentralise launching additional Bolt Plus markets (not possible to decentralise).\n** Reviewed the document, provided feedback from our side.\n*** [Link|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JIN5wBe6PDIiR3xYdydEBSw7BKWoQ_zKn78_FY9RPCg/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.1x39olxk8a66]\n* *Bolt Plus Marketing KPIs*\n** *Context:* Vertical Marketing is working on a reporting system for market launches.\n** Reviewed the potential report from our side, provided feedback.\n* *Drop-offs in user journeys*\n** *Context:* Product team provided a Figma with the user journeys for Bolt Plus. The goal is to understand where the drop-offs are and based on that, map out potential action items for the future.\n** Reviewed the Figma from our side, provided feedback. \n** [Slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C089FNNR3A8/p1767029840000879]\n* *Comms audit*\n** Reviewing Bolt Plus auto comms to ensure everything’s good → in Q4, there were so many changes and launches, so I’d like to ensure nothing slipped through the cracks (and if it did, we’re now on top of it).\n* *Next steps:*\n** *26Q1 items:* Getting full clarity and starting on the projects planned for 26Q1, including continuing to prepare for the upcoming market launches and creating a new Jira epic.\n** *Uplift validation: Experiment on Plus-ready modals*\n*** Monitoring the enrolments.\n** *Bi-weekly sync with Vertical Marketing*","2026-01-08T13:54:16.488Z"],["3796351","LSS-59845","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nWe aim to start with a USD 32,544 commitment, realistically scaling up to a maximum of USD 81,724 annually.\n\nI have added you to the InfoSec ticket here [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ISS-1119|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ISS-1119|smart-link] \n\nI am also attaching the draft Order Form, which is subject to change, as we have requested an update to the pricing.\n\nThank you.\n\n\n\n[^Draft Sentry Order Form for Bolt (4M Errors + Growth Tiers).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T13:58:02.623Z"],["3796353","L10N-26520","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.180Z"],["3796354","L10N-26518","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.261Z"],["3796355","L10N-26526","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.411Z"],["3796356","L10N-26524","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.443Z"],["3796357","L10N-26517","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.451Z"],["3796358","L10N-26512","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.498Z"],["3796359","L10N-26511","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.511Z"],["3796360","L10N-26521","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.516Z"],["3796361","L10N-26514","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.586Z"],["3796362","L10N-26527","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.591Z"],["3796363","L10N-26516","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.680Z"],["3796364","L10N-26510","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.679Z"],["3796365","L10N-26525","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.709Z"],["3796366","L10N-26519","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.691Z"],["3796367","L10N-26509","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.761Z"],["3796368","L10N-26528","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.768Z"],["3796370","L10N-26515","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.861Z"],["3796371","L10N-26522","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.859Z"],["3796372","L10N-26513","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.925Z"],["3796373","L10N-26523","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:27.947Z"],["3796374","L10N-26499","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:30.431Z"],["3796375","L10N-26506","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:31.180Z"],["3796376","L10N-26507","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:31.217Z"],["3796377","L10N-26502","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.463Z"],["3796378","L10N-26500","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.489Z"],["3796379","L10N-26495","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.592Z"],["3796380","L10N-26501","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.593Z"],["3796381","L10N-26508","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.606Z"],["3796382","L10N-26497","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.666Z"],["3796383","L10N-26503","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.741Z"],["3796384","L10N-26494","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.771Z"],["3796385","L10N-26496","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.822Z"],["3796386","L10N-26505","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.903Z"],["3796387","L10N-26504","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.888Z"],["3796388","L10N-26498","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:32.915Z"],["3796389","L10N-26493","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-08T13:58:33.292Z"],["3796392","FRAUDOPS-286","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/968245790/18|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/968245790/18]\n\nthis is the original example. driver did the ride and finished with a price of 1 euro through a manual correction. ","2026-01-08T13:59:23.352Z"],["3796393","PC-4769","PC","alexey.efimov@bolt.eu","Alexey Efimov","Micromobility team going to change behaviour and start using {{use_balance: false}} for flow pass buy & order ride.","2026-01-08T13:59:44.749Z"],["3796395","FRAUDOPS-286","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","{code:sql}WITH negative_corrections AS (\nSELECT DISTINCT\ntpr.order_try_id,\ntpr.city_id \nFROM ng_public_spark.company_order_try_price_row tpr\nWHERE tpr.created_date >= date '2025-11-01'\nAND tpr.type = 'correction'\nAND COALESCE(tpr.price, 0) < 0\n)\nSELECT \ni.meta.order_id,\ni.meta.city_id, \nget_json_object(i.input,'$.data.order.payment_method.type') AS payment_method_type\nFROM sel_fraud_checks_pii_spark.driver_overcharge_check i\nJOIN negative_corrections nc ON nc.order_try_id = get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.order.order_try_id') AND nc.city_id = i.meta.city_id\nWHERE i.created_date >= date '2025-11-01'\nAND ((ROUND(\n  2 * 6371000 * ASIN(\n    SQRT(\n      POW(SIN( (RADIANS(CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.driver_location.arrived_to_destination.lat') AS DOUBLE)\n                           - CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.client_location.destination.lat') AS DOUBLE)))/2 ), 2)\n      + COS(RADIANS(CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.client_location.destination.lat') AS DOUBLE)))\n        * COS(RADIANS(CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.driver_location.arrived_to_destination.lat') AS DOUBLE)))\n        * POW(SIN( (RADIANS(CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.driver_location.arrived_to_destination.lng') AS DOUBLE)\n                           - CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.client_location.destination.lng') AS DOUBLE)))/2 ), 2)\n    )\n  ),\n  0\n) < 300)) -- real destination vs requested destination < 300 meters\n--OR CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.actual_info.duration_in_min') AS REAL)/CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.prediction_info.duration_in_min') AS REAL) >= 0.7 -- at least 70% of predicted duration passed\n--OR CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.actual_info.distance_in_meters') AS REAL)/CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.prediction_info.distance_in_meters') AS REAL) >= 0.7) -- at least 70% of predicted distance driven\nAND CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.actual_info.price') AS REAL)/CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.prediction_info.price') AS REAL) < 0.3\nLIMIT 1000{code}\n\nran the above to check orders that had a final price below 30% prediction and that were finished within 300m of the requested destination. only got 10 rows as result. \n\nthe scheme is sound. drivers could easily abuse us into not paying commission by using this strategy, but apparently, they don’t. ","2026-01-08T14:00:34.711Z"],["3796396","HS-28534","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountid:5e4655bb691b8a0c95c27708], we haven’t heard from you in a while. \n\nIf you’d like to keep this request open or have any additional information, please leave a comment, and we’ll get back to you as soon as possible.\n\nIf we don’t hear from you soon, we’ll proceed with closing the ticket, but feel free to reopen it anytime if needed.","2026-01-08T14:00:39.100Z"],["3796397","BEE-3618","BEE","michal.bielecki@bolt.eu","Michał Bielecki","Idea is to start measuring the time of Sinch client initializing successfully/failing on the frontend and propagating to mixpanel to at least understand the volumes of this types of issues.","2026-01-08T14:00:43.652Z"],["3796399","LSS-61288","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-08T14:01:19.211Z"],["3796400","PFI-830944","PFI","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Hey, [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea]\n\nWhen I hover over the “delete account” button and “archive” button, I see different views:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 15.59.43.png|width=460,height=361,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 15.59.43.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 16.01.19.png|width=485,height=360,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 16.01.19.png\"!\n\nPlease review the case one more time 🙏\n\n*Can we forgive the user for the “unpaid order”?*","2026-01-08T14:02:13.754Z"],["3796401","DO-5774","DO","moustafa.aboulatta@bolt.eu","Moustafa Aboulatta","Thanks Felix, I missed the DAG being turned off and I didn’t know that I have to turn it manually.\nThank you!! ","2026-01-08T14:02:19.001Z"],["3796402","SRED-985","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done. Developers stuck with delivery_provider_metadata, so I'll remove it later(c).\n\nUPD: Usage removed this week, so all unused redises removed.","2026-01-08T14:03:22.469Z"],["3796406","LSS-55043","LSS","triin.soonkoster@bolt.eu","Triin Soon-Köster","Hi, they shared that they prefer to sign it in DocuSign and they can initiate the process. To whom should we address this from our end? To Ahto (and [signing@bolt.eu|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] in cc)?\n\n","2026-01-08T14:03:46.146Z"],["3796407","PFI-830970","PFI","liisa-ingrid.kerson@bolt.eu","Liisa-Ingrid Kerson","Please also opt out the dept balances","2026-01-08T14:04:12.128Z"],["3796410","FRAUDOPS-1058","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","What do we want to see? This case is built with the idea of France. \n\n# Fleets with a lot of drivers with comments and that fleet GMV\n## From which drivers bad GMV comes from - comment drivers?\n# Partners with multiple comments across different driver profiles \n## The partner GMV + bad GMV\n# Drivers/Partners leading up to comment pattern\n\n----\n\nProblem 1 is that some comments are recorded across all partner profiles looking like each of those profiles has a comment on the driver level but it is the same incident. So let’s say there is a partner with 5 profiles then it looks like there are 5 comments.\n\n* I’ve managed to cover this issue via reading unique comments only regardless of the driver level. ✅ \n\nProblem 2 Checked also tickets with similar reports and it seems the France as the inspiration uses alternative comms, infopip not beehive. There was barely any reports in support tickets. \n\n* Excluded tickets from the case \n\n\n\n----","2026-01-08T14:04:27.293Z"],["3796411","LSS-61282","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^PoA_Bolt Services AZ LLC_Mammadov_Aliyev_Majidli_Hasanli_Bayramov_Adilzade_Karimova_08.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T14:04:36.311Z"],["3796413","BEE-3618","BEE","piotr.musiol@bolt.eu","Piotr Musioł","[https://developers.sinch.com/docs/in-app-calling/js/release-notes|https://developers.sinch.com/docs/in-app-calling/js/release-notes|smart-link] \n\n* Improve error messages thrown when Sinch client fails to start due to push related problem.\n\n\nwe should also bump version of Sinch Client to the latest one","2026-01-08T14:05:35.334Z"],["3796417","FX-3583","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767881171540519]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3583] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T14:06:25.589Z"],["3796419","LSS-57372","LSS","dominik.lopuch@bolt.eu","Dominik Lopuch","Hi [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] want to ask you if document is still live? I’m going to visit the partner in person tomorrow so want to be sure that link works, thanks.","2026-01-08T14:07:04.699Z"],["3796422","PAR-3839","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","[@narmin.mammadli|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b] I just released the change, Please let me know if you noticed unexpected behaviour or the rate of unmatched increased","2026-01-08T14:07:28.254Z"],["3796424","SREP-1036","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* EKS upgraded \n* Kube-proxy bumped \n* Node reprovisioned:\n* !image-20260108-140728.png|width=754,alt=\"image-20260108-140728.png\"!\n\nNo issues so far ","2026-01-08T14:07:42.061Z"],["3796426","DO-5774","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","No worries 😉 ","2026-01-08T14:07:45.455Z"],["3796431","PFI-826411","PFI","rufana.guliyeva@bolt-outsource.eu","Rufana Guliyeva","Hello,\n\nCan you help us upload proof of payment? We don't have access.","2026-01-08T14:09:54.135Z"],["3796432","MTE-1275","MTE","sergei.drondin@bolt.eu","Sergei Drondin","[~accountid:6321aad6cf721d09b0166767] I created the transformation and attached it to the Google Ads Offline Conversions Delivery destination","2026-01-08T14:10:02.057Z"],["3796434","PIF-3209","PIF","yevgeniy.mechsheryakov@bolt.eu","Yevgeniy Mechsheryakov","Such link already exists","2026-01-08T14:10:29.949Z"],["3796435","C3HW-75","C3HW","endrik.salak@bolt.eu","Endrik Salak","Prototype order ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1080/HWINT-232|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1080/HWINT-232|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T14:10:30.475Z"],["3796436","EBIKE1-400","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] I think that I have the majority of the vehicle detection features in place.\n\nPlease review the following documents which have been updated: \n\n*_Note:_* _A flowchart has been implemented into the vehicle configuration matrix document which should make it more understandable how the whole vehicle detection flow should work, therefore I would recommend having a look at that flowchart and CAN protocol draft in parallel for better understanding_\n\n[Vehicle configuration matrix|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LdBVIMrFiteme1ryWymSexsqez-BniHRaoh4RlZbwGY/edit?gid=0#gid=0]\n\n[CAN protocol DRAFT|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ViBWdXE3ZClJHqfVkYKCjJzaXmene84RIG5uSACidbU/edit?tab=t.0]\n\n\n\nThere is also one open topic already from my side which also needs Your input:\n\n# How should the controller behave when it is in “Vehicle type not detected” state?\n## Should it report ALL errors?\n### The controller must perform vehicle detection after each power cycle because it might have been moved from one vehicle to another for example. If some vehicles do not use primary vehicle detection and they have a broken motor or broken torque sensor, then vehicle detection is not possible.\n#### In such cases it is not known as to which vehicle the controller must behave (scooters can start reporting hall sensor errors etc). How to handle such cases?\n\nIn my opinion, the controller should report all errors in this case and IoT should make _an educated decision_ how the situation is handled.\n\nAfter You have reviewed the documents, I propose to set up a meeting to go through the feature together as well.\n\nIf we think that the application is good enough, we should also get input from [~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390]'s FAE team.","2026-01-08T14:10:30.896Z"],["3796438","FX-3584","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767881430499589]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3584] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T14:10:42.397Z"],["3796440","HS-28749","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:619e65173618cd006f8b68c9],\n\nPlease send me your Work Certificate(s) (Świadectwo Pracy) from your previous employer(s). If you worked outside of Poland and your previous employer does not issue Work Certificates, please send an Employment Confirmation letter signed by a representative of that company.\n\nBest regards, \n\nKerilin","2026-01-08T14:11:07.236Z"],["3796441","PIF-2353","PIF","razvan.nastase@bolt.eu","Răzvan Năstase","{quote}Separately, if you open any commit in Github, you can see the PR which introduced the commit. Example for commit: [+ca16a7981064806e4e92b4eb2ee59e702f4ce4a8+|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/commit/ca16a7981064806e4e92b4eb2ee59e702f4ce4a8], check the top header for {{develop(#159433)}}, it’s a link to [+the PR+|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159433].{quote}\n\nThis is sufficient, thank you! We can close this ticket.","2026-01-08T14:11:25.737Z"],["3796442","PFI-827161","PFI","helio.cheong@bolt.eu","Hélio Cheong","Hello [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e],\n\nHope you are doing well.\n\nI have received the following feedback from the client’s finance team:\n\n“Unfortunately, the documents you provided are not accepted by our financial services as official bank documents, even though they are stamped. Due to the VOP system, the process has become more stringent, and the fact that the documents do not include the bank’s official letterhead (only a footer) raises some concerns.\n\nWe kindly ask you to try to obtain an official IBAN confirmation document from the bank for each account, instead of the confirmation letters previously shared.”\n\nCould you please help us by providing an official IBAN certificate or confirmation document issued directly by the bank (with official letterhead) for each IBAN?\n\nThank you very much for your support.\n\n","2026-01-08T14:11:38.363Z"],["3796446","WFM-9905","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, role granted. Is there a need for him to see support volume page? If yes, please provide queues he should be assigned for","2026-01-08T14:11:47.235Z"],["3796447","LSS-61268","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Audit confirmation letter_Bolt Services AZ LLC_ABB_08.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T14:12:03.410Z"],["3796448","PFI-827169","PFI","helio.cheong@bolt.eu","Hélio Cheong","Hello [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e],\n\nHope you are doing well.\n\nI have received the following feedback from the client’s finance team:\n\n“Unfortunately, the documents you provided are not accepted by our financial services as official bank documents, even though they are stamped. Due to the VOP system, the process has become more stringent, and the fact that the documents do not include the bank’s official letterhead (only a footer) raises some concerns.\n\nWe kindly ask you to try to obtain an official IBAN confirmation document from the bank for each account, instead of the confirmation letters previously shared.”\n\nCould you please help us by providing an official IBAN certificate or confirmation document issued directly by the bank (with official letterhead) for each IBAN?\n\nThank you very much for your support.","2026-01-08T14:12:04.218Z"],["3796449","PAW-14470","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-njsc-db, pint-product-backend-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-08T14:12:04.578Z"],["3796450","PIF-3242","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-component-builder, pint-product-continuous-integration-and-deployment-platform, pint-capability-ci-cd\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-08T14:12:09.606Z"],["3796451","SRED-928","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, all updated","2026-01-08T14:12:16.976Z"],["3796452","RDS-1352","RDS","andres.tack@bolt.eu","Andres Jaan Tack","Confirmed with [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9]  — this idea is *not* a priority for 2026 and Uppsala, because it’s literally not doable (NordicPort has not implemented an API to accept documentation). We will go manual.\n\nAccordingly, dropping this to lowest priority. If we furthermore find out that this isn’t going to be a systematic problem across tenders, we will close it “Won’t Do.”","2026-01-08T14:12:24.419Z"],["3796454","EBIKE1-367","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","The drafts are ready and waiting for [~accountid:5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] feedback.\n\nThe following documents have been updated: \n\n*_Note:_* _A flowchart has been implemented into the vehicle configuration matrix document which should make it more understandable how the whole vehicle detection flow should work, therefore I would recommend having a look at that flowchart and CAN protocol draft in parallel for better understanding_\n\n[Vehicle configuration matrix|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LdBVIMrFiteme1ryWymSexsqez-BniHRaoh4RlZbwGY/edit?gid=0#gid=0]\n\n[CAN protocol DRAFT|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ViBWdXE3ZClJHqfVkYKCjJzaXmene84RIG5uSACidbU/edit?tab=t.0]\n\n\n\nThere is also one open topic already from my side which also needs input:\n\n# How should the controller behave when it is in “Vehicle type not detected” state?\n## Should it report ALL errors?\n### The controller must perform vehicle detection after each power cycle because it might have been moved from one vehicle to another for example. If some vehicles do not use primary vehicle detection and they have a broken motor or broken torque sensor, then vehicle detection is not possible.\n#### In such cases it is not known as to which vehicle the controller must behave (scooters can start reporting hall sensor errors etc). How to handle such cases?\n\nIn my opinion, the controller should report all errors in this case and IoT should make _an educated decision_ how the situation is handled.","2026-01-08T14:12:36.042Z"],["3796455","PFI-827168","PFI","helio.cheong@bolt.eu","Hélio Cheong","Hello [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e],\n\nHope you are doing well.\n\nI have received the following feedback from the client’s finance team:\n\n“Unfortunately, the documents you provided are not accepted by our financial services as official bank documents, even though they are stamped. Due to the VOP system, the process has become more stringent, and the fact that the documents do not include the bank’s official letterhead (only a footer) raises some concerns.\n\nWe kindly ask you to try to obtain an official IBAN confirmation document from the bank for each account, instead of the confirmation letters previously shared.”\n\nCould you please help us by providing an official IBAN certificate or confirmation document issued directly by the bank (with official letterhead) for each IBAN?\n\nThank you very much for your support.","2026-01-08T14:12:38.473Z"],["3796456","WFM-9827","WFM","michael.wanjiku@bolt-outsource.eu","Michael Wanjiku","Thank you\n\n","2026-01-08T14:12:44.903Z"],["3796458","L10N-26619","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26609](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26609)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T14:13:22.985Z"],["3796459","L10N-26618","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26609](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26609)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T14:13:23.369Z"],["3796460","L10N-26621","L10N",null,"Autom