eep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26609](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26609)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T14:13:31.486Z"],["3796468","L10N-26634","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26609](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26609)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T14:13:32.206Z"],["3796470","L10N-26637","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26609](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26609)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T14:13:33.631Z"],["3796471","L10N-26640","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26609](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26609)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T14:13:34.913Z"],["3796472","L10N-26639","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26609](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26609)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T14:13:35.322Z"],["3796476","PIF-2353","PIF","cristian.lupu@bolt.eu","Cristian Lupu","I’ve rejected the proposal of rewriting commit messages with PR info then 🙂\n\nIn case this request appears again, it’s worth noting that git flow is {{commit}}(s) then push then create a PR\n\nAn automation would need to rewrite already pushed commits, which I don’t believe we want to.\n\nAt the very least, such an automation would invalidate the local branch of the developer due to the rewritten commits.","2026-01-08T14:13:58.129Z"],["3796477","PFI-813997","PFI","anastasija.lagusnika@bolt-outsource.eu","Anastasija Lagusnika","Hey! \n\nWe noticed a conflict in reporting.  Fleet portal showed a balance of -€56.42, while the Admin panel showed -€33.12. Why is there a discrepancy between these two ?\n\n","2026-01-08T14:14:03.948Z"],["3796479","LSS-61271","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Audit confirmation letter_Bolt Services (ZA) Pty Ltd_First National Bank_08.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T14:14:10.080Z"],["3796481","PFI-830944","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f],\n\nInteresting, now when I opened it up again I see the same as you mention.\nNot sure what happened there. Even via our simulations the user did not get stuck.\nJust to be on the safer side, we added the user to the whitelist nevertheless.\nKindly note that it may take until tomorrow (9th January) before the changes within rule go live.\n\nMarten","2026-01-08T14:14:16.313Z"],["3796482","FRAUDOPS-286","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","turns out I’ve found out that the overcharge check doesn't have the price with driver correction in it. correction happens after it seems.\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/968245790/18?orderTryId=1143342396|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/968245790/18?orderTryId=1143342396]\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/driver_overcharge_check/65209701|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/driver_overcharge_check/65209701]\nactual price shows 80.9, but it was 1 with the driver correction\n\nwill re-run the above price, but using price from company_order_try instead of overcharge input for the actual_price","2026-01-08T14:14:27.638Z"],["3796483","LSS-61272","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Audit confirmation letter_Bolt Services CA Inc._Airwallex_08.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T14:14:52.151Z"],["3796484","PFI-830556","PFI","rita.goncalves@bolt.eu","Rita Teles Gonçalves","Hi team, do you have any updates to this request? Thank you","2026-01-08T14:15:01.988Z"],["3796486","SREP-1037","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* EKS upgraded\n* Kube-proxy bumped\n* Node reprovisioned, no issues so far \n!image-20260108-141519.png|width=604,alt=\"image-20260108-141519.png\"!","2026-01-08T14:15:31.082Z"],["3796487","LSS-60660","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (08.01)*+\n\n* Auth team consulted [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06R63EQ6CS/p1766054874981439].\n** Phone number removed from the account. As a result, “_user 122661268 will lose access to this account. The user will be able to access this account logging in with the Google account linked to the Bolt account_” (i.e. Chase cannot access the account - this is fine, as Chase has been informed and offered a copy of their data, and they seem fine wit the result).\n** “_Only the user who setup Google social account in May 2022 may have access to this account and setup a new phone number there. The user who setup Google social account is quite likely the original user who created this account who hasn't been active in this account since Sep 2025_”.\n* Thoughts:\n** Based on the facts, it is extremely unlikely that Lukas is the user that set up the Google account, given that the issue is only from last year whereas the Google account was created a few years prior. Given that the phone number has been removed, it appears that Lukas has no other means of accessing the account. As such, the unauthorised access appears to no longer be ongoing, and so this matter can be considered as {color:#36b37e}*resolved*{color} ✅ ","2026-01-08T14:15:32.484Z"],["3796488","FX-3584","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Ernests Rudzītis [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767881724037689]*{color}:\nI checked his state logs in the admin profile. He we online at ~15:00 and continued his work till the end of day according to logs\n{quote}","2026-01-08T14:15:37.008Z"],["3796489","FX-3583","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767881723220979]*{color}:\n<@U05A7SK0P8B> this and the following might be due to [this|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02ESLTCH70/p1767094256112359], if they had scheduled rides!\n\nLinked messages:\n[December 30th, 2025 3:30 AM] carlo.fanton: hello, i am investigating [this|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0576CT9MQD/p1767026453789239] and it looks to me that we have an issue about displaying correct values of driver activity: the online time we show in *drivers performance* page (:one:) does not match the online time we show in the *detailed driver activity* page (:two:)\n\n:one: *driver performance* page data [screen 1] is computed via , that either goes to or tables, based on cutoff date (2024-11-01)\n    ◦ more about this in [this doc|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/6339919969/2025-05+Driver+Performance+Insights] =&gt; simpler approach is to get data from online-hours table\n:two: *detailed activity* page [screen 2] gets data via flow, that AFAIU computes the timeline for building the UI. That timeline is built based on timestamps of driver state changes. And then aggregated to compute the driver online-activity breakdown.\n\nIdeal solution would be to find the reason of mismatching, but I guess that this would imply heavy investigations/rework since :two: queries very different sources (order-history, dispatch-pref) than :one:.\n\nPossible alternative: for the *Activity Summary*, just fetch the same data as :one:\nFor \"hourly overview\" and \"detailed activity\" keep calculations as it is\n• we need state change granularity to build timeline\n• mismatch would be very less noticeable, as i doubt a FO would sum all the little timings on their own\nthoughts?\n{quote}","2026-01-08T14:15:37.772Z"],["3796492","LSS-60660","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:d94524c3-94e8-4fa9-95f2-5afd20cbd32c] - In which case, given that it it appears that Lukas no longer has any means of accessing the account at-issue (although do correct me if I am wrong), we can consider this matter as *resolved* for now. I will therefore close the ticket ✅ \n\nLet me know if anything further is needed from my side 🙂 ","2026-01-08T14:16:49.386Z"],["3796493","DPM-2289","DPM","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","Hey [~accountid:712020:a5a9bde0-6d51-468a-85a6-ee3e42b31f73] , I am thinking about other strings like options, option groups, categories, etc. We need to be able to submit all of these in any one language, not just item names and descriptions. Let’s include this into the ticket’s scope","2026-01-08T14:16:57.977Z"],["3796494","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","Can you please also give me a reference to your handler?","2026-01-08T14:16:58.514Z"],["3796496","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","Path to a file is enough","2026-01-08T14:17:15.612Z"],["3796498","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","Also. are these cases related to this issue?\n\n{quote}1. Hey! This <https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8305087?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FLondon|driver{quote}\n\n> didn't get his payment from flex on Monday. I know there has been some delays in flex payments recently, but usually this would be paid by now. Would you know what the issue would be with this?\n\n{quote}2. Another <https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/240424?tab=profile|driver{quote}\n\n> who hasn't received payment for the last 5 weeks from flex, can this also be looked into?\n\n{quote}3. This <https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8153655?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FLondon|driver{quote}\n\n> is having the same issue of not receiving flex payment, bank details were updated in hub and payment still not sent/received\n\n{quote}4. these two drivers <https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8420956|1{quote}\n\n>, [2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8208657] - they are also having the same issue. It is saying no payment, or £0 from our side, but on their side, it is saying they have money to cash out\n\n{quote}5. we have <https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8353931?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FLondon|another{quote}\n\n>\n\n[@ahmed.farghaly|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63fc5f040a4a47fb8d20cf92]","2026-01-08T14:18:53.001Z"],["3796499","BD-1965","BD","ave.tarend@bolt.eu","Ave Tarend","In progress. Changes will be done both in server repo and admin-panel side.","2026-01-08T14:19:54.810Z"],["3796500","LSS-61009","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Thank you for the context and further information, [~accountid:712020:62f06c58-8a02-4e87-b219-9d3a11c1c4fb], [~accountid:60f2a71843c956007065f2ad]. I have provided my comments and suggestions to the draft proposals. Please let me know if you have any questions or require further support. I understand that the voting on the draft will happen on 14th of January. Due to time pressure it won’t be possible to engage the external legal counsels for this task, but we can engage them in case the authorities will be cooperative following the review of current proposals.","2026-01-08T14:20:48.428Z"],["3796501","DSR-3589","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-08T14:21:09.252Z"],["3796502","DPM-2162","DPM","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","I’d like more details here, please. Can’t figure out the priority of the ticket otherwise","2026-01-08T14:21:18.205Z"],["3796505","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","This is the handler {{SyncPayoutClientOnDriverCreated.ts}}\nI believe yes we don't send payout if client-account not exist","2026-01-08T14:21:34.957Z"],["3796507","DO-5767","DO","kostiantyn.tsykulenko@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Tsykulenko","it’s same service desk but it’s a different team within DAP (Insights), so you need 2 separate tickets","2026-01-08T14:22:33.880Z"],["3796508","DPM-2289","DPM","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] Sure, I will provide soon a new estimation taking into count the extended requirements. The previous scope was 95% done and I started testing it, just FYI.","2026-01-08T14:22:38.029Z"],["3796509","DBRE-8218","DBRE","andrei.fedorov@bolt.eu","Andrei Fedorov","fixes implemented in [https://github.com/bolteu/db-tiup-mirror/pull/39|https://github.com/bolteu/db-tiup-mirror/pull/39|smart-link] \n\nnow we reuse the mirror, that should make manifest maintenance work as expected ","2026-01-08T14:22:38.916Z"],["3796510","LSS-61289","LSS","dovile.zykute@bolt.eu","Dovilė Zykutė","[^Bolt Services LT, UAB Subtiekėjo sutikimas.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T14:22:50.346Z"],["3796512","LSS-59295","LSS","ivan.falco@bolt.eu","Ivan Falco","Hello [~accountid:712020:209f6e12-e421-4fbf-9a9f-60d100117bab] we worked with the videographer to create three additional ads from the initiative, which would help further promote the topic across the driver community.\nPlease have a look at them in the Slack convo [here|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/GDEAZHCUV/p1767866962761729?thread_ts=1761757991.229719&cid=GDEAZHCUV], these should be fine as they are based on the already validated video. Could you please give us the green light so we can finalise them?\nThanks!\n\n","2026-01-08T14:23:11.009Z"],["3796513","LSS-60970","LSS","kai.vainola@bolt.eu","Kai Vainola","this is not a ticket for corporate legal. Please make sure to create a correct ticket.","2026-01-08T14:23:21.535Z"],["3796517","BEE-3629","BEE","michal.bielecki@bolt.eu","Michał Bielecki","[~accountid:641aac4c5534b0bf74419b31] could you please create design task for yourself and link it to this story?","2026-01-08T14:23:56.429Z"],["3796518","XP-3036","XP","yaroslav.morozevych@bolt.eu","Yaroslav Morozevych","h2. Results [[PR|https://github.com/bolteu/data-experimentation/pull/1114]]\n\n* Doubled the {{gunicorn}} worker timeout configuration from {{60}} to {{120}} seconds.","2026-01-08T14:24:04.148Z"],["3796520","WD-21984","WD","carmen.vaher@bolt.eu","Carmen Vaher","[^EIB file for supplier groups (1).xlsx]\n\nUpdated file attached. ","2026-01-08T14:24:17.804Z"],["3796521","HS-28078","HS","bohdana.kalytchuk@bolt.eu","Bohdana Kalytchuk","[~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0] the link doesn’t work so I’m attaching both certificates here \n\n[^Levchuk Anton Certificate 11.pdf]\n[^Levchuk Anton Certificate 2.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T14:24:23.287Z"],["3796522","LSS-57372","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, link is still active!","2026-01-08T14:24:29.549Z"],["3796525","DO-5767","DO","pedro.paiva@bolt.eu","Pedro Paiva","Ah, right\nOk, opening a new ticket for them here as well 🙂","2026-01-08T14:25:44.131Z"],["3796526","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","I would like to cross-check driver table with your client table in our Data Warehouse (spark).\nTo see how many rows are missing.\nThe row should be in *taxify_payout_client_account*{{.}}*client* but is not saved, right?","2026-01-08T14:25:59.413Z"],["3796529","DO-5765","DO","kostiantyn.tsykulenko@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Tsykulenko","today-tomorrow","2026-01-08T14:26:23.691Z"],["3796530","GEORM-18","GEORM","horatiu.bota@bolt.eu","Horațiu Bota","AB test is finished, you can find a write-up of results [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GBM/pages/6833111045/Delivery+Parking+Detection+at+Provider+AB+Test+with+Annotated+Parking+Locations]. Results are neutral and there is no evidence parking suggestions improve last-mile efficiency at pickup. cc: [~accountid:63a562e8082abdd71bb435b6] ","2026-01-08T14:26:35.727Z"],["3796533","LSS-61124","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nFeedback from them:\n\n{quote}Just to confirm, this wording currently is on the second page of the Order Form.\n\nDoes the legal team wish to only include changes related to Section 13 and include the language they provided verbatim?{quote}\n\nThanks!","2026-01-08T14:27:19.456Z"],["3796534","HS-28700","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No amendment needed, confirmed with Marie Vainumets.","2026-01-08T14:27:19.770Z"],["3796537","PFI-810058","PFI","martina.jankiene@bolt.eu","Martina Jocyte Jankiene","Hello.\n\nWe made wrong kind of request, you can close it. Solving further here PFI-823304: Courier's final payout\n","2026-01-08T14:28:42.554Z"],["3796540","FX-3583","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767882529612399]*{color}:\n<@U786JU78U> i had also done this ticket because i was worried about back to back rides - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3384]\n\nLinked messages:\n[no preview available]\n{quote}","2026-01-08T14:29:02.958Z"],["3796543","LEG-1267","LEG","indrek.eelmets@bolt.eu","Indrek Eelmets","Hi [~accountid:712020:6d85a924-1008-400c-a07e-8ce47163c21c] - Here is the first [draft|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ejRP_ndIECsFIWvtBPOUBX1egXwCry2yAnSQXLU9xR4/edit?tab=t.0] of the trade mark licence agreement. Let’s discuss whether we should refer to the Partnership Agreement or not. ","2026-01-08T14:29:43.030Z"],["3796545","FX-3583","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767882587813509]*{color}:\nmy worry is that, as we saw when doing the detailed activity page, we consider rides to 'start' when the order is accepted. it was double counting minutes when the order was accepted but you were on another order originally\n{quote}","2026-01-08T14:30:02.855Z"],["3796546","RDS-1173","RDS","vivaksha.singh@bolt.eu","Vivaksha Singh","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] Specific to above situation ,yes it would impact AR. \nIn general back to back(B2B) orders are welcome by driver, as they keep their utilisation high. But during the times like above (want to complete current order process + high demand) it becomes particularly frustrating. We did build a temporal solution by providing  a configuration setting on [admin panel |https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-matching-config/matching/city/1016] at city level where the pause window can be configured. \n\nProbably a better solution would be to handle this globally, and different usecases. We plan to review the B2B feature end to end, it has been a legacy feature which over time has gone through patch works or being used to solve/address new needs like “Wait & Save”. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 15.24.24.png|width=1225,height=348,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 15.24.24.png\"!","2026-01-08T14:30:05.952Z"],["3796547","HS-28654","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:dc4824f4-a6bc-41f2-af89-59d155dc0cc8],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-08T14:30:07.101Z"],["3796552","LSS-60984","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:5f7aaad6021acf0076d55a90] , please see my comments below 🙏 \n\n* It’s great that the police confirmed that it relates to a Bolt ride, but we need the official request to be re-issued. The request needs to be issued to *Bolt* +*not Uber*+\n* The cited law is not a valid legal basis 🔴 Art.° 6° da Lei 49/2008, de 27 de Agosto just states the general powers of authorities; what we’re looking for is an article that allows the authority to request personal data. We need to ask them to cite the correct legal basis. FYI [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] \n\nCan you please send the following message to the police (templates are here: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/83887|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/83887]):\n\n{quote} Hi ${user_firstname},\n\nwe acknowledge your request *EDIT: Specify an ongoing document or file number*, dated *EDIT: Specify the date request received.*\n\nFirstly, we wanted to assure you that Bolt understands the seriousness of this request and we look to assist law enforcement whenever we are able to.\n\nAt Bolt, we take the privacy and security of our customers, employees, and independent contractors very seriously. We only engage in data sharing with third parties where we are satisfied that the requirements of our third party data sharing policy have been met. This means that the request for data is lawful, necessary, proportionate, and limited to the specific purpose outlined in the request.\n\nAfter carefully reviewing your request, we have determined that you have not provided us with a reference to the specific law or regulation that obliges Bolt to disclose the data requested. In this instance, Bolt will be unable to meet its legal requirements for establishing a legal basis for data disclosure.\n\nTo allow us to validate your request, we kindly advise you to provide a reference to the specific law or regulation which allows Bolt to release this data. Providing the necessary details will enable us to properly process your request in accordance with applicable privacy laws and regulations.\n\nIn addition to that, we have noticed that the request was mistakenly addressed to an incorrect company. Please re-issue the request to Bolt.{quote}\n\nPlease do not send yet - [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] do you have anything to add?","2026-01-08T14:31:14.391Z"],["3796554","WD-14199","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:61c07bf9a54af90069a42e2f] sorry for delay, please try task *Fix Unbalanced Journal from Supplier Invoice* to fixed supplier invoice. For customer i do not have an update yet.","2026-01-08T14:31:39.354Z"],["3796559","LSS-55393","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Sharing some of the documents that have now been signed from our side. \n\nDocuments currently missing: PL (Senago), TH & AZ (pending on stamp from the local team), but reached out to all relevant directors as well.\n[^PoA_Bolt Operations Ukraine LLC_Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf] [^PoA_LLC TY Services Ukraine_Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf] [^PoA_Bolt Poland sp. z o.o._Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf] [^PoA_Bolt Rides PL sp. z o.o._Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf] [^PoA_Bolt Services CZ s.r.o._Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf] [^PoA_Bolt Services PL sp. z o.o._Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf] [^PoA_Bolt Services SK s.r.o._Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf] [^PoA_Bolt Services SL d.o.o._Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf] [^PoA_Bolt Support Services BG EOOD_Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf] [^PoA_Nicchiano z o.o._Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf] ","2026-01-08T14:33:14.570Z"],["3796560","PFI-830745","PFI","israel.kizito@bolt-outsource.eu","Israel Kizito","Below is the customer’s bank account details for refund processing:\nBank name: Palmpay\nAccount name: Moses Success Oforishe\nAccount number: 7035008962","2026-01-08T14:33:50.952Z"],["3796561","WD-22522","WD","mihut.arsene@bolt.eu","Mihuț-Andrei Arsene","Hi Barbara,\n\nThe issue should now be fixed. Please try to access the WD sandbox and let me know if you still encounter issues!\n\nMany thanks,\n\nMihut","2026-01-08T14:34:02.619Z"],["3796563","TAXP-2287","TAXP","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","TSD Annexes 7 submitted to declare foreign withholding taxes to be used as credit against CIT due in the future. ","2026-01-08T14:34:08.713Z"],["3796565","CSDT-951","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","PR for enriching dim_support_case_tier_history: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15246|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15246]","2026-01-08T14:35:26.270Z"],["3796566","LSS-61124","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] I see the wording is already included, indeed.\n\nWe will send for signing then ","2026-01-08T14:35:27.845Z"],["3796567","LSS-53738","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (08.01.26)*+\n\n*EXTERNAL COUNSEL*\n\n* Fee estimations have been received:\n** *KVDL* (firm that originally provided the advice): *EUR 1600* (exclusive of VAT)\n** *Fieldfisher* (new firm): *GBP 4000* (exclusive of taxes)\n* *Conclusion*: +KVDL+ seem like the best option. They are cheaper, and have more context behind the question.\n** Gab has approved ([link|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D074131T54N/p1767884957829409]). I have instructed KVDL to proceed. Waiting on advice :loading: ","2026-01-08T14:35:28.821Z"],["3796568","LSS-60766","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","Thanks [~accountid:712020:209f6e12-e421-4fbf-9a9f-60d100117bab] I fully agree with your suggested approach. Feel free agree to proceed and please let me know if you need any additional information or support on my end.\n\n","2026-01-08T14:35:47.443Z"],["3796569","RNTL-30272","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","[@norman.tamm|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:8d272f38-d046-4ad2-a5b3-a47b219e9fa1] I’ve created a Jira task for it with due date Jan 23","2026-01-08T14:35:48.813Z"],["3796570","LSS-61124","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[^Order Form (6bdb7169-35a7-462b-9635-32a28477d74b).pdf]\n\nHi Legal Ops \n\nPlease sign document by Ahto ","2026-01-08T14:36:10.233Z"],["3796571","PFI-831038","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T14:36:50.797Z"],["3796574","PFI-830847","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Hey , seems like some issues with auto matching , i will look into this !","2026-01-08T14:37:15.601Z"],["3796576","SAI-1398","SAI","anton.belski@bolt.eu","Anton Belski","{quote}*= 2*{quote}\n\n:warning: *WARNING :: support-bot :: [support-bot] AI bot unhandled exceptions* Triggered with value *2.03* ","2026-01-08T14:37:33.690Z"],["3796577","SAI-1398","SAI",null,"Slack","[Anton Belski|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:de49345c-1803-4c3b-a519-8499b60153fe] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C060Y4GTY6R/p1767869871445109?thread_ts=1767869871.445109&cid=C060Y4GTY6R|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C060Y4GTY6R/p1767869871445109?thread_ts=1767869871.445109&cid=C060Y4GTY6R|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-08T14:37:34.897Z"],["3796578","SAI-1398","SAI","anton.belski@bolt.eu","Anton Belski","delivery refund exceptions caused by validation\n\n{noformat}                  {\n                    \"error\": \"Number should be greater than zero\",\n                    \"property\": \"unit_amount\"\n                  }{noformat}\n\nsome items in the basket could have 0 unit_amount, e.g sauce or promo\n\n{noformat}                    \"options\": [\n                        {\n                            \"count\": 1,\n                            \"item\": \"Garlic Sauce\",\n                            \"item_id\": 2239569789,\n                            \"total_unit_price\": 0,\n                            \"type\": \"dish\",\n                            \"unit_price\": 0\n                        }\n                    ],{noformat}\n\nwhen users complaining about such missing items, llm will return 0 as unit_amount in action_params which violates tPositiveNumber validation in support-suggestions","2026-01-08T14:37:35.262Z"],["3796579","RDS-1363","RDS","vivaksha.singh@bolt.eu","Vivaksha Singh","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] There is no feature channel yet, but only the RFC. [https://docs.google.com/document/d/13GnTgdiE6A1mTF3VtWEZr5vmoveDHZ0wlzhuuEun3IE/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/13GnTgdiE6A1mTF3VtWEZr5vmoveDHZ0wlzhuuEun3IE/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]  in development. \nIf you are asking for matching support channel #*dev-rides-matching-support*","2026-01-08T14:37:35.424Z"],["3796581","LSS-61279","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432],\n\nCould you please help us obtain Ahto’s signature on the agreement attached to this ticket?\n\nMany thanks!","2026-01-08T14:38:23.382Z"],["3796582","SUPX-2305","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","What we agreed with [~accountid:630e0b9a9796033b256bd3a5] and [~accountid:5ae966399abb77267ba68b16] :\n\n* we should update the existing, typed, targeting events, to allow specifying not only {{support_flow}} parameter, but also an optional {{issue_keys}} parameter that would allow enabling the flow only for certain issue keys\n* with the above, the {{suggested_for_issue_keys}} flow registry config should include the full list of issue keys for which the flow is supported and *could be enabled*, and the targeting event should allow to narrow this list to specific issue keys.","2026-01-08T14:38:36.393Z"],["3796583","RDS-1397","RDS","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","Trigger Find new driver after cancelling existing driver, right?","2026-01-08T14:38:37.753Z"],["3796586","SAI-1398","SAI","anton.belski@bolt.eu","Anton Belski","need either to prompt LLM to not include items with 0 price into refund, or implement some post-processing for routines","2026-01-08T14:39:04.481Z"],["3796587","PFI-831039","PFI","juri.zuravljov@bolt.eu","Juri Žuravljov","[^Vorm_TööTASU ARESTIMISE AKT_RNA - BOLT_025-2025-2404-18.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-08T14:39:14.912Z"],["3796589","BP-13320","BP","fahad.khan@bolt.eu","Fahad Ahmed Khan","We can do something like {{INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS}} so it can cover PP & CC companies (although API users should mostly be PP though). Order system I believe throws a similar error (“PAYMENT_INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS”)","2026-01-08T14:39:42.764Z"],["3796591","LSS-61289","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey, sent out the request","2026-01-08T14:40:14.051Z"],["3796592","PFI-831040","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T14:40:14.607Z"],["3796593","DPM-2289","DPM","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","Expanding scope per [~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] to include title logic updates for Options, Option Groups, and Categories (FE/BE). This covers both the PIM UI and CSV imports. Note: A title in the default language is no longer strictly required; however, a title in *at least one language* must be provided. The original estimation will be increased by *3* *days*, to the *6 days in total*. ","2026-01-08T14:40:24.448Z"],["3796594","BP-12491","BP","kacper.jasinski@bolt.eu","Kacper Jasiński","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/50/SREDESK-7392?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/50/SREDESK-7392?created=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T14:40:34.881Z"],["3796595","PFI-830791","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","payment has been matched to 401341","2026-01-08T14:40:37.120Z"],["3796596","LSS-61289","LSS","dovile.zykute@bolt.eu","Dovilė Zykutė","Thank youuu","2026-01-08T14:40:38.067Z"],["3796597","LSS-61124","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] and Legal Ops,\n\nPlease wait a bit. We expect to have final business approval on Monday, after which we should be able to sign.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-08T14:40:40.287Z"],["3796598","SAI-1398","SAI","anton.belski@bolt.eu","Anton Belski","support cases\n\n{{719707118}}\n\n{{719651058}}","2026-01-08T14:40:54.598Z"],["3796599","PFI-819853","PFI","tuukka.tammela@bolt.eu","Tuukka Tammela","Could we get help with this one?\n\n","2026-01-08T14:41:01.930Z"],["3796600","LSS-61124","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","On hold until Monday","2026-01-08T14:41:05.912Z"],["3796602","LSS-61155","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Just got the signed version. Please find it attached.\n\n[^Motor vehicle sale agreement_Bolt Services LV SIA_V43 SIA_06.01.26.edoc]\n\n","2026-01-08T14:41:44.656Z"],["3796603","LSS-55676","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hi, [~accountid:5c010fa68ce9b546efc49454] and [~accountid:5bb399378eb5ad7760adb25e] any updates here?","2026-01-08T14:42:49.188Z"],["3796605","HS-28448","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Employee will cancel the request.","2026-01-08T14:43:12.912Z"],["3796606","RDS-1173","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:d2a0e53f-83a4-4e81-aebd-74db6f57d6fa] exactly, I think a global solution is best. The Admin config setting is great, but the default cooldown period is {{0 seconds}}, so it doesn’t fix the issue and we continue to get frustrated feedback about this. \n\nI’d simply change the global default to 3 seconds and be done with it. We can always make market-specific adjustments, if needed.\n\n[~accountid:61386b11a4f86e0069546dff] is on board and can make the change — we were only waiting on approval.  ","2026-01-08T14:43:14.346Z"],["3796607","PFI-830745","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThank you for providing the refund details. I have reached out to Paystack to issue the refund to the customer. Will be able to provide further details as soon as we receive an update. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-08T14:43:17.848Z"],["3796608","L10N-26656","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26652](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26652)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T14:43:25.658Z"],["3796609","LSS-61265","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Amserv 2026 Q1 cars returns_Bolt Services LV SIA_Amserv Motors SIA_08.01.26.edoc]\n\n","2026-01-08T14:43:26.624Z"],["3796610","L10N-26659","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26652](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26652)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T14:43:26.037Z"],["3796611","L10N-26664","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26652](https://taxify.atlassian.net