,"Another client: [facturacaopt@mawdy.com|mailto:facturacaopt@mawdy.com]\nThis seems like a general issue","2026-01-08T14:59:48.309Z"],["3796690","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","You are right, the missing is client-account not the client\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8DFC2A0G/screenshot_2026-01-08_at_15.59.39.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8DFC2A0G/screenshot_2026-01-08_at_15.59.39.png|smart-link]","2026-01-08T14:59:55.081Z"],["3796692","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","The query I used was inner-join which didn't return a result because client-account not exist","2026-01-08T15:00:35.217Z"],["3796694","LSS-61157","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a]  [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340023|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340023|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T15:00:41.149Z"],["3796695","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","How is client_account populated?","2026-01-08T15:00:47.243Z"],["3796696","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","When the client update the payout details","2026-01-08T15:01:17.977Z"],["3796697","PAR-3841","PAR",null,"Slack","Can you please advise on how to respond to drivers for the time being if they fulfill all requirements? Such as [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719621183]","2026-01-08T15:01:41.346Z"],["3796698","HS-28028","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","waiting for the information from manager","2026-01-08T15:01:41.602Z"],["3796700","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","Another question - do you have logs in Partner Payment about attempt to make payout in case it was rejected by bank?\nCan I see it in Kibana?","2026-01-08T15:01:47.582Z"],["3796701","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","Which I believe in this case ( Flex ) not needed","2026-01-08T15:01:48.229Z"],["3796703","HS-28736","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","task went for Mobility approval","2026-01-08T15:02:18.717Z"],["3796704","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","{quote}When the client update the payout details{quote}\n\nIf they don't - there will not be client_acoount  row? Is it fine?","2026-01-08T15:02:24.096Z"],["3796707","PAR-3841","PAR",null,"Slack","[@maria.cianciuolo|https://taxify.slack.com/team/U09RB1LNY73] please advise driver that Early Cashout is still being tested, and that he must rely on weekly payouts for now. If he continues to complain please DM me, I will work with the driver to find a short term solution.","2026-01-08T15:03:08.680Z"],["3796710","RDXENG-3988","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","Not behind FF, but in dynamic config → [https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/dynamic-config/entity/edit/cGF5bWVudC1wcm92aWRlci1wcm9jZXNzb3V0L2FwcGxlcGF5L2NhcmRfbmV0d29ya3M=/:shard|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/dynamic-config/entity/edit/cGF5bWVudC1wcm92aWRlci1wcm9jZXNzb3V0L2FwcGxlcGF5L2NhcmRfbmV0d29ya3M=/:shard]","2026-01-08T15:03:18.462Z"],["3796711","LSS-61279","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Interfunerarias_Signed (9d1d7c2b-c8df-45d6-b8f6-659b154879a2).pdf] ","2026-01-08T15:03:40.226Z"],["3796712","PFI-830556","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hi, please note that the reason of the rejected is described in the payout. The payout was rejected because their account is invalid. The beneficiary name is invalid with invalid characters. You can see that their name: PALPITE D`ARROMBA, LDA has a (' and ,) which are not accepted. Please remove this information from their name and we will be able to resend the payout accordingly. ","2026-01-08T15:04:16.038Z"],["3796713","FX-3584","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Meruzhan Kerobyan [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767884660302219]*{color}:\nEven on the same page, discrepancy is visible,  has correct data\n\nLinked files:\n* [image.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A7H6FPHL6/image.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-08T15:04:41.745Z"],["3796715","LSS-59845","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] Order looks fine, we just need to add to the Order a wording: \n\n“This Order shall not be automatically renewed. This Order may be renewed only by a written agreement of both Parties”.","2026-01-08T15:05:18.794Z"],["3796716","PFI-831050","PFI","jane.dike@bolt-outsource.eu","Jane Dike","[^ProofOfPaymentNotification 27.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-08T15:05:22.600Z"],["3796717","RDS-1074","RDS","vivaksha.singh@bolt.eu","Vivaksha Singh","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] Latter, local team promised 95% to gain access to the prio lane. I do not think this requirement is binding, because the binding agreement requirement was fulfilled by November 2025. It was more around creating specific dispatch areas and visibility of these dispatch areas for this specific fleet drivers. ","2026-01-08T15:05:23.465Z"],["3796720","DSR-3593","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-08T15:06:09.449Z"],["3796721","PFI-831051","PFI","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","[^32109618-TZ1126-45.pdf]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 17.58.57.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 17.59.43.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.04.14.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T15:06:36.844Z"],["3796722","PFI-831051","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T15:06:39.168Z"],["3796723","PAW-14750","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Severity: 8\n• Reproducibility: 8\n• Priority: N/A\n• Accept: 1\n• Suggested improvements: Sufficient for triage","2026-01-08T15:06:44.966Z"],["3796724","HS-28588","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","Hey Klaudia,\n\nThanks! Should be all good now. 🙂 \n\nKind regards,\n\nKristin - People Ops","2026-01-08T15:06:48.905Z"],["3796725","PIF-2276","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 7\n• Relevance: 8\n• Problem Definition: 7\n• Accept: 7\n• Suggested improvements: The user story needs more detail to achieve higher clarity. Enhance the clarity by outlining specific requirements for how podStatuses should be retrieved and displayed. Relevance is moderately clear, as understanding pod statuses can improve response times and efficiency for handling deployment issues. While acceptance criteria are implied, they should be explicitly stated, such as specifying what constitutes a successful retrieval and display of podStatuses. The problem definition should explain why this improvement is needed, with more detail on how current limitations impact deployment effectiveness. Additionally, including a more comprehensive description of the current workflow and specific pain points related to the health check failures would improve the story.","2026-01-08T15:06:51.418Z"],["3796726","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","Take this driver for example, working perfectly because it has active client-account\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7NRV60JG/screenshot_2026-01-08_at_16.06.13.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7NRV60JG/screenshot_2026-01-08_at_16.06.13.png|smart-link]","2026-01-08T15:07:22.443Z"],["3796727","PFI-831052","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T15:07:34.518Z"],["3796728","CSXRD-232","CSXRD","justus.debruin@bolt.eu","Justus de Bruin","[~accountid:5f1a9692b385da00156b98be] French and Arabic content have been uploaded to FAQ (/) ","2026-01-08T15:07:37.451Z"],["3796729","PIF-2276","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft effectively communicates the new feature that helps users understand deployment failures better, which addresses the problem of multiple support requests. The internal stakeholders need clarity on where this feature can be accessed and further documentation, which the placeholders indicate. Essential details such as the specific admin panel view and any associated user guides are missing.","2026-01-08T15:07:44.332Z"],["3796731","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","[@ahmed.farghaly|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63fc5f040a4a47fb8d20cf92] I do not understand. Please explain:\n• driver is created\n• \"Driver Created\" event is sent\n• you listen to this event and create row in \"client\" table\n• no row in \"client_account\" table\n• driver can't receive payments\nIs it correct?","2026-01-08T15:09:24.704Z"],["3796733","LSS-61292","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","LOI for review, shared with stakeholders in slack: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/11WZFb5SCnCBBlheCLhP55Ulm0Z5zZ-Fu/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=113263363537883010627&rtpof=true&sd=true|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11WZFb5SCnCBBlheCLhP55Ulm0Z5zZ-Fu/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=113263363537883010627&rtpof=true&sd=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T15:10:10.223Z"],["3796735","DRX-27615","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Automation is done, but similar auto navigation tests are flaky ","2026-01-08T15:10:35.827Z"],["3796736","LSS-53093","LSS","dominik.lopuch@bolt.eu","Dominik Lopuch","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] please close it, thanks.","2026-01-08T15:10:40.608Z"],["3796737","SREDESK-7389","SREDESK","andrus.viik@bolt.eu","Andrus Viik","sa’screated \n\n{noformat} itgc-gdrive-audit-live@bolt-pint-automation.iam.gserviceaccount.com\t\t\n itgc-gdrive-audit-prelive@bolt-pint-automation.iam.gserviceaccount.com{noformat}","2026-01-08T15:10:53.424Z"],["3796740","HS-28662","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:60bf5e79b1f93b0069640a64],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-08T15:11:45.029Z"],["3796743","DO-5765","DO","kostiantyn.tsykulenko@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Tsykulenko","it’s available now","2026-01-08T15:13:15.750Z"],["3796744","PFI-831053","PFI","pedro.ferreira@bolt-outsource.eu","Pedro Ferreira","!IMG_20260105_170612.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T15:13:16.976Z"],["3796753","WFM-9886","WFM","francisco.silva@bolt-outsource.eu","Francisco Moreira Da Silva","Hi [~accountid:5ee36bc3283ae50ab5999c9e] thank you for your help!\n[~accountid:712020:a4f6dc7f-ea2b-4b6c-87be-3ca7829f155a] is currently without access, can you add the queues manually to her too?\n\nBest regards","2026-01-08T15:16:25.208Z"],["3796755","PIF-2276","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 8\n• Relevance: 9\n• Problem Definition: 8\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: The story identifies a need for improved visibility during health check failures but could benefit from more structured acceptance criteria. Provide clearer metrics for success and define how the visibility improvements will be measured. Expanding the problem description with specific examples of the impact on deployment processes and adding screenshots or links to 'pic 1' for context would enhance clarity. Additionally, explicitly enumerating the pod statuses to be monitored and reported would improve the acceptance criteria quality.","2026-01-08T15:18:55.932Z"],["3796756","WFM-9905","WFM","gaurav.singh@bolt-outsource.eu","Gaurav Singh","Hi Marcin, employee is going to support RH Latam team, so you can map 05 BU_Paraguay_business under Teleperformance - Colombia, Baranquilla.\n\n","2026-01-08T15:19:39.322Z"],["3796759","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","Yes, client account is required and if it's not exist or not active we consider this client not exist","2026-01-08T15:22:34.269Z"],["3796761","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","Why don't we create row in client_account on driver create event?","2026-01-08T15:23:06.570Z"],["3796762","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","Can you please point me to the place where client_account row is added for drivers?","2026-01-08T15:23:28.327Z"],["3796764","WFM-9905","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Thanks for info, it's done like that","2026-01-08T15:23:31.397Z"],["3796765","PFI-830745","PFI","israel.kizito@bolt-outsource.eu","Israel Kizito","Thank you for your response.\nCheers,\nIsrael.","2026-01-08T15:23:32.258Z"],["3796768","DLSP-1973","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","Decided to stop using this endpoint in a new implementation","2026-01-08T15:23:58.002Z"],["3796770","INT-770","INT","hans.tulmin@bolt.eu","Hans-Peeter Tulmin","The German CT wants to run Bolt Club in Germany like this. Budget towards Dortmund but rides counts in all of the industrial heart of Germany. Another idea would be city-groups or a similar solution","2026-01-08T15:24:36.021Z"],["3796772","PFI-831051","PFI","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:5f1fbb0eef11df002588080f] - for your visibility","2026-01-08T15:26:45.485Z"],["3796773","PFI-831058","PFI","liam.james@bolt.eu","Liam James","[^Searcys - Payment Import - 08_01 - UK Payment Import.csv]","2026-01-08T15:27:48.376Z"],["3796774","LSS-60557","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hi, [~accountid:712020:5edd7b8a-e535-468c-85fd-63f0b6de01b2] and [~accountid:61debf39e67ea2006b3a1cb5] ! could you please share the main agreement with them?","2026-01-08T15:28:18.327Z"],["3796775","PFI-830555","PFI","afonso.freitasecosta@bolt.eu","Afonso Freitas e Costa","Hi [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea],\n\nThanks for the feedback.\n\nCan you pls run a fraud check in the same instances to this company \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/800720?tab=business_company|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/800720?tab=business_company] \n\nand these users specifically \n\n\n+351910166083\n\n+351938971990\n\n\n\nThis fraudulent user was referred by this company.\n\nThanks.\n\n\n","2026-01-08T15:28:24.236Z"],["3796776","L10N-26724","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26720](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26720)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T15:28:27.603Z"],["3796777","L10N-26727","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26720](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26720)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T15:28:28.405Z"],["3796778","L10N-26726","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket abo