ra","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26720](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26720)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T15:28:41.443Z"],["3796791","WEB-9598","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] \n\nLiisi has resolved all feedback from the f[+eedback file+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1_rHIKmOGVqaFq63mWE0ykEtCZtdywvRJ52kbdPb75j0/edit?usp=sharing] and updated the content [+doc+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKVSYG-c6k_Dk8iRzRdBFVT3aU2nAsA5pKRZ8nCpllI/edit?tab=t.0] accordingly. Since the content has changed quite a bit, it might be easier to review the file from the beginning rather than relying on version history.\n\nLet me know if there’s anything I can help with. Thanks! ","2026-01-08T15:29:23.848Z"],["3796792","LSS-59377","LSS","meda.baltramonaityte@bolt.eu","Meda Baltramonaitytė","Hi, sorry for ping, but maybe you could specify when it will be possible for you to review this request? Thank you in advance [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] ","2026-01-08T15:29:40.667Z"],["3796794","RDS-82","RDS","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","What’s the status here?","2026-01-08T15:30:04.922Z"],["3796796","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","Because this data not available at the time  client creation and we allow the client to add this data later.","2026-01-08T15:30:36.231Z"],["3796800","LSS-50442","LSS","edik.davtian@bolt.eu","Edik Davtian","just to make sure ticket would not close.\n\nLiki24 meeting is tomorrow 09.01, please expect some updates.","2026-01-08T15:31:45.437Z"],["3796802","PAW-14738","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T15:31:56.868Z"],["3796804","LSS-61207","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hello Philippine,\n\npourrais-tu revoir le LOI que Zohra a partagé et voir si il est en ligne avec celui-ci [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NkHfcy1m_iEYaZwUqcxZkEetNyC2rqCx/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NkHfcy1m_iEYaZwUqcxZkEetNyC2rqCx/edit|smart-link]  qu’on avait revu ensemble cet été? 9a me semble OK, mais je préfère qu’on fasse un double check! \n\nmerci beaucoup\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-08T15:32:15.343Z"],["3796805","DBRE-8619","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","📢 *VictoriaMetrics Deployment — GAMMA (Completed)*\n\nThe VictoriaMetrics rollout for the *GAMMA* cluster has been completed successfully.\nMetrics ingestion, alerting, and Grafana dashboards are operating normally, with no observed impact.\n\n*Key highlights*\n\n* Scrape success rate: *100%*\n* ~62k rows/sec ingestion, no backlog\n* 806 active scrape targets\n* No active alerts\n\n*Dashboards*\n\n* GAMMA dedicated dashboards:\n[http://gamma-monitor.sqldb:3000/d/bolt-000000011/gamma-tidb?orgId=1&refresh=30s|http://gamma-monitor.sqldb:3000/d/bolt-000000011/gamma-tidb?orgId=1&refresh=30s]\n* Centralized TiDB dashboard (GAMMA view):\n[https://monitor.boltint.net/d/tidb-v8-5-1-tidb/tidb-v8-5-1?orgId=1&refresh=1m&var-k8s_cluster=tidb-gamma&var-tidb_cluster=gamma|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/tidb-v8-5-1-tidb/tidb-v8-5-1?orgId=1&refresh=1m&var-k8s_cluster=tidb-gamma&var-tidb_cluster=gamma]\n\n*Migration validation*\n\n* VictoriaMetrics migration report:\n[http://gamma-monitor.sqldb:3000/d/vm-migration-report/migration-report?orgId=1|http://gamma-monitor.sqldb:3000/d/vm-migration-report/migration-report?orgId=1]\n\n*Deployment logs (Rundeck)*\n\n* [https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/138798|https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/138798]\n* [https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/138810|https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/138810]\n\nNo action required. Please flag if you notice anything unexpected.","2026-01-08T15:32:37.190Z"],["3796807","LSS-58746","LSS","azza.ltifi@bolt.eu","Azza Letifi","Hi team, please cancel this ticket. The partner is no longer interested in continuing. Thank you!","2026-01-08T15:33:00.507Z"],["3796808","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","You call this API  {{/internal/savePayoutClientAccount}}  here {{/rides/driver/fleet/main/common/service/DriverAccountInfoService.ts}}","2026-01-08T15:33:26.724Z"],["3796809","PFI-830687","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hi, adjusment should be done and approved internally by your team. ","2026-01-08T15:33:30.355Z"],["3796811","LSS-61294","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] assigning to you as Infosec-related, cc [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] ","2026-01-08T15:33:41.431Z"],["3796812","LSS-61259","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","hi [~accountid:712020:af076e83-bb33-4eb6-8634-6e435217c5e4] , thanks for your patience. Kudos to you and [~accountid:712020:dbc22d70-1983-4414-80b3-27f087787ae4] for the thorough pre-investigation of the incident - this was extremely helpful and helped us narrow down the issue a lot faster.\n\nThe investigation with our colleagues from InfoSec has now been concluded. Below is an overview, which was also based on your own research. \n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n*Overview*\n{panel}\n\n* On 26 December 2025, suspicious login attempts from Bangladesh and USA took place. As per our processes, automatic emails reflecting this issue were sent to the FO ([+medrivesas@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesas@gmail.com]) to warn them about the issue.\n* On {{2025-12-28}}, the Fleet Account was updated from [+medrivesas@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesas@gmail.com] (original one) to [+medrivesass@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesass@gmail.com]. Logs ([+fleet manager change log+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-manager/managers/edit/70795?tab=change_log]) confirm the email change was performed by the Fleet Manager account itself (ID [+70795+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-manager/managers/edit/70795]) but from a suspicious IP address: 103.151.40.239> This location was deemed inconsistent with the partner's usual activity. The account also subsequently showed multiple language updates.\n* On {{2025-12-30}}, the Fleet Account’s RIB was updated from a BE IBAN to a DE IBAN. This request for change was made by the fleet account itself via [Beehive|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/712603150]. It is confirmed that CS followed the usual procedure before approving and actioning the request, i.e. a KBis and a bank statement with valid information were provided, and the email address was verified at this time. \n* On {{2026-01-05}}, a EUR 19.907,36 [payout|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/232472558?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] was created. On {{2026-01-06}}, the payout was marked as _finished_ and _Sent / The money was debited from our account on 2026-01-05._\n* Also on {{2026-01-05}}, a [BH|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/717620544] was opened via the [+medrivesass@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesass@gmail.com] (the fraudulent email) email address, requesting that the IBAN be updated back to the BE IBAN. \nThis is not uncommon - fraudulent actors have been known to change the IBAN back and forth around payout schedules to reduce suspicion. It could also be that the fraudulent actor did not plan on stealing more than one payout, and requested that the original RIB be reinstated in order to cover their actions. Alternatively, it is also possible that one same person is behind both email addresses, and that this change was done in order to get the payout done in a different country (this is also not unheard of). \n* On {{2026-01-06}}, the email address associated with the fleet account was changed back from [+medrivesass@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesass@gmail.com] to [+medrivesas@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesas@gmail.com] (original one) by the FO, from IP 62.93.179.110 - the potential explanations for this are the same as in the previous point.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nIn light of the above, InfoSec concluded:\n{panel}\n\n* It cannot be confirmed with confidence whether the _email address_ [+medrivesas@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesas@gmail.com] (original one) itself was compromised. However, the fleet account’s _password_ was definitely compromised, as the malicious actor was able to log in the account via the password and _then_ changed the email address associated with the account from  [+medrivesas@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesas@gmail.com] (original one) to [+medrivesass@gmail.com+|mailto:medrivesass@gmail.com].\n* Next steps:\n** The FO needs to update their fleet account’s password, if not done already;\n** The IBAN can be corrected to the original IBAN (BE);\n** Once this is done, the payouts may resume. \n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nFrom a Privacy POV:\n{panel}\n\n* I will log this incident internally, as per our processes;\n* I believe that the information in this ticket answers all four questions asked by the FO, namely:\n** Une explication sur la raison de ce changement de RIB non autorisé → We can explain that from our investigation, logs show that a successful log in occurred via the fleet’s credentials from IP addresses which were not consistent with their usual activity. I recommend highlighting that (several?) email(s) were sent to the FO to warn them of this issue at the time it occurred - we may refer to the specific date and time to support this point. Once the individual successfully logged in, they were able to update (change) the email address as well as the RIB associated with the account, as they provided all required supporting documents to do so (KBis and a bank statement with valid information, along with the (new) email address being verified at the time). This did not raise suspicion on our end.\n** La confirmation du RIB actuellement enregistré sur mon compte Bolt → not sure what RIB is currently associated with the account. I trust this can be handled as per your team’s processes.\n** Les mesures prises pour récupérer ou régulariser le montant que je n’ai pas reçu → Advise him to report this to the police. Since there was no confirmed breach on Bolt’s side, no refund can be issued for this - please confirm with [Cesar Echeverria|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/D08V62B8GJV]. Also mention to the FO that should the police contact us on this matter, we will cooperate fully (this is important for compliance reasons).\n** La garantie que ce type d’erreur ne se reproduira plus → As long as the FO ensures that his credentials (Bolt and others) are kept up to date, there should not be any further issues of this type.\n* If you need my support with the comms to the FO, please let me know. I can review the draft in English or French, whatever is easier for you 😊 ","2026-01-08T15:35:08.556Z"],["3796813","WFM-9905","WFM","gaurav.singh@bolt-outsource.eu","Gaurav Singh","thank you Marcin, appreciated 🙂 ","2026-01-08T15:35:37.318Z"],["3796815","DO-5777","DO","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","hey, this job was disabled at some point (after a few unsuccessful runs)\n\n[https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/608322224980680?o=3598988355446810|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/608322224980680?o=3598988355446810]\nhow can I enable it back?","2026-01-08T15:37:26.498Z"],["3796816","LSS-60863","LSS","barbara.duartecosta@bolt.eu","Bárbara Duarte Costa","Hello!\n\nAccording to ou accounts payable specialist, everything is paid. Due to holidays season there was a delay in the payment of the last invoices but they were paid just a few days ago.\n\nNo addendum will be made. It’s indeed the formalisation of something that has already taken place and gone well. 🙂\n\nIn attach you can find the Annex.\n\n[^Anexo I - Condicoes Gerais de C ontratação JCDecaux Airport.pdf]\n\nLet me know if you need anything else.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-08T15:37:38.855Z"],["3796818","DO-5777","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","You can enable its Aiflow DAG: [https://airflow-common.data.boltint.net/dags/dbt_micromobility_supply_by_deployment_spots/grid?search=dbt_micromobility_supply_by_deployment_spots|https://airflow-common.data.boltint.net/dags/dbt_micromobility_supply_by_deployment_spots/grid?search=dbt_micromobility_supply_by_deployment_spots]\n\nDoes this solve your problem?","2026-01-08T15:38:01.909Z"],["3796819","PFI-735118","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Upon the review from engineering team, they confirmed that the last date of the month is used for all of the clients in EE, based on guidelines of our e-invoicing provider, indicating the duration of the service provided.","2026-01-08T15:38:39.345Z"],["3796820","DO-5777","DO","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","right, forgot about that. Thought this interface is not relevant anymore after migration to dtabricks jobs","2026-01-08T15:39:09.821Z"],["3796821","DO-5777","DO","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","thanks!","2026-01-08T15:39:11.863Z"],["3796822","DO-5777","DO","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","should solve","2026-01-08T15:39:18.794Z"],["3796823","DO-5778","DO","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","Hi *group-S05FGH5B82W*, I need to drop a table, the reason is in the description.\nHere is the [PR|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15251]. Could you please help? Thank you :pray:","2026-01-08T15:39:32.493Z"],["3796824","PFI-831051","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Would just reissuing the Ride Invoice + transferring the cost between accounts be sufficient?\n\nThis way the Statements + SF Invoices wouldn’t be affected and stay the same, the “rebalancing” will appear as a a negative/positive Charge in the Balance Box.\n\nFor context, if the Statement + SF invoice have to be reissued, this would be much more complex.","2026-01-08T15:40:17.539Z"],["3796825","DO-5777","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","No worries. There are also Databricks triggers that could have triggered this job. But this one runs on Airflow, which is our standard approach. :wink:","2026-01-08T15:40:53.404Z"],["3796826","C2-455","C2","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LCdTbCZjp5vyr84UlcNd9sgQwCWFooum8OONzIk07IY/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LCdTbCZjp5vyr84UlcNd9sgQwCWFooum8OONzIk07IY/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] \n\nTL:DR:\n\n* Cell imbalance - 10 pcs (67%)\n* Quality issue - 3 pcs (20%)\n* BMS issue - 2 pcs (13%)\n\nSome batteries had already been opened & diagnosed by repair partner (missing connector/fasteners/heastshrink from corepack removed), but don’t remember asking them to do so.\n\nBMS issue root causes we are investigating still:\n\n* 1 BMS charging circuit diode D5 had been mechanically damaged, possibly during potting removal. After removing/short circuiting the diode pins, charging worked (quality issue).\n* 2 BMS sampling circuits somewhat faulty, investigation still ongoing. 1st PCB desoldered & waiting for investigation, 2nd needs to be checked still in more detail as it heats up.\n\nRE *assembly quality* - no distinct negative feedback to give (only judging batteries which were completely assembled, ~30% weren’t.)","2026-01-08T15:41:26.455Z"],["3796827","LSS-61295","LSS","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","Beehive [Ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719804338]: \n\n!image-20260108-154050.png|width=655,height=667,alt=\"image-20260108-154050.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-08T15:41:27.391Z"],["3796829","LSS-55276","LSS","klara.bradova@bolt.eu","Klára Bradová","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c], sorry about not updating, you can close it. Coca-Cola found other way to register us as vendor. Many thanks for your support here, though! 🙂 ","2026-01-08T15:42:38.346Z"],["3796830","FX-3276","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","sure, we are targeting around 23rd of January (other tasks right now have a bit higher priority). Is this timeline ok for you?\n\n_This comment was left via Slack._","2026-01-08T15:43:31.937Z"],["3796831","WD-22478","WD","mariaadelina.stana@bolt.eu","Maria Adelina Stana","Thank you!","2026-01-08T15:43:50.906Z"],["3796832","LSS-59991","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hello [~accountid:60536b5060d39e006f7dae01] and [~accountid:712020:b467cd93-0037-45b9-9f33-992ba5f38b42],\n\nMany thanks for your response regarding CapitanSpec and the integration requests that we use at Bolt.\n\nIn relation to this matter, we have the following comments:\n\n# We continue to agree that it is a business decision to grant or deny a vendor the possibility to integrate to Bolt via API. There is no law that we know of, obliging Bolt to grant access to everyone that requests it.\n# Bolt Food is not a dominant player in the Cyprus market, and therefore has no reinforced obligation to grant access to its system.\n# Given that Bolt has granted access to various third party integrators (CaptainSpec being only one of them), Bolt would not be favouring any particular provider with the aim of restricting competition in the market, or to impede the entry of new players (such as Evolution) to the market.\n# In connection with Trojan Economics’ email, even if they are mentioning that they will file a complaint against Bolt before the Competition Authority, we do not see any major risk if they finally proceed with the complaint, for the reasons mentioned above. \n# A possible future scenario could be a requirement from the Competition Authority asking Bolt to provide explanations on their decision-making process for accepting new vendors. If this arises, we believe that we are in a good position to answer an eventual requirement by the Competition Authority.\n\n \n\nIn light of the above, we suggest that you reply to the email sent by Trojan Economics, in an amicable and open manner. Below you will find a suggestion of the wording for the response. Please feel free to adapt the wording, according to your context.\n\nPlease let us know if you have any further comments or questions.\n\nBest,\n\nAngela\n\n\n\n“Dear Panayiotis,\n\nMany thanks for your message, which we have shared with our internal legal department. In line  with their analysis and in connection with your questions, please be advised:\n\n# As we have already informed your clients, we are open to integrate new vendors and aggregators to Bolt Food via API, who will need to:\n\n* Meet the requirements listed in Bolt’s [+developer portal+|https://developer.bolt.eu/] which is of public access and can be consulted at any time.\n* Fill in the following form (see [+here+|https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSez67FYBsYWLieW7DcC03hMkZSUnaN0EQZY9LdTkpVpJ8SkJg/viewform]) \n* In addition to the above, Bolt analyses each request on a case-by-case basis to understand whether there are any particular technical needs for the onboarding, and if the potential vendor is attractive from a business perspective. In all cases, Bolt reserves the right to accept or deny the requests.\n\n# In the case of your clients Christos Hirodontis and Rodionas Papadopoulos, please note that:\n\n* We have received their request to integrate via API. \n* After analysis from our integrations team, we concluded that we do not yet envisage their integration to Bolt Food, as their business is still in a very early stage, and it would require significant time and effort from the Technical Support team — including creating a test setup, providing daily support, answering technical questions, and conducting test calls.\n* We have repeatedly communicated our reasons to your clients, and we look forward to reviewing their case once their business is in a more developed stage.\n* As expressed above, according to our business metrics and perspectives, we reserve the right to accept or reject requests from third parties.\n\n# Finally, from an antitrust perspective, Bolt Food:\n\n* Does not hold a dominant position in the market\n* Does not develop a public service or an essential facility\n* Is not obligated by law to grant indiscriminate access to its services to third parties\n* Has business autonomy and liberty to decide whether to engage or not with third parties. \n\n \n\nWe trust that this information is sufficient to clarify our position, and that it will avoid any further discontent with your clients.\n\nKind regards,”","2026-01-08T15:43:56.533Z"],["3796834","FPD-1414","FPD","matteo.casolari@bolt.eu","Matteo Casolari","*Update:*\n\n* Launched new backtests with *30* and *100* hyperparameter tuning trials.\n* During execution, the Databricks experiment hit the *maximum number of runs* limit (500K).\n* Attempted to delete old MLflow runs, but this proved to be very slow and not scalable.\n* To unblock progress, updated the backtest to *save artifacts to S3 instead of MLflow*, removing the run-count limitation.\n* This required also changing the *default location where* {{MarketplaceModel}} *reads/writes files* to point to S3.\n* After these changes, I’m seeing frequent backtest failures with errors like:\n{{Exception: Failed to generate marketplace model predictions: NoCredentialsError: Unable to locate credentials}}.\n\nCurrently investigating the credential-related failures.","2026-01-08T15:44:41.342Z"],["3796836","FPD-1434","FPD","matteo.casolari@bolt.eu","Matteo Casolari","Summary document available [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/k4DwsAE].","2026-01-08T15:45:28.564Z"],["3796838","WD-22523","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:614ad8f9fac3ce0069e51a4c] , you'll have to raise the topic under the following Service Desk: \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/28|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/28|smart-link]  ","2026-01-08T15:45:58.895Z"],["3796839","LSS-61295","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-08T15:46:36.907Z"],["3796840","PRIV-512","PRIV","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (08.01)*+\n\n* There seems to be a diverge in opinion of who is responsible for direct marketing:\n** Ops Manager ([+link+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09258PDYE9/p1767643699459419?thread_ts=1767605626.101269&cid=C09258PDYE9]): *Bolt* will handle the processing and delivery of email and SMS communications. Parter will handle localisation and ad hoc messages.\n** Legal ([link|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09258PDYE9/p1767814568337039?thread_ts=1767605626.101269&cid=C09258PDYE9]) & Agreement ([link|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1s2xGXXAWjVkA_m44Swia8fI8yv8CSwF1/edit]): *Partner* is responsible for marketing. Bolt will only provide support services.\n*** Ban has asked Rostislav to clarify this discrepancy.\n* Depending on advice:\n** (a) Bolt responsible for collecting consent / sending marketing:\n*** We should include opt-in consent for email/SMS in the order flow.\n*** We should ensure consents / opt-outs are shared with the partner.\n** (b) Partner responsible for collecting consent / sending marketing:\n*** Push partner to include opt-in consent for email/SMS in the order flow.\n*** Push partner to share consents / opt-outs with Bolt.\n\n----\n\nIn terms of what consent will need to look like in practice:\n\n* *Opt-in*: Driver registration flow should ask for opt-in consent for *email/SMS* marketing to send the user *both Bolt and third-party marketing*. It should include a link to the privacy notice, and flag *opt-out right*.\n** At this point, I would need to see the proposed language / ask Kostya what the standard disclaimers and practices are here, so that I can sure close alignment where possible.\n*** Language may look something like (e.g., [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08PFDXTJF6/p1762527667636669?thread_ts=1760716268.432169&cid=C08PFDXTJF6]), assuming that we go for the higher opt-in standard (if not, then I will need to consider current language elsewhere with Kostya):\n**** Tickbox - “Do you agree to receive marketing communications?”\n**** Disclaimer - “I agree to receive marketing communications, including updates, special offers and promotions, from Bolt via email, SMS, or other {color:#403294}relevant{color} channels. I understand {color:#403294}that Bolt may send me marketing relating to both Bolt services and those of third-party controllers, {color}that I can unsubscribe at any time{color:#403294}, and that further information on privacy can be found HERE{color}”.\n*** NB. We should only ask for email/SMS opt-in consent if we are going to respect this. If we will not, then no point pushing for this language, as we would be publicly acknowledging our position and digging ourselves into a hole.\n** In an ideal world, we would collect separate consents to email, SMS and push notifications. However, I doubt the business will be willing to be this granular.\n*** NB. If the business does not accept opt-in consent for email/SMS, then: (i) flag general risks to the business; (ii) ensure no SCD/criminal data; (iii) ensure that the disclaimer language is clear and mentions third-party marketing; and (iv) the right to opt-out is prevalent.\n** We can otherwise sent third-party marketing to Bolt users without consent provided that the channels are not email/SMS, as the above language/process would trigger the exception.\n*** If the business does not go for the email/SMS opt-in, Plan A would be to advise them that they do not need it for mediums other than email/SMS, and Plan B would be to say that they can go ahead with email/SMS (as we are covered process-wise) but that this is a grey area and riskier (and so not recommended).\n* *Opt-out*: In the Bolt app / platform, the user should have toggles for the usual categories (Bolt Products, Partner Offers, Promotions etc., with toggles for email, SMS and push notifications), so that the user can easily opt-out.","2026-01-08T15:47:35.275Z"],["3796841","PFI-831051","PFI","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Yes, I think reissuing the Ride Invoice (from South Africa to Tanzania account) plus transferring the cost between accounts should be sufficient.  From my reading of their email, screen shots shared, I believe that’s what they are proposing. \n\nBut my apologies I am not sure about the impplications of Statements and SF Invoices.  Do you mean when the monthly bill for January is issued, the transfer would not be reflected, as that wouldn’t make sense to me.  Plus not sure what SF invoices refers too.  As the trip was taken in this month, would the statement issue even apply as it’s not out yet?   Please advise as I may be missing your point as am not familiar with the statement + SF invoice from a billings work flow perspective. ","2026-01-08T15:48:11.404Z"],["3796843","PFI-830556","PFI","rita.goncalves@bolt.eu","Rita Teles Gonçalves","Thank you! Can you please confirm that if changed now, all the payments will be made in the next cycle (next Monday)?\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:9d55cde8-4889-4cc5-9d25-472a197c7697] for vis for a possible onboarding rules review?","2026-01-08T15:48:15.513Z"],["3796844","LSS-59991","LSS","alexandros.lamprou@bolt.eu","Alexandros Lamprou","thank you Angela, is it ok if I cc you on the answer?","2026-01-08T15:48:47.480Z"],["3796846","DRX-28007","DRX","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","Link for investigation [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"start\"%3A1766962800%2C\"show_empty_rejection_code\"%3Afalse%2C\"show_total\"%3Afalse%2C\"external_client_id\"%3A240424}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1766962800%2C%22show_empty_rejection_code%22%3Afalse%2C%22show_total%22%3Afalse%2C%22external_client_id%22%3A240424%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] ","2026-01-08T15:50:12.284Z"],["3796849","PFI-830556","PFI","rita.goncalves@bolt.eu","Rita Teles Gonçalves","And, for clarity, does this affect all the beneficiary names that have these kinds of characters? Because I see accepted payments for other accounts with the same ones.\nThank you ","2026-01-08T15:52:13.080Z"],["3796851","DO-5778","DO","felix.woll@bolt.eu","Felix Wöll","Your Table has been dropped.\nI will merge the PR :wink:","2026-01-08T15:53:58.049Z"],["3796855","LSS-61289","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey [~accountid:60c88e6e8f2cc1006909fcf6] - Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Bolt Services LT, UAB Subtiekėjo sutikimas.adoc]\n\n","2026-01-08T15:54:32.759Z"],["3796856","DO-5778","DO","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","Thank you!","2026-01-08T15:54:40.813Z"],["3796858","RDS-688","RDS","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] there are multiple settings that drivers can select as their preferences. And more often than not, it is counterproductive to them, in terms of utilization and earnings.\n\nThe idea is to expose this information to drivers, with the data of how many orders they have missed, how many time they have been filtered out by matching system and by what reasons, and what they can do to improve their performance","2026-01-08T15:55:24.917Z"],["3796859","LSS-61259","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hey [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]! Thank you a lot for this insight. Bank details are back to their initial states, and fraudulent document has been rejected on Fleet Profile. I’ve re-activated payouts.\n[~accountid:712020:af076e83-bb33-4eb6-8634-6e435217c5e4] I’m letting you take it from here, please let me know if you need us to inform the FO or if you need any other info 🙂 ","2026-01-08T15:55:38.332Z"],["3796860","BDB-1494","BDB","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","Thanks [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] ! feel free to proceed with creating the files","2026-01-08T15:56:29.309Z"],["3796861","WD-14199","WD","kristiina.vaik@bolt.eu","Kristiina Vaik","Thank you! I can’t see the task 🤔 . I don’t mind if you run the task yourself 🙂 \n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 17.55.53.png|width=539,height=196,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 17.55.53.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 17.55.29.png|width=443,height=195,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 17.55.29.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-08T15:57:41.420Z"],["3796862","HS-28745","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","Hi Razvan \n\nPlease specify what kind of letter you need specifically. \n\nThanks ahead\nAlice, Senior People Operations Specialist ","2026-01-08T15:58:01.827Z"],["3796863","WFM-9903","WFM","shivam.pal@bolt-outsource.eu","Shivam Pal","thank you for your help","2026-01-08T15:58:47.319Z"],["3796864","INSUR-175","INSUR","alessandro@bolt.eu","Alessandro Milici","h3. *1. Scope of Coverage & Activation*\n\n* *Insured Parties:* All drivers and passengers registered on the Bolt platform.\n* *Vehicle Capacity:* \n** *Cars:* 1 Driver + 4 Passengers.\n** *Motorcycles:* 1 Driver + 1 Passenger.\n* *Coverage Trigger:* Must include the \"En Route\" phase (from trip acceptance) and the trip itself, as well as a *30-minute extension post-trip*.\n\nh3. *2. Required Coverage Limits (Per Person)*\n\nPlease quote for both options below. All limits are per person:\n\n|*Coverage Item*|*Option A (Gs.)*|*Option A (€ approx.)*|*Option B (Gs.)*|*Option B (€ approx.)*|\n|*Death (< 65 years)*|₲ 107.627.000|*€ 12.915*|₲ 180.000.000|*€ 21.600*|\n|*Death (65+ years)*|₲ 53.813.500|*€ 6.458*|₲ 180.000.000|*€ 21.600*|\n|*Death (Unborn Persons)*|₲ 53.813.500|*€ 6.458*|₲ 180.000.000|*€ 21.600*|\n|*Total & Permanent Disability*|₲ 107.627.000|*€ 12.915*|₲ 180.000.000|*€ 21.600*|\n|*Medical/Hospital Expenses*|₲ 16.144.050|*€ 1.937*|₲ 14.000.000|*€ 1.680*|\n|*Adult Recovery (Reposo)*|₲ 6.457.620|*€ 775*|₲ 10.000.000|*€ 1.200*|\n|*Minor Recovery (Reposo)*|₲ 3.874.572|*€ 465*|₲ 10.000.000|*€ 1.200*|\n|*Funeral Expenses*|₲ 12.000.000|*€ 1.440*|₲ 36.000.000|*€ 4.320*|\n\nh3. *3. Global Limits & Pricing Model*\n\n* *Catastrophic Limit: Gs. 6,600,000,000.* This represents the maximum limit the insurer would cover in the event of an accident involving multiple victims arising from the same catastrophic incident. This limit is set by reinsurers for the insurers. As a reference, to reach this amount, the number of fatalities from a single incident/accident would need to be 61 people, with an insured sum of Gs. 107,627,000 each (in Option 2), totalling Gs. 6,565,247,000.\n* *Reinstatement: 1 reinstatement at no cost.* This means the maximum limit covered by the insurer during the policy term in the event of claims can be up to 2 times the catastrophic limit, i.e., Gs. 13,200,000,000 (approximately *equivalent to 123 fatalities within the policy term).*\n* *Pricing Structure:* A monthly floating premium based on active drivers. We require a *Siniestralidad (Claim Ratio) Adjustment Model*.\n** _Note:_ The premium should only move to a higher \"Level\" if the claim ratio (paid claims/premium) exceeds *60%*.\n\nh3. *4. Key Service Requirements*\n\n* *Real-time Claims Consulting:* Access to a digital platform for Bolt to track claim statuses.\n* *Customer Support:* Online claim forms and WhatsApp support for claimants.\n* *Fast-Track Death Benefits:* Provision for immediate payout via notarised agreement with direct family members.\n* *Additional Clauses:* Coverage must include Assault, Riots/Strikes, and specific Driver Accident coverage.\n\nh3. *5. Operational Context & Projections*\n\nTo assist in your assessment, please find our operational data below:\n\n* *Total Finished Trips (2025 Actuals):* [Insert Data]\n* *Projected Finished Trips (2026):* [Insert Data]\n* *Total GMV (2025 Actuals):* [Insert Data]\n* *Projected GMV (2026):* [Insert Data]\n* *Current/Projected Number of Active Drivers (2026):* [Insert Data]\n\n----\n\nWaiting for data, so I can send this out to our broker. [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nco3WHJxN3qP9hO839mc0-eIrjkd2wkK_bujCHmi8os/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nco3WHJxN3qP9hO839mc0-eIrjkd2wkK_bujCHmi8os/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T15:59:13.527Z"],["3796865","HS-28699","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-08T15:59:32.124Z"],["3796867","LSS-61258","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","PL\n\nPełnomocnictwo to obowiązuje w stosunku do każdego z pełnomocników od 01.01.2026 do 31.12.2026 chyba, że zostanie wcześniej odwołane przez Spółkę wobec danego pełnomocnika poprzez złożenie oświadczenia o odwołaniu lub do dnia zakończenia umowy o pracę pomiędzy Spółką a danym pełnomocnikiem (w zależności od tego, które z tych zdarzeń wystąpi wcześniej). Niniejsze Pełnomocnictwo zostaje udzielone bez prawa delegacji upoważnienia.\n\nENG\n\nThis power of attorney shall be valid for each of the attorneys from January 1, 2026, to December 31, 2026, unless it is revoked earlier by the Company with respect to a given attorney by submitting a statement of revocation or until the date of termination of the employment contract between the Company and a given attorney (whichever occurs first). This Power of Attorney is granted without the right to delegate authority.","2026-01-08T16:02:36.333Z"],["3796868","LSS-61258","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hello [~accountid:5bb399378eb5ad7760adb25e]! Please add a link to an editable version of this PoA, thank you! ","2026-01-08T16:03:02.382Z"],["3796869","PFI-830952","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Payout now resent. ","2026-01-08T16:03:42.109Z"],["3796873","LSS-60347","LSS","kaija.riismaa@bolt.eu","Kaija Riismaa","Seems that there were two different tickets created for this request from Language Board and the response to it has already been drafted and submitted. \n\nOther ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LSS/issue/LSS-60609|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LSS/issue/LSS-60609]\n\nResponse: [^Vastus_Keeleamet.asice] \n\nClosing the ticket as it is completed already. ","2026-01-08T16:05:39.748Z"],["3796874","HS-28745","HS","razvan.nastase@bolt.eu","Răzvan Năstase","Hello!  I need an employment certificate for my family doctor confirming that I am employed and covered by the public health insurance system.","2026-01-08T16:06:25.894Z"],["3796875","DRAG101-471","DRAG101","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] Absolutely, [~accountid:5eb363355862510b794e3507] & [~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] will arrange 3 samples of the vehicle to HQ, and when we receive them, we can do the upfitting guide.","2026-01-08T16:06:26.645Z"],["3796879","DRX-28007","DRX","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","Investigation results:\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yXxlZfIEUa66LQK0WRMMEiAaqPRSr-c4l2s6_tXEFyE/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yXxlZfIEUa66LQK0WRMMEiAaqPRSr-c4l2s6_tXEFyE/edit?gid=0#gid=0]","2026-01-08T16:11:33.672Z"],["3796882","PAW-14742","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-08T16:13:16.089Z"],["3796883","PRF-814","PRF","britt.doll@bolt.eu","Britt Doll","[~accountid:5d639884388d780dac23dfe7] Could you let me know if we have since paused these ads from actively running as our rights have now expired as we’re past Dec 31? ","2026-01-08T16:13:17.798Z"],["3796884","L10N-26759","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26757](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26757)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T16:13:20.668Z"],["3796885","L10N-26760","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epi