nd discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26757](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26757)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T16:13:32.956Z"],["3796894","L10N-26783","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26757](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26757)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-08T16:13:33.373Z"],["3796895","LSS-61296","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*BACKGROUND*+\n\n* On 19 November 2025, an Estonian rider (Ardo Aari) emailed Bolt CS ([link|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/688842467]).\n** Recently, an adult family member of the complainant used the Bolt app but paid for the ride using the complainant’s bank card. \n** This was allegedly done “_without the platform identifying or verifying the actual legitimate user of the transaction_”, and so the complainant is concerned.\n*** Complainant uses a ‘kitchen sink’ approach in alleging possible violations, and alleges that Bolt does not ensure security, is not transparent, processes without a legal basis, has caused a data breach that was not notified to AKI (on the basis that there was “_unauthorised access or identity use in transactions_”. The complainant has not provided evidence / elaborated on why.\n** Complainant asked the following questions:\n*** (1) “_How does Bolt Operations OÜ verify that the person associated with the payment instrument is either the person performing the transaction or has given their explicit consent for its use?_”\n*** (2) “_What risk prevention and fraud detection measures are implemented to detect unauthorized payments?_”\n*** (3) “_How does Bolt Operations OÜ ensure that the situation described does not conflict with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) or the requirements of the Personal Data Protection Act (IKS)?_”\n*** (4) “_What are the company's official procedures for handling cases where there is suspicion of identity theft, unauthorized transactions, or possible data breaches?_”\n** Complainant demanded a response by 3 December 2025. Threatened to go to AKI if no responses received.\n* On the same day, CS did not respond, but instead noted as an internal comment “_User didn't reply to the webform, so case was closed automatically_”.\n** As a result, the complainant submitted a complaint to AKI.\n* On 8 January 2026, AKI forwarded the complaint to Bolt. AKI is focused on the fact that Bolt did not respond to the complainant’s DSAR (and not the other allegations).\n** AKI has requested the following:\n*** (1) Either: (a) confirm when the complainant’s DSAR was responded to (and provide a copy); or (b) explain why the complainant’s DSAR was not responded to and when we intend to respond.\n*** (2) Provide “_explanations and reasons that you consider necessary in this matter_”.\n** Response is due by 23 January 2026. \n\n+*INVESTIGATION*+\n\n* Rider profile is active ([profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/5947130/overview]). Last order on 7 January 2026. \n* Two active payment methods on the account, created in July and November 2025.\n* No other emails from the complainant. However, this CS in-app thread ([LINK|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/685488858]) appears to be relevant to the complainant’s complaint. \n** NB. This applies to the complainant as a *_scooter rider_*_._ CS seems to think this is micro mobility related, due to the relevant order (below).\n** On 13 November 2025, complainant claimed “_There has been an unknown payment on my account_”. \n*** Based on EUR 0.8 being reserved from their account, which they did not recognise.\n** Complainant provided a bank statement / card payment receipt from complainant to Bolt. \n*** Amount of EUR 0.78, due to trip on 3 November, paid for with card ending in 4242 (which is an active card on the complainant’s profile, added in Nov 2025 - complainant confirmed the details); transaction number and date were RO4016840669 04/11/2025.\n** CS searched for the corresponding charge internally. \n*** Only charge from Nov 2025 is here ([LINK|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3840591154] / [LINK|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2246534806/1?orderTryId=2849184558] - RH), where details do not match (EUR 5.40, on 10 Nov).\n*** Later on, CS Ops (Monica Kartsev) found this payment ([LINK|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-balance/trxHistory/user/5947130/booking/1265142736] - MM) of EUR 0.78 for the complainant, but it is from 13 August 2023.\n*** After that, another member of CS Ops (Juri Žuravljov) found this payment of EUR 0.78 ([LINK|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3820156949]). However, this concerns the rider _Oscar_ Aari ([profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/177896590]), and a separate payment method (ending in 5042, which has never appeared on the complainant’s profile). There is no obvious nexus to the complainant’s profile / trips. As such, {color:#ff5630}*it appears that Juri flagged this in error*{color}.\n** It appears that Outsourced CS (Kiril Pahhomov) then{color:#ff5630} *miscommunicated the situation to the complainant*{color} (“_We have checked and found that a person named Oscar with the phone number +372xxxx2622 has used your payment method_”).\n*** This is not correct - Oscar used their own payment method for a completely separate trip.\n*** Given the surname, and the fact that AKI flagged that an adult family member is involved, logically this must be the complainant’s family member.\n** This then concerned the complainant (“_How is it possible that someone else is using my card?… Has my data been leaked from Bolt's server? Or can anyone who has ever seen my card number use it freely? Bolt does not ask for confirmation from the bank or the cardholder to verify the card_”).\n*** In reality, the complainant’s data has not been leaked. No-one else has been using their card.\n\n+*THOUGHTS*+\n\n* General:\n** This is a case of a CS Ops / Outsourced CS error blowing things way out of proportion.\n*** CS Ops identified the wrong user. Outsourced CS did not choose their words carefully and created the impression that a separate user has used the complainants payment method, whereas in reality it does not look like this is the case.\n** Ultimately, this case does not require detailed answers to every single issue raised by the complainant, for the following reasons:\n*** (a) The extent of the complainant’s questions seems a tad ridiculous. They have suffered no obvious harm here (a _family member_ at best would have used their card to take a Bolt trip), and so this hardly amounts to ‘identity theft’ or a ‘reportable personal data breach’.\n*** (b) The complainant’s core concern is non-existent - this was a case of poorly chosen words, not a data breach. We should focus on that.\n*** (c) It is notable that AKI is primarily focused on the DSAR, and is not asking follow-ups of its own. This may indicate that AKI recognises the situation here, and so is only focused on the 'serious issue'\n* Responses to the questions:\n** AKI:\n*** DSAR Issue:\n**** Not responded to due to human error. We can say that we are reviewing processes and discussing with the relevant stakeholders.\n**** Either: (a) we have now responded; or (b) we will shortly respond, and provide a copy in either case.\n*** Otherwise, hit home that this was a phrasing error, and the complainant’s payment method is in no way at risk.\n** Complainant:\n*** Headline point - There has been no data breach here, and no unauthorised payment. This was a simple miscommunication error. We respectfully reject allegations that there are been privacy violations here.\n**** Offer the rider a copy of their personal data if they want it.\n*** (1) How Bolt verifies that the owner of a payment method is the person performing the transaction (i.e., taking a trip) or has consented to its use.\n**** {color:#ff5630}TBC whether we initially verify payment methods.{color}\n**** We mention how this is an appropriate security measure (per A5(1)(f), A24 and A32), when paired with other security measures to safeguard accounts (including any other applicable rider _identity_ checks). Data protection by design and default is deployed for such systems (per A25).\n**** Nothing else is needed. Bolt does not need to verify payment method every time (this is not sustainable - users expect a smooth process), and we would not know if a user has given their “consent” for others to use their payment method.\n*** (2) Bolt’s risk prevention / fraud detection measures that detect unauthorised payments.\n**** {color:#ff5630}TBC a high-level overview of how we detect unauthorised payments{color}. These are appropriate in light of A5(1)(f), A24 and A32.\n**** We cannot specify triggers, as such information threatens rights and freedoms of other users.\n*** (3) How Bolt ensures compliance with data protection laws regarding payments / authorised transactions.\n**** No need to go into detail here - we will do so as we answer. \n**** We can otherwise say that Bolt ensures it has has an appropriate legal basis of processing, as listed in our privacy notice (this covers A6 and transparency points).\n*** (4) How Bolt handles cases where there is suspicion of identity theft, unauthorised transactions or possible data breaches.\n**** {color:#ff5630}TBC an overview of how identity theft / unauthorised transaction cases are escalated and dealt with{color}.\n**** Re PDBs, we can summarise the process. Incident is escalated to the privacy team, who records it and reviews it in line with GDPR requirements. If the incident meets reporting thresholds (per A34/34), then it is escalated. \n**** Reiterate that no such incident has occurred here. As such, no notifications required at this time.\n\n+*NEXT STEPS*+\n\n* QUESTIONS ([LINK|https://docs.google.com/document/d/10ESAe2PmAKTtUNPc0Tf-ozrHrwU7sL2tpRZ1VSYqFLY/edit?tab=t.0]).\n* Draft responses once information received.","2026-01-08T16:13:34.475Z"],["3796903","LSS-61210","LSS","marc.naether@bolt.eu","Marc Naether","Hi, would it be possible to get this document signed by tomorrow morning? Many thanks!","2026-01-08T16:18:35.584Z"],["3796904","LSS-61105","LSS","ramone.edwards@bolt.eu","Ramone Edwards","[~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] The driver’s access has been reinstated as of yesterday. ","2026-01-08T16:19:29.885Z"],["3796906","SRED-1043","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done","2026-01-08T16:21:14.783Z"],["3796907","SRED-1044","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done","2026-01-08T16:21:21.876Z"],["3796908","LSS-61259","LSS","raphael.perna@bolt.eu","Raphaël Samy Perna","Thank you [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] and your team for the detailed investigation and the clear timeline.\n\nI will proceed immediately with all your recommendations regarding this Fleet Owner. \n\nThanks! [~accountid:712020:dbc22d70-1983-4414-80b3-27f087787ae4]  I will handle the communication with the FO.\n\nThe overview you provided is very clear, so I have everything I need to explain the situation to him and close the loop. I'll let you know if any further questions arise\n\n","2026-01-08T16:21:41.758Z"],["3796909","PFI-831077","PFI","chinedu.ukaegbu@bolt-outsource.eu","Chinedu Ukaegbu","!JPEG_1767613180267_1047899208090448900.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T16:22:04.029Z"],["3796911","DSR-3595","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-08T16:26:46.896Z"],["3796912","SREDESK-7392","SREDESK","andrus.viik@bolt.eu","Andrus Viik","Waiting for approvals","2026-01-08T16:27:36.814Z"],["3796913","PFI-830769","PFI","beatriz.almeida@bolt-outsource.eu","Beatriz Almeida","This is the only information the user is able to provide that is already on the support case.\n\n!image-20260108-162733.png|width=1800,height=4000,alt=\"image-20260108-162733.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-08T16:27:58.713Z"],["3796914","FX-3585","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767889679102239]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@pavel.grigorev>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3585] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T16:28:11.505Z"],["3796915","FX-3585","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767889692460119]*{color}:\ndetails:\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02EZE0V0FM/p1767881973504689]\n\nLinked messages:\n[January 8th, 2026 6:19 AM] alerter: :redalert: *ERROR :: fleet-car-data :: [K8S][live-euc-1-federated] Pod has been restarting in the last 5 minutes* *1.13* pods have been restarted for the last 5 minutes. Please pay attention to your service\n{quote}","2026-01-08T16:28:45.048Z"],["3796916","LSS-61259","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Great, thank you both. Wishing you a nice evening! ","2026-01-08T16:29:01.627Z"],["3796917","LSS-61140","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a], thank you very much for your prompt review and the detailed feedback with your privacy recommendations in the documents. We have reviewed your feedback and amendments with [~accountid:712020:cf457436-e17c-4575-8d48-f2b9135ccc82] and [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9]. We are fully aligned with your recommendations.\n\nAs you have suggested, I have put these edits in the FR document with the explanatory comments as well for ARPE to review. In case they push back, the non-negotiable push back should be focused on removing Recital (D) and editing Clause 3.2.\n\nIn response to your questions:\n\n# Yes, only the VTC number + confirmation of whether they are under fleet or not;\n# Yes, our local compliance team will extract the data and use the algorithm in order to pseudonymise the data before sharing.\n\n[~accountid:712020:cf457436-e17c-4575-8d48-f2b9135ccc82] please find attached the downloaded document with the visible tracked changes to be shared with ARPE. If you have any questions for Regional Legal or Privacy before sending the convention for review, please let us know.\n\nThank you \n\n[^CONVENTION ARPE - partage et traitement de données _ Bolt.docx] \n\n\n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] [~accountid:5be58278903b2054a70c21b9] ","2026-01-08T16:29:04.255Z"],["3796919","SUPX-2204","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","Why is this marked as triaged if we don’t know how to approach this [~accountid:712020:05337a38-da5a-4860-91ed-01ab7b7b6cca] ?","2026-01-08T16:29:59.866Z"],["3796920","XP-2978","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","Expanded scope to account for Average Power concept from this [paper|https://assets.amazon.science/dd/9d/c57c3b78497d95893ec0c3010cdf/rethinkingpower-fv.pdf] presented at MITCode","2026-01-08T16:31:04.446Z"],["3796921","LSS-61297","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-08T16:31:07.168Z"],["3796923","DO-5771","DO","michal.konarski@bolt.eu","Michał Konarski","Hi! Access to Databricks itself is managed by IT. Please submit your ticket here:[ |https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/group/1/create/932][https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/group/1/create/932|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/group/1/create/932|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T16:33:56.655Z"],["3796924","DO-5776","DO","michal.konarski@bolt.eu","Michał Konarski","Access granted.","2026-01-08T16:35:34.102Z"],["3796925","DSR-3597","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-08T16:36:09.508Z"],["3796928","BP-13390","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","[~accountid:712020:3c6bcc42-4172-4c4d-b924-e17fb5f0a336] do we have BE endpoint to get the data?","2026-01-08T16:41:50.003Z"],["3796929","HS-28252","HS","dmitriy.rassadkin@bolt.eu","Dmytro Rassadkin","Hey, any update?","2026-01-08T16:42:40.994Z"],["3796931","DO-5770","DO","michal.konarski@bolt.eu","Michał Konarski","Hi!\n\nWe (Data Platform) do not manage the Salesforce platform. I suppose you can seek help on Slack. #salesforce-rollout-global seems to be an active channel. ","2026-01-08T16:44:13.316Z"],["3796932","LSS-61295","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41] ,\nMy recommendation is to send the following response:\n\n_“Exmo. Senhor Inspetor Miguel Padela,_\n\n_Agradecemos o seu contacto._\n\n_A Bolt manifesta total disponibilidade para colaborar com as autoridades competentes no âmbito do inquérito em referência. No entanto, considerando a estrutura da empresa e o facto de a sua atividade se desenvolver através de diferentes vertentes operacionais — nomeadamente transporte de passageiros (ride-hailing), entregas (Bolt Food), e micromobilidade (Rentals), entre outros — seria importante obter, ainda que de forma genérica, uma indicação sobre o tema ou contexto a que respeita o processo._\n\n_Essa informação permitir-nos-á identificar a pessoa mais adequada para comparecer e prestar os esclarecimentos necessários, assegurando que dispõe do conhecimento relevante no âmbito do inquérito._\n\n_Ficamos a aguardar o seu esclarecimento para podermos proceder em conformidade._\n\n_Entretanto, mantemo-nos ao dispor para qualquer esclarecimento adicional._\n\n_Com os melhores cumprimentos,”_\n\n\n\nThank you!","2026-01-08T16:44:49.547Z"],["3796933","FX-3586","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767890839150499]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@chantel.rowe>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3586] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-08T16:47:30.649Z"],["3796934","HS-28766","HS","leonora.lukoviczki@bolt.eu","Leonóra Lukoviczki","!Dustin Williams_Parental leave.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T16:47:39.248Z"],["3796936","LSS-60617","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:c428e4fe-c7e8-428c-98b9-afce638acb45] [~accountid:5fc514a09592df00761a5d3d] \n\n*Summary – Legal Review Outcome*\n\nThe following points are approved by [~accountid:5fc514a09592df00761a5d3d]  and accepted:\n\n* Fixed term of 5 years with automatic 1-year extension\n* One-time special termination right after 2.5 years (*with a 6-month notice period*)\n* Cap for Schönheitsreparaturen and Wartung at 5% of the annual net rent\n\n*Remaining risks and recommendations are set out below:*\n\n\n*Key Risk – 6-Month Notice Period for Break Option (§ 2.3)*\n\nThe special termination right after 2.5 years can only be exercised once and requires a strict 6-month notice period by registered letter.\n\nImpact\nIf the deadline is missed, Bolt is bound until the end of the fixed term (31.12.2030) and may incur several years of additional rent despite loss of commercial relevance of the site.\n\nRecommendation\nTreat the notice deadline as a fixed contractual milestone. Ops and Finance must diarise the deadline early and decide in advance whether the break option will be exercised.\n\n\n*Power Capacity – Missing Contractual Guarantee*\n\nThe lease does not contain a binding guarantee on minimum power capacity, timing of availability, or cost allocation for upgrades.\n\nImpact\nRisk of delayed or limited operability and unplanned investment by Bolt.\n\nRecommendation\nAsk the landlord to include a short contractual guarantee confirming sufficient power capacity for Bolt’s intended use as of handover (or by a fixed deadline) and to clarify who bears upgrade costs. If the contract is not reopened, obtain written confirmation at handover. Otherwise we have the option to terminate the contract still.\n\n\n*Index Clause – Outdated Reference (§ 6)*\n\nThe rent adjustment clause refers to a consumer index that is no longer published by the German Federal Statistical Office.\n\nImpact\nPotential ambiguity or dispute in future rent adjustments.\n\nRecommendation\nIf the contract is amended, replace the clause with a reference to the German Consumer Price Index (VPI). Otherwise, accept as low risk.\n\n\n*Overall Assessment*\n\nThe contract is acceptable following GM approval for all remaining risks or in case we can still negotiate them. \n\nClarification of power capacity are strongly recommended.","2026-01-08T16:49:48.151Z"],["3796939","HS-28767","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-08T16:53:29.778Z"],["3796940","SREDESK-7394","SREDESK","konstantin.mitrakov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Mitrakov","If it matters for a potential cluster, the schema is from taxify_rental_car_order_scheduled, taxify_rental_car_order family","2026-01-08T16:55:22.379Z"],["3796941","INT-759","INT","guru.prasath@bolt.eu","Guru .","[~accountid:712020:6f095333-c438-429c-9660-a9de5d845fe7] Sharing the requirements scope: \n\nh2. *Spend alerts requirements*\n\n* GAs should receive automated Slack alerts in the existing country-level Delivery campaign channels.\n* Alerts should trigger when weekly Bolt Plus spend crosses a GA-defined threshold.\n* GAs should be able to specify the below particulars on admin panel :\n** Start and end dates of the MD campaign period \n** Set weekly spend thresholds \n\n*How spend thresholds are defined and used?*\n\n* As part of the monthly capital allocation, a total Bolt Plus spend is approved. This covers all delivery benefits: FD, MD, and SF.\n* GAs split this monthly budget into weekly spend targets, based on seasonality and planned investments (front/back loaded). [+Monthly Spend Execution Planner (June)+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1h1Ecxt1GfigxK8OHDuD5YYJP03i2GGrD7z5734w5qdM/edit?gid=1875914598#gid=1875914598]\n* Bolt Plus MD campaigns usually run for a period of one week, typically in the 3rd week of the month when organic demand dips. These campaigns often span across two calendar weeks [+Bolt Plus MD - Calendar+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1D09slZ25-ZULT50VQtoz2Orr_qRhWc-oZl4Ud6tleQg/edit?gid=180310267#gid=180310267]\n* For the calendar weeks the MD campaigns are running:\n** Actual weekly Bolt Plus spend (MD + FD + SF) is tracked against the defined weekly threshold.\n** If spend crosses the threshold, a Slack alert is sent.\n** Based on these alerts, GAs coordinate with local teams to decide on campaign adjustments (scale down MD depths, remove providers, pause, reallocate, etc.)","2026-01-08T16:56:26.537Z"],["3796943","FRAUDOPS-1058","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","# *Drivers*\n\nThe hypothesis of this being a France problem is quite clear. Limited to drivers that have more than 1 comment about sharing or impersonation. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 17.44.13.png|width=494,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 17.44.13.png\"!\n\nDrivers with more than one impersonation or account sharing comment and actual order volume. Past 3 months. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 17.02.08.png|width=1036,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 17.02.08.png\"!\n\nWe can see that most drivers are at a third report/comment but the most ‘problematic' is the 2nd report. This is supported by the supposed process that on third report the drivers should be permanently suspended. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.08.33.png|width=936,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.08.33.png\"!\n\n🚩  We can see that there are about 5K in FR accounts that have comments but only 1K of them have produced order volume. Either these are abandoned, recently suspended or sleeper accounts. \n\nLet’s check only account that are active and created after 1/2024\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.15.42.png|width=424,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.15.42.png\"!\n\nHidden accounts can be accounts that have been hibernated due to fleet move. 3.3K active ‘new’ drivers. \nThe creation of these accounts really took off around April 2025.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.19.49.png|width=1800,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.19.49.png\"!\n\nWe can see that some accounts with reports have ‘matured’ earlier → e.g. it is logical that the earlier your account is created, the earlier your reach more reports.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.24.48.png|width=1239,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.24.48.png\"!\n\n*Now to compare with fraud volumes:* \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.40.23.png|width=1239,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.40.23.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.59.17.png|width=1239,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 18.59.17.png\"!","2026-01-08T16:59:40.862Z"],["3796944","LSS-61258","LSS","sylwia.wiktorowska@bolt.eu","Sylwia Wiktorowska","Hi, sure! [Here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1u_lJap_MtqCCnO12ljqPhQQsj8pXOQeTmwQ9tw5tEho/edit?usp=sharing]\n\n","2026-01-08T17:00:29.961Z"],["3796945","PFI-831038","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-08T17:00:54.075Z"],["3796946","PFI-831018","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-08T17:00:55.052Z"],["3796950","LSS-61299","LSS","katarzyna.karwan@bolt.eu","Katarzyna Karwan","[^Katarzyna Karwan PEL Bolt Poland.pdf] _(248 kB)_","2026-01-08T17:07:27.236Z"],["3796951","LSS-61298","LSS","azza.ltifi@bolt.eu","Azza Letifi","I am not sure how that “_KPIs (set monthly thresholds - remove all metrics that aren’t applicable)_” appeared after submitting the ticket. Please ignore","2026-01-08T17:07:38.310Z"],["3796953","PFI-813839","PFI","auguste.rakauskaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Augustė Rakauskaitė","Are there any updates on this? ","2026-01-08T17:09:42.439Z"],["3796954","BIZ-290","BIZ","ana.abenza@bolt.eu","Ana Abenza","Hi all, added the one-pager and description to this Jira MVRA project now for everyone’s reference.\n\n[~accountid:712020:a0124a71-9df9-4683-aa0c-9dea10fcc90e] and [~accountid:712020:8664dd4c-2e90-4dfb-b1bf-6b699c019bd4] in my team will be Project Managing this initiative.","2026-01-08T17:12:06.814Z"],["3796959","LSS-61298","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-08T17:16:09.636Z"],["3796961","LEG-1133","LEG","ana.abenza@bolt.eu","Ana Abenza","Hey [~accountid:612f31d89976c300693ebaf7] just following up on this to check if we can close the ticket","2026-01-08T17:19:00.895Z"],["3796963","LSS-61128","LSS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","Hi Giulia, sure! \n\nCould you please kindly make it indefinite? I didn’t put any dates on purpose. \n\nThanks! \nEwa\n\n[^Ewa Ożańska PEL Bolt Poland.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-08T17:20:31.318Z"],["3796967","LSS-61300","LSS","declan.giles@bolt.eu","Declan Giles","[^Vollmacht.pdf] _(157 kB)_\n\n[^Klageabweisungsantrag_an_Landgericht_Berlin_II__1_Instanz_.pdf.pdf] _(153 kB)_","2026-01-08T17:23:52.904Z"],["3796969","HS-28534","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hei Ardo, annan teada, et OTP on nüüd WD-s kinnitatud ja on edastatud Yizhoule väljamakseks. Sulgen selle pileti. ","2026-01-08T17:24:18.368Z"],["3796970","LSS-60766","LSS","ieva.fowler@bolt.eu","Ieva Fowler","Thanks [~accountid:712020:1d5390cd-af56-43c8-9d12-f431b20183ba] \n\nHere is the draft FOIA that you can send. \n\n_”Dear Sir/Madam,_\n\n_We are writing to request information under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 in relation to the WMCA Micromobility Scheme tender._\n\n_Following receipt of the Assessment Summary dated 19 December 2025 (please see attached), we would like some further information to better understand how the evaluation and scoring process was applied overall._\n\n_In particular, we are requesting the following information in relation to the above tender:_\n\n* _the final overall ranking of all compliant bidders ranked above Bolt Operations UK Limited;_\n* _the overall weighted scores achieved by each bidder ranked above Bolt Operations UK Limited, broken down by evaluation category where available; and_\n* _any moderation records, moderation summaries, or evaluator consensus notes used to finalise scores across evaluators, in redacted form if needed to protect commercially sensitive information or personal data._\n\n_We are not seeking disclosure of commercially sensitive bid content. This request is focused on transparency of the evaluation methodology, ranking, and moderation process applied by the Authority._\n\n_If any part of this request is considered exempt, please provide the non exempt information that can reasonably be disclosed and explain the basis for any exemption relied upon._\n\n_If you need anything further from us to progress this request, please let us know._\n\n\n_Kind Regards_\n_Giulio del Balzo Caprigliano”_","2026-01-08T17:27:37.157Z"],["3796976","LSS-60766","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","Request sent. Thanks!","2026-01-08T17:31:58.467Z"],["3796977","WD-22514","WD","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska","Hi. Fixed.","2026-01-08T17:35:16.592Z"],["3796983","LSS-60304","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41]. Considering the time that has elapsed since the ride took place, I don’t believe it makes a difference now, in the outcome of this complaint, that we try to obtain clarification from the driver.\n\nCould you please provide the [following response|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11MzEr3uaCjZMBPT-xxvC15IH6vFjA9DKFGLcz2daLXA/edit?tab=t.0] to the complainant? [https://docs.google.com/document/d/11MzEr3uaCjZMBPT-xxvC15IH6vFjA9DKFGLcz2daLXA/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11MzEr3uaCjZMBPT-xxvC15IH6vFjA9DKFGLcz2daLXA/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nIn the response, I’m proposing to her the offer of 25€ in balance for future rides, since this is a similar amount to the one she claims to have spent in new bus tickets, but without framing this amount as a compensation for those costs, for which we are not responsible. And considering that this amount is not a refund, it is not possible to proceed with any transfers directly to her IBAN or selected method of payment.\n\nThe intention is that she feels “sufficiently reimbursed” of the extra amount she claims to have spent in the bus tickets and does not proceed with further litigation. \n\nHowever, she mentions that she already presented a complaint with AMT, so I’m expecting that this complaint is eventually forwarded to us. If this happens, we may be inquired by AMT about this refusal of service by the driver and we might need to further investigate the situation. But I believe we should wait to see if AMT contacts us regarding this complaint.","2026-01-08T17:46:26.072Z"],["3796984","WD-22498","WD","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska","Hi. Wrong helpdesk. Please create a ticket here [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2512/create/6145|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2512/create/6145|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T17:46:36.744Z"],["3796985","LSS-60766","LSS","ieva.fowler@bolt.eu","Ieva Fowler","Great! Thanks for the update. I’ll close this ticket for now. Feel free to re-open it in case you have any further questions/requests. ","2026-01-08T17:47:31.419Z"],["3796988","HS-28252","HS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","Hi Everyone, \nso sorry - I missed this ticket, so thank you for the follow up! \nSure, [~accountid:712020:e1427b30-bc75-43cd-9e45-85c863998272], please cancel the request. \nThanks! \nEwa","2026-01-08T17:53:25.497Z"],["3796990","LSS-61179","LSS","emilie.chesse@bolt.eu","Emilie Chesse","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac]  - Well done and thank you, this is spot on, and I have nothing to add! \n\nPerhaps I’d loop in Lisette, so she’s aware - but I don’t expect her to have a different view.\n\nThanks again!","2026-01-08T17:57:08.945Z"],["3796993","LSS-58409","LSS","alexandre.lancastre@bolt.eu","Alexandre Lancastre","[^Bolt Business_Adenda_TCs_Mediapro (1) (2).docx]\n\nHey Beatriz,\n\nI just came back from holidays, hope everything is great and I wish a very happy new year.\n\nPlease find attached the word version of it.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlexandre Lancastre","2026-01-08T18:00:11.699Z"],["3796995","LSS-61230","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] I will ask and come back to you.\n\nAs for the entity I believe that’s up to us to define, not them. I would go with Bolt Operations OU, as it covers the entire region and the main purpose of this agreement is a Marketing campaign.  \nPlease let me know if this is correct or if there’s a reason why we should go with  Bolt Technology OU.","2026-01-08T18:14:01.334Z"],["3796997","PFI-831118","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","[^RO1526-4240.pdf]","2026-01-08T18:21:45.569Z"],["3796998","PFI-831118","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T18:21:47.810Z"],["3796999","LSS-61157","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bolt_MNDA (1).pdf] ","2026-01-08T18:22:55.559Z"],["3797000","LSS-61302","LSS","gauchar.alibayeva@bolt.eu","Gauchar Alibayeva","[^Bolt Business AB Inbev Master Agreement.docx] _(212 kB)_","2026-01-08T18:25:49.976Z"],["3797001","PFI-825080","PFI","lenka.galbava@bolt-outsource.eu","Lenka Galbavá","update pls?","2026-01-08T18:30:14.494Z"],["3797002","LSS-61302","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-08T18:31:06.636Z"],["3797003","PFI-831120","PFI","marylynda.onu@bolt-outsource.eu","Marylynda Onu","!image-20260108-183126.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T18:31:48.075Z"],["3797005","WD-22501","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi Fede, \nI had a bug in the rule, it’s been fixed and tested now. Everything should be working as before.","2026-01-08T18:38:45.213Z"],["3797006","WDFT-3605","WDFT","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Ticket just because an integration improvement. Re-assigned the ticket to [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] .","2026-01-08T18:40:03.737Z"],["3797007","FRAUDOPS-1058","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","# *Partners*\n\nAs especially in fleet markets it is very normal for drivers to hop between profiles. Let’s look how the counts and numbers change if we were to group the driver profiles onto one persona. Included are only cases with more that one comment profile. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 19.43.21.png|width=1800,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 19.43.21.png\"!\n\nSo for the 5.9K driver accounts we only have 1.5K partner personas. Rough math says that for each partner there is about three accounts. \n\nLooking at the ratio of driver profiles that have comments under partner: \n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.16.20.png|width=1217,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.16.20.png\"!\n\nIt can be seen that around 0.3-0.4 ratio, we are most vulnerable. However, this is skewed due to counts being actually low. \n\nSimilarily to driver level, we can see that most happens to partners at the 3rd instance. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.25.27.png|width=1239,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.25.27.png\"!\n\nLooking at the progress of problematic orders, it seems to stay stable: \n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.32.32.png|width=1199,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.32.32.png\"!\n\nLet’s compare the counts comments as well: \n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.41.37.png|width=1195,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.41.37.png\"!\n\nInterestingly there is a trend of 3 & 5 comment partners being more ‘fraudulent’. This makes sense for the 3rd report as we can expect this is ‘last hurray’ for the partner before potential offboarding but 5 count shows already habitual misuse. ","2026-01-08T18:45:13.488Z"],["3797010","HS-28580","HS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","Hi, \nthis is ready to be collected from my desk - 35th floor, HQ functions, desk next to 2.12. Thanks! \nEwa","2026-01-08T18:58:59.679Z"],["3797011","LSS-60621","LSS","tom.bishop@bolt.eu","Tom Bishop","That’s the right approach, yes\nWhen we onboard a new customer we will create a Ride Booker account for each client, and either we’ll ensure they are signed up to the Bolt Ts and Cs or a similar contract from their side","2026-01-08T19:03:09.045Z"],["3797013","LSS-61303","LSS","yasir.mazumder@bolt.eu","Yasir Kabir Mazumder","[^BOLT Operations NDA (Mutual) with Mr.Lube - 12.2025 (1).docx] _(1.86 MB)_\n\n[^BOLT Operations NDA (Mutual) with Mr.Lube - 12.2025.pdf] _(279 kB)_","2026-01-08T19:04:39.000Z"],["3797014","INT-484","INT","sandeep.jaiswal@bolt.eu","Sandeep Prasad Jaiswal","26W01: i’m working on the design doc right now for the 2 requirements that we have clarity on\n\n* Popular item campaigns from traitless sheet\n* improve campaign tags setup from admin panel\n\ni’m on vacation next week, so probably we don’t have much updates next week, but once i’m back we’ll start working on these 2 requirements full blown while gathering more info on the other requirements. ","2026-01-08T19:05:45.426Z"],["3797015","IDC-2237","IDC","sandeep.jaiswal@bolt.eu","Sandeep Prasad Jaiswal","BE PR is ready for review. will deploy it once i’m back from vacation","2026-01-08T19:10:36.520Z"],["3797016","IDC-2433","IDC","sandeep.jaiswal@bolt.eu","Sandeep Prasad Jaiswal","PR is ready and approved. will deploy it once i’m back from vacation","2026-01-08T19:10:54.462Z"],["3797017","PFI-830974","PFI","ken.barasa@bolt-outsource.eu","Ken Barasa","Attached to the case is the requested bank statement that the rider has sent ","2026-01-08T19:13:51.040Z"],["3797018","SRED-990","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Self-review is done, later need to fill couple more afaik, deadline somewhere in the end of January.","2026-01-08T19:14:32.013Z"],["3797019","PFI-831130","PFI","watanyu.lukkason@bolt-outsource.eu","Watanyu Lukkason","!JPEG_1767895481130_2796349850931536810.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T19:15:34.223Z"],["3797020","LSS-61304","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter Goldman Sachs (Bolt Services UK Limited).docx] _(2.79 MB)_\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter Papaya Global Ltd (Bolt Services UK Limited).docx] _(2.79 MB)_","2026-01-08T19:15:38.235Z"],["3797023","LSS-61305","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter UNIVERSAL BANK (Bolt Operations Ukraine).docx] _(2.79 MB)_","2026-01-08T19:18:05.632Z"],["3797024","LSS-61306","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter AS Swedbank (SIA Bolt Services LV).docx] _(2.79 MB)_\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter AS LHV PANK (SIA Bolt Services LV).docx] _(2.79 MB)_","2026-01-08T19:20:16.538Z"],["3797025","PFI-831135","PFI","ken.barasa@bolt-outsource.eu","Ken Barasa","[^3-Month statement (1) (1).pdf]","2026-01-08T19:20:58.221Z"],["3797026","PFI-831136","PFI","watanyu.lukkason@bolt-outsource.eu","Watanyu Lukkason","!JPEG_1767895504407_4586846457903769731.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T19:21:38.958Z"],["3797027","PFI-831139","PFI","ricardo.otazu@bolt.eu","Enrique Otazu","[^Pago Factura Agosto.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-08T19:28:02.672Z"],["3797028","LSS-61230","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] yes, we only need to fill in the first page (General Information)","2026-01-08T19:28:53.286Z"],["3797029","PFI-831143","PFI","ricardo.otazu@bolt.eu","Enrique Otazu","[^Pago Factura Setiembre.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-08T19:32:48.980Z"],["3797030","LSS-61303","LSS","yasir.mazumder@bolt.eu","Yasir Kabir Mazumder","One minor change was made in *Section 12.3* to specify that *Canadian law*, rather than Estonian law, will govern the agreement, reflecting that the relationship pertains to Mr. Lube’s Canadian operations and activities in Canada.","2026-01-08T19:34:23.517Z"],["3797031","PAW-14733","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @sergey-seleznev\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160127\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-08 19:36:11 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-08T19:36:11.668Z"],["3797033","FRAUDOPS-1058","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","# *Fleets*\n\nNow, fleets may just be the most interesting portion of this research as we’d noticed the trend through fleet fraud. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.50.49.png|width=1120,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.50.49.png\"!\n\n\n\n*Cases where drivers under fleet have had more than one report:*\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.53.43.png|width=1179,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.53.43.png\"!\n\nSo we can see that we have quite few companies that have at least 10 comments for drivers being reported for issues more than once. \n\nLet’s check how many companies we have for each ratio of reports.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.57.34.png|width=952,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 20.57.34.png\"!\n\nSo we have few companies with ACTUAL high percent of reports for drivers with MORE THAN ONE case. Let’s check those top scenarios against reports. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 21.02.34.png|width=841,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 21.02.34.png\"!\n\nSo it can be seen that most volume again shifts onto lower ratio and lower comments suggesting that overall the problem with fleets is specific and not generic. \n\nLet’s check top fleets: \n\n|driver_company_id|company_country_code|count_drivers|count_imp_drivers|ratio_driver|unique_comment_cnt|\n|119000|fr|107|31|0.3|102|\n|110593|fr|111|28|0.3|89|\n|129026|fr|81|26|0.3|90|\n|140527|fr|75|20|0.3|66|\n|88167|fr|67|18|0.3|76|\n|131377|fr|52|15|0.3|50|\n|107195|fr|39|15|0.4|59|\n|142522|fr|51|14|0.3|47|\n|111706|fr|47|13|0.3|43|\n|106223|fr|49|13|0.3|43|\n|108456|fr|36|13|0.4|50|\n|188124|fr|33|12|0.4|33|\n|72962|fr|35|12|0.3|35|\n|172970|fr|31|10|0.3|29|\n|107515|fr|36|10|0.3|33|\n|113262|fr|37|10|0.3|33|\n\nSo it seems the top ‘abusers’ are staying around 30% of fleet ratio stat. \n\nFleets with at least 30% repeat issue driver ratio have produced the following GMV: \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 21.17.12.png|width=837,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 21.17.12.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 21.29.19.png|width=1239,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 21.29.19.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 21.35.04.png|width=861,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 21.35.04.png\"!\n\n*So around 33% of the total issue is from the multi-report drivers specifically.* Top fleets show that portion of the irregular sum comes from these issue prone drivers. \n\nLooking at problematic volumes, it seems to correlate more with the first visible spike in driver cases. \n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 21.43.22.png|width=1203,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 21.43.22.png\"!\n\n\n\nIt seems like the issue case drivers do hold a constant portion of payment problems, however, it does not seem like these drivers cause spikes on their own. Meaning we may not have a good approach to detecting fraud just based on the reports.\n\n\n\n|{color:#ffffff}driver_company_id{color}|{color:#ffffff}unique_comment_cnt{color}|{color:#ffffff}count_imp_drivers{color}|{color:#ffffff}ratio_driver{color}|{color:#ffffff}count_distinct_driver{color}|{color:#ffffff}count_finished{color}|{color:#ffffff}sum_finished_eur{color}|{color:#ffffff}sum_imp_finished_eur{color}|{color:#ffffff}count_finished_problem_trip{color}|{color:#ffffff}sum_finished_problem_eur{color}|{color:#ffffff}sum_imp_finished_problem_eur{color}|\n|72962|35|12|0.3|35|9029|216825|85581|1076|14487|3511|\n|129026|90|26|0.3|81|14413|306737|87802|711|9725|7343|\n|113262|33|10|0.3|37|5591|134358|27060|655|8307|1878|\n|110593|89|28|0.3|111|15407|315928|96615|263|3815|399|\n|74548|4|2|0.3|6|1473|36743|33960|231|3198|3181|\n|188124|33|12|0.4|33|9367|183526|85543|147|2580|1803|\n|110836|14|5|0.3|19|502|15651|15651|107|1338|1338|\n|140527|66|20|0.3|75|12067|244595|70843|68|703|191|\n|119000|102|31|0.3|107|11622|226693|67476|71|697|161|\n|142522|47|14|0.3|51|6647|131962|26739|40|612|130|\n|125835|23|8|0.3|26|6789|121157|78953|46|584|447|\n|135316|18|5|0.3|16|2586|49656|0|55|581|0|\n|155106|19|6|0.3|23|5726|109333|31502|56|523|88|\n|172970|29|10|0.3|31|7047|142983|32548|33|499|19|\n|134538|10|2|0.3|8|1400|34141|0|33|473|0|\n|111706|43|13|0.3|47|4508|99041|13744|24|459|18|\n|115693|14|5|0.3|16|876|24855|7190|15|383|100|\n|150073|19|7|0.4|18|3614|71061|0|22|375|0|\n|170511|13|3|0.4|8|2311|53041|12632|17|362|70|\n|88167|76|18|0.3|67|3175|71563|34895|16|318|200|\n|149231|24|9|0.3|34|2674|59200|23546|24|250|103|\n|89025|20|6|0.5|12|1488|28355|0|15|233|0|\n|58838|23|7|0.3|22|2931|61842|0|16|225|0|\n|177256|12|3|0.3|11|1422|46860|19299|7|202|121|\n|178833|17|5|0.5|10|1560|34418|16885|8|194|132|\n|157302|17|4|0.3|13|2813|57481|14002|17|189|0|\n|175854|6|2|0.5|4|755|17516|0|4|173|0|\n|117457|27|7|0.3|27|3298|60692|34655|20|169|47|\n|156113|6|2|0.4|5|877|15749|6398|5|167|0|\n|158576|20|6|0.3|23|3406|58111|13047|19|160|0|\n|121975|21|7|0.3|25|1024|21060|0|4|141|0|\n|66880|13|6|0.3|18|1987|44629|33181|13|134|122|\n|108456|50|13|0.4|36|3331|68918|38411|11|116|40|\n|157070|9|3|0.3|12|941|23210|0|6|116|0|\n|148427|9|3|0.4|7|882|16763|16763|10|115|115|\n|123271|13|3|0.3|11|2583|53282|0|10|107|0|\n|131377|50|15|0.3|52|2035|41109|16174|15|97|63|\n|74895|11|3|0.3|11|1390|35656|13898|6|95|0|\n|130061|11|4|0.3|13|890|15454|6089|6|85|0|\n|74320|5|2|0.3|6|1350|26230|17080|7|84|46|\n|119713|27|7|0.3|21|3721|78876|14127|7|72|29|\n|179841|4|2|0.7|3|527|11336|9273|3|69|69|\n|105250|14|4|0.3|12|1226|24935|10206|5|61|35|\n|183962|7|2|0.3|8|1689|32699|12777|6|51|39|\n|177237|26|8|0.4|22|1013|18104|4578|5|50|0|\n|94138|13|3|0.3|11|545|10572|2739|3|38|0|\n|145102|8|4|0.3|13|1282|25270|5198|3|32|14|\n|110541|18|4|0.3|15|957|18344|0|6|29|0|\n|107195|59|15|0.4|39|1022|22956|11805|6|27|27|\n|141331|6|2|0.4|5|706|13846|13846|1|27|27|\n|114023|13|4|0.3|16|795|16590|0|4|26|0|\n|98001|10|3|0.4|7|654|11944|10875|1|23|0|\n|93806|5|2|0.7|3|433|8915|8915|2|21|21|\n|109293|7|2|0.3|7|809|18368|0|2|13|0|\n|150860|10|2|0.7|3|332|5291|0|1|13|0|\n|168849|16|4|0.4|9|1838|44921|27208|6|12|0|\n|173012|6|2|0.5|4|43|658|0|1|12|0|\n|83329|8|2|0.3|7|205|5741|3828|1|0|0|\n|92741|7|2|1|2|105|2833|2833|0|0|0|\n|111249|13|3|0.3|12|69|1295|224|1|0|0|\n|118659|6|2|0.7|3|469|9062|9062|2|0|0|\n|131542|5|2|1|2|164|3690|3690|0|0|0|\n|136418|12|4|0.3|15|892|16516|1483|0|0|0|\n|156308|11|3|0.3|9|17|364|364|0|0|0|","2026-01-08T19:36:51.601Z"],["3797034","PFI-831144","PFI","ricardo.otazu@bolt.eu","Enrique Otazu","[^Pago Factura Octubre.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-08T19:38:39.758Z"],["3797036","PFI-831145","PFI","ricardo.otazu@bolt.eu","Enrique Otazu","[^Pago Factura Noviembre.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-08T19:42:05.713Z"],["3797037","ROPSC-480","ROPSC","riin@bolt.eu","Riin Kotsalainen","Profiles were updated and corrected by local teams. \nBilling analytics will update looker dashboard with new rule. \nSlack confirmation: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C045B2ATEN4/p1767865958503969?thread_ts=1767797486.851539&cid=C045B2ATEN4|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C045B2ATEN4/p1767865958503969?thread_ts=1767797486.851539&cid=C045B2ATEN4|smart-link] ","2026-01-08T19:45:08.640Z"],["3797039","LSS-47932","LSS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","I added you to the email chain 🙏 ","2026-01-08T20:06:36.990Z"],["3797043","FC-427","FC","kerli.uibo@bolt.eu","Kerli Uibo","Vientam launch was cancelled. ","2026-01-08T20:22:57.196Z"],["3797044","BEE-3626","BEE",null,"Slack","Thanks for raising this, the counter in Beehive and our plans around it made me actually to post this request,  I also had an internal discussion with Himanshu and JZ to get a second opinion and align on the implications.\nWe all agree that having a difference can be confusing if the intent is not clear, but we also concluded that the difference is intentional and justified given the audiences and use cases.\nIn Beehive, the reopen counter showing the number of times a case was reopened due to both AI and agent responses makes sense. From an agent’s perspective, this reflects how many times the customer had to come back and re-explain their issue, and it’s useful when taking into account how to approach the customer communication.\n• In the Queue Dashboard, however, the goal is different. This view is primarily for TLs and QAs to spot cases that need attention from an agent quality and coaching perspective. Including AI-driven reopens here would introduce volatility — especially if AI behavior changes — which would make it difficult to define and maintain stable, standardized thresholds for monitoring and action.\nBecause of that, we would not prefer to unify the logic across both surfaces. Instead, our preference is to keep the counts separate and make sure there is a clear definition/description of what is being displayed in each place, so expectations are set correctly.\nSo effectively, we lean toward:\n• Keeping the current separation (similar to option 1), with clearer labeling/definitions, rather than forcing unification that could reduce the usefulness of the Queue Dashboard metrics.\nHappy to discuss further if needed, but this feels like the most pragmatic and least risky approach for now.","2026-01-08T20:28:15.330Z"],["3797046","PFI-812434","PFI","julia.lechwar@bolt-outsource.eu","Julia Lechwar","update?\n\n","2026-01-08T20:51:21.102Z"],["3797047","RDS-1203","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","Mentioned this on the call, but want to ask again — can’t we get some probabilistic data around ETA accuracy? \n\nFor example, if we suggest 3 min ETA and there are 9 drivers nearby that are roughly equally distant from the rider, I think it’s a pretty accurate estimate. Even if several drivers reject the order, probably 1 of the 9 will accept, and the ETA should be correct. \n\nOn the other hand, if we suggest 3 min ETA and there is only _1_ driver nearby that’s 3 min away, and the next driver is 10 min away, then actually there’s a strong likelihood our ETA will be off (in this case, way off). \n\nSo in the first example, I don’t think showing an ETA range really helps us. It introduces rider doubt/confusion when we actually don’t need to show a range. In the second example, though, it would be far more transparent to say something like 3-10 min so that the rider isn’t furious when their ETA jumps from 3 min to 10 min after the first driver rejects (which is not unlikely). \n\nTLDR; maybe we can consider a different targeting approach based on # of available drivers with similar ETAs","2026-01-08T20:51:36.708Z"],["3797048","PFI-831161","PFI","kasidid.witthayanukhraoh@bolt-outsource.eu","Kasidid Witthayanukhraoh","!image-20260108-205952.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260108-210004.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T21:04:27.381Z"],["3797051","PFI-817417","PFI","helena.lieblova@bolt-outsource.eu","Helena Lieblova","Any update?","2026-01-08T21:09:16.835Z"],["3797052","PFI-831162","PFI","julija.gorskova@bolt-outsource.eu","Julija Gorskova","*Apologies, order link is irrelevant to the case!*","2026-01-08T21:13:30.254Z"],["3797055","PFI-831167","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-08T21:38:23.263Z"],["3797057","LSS-59295","LSS","ieva.fowler@bolt.eu","Ieva Fowler","Hi [~accountid:622b6eb2302c6b006af70509] \n\nAll good from the legal side. I’ll close this ticket now. Feel free to re-open if you have any further questions. \n","2026-01-08T21:44:25.028Z"],["3797058","PAW-14620","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was closed\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159672\nStatus: closed\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-08 21:49:48 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-08T21:49:48.903Z"],["3797059","PFI-826631","PFI","anastasiia.levytska@bolt-outsource.eu","Anastasiia Levytska","Hi! We have still have this problem, can you please check?","2026-01-08T21:59:28.007Z"],["3797060","PFI-823944","PFI","anastasiia.levytska@bolt-outsource.eu","Anastasiia Levytska","Hi! We have still have this problem, can you please check?\n\n\n\n","2026-01-08T21:59:43.613Z"],["3797063","PFI-828963","PFI","daniela.gonzalez@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniela Jazmin Aleman Gonzalez","Hello team, is there any possibility you could review this ticket? The driver is requesting answers. Thank you in advance.","2026-01-08T22:27:52.591Z"],["3797065","PFI-831176","PFI","afsana.huseynova@bolt-outsource.eu","Afsana Huseynova","!şəkil.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-08T22:56:39.758Z"],["3797068","INS-908","INS","pawel.kupidura@bolt.eu","Paweł Kupidura","Workaround was released to the following projects in this PR [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15219|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15219|smart-link] \n\n* {{bolt_dbt}}\n* {{common}}\n* {{data_platform}}\n* {{legacy}}\n\nWorks as expected, no side effects. ","2026-01-08T23:12:49.745Z"],["3797075","PFI-830940","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-09T01:00:42.843Z"],["3797077","PFI-813891","PFI","pisut.thongpan@bolt-outsource.eu","Pisut Thongpan","Kindly follow up for any updates.","2026-01-09T01:05:46.556Z"],["3797079","EBIKE1-350","EBIKE1","xiangxue.hu@bolt.eu","Xiangxue Hu","|!8fffc4c54748eaa4b18aaf90f40de37c-20260109-014535.png|width=263,alt=\"8fffc4c54748eaa4b18aaf90f40de37c-20260109-014535.png\"!|!8b4a505b655142758be10ab4c5924b6a-20260109-014542.png|width=263,alt=\"8b4a505b655142758be10ab4c5924b6a-20260109-014542.png\"!|!c56151f942dfdf57e9581d62b62421c4-20260109-014547.png|width=263,alt=\"c56151f942dfdf57e9581d62b62421c4-20260109-014547.png\"!|\n\nYiyo designed the checking jig , all the key dimensions can be checked by it, The jig will be ready by {{2026-01-30}} ","2026-01-09T01:47:42.918Z"],["3797081","WEBSD-1313","WEBSD","daryl.teoh@bolt.eu","Daryl Teoh","Hi Hector, many thanks on working on this, i think you might have input the other section which is “*E-hailing vehicle permit*” into “*Road Tax Renewal Guide*”, could you refer back to [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1clrT0LjwCEwcaAWXaAfTHd6iicl9EcrKp2B02og2_NM/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.o67paxu8oq7d], including the faq section.\n\n\n\nAlso, i tried looking at other languages, and it seems like the infographic is all in english still :o, do you happen to know why?\n\n","2026-01-09T02:47:10.411Z"],["3797082","PFI-831193","PFI","chalitta.srisit@bolt-outsource.eu","Chalitta Srisit","!image-20260109-024243.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260109-024305.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260109-024343.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T02:47:24.774Z"],["3797083","PFI-831193","PFI","chalitta.srisit@bolt-outsource.eu","Chalitta Srisit","*I apologize for the misinformation provided earlier.*\n\nDear payment team,\nThe driver paid commission to the incorrect Bolt virtual bank account with the amount of *500THB* on 06/01/2026\n\n486256134*3* ✅\n486256134*5* ⛔️\n\nPlease assist in updating the driver's data, and thank you for considering my request.","2026-01-09T02:52:09.152Z"],["3797084","PFI-811994","PFI","pisut.thongpan@bolt-outsource.eu","Pisut Thongpan","Kindly follow up for any updates.","2026-01-09T02:53:10.613Z"],["3797085","PFI-831194","PFI","chalitta.srisit@bolt-outsource.eu","Chalitta Srisit","!image-20260109-024942.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260109-025000.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260109-025016.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T02:53:16.009Z"],["3797086","FDBT-4731","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_bank_payments fails on 2026-01-08 02:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **exe