rolled out on Nov 28. Inquiring from [~accountid:6017bc27a41ea5006a86f73b] how does this feature look like in Admin. ","2026-01-09T06:57:20.991Z"],["3797196","DRX-27952","DRX","sander.saarend@bolt.eu","Sander Saarend","Investigation result:\n\nEvents from Trapeze include event_datetime with only 1-second precision (e.g., \"2025-12-29 12:42:20\"), making it impossible to determine correct processing order when multiple events arrive within the same second. Without sequence numbers or sub-second timestamps, there's a 50% chance of processing events like METER_VACANT → METER_ENGAGED in reverse order, causing state desynchronization.\n\n*Requires communication with Trapeze to request either sub-second timestamp precision or sequence numbers in event payloads to enable proper ordering.*","2026-01-09T06:57:50.734Z"],["3797197","DRX-27952","DRX","sander.saarend@bolt.eu","Sander Saarend","Marking this investigation as complete for now, further steps will happen as a result of discussions with Trapeze: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09QGNFHC0G/p1767941639069019|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09QGNFHC0G/p1767941639069019|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T06:58:24.883Z"],["3797198","DRAG101-436","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","The issue regarding the surface pattern not matching the initial specifications has been discussed with the supplier.\n\nIt was too fine compared to the rougher one specified in the drawings.\n\nSS confirmed that we can implement a rougher surface pattern for the grips as originally specified.\n\n*Rougher surface pattern is being currently implemented* to the grips.","2026-01-09T06:58:43.310Z"],["3797204","HWMISC-776","HWMISC","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","Opening molds for brake upgrades will take 30 days + initial testing time. \n\nThere will be no mold cost for the us.\n\nStill waiting for LD to confirm the unit price :loading: \n\n\n\nHowever, after checking with the supply chain guys, it seems that we are stocked with EB100 brakes for a very long time:\n\n\n\n|| ||*Front brake*|| ||\n|Yearly consumption|-720|-570|\n|In stock|+328|+704|\n|In transit|+600|+600|\n|combined stock will last|~15 months|~27 months|\n\nFront brakes we have for well over a year and rears even for two years ⬆️ \n\n\n\nIn two years time, will the EB100 still even be up and running? \n\nIn my opinion, unless we can start replacing to the new brakes proactively despite having big stock of old model, it makes no sense to even order prototypes for now.","2026-01-09T07:00:30.863Z"],["3797225","LSS-58622","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Oliver Martyn Vahar,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-09T07:01:09.384Z"],["3797232","LSS-60150","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Joana Duó,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-09T07:01:11.528Z"],["3797234","LSS-58827","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Aleksandra Koroleva,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-09T07:01:12.040Z"],["3797237","LSS-59868","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Jack Cook,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-09T07:01:13.214Z"],["3797239","LSS-57481","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Kyriakos Tjionis,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-09T07:01:15.832Z"],["3797242","PFI-826753","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Borys Sypniewski,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T07:01:17.759Z"],["3797243","PFI-828705","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Francisco Vidrago,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T07:01:17.862Z"],["3797244","PFI-828940","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Ionut Gabriel Florescu,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T07:01:17.867Z"],["3797245","PFI-823715","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Anastasiya Nikolayeva,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T07:01:17.986Z"],["3797246","LSS-55517","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Rachael Irimu,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-09T07:01:19.529Z"],["3797247","PFI-827376","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Parvin Alirrzayeva,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T07:01:19.669Z"],["3797248","PFI-821008","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hugo Silva,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T07:01:20.253Z"],["3797249","LSS-50214","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Anusha Balachandre,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-09T07:01:25.827Z"],["3797250","LSS-48561","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Julia Bitello,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-09T07:01:25.883Z"],["3797252","EBIKE1-226","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","Information and 3D model sent to TWS. They also agreed that this could help and will make test run to assemble 10 pcs batteries with assembly workers ","2026-01-09T07:01:47.093Z"],["3797253","LSS-60145","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Julia Maal,\n\nThere hasn't been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days. Please:\n1) Close the ticket if the issue has been resolved or is not relevant anymore; or\n2) Give an update; or\n3) Change to “Waiting for customer” status if you are waiting to hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T07:02:01.902Z"],["3797254","LSS-59397","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Thale Marie Bø,\n\nTh