10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Cancel*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and cancel the ticket.","2026-01-09T07:31:09.478Z"],["3797342","HS-28305","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Cancel*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and cancel the ticket.","2026-01-09T07:31:09.947Z"],["3797343","HS-28435","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Cancel*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and cancel the ticket.","2026-01-09T07:31:25.214Z"],["3797344","HS-28347","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:e1427b30-bc75-43cd-9e45-85c863998272],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-09T07:31:26.326Z"],["3797349","PFI-830473","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! I’m experiencing an error with the reissue - I’ve asked engineering to look into the issue 🙂 \n\nWhile we wait, can you please specify if the invoice for period 11/24/2025-11/30/2025 that’s issued on 12/1/2025 also need to be reissued? ","2026-01-09T07:32:28.800Z"],["3797352","FX-3217","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767943969647909]*{color}:\n?\n{quote}","2026-01-09T07:33:04.952Z"],["3797355","EBIKE1-392","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Conclusion:\n\n* Footrests may need modification near the kickstand mount to fit the kickstand\n\n!d501a088d0e8e8b59cdceccecb423a2c-20260109-073200.jpg|width=163,alt=\"d501a088d0e8e8b59cdceccecb423a2c-20260109-073200.jpg\"!\n\n* It fits well onto the kickstand mount on the main frame.\n\n!image-20260109-073752.png|width=166,alt=\"image-20260109-073752.png\"!\n\n* No need to re-open any tube bending molds:\n** If the tube part of the original off-the-shelf kickstand leg has been shortened by 40mm,\n** If the tube tips are made of sheet metal stamping parts,\n*** Stamping mold is required.\n* Next, test usability on the EB1 and Cruiser.\n* Measure the lean angle on a tilted surface and compare it with Okai.\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"fcf3ca49-7f22-4af8-bb10-eaa7c952efe2\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The kickstand original leg length has been shortened by 40mm form the tube.\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"3D printed parts were added to simulate sheet metal stamping parts\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":221,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"78fcc7814bb8504fbe02fd4dc04d3702-20260109-072843.jpg\",\"alt\":\"78fcc7814bb8504fbe02fd4dc04d3702-20260109-072843.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":226,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"7a46d51db01c06f5de093e793f1d7daf-20260109-072911.jpg\",\"alt\":\"7a46d51db01c06f5de093e793f1d7daf-20260109-072911.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":174,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"5017ec69d85fc905b151bb0408619daf-20260109-073109.jpg\",\"alt\":\"5017ec69d85fc905b151bb0408619daf-20260109-073109.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":306,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"a1fa43893d2e1425d7d0fe454c2fdc97-20260109-072810.jpg\",\"alt\":\"a1fa43893d2e1425d7d0fe454c2fdc97-20260109-072810.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":221,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"d9c3dcb777e4998398bb10cbb27a43f3-20260109-072822.jpg\",\"alt\":\"d9c3dcb777e4998398bb10cbb27a43f3-20260109-072822.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-09T07:34:53.381Z"],["3797357","LSS-57542","LSS","federico.michelini@bolt.eu","Federico Michelini","Signatories on behalf of Stella Energy Sweden AB are:\n\n* Mads Wind - [mads@stellaenergy.com|mailto:mads@stellaenergy.com]\n* Kim Meikel Rose - [kimi@stellaenergy.com|mailto:kimi@stellaenergy.com]\n\n","2026-01-09T07:34:55.534Z"],["3797358","PFI-830447","PFI","erik.semet@bolt-outsource.eu","Erik Šemet","Hello [~accountid:5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b], Fleet Owner complains that he checked all his details and everything is correct. He also contacted his bank where they told him that they do not reject incoming payments unless they are from a suspicious sender. So the driver wants us to provide a confirmation where the payment rejection code will be so that his bank can verify it. Or, let's send him the payment again. Is any of these options possible?\n\nThis is the case [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/718141009]. Rejected payout [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/232364950?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FPrague].\n\n","2026-01-09T07:34:59.438Z"],["3797359","LSS-60573","LSS","fredi.sepp@bolt.eu","Fredi Sepp","Hi [~accountid:618d2fe286c210006aa6241e] [~accountid:712020:d8161849-388c-4312-84ee-638c0b0ece4f] \n\nIs it possible to arrange signing the PoA with a standard electronic signature in .asice format as requested?","2026-01-09T07:35:12.249Z"],["3797361","PFI-831247","PFI","yuliia-diana.pikh@bolt-outsource.eu","Yuliia-Diana Pikh","[^6b969e64-1d1e-4942-b9a7-c567e806595e.pdf]","2026-01-09T07:36:25.126Z"],["3797362","DRAG101-405","DRAG101","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Next week they might be able to do the ride test. ","2026-01-09T07:36:42.628Z"],["3797363","CSXDL-143","CSXDL","kristiina.himma@bolt.eu","Kristiina Himma","Meeting held on Nov 21, 2025","2026-01-09T07:37:01.752Z"],["3797367","LSS-60573","LSS","liisa.daniel@bolt.eu","Liisa Daniel-Dixon","Many thanks for your email. \n\nPlease note that I am currently out of office, sick. I will respond as soon as I can on my return to the office. If the matter is urgent and cannot await my return please reach out to another team member. \n\nBest, \n\nLiisa","2026-01-09T07:38:35.077Z"],["3797368","PFI-831248","PFI","elijah.ojeamien@bolt-outsource.eu","Elijah Ojeamien","[^BOLT_payment_receipt (7).pdf]","2026-01-09T07:39:06.414Z"],["3797371","LSS-57542","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team,\n\n[~accountid:712020:d3fd53e6-f124-4770-a577-b09d6688566f], thank you for sharing this information! \n[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] can we please collect signatures for this document here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Dg3UQjrUiz5wOV3TLKyNHD9ke_0O5x0H/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Dg3UQjrUiz5wOV3TLKyNHD9ke_0O5x0H/edit|smart-link] \nSignatories on behalf of Stella Energy Sweden AB are:\n\n* Mads Wind - [mads@stellaenergy.com|mailto:mads@stellaenergy.com]\n* Kim Meikel Rose - [kimi@stellaenergy.com|mailto:kimi@stellaenergy.com]\n\nIf you have any other questions, please let me know!\n\nThank you very much! \n","2026-01-09T07:41:36.229Z"],["3797372","LSS-58990","LSS","beatrice.krasenko@bolt.eu","Beatričė Krašenko","hi, let's keep waiting, they will sign, owner is getting back from vacation","2026-01-09T07:42:32.542Z"],["3797373","LSS-61058","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] thank you for your support on this request. When I open the global link you have shared I can see the update however, when I look at the link from the Belgian portal, the update has not synced: [https://bolt.eu/fr-be/privacy/privacy-controller-list/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/fr-be/privacy/privacy-controller-list/?category=rides|smart-link] \n\n\nPlease could you have a look and let me know?\n\nThank you !","2026-01-09T07:42:54.969Z"],["3797375","HS-28664","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:7bf10d32-47fc-4fe5-8a9d-9cb9296e4e34],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-09T07:43:31.595Z"],["3797377","PFI-831051","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Okay, I see both companies have 0% Service Fee → i.e. SF is not applicable to them.\n\nEach month for Intermediary Companies → Statement is issued. It’s a document where we aggregate all rides (not applicable to VAT recovery). E.g.: TZ6525-13053 → Does it have to be changed? [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5819128114|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5819128114]","2026-01-09T07:43:51.419Z"],["3797379","LSS-55755","LSS","federico.michelini@bolt.eu","Federico Michelini","Hi [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] , sharing below the edited versions by Stella of:\n\n\n\n* [Annex n.3|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tmNTj9ewDSs49PQ8WTmzEvg4Pd5sCkod/edit] for Operator Rewards to be added to the general agreement\n* [Amendment form|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GnZXW5tldjTGFPqr_52FVaPJV0nCSenC6kaNj5kj6n0/edit?tab=t.0] for changes to the general agreement clauses 8.2.1, 1.a.i.1 and clause 3b in Appendix 1\n\nThe only open question is the naming of the annex to be consistent with the structure of the agreement, which Stella would like confirmation from you about.\n\nOther points have been accepted/resolved.\n\nPlease let me know if you need any other info, thanks.\n\n","2026-01-09T07:44:13.512Z"],["3797380","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767944686672809]*{color}:\nGood morning! It seems that the test that Shreya posted was not approved and is not live. What happened? I understood that Sudipto was going to approve it. Did something go wrong?\n{quote}","2026-01-09T07:45:01.622Z"],["3797382","PFI-831249","PFI","anna.zaritska@bolt.eu","Anna Zaritska","[^UA_Manual payout template - 09.01.26.csv]","2026-01-09T07:45:19.919Z"],["3797384","PFI-830494","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Billing does not handle this, please reach out to payments team. Thanks! ","2026-01-09T07:45:36.187Z"],["3797385","LSS-61040","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Interim letter sent to PTAC: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zADMKdZVDFY7pjadllx4XZaoCSSS-cAmwR029Gy0lqw/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zADMKdZVDFY7pjadllx4XZaoCSSS-cAmwR029Gy0lqw/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T07:45:36.208Z"],["3797386","LSS-61009","LSS","teodor.rachev@bolt.eu","Teodor Rachev","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2]! In this case, we will send the letter with your adjustments and initiate new communication with the Road Safety agency. ","2026-01-09T07:45:38.374Z"],["3797387","PFI-830494","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Partner Payments] Business made payment, but didn't reflect: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306\n- [Customer Payments] Business had issues with their credit card: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/303\n\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/304\n\n[Billing] - Business invoicing and balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305\n\n[Billing/Tax Tech]- Business invoice has not been reported (Fiscalized) : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T07:45:42.183Z"],["3797390","PFI-830940","PFI","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","[~accountid:712020:fc661671-1d51-4372-9578-b46465bd51ac], with this kind of issue, kindly advise on the correct team it can be escalated to.","2026-01-09T07:46:51.684Z"],["3797391","G3IOT-1190","G3IOT","enari.saar@bolt.eu","Enari Saar","Firmware is installed, waiting for wires to be connected to test.","2026-01-09T07:47:03.138Z"],["3797392","DRX-27677","DRX","sander.saarend@bolt.eu","Sander Saarend","Currently blocked, as it’s pending on further changes from Trapeze","2026-01-09T07:47:19.458Z"],["3797393","G3IOT-1192","G3IOT","enari.saar@bolt.eu","Enari Saar","Components are all setup. UART Adapters need to wired to tester.","2026-01-09T07:47:33.343Z"],["3797396","LSS-61275","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:5fc110f70d2f61006f7604a9], thank you for the ticket.\nHowever, I’m unable to open any of the links shared (for the two requested accesses). \n\nAdditionally, I see that the r*esponse to the authorities’ inquiry was due by September 2025.*\n\nDo we have any updates on what has happened with the case up until now?\n\n\nThanks. ","2026-01-09T07:48:12.381Z"],["3797399","PFI-830110","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Since it’s an intermediary model, not resale, we can’t reissue with Bolt as the invoice issuer name. ","2026-01-09T07:48:49.872Z"],["3797400","LSS-61040","LSS","marcis.bakis@bolt.eu","Mārcis Baķis","Adding the signed version here as well\n\n[^Bolt jautājumi PTAC 08.01.25..edoc]\n\n 🙏 ","2026-01-09T07:49:28.514Z"],["3797403","LSS-61311","LSS","fredi.sepp@bolt.eu","Fredi Sepp","[^Fredi Sepp PoA - Circle K_17.04.2025 (1).asice] _(50 kB)_","2026-01-09T07:49:33.514Z"],["3797404","LSS-59377","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:62bdcba29e6ba34c99375ad9], thank you for your ticket. \nApologies for the long wait. \nI’ll review it next week, would that work for you?\nThank you! ","2026-01-09T07:49:48.185Z"],["3797405","DELIVERY-1758","DELIVERY","quinn.feller@bolt.eu","Quinn Darby Feller","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08T2Q5KASH/p1767944584364169?thread_ts=1767852720.992449&cid=C08T2Q5KASH|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08T2Q5KASH/p1767944584364169?thread_ts=1767852720.992449&cid=C08T2Q5KASH|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T07:50:44.019Z"],["3797406","FX-3217","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767945032405829]*{color}:\nThis took a little longer to complete than expected, but this should now be done next week. \n{quote}","2026-01-09T07:50:47.741Z"],["3797408","MLC-1378","MLC","durrah.abdullah@bolt.eu","Durrah Abdullah","*Update*: Remaining markets launched for full churn LV, MY, MD, PL, RO, SK, ES, TW & UA. \n*Next Steps*: Only FI & SE are pending while new market churn comms would be made live as part of launch timelines","2026-01-09T07:51:34.988Z"],["3797409","LSS-56917","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:712020:ef6a9562-f9aa-4bb5-a4d5-2b18cc77085b], thank you for sharing the link. \nI’ll review the updates next week, thanks.","2026-01-09T07:52:18.198Z"],["3797410","EBIKE1-87","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Erki will provide the improved version 3D to the supplier. ","2026-01-09T07:52:23.453Z"],["3797411","PFI-830875","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! It seems like the business didn’t have any orders in December, hence no invoice either. ","2026-01-09T07:52:28.380Z"],["3797412","HS-28747","HS","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Hi Michal, hope you are well. the payments are processed once a month during the first week. if your referred employee  stated this week then the payment will be captured in the first week of Feb 2026, and depending when your payroll cut off is the payment will reflect in the following salary. ","2026-01-09T07:52:51.795Z"],["3797413","WEBSD-1445","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:ab839114-2a25-415e-ba75-ae805049693d]  👋 \n\nMaybe you can provide the french translation so I can added in Crowding myself and you can have the version need it. \n\nRegards,","2026-01-09T07:53:05.247Z"],["3797418","WD-22480","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Hi Andrei, appreciate the feedback and thanks for flagging!","2026-01-09T07:53:58.544Z"],["3797419","LSS-59377","LSS","meda.baltramonaityte@bolt.eu","Meda Baltramonaitytė","Hey, yes, thank you! 🙏 ","2026-01-09T07:54:11.015Z"],["3797420","DELIVERY-1759","DELIVERY","raj.parekh@bolt.eu","Raj Parekh","This as I see is already done\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 13.24.06.png|width=390,height=323,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 13.24.06.png\"!","2026-01-09T07:54:16.603Z"],["3797421","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Shreya Bhandari [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767945247970689]*{color}:\n<@URVM3U4RF> you can change the time to today and approve it. \n{quote}","2026-01-09T07:54:21.034Z"],["3797423","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767945283054819]*{color}:\nOk, what time would be OK for it to actually start?\n{quote}","2026-01-09T07:54:54.941Z"],["3797424","DSR-3547","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Response from verification:\nFrom what I see, the driver has been blocked because of Superman issue - a fraud attempt.Basically, verification started from a device in a set point A, and selfie was uploaded from another device in point B.These locations are 3.20km from each other, and verification was completed in 36 seconds.\nThis means that driver's speed should have been around 321.22km/h, which is unrealistic.The driver will not be unblocked unfortunately.Hope this clarifies!\nPlease *do not share the details with the driver*.\n\n\n*Picture of map*\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 10.52.43.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-07 at 10.52.43.png\"!\n","2026-01-09T07:55:17.603Z"],["3797426","FX-3217","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767945366428679]*{color}:\nThanks for the update\n{quote}","2026-01-09T07:56:18.314Z"],["3797431","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767945457666449]*{color}:\nOr can I just start it ASAP?\n{quote}","2026-01-09T07:57:49.847Z"],["3797434","DSR-3547","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] I have finalised the response letter. Please let us know if we need to add anything else or we can share it with user?","2026-01-09T07:59:13.233Z"],["3797437","PFI-829951","PFI","support@flitt.com","support@flitt.com","გამარჯობა,\n\nრით შეგვიძლია დაგეხმაროთ?\nპატივისცემით,\n\nNino Pachulia\n\n{color:#1d1c1d}Support Specialist{color}\n\n\n\n{color:#222222}+995 325 00 01 02{color}\n\n[npachulia@flitt.com|mailto:npachulia@flitt.com] | [LinkedIn|https://www.linkedin.com/in/nino-pachulia/] | [www.flitt.com|https://flitt.com/]{color:#202124}{color}{color:#202124}{color}\n\n\n\n\n!https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdesUJg1p54UqXLenrFQFanpvXuj_umTqEFnw1W5JR9LBf8O3m6bGImWLGpg2ulKBMgaF3p6b25v6bmXHIHIZutpHE-jvRov39TlA4JBIsOA1TnvQv9Hi1Pl6DSaGos3E_cDDVNa_WgN0NWjc5AHd9dzQAW?key=gAVmix1twk-tFXoz-xQXqA!{color:#202124}{color}\n\n\n---- on Thu, 08 Jan 2026 10:21:45 +0400  *\"pfi\"<pfi@taxify.atlassian.net>*  wrote ---- \n\n\n{quote}\n\n\n\n{color:#333333}{color}{color:#999999} —-—-—-—{color} {color:#333333}\n{color}{color:#999999} Reply above this line.{color} {color:#333333}\n\n\nchargeback_reports commented:\n\nHello\n\nPlease get back with an answer\n\nპატივისცემით\n\n +Best Regards+\n\n{color}{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#333333}{color}{color:#595959} -{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#595959}მირა წოწორია / Miranda{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#595959}Mira{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#595959} tsotsoria{color}{color:#333333}\n\n{color}{color:#595959}Customer Journey Expert{color}{color:#333333}\n\n{color}{color:#595959}Payments Development Tribe{color}{color:#333333}{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#333333}{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge/]{color:#333333}{color}\n {color:#333333}{color} !1767942492548013_292097426.png|thumbnail!{color:#333333}  <[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/request/2972373/attachment/1103910]>{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:#3572b0}View request{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-829951?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6IjJkOGQxMmYwNGQ0ODVkNGYyMGVhMTA3ZjFjNjI2NjEzYWFjMTA5YmY0YmQwZmYzZTRhMzQzYjlkM2NmNWY2ZTciLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiNTM4MDYiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IlBGSS04Mjk5NTEifSwiZXhwIjoxNzcwMjcyNTA0LCJpYXQiOjE3Njc4NTMzMDR9.wnUTe_K4gfU6DGVipfqXZlOK9uvJQSGWSoPr2aFUSkk&sda_source=notification-email]{color:#3572b0}{color}{color:#333333} ·{color} [{color:#333333}{color}{color:#3572b0}Turn off this request's notifications{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-829951/unsubscribe?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..l6HNJXxOKl5kZ6lF-KChMUGSAigZLeaFUf-BFcriUlU]{color:#3572b0}{color}{color:#333333}\n\n{color}{color:#707070}This is shared with chargeback_reports and{color} [{color:#707070}support@flitt.com{color}|mailto:support@flitt.com]{color:#707070}.{color}{color:#333333}{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:#707070}Powered by Jira Service Management{color}|https://www.atlassian.com/software/jira/service-desk/powered-by?utm_medium=jira-in-product&utm_source=jira_service_desk_email_footer&utm_content=taxify]{color:#707070}{color}{color:#333333}\n Sent on January 8, 2026 8:21:44 AM EET{color} \n!http://usw2-track.atlassian.com/CI0/0101019b9c44af93-425e88af-77fa-47f2-a62b-9b892499dba1-000000/WRgEWjMPGNzdxMf0LMsOAFFCNWlXLp0dT2o5zB5Nklo=439!{color:#333333}{color} {quote}","2026-01-09T08:01:02.988Z"],["3797438","XP-3014","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","The issue has not been updated in the past week.\n\nPlease update the status and/or comment about the progress.","2026-01-09T08:01:25.017Z"],["3797439","XP-3013","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","The issue has not been updated in the past week.\n\nPlease update the status and/or comment about the progress.","2026-01-09T08:01:25.114Z"],["3797440","XP-2973","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","The issue has not been updated in the past week.\n\nPlease update the status and/or comment about the progress.","2026-01-09T08:01:27.786Z"],["3797443","XP-3033","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:40cb7816-0b3b-4f87-ae87-8ac607ccf2c0], \nPlease link the ticket to an epic (so it's visible on the Product Discovery board).","2026-01-09T08:01:53.778Z"],["3797444","XP-3027","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:469d02b5-abf2-42fb-9357-94b8c8901f09], \nPlease link the ticket to an epic (so it's visible on the Product Discovery board).","2026-01-09T08:01:53.821Z"],["3797445","XP-3035","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:641d5e7c9796ea0a8718ca5e], \nPlease link the ticket to an epic (so it's visible on the Product Discovery board).","2026-01-09T08:01:53.864Z"],["3797447","PFI-822715","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi, this ticket will be closed. Please follow advice from previous responses and reach out / create new ticket if further help is needed.","2026-01-09T08:02:13.895Z"],["3797448","PFI-830966","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have checked with the Fraud team and they confirmed the refunding option not available at the moment due to an active dispute. \nWe are currently not able to issue the refund to the OPM. The payment will be released as soon as the dispute process has concluded. \n\nIf the customer wins the chargeback dispute they will be automatically refunded. \nIf the customer doesn’t win the dispute the refunding option will become available. \n\nLet me know if you have any questions. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T08:02:52.634Z"],["3797451","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","[@ahmed.farghaly|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63fc5f040a4a47fb8d20cf92] since this driver is Flex driver, payments should not go to the Driver, but to the Fleet (company).\nI checked, and found that for driver's company:\n• there is \"client\" row. id=41217891. created on Nov 19th\n• there is \"client_account\" row, id = 24694520, created on Nov 19th\nMaybe your systems has not correctly picked up that this driver is {{fleet-equipped}}? I mean this logic added by [@volodymyr.hadomskyi|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:fc7ada41-3f9c-4d74-95f1-90300ecbe201] in next PRs ([https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/156147|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/156147], [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/156587|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/156587], [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/156642|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/156642], [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/156677|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/156677], [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/156858|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/156858], [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/157256|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/157256])","2026-01-09T08:03:53.855Z"],["3797453","HS-28188","HS","peter.moulding@bolt.eu","Peter Evan Moulding","[~accountid:62ee23c696eb272011a918c4] I didn’t yet receive the official Arbeitszeugnis in German and English. Where can I find it? ","2026-01-09T08:03:56.260Z"],["3797454","RNTL-29676","RNTL","risqi.berliandie@bolt.eu","Risqi Berliandie Rubiandini","Result summary in this doc: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ITk3VCF2WhHRwKxuSwYFmDrsxxgH8V2GsHOHayObKig/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.jt07chxzpz4|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ITk3VCF2WhHRwKxuSwYFmDrsxxgH8V2GsHOHayObKig/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.jt07chxzpz4|smart-link] \n\nRaw data and calculation: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1C3t6oKWF16xdFGvkwQ-AS34QmF9mxkaySasMFbe0528/edit?gid=1786461364#gid=1786461364|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1C3t6oKWF16xdFGvkwQ-AS34QmF9mxkaySasMFbe0528/edit?gid=1786461364#gid=1786461364|smart-link] \n\n[Databricks notebook|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/1375447385069189?o=3598988355446810#command/7641820064993451]","2026-01-09T08:04:13.637Z"],["3797455","HS-28221","HS","patryk.stachewicz@bolt.eu","Patryk Stachewicz","Hi [~accountid:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db], it’s finally here. Apologies for the delay, hope it’s better late than never 🙂 \n\n[^20260108152904_001.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T08:04:30.368Z"],["3797456","PFI-831245","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 20.00 ZAR on 21/12/2025, 11:46:09UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 20th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-09T08:04:52.115Z"],["3797457","PRF-1765","PRF","carelin.magi@bolt.eu","Carelin Mägi","Hey [~accountid:712020:40dff97c-26b0-48f4-b19d-0b071f574f5a] I added you as an assignee but we can add the creatives together, once we’re launching our full-funnel campaigns on Meta. These are more suitable for reach campaigns","2026-01-09T08:04:55.328Z"],["3797460","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Shreya Bhandari [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767945931674399]*{color}:\nYou may start asap \n{quote}","2026-01-09T08:05:44.411Z"],["3797461","CSP-370","CSP","olga.kuchina@bolt.eu","Olga Kuchina","26W2: Added Cross Validation for more stable validation and correct selection of the best performing model","2026-01-09T08:05:50.286Z"],["3797470","DSR-3605","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Data sent","2026-01-09T08:07:55.732Z"],["3797472","PFI-829819","PFI","pauline.kamau@bolt-outsource.eu","Pauline Kamau","NB; Here is the payment link- [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/76150092?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Africa%2FNairobi|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/76150092?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Africa%2FNairobi]","2026-01-09T08:08:09.952Z"],["3797486","MLC-414","MLC","durrah.abdullah@bolt.eu","Durrah Abdullah","*Update*: For improvement, PRD reviewed & feedback shared for [Suspension Recovery|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uVOxSttegTVU6VfrX0T_PSpMDVPLKXOmOiqsTjUUd20/edit?tab=t.0]. Suspension-related blocking reasons currently lack document name property hence would require engineering support.\n\n*Next Steps*:  Align on timelines and scope for phase 1 part of the project with Staņislavs Kuļšs","2026-01-09T08:08:18.739Z"],["3797487","PFI-831235","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe user received a negative balance of 3.44 EUR from a cash order. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280596242?cityId=1&showUserTz=false|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280596242?cityId=1&showUserTz=false]\n\nThe order price was 17.84 EUR, but the courier marked they received 14.40 EUR from the customer. Which created a negative balance. \n\nIf the courier marked the amount incorrectly the user should be refunded. \nThere are a couple of options that you could try. \n\n1. Make an adjustment on the cash order. \n2. Issue a 3.44 EUR refund to the Bolt balance. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T08:08:20.994Z"],["3797489","PFI-819111","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment has been manually recovered https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75021715 ","2026-01-09T08:09:03.257Z"],["3797490","LSS-59991","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Yes Alexandros, feel free to cc me in the answer. ","2026-01-09T08:09:13.142Z"],["3797493","PFI-831255","PFI","uzoamaka.ikwuazom@bolt-outsource.eu","Uzoamaka Ikwuazom","!IMG-20250925-WA0011(1).jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T08:09:24.205Z"],["3797494","PFI-830547","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, is the general question about:\n\n* companies not receiving emails?\n* Fiscalization not working; I see there’re fiscalization error for the invoice for the company attached","2026-01-09T08:10:05.665Z"],["3797496","SREDESK-7394","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","[~accountid:604aad6558aa8d00722fb033] {{taxify_rental_car_order_scheduled}} schema location is on Beta cluster.\nWe would like to avoid creating a new schema in the Beta cluster, because the Beta cluster is quite loaded already.\nIs it OK to create the schema in Gamma cluster instead of Beta?","2026-01-09T08:11:11.717Z"],["3797500","PFI-831256","PFI","ketlin.kruger@bolt-outsource.eu","Ketlin Kruger","!Screenshot_20260108_193214_LHV.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T08:12:10.054Z"],["3797501","PFI-831256","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-09T08:12:12.830Z"],["3797502","LSS-61099","LSS","olesja.timofejeva@bolt.eu","Olesja Timofejeva","Hey! Could you please contact him and notify about the urgency :pray::skin-tone-2:?","2026-01-09T08:12:32.021Z"],["3797503","LSS-47932","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","status update: waiting for the final document from the counterparty","2026-01-09T08:12:42.997Z"],["3797504","PRTEAM-263","PRTEAM","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","Hi [~accountid:712020:9f920389-9b88-4c5d-9768-f418248e5ee1]. You can find the benefits briefed in the Initiative (% of cashbacks are still getting finalised). Given that, could we start discussions for organic or paid PR? \nHappy to share anything you need or clarify details if you’re looking for something specific. Cheers!","2026-01-09T08:12:58.178Z"],["3797522","PFI-831257","PFI","ionut.florescu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ionut Gabriel Florescu","!IMG_1341 (71619bec-f01c-4f9c-90ca-8b0609e949ad).png|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_1342 (51c11df6-a3ac-4d3f-ad26-c00399fc8647).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T08:14:18.462Z"],["3797524","HS-28781","HS","sweta.sahu@bolt.eu","Sweta Sahu","[^FS4_jan26 (1).pdf]","2026-01-09T08:14:55.418Z"],["3797525","LSS-60557","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","[^Bolt Services PL Sp. z o.o._Erykiem Polec, Wlasciciel firmy_PL_24.09.2021 (1).pdf]\n\nSure, here it is 🙂 ","2026-01-09T08:16:38.800Z"],["3797526","FDBT-4756","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-09T08:17:10.974Z"],["3797529","DRX-27883","DRX","mykola.mozghovyi@bolt.eu","Mykola Mozghovyi","track: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C095MKW43V0/p1767946657064189?thread_ts=1765983843.361549&cid=C095MKW43V0|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C095MKW43V0/p1767946657064189?thread_ts=1765983843.361549&cid=C095MKW43V0]","2026-01-09T08:18:06.282Z"],["3797533","DSR-3465","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","_Internal note: Will have a meeting on the 14th January about the process_ ⏳","2026-01-09T08:19:02.630Z"],["3797536","PFI-831247","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe initial price for the order was 821.65 UAH. \nHowever, since some of the items were not available the final capture was only 723.20 UAH. \n\nThe authorization for 821.65 UAH has been released by Bolt. \nPlease treat this as a pre-authorization not released case. \n\nThe authorization is usually released within 14 days, but can take up to 30 days. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T08:19:27.707Z"],["3797537","PAI-925","PAI","hanshendrik.karro@bolt.eu","Hans-Hendrik Karro","Blocked. Pending dedicated AE support.","2026-01-09T08:19:28.157Z"],["3797538","RDXENG-4588","RDXENG","evgenii.sukhanov@bolt.eu","Evgenii Sukhanov","\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1767868150867489|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1767868150867489|smart-card]","2026-01-09T08:19:28.339Z"],["3797539","LSS-61312","LSS","kerubo.ombati@bolt.eu","Kerubo Ombati","[^BOLT Operations NDA (Mutual)_signed.pdf] _(412 kB)_","2026-01-09T08:19:47.986Z"],["3797540","PFI-830940","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey\nI actually do not know 🤔 \nit is not to our team - but which exactly - idk.","2026-01-09T08:20:02.247Z"],["3797541","PFI-831051","PFI","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] - thanks for clarify about SF and yes it wouldn’t apply to them.   \n\nRegarding the statement, I am still confused and need your help.  I am afraid I don't understand about the change in the statement.  As the ride in question happened in January 2026, the statement for January 2026 will be out on 3rd Feb 2026, so it's not out yet.  So by moving the ride cost for the 8th Jan trip from Huawei South Africa Account to Huawei Tanzania account, wouldn’t that correct in itself take care of the change of statement for Jan when its issued in Feb.  Am I missing something?  I would be happy to get on a call so you can advise me/clarify further, as I am not understanding the question. But yes the statement for Jan 2026 should show the ride that happened in Tanzania under the Huawei Tanzania account and not the South Africa account as it is Huawei Tanzania that will be paying for that trip.  So both the ride receipt and the statement for Jan should reflect the trip that happened and should be under Huawei Tanzania account, not Huawei South africa account.  I took a look at the example you gave but that was for a statement created on 2nd December 2025 for month of November. ","2026-01-09T08:20:23.987Z"],["3797542","BPPA-40","BPPA","hanshendrik.karro@bolt.eu","Hans-Hendrik Karro","Results: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BP/pages/6972539260/Bolt+Plus+Measuring+Incremental+Impact+Results|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BP/pages/6972539260/Bolt+Plus+Measuring+Incremental+Impact+Results|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T08:20:40.460Z"],["3797544","WD-14199","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:61c07bf9a54af90069a42e2f] please try again i updated securities","2026-01-09T08:20:47.939Z"],["3797545","PFI-831051","PFI","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:5f1fbb0eef11df002588080f] - perhaps you can advise, If I have misunderstood the query from [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] ","2026-01-09T08:22:51.835Z"],["3797546","WD-22436","WD","peggy.dano@bolt.eu","Peggy Stefany Dano","Hi [~accountid:712020:6850b463-f3bb-4458-b00b-b094810b5bcd] ,\n\nIt seems that my workday access for new zealand is still not yet available. Could you please review the access again?\n\nThank you for your help. ","2026-01-09T08:22:57.346Z"],["3797547","PFI-831191","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm that no refund has been issued to the customer. \n\nThe refund 82.38 RON most likely failed because the amount selected exceeded the captured amount. \nThe refund cannot be higher than the amount we received from the customer. \n\nPlease note the order price was 82.32 RON. \nCaptured from the customers card 79.71 RON\nPaid with Bolt balance 2.67 RON. \n\nIf you would like to fully refund the customer then you should issue an OPM refund for 79.71 RON and a BB refund for 2.67 RON. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T08:23:10.808Z"],["3797550","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767947028657929]*{color}:\nThe test is now running and the disabling feature flag is de-activated to make sure there are no conflicts.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T08:24:02.522Z"],["3797551","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Shreya Bhandari [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767947031447979]*{color}:\nI will disable the ff\n{quote}","2026-01-09T08:24:04.346Z"],["3797554","GRWA-1465","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","Data has been updated in the google sheet and backend table.","2026-01-09T08:24:17.099Z"],["3797555","BP-8155","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","cc [~accountid:5db2cd1c72d6f20c33d19e79] [~accountid:634684f353df3c0123201010] \n\nOn January 9, a new discrepancy has appeared in the schema:\n\n{noformat}--- build/db/schema/local_mysql_57/taxify_business/order_finished_event_queue.sql\t2026-01-08 23:01:47.333372798 +0000\n+++ build/db/schema/live_mysql_57/taxify_business/order_finished_event_queue.sql\t2026-01-08 23:01:47.477372446 +0000\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@\n   `retry_count` bigint unsigned NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n   `error_reason` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n   `order_id` bigint unsigned NOT NULL,\n-  `order_try_id` bigint unsigned DEFAULT NULL,\n+  `order_try_id` bigint unsigned NOT NULL,\n   `order_type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n   `order_created_by` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n   `order_created` timestamp(6) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1970-01-01 00:00:01.000000',\n@@ -22,5 +22,5 @@\n   `user_id` bigint unsigned NOT NULL,\n   PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n   UNIQUE KEY `idx_tb_ofeq_order_try_id_order_id_city_id_UNIQUE` (`order_try_id`,`order_id`,`city_id`),\n-  KEY `idx_tb_ofeq_created_status` (`created`,`status`)\n+  KEY `idx_tb_ofeq_created_status_retry_count` (`created`,`status`,`retry_count`)\n ) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4;\n\n{noformat}\n\nThis discrepancy will be disregarded within the scope of this task because of being related to this PR, which is expected to be merged soon:\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159264|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159264|smart-link]","2026-01-09T08:24:18.611Z"],["3797556","PFI-831177","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for EUR 11.74 on Dec 23, 2025, 20:02:00 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 74987505357003906805224  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 23rd of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_Q3RNXQ2BWBXMS6G3_RNDN62RHPFTZCPQ9.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-09T08:24:23.611Z"],["3797558","PFI-812894","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Please raise a ticket to billing team to generate weekly reports for this client. ","2026-01-09T08:24:32.505Z"],["3797559","CCM-22240","CCM","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","Aligned with [~accountid:5e4fb22d2a59dc0c8fe5905d] via Slack, she can pick up this request\nWe just need to wait for Raluca’s Articulate license  ","2026-01-09T08:24:33.321Z"],["3797561","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Shreya Bhandari [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767947065552169]*{color}:\nAwesome :raised_hands::skin-tone-3: you did it already :fire:\n{quote}","2026-01-09T08:24:37.841Z"],["3797562","RCE-328","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767947065707049]*{color}:\nJust did it - waited a few minutes just to make sure that the test change is synced.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T08:24:38.441Z"],["3797563","WD-14199","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","I also have an update for customer invoice from Workday support: \n\nThe tenant had the optional worktag Business Line turned ON when invoice C-EE003-23-000374 was created on 8/8/2023. However, the balancing worktag was turned OFF by the time adjustment CAC-EE003-24-000133 was applied on 1/25/2024.  According to development, Workday does not support \"in-flight\" transactions where a worktag is toggled on and off.\n\nIn this case, development suggests following the workaround outlined below:\n\n*1-Cancel the payment: VISA International Service Association – 01/25/2024 (ID 5746$564).* \n\n*2-Cancel invoice: C-EE003-23-000374 (ID 964$4902).*  \n\n*3-Recreate the invoice while the worktag balancing is turned off.*  \n\n*4-Re-apply the adjustment.*","2026-01-09T08:24:56.394Z"],["3797564","PAW-14673","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @tomekt-bolt\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/pull/3073\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-09 08:24:58 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-09T08:24:58.504Z"],["3797565","PRODSEC-675","PRODSEC","aghadadash.guliyev@bolt.eu","Dadash Guliyev","Using Github is not useful, problem: Not all github codes end in Prod, feasible as a compliance checkmark.\nUsing Jfrog: Terrible idea, no official way of pulling the latest image without knowing the hashsum? (stupid)\n","2026-01-09T08:25:19.930Z"],["3797566","DRX-28021","DRX","mykola.mozghovyi@bolt.eu","Mykola Mozghovyi","possible reference documentation: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/h4O08g|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/h4O08g|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T08:25:36.353Z"],["3797568","PC-4926","PC","pavel.makarov@bolt.eu","Pavel Makarov","[~accountid:712020:71558a29-6aa8-4ba9-a65c-35de451da5e6] most of the logic related to {{co-badged}} cards is covered with Carte Bancair implementation, yet there are some difference in processing requirement.\n\nWould you please clarify following:\n\n* shall the routing ({{mada}} vs other schemes) be based on the user’s location defined by the App?\n* when {{mada}} card is first added outside of Saudi Arabia, should be the logo shown as Visa / Mastercard?\n* is that correct, that same card’s payments from the same user might be processed via different schemes (mada / visa / mastercard) based on the user’s location (Saudi Arabia / rest of the world)?\n* how do we distinguish {{mada}} cards? For {{Carte Bancair}} we have bin range list, is that the case for {{mada}} as well?","2026-01-09T08:26:12.826Z"],["3797569","LSS-60150","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Discussions were held in slack on 09.01.2026. Legal need to update the terms now and update stakeholders accordingly. ","2026-01-09T08:26:33.718Z"],["3797572","PFI-831176","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nYou can provide the user the RRN code 535365010357 to locate the payment. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-09T08:28:04.585Z"],["3797573","L10N-26789","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26784](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26784)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T