amann","[~accountid:712020:ab58e2f4-f31f-4230-9a41-30c28c8bd545] I created a task [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13429|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13429|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T08:29:31.237Z"],["3797589","HS-28673","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:dc4824f4-a6bc-41f2-af89-59d155dc0cc8],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-09T08:30:19.346Z"],["3797590","HS-28784","HS","oleh.pater@bolt.eu","Oleh Pater","!Image.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T08:30:25.440Z"],["3797592","SREDESK-7394","SREDESK","konstantin.mitrakov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Mitrakov","yes, it’s fine","2026-01-09T08:30:43.181Z"],["3797593","CEBF-1820","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","[~accountid:5da9bc599aebed0c29c2acb8] Task is completed. Please verify. Thanks","2026-01-09T08:30:46.346Z"],["3797594","PFI-829363","PFI","anastacia.njunge@bolt.eu","Anastacia Njunge","Hi Team, Any update on this case? ","2026-01-09T08:31:18.341Z"],["3797595","DBRE-8590","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}There are some nodes can be pruned:\n\tNodes: [internal-kv1-13.sqldb:20160 internal-kv1-14.sqldb:20160 internal-kv1-15.sqldb:20160]\n\tYou can destroy them with the command: `tiup cluster prune internal`{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster display internal | grep tikv | awk '{print $1, $6}'\ninternal-kv1-1.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-10.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-11.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-12.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-13.sqldb:20160 Tombstone\ninternal-kv1-14.sqldb:20160 Tombstone\ninternal-kv1-15.sqldb:20160 Tombstone\ninternal-kv1-2.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-3.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-4.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-5.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-6.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-7.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-8.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-9.sqldb:20160 Up{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569245 | grep \"region_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569245\n    \"region_count\": 0,\n    \nroot@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569246 | grep \"region_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569246\n    \"region_count\": 0,\n    \nroot@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569247 | grep \"region_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u internal-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store 104569247\n    \"region_count\": 0,{noformat}\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 08.30.56.png|width=843,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 08.30.56.png\"!","2026-01-09T08:31:24.521Z"],["3797596","CNT-377","CNT","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","Hi [~accountid:61cac1b0326554006c9b5945]. With regards to discussion [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08RK1ST2CV/p1767775686620949?thread_ts=1767691901.652189&cid=C08RK1ST2CV], need support for CA HoppPlus. New benefit introduced is exclusive discounts (besides the cashbacks).\nHappy to share anything you need or clarify details if you’re looking for something specific. ","2026-01-09T08:31:29.762Z"],["3797598","LSS-61101","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","Hi [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] let me ask LL 🙂 ","2026-01-09T08:31:38.591Z"],["3797600","PFI-818124","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","It has failed ","2026-01-09T08:31:44.089Z"],["3797603","HS-28726","HS","ingrid.valgejarv@bolt.eu","Ingrid Valgejärv","Hello!\n\nThe employment confirmation letter was shared via email. Please let me know if there is anything else I can help with!\n\nKind regards\n\nIngrid","2026-01-09T08:32:37.809Z"],["3797604","PAW-14748","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-09T08:32:39.397Z"],["3797605","PAW-14747","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-09T08:32:41.746Z"],["3797607","WEBSD-1461","WEBSD","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:60528926695c3900706cc79e] \n\nI’ve updated the text but please note that the link to the blog post under “Bolt Flex” in the text you sent, does not work. ","2026-01-09T08:33:13.093Z"],["3797610","LSS-59752","LSS","mykyta.rozhok@bolt.eu","Mykyta Rozhok","Here is the IBAN: *LT87 3250 0376 6902 0019*. Recipient name: *Martin Bendl*.\n\nCan I inform the user about the amount we will transfer? What is the final amount in EUR? And will it be possible to share confirmation of the payment in case the user requests it?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T08:34:13.247Z"],["3797612","LSS-61314","LSS","aleksis.anijarv@bolt.eu","Aleksis Anijärv","[^BOLT LUXURY Training.pdf] _(179 kB)_","2026-01-09T08:34:29.521Z"],["3797616","DBRE-8590","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster prune internal\n...\n+ [ Serial ] - FindTomestoneNodes\nWill destroy these nodes: [internal-kv1-13.sqldb:20160 internal-kv1-14.sqldb:20160 internal-kv1-15.sqldb:20160]\nDo you confirm this action? [y/N]:(default=N) y\n...\n+ [ Serial ] - RemoveTomestoneNodesInPD\nDestroy success{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster display internal | grep tikv | awk '{print $1, $6}'\ninternal-kv1-1.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-10.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-11.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-12.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-2.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-3.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-4.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-5.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-6.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-7.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-8.sqldb:20160 Up\ninternal-kv1-9.sqldb:20160 Up{noformat}","2026-01-09T08:34:59.904Z"],["3797618","WEBSD-1458","WEBSD","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi! \n\nThanks for reaching out! However, please note that Blog is managed by the Content team, please reach out to them instead. \n\nThanks! ","2026-01-09T08:35:09.009Z"],["3797619","LSS-60050","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hello, [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] 😉 May I ask you for the confirmation that the Dokobit sugnatire is valid? Maybe the checking through the governmental website is not successfull as this is a foreign signature and it is still valid? \n\nBtw. how the SpotDraft signing of another document is going? Can we get this today? ","2026-01-09T08:35:25.213Z"],["3797620","PFI-830968","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","payments have been matched please check this with billing !","2026-01-09T08:35:38.290Z"],["3797621","WEBSD-1449","WEBSD","zoe.johnson@bolt.eu","Zoë Johnson","!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 09.34.31.png|width=419,height=313,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 09.34.31.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 09.34.22.png|width=533,height=312,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 09.34.22.png\"!\n\nThank you @hector! Here are the requested Images \n\nWe also thought first a Blog Post - ut this event happens yearly, so we decided on a page. \n\nWe will keep it only in english for this year, as due to time constrains no localization is possible ","2026-01-09T08:35:57.448Z"],["3797622","PFI-830915","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment not found. Please confirm with the partner if the payment has bounced back from their bank. If already checked, add a comment here and we’ll investigate further.","2026-01-09T08:35:58.661Z"],["3797625","DSR-3607","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-09T08:36:22.385Z"],["3797627","HS-28779","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Waiting for PQ.","2026-01-09T08:37:04.124Z"],["3797630","LSS-61314","LSS","aleksis.anijarv@bolt.eu","Aleksis Anijärv","Discussion is here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C056CRXFXC1/p1762346426588899|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C056CRXFXC1/p1762346426588899|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T08:37:21.352Z"],["3797631","FX-3456","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Caroliina Laantee [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767947829234769]*{color}:\nMarking this as solved because couldn't find a source cause for this. Can be picked up again when reoccurs. Currently added audit logs for car application creation from Fleet Portal which were missing so far.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T08:37:24.447Z"],["3797633","PFI-831272","PFI","tiberiu.dosescu@bolt.eu","Tiberiu-Valeriu Dosescu","!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 10.36.57.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T08:37:36.163Z"],["3797634","SREDO-399","SREDO","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","To resolve the issue, I took two actions:\n\n* Excluded this repo from backup-daily: {{docker-bart-local}}\n* Remove backup data directory for this repo: {{docker-bart-local}}","2026-01-09T08:38:02.448Z"],["3797635","FX-3456","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767947875425479]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3456 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T08:38:07.336Z"],["3797636","MLC-3812","MLC","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","[Tracking sheet|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xeDbPwX90b_DHknd_STMnhiPpNMs3ILZLEpgbGH03xM/edit?gid=1322202513#gid=1322202513]","2026-01-09T08:38:11.361Z"],["3797637","WFM-9904","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello [~accountid:712020:cde6e2fa-0f48-44e8-b1c7-2a3a70d10b33],\n\nYou already have the necessary role to access Beehive. Could you please let me know if you’re still facing any issues?","2026-01-09T08:38:16.751Z"],["3797645","PFI-820892","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! I have added the 10% BFC-s\nCash blocking: -2000\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 10.37.54.png|width=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 10.37.54.png\"!\n\n\n\nDo I understand correctly that the current Bolt Ålesund should also be changed so that existing drivers also would have 10% commission? ","2026-01-09T08:39:14.079Z"],["3797646","PFI-830449","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","We do not let companies to split payments transfers will be done separately  !","2026-01-09T08:39:25.149Z"],["3797648","PFI-788621","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Clearing backlog !","2026-01-09T08:40:33.885Z"],["3797650","LSS-56257","LSS","kristina.pugaca@bolt.eu","Kristina Pugaca","Hello team, The MCAA agreed on a €20 compensation.\n[~accountid:712020:1e9398f2-efcd-4dcd-8ece-28e6f8578e37]  could you please help with the promo codes? Alternatively, I can issue €3 ones if that works.\n\n!image-20260109-082531.png|width=612,height=375,alt=\"image-20260109-082531.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-09T08:40:44.115Z"],["3797651","PFI-788721","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Clearing Backlog !","2026-01-09T08:40:50.113Z"],["3797653","WEBSD-1447","WEBSD","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi Kadi! \n\nThanks for flagging! Could you please add reasoning why CarbonNeutral PDF links as images should be removed and added as simple hyperlinks under the section for partners.","2026-01-09T08:41:01.531Z"],["3797655","HS-28781","HS","loredana.panait@bolt.eu","Loredana Panait","Hi Team, \n\n[~accountid:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d] - kindly note that the template will replace the one previously used in 2025. For all 2026 new hires, or in case an active employee will need a tax rate change and they will have to fill in the FS 4 form, the attached file will be used for all of them. \n\nThank you for support, \n\nLore","2026-01-09T08:41:16.041Z"],["3797657","DBRE-8586","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Internal down scale\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03055EHHPS/p1767947653936269|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03055EHHPS/p1767947653936269]","2026-01-09T08:41:33.605Z"],["3797658","PFI-831273","PFI","martin.marek@bolt-outsource.eu","Martin Marek","!image-20260109-083727.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260109-083806.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T08:41:41.411Z"],["3797664","LSS-61314","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","The recommendations to the business provided here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fkT1NKRaJoJgbdJt8akIOJ_Bqxs8fmtrRWQblKUkL-c/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fkT1NKRaJoJgbdJt8akIOJ_Bqxs8fmtrRWQblKUkL-c/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]  ","2026-01-09T08:42:38.445Z"],["3797666","PFI-789942","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Clearing backlog if issue still exists please drop a comment !","2026-01-09T08:42:43.690Z"],["3797667","WEBSD-1446","WEBSD","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi Kadi! \n\nThanks for flagging this too! However, we don’t manage the translations ourselves, but the Localisation team does. Could you please contact them instead: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/group/175|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/group/175|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T08:42:49.419Z"],["3797668","CSP-277","CSP","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","26W02: Displaying aggregated fallback assignment stats on queue overview is done. 100% of planned features done. We’ll now clean up the feature flag and expose the feature to all permitted admin users.","2026-01-09T08:42:57.980Z"],["3797675","INT-568","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","pending is the analysis of PT Annual discount\n\nFollow up from the [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/INT-568|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/INT-568|smart-link] \n\n\n\nFYI for group: we have preliminary analysis but will need to check back in at end of Jan/ beg of Feb when we see users trial period ending\n\n \n\nprelim post-Dec initial analysis from [~accountid:610be972a539cb0068adf129] : [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Z-mO83jFcvU4Wig4vf30K4KKgLbq-f6atpdF1Z3nZvY/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.pfksmqgtwo34|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Z-mO83jFcvU4Wig4vf30K4KKgLbq-f6atpdF1Z3nZvY/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.pfksmqgtwo34|smart-link]\n\n* FYI: previous 2 weeks were our lowest in a long time. Although share of annual subscriptions went up, the overall volume in PT was below expectations ([+source+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/25196?Country=Portugal]).","2026-01-09T08:43:16.659Z"],["3797677","PFI-801155","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Clearing backlog if issue is still pending please drop a comment !","2026-01-09T08:43:41.016Z"],["3797679","L10N-26816","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26784](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26784)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:43:57.252Z"],["3797680","L10N-26817","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26784](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26784)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:43:58.003Z"],["3797681","L10N-26818","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26784](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26784)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:43:58.879Z"],["3797682","L10N-26821","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26784](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26784)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:44:02.510Z"],["3797683","L10N-26823","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26784](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26784)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:44:04.264Z"],["3797684","L10N-26825","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26784](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26784)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:44:04.941Z"],["3797685","CRC-2360","CRC","noud.ottens@bolt.eu","Noud Ottens","Hi![~accountid:712020:29d8b602-d17f-40cd-9cae-5653bc2c54b7] Apologies for the delay on my end. See below the answers to your questions, please let me know if anything is unclear.\n\n# Are both private hire ride-hailing service providers as well as taxi service providers offering rides via the Bolt platform? If relevant, in case of taxi services - how/by who is the ride fare determined?\nAll providers of taxi services in the Netherlands operate with a valid Chamber of Commerce registration and a KIWA taxi licence. Around 70% of Dutch drivers are sole proprietors, each with their own business registration and KIWA licence. The remaining 30% operate through a fleet, using the fleet’s business registration and KIWA licence. In all cases, billing is carried out directly by the driver or fleet to the rider. Fares are generally determined uniformly for all drivers, although price bidding is active in some cities (see below).\n# Do we have the app’s “price bidding” feature or the “driver counter offer” enabled in the NL?\nWe have Price Bidding enabled in 9 cities, that roughly represent 5% of total GMV. Counter offer was active in the past, but no longer.\n# Does the Bolt NL itself charge any platform fees to the riders (platform to rider fee)?\nWe charge booking fees on Airports (i.e. Schiphol), this is added to the ride fare, collected by the driver, paid to Bolt and Bolt consecutively pays it to the Airport.\n\nCC: [~accountid:6215e9f4347c690072f6f91d] ","2026-01-09T08:44:17.544Z"],["3797687","RENT-212","RENT","guillermo.salceda@bolt.eu","Guillermo Salceda Pacheco","Hello [~accountid:712020:95b78488-64d1-4339-8cfa-92c573553913] and [~accountid:5d8de3206c173a0d56fa6d29] Is this project a continuation of this one ([https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RENT-162|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RENT-162|smart-link] ) in which we worked in 25Q4? I guess so, so there’s no need to estimate additional working hours. If this is a new one, please add a description document.\n\nThank you!\n\nc.c. [~accountid:62615f256cb53d006a6a3fe1] [~accountid:712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] ","2026-01-09T08:44:34.380Z"],["3797688","PFI-830473","PFI","laura.ernestova@bolt.eu","Laura Ernestová","Hey Ketlin, No worries, we’ll wait! No, the invoice for 11/24-30 doesn’t need to be invoiced.:) \n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T08:44:37.078Z"],["3797689","EBIKE1-398","EBIKE1","susan.shao@bolt.eu","Cancan Shao","[^Cruiser fixed seat frame座椅支架报价单Q20260109.pdf]\n[^座椅支架组DFM.pptx]\n\n[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] [~accountid:624b3bdf8678e900705d9004]  We just got the quotation from Minta, Unit price is 110RMB while the tooling cost is 173,200RMB. The material quoted was all aluminum, while LY’s proposal was steel for the seatpost and sheet metal under seat.  ","2026-01-09T08:44:55.238Z"],["3797692","XP-2950","XP","yaroslav.morozevych@bolt.eu","Yaroslav Morozevych","h2. Results [[PR|https://github.com/bolteu/data-experimentation/pull/1116/]]\n\n* Deprecated v3 {{food}} metrics, including *Delivery*, *CS*, *Fraud*, and *Payments* food metrics (398 metrics) except for {{v3/metrics/targeting_user/food/pricing/*_report.yaml}} metrics as they still might be used for reporting.\n** Deprecation of these metrics means that these *metrics won't be picked up for processing by default by AB Processor* for exploratory (non-hypothesis, non-guardrails) dashboards, unless configured otherwise in the metric YAML.\n** For old scorecards, for guardrails and hypothesis dashboards, these metrics could still be processed if scorecard update is requested.\n\nList of {{v3}} metrics that are deprecated:\n\n{noformat}/targeting_user/food: 231\n/targeting_time_slice/food: 48\n/targeting_time_slice/food_dispatching: 47\n/targeting_user/cs_food: 40\n/targeting_user/payments_food: 32{noformat}","2026-01-09T08:46:02.764Z"],["3797693","LSS-61099","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! I sent a reminder to him yesterday already 😕 ","2026-01-09T08:46:06.409Z"],["3797695","PFI-831154","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nLet me follow up with payment developers to understand why the full amount was not captured. \nWill let you know once we have an update. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T08:46:58.003Z"],["3797696","PFI-831154","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1767948365288869|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1767948365288869]","2026-01-09T08:47:04.198Z"],["3797698","PFI-831149","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nYou can provide the user the RRN code {{535365010357}} to locate the payment with their bank. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-09T08:47:48.589Z"],["3797700","LSS-59752","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hey, [~accountid:616e87debcb5740068039c0c] , yes, you can inform about the amount (please do +*not*+ use a term “+*compensation*+” or sth like this. Use terms like *“Voluntary contribution”.*\n\nAs to*:*\n\n# *final amount in EUR*: this is not subject to legal - *please contact Ops Team.*\n# *Share confirmation of the payment in case the user requests it* - yes, you can share a document of payment confirmation on user’s request. Once you make a payment, you can just notify him about the payment through the message. \n\n*Important note:* Legal team does not open tickets or requests for making payments in such cases - *this is up to Ops Team.*","2026-01-09T08:48:28.920Z"],["3797702","LSS-58827","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Asked Lisanna and Ketter for help: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06GRMZDE4Q/p1767948547842469|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06GRMZDE4Q/p1767948547842469]","2026-01-09T08:49:29.991Z"],["3797703","LSS-57924","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","The parties agreed on a new version of the agreement. The counterparty has already signed the service agreement, annex 1 and annex 2. The Counterparty requested to sign documents with QES.\n\n[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] , [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432], can you please help to acquire Ahto’s signature for the attached documents via QES platform (Dokobit, DocuSign)? Thank you!\n\nThe signatures need to be on:\n\n* Service Agreement - page 13 (both on the right and left side)\n* Annex 1 - page 1, right side\n* Annex 2 - page 12, right side\n\n\n\n[^2026.01 Buolt Support Services Motion Arts Service Agreement Annex 2.pdf]\n[^2026.01 Buolt Support Services Motion Arts Service Agreement Annex 1.pdf]\n[^2026.01 Bolt Support Services Motion Arts Service Agreement (Договор 2852).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T08:49:33.035Z"],["3797706","WD-22436","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","Hi [~accountid:60ab52d6411c2200681a75e4] \nIt’s fixed now, sorry for unconvinience!","2026-01-09T08:50:12.247Z"],["3797707","WEBSD-1445","WEBSD","marc.chaffaut@bolt.eu","Marc du Chaffaut","h2. Votre location de voiture à prix réduit !\n\nVous cherchez un véhicule pour votre activité de chauffeur VTC ?  Nous avons la solution idéale pour vous : profitez de grandes réductions sur votre location hebdomadaire auprès de nos partenaires loueurs grâce aux trajets que vous effectuez sur notre plateforme !  \n\n# *Gagnez 3€ supplémentaires par course Bolt* (jusqu'à 90 courses par semaine), *soit jusqu'à 270€ par semaine* !\n# *Branding Bolt* (optionnelle chez Hertz, obligatoire chez CityCar) : *bénéficiez d’une rétro-commission hebdomadaire de 8 % sur votre chiffre d'affaires brut Bolt* si vous apposez un autocollant Bolt sur votre voiture (frais de pose couverts par Bolt).\n\nh2. Trouvez ici l'offre de location qui vous convient\n\nh2. CityCar\n\n* Engagement minimum de 6 mois avec véhicules brandés (obligatoire)\n* Location avec option d’achat (LOA)\n* 6 000 km par mois inclus\n* Assurance, entretien, assistance 0 km et remplacement du véhicule inclus\n\n[CityCar|https://www.city-car.fr/vtc]\n\nh2. Hertz\n\n* Contrats flexibles : à partir de 1 semaine (sans branding) ou 12 semaines (branding)\n* 1 350 km par semaine inclus\n* Assurance, entretien et remplacement du véhicule inclus\n\n[Hertz|https://www.hertz.fr/p/vtc]","2026-01-09T08:50:16.970Z"],["3797711","LSS-58622","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:6166d4c799b4b8006a26023e] what’s the status of this? Did we launch it? If so, where and how’s it going? 🙂 ","2026-01-09T08:51:37.188Z"],["3797712","FX-3586","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Marek Pagel [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767948684181669]*{color}:\nthere is a bug in admin code which results in the column being sorted by ID (column name mismatches, ID is the fallback). But even if it did work, it would only order by driver status, ignoring partner and suspensions statuses. Could be reported to <#C02H52XUKPG|>\n{quote}","2026-01-09T08:51:37.244Z"],["3797713","PFI-831138","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 4.00 EUR on 17/12/2025, 18:58:45UTC\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 72700925351169033832146  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 17th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n\n[^Proof of Refund 17-12-2025.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-09T08:51:38.761Z"],["3797714","HS-28770","HS","henelin.lohmus@bolt.eu","Henelin Lõhmus","Hey Ewa, thanks for raising this.\n\nUnfortunately, we don’t currently have a suitable technical solution to complete the audit automatically, and given the current workload, we’re not able to support it manually either.\nWe’ll need to put this request on pause for now and can revisit it once an alternative approach becomes available (which we’re currently working on). In the meantime, if you need to check a specific employee, please let us know and we can support that.\n\nHappy to discuss further if needed.\n\nHenelin","2026-01-09T08:51:47.246Z"],["3797715","PFI-808410","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Please send me a payment import file via slack i will share a template  as well !","2026-01-09T08:52:13.049Z"],["3797716","PFI-808909","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment not found. Please confirm with the partner if the payment has bounced back from their bank. If already checked, add a comment here and we’ll investigate further.","2026-01-09T08:52:41.593Z"],["3797719","PFI-831135","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Case solved in another ticket. Closing this duplicate request. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-830974|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-830974|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T08:53:02.870Z"],["3797720","CSP-344","CSP","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","26W02: Feature exposed for canary testing to a small pool of agents behind a feature flag. One issue discovered during canary tests which we will need to fix before further rollout.","2026-01-09T08:53:46.433Z"],["3797721","PFI-831124","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 54.00 ZAR on 22/12/2025, 09:27:10UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 20th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-09T08:53:59.656Z"],["3797722","SREDO-396","SREDO","tashik.moin@bolt.eu","Tashik Moin","81 euros / month increase","2026-01-09T08:54:31.071Z"],["3797723","DSR-3295","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","Contacted Norway SIS regarding the riders suspension and it’s necessity. \n\n* No real evidence so the rider will be unblocked. \n* SIS informed the relevant team to unblock them \n* Currently at 09/01/2026 14:55 the block is still there. *Before responding to the user, please check that the user is unblocked.*\n\n[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] Once the rider is unblocked what should our response be? Should we prepare the redacted driver ticket as evidence. Or as the rider will be unblocked a brief response regarding the unblocking and an overview is enough? ","2026-01-09T08:54:36.221Z"],["3797724","LEG-1068","LEG","kristjan.okas@bolt.eu","Kristjan Okas","Reopening the ticket, and we are expecting first feedback from the external counsels next week.","2026-01-09T08:54:36.583Z"],["3797726","PFI-831280","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-09T08:55:39.716Z"],["3797727","LSS-61101","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","[~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f]\n I’ve received the answer that they are not using (qualified electronic signature). An alternative option for them is to use trusted profile. \n\nHowever, it seems to me that both parties can sign in a different way, right? I also asked if its ok, that we will sign it by qualified electronic signature and they’re ok with this 🙂 ","2026-01-09T08:56:29.704Z"],["3797728","LSS-48622","LSS","kristjan.okas@bolt.eu","Kristjan Okas","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1079/WEBSD-1369|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1079/WEBSD-1369|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T08:57:06.563Z"],["3797729","DSO-45","DSO","ivanna.symonovych@bolt.eu","Ivanna Symonovych","[~accountid:641c083767102fc717c1538c] , this already completed, right? Should we link the doc and close the the project?","2026-01-09T08:57:08.546Z"],["3797730","LSS-48623","LSS","kristjan.okas@bolt.eu","Kristjan Okas","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1079/WEBSD-1369|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1079/WEBSD-1369|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T08:57:27.990Z"],["3797731","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] \nThank you! Please also provide translation for CTA (Download the Bolt app). ","2026-01-09T08:57:35.436Z"],["3797732","LSS-48624","LSS","kristjan.okas@bolt.eu","Kristjan Okas","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1079/WEBSD-1369|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1079/WEBSD-1369|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T08:57:45.027Z"],["3797733","L10N-26832","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26827](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26827)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:58:23.660Z"],["3797734","L10N-26833","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26827](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26827)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:58:24.428Z"],["3797735","L10N-26835","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26827](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26827)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:58:26.207Z"],["3797736","L10N-26836","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26827](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26827)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:58:26.405Z"],["3797737","L10N-26838","