te discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26827](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26827)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:58:29.056Z"],["3797740","L10N-26843","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26827](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26827)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T08:58:30.092Z"],["3797741","LSS-60455","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:61542c1e07ac3c0068bc7768], thank you for this ticket. \nWe’ll review this ticket in the first half of next week. Hope that works for you. \nThanks.","2026-01-09T08:58:33.056Z"],["3797742","LSS-61230","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:a9500cde-28bc-4a8e-95d6-7818a2252cf8] I added info for bolt operations. I aksed about Bolt technology because may old marketing contacts are signed by Bolt Technology \n\nYou can share file with Apple ","2026-01-09T08:58:33.655Z"],["3797743","PFI-817337","PFI","jelena.griciva@bolt-outsource.eu","Jelena Griciva","Payout amount was added to the next [payout |https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records/28356044490]on December 22, that went through.","2026-01-09T08:58:35.975Z"],["3797744","BDB-1494","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey[~accountid:628e5c9d8026a10068b1e457]  \nGreat!\nWould Mon be ok for you? Thank you!","2026-01-09T08:58:38.127Z"],["3797746","CNT-377","CNT","aleksandra.onutsina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Onutšina","[~accountid:712020:f172cd28-e81b-4011-8942-5ec6b2912f37] hi, thanks ! What would be the desired deadline here?","2026-01-09T08:59:31.460Z"],["3797747","HS-28784","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:73528ba9-f129-4b0c-b65d-38a479119ccc], \n\nThank you for raising this. I see that my colleague added your Visa details without an expiration date. Were you attempting to update the information she entered? If so, please forward me the details that need to be changed.\n\nIf the current information is correct, please try to submit the task without making any changes. You can click 'Cancel' to reset any accidental edits, and then attempt to submit the task again.\n\nIf the details are correct but Workday still won't let you submit, please let me know.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 10.53.00.png|width=823,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 10.53.00.png\"!","2026-01-09T08:59:41.174Z"],["3797748","DSO-55","DSO","ivanna.symonovych@bolt.eu","Ivanna Symonovych","[~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] , this is currently in progress, right? Do you still own this project? I do I recall right that a first draft must be ready in Jan 2026?","2026-01-09T08:59:45.251Z"],["3797750","PFI-831060","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-09T08:59:53.213Z"],["3797751","PFI-810220","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment not found. Please confirm with the partner if the payment has bounced back from their bank. If already checked, add a comment here and we’ll investigate further.","2026-01-09T09:00:00.225Z"],["3797753","PFI-831057","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-09T09:00:31.522Z"],["3797754","MKP-9749","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7374471354/2026+Q1+WIP+-+Matching+throttling|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7374471354/2026+Q1+WIP+-+Matching+throttling|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T09:00:36.618Z"],["3797757","PFI-831027","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe payment failed with an error message PAYMENT_EXPIRED (448). \nThis means the user did not complete the payment verification within 2 minutes and the payment expired. \nCould you please ask the user to try again. \n\nPlease let us know if the user is having issues with the verification. Please provide a detailed explanation of what is going wrong with the payment verification and provide screenshots if possible. \nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nPlease note that Bolt did not charge the customer. There was no authorization nor capture. \n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-09T09:01:12.567Z"],["3797761","CCM-22265","CCM","gustav.borjesson@bolt-outsource.eu","Gustav Eric Alexander Borjesson","!Screenshot 2026-01-09 090230.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T09:03:06.370Z"],["3797762","DSR-2997","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey CSPC!\n\n# Please download the following:\n\n* Communication history between you and Bolt\n* User blocks\n* User carsharing fine history\n\n\n\n# Please share the following response with the User:\n\n{quote}Dear *[User]*,\n\nThank you for your data subject request, which was received by us on *9 December 2025*. In your request you asked us to provide the following:\n\n# All information and documentation related to the accident reported on 30/04/2024.\n# All information related to the decision to permanently block your account.\n\n\n\n# Accident related information\n\nWe have reviewed your request regarding the accident reported on 30/04/2024. Based on our records, the reported damage concerned a third party vehicle. The investigation of this accident is handled by the relevant insurance providers and law enforcement authorities. Bolt does not conduct the accident investigation in this case and does not hold the accident investigation files, reports, or documentation created by insurers or third parties. As a result, we are not able to provide accident investigation documentation, as this data is not processed by Bolt.\n\n\n\nWe are sharing all relevant personal data within your search scope held by Bolt, including:\n\n* Communication history between you and Bolt\n* User blocks\n* User carsharing fine history\n\n\n\n# Bolt Drive suspension decision{quote}\n\n{quote}Your Bolt Drive account was suspended following an incident involving a Bolt vehicle. The incident was reported to us by the competent authorities after it occurred. We also note that the incident was not proactively reported to Bolt by you at the time.\n\nBased on the information available to us, this incident constituted a breach of our Terms and Conditions and involved unlawful conduct. For this reason, a contractual fee was initially applied in connection with the damage caused.\n\nFollowing a review of the circumstances, a decision was taken to permanently block access to Bolt Drive services. Permanent blocks are applied in cases where a user’s conduct creates a significant risk to Bolt, its property, or third parties. This measure is intended to protect Bolt vehicles and ensure the safety and integrity of our services.\n\nFor information on how we process relevant personal data, we refer you to our Privacy Notice at[ |https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/][https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|smart-link] , which includes further information about:\n\n* The categories of personal data we process;\n* The purposes for which we process personal data;\n* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom the personal data has been or will be disclosed;\n* The criteria we use to determine how long to retain personal data;\n* The sources of personal data received from other parties;\n* Your rights in relation to your personal data;\n* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making or profiling of personal data; and\n* Details of any transfer of your personal data to third countries or international organisations and the safeguards used for any such transfers.\n\n\n\n*Your rights*\n\nIn addition to your right to access any personal data we hold about you, you have the right to request us to rectify or erase your personal data, restrict the processing of your personal data, or object to such processing. Any such requests will be assessed in line with applicable data protection laws.\n\nIf you are dissatisfied with this response or with any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, you may contact us to seek further clarification. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection or supervisory authority and, where applicable, to seek a judicial remedy.\n\nIf you have any additional questions, please contact our Customer Support Team by replying to this email.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nBolt{quote}","2026-01-09T09:03:20.553Z"],["3797766","DSR-3363","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","From BH ticket: \n\n* From local ops perspective should be unblocked\n* Verification just repeated their usual line and the driver remained blocked \n* Local ops sent a response and solved the ticket.\n\nContacted local ops cs team lead to verify if the driver should actually remain blocked as CSPC instructions were not followed. ","2026-01-09T09:03:52.979Z"],["3797768","FX-3350","FX","jana.lutus@bolt.eu","Jana Lutus","Blocked until error handling is added to driver portal and admin-panel. ","2026-01-09T09:04:20.060Z"],["3797770","LSS-61315","LSS","jelena.glavas@bolt.eu","Jelena Glavaš","[^Ugovor o certificiranju (1).pdf] _(382 kB)_\n\n[^Zahtjev (1).pdf] _(328 kB)_","2026-01-09T09:04:24.381Z"],["3797771","LSS-61315","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nJelena Glavaš has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-09T09:04:26.533Z"],["3797772","WFM-9843","WFM","jalal.safarli@bolt.eu","Jalal Safarli","Hey [~accountid:5b31360d7b8c14625a47e4f5] , any updates?🙏 ","2026-01-09T09:04:45.019Z"],["3797774","MLC-3793","MLC","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","*Riding Score:*\n\n* If we get a user property that checks for the rider’s score, we could start with the following comms:\n** Regular awareness blocks in specific comms, e.g. for newer users: Did you know that safe rides increase your Riding Score? Your Riding Score is XX. Increasing your score can unlock different perks. Check the available benefits in the app. \n** X points missing from the next benefit \n** If score is lower than X → Top riders unlock extra perks like free reservation minutes and skipping end-of-ride pictures. Maintain a high score to earn more benefits & contribute to a safer city.\n** If score is higher than X → You’re a top rider with a XX score! + thanks for helping make the city better for people. Did you know about the perks that come with your riding skill? Check the app to see.\n*** If most users have a high score, create different versions of this so they can see different things?\n** If a new benefit was unlocked: You unlocked a new perk by riding responsibly! Check the app to see which ones you’ve unlocked so far. Your next perk is a few rides away.\n\n*NFC*:\n\nI don’t think we can support with anything else besides ad hoc comms for the launch. Prepping some ideas soon :loading: ","2026-01-09T09:05:04.126Z"],["3797775","PFI-830547","PFI","catarina.silva@bolt.eu","Catarina Caneira da Silva","Hello [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] \nthis ticket alone is for the companies not receiving the emails and it seems like a general problem in Portugal","2026-01-09T09:05:19.435Z"],["3797777","PC-4926","PC","kaupo.kask@bolt.eu","Kaupo Kask","[~accountid:60717fb3edc14f0076ca5a3e] Hi! Good questions 😉\n\n# Q: shall the routing ({{mada}} vs other schemes) be based on the user’s location defined by the App?\n## A: Yes, we are routing it depend the metadata - country. Routing happens in ProcessOUt side and depend which PSP Merchant account we are routing them, than it acts like local MADA Scheme. \n### [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4020228792|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4020228792] \n#### PS! Where we take the country info from → I don’t know 😕. I remember , there are multiple options, is it taken from the customer or driver or third party side 😕 \n#### !image-20260109-084702.png|width=459,alt=\"image-20260109-084702.png\"!\n\n# Q: when {{mada}} card is first added outside of Saudi Arabia, should be the logo shown as Visa / Mastercard?\n## A: I didn’t find any solid confirmation from the Guideline and as well from the email’s (under Source - [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/7240680175/Mada+Cards+in+Saudi+Arabia+Capabilities+Constraints+Comparison+Matrix#Source%3A]) → So, let’s keep it simple and use all the time mada logo and not adding dependence, where it is added. \n# Q: is that correct, that same card’s payments from the same user might be processed via different schemes (mada / visa / mastercard) based on the user’s location (Saudi Arabia / rest of the world)?\n## Yes, that is correct. Our Rule should be for routing: \n### {{Currency = SAR}} → {{Country = SA}} → {{Card type = MADA}} → Route it to Local CKO merchant account (Which treats MADA as Local)\n### If the same MADA card does not meet the above rules, than it works depend other country rules see’s it\n# how do we distinguish {{mada}} cards? For {{Carte Bancair}} we have bin range list, is that the case for {{mada}} as well?\n## *Yes*, we can easily download BIN list  [here|https://www.checkout.com/docs/files/Mada_BINs.csv] and the Link is also shoed out Mada page, [HERE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/edit-v2/7240680175]  ","2026-01-09T09:05:45.924Z"],["3797778","WD-21923","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:637f26822acfad92d7b13ddb] , rule applied to these entities in PRD","2026-01-09T09:06:05.557Z"],["3797781","PFI-831033","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have checked the case and I can confirm we are not seeing any double charges from Bolt’s end. \nYou have done a great job explaining the payment to the customer. \n\nUser was authorized 46.60 EUR and the final capture amount was 47.50 EUR. \nThe authorization for 46.60 EUR has been released from Bolt’s end. \n\nPlease note that some banks might have have some issues when processing an authorization adjustment and the pre-authorization release might take the 30 days. \n\nYou can provide the ARN code 534473784634 to the customer to locate the reserved payment with their bank.\n\nPlease also note there is a pending chargeback issued by the customer. \n\n\n\n!image-20260109-090730.png|width=1370,height=300!\n\n\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T09:07:33.789Z"],["3797783","CEBF-1570","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","BulkUpdateControllerTest 79%\n\nLogActivityOnRevenueControllerTest 100%","2026-01-09T09:07:48.256Z"],["3797785","UXA-2164","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","The issue is the result of increased number of fraudulent requests from VN on CA - more then 95% of them were failing app integrity check.   114K attempts made by 865 unique phones.","2026-01-09T09:08:07.886Z"],["3797790","CSP-451","CSP","quentin.legrand@bolt.eu","Quentin Émile N. Legrand","26W2: started data explorations and initial reflections on the project ([here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CD/pages/7367098425/2026-01+FRT+prediction+-+initial+thoughts] and [here|https://chatgpt.com/share/e/6960c453-59e4-800e-9b39-4098bee877b4])","2026-01-09T09:08:56.890Z"],["3797791","HS-28221","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Thank you and no worries 🙂 \n\nYou can now see the change reflected in your Workday, that means 26 days of annual leave in 2026 and onwards, plus I added 3 days retroactively for 2025, as you had already reached seniority back then (and you worked with us for 6 months in 2025). It will be reflected in your carryover balance\n\nLet me know in case of any questions and have a great weekend ahead! ","2026-01-09T09:09:01.935Z"],["3797792","FX-3586","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767949753249509]*{color}:\nthx!\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:09:26.619Z"],["3797795","WFM-9910","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","[Request|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571655]","2026-01-09T09:10:16.786Z"],["3797796","ADS-138","ADS","daria.ryazhskikh@bolt.eu","Daria Ryazhskikh","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17017|https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17017|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T09:10:16.814Z"],["3797797","SREP-1073","SREP","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","{quote}Investigate that APT-S3 safe to terminate{quote}\n\nIt’s not: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8677?focusedCommentId=2712276|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8677?focusedCommentId=2712276|smart-link].\n\nAlter Agent and Alter Supervisor are still uploaded to APT-S3 but not JFrog.","2026-01-09T09:10:22.017Z"],["3797799","LSS-61318","LSS","werner.laaneots@bolt.eu","Werner Robert Laaneots","[^Long Term Leping (2).pdf] _(265 kB)_","2026-01-09T09:11:02.985Z"],["3797800","MARTECH-6561","MARTECH","maarja.maarjakoiv@bolt.eu","Maarja Maarjakõiv","*Update:* Will have a kick off meeting with [~accountid:5d6e089134b3d20d9777ef90] how to start with this project next or upcoming week.\nStarting point is Rider team since most critical to move forward (enabling AEM through storing user_agent identifier for example).","2026-01-09T09:11:40.108Z"],["3797801","PFI-831154","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have investigated the case and would like to share some findings. \n\nThe authorized amount was 5.60 GEL but the final price was increased to 10.90 GEL. \nBolt was not able to capture the full amount and created a negative balance of 5.30 GEL. \n\nPlease note that usually in these case we try to do an Overcapture, but Adyen does not support it in Georgia. \nIf overcaptures are not allowed the Bolt tries to do an MIT (Merchant initiated transaction) payment for the updated final amount. \nIn this case the MIT was blocked by our fraud teams rules. \n\nPlease ask the user to top up their balance or cover the debt with their next order. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T09:11:43.751Z"],["3797804","PFI-831287","PFI","joseph.kamange@bolt-outsource.eu","Joseph Kamange","!{12DF3B7A-1296-4E80-B28F-27B3F0C99DAA}-20260109-091215.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T09:12:34.011Z"],["3797807","HS-28780","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Sick leave from 12.01, no sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-09T09:12:48.207Z"],["3797808","CSP-440","CSP","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","26W02:\n\n(/) Landing page\n\n(/) Support case list + support case\n\n(/) Icons ","2026-01-09T09:13:02.853Z"],["3797810","L10N-26845","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26844](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26844)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T09:13:16.849Z"],["3797811","L10N-26846","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26844](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26844)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T09:13:17.775Z"],["3797812","L10N-26852","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queri