licate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26844](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26844)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T09:13:31.003Z"],["3797824","PFI-830547","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Based on the Internal tool, I believe emails have been sent:\n\n* [mpacifico@tap.pt|mailto:mpacifico@tap.pt]: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/sent/7416000005|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/sent/7416000005]\n* [ines_lnraposo@cm-loures.pt|mailto:ines_lnraposo@cm-loures.pt]: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/sent/7416176002|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/sent/7416176002]\n* [scabecinha@tap.pt|mailto:scabecinha@tap.pt]: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/sent/7415918277|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/sent/7415918277]\n\nMaybe Comms team (*dev-comms-support*) can help validating why Clients don’t see emails?; They are also the owner of the view above.","2026-01-09T09:14:16.877Z"],["3797825","MARTECH-6558","MARTECH","maarja.maarjakoiv@bolt.eu","Maarja Maarjakõiv","*Update:* \nWe are in the phase to add SIngular destination to event service so we could start sending in-app events to Singular from our backend (relevant task attached)","2026-01-09T09:14:22.360Z"],["3797826","LSS-57822","LSS","lisette.suik@bolt.eu","Lisette Suik","hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ! Sorry for the delay, getting up to speed after the Christmas break 🙂 \n\nThis is not something I’ve seen being used in other markets. However, I totally agree with you and I do not see any risk (especially from the reclassification side) of prompting the selfie check if any courier data (e.g. email or phone number) or if we suspect fraud. \n\nI will pick this up with the privacy team to check if we need to update any privacy document, but from first glance, it seems our [privacy notice|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-couriers/?category=delivery] is already drafted quite vaguely and I think we can proceed without any immediate changes: “_To authenticate your account and verify your identity  - We collect information to verify who you say you are either upon registration_ *_or as a result of unusual activity being detected on your Bolt account_*_. “_ \n\nI understand that the team would like to use this selfie check feature only in cases where they suspect fraud with the email/phone number changes? And not each time contact details are changed? In that case, I don’t think any changes are needed to our terms / privacy policy as this is already covered under the policy. \n\n\nAlso, do you need me to check with the engineers whether re-prompting the selfie check for fraud prevention is already possible from the technical side, or has the PT team already confirmed they can manually prompt it? Thanks!","2026-01-09T09:14:45.705Z"],["3797827","LSS-60533","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nCould you please advise whether I should add Legal Ops to get this signed?\n\nThanks!\n\n","2026-01-09T09:14:54.349Z"],["3797828","LSS-61304","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed documents attached.\n\n[^Audit confirmation letter_Bolt Services UK Limited_Papaya Global Ltd_08.01.26.pdf]\n[^Audit confirmation letter_Bolt Services UK Limited_Goldman Sachs_08.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T09:15:15.110Z"],["3797831","WD-22507","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:605ee2ff2f7d900070c2e481] please let us know which type of location it is?\n\n!image-20260109-091547.png|width=801,alt=\"image-20260109-091547.png\"!","2026-01-09T09:15:53.777Z"],["3797833","PFI-831288","PFI","punyawee.kangwanwongs@bolt-outsource.eu","Punyawee Kangwanwongs","[^Manual payouts requested, January 2026, Week 2.csv]","2026-01-09T09:16:10.160Z"],["3797834","LSS-61318","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-09T09:16:25.989Z"],["3797835","LSS-61316","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-09T09:16:26.115Z"],["3797836","LSS-61255","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","Hi there, please see attached first draft of lease agreement. I am also reviewing myself today. \n\n[^Anlage 1.1bis25.9 zum draft_Bolt.pdf]\n[^21024_251219_Lease agreement_draft_Bolt.docx]\n\n","2026-01-09T09:16:51.616Z"],["3797837","LSS-61319","LSS","andrea.rietmeijer@bolt.eu","Andrea Rietmeijer","[^Branding Contract - Bolt Club - Ka-Ra GmbH.pdf] _(139 kB)_","2026-01-09T09:16:52.039Z"],["3797838","PFI-830688","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThank you for escalating! \nThe error message 998: Provider call to add instrument failed is a generic error message and means the PSP rejected the attempt or the attempt failed internally. \n\nCould you please ask the user to try again in case the card adding failed due to temporary technical issues? \nAre they getting similar errors with different payment methods? \n\nPlease let me know if the user would receive the same error again and the customer payments team would investigate further with the engineers. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T09:17:18.165Z"],["3797839","LSS-55393","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the remaining documents attached!\n\n[^PoA_Bolt Support Services (Thailand) Limited_Andrzej Lipson_09.01.26.pdf]\n[^PoA_Senago z. o.o._Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf]\n[^PoA_Bolt Services AZ LLC_Andrzej Lipson_08.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T09:17:19.605Z"],["3797842","LSS-60533","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] please support with signing of the document below ","2026-01-09T09:17:43.486Z"],["3797847","LSS-60455","LSS","jens.ohgren@bolt.eu","Jens Öhgren","[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] appreciate that, and thank you for the update. If we can get it done next week that be great, sooner the better. ","2026-01-09T09:18:38.413Z"],["3797848","PFI-830684","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nConfirmed with Pawapay the payment has been refunded to the user. \n\nPlease find the proof of refund attached. \n\n[^payout_UA8H73AYYG.pdf]\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T09:19:10.445Z"],["3797849","PFI-831051","PFI","alexander.skea@bolt.eu","Alexander Skea","||*ID*||*Created*||*Amount*||*Comment*|| ||\n|1509|9 Jan 2026, 11:18:44 (UTC+02:00)|170.85 ZAR|Tanzania Ride| |\n\nApology Credit issued to ZA Account","2026-01-09T09:19:25.918Z"],["3797850","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767950367440149]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-334] `Check document access issues for users` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:19:39.928Z"],["3797851","HS-28774","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Hi Felix,\n\nThanks for reaching out!\nI sent the letter to your personal email.\nHave a great weekend!\n\nKind regards,\nAike-Maris","2026-01-09T09:20:05.238Z"],["3797852","LSS-60142","LSS","karolis.simkus@bolt.eu","Karolis Šimkus","Hello!\n\n[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] they came back with a standart form of “Priėmimo-perdavimo” aktas. Would that work from our side?\n\n\n\n[^Bolt.docx]\n\n","2026-01-09T09:20:20.037Z"],["3797854","PFI-816513","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Thanks for your patience here. \n \nPlease find all payment confirmations for the payouts mentioned attached. Airwallex team confirmed that they have not received rejections from the beneficiary bank for any of them or been made aware of any issues by their banking partner.\n \nFeel free to pass this to the client to investigate further with their bank. \n\n!P251201-3CBKID7.png|width=862,alt=\"P251201-3CBKID7.png\"!\n\n!P251124-DBJHWFV.png|width=862,alt=\"P251124-DBJHWFV.png\"!\n\n!P251215-LLGAMOT.png|width=862,alt=\"P251215-LLGAMOT.png\"!\n\n!P251208-7QVIR37.png|width=862,alt=\"P251208-7QVIR37.png\"!\n\n!P251020-PRLV486.png|width=862,alt=\"P251020-PRLV486.png\"!\n\n!P251117-IQHWTWK.png|width=862,alt=\"P251117-IQHWTWK.png\"!","2026-01-09T09:20:47.641Z"],["3797855","LSS-60142","LSS","karolis.simkus@bolt.eu","Karolis Šimkus","They as well asked to fill in underlined parts. I should add Benas information there, right?","2026-01-09T09:21:08.370Z"],["3797858","PFI-830514","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, this is fixed now; Please, download the invoice from the Admin","2026-01-09T09:21:53.720Z"],["3797860","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767950505849369]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-334 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:21:58.011Z"],["3797863","SUPX-2310","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","*Krzysztof Szlachetka* [Jan 6, 2026 2:00 PM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08T3PV9BDX/p1767700830742249?thread_ts=1767700830.742249&cid=C08T3PV9BDX] in Slack channel [#feature-self-serve-refunds-overcharge|https://slack.com/app_redirect?channel=C08T3PV9BDX]\n\n{quote}*Delivery order payments*\n{quote}\n\nHi *@user-U04C2RMG78V*!\n\nI have created a [test delivery order |https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/168637841?cityId=1]in prelive using [create orders github action|https://github.com/bolteu/e2e-test-client/actions/runs/20744092279].\nUnfortunately, the payments API does not return any results for this order, although there seems to be a [payment|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22userType%22%3A%22user%22%2C%22from%22%3A1751760000.032%2C%22to%22%3A1767743999.032%2C%22userId%22%3A296693386%7D%7D] for this [user|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/users/299573801?tab=details] that is associated with this order.\n\nCould you please check why do we not get anything there?\n\n(please keep in mind that test delivery orders in prelive are erased on a daily basis)\n\nThanks!","2026-01-09T09:22:15.514Z"],["3797865","PFI-829558","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-09T09:22:59.734Z"],["3797868","PFI-830682","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nInteresting case. \n\nI can confirm there haven’t been any refunds issued to the customer. \n\nOrder was placed 20/12/2025, 18:37:01UTC\nPlease note the payment capture was delayed (22/12/2025, 14:23:50UTC) due to technical issues. \nIf you would have issued a refund before the capture happened then it would fail as we are not able to refund more than we have captured. \n\nCould you please try to issue the refund again? \nIf you are having issues with the refund then please let me know and the customer payments team could check if we are able to issue the refund straight from the Fondy portal. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T09:23:32.522Z"],["3797870","LSS-60426","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:712020:5974a8c8-1b42-487b-ac1c-cd7b831937d4] Do we have any updates here or can the ticket be closed?","2026-01-09T09:24:00.489Z"],["3797873","LSS-55043","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Waiting for document to be set up for signing by the partner.","2026-01-09T09:24:42.274Z"],["3797877","WFM-9910","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello [~accountid:712020:d411dadd-7821-4241-975e-2860825cf533],\n\nAccess granted. Have a nice day!","2026-01-09T09:25:05.112Z"],["3797879","PFI-830658","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customers refund failed. The customer payments team has checked with our payment service provider monobank and have been advised the following. \nThe refund for this invoice was unsuccessful and returned with error code 50, which means \"card spending is restricted.\", this issue originates from the issuing bank of the card. This is a SENSE BANK issue. \n\nPlease ask the user to check with their bank about spending restrictions on their account. Alternatively, you can issue a refund to the customer Bolt Balance instead.\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T09:25:50.665Z"],["3797882","WD-20427","WD","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Hi! updated the payment elections options to Euro for all Bulgarian employees.\n\nthanks\n\nOana","2026-01-09T09:26:06.596Z"],["3797885","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767950793518269]*{color}:\n<@U0A0XSSC68N>, this is possibly related to your task. The underlying error is INVALID_METADATA_CONFIG since 10:20 EEST today.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:26:45.751Z"],["3797886","MKP-9548","MKP","uchechukwu.emmanuel@bolt.eu","Uchechukwu Shadrack Emmanuel","Hi Haris,\n\nJust discussed this ticket with team and the current behavior is the agreed requirement, so this will be rejected. cc: [@buin.dylgyrzhapov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/60c491bfa174630070be2870]","2026-01-09T09:26:53.978Z"],["3797887","PFI-831292","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-09T09:26:57.997Z"],["3797888","LSS-61319","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340268|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340268|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T09:27:17.553Z"],["3797890","DMB-1690","DMB","raj.parekh@bolt.eu","Raj Parekh","Disabled tests team report (as of 2026/01/07)","2026-01-09T09:27:38.762Z"],["3797891","DMB-1690","DMB",null,"Slack","[Raj Parekh|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:4f942aed-943f-4064-8f79-c74a8d53be2e] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1767745400790479?thread_ts=1767745400.790479&cid=C08QTPU0GQY|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1767745400790479?thread_ts=1767745400.790479&cid=C08QTPU0GQY|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-09T09:27:40.077Z"],["3797892","DMB-1690","DMB","nikita.koshcheev@bolt.eu","Nikita Koshcheev","Hey [@raj.parekh|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:4f942aed-943f-4064-8f79-c74a8d53be2e]\nCould you please check [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159698/|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159698/] when you have time?\nIt's related to BGN currency change\nDo we still need this test?","2026-01-09T09:27:40.313Z"],["3797893","DMB-1690","DMB","raj.parekh@bolt.eu","Raj Parekh","We can delete it, its probably failing because its new year already","2026-01-09T09:27:41.304Z"],["3797896","HS-28188","HS","leonora.lukoviczki@bolt.eu","Leonóra Lukoviczki","Good morning Peter, \n\nwe send out Arbeitszeugnis earliest on your last official working day. If needed, in the meantime we can create a Zwischenzeugnis for you.\n\n\n\nBest regards, ","2026-01-09T09:28:00.724Z"],["3797912","WFM-9843","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! Permissions were approved, keep in mind they will expire 07/04/2026 00:00; Wish you a great day! ","2026-01-09T09:28:15.786Z"],["3797913","MKP-9695","MKP","buin.dylgyrzhapov@bolt.eu","Buin-Dylgyrzhap Dylgyrzhapov","Limit of the number of stops is on RiderX and Geo teams","2026-01-09T09:28:19.674Z"],["3797914","LSS-61275","LSS","girts.tretjakovs@bolt.eu","Ģirts Tretjakovs","Hi Beatričė,\n\nThe links for those two accesses were only active for 30 days which is why they are not opening now. We did ask the authorities to send over statement again, but they told us we need to contact the user directly to get it…\n\nThe State Consumer Rights Protection Authority officially extended the deadline to *14.01.26*\n\nContext on why this dropped off the radar: I mistakenly closed the ticket earlier. 😞  Back in October - I asked the Ops team to call the authorities and ask which cases were still open, and this one was reported as closed. \n\n\n\n","2026-01-09T09:28:26.755Z"],["3797915","FX-3586","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767950897837009]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3586 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:28:28.769Z"],["3797916","LSS-61277","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","Hey, will I get these before weekend?","2026-01-09T09:28:44.198Z"],["3797917","PFI-831009","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, I believe I don’t understand the question. \n\nSo, there was a charge for the amount of 4060 huf, right? (would be great if you could provide a link to it/date when it happened). \n\nBefore that, there was a trip attached for the same amount?","2026-01-09T09:28:46.545Z"],["3797918","HS-28298","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Letter went for signing. ","2026-01-09T09:28:59.326Z"],["3797919","HS-28188","HS","peter.moulding@bolt.eu","Peter Evan Moulding","No, no problem. Happy to receive it on my last working day. Thanks 🙂 ","2026-01-09T09:29:05.857Z"],["3797924","LSS-46740","LSS","subarna.sharna@bolt.eu","Subarna Islam Sharna","Hi [~accountid:712020:523b0039-eb47-4ccc-aca3-88d82c0c880a] ,\n\nPlease share the latest progress on this request 🙏 \n\n*Warm Regards,*\nSubarna","2026-01-09T09:29:22.403Z"],["3797926","PFI-830646","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have checked the users balances and they don’t have a negative balance anymore. \nThere could have been a temporary negative balance Ft 6,050.00 from this payment. \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4009535158|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4009535158]\n\nThe payment has now been successfully cancelled. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T09:29:26.270Z"],["3797927","LSS-59694","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","+New response from the association received 09.01+ : \n\n[^Fwd Mise en demeure avant saisine du tribunal de commerce de Nice.pdf] \n\n--> Waiting for attachment from email","2026-01-09T09:29:33.318Z"],["3797928","PFI-830555","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:5fa511639e35e50068b366f0],\n\nThe business is fraudulent without a shadow of a doubt, I can already see that the business profile was blocked after they managed to go into roughly -12.5K€ Debt. Seems to be a similar case to the one brought out previously.\n\nRegarding the users that you have specifically requested, then I can confirm that both of the users are fraudulent. The biggest giveaway is the amount of different US cards that they have added and failed a verification with, this is a common tactic among CC fraud. Additionally, it is visible that they have CCs from different countries.\n\nAs both of the users were included in the business fraud, then I have fraud-blocked both of the users to restrict their actions on our platform.\n\nIf you have any other questions, then please do let me know.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-09T09:29:40.341Z"],["3797931","PFI-830961","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-09T09:30:23.096Z"],["3797935","PFI-830939","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-09T09:30:40.058Z"],["3797936","EBIKE1-398","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","[~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e]  thanks, we will take a look","2026-01-09T09:30:48.410Z"],["3797937","PFI-830634","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 419.00 ZAR on 13/12/2025, 17:03:26UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 12th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-09T09:31:00.352Z"],["3797938","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767951057194459]*{color}:\n[https://kibana-logs.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/r/s/Tew8N]\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:31:11.061Z"],["3797939","DRX-26216","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Please test registration webpage logic + forgot password web page.","2026-01-09T09:31:14.320Z"],["3797941","LSS-46740","LSS","rustem.aidarkhanov@bolt.eu","Rustem Aidarkhanov","Hi! [~accountid:638476d83e79f12e572272f3] \n\nI delivered the documents to KPMG yesterday and notified Botagoz Bassanova.","2026-01-09T09:31:24.918Z"],["3797942","WEBSD-1458","WEBSD","wisutta.maensittirote@bolt.eu","Wisutta Maensittirote","I’ve submitted the request to Content, thanks for getting back.","2026-01-09T09:31:51.174Z"],["3797943","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Polina Eller [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767951108825149]*{color}:\nIt is. looks like there are legacy values in DB stored without correct validation. I'm going to rollback the package\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:32:06.815Z"],["3797944","LSS-59694","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] please could you review the content of this ticket? A mise en demeure was raised in a ticket by Coline, who also shared the reasons for blocking the driver’s account. Our letter of response confirmed the maintenance of the block because no elements indicated that we were not in conformity or that an error was made.\n\nThe association is pushing back hard, and the driver is willing to sign an affidavit that he did share his account. Please could you review the facts of the case again and confirm whether the reasons are legit and that we followed the proper procedure to block this driver?\n\nDriver name: Ameur Ben sik ali\nPartner ID: 11256819\n\nThank you ! 🙏 ","2026-01-09T09:32:34.074Z"],["3797945","LSS-46740","LSS","subarna.sharna@bolt.eu","Subarna Islam Sharna","Thanks Rustem for your proaction. Would you have any scanned version of the document?\n\nSubarna.","2026-01-09T09:32:38.216Z"],["3797946","HS-28779","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","With global mobility.","2026-01-09T09:32:57.865Z"],["3797951","LSS-53784","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:63985ce2f7f0ee492fcea284] May I please ask what’s the update with this project? ","2026-01-09T09:33:19.553Z"],["3797952","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767951181893429]*{color}:\nThis is the change that was release yesterday? I do nit see open deployments for fleet documents.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:33:23.030Z"],["3797953","PFI-830882","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Invoices are issued for the services provided, and not for the payments. A payments is done for the oustanding amount, and could aggregate few Balance Entries.\n\nPlease, consult the Balance Entries tab with the Payment Data and consider which Claims consist a Payment","2026-01-09T09:33:23.732Z"],["3797959","PFI-829380","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Closing this ticket, as the issue has been solved and all invoices issued properly now.","2026-01-09T09:34:04.093Z"],["3797960","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767951217867799]*{color}:\nPlease be aware that Joel deployed changes after you, so just deploying older package is likely not safe.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:34:05.467Z"],["3797961","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767951236531949]*{color}:\nDo you want to jump on a call and discuss the plan?\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:34:08.392Z"],["3797962","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Polina Eller [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767951238413009]*{color}:\nYes, It is finished. So only fix then\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:34:11.233Z"],["3797963","PFI-829444","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Closing this ticket, as the issue has been solved and all invoices issued properly now.","2026-01-09T09:34:12.824Z"],["3797964","PRF-1765","PRF","beste.dulger@bolt.eu","Beste Dülger","[~accountid:5d639884388d780dac23dfe7] Okito, thanks! ","2026-01-09T09:34:13.060Z"],["3797967","PFI-818583","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-09T09:34:52.859Z"],["3797971","PFI-830957","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-09T09:35:50.374Z"],["3797973","LSS-59769","LSS","indrek.eelmets@bolt.eu","Indrek Eelmets","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] As a general rule, Bolt does not grant any publicity rights (including referring to Bolt as a customer or cooperation partner, or using the Bolt trade mark), unless we receive something significant in return, such as a meaningful dedicated discount or other strong business reasons. Regular cooperation alone is usually not a strong enough business reason.\n\nApologies for missing this ticket and for the delayed reply.","2026-01-09T09:36:09.507Z"],["3797974","PFI-830963","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-09T09:36:30.470Z"],["3797979","PFI-831258","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:893a1737-0464-48d8-a7fb-6f2f19b5479d],\n\nBesides this [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2325851305/332?orderTryId=2985164918], then everything seems rather normal, did not detect any oddities.\nIt seems to have been a mix of irregular happenings at the same time.\nIn this case, the driver has a campaign added on themselves and most of their passengers were also either first timers or had some sort of campaign applied, all of this caused a conflict.\n\nWhile this is suspicious from our perspective, then this is not something that means 100% guaranteed fraud. We will be unblocking the driver for now, however, if this happens again we may be required to remove cash payment option from the driver - this is not a common occurrence after all.\n\nThe driver is unblocked.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-09T09:37:16.017Z"],["3797982","PFI-830758","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","What is the charge (which amount, date, etc?), what is the problem with the charge. Please, provide exact links and clearly what is the issue the customer experiences","2026-01-09T09:37:39.584Z"],["3797983","LSS-61135","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hi [~accountid:712020:5127ca3d-3864-43c1-abe3-509900e83a2f] thanks for raising the ticket to us!\n\n\n\nI have reviewed the comms history and account history. This appears as OTP sharing (when User shares their OTP code with a scammer). To log in to Bolt app, you receive this OTP code to an SMS. If this is shared, anyone can access your account. \n\n\n\nOTP sharing because:\n\n:green-check: In BH conversation user mentions someone called them asking to confirm a code\n\n:green-check: Payment was attempted from User’s account\n\n\n\nPlease communicate the following to the User:\n\n\n\n{quote}Dear *[User]*,\n\n\n\nThank you for your patience while our teams carefully investigated your issue. The new device logged in to your account via: \n\n* Entering a valid one-time password (OTP) sent via SMS to the phone number linked to your Bolt account.\n\n\n\nWe have taken the necessary steps to secure your account and mitigate the issue. Our Customer Support representative logged all devices out of your Bolt account, allowing only your current device to log back in.\n\n\n\nTo increase your Bolt account security, ensure that:\n\n\n\n* Your phone number linked to the account is up to date;\n* Your email address linked to the account is verified; and\n* You enable multi-factor authentication by clicking to _“My account > Log in and security > Turn on Two-Step Verification”_;\n* You never share your passkey, or OTP code sent via SMS with anyone.\n\n\n\nIf you notice any suspicious activity in your account, or receive an email about new device log in, contact our Customer Support Team immediately.{quote}\n\n\n\nIf User wants to delete their account, please proceed as with standard deletion requests.","2026-01-09T09:37:39.890Z"],["3797984","LSS-59324","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:712020:e9966afc-8926-48fe-bacc-f9daa6118aad] May I please ask for an update here? 🙂 ","2026-01-09T09:37:48.348Z"],["3797989","LSS-61318","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hey [~accountid:712020:28f7389c-dc34-43f9-b4fc-4a3718af00ff] , thank you. Please share this agreement in Word format instead of PDF, so I can amend it. ","2026-01-09T09:38:38.783Z"],["3797990","WFM-9909","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541644|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541644]","2026-01-09T09:38:45.276Z"],["3797992","WFM-9909","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! Roles were requested, waiting for approval, will let you know once ready","2026-01-09T09:39:11.057Z"],["3797993","PFI-831301","PFI","ornyanee.juntarat@bolt-outsource.eu","Ornyanee Juntarat","!image-20260109-093657.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260109-093716.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T09:39:17.043Z"],["3797994","CSP-79","CSP","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","26W02: Work on enabling the flow for delivery and rentals still in progress (ran into some issues, details [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08T3PV9BDX/p1767712970745389]). Second A/B test for ridehailing finished today; analysis and feature enablement in new UX markets planned for early next week.","2026-01-09T09:39:29.033Z"],["3797996","PFI-829476","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued invoice","2026-01-09T09:40:08.937Z"],["3797997","PFI-829471","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Closing this as the issue has been solved for all BAs. All invoices should be avaiable.","2026-01-09T09:40:49.111Z"],["3797999","DBRE-8678","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Heavy load is gone.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 09.40.39.png|width=1152,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 09.40.39.png\"!","2026-01-09T09:41:13.645Z"],["3798000","WD-20427","WD","anett.suurkask@bolt.eu","Anett Suurkask","Hi! [~accountid:712020:80f31809-0e9d-4c0f-8939-db5dd3d77922] but we currently have 4 expense reports with in progress status, payment value is still showed in BGN although employees inserted in EUR. How we should proccess those? :pleading_face: example: [EX-BG002-26-000004|https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/1$1356/1356$102030.htmld]\n\n","2026-01-09T09:41:53.167Z"],["3798001","PFI-831302","PFI","victoria.ebube@bolt-outsource.eu","Victoria Ebube","!{EC66B2BB-E1EC-4E6B-AEDE-5FD318447F53}-20260109-094120.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T09:41:54.049Z"],["3798002","CCM-22265","CCM","miroslava.solarova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Solárová","Hello Gustav,\n\nI have enrolled Markku in the Ride-Hailing Onboarding course. \n\nHave a lovely rest of your day! \n\nMirka 🙂 ","2026-01-09T09:42:30.305Z"],["3798004","SCM-1108","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","Slack thread link: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/G01PR2HTD2B/p1767689411807459|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/G01PR2HTD2B/p1767689411807459|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T09:43:34.118Z"],["3798005","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767951803715529]*{color}:\n<@UCVT712UR>, it is an issue in the document service. Polina is working on a fix right now.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:43:35.983Z"],["3798006","PFI-831303","PFI","patryk.flakowski@bolt.eu","Patryk Flakowski","[^BoltEuPolandServicesPayroll_30-11-2025_Payslip_PatrykFlakowski(E011998).pdf]\n\n[^BoltEuPolandServicesPayroll_31-12-2025_Payslip_PatrykFlakowski(E011998).pdf]","2026-01-09T09:43:40.048Z"],["3798007","PFI-831303","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-09T09:43:42.301Z"],["3798009","LSS-61318","LSS","werner.laaneots@bolt.eu","Werner Robert Laaneots","[^Long Term Leping (2).docx]\n\nCorrect format added","2026-01-09T09:43:45.419Z"],["3798010","PFI-830633","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI could not see any records of refunds being issued to the customer for the payment created on 11th September 2020. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/289729302|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/289729302]\n\nThe payment is too old to see any details from the Adyen portal and the payment logs have expired. \n\nI would advise to find an alternative way to compensate the customer. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T09:43:47.804Z"],["3798011","PFI-820550","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Invoice reissued","2026-01-09T09:43:51.408Z"],["3798013","PFI-831304","PFI","ornyanee.juntarat@bolt-outsource.eu","Ornyanee Juntarat","!image-20260109-094238.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260109-094252.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T09:44:02.597Z"],["3798016","PFI-831162","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:2326a9a7-ea2c-4b51-9a9a-d8952ceeabe5],\n\nMay I kindly ask you to double check the user that has been linked?\nCurrently I do not see any kind of blocks on the user profile.\nFrom the logs I do not even see any attempts for orders. Could you perhaps provide me with a link where the block is visible?\nAdditionally, checked the user relations, and what is visible, is that there is one user and 3 different devices.\nI am afraid this might belong to the Verification team instead of the Fraud team, however, currently I do not have any information.\n\nIf possible, please provide me with the links where the information you have mentioned is visible. Thanks!\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you,\nMarten","2026-01-09T09:44:09.362Z"],["3798017","PFI-819081","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","If it’s visible under the Payments section, what is the problem then?","2026-01-09T09:44:42.789Z"],["3798018","LSS-61315","LSS","ivan.halapa@bolt.eu","Ivan Halapa","Hey team,\n\nSending a request for the FINA certificate filled and signed from my side. We need (wet-ink) signature from Ahto Kink.\n\nAlso attached scan of my legal document (ID)\n\n\n\n[^ih osobna.pdf]\n[^FINA Certificate.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T09:44:50.157Z"],["3798019","LSS-60403","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Good day Philippine,\n\n\n\nI will proceed and send them the payments made bybolt\n\n\n\nThank you\n\nDolinda","2026-01-09T09:45:20.636Z"],["3798022","LSS-61303","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey [~accountid:61addb80b0b630006a695081] - Indeed we can sign the already signed version in SpotDraft.","2026-01-09T09:45:51.345Z"],["3798024","MKP-9753","MKP","uchechukwu.emmanuel@bolt.eu","Uchechukwu Shadrack Emmanuel","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7361561225/Pricing+Core+-+Price+Confirmation+Auto-Acceptance|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7361561225/Pricing+Core+-+Price+Confirmation+Auto-Acceptance|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T09:46:10.901Z"],["3798025","CNT-377","CNT","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","[~accountid:61cac1b0326554006c9b5945] {{2026-01-15}} doable? We (Vertical Marketing) can review with Product and share feedback then 👯‍♀️ ","2026-01-09T09:46:27.503Z"],["3798026","LSS-55517","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] following up on this ticket. ","2026-01-09T09:47:07.110Z"],["3798027","PFI-831311","PFI","kipyegon.hezekiah@bolt-outsource.eu","Kipyegon Hezekiah","!Screenshot 2026-01-09 12.46.03 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T09:47:39.784Z"],["3798028","PFI-814662","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","reissued","2026-01-09T09:48:00.089Z"],["3798029","LSS-60865","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","Hi [~accountid:6017bc19dc29b4006a7f1025] Do we have an update here? ","2026-01-09T09:48:04.257Z"],["3798030","PFI-831312","PFI","ornyanee.juntarat@bolt-outsource.eu","Ornyanee Juntarat","!image-20260109-094602.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260109-094621.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T09:48:11.051Z"],["3798031","PFI-831313","PFI","yaroslav.kovalchuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Yaroslav Kovalchuk","!9838141b-8b32-4eb6-8b14-dfe909e3ddc8.jfif|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T09:48:12.449Z"],["3798032","LSS-61203","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Hi [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] \n\nI will assign this ticket for myself since stakeholder in reality wants the same overview for other markets as well. \n\nLatvia and UA will be on focus for initial feedback, hence I will still need to ask your support on this on validating the overview for Latvia. I will conduct the first search myself and then ask you to review and approve to save your time. \n\nETA for me is end of January. So if any way possible please find time to review the summary when I share it with you. 🙏 \n\nLiisa","2026-01-09T09:48:24.904Z"],["3798033","LSS-61321","LSS","bianca.alvesdeandrade@bolt.eu","Bianca Alves de Andrade","[^Branding Contract - Bolt Club German Driver GmbH Jan2026 (1).pdf] _(154 kB)_","2026-01-09T09:48:32.843Z"],["3798034","PFI-830473","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Gotcha! Also, we found the issue: the cs-ZZ field on the provider profile must be maximum 255 characters, so right now it’s exceeding the limits and creating issues with reissuing. Can you please help change this so I can reissue? Thanks! \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 11.47.21.png|width=240,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 11.47.21.png\"!","2026-01-09T09:48:50.228Z"],["3798035","LSS-61261","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed document attached from our side.\n\n[^Binding order_Bolt Services SK s.r.o._Letisko M.R. Štefánika – Airport Bratislava, a.s. (BTS)  _08.01.26 .pdf]\n\nOnce getting this countersigned please send it to [contracts@bolt.eu|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] with a ticket number for archiving purposes and attach the document here for our own records.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T09:48:50.923Z"],["3798036","PFI-830758","PFI","paulina.grigaliunaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Paulina Grigaliūnaitė","Hello, I have checked the information, and it appears that this is a service fee. ","2026-01-09T09:48:52.045Z"],["3798037","PRTEAM-263","PRTEAM","daniel.howell@bolt.eu","Daniel Howell","Hi [~accountid:712020:f172cd28-e81b-4011-8942-5ec6b2912f37] can you send me links to the docs etc on slack please?","2026-01-09T09:48:56.552Z"],["3798038","LSS-60119","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] following up on this - kindly provide us with an update","2026-01-09T09:49:00.855Z"],["3798039","PFI-831303","PFI","patryk.flakowski@bolt.eu","Patryk Flakowski","wrong files","2026-01-09T09:49:20.697Z"],["3798040","PFI-831303","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T09:49:24.142Z"],["3798041","PFI-830803","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Invoices are issued for the services provided, not for the payments. Please, consult invoices in the Invoices section of the Business Admin.","2026-01-09T09:49:25.391Z"],["3798042","LSS-61203","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Meeting with a stakeholder on 09.01.2026: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/10p_tcH_q8hq_bGvr_f-0cnOmb2x08yXfAw8lNqUlzsE/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/10p_tcH_q8hq_bGvr_f-0cnOmb2x08yXfAw8lNqUlzsE/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T09:49:35.528Z"],["3798043","INS-908","INS","pawel.kupidura@bolt.eu","Paweł Kupidura",":yellowpng: *Missing dbt runtime data*\nFix applied on Wednesday on 4 projects helped and the data is flowing. We need to add this entry to each {{dbt_project.yml}}, as described in the ticket. I won’t be able to complete it today, so I’ll need someone to take it over. [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/INS-908|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/INS-908|smart-link]\n\nI have a backfill in progress, if I don’t manage to do a full backfill I’ll hand over the backfill script (it’s mostly in Databricks).","2026-01-09T09:49:36.008Z"],["3798044","INS-908","INS",null,"Slack","[Paweł Kupidura|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5caaf6edc39f203c28213595] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03R7EKKNJV/p1767947753200069?thread_ts=1767947753.200069&cid=C03R7EKKNJV|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03R7EKKNJV/p1767947753200069?thread_ts=1767947753.200069&cid=C03R7EKKNJV|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-09T09:49:37.300Z"],["3798045","INS-908","INS","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","I can take over, please send me all the details.","2026-01-09T09:49:39.533Z"],["3798046","INS-908","INS","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","although, I am off on monday due to my flight. i can take a look on tuesday.","2026-01-09T09:49:40.120Z"],["3798047","INS-908","INS","pawel.kupidura@bolt.eu","Paweł Kupidura","It’s been out for weeks so the weekend won’t make a difference. I’ll add info to this bug and the task about backfill.\n\nMost important is to get the data flowing again. If backfill takes some more time, it’s not the end of the world.","2026-01-09T09:49:40.847Z"],["3798050","PFI-830758","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Thank you, is there still some concerns from a Billing side or we can close a ticket","2026-01-09T09:50:04.944Z"],["3798051","INS-908","INS","pawel.kupidura@bolt.eu","Paweł Kupidura","Haven’t seen this feature before :wow: Sync of comments from thread with an arbitrary Jira task mentioned in the main message.","2026-01-09T09:50:11.237Z"],["3798052","LSS-61278","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached. Unfortunately had to add checkmarks in the system again therefore they look like that. Hopefully that’s okay.\n\n[^Declaration of eligibility for benefits - CA_Bolt Holdings OÜ_Canada Revenue Agency_08.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T09:50:16.627Z"],["3798054","LSS-61135","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","[https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyoü/personaldatabreachriskassessment/1-all-entries/281|https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyo%C3%BC/personaldatabreachriskassessment/1-all-entries/281]\n\n\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0678KJ49UH/p1767952919500609|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0678KJ49UH/p1767952919500609|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T09:50:22.335Z"],["3798057","LSS-60694","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached. Hopefully the signatures made it to correct places. \n\n[^Conference sponsorship contract - Velo-city conference 2026_Bolt Operations OÜ_AIM Italy srl_18.12.25.pdf]\n\nOnce getting this countersigned please send it to [contracts@bolt.eu|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] with a ticket number for archiving purposes and attach the document here for our own records.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T09:51:58.486Z"],["3798058","PFI-831256","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, it was a charge for the Ride. The company is under the Resale Billing Model, the invoice will be issued at the end of the month for all Rides during a period.","2026-01-09T09:52:05.357Z"],["3798059","PFI-819081","PFI","filip.kieronczyk@bolt-outsource.eu","Filip Kieronczyk","hi, they are not proceeded in the system and company’s account is blocked","2026-01-09T09:52:11.642Z"],["3798060","LSS-61203","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hello [~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2] , agreed, thank you very much! 💚 ","2026-01-09T09:52:13.066Z"],["3798061","LSS-61209","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Collective insurance agreement - Allianz_Bolt Operations OÜ_AWP Health & Life AS_01.01.26 (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T09:52:53.848Z"],["3798062","SREP-1076","SREP","lauri.linros@bolt.eu","Lauri Linros","when trying to connect from netbird.","2026-01-09T09:53:02.608Z"],["3798066","LSS-60694","LSS","irene.cobian@bolt.eu","Irene Cobian Martin","I’ll share it with the provider now. Thank you!!!","2026-01-09T09:53:38.123Z"],["3798067","LSS-61239","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Engagement Letter_Bolt Services US Inc._Crowe LLP_25.11.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T09:53:40.428Z"],["3798068","LSS-60403","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","HI [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b] apologies I think that there has been a misalignement. \n\nI was asking you about the question you were not sure about. \n\nIf they are resquesting from proof of payment, I would say that this may be disproportionate. Please could you confirm what payment information they are asking for?\n\ncc. [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] ","2026-01-09T09:53:40.965Z"],["3798069","PFI-831280","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Which invoices are they receiving? Do they have an example? We haven’t issued commission invoices to them since mid-october\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 11.53.36.png|width=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 11.53.36.png\"!","2026-01-09T09:53:46.279Z"],["3798071","PFI-831052","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, first time hearing about this 🙂. If this is related to the Bank Accounts, then, please, consult with the Partner Payments Team.\n\nIf this is related to some document confirming the Legal/Tax entity of the Bolt Business entity that contract is signed with, please, raise it with the Legal.","2026-01-09T09:53:52.342Z"],["3798072","LSS-60974","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:63e354e3010d35637974a02c], could you please request from Warp their Enterprise Plan Agreement and relevant Data Processing terms for our review? ","2026-01-09T09:53:56.308Z"],["3798073","LSS-55393","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","thank you [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] !!! \n\n[~accountid:712020:0db6c6e6-af60-46ff-ba53-133f0ab23c9b] please know that each PoA terminates on {{2026-12-31}}. Then, the renewal (new PoA) will be required for you.\n\nThe scope of the actions you can take on behalf of Bolt:\n\na. To sign civil-law and employment contracts, job descriptions, annexes, mutual agreements, and termination documents. \n\nb. To sign and prepare all documentation related to disciplinary actions, poor performance, leaves, and internal compliance procedures.","2026-01-09T09:53:58.171Z"],["3798074","PFI-831052","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Partner Payments] Business made payment, but didn't reflect: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306\n- [Customer Payments] Business had issues with their credit card: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/303\n\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/304\n\n[Billing] - Business invoicing and balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305\n\n[Billing/Tax Tech]- Business invoice has not been reported (Fiscalized) : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T09:53:58.209Z"],["3798076","PFI-830985","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-09T09:54:30.693Z"],["3798079","PC-2998","PC","alexey.efimov@bolt.eu","Alexey Efimov","All of current warning are “Payment instrument not found“. Latest Kibana: [https://kibana-logs.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/r/s/dOqln|https://kibana-logs.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/r/s/dOqln]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 11.54.43.png|width=1070,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 11.54.43.png\"!","2026-01-09T09:54:59.326Z"],["3798080","PRTEAM-263","PRTEAM","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","[~accountid:712020:9f920389-9b88-4c5d-9768-f418248e5ee1] It’s a running discussion as of now. [Thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09FF7S5JV9/p1767893244026499?thread_ts=1766488980.876939&cid=C09FF7S5JV9]","2026-01-09T09:55:16.301Z"],["3798081","DPO-145","DPO","quinn.feller@bolt.eu","Quinn Darby Feller","Cancelled in favor of new approach, including all market emails in guide","2026-01-09T09:55:38.412Z"],["3798083","PFI-830617","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, proceed to correcting it yourself in the Admin. If the permissions are lacking, please, raise it with your Team Lead.\n\nIf any Billing Documents (invoices) have to be changed/reissued, please, provide links to those.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T09:55:49.862Z"],["3798085","DSR-3609","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-09T09:56:22.534Z"],["3798086","DSR-3611","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-09T09:56:22.554Z"],["3798087","PFI-830137","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, refunds are owned by the Customer Payments Team. Please, consult with them.","2026-01-09T09:56:30.234Z"],["3798088","PFI-830137","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Partner Payments] Business made payment, but didn't reflect: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306\n- [Customer Payments] Business had issues with their credit card: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/303\n\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/304\n\n[Billing] - Business invoicing and balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305\n\n[Billing/Tax Tech]- Business invoice has not been reported (Fiscalized) : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T09:56:34.833Z"],["3798091","DRX-27973","DRX","ajinkya.deshmukh@bolt.eu","Ajinkya Suhas Deshmukh","Tested partner offers banner on DA and DI\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-09-2026 11-55-58_1.MP4]","2026-01-09T09:56:45.992Z"],["3798092","PFI-829474","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, provide links to invoices","2026-01-09T09:56:59.734Z"],["3798094","HS-28791","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c], \n\nData as of 09.01.2026:\n\n# Total workforce: *54* employees (including 1 On Leave employee) \n# Number of full-time employees: *54* (including 1 On Leave employee) \n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-09T09:57:25.485Z"],["3798095","LSS-61210","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:6169660ebfa2c1006b56c18f] ! The document will be ready shortly","2026-01-09T09:58:33.831Z"],["3798097","LSS-61322","LSS","justas.gaizauskas@bolt.eu","Justas Gaižauskas","[^LT1525-35647.pdf] _(57 kB)_","2026-01-09T09:59:07.750Z"],["3798098","WFM-9915","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello [~accountid:712020:a4969d25-8e58-49a1-a0b4-179bb77e9ff8],\n\nCan you please share a screenshot of the error? Everything looks fine from our end.","2026-01-09T09:59:12.940Z"],["3798101","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767952775367239]*{color}:\n&gt; Please be aware that Joel deployed changes after you, so just deploying older package is likely not safe.\nI deployed admin panel, and Polina deployed server. Rollback would be possible\n{quote}","2026-01-09T09:59:48.024Z"],["3798102","RLONE-469","RLONE","anton.berggren@bolt.eu","Anton Berggren","[Deep Dive|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CH24V3144/p1765893451429279?thread_ts=1764842385.022159&cid=CH24V3144] conducted by CS of “_I didn’t receive my bonus or campaign_” - Top 5 complaint amongst partners.  Deep dive initiated due to increased nr of tickets: \nNov: 70% MoM,\nDec: 16% MoM\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 09.47.57.png|width=654,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 09.47.57.png\"!\n\n*TLDR Conclusion:* \n\n* 80% of tickets were related to not receiving bonus, some due to fraud, requirements not met and some were actually paid out. - Nothing that stands out\n* Nothing extraordinary events that would fully explain the spike\n\n\n\nI don’t find any actions for local Ops here.","2026-01-09T09:59:58.252Z"],["3798105","LSS-61322","LSS","justas.gaizauskas@bolt.eu","Justas Gaižauskas","[^Jaunimo reikalų agentūra. Specialiosios sąlygos. Bolt Business..docx]\n\nwrong attachment, correct one here","2026-01-09T10:00:12.180Z"],["3798106","LSS-57888","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","*October 2025 following input was shared with Google team via Bolt marketing POC (Rinaldi Yudakusumah):*\n\n_Business case: We want to display Google reviews of specific restaurants via Bolt Food app under the DineOut section. Potentially in the future also under usual Homepage restaurants/stores._ \n\n_How should it work? Bolt Food user opens up the Bolt Food app, clicks on DineOut section. Selects the restaurant where they want to dine in. Under the restaurant profile there will be info about the restaurant. This includes Google map (already exists), opening hours, contact info, address. We want to add there now also Google reviews of the restaurants._\n\n_The question for Google should be: what would be the complaint way for us to display those ratings. And what T&Cs and API instructions we should exactly follow._\n\n_You may mention that in addition to DineOut we might be interested in the future to show ratings also under the “usual” Homepage providers profiles. And ask whether that would change something or the same process would apply. I would assume that same process since from product vice there shouldn’t be any differences. But just to be sure, it would be good to check over._\n\n_Latest feedback from Google POC was on December 2025:_\n_“For now discussing using deals and offers for Bolt is still quite early, we only have this feature launched in India, Japan and Brasil._\n_We currently don’t have visibility into the roadmap for next year and from my knowledge in the markets already launched the existing contracts covered this new feature._\n_I will keep you updated once we have more information and will revive this thread if any legal work is required.”_\n\n_Demo for DineOut and where we would like to show the rating. NB! In real app for now we only have our own internal rating displayed._\n\n*October 20, 2025 feedback from Google via Bolt marketing POC:*\n\n_Hi_ [_@liisa.puu_|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U05LKNHAZGA]\n_quick update on Google ratings for Dine Out:_\n\n* _There’s no public Google API for Dine Out ratings at the moment. Now, the Google team is still checking internally if/how we can use or display this data._\n* _We’ve also asked for their guidance on compliant display (attribution, star format/rounding, refresh/caching) and the relevant T&Cs._\n\n_I’ll share their response once we hear back._\n\n*December 4,  2025 2025 feedback from Google via Bolt  marketing POC:*\n\n_Hey_ [_@liisa.puu_|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U05LKNHAZGA]\n_At the moment, there’s no public Google API for Dine Out ratings._\n_Do you want me to introduce you to other relevant stakeholders from Google?_\n\n*December 8, 2025 feedback from Google POC Kamel Ghosn (Product Partnerships Manager)* *via email to Bolt legal:*\n\n_Hey Rinaldi,_\n\n_Thank you for the intro. For now discussing using deals and offers for Bolt is still quite early, we only have this feature launched in India, Japan and Brasil. We currently don't have visibility into the roadmap for next year and from my knowledge in the markets already launched the existing contracts covered this new feature._\n\n_I will keep you updated once we have more information and will revive this thread if any legal work is required._\n\n_Best_\n\n_Kamel_ \n\ncc: [~accountid:557058:67e15ba9-0972-4bf7-9e81-826e62fc001b] [~accountid:5f8d84bfddb0df006e611144] [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03] ","2026-01-09T10:00:16.159Z"],["3798112","PFI-807245","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! FYI: Due to capacity limitations, we were unable to do the reissues in 2025. As Bulgaria switched from BGN to EUR from 01.01.2026, the reissued records need to be uploaded in EUR. ","2026-01-09T10:00:51.183Z"],["3798114","LSS-61322","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-09T10:01:10.556Z"],["3798116","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767952898412589]*{color}:\nGood point! In that case, I will deploy older server package to mitigate immediate issue and Polina can continue looking into proper fix.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T10:01:52.871Z"],["3798117","GRWA-1478","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","Jan 2026 budget for Vilnius was manually updated in [Campaigns Tracking|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/196fkMEDScNxMBv4FTZy-u9LLmarN41lXpv8RfgDXn64/edit?gid=1482776815#gid=1482776815].","2026-01-09T10:02:22.042Z"],["3798118","CRC-2360","CRC","kristiina.taube@bolt.eu","Kristiina Taube","[~accountid:5f23e67bfa591d0015b8af39] Thanks a lot! \n\nQuick follow-ups so that I for sure understand everything correct:\n\n* so all of the drivers/fleets who are on the Bolt platform in the NL are taxi service providers? Meaning, there are no private hire drivers without a taxi license offering rides on the Bolt platform? \n* “Fares are generally determined uniformly for all drivers” - Is it Bolt who determines the fares? Or are there uniformly set taxi fares determined by local authority or similar and Bolt app just calculates the full ride price based on that?  ","2026-01-09T10:02:28.173Z"],["3798121","LSS-61323","LSS","ab.moula@bolt.eu","AB Moula","[^ADDENDUM TO COOPERATION AGREEMENT_Bolt Operations_Feenix Technologies (2).pdf] _(171 kB)_\n\n[^Bolt x Feenix Signed Contract (4).pdf] _(482 kB)_","2026-01-09T10:02:41.644Z"],["3798123","DSR-3069","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","[~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] This ticket can be closed as the response was sent to the data subject [https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Bv8zALXHhpWqhR4DVIL5KJ_jYAN-N9Z0/view?usp=drive_link|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Bv8zALXHhpWqhR4DVIL5KJ_jYAN-N9Z0/view?usp=drive_link|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T10:03:15.826Z"],["3798124","LSS-61324","LSS","maarifa.pashayeva@bolt.eu","Maarifa Pashayeva","[^NDA.pdf] _(283 kB)_","2026-01-09T10:03:19.350Z"],["3798125","GS-71","GS","radu.vasiliu@bolt.eu","Radu Vasiliu","ETA: 2026-01-30\nStatus: Implementation\n\nSummary: \nMinor progress, due to NYE on-call and team-duty, The update is the same:\n\nWork in progress on Alternative #2: Specific Override (ideal outcome): \"The ability to configure unique wayfinding instructions for chauffeur categories on a per-airport basis.\"\n\nBlockers: \n\n\nDetails:\nADR:https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7053639713/2025+Oct+-+Airport+meet+greet+instructions+for+Lux+riders+-+Bolt+Chauffeur+-+ADR ( )https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7053639713/2025+Oct+-+Airport+meet+greet+instructions+for+Lux+riders+-+Bolt+Chauffeur+-+ADR (2025 Oct - Airport meet &amp;amp;amp; greet instructions for Lux riders - Bolt Chauffeur - ADR)\n\n- :done: implementation of \"Alternative #2\" is mostly done\n- :loading: working on comp tests\n- :next: integration with admin-panel: new UI fields to support editing of directions with search_category_group","2026-01-09T10:03:33.461Z"],["3798126","GC-3171","GC","radu.vasiliu@bolt.eu","Radu Vasiliu","ETA: 2026-01-30\nStatus: Implementation\n\nSummary: \nMinor progress, due to NYE on-call and team-duty, The update is the same:\n\n- :loading: Admin-panel Tooling: working on Admin-panel page for testing our internal solution: Route-Tolls with EdgeDetection\n\nBlockers: \n\n\nDetails:\n- :done: implementation complete, last PR was merged this week.\n- :done: Run silent-live test for comparing EdgeDetection vs TollGuru,  in Thailand.\n- :done: Extract silent-live results\n- :done: Map OPs team found some bugs while analysing the last silent-live test: EdgeDetection vs TollGuru in  Thailand).\n- :loading: BUG: TollRoad detection at large distance (few km away): causes EdgeDetection to estimate too many tolls. Analysis & testing in progress\n- :loading: Tooling: working on Admin-panel page for testing our internal solution: Route-Tolls","2026-01-09T10:03:33.677Z"],["3798130","PFI-818860","PFI","nantawat.boonchu@bolt-outsource.eu","Nantawat Boonchu","Dear payment team,\n\nKindly follow up on updating paid commission in driver balance.\n\nThank you in advance.","2026-01-09T10:04:55.356Z"],["3798132","WEBSD-1466","WEBSD","yaroslav.svishchenko@bolt.eu","Yaroslav Svishchenko","!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 11.35.29.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 11.35.49.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T10:05:47.865Z"],["3798133","LSS-57924","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Documents will be signed via DocuSign as signatures are required to be in designated spots. ","2026-01-09T10:05:57.541Z"],["3798134","PIF-2266","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED, ADR_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft concisely captures the essence of the update: dynamically adjusting per-instance DB connection limits based on the global limit, thus improving service efficiency and load management. Essential information like where to check this feature and guides for implementation are placeholders as the specific URLs and guides are not provided.","2026-01-09T10:06:10.458Z"],["3798138","PAW-14751","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-09T10:07:19.195Z"],["3798140","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767953243487579]*{color}:\nService was rolled back, I'll keep the lock for live fleetdocuments until we have a fix.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T10:08:08.603Z"],["3798142","PFI-831320","PFI","martin.canek@bolt-outsource.eu","Martin Canek","!3a4461ec-d05f-4601-9b34-419ec6bebd1a.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!94febdb9-66df-40f6-9392-7dabf79251e4.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!e873acee-60fc-48c7-9124-9e25e6b7da72.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T10:08:27.835Z"],["3798145","XVER-314","XVER","guillermo.salceda@bolt.eu","Guillermo Salceda Pacheco","Hi [~accountid:712020:bba87790-3d07-4531-9af3-f5df86d0d56a] \n\nAlthough we provided tax advice and support on the expansion to CA in 25Q4, I’m adding 20 extra working hours for 26Q1 in case any further support is needed. \n\nc.c. [~accountid:712020:8bcb68bd-f8da-4da1-8320-2536f6bb0c0c] ","2026-01-09T10:08:40.521Z"],["3798148","FPD-1385","FPD","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","Done by RF","2026-01-09T10:09:08.238Z"],["3798150","LSS-50276","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:feba077c-0585-4e5b-8e4d-2cdc0e19ecf8] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the DPA. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:10:25.821Z"],["3798151","PAW-14514","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-njsc-db, pint-product-backend-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-09T10:10:32.351Z"],["3798152","LSS-58302","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:6406fa52314f50881383a238] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:11:31.812Z"],["3798153","FX-3587","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767953499214349]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3587] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T10:11:51.710Z"],["3798154","PC-4871","PC","kevin.kanarbik@bolt.eu","Kevin Kanarbik","Alright so it seems payment domain-wise this is not an actual problem aka shouldn’t be logged as an {{error}} \nMostly the issues come from UP/Yigim and nothing to do about their timeouts BUT we have cron processes in place that work if synchronous authorizations fail, then async cron jobs take over and eventually succeed in processing the payment. This problem and solution discussed in a earlier thread here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C010VCJ4T3Q/p1747233533593049?thread_ts=1744381509.896589&cid=C010VCJ4T3Q|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C010VCJ4T3Q/p1747233533593049?thread_ts=1744381509.896589&cid=C010VCJ4T3Q|smart-link] \n\nSo the solution is to just avoid logging this as an error and to do this we can add {{expected_errors: [CommonResponseCodes.CLIENT_TIMEOUT]}} when CCP does a {{/internal/confirm/googlepay}} request to {{payment-provider-processout}}. This solution is similar to this [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PC-3257|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PC-3257|smart-link]  where the expected error was added to ApplePay’s confirm request. \n\nMight as well us the same logic on GooglePay 🙂  [~accountid:61de8e0e7c6f980070b38d2b] can you confirm and approve?","2026-01-09T10:12:01.448Z"],["3798155","LSS-59076","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:9cfda827-f644-48a1-9da8-aff3fd427bf9] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:12:05.712Z"],["3798158","LSS-59305","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:12:58.066Z"],["3798159","LSS-61295","LSS","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","Message sent (/) \n\nThank you, [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ","2026-01-09T10:13:07.620Z"],["3798175","PFI-831280","PFI","patrycja.matus@bolt.eu","Patrycja Matus","Hello :) \nThis one : \n!image.png|thumbnail!\n\nand another one in attachment:){adf}{\"type\":\"expand\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Łączę pozdrowienia,\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#222222\"}}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" \"},{\"type\":\"hardBreak\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Patrycja Matus\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"},{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#222222\"}}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#222222\"}}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" \"}]},{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"default\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Account Specialist : Poland\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#2f313f\"}}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"layout\":\"center\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"external\",\"url\":\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/mail-sig/AIorK4zEnmedq0QG20wYuzENFWAYDDMyf1VJ0bMZIARC6nx8gtx8kB6sxhkBBiMPa-I7zHxcZMcBt3LEaK22\",\"height\":183,\"width\":200}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" \"}]},{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"default\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"layout\":\"center\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"external\",\"url\":\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/hosting-dc1bb.appspot.com/o/emailIcon.png?alt=media&token=5f2f566c-ce11-4cb4-b5bc-5146bb93e1fc\",\"height\":183,\"width\":200}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"patrycja.matus@bolt.eu\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#1155cc\"}},{\"type\":\"link\",\"attrs\":{\"href\":\"mailto:aleksandra.borkowska@bolt.eu\"}}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"layout\":\"center\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"external\",\"url\":\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/hosting-dc1bb.appspot.com/o/webIcon.png?alt=media&token=24cd9635-0ac1-4ae4-8d3e-847b757043de\",\"height\":183,\"width\":200}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"blog.bolt.eu\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#1155cc\"}},{\"type\":\"link\",\"attrs\":{\"href\":\"http://blog.bolt.eu/\"}}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"layout\":\"center\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"external\",\"url\":\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/hosting-dc1bb.appspot.com/o/boltFoodLogo.png?alt=media&token=dd086d95-234d-4b3a-9c47-24b59bd5b4a3\",\"height\":183,\"width\":200}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#747682\"}}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"https://food.bolt.eu/\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"link\",\"attrs\":{\"href\":\"https://food.bolt.eu/\"}},{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#747682\"}}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\">\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#747682\"}}]}]}],\"attrs\":{\"title\":\"Signature\"}}{adf}\n\n[^2025-12-08 -- 2025-12-15 PiwoWar Ursynow Weekly Report (1).pdf] _(38 kB)_","2026-01-09T10:13:34.187Z"],["3798176","LSS-59309","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signatures are still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:13:46.063Z"],["3798177","LSS-59097","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Reviewed template in parent ticket and approved it.","2026-01-09T10:14:23.685Z"],["3798178","LSS-59317","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:14:25.618Z"],["3798179","PFI-831323","PFI","patryk.flakowski@bolt.eu","Patryk Flakowski","!IMG_5727.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_5728.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T10:14:32.046Z"],["3798180","LSS-59913","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","Hey [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a], I agree that the AI onboarding ticket should sit with me - I’ve reassigned it back accordingly.\n\nThat said, before we review or onboard any related AI tool, I think we should first:\n\n# complete the relevant privacy risk assessments for the proposed processing activity; and\n# provide the team with clear guidance on how to implement this employee monitoring process in a compliant way (both operationally and from a transparency perspective).\n\nI’d consider this work MVRA-worthy (either under Bolt Business or People vertical). Happy to align on how best to divide this work.","2026-01-09T10:14:32.282Z"],["3798182","PFI-831323","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-09T10:14:34.512Z"],["3798185","LSS-59634","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:5ece16662490cf0c09d78cae] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Feeling Group Vehicle’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:15:08.242Z"],["3798186","FX-3276","FX","anastasia.kaivel@bolt.eu","Anastasia Kaivel","Yes, thank you, it will work - asked more to get the understanding of how to plan things from our side. ","2026-01-09T10:15:25.207Z"],["3798187","HS-28745","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","Hi Răzvan, I can absolutely appreciate the urgency but please keep in mind that our working hours are 9.00-17.00 Estonian time and these docments have to be separately requested from a vendor which unfortunately means that it takes some time. \n\nI’m attaching a document we already have on file. Please note that this document is not finalised and not signed. I simply need you to tell me if this would be sufficient for your doctor. If this is enough, I will send it for signing and send you the signed version.  If not, I will request a different file from our vendor. \n[^NASTASE MADALIN-RAZVAN Adverinta.pdf] \n\nI’ll be looking forward to your feedback. \n\nBest\nAlice, Senior People Operations Specialist","2026-01-09T10:15:31.718Z"],["3798188","PFI-830688","PFI","sylwia.siwek@bolt-outsource.eu","Sylwia Siwek","hi! asked the user","2026-01-09T10:15:37.777Z"],["3798189","LSS-59745","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:602d7a68-8a81-4bea-98bf-acb7026b1a56] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:15:45.214Z"],["3798190","LSS-61157","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:10c3f4ef-f975-47a3-8af8-927b01cd9521] if we also sign Order form  we need to keep the ticket open, please let me know what’s the plan for trial ","2026-01-09T10:15:52.105Z"],["3798194","LSS-60080","LSS","mbali.mkize@bolt.eu","Mbali Paula Mkize","Hi [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] - please see response to the questions above.\n1. We cannot say for certain that the driver was the one who actually took the phone. The driver was contacted and reported not finding the phone","2026-01-09T10:16:03.730Z"],["3798195","FX-3587","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767953755310109]*{color}:\nHey! Isn't this related to drivers adding a car in driver app?\n{quote}","2026-01-09T10:16:08.700Z"],["3798196","LSS-61325","LSS","fareed.mahaini@bolt.eu","Fareed Mahaini","[^AUTO1 Remarketing GmbH Bolt Drive Sales Agreement.docx.pdf] _(194 kB)_","2026-01-09T10:16:20.930Z"],["3798197","LSS-59835","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signatures are still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:16:22.314Z"],["3798199","RDXENG-4590","RDXENG","evgenii.sukhanov@bolt.eu","Evgenii Sukhanov","\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1767948603437459|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1767948603437459|smart-card]","2026-01-09T10:16:24.620Z"],["3798200","LSS-61323","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-09T10:16:26.738Z"],["3798201","LSS-58367","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hey [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] \n\nWe must sign this agreement using our local Taiwan entity to comply with the Taiwan Company Act, which prohibits foreign companies from 'transacting business' (such as executing ongoing service contracts) in Taiwan without a registered presence. Signing directly with the foreign parent would flag our active marketing operations as unregistered business conduct, exposing the company and its signatories to potential criminal penalties and civil liability. \n\nAdditionally, the contract mandates a 5% VAT payment which is only reclaimable by a local entity; a foreign signatory would be unable to claim this input tax, resulting in unnecessary sunk costs.\n\nHope this clears things up 😊 ","2026-01-09T10:16:29.164Z"],["3798203","CRC-2360","CRC","noud.ottens@bolt.eu","Noud Ottens","[~accountid:712020:29d8b602-d17f-40cd-9cae-5653bc2c54b7] Sure!\n\n\n* _so all of the drivers/fleets who are on the Bolt platform in the NL are taxi service providers? Meaning, there are no private hire drivers without a taxi license offering rides on the Bolt platform?_\nEvery driver on the Bolt platform operates under a taxi license, either their own, or the license from the fleet under which they’re active.\n\n* _“Fares are generally determined uniformly for all drivers” - Is it Bolt who determines the fares? Or are there uniformly set taxi fares determined by local authority or similar and Bolt app just calculates the full ride price based on that?_\nBolt determines the ride fares for drivers. There is no legislation that sets maximum or minimum pricing for pre-ordered rides, under which our rides fall. The only minor exception is one specific fleet that operates street taxis (from Schiphol only). In this case, we apply the legally determined fares (which include maximum fares) under the WP2000, the law governing taxi services in the Netherlands.\n\nLet me know if you more details!","2026-01-09T10:16:35.383Z"],["3798204","PIF-2266","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 10\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: ","2026-01-09T10:16:51.237Z"],["3798205","PFI-831280","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! The provider account link in the ticket does not seem to be the correct one as the name does not match the report. Can you please review? ","2026-01-09T10:16:56.382Z"],["3798209","LSS-59882","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - Any updates regarding the signatures? One of the signatures is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:17:10.198Z"],["3798213","HS-28745","HS","razvan.nastase@bolt.eu","Răzvan Năstase","Hello! Yes, that document is good - if I can get a similar one it would be great. Thank you!","2026-01-09T10:17:52.688Z"],["3798214","LSS-59914","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - Any updates regarding the signatures? One of the signatures is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:17:55.857Z"],["3798216","LSS-60403","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 12.16.33.png|width=923,height=155,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 12.16.33.png\"!\n\nYou will find written in red what they are asking for. i was not sure, hence I contacted you to find out whether I could share this or not.\n\nI did check with the Tax department, who responded that this is not within their expertise, hence I turned to legal.\n\n\n\nThank you\n\nDOlinda\n\n\n\n\n\n","2026-01-09T10:18:19.818Z"],["3798218","LSS-60941","LSS","matej.crne@bolt.eu","Matej Črne","Hello. I received feedback from supplier side, commented in the file: \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BLHx5XeDNF0lL0LmugT2Tw633huAXjkK/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BLHx5XeDNF0lL0LmugT2Tw633huAXjkK/edit|smart-link] \n\n\n\nPlease take a look, and let me know if edits are acceptable for us","2026-01-09T10:18:32.277Z"],["3798219","LSS-60080","LSS","mbali.mkize@bolt.eu","Mbali Paula Mkize","# The rider has not received their phone back.\n# The driver will not be permanently blocked as he reported not seeing the phone. The rider has been advised to log a case with the local authorities.\n# We have assisted the rider by revoking all tokens. \n\n","2026-01-09T10:18:35.166Z"],["3798220","LSS-59769","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:6172754ef485cd006863a3a8] thank you for your response ! The requestor never followed up, therefore I won’t engage the offer again, however your response is insightful for any future requests. \n\nYou can close this ticket, thank you !","2026-01-09T10:18:35.490Z"],["3798221","LSS-59922","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signatures are still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:18:47.483Z"],["3798223","LSS-59947","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:5ece16662490cf0c09d78cae] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:19:24.049Z"],["3798227","XP-2738","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","[~accountid:641d5e7c9796ea0a8718ca5e] A low effort alternative solution to avoiding conflicts would be to ONLY allow interleaved designs (most people use anyways), then follow the rest of the same recommendations:\n\n* set switch time default to midnight UTC (possibly hide switch time in AP also)\n* only allow test durations that are 2 week multiples\n* only allow tests to start every 4 hours (UTC)\n* allow only time-slice duration options: 30 min, 60 min, 120 min, 240 min\n* parallel tests cannot use the same length time-slice durations - must be different (ignore - we will highlight this in the scheduler) \n* only 2 tests in parallel allowed per vertical (already restricted i believe)\n* burn in period - a dropdown of values: 5/10/20 mins (AB processor out of scope)","2026-01-09T10:19:41.834Z"],["3798229","LSS-60104","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:6f563341-b27c-4653-b7d4-c67e881cc931] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:19:48.155Z"],["3798232","LSS-60361","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:6423e317b05b4e3e7dabadb6] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:20:12.648Z"],["3798233","MVRT-1446","MVRT","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","Hey! Letting you know that all in-app comms are set up and ready to go from our side (/)  Previews can be seen [here|https://www.figma.com/design/HC6W8PXNxKFtefWDR8MOgr/Rentals-LCM--Micromobility-communications?node-id=2372-4&t=sweGIFSPgFs16lxO-0]. *It’s important to note that for the stories, I did not add the button on every single slide* since clicking on it would close the story. This would mean lots of users could open the stories, and only go through the first one = much lower visibility on the features we’re highlighting. If you don’t agree, please let me know, and I’ll edit.\n\n*Regarding the frequency of the banners*:\n\n* Vertical banner on RH view - since the view is not owned by our team, I am checking with the relevant people what the suggested approach is. \n* Floating banner on Micromobility view - I’d suggest showing it around 5-7 times per user, with at least 3 days in between. If the user dismisses it 2x, we’ll stop showing it to that specific user. We can monitor the stats after launch and adjust if necessary.\n\nLet me know if you see any issues with this approach 🙏 ","2026-01-09T10:20:14.000Z"],["3798235","LSS-60382","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:20:43.747Z"],["3798237","LSS-59913","LSS","tatsiana.sivukha@bolt.eu","Tatsiana Sivukha","Hey [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] \n\nthanks a lot for the input.\n\nI will propose the following options:\n\n# Our department do the onboarding of AI tools, but the very processing activity assessment is done by the respective counsel as per verticals/areas; OR\n# We divide AI tools onboarding based on verticals/areas\n\n\n\n[~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] let’s discuss on our next trio call.","2026-01-09T10:21:05.639Z"],["3798238","LSS-61317","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:45592015-305a-48b0-9778-976fd761612d] please create not a legal ticket but infosec ticket for [~accountid:5c987f2c0cf73c3215ff6aa7] \n\nPlease use InfoSec Service Desk for this, I shared this ticket with [~accountid:5c987f2c0cf73c3215ff6aa7] ","2026-01-09T10:21:10.616Z"],["3798242","HS-28692","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello [~accountid:712020:2280267b-cbd6-417f-8d9b-0da55c5955cc] \n\nI was discussing this topic with the German HR and they also included your manager Matthew Stokell who will update you further about the topic.\n\n\n\nKind regards,\nKadri","2026-01-09T10:21:46.597Z"],["3798244","FDBT-4708","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-09T10:22:17.989Z"],["3798247","FDBT-4709","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-09T10:22:25.777Z"],["3798248","LSS-60282","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:67606a59-d726-4e53-8ba7-862b9e82da34] given that this is only stage 1 and limited documentation has been provided so far by the procurer, no red flags from my end. The only comment is that I notice that *we should submit a document regarding how we handle protected personal data* (in line with Swedish practice). *Do we already have this document so the Privacy Team can take a look?* Ping. [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] (this is a very light stage 1 phase tender currently, no usual tender docs etc so far). The first submission is January 14 (where the below is included). \n\n* _3.3.3 Hantering av skyddade personuppgifter_ \n** _För att säkerställa att leverantören inte löper risk att oavsiktligt lämna ut skyddade personuppgifter ska leverantören ha en beslutad och internt förankrad process/rutin för hantering av skyddade personuppgifter. Processen/rutinen ska utgå från Skatteverkets vägledning för hantering av skyddade personuppgifter i svensk förvaltning. Som bevis ska leverantören bifoga en sammanfattning avseende sin hantering av skyddade personuppgifter som utgår från Skatteverkets vägledning. Sammanfattningen får maximalt vara 3 sidor. I de fall sammanfattningen omfattar mer än 3 sidor kommer kommunen enbart ta hänsyn till de första 3 sidorna._\n* ENG. translation: 3.3.3 Handling of protected personal data\n** _To ensure that the supplier does not risk inadvertently disclosing protected personal data, the supplier must have an established and internally anchored process/procedure for handling protected personal data. The process/procedure shall be based on the Swedish Tax Agency’s (Skatteverket’s) guidance for handling protected personal data in Swedish public administration. As evidence, the supplier shall attach a summary describing its handling of protected personal data, based on the Swedish Tax Agency’s guidance. The summary may be no more than 3 pages. If the summary exceeds 3 pages, the municipality will only consider the first 3 pages._\n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T10:22:39.296Z"],["3798250","LSS-47933","LSS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Hi [~accountid:61b1d141b0b630006a9698e1] , I hope you don’t mind I added you to this ticket as reporter 🙂.\n\nWe have now finalised the initial review of Swedbank EE’s sales and re-sales template agreements with Widen’s comments. Could you please have a look and share your thoughts? We can also schedule a call to discuss.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1b1GApjEN9LgG_M9p6bNYfDI7uN7otblh/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1b1GApjEN9LgG_M9p6bNYfDI7uN7otblh/edit|smart-link] \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ths1VD37BxwSAoNeyRkbLwS1WdncqZhu/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ths1VD37BxwSAoNeyRkbLwS1WdncqZhu/edit|smart-link] \n\nThe idea would be to finalise this one with you and then move to Swedbank LV, LT and to Luminor afterwards.\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] .\n\nThanks and best,\n\nThiago and Veera","2026-01-09T10:22:49.828Z"],["3798251","LSS-53784","LSS","emin.bayramli@bolt.eu","Emin Bayramli","Hi, [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd]. They have already confirmed that the doc is on their side for review. They should be getting back to me soon.","2026-01-09T10:22:52.300Z"],["3798256","PFI-831330","PFI","kutlwano.serame@bolt.eu","Kutlwano Serame","!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 12.22.20.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T10:23:47.665Z"],["3798257","LSS-61261","LSS","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","hey [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] I’m sorry, but the provider now told me that they don’t accept electronic signatures. Would you be so kind as to collect a regular signature and share with me the scan?","2026-01-09T10:24:02.699Z"],["3798260","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Hey! Translation is “Pakua app ya Bolt”","2026-01-09T10:24:14.055Z"],["3798261","CNT-377","CNT","aleksandra.onutsina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Onutšina","[~accountid:712020:f172cd28-e81b-4011-8942-5ec6b2912f37] Sure, I’ll ping you once the first draft is done. ","2026-01-09T10:24:52.755Z"],["3798262","MKP-9779","MKP","aman.mahajan@bolt.eu","Aman Mahajan","Hi Team,\nWe have a few Airport trips in Oslo with decoupling coming from PMC v2 elasticity tests, these trips are supposed to have fixed pricing on fixed routes mainly in Airports. Looking to know if its possible to exclude fixed routes from elasticity tests\n    ◦ [Trip 1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2329012434/74?orderTryId=2990879445]\n    ◦ [Trip 2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2318994536/74?orderTryId=2973295787]","2026-01-09T10:25:13.232Z"],["3798263","MKP-9779","MKP",null,"Slack","[Aman Mahajan|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:a6e5bda4-9922-40e6-9f30-ac79279f361c] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09NS1RC129/p1767936709307919?thread_ts=1767936709.307919&cid=C09NS1RC129|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09NS1RC129/p1767936709307919?thread_ts=1767936709.307919&cid=C09NS1RC129|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-09T10:25:14.091Z"],["3798264","MKP-9779","MKP","giammarco.pavan@bolt.eu","Giammarco Pavan","cc: [@patrick.mayer|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:6501dce9-6008-449b-bef3-328b9147505a], [@aleksei.valiakin|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5cfa3061c756c10f35f2af6f]","2026-01-09T10:25:14.698Z"],["3798265","MKP-9779","MKP","aleksei.valiakin@bolt.eu","Aleksei Valiakin","[@aman.mahajan|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:a6e5bda4-9922-40e6-9f30-ac79279f361c] can you help here?","2026-01-09T10:25:15.786Z"],["3798266","MKP-9779","MKP","aman.mahajan@bolt.eu","Aman Mahajan","Yes, we can exclude fixed routes from PMC v2 price changes.","2026-01-09T10:25:16.566Z"],["3798268","RDS-1276","RDS","katharina.skolimowski@bolt.eu","Katharina Skolimowski","On the live map - should it be visible already on the driver list, or in details? \nConsidering we’re adding shift info, upcoming scheduled ride info to the list item…\nWhat’s the use case to check it?\n \n[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 12.25.17.png|width=758,height=183,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 12.25.17.png\"!","2026-01-09T10:25:31.139Z"],["3798270","LSS-60386","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:25:33.991Z"],["3798271","MKP-9779","MKP","aleksei.valiakin@bolt.eu","Aleksei Valiakin","is it covering both rider and driver pricing exclusion? [@kodimalar.balakrishnan|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:975996ab-baea-4fdf-9afd-c52a2c04bf2a] just double-checking if it is fine only to exclude for rider pricing, where driver commission can be still changed within these routes?","2026-01-09T10:25:53.617Z"],["3798272","LSS-60638","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:602d7a68-8a81-4bea-98bf-acb7026b1a56] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:25:55.598Z"],["3798274","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Also I have updated the “Terms and Conditions apply” text on the media plan. Translation is “Vigezo na Masharti kuzingatiwa”","2026-01-09T10:25:55.993Z"],["3798276","PFI-831271","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:0a6482c4-510b-4c02-a5f0-016cf9d5025f],\n\nThis user has a lot of created accounts, some deleted, which are all connected to one device.\nThis user is not eligible for the aforementioned promo code.\nMost likely they are now trying to phish additional compensation or codes from the CS.\nPlease do not provide them with any compensations and if required, simply let them know that the promotional code is no longer available for them.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-09T10:25:58.873Z"],["3798277","LSS-61210","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:6169660ebfa2c1006b56c18f] , hey! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n\n[^Complete_with_Docusign_uea_555899_Bolt_Suppo.pdf] ","2026-01-09T10:26:05.381Z"],["3798278","LSS-60691","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:63d0eccfa197e05f9dadc837] - Any updates regarding the signatures? Partner’s signature is still missing from the document. Ticket will be closed next week due to inactivity.","2026-01-09T10:26:16.928Z"],["3798286","LSS-61128","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Thank you [~accountid:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb] ! We usually grant PoAs only until the end of a given year. Please let if this would not work in this situation. ","2026-01-09T10:27:51.549Z"],["3798288","L10N-26883","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26881](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26881)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T10:28:19.483Z"],["3798289","L10N-26882","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26881](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26881)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T10:28:20.433Z"],["3798290","L10N-26885","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth