e\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26919](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26919)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T10:43:51.742Z"],["3798391","L10N-26990","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26919](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26919)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T10:43:53.091Z"],["3798392","PFI-831334","PFI","sofiia.yasinska@bolt-outsource.eu","Sofiia Yasinska","!IMG_3929.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T10:43:53.239Z"],["3798394","L10N-26989","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26919](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26919)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T10:43:53.815Z"],["3798396","PFI-831038","PFI","tsitsi.chiwanza@bolt.eu","Tsitsi Chiwanza","The rider has responded as follows;\n\nAm not asking for a new invoice, but a copy of the invoices issued then.\n\nIf you must respond by telling me of compliance to laws, Hou are aware that the law, and especially related to VAT, is that you keep the records for 5 years. In this case it's not even 3 months. So please, I don't want to have to access these through legal means, Consumer Protection, VAT or otherwise.\n\nLooking forward to receiving your response","2026-01-09T10:44:47.208Z"],["3798397","PFI-831335","PFI","natthakan.loetwattanakankul@bolt-outsource.eu","Natthakan Loetwattanakankul","!Payment screenshot.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Payment.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T10:44:55.050Z"],["3798398","PFI-831336","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-09T10:45:03.069Z"],["3798399","PFI-831336","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:61261fa2dd25520076a72c06] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T10:45:04.688Z"],["3798400","PFI-831334","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nYou can provide the user the acquirer reference {{535109258099}} to locate the payment. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-09T10:45:18.783Z"],["3798402","DRX-27665","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: according to the ticket","2026-01-09T10:45:45.835Z"],["3798403","WFM-9920","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","*OPS Specialist* role \n\n[*Roles*|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-user/permissions/edit/766?tab=roles] for the mentioned permission","2026-01-09T10:45:47.766Z"],["3798404","DSR-3015","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:6001a723d364960139286c95] , the responsive data and answer letter can be shared with the user (/) ","2026-01-09T10:46:11.601Z"],["3798406","WFM-9908","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello,\n\nDone.","2026-01-09T10:46:38.727Z"],["3798407","PC-4871","PC","siarhei.hlasouski@bolt.eu","Siarhei Hlasouski","[~accountid:712020:4ff22db6-b452-40af-b802-c2dc3fab0c28] Yes, please go forward with that","2026-01-09T10:46:50.497Z"],["3798408","PFI-831333","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customers refund failed. The customer payments team has checked with our payment service provider monobank and we can confirm the refund has failed. \n\nPlease ask the user to check with their bank about spending restrictions on their account. Alternatively, you can issue a refund to the customer Bolt Balance instead.\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T10:46:53.321Z"],["3798411","PRF-814","PRF","carelin.magi@bolt.eu","Carelin Mägi","[~accountid:712020:6ca2307e-6766-4d7e-a7b5-7f3b9a6cb0b6] Hey, yes they were paused!","2026-01-09T10:47:27.719Z"],["3798414","LSS-61303","LSS","kristjan.okas@bolt.eu","Kristjan Okas","Okay, but let’s do it. Many thanks! 💪 ","2026-01-09T10:48:04.938Z"],["3798415","PFI-831280","PFI","patrycja.matus@bolt.eu","Patrycja Matus","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-provider/providers/157594?tab=info|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-provider/providers/157594?tab=info]","2026-01-09T10:48:15.110Z"],["3798416","LSS-60746","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:615c75e007ac3c0068114285] I’ve taken a look from a privacy perspective and added comments directly to the document (regarding retention periods).\n\nRegarding this question (_What is the driver-facing declaration wording and any privacy notice shown at submission? - CC_ [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] _)_ → we need to have some sort of a disclaimer that we show to drivers, either when inviting them to roll into Rikba or after they send the documents/video. We can help draft the disclaimer.","2026-01-09T10:48:19.231Z"],["3798421","BEE-3637","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Hi! I’m not entirely sure if this sits with the BH team, but I wanted to check whether it would be possible to route Micromobility voicemail BH tickets for specific markets to a dedicated Slack channel.\n\nWe have some time-sensitive markets, such as Estonia, where scooters need to be moved within a defined timeframe following a voicemail report. Having real-time Slack alerts would help support Local Ops in responding within the required SLA. :timer_clock:\n\nFrom earlier discussions with WFM, we understood that these tickets currently can’t be separated from other Tier 1 cases and therefore can not be separately routed to Slack. :question: Could you advise whether there’s a feasible way to enable this, or if there are alternative solutions we could explore?","2026-01-09T10:48:39.179Z"],["3798422","BEE-3637","BEE",null,"Slack","[Andri Jasinski|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d807af94f9cf00d60213212] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C032D4ZGZR6/p1767951960678309?thread_ts=1767951960.678309&cid=C032D4ZGZR6|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C032D4ZGZR6/p1767951960678309?thread_ts=1767951960.678309&cid=C032D4ZGZR6|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-09T10:48:40.256Z"],["3798423","BEE-3637","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Hi! Well, best thing I can think about is if you are able to set up queue that would match only tickets you are interested in, you can leverage slack notification feature that is available in queues","2026-01-09T10:48:40.612Z"],["3798424","BEE-3637","BEE","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","I don't think there's a possibility to make a \"voicemail\" queue, as it's not separated from Tier 1 at all, but is included in the queues :thinking_face:  So we can't make a separate queue.. do you think it would be difficult to separate voicemails as such? Similar to Callbacks?","2026-01-09T10:48:41.439Z"],["3798425","BEE-3637","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","can you share an example beehive link?","2026-01-09T10:48:41.958Z"],["3798426","BEE-3637","BEE","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Yes, example of a voicemail - [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/677451789|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/677451789]","2026-01-09T10:48:42.779Z"],["3798427","BEE-3637","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","I can see it has Source {{Inbound voicemail}} which could probably help you distinguish voicemail cases from the rest in a specific country? Can you share some details about the scale of the problem, potential financial impact if we won't get it implemented?","2026-01-09T10:48:43.302Z"],["3798428","BEE-3637","BEE","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Yes, we can distinguish them in Looker & filter them out - the request here is for the separation when it comes to creating queues, I believe ([@jana.mariakova|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ee36bc3283ae50ab5999c9e], correct me if I'm wrong :smile: ).\n\nFrom the financial side, I don't have the specific numbers, but this could be something that potentially endangers our ability to operate in specific markets if the requests are not answered in a timely manner (this specific request came from EE - CC: [@karl.apsolon|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:282008bf-7f03-4058-8bec-43f7e5a44ace] & [@stella.normak|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/62305e2f1f014e0069cc8021]).\n\nConsidering they're attached to the Tier 1 queue, we can't also ensure they are pushed ahead in the queue for the agents - they'll be there with no ATI & Low SLO, meaning our 3-hour FRT target may mean they're not attended to in time & escalated to Local OPS. Planning with a lower FRT target would have CS Cost implications (don't have the specific numbers, but increasing it from 3 hours to 1 hour for EE language would mean more agents are required for each shift, depending on seasonality and cross-skilling - EE language currently costs us €33.71 per hour).\n\nIn addition to Estonia, this would also help us ensure our sensitive Tender markets, such as Belgium, would have these requests attended in a timely manner as well.","2026-01-09T10:48:44.038Z"],["3798429","BEE-3637","BEE",null,"Slack","Hey both,\nAs far as I understand, we don’t have any way to distinguish these in the Queue settings in Admin. Therefore, I am unable to create a separate queue for them.","2026-01-09T10:48:45.556Z"],["3798430","BEE-3637","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Thank you! I will create a task for our team to add source as a part of queue criteria config :ok_hand::skin-tone-2:","2026-01-09T10:48:46.147Z"],["3798431","PFI-830769","PFI","beatriz.almeida@bolt-outsource.eu","Beatriz Almeida","I understand, Marten, but the user says they use the application regularly and that's all they have access to. I kindly asked them once more to export the December statement, focusing only on the part where that amount appears.","2026-01-09T10:49:02.270Z"],["3798432","SREDESK-7392","SREDESK","andrus.viik@bolt.eu","Andrus Viik","!image-20260109-104839.png|width=744,alt=\"image-20260109-104839.png\"!\n\nPermissions granted.","2026-01-09T10:49:02.941Z"],["3798433","HS-28690","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:5d5149bc92705e0c1c5e519a],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-09T10:49:17.584Z"],["3798434","PFI-831320","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe users attempt to pay the fine have failed with an error message 05 : Do not honor. \nThe user is not able to use this payment method for the payment. \n\nIt’s unfortunate because the user is being asked to use the same payment method as the original order where the fine was created. \n\nI would suggest reaching out to the carsharing operations team. They would be able to generate an invoice for the fine so the customer would be able to pay with a bank transfer instead. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T10:49:46.043Z"],["3798436","PFI-831294","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:627121e402e1c10069bc7e0c],\n\nThis user has created multiple different accounts which are all attached to one device.\nDue to this suspicious behavior the voucher has been removed.\nMost common scenario is, that the voucher has already been used, after which the user creates another account in attempts to use the voucher there as well.\n*Kindly note that the information above is internal and must not be passed onto the user.*\n\nDue to this irregular activitiy, this voucher will not be available for the user.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-09T10:49:55.837Z"],["3798443","LSS-57924","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed documents attached!\n\n[^Summary (4).pdf]\n[^Service Agreement Annex 2_Bolt Support Services BG EOOD__Motion Arts_ Ltd._31.10.25.pdf]\n[^Service Agreement Annex 1_Bolt Support Services BG EOOD__Motion Arts_ Ltd._31.10.25.pdf]\n[^Service Agreement (Договор 2852)_Bolt Support Services BG EOOD__Motion Arts_ Ltd._31.10.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T10:51:17.700Z"],["3798447","PFI-831344","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-09T10:51:49.242Z"],["3798449","LSS-56382","LSS","vitaliia.hrabova@bolt.eu","Vitaliia Hrabova","[~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] Hey! Could you please send the revised contract with this amendments ti share with the partner?","2026-01-09T10:51:54.806Z"],["3798451","WFM-9921","WFM","khritina.batova@bolt-outsource.eu","Khritina Batova","*Agent Site:* [Teleperformance - Czech Republic - Pardubice]","2026-01-09T10:52:07.644Z"],["3798452","PFI-831297","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:d4d76910-741b-450c-8478-b4026441b4ae],\n\nThe user still has “Is blocked” ticked on their profile.\n\nFraud Team does not remove Hard-Blocks from the profiles, we only help in removing the device UID blocks once the investigation has been finalized and the blocks have been removed.\n\nPlease let us know once the profile has been finalized. Picture of the aforementioned tick shown below:\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 12.52.02.png|width=191,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 12.52.02.png\"!\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you,\nMarten","2026-01-09T10:52:09.626Z"],["3798453","HS-28777","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hi [~accountid:618d11745fe6c70069e888a3] \n\nWhat form exactly is needed?\n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-09T10:52:12.320Z"],["3798457","PFI-831345","PFI","kristi.purik@bolt.eu","Kristi Purik","!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 12.51.34.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T10:53:12.785Z"],["3798458","DELIVERY-1303","DELIVERY","bilal.uysal@bolt.eu","Buğra Uysal","26W01: \n\n* Working on the ListItem component in UIKit. Made a really good progress. First variant of BoltListItem is ready. Working on the second variant\n** After that, I will collect feedback from the Engineers and decide which variant to proceed with","2026-01-09T10:53:14.235Z"],["3798463","HS-28777","HS","vishnu.unnikrishnan@bolt.eu","Vishnu Unnikrishnan","Hello ,\nIts called \n{color:#172B4D}„Erklärung zum Beschäftigungsverhältnis{color}\n{color:#172B4D}Its required to be submitted to the auslanderbehorde for visa process{color}","2026-01-09T10:54:40.278Z"],["3798466","DMB-1690","DMB","raj.parekh@bolt.eu","Raj Parekh","[@nikita.koshcheev|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/612f31d8b1894f007170464c] Here is the PR [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160238|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160238] I fixed the tests for now","2026-01-09T10:55:39.862Z"],["3798467","LSS-60533","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340328?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340328?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T10:55:44.388Z"],["3798468","PFI-830808","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Greeting  \n\n  \n\nPlease, \n\nGet back with an answer{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}  \n\n  \n\n  \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n   \n\n პატივისცემით \n\n +Best Regards+ \n\n  \n\n{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#595959} -{color} {color:#595959}მირა წოწორია / Miranda{color} {color:#595959}Mira{color} {color:#595959} tsotsoria{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Customer Journey Expert{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Payments Development Tribe{color}{color:#595959}{color} \n\n[{color:#595959}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#595959}{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge/]{color:#595959}{color}{color:#595959}{color}\n !image001.png|thumbnail!{color:#595959}{color}","2026-01-09T10:55:55.203Z"],["3798469","MP-3460","MP","mirkamal.gasimov@bolt.eu","Mirkamal Gasimov","Looks ok in both dark/light modes\n\n!image-20260109-105410.png|width=353,alt=\"image-20260109-105410.png\"!\n\n!image-20260109-105545.png|width=353,alt=\"image-20260109-105545.png\"!","2026-01-09T10:55:58.724Z"],["3798473","LSS-60701","LSS","svajunas.aliukonis@bolt.eu","Svajūnas Aliukonis","Hi, [~accountid:64083c924307e46ad14725d6] have taken over this deal, I think he has created another ticket and this one needs to be cancelled because there were some changes. Could You please update","2026-01-09T10:56:53.226Z"],["3798476","LSS-61303","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340332|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340332|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T10:57:45.874Z"],["3798479","PFI-810220","PFI","amina.hemed@bolt.eu","Amina Juma Hemed","Hi [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] , kindly check this payment link \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/paymentData/view/242880078?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Africa%2FDar_es_Salaam|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/paymentData/view/242880078?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Africa%2FDar_es_Salaam] ","2026-01-09T10:58:16.092Z"],["3798481","PFI-828876","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have confirmed with pawapay the refund has been issued to the customer. \nPlease find the proof of refund attached. \n\n\n\n[^payout_TLV922H30R.pdf]\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T10:59:00.964Z"],["3798482","RDS-688","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:5b306883ed67e12dd27645e1] I like that a lot!","2026-01-09T10:59:09.793Z"],["3798483","LSS-60746","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey Central Legal Team!\n\nLooping you into this ticket for visibility, as this is a topic that may be relevant at a central level. The relevant category is already enabled in Malta, but our [legal guidance |https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-36226]at the time was that a dedicated policy should be prepared - and the team now aims to put that policy in place.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions, and feel free to add any comments or recommendations.\n\nThanks!\n\n[~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] [~accountid:62722e092db308007024a425] [~accountid:612f31d89976c300693ebaf7] [~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c] ","2026-01-09T10:59:20.682Z"],["3798486","LSS-47893","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Complete_with_Docusign_BOLT_Operations_NDA_-.pdf] ","2026-01-09T10:59:58.632Z"],["3798487","RDS-1074","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:d2a0e53f-83a4-4e81-aebd-74db6f57d6fa] OK, so which of these features are we building, and which not?","2026-01-09T11:00:24.985Z"],["3798489","PFI-830803","PFI","tasneem.ngophaiwan@bolt.eu","Tasneem Ngophaiwan","Hi [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] [~accountid:712020:fb23b49d-78e5-4590-8cdb-51ed81a45ff0] \nI think the client does not receive the receipt. ","2026-01-09T11:00:48.227Z"],["3798490","PFI-828871","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 121.00 ZAR on 08/12/2025, 09:06:38UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 8th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-09T11:01:29.202Z"],["3798491","CRC-2036","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Researching the onboarding process to the cash drop-off networks in some EEA markets. ","2026-01-09T11:01:37.185Z"],["3798492","SREP-1030","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* EKS upgraded \n* Kube-proxy bumped \n* Nodes reprovisioned \n* !image-20260109-110059.png|width=630,alt=\"image-20260109-110059.png\"!\n\nOverall no issue so far (only noise in channel from k8s-event-logger, bumped by [~accountid:712020:2cde92b6-43a3-4918-af4e-3ec327398c59] 🙇‍♂️ ) ","2026-01-09T11:01:42.023Z"],["3798493","C3HW-99","C3HW","endrik.salak@bolt.eu","Endrik Salak","I have given the modified IOTs to [~accountid:5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] ","2026-01-09T11:02:04.685Z"],["3798494","PFI-817535","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, \n\nReissued the stament + SF invoice for November; and all the Ride invoices in November; if there’s anythign else, please, provide links to the Billing Documents/Orders.","2026-01-09T11:02:35.361Z"],["3798495","CRC-2322","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Scheduled work for scoping implementation estimation in January 2026.","2026-01-09T11:02:48.028Z"],["3798497","FRAUDOPS-286","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","aggregated data:\n\n{code:sql}WITH unpaid_rides AS (\nWITH negative_corrections AS (\nSELECT DISTINCT\ntpr.order_try_id,\ntpr.city_id,\ntpr.price*-1 AS correction_amount\nFROM ng_public_spark.company_order_try_price_row tpr\nWHERE tpr.created_date >= date '2025-09-01'\nAND tpr.type = 'correction'\nAND COALESCE(tpr.price, 0) < 0\n)\nSELECT DISTINCT \nCASE\n      WHEN :Timeframe = 'week' THEN DATE_FORMAT(DATE_TRUNC('week', ot.created), 'yyyy-MM-dd')\n      WHEN :Timeframe = 'month' THEN DATE_FORMAT(DATE_TRUNC('month', ot.created), 'yyyy-MM')\nEND AS timeframe,\ni.meta.order_id AS order_id,\ni.meta.city_id, \ni.meta.country AS country,\nCAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.query.price_info.actual_price_eur') AS REAL) AS actual_price_eur,\not.ride_price/x.rate AS final_driver_price_eur,\n(CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.query.price_info.actual_price_eur') AS REAL) - ot.ride_price/x.rate)*0.25 AS estimated_commission_lost_eur,\not.driver_id,\nget_json_object(i.input,'$.data.order.payment_method.type') AS payment_method_type,\nCASE WHEN nc.correction_amount/CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.prediction_info.price') AS REAL) > 0.7 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS correction_alone_lowered_the_price,\nCASE WHEN pr.order_id IS NOT NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS had_pr_with_unpaid_reasons\nFROM sel_fraud_checks_pii_spark.driver_overcharge_check i\nJOIN ng_public_spark.company_order_try ot ON i.meta.order_id = ot.order_id AND i.meta.city_id = ot.city_id \nJOIN negative_corrections nc ON nc.order_try_id = ot.id AND nc.city_id = ot.city_id \nLEFT JOIN ng_public_spark.price_review_price_review pr ON pr.order_id = ot.order_id AND pr.city_id = ot.city_id AND pr.created_date >= date '2025-09-01' AND (pr.finished_reason IN ('client_underpaid','auto_client_did_not_pay','client_did_not_pay','auto_client_underpaid') OR pr.requested_reason IN ('client_underpaid','client_did_not_pay'))\nLEFT JOIN ng_public_spark.vw_currency_exchange_rates AS x ON DATE(x.valid_on) = DATE(ot.created) AND x.currency = ot.price_currency\nWHERE i.created_date >= date '2025-09-01'\nAND ot.created_date >= date '2025-09-01'\nAND ot.state = 'finished'\nAND ((ROUND(\n  2 * 6371000 * ASIN(\n    SQRT(\n      POW(SIN( (RADIANS(CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.driver_location.arrived_to_destination.lat') AS DOUBLE)\n                           - CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.client_location.destination.lat') AS DOUBLE)))/2 ), 2)\n      + COS(RADIANS(CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.client_location.destination.lat') AS DOUBLE)))\n        * COS(RADIANS(CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.driver_location.arrived_to_destination.lat') AS DOUBLE)))\n        * POW(SIN( (RADIANS(CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.driver_location.arrived_to_destination.lng') AS DOUBLE)\n                           - CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.client_location.destination.lng') AS DOUBLE)))/2 ), 2)\n    )\n  ),\n  0\n) <= 300)) -- real destination vs requested destination < 300 meters\n-- OR CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.actual_info.duration_in_min') AS REAL)/CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.prediction_info.duration_in_min') AS REAL) >= 0.7 -- at least 70% of predicted duration passed\n-- OR CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.actual_info.distance_in_meters') AS REAL)/CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.prediction_info.distance_in_meters') AS REAL) >= 0.7) -- at least 70% of predicted distance driven\nAND ot.ride_price/CAST(get_json_object(i.input,'$.data.prediction_info.price') AS REAL) < 0.3\n)\nSELECT \nu.timeframe,\nu.country,\nu.payment_method_type,\nu.correction_alone_lowered_the_price,\nu.had_pr_with_unpaid_reasons,\nCOUNT(DISTINCT u.order_id) AS count_orders,\nCOUNT(DISTINCT u.driver_id) AS count_drivers,\nROUND(SUM(u.actual_price_eur),0) AS sum_actual_price_eur,\nROUND(SUM(u.final_driver_price_eur),0) AS sum_final_driver_price_eur,\nROUND(SUM(u.estimated_commission_lost_eur),0) AS sum_estimated_commission_lost_eur\nFROM unpaid_rides u\nGROUP BY 1,2,3,4,5{code}","2026-01-09T11:02:50.912Z"],["3798498","SREP-1031","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* EKS upgraded\n* Kube-proxy bumped\n* Nodes reprovisioned\n\n!image-20260109-110251.png|width=654,alt=\"image-20260109-110251.png\"!\n\n\n\nNo issues so far ","2026-01-09T11:02:57.488Z"],["3798499","LSS-59324","LSS","tasneem.ngophaiwan@bolt.eu","Tasneem Ngophaiwan","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] \n\nUnfortunately, the client does not want to continue with the Ridebooker meaning that there is no need to sign contract. \n\nThank you very much for your support. \n","2026-01-09T11:02:57.784Z"],["3798511","PFI-817535","PFI","jasmina.vaclavkova@bolt.eu","Jasmina Vaclavkova","Thank you dear Artem. 🙏 ","2026-01-09T11:04:24.987Z"],["3798514","LSS-61233","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (09.01)*+\n\n* Streaming features are driver features that are calculated near real-time (recalculated every minute, and use last 15 and 60 mins of history). They all relate to order try rejection and acceptance rate. “_All the other features the model uses are not driver-specific and relate either to the order or general marketplace conditions_”.\n\n*Streaming features*\n\n{{# driver last 15 min activity }}\n{{'last_15_min_driver_did_not_respond_num', }}\n{{'last_15_min_driver_rejected_num', 'last_15_min_offer_rejected_num', }}\n{{'last_15_min_finished_num', }}\n{{'last_15_min_accepted_num', }}\n{{'last_15_min_client_did_not_show_num', }}\n{{'last_15_total_ot_num', }}\n{{'last_15_min_driver_did_not_respond_share', }}\n{{'last_15_min_offer_rejected_share', }}\n{{'last_15_min_driver_rejected_share', }}\n{{'last_15_min_driver_did_not_respond_and_offer_rejected_share',  }}\n----\n{{# driver last 60 min activity }}\n{{'last_60_min_driver_did_not_respond_num', }}\n{{'last_60_min_driver_rejected_num', }}\n{{'last_60_min_offer_rejected_num', }}\n{{'last_60_min_finished_num', }}\n{{'last_60_min_accepted_num', }}\n{{'last_60_min_client_did_not_show_num', }}\n{{'last_60_total_ot_num', }}\n{{'last_60_min_driver_did_not_respond_share', }}\n{{'last_60_min_offer_rejected_share', }}\n{{'last_60_min_driver_rejected_share', }}\n{{'last_60_min_driver_did_not_respond_and_offer_rejected_share'}}\n\n* Deprioritisation is only for short intervals. Drivers would be back to normal in the queue after X time (15/50/60mins, depending on configuration in the market).\n* Business has been advised on both the test and final feature here ([LINK|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02N479PM9T/p1767959998921519?thread_ts=1767795871.743879&cid=C02N479PM9T]).\n** Main outstanding Q is whether this will impact driver earnings (unlikely, but worth asking the question since this is a sensitive topic). If not, then we can argue it does not have a significant effect, and we should be fine to roll out.\n** Otherwise, we will need to internally complete a LIA/DPIA/AIA.","2026-01-09T11:05:07.983Z"],["3798515","PFI-827379","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","ETA for now is 23.01, while working on it, ENGs might have somme additional questions which I’ll raise it here in order to confirm with you.\n\nRegarding Dec monthly invoices generated in January, since the law was live starting from 01.01 it shouldn’t affect the Dec invoices but Jan invoices (be generated in Feb) will reflect the changes.","2026-01-09T11:05:11.039Z"],["3798516","LSS-60050","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] ! I actually checked one more time and Dokobit shows that both signatures are valid, so maybe it was jsut an Adobe trouble\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 13.05.10.png|width=494,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 13.05.10.png\"!\n\n\n\nPlease find the second signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Zawiadomienia o przelewie Alior AR1 (1)-kopia (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T11:05:20.415Z"],["3798517","PFI-828870","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nYou can provide the user the acquirer reference {{017523212476065}} to locate the payment with their bank. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-09T11:05:23.664Z"],["3798518","LSS-56382","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:639b104bf134138b5a515e5b] hey Vitaliia, in order for me to make the final amendments, please confirm re the answers re my below questions:\n\nClauses Re 27 and 28 (refunds) - the partner wanted to sign separate acts for each case, but as this is not practical, I can just indicate that these amounts will be reflected in the agent report that we sent to the partner. *Please confirm this is fine for the partner.*\n\nClause 32 - *please let me know if we can accept this from the business side.*","2026-01-09T11:05:31.225Z"],["3798519","WEBSD-1459","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi 👋 \n\nI think all should be fine now.\n\n[https://bolt.eu/en-fr/driver/guide/offers/|https://bolt.eu/en-fr/driver/guide/offers/|smart-link] \n\nRegards,","2026-01-09T11:05:40.341Z"],["3798521","FX-3587","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Ernests Rudzītis [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767956733849559]*{color}:\nThis option is also present in regular car application form\n{quote}","2026-01-09T11:05:50.498Z"],["3798522","TA-263","TA","jorick.polderman@bolt.eu","Jorick Thijs Polderman","Not recommend to move forward:\n\n* *Time to value:* It takes a lot of time to train and fine-tune the search, and even after adjustments we’re still not getting the quality of results we need.\n* *Inconsistent result limits:* Some users were limited in how many results they could retrieve, and the controls to adjust the assistant’s settings were buried and not intuitive to find.\n* *Location accuracy:* It doesn’t handle location-specific criteria well, even when prompts are explicit and detailed.\n* *Weak LinkedIn integration:* It isn’t tightly integrated with LinkedIn workflows—for example, we still have to manually copy/paste job descriptions into prompts.\n* *Hiring impact:* We haven’t made a single hire through it to date.\n* *Outbound quality:* The personalization for outbound messaging isn’t at the level we expect.\n* *Best fit seems limited:* It feels better suited to lower-priority roles, where you can accept less precision and spend less time training the assistant.","2026-01-09T11:05:51.750Z"],["3798523","PFI-828845","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team is unfortunately not able to assist with pricing, discount or promo code related questions. \nPricing is decided by the vertical and the customer payments team does not have any impact on it. \nCould you please raise a ticket with the verticals technical support team instead. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2]\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-09T11:05:53.821Z"],["3798524","PFI-828833","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-09T11:06:07.168Z"],["3798525","PFI-828821","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-09T11:06:22.474Z"],["3798526","LSS-59947","LSS","petr.kratky@bolt.eu","Petr Krátký","Please, close the ticket. thank you","2026-01-09T11:06:24.642Z"],["3798528","LSS-61277","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] ! The documents will be ready shortly.","2026-01-09T11:06:49.829Z"],["3798529","DSO-43","DSO","martin.schmidt@bolt.eu","Martin Schmidt","Deprioritized in 2026, we will not be able to commit to changes on the release process. We still plan to make changes to the picker app, based on BDM feedback. But it will be reactive, and we won't be able to commit to running proactive discovery on potential further improvements.","2026-01-09T11:06:53.354Z"],["3798530","PFI-831280","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! There was a tablet rent adjustment made on 12th of December, hence why there was an invoice. This adjustment is applied by the local team, so I’m not sure if this was intentional or not, maybe you can advise here? \n\nRegarding the payout, it seems like the last payouts have failed, so Partner Payments team is able to help with that (the team that you created the previous ticket to) ","2026-01-09T11:06:55.760Z"],["3798531","PFI-828812","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 111.12 ZAR on 23/11/2025, 14:05:13UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 23rd of November until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-09T11:07:03.944Z"],["3798532","WEBSD-1445","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi 👋 \n\nAll the changes should be there.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-09T11:07:10.460Z"],["3798534","PFI-830803","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","All invoices are available in the Admin. For the Monthly Statements/Invoices/SF Invoices, please, find those in the Invoices tab in the Business Invoicing Admin Panel. For the Ride Invoices, it’s possible to find Order links, when filtering via Claims in the Balance Entries Tab.\n\nIf there’s Invoice for the Ride/Monthly Invoice missing from there, please, provide links and I’d be happy to help","2026-01-09T11:07:30.342Z"],["3798537","PFI-828799","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-09T11:07:41.867Z"],["3798539","PFI-830803","PFI","pakrampar.silrapasangchai@bolt.eu","Pakrampar Silrapasangchai","Hi team, \n\nYes, I mean the receipt is the same as [~accountid:712020:e9966afc-8926-48fe-bacc-f9daa6118aad] said. Sorry for the inconvenience. 🙏 ","2026-01-09T11:07:53.624Z"],["3798542","MVRT-1446","MVRT","lorrayne.oliveira@bolt.eu","Lorrayne Corais","* Push notifications created, proofread and approved by language specialist. (/) \n*Note*: Push notification 5 still missing the price. \n* Waiting for the new email templates to start working on it. :loading: ","2026-01-09T11:07:59.115Z"],["3798544","SUPX-2312","SUPX","artem.kudlaienko@bolt.eu","Artem Kudlaienko","Spike in interaction_invalidated support-case-update-event backlog after bulk case closure, we should increase SQS consumer parallelism","2026-01-09T11:09:16.326Z"],["3798546","SUPX-2312","SUPX",null,"Slack","[Artem Kudlaienko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/630e0b9a9796033b256bd3a5] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C061Q2ULEU8/p1767956911078929?thread_ts=1767956018.163269&cid=C061Q2ULEU8|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C061Q2ULEU8/p1767956911078929?thread_ts=1767956018.163269&cid=C061Q2ULEU8|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-09T11:09:17.619Z"],["3798547","PFI-831344","PFI","pakrampar.silrapasangchai@bolt.eu","Pakrampar Silrapasangchai","continue conversation in the previous SD: PFI-830803.","2026-01-09T11:10:00.132Z"],["3798548","PFI-831344","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T11:10:03.527Z"],["3798549","LSS-47893","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","thanks ! [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-09T11:10:19.711Z"],["3798550","WFM-9911","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, you should be able to filter tickets now","2026-01-09T11:11:01.573Z"],["3798552","WFM-9911","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Please let me know if you can filter now","2026-01-09T11:11:27.684Z"],["3798562","LSS-61277","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bank confirmation letter Standard Chartered Bank Ghana PLC (Bolt Holdings OU).pdf]\n[^Bank confirmation letter Standard Chartered Bank Ghana PLC (Bolt Holdings OU (Ghana branch)).pdf]\n[^Bank confirmation letter PayPal (Bolt Operations OU).pdf]\n[^Bank confirmation letter PawaPay (Bolt Operations OU).pdf]\n[^Bank confirmation letter Goldman Sachs (Bolt Holdings OU).pdf]\n[^Bank confirmation letter Citigroup Inc (Bolt Operations OU).pdf]\n[^Bank confirmation letter BNP Paribas S.A., Bankfilial Sverige  (Bolt Technology OU).pdf]\n[^Bank confirmation letter Black Rock (Bolt Holdings OU).pdf]\n[^Bank confirmation letter Bank of Georgia Group PLC (Bolt Operations OU).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T11:12:56.373Z"],["3798564","PFI-828754","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe negative balance is correct. \nThe user had two order attempts. \n\nFirst one happened on 01/01/2026, 01:39, but the booking was cancelled. The payment was successful. However, since the booking was cancelled then the funds were returned to the customer. Since BLIK is an alternative payment method then it doesn’t support authorization + capture. There is just Capture. If the payment is cancelled we issue a refund. \n\nThe second attempt on 01/01/2026, 02:12 the order was successful, but the Blik payment method failed. Since the payment failed it caused a negative balance for the user. \n\nThe order amount was 58 PLN and the user had a previous negative balance of 1.33 PLN. Total for the negative balance is 59.33 PLN. \n\nPlease ask the user to top up their balance or cover the debt with their next order. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T11:13:10.773Z"],["3798567","LSS-61177","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[^Bolt Operations NDA (Mutual) templ_PAVE Europe.pdf]\n\nhi [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] please sign by Ahto today !","2026-01-09T11:13:25.148Z"],["3798568","LSS-60104","LSS","darius.poursiami@bolt.eu","Darius Poursiami","Hey [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85], is there any way we can keep the date the contract comes into effect flexible?","2026-01-09T11:14:32.249Z"],["3798572","PFI-807476","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Dear Bolt{color:#172B4D},{color}\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI've attached the file for the chargeback for Nove