4D}0.00{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}36,772,072.13{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}354.00{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}0.00{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} | \n|{color:#172B4D}December{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}Bolt Support Services (Thailand) Limited{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}THB{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}352,257{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}11{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}0.00{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}37,607,908.68{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}2,206.00{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}0.01{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} | \n|{color:#172B4D}TOTAL{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}4,158,863{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}94{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}0.00{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}375,351,288.32{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}321,335.22{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |{color:#172B4D}0.09{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} |\n\n[^Bolt 202511-12.xlsx] _(14 kB)_","2026-01-09T11:15:17.089Z"],["3798574","LSS-61179","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:9cfda827-f644-48a1-9da8-aff3fd427bf9] ,\n\nThank you for raising this ticket. And thank you [~accountid:5a670f010c10ac2e28964251] for the additional context.\n\nLegal view is the following:\n\n*Re reclassification risk:*\n\nThe key legal concern here is the potential for reclassification of couriers into employees, if the jackets are seen as a reward or benefit provided directly by Bolt in exchange for performance.\n\nHowever, based on what was described:\n\n* The initiative is routed entirely via the fleet, not directly by Bolt.\n* Fleets define and manage the selection based on their own performance criteria.\n* Bolt is simply providing material (jackets) in a pass-through manner, with no direct courier communication of incentive or reward.\n\nAs long as Bolt is not perceived as evaluating or rewarding individual courier performance, the reclassification risk remains low.\n\n*Re courier communication, my advice would be:*\n\nIdeally the messages shouldn’t be sent to couriers. However, if the team wants to move forward with this, our advice is:\n\n# The message should clearly state that:\n\n* The jackets are distributed by the fleet;\n* The criteria are set and applied by the fleet;\n* Bolt is not selecting who receives jackets nor evaluating courier performance;\n* This is not part of any employment or contractual reward system.\n\n# This should not framed as an “incentive” or “reward” program by Bolt. Instead, it should be presented as a material support provided to fleets, which may choose to distribute it to couriers based on their own internal criteria.\n\nPlease let us know if you have any additional question.\n\nThank you!\n\n\n\ncc: [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03] ","2026-01-09T11:16:01.059Z"],["3798575","PFI-831297","PFI","afonso.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu","Afonso Fernandes","Hi [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] Thank you very much for the feedback, I inform you that this option is already deactivated!","2026-01-09T11:16:01.938Z"],["3798576","PFI-828722","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nMy apologies for a delayed response! \nI can see the user has placed a cash order since this ticket was escalated. \n\nPlease let me know if the user is still having any issues and I will take another look. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T11:16:16.468Z"],["3798577","PFI-830195","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","This payment is not to be found please reach out the partner to check with their bank !","2026-01-09T11:17:00.526Z"],["3798579","URRIK-2715","URRIK","akram.yacob@bolt.eu","Akram Yacob","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zimZSX7HjAEZNAZur1IL0x0Sp95EZOKWrcvgxRMDZRE/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zimZSX7HjAEZNAZur1IL0x0Sp95EZOKWrcvgxRMDZRE/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] reviewed and advised by Kristina","2026-01-09T11:17:30.724Z"],["3798580","PFI-810265","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Checking for any updates with dLocal","2026-01-09T11:17:44.796Z"],["3798581","FX-3587","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767957468787569]*{color}:\ncan you show me where sorry? for fleet adding a car I don't see any 'delete my car' or anything\n{quote}","2026-01-09T11:18:01.932Z"],["3798588","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767957547394289]*{color}:\n<@U04FV4Z0GQ4> can you confirm if we have the possibility to proceed with your suggestion, if yes it would be very helpful and potentially unblock some very financial and compliance issues we are facing here on the ground.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T11:19:21.930Z"],["3798589","PFI-830940","PFI","samuel.ojo@bolt.eu","Samuel Ojo","[~accountid:712020:7f456fc3-1ae4-4f6a-923a-a0a2d2ef5030] Let’s escalate to *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [+Link+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]","2026-01-09T11:19:28.371Z"],["3798590","LSS-60691","LSS","dominik.lopuch@bolt.eu","Dominik Lopuch","Hi [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] the last update from yesterday 8 Jan is that due to christmas holidays there were not able to take a look at it. Partner will do so next week. Please remain the ticket open, thanks.","2026-01-09T11:19:29.626Z"],["3798593","SCM-803","SCM","federico.levi@bolt.eu","Federico Levi","[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] \nHello, i’ve been slowed down by the Allocation dashboard formulas fix.\nWill need to work on it this+next week!\nSprint set for Monday afternoon → Tuesday Morning\n\nWill bring updates then","2026-01-09T11:20:05.440Z"],["3798596","LSS-55043","LSS","triin.soonkoster@bolt.eu","Triin Soon-Köster","Thank you! Will notify the partner.","2026-01-09T11:21:06.261Z"],["3798597","RS-1938","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hello! \n\nThank you for submitting your request. \n\nAs discussed on Slack, I have scheduled time for this next week.\n\nThank you for your patience!\n\nKadi ","2026-01-09T11:21:47.252Z"],["3798599","PFI-831118","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, invoice reissued","2026-01-09T11:22:14.494Z"],["3798600","SCM-803","SCM","federico.levi@bolt.eu","Federico Levi","ETA moved to {{2026-01-16}}","2026-01-09T11:22:18.866Z"],["3798602","PFI-828704","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the user was refunded for UAH 474.00 on Jan 2, 2026, 23:20:40 GMT+2. Please find the refund letter attached. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_BCP2BVVP6F25DWG6_ZCG9W4GB36WVRBG6.pdf]\n\nPlease note the order of the transactions on the customers mobile banking app depends on how users bank processes them. \nIt seems like the customers bank were able to process the refund before the capture transaction. \n\nEverything seems fine on Bolt’s end. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T11:22:26.553Z"],["3798603","WFM-9916","WFM","ana.radmilo@bolt.eu","Ana Radmilo","Hi, I'm not sure if Imer has been assigned the Team Lead role, since he has been added to the 11 EX_Croatia_External Checks queue, but he can’t see the performance overview. Could you please check? Thank you!\n\n","2026-01-09T11:22:30.920Z"],["3798604","PAW-14754","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/autocode/pull/51\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-09 11:22:36 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-09T11:22:36.899Z"],["3798606","LSS-59324","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","I’m sorry to hear that! Appreciate your feedback.\n\nWishing you a lovely upcoming weekend!","2026-01-09T11:23:17.188Z"],["3798607","PFI-831323","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Link to the BUsiness Account is missing. Please, provide it.","2026-01-09T11:23:33.654Z"],["3798609","LSS-61234","LSS","jack.cook@bolt.eu","Jack Cook","Yep that works thanks Julia 👍 ","2026-01-09T11:23:49.969Z"],["3798610","RDXENG-3425","RDXENG","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","Request here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CND9AL5LY/p1767957763536799|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CND9AL5LY/p1767957763536799|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T11:24:24.816Z"],["3798611","HS-28804","HS","magdalena.jesiotr@bolt.eu","Magdalena Jesiotr","[^Świadectwa pracy- Magda Jesiotr .pdf]\n\n[^Zaświadczenie o ukończeniu studiów.pdf]","2026-01-09T11:25:31.862Z"],["3798613","DRAG-686","DRAG","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","There was an issue that the new version of the controller “U2”, which is also a UL compliant controller had incorrect MCU in its schematic which is not compatible with the UL version controller.\n\nFortunately, the mistake was in schematic only and the actual samples and the testing was done with correct MCU.\n\nGenfo fixed the schematics and the schematics are now up to date.","2026-01-09T11:25:46.700Z"],["3798614","PFI-821653","PFI","nikita.bogomazovs@bolt-outsource.eu","Nikita Bogomazovs","Hey! How’s the progress? ","2026-01-09T11:26:10.834Z"],["3798616","IOTTEAM-219","IOTTEAM","endrik.salak@bolt.eu","Endrik Salak","Needed changes:\n\n* Swap ESP Rx and Tx pins on the tag-connect pads.\n* Specify the exact part number of the LTE modem as *EG800KEULC* since it allows for PPP functionality in the modem, enabling access to the internet.\n* Change net name GNSS_VCC_DIS to GNSS_VCC_EN to create functional clarity.\n* For TAS2505IRGER remove I2S_DOUT connection, and use I2S_DIN instead.\n* IMU U14 pin 5 VDDIO must be connected to MAIN_3V3. It is currently not connected to any supply rail.\n* LED changes:\n** Change resistors R37, R38, R39 values to 62R to increase LED current.\n** Make the LED D17 supply switchable through FETs.\n** Move LED control pins from IO Expander to MCU pins 27, 47, 51.\n*** EXT_IO_INT net on pin 27 will be deleted from the design. This pin is not needed.\n*** LTE_STATUS net on pin 51 will be moved to IO Expander\n*** Pin 47 is currently free to use and should be used for LED control signal\n* Audio amplifier U17 needs to have a 10k pull-down resistor added to pin 2 RST, net TSA_RST. Remove pull-up resistor R68. \n* Change main regulator feedback resistor R2 value from 240k to 215k to yield ~4.5V output voltage of the main regulator. This is due to the LTE modem’s maximum functional voltage being 4.3V. The voltage to the LTE modem supply is provided through a diode power MUX. Taking the diode voltage drop into account, the LTE modem will receive around 4.25V.\n* Make sure the USB line vias are surrounded by GND copper for shielding purposes:\n!image-20260112-131741.png|width=519,alt=\"image-20260112-131741.png\"!","2026-01-09T11:26:12.562Z"],["3798617","PFI-831323","PFI","patryk.flakowski@bolt.eu","Patryk Flakowski","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/336593?tab=business_company|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/336593?tab=business_company]","2026-01-09T11:26:17.783Z"],["3798618","LSS-61330","LSS","kertu.hiet@bolt.eu","Kertu Hiet","[^Bolt's PO_bags_Azerbaijan_JAN 2 6.xlsx - PO_AZ_JAN26 (1) Stamped.pdf] _(136 kB)_\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 13.25.49.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T11:26:30.427Z"],["3798620","SCM-799","SCM","federico.levi@bolt.eu","Federico Levi","[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] \nManaged to have this working via AppScript! today’s morning test worked!\n\nI will try and see how to implement it into the dashboard - ETA moved to {{2026-01-16}}","2026-01-09T11:26:48.717Z"],["3798623","SCM-803","SCM","federico.levi@bolt.eu","Federico Levi","replied above","2026-01-09T11:27:22.043Z"],["3798626","LSS-60104","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey [~accountid:712020:6f563341-b27c-4653-b7d4-c67e881cc931] - I believe so yes, the wording can state that the agreement becomes effective as of the last signature or something along these lines.","2026-01-09T11:28:27.887Z"],["3798627","RDS-1074","RDS","vivaksha.singh@bolt.eu","Vivaksha Singh","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] Now we are working on building the requirement to prioritise this specific fleet drivers from city to airport. \n\nThis functionality is also needed by Thailand, and could possibly be expanded to other markets, where we prioritise high performing drivers to airport…i.e. it can also be introduced as one of the rewards in loyalty program. Did discuss this with [~accountid:712020:9db8be0f-eb61-4ebc-bac7-a9563c14e4b0]  also.\n\nThe way matching can prioritise is by giving ETA boosts i.e. in a driver queue for an order, if there were 2 drivers D1(non fleet, 3 mins eta), D2(fleet driver, 4 mins ETA) : in this scenario order will go to D1 first, for priority : we can configure to give 2 mins ETA priority/boost to this “selected group” of drivers i.e. in the queue D2 eta would be read as 2 mins, and D1 ; same as before 3 mins, so now queue is (D2 :2mins, D1:3 mins), so now the order would be dispatched to D2 first. \n\nWe are currently in process to determine how much “ETA boost” we should give while balancing rider cancellation due to increased ETAs. Goal 1(immediate goal) would be to optimise for higher orders to this group of drivers without hurting O2F. \n\nGoal 2 : long term would be to figure out the gain we get by prioritizing these drivers, i.e. other than immediate acceptance rates, their loyalty and high quality on platform also are gains. How can we calculate this gain value, feed into the model to say in short term we can compromise “x” rider cancellation gate to have this long term gain. \n\nGoal 1, we plan to have first POC by end of Jan and we will continue building on that. ","2026-01-09T11:28:40.490Z"],["3798628","CAMLE-9415","CAMLE","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","status update [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A7QN72NG2/p1767957627617229]","2026-01-09T11:28:45.498Z"],["3798630","MAB-229","MAB","balaji.senthilkumar@bolt.eu","Balaji Senthilkumar","Shared the list of accounts which has been activated in the last two months, for which we are missing out Sales manger name.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1m3qtWhyMJO5aEUL-alibWSxyBwGvfRSp9sD0sntFw6c/edit?gid=179579756#gid=179579756|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1m3qtWhyMJO5aEUL-alibWSxyBwGvfRSp9sD0sntFw6c/edit?gid=179579756#gid=179579756|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T11:29:08.365Z"],["3798632","PFI-831354","PFI","wojciech.nawracala@bolt-outsource.eu","Wojciech Nawracala","[^58198743_82974.pdf]","2026-01-09T11:29:26.015Z"],["3798634","HS-28745","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","Wonderful! The document is currently being signed. You will receive a copy to your personal email immediately after it’s done. I have separately reminded the responsible person to prioritise this. \n\nHope everything goes well with your license renewal! \n\nBest\nAlice","2026-01-09T11:29:52.356Z"],["3798635","DSR-3467","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","Also forwarding the response from UK Case Managers. The driver will not be reinstated.\n\n[^Milton Keynes - Termination - Zain-Al-Abidin Hussain - C0502.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T11:30:10.520Z"],["3798638","PFI-830647","PFI","laura.loaiza@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Muñoz","Hello [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] , where can we see the invoice for the previous services? It is not reflected in the business account [~accountid:712020:53555a79-b384-46b1-8f21-2b13cb2c655a] was it possible for you to find those invoices? This is a really odd case. How can we justify to the company the charge without an invoice? ","2026-01-09T11:30:57.503Z"],["3798643","GDEXP-876","GDEXP","brindusa.niculae@bolt.eu","Brîndușa Niculae","results: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049HKSJX51/p1766504361373759|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049HKSJX51/p1766504361373759|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T11:32:04.567Z"],["3798644","GDEXP-471","GDEXP","brindusa.niculae@bolt.eu","Brîndușa Niculae","results: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049HKSJX51/p1767876846717609|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049HKSJX51/p1767876846717609|smart-link] \nalso here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07JF0EPY2Z/p1767882005072469|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07JF0EPY2Z/p1767882005072469|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T11:32:17.648Z"],["3798645","LSS-60426","LSS","laman.huseynova@bolt.eu","Laman Huseynova","Hi Liivika!\n\nThe client has not replied yet, but for now, yes the ticket can be closed.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T11:32:58.227Z"],["3798646","HS-28306","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:dc0e5673-b376-43a7-acc2-defd031fd9cf],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-09T11:33:00.456Z"],["3798647","LSS-61316","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Hi [~accountid:5cefa7d5c32afb0f1eb85f25] please see below the link to the annex with my revisions. Please also check Annex 1 to confirm  its terms (list of services, price, payment term etc.) correspond to the commercial agreements. \n\n[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] can you please also check the draft as we need to indicate the correct name of the trademark and provide the logo example?\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ri4ZjB1_YygjfZNMsJ5iEAZ9QeRTgiN4rfvFUXWCA5E/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ri4ZjB1_YygjfZNMsJ5iEAZ9QeRTgiN4rfvFUXWCA5E/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T11:33:07.562Z"],["3798648","PFI-831297","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hey [~accountid:712020:d4d76910-741b-450c-8478-b4026441b4ae],\n\nCheers for getting back to me and notifying.\nThe device UID suspensions have now been lifted.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-09T11:33:12.976Z"],["3798649","HS-28697","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-09T11:33:13.710Z"],["3798650","LSS-61333","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nAnna Surga has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-09T11:33:44.555Z"],["3798651","WEB-7906","WEB","vishal.kapoor@bolt.eu","Vishal Kapoor","Hi [~accountid:63874527f6c85b343c0b7f4b] \nThe SEO tags remains the same?","2026-01-09T11:33:48.071Z"],["3798653","BDB-1494","BDB","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Yes Monday is ok, thanks!","2026-01-09T11:34:40.766Z"],["3798654","PFI-831306","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:f9063bf4-7d66-4270-b524-edfd2889c4fe]\n\nThe user still has “Is blocked” ticked on their profile.\n\nFraud Team does not remove Hard-Blocks from the profiles, we only help in removing the device UID blocks once the investigation has been finalized and the blocks have been removed.\n\nPlease let us know once the profile has been finalized. Picture of the aforementioned tick shown below:\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 13.34.24.png|width=227,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 13.34.24.png\"!\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you,\nMarten","2026-01-09T11:35:02.342Z"],["3798657","PFI-831268","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi,\n\nEC has been disabled for the aforementioned driver.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-09T11:36:01.750Z"],["3798658","PFI-831267","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi,\n\nEC has been disabled for the aforementioned driver.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-09T11:36:06.097Z"],["3798659","XP-2738","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","[~accountid:641d5e7c9796ea0a8718ca5e] one think to keep an eye out for here is that most teams set up tests through the interleaved planner tool currently","2026-01-09T11:36:53.212Z"],["3798660","CSDA-275","CSDA","laimdota.vilistere@bolt.eu","Laimdota Vilistere","How should we identify them now by tier or another method?\n\n* at the moment I can think of one method how to identify the user - from the e-mail they are writing to us. API partners use one ot two e-mails to reach out to us via e-mail. Maybe there is other method? OPS measures trips made through partner, how can they identify how many trips come from one partner? POC Tom Bishop\n\nCould you clarify how the ticket volume is expected to increase and what the main source channels for these tickets will be?\n\n* ticket volume has increased from 41 tickets  in April 2025 to 1420 tickets in December and the fastest growth happened in the last 3-4 months (Sep 299; Oct 836; Nov 1222, Dec 1420). OPS strategy focuses on new API partner onboarding and this segment will continue to grow.\n* tickets now come only from API partner e-mail to our e-mail. [apipartners@bolt-business.com|mailto:apipartners@bolt-business.com]. All API partners write to one e-mail. I need to work with Product team to develop a direct connection from Ride Booker to Beehive to eliminate the e-mail, but that depends on the product team. No ETA.\n\nRegarding the orders, have you checked with the Bolt Business team whether they can provide data or a source for both actual and forecasted orders, since this information mainly comes from the vertical?\n\n* I have requested Tom Bishop to provide details on the source and forecasting. \n\n","2026-01-09T11:37:25.425Z"],["3798661","WD-22529","WD","tatjana.ainson@bolt.eu","Tatjana Ainson","[^Bolt HTX Kft C-EE003-25-000893 2025-11-17.pdf]\n\n[^Bolt HTX Kft C-EE003-25-000974 2025-12-18.pdf]","2026-01-09T11:37:37.117Z"],["3798662","DBRE-8591","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster display ti-iot | grep tikv | awk '{print $1, $6}'\nti-iot-kv-1.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-10.sqldb:20160 Tombstone\nti-iot-kv-11.sqldb:20160 Tombstone\nti-iot-kv-12.sqldb:20160 Tombstone\nti-iot-kv-2.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-3.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-4.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-5.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-6.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-7.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-8.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-9.sqldb:20160 Up{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008779 | grep \"region_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008779\n    \"region_count\": 0,\n\nroot@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008780 | grep \"region_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008780\n    \"region_count\": 0,\n\nroot@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008781 | grep \"region_count\"\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u ti-iot-pd-2.sqldb:2379 store 9801008781\n    \"region_count\": 0,{noformat}\n\n{noformat}There are some nodes can be pruned:\n\tNodes: [ti-iot-kv-10.sqldb:20160 ti-iot-kv-11.sqldb:20160 ti-iot-kv-12.sqldb:20160]\n\tYou can destroy them with the command: `tiup cluster prune ti-iot`{noformat}\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 11.37.46.png|width=860,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 11.37.46.png\"!","2026-01-09T11:38:06.298Z"],["3798663","RDXENG-4562","RDXENG","mustafa.ogun@bolt.eu","Mustafa Ogün Öztürk","Hey [~accountid:712020:23b54a2f-1913-42e1-9019-8b2c32303d27]! You may also take over this one. I think it is good task to get to understand the address search rib.","2026-01-09T11:38:16.146Z"],["3798664","DSR-2997","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","Data downloaded and shared with the user alongside the response. Thank you!","2026-01-09T11:38:24.585Z"],["3798665","PAR-3724","PAR","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","I understand this is currently terminal state, but is there possibility to consider that it will not be a terminal state in the future and there is path of rollback to previous state instead?\nDid we set the terminal state or is this requirement coming from other teams?\n","2026-01-09T11:39:00.502Z"],["3798667","URRIK-2731","URRIK","akram.yacob@bolt.eu","Akram Yacob","From Akos\n\nNew PDI UX research on *Drivers' current contribution habits for improving navigation*\n\nAt Geo we focus on bringing proper, high quality navigation to the Driver app. To ensure that we capture all relevant live traffic information, we aim to gather user generated reports from our Drivers. We ran a survey (and received 6100+ responses across 4 cities) and conducted 17 follow-up interviews to inform our product priorities and design choices.Top 10 Insights\n\n# *Waze dominates driver navigation:* 90% of Bucharest, 89% of Lisbon, 59% of Warsaw and 61% of Johannesburg drivers use Waze daily, while only 6–13% do so with Bolt in Europe and 36% in Johannesburg.\n# *Weak traffic intelligence is a key reason to leave Bolt nav:* among drivers who prefer another navigation app, 58–64% in each European city cite “better traffic information” and ~30% cite “has user-reported events” as reasons for choosing competing navigation over Bolt. If traffic is not shown in app AND ETAs are off, perception is that there is no congestion taken into account.\n# *Live traffic events are critical:* Across all cities, 86% of drivers pay daily attention to traffic events while driving and are already used to consuming this type of information.\n# *Event reporting behavior is already strong:* 75–81% of drivers in each city say they report traffic events “often” or “always” in navigation apps, meaning the underlying behaviour we need already exists (77% Bucharest, 81% Lisbon, 77% Warsaw, 75% Johannesburg). Johannesburg stands out as more polarised – more “super-reporters” and more “never reporters”\n# *Three event types are globally critical:* “Traffic jams” are selected as one of the top three most important events by 78–87% of drivers across cities, “Accidents” by 45–73%, and “Closed roads” by 43–75%, making them the must-have core of any reporting and display system, followed by local emphasis on police presence, hazards, road works, and speed cameras.\n# What drivers *care about most* is largely what they *actually report*, which is good news: improving the UX for those event types will directly improve perceived usefulness.\n# *Safety and workload are the main blockers to reporting and confirmations:* when drivers ignore confirmation messages, 59–71% say they are “too busy driving” and 24–27% in Europe (rising to 42% in Johannesburg) say it is “unsafe” to respond while driving.\n# *Motivation is overwhelmingly pro-social, not gamified:* 78–85% of drivers in all markets report events “to help other users”, 23–37% “to make the application better for me”, while only 2–6% mention reaching a score or rank as a motivator.\n# *Reporting engagement patterns differ by city:* Warsaw and Johannesburg stand out as highly engaged markets for confirmations and reporting (44% of Warsaw and 52% of Johannesburg drivers say they “always” report or respond to confirmation messages), while Bucharest and Lisbon are more sensitive to visual distraction and workload.\n# *Misalignment between what pickup the customer sees and what the driver sees*: Drivers frequently report that pickup points are often behind the building instead of in front, inside courtyards, or on the wrong side of large complexes and do not match where the passenger actually is, leading to extra circling, calls, and cancellations. Wrong or imprecise pins placed by passengers compound this problem, but drivers still experience it as a navigation pain point.\n\nRecommended actions\n\n* Focus improvement efforts on addressing *traffic congestion, closed roads, and accidents*, as these are the most critical navigation issues for drivers.\n* Instead of trying to convert all drivers, concentrate on improving the experience and recognition for *drivers who already have reporting habits*.\n** Emphasize *altruism and reciprocity* in messaging to encourage reporting.\n** Foster a *sense of community* among drivers who contribute to keeping the app data accurate and up-to-date.\n* Design the reporting mechanism to be *safe and extremely convenient* for drivers to use, ensuring it does not interfere with driving. This includes:\n* Implementing a *simple interface* with the *fewest taps possible*.\n* Exploring options like *voice reporting*.\n* When prompting drivers to confirm traffic events, target specific low-risk moments, low speed situations and the pickup leg, before the customer is in the car.\n* Position Bolt's system as superior to generic public reporting tools (like Waze) by emphasizing:\n** The *higher trust in a Driver-to-Driver community*.\n** The ability to cater to specific driver needs, such as guidance *around the pickup location*, which competitor apps may not offer.\n\nLink to docs for more details:\n\n* Survey [results write-up|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HJ6Oy2npTDsfiXdgJzYLNqO-nyIJKRCHsmh_GGdPxZw/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.uclczeqivfq0] and [statistics|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1UbWuCf7HKVMrD99mrL2gof8T6jotupKhPWU64lu6Zag/edit?gid=1261517594#gid=1261517594]","2026-01-09T11:39:22.988Z"],["3798668","LSS-61295","LSS","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","Hello [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac], they’ve replied. Would you prefer that we keep the support ticket open so we can reply through it later when we have all the requested information?\n\n{quote}_Exmos. Srs._\n\n_Venho pelo presente informar que entretanto foi estabelecido contacto com a Dra. Catarina Faria, tendo assim sido fornecido, à Dra., mais elementos relativamente ao inquérito._\n\n_Conforme combinado com a Dra., ficamos assim a aguardar resposta da vossa parte._\n\n_Com os melhores cumprimentos,_{quote}\n\n","2026-01-09T11:39:23.468Z"],["3798669","PFI-831347","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:92de8b35-6a42-4290-a24d-a4656c69eaa7],\n\nTopping up would not be possible, since they are now in another country, therefore, deletion would be the only step.\nWe have made changes within our rules, meaning that the user can now delete their account.\nPlease keep in mind that it may take up to 1-2hours before the changes go live, once they do, you may proceed.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-09T11:39:34.369Z"],["3798670","LSS-61334","LSS","fabricia.silva@bolt.eu","Fabrícia Silva Alcântara","Please do not consider this request. \nThe fleet owner requested that the fleet be terminated next week. ","2026-01-09T11:40:15.079Z"],["3798671","PFI-821653","PFI","mariia.patrakova@bolt.eu","Masha Patrakov","Hi Nikita, our campaign analyst is still on vacation, we will update you when this has been checked.","2026-01-09T11:40:31.279Z"],["3798673","RCE-335","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767958844403959]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-335] `Define alerting channel for external checks cron` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T11:40:56.505Z"],["3798674","PFI-829474","PFI","patryk.flakowski@bolt.eu","Patryk Flakowski","# [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5991233048?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FWarsaw|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5991233048?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FWarsaw]\n# [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5991090351?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FWarsaw|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5991090351?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FWarsaw]\n\n","2026-01-09T11:41:12.522Z"],["3798675","DBRE-8591","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster prune ti-iot\n...\n+ [ Serial ] - FindTomestoneNodes\nWill destroy these nodes: [ti-iot-kv-10.sqldb:20160 ti-iot-kv-11.sqldb:20160 ti-iot-kv-12.sqldb:20160]\nDo you confirm this action? [y/N]:(default=N) y\nStart destroy Tombstone nodes: [ti-iot-kv-10.sqldb:20160 ti-iot-kv-11.sqldb:20160 ti-iot-kv-12.sqldb:20160] ...\n...\n+ [ Serial ] - RemoveTomestoneNodesInPD\nDestroy success{noformat}\n\n{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup cluster display ti-iot | grep tikv | awk '{print $1, $6}'\nti-iot-kv-1.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-2.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-3.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-4.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-5.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-6.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-7.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-8.sqldb:20160 Up\nti-iot-kv-9.sqldb:20160 Up{noformat}","2026-01-09T11:41:13.879Z"],["3798676","PFI-831300","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:f370e2a2-c96b-43e0-a40e-ca32196cca7d],\n\nThank you for providing us with the information.\nI have looked over the situation, and it seems that we are dealing with a false-positive in this case.\n\nKindly manually compensate the driver for the loss of their earnings.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-09T11:41:21.798Z"],["3798677","DSR-3015","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","Responsive data and answer letter sent out. ","2026-01-09T11:41:37.824Z"],["3798678","SREP-1032","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* EKS upgraded\n* Kube-proxy bumped\n* Nodes reprovisioned\n\n!image-20260109-114135.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260109-114135.png\"!","2026-01-09T11:41:43.676Z"],["3798679","WFM-9921","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-09T11:42:16.150Z"],["3798681","DBRE-8593","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 08.31.59.png|width=860,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 08.31.59.png\"!","2026-01-09T11:42:57.558Z"],["3798682","HS-28745","HS","razvan.nastase@bolt.eu","Răzvan Năstase","Thank you! Really appreciate it. Everything is fine, it’s just lots of bureaucracy: I need this certificate (from Bolt) to pass it to my family doctor so the family doctor can issue yet another certificate so I can forward that certificate to another medical facility so that medical facility can issue yet another certificate to forward to the police - all this just to renew the driving license.\n\nAnyways, appreciate your support. Have a nice day!","2026-01-09T11:42:58.422Z"],["3798684","CEBF-1821","CEBF","pavlo.savenko@bolt.eu","Pavlo Savenko","cant reproduce","2026-01-09T11:43:02.114Z"],["3798685","BP-13390","BP","johannes.laamann@bolt.eu","Johannes Erik Laamann","[~accountid:712020:ab58e2f4-f31f-4230-9a41-30c28c8bd545] actually I think we can already use the existing \n\n{noformat}authRouter.postWithArgs(\"/workProfilePortal/resolveCurrentUser\", userAssociationController.resolveCurrentUser);{noformat}\n\nI will update it to return data from the new company details table if an entry exists. Right now it should already return the existing work profile.","2026-01-09T11:43:18.847Z"],["3798687","LSS-61324","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached. Effective date wasn’t marked on the document. Original will be posted for delivery as soon as possible. Please ensure that they send a scan back once it has been signed from their side and kindly forward it to [contracts@bolt.eu|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] for archiving with a ticket number. \n\n[^NDA_Bolt Services AZ LLC_Innovation and Digital Development Agency (IDDA)_09.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T11:44:00.700Z"],["3798690","DSR-3077","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Thanks [~accountid:6001a723d364960139286c95] - reviewed and amended the letter (/)  both the answer and the responsive data can be shared with the driver.\n\nEDIT: apologies, I posted this before answering your question. Even if the driver has been reinstated, it doesn’t impact his DSAR in practice: we must still answer it in full 😊 ","2026-01-09T11:44:46.457Z"],["3798695","LSS-58462","LSS","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi team! Is there any update regarding this? [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301].","2026-01-09T11:45:50.252Z"],["3798696","LSS-61333","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-09T11:46:08.895Z"],["3798697","LSS-61172","LSS","ieva.fowler@bolt.eu","Ieva Fowler","Thank you for raising the ticket [~accountid:5f17f7301084620015f4972a] \n\n[~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] \n\n\nIt looks like we’ve received a request from DWF Law LLP acting for Aviva in relation to a personal injury claim. They’ve provided a signed authority from the claimant authorising the release of personnel, attendance, salary and occupational health records.\n\nOne important point to flag upfront is that the claimant wasn’t an employee but an independent contractor, so some of the categories they refer to may not exist or may not apply in the way the request is framed.\n\nFrom a legal point of view, the authority looks valid and gives us enough to engage, but it’s quite broad. I don’t think we should disclose everything wholesale, and we’ll need to apply data minimisation and relevance.\n\nWhat’s missing or unclear to me at this stage is:\n\n* the relevant contractor engagement dates\n* the exact time period they’re asking for\n* any clear deadline we’re expected to meet\n\nI’m happy to go back to DWF to acknowledge the request and ask them to clarify these points.\n\nLet me know if you’re comfortable with that approach and with my overall view on how we should handle disclosure.","2026-01-09T11:46:12.064Z"],["3798699","BP-13429","BP","johannes.laamann@bolt.eu","Johannes Erik Laamann","Might not be needed since there’s {{resolveCurrentUser}} endpoint [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13390?focusedCommentId=3798685|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13390?focusedCommentId=3798685|smart-link]. I will update this endpoint to return validated company details in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13407|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13407|smart-link]  ","2026-01-09T11:47:28.750Z"],["3798700","SRED-704","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Discussed with [~accountid:5fd343ae4d2179006eb6279d]  - with scope including all accounts we have it would be quite hard to provide IAM roles for all of them to allow terraform plan. Also soon SREC plans to switch account management, so it will be even more complicated.\n\n\n\nHacky way - is to create PR with changes in every security-groups and then parse results of Atlantis.\n\n\n\nOne more way - use Atlantis API [https://www.runatlantis.io/docs/api-endpoints|https://www.runatlantis.io/docs/api-endpoints|smart-link] , but it will require deployment of service somewhere internally or self-hosted GH runner to access API.","2026-01-09T11:47:28.999Z"],["3798702","RS-1936","RS","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hello team! (cc [~accountid:712020:b0d06119-b7c8-4491-85a9-a5cb1e609b96])\n\n\nHope you’re doing well, and thanks again for the time and attention you’ve given to this review.\n\n\nAs I’ve been reflecting on the information shared so far, I wanted to clarify a few points to ensure the context is fully understood:\n\n\n* This is a partner-hosted event to multiple clients, with a business-focused session aimed at reviewing current processes, service performance, and operational metrics, followed by hosted hospitality later in the day.\n\n* This was my first time raising a request of this nature, and I recognize that the initial framing may not have clearly captured the structure of the event, particularly given the more informal communication style of the partner, whose main operations are based in Nairobi.\n\n* pawaPay is an established payment service provider for Bolt across multiple African markets, and the relationship has been transparent and operationally sound to date.\n\nI completely understand the considerations around proportionality and optics, as more information were already shared. If possible, I’d really appreciate an update on the status of the review, as the event is scheduled for next Tuesday and the partner is currently finalising logistics.\n\nThanks again for your time and guidance.\n\nKind regards,\nJoao","2026-01-09T11:47:53.857Z"],["3798703","WFM-9909","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Done! Roles were added; Wish you a great day!!","2026-01-09T11:47:56.715Z"],["3798704","HS-28784","HS","oleh.pater@bolt.eu","Oleh Pater","Hello [~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0] ,\n\nThank you for a prompt response. If memory serves, I haven’t tried to edit the _proposed ID section_. To be sure, I double checked the details you have on your screenshot are correct - checked that with the documents once more.\n\nJust one thing that I noticed is that the document with the i*dentification #* _“wniosek”_ is not technically a permanent residence, but since there’s no other option that closely matches the document type among the identifiers, I’m leaving it this way within the proposed documents. \n\nThe only parts I modified were the _comments_ and the _attachments_. I added both documents as files along with their descriptions when I tried to resolve the error below. In the comments I noted about the issue and tried to resolve the issue by following the issue prompt below. \n\n!image-20260109-114307.png|width=1055,height=156,alt=\"image-20260109-114307.png\"!\n\n\n\nStill, after having tried to submit, I get the error below and it doesn’t let me finish the task.\n\n!image-20260109-113724.png|width=548,height=286,alt=\"image-20260109-113724.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","2026-01-09T11:48:03.753Z"],["3798705","PAW-14753","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160224\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-09 11:48:31 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-09T11:48:31.498Z"],["3798706","WFM-9919","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, queues assigned","2026-01-09T11:48:40.838Z"],["3798708","WFM-9919","WFM","cheila.aniceto@bolt.eu","Cheila Aniceto","Thank you [~accountid:712020:a4db27c0-87f6-4a6d-ace2-ec23e6b8f1aa]","2026-01-09T11:49:10.991Z"],["3798709","PFI-831323","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Well, there’s no December invoice, the service hasn’t been used during that time. \n\nRegarding the payment allocation, payments are automatically matched to the oldest outstanding part of the invoice, and not to the one particular invoice. It’s not possible to reallocate the Payments.","2026-01-09T11:49:13.279Z"],["3798710","LSS-60701","LSS","andrius.mikenas@bolt.eu","Andrius Mikėnas","Another ticket is invoice ticket, but I noticed that renewed annex uploaded there. Here is new annex (18 cars instead of24).\n\n[^ANNEX 2  to LT251043-LT251060_AT agreement (1) (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T11:49:14.248Z"],["3798712","WD-20427","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","the currency on these lines should also be updated:\n\n!image-20260109-114925.png|width=786,alt=\"image-20260109-114925.png\"!","2026-01-09T11:49:32.897Z"],["3798719","LSS-61172","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:209f6e12-e421-4fbf-9a9f-60d100117bab] - so just to be clear on this, DWF is requesting personal data about Mr Eldaim, and Mr Eldaim has provided written authorisation for DWF to request this information from Bolt?\n\nIf the above is correct (please confirm), then although this is not explicitly a DSAR, we can effectively treat it as one by proxy (subject to data minimisation / scoping as you have flagged). In which case, please could you reassign to Estelle, and I would be happy to support as needed 🙂 ","2026-01-09T11:50:42.637Z"],["3798720","INT-625","INT","daniel.kamkha@bolt.eu","Daniel Kamkha","*W02:* No progress, focusing on other tasks instead.","2026-01-09T11:51:09.375Z"],["3798722","INT-595","INT","daniel.kamkha@bolt.eu","Daniel Kamkha","*W02*: Finished working on fixes and improvements proposed from the e2e testing session.","2026-01-09T11:51:58.072Z"],["3798726","WFM-9914","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Looks like OPS role is missing, SCC please check","2026-01-09T11:53:10.163Z"],["3798727","WD-22528","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:712020:2261816b-1a2b-4b75-b1dc-d5fce431ad15] access granted","2026-01-09T11:53:32.368Z"],["3798729","LSS-61195","LSS","brian.malago@bolt.eu","Brian Malago Ogollo","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MuKnv-y8n_FVsEGRa_2C-ef0rdiZBK1TTzqLyCrYd_0/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MuKnv-y8n_FVsEGRa_2C-ef0rdiZBK1TTzqLyCrYd_0/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nHi Kerubo\n\nKindly see our revised version of the MOU for your confirmation and approval.\nThanks","2026-01-09T11:53:42.670Z"],["3798733","DBRE-8678","DBRE",null,"Slack","This conversation thread has been automatically unsynced from the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0875S9HGAF/p1767785302672039|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0875S9HGAF/p1767785302672039|smart-link] because [@Leandro Morgado|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f5b4e070e396800690aa153] removed the connected work item unfurl on Slack.\n\nFuture replies will no longer sync or update across Slack and Jira.","2026-01-09T11:54:43.756Z"],["3798734","LSS-61339","LSS","iryna.yatsyna@bolt.eu","Iryna Yatsyna","[^Act of acceptance KZ (2) (2).docx] _(3.20 MB)_","2026-01-09T11:54:52.230Z"],["3798735","DSR-3079","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:6001a723d364960139286c95] , thanks! \n\nI reviewed the response letter and the responsive data. I note that in BH, the driver asked (among many other things): “1. Copies of all my personal data processed by Bolt.”. As such, I trust that it would be most appropriate to send him a full PDE in this case.\n\nConscious that the PDE takes time due to the telemetry plugin, and considering that I will be OOO on Monday 12 Jan (same day as the deadline for this case), please run a full PDE and then send the [answer letter|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2kdVYnuxKMiD8vqkQBxp2iYD1VTL-qb8yPUotp_iRw/edit?usp=drive_link] (which I have reviewed) once it is complete. \n\nTo be fully clear: this ticket does not need my review again once the PDE has been sourced. The full PDE can be sent along with the answer letter (/) ","2026-01-09T11:54:52.693Z"],["3798738","PFI-817780","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Anything else required from my side here?","2026-01-09T11:55:14.741Z"],["3798741","WFM-9902","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-09T11:55:48.846Z"],["3798742","RS-1936","RS","aviv.geron@bolt.eu","Aviv Geron","Hi [@joao.santana|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U07ADRLNWMB], \n\nthank you for bearing with us. You can find below the team's reply:While the new context provides a defined business agenda, the total package (a high-value, multi-day trip including flights, lodging, and premium sports hospitality) is deemed excessive and disproportionate to the stated 4-hour business objective. The ABAC policy emphasizes *modest* and *appropriate* gifts/entertainment. The proposed trip strongly conflicts with the policy's intention to prohibit excessive hospitality and to maintain a _zero-tolerance approach_ to anything that could _appear_ to influence a business decision. Therefore the decision to decline remains consistent with the policy's principles and will not changed.\n\nLet me know if you have any further questions, will be happy to help.\n\nBest,\n\nAviv","2026-01-09T11:55:54.729Z"],["3798743","WFM-9922","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601614|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601614]","2026-01-09T11:56:06.864Z"],["3798744","RNTL-30285","RNTL","karolina.epifantseva@bolt.eu","Karolina Epifantseva","duplicate, fixed","2026-01-09T11:56:18.154Z"],["3798745","WD-22530","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Mapping is created ","2026-01-09T11:56:24.591Z"],["3798749","WFM-9912","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! will close this with no resolution then; Wish you a great day!","2026-01-09T11:57:18.893Z"],["3798750","PFI-831271","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:0a6482c4-510b-4c02-a5f0-016cf9d5025f],\n\nThe promo code may be from the 3rd party, however, the rule logic is still the same.\nUnfortunately we also can not whitelist this specific user from the said rules, main reasoning being that it seems that the user is attempting to maliciously use our services.\n\nI went over all of the users that are connected to this specific users, and there are a lot of refunded payments/failed payments and cancelled payments.\nDue to everything mentioned above, this customer is considered as not trusted, however, they can still make regular orders. Whitelisting them will not be considered.\n\nPlease do let me know if you have any additional questions regarding this, I’d be more than glad to answer.\nAs a reminder, then by tagging me within this ticket I can always re-open it.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-09T11:57:26.733Z"],["3798751","DELIVERY-895","DELIVERY","yonatan.kalman@bolt.eu","Yonatan Kalman","26W2: Performance improvements released to 102. Other bug fixes been merged to next version. Delete button on results screen to be implemented again after receiving plenty of feedback it’s needed.","2026-01-09T11:58:29.851Z"],["3798752","RNTL-30285","RNTL","karolina.epifantseva@bolt.eu","Karolina Epifantseva","\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08TCCLKKH7/p1767359585421079|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08TCCLKKH7/p1767359585421079|smart-card]","2026-01-09T11:59:25.808Z"],["3798754","LSS-61292","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","09.01.2026: LOI reviewed and feedback provided to stakeholders in dedicated [slack |https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08PTDELW6L/p1767959782633949?thread_ts=1767885247.577119&cid=C08PTDELW6L]channel. ","2026-01-09T11:59:52.672Z"],["3798755","LSS-60462","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Amendment_Bolt Services NO AS_Signicat AB_08.01.2026.pdf] ","2026-01-09T11:59:57.136Z"],["3798756","PLUS-73","PLUS","artem.markov@bolt.eu","Artem Markov","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-100756?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-100756?created=true]","2026-01-09T12:01:05.638Z"],["3798758","LSS-61341","LSS","bianca.alvesdeandrade@bolt.eu","Bianca Alves de Andrade","[^Branding Contract - Bolt Club Unlimited Drive.pdf] _(166 kB)_","2026-01-09T12:01:07.656Z"],["3798759","DSR-3613","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-09T12:01:13.233Z"],["3798760","SREP-1033","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* EKS upgraded\n* Kube-proxy bumped\n* Nodes reprovisioned\n\n!image-20260109-120128.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260109-120128.png\"!","2026-01-09T12:01:31.850Z"],["3798761","HS-28777","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello!\n\nErklärung zum Beschäftigungsverhältnis document will be filled out by our Mobility team. Could you please raise this ticket with them.\n\n\n\nKind regards,\n\nKadri","2026-01-09T12:02:00.314Z"],["3798764","CEBF-1821","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Bug is fixed. We will show only one unique issue/account\n\n!image-20260109-120223.png|width=468,alt=\"image-20260109-120223.png\"!","2026-01-09T12:02:28.097Z"],["3798765","LSS-58750","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[~accountid:615c75e007ac3c0068114285] , the partner should not receive notifications anymore.\n\n[^Alliance- BR Agreement_encrypted_ (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T12:02:40.110Z"],["3798768","PFI-831296","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:6254ba80-2872-4956-add5-04a506f589d9],\n\nWe can confirm that this is campaign abuse with driver fraud.\nHowever, we have decided not to block the driver, as they do have good GMV with us, and most likely now that they see that they got caught, they will stop their attempts.\nIf they continue with their attempts, then we will of course suspend them from our platform.\n\nDo not rectify the driver’s balance as everything is working as intended.\nI hope that you happen to have the regular macro that is used to give a generalized answer to fraudulent drivers.\n*Please do not give out any information that has been mentioned above, as it is all strictly internal.*\nIf you do not happen to have a macro and need to provide an answer, then firstly refuse the balance adjustment and reasoning can be that irregular activities were detected, something between those lines. Once again, please avoid giving out information to the driver, as we do not want them to know what exactly we caught them by.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-09T12:02:58.758Z"],["3798772","HS-28777","HS","vishnu.unnikrishnan@bolt.eu","Vishnu Unnikrishnan","Ok thank you","2026-01-09T12:03:40.099Z"],["3798774","PFI-828351","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Can you please provide a ticket example where a similar case was fixed before? ","2026-01-09T12:04:40.995Z"],["3798775","LSS-61343","LSS","helena.rachao@bolt.eu","Helena Rachão","[^RFI_21_uk.pdf] _(737 kB)_","2026-01-09T12:04:42.509Z"],["3798776","PFI-829470","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","I believe the contact email addresses could be updated from the Admin and Business Portal. Probably the Local Business CS Team can help.","2026-01-09T12:04:43.558Z"],["3798777","MVRT-1446","MVRT","evamaria.ots@bolt.eu","Eva Maria Ots","[~accountid:5fa51169b38e61007151d47e] Sweet, thanks! I agree with the stories approach, we want them to see all features of the bike. ","2026-01-09T12:04:48.296Z"],["3798779","DRX-28048","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Sumit Lakra, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-09T12:05:07.258Z"],["3798781","LSS-60360","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Fleet Agreement - Sidnei Faria, Unipessoal, Lda_encrypted_ (1).pdf] ","2026-01-09T12:05:18.310Z"],["3798782","MVRT-1446","MVRT","evamaria.ots@bolt.eu","Eva Maria Ots","[~accountid:712020:a68bad68-4d18-4aca-aaf7-10e00df84534] Having troubles getting the pricing from ops, they are busy assembling the bike, but will get it next week. ","2026-01-09T12:05:30.179Z"],["3798785","PFI-831118","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","Hi,\nThe CIF number is still 0000000000000, please assist. \nThank you","2026-01-09T12:05:57.909Z"],["3798786","PFI-831118","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T12:06:01.719Z"],["3798787","RDS-126","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* Bugs mostly fixed. Dmitry may still need Nikita input on designs\n* iOS bottleneck still existing","2026-01-09T12:06:19.419Z"],["3798788","EBIKE1-369","EBIKE1","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","Haizhu will send us the Nord Lock washer samples for 15 bikes.\n\nWe got also pricelist for washers in size M3 to M12: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1oCUFj9kDVZhE_oXdz2JMiELhErrDWINf?rtpof=true&usp=drive_fs|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1oCUFj9kDVZhE_oXdz2JMiELhErrDWINf?rtpof=true&usp=drive_fs]\n\n\n\n!image-20260109-120622.png|width=196,alt=\"image-20260109-120622.png\"!","2026-01-09T12:06:24.311Z"],["3798789","DBRE-8458","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","PR created for README documentation update:\n\n*PR #5552*: [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify\\-ansible/pull/5552|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5552]\n\n*Branch*: DBRE\\-8458\\-rollout\\-vm\\-dedicated\\-dashboards\n\n*Changes*:\n\\- Updated db\\_tidb\\_grafana\\_dashboards README with comprehensive documentation\n\\- Added per\\-file change detection architecture details\n\\- Added TiDB Grafana deployment context \\(TiUP paths, service details\\)\n\\- Added key capabilities, configuration reference, usage examples\n\\- Added troubleshooting guide and performance metrics\n\nThis is the first commit for the dashboard deployment work. Additional changes for the actual dashboard files and tasks will follow.\n\n","2026-01-09T12:06:24.424Z"],["3798795","INT-723","INT","ishan.rayeen@bolt.eu","Ishan Rayeen","*26W02:* Picked up the project, UI designs are not ready but I will start brainstorming the underlying architecture for offer bundles and discounting for paid visibility.","2026-01-09T12:08:22.821Z"],["3798800","DBRE-8218","DBRE","andrei.fedorov@bolt.eu","Andrei Fedorov","also added versioning for recovery\\fallback purposes: https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15305","2026-01-09T12:09:20.953Z"],["3798801","SREDESK-7394","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","The target schema is created in Prelive/Gamma cluster.\nBegin working on a fix for {{map_error}}","2026-01-09T12:09:25.184Z"],["3798802","UXA-2165","UXA","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: - will be checked by developers","2026-01-09T12:09:49.740Z"],["3798803","PFI-831118","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Then, Agent Profile is not updated. Please, update it: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6803423312/Romania+E-invoicing+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6803423312/Romania+E-invoicing+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|smart-link]  ","2026-01-09T12:09:51.668Z"],["3798806","RDS-1223","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* Redoing release priorities based on RiderX alignment\n* [~accountid:61386b11a4f86e0069546dff] requests looking into market specific t&c for bolt send (the banner during order)","2026-01-09T12:10:07.966Z"],["3798809","INT-723","INT","ishan.rayeen@bolt.eu","Ishan Rayeen","[~accountid:62a9857bd0132d0068809cdd]  From the looks of it, 2 weeks might no longer be a valid estimate, as 2 week solution was already delivered for Ghana that will also work for all other countries. \nI will come up with the new estimates soon","2026-01-09T12:10:26.454Z"],["3798812","LSS-58430","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:712020:8af2b159-71c0-448a-80ba-ff5059bb02f6]  has shared the latest update on the Cross Platform Ban project, and it’s been adjusted. Based on this, I am closing this ticket for now and we will be revisiting the issue when it becomes relevant again.","2026-01-09T12:11:28.139Z"],["3798815","RDS-1276","RDS","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:712020:505aebee-5cf4-438e-8909-a5524bd7a634] i think we can add to driver view, it’s part of checking the kind of 'why has this driver been waiting 50 mins? they have good categories, they have smart accept on, they can get scheduled rides….. '","2026-01-09T12:12:09.664Z"],["3798816","SREDESK-7397","SREDESK","andrus.viik@bolt.eu","Andrus Viik","{{arn:aws:iam::737418964414:user/S3-bolt-swarmia-data-exporter}} created","2026-01-09T12:12:26.208Z"],["3798817","RDS-636","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* [~accountid:712020:eb64fa24-b70d-49d6-b62c-e4560e7e1457]\n** ready to resume proper employee testing\n** feature doesn’t work when ordering ride for someone else. RiderX fixing from their side. for a/b testing this feature is being disabled","2026-01-09T12:12:29.716Z"],["3798821","SREP-1074","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","!image-20260109-121340.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260109-121340.png\"!\n\n* EKS upgraded\n* Kube-proxy bumped\n* Nodes reprovisioned","2026-01-09T12:13:51.185Z"],["3798822","LSS-60422","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hello [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] ! \nLetting you know that I am now taking over this matter, and will share the amended agreement next week 🙂 Thank you for your patience! ","2026-01-09T12:13:59.493Z"],["3798825","DBRE-8458","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","Implementation complete \\- all acceptance criteria met:\n\n*PR #5552*: [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify\\-ansible/pull/5552|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5552]\n\n*Commits*:\n1. docs: README update with deployment architecture\n2. feat: static dashboard deployment with per\\-file change detection\n\n*Acceptance Criteria Status*:\n✅ Roll out PingCAP VM and dashboards \\- 30 dashboards as static files\n✅ Fetch deployed VM dashboards \\- integrated from ti\\-restore\\-test\\-monitor\n✅ Integrate dashboards as static files \\- files/dashboards/ directory\n✅ Deploy dedicated datasource 'Bolt' \\- Bolt\\-VictoriaMetrics configured\n✅ All dashboards under one directory \\- Bolt folder in Grafana\n✅ Change datasource in every dashboard \\- Python transformer at deploy time\n✅ Clean up old folder remnants \\- rollback\\-ver1.yaml task\n\n*Key Changes*:\n\\- 30 TiDB/TiKV/PD/TiCDC/TiFlash monitoring dashboards\n\\- update\\_dashboard\\_datasource.py for on\\-the\\-fly transformation\n\\- Per\\-file change detection with exit codes \\(0=unchanged, 2=changed\\)\n\\- Automatic rollback of old Grafana folders \\(Common, TiDB, TiKV\\)\n\\- Removed old migration machinery and test files\n\nReady for review and merge.\n\n","2026-01-09T12:15:19.250Z"],["3798826","PFI-829356","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments initiated the payout. Please check if the payout has reached FINISHED state","2026-01-09T12:15:23.396Z"],["3798827","PFI-829796","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments initiated the payout. Please check if the payout has reached FINISHED state","2026-01-09T12:15:25.677Z"],["3798828","PFI-829008","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments initiated the payout. Please check if the payo