r all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27000](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27000)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T12:22:20.729Z"],["3798926","L10N-27078","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27000](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27000)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T12:22:20.846Z"],["3798927","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Kerli Uibo [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767961329764559]*{color}:\nAs it affects invoices, if you would use the regular manual adjustment types, then tax needs to approve it <@U06217N0RJ5> <@U08RWJ9TRAA>.\nFor cases which are not related to the balance transfer, I do not have answer right now. There should be some solution for these separately, as we should not be mixing these with regular manual adjustments. If it is a deposit payback, then maybe would be possible to use compensation types -&gt; meaning these will be presented on a separate compensation invoice, and will not mix with the monthly invoice.\nMaybe worth to have a discussion together with <@U03P58BK5FY>\n{quote}","2026-01-09T12:22:24.600Z"],["3798929","LSS-52572","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hi, [~accountid:712020:0b391d02-6c8a-4494-99fd-3d2ff0d7ef37] \n\n[Here is the file with details|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dJ26FhaV7g2SQJjPG_07HhU5vICck2O6MypNhK_RznE/edit?tab=t.0] to be filled in the questionnaire form for Auchan. \n\n\n\nAs before, we *need a separate declaration of Ahto Kink on not subcontracting* of the intermediary’s requirements to third parties by Bolt Poland. I’ve prepared a template to be signed off by [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] (SpotDraft shall be sufficient) and t*o be attached to this questionnaire form*. I am raising a subticket to Legal Ops for signing this declaration.\n\nThe template to be signed by Ahto Kink. [^2026 Declaration_Bolt_Poland_KYP Auchan.docx.pdf] / [https://docs.google.com/document/d/16cIVwH_045wfkwyrGYF5jJA9GhLrv_u1/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/16cIVwH_045wfkwyrGYF5jJA9GhLrv_u1/edit|smart-link]  (same files)\n\nOnce the declaration is signed, you [~accountid:712020:0b391d02-6c8a-4494-99fd-3d2ff0d7ef37] or somebody from Legal Ops (as previously) can fill the gaps in the form with the details I am attaching [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dJ26FhaV7g2SQJjPG_07HhU5vICck2O6MypNhK_RznE/edit?tab=t.0] and send back to Auchan (we can follow the same way as before). ","2026-01-09T12:22:57.051Z"],["3798932","LSS-61213","LSS","nina.paragoso@bolt.eu","Nina Paragoso","Hello, can you please let me know if this was sent to TalTech so we can ping them and follow up on the signature? Thanks!\n\n","2026-01-09T12:24:34.331Z"],["3798933","LSS-58788","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Received an update that the cross-platform ban initiative for sexual harassment offenders in Poland is being put on hold. After a sync with the Poland Public Policy team, the decision was to wait for the proposed regulation to pass before moving forward, to avoid potential privacy and compliance issues.\n\nPublic Policy has already spoken with Uber and Free Now, and while there is interest from all sides, the preference is to proceed only once the regulatory framework is in place.\n\nAs discussed with [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] , I’m closing this ticket for now. We can revisit the topic once the Product team picks this up again. \n\ncc: [~accountid:62722e092db308007024a425] [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] ","2026-01-09T12:24:48.845Z"],["3798934","RDS-928","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","[~accountid:620e7f2eef2bd5006aead114] \n\n* info architecture project ongoing\n* design doc added\n* moving this to Vanessa’s team","2026-01-09T12:24:49.868Z"],["3798936","LSS-56160","LSS","dmytro.huminetskyi@bolt.eu","Dmytro Huminetskyi","Hey team! \nHere is the answer:\n\n{quote} Can we confirm whether the account was actually compromised, and if so, *when exactly*? The earliest changes appear around *17 May 2025*, but the user reported it on *05 Sep 2025*.{quote}\n\nThe only suspected login session is from device id FD936449-2637-40A5-9335-2C8EF7F53AE2 created on 17 May 2025, 20:56 (UTC+03:00).\n\n{quote} Can we verify that the user currently contacting support is the *original account owner*?{quote}\n\nThe ticket was created from the app, CA.175.0, so it’s eRKglR-aRvapZWwar2-WjP device id. For this device id there is a login session created on 26 Jun 2023 - 1 day after account creation, so likely it’s an original owner of the account.\n\n{quote} We see a *passkey login on 5 September* – can you clarify what this represents (creation vs usage), and whether it could indicate unauthorised access?{quote}\n\nYou can go to “Authentication methods” to see that the passkey was created on 5 Sept 2025, 09:21 (UTC+03:00) and last used on 20 Oct 2025, 15:17 (UTC+03:00).\n\n{quote} If the passkey is linked to a suspected compromise and is still active, should it be *revoked* to ensure the incident is no longer ongoing?{quote}\n\nPasskey was used by the legit device id -eRKglR-aRvapZWwar2-WjP - so it’s ok.","2026-01-09T12:25:12.949Z"],["3798938","RDS-1276","RDS","katharina.skolimowski@bolt.eu","Katharina Skolimowski","Ok. I have unfortunately little knowledge on how the scheduled rides are handled by fleets - let’s say in Dubai. A client calls in, asks for a ride for their wife/mom from jewlery shop to home, how is the fleet picking the driver? Based on live-map location? I wonder if live map can help in such situations. The feature was done with a hurry and no research was done unfortunately. \nWe can investigate it alongside with some other matters.","2026-01-09T12:26:04.979Z"],["3798939","DSR-3081","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hey [~accountid:6001a723d364960139286c95] - I downloaded the [data|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1bvb-zAJkLQMT6ZQDx5td5yFHE41ZkcHp?usp=drive_link] linked to the (disputed) profile created under Fleet 3M Drivers Olsztyn. I also prepared the answer [letter|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Jl9qOYFhHEmLVpTW-SdA2YBJx1mWt3Tj6kVCItM8JnI/edit?usp=drive_link]. Both can be sent to the driver (/) \n\nI expect follow-up questions on this, at which point it will be relevant to engage Local Ops and clarify the situation.  ","2026-01-09T12:26:11.733Z"],["3798941","DPM-2211","DPM","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","[~accountid:712020:ddfe83d1-e2c1-4238-8459-1dfffb836745] shall we tidy this epic up? We can move whatever is not done if anything under DPM-2212","2026-01-09T12:26:32.205Z"],["3798943","LSS-60050","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] thank you so much for the confrmation and another file signed 😉 ❤️ ","2026-01-09T12:27:08.192Z"],["3798946","PRODSEC-577","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Will consider it done as notebooks are working. Missing is only S3 for caching","2026-01-09T12:28:30.417Z"],["3798948","HS-28784","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Contacted WD tech","2026-01-09T12:29:25.741Z"],["3798949","DRX-27864","DRX","joonas.lomps@bolt.eu","Joonas Lõmps","[~accountid:5e65e969c54d0a0d04427b8c] We need some more input here\nSome markets don’t want to task to be created when onboarding status is reached.\nSome do.\nHow do we want to handle this?","2026-01-09T12:29:36.405Z"],["3798950","PFI-831296","PFI","sofja.kissina@bolt.eu","Sofja Kissina","[~accountid:712020:6d5640ba-c28b-492d-b071-2c5df1c7e01b] 👀 ","2026-01-09T12:29:59.678Z"],["3798955","DSR-3069","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","[~accountid:712020:3d29a498-3ef1-4867-a3ad-7aeb77a221e9] Thank you!","2026-01-09T12:30:27.042Z"],["3798958","LSS-60050","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","[~accountid:61debf39e67ea2006b3a1cb5] as we have the notification and agreement signed, you can: \n\n# send back the notification to the landlord via e-mail\n# ask the landlord for confirmation that we can proceed with making payment for security deposit (kaucja) to one of the two bank accounts indicated in the notification. This payment should be made before 14.01 (confirmation of the payment should be sent back via e-mail to the landlord as well).\n# once you get the confirmation, you can ask the Finance Team for the payment proceeding.","2026-01-09T12:30:51.114Z"],["3798959","FPD-1505","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","First draft of PR is being worked on: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-data-science-libraries/pull/229|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-data-science-libraries/pull/229|smart-link] \nCurrently testing if marketplace model predictions are working in production and if results are also correct","2026-01-09T12:31:01.893Z"],["3798961","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","Hey [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] When do we expect the artwork, we were hoping to flight over the weekend","2026-01-09T12:31:16.537Z"],["3798967","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767961873248569]*{color}:\nBrief update:\n• Rollback resolved the issue for the moment.\n• We cleaned up incorrect configurations from the DB, so deploying code from develop should not cause further errors.\n• An update to document type configuration could still write an invalid value to the DB. To not rush releasing changes for that right before release freeze, I plan to keep the old version deployed for now so even in the unlikely case of document metadata configuration changes over the weekend the issue will not be triggered.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T12:31:27.393Z"],["3798968","LSS-61264","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:cb7d1436-9800-43db-821c-db7028a6ff03] !\nThank you for raising this ticket and the context provided.\nThis is a privacy matter, so I will loop in the privacy team.\nThank you!","2026-01-09T12:31:43.480Z"],["3798969","PRODSEC-576","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Schedule can be done through Databricks notebook but will require figuring out frequency and getting S3 bucket connected to Databricks ","2026-01-09T12:31:43.904Z"],["3798970","DRAG-636","DRAG","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] I have my own D1 here and I hope that the final validation can be done by end of Week 3.\n\nThe current blocker is that we need the final firmware from Genfo and we need to verify with that firmware that everything is working.\n\nAlso, we would need IoT firmwares for D1/2 Germany tests to validate all the necessary functionality.","2026-01-09T12:32:03.091Z"],["3798974","LSS-61264","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] !\nI believe this is a topic for your team to handle?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T12:32:32.049Z"],["3798976","RDS-630","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","Nikita\n\n* Need to communicate short timer on Blast Dispatch (BS)\n** existing countdown implies full time is available\n** solution: remove countdown on BS orders. Add animation to indicate BS order\n* Also want to mark “exclusive” orders\n** Add label for Exclusive orders\n* Joonas to Discuss this with [~accountid:712020:d2a0e53f-83a4-4e81-aebd-74db6f57d6fa] ","2026-01-09T12:32:47.853Z"],["3798978","RS-1875","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] ,\n\nWe had a chat with [~accountid:5f1538051c682d00295dbb61] . She is going to prepare the data next week, so no action from your side ","2026-01-09T12:33:45.392Z"],["3798979","PFI-829975","PFI","joseph.kamange@bolt-outsource.eu","Joseph Kamange","Please assist in resolving payment issue. \n\n","2026-01-09T12:33:53.669Z"],["3798980","PAW-14756","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-09T12:33:57.288Z"],["3798981","SREP-1039","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","!image-20260109-123349.png|width=654,alt=\"image-20260109-123349.png\"!\n\n* EKS upgraded\n* Kube-proxy bumped\n* Nodes reprovisioned","2026-01-09T12:34:07.740Z"],["3798986","EBIKE1-418","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:712020:8d272f38-d046-4ad2-a5b3-a47b219e9fa1] For Dragon, the power limiter sets the current to 18A and the Dragon battery is 5P, compared to EB1 battery which is 3P.\n\nI would assume based on the results from [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRAG-674?focusedCommentId=3790613|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRAG-674?focusedCommentId=3790613|smart-link]  that if Dragon batteries drop to 0 with 18A, then 20A certainly would not improve the situation for EB1. I would say that in order to achieve similar results to the Dragon power profiles, the current would have to be 3/5 * 18A ~ 11A.\nI think that limiting current to 20A does not provide much effect, especially in sub zero temperatures for the EB1 battery.","2026-01-09T12:34:52.580Z"],["3798988","PFI-814717","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Based on the balance, the courier has negative balance that’s due to cash orders made. You can review the balance from here before November 2024: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-courier/couriers/325790?tab=INVOICING_BALANCE&tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter={\"start_date_ts\"%3A1698354000%2C\"end_date_ts\"%3A1729587600%2C\"external_id\"%3A325790%2C\"namespace\"%3Anull%2C\"types\"%3A[\"food_courier\"%2C\"food_courier_cash\"]%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"limit\"%3A25}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-courier/couriers/325790?tab=INVOICING_BALANCE&tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22start_date_ts%22%3A1698354000%2C%22end_date_ts%22%3A1729587600%2C%22external_id%22%3A325790%2C%22namespace%22%3Anull%2C%22types%22%3A%5B%22food_courier%22%2C%22food_courier_cash%22%5D%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22limit%22%3A25%7D]","2026-01-09T12:35:03.494Z"],["3798989","RDS-1178","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","[~accountid:712020:eb64fa24-b70d-49d6-b62c-e4560e7e1457] \n\n* still waiting on FE eng capacity\n* a/b test was set up\n** [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GBM/pages/7308640272/Prevent+early+driver-arrived+-+AB+test|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GBM/pages/7308640272/Prevent+early+driver-arrived+-+AB+test|smart-link] \n* first iteration won’t change rider side\n** waiting for driver side experiment results\n* GTM with Alex","2026-01-09T12:35:31.652Z"],["3798991","DSR-3615","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-09T12:36:07.696Z"],["3798993","RNTL-30028","RNTL","karolina.epifantseva@bolt.eu","Karolina Epifantseva","problem still persist","2026-01-09T12:37:05.950Z"],["3798994","CSDA-275","CSDA","laimdota.vilistere@bolt.eu","Laimdota Vilistere","I've just received confirmation - expected growth of 3-5 times in API Partner trips by EOY 2026.  \n\n","2026-01-09T12:37:31.165Z"],["3798997","PFI-831333","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:616e87debcb5740068039c0c] \n\nUnfortunately, I don’t have the best overview of the refunds due to lack of access. \n\nYou could potentially check with your team lead. They have higher permissions to issue refunds and might be able to force the refund to the balance. \n\nLet me know if they are able to assist you. \n","2026-01-09T12:38:22.811Z"],["3798999","DELIVERY-751","DELIVERY","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","\n\n26W2\n\n*Backend*\n\n* During testing found a problem. The solution has been aligned and the development will be started next week\n\n*Front*\n\n* Development and fixing found bugs is in progress","2026-01-09T12:38:44.486Z"],["3799000","DRAG-695","DRAG","norman.tamm@bolt.eu","Norman Tamm","*TWS glue passed the IPx7 test.*\nBefore gluing I applied TWS sent primer. The test was done without BMS wires, with the humidity hole fully glued.","2026-01-09T12:38:48.272Z"],["3799003","SREP-1040","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* EKS upgraded\n* Kube-proxy bumped\n* Nodes reprovisioned\n\n!image-20260109-123732.png|width=654,alt=\"image-20260109-123732.png\"!","2026-01-09T12:39:34.058Z"],["3799004","LSS-61264","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Yes [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] - I will re-assign to my team, thanks!","2026-01-09T12:39:33.581Z"],["3799010","DELIVERY-1125","DELIVERY","meiko.udras@bolt.eu","Meiko Udras","26W02: Design doc finished and aligned with GROX team. Development started with bootstrapping the new basket replacements service.","2026-01-09T12:41:06.683Z"],["3799012","PFI-831386","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^BOLT (3).pdf]","2026-01-09T12:41:16.590Z"],["3799016","PFI-814652","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Reviewed: there indeed was an adjustment internally, but this didn’t affect courier balance in any way, as the two adjustments cancelled itself out. After reviewing the balance, the courier has some cash debt which causes the negative balance. ","2026-01-09T12:43:23.211Z"],["3799017","MLC-3779","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W2:\n\n* Had meeting to onboard Annie to the ad-hoc process. Will support her in W3 if EE has new enrollments\n* Confirmed Klāvs will be the main POC for Bolt Plus now on the merchant side. Will follow up with him on next steps for the Q1 country launches. ","2026-01-09T12:43:24.642Z"],["3799022","RDS-1106","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* Project Green part of Marketplace team. No driverx RDS needed\n* FIFO - no new work here\n* dubai ios streethailing - expansion team domain not us\n\nVanessa:\n\n* There was some issue with FIFO+ price bidding. But it’s fixed now","2026-01-09T12:44:02.788Z"],["3799023","LSS-56382","LSS","vitaliia.hrabova@bolt.eu","Vitaliia Hrabova","[~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] The partner informed that their lawyer has not reviewed these points separately, as their legal team reviews only the contract as a whole. They asked us to incorporate the proposed points as amendments into the contract and send the revised full version.\n\nThey also mentioned that they are currently changing their lawyer, so they need to submit the entire contract for review.\n\nPlease let me know how we should proceed from our side.","2026-01-09T12:44:14.699Z"],["3799026","HS-28792","HS","ingrid.valgejarv@bolt.eu","Ingrid Valgejärv","Waiting for PP confirmation and NC info","2026-01-09T12:44:40.405Z"],["3799027","GRWA-1479","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","Here is the complete [detail|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08UX5MD6AH/p1767961535774259?thread_ts=1767958468.617279&cid=C08UX5MD6AH]","2026-01-09T12:44:43.271Z"],["3799028","LSS-58930","LSS","afonso.azevedo@bolt.eu","Afonso Varão de Azevedo","Hi [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] \n\nThanks for the review. \n\nI’ll ask the scope of coverage to Advantage Saúde. \n\n*Can you please clarify what is the benefit for Advantage Saude with this partnership?*\nAdvantage Saúde has partnerships with clinics and they get a compensation for everyone that goes to a clinic with their card. \n\nThank you!\n\n\n","2026-01-09T12:44:43.922Z"],["3799029","MLC-660","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W2:\n\n* Annie updated the canvas with new templates. Will coordinate with Agnė to launch it, likely today. \n* Followed up with dev-logistics and martech to troubleshoot onelink issues, which they will follow up on in W3. [Slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1767956536316379?thread_ts=1767947797.444719&cid=C08QTPU0GQY].\n* No update on the event yet for the follow-up message, but the improved comms and templates are still a major improvement.","2026-01-09T12:44:58.672Z"],["3799031","FX-3581","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767962704133389]*{color}:\n<@U09D62DKH9P> As a ready-made solution to retrieve a single fleet_owner, you can insert the ID into this URL: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-manager/managers/edit/{fleet_owner_id}] (replace {fleet_owner_id} with an existing ID).\n\nIf you additionally need a field where you can enter an ID/IDs and get the result, we would need to make further improvements.\n\nDoes the URL-based solution work for you, or would you prefer an input field on the search page?\n{quote}","2026-01-09T12:45:19.202Z"],["3799032","RIDE-542","RIDE","federico.michelini@bolt.eu","Federico Michelini","Hi [~accountid:638476d83e79f12e572272f3] , I saw that you marked 0 for Finance - Accounting hours. Flagging that this partnership agreement will likely need Accounting support as it will include some potential payments between Bolt and Stella in the form of revenue guarantees and subsidies to charging price discounts.\n\nPlease let me know if you need more info to estimate resourcing.","2026-01-09T12:45:19.364Z"],["3799033","RDS-1273","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* Moving to Vanessa’s Driver Progression team","2026-01-09T12:45:31.889Z"],["3799034","FX-3581","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767962763026919]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3581 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T12:46:17.557Z"],["3799036","FX-3582","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767962768416209]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3582 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T12:46:22.100Z"],["3799038","RDS-1143","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* safety team is redesigning entire safety label/unified safety score. nothing for us","2026-01-09T12:46:54.082Z"],["3799039","MLC-3299","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W2:\n\n* A/B test will likely start W3 or W4 where we will launch the announcement comms, dependent on when MOPS gets localised guides back.\n* Full launch will follow up a few weeks later where we will send the full launch comms.\n* Comms will include updated Merchant Portal guides and highlight the improvements to the portal and how it helps the owners with insights and a better understanding of their performance on Bolt Food.","2026-01-09T12:47:00.446Z"],["3799040","PFI-829476","PFI","felicia.oprea@bolt-outsource.eu","Felicia Ștefania Oprea","Hello [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] \n\nThe VAT code has been added and the company details updated. \n\nCan you please reissue invoice with corrected data? \n\nThank you!\n\n","2026-01-09T12:47:11.243Z"],["3799041","FX-3585","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767962848459219]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3585 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T12:47:41.987Z"],["3799042","WD-22529","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:62b1977ddcafd965c5ddc33e] !\n\nI believe this ticket is connected with Invoice layout. Can you take a look? ","2026-01-09T12:47:49.570Z"],["3799043","SUPX-2190","SUPX","radoslaw.wielonski@bolt.eu","Radosław Wieloński","There is difference between these 2 interfaces, especially last_message would need specific handling. In {{SupportCaseListData}} it’s nullable, because we can have a draft support case which can be shown in some part of the system.\n\nHere are our options:\n\n* leave it as it is - when interface is extending we will be missing keys, like we are missing {{brand}} and {{support_case_flow_id}} right now, \n* use{{SupportCaseSummary}} and override left_message with nullable type - type won’t be exactly the same as data which is not ideal `{{SupportCaseListData extends Omit<SupportCaseSummary, 'last_message'> {last_message: SupportCaseMessage | null}}},\n* I think the best one - where we are using {{DraftCaseSummary}} and {{SupportCaseSummary}}we can use union between these types and make sure we are handling it properly.\n\nwe can also rename {{DraftCaseSummary}} to {{DraftSupportCaseSummary}}along the way if there are no objections.\n\n!image-20260109-124649.png|width=769,alt=\"image-20260109-124649.png\"!\n\n[~accountid:5ae966399abb77267ba68b16] could you please give your perspective on that? If you don’t have strong opinion we can discuss this on grooming.","2026-01-09T12:48:18.113Z"],["3799044","DSR-3079","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","* Response [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2kdVYnuxKMiD8vqkQBxp2iYD1VTL-qb8yPUotp_iRw/edit?tab=t.0]\n* All driver personal data *(Except Telemetry)* [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/1LLQo7Y93JBnXXJcntQVZbDsF1JZCTo8u]. Average rating, acceptance rate also added, no call recordings, fleet driver. Document sizes already decreased. \n* Driver telemetry plugin export [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/personal-data-export/exports/1267166?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D].\n* Response approved by [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] and all data and response can be sent out once telemetry export finishes and is included in the data. ","2026-01-09T12:48:30.834Z"],["3799047","LSS-60701","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! updated document has been sent out instead. Please let them know. Thanks!","2026-01-09T12:49:48.462Z"],["3799051","LSS-61348","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Hi team \n\nRequest you to please help with signing process of the agreement. Details below 👇 \n\nUploading the final agreement as agreed by the parties here : [^Master Service Agreement with DTI 09.01.2026 (v1) (2).docx] \n\nName of the counterparty: Chuck Harper\nEmail: [chuck@drivertechnologies.com|mailto:chuck@drivertechnologies.com] \n\nDo let me know in case you have any questions\nThanks\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:2449585e-020b-4bbc-ac29-8780f94f6823] ","2026-01-09T12:50:46.775Z"],["3799054","PFI-831296","PFI","annika.helimets@bolt.eu","Annika Helimets","Hello, [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] !\n\nCan you please provide me more details about “campaign abuse with driver fraud”. Does it mean, that driver using stolen card cashed out money by making fake orders with fake rider accounts?\n\nAnnika","2026-01-09T12:51:07.105Z"],["3799055","L10N-27088","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27084](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27084)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T12:51:25.033Z"],["3799056","L10N-27090","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27084](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27084)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T12:51:26.686Z"],["3799057","L10N-27093","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27084](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27084)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T12:51:27.418Z"],["3799058","L10N-27095","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27084](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27084)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T12:51:28.709Z"],["3799059","L10N-27096","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on