26-01-09T12:51:42.272Z"],["3799072","DRAG101-471","DRAG101","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] What would be air freight costs for the scooters shipping vs train? Locals already want to plan resources, tools & materials for the upfitting of the vehicles as soon as they arrive in {{2026-03-06}} already in Belgium, so creating the upfitting SOP by beginning of February would be quite important.\n\nWe can’t do any SOPs or upfitting if we don’t have the vehicles ourselves, 40 days seems already too long 😕 ","2026-01-09T12:51:43.804Z"],["3799073","L10N-27131","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27097](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27097)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-09T12:51:45.228Z"],["3799074","L10N-27132","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and tea