tant driver complaint\n* Fresh design eyes ([~accountid:712020:6268e700-78a8-48c2-9014-7ac2ed0d176b] ) could help\n* could be some conflict between price bidding and break mode\n** [~accountid:712020:47e6816d-876b-4d46-8a97-5225889a64c8] to share ticket later\n** [~accountid:61386b11a4f86e0069546dff] \n*** Two modes exist because of fleet\n**** Reach out to fleet on ideas to fix\n*** Need both offline/break for fleet shifts\n* Also b2b order break mode issues","2026-01-09T12:52:32.167Z"],["3799082","PFI-831397","PFI","alejandro.duarte@bolt.eu","Alejandro Kowalewski","[^Comprobante-408880001090823Bolt_Services_PY_FPY1526-125.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-09T12:52:34.621Z"],["3799084","MLC-3151","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W2:\n\n* Prepared updated screenshots and video overviews\n* Started the new Confluence but haven’t completed it. Will share with the team in W3 before publishing. \n* Will incorporate the additional content blocks and images that Yulia added this week.","2026-01-09T12:52:45.126Z"],["3799085","SREDESK-7394","SREDESK","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","`map_error` is also fixed.","2026-01-09T12:52:51.122Z"],["3799086","HS-28717","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Document signed by both parties. ","2026-01-09T12:53:19.949Z"],["3799087","MLC-1727","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W2:\n\n* Received next solution from Braze to solve the “first_session” issue but need to run it to confirm it works first. ","2026-01-09T12:53:27.787Z"],["3799088","SREP-1034","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","!image-20260109-125259.png|width=654,alt=\"image-20260109-125259.png\"!\n\n* EKS upgraded\n* Kube-proxy bumped\n* Nodes reprovisioned","2026-01-09T12:53:32.657Z"],["3799089","WFM-9924","WFM","elvyra.antanaviciene@bolt.eu","Elvyra Antanavičienė","Sorry, not reactive, but proactive. \n\n","2026-01-09T12:53:32.221Z"],["3799090","RDS-848","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-27589|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-27589|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T12:53:38.394Z"],["3799091","LSS-58474","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:60536b5060d39e006f7dae01] ,\n\nIn relation to your questions, and according to the advice provided by our external legal counsel, please note that in order to comply with existing regulatory requirements, Bolt should:\n\n* expressly prohibit the listing, sale, or distribution of prescription veterinary medicinal products through its platform;\n* contractually allocate full regulatory compliance responsibility to merchants; and\n* maintain and applies demonstrable mechanisms for the prompt removal of non-compliant listings and prevention of recurrence,\n\nTherefore, we advice:\n\n# Do we need to update existing merchant agreements?\n\n*A/ Yes, we need to do it as soon as possible for the agreements that we already have in place with pharmacies and pet shops.*\n\n# Should we add specific terms/clauses for new pet shop and pharmacy agreements?\n\n*A/ Yes. We should add the specific prohibition, and allocate responsibility to merchants.*\n\n# If required, could you please provide the relevant clause wording or an addendum template, or advise on next steps?\n\n*A/ Yes. In order to provide the wording, please share with us the current version of the agreement you have in place.* \n\nThank you!\n\nAngela","2026-01-09T12:53:45.245Z"],["3799093","INSUR-175","INSUR","alessandro@bolt.eu","Alessandro Milici","Next steps: \n\n* Send info to Carlo so we can get new quotes\n** Get new quotes\n* Check with Dan how the relationship between Marsh and [+Mujica Seguros+|https://www.mujicaseguros.com/2024/] (Marsh partner is PY). Based on this information, \n** Contact Alianza (through the local team) to check whether they are willing to work with us while we procure a new broker \n* Possibly check whether Carlo might be able to take over the renewal from Alianza. ","2026-01-09T12:54:03.828Z"],["3799094","PC-3257","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-4871 has been resolved","2026-01-09T12:54:25.614Z"],["3799095","LSS-61331","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340405|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340405|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T12:54:39.397Z"],["3799099","LSS-52369","LSS","kristiina.klemm@bolt.eu","Kristiina Klemm","[~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] The next is scheduled call for Monday afternoon, we will have meeting including Zellis' legal team, I would appreciate if we all would be ready with any questions by that time in case there are any. Thank you very much! 🙏 ","2026-01-09T12:55:21.433Z"],["3799100","PFI-831398","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-09T12:55:34.202Z"],["3799101","LSS-61332","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] - Please grant access to the document.","2026-01-09T12:56:12.120Z"],["3799102","SUPX-2309","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","Under discussion ([thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C091TUEKZNE/p1767868380581359])\n\nNeither {{getLightOrderDetailsByIds}} nor {{getOrderDetailsByIds}}, nor any other {{delivery-eater-order}} API that we can call for a single, individual order seems to be providing the relevant data right now. This must be fixed by eater-grox.","2026-01-09T12:56:26.134Z"],["3799103","LSS-61334","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Thanks for letting me know. Will be closing the ticket.","2026-01-09T12:56:32.121Z"],["3799104","RDS-1168","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","joonas to do analysis of this request","2026-01-09T12:57:13.796Z"],["3799106","PFI-829476","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-09T12:57:19.259Z"],["3799107","PFI-828863","PFI","daniele.fondjeutagouang@bolt.eu","Daniele Fondjeu Tagouang","Hi! The payout is still in rejected state.","2026-01-09T12:57:46.700Z"],["3799108","DRAG-720","DRAG","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","Waiting for V128 firmware from Genfo to start testing\n\n* Implemented tri-linear throttle curve\n* Modified power limiter to match D3.","2026-01-09T12:57:47.377Z"],["3799111","PFI-831009","PFI","norbert.kato@bolt.eu","Norbert Kato","Hi there! \nI have copied the problematic trip, and where the issue occurred, it shows that a deduction of 4,060 was made, followed by another amount—this is the item in question:\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3762471285|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3762471285]\n\nPreviously, a smaller amount is also visible, and what I don’t understand is that it seems to have been used abroad, because the amounts do not end in 0 or 50, which is typical for payments in Hungary. Perhaps there was some outstanding balance here that the system deducted later? However, these trips took place on September 28, and they had further travel afterward. One thing is certain: the 2,953.32 deduction was not for a domestic (Hungarian) trip, and at the moment of the deduction, it was not used abroad either.\nSo may question is, what is this transaction or how could it happen? \n\nAttaching a photo again with all the topup-s and claim-s, everyone has its own pair, but this ride has a strange one. \n\n!Képernyőfotó 2026-01-09 - 13.57.37.png|width=1161,height=582,alt=\"Képernyőfotó 2026-01-09 - 13.57.37.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-09T12:59:04.118Z"],["3799112","LSS-61336","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340406|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340406|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T12:59:17.679Z"],["3799113","LSS-61325","LSS","fareed.mahaini@bolt.eu","Fareed Mahaini","Hi[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432]could you please change the signatories name to this one Katja Ernst. Thank you!","2026-01-09T12:59:19.913Z"],["3799114","SRED-594","SRED","asko.tamm@bolt.eu","Asko Tamm","Example PR from the implemented automation:\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15204|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15204|smart-card]","2026-01-09T13:00:40.809Z"],["3799115","PFI-831378","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-09T13:00:46.275Z"],["3799116","WFM-9924","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hey, \n\nDone.","2026-01-09T13:00:49.985Z"],["3799117","DBRE-8683","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/db\\-rundeck\\-jobs/pull/13|https://github.com/bolteu/db-rundeck-jobs/pull/13]\n\n","2026-01-09T13:01:19.677Z"],["3799120","PAW-14758","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-09T13:01:37.506Z"],["3799121","LSS-61340","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340409|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340409|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:02:25.199Z"],["3799122","MLC-3527","MLC","daria.trokhina@bolt.eu","Daria Trokhina","*Week 2:*\n\n* Created a setup, so martech can work on A/B scorecard for in-apps (all relevant links are added to [this task|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/8/LM-21278]).\n* Tested Singular links (at first they didn’t work properly, so had a session with Singular to figure out how to set them up properly) – latest links work properly on all platforms (iOS, Android, web), utm parameters are populated and stored properly.","2026-01-09T13:02:44.546Z"],["3799123","DSR-3363","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] for you review. Superman case - driver will remain blocked. \n\n* Driver blocks, verifications, driver devices, driver security added [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/1an4t5fWpddnxxbFlPBVUyoBprwH2jn6K] \n* Response [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/1an4t5fWpddnxxbFlPBVUyoBprwH2jn6K]\n\n*Driver request*\n\nPlease confirm:\n# Whether the suspension decision was made solely through automated processing\n# Whether a human reviewer assessed my case and submitted evidence\n# What personal data and verification signals were used in this decision\n\nShould something additional be added to the response to cover the drivers 1. and 2. questions? \n\n*As the current BH case was solved a new outgoing message has to be created.* ","2026-01-09T13:02:51.458Z"],["3799124","DSR-3101","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:6001a723d364960139286c95], please answer the following to the user:\n\n{quote}Dear [*name*],\n\nThank you for your data protection request dated [*date*], in which you exercised your right to object to the processing of your personal data for direct marketing purposes under Article 21 GDPR.\n\nWe confirm that your personal data is not shared or disclosed to partners or third parties for marketing or advertising purposes where this is not permitted by law or where consent has not been provided. According to our records, you are not opted in to marketing communications and your personal data is not currently processed for direct marketing purposes.\n\nWhere Bolt carries out marketing activities, this is done in line with applicable data protection and e-privacy legislation and as described in our Global Privacy Notice for Passengers. In particular, marketing communications are only sent where a valid legal basis applies, and individuals may object to direct marketing at any time. Such objections are respected at the controller level and do not require any action to be taken within the app.\n\nFurther information about how Bolt processes personal data for marketing, the categories of recipients with whom personal data may be shared, and your rights as a data subject is set out in our Privacy Notice:\n[https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders/|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders/|smart-link] \n\nIf you have any further questions regarding the processing of your personal data, do not hesitate to let us know. \n\nSincerely,\n\nBolt{quote}\n\n[~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] , see my answer below to your questions:\n\n*Expand* \n\n# *Are we selling the user’s data?*\nNo. Bolt does not sell personal data.\n# *Are we sharing the user’s data with third parties for marketing or advertising?*\nOnly where there is a valid legal basis (e.g. consent or soft opt-in where permitted), and strictly for marketing and advertising purposes as described in the Privacy Notice. This typically covers:\n* marketing platforms,\n* advertising partners,\n* analytics linked to marketing performance.\n# *What happens when a user unsubscribes or objects to direct marketing?*\nWhen a user unsubscribes or exercises their Article 21 GDPR right to object to direct marketing:\n* Bolt stops processing their personal data for *direct marketing purposes*; and\n* Bolt stops *sharing their personal data with third parties for marketing or advertising purposes*.\nThis applies at the controller level and is not limited to in-app notifications or email preferences.\n# *Does unsubscribing stop* *_all_* *third-party data sharing?*\nNo. This is the key distinction.\nUnsubscribing or objecting to marketing *does not* affect:\n* data sharing necessary to provide the service (e.g. drivers, payment providers, cloud hosting, fraud prevention);\n* legally required disclosures; or\n* operational, security, or compliance-related processing.\nThese activities rely on different legal bases (performance of contract, legal obligation, legitimate interests) and are unaffected by marketing opt-outs.\n# *How does this align with the Privacy Notice wording about pixels and third parties?*\nThe Privacy Notice describes what Bolt _may_ do where marketing is active and permitted. Once a user unsubscribes or objects:\n* tracking linked to marketing emails or campaigns is no longer applied to that user; and\n* their personal data is no longer used or shared for personalised ads or marketing measurement.","2026-01-09T13:03:07.392Z"],["3799125","LSS-59012","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:61374989bba6c7006a2616ba] ,\n\nI just wanted to let you know that we have already worked on the amendments to the Fleet Agreement. We are validating some minor issues with external counsel, and we will get back to you as soon as we hear back from them.\n\nBest,\n\nAngela","2026-01-09T13:03:14.512Z"],["3799127","CSXDL-167","CSXDL","robert.aavik@bolt.eu","Robert Aavik","Research output is here: \n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1o-yvjOQ5yJ8IwYnXjG0NxxvX1gJ3-zJ77QyWQibS50E/edit?tab=t.qhai4w23p6tn#heading=h.1o24g5hrkpot|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1o-yvjOQ5yJ8IwYnXjG0NxxvX1gJ3-zJ77QyWQibS50E/edit?tab=t.qhai4w23p6tn#heading=h.1o24g5hrkpot|smart-link] \n\n*I didn’t look into why the FCR is low for AI*. This is because it requires understanding both the user intent and how AI misread it. \n\nWe anyway plan to solve this within the Routines project, and the biggest place where AI fails is _order_took_longer_eater_. The routine tracking for it is here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-HrxBb1fy6II8BTXiAIbV9SOegyEsA3bm0tFTxMVa5s/edit?tab=t.ybyr1uzaiufx|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-HrxBb1fy6II8BTXiAIbV9SOegyEsA3bm0tFTxMVa5s/edit?tab=t.ybyr1uzaiufx|smart-link] This is our next step to be fixed. \n\nOverall process Routine tracker is here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IRbJoXZ2eEmiOd-vAfYL10puHjnmp1AqIWNey-Sfpp4/edit?tab=t.93tzd3dv3pb6|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IRbJoXZ2eEmiOd-vAfYL10puHjnmp1AqIWNey-Sfpp4/edit?tab=t.93tzd3dv3pb6|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:03:36.684Z"],["3799131","PFI-831403","PFI","ricardo.otazu@bolt.eu","Enrique Otazu","[^BOLT (2).pdf]","2026-01-09T13:04:18.880Z"],["3799133","LSS-61344","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340410|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340410|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:04:34.966Z"],["3799135","MLC-3835","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W2:\n\n* Continued ad-hoc support and approved EE W2 comms. RO W3 comms have been submitted but haven’t had a chance to complete the ticket as of this writing. \n* Supported DineOut Survey request, comms will go out on 11.01\n* Started discussion with cross-pollination for next steps to target Riders\n* Reached out to Martech about Modal testing for the cohort. Ani mentioned that since it’s a small sample size, it might be hard to do testing. Ani will add the request in Jira for the February sprint and will discuss with Jason for priotitisation meeting. ","2026-01-09T13:05:40.413Z"],["3799138","SREP-1035","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* EKS upgraded\n* Kube-proxy bumped\n* Nodes reprovisioned\n\n!image-20260109-130602.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260109-130602.png\"!","2026-01-09T13:06:06.982Z"],["3799139","INT-676","INT","olga.vyrostko@bolt.eu","Olga Vyrostko","26W2: no updates, still blocked. ","2026-01-09T13:06:52.912Z"],["3799140","PFI-831404","PFI","kosisochukwu.ochuaka@bolt-outsource.eu","Kosisochukwu Ochuaka","[^3767985a-2c9a-4d61-8bf4-db60a1649ec1.pdf]","2026-01-09T13:06:59.000Z"],["3799141","WD-22529","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:63dba2fb1b13d42998e22e00] ,  I checked, the account configured for when the currency is HUF is  \n\n!image-20260109-130551.png|width=429,alt=\"image-20260109-130551.png\"!\n\nand not\n\n!image-20260109-130606.png|width=416,alt=\"image-20260109-130606.png\"!\n\n\nIf you would like \n\n!image-20260109-130610.png|width=416,alt=\"image-20260109-130610.png\"!\n\nTo show up for HUF, please let me know and I can update it. I have not seen anyone recently update it to 048 (in the recent past), and hence think that the other layout might have been updated manually. \nRegardless, please let me know and we can make the update. \n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-09T13:07:20.588Z"],["3799143","LSS-61345","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340412|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340412|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:08:00.283Z"],["3799146","PFI-831405","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-09T13:10:03.415Z"],["3799147","PFI-827558","PFI","anastasiia.levytska@bolt-outsource.eu","Anastasiia Levytska","Hi! this driver still has money on the balance, can you check again?","2026-01-09T13:10:14.046Z"],["3799148","MLC-3733","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W2:\n\n* Did not complete templates and slides, will prioritise for beginning of W3","2026-01-09T13:10:19.019Z"],["3799150","PFI-807512","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, invoices were reissued some time ago, didn’t click to send a message, apologies.","2026-01-09T13:10:35.819Z"],["3799151","WFM-9904","WFM","shady.elwaziry@bolt.eu","Shady El Waziry","Hi [~accountid:712020:9c0690de-08a9-41cf-93b1-9184ed368330], \n\nI’m not sure if you mean Beehive Admin Portal or the Tool itself.\n\nWhat I want is the Tool itself to see cases/tickets and knoweldge base.\n\nThanks,","2026-01-09T13:10:38.529Z"],["3799152","RIDE-542","RIDE","subarna.sharna@bolt.eu","Subarna Islam Sharna","[~accountid:712020:d3fd53e6-f124-4770-a577-b09d6688566f] Hi! Thanks. It’s a valuable insight. We’ll allocate 2 hours roughly then. Considering potential back and forth collaboration to handle and process payments","2026-01-09T13:10:44.999Z"],["3799153","FX-3384","FX","jana.lutus@bolt.eu","Jana Lutus","Utilisation is calculated based on the time the driver spends in the {{HAS_ORDER}} status, not the duration of their rides. Since the status doesn’t actually change when multiple rides overlap, the time gets counted from the first acceptance until the last drop-off. So there should be no double-counting. ","2026-01-09T13:10:47.201Z"],["3799154","LSS-52572","LSS","tomasz.symonowicz@bolt.eu","Tomasz Symonowicz","hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] thank you for your support, it would be great if you could submit it : ) ","2026-01-09T13:10:49.453Z"],["3799157","INT-730","INT","dzmitry.kasakouski@bolt.eu","Dzmitry Kasakouski","26W2:\n\n* unrelated tasks: removing city_id from offer, fixing ride cashback eligelibity logic\n* had kick-off meeting for the project\n* working on adding payment plans on green banner on the offer landing page","2026-01-09T13:11:30.888Z"],["3799159","PFI-809177","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Thanks for the response! I believe we can close the ticket and continue it here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/PFI/issue/PFI-808686|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/PFI/issue/PFI-808686]\n\nSince it’s a billing issue I have assigned the ticket to Ride Hailing Billing queue. ","2026-01-09T13:12:33.775Z"],["3799162","SCM-971","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","Process design WIP Google Sheet\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1ghhkOwjWcT93hiO8rXW7nP_ZXPQCudi8NPqYfrlgMKM/edit?gid=470024415#gid=470024415|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1ghhkOwjWcT93hiO8rXW7nP_ZXPQCudi8NPqYfrlgMKM/edit?gid=470024415#gid=470024415|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:13:15.868Z"],["3799167","PFI-813786","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, the payments for the following Order were split ([https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1465493616/96|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1465493616/96])\n\n!image-20260109-131252.png|width=657,alt=\"image-20260109-131252.png\"!\n\nDon’t really know why it was split instead of the having a single payment.","2026-01-09T13:14:10.549Z"],["3799168","WD-21831","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:712020:2261816b-1a2b-4b75-b1dc-d5fce431ad15] , I looked at these requirements and they are a bit unclear, for example, the field: “grounds for issuing the order;” what will this be filed out with on the printed layout for the expense report? \n\n\n\nI think the best way is to do a comparison between an existing expense report and the required expense report and map the fields between the 2. [~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c]  and I are happy to connect for a quick call and review further. \n\n\n\nIn the meantime, I am working on creating the layout structure. \n\n\n\nPlease advice.\n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-09T13:14:20.110Z"],["3799171","SUPX-2313","SUPX","artem.kudlaienko@bolt.eu","Artem Kudlaienko","fyi[~accountid:631f27278738d3ca32254937] [~accountid:712020:33002f0b-c802-4f83-911e-b96c405eae99] I’ve created a task for pending cases reminder we discussed earlier","2026-01-09T13:15:19.810Z"],["3799172","EBIKE1-392","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","New target clearance for the EB1 customised kickstand: around *30mm*\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"5fe808db-26e7-416c-bf80-9250e303f557\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":4},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Okai EB100 rear tire clearance while standing on the kickstand.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"28mm\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"27mm\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":306,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"32b907ec4afd56759f40415ff70fbdd2-20260109-131313.jpg\",\"alt\":\"32b907ec4afd56759f40415ff70fbdd2-20260109-131313.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":306,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"d31b1e2b79fb568c771e9c57f3461d93-20260109-131333.jpg\",\"alt\":\"d31b1e2b79fb568c771e9c57f3461d93-20260109-131333.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":426,\"width\":567}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":226,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"da3690c8e94a0a86b9799a5b14dec894-20260109-131457.jpg\",\"alt\":\"da3690c8e94a0a86b9799a5b14dec894-20260109-131457.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":226,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"c894a3e0ad5b8f999f459b4bf8b06d55-20260109-131451.jpg\",\"alt\":\"c894a3e0ad5b8f999f459b4bf8b06d55-20260109-131451.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-09T13:15:45.400Z"],["3799173","SREP-1078","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","During cluster reprovisioned increased memory utilization, will bump a bit to avoid noise \n\n!image-20260109-131552.png|width=706,alt=\"image-20260109-131552.png\"!","2026-01-09T13:16:19.568Z"],["3799174","PFI-828313","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Closing this ticket; the issue has been solved and invoice now appears with invoice number properly.","2026-01-09T13:16:48.321Z"],["3799176","PFI-831410","PFI","lotanna.nnaji@bolt-outsource.eu","Lotanna Nnaji","!Screenshot_20260108_203903_ee.mtakso.driver.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T13:17:19.055Z"],["3799180","PFI-831412","PFI","lukas.dusek@bolt-outsource.eu","Lukas Dusek","!IMG_3839.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T13:18:04.740Z"],["3799182","DRAG101-471","DRAG101","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390] [~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] can we use cheap air? ","2026-01-09T13:18:15.215Z"],["3799183","OKAI-179","OKAI","norman.tamm@bolt.eu","Norman Tamm","OKAI error collections are now LIVE in log-only mode.\nIoT rulesets have been set in admin: [Link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/rentals-micromobility/vehicles/iot-rulesets/edit/27]\n\n*Next steps:*\nCollect data and check in next week, how many vehicles have been affected and what the impact.","2026-01-09T13:18:56.539Z"],["3799187","PFI-831413","PFI","norbert.kato@bolt.eu","Norbert Kato","!Képernyőfotó 2026-01-09 - 14.19.08.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T13:19:26.174Z"],["3799188","WDFT-3546","WDFT","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044] , for this company, do we use the generic Poland layout for this customer invoice? “ Customer Invoice local - Poland“ ","2026-01-09T13:19:37.622Z"],["3799190","WDFT-3546","WDFT","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Blocked by company not created. ","2026-01-09T13:19:51.939Z"],["3799191","PFI-831414","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-09T13:19:52.481Z"],["3799192","INT-553","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W2: Implementation of provider targeting improvements in progress. Spend period and hour selection bugfixes validated by GA. ENG added approval access for local teams to Account Management traitless sheet - saving GA time.","2026-01-09T13:19:59.173Z"],["3799194","LSS-59845","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nSentry will update the Order Form. May we share our feedback regarding the MSA?\n\nThanks!\n\n","2026-01-09T13:20:20.144Z"],["3799197","LSS-52572","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","[~accountid:712020:0b391d02-6c8a-4494-99fd-3d2ff0d7ef37] by legal ops I meant [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] or [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] 😉 basically, this submission does not require a final Ahto signature, so I think you can submit it by yourself 😉 ","2026-01-09T13:20:57.718Z"],["3799198","DSR-3617","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-09T13:21:09.888Z"],["3799200","INT-647","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W2: Development to start next sprint (in 2w). Will add budget from CSV → S3 and existing automated (ULC Smart Promo) and non-automated campaigns to Market Manager.","2026-01-09T13:21:29.487Z"],["3799201","PFI-831415","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-09T13:21:38.800Z"],["3799202","PAW-14630","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-admin-user, pint-product-identity-and-communication-management, pint-capability-itgc\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-09T13:21:43.732Z"],["3799203","PAW-14627","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-admin-user, pint-product-identity-and-communication-management, pint-capability-itgc\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-09T13:21:49.645Z"],["3799204","PAW-14268","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-njsc-db, pint-product-backend-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-09T13:21:59.888Z"],["3799205","SAI-1399","SAI","przemyslaw.wiczolek@bolt.eu","Przemysław Wiczołek","Hey! I need some feedback regarding Alfred's datapoints :pray: . For now, we have used [this|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CD/pages/6876987536/2025-10+Current+data+available+for+CS+AI#Driver] page for  data mappings in routines, however, I'm not sure whether some part of this might be outdated? I know that payment_context_data was added just recently, plus I'm also struggling with {{payment_pre_authorization}}. Regarding Alfred's data, it should be an object containing {{amount}} and {{is_pre_authorized}}, but instead of this we have a variable \"{{payment_pre_authorization_amount}}\" in context data (and for most of the actual cases it is null so it is difficult to find actual data with non null value). How we should approach this when currently we have it written in routine as an object but it seems not to be so?","2026-01-09T13:22:14.052Z"],["3799206","SAI-1399","SAI",null,"Slack","[Przemysław Wiczołek|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:f3b3e918-2599-4c21-991c-efa4dcddf08d] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09KBMVTYTG/p1767963946294669?thread_ts=1767963946.294669&cid=C09KBMVTYTG|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09KBMVTYTG/p1767963946294669?thread_ts=1767963946.294669&cid=C09KBMVTYTG|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-09T13:22:15.330Z"],["3799207","SAI-1399","SAI","przemyslaw.wiczolek@bolt.eu","Przemysław Wiczołek","Hey, I think you're confusing the 2 context types - the generic context and the mapped context.\n\nThe mapped context is what you, yourself define, the names can be anything, like {{kaie_variable}}\nThis is defined in mapping and then you reference it in the routine.\n\nThe generic context is all of the data points we provide.\nThis is where {{payment_pre_authorization}} is present.\n\nYou defined {{payment_pre_authorization_amount}} as\n\n{noformat}order_context.meta_data.payment_pre_authorization.amount{noformat}\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8LRQJP24/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8LRQJP24/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-09T13:22:15.609Z"],["3799208","SAI-1399","SAI","przemyslaw.wiczolek@bolt.eu","Przemysław Wiczołek","[https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/customer-support-automations/routinestool/edit/360006|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/customer-support-automations/routinestool/edit/360006]","2026-01-09T13:22:16.213Z"],["3799209","SAI-1399","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","The {{is_pre_authorized}} is deprecated, and we should not use it, sorry for the confusion. We don't have any valid pre authorization datapoint, exception is scooter's context, where the vertical exposes such field to us.\n\nFor rides, we used to use {{is_pre_authorized}}  in some hacky workaround on our end, but it is not reliable. We didn't clean it up","2026-01-09T13:22:17.230Z"],["3799210","SAI-1399","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","For scooters we can use: {{order_context.meta_data.preauth_data}} and it is valid datapoint","2026-01-09T13:22:17.724Z"],["3799211","SAI-1399","SAI","przemyslaw.wiczolek@bolt.eu","Przemysław Wiczołek","{quote}*Grzegorz Brotoń*  [2:17 PM]\nThe {{is_pre_authorized}} is deprecated, and we should not use it, sorry for the confusion. We don't have any valid pre authorization datapoint, exception is scooter's context, where the vertical exposes such field to us.\n\nFor rides, we used to use {{is_pre_authorized}}  in some hacky workaround on our end, but it is not reliable. We didn't clean it up{quote}\n\nDon't we have self-serve for this? What does SuppX use?","2026-01-09T13:22:18.223Z"],["3799212","SAI-1399","SAI","kaie.palmaru@bolt.eu","Kaie Palmaru","ah, actually yes, managed to read and reference wrong context, I also wanted to see how it actually looks like, but nevertheless, for riders, it means that we cannot use this at all?","2026-01-09T13:22:19.061Z"],["3799213","SAI-1399","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","{quote}Don't we have self-serve for this? What does SuppX use?{quote}\n\nThey were suppose to get a valid API from rides to get it, but I don't know the current status. Maybe [@oleg.alieksieienko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5bb770688eb5ad7760adbdc3] can help here.\n\n{{is_pre_authorized}}  comes from mid 2024, where we did try to run this hacky workaround, but it didn't work out","2026-01-09T13:22:19.745Z"],["3799214","SAI-1399","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","{quote}but nevertheless, for riders, it means that we cannot use this at all?{quote}\n\nYes, we cannot :sad_cat:","2026-01-09T13:22:20.241Z"],["3799215","INT-652","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W2: Set up brainstorm session next week to help GA with playbooks.","2026-01-09T13:23:04.511Z"],["3799216","LSS-61339","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Act of acceptance_Bolt Operations OÜ_Bolt Services KZ_31.12.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T13:23:05.592Z"],["3799217","INT-650","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W2: Development work in progress.","2026-01-09T13:23:41.708Z"],["3799218","LSS-61324","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Shipment tracking code: [https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=1865396540&submit=1|https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=1865396540&submit=1|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:23:46.294Z"],["3799222","WEBSD-1457","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi!\n\nPlease provide the PDF with the change need it.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-09T13:25:05.308Z"],["3799223","PFI-829509","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! So:\n\n# The invoices issued for Food orders are issued by providers, meaning that Bolt does not issue invoices on behalf of restaurants. \n# The document that’s attached here that we also send to the user is a statement that is not considered a tax document, so this is not relevant. If a user wishes to use documents for accounting purposes, they need to request it from the restaurant. \n# Overall, these changes do not affect us 🙂 ","2026-01-09T13:25:07.567Z"],["3799224","DBRE-8139","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","* (/) {{central-db-1.sqldb}} is fixed in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8650|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8650|smart-link]\n* (/) {{cs-d3.sqldb}} is fixed in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8686|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8686|smart-link]\n* (/) {{fraud-db-1.sqldb}} is fixed in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8649|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8649|smart-link]\n* (/) {{invoicing-d3.sqldb}} is fixed in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8603|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8603|smart-link] \n* (/) {{na-db-3.sqldb}} is fixed in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8602|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8602|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:25:15.475Z"],["3799225","MLC-3171","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","Business Users: HVO ja Promo codes pending review - launching 12.01. \nActivation, Pushing to X Ride, Churn, Retention - LIVE ","2026-01-09T13:25:24.458Z"],["3799227","DBRE-8125","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","* (/) {{central-db-1.sqldb}} is fixed in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8650|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8650|smart-link]\n* (/) {{cs-d3.sqldb}} is fixed in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8686|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8686|smart-link] \n* (/) {{fraud-db-1.sqldb}} is fixed in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8649|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8649|smart-link]\n* (/) {{invoicing-d3.sqldb}} is fixed in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8603|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8603|smart-link] \n* (/) {{na-db-3.sqldb}} is fixed in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8602|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8602|smart-link]","2026-01-09T13:25:37.070Z"],["3799228","INT-653","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W2: Proposal to scale to all cities reviewed and aligned with GA, launching next week. Holdout group assignment automation design doc in review. Launched first measurement test for campaign uplift retention.","2026-01-09T13:25:45.843Z"],["3799230","INT-656","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W2: ENG work ongoing, will start data exploration once done.","2026-01-09T13:26:16.245Z"],["3799231","LSS-59845","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] yes please share reviewed MSA with Sentry [https://docs.google.com/document/d/19MN79tbPIKtWd151uCy50EiaojI1D6jn/edit#heading=h.2s8eyo1|https://docs.google.com/document/d/19MN79tbPIKtWd151uCy50EiaojI1D6jn/edit#heading=h.2s8eyo1|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:26:28.915Z"],["3799232","MLC-1724","MLC","anniecel.malabanan@bolt.eu","Anniecel Malabanan","*Update W2*\n\nWill draft the announcements for the local teams and schedule the comm for launch next week. \nThe list of canvases can be seen [here|https://dashboard-02.braze.eu/engagement/canvas/canvas/660bb2da4a75710056541496?name=%22%5C%22pushing%20to%20add%5C%22%22&sortAscending=true&sortColumn=%22name%22&locale=en].  ","2026-01-09T13:26:39.614Z"],["3799233","INT-657","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W2: Started exploratory data analysis on simple uplift model using recent Bucharest data with global control group. Will share findings in next weeks.","2026-01-09T13:27:07.006Z"],["3799234","WFM-9904","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hey [~accountid:712020:cde6e2fa-0f48-44e8-b1c7-2a3a70d10b33],\n\nNot sure if I got the point. Could you please try to open this link to Beehive [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/] and take a screenshot of the error that is popping up? ","2026-01-09T13:27:14.023Z"],["3799236","PASD-170","PASD","george.matu@bolt.eu","George Matu","Hey hey, in order to correct the delays, we need a human input, and we were OOO during the winter break. I see now both of your days are showing correctly and your overall status for December is that you are compliant. \n\nThanks for the understanding! ","2026-01-09T13:27:26.710Z"],["3799237","PFI-831296","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:6d5640ba-c28b-492d-b071-2c5df1c7e01b],\n\nThat we can not confirm unfortunately due to how business systems are set up, making the businesses themselves look legitimate.\nHowever, essentially what campaign abuse with driver fraud means, is that the driver is acting in a fraudulent manner while abusing the campaigns.\nIn this instance we can not confirm if the driver has stolen the credit cards, however, wether it is alone, or with a 3rd party, then there is a collusion between the driver and the business accounts that are being created - however, we’re quite safe from it since everything gets refunded, therefore there are no losses for Bolt.\n\nPlease do let me know by tagging me within the ticket if there are any other questions.\nMarten","2026-01-09T13:27:32.367Z"],["3799246","WD-22503","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","you will accrue 1.67 per month from Jan to May\n\nKind regards,\n\nOli","2026-01-09T13:29:39.567Z"],["3799247","LSS-61264","LSS","joao.nunes@bolt.eu","João Nunes","Thank you! [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ","2026-01-09T13:30:17.911Z"],["3799248","LSS-61313","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Vendor *Omni Advisory A.A.R.P.I.* has successfully been onboarded to BrightFlag! User account has been created and email with instructions sent. Additional user accounts will be created if requested. Please ensure to add the vendor as a supplier to Workday as well if needed. Guide is available here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BILP/pages/4719673539/Engagement+rules+for+new+suppliers|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BILP/pages/4719673539/Engagement+rules+for+new+suppliers|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:31:10.167Z"],["3799252","LSS-60145","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:c28ac319-83e4-4d10-926a-3e90f309e781] , thank you for the ticket! A few questions:\n\n* Have we signed anything for the pilot?\n* Do you know if we need to sign another agreement with them?","2026-01-09T13:33:02.317Z"],["3799253","PIF-2737","PIF","gabriel.olaru@bolt.eu","Gabriel Olaru","Done by the requester already: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/commit/bc571abc711e649b4f2ce7e4490b8065f12443c1|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/commit/bc571abc711e649b4f2ce7e4490b8065f12443c1|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:33:34.001Z"],["3799254","INT-352","INT","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","26W2: We successfully launched the Annual Reforecasting cycle. Country teams are currently actively reviewing the models. We had a new features onboarding session with CTs and next week we will host it for GAs. ","2026-01-09T13:33:34.885Z"],["3799256","PFI-830507","PFI","lydia.anokye@bolt.eu","Lydia Anokye","Payout Link\n\n[+https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records/27937630764+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records/27937630764]","2026-01-09T13:33:46.777Z"],["3799257","LSS-60711","LSS","ololade.olanipekun@bolt.eu","Ololade Olanipekun","[^Bolt BOLT LEASE AGREEMENT rev 30-12-2025 (tracked).pdf]\n\nHi Team,\n\nI’m pleased to inform you that the landlord has agreed to our proposed changes.\n\nHowever, we noticed a correction in the contract regarding the power cost allocation in section 4e. The contract initially reflected a quarterly charge of 20% of the annual power expense\n(20/100 × 28,952 ÷ 4 = 1,447.6), instead of the agreed 25%\n(25/100 × 28,952 ÷ 4 = 1,809.5). This has now been corrected by the landlord in the contract.\n\nAttached is the signed version of the contract, along with an editable Word version in case we still need to make any further changes.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1775NkrdttFyJZPLA7Bl7FOijUyEJ0ZOD/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1775NkrdttFyJZPLA7Bl7FOijUyEJ0ZOD/edit|smart-link] \n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or need clarifications.\n\nThank you","2026-01-09T13:33:50.454Z"],["3799258","LSS-61041","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team, \nthank you all for your input in preparing the response to the insolvency administrator. \n\nSharing the signed document for visibility purposes: [^2026-01-08 Creditor Claim (Tur Taxi AS)_Bolt Operations OÜ.pdf] \n\nAlso, sharing our response draft in ENG:\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OlWG8Cf5MKFLriSnob5n75eKVVW3YE6sFfYNgmBfTLM/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OlWG8Cf5MKFLriSnob5n75eKVVW3YE6sFfYNgmBfTLM/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:33:57.871Z"],["3799261","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] Thank you!","2026-01-09T13:35:06.421Z"],["3799265","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] let’s do Mon!","2026-01-09T13:35:40.012Z"],["3799266","WFM-9925","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello,\n\nProactive comms are now live!","2026-01-09T13:36:05.561Z"],["3799269","LSS-61351","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","[^pełnomocnictwo Bolt Rides PL korespondencja.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T13:36:55.921Z"],["3799270","DPM-2211","DPM","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] Yes, I think it’s a good idea to move remaining/ongoing tasks into Improvements Epic. ","2026-01-09T13:37:18.430Z"],["3799271","IOTTEAM-243","IOTTEAM","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","For now can’t do anything else until new hardware arrives.","2026-01-09T13:37:47.504Z"],["3799272","LSS-59845","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Thank you [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] .\n\nI have shared with them. Please also find the updated Order Form.\n\n[^Sentry Order Form for Bolt 09012025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T13:38:01.010Z"],["3799273","HS-28483","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Contract should be sent today by Papaya. ","2026-01-09T13:38:26.493Z"],["3799274","PFI-831381","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Answered via Slack.\nDuplicate escalation.","2026-01-09T13:39:07.673Z"],["3799276","PFI-814709","PFI","melanija.pticek@bolt.eu","Melanija Ptiček","Hi, \n\nI’ve already submitted an SD regarding this issue, but so far it’s been two months of the teams passing the case back and forth without any resolution. Billing says it’s Payouts’ responsibility, and Payouts says it’s Billing’s.\n\nThis case involves an incorrect payment, so it’s important to clarify which team is accountable and get it resolved. Could you please review this situation and provide a clear path forward?\n\nThank you for your attention.\n\nBest regards,\n","2026-01-09T13:39:36.715Z"],["3799277","MLC-3532","MLC","anniecel.malabanan@bolt.eu","Anniecel Malabanan","*Update W2*\n\nTreat Yourself Week and Q1 General Comms has been sent out. ","2026-01-09T13:40:06.037Z"],["3799279","PFI-829509","PFI","alexandra.kopcanova@bolt.eu","Alexandra Kopčanová","Great 🙂 thank you for your help.","2026-01-09T13:40:31.620Z"],["3799281","PFI-831423","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-09T13:41:01.820Z"],["3799282","PFI-831378","PFI","daniel.novo@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniel Novo","Still need help\n\n","2026-01-09T13:41:09.178Z"],["3799284","WFM-9904","WFM","shady.elwaziry@bolt.eu","Shady El Waziry","Hey No problem, I just did more steps and the Beehive tool itself is now working - it was giving me 400 Error SSL certificate not available.\n\nAll good now.","2026-01-09T13:41:58.326Z"],["3799285","WEBSD-1457","WEBSD","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^FINAL PL- Global Template_ Customer Terms (Rides) PL.docx.pdf]\n\nHi [~accountid:712020:9e668ce4-0877-43c6-bae9-52f1ecbc753f] ! Please find attached, thank you! ","2026-01-09T13:42:37.902Z"],["3799288","LSS-61213","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:60a37337391e56006e62277c] ! for sure, you may ping the Partner. The contract has been signed from our side.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 15.42.59.png|width=587,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 15.42.59.png\"!","2026-01-09T13:43:07.384Z"],["3799291","PFI-823509","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nSorry for the delayed response. \n\nThe payment has been now released and the payment state has been updated in Admin. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T13:44:01.453Z"],["3799293","PFI-831424","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^TRANSF_BOLT_PY1525-4698.pdf]","2026-01-09T13:44:25.698Z"],["3799295","LEG-1133","LEG","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","Hey[~accountid:712020:96f9e924-98dd-4ef5-a7da-0752de9a24ce] - just refreshing myself on this, I’ll get back to you early next week 👍 ","2026-01-09T13:45:14.307Z"],["3799297","PAW-14760","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-09T13:45:43.323Z"],["3799298","LSS-61041","LSS","martin.foss.johansen@bolt.eu","Martin Foss Johansen","Thank you [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc]!","2026-01-09T13:45:44.129Z"],["3799300","PASD-169","PASD","george.matu@bolt.eu","George Matu","Hey, sorry for the delay, most of our team has been OOO during the winter break. \n\nFrom what I see in your request, we do not have access to _National Insurance numbers_ or to employee home addresses (only assigned work locations). If you still need the data without these data points, let us know so that we can prepare the file. \n\nI am not sure where the insurance numbers are stored, but I would check with someone from either People Ops (Aire Vaigu) or the Regional People for UK Karolyna Tadych (e.g. maybe this info is required in the employee file/ contract).","2026-01-09T13:46:08.103Z"],["3799301","MLC-3791","MLC","anniecel.malabanan@bolt.eu","Anniecel Malabanan","*Update W2*\n\nI will slowly work on the topic and add subtasks on each task that are listed here: [+Merchant Action Items (Maintenance)+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/14TYxG3fdFo1CBAPN3bCmA19VOxZpizuom6JVmCNSbp4/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.2fanurxu3kli]\n\nI plan to do at least one maintenance task each week. Will update the progress on the subtask and also attach a tracker. ","2026-01-09T13:46:15.655Z"],["3799302","LSS-61352","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nCorneliu-Ștefan Radu has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-09T13:46:18.586Z"],["3799303","SUPX-2253","SUPX","artem.kudlaienko@bolt.eu","Artem Kudlaienko","Follow-up task: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SUPX-2313|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SUPX-2313|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:47:04.995Z"],["3799304","PFI-821562","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nMy apologies for a delayed response. \n\nI can confirm the funds have been returned to the customer by the finance team. \n\nPlease let me know if the user is still having any issues and I will reopen the ticket. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T13:47:29.623Z"],["3799305","LSS-61177","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed NDA attached.\n\n[^NDA_Bolt Operations OÜ_PARTNERS FOR AUTOMATED VEHICLE EDUCATION EUROPE ASSOCIATION AISBL (PAVE Europe)_09.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T13:47:32.844Z"],["3799306","WFM-9926","WFM","mwenesi.constantine@bolt-outsource.eu","Mwenesi Constantine","Sorry, I meant queues not roles","2026-01-09T13:47:49.719Z"],["3799307","LSS-61353","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nCorneliu-Ștefan Radu has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-09T13:47:53.105Z"],["3799309","LSS-61303","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed NDA attached.\n\n[^NDA_Bolt Operations OÜ_Mr. Lube Canada G.P. INC._07.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T13:48:07.568Z"],["3799310","DPM-2275","DPM","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","# {{Stores column of the product listing page:}}\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 15.45.59.png|width=775,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 15.45.59.png\"!\n\n# {{right pane that is opened when user clicks on the stores in the Store column (already exists):}}\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 15.47.29.png|width=510,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 15.47.29.png\"!\n\n# {{Stores dropdown selector on the Filters pane:}}\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 15.45.49.png|width=658,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 15.45.49.png\"!\n\n# {{Selling Price column}}:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.44.51.png|width=510,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.44.51.png\"!\n# {{stores selection dropdown and below (existing):}}\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.28.19.png|width=448,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.28.19.png\"!\n# {{Publish page}}\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.28.16.png|width=475,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.28.16.png\"!","2026-01-09T13:48:25.558Z"],["3799313","LSS-61309","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed documents attached. Signed the same way as last time.\n\n[^Appendix 1 - Ride-hailing and business Localisation Assignment Agreement [NL]  (28420826-b5f0-497d-960e-6c5c54a7cec4).pdf]\n[^Ride-hailing and business Localisation Assignment Agreement [NL] - Bolt Rides & Bolt Business_Bolt Operations OÜ_Bolt Support Services NL B.V._01.12.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T13:49:01.423Z"],["3799314","PFI-829509","PFI","adam.ruman@bolt.eu","Adam Ruman","Thanks Ketlin. Would it be possible to hide the VAT columns anyway? Just to be sure we’re not giving ammo to anyone who’d be interested in digging in this topic either eater or merchant. Thanks a million! ","2026-01-09T13:49:06.799Z"],["3799317","LSS-61237","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:616ff0d63e3753006f99a61c] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^20260106_1 police Bolt atbilde.docx.edoc] ","2026-01-09T13:50:26.571Z"],["3799318","LSS-61145","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed PoAs attached.\n\n[^PoA (Bolt Drive_Police_LT-LV-EE)_Valters Lans_07.01.26.pdf]\n[^PoA (Bolt Drive_Police_LT-LV-EE)_Sandis Masulis_07.01.26.pdf]\n[^PoA (Bolt Drive_Police_LT-LV-EE)_Romans Cepurko_07.01.26.pdf]\n[^PoA (Bolt Drive_Police_LT-LV-EE)_Raivis Ruskulis_07.01.26.pdf]\n[^PoA (Bolt Drive_Police_LT-LV-EE)_Nils Vilcāns_07.01.26.pdf]\n[^PoA (Bolt Drive_Police_LT-LV-EE)_Matīss Bogdanovs_07.01.26.pdf]\n[^PoA (Bolt Drive_Police_LT-LV-EE)_Lelde Kaktiņa_07.01.26.pdf]\n[^PoA (Bolt Drive_Police_LT-LV-EE)_Illarions Museridze_07.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-09T13:50:41.844Z"],["3799319","SREDESK-7398","SREDESK","andrus.viik@bolt.eu","Andrus Viik","Have you considered Admin panels s3 bucket access feature \n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03UY0T0WV7/p1758797814692209|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03UY0T0WV7/p1758797814692209|smart-card]","2026-01-09T13:50:42.734Z"],["3799320","LSS-61333","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","Hey [~accountid:61486abca995ad0073aeb016], don’t we already have a co-financing with Abu? ","2026-01-09T13:51:02.607Z"],["3799321","DSR-3619","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-09T13:51:07.382Z"],["3799322","HS-28812","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Integration error/duplicate ticket, no action needed. ","2026-01-09T13:51:11.514Z"],["3799323","L10N-27068","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.553Z"],["3799324","L10N-27079","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.573Z"],["3799325","L10N-27065","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.595Z"],["3799326","L10N-27077","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.667Z"],["3799327","L10N-27080","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.712Z"],["3799328","L10N-27071","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.719Z"],["3799329","L10N-27054","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.777Z"],["3799330","L10N-27069","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.798Z"],["3799331","L10N-27074","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.840Z"],["3799332","L10N-27076","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.848Z"],["3799333","L10N-27073","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.880Z"],["3799334","L10N-27072","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.924Z"],["3799335","L10N-27067","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.937Z"],["3799336","L10N-27075","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.947Z"],["3799337","L10N-27082","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.958Z"],["3799338","L10N-27083","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:23.994Z"],["3799339","L10N-27078","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:24.044Z"],["3799340","L10N-27081","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:24.075Z"],["3799341","L10N-27070","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:24.082Z"],["3799342","L10N-27066","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:24.203Z"],["3799344","L10N-27055","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:27.051Z"],["3799345","L10N-27059","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.353Z"],["3799346","L10N-27063","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.363Z"],["3799347","L10N-27056","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.395Z"],["3799348","L10N-27061","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.411Z"],["3799349","L10N-27064","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.455Z"],["3799350","L10N-27057","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.506Z"],["3799351","L10N-27058","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.591Z"],["3799352","L10N-27060","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.609Z"],["3799353","L10N-27038","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.712Z"],["3799354","L10N-27050","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.757Z"],["3799355","L10N-27051","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.784Z"],["3799356","L10N-27053","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.865Z"],["3799357","L10N-27034","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.975Z"],["3799358","L10N-27049","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:28.987Z"],["3799359","L10N-27052","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T13:51:29.180Z"],["3799360","HS-28810","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","Hey Alice,\n\nPlease initiate transfer to another manager task in Workday. More info: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BMP/pages/4579000801/Workday+for+Managers|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BMP/pages/4579000801/Workday+for+Managers|smart-link]\n\nKind regards,\n\nKristin - People Ops","2026-01-09T13:51:56.640Z"],["3799361","LSS-61299","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:6130bde04a98da0069dcad14] ! Would dokobit signature be sufficient? Thank you! ","2026-01-09T13:52:02.456Z"],["3799363","LSS-61196","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] !\n\n[^Bolt_shareholder decision_employment conditions of new CEO 26.01.06 docx.docx.adoc]\n\n","2026-01-09T13:52:40.655Z"],["3799364","SREDO-295","SREDO","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","As agreed, we will continue using the same approach and update to the next LTS version.","2026-01-09T13:53:03.695Z"],["3799365","SREDO-296","SREDO","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","As agreed, we will continue using the same approach and update to the next LTS version.","2026-01-09T13:53:12.213Z"],["3799366","LSS-61193","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc]! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n [^Indemnification agreement - Bolt .docx.adoc] ","2026-01-09T13:53:31.777Z"],["3799370","MLC-3843","MLC","anniecel.malabanan@bolt.eu","Anniecel Malabanan","*Update W2*\n\nI haven’t started anything yet with this project. I need to find the Documentation made by Carol and proceed with the further steps needed. ","2026-01-09T13:54:28.306Z"],["3799371","LSS-61128","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^Ewa Ożańska PEL Bolt Poland (9532dc48-a74c-4db6-b76f-e7cd6493a176).pdf]\n\nHi Team, please proceed with signing the attached PoA with Ahto’s Dokobit signature. Thank you! ","2026-01-09T13:54:49.737Z"],["3799373","LSS-61298","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:615c75e007ac3c0068114285] ,\n\nThank you for raising this ticket.\n\nWe are starting the review and will get back to you soon.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T13:55:00.152Z"],["3799375","BP-13390","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","[~accountid:712020:3c6bcc42-4172-4c4d-b924-e17fb5f0a336] one more thing - since the company details form is backend-driven, we’ll need a way to associate values with the corresponding form fields.\nWe can continue discussion in Slack if needed :)","2026-01-09T13:55:25.057Z"],["3799376","LSS-45949","LSS","anton.schoeps@bolt.eu","Anton Schöps","Hi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a],  when I checked last in September, it seemed that I had followed everything that was possible at that time. So I considered our part as done. \n","2026-01-09T13:55:35.137Z"],["3799377","LSS-45949","LSS","anton.schoeps@bolt.eu","Anton Schöps","Thank you for reminding us and thank you for your patience! 🙂 ","2026-01-09T13:56:02.424Z"],["3799381","MLC-3716","MLC","yulia.nikitina@bolt.eu","Yulia Nikitina","*W2: Closing this epic, all Activation stage analysis can be found here:*\n\n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7217480129/Couriers+Activation+Stage+Optimisation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7217480129/Couriers+Activation+Stage+Optimisation|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:56:42.011Z"],["3799382","PFI-831427","PFI","alejandro.duarte@bolt.eu","Alejandro Kowalewski","[^Comprobantes Bolt (Julio a Noviembre).pdf.pdf]","2026-01-09T13:56:42.499Z"],["3799385","PFI-831352","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nGreat question! \n\nThe business refunds process has not changed. They are by default only sent to the business balance. \nHowever, this was an exception. \nThe customer payments team has received a request by you to issue the refund to the OPM. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/PFI/queues/custom/379/PFI-806172|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/PFI/queues/custom/379/PFI-806172]\n\nWe have issued a refund to the OPM through the Adyen portal. \n\nUnfortunately, I’m not able to comment on the invoice. I think you need to reopen you case with the billing team. \n\nLet me know if you have any questions. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-09T13:57:10.186Z"],["3799386","WDFT-3546","WDFT","kristiine.murd@bolt.eu","Kristiine Murd","Yes, please use the same invoice layout as for other Poland entities","2026-01-09T13:57:17.925Z"],["3799388","EBIKE1-400","EBIKE1","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[~accountid:712020:ef569842-27e0-4a96-b3b1-ee47d8709209] [~accountid:712020:7636318d-11ba-448e-8ae7-b935370c0640] PTAL at the flowchart & logic","2026-01-09T13:58:05.669Z"],["3799391","MLC-3567","MLC","yulia.nikitina@bolt.eu","Yulia Nikitina","*W2: Closing this task.*\n\n*Updates are all here:*\n\n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7220101217/Couriers+Acquisition+Stage+Optimisation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7220101217/Couriers+Acquisition+Stage+Optimisation|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T13:58:44.792Z"],["3799393","FX-3384","FX","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:61b0e47fef18ca0071ec305a] Awesome, and because it came up in duty, are our total online time, on ride time etc. views on driver profile also okay? ","2026-01-09T13:59:02.436Z"],["3799394","LSS-45949","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:1d600e3f-d3ca-4f4e-b8af-f6c7510bb923] - although I would still appreciate answers to the full list of questions, in particular:\n\n{quote}* Is the fleet profile, in its current suspended state, visible to the fleet owner? What does it look like exactly to the fleet owner if they try to log into this account?\n* Are we confident that, as a result of suspending the account, the fleet owner will not receive any comms from Bolt going forward (e.g., marketing, operational comms, etc)?\n* When you say “_there is not much else we can / are allowed to do_”, are you saying that it is _not operationally feasible_ to follow the steps as for[ +driver account deletion+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360010217173] for this fleet profile, or that you are _not permitted_ to follow those steps (if so, by who)? Just so that I am clear on what the precise blocker here is.{quote}\n\nPlease could you respond on these points ASAP 🙂 ","2026-01-09T13:59:47.320Z"],["3799395","LSS-58423","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Here team,\n\nHere follows the updated response, having in consideration the issuance of the promo code:\n\n\n\n_“Dear Ms Vella,_\n\n_Thank you for your follow-up email, and please accept our apologies for the delay in replying. The intervening holiday period impacted response times, but we appreciate the opportunity to address the additional points raised._\n\n_We understand the main concern being raised is not limited to the route/stop information, but the alleged manner in which the passengers were treated during the trip (including allegations of shouting and asking passengers to exit the vehicle at night and in adverse weather). Bolt takes such allegations seriously. Irrespective of the contractual classification of drivers on the platform, Bolt requires drivers using the Bolt app to maintain professional conduct and to treat passengers with respect throughout the trip._\n\n_Following receipt of the complaint and annexed correspondence, we reviewed the trip information available to us and we also contacted the driver to request their account of events. While the driver’s response did not provide additional clarifying detail, the concerns raised have been escalated internally and will be handled in line with our internal procedures and platform standards._\n\n_With regard to resolution, we note the €3 refund previously issued via in-app support. Without any admission of liability, and in the interest of reaching an amicable solution, Bolt is willing to offer Mr Tanti a promotional benefit consisting of 100% off five (5) rides, redeemable using code LBEZJRJS, valid from today until 31 May 2026. This is offered in full and final settlement of this complaint._\n\n_Bolt remains committed to improving service quality and complaint handling on an ongoing basis, including ensuring that conduct-related concerns are appropriately escalated and assessed._\n\n_Kind regards,”_\n\n\n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T13:59:54.425Z"],["3799398","MLC-3725","MLC","anniecel.malabanan@bolt.eu","Anniecel Malabanan","*Update W2*\n\nNoting down that P3 Content overhaul email templates are going to be included in this list as well. It consist of Status Change comms.\n\nReached out to Mariann regarding the status of the HTML builder, will keep an eye for the updates. Also reached out to Sarah to get a clarification if using flow will make the process shorter when it comes to restructuring previously approved content. ","2026-01-09T14:00:09.428Z"],["3799399","LSS-61196","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432], thank you very much! Have a lovely weekend 🙏 ","2026-01-09T14:00:14.011Z"],["3799401","LSS-48561","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:115f7041-7822-4d70-9ec6-a6159271466a] !\nIs this topic already solved? Can I close the ticket?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-09T14:00:34.945Z"],["3799402","LSS-61196","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] !\n\nHave a great weekend too💚 ","2026-01-09T14:01:22.434Z"],["3799403","LSS-61352","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-09T14:01:49.042Z"],["3799404","LSS-61353","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-09T14:01:49.106Z"],["3799405","FX-3592","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767967285961159]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3592] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T14:02:02.191Z"],["3799407","COP-1880","COP","kartikeya.sharma@bolt.eu","Kartikeya Sharma","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7373718254/Design+doc+Session+based+discounts+budget+matching+for+growth+automation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7373718254/Design+doc+Session+based+discounts+budget+matching+for+growth+automation|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T14:02:18.539Z"],["3799410","EBIKE1-400","EBIKE1","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] This sentence looks unfinished 🙂 \n\n!image-20260109-140239.png|width=953,alt=\"image-20260109-140239.png\"!","2026-01-09T14:02:51.070Z"],["3799411","PFI-831413","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:712020:98578d7d-a19d-4341-a97c-e8099ba8d683] \n\nThe payment is related to the Jan 2 service fees. The service fees total to 671.39 HUF. \n\n\n!image-20260109-135952.png|width=1349,height=207!\n\nI can see there is an error message 79 : Life cycle and {{card.invalid.}}\nCould you please advise the user to confirm if the card details are valid and check with their bank if their payment method is active. \nThey could alternatively try a different payment method. \n\nCheers, \nMarten\n","2026-01-09T14:02:53.419Z"],["3799413","PFI-831256","PFI","monica.kartsev@bolt.eu","Monica Kartsev","Hey [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f]  could you please help us understand the issue with the payment amounts?\n\nIn the admin panel, I can see that the company has two orders, and for both of them, the *Local Sum* differs from the *Sum* (see [link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/805828?tab=balance_entries&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22limit%22%3A50%2C%22business_company_id%22%3A805828%2C%22type%22%3A%22claim%22%7D%7D] and screenshot).\n\nAdditionally, in the order details we can see that the order price was lower, yet the company was charged a higher amount. On the order pages, only the lower amounts are displayed ([order 1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2335903728/1], [order 2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2335118761/1?orderTryId=3000412543] and screenshot).\n\nThe difference between the sums does not appear to include a 10% service fee, as the discrepancy is significantly larger.\n\nCould you clarify why the company was charged more?\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 16.00.02.png|width=1902,height=683,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 16.00.02.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 16.01.47.png|width=1902,height=683,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 16.01.47.png\"!\n\n\n\n","2026-01-09T14:03:15.078Z"],["3799415","DSR-3431","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] for your review. Driver blocked due to offering off-platform ride. Driver unblocked. *Telemetry data currently not included in the all data and needs to be added after the export finishes.*\n\n* Contacted Netherlands SIS regarding the suspension - first report and not that severe. Driver unblocked\n* Message sent to the driver regarding their unblocking [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/720189541]\n* Response prepared [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/12ShmvoU2ZMHYgB2JOmC1PMUAMdbQklwe_lOmbvlJxlA/edit?tab=t.0]\n* Redacted driver and rider ticket [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/1g_k6hzV_rV3K3mXxqtYHxFZLGMOW_-7q]\n* All driver information *(Except Telemetry)* [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/1g_k6hzV_rV3K3mXxqtYHxFZLGMOW_-7q] \n* Telemetry download [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/personal-data-export/exports/1063667?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] *(Needs to be included to the data)*\n* Invoices not included in the data as driver is now active and can access them themselves (Exports just in case: [driver invoices|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-bulk-invoice-download/item/1380024/view], [ride invoices|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-bulk-invoice-download/item/1710005/view])","2026-01-09T14:03:15.840Z"],["3799418","RDXENG-4579","RDXENG","juri.noga@bolt.eu","Juri Noga","Since it’s backend driven let’s explicitly send correct reference colors for the labels.  I’ll update backend response once we have onboarding design and copy finalized.","2026-01-09T14:03:42.077Z"],["3799420","LSS-60533","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^LNKD_ORDER_11437717294.pdf (1) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-09T14:03:59.978Z"],["3799421","RCE-336","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767967429824629]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-336] `Assist with second question regarding login and verification` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T14:04:04.224Z"],["3799423","MLC-3821","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","Ticket for content team: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-100544|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-100544|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T14:04:21.212Z"],["3799426","PFI-826638","PFI","daniel.novo@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniel Novo","Error is “Action refund is blocked, until original is exported“. How should I proceed.","2026-01-09T14:05:37.313Z"],["3799430","PIF-2260","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft provides a concise summary of the new feature, highlighting its benefits for service deploys and monitoring. It conveys why the integration with Grafana is crucial for improving deployment processes across different teams. However, specific URL links to validate or learn more about the implementation are missing, hence the placeholders.","2026-01-09T14:06:48.858Z"],["3799431","PAR-3724","PAR","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","For this case, adjusting the client balance has been done now. \nI think we can close the ticket then.","2026-01-09T14:06:49.172Z"],["3799434","PIF-2260","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 10\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: ","2026-01-09T14:07:16.722Z"],["3799437","DSR-3101","DSR","priit.lehis@bolt.eu","Priit Lehis","Response sent out. ","2026-01-09T14:08:22.078Z"],["3799438","LSS-61128","LSS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","Hi Giulia, \n\nCould you please add the missing letters to the name of the company? 🙏 \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 15.08.21.png|width=942,height=227,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 15.08.21.png\"!\n\n\n\n","2026-01-09T14:08:29.495Z"],["3799442","LSS-61193","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Thank you! 🙏 ","2026-01-09T14:10:49.924Z"],["3799444","WD-22532","WD","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska","!image-20260109-140511.png|width=250,alt=\"image-20260109-140511.png\"!\n\nHe’s the only person with _100854 - Identity Governance Analyst_  Job profile, so adding it to the security group.","2026-01-09T14:11:40.404Z"],["3799447","MLC-2542","MLC","daria.trokhina@bolt.eu","Daria Trokhina","*Week 52-Week2*:\n\n* Ensured that content block {{{{content_blocks.${global_eaters_email_abort_logic}}}}} is added to all emails in AZ, PL and PT. \n* Martech is working on custom attribute “{{is_sunset_email}}“. Once they’ll create it in Braze, Dovainis will add the condition below to the content block:\n\n{{{% elsif {{custom_attribute.${is_sunset_email}}} == true %}{% abort_message('is_sunset_email') %}}}\n\nIt’s not possible to do it now, cause custom attribute is not added to user profiles:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-02 at 12.25.24.png|width=611,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-02 at 12.25.24.png\"!\n\n* Martech will set “true“ value to {{is_sunset_email}} custom attribute of 50% of inactive users, thus they will stop getting the emails. After we’ll get enough data – they’ll do the post analysis.","2026-01-09T14:12:12.896Z"],["3799448","RDXENG-4244","RDXENG","juri.noga@bolt.eu","Juri Noga","[~accountid:712020:ef5f49c9-39d4-4c05-820b-dbad89f985a0] Parcel flow gets reset when going to the home screen, for proper fix we need active order response to tell the app about parcel flow\n\ncc [~accountid:63b8350a8a07cbd184aca826] ","2026-01-09T14:12:56.452Z"],["3799452","PFI-831433","PFI","fabricia.silva@bolt.eu","Fabrícia Silva Alcântara","[^2025-12-15 -- 2025-12-22 Abu Muhammad Nazmul Haque Weekly Report (1).pdf]","2026-01-09T14:13:52.967Z"],["3799453","PFI-831433","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-09T14:13:55.241Z"],["3799456","WFM-9904","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hello [~accountid:712020:cde6e2fa-0f48-44e8-b1c7-2a3a70d10b33] , SCC team here,\n\nIt is likely that it was a certificate issue, rather than access / role missing issue. I am glad that it sorted out.\n\nAs we discussed with my team, and [~accountid:712020:9c0690de-08a9-41cf-93b1-9184ed368330] , you’ve got all the roles that you needed at the moment. In case, if something happens with your certificates again, reach out to #4-itsupport channel.\n\n In case if you need any access, reach out to us with another ticket.\n\nHave a nice day,\n\nKamran","2026-01-09T14:14:38.759Z"],["3799457","RCE-264","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Roman Nikolajev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767968098190249]*{color}:\nHii <@U9T7W8KUP>, hope you are well!\n\nDid you have any time to look into the above during the freeze or after? :pray:\n{quote}","2026-01-09T14:15:13.883Z"],["3799458","DRX-27864","DRX","angela.aland@bolt.eu","Angela Aland","_“Some markets don’t want to task to be created when onboarding status is reached.”_\nWe can keep creation of tasks when lead reaches onboarding status, if these are not processed by OPS then there will not be a queue configured.\n\n\n\nWhat we need to add is and option to configure a queue for Driver Registrations where *all* Onboarding reasons have been resolved (and automation did not auto-accept the lead). \n\n* Would need to listen to *Resolving* Onboarding reasons, when all Reasons are *resolved → create a task*.\n* Add another queue criteria for *Onboarding reasons Resolved*\n\nThen the queue can be configured so that *Registration status* = Onboarding & *Onboarding reasons Resolved* = Yes. But a task trigger in this case would need to be Resolving all reasons (no pending reasons left on registration, all resolved → then wait for automation result → if not auto-accepted create a task)\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 16.13.37.png|width=817,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-09 at 16.13.37.png\"!","2026-01-09T14:15:20.816Z"],["3799459","SUPX-2209","SUPX","radoslaw.wielonski@bolt.eu","Radosław Wieloński","I’ve asked Olha about more details:\nWe can implement just filtering by user persona, so adding just new filter by config to common view of configs and filtering in json column in server. This should be fairly easy.","2026-01-09T14:15:51.447Z"],["3799461","TA-335","TA","alina.murashova@bolt.eu","Alina Murashova","||*Interviewer*||*Interview Team*||*Date*|| ||\n|Alina|Product [+Tara Muruthi+|mailto:tara.muruthi@bolt.eu] |17.12.25|* -Completed-|\n|Alina|Engineering [+Jaana Rästas+|mailto:jaana.rastas@bolt.eu]|22.01.26|* Completed|\n|Alina|Executive [+Gareth Edwards+|mailto:gareth.edwards@bolt.eu]|07.01.26|* -Completed-|\n|Alina|Finance, People and Legal [+Maria Helena Vallikivi+|mailto:maria.vallikivi@bolt.eu]|14.01|* Completed|\n|Alina|[+Gareth Edwards+|mailto:gareth.edwards@bolt.eu] [+Britta Võsu+|mailto:britta.vosu@bolt.eu] [+Maria Helena Vallikivi+|mailto:maria.vallikivi@bolt.eu]|15.01.|* Completed|\n|Andrea|Analytics [+Flora Falussy-Ando+|mailto:flora.falussy-ando@bolt.eu]|15.01|* Completed|\n|Andrea|Sourcers |08.01|* Completed|\n|Andrea|Local Ops [+Britta Võsu+|mailto:britta.vosu@bolt.eu]|14.01|* Completed|\n|Andrea |Sales, Commercial [+João Alves+|mailto:joaofc.alves@bolt.eu]|13.01|* Completed|\n|Andrea|[+Jaana Rästas+|mailto:jaana.rastas@bolt.eu] [+Flora Falussy-Ando+|mailto:flora.falussy-ando@bolt.eu] [+Tara Muruthi+|mailto:tara.muruthi@bolt.eu]|22.01|* Completed|","2026-01-09T14:16:47.628Z"],["3799462","PFI-831256","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, sure.\n\nThe difference is the Resale VAT. We have to apply the Resale VAT on top of the Rides that don’t have VAT (Driver/Fleet is not VAT-liable), when reselling those to the company.\n\n* 5.6 * 1.24 = 6.944\n* 6.8 * 1.24 = 8.43 \n\nThis will be invoiced back on the aggregate invoice.","2026-01-09T14:16:52.735Z"],["3799464","HS-28784","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:73528ba9-f129-4b0c-b65d-38a479119ccc],\n\nI have asked the Workday Tech team to submit the task on your behalf, as you confirmed that the information my colleague added is correct. They have also uploaded the documents you wanted to attach.\n\nI am closing this ticket now, as there are no further actions needed.\n\nBest regards, \n\nKerilin ","2026-01-09T14:18:00.828Z"],["3799465","RCE-264","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1767968270106869]*{color}:\nAmong the top-5 fixes in my mind, but not as taken into work entry yet :see_no_evil:\n\nUnfortunately, there are plenty of cascading dependencies to fix altogether, so it's not a one-shot patch.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T14:18:03.642Z"],["3799466","PFI-831422","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:615c1af4048360006a44e16c],\n\nThere essentially is no point in blocking the emails (also not something that we can do/target).\nThe user is sophisticated enough to create new accounts via new device UIDs, therefore changing the emails would be frankly one of the easiest things that they can do. The way they are currently doing it is actually better for us, since this way we can monitor their behavior more.\n\nFrom what we can see from our side, then sometimes the fraud engine does already kick in and block the accounts for the cancellations/volumes.\nHowever, the Fraud team does not exactly block the users for attempted scams either, at the end of the day it is also the drivers responsibility not to abide suspicious orders.\n\nSuch cases would actually be better to escalate towards either comms or infosec.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-09T14:18:09.579Z"],["3799467","DPM-2317","DPM","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","Bumping priority as this makes the price update flow via the side panel unusable for multi-store items","2026-01-09T14:18:10.755Z"],["3799469","SUPX-2306","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","Copy not ready yet","2026-01-09T14:19:16.908Z"],["3799471","PFI-831439","PFI","alejandro.duarte@bolt.eu","Alejandro Kowalewski","!image.png (2).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-09T14:21:04.333Z"],["3799472","VULN-1118","VULN","allar.lauk@bolt.eu","Allar Lauk","Hey [~accountid:5db2cd1c72d6f20c33d19e79] !  👋 \n\n\n\nHave you had a chance to look into the issues here in linked work items?","2026-01-09T14:21:08.700Z"],["3799473","LSS-58423","LSS","kristina.pugaca@bolt.eu","Kristina Pugaca","Thank you, everyone. I have sent the reply and will let you know if they respond","2026-01-09T14:21:11.703Z"],["3799474","WD-22492","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:637f26822acfad92d7b13ddb] columns are now visible in *Bolt - Find Spend Authorizations* report","2026-01-09T14:21:13.005Z"],["3799477","L10N-26841","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:27.557Z"],["3799478","L10N-26842","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:27.565Z"],["3799479","L10N-26830","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:27.726Z"],["3799480","L10N-26840","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:27.715Z"],["3799481","L10N-26831","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:27.764Z"],["3799482","L10N-26834","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:27.857Z"],["3799483","L10N-26829","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:27.880Z"],["3799484","L10N-26833","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:27.964Z"],["3799485","L10N-26839","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:27.986Z"],["3799486","L10N-26837","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:28.030Z"],["3799487","L10N-26835","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:28.084Z"],["3799488","L10N-26832","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:28.076Z"],["3799489","L10N-26843","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:28.125Z"],["3799490","L10N-26828","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:28.297Z"],["3799491","L10N-26838","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:28.405Z"],["3799492","L10N-26836","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-09T14:21:28.544Z"],["3799493","PFI-831440","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^COMPROBANTE DE PAGO BOLT NOV 2025 FUNDACION BUEN PASTOR.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-09T14:21:48.459Z"],["3799494","PFI-830137","PFI","mia.hartova@bolt.eu","Mia Hartová","Hello [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] \nin the end we need your help as well. I created this ticket [PFI-831352|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-831352]\nThis situation was an exception, but the correction of the invoice is in your hand so is it possible to correct the invoice?","2026-01-09T14:22:39.074Z"],["3799495","PFI-830137","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-09T14:22:42.629Z"],["3799497","LSS-58953","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","*Update:*\n\nWe received another summons regarding this case and Thomas Bugeja already confirmed he will attend.\n\nRegarding the information, I am waiting for Thomas to confirm it what we provided is sufficient.\n\n!image (7).png|width=654,alt=\"image (7).png\"!","2026-01-09T14:23:53.381Z"],["3799498","SREC-367","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","See if there is a reasonable way to set the image version. Previously we used the data source to find the latest stable image, however that will inevitably create terraform drift once a new stable image is added by GCP. Using the full length image name seems a bit too verbose. Try to find a decent middle ground.","2026-01-09T14:24:15.157Z"],["3799499","MVRT-1315","MVRT","tiffany.irianto@bolt.eu","Tiffany Ainnurrahmi Irianto","Hi [~accountid:6101032e0b454a0068b57bef] is eater wave 2 already set and scheduled? Is it still possible to change the link we use to \n\nPush : boltfood://search?filter-traits=traits-12797&open-first=true&utm_source=push&utm_medium=ad-hoc&utm_campaign={{canvas.${api_id}}}&utm_content={{campaign.${message_api_id}}}\n\nCase : There’s a Hesburger branch that also have “Selver” on the branch name so some people might buy burger rather than Selver’s 57% off discount ","2026-01-09T14:24:57.197Z"],["3799500","PFI-831441","PFI","victoria.ebube@bolt-outsource.eu","Victoria Ebube","[^SBSA_Statement_2026-01-09_3months.pdf]","2026-01-09T14:24:57.928Z"],["3799501","PFI-831433","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Looking into this. ","2026-01-09T14:25:13.403Z"],["3799502","FX-3592","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767968752913149]*{color}:\nAnswered: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0576CT9MQD/p1767968429995649?thread_ts=1767962748.507119&amp;cid=C0576CT9MQD]\n\ndriver: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8464971?tab=profile]\ncompany: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/247318]\nI have checked other drivers from the same company:\n\nLinked files:\n* [image.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A85U7KKND/image.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-09T14:26:06.999Z"],["3799503","DRX-21467","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: nothing to test","2026-01-09T14:26:58.460Z"],["3799504","PFI-831446","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^260109084357_0001.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-09T14:27:16.396Z"],["3799506","WD-22362","WD","viktor.kondin@bolt.eu","Viktor Kondin","Hey [~accountid:712020:c6af29d3-64c9-469d-b213-efe8df0b7cee] 👋 \nThank you very much. Hire process should be completed. Could we try moving this position to Alan org now?\n[https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/1$715/4872$12060.htmld#TABTASKID=2998%248427|https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/1$715/4872$12060.htmld#TABTASKID=2998%248427]","2026-01-09T14:29:10.473Z"],["3799507","PFI-830473","PFI","laura.ernestova@bolt.eu","Laura Ernestová","hey! Yes, done!","2026-01-09T14:29:45.878Z"],["3799510","SCM-973","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","Updated and attached Warranty & Compensation process RACI matrix in confluence. [~accountid:5e46c226fd328a0c9ceba7de] \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RNTL/pages/7317783453/Warranty+Compensation+process|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RNTL/pages/7317783453/Warranty+Compensation+process|smart-link] ","2026-01-09T14:30:58.292Z"],["3799515","LSS-57342","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (09.01)*+\n\n* Zellis has reverted with next round of comments on the DPA ([LINK|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HkNTtZXmJ1MW5MHlU1gV29OeJVFsroWr/edit]). We are due to have a call to finalise on Monday, and so in practical terms we only have a few hours to review :melting_face: \n** I have already flagged to Kristiina that this deadline is too tight, but she is reluctant to reschedule the call. When pressed, she has not otherwise specified a hard deadline.\n* Contentious points below (otherwise, comments accepted).\n\n||*Issue*||*Previous wording*||*Zellis edits*||*Bolt comments*||\n|*DSRRs (Timing)*\nClause 7.2|Zellis should notify Bolt of DSRRs within 72 hours.|Zellis has kept the 72-hour time limit, but qualified it as “_using reasonable endeavours_” and “_excluding weekends and UK public holidays_”.\n+Explanation+: “_We want to support Bolt’s compliance with the statutory obligation to respond within 1 month. We can accept the 72 hours on the basis we reflect the practical reality of business hours and how such requests can be received_.”|✅ We can accept this.|\n|*PDBs (Follow-Up)*\nClause 8.3|Zellis should provide Bolt with an explanation of any notification delays.|Zellis has kept this obligation in the agreement, but qualified it as a “_brief_” explanation.\nExplanation: “_We can accept providing notice with information to be shared as it becomes available. This reflects the practical reality of the circumstances_.”|⚠️ I have added in a clarification that the _explanation_ should come within the 48-hour notification period. Hopefully this will be acceptable ✅|\n|*Assistance (Costs)*\nClause 9.1|Bolt should not have to pay for Zellis' assistance per A32-36 obligations.\n\\\\\nWe stated we may be willing to consider Zellis recovering reasonable fees for extraordinary costs (e.g., non-standard documentation) subject to appropriate safeguards, but core cooperation should not be contingent on payment.|Zellis has inserted the following: “_The Customer’s requests for assistance under this paragraph shall be limited to what is reasonably necessary for the Customer’s compliance with Articles 32 to 36 of the UK GDPR, taking into account the nature and scope of the Services. The Supplier may charge the Customer for providing such assistance to the extent that: (a) the assistance is not of a type or volume that would be reasonably expected to be provided in the ordinary course of business in connection with the Services; and/or (b) the assistance is requested in connection with a Personal Data Breach to the extent caused by or contributed to by the Customer’s (or any person under the Customer’s control) negligence, breach of the Agreement or this Schedule, or act or omission. Any such charges shall be agreed in writing in advance (acting reasonably). Where reasonably practicable, the Supplier shall provide an estimate of the charges before incurring them_.”\n+Explanation+: “_We will provide the statutory cooperation required under Articles 32–36 UK GDPR, but requests must be limited to what is reasonably necessary and proportionate. If assistance is outside what would reasonably be expected in the ordinary course (e.g. non-standard reporting, bespoke documentation, extensive investigation support) and/or relates to a Personal Data Breach caused or contributed to by you, we must be able to charge our reasonable costs. Such charges will be pre-agreed in writing in advance_.”|⚠️ I have qualified this by saying that Zellis can charge where Bolt has _materially_ contributed to a PDB, and I have included that such charges must themselves be “_reasonable_”. Otherwise, we can accept this, as charges must be agreed in advance in writing ✅ \n* NB. This should be flagged to the business for their own awareness 📯|\n|*Subprocessors (Contracts)*\nClause 10.2|Zellis must provide Bolt with a copy of a subprocessor contract on request.|Zellis has removed the requirement to provide full subprocessor contracts, and replaced it with a requirement to provide Bolt with  “_details of its subprocessor contract(s) and any subsequent amendments to the same as is demonstrably necessary for the Customer’s compliance with applicable Laws_”.\n+Explanation+: “_We can provide specific details of the contracts on reasonable request if this is necessary for your compliance with GDPR but will not provide full contracts. This isn’t necessary or proportionate_.”|⚠️ I have amended this by including provisions for Zellis to redact the contracts as needed. Ultimately, “details” of these contracts is not sufficient to enable Bolt to verify their compliance and adhere to accountability requirements.\n* If Zellis continues to insist on this, then we can consider defining “_details_” and otherwise accept the change.|\n|*Subprocessors (Authorisation)*\nClause 10.3|We permitted _deemed_ authorisation, provided that: (i) the 30-day notice period still applies; (ii) Zellis must provide Bolt with the information it needs to make a decision; (iii) Bolt cannot be limited to objecting solely on DP grounds; and (iv) Bolt is still able to terminate the relevant services if it objects.|Zellis has done the following:\n# Zellis has accepted the 30-day notice period.\n# Zellis will provide new subprocessor information “_On the Customer’s written request_”.\n# The information provided shall include “_only such information as the Supplier can reasonably provide and which is reasonably necessary to enable the Customer to assess any material risk to its business arising from the proposed appointment and to decide whether to object_”.\n# Zellis has not included edits, but has suggested that Bolt should not have an unfettered right to object.\n+Explanation+: “_We can agree to 30 days and to provide additional information on request. We’ll need to revert to the original position on objection. As drafted, you’d have a right to terminate due to any objection, even where we’ve provided a mechanism for an alternative, which we can’t reasonably support_.”|Responses are as follows:\n# ✅ Great.\n# ❌ I have rejected this. The information should be provided with the notice, as otherwise this gives Bolt even less time to properly review the new subprocessor.\n# ⚠️ We can accept this in principle, but I have listed some categories of information that we will need in all cases (i.e., identity, services, locations, data categories, data subjects, purposes, security measures, international / onward transfers, and transfer mechanisms).\n# ⚠️ I have included some wording saying that, as an intermediary step, Zellis (not Bolt - this is effctively punishing Bolt for objecting) can propose an alternative subprocessor, and then termination right only kicks in if the parties (acting reasonably) are unable to agree. Otherwise, we cannot limit ourselves to just DP objections, and we cannot remove the termination right.|\n|*Subprocessors (Updated list)*\nClause 10.4(c)|We proposed a subscription-based notification model.|Zellis has rejected this, and replaced it with a requirement for Zellis to “publish the details of the subprocessor on [http://solutions.zellis.com/subprocessorlist|http://solutions.zellis.com/subprocessorlist]”\n+Explanation+: “_The Service Schedule includes the hyperlink and notifications are managed by the Customer Portal which is available as part of you implementation. This is not effective from signing the contract but when this is setup during implementation. This aligns with when personal data will be shared._”|✅ We can accept this, as there is a requirement to provide written notice anyway.\n* We should tell the business that when signing up via the Customer Portal, the business should set up appropriate email alerts to [privacy@bolt.eu|mailto:privacy@bolt.eu] 📯|\n|*Audit Rights*\nClause 11|Zellis should make available all necessary information, and allow for and contribute to audits, not just the requirements of the Service Schedule|Zellis has changed “+_in particular,_+ _the audit provisions in the Service Schedule_” to “+_in accordance with_+ _the audit provisions in the Service Schedule_”. Otherwise, accepted.|✅ We can accept this. As previously noted, the Service Schedule is fine.|\n|*Indemnity / Liability Cap*\nClause 13|Pro-Bolt indemnity for DP violations / PDBs, capped at 2m per claim.|Zellis has deleted this wholesale again.\nExplanation: “_Our contract governance does not allow for such indemnification and this is in line with current industry practice. The £1m super-cap is reasonably proportionate to current risk profile of regulatory enforcement, scale of data processing and contract value_.”|❌ We cannot accept this, and I do not agree that this is ‘not in line with industry practice’ (also, it again appears that they are rejecting the cap, rather than the indemnity itself - they have not explained why they keep removing the indemnity). I have therefore reinstated the provision and included a 1m cap per claim as a final position.\n* NB. This should be generally flagged to the business for their own awareness, as this is likely to be the biggest bone of contention. Flag that this will need approval and so cannot be resolved on the call 📯|","2026-01-09T14:34:34.847Z"],["3799517","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Paula Espeja [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767969427149749]*{color}:\nHi! From a Tax perspective, the underlying transactions discussed here (deposit paybacks, balance transfers) are *outside the scope of VAT*, as they do not represent consideration for any taxable supply.\nIdeally, these movements should not be reflected on an invoice at all, however, we understand the need for a short-term workaround to provide visibility, so if possible, using dedicated compensation types presented on *a separate compensation document/invoice* would be the cleanest approach from a tax and audit perspective.\nIf, as a temporary measure, these amounts need to be included in the regular monthly invoice, it is important to ensure they are clearly identified as *out of scope* and do not affect VAT reporting.\n{quote}","2026-01-09T14:37:21.876Z"],["3799519","DSR-3057","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC,\n\nAs discussed in the DSR call this week, we’ll handle this case in two steps:\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n# The DSAR at hand: post-deletion access request \n{panel}\n\n* I prepared and amended the [responsive data|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1fK5qYwFnfu6quSIswmHEnVfl05vM2klV?usp=drive_link] (in line with our retention periods).\n* I prepared the answer letter [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tJP-tJwOxuc9MKdsbAGcIlZJ_7B_b0X-IfC1hkHMSwQ/edit?usp=drive_link].\n** In the answer letter, I clarified to the user that we will be reviewing his [DSAR|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/539053418] from 17.03.25 which was not acknowledged nor answer to by CS. I have set the deadline for our answer to {{2026-01-23}}\n* Please send the answer letter and responsive data by Monday {{2026-01-12}}EOD (/) \n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n# The DSAR that was not handled - Deadline {{2026-01-23}}\n{panel}\n\n* In this [ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/539053418], the user asked the following:\n** A formal explanation of what exactly was found in your investigation,\n** The process followed in reaching this decision, and\n** Any documentation or records used in concluding this matter.\n* We need to review this request as per our usual Suspension DSAR processes, namely:\n** Follow the *Safety* suspension instructions. In doing so:\n*** Contact the relevant team concerning the block, ask about the HB - the usual process. Of course, the account itself cannot be reinstated as it has been deleted, but the HB could (in theory) be lifted for the driver to create a new account if they wish so.\n*** Extract the relevant data. Here, since we will *already* have shared the data that we hold about the driver in our first answer, what still needs to be sourced is the *Rider safety report* that led to the HB. Please extract it, redact it (in _Suggestion_ mode for my review) and look for any other relevant tickets about the blocking decision. No need to source the tickets on the driver’s side: those will have been shared already.\n*** If you find any other data that you believe might be relevant, please flag it to me 🙏\n*** Prepare the answer letter as per the usual template, based on your findings. \n* Once this is done, please ping me for my review.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-09T14:37:47.988Z"],["3799521","DBRE-8589","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{{afr-db-2}} and {{afr-db-3}}were decommissioned.\nMaster switch is scheduled by Monday 12-01-2026 @ 11h30 EET/09h30 UTC","2026-01-09T14:38:35.866Z"],["3799524","PFI-831450","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-09T14:39:25.024Z"],["3799525","PFI-831432","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:22e4319c-bfa6-40b5-aadb-98b2cb85d51c],\n\nSeems like the user still has a *Scheduled block* on their profile, meaning that this has not been submitted to the Safety Team for review or that the process is incomplete.\n\nFraud Team does not remove *Scheduled blocks* from the profiles, we only help in removing the *device UID blocks* once the investigation has been finalized and the rest of the blocks have been removed.\n\nPlease let us know once the profile has been finalized.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you,\nMarten","2026-01-09T14:39:39.685Z"],["3799527","DSR-3621","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-09T14:41:06.447Z"],["3799532","LSS-61128","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb] after downloading the file it is all fine – only in the preview the letters are missing ","2026-01-09T14:42:39.144Z"],["3799533","RDXENG-3901","RDXENG","denis.komissarov@bolt.eu","Denis Komissarov","I reopened the ticket as the previous fix didn’t help much.\nHere’s another attempt to fix it","2026-01-09T14:42:45.779Z"],["3799535","DPX-3536","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","Translations requested: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-100762?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-100762?created=true]","2026-01-09T14:42:55.607Z"],["3799541","LSS-59058","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi! As there is no answer here, I assume the issue is resolved. My comment from Dec 3 is still valid. Closign this ticket. \n\ncc [~accountid:712020:3db0aede-64e8-4fb8-ba39-3f2a1189572b] ","2026-01-09T14:43:54.251Z"],["3799543","DRX-26536","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26537 has been resolved","2026-01-09T14:44:06.503Z"],["3799553","INT-639","INT","daria.ryazhskikh@bolt.eu","Daria Ryazhskikh","*26W2*\n\n* 2/4 story in progress\n* Added Evolution tasks for these two, to accumulate things that are optional/not priority\n\nh3. Setup brand annotations\n\n*Story*: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ADS-132|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ADS-132|smart-link]\n\n*Progress:* 83%. There only left issue is already reviewed and only release is left. The ticket about audit logs is moved under Evolution task\n\n!AnnotationEditor_26w2.mp4|width=1838,height=1080,alt=\"AnnotationEditor_26w2.mp4\"!\n\nh3. Auto-annotate products\n\n*Story*: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ADS-133|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ADS-133|smart-link]\n\n*Progress*: 28%\n\n* Replication of annotations table, so it is accessible in Databricks. Waiting for review\n* No big progress for auto-annotation script itself. The one that is done so far needs a review from a data engineer from Delivery, to make sure we use the right identifiers.\n* Got new input about how the Databricks schedule can be organized, created a ticket ","2026-01-09T14:47:16.898Z"],["3799555","LSS-58216","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi,\n\nI have completed the initial review. [Here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OyzwXlwAMDomW9YMCqExEnehPUwuV8Kt/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=116714997278541814965&rtpof=true&sd=true] is the agreement draft with comments and suggestions and [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1z8b1szZSHNuDbduk00c2AgmGh5GSRSqyLqyFaza734U/edit?usp=sharing] is a table with the key issues to be cleared. [~accountid:5d3ff51eb7f3ac0da80c815c] in going to go over the table and internal comments in the doc. If everything is ok, lets share it with Solidgate. If there is any internal comment that needs discussion or input from Solidgate, lets resolve it and make the relevant comment for the provider so we can share it with them without our internal comments. \n\nIf you have questions please let me know.\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] ","2026-01-09T14:47:21.280Z"],["3799557","HS-27194","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Contract went for signing. ","2026-01-09T14:48:08.700Z"],["3799560","PTWS-2113","PTWS","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","Shayla told me we can turn this on, I had a call in which I explained to her the logic behind it and showcased the automation. She was happy with how it turned out. \n\n\n\nThe last requirement remains: removing people from the channel automatically. Unfortunately, Docebo is missing the “enrollment_status” of each learning plan participant, even though their docs say it should be included, which is quite a set back. Might have to run multiple API calls to get the info we need. Will look into this next. Leaving ticket as in progress for now, but main requirement is completed, up & running.\n\n!image-20260109-144728.png|width=720,alt=\"image-20260109-144728.png\"!","2026-01-09T14:48:24.072Z"],["3799561","PAW-14763","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-09T14:48:25.331Z"],["3799562","LSS-60621","LSS","tom.bishop@bolt.eu","Tom Bishop","[~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] are you able to comment?","2026-01-09T14:49:07.257Z"],["3799563","INT-757","INT","simo.pahk@bolt.eu","Simo Pähk","26W2: Clarified & aligned plans with the WAVE team. Decided that we’ll start migration from simpler components, but will not do a full migration right away as the library is still evolving.","2026-01-09T14:49:32.375Z"],["3799565","HS-28729","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:e1427b30-bc75-43cd-9e45-85c863998272],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-09T14:50:17.509Z"],["3799566","LSS-61198","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:153601bb-a9eb-4650-99f1-af48ee5461e2] I don’t have access to Beehive, please download or take screenshots and compile an Incident Report. ","2026-01-09T14:50:35.413Z"],["3799568","SCM-978","SCM","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:5eb363355862510b794e3507] did this happen during the D3 production? ","2026-01-09T14:50:50.033Z"],["3799571","CRC-1980","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] First attempts to test with employees still unsuccessful as of 17.00 EET JAN 09 / Testing continues","2026-01-09T14:52:32.261Z"],["3799573","LSS-61355","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] can you please coordinate so CSPC takes this?","2026-01-09T14:52:58.326Z"],["3799574","CRC-1591","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Daniil working on issuing certificates, waiting some answers about the email address to be used. ","2026-01-09T14:53:40.026Z"],["3799575","INT-394","INT","marina.gaponova@bolt.eu","Maryna Gaponova","26W2: In progress with business logic filling, no blocker for now","2026-01-09T14:53:58.980Z"],["3799576","PFI-831458","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8