s issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-12T07:01:10.391Z"],["3801119","PFI-826381","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Fabrícia Silva Alcântara,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-12T07:01:12.738Z"],["3801120","LSS-55555","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Bryan de Jesus Seixas,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-12T07:01:14.614Z"],["3801122","LSS-59635","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Thanks [~accountid:712020:82a49ddb-c340-4f47-963d-7acca442cb8b] - in that case, we will close this ticket.\n\nHas any training/education been given to the victim here? Want to ensure that they have completed necessary trainings at Bolt to understand how to be more careful in future.","2026-01-12T07:01:17.110Z"],["3801123","LSS-48761","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Aqida Kaleem,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-12T07:01:22.107Z"],["3801124","LSS-48585","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Laura-Ioana Izvoranu,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-12T07:01:22.120Z"],["3801125","RCE-339","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768201255995149]*{color}:\nThis duty week is recorded @ [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-339]\n<@divyansh.kumar>, please move the task to the `Progress` state, or reassign first.\n\nProgressing of the task is necessary to automate the further reports assignment.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T07:01:34.633Z"],["3801126","DRAG101-464","DRAG101","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","Goal:\n\nBattery modification list {{2026-01-14}} ","2026-01-12T07:01:39.195Z"],["3801127","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Since pre-assembly is complete, Longuye does not want to do any extra work due to a tight timeline.\n\nAdditionally, many employees are leaving the factory for the upcoming New Year event.","2026-01-12T07:02:28.110Z"],["3801128","RCE-340","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768201359954969]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-340] `Update container sizes for rides-compliance services` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T07:03:00.419Z"],["3801129","FX-3598","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768201391036399]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3598] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T07:03:25.458Z"],["3801131","LSS-59330","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Anna Kalabska,\n\nThere hasn't been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days. Please:\n1) Close the ticket if the issue has been resolved or is not relevant anymore; or\n2) Give an update; or\n3) Change to “Waiting for customer” status if you are waiting to hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T07:03:30.543Z"],["3801132","LSS-60396","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Hala Abdulhaq,\n\nThere hasn't been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days. Please:\n1) Close the ticket if the issue has been resolved or is not relevant anymore; or\n2) Give an update; or\n3) Change to “Waiting for customer” status if you are waiting to hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T07:03:33.935Z"],["3801133","HS-28819","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:716b98b3-eb3b-4a3d-b8d8-bbaef921c1be], the form is sent to your e-mail. Closing this ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-12T07:04:05.523Z"],["3801134","DSR-3643","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T07:04:08.826Z"],["3801138","MLC-3857","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W2:\n\n* Discussed next steps for expanding merchant welcome automation. Will include additional email with more details on accepting DineOut orders and making sure employees are aware of how the system works to improve customer experience\n* Discussed Telegram group for DineOut and DineOut merchants/employees where quick updates can be sent out. This will be handled by the DineOut team but we will support with general guidelines/templates if needed.","2026-01-12T07:06:12.572Z"],["3801139","PFI-831957","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-12T07:06:45.881Z"],["3801140","PFI-832119","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-12T07:06:48.683Z"],["3801146","PFI-832238","PFI","elijah.ojeamien@bolt-outsource.eu","Elijah Ojeamien","!image-20260112-070935.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T07:09:47.775Z"],["3801151","LSS-59122","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Work in progress, thus we keep the ticket open. ","2026-01-12T07:12:57.882Z"],["3801152","PFI-831458","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! That’s because based on our system, we gave the provider the cue to start preparing, so Bolt covered the earnings for provider, so the normal fee structure still stands. The screenshotted example is for this order: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/263815014?shard=deliveryglobal&showUserTz=false|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/263815014?shard=deliveryglobal&showUserTz=false]\n\nYou can see that it’s compensated to the provider by Bolt and then a fee is charged on that compensated amount as if it was a regular order (which is expected behaviour). The provider also received payouts for these orders. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 09.12.09.png|width=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 09.12.09.png\"!","2026-01-12T07:13:50.633Z"],["3801155","DSR-3645","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T07:16:07.015Z"],["3801157","PFI-829210","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:6329554614c6b4b2210a39be] \n\nSorry, I must have missed the update here. \nRefund was issued on Wed, {{2026-01-07}}. The customer should have received it by now. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T07:16:21.777Z"],["3801160","LSS-58320","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi All, apologies about the time that has passed on this.\n\nI have reviewed the Form and adjusted its contents. I’ve also left 2 comments for [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897].","2026-01-12T07:16:43.185Z"],["3801161","WEBSD-1451","WEBSD","kerubo.ombati@bolt.eu","Kerubo Ombati","Hi, following up on this.","2026-01-12T07:16:47.114Z"],["3801162","RCE-342","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768202196677889]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-342] `Release live-driveridentityverification module within timeframe` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T07:16:50.141Z"],["3801163","DRX-28083","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey QA Testing, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-12T07:17:11.474Z"],["3801164","EBIKE1-392","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Goals:\n\n# The complete 3D model of the kickstand is missing; only a scanned version exists.\n## I will try to obtain an actual 3D model from the supplier.\n## If the supplier cannot provide it, I will create one.\n# With the new clearance target for the rear wheel set at 30mm, I need to produce new 3D printed parts and test it.\n# It needs to be confirmed which kickstand is the actual product below, as the *sample that was sent to Estonia lacks the reinforcement rib*. [~accountid:5eb363355862510b794e3507] \n\n||*Sample in Estonia*||*2d*||*Sample in China*||\n|!image-20260112-071145.png|width=468,alt=\"image-20260112-071145.png\"!|!image-20260112-071413.png|width=444,alt=\"image-20260112-071413.png\"!|!e88243a6-9b42-408a-b4f9-a5d4a7f6aef6-20251204-090016 (f2435285-b54e-495b-b8af-52d8635ae8ca).jpg|width=306,alt=\"e88243a6-9b42-408a-b4f9-a5d4a7f6aef6-20251204-090016.jpg\"!|","2026-01-12T07:17:34.911Z"],["3801167","PFI-832239","PFI","kenechi.udowelle@bolt-outsource.eu","Kenechi Udowelle","!image-20260112-071736.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T07:17:52.004Z"],["3801168","LSS-61376","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Support provided in the Parent ticket (/) ","2026-01-12T07:18:03.372Z"],["3801173","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Goals:\n\n# Test the bike with the misaligned rear mudguard to assess how much water splashes from the side.\n\n!image-20260112-072109.png|width=120,alt=\"image-20260112-072109.png\"!\n\n# Make a 3D print of the rubber flap.","2026-01-12T07:20:24.832Z"],["3801177","HS-28078","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0], \n\nThe documents are sent via email. I am closing this ticket as no further action is needed. \n\nAll the best,\n\nKerilin ","2026-01-12T07:21:36.463Z"],["3801178","DSR-3467","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","The Driver added additional information:\n\nHe explains that both devices belong to him and added also is phone provider documents as proof.\n\n\n*Full Response*\n\nDear Bolt Support Team,\nIn addition to my previous emails, I felt it necessary to explain the below with some additional evidence which I think will help.\nI acknowledge logging into my account on two devices; however, this is not a breach of Bolt policy, as confirmed by your support team. The secondary login was solely for administrative purposes to upload requested registration documents from my home device. Any closely timed logins can be explained by the fact that my workplace is only 3–4 minutes from my residence. I have attached evidence confirming that both devices belong to me.\nFor the avoidance of any doubt, I confirm that I will not log into the Bolt app on my admin device at any point moving forward and will use only my primary working device for all Bolt-related access.\nI respectfully ask that your IT team verify that I have never accepted or completed rides on more than one device. All trips have always been carried out on a single device, in full compliance with Bolt’s terms. My working pattern since joining Bolt has been consistent—primarily evenings and weekends alongside my full-time employment. I have never attempted to misuse the platform or breach contractual obligations.\nIf I had violated Bolt’s terms in any way, I would not be dedicating substantial time and effort to resolving this matter, including attending the Bolt opening in Milton Keynes, persistently following up by phone, and submitting extensive written correspondence. I am pursuing this review because I am confident I have acted honestly and within policy at all times.\nThis income is vital for supporting my family, and the suspension has caused significant hardship. I respectfully request a fair and thorough review of my account based on the evidence provided.\nThank you for your time and consideration.\nKind regards, Zain\n\nLetter[^Bolt_Formal_Complaint_Zain_Hussain_Dated.pdf (34869a3c-cfe1-44f5-9b7d-617adf8050a0).pdf] \nPhone documents in BH (taking up large space within Jira.)","2026-01-12T07:21:39.504Z"],["3801180","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768202547306289]*{color}:\nHi <@U08RWJ9TRAA>,\n\nThat would also work from ops perspective as a temporary solution until we have something more permanent, what needs to be done here so I can proceed <@U08RWJ9TRAA>?\n{quote}","2026-01-12T07:22:40.647Z"],["3801181","RCE-341","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768202194716509]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-341] `Release prelive-driveridentityverification module` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T07:22:51.693Z"],["3801184","PFI-831271","PFI","yvette.liu@bolt.eu","Yvette Liu","Hi [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] \nThank you for the additional context. \n\nI will relay this to the third party in case they have any questions. Since the user pays a subscription fee on our partner’s app to get additional benefits, such as this promo code, we will explain that this user is an edge case. \n\nThanks, \n\nYvette\n\n","2026-01-12T07:23:41.692Z"],["3801185","LSS-60080","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Thanks [~accountid:712020:da5adcfc-e0e5-4c21-a4df-4e108cffc244].\n\nFrom a Privacy perspective, my key concern is around access to the Rider’s account - can you confirm that we have secured their account now and they have changed their password? \n\nAs for the phone — I assume we have followed all of our processes here — will leave this with CS to manage though.","2026-01-12T07:23:55.842Z"],["3801188","PFI-832246","PFI","nadiya.yasee-ngo@bolt-outsource.eu","Nadiya Yasee-Ngo","!image-20260112-071933.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260112-072143.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T07:25:30.535Z"],["3801189","LSS-59597","LSS","ann.koljalg@bolt.eu","Ann Kõljalg","Hi [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] !\nCould you please let me know when we can expect to receive the reviewed contract back?\n\nFinland team has outgrown the current office, and on some days not everyone has a desk to work from. In addition, the build-out of the new office will take around 4–5 months, so it’s important for us to move forward with the contract as soon as possible.\n\nThanks for the update in advance.\n\nAnn ","2026-01-12T07:27:01.124Z"],["3801198","PFI-832248","PFI","onyinye.osuagwu@bolt.eu","Onyinyechukwu Osuagwu","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 08.29.33.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T07:29:59.006Z"],["3801199","LSS-57924","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Thank you, [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] !\n\n[~accountid:712020:819f454d-2f02-4c88-8877-98b44304a2cb], the documents have been signed","2026-01-12T07:30:05.344Z"],["3801205","PFI-832249","PFI","nadiya.yasee-ngo@bolt-outsource.eu","Nadiya Yasee-Ngo","!29DEC.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260112-072721.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T07:30:56.542Z"],["3801206","MLC-2962","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 9th*+\n\n* *Work Address Travel* - Backfill completed and automation for updating the custom attribute live\n* *Company VAT* - Taqi to finalize the S3 automation this week\n* *Relaunch of Card BINs / Geofencing* - Pending confirmation on how to proceed with the templates. CMS Builder needs updates with latest fixes to HTML before redoing the templates","2026-01-12T07:31:31.319Z"],["3801207","L10N-27140","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27138](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27138)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T07:31:54.617Z"],["3801208","L10N-27142","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions shoul