8048], tomorrow is the deadline of this case.\n\nThe user previously requested this, “Please specify exactly how and on what basis you link my ride to the scooter, including timestamps and internal logging.”\n\nHow do we explain on which basis we link the ride to the scooter, and with timestamps should I just provide the ride? What data should we provide regarding internal logging?\n\n*Last user message*\n\nYou refer back to your terms, but you still have not provided the documentation and the log data I requested under GDPR and which you have yourself confirmed receipt of. This information concerns exactly how my trip and parking are alleged to violate your rules.\nAs long as Bolt cannot or will not present the actual evidence for the alleged breach, liability for payment cannot be established.\nDespite this, you have already charged me.\nI therefore demand a refund of the amount and that the case be put on hold until the requested data has been provided.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T07:32:12.498Z"],["3801224","WDFT-3546","WDFT","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Thank you [~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044] , understood. ","2026-01-12T07:32:17.201Z"],["3801225","HS-28829","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Anja, thank you for you request. I have added Dudu here, she should be able to help. ","2026-01-12T07:32:25.163Z"],["3801226","PC-4468","PC","kevin.kanarbik@bolt.eu","Kevin Kanarbik","As discussed [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Pvf9zpVz2GS-gyCr1yw1IYvOUh-XiGDKBpqkQxj4wjA/edit?disco=AAAByZyyuc8] I’m closing this ticket because the proposed solution is not enough, solution is more complicated but it’s unnecessary because this problem comes up quite rarely, when we’re dealing with SF refund when the first refund failed and the issue is eventually resolved after 24h by the cron. Also because we’re slowly decommissioning SilverFlow as a provider anyway","2026-01-12T07:32:31.126Z"],["3801227","LSS-59751","LSS","chirag.yadav@bolt.eu","Chirag Yadav","Hi, we are waiting for Pipedrive’s Legal team to respond to our highlighted risks. They will let us know if they can sign a separate service agreement and DPA. ","2026-01-12T07:32:49.580Z"],["3801228","WDFT-3546","WDFT","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] , as discussed then in this case it will be the default poland layout for the time being. 🙂 one the company is created.\n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi\n\n\n\ncc: [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] ","2026-01-12T07:32:58.010Z"],["3801229","MLC-1564","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 9th*+\n\n* Missing translations filled in\n* Missing slides for Scheduled Rides African variants updated with new designs","2026-01-12T07:33:07.510Z"],["3801230","LSS-60240","LSS","natakun.punnahataivej@bolt.eu","Natakun Punnahataivej","[~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] The Thai translation has already been completed. Could you please help review it once more before uploading it to the website? Thank you.\n\n","2026-01-12T07:33:15.580Z"],["3801231","PFI-829943","PFI","daniele.fondjeutagouang@bolt.eu","Daniele Fondjeu Tagouang","Hi [~accountid:5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b] , could you please download the proof of payment on your side so we can provide this to the driver? The option is not active on our end.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T07:33:24.141Z"],["3801232","LSS-60870","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:712020:02460be7-393b-4b9b-840f-e649a77ff874]! \nPlease see the PoA:\n\n# [For Latvia|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YO3hfrArECENYfFtCrBNe7DgPaPghlcW/edit], it needs to be signed by Ahto. \n# [For Lithuania|https://docs.google.com/document/d/131nB2ADYGi0PFJH_nGnAR-5LTxzrBhEF/edit], it needs t be signed by Benas. \n\nLegal Ops, kindly assist with collecting signatures. Thank you! ","2026-01-12T07:33:38.981Z"],["3801233","G3IOT-1003","G3IOT","endrik.salak@bolt.eu","Endrik Salak","[~accountid:5b7bbf35ed4f842a6ddb4648] 2 modified proto samples have been made. They are currently in [~accountid:5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] possession.","2026-01-12T07:33:43.021Z"],["3801234","MLC-2749","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 9th - No Updates*+\n\n* +*Status*+\n** Discussed with Mostafa on the validity of the query and he proposed a simpler approach.\n** Instead of calculating the difference between first order in period & next order, to use a different, simpler query by using the churn etl that will help us calculate the average number of days since last order to the previous order.\n** Using the average lookback days and calculating the 20th percentile per tier will give us the insights we need to define the entry point for the Churn automation.\n** Will move on to calculate this per tier and compare to current entry point.\n* +*Next steps*+\n** Adjust segments with the new definitions.\n** Clone out for the rest of the markets.\n** 2026: Redo templates after confirmation on working template.\n** Dummy templates in translations\n** Implement for CEE markets","2026-01-12T07:34:00.985Z"],["3801237","WDFT-3529","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044] !\n\nRegarding point (1), I would recommend that instead of using *“Asset Intercompany Transfer,”* you consider *disposing of the assets in PL003* and then *registering them in PL002 using the EIB “Register Asset”* process. When preparing the template, please include the *original acquisition cost* and *historical accumulated depreciation* of the assets.\n\nIf the *“Asset Intercompany Transfer”* task is used, Workday will recognize the assets in the new entity at their *net book value (NBV)* as of the transfer date. However, since this is an *intercompany transfer at the Group level*, the assets should continue to be accounted for in PL002 in the same way as they were in PL003.\n\nThe *Bolt Find Assets* report is very helpful for completing the *“Register Asset”* template, as it includes details such as original cost, accumulated depreciation, and all relevant dimensions.\n\nPlease let me know if you need any assistance with completing the template.\n\n\n\nContinue working on other points of your request and will get back shortly ","2026-01-12T07:34:25.154Z"],["3801240","PFI-832253","PFI","onyinye.osuagwu@bolt.eu","Onyinyechukwu Osuagwu","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 08.34.10.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T07:34:48.866Z"],["3801241","WFM-9923","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Do I need to add *CS - Business* role and the queues, correct?","2026-01-12T07:34:50.806Z"],["3801242","MLC-2350","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 9th*+\n\n* Pulled December numbers and updated the report\n* Deepdives in progress. To be finalized by Tuesday","2026-01-12T07:35:23.400Z"],["3801243","DRAG101-405","DRAG101","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Dekra needs to do speedometer test; they don’t need to do the full test. \n\nMotor test is done and result is around 420W. We need to make correct info label now. ","2026-01-12T07:35:34.608Z"],["3801245","PFI-814507","PFI","alina.solomka@bolt.eu","Alina Solomka","Hey, it has been a while already and we still deal with wrong invoices","2026-01-12T07:36:31.069Z"],["3801246","LSS-61379","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","On 9 January 2026 the email was sent to Stellantis to clarify our position regarding export control laws.","2026-01-12T07:36:45.372Z"],["3801247","BP-13226","BP","mammad.imanov@bolt.eu","Mammad Imanov","Had a meeting with Hoppa side and they promised to fix the issue on their side during this week. So I will monitor more and then close this task","2026-01-12T07:37:06.924Z"],["3801248","LSS-50765","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:8932485a-0def-498a-8bfd-84cad616ae37] thank you for your patience. \n\nPlease find below two documents: \n\n(1) translation in French of the complete Service Agreement: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cytkG-9bRzByhaqwVzzoI38GrQe_cksj/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cytkG-9bRzByhaqwVzzoI38GrQe_cksj/edit|smart-link] ;\n\n(2) a short-form agreement to cover promotional campaigns where no financial compensation is being offered: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tQsDOPrM8jdpr6Eg5BNjwwkoWfwTHEFt/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tQsDOPrM8jdpr6Eg5BNjwwkoWfwTHEFt/edit|smart-link] .\n\n\n\nOur recommendation would be to always push for the long form in French, which is our standard agreement, and only use the short form in cases where the partner is a small company that is not used to working with long agreements - agreement should be short-term and zero value as well.\n\nPlease review and let me know if this meets your needs. \n\nThank you !","2026-01-12T07:37:11.569Z"],["3801249","PFI-832254","PFI","alexander.skea@bolt.eu","Alexander Skea","[^CFAO Toyota's - Payment Split - Jan26 - Sheet1.csv]","2026-01-12T07:37:16.020Z"],["3801250","PFI-832255","PFI","onyinye.osuagwu@bolt.eu","Onyinyechukwu Osuagwu","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 08.37.03.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T07:37:23.606Z"],["3801252","WFM-9899","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","I can’t see the request. Could you pls check and approve it?","2026-01-12T07:37:40.892Z"],["3801254","HS-28533","HS","fidan.karimli@bolt.eu","Fidan Karimli","Hi all! \nI am back from vacation, please send me the letter, so I can print and sign it. \n\nThanks! ","2026-01-12T07:38:04.035Z"],["3801256","DRAG101-498","DRAG101","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","German tests need to be completed for this certification, it will be a first step.","2026-01-12T07:38:37.636Z"],["3801259","PFI-832256","PFI","onyinye.osuagwu@bolt.eu","Onyinyechukwu Osuagwu","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 08.39.33.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T07:39:53.916Z"],["3801260","HS-28809","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Waiting term doc","2026-01-12T07:40:12.448Z"],["3801267","FRAUDOPS-1106","FRAUDOPS","mark@bolt.eu","Mark-Erik Valge","Implemented a solution in: [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/projects/commerce/files/fraud/databricks_views/fraud_funnel_rentals_aggregated.view.lkml|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/projects/commerce/files/fraud/databricks_views/fraud_funnel_rentals_aggregated.view.lkml]\n\nApparently there already existed a session_id which we can utilise. But this session_id is disputed by Felix and we will attempt to convince the stakeholder (MM DAM) to modify it accordingly. Meeting is held on Monday, January 19 *(*16:30 – 17:00)","2026-01-12T07:42:00.773Z"],["3801270","FDBT-4770","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_delivery fails on 2026-01-11 07:00:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task pl_and_ledger_task failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details. This caused all downstream tasks to get skipped.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 807779448467737, 'task_key': 'pl_and_ledger_task'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_delivery/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-11T07%3A00%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=delivery_market.delivery_market&base_date=2026-01-11T07%3A00%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-12T07:43:27.557Z"],["3801271","LSS-57242","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:dc5a9fc0-ec62-423d-a2f8-435f02007669], we are reviewing the documents we have and establishing any legal pathways that may be available to help the business take a decision regarding this site. \n\nPlease could you provide some feedback on the following :\n\n# Do we have any written exchanges (emails, visit notes) where the landlord addressed the ERP classification or public access suitability? \n# Was the insurance policy ever formally put in place for this site? \n# Do we have any indication that the premises could attract another tenant not subject to ERP rules (e.g. back office, storage, non-public access use)? \n# Do we have a broker view or any precedent (maybe Devon knows) on what level of indemnity might be acceptable for early exit in similar Paris-area commercial leases? \n\n\n\nThank you !","2026-01-12T07:43:43.044Z"],["3801272","WFM-9709","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Agent ID: 622513\n\nI can’t see the request. TLs, could you pls check?","2026-01-12T07:43:48.174Z"],["3801273","CEBF-1802","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Task is completed. When we marked Task as Resolve and the issue was not actually resolved then it will be back after refreshing with the date update\n\n!2026-01-12_09-42-10.mp4|width=649,alt=\"2026-01-12_09-42-10.mp4\"!","2026-01-12T07:44:03.037Z"],["3801274","RCE-336","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768203835271759]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-336 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T07:44:07.813Z"],["3801278","LSS-60915","LSS","karlo.masnjak@bolt.eu","Karlo Masnjak","Hi [~accountid:712020:876960aa-09c5-44ff-9c52-2cb24c637062] , According to the procedure, I generated a letter in English and reported the same through #dac7-delivery-support and sent it to the provider. \n\nThe Provider replied that he wanted a letter in the local language and signed by a responsible person from Bolt. I could personally translate the letter into the local language, but I cannot sign the same. So the question is, what should I communicate further to the provider?","2026-01-12T07:44:38.540Z"],["3801279","LSS-61380","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","On 8 January 2026 a call took place where the support functions were almost aligned that the proposed model works. Summary of the call may be found [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C076GDSHQLE/p1767873620321519].","2026-01-12T07:45:06.664Z"],["3801280","G3IOT-1174","G3IOT","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Nimble doesn’t actually provide that much of the gain. Will not use it.","2026-01-12T07:45:13.344Z"],["3801287","EBIKE1-380","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","3 different samples are received. Erki will check them. \n\nAlso, the current supplier is sending new reinforced arms are on the way to HQ. They will arrive in few days. ","2026-01-12T07:46:35.146Z"],["3801289","PFI-831162","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:9d4f9e6c-ca08-4e22-a659-b653d7fb9f11],\n\nThank you for bringing out all the information, this was very helpful!\n\nI have taken a look at all of the profiles, and it seems that our Fraud engine is working as intended on these users, taking account all the dupes/activities.\n\nIt seems that the main user themselves also realized that they have been completely caught, however, no further action at this point is required.\n\nThey are bringing us in positive GMV and their actions have not caused us any financial loss.\nDue to this there is no further need to permanently block the main user from the platform.\n\nOur Fraud engine has also picked up this pattern, meaning that further attempts on other verticals will completely hard-block them from our platform.\n\nPlease note, that the current restrictions that they do have will remain in place. The customer is only sorry for getting caught. They are free to use our other verticals.\nThey may be warned that any further attempts may lead to permanent suspension off the entire platform.\n\nIf you have any further questions, then please do let me know by tagging me within the ticket.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-12T07:46:53.414Z"],["3801291","RCE-338","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768203678888699]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-338 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T07:47:35.699Z"],["3801293","PRIV-485","PRIV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] – I have just started working on this! Will reach out after I catch up on the Slack thread and Lisette’s work.","2026-01-12T07:48:00.192Z"],["3801295","C2-450","C2","yong.lin@bolt.eu","Yong Lin","[~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] I got the samples. I think the spring is needed also?\n\n!e4586059-5451-4a6a-af64-d6196bcbbf60-20260112-074640.jpg|width=720,alt=\"e4586059-5451-4a6a-af64-d6196bcbbf60-20260112-074640.jpg\"!","2026-01-12T07:48:01.758Z"],["3801297","EBIKE1-87","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Supplier modified the 3D and sent to us but it won’t solve our issue. \n\nAt the moment, supplier is checking our suggestion and we are waiting supplier’s answer if it is accaptable from their side. ","2026-01-12T07:48:27.925Z"],["3801298","CSDA-292","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review ad-hoc requests once a day. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-12T07:48:28.694Z"],["3801301","CEBF-1803","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Bug is fixed\n\n!image-20260112-074842.png|width=840,alt=\"image-20260112-074842.png\"!","2026-01-12T07:48:47.144Z"],["3801311","WD-22494","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Thank you [~accountid:6390559a2acfad92d7b59f11] , i am closing this ticket now. \n\n\n\nHave a lovely day! 🙂 \n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-12T07:51:19.647Z"],["3801315","HS-28829","HS","duduzile.langa@bolt.eu","Duduzile Langa","Hi Anja, please log a ticket with people tech and they will assist you\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/26/group/1274/create/2246|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/26/group/1274/create/2246|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T07:51:57.469Z"],["3801322","TAX2-563","TAX2","fernando.souzademan@bolt.eu","Fernando Souza de Man","There has been no update by POC on project status for 26Q1","2026-01-12T07:53:46.163Z"],["3801325","PFI-828164","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Dear Bolt,\n\n\nThe chargeback was processed to close the dispute. \n|  *{color:white} *#*{color}*{color:white}{color} |  *{color:white} *Merchant*{color}*{color:white}{color} | {color:white} *{color}[{color:white} {color}{color:white} *Invoice No.*{color}{color:white} {color}|https://admin.2c2p.com/Home/SortTransactionListData?sortBy=invoice]{color:white} {color}*{color:white}{color} |  *{color:white} *Approval Code*{color}*{color:white}{color} |  *{color:white} *Credit Card No*{color}*{color:white}{color} | {color:white} *{color}[{color:white} {color}{color:white} *Date / Time*{color}{color:white} {color}|https://admin.2c2p.com/Home/SortTransactionListData?sortBy=date]{color:white} {color}*{color:white}{color} |  *{color:white} *Total Amount*{color}*{color:white}{color} |  *{color:white} *Status*{color}*{color:white}{color} | | \n| {color:#172B4D}1{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}Bolt Support Services (Thailand) Limited{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}hrnuzeh2HWXiOu8mcqFl{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}170220{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}434076XXXXXX5615{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}12/01/2026 09:17:07{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}THB 280.00{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}Chargeback{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | | \n| {color:#172B4D}2{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}Bolt Support Services (Thailand) Limited{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}XyMhApMQcbMCVijHwxRA{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}001631{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}441770XXXXXX9214{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}12/01/2026 09:15:10{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}THB 373.00{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | {color:#172B4D}Chargeback{color}{color:#134f5c}{color} | |","2026-01-12T07:54:08.513Z"],["3801326","WFM-9923","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Requested CS - Business role [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571666] and [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541665]","2026-01-12T07:54:12.645Z"],["3801328","PFI-832264","PFI","innaaime.kalju@bolt.eu","Inna Aime Kalju","[^Transaktion.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-12T07:55:15.991Z"],["3801331","LSS-60324","LSS","ksenia.romanenko@bolt.eu","Ksenia Romanenko","Hello! Sorry I was on vacation. \n\nTicket can be closed since employee left the company. ","2026-01-12T07:55:42.563Z"],["3801332","LSS-60915","LSS","tyler.ison@bolt.eu","Tyler Hamilton Ison","Hi [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] apologies to lob this back over but I think indeed the ask is legal-related,  i.e., translation of the letter to local language and signature by responsible person. Questions being \n- Translation - does this need to be an official translation or can [~accountid:5ee36bc8e31f620aba841240] personally translate?\n- Signature - appears the original wasn’t signed just says “digitally signed” - given it’s not a contract, likely docusign not the right signature. Wondering if could do an image of a wet signature as it’s more of a blast / boilerplate communication?","2026-01-12T07:55:47.039Z"],["3801333","DSR-3647","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T07:56:05.881Z"],["3801335","HS-28823","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Udval! Thank you for letting us know. I see from the system that they were still importing your information from our system, but I have added you manually now, so you should soon receive an email from MinuDoc that you have been added to their platform.\n\nLet me know if you still don’t receive an email from them and I’ll look into it again.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-12T07:56:11.814Z"],["3801336","LSS-61381","LSS","igne.martutaityte@bolt.eu","Ignė Martutaitytė","[^PoA (Bolt) (Swedbank Agreements) (EE) - clean - 21.03.2025.asice] _(65 kB)_\n\n[^PoA (Bolt Operations) (Luminor Agreements) (EE) - update 28.03.2025 (2).asice] _(63 kB)_\n\n[^PoA (Bolt) (Luminor Agreements) (EE) - update 26.03.2025 (2).asice] _(64 kB)_","2026-01-12T07:57:20.074Z"],["3801337","LSS-61352","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hey, [~accountid:712020:a975e2d9-679b-4d8a-a063-b831aafacd02]! Thank you for reaching out.\n\nI have reviewed the draft of the addendum that you linked in the ticket and I found these issues:\n\n# You have been using an old template, please use one of the newer templates that we prepared for sign-up bonuses:\n## Short version (includes only most popular provisions): [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i2dhamHslkBf4haq5xoHbGaatxJ2lWQg/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i2dhamHslkBf4haq5xoHbGaatxJ2lWQg/edit|smart-link] \n## Long version (includes all standard provisions): [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jIZgH3tKdncr6LUxUCHozt8-klDIZdpf/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jIZgH3tKdncr6LUxUCHozt8-klDIZdpf/edit|smart-link]  \n# You state in clause 2.2 that bonus should be paid in instalments, but you have not added Appendix 2 that gives details about instalments. Should bonus be paid in a lump sum?\n\nI have prepared a new draft of the addendum using new template here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P24hWLZGcueeBI03TtmiU1jPkVmZlOsQ/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P24hWLZGcueeBI03TtmiU1jPkVmZlOsQ/edit|smart-link]. Please review clause 2.2 and remove appendix 2 if it is unnecessary or provide the details.\n\nPlease let me know when the new draft is finalised so that I could assist you with signing. Also, please provide me the email address and name of a person signing the agreement if you wish it to be signed via Spotdraft or let me know what is the preferred signing method. I see that Larisa-Ioana Torjoc is the director of the company, so I assume it will be her signing the agreement (it is preferred person).","2026-01-12T07:57:44.978Z"],["3801338","CEBF-1570","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","[~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] I believe we need to fix all tests for Opportunity Lost Closing, because of validations from the [https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.lightning.force.com/builder_platform_interaction/flowBuilder.app?flowId=301dt00000AyljFAAR#/|https://boltfood--staging.sandbox.lightning.force.com/builder_platform_interaction/flowBuilder.app?flowId=301dt00000AyljFAAR#/]\nWhat do you think?","2026-01-12T07:57:49.134Z"],["3801341","LSS-61357","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] Please attach new order for the review when we have it  ","2026-01-12T07:58:44.521Z"],["3801342","DO-5782","DO","kristo.sarnets@bolt.eu","Kristo Sarnets","We don’t have a schema.\nWe’d need 2 schemas in the end, but this one would be for ingestion and then we’d need another one for DBT, which I can make a separate ticket if needed.","2026-01-12T07:59:47.149Z"],["3801345","LSS-61362","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] please support with UK specific ticket ","2026-01-12T08:00:05.631Z"],["3801346","FRAUDOPS-1077","FRAUDOPS","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","WIP - [dashboard|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/sql/dashboardsv3/01f0ed524f451fae92dea7f9bdf6f2b1/datasets/ce95a3e4?o=3598988355446810]","2026-01-12T08:00:08.062Z"],["3801347","PFI-832266","PFI","ivana.hrupacki@bolt.eu","Ivana De Marchi Hrupacki","!Screenshot_20260111_111551_Bolt Driver.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot_20260111_113149_Bolt Driver.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot_20260111_113156_Bolt Driver.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T08:00:11.922Z"],["3801348","PFI-832266","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T08:00:14.048Z"],["3801351","LSS-59915","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] could you please support with signing again in the format requested by EY 🙏 ","2026-01-12T08:01:55.561Z"],["3801355","LSS-50913","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95], thank you for the update. \nThanks, everyone, for your input - good job! 👏 ","2026-01-12T08:02:32.977Z"],["3801362","PAW-14195","PAW","mihai.casandra@bolt.eu","Mihai Casandra","Will be handled by InfoSec after all. Nothing to do on the PINT side.","2026-01-12T08:04:09.936Z"],["3801363","FRAUDOPS-286","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","business case is still pretty low for us to consider anything. especially because the action isn’t clear. what we’re gonna do? can’t remove correction feature from drivers. how can we even prove they got paid? action would prolly be around blocking for drivers with high ratio. with these numbers, just not worth it to proceed further.\n\n* per payment method:\n** !Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.02.52.png|width=978,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.02.52.png\"!\nas expected, 95% is cash\n* per month\n** !Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.03.32.png|width=978,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.03.32.png\"!\n* per country\n** !Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.04.05.png|width=975,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.04.05.png\"!\n","2026-01-12T08:04:11.680Z"],["3801364","LSS-58680","LSS","gabriel.souza@bolt.eu","Gabriel Gonçalo","Hello team! This ticket can be closed, thank you! ","2026-01-12T08:04:20.599Z"],["3801366","LSS-59597","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey [~accountid:712020:e81c1984-54f1-46ce-bc81-864b3748de94], thank you for the access and the updates.\nI will review this agreement this week. I hope that works for you! \nThanks 🙏  ","2026-01-12T08:04:45.709Z"],["3801369","WD-22485","WD","janeli.niinemaa@bolt.eu","Janeli Niinemaa","[~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] Sorry, here is the updated file of the ER-s that should be cancelled. \n\nThanks a lot!\n\n[^Old ER reports to be cancelled.xlsx]\n\n","2026-01-12T08:05:47.152Z"],["3801371","FX-3599","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768205163629039]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3599] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:06:16.363Z"],["3801372","FRAUDOPS-286","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","MX is the only one that has signs where we could prolly take actions. avg of 60 orders per driver is just massive. there’s a few guys there doing fraud without a doubt. numbers are too small tho. ","2026-01-12T08:06:37.358Z"],["3801373","FX-3599","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Halavan [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768205185786459]*{color}:\nGradually ramp up drivers sorting limit count to test if [fix|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160255] is working on the bigger amount of records\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:06:40.504Z"],["3801374","AIOT-532","AIOT","enari.saar@bolt.eu","Enari Saar","Wont do","2026-01-12T08:07:01.447Z"],["3801376","PC-4078","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","Back to backlog. Next FF, please, investigate.","2026-01-12T08:07:26.942Z"],["3801378","LSS-61280","LSS","davis.baltvilks@bolt.eu","Dāvis Baltvilks","[~accountid:712020:95922f19-94a5-49f1-b3c6-43a9c9ddd746] - did you get a chance to look at this?","2026-01-12T08:08:21.733Z"],["3801382","CRC-2321","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] First LIVE Test payment successfully completed on 10 JAN in Kenya. All employees test initiating this week.","2026-01-12T08:08:46.297Z"],["3801383","CRC-1980","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] First LIVE Test payment successfully completed on 10 JAN in Kenya. All employees test initiating this week.","2026-01-12T08:08:52.775Z"],["3801386","PFI-831413","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:712020:98578d7d-a19d-4341-a97c-e8099ba8d683] \nUnfortunately, this is something that I would not be able to advise on as it’s not payment related. \n\nYou could either raise a new ticket with the business billing or check with the business support team in Slack. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T08:09:33.065Z"],["3801387","HS-28830","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-12T08:10:00.363Z"],["3801388","PFI-832251","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-12T08:10:05.504Z"],["3801389","PFI-832278","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team is unfortunately not able to assist with pricing, discount or promo code related questions. \nPricing is decided by the vertical and the customer payments team does not have any impact on it. \nCould you please raise a ticket with the verticals technical support team instead. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2]\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-12T08:10:21.736Z"],["3801391","PFI-832263","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-12T08:11:06.259Z"],["3801393","PAR-3815","PAR","kateryna.oliferchuk@bolt.eu","Kateryna Oliferchuk","All client types except food_courier were synced. The food_courier can be synced after the [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAR-3846|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAR-3846|smart-link]  is fixed. ","2026-01-12T08:11:47.219Z"],["3801397","DRX-27507","DRX","aleksandr.stegnienko@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Stegnienko","\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1f_x2tjhDr0rMhEELZ90z-ygUSbrX1n33XR3jfUMHYPA/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1f_x2tjhDr0rMhEELZ90z-ygUSbrX1n33XR3jfUMHYPA/edit?tab=t.0|smart-card]","2026-01-12T08:12:29.711Z"],["3801398","PFI-813067","PFI","gabriel.souza@bolt.eu","Gabriel Gonçalo","Hello team! Any updates on this case? \n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T08:13:09.435Z"],["3801399","PFI-820114","PFI","ernesta.kleme@bolt.eu","Ernesta Klemė","Hello, I don't have any examples saved at the moment, but Bolt IH assured me that in such cases it was always corrected, to avoid any necessary issues for the future. ","2026-01-12T08:13:17.049Z"],["3801400","PFI-832199","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","asking for a double approval to cancel the payment. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768205575296?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768205575296?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n\nPre/auth released in UP portal ","2026-01-12T08:13:19.547Z"],["3801403","WEBSD-1451","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi 👋 \n\nWorking on it.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-12T08:13:40.337Z"],["3801408","LSS-55945","LSS","svenkristjan.bormann@bolt.eu","Sven-Kristjan Bormann","I will close the case now from our side, because there was no follow up from the lawyer during the last two months.","2026-01-12T08:14:48.199Z"],["3801409","PAW-14195","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-admin-user, pint-product-identity-and-communication-management, pint-capability-itgc\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-12T08:14:50.542Z"],["3801410","HS-28828","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-12T08:14:56.940Z"],["3801413","FX-3595","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768205702813869]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3595 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:15:15.630Z"],["3801416","FDBT-4780","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-12T08:15:57.165Z"],["3801419","PFI-832176","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-12T08:16:40.838Z"],["3801420","PFI-831489","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:a65fbd35-40e8-465a-b00a-02c5c115eff0],\n\nThe business account is active and there are no Fraud suspensions on the business account itself.\nI can also see that the business has no failed payments as of late.\nCould you perhaps forward the user who is having issues? What is their phone number?\nDue to lack of information currently we can not say for certain where the issue might be.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you,\nMarten","2026-01-12T08:16:46.823Z"],["3801421","RCE-334","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768205807048979]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-334 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:16:59.603Z"],["3801422","RCE-335","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768205814671079]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-335 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:17:07.170Z"],["3801426","DRX-27944","DRX","yuriy.melnykov@bolt.eu","Yuriy Melnykov","Postmortem [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7357071801/2026-01-05+Missing+and+stale+Driver+profiling+data|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7357071801/2026-01-05+Missing+and+stale+Driver+profiling+data|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T08:17:40.464Z"],["3801427","RCE-340","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768205851556689]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-340 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:17:44.924Z"],["3801428","PFI-829960","PFI","ernestas.jurasius@bolt-outsource.eu","Ernestas Jurasius","Hey [~accountid:712020:fc661671-1d51-4372-9578-b46465bd51ac] , we would appreciate an update on this. Thank you. ","2026-01-12T08:18:00.388Z"],["3801429","LSS-61353","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hey, [~accountid:712020:a975e2d9-679b-4d8a-a063-b831aafacd02]! Thank you for your request\n\nI have reviewed the draft of the addendum that you linked in the ticket and I found these issues:\n\n# You have been using an old template, please use one of the up-to-date templates (Links: [short|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i2dhamHslkBf4haq5xoHbGaatxJ2lWQg/edit] / [long|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jIZgH3tKdncr6LUxUCHozt8-klDIZdpf/edit]).\n# You state in clause 2.2 that bonus should be paid in instalments, but you have not added Appendix 2 that gives details about instalments. Should bonus be paid in a lump sum?\n# The amount of bonus has an extra 0 in English version, please pay attention to this to avoid creating confusion and doubts.\n# KPIs in English version and Romanian are different. Please double check.\n# I have noticed a new clause 6.2 regarding terms of changing the Agency Fee - such clauses should be part of the Special Terms. Please don’t use the sign-up bonus addendum for these. Always let the legal team know if you need some custom clauses for the addendum rather than insert them yourself.\n\nI have prepared a new draft of the addendum using new template here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SugB057yMXBbNc4O_CWh9ypqDn8EThy4/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SugB057yMXBbNc4O_CWh9ypqDn8EThy4/edit|smart-link]. Please review clauses mentioned above and in particular clause 2.2 and remove appendix 2 if it is unnecessary or provide the details.\n\nPlease let me know when the new draft is finalised so that I could assist you with signing. Also, please provide me the email address of Mihai-Alin Torjoc if you wish it to be signed via Spotdraft or let me know what is the preferred signing method.","2026-01-12T08:18:04.251Z"],["3801430","LSS-61382","LSS","davis.baltvilks@bolt.eu","Dāvis Baltvilks","[^Bolt_Pasts_Final_Project.pdf] _(194 kB)_","2026-01-12T08:18:05.209Z"],["3801433","FC-921","FC","matvei.ljasenko@bolt.eu","Matvei Ljašenko","[^UK GMV per model.xlsx]\n\n","2026-01-12T08:18:22.264Z"],["3801434","FX-3599","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768205897524019]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3599 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:18:29.365Z"],["3801435","PFI-831457","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi,\n\nEC has been disabled for the aforementioned driver.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-12T08:18:36.187Z"],["3801437","PFI-832067","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi,\n\nEC has been disabled for the aforementioned driver.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-12T08:18:41.506Z"],["3801439","SREDESK-7399","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","Editor access has been granted to your account. [~accountid:5ff6fd9c64208901410c741c] ","2026-01-12T08:18:46.000Z"],["3801441","FX-3600","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Halavan [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768205936973049]*{color}:\nGradually ramp up drivers sorting limit count to test if [fix|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160255] is working on the bigger amount of records\nWorks good on 4k. Proceed to 9k limits\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:19:07.822Z"],["3801442","FX-3600","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768205939496989]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3600] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:19:11.067Z"],["3801443","TAXP-2287","TAXP","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","Added returns of Bolt Operations OÜ. No additional annexes by Bolt Technology OÜ.","2026-01-12T08:19:21.153Z"],["3801445","UXA-2190","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","PINT team described how external IP can be extracted: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1768204633733799?thread_ts=1767952973.041899&cid=C049U1GKWQN|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1768204633733799?thread_ts=1767952973.041899&cid=C049U1GKWQN|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T08:19:47.668Z"],["3801448","CEBF-1814","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Bug is fixed\n\n!2026-01-12_10-20-23.mp4|width=649,alt=\"2026-01-12_10-20-23.mp4\"!","2026-01-12T08:20:42.008Z"],["3801449","PFI-819132","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Greeting \n\n  \n\nThe chargeback has been lost.{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}  \n\n  \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n   \n\n პატივისცემით \n\n +Best Regards+ \n\n  \n\n{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#595959} -{color} {color:#595959}მირა წოწორია / Miranda{color} {color:#595959}Mira{color} {color:#595959} tsotsoria{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Customer Journey Expert{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Payments Development Tribe{color}{color:#595959}{color} \n\n[{color:#595959}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#595959}{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge/]{color:#595959}{color}{color:#595959}{color}\n !image001.png|thumbnail!{color:#595959}{color}","2026-01-12T08:20:46.165Z"],["3801450","WDFT-3529","WDFT","kristiine.murd@bolt.eu","Kristiine Murd","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] \nBut in that case I will need to book the correction in PL003 as this entity should never have loss from asset disposal and the movement should be booked to GL 2112 Trade Payments on both sides. And if I remember correctly then using *“Asset Intercompany Transfer”* the booking was done automatically in WD.","2026-01-12T08:20:49.743Z"],["3801451","EBIKE1-419","EBIKE1","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","IOT replacement had no effect. Asked LOPS to test with a new ECU and check battery connectors.\n\nPinging them every day, no answer since Friday.\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A3R8M6DC4/p1768203571864119?thread_ts=1767347006.083579&cid=C0A3R8M6DC4|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A3R8M6DC4/p1768203571864119?thread_ts=1767347006.083579&cid=C0A3R8M6DC4]","2026-01-12T08:21:03.417Z"],["3801452","DRX-27935","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27936 has been resolved","2026-01-12T08:21:15.110Z"],["3801456","LSS-60920","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:f2997f1b-74b8-443e-a7cc-28b3ace90931], \n\nPlease find hereafter a link to the driver guide reviewed by Elisabetta and me: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/17Dv8P1ovTl8oLvQ-kU6SDNF9002VtYoW6gxuC-CwaJM/edit?tab=t.27k3z0y5lnbj|https://docs.google.com/document/d/17Dv8P1ovTl8oLvQ-kU6SDNF9002VtYoW6gxuC-CwaJM/edit?tab=t.27k3z0y5lnbj|smart-link]  \n\nCan you review and share your thoughts on the changes we have suggested? \n\nThank you !","2026-01-12T08:22:12.743Z"],["3801458","RCE-84","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768206143231409]*{color}:\n<@U04RDTQ5AJC> ptal ^\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:22:35.699Z"],["3801460","PFI-819132","PFI","support@flitt.com","support@flitt.com","გამარჯობა,\n\nრით შეგვიძლია დაგეხმაროთ?\n\nპატივისცემით,\n\nNino Pachulia\n\n{color:#1d1c1d}Support Specialist{color}\n\n\n\n{color:#222222}+995 325 00 01 02{color}\n\n[npachulia@flitt.com|mailto:npachulia@flitt.com] | [LinkedIn|https://www.linkedin.com/in/nino-pachulia/] | [www.flitt.com|https://flitt.com/]{color:#202124}{color}{color:#202124}{color}\n\n\n\n\n!https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdesUJg1p54UqXLenrFQFanpvXuj_umTqEFnw1W5JR9LBf8O3m6bGImWLGpg2ulKBMgaF3p6b25v6bmXHIHIZutpHE-jvRov39TlA4JBIsOA1TnvQv9Hi1Pl6DSaGos3E_cDDVNa_WgN0NWjc5AHd9dzQAW?key=gAVmix1twk-tFXoz-xQXqA!{color:#202124}{color}\n\n\n---- on Mon, 12 Jan 2026 12:21:04 +0400  *\"pfi\"<pfi@taxify.atlassian.net>*  wrote ---- \n\n\n{quote}\n\n\n\n{color:#333333}{color}{color:#999999} —-—-—-—{color} {color:#333333}\n{color}{color:#999999} Reply above this line.{color} {color:#333333}\n\n\nchargeback_reports commented:\n\nGreeting\n\nThe chargeback has been lost.\n\nპატივისცემით\n\n +Best Regards+\n\n{color}{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#333333}{col