33333}\n Sent on January 12, 2026 10:21:02 AM EET{color} \n!http://usw2-track.atlassian.com/CI0/0101019bb14b5c17-f51d27d6-77c7-4e16-b831-c6d10c119366-000000/089TJceL73JSghGVvD7E_WWwr9lmtvsTTY3-2lSHtDU=439!{color:#333333}{color} {quote}","2026-01-12T08:22:56.450Z"],["3801461","DBRE-8591","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","Instances are still there: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07DLM8J9GX/p1768193645076239|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07DLM8J9GX/p1768193645076239|smart-link] – reopening…","2026-01-12T08:22:57.939Z"],["3801462","PFI-801678","PFI","gabriel.souza@bolt.eu","Gabriel Gonçalo","Hello [~accountid:610279973900e60070a3495c] Could you please look into this matter? We need help explaining this situation to the company. \n\nThank you! ","2026-01-12T08:22:59.599Z"],["3801464","LSS-57985","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Marking this as “Done” as the agreement has been taken forward for signatures. New ticket created here [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-61348?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-61348?created=true|smart-link]  ","2026-01-12T08:23:06.259Z"],["3801469","FX-3598","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768206233358809]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3598 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:24:06.213Z"],["3801471","PAW-14761","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160281\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 08:24:48 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T08:24:48.798Z"],["3801472","LSS-57129","LSS","svenkristjan.bormann@bolt.eu","Sven-Kristjan Bormann","I will close the ticket now from our side.","2026-01-12T08:24:52.714Z"],["3801473","LSS-61383","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDmitri Issatšenko has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-12T08:24:59.020Z"],["3801474","RDXENG-4570","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","Targeting event: {{Active Order Session (user_id)}}\n\nTargeting parameters:\n\n{code:json}{\n    \"is_upsell_in_cancellation_flow_enabled\": true,\n    \"price_increase_upsell_config\": {\n        \"minimum_order_age_s\": 20,\n        \"driver_rejections_or_did_not_respond_count\": 3,\n        \"price_increase_by_percentage\": 20,\n        \"rider_confirmation_timeout_sec\": 240\n    },\n  \"is_prioritize_copy_for_upsell_in_cancellation_flow_enabled\" : true\n}{code}\n\n\n\n{{is_prioritize_copy_for_upsell_in_cancellation_flow_enabled}} is the parameter which decides whether to show {{Prioritise}} copy or {{Raise offer}} copy.\n\ncc: [~accountid:627b6b8f19b1290068296d3b] ","2026-01-12T08:25:15.346Z"],["3801475","PFI-741241","PFI","gabriel.souza@bolt.eu","Gabriel Gonçalo","Hello team! Any updates on this case? \n\nThank you! ","2026-01-12T08:25:21.329Z"],["3801479","MLC-3290","MLC","robert.pirnuta@bolt.eu","Robert-Mihai Pîrnuță","The launch date has been moved to the first week of Feb","2026-01-12T08:26:22.359Z"],["3801483","DLSP-1947","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","we don’t need it","2026-01-12T08:28:12.169Z"],["3801484","DO-5782","DO","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Done, have a good day!","2026-01-12T08:28:27.941Z"],["3801485","RDXENG-4594","RDXENG","sergei.emelianov@bolt.eu","Sergey Emeliyanov","For QA: Issue is due to race condition and may not reproduce on emulators or slow devices. Use a modern Android to test.","2026-01-12T08:28:43.505Z"],["3801486","HS-28824","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","With global mobility.","2026-01-12T08:28:52.068Z"],["3801492","WEBSD-1443","WEBSD","tom.gander@bolt.eu","Tom Gander","Hi [~accountid:712020:e6db7bf1-81f8-43b5-b50b-2b4bb57ce924] apologies.\n\nI will do it today 🙏 ","2026-01-12T08:30:08.059Z"],["3801493","LEG-1238","LEG","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Communication rolled out to Regional legal counsels. Marking this as “Done”.","2026-01-12T08:30:20.081Z"],["3801498","LSS-61382","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T08:31:33.692Z"],["3801499","RCE-84","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sudipto Das [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768206685971249]*{color}:\nHi <@U06T0J3AHEK> Need clarification here, apologies coming to this now. :pray::skin-tone-3:\n\nI need some details on the problem space and what do we exactly need to support the market\n• Is there some regulation which is enforceable for us? Please can you share that, esp why waybill and not trip receipts are required?\n• Why do we as Ops need to download the waybills? Is the liability not with Fleets who need to be able to do this?\n• On Problem\n    ◦ How is this impacting onboarding of Fleets, by design that Fleet will have 0 trips, so the problem is unclear here for me\n    ◦ What are the CS Costs associated here? Please can you share weekly/monthly vols\nPlease can you share a doc with all the requisite details and the biz case around the ask. Thank you!\n\n<@U01NNTGRXD0> <@U01TJ1KU55M>\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:31:40.748Z"],["3801502","LSS-61383","LSS","dmitri.issatsenko@bolt.eu","Dmitri Issatšenko","Adding example Business Resale contracts to review and few invoice examples to illustrate the problems \n\n[^6PS-24-237 (1) (1) (2).adoc]\n[^e paraksts_par darbinieku pārvadāšanu_Bolt Operations OÜ (1) (3).edoc]\n[^Invoice-resale.pdf]\n[^c6c7576d-f24e-43c6-8ea2-bbe1f7d088bc.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T08:31:59.879Z"],["3801507","LSS-61313","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] ! 🙏 ","2026-01-12T08:33:08.051Z"],["3801508","DLSP-1990","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","This issue has been reproduced/noticed by developers during the development → I will reject it. If the problem is reported, we will investigate it","2026-01-12T08:33:21.215Z"],["3801509","FX-3600","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768206802141189]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3600 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T08:33:37.494Z"],["3801513","LSS-46865","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Marking this ticket as “Done”. The MVRA ticket ([https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LEG-866?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNTkyOTQzNjU5MjA3NDY4OGJlYTMwMWFmNmRmOGFlNzUiLCJwIjoiaiJ9|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LEG-866?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNTkyOTQzNjU5MjA3NDY4OGJlYTMwMWFmNmRmOGFlNzUiLCJwIjoiaiJ9|smart-link] ) covers the most recent update on this topic. \n\ncc: [~accountid:62722e092db308007024a425] [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] ","2026-01-12T08:34:03.750Z"],["3801519","CSXDL-177","CSXDL","robert.aavik@bolt.eu","Robert Aavik","Output: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-HrxBb1fy6II8BTXiAIbV9SOegyEsA3bm0tFTxMVa5s/edit?tab=t.ybyr1uzaiufx|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-HrxBb1fy6II8BTXiAIbV9SOegyEsA3bm0tFTxMVa5s/edit?tab=t.ybyr1uzaiufx|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T08:34:30.235Z"],["3801521","PFI-832292","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-12T08:34:37.310Z"],["3801523","PFI-832292","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:5cbf158a6fbf5a10040d1d63] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-12T08:34:38.888Z"],["3801529","DSR-3649","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T08:36:07.077Z"],["3801530","PFI-713390","PFI","gabriel.souza@bolt.eu","Gabriel Gonçalo","Hello team! Any updates on this case? \n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T08:36:10.467Z"],["3801532","LSS-61384","LSS","davis.baltvilks@bolt.eu","Dāvis Baltvilks","[^Vienosanas_Nr.1_Bolt_.docx] _(32 kB)_","2026-01-12T08:37:17.237Z"],["3801536","PFI-832127","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nConfirming the user has created a top up for 7 EUR on 11/01/2026, 22:30. \nPlease let me know if the user is still having any issues and I will reopen the ticket. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T08:38:03.022Z"],["3801539","LSS-61266","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] \n\nMany thanks for the ticket. \n\nI wanted to clarify the agreement value, please. I see that a figure of EUR 20m has been indicated on the ticket, however, the annexes relating to costs in the agreement are currently empty.\n\nTo accurately assess the associated risk and liability, could you please confirm what the expected value of the agreement will be (whether calculated on an annual basis or over the full three-year term), excluding any potential separate agreements for vehicle purchases?\n\nMany thanks for your help.\n\nVeera","2026-01-12T08:38:28.093Z"],["3801540","DRX-26922","DRX","anton.grunichev@bolt.eu","Anton Grunichev","Hey [~accountid:63184a43b433b060db570f4b] , what is the status?","2026-01-12T08:38:38.335Z"],["3801541","G3IOT-1148","G3IOT","tarmo.kuuse@bolt.eu","Tarmo Kuuse","Current functionality implemented as:\n\nNVS partition remains where it is. Encryption depends only on how the partition is named.\n\n* {{nvs}} holds cleartext NVS.\n* {{nvs_encr}} holds encrypted NVS.\n\nUntil NVS data is migrated to encrypted partition, rollback is not limited in any way.\n\nFuture plans for migrating data from cleartext to encrypted NVS:\n\n# nothing changes in field or manufacturing. Both scooter and paneltester firmware targets support encrypted NVS, but there's no {{nvs_encr}} partition where to activate it.\n# existing manufacturing flow in InCap switches over to encrypted NVS (not full blown zero-trust manufacturing, just the NVS partition).\n# replace current provisioning flow in manufacturing with zero trust manufacturing.\n# migrate field devices to encrypted NVS. We can have them create a new partition at the end of flash and move data over there. (edited) ","2026-01-12T08:38:40.805Z"],["3801546","WDFT-3535","WDFT","kristiine.murd@bolt.eu","Kristiine Murd","Entity VAT code (Polish NIP): 5253063714\nRegon: 542910283\nKRS number: 0001198241\n\n*Bank accounts mBank S.A* [~accountid:712020:b91275f1-415a-4b3c-8490-974f09f14a0d] \nFinance account (main) IBAN: PL39114010100000770883001001 (PLN)\nEUR account IBAN: PL12114010100000770883001002 (EUR)\nVAT bank account IBAN: PL82114010100000770883001003 (PLN)\n\n[~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] please adde the same Customer invoice layout as for other Polish entities","2026-01-12T08:39:45.043Z"],["3801547","AER-67","AER","kevin.sutanto@bolt.eu","Kevin Sutanto","*Phase 1 is completed*. Output can be seen in the following documents\n\n# [Data & AI Space|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3411616445563947?o=3598988355446810#command/4778047099185932]\n# [AI in Analytics 2026 Strategy |https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XmjwRWkIajsvhfZnEGUtEv0hM-mSSyNsRHtGoFN1UW0/edit?tab=t.2kvme0vefqlq#heading=h.xerel6yargat] ","2026-01-12T08:39:48.461Z"],["3801548","DRX-27944","DRX","yuriy.melnykov@bolt.eu","Yuriy Melnykov","{quote}Closing this ticket, but but ask ML-platform team about possible solution to avoid this in the future, see [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C089BFQABB4/p1768207022016209?thread_ts=1767597240.998439&cid=C089BFQABB4]\n\n[~accountid:5b8cea0ad0b4022bdc51a8a2] How can we propagate this information to the clients, such as Driver domain?\n\nWe get data from this endpoint {{/internal/getDriverProfile}} and the way it works, all the properties are {{nullable}} , because of Redis optimization where {{0}} values are stored as {{null}}. So, how should client as us, knows if data is stale, so that we would not store it as {{0}} in our replica. Currently, we cannot distinguish this events, {{0}} - is legitimate number.{quote}\n\n\nThe possible fix will be done in the next ticket.\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:eb64fa24-b70d-49d6-b62c-e4560e7e1457] ","2026-01-12T08:39:53.514Z"],["3801551","PFI-817490","PFI","kristina.pugaca@bolt.eu","Kristina Pugaca","hello team, can we please have an update ","2026-01-12T08:39:59.906Z"],["3801552","LSS-52572","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] this one should be signed:\n\n [^2026 Declaration_Bolt_Poland_KYP Auchan.docx (68c5d1e1-04a9-4ff4-9f6a-6e4e219a2e68).pdf] / [https://docs.google.com/document/d/16cIVwH_045wfkwyrGYF5jJA9GhLrv_u1/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/16cIVwH_045wfkwyrGYF5jJA9GhLrv_u1/edit|smart-link]  (same files)\n\nThe questionnaire does not require to be signed itself so [~accountid:712020:0b391d02-6c8a-4494-99fd-3d2ff0d7ef37] could fill it in by himself 😉 ","2026-01-12T08:40:11.701Z"],["3801555","SCM-1069","SCM","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","Second Drum test report: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RNTL/pages/7360643073|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RNTL/pages/7360643073|smart-link] \n\n{color:#36B37E}*[ PASSED ]*{color} ","2026-01-12T08:40:17.853Z"],["3801556","G3IOT-1148","G3IOT","tarmo.kuuse@bolt.eu","Tarmo Kuuse","Currently testing on field in a few vehicles in Oslo and Brussels.\n\nInstalled current master + NVS-encryption-support {{scooter-v3.55.0-g8469a571.gz}} into a few live scooters:\nOslo: {{10541274|12594961|a010be16|8d9c8748}}\nBrussels:  {{ddee794b|0e8c16c2}}","2026-01-12T08:40:39.753Z"],["3801561","ML-3696","ML","yuriy.melnykov@bolt.eu","Yuriy Melnykov","My comment in Postmortem:\n\n\n{quote}How can we propagate this information to the clients, such as Driver domain?\n\nWe get data from this endpoint {{/internal/getDriverProfile}} and the way it works, all the properties are {{nullable}} , because of Redis optimization where {{0}} values are stored as {{null}}. So, how should client as us, knows if data is stale, so that we would not store it as {{0}} in our replica. Currently, we cannot distinguish this events, {{0}} - is legitimate number.{quote}","2026-01-12T08:41:10.001Z"],["3801571","DRX-27736","DRX","taxifyqa@bolt.eu","QA Testing","PR comment for QA:\nPlease check worktime banner position(s) in diferent cases.","2026-01-12T08:43:21.567Z"],["3801573","MLC-3762","MLC","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","+*Week 2*+\n\n* I finalised the [pre-analysis|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/17KxdQup2rGJ3waH38fkan9juGOMhxhBmYYzy2_UIVUA/edit?usp=sharing] and chose new markets for the experiment.\n** Markets: CZ, EE, UA, and GH\n** Duration: 2-3 weeks.\n** Hypothesis\n*** We hypothesise that sending communication to inform users about received incentive offer could increase the conversion towards Order Delivered by 0.04-0.26 pp.\n*** We hypothesise if we send less incentive comms in a week (from 4 to 2 comms per week), the number of converting users will stay the same.\n* Created a Confluence page – [2026-01 Eater, Incentives, Frequency Experiment|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7363166211/2026-01+Eater+Incentives+Frequency+Experiment]\n* Had a sync with Ani (MarTech) to align on the experiment. He approved the pre-analysis and understood how and what help I need from him with the post-analysis.\n* Next week, I’ll prepare the experiment setups in Braze and launch them from Wednesday. I’ll also share it with the Growth team.","2026-01-12T08:43:38.447Z"],["3801574","LSS-56257","LSS","natalia.fronczuk@bolt.eu","Natalia Frończuk","Hi Team, code is *DZZ1JF49.* Valid until the end of May.","2026-01-12T08:43:38.648Z"],["3801575","PFI-820537","PFI","janek.vassin@bolt.eu","Janek Vassin","Hey [~accountid:619df382b43d5b006a0196e7]! Are there any updates?","2026-01-12T08:43:39.609Z"],["3801576","UXA-2130","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","An idea to create mechanism to track re-installations: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/ID/ideas/view/6618745?selectedIssue=ID-1031|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/ID/ideas/view/6618745?selectedIssue=ID-1031|smart-link] .","2026-01-12T08:43:53.486Z"],["3801577","LSS-57756","LSS","jakub.pniewski@bolt.eu","Jakub Pniewski","Hey [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f], \nWe can close this ticket and re-open as needed.\nThere are some changes in entity of the fleet. \n\nTIA 🤝","2026-01-12T08:44:13.294Z"],["3801579","CEBF-1543","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Task is completed\n\n!image-20260112-084444.png|width=649,alt=\"image-20260112-084444.png\"!","2026-01-12T08:44:49.218Z"],["3801582","LSS-61384","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T08:46:07.565Z"],["3801587","PFI-832264","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:6012aaf8a41ea5006a613a63] \n\nI have found a user with matching payment history. \nYou can find these payments from here. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments?userId=288990213&tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"userType\"%3A\"user\"%2C\"from\"%3A1752278400.88%2C\"to\"%3A1768262399.88%2C\"userId\"%3A288990213}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments?userId=288990213&tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22userType%22%3A%22user%22%2C%22from%22%3A1752278400.88%2C%22to%22%3A1768262399.88%2C%22userId%22%3A288990213%7D%7D]\n\nSince this is PayPal I would not be able to confirm 100% what was the payment method used. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T08:46:38.026Z"],["3801588","L10N-27178","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find