on for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27176](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27176)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T08:47:20.075Z"],["3801598","L10N-27205","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27176](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27176)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T08:47:20.624Z"],["3801599","L10N-27204","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27176](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27176)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T08:47:21.053Z"],["3801600","WFM-9928","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Hello [~accountid:642a97a99f314a0a30143c18], \r\n\r\nThe agent received the role and the queue. \r\nHave a great day!","2026-01-12T08:47:21.155Z"],["3801606","WFM-9928","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:74b4c3fb-6caf-4d5d-b7f8-c2ea38318e58], [~accountid:712020:824016bc-1a7a-4038-a3aa-448d64c000d1] , for the assignment. ","2026-01-12T08:47:56.401Z"],["3801612","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d15dd8c0d64020c403ae98c], I hope that you are well. \n\nPlease could you let me know if you have enough information with the below to find the passenger and the ride in question?\n\nPassenger name: {{MASSAQ EP SAKHRAOUI Hend}}\n\nRide: 23 décembre 2025 à 23h17 from the airport CDG to 20, avenue du Pays de Galie, 78860 Saint-Nom-la-Bretèche.\n\n\nThank you ! ","2026-01-12T08:48:10.336Z"],["3801616","DRX-27981","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.127.0 Release build on Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\nWestern Sahara is not shown as an option on login/register/add trusted contact screens under {{Country codes}}\n\n||*Login*||*Register*||*Add/Edit trusted contact*||\n|!Screenshot_20260112-103040.png|width=205,alt=\"Screenshot_20260112-103040.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260112-103111.png|width=205,alt=\"Screenshot_20260112-103111.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260112-103310.png|width=205,alt=\"Screenshot_20260112-103310.png\"!|","2026-01-12T08:49:04.670Z"],["3801618","DRX-27873","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27981 has been resolved","2026-01-12T08:49:11.346Z"],["3801619","IOTTEAM-234","IOTTEAM","enari.saar@bolt.eu","Enari Saar","Needs \n\n{noformat}continue-on-error: true{noformat}\n\n modifier to make it non critical step even if it fails. It will pass the workflow.","2026-01-12T08:49:23.202Z"],["3801620","PFI-832294","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have a hunch this is related to a business billing bug. \nCould you please raise a new ticket with the business billing from here? \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305]\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T08:49:23.317Z"],["3801621","DSR-3085","DSR","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3], to address basis you can use this:\n\n_To enable micromobility rental service, a ride is linked to a specific scooter when the user unlocks a scooter through the app. At that moment, the scooter’s unique identifier is recorded and associated with the user’s account and a newly created ride session. All subsequent ride data (duration, distance, cost) is linked to that scooter via this identifier._ \n\nYou should provide *ride-level timestamps*, not system-level logs. Typically sufficient:\n\n* Ride start timestamp\n* Ride end timestamp\n* (Optional) unlock timestamp if distinct from start\n* (Optional) lock/end confirmation timestamp\n\nIf the ride record already contains these, yes - providing the ride record itself is usually sufficient, as long as it clearly shows:\n\n* Which scooter was used\n* When the association started and ended","2026-01-12T08:49:33.769Z"],["3801624","PFI-832090","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-12T08:49:44.927Z"],["3801625","PFI-832089","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-12T08:49:58.944Z"],["3801626","DRX-27235","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27797 has been resolved","2026-01-12T08:49:59.330Z"],["3801627","EBIKE1-390","EBIKE1","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","Samples from WheelTop have arrived. Testing will take place when we receive also new samples from our current supplier ETA {{2026-01-16}} \n\n\n\nThe problem with the received cranks is that the chainwheel is merged with the crank arm and it can not be ordered without the chainwheel. Will double check the model number with Hendrik to be sure that we got correct model.","2026-01-12T08:49:59.711Z"],["3801628","HS-28135","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Pinged for signature 12.01","2026-01-12T08:50:10.591Z"],["3801629","DRX-27749","DRX","aleksandr.stegnienko@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Stegnienko","Cache will not be extended with the new fields","2026-01-12T08:50:19.384Z"],["3801630","LSS-61383","LSS","dmitri.issatsenko@bolt.eu","Dmitri Issatšenko","!image-20260112-084947.png|width=810,height=960,alt=\"image-20260112-084947.png\"!\n\nExample of current monthly invoice in Business Resale. Both Surcharge and Ride fee are bundled together as a single invoice line ","2026-01-12T08:50:25.155Z"],["3801633","SUPX-2315","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","{quote}*= 0.25*{quote}\n\n:warning: *WARNING :: support-webapp-gateway-rider :: [RC] responses* Triggered with value *0.28*  The ratio of *non-OK responses* endpoint returns to users has exceeded the threshold.","2026-01-12T08:50:33.004Z"],["3801634","SUPX-2315","SUPX",null,"Slack","[Christian Kalme|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ae966399abb77267ba68b16] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C061Q2ULEU8/p1768207118987299?thread_ts=1768207118.987299&cid=C061Q2ULEU8|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C061Q2ULEU8/p1768207118987299?thread_ts=1768207118.987299&cid=C061Q2ULEU8|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-12T08:50:34.142Z"],["3801635","SUPX-2315","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","[@artem.kudlaienko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/630e0b9a9796033b256bd3a5] [@christian.kalme|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ae966399abb77267ba68b16] ^","2026-01-12T08:50:34.648Z"],["3801637","SUPX-2315","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Seems user was able to click back and we tried to load a page that user no longer should have access to.","2026-01-12T08:50:35.424Z"],["3801638","PFI-830808","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Greeting \n\n   \n\n   \n\n We kindly request that you provide your official position along with the relevant supporting documentation immediately, but no later than within one (1) business day. \n\n Upon expiration of the aforementioned deadline, the bank will proceed with initiating a chargeback to refund the amount to the customer, and the respective sum will be debited from your company’s account without acceptance. \n\n Thank you for your cooperation.{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} \n\n  \n\n  \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n   \n\n პატივისცემით \n\n +Best Regards+ \n\n  \n\n{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#595959} -{color} {color:#595959}მირა წოწორია / Miranda{color} {color:#595959}Mira{color} {color:#595959} tsotsoria{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Customer Journey Expert{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Payments Development Tribe{color}{color:#595959}{color} \n\n[{color:#595959}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#595959}{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge/]{color:#595959}{color}{color:#595959}{color}\n !image001.png|thumbnail!{color:#595959}{color}","2026-01-12T08:50:51.920Z"],["3801639","PFI-832069","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-12T08:50:59.093Z"],["3801640","GN-81","GN","aleksei.getman@bolt.eu","Aleksei Getman","Crash in debug build 100% reproducible if you first make sure that default navigation mode is \"overview\" (when we show on map the overview of the whole route), then you have to relaunch the app and accept the new order → crash as MapBox is not yet laid out to setup the correct camera","2026-01-12T08:51:04.992Z"],["3801641","LSS-54833","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:2f68ebec-bff7-4acf-a855-0eeaf1c88737]! Would you provide me with access to the doc with IWG’s last amendments please? Thank you! ","2026-01-12T08:51:07.211Z"],["3801642","DSR-3651","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T08:51:08.018Z"],["3801644","PAW-14775","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-12T08:51:33.798Z"],["3801647","LSS-61020","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] , please could I ask for your help to review the grounds for blocking this driver and confirm whether the block should be maintained or block? Has this driver received an email to notify him of the blocking and the available resources to contest this decision?\n\nDriver: BENSACI YASSINE \n\n2 RUE PILON DU ROI 13127 VITROLLES \n\n0622589322/0649952335\n\n[benyass.cab@gmail.com|mailto:benyass.cab@gmail.com]\n\nThank you ! 🙏 ","2026-01-12T08:52:01.323Z"],["3801649","PFI-829490","PFI","leticija.jurjevic@bolt.eu","Leticija Jurjević","agent needed ","2026-01-12T08:52:36.626Z"],["3801650","WFM-9929","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Thank you, Rodolfo! ","2026-01-12T08:52:43.598Z"],["3801653","PFI-829951","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Greeting \n\n   \n\n   \n\n We kindly request that you provide your official position along with the relevant supporting documentation immediately, but no later than within one (1) business day. \n\n Upon expiration of the aforementioned deadline, the bank will proceed with initiating a chargeback to refund the amount to the customer, and the respective sum will be debited from your company’s account without acceptance. \n\n Thank you for your cooperation.{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} \n\n  \n\n  \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n   \n\n პატივისცემით \n\n +Best Regards+ \n\n  \n\n{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#595959} -{color} {color:#595959}მირა წოწორია / Miranda{color} {color:#595959}Mira{color} {color:#595959} tsotsoria{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Customer Journey Expert{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Payments Development Tribe{color}{color:#595959}{color} \n\n[{color:#595959}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#595959}{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge/]{color:#595959}{color}{color:#595959}{color}\n !image001.png|thumbnail!{color:#595959}{color}","2026-01-12T08:52:51.380Z"],["3801654","WFM-9929","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Hey [~accountid:642a97a99f314a0a30143c18], \r\n\r\nAgents assigned. ","2026-01-12T08:53:03.064Z"],["3801656","DRX-27684","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","Tested and verified on DA.127.0 (release variant) using OPPO Reno 13, Android 15\n\nverified buttons order and style during\n\n* continue registration phase\n* log in ./ sign in phase\n* New registration phase\n* Verified order is maintained when app is killed and restarted\n\n\n\n!mobizen_20260112_103557.mp4|width=414,alt=\"mobizen_20260112_103557.mp4\"!\n\n!mobizen_20260112_103249.mp4|width=399,alt=\"mobizen_20260112_103249.mp4\"!\n\n!Screenshot_2026-01-12-10-36-39-59_1230af561eaac2e01ffb941d4d013932.jpg|width=487,alt=\"Screenshot_2026-01-12-10-36-39-59_1230af561eaac2e01ffb941d4d013932.jpg\"!\n\n!Screenshot_2026-01-12-10-32-35-84_1230af561eaac2e01ffb941d4d013932.jpg|width=497,alt=\"Screenshot_2026-01-12-10-32-35-84_1230af561eaac2e01ffb941d4d013932.jpg\"!","2026-01-12T08:53:14.786Z"],["3801657","DRX-27683","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27684 has been resolved","2026-01-12T08:53:22.420Z"],["3801666","MLC-1378","MLC","robert.pirnuta@bolt.eu","Robert-Mihai Pîrnuță","*Update*: SE has been launched on Friday, {{2026-01-09}}\n\n*Next Steps*: FI is pending; I have sent a follow up on the local team slack channel on Friday","2026-01-12T08:54:56.377Z"],["3801669","PFI-832068","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-12T08:55:15.313Z"],["3801672","WD-22533","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","Hi [~accountid:61b1d141b0b630006a9698e1] \nThe changes are done, please feel free to check and let me know if something else is needed.\n\nKins regards,\n\nDarja Netjaga","2026-01-12T08:55:44.473Z"],["3801673","LSS-61299","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^Katarzyna Karwan PEL Bolt Poland (9617d01c-9149-4751-9c82-7c0816eff949).pdf]\n\nHi Team, please proceed with signing the attached PoA with Ahto’s Dokobit signature. Thank you! ","2026-01-12T08:55:57.103Z"],["3801674","PFI-832066","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe payment is here \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4021346088|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4021346088]\n\nThe user is reporting a double-charge because of incremental authorization.\nIncremental authorization in card payments refers to the process of requesting an additional authorization on a customer’s card when the original authorized amount is insufficient to cover the final transaction cost. This typically happens in scenarios where the final amount of the transaction is not known upfront or may change.\n\nI have checked the case and everything looks good on Bolt’s end. The pre-authorization has been released to the customer. \nYou can ask the customer to reach out to their bank in order to confirm the authorized funds have been released. Their bank can locate the funds with the authorization date and amount. \n\n\nPlease let me know if you have any other questions.\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-12T08:56:04.601Z"],["3801677","WEB-7906","WEB","roberts.calijs@bolt.eu","Robert Chaliy","[~accountid:712020:e8f2de02-6346-4839-a1e5-fc656f320d5e] Hello! Will send it over today! ","2026-01-12T08:56:25.564Z"],["3801678","SFLEET-117","SFLEET","charles.franca@bolt.eu","Charles França","[~accountid:712020:a1e1cc21-901c-43ed-b15e-7737d865bb5c] Can you provide an update on what’s pending from what you have created so far?","2026-01-12T08:56:25.904Z"],["3801681","DSR-2905","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","just FYI - Driver send another follow up asking for an update","2026-01-12T08:56:55.454Z"],["3801682","WDFT-3529","WDFT","kristiine.murd@bolt.eu","Kristiine Murd","Here is one example from last time: \n\nPL001 asset +BA-006623+ was transferred to PL003 creating linked asset card +BA-006623-01+. In ‘Cost details’ I can get to the transaction (Journal Sequence Number [BAS-2023-000035|https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/7107$36/rel-task/2997$4705.htmld]) and in there I can see, that this transaction created only Balance Sheet account related postings and the value was booked to GL 2112.","2026-01-12T08:56:58.113Z"],["3801687","PFI-741241","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, this case is under consideration by the Product Team to scope and implement the required changes.","2026-01-12T08:57:54.162Z"],["3801688","PFI-830647","PFI","jose.vietto@bolt.eu","Jose Ignacio Gutierrez Vietto","Hello [~accountid:712020:c2c173c3-935e-4969-82d9-b55800b32d30] \n\nNo i cant find them i still don’t know where those payments come from. ","2026-01-12T08:57:57.953Z"],["3801689","DBRE-8586","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Central cluster Alter automation paused due to a lack of disk space.\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNKLBL33P/p1768207037323769|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNKLBL33P/p1768207037323769|smart-link] \n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8688|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8688|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T08:58:00.065Z"],["3801690","DBRE-8586","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Done","2026-01-12T08:58:10.000Z"],["3801691","PFI-832055","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-12T08:58:15.986Z"],["3801693","FRAUD-5738","FRAUD","ivan.honchar@bolt.eu","Ivan Honchar","This ticket has very low priority unless we see this problem again.\n\nMainly I’ve created the ticket to collect all previous investigation in one place","2026-01-12T08:58:37.905Z"],["3801697","BDB-1528","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:619cad8cb43d5b006af304cc] \n\nCould you please request the SDG logo in pdf or ai format, in CMYK?\nAdditionally, if we plan to use any of their graphics, we’ll need those in vector format as well (pdf, ai, or svg).\nAlso, would you like to include a specific message? If so, we’ll need a copywriter’s help.\n\ncc: [~accountid:6012ba328fb6ea014a8294ce] \n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T08:59:04.649Z"],["3801698","PFI-831386","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","duplicate!","2026-01-12T08:59:07.845Z"],["3801700","LSS-61234","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:ae4fba9f-a97d-41eb-8fd7-bec2a5bc17d0], currently having a look at the doc and I think I am not the correct POC to answer those (sorry!). I assume these questions should sit with InfoSec team that helped you with the responses in the first place. Who was the one helping you with that initially? ","2026-01-12T08:59:42.267Z"],["3801701","FRAUDOPS-286","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","found a perfect example of abuse:\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/6181343?tab=profile&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Atlantic%2FSt_Helena|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/6181343?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Atlantic%2FSt_Helena]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"start_timestamp\"%3A1767304800%2C\"end_timestamp\"%3A1768255199.999%2C\"all_order_try_states\"%3Atrue%2C\"driver_id\"%3A6181343%2C\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"order_try_state\"%3A\"finished\"}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_timestamp%22%3A1767304800%2C%22end_timestamp%22%3A1768255199.999%2C%22all_order_try_states%22%3Atrue%2C%22driver_id%22%3A6181343%2C%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22order_try_state%22%3A%22finished%22%7D%7D]\n\nevery order the driver has, he adjusts to 5 pesos at the end, which is 0.2 euros. regardless of the actual ride price. \n\nscheme is legit. and drivers can easily abuse just like this dude. unfortunately, or fortunately I guess, business case is still not worth for us to proceed. ","2026-01-12T08:59:49.834Z"],["3801703","LSS-60808","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nHappy Monday!\n\nDo you have any updates on this? 🥺 \n\nThank you.","2026-01-12T09:00:09.386Z"],["3801704","CCM-22266","CCM","theeranart.seatia@bolt-outsource.eu","Theeranart Seatia","[^Request training material.txt]","2026-01-12T09:00:12.382Z"],["3801705","PFI-819864","PFI","lev.melnikov@bolt.eu","Leo Melnikov","Hello [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea],\n\nAfter reaching out to the relevant teams, we [received an update|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C017T6D3D7Y/p1767601774934339?thread_ts=1766325648.679419&cid=C017T6D3D7Y] from [~accountid:712020:af78323e-6288-4c00-99e9-c4d970e264da] that the account in questions has been re-reviewed and subsequently deactivated. ","2026-01-12T09:00:25.177Z"],["3801706","PFI-832266","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Adjustments, Compensations*\n* If driver was compensated a while ago in some CS ticket - and this compensation is still not added to driver's balance -> please raise it with Local operations.\n\n*Why?* \nWhen Compensation is created in CS ticket -> it gets added to a csv file. Then local ops take it once a month and submit it into Manual Adjustment tool. They might submit it late, or submitting csv file gets delayed.\n\n\n*Campaign Bonus*\n* If driver did not recevei a bonus for a campaign -> please raise it with campaign team.\n\n*Why?*\nBilling team does not handle campaign setups. So we do not know when, why, how drivers should receive bonuses.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-12T09:00:26.116Z"],["3801708","WD-18345","WD",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi, we haven't heard from you in a 14 days. ","2026-01-12T09:00:58.890Z"],["3801709","WD-18345","WD",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi, we haven't heard from you in a in 21 days. The ticket will be closed due to no response in 7 days. \n\n","2026-01-12T09:00:59.752Z"],["3801710","PFI-831504","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:64dc6ab2-0c75-4297-9f61-3b2aacbf9eb4],\n\nSeems like the user still has a *Hard block* on their profile, meaning that this has not been submitted to the Safety Team for review or that the process is incomplete.\n\nFraud Team does not remove *Hard-Blocks* from the profiles, we only help in removing the *device UID blocks* once the investigation has been finalized and the rest of the blocks have been removed.\nKindly see below which block exactly I’m talking about:\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.01.05.png|width=253,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.01.05.png\"!\n\nPlease let us know once the profile has been finalized.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you,\nMarten","2026-01-12T09:01:14.755Z"],["3801711","WD-18345","WD",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi, we haven't heard from you in a while. The ticket will be closed due to no response in over 28 days. If the matter is still relevant, please submit a new ticket.\n","2026-01-12T09:01:22.203Z"],["3801713","WD-18345","WD",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi, we haven't heard from you in 7 days.","2026-01-12T09:01:35.921Z"],["3801714","DSR-3653","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T09:01:46.102Z"],["3801716","HS-28730","HS","michal.gebal@bolt.eu","Michał Gębal","Hi [~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0] \n\nDawid would like it stamped and signed, just like last time. If Ewa Ożańska signs it, all she needs to do is send him a scan of the document.","2026-01-12T09:01:57.571Z"],["3801717","PFI-832044","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have checked the case on Customer payments side and I can confirm there haven’t been any payment related issues that prevented the order from happening. \n\nWe also did not observe any fraud rejections for the user. \n\nI would suggest checking with the rides technical support team why the orders did not go through. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T09:02:01.105Z"],["3801718","INT-600","INT","dane.david@bolt.eu","Dane David","26W02: Development for MVP done. Live rollout & testing in for employees & in select cities to be done this week.","2026-01-12T09:02:02.782Z"],["3801719","L10N-27211","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27176](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27176)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T09:02:14.967Z"],["3801720","L10N-27212","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27176](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27176)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T09:02:15.015Z"],["3801721","PFI-819864","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:afe65d22-4d8b-4fc8-88bd-436ffb41adb9],\n\nThank you for keeping us in the loop, much appreciated.\nWe will be closing the ticket, if there are any further questions, please do let us know.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-12T09:02:46.660Z"],["3801722","LSS-61228","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ! Emilie is off today, but here are the informations you’re looking for : \n\n[Order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1494055239/18?orderTryId=2824714159] - [Rider|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/293952193] - [Beehive case|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/710550573]\nComment on the order from the rider to the driver : \n\n{quote}Une surfacturation dûe à un problème technique de l’application, reconnu par le support, Chauffeur avait accepté le tarif initial et a changé d’avis lorsque le montant a été mis à jour. conduite imprudente. Très mauvaise expérience.{quote}\n\nThe issue is due to the pricing tests in France : Fleet prices are set lower, but independent drivers has to be paid 1€ per km. \n\nHere, the rider was shown the price the order would be with a fleet driver (52.10€), but since the driver is an independant, the price was modified to respect this 1€ per km treshold (74.60€). Since the rider has a 15€ discount, he paid in cash 59.60€ instead of 37.10€.\n\nThe difference is 22.50€. Customer Support offered the rider a 15€ campaign enrollment, plus a 10€ promo code expiring November 14, 2027, making the total compensation 25€.\n\nThe rider is unhappy with this resolution and asks for a 100€ top-up on his Bolt Balance.\n\nLast message from rider \n\n{quote}Bonjour, Vous reconnaissez par écrit qu’un dysfonctionnement de votre plateforme a entraîné une surfacturation. Le paiement en espèces, mode proposé par Bolt, ne peut justifier ni la non-restitution du trop-perçu, ni l’imposition d’un crédit conditionné. Soit vous procédez à une solution commerciale acceptable, à savoir un crédit Bolt de 100 € sans limitation de durée, soit je poursuis immédiatement les démarches nécessaires (signalement DGCCRF, organismes consommateurs, diffusion factuelle du dossier), l’ensemble des éléments étant tracés et documentés, y compris votre reconnaissance écrite de l’erreur. Merci de me confirmer votre position dans la journée.{quote}\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything 😉 ","2026-01-12T09:02:53.352Z"],["3801725","PIF-2276","PIF","andrei.troskov@bolt.eu","Andrei Troškov","Extend the health check view with pod status information. This information has to be fetched from Kubernetes and persisted in the database. It should not affect the health check itself, but just extend the health check view.","2026-01-12T09:04:09.153Z"],["3801726","RDXENG-4358","RDXENG","sergei.emelianov@bolt.eu","Sergey Emeliyanov","No testing needed, infrastractural changes","2026-01-12T09:04:25.698Z"],["3801727","RDXENG-4570","RDXENG","dias.sadykov@bolt.eu","Dias Sadykov","Hey [~accountid:6358f09ab0b6ef03564955ba] I mistakenly put a wrong description in this ticket, updated the copy in correct one[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDXENG-4605|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDXENG-4605|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T09:05:03.215Z"],["3801728","LSS-61386","LSS","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","[^Bolt_NR acct CRA auth for signature.pdf] _(2.42 MB)_","2026-01-12T09:05:03.603Z"],["3801729","PFI-813004","PFI","reinis.levanovics@bolt.eu","Reinis Levanovičs","Hiii [~accountid:712020:fc661671-1d51-4372-9578-b46465bd51ac] is there any update regards this 🤗 ?","2026-01-12T09:05:05.358Z"],["3801731","RDXENG-4381","RDXENG","sergei.emelianov@bolt.eu","Sergey Emeliyanov","No testing needed, infrastructural changes","2026-01-12T09:05:10.056Z"],["3801732","LSS-61106","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:6f5035f8-0acf-4590-9698-5bd8e7d51601] this was previously addressed in the following ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-55574|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-55574|smart-link]. Please could you confirm whether you have reviewed the following memo on Branding for Taxis: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OMGv5Y6blN0Lp9yovBc-PRmGhi7TUnzndEK8BvCpu0w/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OMGv5Y6blN0Lp9yovBc-PRmGhi7TUnzndEK8BvCpu0w/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ?\n\nFollowing your review, can you confirm whether the mitigation recommendations have been taken into consideration in the initiative you wish to launch ?\n\nTo answer your questions: \n\n* Yes a tailored contract will need to be drafted for Taxis;\n* No need to add a paragraph in the T&Cs because this is a separate contract for advertising services.\n\nThank you !","2026-01-12T09:05:14.065Z"],["3801736","DPM-2289","DPM","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","[~accountid:712020:a5a9bde0-6d51-468a-85a6-ee3e42b31f73] Am I reading it right that [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPM-2321|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPM-2321|smart-link]  will be covered as part of this task?","2026-01-12T09:05:40.276Z"],["3801737","LSS-61387","LSS","aytan.huseynli@bolt.eu","Aytan Huseynli","[^_S-OFS-2025-549_signed by BH (1).pdf] _(909 kB)_","2026-01-12T09:05:42.289Z"],["3801738","LSS-57592","LSS","monika.civrag@bolt.eu","Monika Čivrag","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], we wish you a happy New Year as well!\n\n\nFrom what we know, the driver only has one device connected to his account since the first activation of his driver profile. We contacted [~accountid:712020:b2d15fe0-4ac2-48c5-9e25-34268c88fe65] for help, so I’m sending you her findings and explanation:\n\n''So this driver was operating under the fleet *DADO – ANDREJ TRANSPORTI j.d.o.o.*, and the transfer to the fleet *MARKOMAR TRANS j.d.o.o.* took place on *September 4th*, which is most likely the reason for the complaint, as the transfer occurred.\n\nI changed the email on *September 11th* because after the transfer, the [driver’s registration|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/driver-registration/driverRegistrations/edit/28250055?tab=details&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FZagreb] was submitted for the fleet *Dinzol Trade j.d.o.o.*, where the email [*legacyadria@gmail.com*|mailto:legacyadria@gmail.com] was listed. Our standard procedure is that if a new phone number and email are provided during registration, we update them on the driver’s most recent profile.''\n\nPlease let us know if there is anything else we can do.","2026-01-12T09:05:47.368Z"],["3801739","DPM-2289","DPM","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] Yes","2026-01-12T09:06:16.491Z"],["3801742","DSR-3079","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Data and response letter have been sent to the user\n\n[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] FYI Because the driver has always been a fleet driver I removed the billing details from all data and advised to contact fleet for that info. ","2026-01-12T09:07:41.384Z"],["3801745","PFI-827148","PFI","jan.dohnal@bolt-outsource.eu","Jan Dohnal","Hey team, any updates?","2026-01-12T09:08:38.104Z"],["3801746","LSS-61049","LSS","jan.uhlir@bolt.eu","Jan Uhlíř","Hey team, what’s the expected timeline for this to be done?","2026-01-12T09:08:52.724Z"],["3801751","LSS-61254","LSS","onyinye.osuagwu@bolt.eu","Onyinyechukwu Osuagwu","Hello [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] \nCould you please provide update on this? ","2026-01-12T09:10:23.861Z"],["3801755","AER-72","AER","kevin.sutanto@bolt.eu","Kevin Sutanto","This is completed \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Fi7yiuO4wzzxKSJilKppIw0L9DXSsiqOxKn8050wxkc/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.velq4s7i1zhc|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Fi7yiuO4wzzxKSJilKppIw0L9DXSsiqOxKn8050wxkc/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.velq4s7i1zhc|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T09:11:25.695Z"],["3801758","PFI-832308","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T09:11:34.254Z"],["3801760","LSS-60630","LSS","oluwatosin.ogunsanwo@bolt.eu","Oluwatosin Ogunsanwo","Hello [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] \nAny update on this, please?","2026-01-12T09:11:39.773Z"],["3801762","DAEN-930","DAEN","kevin.sutanto@bolt.eu","Kevin Sutanto","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Fi7yiuO4wzzxKSJilKppIw0L9DXSsiqOxKn8050wxkc/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.velq4s7i1zhc|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Fi7yiuO4wzzxKSJilKppIw0L9DXSsiqOxKn8050wxkc/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.velq4s7i1zhc|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T09:11:47.215Z"],["3801767","DAEN-931","DAEN","kevin.sutanto@bolt.eu","Kevin Sutanto","Cancelled as this will be done by new Analytics Engineer coming in to the team.","2026-01-12T09:12:51.219Z"],["3801770","FC-156","FC","tatjana.ainson@bolt.eu","Tatjana Ainson","Manual booking, cost reduction 250K","2026-01-12T09:13:07.719Z"],["3801771","CEBF-1818","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Task is completed. when updating from Opted-Out to Opted-In, then we create a new Account Scheduled Commission\n\n!2026-01-12_11-12-33.mp4|width=649,alt=\"2026-01-12_11-12-33.mp4\"!","2026-01-12T09:13:21.004Z"],["3801774","PFI-827069","PFI","sasha.maletskaya@bolt.eu","Aliaksandra Maletskaya","Hi\nAny updates?","2026-01-12T09:14:01.700Z"],["3801775","FC-922","FC","tatjana.ainson@bolt.eu","Tatjana Ainson","Data provided to Marleen","2026-01-12T09:14:13.790Z"],["3801778","PFI-831579","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:ddbe99ab-1bc1-41b8-80c2-8b83f5dd5fd3],\n\nThis is not a normal trip. It took 30 seconds to finish up this order which is not normal.\nAdditionally, this was a cash payment trip, therefore, the driver did not really lose anything theoretically.\nNo further action is currently required, this behaviour is automatically registered within our Fraud engine pattern recognition, meaning that similar cases may lead to further actions taken from our side.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-12T09:14:52.345Z"],["3801781","LSS-61308","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] ! Thanks for letting me know!","2026-01-12T09:15:22.866Z"],["3801784","LSS-56917","LSS","davis.baltvilks@bolt.eu","Dāvis Baltvilks","Hello [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] - can you please give any updates?","2026-01-12T09:15:42.948Z"],["3801787","LSS-61387","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T09:16:10.705Z"],["3801790","LSS-61288","LSS","stephanie.oreoluwa@bolt.eu","Stephanie Oreoluwa","[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] Good morning, please what’s the update on the contract?","2026-01-12T09:16:59.277Z"],["3801792","L10N-27215","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27213](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27213)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T09:17:14.017Z"],["3801793","L10N-27216","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27213](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27213)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T09:17:1