prioritizations","2026-01-12T09:18:26.806Z"],["3801823","TA-320","TA","razvan.lapuste@bolt.eu","Razvan Lapuste","+ [~accountid:712020:5f494197-2d0e-454f-918b-48f52a220ab9] ","2026-01-12T09:18:48.694Z"],["3801825","LSS-61365","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey [~accountid:712020:602d7a68-8a81-4bea-98bf-acb7026b1a56] - Please confirm the date is it supposed to be 01.02.25 or did you mean 01.02.26? Thank You in advance!","2026-01-12T09:19:01.325Z"],["3801833","TA-321","TA","razvan.lapuste@bolt.eu","Razvan Lapuste","+ [~accountid:712020:5f494197-2d0e-454f-918b-48f52a220ab9] + [~accountid:712020:a7f24c35-13af-47c1-b146-05c4a36324d4] ","2026-01-12T09:19:39.818Z"],["3801837","LSS-61365","LSS","robin.schneider@bolt.eu","Robin Schneider","Hey [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85], thanks for pointing it out! Needs to be 01.02.26. Do I need to send a new contract, or can you correct it?","2026-01-12T09:20:06.593Z"],["3801841","LSS-61348","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached!\n\n[^Master Services Agreement - CCTV_Bolt Operations OÜ_Driver Technologies, Inc._09.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T09:20:38.449Z"],["3801843","AER-73","AER","kevin.sutanto@bolt.eu","Kevin Sutanto","Still in-progress. Can be tracked further in CS AE Scorecard [*here*|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1NIIt7x0l_s1dA74AgeTI-SUN_XAEr2iRaZ0x-52IJdg/edit?gid=1314477167#gid=1314477167]","2026-01-12T09:20:48.437Z"],["3801844","LSS-61341","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Branding Contract - Bolt Club_Bolt Operations OÜ_Unlimited Drive GmbH_09.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T09:21:17.451Z"],["3801846","PFI-831832","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:c5150fbe-38eb-45f0-948e-37f0fe3048d5],\n\nThis is a behavioral issue and not Fraud. This should be dealt by the quality team (DriverX Standard team).\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-12T09:21:33.968Z"],["3801849","BD-1931","BD","agnes.kuus@bolt.eu","Agnes Kuus","I investigated the code and while I found no issues in the code, the issue must have been caused by a delay in data synchronization.\n\nThe invoice row is in the language that was sent with the request (en-us). The overall invoice is in the language that comes from the user’s chosen locale settings. \n\nI spoke to Antero Kevin Leedu to ask further questions about the issue. He confirmed that during the day he changed the locale several times (including bg) in his *webapp* settings - [https://food.bolt.eu/|https://food.bolt.eu/|smart-link]  \n\nThe locale change is done via POST request to {{/deliveryClient/updateDeliveryUserProfile}} and could be further investigated by {{eater-grox}} team.\n\nHowever, Antero also confirmed that he has since done another DineOut order to test it, specifically looked at the language of the invoice, and it was correctly in English. Thus, the language issue for him is resolved.\n\nI will close the ticket for us, since it seems closely related to Antero’s locale testing during the day and a delay in locale synchronization, not an issue with invoice generation itself. In addition, the language problem for him has resolved itself and he is receiving the invoices in correct language.","2026-01-12T09:21:41.996Z"],["3801853","TA-322","TA","razvan.lapuste@bolt.eu","Razvan Lapuste","+ [~accountid:712020:5f494197-2d0e-454f-918b-48f52a220ab9] + [~accountid:712020:c2c1dc15-1e04-485d-a84b-65d5410f5fda] ","2026-01-12T09:22:42.024Z"],["3801854","MLC-3758","MLC","jason.torion@bolt.eu","Jason Torion","[~accountid:712020:d6329bde-8ac9-46e0-8c20-8ca2102c07a3] is this epic needed? I believe [~accountid:5bc9c3edbc49ac2bb1553bd2] took care of this?  ","2026-01-12T09:22:50.279Z"],["3801857","LSS-61365","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! I can fix this from my side, no worries! Thanks for confirming","2026-01-12T09:23:12.050Z"],["3801858","CLIENTAPP-38771","CLIENTAPP","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","UI tests execution has been completed. Test cycle created: \"https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/CLIENTAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin%3Acom.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/testPlayer/CLIENTAPP-R2991\"","2026-01-12T09:23:14.935Z"],["3801859","LSS-60808","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] \n\nWe’re checking doc shared by Mapbox, we will come back with reply today ","2026-01-12T09:23:19.796Z"],["3801866","MTE-1309","MTE","maarja.maarjakoiv@bolt.eu","Maarja Maarjakõiv","[~accountid:712020:58a7e028-638f-408f-9e26-27a3421d3972] discussed with [~accountid:5d6e089134b3d20d9777ef90] and in this case it is fine if consent is GRANTED by default.","2026-01-12T09:24:35.395Z"],["3801868","PRIV-485","PRIV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GV0q5cVe0xJ1DufxPsheqs04SjoIKce4YzlmOXfMO6c/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GV0q5cVe0xJ1DufxPsheqs04SjoIKce4YzlmOXfMO6c/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]  Draft with feedback – reflected on Privacy Section ✅ \n\n*Tasks:*\n\n* -Discuss updates with Tatsiana-\n* Align with Alon on 6.2. (link to supplier requirements)\n* -Create Confluence Playbook-\n* Align with Edik on API agreeements","2026-01-12T09:24:39.537Z"],["3801869","LSS-61365","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340662|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340662|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T09:24:39.557Z"],["3801872","TA-326","TA","razvan.lapuste@bolt.eu","Razvan Lapuste","+ [~accountid:712020:c2c1dc15-1e04-485d-a84b-65d5410f5fda] + [~accountid:712020:5f494197-2d0e-454f-918b-48f52a220ab9] ","2026-01-12T09:25:06.207Z"],["3801873","LSS-60123","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","[~accountid:712020:8af2b159-71c0-448a-80ba-ff5059bb02f6] Thanks for the ticket. Please find below our comment on the guidelines. \n\n”*Legal Position on W4W Eligibility and Inclusivity*\nWomen-for-Women (W4W) is an optional safety-focused sub-category on the Bolt platform, designed to reduce documented gender-based safety risks and increase participation of women riders and drivers. W4W does not restrict access to Bolt’s services, as all users continue to have full access to standard ride categories at all times.\n\nEligibility for W4W is verified primarily on the basis of government-issued identification reflecting the user’s legally registered sex, combined with selfie verification. This verification standard is necessary to ensure user safety, prevent impersonation and misuse, and maintain a consistent, objective, and legally defensible process.\n\nBolt remains an inclusive platform. The existence of W4W does not create an exclusive service, but rather introduces a narrowly tailored safety option in response to well-documented risks. Any exceptions to standard verification requirements must be handled on a strictly case-by-case basis, subject to escalation and documentation, and must not undermine the core safety and integrity of the W4W category.”\n\nPlease let me know in case you have any further questions. Many thanks. \n\ncc: [~accountid:62722e092db308007024a425] [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] ","2026-01-12T09:25:08.251Z"],["3801877","DBRE-8689","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","[Alertmanager] HostTcpPacketLoss","2026-01-12T09:25:53.397Z"],["3801878","DBRE-8689","DBRE",null,"Slack","[Andres Kepler|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6215e9ed2d1a9d0069952697] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03055EHHPS/p1768209005512399|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03055EHHPS/p1768209005512399|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-12T09:25:54.299Z"],["3801879","FX-3601","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768209948988019]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3601] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T09:26:01.758Z"],["3801882","PFI-830473","PFI","laura.ernestova@bolt.eu","Laura Ernestová","Thank you so much! Have a great day!","2026-01-12T09:26:16.980Z"],["3801883","LSS-60870","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed PoA for LT attached.\n\n[^PoA_Bolt Services LT UAB_Leila Mäll_12.01.26.adoc]\n\n","2026-01-12T09:26:21.027Z"],["3801884","MARTECH3-1506","MARTECH3","anirudhan.anbuchezhian@bolt.eu","Ani rudhan","*Update 12.01.2026*\n\n* Had an initial call with Tomasz to understand the query requirements for building the ETL.\n* Aligned with Ifan on the logic used to create the ETL for drivers comms coverage.\n* Started the initial query and will complete and share it with Tomasz by the end of this week.\n\n\n*Next steps*\n\n* Waiting for confirmation from the ML team that maintains the ng_profiling_spark schema to understand the usage of this table.","2026-01-12T09:26:21.575Z"],["3801888","MLC-2458","MLC","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","+*Week 2*+\n\n* Shared the results and conclusions from our experiment with other teams [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09LW336KD0/p1767966979531899]. \n* *Experiment results:*\n** 🇬🇭 old template\n*** Sends: 79K\n*** OR: 11.24%\n** 🇬🇭 storytelling template\n*** Sends: 73K\n*** OR: 13.29% (🟢 18.32% vs. old template)\n** 🇱🇹 old template\n*** Sends: 80K\n*** OR: 18.14%\n** 🇱🇹 storytelling template\n*** Sends: 79K\n*** OR: 21.45% (🟢 18.24% vs. old template)\n** 🇺🇦 old template\n*** Sends: 147K\n*** OR: 17.85%\n** 🇺🇦 storytelling template\n*** Sends: 144K\n*** OR: 18.78% (🟢 5.23% vs. old template)\n* Based on the results, we can *scale the storytelling soft churn flow to the rest of the markets* and begin preparing other cohorts for storytelling as well. More detailed results here – [+Storytelling Flow, Experiment, Weekly Results+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1WKz87pyWvzBNijGz5CHU-tDE5kb5XMuZdcL0TnWwXjE/edit?gid=380694253#gid=380694253].\n* Had a sync with Dasha and Sergio to show them how the templates were made and which ones to use for Growth enrolment templates.\n* For next week, I’ll request the latest changes to the HTML template from Dovainis. And prepare and request Soft Churn template localisations for the rest of the markets. ","2026-01-12T09:26:58.442Z"],["3801889","MLC-3725","MLC","jason.torion@bolt.eu","Jason Torion","[~accountid:712020:778f9851-345e-4997-bb18-8183eae5cf90] I believe we can get started with the content, so let’s get that done. Along with creating new epics for Couriers please. Thanks. ","2026-01-12T09:27:05.734Z"],["3801890","FX-3592","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768210013676469]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3592 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T09:27:06.784Z"],["3801892","PFI-831878","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:2dd1d661-845e-473a-892f-367f7fb42e07],\n\nThis user is not fraudulent, and I can not see from our side that our Fraud rules would be stopping them in any way.\nWe would recommend perhaps reaching out to the Tech team as we do not have visibility on technical issues.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-12T09:27:13.024Z"],["3801894","LSS-61388","LSS","paolo.catani@bolt.eu","Paolo Catani","[^E03 - D1 Private Confirmation - Bolt_V1.pdf] _(484 kB)_","2026-01-12T09:27:23.102Z"],["3801895","HS-28820","HS","leonora.lukoviczki@bolt.eu","Leonóra Lukoviczki","Hello [~accountid:616d446d25f313007032c83c] \nThe off-boarding task is in your inbox now for approval. Please approve it asap. \n\nThank you! ","2026-01-12T09:27:27.718Z"],["3801899","PFI-832314","PFI","elijah.ojeamien@bolt-outsource.eu","Elijah Ojeamien","!image-20260112-092759.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T09:28:12.196Z"],["3801901","DRX-27706","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","Tested and verified on DA.127.0 (release variant) using OPPO Reno 13, Android 15\n\n* use deeplink when {{skip_confirmation=false}}for driver\n* use deeplink when {{skip_confirmation=true}}for driver\n* use deeplink when {{skip_confirmation=false}} for lead\n* use deeplink when {{skip_confirmation=true}} for lead\n\n\n\n!mobizen_20260112_110759.mp4|width=423,alt=\"mobizen_20260112_110759.mp4\"!\n\n!mobizen_20260112_112022.mp4|width=431,alt=\"mobizen_20260112_112022.mp4\"!","2026-01-12T09:28:28.904Z"],["3801904","DRX-27705","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27706 has been resolved","2026-01-12T09:28:37.722Z"],["3801905","CCM-22267","CCM","toyosi.olusesi@bolt-outsource.eu","Toyosi Olusesi","[^New Training Request form _ Teleperformance.xlsx]","2026-01-12T09:28:43.231Z"],["3801906","LSS-60824","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:61cc1c959ee70a00680edd89] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^BOLT Operations NDA (Mutual) (Arnon-12.24.2025) - rev Bolt (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T09:28:54.900Z"],["3801907","CLIENTAPP-38771","CLIENTAPP","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","UI tests execution has been completed. Test cycle created: \"https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/CLIENTAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin%3Acom.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/testPlayer/CLIENTAPP-R2994\"","2026-01-12T09:28:59.833Z"],["3801908","LSS-59767","LSS","oluwatosin.ogunsanwo@bolt.eu","Oluwatosin Ogunsanwo","Hello [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] \nHappy New Year, and thanks for the response.\n\nRegarding *Section 1 (scope clarification)*, the data Bolt will be required to share aligns with the standard data we provide to all Bolt Business clients. That said, they’ve also requested that we complete an assessment form, which requires additional information from our side. Please take a look at [this sheet|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1w7CDmbtYbCSjK5f1schDBDApPXXREBw-ieanzUBQXAU/edit?usp=sharing] for the full list of requested details and advise on the next steps.\n\nFor *Section 18 (notification carve-out)*, I’ll share your feedback with them.\n\nMany thanks!","2026-01-12T09:29:05.922Z"],["3801909","WAVE-200","WAVE","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","Scope - Homepage","2026-01-12T09:29:14.887Z"],["3801910","RCE-344","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768210142443039]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@mykola.mozghovyi>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-344] `New safety block rendering for admin panel` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T09:29:23.168Z"],["3801911","SUPX-2315","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","You didn't parent this bug anywhere [@christian.kalme|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ae966399abb77267ba68b16]","2026-01-12T09:29:43.937Z"],["3801913","AER-75","AER","kevin.sutanto@bolt.eu","Kevin Sutanto","This is done for metrics that are used by verticals\n\n* ✅ [+Eater+|https://github.com/bolteu/data-experimentation/commit/8d8ee9084552d89dc8ca5aeff61292acfea06810]\n* ✅ [+Rider+|https://github.com/bolteu/data-experimentation/pull/1100]","2026-01-12T09:29:47.654Z"],["3801923","SUPX-2315","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme",":ok_hand::skin-tone-2: :done-emoji-green:","2026-01-12T09:30:34.331Z"],["3801924","PAW-14776","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-alex-somai\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160347\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 09:30:37 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T09:30:37.359Z"],["3801928","PAW-14717","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was closed\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/n8n-nodes-bolt/pull/68\nStatus: closed\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 09:31:04 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T09:31:04.782Z"],["3801930","PFI-808950","PFI","alexandra.pakkonen@bolt.eu","Alexandra Pakkonen","Heya [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e], can you update?","2026-01-12T09:31:17.757Z"],["3801931","DISC-3725","DISC","oleh.zasadnyy@bolt.eu","Oleh Zasadnyy","Web: [https://da7c477d.eater-app-prelive.pages.dev/|https://da7c477d.eater-app-prelive.pages.dev/]\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-12 at 11.30.38@2x.png|width=635,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-12 at 11.30.38@2x.png\"!","2026-01-12T09:31:18.665Z"],["3801933","PAW-14683","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @alexnix\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17058\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 09:31:21 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T09:31:21.864Z"],["3801937","L10N-27231","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:05.564Z"],["3801938","L10N-27239","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:05.662Z"],["3801939","L10N-27235","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:05.670Z"],["3801940","L10N-27230","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:05.717Z"],["3801941","L10N-27233","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:05.770Z"],["3801942","L10N-27236","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:05.771Z"],["3801943","L10N-27248","