9:32:11.139Z"],["3801961","L10N-27220","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.266Z"],["3801962","L10N-27226","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.301Z"],["3801963","L10N-27227","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.312Z"],["3801964","L10N-27215","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.348Z"],["3801965","L10N-27221","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.367Z"],["3801966","L10N-27219","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.406Z"],["3801967","L10N-27224","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.450Z"],["3801968","L10N-27223","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.511Z"],["3801969","L10N-27225","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.493Z"],["3801970","L10N-27214","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.605Z"],["3801971","L10N-27216","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.603Z"],["3801972","L10N-27228","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:11.737Z"],["3801973","L10N-27249","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:32:18.519Z"],["3801981","CLOUDSEC-701","CLOUDSEC","farshid.sajadi@bolt.eu","Farshid Sajadi","7 detection rules were created for the Pigment.","2026-01-12T09:33:39.846Z"],["3801987","DRX-27801","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.127.0 Release (debug) build on Samsung A12, OS:13\n\n||*Portrait*||*Landscape*||\n|!Screenshot_20260112_112611_Bolt Driver.jpg|width=317,alt=\"Screenshot_20260112_112611_Bolt Driver.jpg\"!|!Screenshot_20260112_112622_Bolt Driver.jpg|width=317,alt=\"Screenshot_20260112_112622_Bolt Driver.jpg\"!|\n|!Screenshot_20260112_112319_Bolt Driver.jpg|width=317,alt=\"Screenshot_20260112_112319_Bolt Driver.jpg\"!|!Screenshot_20260112_112333_Bolt Driver.jpg|width=317,alt=\"Screenshot_20260112_112333_Bolt Driver.jpg\"!|\n|!Screenshot_20260112_112443_Bolt Driver.jpg|width=317,alt=\"Screenshot_20260112_112443_Bolt Driver.jpg\"!|!Screenshot_20260112_112455_Bolt Driver.jpg|width=317,alt=\"Screenshot_20260112_112455_Bolt Driver.jpg\"!|","2026-01-12T09:35:09.913Z"],["3801989","LSS-58081","LSS","felix.antwi@bolt.eu","Felix Antwi","Hello [~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c] \nSorry for the delay. Yes, kindly proceed with this approach. ","2026-01-12T09:35:37.064Z"],["3801995","LSS-61106","LSS","simon.fournier@bolt.eu","Simon Fournier","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742], \n\nThanks a lot for sharing this memo. First time I’m seeing it but even better. All align with the recommandations (excepted the amount, We will probably offer a slightly higher amount, at 200€). \n[~accountid:61b9ef0e9e8a370068af893c] [~accountid:712020:2bcade9f-e145-453c-a43f-d0cf00dd962b] [~accountid:712020:cb6fc720-3c42-4171-99dd-eaefef0e51eb] FYI","2026-01-12T09:36:03.658Z"],["3801996","LSS-61389","LSS","annika.helimets@bolt.eu","Annika Helimets","[^Bolt teenusleping taksofirmaga HC Dynamo Tallinn OÜ.asice.asice]\n\n","2026-01-12T09:36:17.351Z"],["3802001","PFI-832320","PFI","victoria.ebube@bolt-outsource.eu","Victoria Ebube","!{680E7E32-5B1E-448C-AA8F-ECAC5B7C6046}-20260112-093632.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T09:37:14.067Z"],["3802004","LSS-60557","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hi, [~accountid:712020:5edd7b8a-e535-468c-85fd-63f0b6de01b2] ! I put minor changes to the agreements. As this is not our template, please send back the files to ERPOL to accept the final versions before we proceed with signing. *A wet ink of* [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] is required for each annex. \n\nBest 😉 \n\nJola\n\n[^Aneks do umowy Bolt Food Grzybowska 3.docx]\n[^Aneks do umowy Bolt Food Grójecka.docx]\n[^Aneks do umowy Bolt Food Dolna.docx]\n[^Aneks do umowy Bolt Food Banderii.docx]\n[^Aneks do umowy Bolt Food Al KEN (1).docx]\n\n","2026-01-12T09:37:49.356Z"],["3802005","PFI-831929","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:1e970c0a-4dd7-44a2-ad38-6aa790d1a79b],\n\nWe have made some changes from our side which will now allow the user to access the aforementioned discount.\nPlease note that it may take up to 2-3hours before the changes go live from our side, only after that should the user try again.\nIf the user is not capable of adding a promo code afterwards, then after confirming that it shows an error, please provide them with a new promo code as it is possible that the code got deleted due to the rule we had.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-12T09:38:03.941Z"],["3802008","PIF-3276","PIF",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the User Story!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-12T09:38:10.362Z"],["3802013","MLC-3860","MLC","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","+*Week 2*+\n\n* MarTech launched their fix to their Journey Manager event, so that when cloning, each setup would have a unique ID. [Thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C077UMEENTE/p1767604657943989?thread_ts=1765527457.967539&cid=C077UMEENTE]\n* I tested the Cart Abandoned enrolments again in Journey Manager, and we got them to work correctly. We just had to change the property {{journey_config_id}} type from numeric to string. on the Braze side.\n* Migrated all the Restaurants and Bolt Market Cart Abandoned setups from Braze enrolments to Journey Manager ones. \n* Next week, the focus is on testing the newly launched features in the Journey Manager. [Listed here.|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Wdz3GjvU0OF98dAeZtdk-hXsNxSwZM2F2XpglCJccdw/edit?gid=0#gid=0]","2026-01-12T09:39:21.496Z"],["3802014","LSS-61316","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] [~accountid:5cefa7d5c32afb0f1eb85f25] I added Bolt trademarks and also added reference to Bolt brand guidelines [https://www.lingoapp.com/93471/k/Bolt-Brand-Guidelines-o4j44D|https://www.lingoapp.com/93471/k/Bolt-Brand-Guidelines-o4j44D|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T09:39:24.769Z"],["3802015","RCE-344","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768210772987859]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-344 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T09:39:45.841Z"],["3802016","DBRE-8689","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","Some heavy disk access. I assume {{it ng-monitor}} is doing ts {{docsdb}} flattening.\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7YEV6V43/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7YEV6V43/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-12T09:40:23.157Z"],["3802019","DBRE-8689","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A82R5TS6A/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A82R5TS6A/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-12T09:40:49.468Z"],["3802020","PFI-830875","PFI","patryk.flakowski@bolt.eu","Patryk Flakowski","The client disputes this. She confirms she completed rides in December totaling several hundred PLN using the app. She has provided a business report received from us on Jan 3rd which confirms these trips. Please see the attached report and re-investigate why the invoice was not generated.\n\n","2026-01-12T09:40:58.375Z"],["3802021","PFI-830875","PFI","patryk.flakowski@bolt.eu","Patryk Flakowski","!image-20260112-094101.png|width=1858,height=419,alt=\"image-20260112-094101.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-12T09:41:07.537Z"],["3802022","SUPX-2186","SUPX","radoslaw.wielonski@bolt.eu","Radosław Wieloński","blocked, waiting for response from automation team: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768207409833949|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768207409833949|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T09:41:22.446Z"],["3802026","PAW-17582","PAW","andrei.troskov@bolt.eu","Andrei Troškov","Lets create a common rule that will trigger an alert if the pod is in a “not ready” state for too long (lets say more than 15 minutes). PodNotReady could be a valid state, for example, when the rolling deployment is happening, the new pods are not immediately available. But if the pod is in a “not ready” state for too long, this is a clear signal that something is not right.\n\nSRE have the following alert on their side:\n\n{noformat}        - alert: KubePodNotReady\n          annotations:\n            description: Pod {{ $labels.namespace }} / {{ $labels.pod }} has been in a non-ready state for longer than 9 minutes.\n            summary: Pod has been in a non-ready state for more than 14 minutes.\n          expr: |-\n            sum by (namespace, pod) (\n              max by(namespace, pod) (\n                kube_pod_status_phase{job=\"kube-state-metrics\", phase=~\"Pending|Unknown|Failed\"}\n              ) * on(namespace, pod) group_left(owner_kind) topk by(namespace, pod) (\n                1, max by(namespace, pod, owner_kind) (kube_pod_owner)\n              )\n            ) > 0\n          # Do not decrease `for` since it'd trigger unactionable alerts for Pods on fresh nodes\n          for: 14m\n          labels:\n            severity: warning{noformat}\n\nOur alreting does not support {{for}} loops, but the expression still might be helpful. Please review it and decide if we can reuse it or not.","2026-01-12T09:41:54.027Z"],["3802027","TAXP-1148","TAXP","tyler.ison@bolt.eu","Tyler Hamilton Ison","[~accountid:61b9ad7c2900b00071da0b68] - this appears to be a transmittal letter for the *seller reporting obligation*, which is where we send a copy of the information we report to the NZ tax authority, and is separate from due diligence verification comms. Both the tax authority and seller 2025 reporting is due by 7 Feb 2026. Due diligence verification is due by 31 December 2025\n\nThe letter looks ok, with a few considerations: \n\n* Asking the sellers to verify the 2025 data may create some confusion as the 2025 due diligence period ended 31 December. We wouldn’t be able to easily change the data without and amendment. Do we have a separate due diligence comms that asks sellers to verify their non-income information by 31 December? This may help identify whether there was a change in business.\n* As a result, I would normally suggest we have a date by which sellers must contact our support team with any discrepancies, but as this is not a due diligence comm, it is not relevant. We fulfill our seller reporting obligation  be sending a copy of the report we send to NZ tax authority to the seller with nothing more. For this reason, I suggest deleting the next steps paragraph of this comms (added as tracked change in the file)","2026-01-12T09:41:55.888Z"],["3802029","LSS-61390","LSS","lisette.suik@bolt.eu","Lisette Suik","Under the DSA, a phone number is required. [Article 30|https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex%3A32022R2065](1)(a) obliges us to *collect* the trader’s phone number, and Article 30(7) requires us to *make that information available on the Bolt Food interface where the service is presented*. So strictly speaking, the phone number should be visible to consumers.On Wolt: my read is that they’ve taken a risk-based approach. Technically, this setup is not compliant with the DSA, but it’s unlikely to be picked up by regulators. Notably, they seem to have made this exception only for this one provider, all other providers in LT still have phone numbers displayed.Can we do the same? Potentially yes, if this provider is  important and we’re comfortable with the risk. If we go down this route:\n\n* we should be transparent with the restaurant that, if a regulator raises this, we may need to re-insert the phone number quickly;\n* we should still collect and store the phone number in our systems; and\n* CS should be able to share the number with consumers upon request.\n\nAny enforcement risk by regulators is low. If there is any trouble, it’s likely we would be asked to re-display the number and we can quickly do it.","2026-01-12T09:42:02.171Z"],["3802031","PFI-817793","PFI","ivana.hrupacki@bolt.eu","Ivana De Marchi Hrupacki","Hi, is there any new info in these cases? Thank you!\n\nIvana","2026-01-12T09:42:17.865Z"],["3802032","PFI-832322","PFI","mykyta.rozhok@bolt.eu","Mykyta Rozhok","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.38.13.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T09:42:30.746Z"],["3802033","PFI-832040","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:f0483e6f-9431-49e7-a277-4b663093c39c],\n\nFrom what we can see from our side, is that we are not restricting the user from using cash payment option.\nHowever, if this option is currently not available for them, then in the meanwhile recommend them to use another payment option until the cash option becomes available again.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-12T09:42:32.314Z"],["3802034","LSS-55517","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","[~accountid:712020:240e5e60-baab-4e72-a388-591f4f4ec6a2] \n\nHello and happy new year. \n\n*Clause 11.1:* I have added additional limitation and caps to this clause, further reducing Bolt’s scope of risk and liability.\n\n*Clause 11.8 & 11.9:* Follow up comments added for RC’s feedback. \n\n{color:#0747a6}*Clauses 3.5 & 5.1:*{color}{color:#0747a6} Awaiting feedback {color}\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1w8rHGoY7FvKtnBV3T8pZShGWn2NUhono/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1w8rHGoY7FvKtnBV3T8pZShGWn2NUhono/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T09:42:32.909Z"],["3802040","RDS-1286","RDS","abhishek.rawat@bolt.eu","Abhishek Rawat","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] With Project green in UK, the supply is split. Riders see Flex (Agency model) and Standard (Principal model) as two separate categories leading to different price points and ETAs etc. A driver then chooses the profile, and is only matched based on the Bolt Standard or Flex orders. From what I understand, drivers like to use flex at certain periods of the day as a personal choice.\n\nRegarding numbers.\n\n* Number of switch requests per week are around 22-25k.\n* Overall Per driver average is around ~6 times per day.\n* For frequent switchers, referring to last 24 hrs, highest switching was 47 times. And top 10 was from 47-20 times.","2026-01-12T09:43:41.401Z"],["3802041","SUPX-2288","SUPX","iryna.mitsko@bolt.eu","Iryna Mitsko","Hi [@michal.bielecki|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/62e0e5a85b8cc57412052cb6] [@krzysztof.szlachetka|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:eba3c46d-5b67-4363-896f-8bc6e1642c6f] [@adam.kudybinski|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ff4436491bb2e0108d1548d], could you share more details on the long-term solution for the issue?\n\nThis year we expect to grow API by 5x vs. Dec 2025. In December 2025, we received ~1.4 support cases from API partners globally (not accounting for those dropped as spam). With anticipated growth, we want to provide partners with consistent support experience. Inability to reach out CS or dropping their inquires as spam is simply bad experience which negatively affects partnerships.","2026-01-12T09:43:42.662Z"],["3802043","LEG-1264","LEG","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","The following concerns HQ support team alignment on circumstances where Bolt is being charged money by airports and intends to collect fees from riders on a per ride basis to offset this cost.\n\n* *Financial regulatory support:* Fin. reg. requested alternative wording that avoids “passengers requesting services” on the basis that this could suggest that Bolt is acting for riders, not drivers. [+Michael Roberts+|mailto:michael.roberts@bolt.eu] observed that passengers will always request rides regardless of whoever Bolt is acting for, but nevertheless provided alternative drafting for review that avoided the conflict of concerns, for the sake of agreeing drafting.\n* *Tax support:* Tax and [+Michael Roberts+|mailto:michael.roberts@bolt.eu] discussed the intended use case for “Platform Fees” and aligned that the intention is for this phrase to merely indicate that a fee is being charged by Bolt. Tax subsequently raised that the ‘platform fees’ labeling might increase audit risk, as Bolt would intend is to help avoid booking these fees as revenue if we are passing them through to the airport. [+Michael Roberts+|mailto:michael.roberts@bolt.eu] recommended that Tax review the entirety of the existing drafting to determine whether this was an issue. This is being reviewed by Tax.","2026-01-12T09:43:49.335Z"],["3802045","DBRE-8689","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","ng-monitor is doing heavy IO on disk without limits. This causing interruptions. \n\n\n\n\n\n!image-20260112-094345.png|width=516,alt=\"image-20260112-094345.png\"!\n\n!image-20260112-094250.png|width=516,alt=\"image-20260112-094250.png\"!\n\n\n[+https://monitor.boltint.net/d/100000001/tidb-cluster-node_exporter?orgId=1&var-dataSou[…]0&var-buddyinfozone=All&from=1768205474288&to=1768210687328+|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/100000001/tidb-cluster-node_exporter?orgId=1&var-dataSource=P6237D77CFC036D82&var-interval=1m&var-host=ti-delivery-monitor.sqldb:9100&var-buddyinfozone=All&from=1768205474288&to=1768210687328]","2026-01-12T09:44:01.016Z"],["3802046","RCE-344","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alisher Matkurbanov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768211043927049]*{color}:\nHi <@U027N9G59KP>\nLeft 1 comment, please take a look\n{quote}","2026-01-12T09:44:16.326Z"],["3802049","LSS-57226","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Update: \n\nWe have shared the draft with our feedback with the bank today. Waiting to hear back from them. ","2026-01-12T09:44:46.352Z"],["3802052","WD-22535","WD","carla.panaite@bolt.eu","Carla Panaite","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.42.40.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.43.18.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.43.47.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T09:44:57.620Z"],["3802053","CCM-22268","CCM","ademola.oloja@bolt-outsource.eu","Ademola Oloja","[^New Training Request form.xlsx]","2026-01-12T09:45:10.517Z"],["3802056","LSS-61316","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Thank you [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a]!\n\n[~accountid:5cefa7d5c32afb0f1eb85f25] please check the draft and comments so we can finalize it.","2026-01-12T09:45:26.486Z"],["3802058","WFM-9940","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Access granted [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541673|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541673]","2026-01-12T09:45:40.229Z"],["3802061","DSR-3057","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","DM sent to Maaike Boogaers","2026-01-12T09:46:10.773Z"],["3802062","DSR-3653","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","*More info from Tier 2:*\n\nHey team! This guarantee is for independant drivers in France :\n* Each hour should be paid 30€ at least (compensated by the end of the month based on the average revenue and hour worked -calculations are seen on this [sheet|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1eLvn1eJ8EIKQXSTbMthRv4xWaKufBSoQrqAbaB4UySI/edit?gid=560827052#gid=560827052], but it is not updated since november)\n* Each kilometer should be paid 1€, this is calculated directly on the order\n* Each order should be minimum 9€\nThis is based on this [agreement|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Accord-revenu-minimal-horaire-et-euro-kilometrique-19-Decembre-2023.pdf].\nDriver is now under a fleet, but was independant until the 06/01/2026 under id [5760201|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/5760201?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn].\nSearching this ID in the above sheet shows a result of 0€ compensation in november for example, as RPH was 32.78€ (so above 30€ per hour). Same goes for October, and in September for example RPH was 27.99€, so we compensated 29.4€ as shown in the last column. It's been paid [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records/26874495472] on the 31/10.\nWe do not have the data for December, this whole process is managed by Local Ops.\nDo you have an efficient way to compile the data the driver is asking for?\n* time spent during orders\n* time spent driving to pick up points\nFrom January to December 2025, separated by month.\nIf not, please send back and I'll try to prepare the data I can see from the sheet and send back for approval. Thanks!\n\nCurrently I asked Tier 2 and Local OPS to handle this to see if the driver actually was paid less or not.\n\nI also asked to inform CSPC about the outcome so we could see if there is any extra support needed.","2026-01-12T09:46:12.774Z"],["3802064","DBRE-8689","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","solution what worked last time with ti-iot cluster was just flush docdb folder. I assume it has a corrupted files in like it was with ti-iot cluster\n\n{noformat}rm -rf /tidb-data/prometheus-9090/docdb{noformat}","2026-01-12T09:46:43.180Z"],["3802067","L10N-27244","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:07.392Z"],["3802068","L10N-27247","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:07.449Z"],["3802069","L10N-27245","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:07.451Z"],["38