dated.","2026-01-12T09:47:08.312Z"],["3802088","L10N-27231","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:12.470Z"],["3802089","L10N-27224","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:12.639Z"],["3802090","L10N-27229","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:12.821Z"],["3802091","L10N-27223","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:12.896Z"],["3802092","L10N-27228","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:12.939Z"],["3802093","L10N-27222","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:12.964Z"],["3802094","L10N-27220","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:12.979Z"],["3802095","L10N-27221","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:13.003Z"],["3802096","L10N-27217","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:13.009Z"],["3802097","L10N-27214","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:13.011Z"],["3802098","L10N-27227","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:13.011Z"],["3802099","L10N-27218","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:13.016Z"],["3802100","L10N-27225","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:13.170Z"],["3802101","L10N-27219","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:13.203Z"],["3802102","L10N-27215","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:13.339Z"],["3802103","L10N-27216","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T09:47:13.304Z"],["3802104","LSS-60929","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] has Vincent signed? Thank you! ","2026-01-12T09:47:30.882Z"],["3802109","RCE-345","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768211274636869]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@divyansh.kumar>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-345] `Investigate haldas integration issue with drivers` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T09:48:09.456Z"],["3802110","BB-2274","BB","yeshwant.kumar@bolt.eu","Yeshwant Kumar","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7343833400/2026-01+RFC+Simplified+credit+row+matching|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7343833400/2026-01+RFC+Simplified+credit+row+matching|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T09:48:10.921Z"],["3802115","PFI-823453","PFI","ivana.hrupacki@bolt.eu","Ivana De Marchi Hrupacki","Hi, is there any new info here? Thank you!\n\nIvana","2026-01-12T09:48:40.668Z"],["3802116","MTE-1309","MTE","sergei.drondin@bolt.eu","Sergei Drondin","[~accountid:6321aad6cf721d09b0166767] I set driver registration consents to GRANTED unless explicitly denied (currently there is no way to explicitly deny them, but let’s keep the check there just in case).","2026-01-12T09:48:47.735Z"],["3802117","LSS-61049","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:628dd71cf2ee4a0069dfba72] I will come back to you today, sorry for the delay! ","2026-01-12T09:49:05.740Z"],["3802119","WD-22535","WD","carla.panaite@bolt.eu","Carla Panaite","*Sorry, I meant 2 weeks ago, not months* 😅 ","2026-01-12T09:49:35.391Z"],["3802122","SUPX-2288","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","[@michal.rapinczuk|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:05337a38-da5a-4860-91ed-01ab7b7b6cca] [@pranav.dineshkumar|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:33002f0b-c802-4f83-911e-b96c405eae99] FYI ^^ Adjusting this logic should be discussed as a change request (as it won't be a simple team duty task), we need to agree on the ownership between us and Beehive and put it on the roadmap","2026-01-12T09:49:47.182Z"],["3802125","PA-575","PA","maryna.zhuravlova@bolt.eu","Maryna Zhuravlova","\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jHKfBLbnX90c46fTQT1aPU8eJ4HrHgevEZnBj5evUdA/edit?gid=1916669476#gid=1916669476|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jHKfBLbnX90c46fTQT1aPU8eJ4HrHgevEZnBj5evUdA/edit?gid=1916669476#gid=1916669476|smart-card]","2026-01-12T09:50:12.754Z"],["3802126","PFI-832336","PFI","viktorija.suseja@bolt-outsource.eu","Viktorija Suseja","!customer_screenshot.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T09:50:14.281Z"],["3802128","PAW-14777","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-12T09:50:39.650Z"],["3802132","PA-574","PA","maryna.zhuravlova@bolt.eu","Maryna Zhuravlova","\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1KTWl6ZCwFNvjqZggzLHDs_tWsVwDIrcCESIBcjC5QYE/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1KTWl6ZCwFNvjqZggzLHDs_tWsVwDIrcCESIBcjC5QYE/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-card]\n\n ","2026-01-12T09:50:50.218Z"],["3802133","DSR-3655","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T09:51:06.928Z"],["3802135","DBRE-8589","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 09.50.09.png|width=1018,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 09.50.09.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 09.50.34.png|width=1044,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 09.50.34.png\"!\n\nThe switch is complete. \nThe previous master, {{afr-db-1}}, is ready for decommission.","2026-01-12T09:51:31.193Z"],["3802143","DBRE-8589","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 09.52.11.png|width=1044,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 09.52.11.png\"!","2026-01-12T09:52:39.577Z"],["3802144","PFI-832337","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T09:52:45.143Z"],["3802145","C2-455","C2","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","Higo has checked their inventory and found also connectors where the gap of the opposite side female pin was larger than the other side.\n\nThey have checked also the individual pins and all the pins they checked were in tolerance range. So the difference between of the sides is caused probably by the plastic casing that surrounds the pins - if the slot for the pin is slightly smaller then it will press the female pin together and the gap will be smaller. But all the measured values are in the tolerance today.\n\n\n\nThe answerer to the question is it possible to make the pin tolerance smaller was that they prefer to change it to: 1 + 0.1/-0.2 mm \n\n\n\nI have asked Higo to update the drawings based on that new tolerance","2026-01-12T09:52:49.213Z"],["3802146","PA-574","PA","maryna.zhuravlova@bolt.eu","Maryna Zhuravlova","Rates uploaded: 12.01.2026. Changes: [Rides|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XhJrgAWglrLEVIiK65XWMuzPq50M3nsSxduw3yzaE6I/edit?tab=t.0] and [Delivery|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QcaUnIaJipY02SD41qNCAJ2iWz54XirrEYkHEx_0DTA/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-12T09:52:50.917Z"],["3802150","LSS-58941","LSS","sudipto.das@bolt.eu","Sudipto Das","Hey, [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] please can you set up a call if the below does not address your questions.\n\nDriver side generic details, Gender is a mandatory or required field based on the details. And the document for gender is dependent on the local regulation, eg in DE the gender field is in DL, while in EE its not. So its market specific consideration we have to take. [https://prelive.bolt.eu/en-ee/driver/|https://prelive.bolt.eu/en-ee/driver/|smart-link] Please review the UX here for EE to get a reference. Technical side, we use the same core services, but as mentioned the process can differ.\n\n\n\nRider side, yup thats the same view AFAIK. Rider verification is a safety feature to ensure the account is safe. Sure there is a Privacy notice, but for verification I would argue I would need something more generic, or else link management per market per feature becomes a huge maintenance overhead. Alternative is for them to use any other category which is not W4W, they can do it without verification.","2026-01-12T09:53:14.127Z"],["3802155","PFI-832262","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:f7a5b04d-b48e-4f8c-a4a0-34159bbb7f81],\n\nSeems like the user still has a *Scheduled block and Hard block* on their profile, meaning that this has not been submitted to the Safety Team for review or that the process is incomplete.\n\nFraud Team does not remove *Hard-Blocks* nor *Scheduled blocks* from the profiles, we only help in removing the *device UID blocks* once the investigation has been finalized and the rest of the blocks have been removed.\n\nPlease let us know once the profile has been finalized.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you,\nMarten","2026-01-12T09:53:55.644Z"],["3802157","LSS-61231","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:262f6569-8615-451c-9647-ce9929ef2eb6] please find attached the NDA reviewed with my comments.\n\nMost changes have been reviewed but I have pushed back on two elements: \n\n* *Article 2 - Confidential Information Exclusions:* The partner should clarify why they would like personal data to be excluded from the defined Confidential Information.\n* *Article 8 - Return of Confidential Information:* We cannot accept that Confidential Information is retained under a blanket cover that copies have been retained on backup systems or electronic caches. \n\nPlease send the attached document for them to review. \n\nThank you !\n\n[^Bolt NDA (Non-disclosure agreement)_Bolt review 12.01.2026 (3).docx]\n\n","2026-01-12T09:54:07.544Z"],["3802159","PFI-832336","PFI","viktorija.suseja@bolt-outsource.eu","Viktorija Suseja","I am sorry, signed up in January ","2026-01-12T09:54:17.417Z"],["3802163","WFM-9940","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","WFM team, please review and grant them access to the Business queues they request. Thank you!","2026-01-12T09:54:25.971Z"],["3802164","LSS-60758","LSS","polina.racheeva@bolt.eu","Polina Racheeva","Hi, any updates?","2026-01-12T09:54:41.276Z"],["3802165","EBIKE1-87","EBIKE1","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","{{2026-01-09}} our 3D model was sent to supplier to check are the changes ok for them that I did or not","2026-01-12T09:54:53.701Z"],["3802166","LSS-57974","LSS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","No responses, closing the case 📕","2026-01-12T09:54:56.301Z"],["3802167","LSS-61394","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nGrigoria Papageorgiou has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-12T09:54:58.225Z"],["3802169","LSS-60929","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] ! \n\nNo – Vincent is currently having issues accessing Dokobit, so we’re working on resolving this.","2026-01-12T09:55:03.106Z"],["3802170","PFI-828214","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have double-checked the refund status with dLocal and everything seems correct on our side. Here is the information that’s available for us. Please do not share it with the customer. \n\n\n!image-20260112-095140.png|width=674,height=615!\n\nFor other banks like CAPTIC BANK the refunds are listed under pending payments in a different section. \n\nThe bank statement the user submitted is partial from multiple different screenshots. It might be missing a section for pending payments. \n\n\nAccording to the user bank statement the refund indeed does not appear on 16th of December. We would suggest the user to reach out to their bank to confirm if there have been any refunds issued. \nAlternatively the user could submit a full PDF file. Will be able to investigate further once the full statement is received. \n\nCheers, \nMarten\n\n\n\n","2026-01-12T09:55:03.416Z"],["3802173","MARTECH3-1499","MARTECH3","anirudhan.anbuchezhian@bolt.eu","Ani rudhan","*Update 12.01.2026*\n\n* Had the initial call with Anette to understand the support she needs from my side.\n* She is launching an experiment in 3–4 countries with a duration of up to two weeks. The experiment is expected to launch soon.\n* She needs support with the post-analysis, which will be provided in February once the experiment is complete.\n* Currently, the plan is to use the Braze query builder to extract the experiment data.\n** The issue is that the query builder only allows exporting up to 1,000 rows, which requires multiple execution of the query. \n\n*Next steps*\n\n* looking to see where the data is stored in the backend to see if i use specific tables to get the data for post analysis.","2026-01-12T09:55:43.312Z"],["3802175","LSS-61100","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] – is this order form related to this ticket? [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-60608?search_id=0861da0f-2a1f-47df-9a7a-b1f5dabea157|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-60608?search_id=0861da0f-2a1f-47df-9a7a-b1f5dabea157|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T09:56:06.793Z"],["3802177","PFI-832177","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:a18946fe-4496-40ee-a768-c12b53889274],\n\nIt looks like the user was too late with confirming their e-mail address.\nWe would recommend that the user logs into their application via another method (SMS for example).\nOnce they have logged in, they can once again enter their e-mail address and then validate it via their own email.\nOtherwise their account nor email address are not restricted.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-12T09:56:18.740Z"],["3802180","LSS-61049","LSS","jan.uhlir@bolt.eu","Jan Uhlíř","Thank you!\n\n","2026-01-12T09:56:39.924Z"],["3802181","LSS-52572","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] 🙌 💚 ","2026-01-12T09:56:44.707Z"],["3802184","FDBT-4781","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-12T09:57:15.653Z"],["3802186","LSS-61352","LSS","corneliu.radu@bolt.eu","Corneliu-Ștefan Radu","Hey [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2]! Happy new year! Thank you for your assistance and help, indeed, I was in a hurry.Regarding the correction, payment will be made in a single installment. I will modify it immediately!","2026-01-12T09:57:44.266Z"],["3802187","FRAUDOPS-286","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","if we look only at price reviews closed at 0 with:\n\n{{(pr.finished_reason IN ('client_underpaid','auto_client_did_not_pay','client_did_not_pay','auto_client_underpaid') OR pr.requested_reason IN ('client_underpaid','client_did_not_pay'))}}\n\nthen numbers are considerable. but at a high level, we already see a high ratio of order/driver, which means that there are not a lot of drivers with multiple orders reported as unpaid. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.55.28.png|width=869,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.55.28.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.55.37.png|width=867,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.55.37.png\"!","2026-01-12T09:58:05.695Z"],["3802188","WD-22519","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Confirmed in SBX","2026-01-12T09:58:09.384Z"],["3802189","LSS-61395","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","Background: The new global terms templates include wording for Bolt Send, replacing the need to have separate terms for new markets. Julia Maal, Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu and Michael Roberts discussed whether this would have an impact on how our terms are shown in-app, and whether changes would cause issues for CS teams. Michael Roberts suggested that future uncertainties could be avoided by always referring to the legal landing page (rides / riders) instead of specific terms, as this avoids any links becoming ‘old / outdated’, and further set out a summary of issues (on [slack|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C040ZQX2RSA/p1767896208850489] - copy below) for Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu to discuss with Bolt Send stakeholders:\n\n\n----\n\n# Quick flag to stakeholders that as part of a wider terms update exercise, our new rides terms templates (currently with regional teams for rollout) now include Bolt Send provisions, so separate terms are not necessary for new markets. Existing markets with separate terms may also migrate Bolt Send terms into 'main terms', when they update them.\n#* F_or reference only:_\n#** _For new provisions see_ [_customer terms 5.24 onwards_|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JrmLsb6-IcFWfMBepu7yT6agndi4P0EZZ401YsB1FXs/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=kix.ijep035ib7g6] _/_ [_service provider terms 5.27 onwards_|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1RVNXe1lW1DprrmpSnXUdty4r6PZ9V4qm8I6AoGmDinU/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.8aex3dl4ckyh]_._\n#*** _5.27 in the customer terms makes clear that everything sits with the passenger._\n#** _The old 'separate terms template' is_ [_here_|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hZq5MNtVtHUAbvsypTYmC32S9KVNPdNJJaW0rHgqpDg/edit?tab=t.0]_._\n#** _Any regional counsel with bespoke Bolt Send terns should - you would hope - localise their new customers terms accordingly (i.e. if they want to adopt the new short form Bolt Send wording)._\n#** _See_ [_here_|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C040NCWV75H/p1756306860608709?thread_ts=1756280738.049729&cid=C040NCWV75H] _for my messaging to Regional Legal on this._\n# To avoid links in our app going 'dead' etc., any T&C links in-app or elsewhere should now simply link to the market landing page for rides passengers (rather than any specific terms / document). That ensures riders always reach the correct terms in each market, whether Bolt Send terms are standalone or not\n#* _For reference only:_\n#** _This does assume that standalone Bolt Send terms are available on our website for those markets, which we think is correct but it's worth double-checking. You could ask for an up to date list of Bolt Send markets to check this._\n#** _An alternative is to still keep links updated on a market-by-market basis, but it's a bit fiddly and requires upkeep for new launches etc.._\n# This is a good opportunity to check-in on the existing Bolt Send in-app messaging / web-landing pages to see if you can anticipate any other issues (existing or new). On the basis that users shouldn't have to read T&Cs to figure out how the service practically works (book, pack your parcel etc., contact CS if issues) then there may be nothing to do.\n# Beyond that, it's just a case of checking in with CS teams / Bolt Send teams are still OK with dealing with issues as they arise on an ongoing basis.\n#* Nothing is practically changing in terms in respect of responsibilities etc. Every parcel remains the passenger's responsibility. Drivers are prohibited from stealing etc.\n#* As above, if users and CS are already clear on expectations and what they tell drivers, there shouldn't be anything to do.","2026-01-12T09:59:02.932Z"],["3802190","PAR-3618","PAR","yusuf.daniju@bolt.eu","Yusuf Daniju","[~accountid:63fc5f040a4a47fb8d20cf92] Can you tell me what this ticket is about?","2026-01-12T09:59:15.773Z"],["3802191","PAR-3839","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","Hi [@narmin.mammadli|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b] this [payment|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/76737333?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] was moved to {{no-client}} state because client not exist, Please confirm if everything is Ok","2026-01-12T09:59:26.848Z"],["3802193","LSS-61266","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","Hi, [~accountid:62a88aabd0132d0068800eba] \nThis contract is general agreement of cooperation with Hyundai manufacturer. All purchases will be via local dealers (separate purchase contracts). Amount is a total amount for all 3 years (expected). There is no commitment, just cooperation, discount agreements, conditions. \n","2026-01-12T09:59:42.859Z"],["3802202","WD-22331","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hey [~accountid:627aae199311100068a00836] , not an issue. \nI’ll handle it this week or latest next one. But I do need instructions on where to drop the data.","2026-01-12T10:00:49.293Z"],["3802203","LSS-61393","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T10:01:08.850Z"],["3802204","FRAUDOPS-286","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","for the PR angle, there are multiple markets where I would expect big numbers, but I don’t see it. I suspect other teams already took actions to limit this abuse, for example, not allowing cash price reviews. \n\nconsidering actions are limited and multiple stakeholders involved, I’ll drop this for now. \n\nimho, the correction angle is easier for drivers to abuse because it’s more hidden and way tougher for us to do anything about it. but didn’t spread it yet. more word of mouth is gonna be needed for abuse to grow. ","2026-01-12T10:01:08.982Z"],["3802205","PFI-829364","PFI","kutlwano.tsetsewa@bolt.eu","Kutlwano Tsetsewa","Hi [~accountid:627cf5040d1e73006f7d2aa9] any update on this? ","2026-01-12T10:01:13.500Z"],["3802207","L10N-27253","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27250](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27250)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T10:01:58.842Z"],["3802208","L10N-27255","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all commen