licate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27250](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27250)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T10:02:13.338Z"],["3802217","L10N-27273","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27250](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27250)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T10:02:14.347Z"],["3802218","L10N-27274","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27250](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27250)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T10:02:14.631Z"],["3802220","LSS-61352","LSS","corneliu.radu@bolt.eu","Corneliu-Ștefan Radu","Done. \n\n","2026-01-12T10:02:37.658Z"],["3802221","DBRE-8591","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","The instances were destroyed.","2026-01-12T10:02:42.026Z"],["3802222","DSR-3643","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Issue with comms plugin, [Slack|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CND9AL5LY/p1766403889743399]","2026-01-12T10:03:05.412Z"],["3802225","SREP-1080","SREP","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","We would like to build security alert rules on kube-apiserver audit events. For example, here’s an open source repo with some basic kubernetes audit events: [https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/tree/master/rules/application/kubernetes/audit|https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/tree/master/rules/application/kubernetes/audit|smart-link]  \n\nThe tool of choice for CloudSec is Elastic Cloud. We usually ingest logs to Elastic Cloud using a flow of service X → S3 → CloudSec ingestion system → Elastic Cloud. Your assistance would be much appreciated on the “service X → S3” side of things. \n\nI think for EKS “service X” is Amazon CloudWatch, right?\n\nIf you already stream kube-apiserver audits somewhere, maybe there’s an alternative path we should use to ingest these logs.\n\n\n\nAsked for more info internally on the kube-apiserver audit logs ingestion project as well","2026-01-12T10:03:43.644Z"],["3802226","DSR-3645","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Issue with comms plugin, [Slack|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CND9AL5LY/p1766403889743399]","2026-01-12T10:03:48.105Z"],["3802228","CCM-22268","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hello Ademola 👋 \n\nI added you the Food Delivery onboarding. Do you need some other courses?\n\nIf you need other courses from Delivery, could you let me know which markets are you supporting?\n\nThank you in advance,\nIrena","2026-01-12T10:04:13.915Z"],["3802230","CRC-2075","CRC","daniil.musienko@bolt.eu","Daniil Musienko","[update]\n\nProgress: Adyen has changed the configuration, bugs have been fixed, and flows have been tested.\n\nNext: 12.01 - enable for some BIN, 15.01 - enable globally","2026-01-12T10:04:28.616Z"],["3802231","LSS-61100","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] it’s a different one - the one that you shared was for the People team and currently we’re reviewing terms for CS [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61096|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61096|smart-link] \n\nBut, basically, terms are the same ","2026-01-12T10:04:49.157Z"],["3802234","CCM-22268","CCM","ademola.oloja@bolt-outsource.eu","Ademola Oloja","I am a trainer and I will be supporting GEQ market","2026-01-12T10:05:35.855Z"],["3802235","PAW-14778","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-gabriel-olaru\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17085\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 10:05:42 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T10:05:43.087Z"],["3802236","LSS-61353","LSS","corneliu.radu@bolt.eu","Corneliu-Ștefan Radu","[~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] Hi Debora! Please give me editing access so I can fix the issues.","2026-01-12T10:05:50.517Z"],["3802239","WD-22517","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:60ab52d6411c2200681a75e4] , I have just received this ticket. I will review and work on it soon. Will keep you posted.\n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-12T10:06:33.755Z"],["3802241","LSS-61020","LSS","aba.koita@bolt.eu","Aba Koita","Hello [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742], \n\n\n\nI’ve reviewed the driver’s account and everything is legitimate. The driver was first warned about fraudulent use of the account in February 2025. He was warned again and suspended for seven days on July 25, and ultimately permanently banned on August 21 for continued violations. (Superman is not real).\n\nPlease find below the last message sent to the driver on August 25th:\n\n\nCher Yassine Bensaci,\n\nVous avez partagé votre compte, ce qui constitue une violation des conditions d'utilisation des chauffeurs. Par conséquent, conformément aux articles 13.5 et 13.6 de nos conditions générales d'utilisation des chauffeurs, votre compte est résilié. Vous disposez du droit de contester toute mesure de suspension via le Système Interne de Traitement des Plaintes, tel que décrit aux articles 14.6 et 14.7.\"\n\nNous vous souhaitons le meilleur pour la suite.\n\nL’équipe Bolt\n\nThe driver can submit a reactivation claim starting in February using the following link: [https://bolt.eu/fr-fr/support/articles/26895/|https://bolt.eu/fr-fr/support/articles/26895/|smart-link] \n\nLet me know if you need anything else.\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.33.06.png|width=1022,height=718,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 11.33.06.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-12T10:06:44.242Z"],["3802242","WD-22331","WD","federico.levi@bolt.eu","Federico Levi","hello, ok thanks!\nwhen you are ready, let’s discuss details","2026-01-12T10:06:43.465Z"],["3802244","CEBF-1621","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","[~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] can we deploy this one? Sales is requesting Owner’s info edit access on account level because they want to send contract to the owner with the correct info.","2026-01-12T10:07:07.446Z"],["3802245","DBRE-8688","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","{noformat}+------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+------------+-----------+---------------------+---------------------+\n| TABLE_SCHEMA                 | TABLE_NAME                                             | TABLE_ROWS | size in G | CREATE_TIME         | UPDATE_TIME         |\n+------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+------------+-----------+---------------------+---------------------+\n| taxify_admin                 | _search_category_icon_check_result_ghc                 |          3 | 0G        | 2024-11-06 11:24:45 | NULL                |\n| taxify_admin                 | _search_category_icon_check_result_gho                 |          0 | 0G        | 2024-11-06 11:24:45 | NULL                |\n| taxify_business              | _business_admin_user_20260109083030_del                |     780511 | 0G        | 2026-01-09 08:31:23 | 2026-01-09 08:29:46 |\n| taxify_business              | _business_approval_ride_request_20260109094908_del     |      48235 | 0G        | 2026-01-09 09:49:28 | 2026-01-09 09:49:23 |\n| taxify_business              | _business_voucher_distribution_comm_20260108134804_del |      10582 | 0G        | 2026-01-08 13:48:09 | 2026-01-08 12:27:14 |\n| taxify_business              | _order_finished_event_queue_20260108141116_del         |    3785886 | 1G        | 2026-01-08 14:13:40 | 2025-12-19 17:37:56 |\n| taxify_category_stats        | _category_stats_ghc                                    |      45832 | 0G        | 2025-03-10 09:08:56 | NULL                |\n| taxify_category_stats        | _category_stats_gho                                    |   15278522 | 3G        | 2025-03-10 09:08:57 | NULL                |\n| taxify_category_stats        | _category_stats_old                                    |  649102500 | 241G      | 2025-03-11 12:45:49 | NULL                |\n| taxify_event                 | _migrator_hb                                           |          0 | 0G        | 2025-03-17 09:59:31 | NULL                |\n| taxify_identity_verification | _check_run_ghc_20260112083252_del                      |      99695 | 0G        | 2026-01-12 08:32:52 | 2026-01-10 09:44:06 |\n| taxify_identity_verification | _check_run_gho_20260112083252_del                      |  488394038 | 391G      | 2026-01-12 08:32:52 | 2026-01-09 16:20:06 |\n+------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+------------+-----------+---------------------+---------------------+{noformat}","2026-01-12T10:07:16.520Z"],["3802246","PIF-2256","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft concisely outlines the new feature that allows a different root hash for each item in an MQ batch, which will help track items individually. Missing information includes where in the platform this can be seen and resources for further reading.","2026-01-12T10:07:17.656Z"],["3802247","CRC-2190","CRC","daniil.musienko@bolt.eu","Daniil Musienko","[update]\n\nProgress: The PR with changes has been approved\n\nNext: 12.01 - deploy changes and start testing, 19.01 - full rollout","2026-01-12T10:07:21.146Z"],["3802249","LSS-50276","LSS","ana.cordoba@bolt.eu","Ana de Córdoba","Hi team, following back with Iberdrola’s team right now, will update asap","2026-01-12T10:07:40.110Z"],["3802251","PIF-2256","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 7\n• Relevance: 8\n• Problem Definition: 6\n• Accept: 7\n• Suggested improvements: The user story needs a clearer definition of the existing problem and its impact. Describe the current limitations with tracking items individually in an MQ batch and why having distinct root hashes for each item is necessary. The acceptance criteria should include more specific conditions, such as how the suffixed root hash will be verified or measured. Consider adding examples or cases that illustrate the need for individual tracking of the items. Provide context or insights about how this change will improve user experience or platform efficiency.","2026-01-12T10:07:48.292Z"],["3802252","RCE-344","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alisher Matkurbanov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768212462066379]*{color}:\n<@U027N9G59KP> approved\n{quote}","2026-01-12T10:07:53.928Z"],["3802253","RCE-344","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768212469173619]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-344 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T10:08:02.235Z"],["3802255","WEBSD-1443","WEBSD","tom.gander@bolt.eu","Tom Gander","Data: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XkfQig14ltQPdez-5C9GH2XiLfDkXnTTQoB7oSk4WVI/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XkfQig14ltQPdez-5C9GH2XiLfDkXnTTQoB7oSk4WVI/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T10:08:35.199Z"],["3802256","LSS-56257","LSS","kristina.pugaca@bolt.eu","Kristina Pugaca","Thank you, everyone. [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] The ticket can be closed.","2026-01-12T10:08:37.704Z"],["3802257","CRC-2300","CRC","daniil.musienko@bolt.eu","Daniil Musienko","[update]\n\nProgress: The implementation is in progress\n\nNext: Implementation, no milestones to highlight. ","2026-01-12T10:09:02.262Z"],["3802259","PAW-14782","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-12T10:09:09.574Z"],["3802261","CRC-2212","CRC","daniil.musienko@bolt.eu","Daniil Musienko","[update]\n\nProgress: no progress\n\nNext:  Do more tests between EU and US tokens. NL and CH accounts will be ready for testing in the middle of Jan.","2026-01-12T10:09:29.201Z"],["3802262","LSS-56257","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you [~accountid:60bf496ea01e11006ac62a66] ! I will close it then 🙂 ","2026-01-12T10:09:35.042Z"],["3802263","DSR-3655","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","First download no results. New download [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-bulk-invoice-download/item/1650010/view] ","2026-01-12T10:09:38.763Z"],["3802264","WD-22520","WD","andrea.figueroa@bolt.eu","Andrea Figueroa","Hi team, \n\nI’m following up on this request, just to see if there are any updates. We need to update Andrea Vota’s status as soon as possible. \n\n\n\nThank you","2026-01-12T10:09:39.422Z"],["3802266","CAMLE-8979","CAMLE","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","This is ready for release.\nplanning to release after doing sanity checks with automations. more context [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C062Z0FU5KN/p1768212480634779?thread_ts=1767869527.881769&cid=C062Z0FU5KN]","2026-01-12T10:10:07.457Z"],["3802267","BEE-3626","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko",":wave: thanks for your answers, I think it's all clear now :bowing:\n\nalso one small update: we included this item into current sprint (which starts today) plan, so it should be delivered till end of next week (likely somewhat earlier)","2026-01-12T10:10:22.086Z"],["3802268","LSS-61396","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","The above was discussed on a call - meeting notes [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/18lwaz6Uy4pT5zGXo9KluXj-omKEKWArVOQ3TCheTkvA/edit?tab=t.f835x2a2ar4a]. ","2026-01-12T10:10:32.929Z"],["3802270","LSS-61157","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:10c3f4ef-f975-47a3-8af8-927b01cd9521] could you reply to my questions please ?\n\n will we sign for the trial any order form ?\n\nWe need also to add the wording about compliance with Bolt’s InfoSec Code [Information security code of practice | Security|https://bolt.eu/en/security/supplier-requirements/]. “The Parties will comply with Customer’s Information Security Code of Practice [Information security code of practice | Security|https://bolt.eu/en/security/supplier-requirements/] in the course of providing the services”.\n\nPlease share the link with partner and ask to review","2026-01-12T10:11:04.069Z"],["3802272","BDB-1461","BDB","britt.peet@bolt.eu","Bo Britt Peet","*Update*: Design is waiting once copy is finalised (content ticket [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CNT-377?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiYTMzZGMzYmFkYmFjNGEzNjgzYjI1ZTVlNmJjYTI1NmMiLCJwIjoiaiJ9]). From our side, designer is [~accountid:60ab71565dc18500701cae80] . \n\n[~accountid:712020:f172cd28-e81b-4011-8942-5ec6b2912f37] to ping us once wel have the OOH media plan.  ","2026-01-12T10:11:08.926Z"],["3802274","BP-13229","BP","sebastian.kurpios@bolt.eu","Sebastian Kurpios","*Important note*\nHow deeplinks work for IP SMS and emails?\n\n* when mobile user without app → redirects to App Store / Google Play\n* when mobile user with app → redirects to payment setup for IP OR selecting payment method for non-IP (this case can only occur when the link is fired manually)\n* when desktop user → redirects to Bolt/Hopp landing page\n\nLinks: [https://bolt.onelink.me/sbJ2/ffce81ec|https://bolt.onelink.me/sbJ2/ffce81ec|smart-link]  and [https://gethopp.onelink.me/17bw/azolqbov|https://gethopp.onelink.me/17bw/azolqbov|smart-link]  \n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:e2c955ca-33bb-4f61-9a12-3b0fb520b3fd] - unfortunately, this time the testing will be at the very end, because due to the lack of changes on the part of other teams, we are relying on mocks.","2026-01-12T10:11:23.510Z"],["3802276","WEB-9762","WEB","samuel.oyekeye@bolt.eu","Samuel Oluseyi Oyekeye","[~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] does this change apply to videos in the header as well?","2026-01-12T10:11:44.267Z"],["3802277","CRC-2366","CRC","daniil.musienko@bolt.eu","Daniil Musienko","[update]\n\nProgress: The flow has been tested. The automation of drivers’ onboarding has been discussed. No much progress due to sick leave.\n\nNext: no progress in the next 2 weeks due to the FF shift and a vacation. ","2026-01-12T10:11:44.355Z"],["3802278","LSS-52572","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340704|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340704|smart-link]  ","2026-01-12T10:11:55.661Z"],["3802279","LSS-60824","LSS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] fyi","2026-01-12T10:12:20.055Z"],["3802280","PAW-14766","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-data-archiving, pint-product-data-management, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-12T10:12:23.159Z"],["3802281","PIF-3276","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-njsc-db, pint-product-backend-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-12T10:12:30.204Z"],["3802284","LSS-58423","LSS","kristina.pugaca@bolt.eu","Kristina Pugaca","[~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] I think this ticket can be closed as well. If the authority comes back with a reply, I will reopen the ticket.","2026-01-12T10:12:56.642Z"],["3802285","WFM-9939","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","To add the apps in the OKTA Dashboard they need to raise a Jira for [Internal IT Support|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1]\n","2026-01-12T10:13:07.244Z"],["3802298","MKP-8186","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Maybe a better option than the order_try_driver. Explore and reject if not","2026-01-12T10:13:33.906Z"],["3802302","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Paula Espeja [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768212832061739]*{color}:\nHi <@U090E7WNXUG> as mentioned ideally, these movements should not be reflected on an invoice at all as they are out of scope of VAT. However, as a temporary solution is needed, the steps could be:\n1. If technically possible, use *dedicated compensation types presented on a separate compensation invoice/document*, rather than the regular monthly invoice.\n2. Ensure these compensation types are clearly labelled as *non-revenue* and *out of scope / VAT 0%*.\n3. Confirm that these amounts do *not flow into VAT reporting* or impact revenue figures.\n4. Limit the use strictly to *deposit paybacks / offboarding-related cases* as a temporary solution.\n5. Document this as an *exceptional workaround*, pending a proper product fix.\nIf using a separate compensation invoice is not possible and the amounts need to be included in the monthly invoice temporarily, then at a minimum they should be *clearly identified as out of scope and no VAT should be charged.*\n{quote}","2026-01-12T10:14:07.896Z"],["3802303","MKP-8501","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Cancelled until a better time. No plans to work on it","2026-01-12T10:14:15.083Z"],["3802310","LSS-60557","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c], sure will send them. I’ll be back with the information. ","2026-01-12T10:15:10.862Z"],["3802311","LSS-58423","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Deal, [~accountid:60bf496ea01e11006ac62a66] . I will close it. Please let me know if something comes up 🙂 ","2026-01-12T10:15:12.593Z"],["3802313","LSS-60746","LSS","azza.ltifi@bolt.eu","Azza Letifi","Hi [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd], Thank you for your comments. I shared my replies in the document. \n\nFor _the driver-facing declaration,_ we do not have anything in place right now. The process will be like the following: \n\n* Certificate: to be submitted with other documents like ID, Licence ..etc\n* Video: to be sent through Beehive, and CS confirms adding the category to the profile\n* Interview: face-to-face conversation. \n\nI would like to understand how the disclaimer will be sent, especially when uploading the certificate or in the interview. \n\nI would really appreciate your help in drafting the disclaimer as well. \n\nThank you!\n\n","2026-01-12T10:15:21.783Z"],["3802314","LSS-60293","LSS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","No responses, sent the suggested response (from 22.12.2025).","2026-01-12T10:15:21.837Z"],["3802320","LSS-61396","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T10:16:09.233Z"],["3802321","LSS-57542","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340721|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340721|smart-link]  ","2026-01-12T10:16:42.922Z"],["3802322","LSS-61121","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","Follow up call on Tuesday 6 January:\n\n[+Michael Roberts+|mailto:michael.roberts@bolt.eu] confirmed that use of the substitution feature is considered necessary to defend the Bolt Flex model and the legal background regarding ‘personal service’ making this a difficult line of defence for Bolt. [+Sudipto Das+|mailto:sudipto.das@bolt.eu] agreed to review the [+Project Green 3.0 development requests+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ueD8ddUkKSt8cyeX-vH21rlYW2THVFa46UjGEWNsKAg/edit?tab=t.0] and that he would reach out to [+Michael Roberts+|mailto:michael.roberts@bolt.eu] for further input as needed.","2026-01-12T10:17:02.854Z"],["3802323","L10N-27293","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27284](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27284)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T10:17:08.494Z"],["3802324","L10N-27289","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27284](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27284)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T10:17:08.640Z"],["3802326","L10N-27290","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s whe