atest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27250](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27250)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T10:17:20.566Z"],["3802332","LSS-61307","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","Hi [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] , we are currently proceeding with changes to the Supervisory Board, replacing two members with new ones. The new members will be formally appointed at the end of January, once the shareholder vote is finalised.\n\nCould you please confirm with the auditors that we can provide the updated information after the shareholder vote has been finalised?","2026-01-12T10:17:27.420Z"],["3802335","PFI-805526","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Hello \n\n  \n\nSending chargeback report \n\n  \n\nSincerely \n\n *{color:#767171} {color}* \n\n *{color:#767171} *Nino Kabulashvili*{color}*\n{color:#767171} E-Commerce Partners Relationship Senior Manager{color} {color:#767171}| Payments Business |{color}{color:#767171}{color} {color:#767171}Bank of Georgia\n Bank of Georgia: Tbilisi, 29A Gagarini Str., 0160 | E-mail:{color} [{color:#767171} {color}{color:#767171}NKabulashvili@bog.ge{color}{color:#767171}{color}|mailto:NKabulashvili@bog.ge]{color:#767171}\n Phone: (+995 32) 2444 444 (ext. 7492) | Mobile: (+995 555) 444405{color}{color:#767171}{color}{color:#767171}{color}{color:#1F497D}{color}{color:blue}{color}  \n\n  \n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://bankofgeorgia.ge/retail]>{color:blue}{color}!image002.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[https://www.facebook.com/119630781428450]>{color:blue}{color}!image003.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://instagram.com/bankofgeorgia]>{color:blue}{color}!image004.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://www.youtube.com/bankofgeorgiatv]>{color:blue}{color}!image005.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://www.linkedin.com/company/bank-of-georgia]>{color:#1F497D}{color}\n\n[^WOLT 22-31 December.xlsx] _(11 kB)_","2026-01-12T10:17:57.697Z"],["3802341","PTWS-2123","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","check where it’s used and update it to the new fields _Job level primary position -_ check with Steve for more details\n\n!image-20260112-101719.png|width=951,alt=\"image-20260112-101719.png\"!","2026-01-12T10:18:49.404Z"],["3802342","EBIKE1-422","EBIKE1","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","I asked local team to collect the bike so we can investigate :loading: ","2026-01-12T10:19:15.977Z"],["3802359","LSS-57822","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] !\n\nRegarding this topic, we have the two following questions:\n1. The team wants to use this selfie check feature only in cases where there is suspected fraud with the email/phone number changes OR do you want to use it each time contact details are changed?\n2. Has the team already confirmed with the engineers if re-prompting the selfie check for fraud prevention is already possible from the technical side?\nThank you!","2026-01-12T10:20:53.296Z"],["3802368","PAR-3841","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","[@alexander.fokau|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6083d099cbff1b0070445fea]  This client account has indeed been created, but it’s allocated to a ride-hailing fleet. In our system, these are two different and unrelated accounts. When creating an early cashout for a ride-hailing driver, we check for a driver client account, even if he is {{fleet-equipped.}}  I need to discuss this with [@volodymyr.hadomskyi|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:fc7ada41-3f9c-4d74-95f1-90300ecbe201] when he’s back tomorrow.","2026-01-12T10:21:43.607Z"],["3802372","MKP-7754","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","[~accountid:5b839377eb18d0589b9b30d4] seems like you have a merged PR for the issue. Should we consider it done?","2026-01-12T10:22:21.039Z"],["3802373","DBRE-8688","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Contact related team\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02LWCMELDD/p1768213325141419|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02LWCMELDD/p1768213325141419|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T10:22:31.608Z"],["3802377","HS-28839","HS","ingrid.valgejarv@bolt.eu","Ingrid Valgejärv","Hey!\n\nThank you for reaching out! I have shared the Drive folder with their contract [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1VCN5bLiMzkUIkw8ghf0ge391SI4hgKw_?usp=sharing].\n\nKind regards\n\nIngrid","2026-01-12T10:23:08.629Z"],["3802378","DBRE-8688","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Checking the status\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1768212401037699|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1768212401037699|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T10:23:10.663Z"],["3802381","LSS-61370","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:712020:50554e69-c5e6-483a-a43b-b48bec17d7bb]. Could you inform:\n\n* if both accounts are currently blocked?\n* what do you mean exactly with “he proceeded to use Bolt Business fraudulently”?\n* were there any issues regarding payments? Meaning, did these clients not pay their monthly invoices?\n* post here the Special Terms that were signed?","2026-01-12T10:23:24.435Z"],["3802384","MLC-3575","MLC","yulia.nikitina@bolt.eu","Yulia Nikitina","*W3: Moved to new epic* [*here*|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/MLC/boards/3652?assignee=5bc9c3edbc49ac2bb1553bd2&issueType=10000&selectedIssue=MLC-3869]","2026-01-12T10:23:48.841Z"],["3802385","PAW-14784","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-12T10:23:58.396Z"],["3802389","MKP-7637","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","We will review all tests as part of the general activity to keep tests up-to-date","2026-01-12T10:24:19.104Z"],["3802392","PRF-1452","PRF","marit.ausmees@bolt.eu","Marit Ausmees","Hey, [~accountid:712020:9c4c0927-aeb3-4a47-9ea9-68428dc00be8] What would be the next steps for this ticket? Anything currently needed from my side?","2026-01-12T10:24:41.819Z"],["3802404","LSS-61397","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","Ticket created to record discussions.","2026-01-12T10:26:11.131Z"],["3802405","BB-2230","BB","ahmad.eldefrawy@bolt.eu","Ahmad ElDefrawy","The initiative is being decommissioned ","2026-01-12T10:26:14.364Z"],["3802410","LSS-61397","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","[~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] response on slack:\n\nHey [@lars.speekenbrink|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/UV12705K9], welcome back and happy New Year, I hope you managed to get some distance from work over the [break.My|http://break.My] understanding is that for OC to be comfortable confirming a reclassification risk below 50%, we would need to show that the feature is not merely theoretical but has a real-life effect (as mass reclassification is unlikely at this point, at least for a defined group of drivers). Even limited but genuine use could already be sufficient to reduce the risk for that group below the 50% threshold.While “real-life impact” is not clearly defined, it seems reasonable that this would require evidence that drivers can and do actually use the feature, meaning they can assign, or at least attempt to assign, trips to a substitute. Even one-off or occasional use should help demonstrate that the option exists beyond paper and has practical relevance.Obviously, higher adoption strengthens the argument. However, even usage by smaller groups can already support the point that substitution is not only contractually permitted but is actively provided by Bolt as a tool to increase drivers’ entrepreneurial freedom, allowing them to decide whether to perform the work themselves or assign it to a chosen substitute, and that this possibility is real and usable in practice.","2026-01-12T10:26:38.999Z"],["3802412","WEB-7906","WEB","roberts.calijs@bolt.eu","Robert Chaliy","[~accountid:712020:e8f2de02-6346-4839-a1e5-fc656f320d5e] \n\n* Meta title: Women driver partners | Safe and flexible earnings\n* Meta description: Start driving on your terms with Bolt. Make money on your schedule with tailored safety tools, bonuses and supportive benefits that help you get on the road.","2026-01-12T10:26:51.620Z"],["3802418","FX-3501","FX","carlo.fanton@bolt.eu","Carlo Leone Fanton","field can be updated via admin-panel-automation {{FleetX - Company - Ad-hoc company updates}} (/) ([link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-panel-automation/pipeline/edit/server/750016])\n\n\n!image-20260112-102636.png|width=751,alt=\"image-20260112-102636.png\"!","2026-01-12T10:27:13.764Z"],["3802419","LSS-61397","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","[~accountid:612f31d89976c300693ebaf7] response on slack:\n\n*Ask:* Do you think this would have an impact on how external council will review the relevance of the feature and therefor the impact of assessment of the reclassification risk?\n\nIn a word: yes. Arguing that substitution is “real” based only on formal or theoretical reasoning will be difficult. We need to show that it is real in practice, not just on paper. Usage _is_ the best way of evidencing this, but the core question is whether substitution is genuinely available and operable for drivers. The narrative we should anchor to, regardless of uptake, is:\n\n* Every relevant driver has the right to substitute.\n* Every relevant driver is clearly informed what substitution is and that they can use it if they choose. This is critical.\n* Every relevant driver can exercise substitution easily and without friction.\n* We should not suggest that substitution is a feature intended for universal adoption. It is designed for drivers who want to work in a more entrepreneurial way. Bolt’s role is to enable that option and to support multiple ways of working, not to push all drivers into a single model.\n\nUK context: the feature has not yet been actively promoted by the local team. That is because further product development has been requested. In the absence of promotion, limited usage is unsurprising. The main request from the UK team is functionality allowing riders to favourite drivers or fleets so they can be more visible during price bidding. Product is reviewing feasibility.Plan of attack should be: roll out ASAP, continue to work on uptake / visibility\n\n{quote}And is there a way we can steer this to external council so that it does impact their re-assessment?{quote}\n\nLet's use a call to be clear on the ask / aims","2026-01-12T10:27:18.842Z"],["3802422","LSS-61397","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","Call arranged for Wednesday 14 January to discuss.","2026-01-12T10:27:39.851Z"],["3802423","PFI-830450","PFI","santiago.zarate@bolt-outsource.eu","Santiago Daniel Segovia Zárate","Hello team. Can you please check on this request?","2026-01-12T10:27:48.016Z"],["3802427","LSS-61399","LSS","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","As per main ticket:\n\n[~accountid:612f31d89976c300693ebaf7] response on slack:\n\n*Ask:* Do you think this would have an impact on how external council will review the relevance of the feature and therefor the impact of assessment of the reclassification risk?\n\nIn a word: yes. Arguing that substitution is “real” based only on formal or theoretical reasoning will be difficult. We need to show that it is real in practice, not just on paper. Usage _is_ the best way of evidencing this, but the core question is whether substitution is genuinely available and operable for drivers. The narrative we should anchor to, regardless of uptake, is:\n\n* Every relevant driver has the right to substitute.\n* Every relevant driver is clearly informed what substitution is and that they can use it if they choose. This is critical.\n* Every relevant driver can exercise substitution easily and without friction.\n* We should not suggest that substitution is a feature intended for universal adoption. It is designed for drivers who want to work in a more entrepreneurial way. Bolt’s role is to enable that option and to support multiple ways of working, not to push all drivers into a single model.\n\nUK context: the feature has not yet been actively promoted by the local team. That is because further product development has been requested. In the absence of promotion, limited usage is unsurprising. The main request from the UK team is functionality allowing riders to favourite drivers or fleets so they can be more visible during price bidding. Product is reviewing feasibility.Plan of attack should be: roll out ASAP, continue to work on uptake / visibility\n\n{quote}And is there a way we can steer this to external council so that it does impact their re-assessment?{quote}\n\nLet's use a call to be clear on the ask / aims","2026-01-12T10:28:46.780Z"],["3802429","INT-749","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","[~accountid:712020:6f095333-c438-429c-9660-a9de5d845fe7] Would we need MVRA support for Phase 2? or all good? ","2026-01-12T10:28:54.881Z"],["3802437","CSDT-951","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Removed versioning from dim_support_case_tier_history, so view representation is not needed as the table will not be exposed in Looker","2026-01-12T10:30:25.438Z"],["3802446","DSR-3657","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T10:31:32.828Z"],["3802447","LSS-61369","LSS","indrek.eelmets@bolt.eu","Indrek Eelmets","Hi [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] - Assigning this case to you, as it is a local matter and does not appear to be an IP case. ","2026-01-12T10:31:33.903Z"],["3802448","LSS-61398","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T10:31:33.985Z"],["3802451","L10N-27300","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27284](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27284)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T10:32:06.482Z"],["3802452","L10N-27302","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27284](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27284)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T10:32:07.713Z"],["3802453","PFI-832345","PFI","blessing.eriaremhen@bolt-outsource.eu","Blessing Eriaremhen","!{08E6C644-D2E7-42DD-A593-AD3663928022}-20260112-103136.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T10:32:17.623Z"],["3802454","PFI-832345","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T10:32:20.355Z"],["3802460","MKP-6101","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Consider asking payments team either for context or for contributing to this part of order details","2026-01-12T10:33:43.546Z"],["3802464","LSS-61384","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thank you! Approved for signing by [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] . ","2026-01-12T10:34:49.669Z"],["3802467","LSS-61157","LSS","mikk.vachtmeister@bolt.eu","Mikk Vachtmeister","{quote}will we sign for the trial any order form ?{quote}\n\nNot now, we’ll share example documents with them that they are going to process. \n\n{quote}We need also to add the wording about compliance with Bolt’s InfoSec Code [Information security code of practice | Security|https://bolt.eu/en/security/supplier-requirements/]. “The Parties will comply with Customer’s Information Security Code of Practice [Information security code of practice | Security|https://bolt.eu/en/security/supplier-requirements/] in the course of providing the services”.{quote}\n\nDo you mean if we plan to sign the order form?\n\n","2026-01-12T10:35:30.472Z"],["3802468","LSS-55517","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] Happy New Year!\n\nThanks! this has been shared with Rescue","2026-01-12T10:35:34.718Z"],["3802478","WFM-9939","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Hello [~accountid:712020:ccc9b680-8f4f-457d-95e9-2d2e60497d90] this is OKTA-specific so please raise a Jira for [+Internal IT Support+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1]+.+\nPlease go to Slack channel #ext-support for support","2026-01-12T10:36:52.007Z"],["3802480","DMB-1693","DMB","rachit.dua@bolt.eu","Rachit Dua","Hey Team, anothe courier ([849025|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-courier/couriers/849025]) faces a problem regarding campaigns visibility. In this case the courier is not enrolled to a campaign but the campaigns tab is giving 404 error both in the app and via web. How should I navigate?","2026-01-12T10:37:38.770Z"],["3802481","DMB-1693","DMB",null,"Slack","[Rachit Dua|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/633d4448a84c7f79c38920be] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1768212828676339?thread_ts=1768212828.676339&cid=C08QTPU0GQY|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1768212828676339?thread_ts=1768212828.676339&cid=C08QTPU0GQY|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-12T10:37:39.617Z"],["3802482","DMB-1693","DMB","ivan.koscheev@bolt.eu","Ivan Koshcheev","Hey,\n\nDo you have screenshot from courier?\nWhat do you mean by 404 via web? I don't think, that we have campaigns in Courier Portal (only registration)\n\ncc: [@rachit.dua|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/633d4448a84c7f79c38920be]","2026-01-12T10:37:40.511Z"],["3802483","DMB-1693","DMB",null,"Slack","*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8545DGQJ/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8545DGQJ/image.png|smart-link]\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8J295H09/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8J295H09/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-12T10:37:42.002Z"],["3802484","MLC-3725","MLC","anniecel.malabanan@bolt.eu","Anniecel Malabanan","[~accountid:712020:6cf755e4-2536-45f4-814b-7e7ef0cdbd97] Yes, I’m on it. Thank you! Creating the Epic for Couriers now as well. ","2026-01-12T10:37:42.110Z"],["3802485","DMB-1693","DMB","rachit.dua@bolt.eu","Rachit Dua","Then campaigns are not a web view, they shouldn't give \"404\" :thinking_face:\nIt looks like \"partner benefits\" to me","2026-01-12T10:37:42.765Z"],["3802486","DMB-1693","DMB","rachit.dua@bolt.eu","Rachit Dua","Yup, partner benefits. I will quickly check it out!\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8J4248EM/screenshot_2026-01-12_at_12.34.54.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8J4248EM/screenshot_2026-01-12_at_12.34.54.png|smart-link]","2026-01-12T10:37:43.436Z"],["3802489","BRND-286","BRND","aliis.topssalulaid@bolt.eu","Aliis Tops-Salulaid","*Bolt Driver Commissions*  \n\nMotions - [here|https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/uwi4eo9s735ojoak0xqvm/AOv8uMTQ8mwbueJZ1clYZ_I?rlkey=ofqqbtojenln8k8efse7w8naa&st=ageeg3o0&dl=0]\nStatics – [here|https://www.figma.com/design/t2CC4p7oozZ48RcWpGr2LW/Performance?node-id=21742-1160&t=elGiioBYitH7dUPU-1]\nText Assets - [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1QBWYG52e3rBKfP2lWoYQnsgP9Ue5DITtBGdZIw0BtsQ/edit?usp=sharing]","2026-01-12T10:38:05.817Z"],["3802490","DMC-353","DMC","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","On first attempt I was not able to reproduce it, will have to retry","2026-01-12T10:38:13.564Z"],["3802493","DMB-1693","DMB",null,"Slack","[Rachit Dua|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/633d4448a84c7f79c38920be] unsynced this conversation thread from the Slack thread - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1768212828676339|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1768212828676339|smart-link]. Future replies will no longer sync or update across Slack and Jira.","2026-01-12T10:38:47.428Z"],["3802496","CSXPC-290","CSXPC","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","Looker explore examples:\n\n[https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/support/support_data?qid=mnUPuEZhn4XKECC88hWunx&origin_space=3904&toggle=pik|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/support/support_data?qid=mnUPuEZhn4XKECC88hWunx&origin_space=3904&toggle=pik]\n\n[https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/support/support_data?qid=LuYEZVTSPYamUb9KH0yr2L&origin_space=3904|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/support/support_data?qid=LuYEZVTSPYamUb9KH0yr2L&origin_space=3904]","2026-01-12T10:38:59.698Z"],["3802497","PFI-832348","PFI","clara.machado@bolt.eu","Clara Oliveira Machado","[^4807-PT1425-311076 (1).pdf]\n\n[^847-PT1425-848096 (1).pdf]\n\n[^95047-PT1425-135907 (1).pdf]\n\n[^Bolt Food .xlsx]","2026-01-12T10:39:10.341Z"],["3802499","PFI-832348","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T10:39:13.440Z"],["3802510","WFM-9938","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","For both patrique.soares and jose.ruivo, they should have access now to Assembled. If they need to enter company, please enter Bolt OU. Let me know if further help is needed.","2026-01-12T10:40:34.401Z"],["3802514","WEB-9762","WEB","conor.mclaughlin@bolt.eu","Conor McLaughlin","Yes, applies to videos too :)\n\n_This comment was left via Slack._","2026-01-12T10:41:28.873Z"],["3802517","MLC-2749","MLC","shubham.sureka@bolt.eu","Shubham Sureka","[~accountid:6336b241a84c7f79c387c386] Do you want to update this task after your discussion with Mostafa that i can also the wider group.","2026-01-12T10:42:03.979Z"],["3802518","PTWS-2124","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","New contigent worker types are:\n\n\n|*Category*|*Definition*|*Do’s*|*Don’ts*|\n|*Agency Temps / Staff-Augmentation*|Individuals employed by a staffing vendor but working under Bolt’s supervision and integrated into Bolt’s operations. The vendor remains the legal employer responsible for pay, benefits, and compliance (e.g., EU Temporary Agency Work Directive, Germany AÜG, UK AWR).|* Ensure vendor holds required permits (e.g., AÜG).\n* Define in the contract that Vendor is fully responsible for employment and taxes.\n* Manage via vendor contract, not directly with individuals.\n* Limit control to operational supervision.\n* Use for time-limited or project-based needs.|* Don’t contract or pay individuals directly.\n* Don’t manage HR matters (salary, leave, benefits).\n* Don’t promise or imply permanent employment.\n* Don’t extend indefinitely.\n* Don’t use for ongoing employee roles.\n* Don’t include in employee programs or reviews.|\n|*Outcome-based services/Managed services*|Third-party provider delivering defined outcomes/services with its own staff and management.|* Contract for results/outcomes.\n* Let the vendor manage staff.\n* Define SLAs/deliverables, but the provider makes sure how to reach those. \n* Treat as an external company.\n* Solve issues via vendor manager and not directly with their employees offering the service. |* Don’t supervise vendor staff.\n* Don’t set working time.\n* Don’t integrate into internal systems.\n* Don’t use as a substitute for employees.|\n|*Individual contractors*|Independent individuals engaged for specific projects or deliverables.|* Define work as projects/deliverables\n* Bolt exercises partial control over day-to-day tasks, hours, or methodologies. \n* Use contracts clarifying non-employee status.\n* Bolt is obligated to provide work, and the individual is obligated to perform it. \n* Pay via invoices.\n* Limit system access.\n* Fixed-term or project-based duration of the contract|•Don't allow to substitute somebody else to perform the work.\n* Don’t give job titles/org chart roles\n* Don’t fix working hours\n* Don’t involve in core decisions\n* Don’t include in employee programs/events.|\n|*Consultants*|External experts/advisors providing knowledge, analysis, and recommendations.|* Use for expertise/advice\n•May substitute somebody else to perform the work. \n* Expect reports/strategies\n* Treat as temporary advisors\n* Define scope as advisory outputs\n* Allow info-gathering from stakeholders\n* Contract for short-term or periodic advisory role\n* Pay via invoices|* Can’t rely on Bolt for their primary income. \n* Don’t assign employee-like responsibilities.\n* Don’t use for operational gaps.\n* Bolt doesn’t exercise control over day-to-day tasks, hours, or methodologies. \n* Don’t integrate into daily company routines.\n* Bolt is not obligated to provide work and the individual is not obligated to perform it.\n* Don’t extend the role indefinitely.|","2026-01-12T10:42:15.111Z"],["3802519","WFM-9937","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Queue accesses assigned","2026-01-12T10:42:22.387Z"],["3802520","MKP-5611","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","[~accountid:5b839377eb18d0589b9b30d4] do you still want to create it?","2026-01-12T10:42:23.976Z"],["3802533","PFI-832350","PFI","andrea.caceres@bolt-outsource.eu","Andrea Luján Chávez Cáceres","!Screenshot_20260112_111538_Bolt.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260112-104222.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T10:43:15.077Z"],["3802536","PFI-832349","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-12T10:43:21.785Z"],["3802537","PFI-832350","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T10:43:22.323Z"],["3802540","PFI-832351","PFI","kotryna.savukynaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Kotryna Savukynaitė","!image-20260112-104222.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T10:43:33.449Z"],["3802541","WFM-9944","WFM","bolajoko.kufoniyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Bolajoko Kufoniyi","!image-20260112-104334.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T10:43:40.895Z"],["3802545","MVRT-1450","MVRT","marit.ausmees@bolt.eu","Marit Ausmees","Hey, [~accountid:712020:9c4c0927-aeb3-4a47-9ea9-68428dc00be8] What cities should I target with these ads?","2026-01-12T10:44:51.028Z"],["3802546","MKP-5035","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Continuous work. We have dedicated tasks to scope particular areas","2026-01-12T10:44:52.168Z"],["3802548","HS-28849","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet. ","2026-01-12T10:45:59.599Z"],["3802549","DSR-3659","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T10:46:07.275Z"],["3802550","DSR-3661","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T10:46:07.301Z"],["3802553","WFM-9709","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","hey [~accountid:5f80303a25fbdf0068910efb] missing fleet management role was finally approved; Let us know if all good now ","2026-01-12T10:46:29.437Z"],["3802555","WFM-9945","WFM","bolajoko.kufoniyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Bolajoko Kufoniyi","!image-20260112-104618.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T10:46:31.318Z"],["3802556","WFM-9923","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Access granted to CS - Business ","2026-01-12T10:46:36.703Z"],["3802558","WFM-9891","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Hello [~accountid:637b64078fd2d2d5f12d4259] queue accesses assigned. Please check again if additional markets are needed.","2026-01-12T10:46:38.806Z"],["3802559","LSS-60426","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Thank you [~accountid:712020:5974a8c8-1b42-487b-ac1c-cd7b831937d4] Feel free to ping me or reopen the ticket once it becomes relevant again!","2026-01-12T10:46:40.852Z"],["3802567","WFM-9920","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! This permission is part only of OPS roles; Please explain why you need this permission and share the procedure where this is mentioned 🙏 ","2026-01-12T10:47:45.217Z"],["3802568","CRC-2196","CRC","ekaterina.matson@bolt.eu","Ekaterina Matson","[update] A/B test in Romania blocked due to unfinished interface changes, discussion planned for today. Approx. start 2025-01-14. First live test with drivers expected today.","2026-01-12T10:47:47.200Z"],["3802570","WFM-9946","WFM","bolajoko.kufoniyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Bolajoko Kufoniyi","!image-20260112-104750.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T10:47:56.318Z"],["3802575","CRC-1957","CRC","ekaterina.matson@bolt.eu","Ekaterina Matson","[update] No update, still waiting for the contract signing.","2026-01-12T10:48:46.259Z"],["3802579","WFM-9947","WFM","bolajoko.kufoniyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Bolajoko Kufoniyi","!image-20260112-104909.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T10:49:12.977Z"],["3802583","RLONE-379","RLONE","niklas.svegeboe@bolt.eu","Niklas Svegeboe","New feature for adding stops “mid-ride”, that requires consent of both Driver and Rider","2026-01-12T10:49:40.292Z"],["3802587","LSS-61387","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:712020:ead1b4e1-6cf2-4677-91f9-a3796e3901ba] Thank you for raising the ticket!\n\nAs we got this solved via Slack already, I’ll be closing the ticket here. Should you require any further support from me, please do not hesitate to reach out!","2026-01-12T10:50:31.571Z"],["3802588","WFM-9948","WFM","bolajoko.kufoniyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Bolajoko Kufoniyi","!image-20260112-105031.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T10:50:36.063Z"],["3802589","LSS-59915","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ! Your document(s) have been sent for signing via Dokobit.","2026-01-12T10:50:38.899Z"],["3802591","SOBB-961","SOBB","lucas.santossilva@bolt.eu","Lucas Oliveira dos Santos Silva","[~accountid:712020:7d95934d-5639-4088-90fe-77e85828226f]   and [~accountid:712020:b996cecd-aad9-4981-9528-5e20041886f2], tested and looks fine in Staging. Tests with payload and respective SFDC record can be found here: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dACE1_UMGGBg0OhOlZ36yT5zRRobcSNZWx6N2zC9HvI/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dACE1_UMGGBg0OhOlZ36yT5zRRobcSNZWx6N2zC9HvI/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T10:50:49.592Z"],["3802592","PFI-832362","PFI","darren.seruwagi@bolt.eu","Darren Mbigiridde Seruwagi","[^159.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^307.pdf (1).pdf]","2026-01-12T10:51:03.603Z"],["3802593","LSS-58103","LSS","elnara.nabiyeva@bolt.eu","Elnara Nabiyeva","Hi [~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2] , contract is accepted by the partner, thank you very much for your help, lets close this ticket","2026-01-12T10:51:06.386Z"],["3802594","MKP-709","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Too old to be considered valid.","2026-01-12T10:51:30.852Z"],["3802596","SREDESK-7401","SREDESK","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Created instead: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7402|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7402|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T10:51:39.083Z"],["3802601","LSS-61160","LSS","kevin.wawire@bolt.eu","Kevin Wawire","Hi \n\n[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] please have a look and let me know what ypu think.\n\n\n\nThanks","2026-01-12T10:52:22.255Z"],["3802602","C2-440","C2","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","The Cobra EMC testing on {{2026-01-12}} was successful with new EMC firmware v990.\n\n13km/h testing results:\n\n!image-20260112-103527.png|width=782,alt=\"image-20260112-103527.png\"!\n\nZoomed in speeds:\n\n!image-20260112-103652.png|width=763,alt=\"image-20260112-103652.png\"!\n\nThe critical point is in 20-80MHz test where it can be seen that the throttle input drops a little bit. The speed deviation is for brief moments 0.5 km/h which is acceptable.\n\n\n\nBrake test results: Similarly to 13kmh test, the brake test results were OK, with some deviations in the 20-80MHz spectrum but within allowed tolerances (Brake light did not turn off or flash).\n\n\n\n!image-20260112-105038.png|width=763,alt=\"image-20260112-105038.png\"!\n\n\n\nNow I need to confirm the shipping date for the Cobra controllers.","2026-01-12T10:52:27.189Z"],["3802604","LSS-61351","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^pełnomocnictwo Bolt Rides PL korespondencja (1).pdf] \n\n[^img20260112_09005103.pdf]\n\nI will share the tracking number via Slack a bit later","2026-01-12T10:52:49.738Z"],["3802610","PFI-832364","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T10:53:07.071Z"],["3802611","MKP-263","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Seemed too old to be still valid","2026-01-12T10:53:17.986Z"],["3802613","LSS-61301","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document, signed via Dokobit.\n\n[^PoA - ZUS - PEL_Bolt Services PL Sp. z o.o._Ewa Ożańska_09.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T10:53:30.643Z"],["3802614","LSS-61330","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:61fba8d88d9e3c00688fac2e] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bolt's PO_bags_Azerbaijan_JAN 2 6.xlsx - PO_AZ_JAN26 (1) Stamped (1).pdf] ","2026-01-12T10:53:33.751Z"],["3802616","DBRE-8688","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","\n\n{noformat}mysql> USE `taxify_identity_verification`;\nDatabase changed\nmysql> show create table _check_run_ghc_20260112083252_del\\G\n*************************** 1. row ***************************\n       Table: _check_run_ghc_20260112083252_del\nCreate Table: CREATE TABLE `_check_run_ghc_20260112083252_del` (\n  `id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `last_update` timestamp NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `hint` varchar(64) CHARACTER SET ascii NOT NULL,\n  `value` varchar(4096) CHARACTER SET ascii NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `hint_uidx` (`hint`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=197768 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COMMENT='gh-ost changelog'\n1 row in set (0.00 sec)\n\nmysql> RENAME TABLE `_check_run_ghc_20260112083252_del` TO `_check_run_ghc_20250112083252_del`;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected (0.00 sec)\n\nmysql> show create table _check_run_gho_20260112083252_del\\G\n*************************** 1. row ***************************\n       Table: _check_run_gho_20260112083252_del\nCreate Table: CREATE TABLE `_check_run_gho_20260112083252_del` (\n  `id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT COMMENT 'DataType:PKBID',\n  `created` timestamp NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP COMMENT 'DataType:CREATED',\n  `last_update` timestamp NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP COMMENT 'DataType:LAST_UPDATE',\n  `flow_run_id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL COMMENT 'DataType:FKBID;ForeignKey:taxify_identity_verification.flow_run.id',\n  `provider` varchar(64) NOT NULL,\n  `check_type` varchar(64) NOT NULL,\n  `status` enum('created','failed','cancelled','undetermined','succeeded') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'created',\n  `context` json DEFAULT NULL,\n  `result` json DEFAULT NULL,\n  `previous_attempt_check_run_id` bigint(20) unsigned DEFAULT NULL COMMENT 'DataType:FKBID;ForeignKey:taxify_identity_verification.check_run.id',\n  `check_config_uuid` varchar(36) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `significance` enum('must_happen','optional') DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `flow_run_id_idx` (`flow_run_id`),\n  KEY `status_idx` (`status`),\n  KEY `created_idx` (`created`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=576287048 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4\n1 row in set (0.00 sec)\n\nmysql> RENAME TABLE `_check_run_gho_20260112083252_del` TO `_check_run_gho_20250112083252_del`;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected (0.00 sec){noformat}","2026-01-12T10:53:51.837Z"],["3802618","MKP-188","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Seemed too old to be still valid","2026-01-12T10:54:09.318Z"],["3802619","C2-275","C2","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] Cobra pre-compliance EMC testing was successful on {{2026-01-12}} More info in [this task|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/HWMISC/boards/2243?assignee=6215e9f275803500683497d5&selectedIssue=C2-440].\nThe samples should be sent out on {{2026-01-15}} But I will confirm this with Genfo.","2026-01-12T10:54:13.762Z"],["3802622","LSS-60870","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Please find the signed PoA for LV.\n\n[^PoA_SIA Bolt Services LV_Leila Mäll_12.01.26.edoc]\n\n","2026-01-12T10:54:44.123Z"],["3802623","LSS-60240","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:712020:4f73f350-0bf3-4887-9902-fd54848247b3] Can you please confirm that the heading is also correctly reflected in the translation?\n\nIf yes, then I’ll proceed with uploading them to the web.","2026-01-12T10:54:45.732Z"],["3802624","WFM-9949","WFM","bolajoko.kufoniyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Bolajoko Kufoniyi","!image-20260112-105444.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T10:54:52.204Z"],["3802627","LSS-56686","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] ! The documents will be sen on Wednesday","2026-01-12T10:56:00.078Z"],["3802628","LSS-61402","LSS","liis.miiter@bolt.eu","Liis Miiter","[^BOLT Operations NDA (Mutual)_Private person.pdf] _(112 kB)_","2026-01-12T10:56:12.670Z"],["3802629","LSS-61402","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nLiis Miiter has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-12T10:56:14.531Z"],["3802631","LSS-61389","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Bolt teenusleping taksofirmaga HC Dynamo Tallinn OÜ.asice]\n\n","2026-01-12T10:56:39.168Z"],["3802639","LSS-58830","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","Thanks all.\n\n[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] I have shared the document with the supplier - kindly grant them access - at the moment only Bolt employees have access","2026-01-12T10:57:27.644Z"],["3802640","WFM-9923","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Hey, WFM team, please provide them an access to the Business queues they request. Thank you!","2026-01-12T10:58:02.863Z"],["3802642","LSS-58510","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:0b391d02-6c8a-4494-99fd-3d2ff0d7ef37] ! I ve got a question regarding this sttement: “Strony zgodnie postanawiają, że ze względu na to, iż Bolt Rides PL Sp. z o.o. z siedzibą w Warszawie nie jest firmą produkcyjną, postanowienia dotyczące kontroli miejsca produkcji oraz konsekwencji z nią związanych, nie mają zastosowania do zawartej przez Strony Umowy świadczenia usług Bolt Business” \n\nWhere namely it needs to be added? In the end of the doc?\n\nMany thanks!","2026-01-12T10:58:25.267Z"],["3802643","SREDESK-7402","SREDESK","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Will be done soon","2026-01-12T10:58:35.758Z"],["3802644","LSS-61384","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Amendment agreement - Bolt Business Special terms_Bolt Operations OÜ_Swedbank_12.01.26.edoc]\n\nOnce getting this countersigned please send it to [contracts@bolt.eu|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] with a ticket number for archiving purposes and attach the document here for our own records.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T10:58:47.302Z"],["3802645","MKP-425","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","One day, to be rejected and restored as a dedicated activity","2026-01-12T10:58:52.924Z"],["3802647","WEBSD-1462","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:615c75e007ac3c0068114285] 👋 \n\nThis info is not under our Driver Guides because this is an article.\n\nYou can check [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/4] under : *Process and Content Update* request has been moved to CS Experience Service Desk: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2479|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2479|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T10:59:45.864Z"],["3802652","PFI-832351","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:573937f7-b8f1-45be-a6f4-bbcfe5632d63],\n\nThe information provided does not add up with the details that are visible to us.\nYou have escalated that the user with ID 290475144 is not able to log in, however, from the ride history it is visible that they have been making orders and cancelling them.\nPlease see the picture below:\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 12.55.21.png|width=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 12.55.21.png\"!\n\nThe related user that is hard-blocked is also blocked for order-cancellation fraud, seems like this user is doing the same, meaning that most likely they will soon be hard-blocked as well if they continue the same behavioural pattern.\n\nFrom the Fraud team side, there is currently nothing that is restricting the user.\n\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:00:22.850Z"],["3802660","MKP-287","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Potentially moved to be owned by Matching. Figure out actual state when the time is right","2026-01-12T11:01:40.121Z"],["3802661","SRED-1049","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Finished","2026-01-12T11:01:53.456Z"],["3802664","SREDESK-7345","SREDESK","yehor.naumenko@bolt.eu","Yehor Naumenko","Just set to 30 days now.\nWill set to 10 tomorrow. After tomorrow will set to 3 and will close the ticket.","2026-01-12T11:02:28.430Z"],["3802666","SRED-1049","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","ECK Cluster costs are lower by 30% comparing tro EC2 Based.","2026-01-12T11:02:29.903Z"],["3802667","LSS-61049","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[~accountid:628dd71cf2ee4a0069dfba72] here is the annex to the agreement including Bolt Send provisions: [Annex to Special Terms. Bolt Business_Antonínovo pekařství sro cs.docx|https://docs.google.com/document/d/14hsakzIQy_JjtYQS7EY2YHVhuY_l7ozP/edit]  Please verify the wording as this is a machine translation. Please let me know if you would like to proceed with signing and what is the preferred signing method (in case it will be signed electronically the other party's details will be needed – name & email). Thank you!","2026-01-12T11:02:31.019Z"],["3802668","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768215688815409]*{color}:\nHi <@U03P58BK5FY>,\n\nAre you the right person to help us implement the approach outlined above, or should this be handled by someone else from Billing / Finance?\n\n<@U08RWJ9TRAA>, from an Operations perspective, we can proceed with creating a dedicated compensation file where we:\n• Ensure clear and explicit labelling in the comments (non-revenue, out of scope / VAT 0%)\n• Include only deposit payback and offboarding-related cases\n• Strictly limit the use of this flow to those scenarios as a temporary solution\n• Document this as an exceptional workaround, pending a proper product fix\n[Here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1GW3Go9fNjoS2wfcnCadGlo4vPT6HSUWAvnAESkDxO_4/edit?gid=0#gid=0] is an example of the proposed file. However, before proceeding, we still need clarification on the following points:\n• Which adjustment subtype should be used for these cases? (Do we need to create a new one or use existing one?)\n• How can we ensure and confirm that these amounts do not flow into VAT reporting or impact revenue figures?\nThank you in advance.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T11:02:38.505Z"],["3802672","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Paula Espeja [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768215774105229]*{color}:\nHello <@U04FV4Z0GQ4> could you please check the queries below? I believe you have the visibility for this\n{quote}","2026-01-12T11:03:20.017Z"],["3802673","MKP-8768","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","[~accountid:5b839377eb18d0589b9b30d4] still working on it?","2026-01-12T11:03:46.873Z"],["3802679","C2-275","C2","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] Confirmed with Genfo that the samples will be shipped out {{2026-01-15}} ","2026-01-12T11:04:35.168Z"],["3802682","C2-440","C2","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","Samples will be shipped out from Genfo on {{2026-01-15}} ","2026-01-12T11:05:07.303Z"],["3802686","PC-4345","PC","roman.zavodskikh@bolt.eu","Roman Zavodskikh","Actually, the {{payment-payment-event}} [queue|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/27e6fdf9ce13b787b0cea94e7cf682adc8b936e0/gen/asyncApi/payment_core/PaymentEventSubscriberMqApi.ts#L12] is subscribed in a lot of places all about bolt-server repo. That is why *it does make sense to use SNS here* to ensure it the events are correctly delivered to all subscribers:\n\n* balance_user, [link|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/27e6fdf9ce13b787b0cea94e7cf682adc8b936e0/src/platform/commerce/balance_user/main/Bootstrap.ts#L773]\n* business_invoicing, [link|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/27e6fdf9ce13b787b0cea94e7cf682adc8b936e0/src/business/commerce/business_invoicing/main/payment_card/Bootstrap.ts#L33]\n* payment_reporting_globalpayments, [link|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/27e6fdf9ce13b787b0cea94e7cf682adc8b936e0/src/platform/payment/payment_reporting_globalpayments/main/Bootstrap.ts#L136]\n* fraud_data, [link|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/27e6fdf9ce13b787b0cea94e7cf682adc8b936e0/src/platform/commerce/fraud_data/main/payment_data/BootstrapSync.ts#L123]\n* invoicing_payment, [link|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/27e6fdf9ce13b787b0cea94e7cf682adc8b936e0/src/platform/commerce/invoicing_payment/main/Bootstrap.ts#L468]\n* payment_ledger, [link|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/27e6fdf9ce13b787b0cea94e7cf682adc8b936e0/src/platform/payment/payment_ledger/main/Bootstrap.ts#L86]\n* rental_billing, [link|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/27e6fdf9ce13b787b0cea94e7cf682adc8b936e0/src/rental/marketplace/rental_billing/main/Bootstrap.ts#L577]","2026-01-12T11:05:45.418Z"],["3802690","PFI-829598","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:75cc9b72-db8b-4dff-9671-3ed8fde897df],\n\nThe riders and businesses involved were confirmed to be fraudulent, therefore, most likely the driver collaborated with this fraudulent scheme, therefore, they should not be compensated any of the refunded fees.\n\nThe driver will not be suspended, as they still provide us with positive GMV and we lost nothing by this attempt that they tried.\n\nPlease note, that when answering the driver, they should not be accused of Fraud and what we found, this is all internal information.\nHowever, please do let them know that these funds will not be compensated in any form to them as ToS agreement was broken.\n\nThank you for your patience.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:06:10.384Z"],["3802692","MKP-2824","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Seemed too old to be still valid","2026-01-12T11:06:31.088Z"],["3802693","CCM-22267","CCM","edwina@bolt.eu","Edwina Thebe","Hi Toyosi, \n\nWe have enrolled you to the requested courses - they should now appear in your LMS. \n\nRegards, \n\nThe CS Training team ","2026-01-12T11:06:43.242Z"],["3802694","HS-28369","HS","ingrid.valgejarv@bolt.eu","Ingrid Valgejärv","no sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet","2026-01-12T11:06:43.383Z"],["3802695","CSXDL-147","CSXDL","robert.aavik@bolt.eu","Robert Aavik","Output: [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/46532|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/46532]\nImportant things: \n* the output contains only eater tickets, but it’s enough for now to compare the ROD tickets apples to apples. Important (as I understand) is to look at the share of ROD tickets from all.","2026-01-12T11:07:07.656Z"],["3802697","BD-1838","BD",null,"Vishal Arora","[https://rootly.com/account/incidents/148-delivery-fee-discounts-were-not-applied-resulting-in-overcharging-customers?tab=retrospective|https://rootly.com/account/incidents/148-delivery-fee-discounts-were-not-applied-resulting-in-overcharging-customers?tab=retrospective|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T11:07:32.265Z"],["3802700","BD-1838","BD",null,"Vishal Arora","Done","2026-01-12T11:07:39.923Z"],["3802702","MKP-2826","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Seemed too old to be still valid","2026-01-12T11:07:53.301Z"],["3802704","LSS-54244","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","+Update 12.01+: reviewed T&Cs and aligned with Elisabetta.\n\n+Next checks:+\n\n* with Ops to verify fonctionality;\n* with Privacy to verify data shared within the account.","2026-01-12T11:08:14.537Z"],["3802706","FRAUDOPS-1018","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","Vietnam launch has been cancelled so this ticket is no longer applicable. ","2026-01-12T11:08:20.639Z"],["3802707","PFI-831543","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Do they mean the invoices that were issued? ","2026-01-12T11:08:25.239Z"],["3802709","LSS-56917","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:712020:ef6a9562-f9aa-4bb5-a4d5-2b18cc77085b], I’ve already reviewed the updated Special Terms and left one question in the document - please have a look.\n\nI’ve also tagged [~accountid:63e354dd8978d7a4353ce08d] in the document regarding the amendments on exchange rates when billing. So [~accountid:712020:ef6a9562-f9aa-4bb5-a4d5-2b18cc77085b], before sharing our position with the customer, let’s please first wait for [~accountid:63e354dd8978d7a4353ce08d] input, thanks.\n\n\n[~accountid:712020:ef6a9562-f9aa-4bb5-a4d5-2b18cc77085b] taking into account the contract value, I believe this should be considered our final offer regarding the wording. I do not think that further negotiations on the contractual terms would be appropriate.\n\nPlease let us know whether the client agrees with the wording we have proposed.\n\n\nThank you.","2026-01-12T11:08:43.235Z"],["3802710","MKP-3147","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Seemed too old to be still valid","2026-01-12T11:09:06.079Z"],["3802714","MKP-4319","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","[~accountid:712020:5290f272-66ef-467e-a008-8904b3bc928d] probably something for Pricing Backlog?","2026-01-12T11:09:44.286Z"],["3802717","PAW-14781","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-njsc-db, pint-product-backend-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-12T11:10:11.624Z"],["3802719","HS-28781","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:63934c5900cb2fc3f98c7e44] the employees had the info to contact people ops, when they need to fill a new form. New document is added to our Box templates. Closing this ticket. Thank you!\n","2026-01-12T11:10:26.904Z"],["3802720","LSS-59809","LSS","joaomaria.silva@bolt.eu","João Maria Silva","Hi Mariana, The contract reviewed by Repsol.\nWill wait for your feedback.\n\n\n[^2026.01.09_Contrato Promoção_Bolt-Repsol Portuguesa rev. LegalBolt rev. LegalRPT.docx]\n\n","2026-01-12T11:10:28.576Z"],["3802721","MLC-657","MLC","shubham.sureka@bolt.eu","Shubham Sureka","[~accountid:712020:95d982df-1e72-4ba8-87c6-567f41fd157f] I don’t see your updates here, can you please add them on priority.","2026-01-12T11:10:34.412Z"],["3802723","WFM-9918","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","queue assigned","2026-01-12T11:10:54.683Z"],["3802725","TAXP-2304","TAXP","pedro.yaguezbovio@bolt.eu","Pedro Yaguez Bovio","A new CbCR notification shall only be submitted if the information differs from that provided in respect of previous reporting periods. The first CbCR Notification submitted in Belgium was for FY2023. As the information does not differ from what was provided for FY2023, the submission of the CbCR Notification for FY2024 is not required.","2026-01-12T11:11:36.632Z"],["3802728","MVRT-1450","MVRT","tiffany.irianto@bolt.eu","Tiffany Ainnurrahmi Irianto","[~accountid:614ad8fe47a8b5006f846ec4] Hi! You can target : \n\n* Tallinn\n* Tartu\n* Narva\n* Pärnu\n* Haapsalu\n\n\n\n","2026-01-12T11:12:19.387Z"],["3802729","HS-28512","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:8453f4ee-43dd-40c2-8a84-35e3b6958e51], employees were reminded for the second time before the end of the week, and no requests for the new form were received. Closing this ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-12T11:12:35.851Z"],["3802733","PFI-819091","PFI","joaomaria.silva@bolt.eu","João Maria Silva","Hey Team,\n\nAny updated here. The client really need this.\n\nThanks,","2026-01-12T11:13:09.995Z"],["3802734","DRX-25662","DRX","katlin.parl@bolt.eu","Kätlin Pärl","Hey [~accountid:637dde46a593cb822e941d5a] any updates regarding this change? ","2026-01-12T11:13:17.431Z"],["3802736","LSS-61168","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Thank you [~accountid:627121e402e1c10069bc7e0c] I confirm that the user is not entitled to the refund according to the T&Cs (specifically point 7.2.1. of the T&Cs states that Bolt may charge the user the full price of the order if the user is not at the delivery location within 5 minutes of the delivery partner's arrival). Please let me know if you require further assistance.","2026-01-12T11:13:25.448Z"],["3802738","PFI-830833","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","{color:#1F4E79}გამარჯობა,{color}{color:#1F4E79}{color}{color:#1F4E79}{color}  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n{color:#1F4E79}Please response.{color}{color:#1F4E79}{color}{color:#1F4E79}{color}{color:#1F4E79}{color}  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n{color:#1F4E79}პატივისცემით,{color}{color:#1F4E79}{color}{color:#1F4E79}{color} \n{color:#1F497D}{color}{color:#0093D3}{color}\n----\n{color:#0093D3}{color}{color:#1F497D}{color}{color:#1F4E79}{color} \n|  *{color:#2E74B5} *თიკო ბროლაშვილი/*{color}*  *{color:#2E74B5} *Tiko Brolashvili*{color}*  *{color:#2E74B5} *ბარათების მენეჯერი/*{color}*  *{color:#2E74B5} *Card Manager*{color}*{color:#2E74B5}{color}  *{color:#2E74B5} *მომხმარებელთა მხარდაჭერის განყოფილება*{color}**{color:#2E74B5} */*{color}**{color:#2E74B5} *Customer Support*{color}*  *{color:#2E74B5} *Department*{color}*{color:#2E74B5}{color} {color:#2E74B5}{color}  *{color:#2E74B5} *Tel*{color}**{color:#2E74B5} {color}*{color:#2E74B5}+(995 32) 2 27 27 37 (*{color}{color:#2E74B5}4{color}{color:#2E74B5}){color} {color:#2E74B5}{color}{color:#2E74B5}54{color}{color:#2E74B5}114{color}{color:#2E74B5}{color}  *{color:#2E74B5} *Mob:*{color}* {color:#2E74B5}+(995) 595 77 97 47{color}  *{color:#18355E} {color}* | |\n \n\n!image003.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T11:13:51.059Z"],["3802739","LSS-61404","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qzvvd65REC3GQJSns7J2MUQBypTgqg3_/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qzvvd65REC3GQJSns7J2MUQBypTgqg3_/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T11:14:05.351Z"],["3802740","PFI-827404","PFI","zoe.johnson@bolt.eu","Zoë Johnson","hi [~accountid:712020:1a99e337-a650-4a85-a8ed-f0825a04e850] could you support me here please?","2026-01-12T11:14:14.790Z"],["3802741","SREDO-336","SREDO","tonis.markus@bolt.eu","Tõnis Markus","Duplicate to SREDO-358","2026-01-12T11:14:19.165Z"],["3802742","WFM-9942","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Access requested [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541675|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541675]","2026-01-12T11:14:24.683Z"],["3802743","PFI-831768","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! For some reason the cash payment was added to balance a bit later (on the 29th). You can see on the screenshot that the cash payment for order 278248812 was applied to balance. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 13.11.45.png|width=948,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 13.11.45.png\"!","2026-01-12T11:14:25.922Z"],["3802744","MKP-4956","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","[~accountid:62e0e5ab3aaeedcae7561154] do you know if we still need this table? It has only inserts and never any reads?","2026-01-12T11:14:27.744Z"],["3802749","WD-22536","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:712020:240e5e60-baab-4e72-a388-591f4f4ec6a2] , I created this report for you “Bolt P2P - PO details”, please check does it fit your requirements 🙂 ","2026-01-12T11:15:09.314Z"],["3802750","LSS-61405","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","[^Bolt response to Kanyi Kiruchi & Co Advocates.pdf] _(133 kB)_","2026-01-12T11:15:20.290Z"],["3802753","PFI-832372","PFI","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 12.19.34.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T11:15:36.453Z"],["3802755","LSS-55676","LSS","weronika.ners@bolt.eu","Weronika Ners","Still in progress, I’ll send the comments today to the city offcials 🙂 ","2026-01-12T11:15:43.900Z"],["3802756","PFI-829905","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","{color:#172B4D}Добрый день, коллеги! Прошу Вас предоставить ответ по данному ЧБК с РРН  528101694278 528601093297 528601870966 528801745518 до 13.01.2026 года иначе сумма будет удержана с Вас. Ожидаем ответа. Благодарю!{color} \n----\n \n{color:#172B4D}{color}{adf}{\"type\":\"expand\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"  \"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"With respect,\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#172b4d\"}}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"  \"},{\"type\":\"hardBreak\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Ramazanov Bektemir Erikuly\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#172b4d\"}}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"  \"},{\"type\":\"hardBreak\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Dispute Resolution Specialist\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#172b4d\"}}]}]}],\"attrs\":{\"title\":\"Signature\"}}{adf}","2026-01-12T11:15:56.506Z"],["3802758","LSS-61227","LSS","taras.stomin@bolt.eu","Taras Stomin","Hello [~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] and [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] 🙂\nCan you please help me and advise on possible ETA on this matter, Universal bank is asking if there is any results already and I don’t want to mislead them with timing, appreciate your help) ","2026-01-12T11:16:01.475Z"],["3802760","PFI-832373","PFI","monika.civrag@bolt.eu","Monika Čivrag","!Slika zaslona 2026-01-12 u 11.51.20.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T11:16:12.049Z"],["3802761","LSS-59671","LSS","klaudia.bochenko@bolt.eu","Klaudia Bochenko","Hi, [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] I’ve reviewed your suggestions and incorporated the relevant changes into the [{color:#b3d4ff}*draft*{color}|https://docs.google.com/document/d/16AqvGX5ZMq0NqbzSTJhOhzH5A5f2vUjuthhyawXVbZU/edit?tab=t.fkxuosp14kg5]{color:#4c9aff}.{color} Is this version okay now? I also have a question: should we still respond as Bolt Rides, since the questions were addressed to that entity, or should we already respond as Bolt Poland, under which we currently operate?","2026-01-12T11:16:26.953Z"],["3802763","L10N-27288","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:51.693Z"],["3802764","L10N-27293","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:51.733Z"],["3802765","L10N-27300","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:51.758Z"],["3802766","L10N-27299","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:51.760Z"],["3802767","L10N-27291","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:51.784Z"],["3802768","L10N-27295","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:51.785Z"],["3802769","L10N-27294","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:51.819Z"],["3802770","L10N-27285","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:51.835Z"],["3802771","L10N-27290","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:51.829Z"],["3802772","L10N-27289","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:51.939Z"],["3802773","L10N-27292","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:51.969Z"],["3802774","L10N-27286","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:52.029Z"],["3802775","L10N-27287","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:52.028Z"],["3802776","L10N-27301","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:52.044Z"],["3802777","L10N-27303","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:52.134Z"],["3802778","L10N-27302","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T11:16:52.461Z"],["3802779","WFM-9950","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","[~accountid:712020:a5fe5124-0fb9-4d70-9825-65b9bec4bc53] ","2026-01-12T11:17:30.882Z"],["3802782","MKP-4956","MKP","aleksandr.leontev@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Leontev","[~accountid:5b306883ed67e12dd27645e1] I think we use them somewhere already, so that’s weird we don’t have any reads there 🤔 \n[~accountid:712020:c2b6ad0f-ebef-4615-8ab7-22b2786cdf4c] do you know which team in DriverX uses it perhaps?","2026-01-12T11:17:58.810Z"],["3802783","PFI-832359","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have investigate the case and could see the user had two failed payments with BLIK. \n\nFirst payment failed with an error message “TIMEOUT”. It seems there have been some connectivity issues with BLIK and the user should try again. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4028931476|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4028931476]\n\nSecond payment failed with an error message “ER_WRONG_TICKET”. I have checked with Adyen and received this response “The BLIK code did not match any code generated within the last 180 seconds. Ask the shopper to try again and to check that they are using a valid code.”\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4028983744|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4028983744]\n\nPlease ask the user to try again. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T11:18:10.824Z"],["3802784","MKP-9789","MKP","abdelhalim.machehalek@bolt.eu","Abdelhalim Machehalek","*@user-U064V574XDJ* can we allocate some time to fix this? Basically here in step 6 we want to _not_ send the offer to the same drivers again. In other words, if a driver saw the order once, they shouldn't see it again.\n\n{quote}1. we offered the same order with driver counter-offer options to multiple drivers\n2. multiple drivers picked the counter-offer price\n3. we chose driver with the lowest price (and if price is the same, with lower ETA)\n4. send the offer to rider, locking the chosen driver and releasing all other drivers (like the one in the example above)\n5. rider rejected the offer\n6. we send the offer to the driver who we released at step 4 but without counter-offer options (we have only 1 round of counter-offers){quote}","2026-01-12T11:18:18.909Z"],["3802785","MKP-9789","MKP",null,"Slack","[Abdelhalim Machehalek|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:5290f272-66ef-467e-a008-8904b3bc928d] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07UVPNKN1M/p1768216262140719?thread_ts=1768214020.439479&cid=C07UVPNKN1M|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07UVPNKN1M/p1768216262140719?thread_ts=1768214020.439479&cid=C07UVPNKN1M|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-12T11:18:19.861Z"],["3802786","GEORM-375","GEORM","kenneth.tenny@bolt.eu","Kenneth Tenny","[~accountid:5bc0b0839dce9f1069b478b7], I don’t think we need designs for this. Low effort. Ready to be picked up.","2026-01-12T11:18:26.569Z"],["3802787","HS-28715","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","[~accountid:712020:968f9b18-e4cc-4bff-b0fd-f9b52cc452f0] please let me know if there is anything I’m missing or should we close this ticket for now, thanks!","2026-01-12T11:18:27.633Z"],["3802789","WFM-9930","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","[~accountid:712020:a5fe5124-0fb9-4d70-9825-65b9bec4bc53] to assigne BU role instead","2026-01-12T11:19:16.866Z"],["3802790","HS-28776","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hi Jakub, thank you for letting me know. A new medical referral will be sent to his personal email today, so he can book it. Best!","2026-01-12T11:19:21.665Z"],["3802792","BP-9869","BP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","[~accountid:634684f353df3c0123201010] is it still valid? We have a follow-up task after your task, but as it almost 2 years old… Should we reject them all?","2026-01-12T11:20:00.085Z"],["3802793","PFI-832383","PFI","roksolana.stasiuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Roksolana Stasiuk","!Screenshot_2026-01-12-11-10-35-24_a405b311938ce8f3cf5e60bee460cd72.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T11:20:06.948Z"],["3802794","GEORM-423","GEORM","kenneth.tenny@bolt.eu","Kenneth Tenny","[~accountid:5bc0b0839dce9f1069b478b7], I think [~accountid:712020:ab1787cc-8432-4ebc-b628-abe39d0d6320] is working on this, right? Might want to change the status for this. ","2026-01-12T11:20:13.774Z"],["3802795","WFM-9725","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","DMed approver. awaiting response","2026-01-12T11:20:34.460Z"],["3802796","HS-28730","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb],\n\nCan you please print, sign, stamp and give/send [*this document*|https://bolt.box.com/s/jsxs5wpl1l2aw96tia8e0gb57vkdp9x4] to [~accountid:712020:741e7035-04c9-4583-9018-71712110af97]?\n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-12T11:20:35.149Z"],["3802803","WFM-9926","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","Registration via BH - Agent (Play mode only) already assigned","2026-01-12T11:21:39.727Z"],["3802804","LSS-58510","LSS","tomasz.symonowicz@bolt.eu","Tomasz Symonowicz","hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] - thanks for your reply, ideally it would be on the top of 2nd or 3rd page;","2026-01-12T11:21:46.650Z"],["3802806","GEORM-422","GEORM","kenneth.tenny@bolt.eu","Kenneth Tenny","[~accountid:5bc0b0839dce9f1069b478b7], I think we can move this to later. 😁 ","2026-01-12T11:22:02.044Z"],["3802807","LSS-58081","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","[~accountid:5d1b218591943f0d2ac52db0] In that case please share the SoW for Driver Capacity Building Courses. Thanks. ","2026-01-12T11:22:05.173Z"],["3802811","DSR-3655","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","All invoices sent to user, work profile not active ","2026-01-12T11:23:02.731Z"],["3802814","LSS-55531","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","Hi [~accountid:712020:52c03b81-3e44-455b-a71d-0e9088f7c7ad] can you advise who has taken over this case? Thank you!\n\ncc: [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] ","2026-01-12T11:23:31.487Z"],["3802817","RNTL-30307","RNTL","vinicius.ambrosi@bolt.eu","Vinicius Ambrosi","High level items:\n\n# Infrastructure required:\n## Text orientation/alignment is not vertically centralized anymore (RFC, BE, CE)\n# Adding the FAB button on home screen (BE)\n# Apply the design changes to screen (BE)\n\nEstimates:\n\n# Client: 1D\n# Backend: 4D\n\nOld Estimates:\n5d BE + 3D CI + 3D CA\n\nConsiderations:\n\n# iOS and Android render these pages slightly different - we are keeping it that way as it was agreed during kick off with designers, pms and managers","2026-01-12T11:24:18.169Z"],["3802819","PFI-832292","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\ndone, will apply tomorrow","2026-01-12T11:24:40.356Z"],["3802820","DELIVERY-1421","DELIVERY","antero.leedu@bolt.eu","Antero Leedu","26W3: Positive test results support global rollout. This improvement results in *an estimated CP increase by 247,000 EUR*.","2026-01-12T11:24:49.478Z"],["3802824","MLC-657","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","*Finland:*  \n\n* BU: HVO ja Promo codes - pending. \n* BU: Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Churn, Retention - LIVE\n* BA: Onboarding, Churn - LIVE\n* BA: Product Education, 0 orders, Awareness, HVO, Promo codes - pending. \n\n*Dubai:*\n\n* WP: Acquisition, Activation - LIVE\n* *Prio:* BA - in progress all stages - will launch by 16Jan\n* *Prio:* BU - in progress all stages - will launch by 16Jan\n\n*Angola:*\n\n* WP: Acquisition, Activation - LIVE\n\n*Moldova:* \n\n* WP: Acquisition, Activation - LIVE\n\n*New Zealand:*\n\n* WP: Acquisition, Activation - LIVE","2026-01-12T11:25:39.051Z"],["3802827","LSS-52225","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","T&Cs published: [https://bolt.eu/cs-cz/legal/tnc-drivers/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/cs-cz/legal/tnc-drivers/?category=rides|smart-link] \nComms sent on 5.01, planned entry into force: 22.01.2026","2026-01-12T11:26:10.294Z"],["3802828","PFI-826281","PFI","mariia.patrakova@bolt.eu","Masha Patrakov","Hi!\r\nCampaigns team has now fixed the bug","2026-01-12T11:26:15.386Z"],["3802829","WEBSD-1313","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","This section is new and goes under Road Tax renewal right?\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 13.23.48.png|width=647,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 13.23.48.png\"!\n\nscenario 2…\nscenario 3…\n\netc..\n\nI will include the FAQ because its different from what we have currently.\n\n\nIf you confirm this is correct I can move and make it happen in one day.\n\nPlease let me know your comments so we are in the same channel.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-12T11:26:21.236Z"],["3802830","LSS-61406","LSS","andrei.ivanov@bolt.eu","Andrei Ivanov","[^Bolt - Credits System_08012026.docx] _(448 kB)_\n\n[^Bolt_Credit System_08012026.xlsx] _(36 kB)_","2026-01-12T11:26:21.096Z"],["3802831","TAXP-790","TAXP","tung.lok@bolt.eu","Zip Lok","Hi [~accountid:61b9ad7c2900b00071da0b68], Mazars updated last week that the integration issue has been resolved and would proceed to compete the declaration.  I followed up earlier today to confirm on the submission status, will keep you posted.  Thank you.","2026-01-12T11:26:25.636Z"],["3802836","LSS-47809","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","[~accountid:5d1b218591943f0d2ac52db0] Have we received any reply back from them? Please let me know in case we are not going ahead with this partnership- I will then close the ticket. Thanks.  ","2026-01-12T11:27:25.780Z"],["3802837","LSS-61157","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:10c3f4ef-f975-47a3-8af8-927b01cd9521] yes, do we sign order form for trial?","2026-01-12T11:28:05.093Z"],["3802840","LSS-57822","LSS","alijan.dias@bolt.eu","Alijan Keval","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] \n\n# Each time contacts are changed as a way to deter fraud. At the time we are getting tickets that report fraud, so there are likely fraud cases happening that are being reported and go unnoticed, hence why we would want to do it everytime. \n# This change is usually executed by the CS team, so we would simply add an additional manual step.\n\n","2026-01-12T11:28:44.545Z"],["3802844","PFI-832372","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team is unfortunately not able to assist with pricing, discount or promo code related questions. \nPricing is decided by the vertical and the customer payments team does not have any impact on it. \nCould you please raise a ticket with the verticals technical support team instead. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2]\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:29:04.327Z"],["3802846","C2-450","C2","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[~accountid:5eb363355862510b794e3507] yes, the spring should be included. They will probably get rusted over time and while at it, it is good to replace.\n\nDo you have Cobra levers so you could test fit? ","2026-01-12T11:29:22.070Z"],["3802847","RNTL-30309","RNTL","vinicius.ambrosi@bolt.eu","Vinicius Ambrosi","High level items:\n\nSee the mapped work items in the story, no new scope for estimation.\n\nEstimates:\n\n# Backend: 4W\n# Client: nothing.\n\nOld Estimates:\n\n# Backend: 3W + 2D\n# Client: nothing.\n\nFurther out of scope:\n\n# City area icon location:\n## Some places have arbitrary icon placement (center, left, middle, de-centralized, etc) - this was not called out during any kick off meeting, so considering as out of scope until further validation\n# Border width changes and/or dynamic sizing:\n## Today the border has fixed 1px width and it doesn’t change any time","2026-01-12T11:29:25.674Z"],["3802848","LSS-61404","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hey [~accountid:712020:46ca1bd4-650e-4217-b42f-78a9deb502a3] I requested access ","2026-01-12T11:29:53.180Z"],["3802854","PFI-822312","PFI","daniel.petrea@bolt.eu","Daniel Petrea","Hello. \nCan you tell me if this ticket has been done?","2026-01-12T11:30:22.251Z"],["3802857","GEORM-424","GEORM","kenneth.tenny@bolt.eu","Kenneth Tenny","Started conversation here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08TCBJF4KY/p1768217414718299?thread_ts=1764775532.843439&cid=C08TCBJF4KY|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08TCBJF4KY/p1768217414718299?thread_ts=1764775532.843439&cid=C08TCBJF4KY|smart-link] \n\nWe can move this to later.","2026-01-12T11:30:38.781Z"],["3802859","LSS-58830","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:240e5e60-baab-4e72-a388-591f4f4ec6a2]  please share word document with the partner, we can’t grant external access to links from G-drives of the Legal team ","2026-01-12T11:31:01.757Z"],["3802861","WFM-9845","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","closing as there is no answer","2026-01-12T11:31:07.180Z"],["3802862","DSR-3663","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T11:31:07.205Z"],["3802863","PFI-817653","PFI","daniel.petrea@bolt.eu","Daniel Petrea","Hello. \nCan you tell me if this ticket has been done?","2026-01-12T11:31:15.328Z"],["3802864","HS-28851","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-12T11:31:28.780Z"],["3802865","LSS-61227","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:712020:b626c2f4-9efb-4dc8-8fce-d12835a10c67] did you aligned with [~accountid:712020:f591bec1-eb45-451b-8e04-31edceeaabd0] and/or [~accountid:5b4c96fbda498c2c21cb8544] on this matter already? \n\nWhat is the decision? I will gladly review this as soon as possible if approved by either of them. \n\nThank you. ","2026-01-12T11:31:40.801Z"],["3802866","CNT-339","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","Just as an update: the blog is in review with the editors, and the LinkedIn carousel design is in review with Design.","2026-01-12T11:31:42.625Z"],["3802868","FX-3603","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768217511471189]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3603] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T11:32:03.677Z"],["3802869","L10N-27306","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27305](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27305)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T11:32:03.998Z"],["3802870","L10N-27308","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27305](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27305)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T11:32:04.450Z"],["3802871","L10N-27311","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27305](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27305)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T11:32:05.783Z"],["3802