ates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27304](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27304)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T11:32:17.340Z"],["3802883","L10N-27319","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27304](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27304)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T11:32:17.417Z"],["3802884","L10N-27322","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27304](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27304)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T11:32:17.658Z"],["3802885","L10N-27323","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27304](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27304)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T11:32:18.778Z"],["3802888","WFM-9933","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-12T11:32:44.438Z"],["3802889","CNT-341","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","Just an update: the copy review deadline for the editors is today, now just waiting on the photos to finish the LinkedIn carousel design.","2026-01-12T11:32:53.765Z"],["3802890","PFI-831888","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! I see a 41.6€ adjustment done on 9.01 → is it for the same order? ","2026-01-12T11:32:54.823Z"],["3802893","MLC-3758","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","[~accountid:712020:6cf755e4-2536-45f4-814b-7e7ef0cdbd97] Yes, marked as complete now","2026-01-12T11:33:19.377Z"],["3802895","DRX-27879","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Described what to test in ticket description","2026-01-12T11:33:38.544Z"],["3802897","FX-3603","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768217620180239]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3603 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T11:33:52.142Z"],["3802899","PFI-832336","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nUnfortunately, the customer payments team is not able to assist with this case. \nWe don’t have access to the subscription page. \n\nThe Bolt Plus team decides when the payments are made. Could you please reach out to them for clarifications. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T11:34:22.508Z"],["3802900","PIF-3248","PIF","kristo.koert@bolt.eu","Kristo Koert","Unused clients of this kind are not causing _massive_ increases to code size today (~2k lines of dead code detected at one point). Though usage of internal private API clients has increased considerably recently. This lint would offload any mental bandwith around having to do cleanup and leaving it to tooling.\n\nA considerable value add would be exercising the *_pattern_* of [fast lint scripts|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/pull/3060#discussion_r2631836817] - using tools like rg to analyze the whole project in a few seconds to keep all manner of dead generated code from sticking around in the repo. This would mean considering this internal private API clients case as just a way to set up the *_pattern_* itself. We know we have bigger amounts of generated code that could also benefit from the same concept. Some question around the pattern:\n\n* How to structure such lints?\n* When to run such lints?\n* Pattern of “fast lints” (like using {{rg}} to quickly get a global view to then pass the relevant context to node for logic)","2026-01-12T11:34:24.113Z"],["3802904","LSS-55531","LSS","gauchar.alibayeva@bolt.eu","Gauchar Alibayeva","Hi [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] , \n\n[~accountid:61c2f85f90cfd20071570ff8] will take it over\n\nthanks\n\nGauchar","2026-01-12T11:34:42.946Z"],["3802905","WFM-9950","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Access requested\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601630|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601630]\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601631|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601631]\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571675|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571675]\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541676|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541676]","2026-01-12T11:34:43.168Z"],["3802907","PFI-832324","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-12T11:34:49.029Z"],["3802909","DRAG-713","DRAG","janeli.takk@bolt.eu","Janeli Takk","In review \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jk7v-X5KWYGUxzguP3fALDGm4xqSwG_d/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=104467463344987876651&rtpof=true&sd=true|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jk7v-X5KWYGUxzguP3fALDGm4xqSwG_d/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=104467463344987876651&rtpof=true&sd=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T11:34:57.147Z"],["3802911","PFI-832373","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:16feeee2-7721-43a0-8e2d-529b2d00b3e8],\n\nThis user was shortly created before trying to apply the code, additionally, they also tried to change destinations on multiple occasions.\nThis is a pattern used for destination change abuse, elevating the cost of the trip.\nThere are multiple red flags for this user, due to which we will not be whitelisting them nor making an exception.\n\nAs *internal information*, then one of the basic requirements is that the user and/or device is at least 30 days old when using a high-value voucher.\n\nAdditionally, from the logs I can see that for the second order they did not even try to apply the voucher, the attempt was only made on the first one.\n\nNow that the user has been on our platform for 30 days, now they would be able to use the voucher, however, the business would need to generate a new voucher for them, since our rules have disabled the initial voucher due to irregular activities.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any other questions regarding this matter. I will be closing the ticket for now, however, if you tag me within the ticket, then I can see the response and re-open the ticket if required.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:35:25.577Z"],["3802912","LSS-58912","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","Hei [~accountid:61268a403ef46a00706be25d] , we have obtained further information regarding this case, namely:\n- The case revolves around a driver who during a ride, stopped on a secluded road, stepped out of the car and then got on back on the back seat where he touched the female victim inappropriately (in intimate places), trying to convince her to have sexual intercourse. After a while, when she started crying, he brought her home;\n- The victim and the aggressor have known each other for the last 7 years and the victim called upon the driver for taxi services. It appears she called the driver directly, through an SMS and not through the app. The incident occurred apparently on *19.05.2025 around 2 AM, in a Skoda car licence plate number BC-12-BIW;*\n- The name of the driver is indeed Moraru Vasilica and the name of the victim Poraicu (former Pâslă) Alexandra-Nicoleta.\n\nSo, what would be needed now from external counsel currently addressing this court file, is to:\n- inquire if the victim did have a Bolt account?\n- details on the ride, if such was applicable and took place;\n- to investigate if the ride was registered in the app or completely off the books, and if yes who was the client. \n{color:#bf2600}Please treat this request as urgent!{color}\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex","2026-01-12T11:35:40.534Z"],["3802914","PFI-830931","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nthe change will apply starting tomorrow for companies in your list.","2026-01-12T11:36:11.368Z"],["3802915","DSR-3667","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T11:36:17.909Z"],["3802916","DSR-3665","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T11:36:18.172Z"],["3802917","MKP-9791","MKP","buin.dylgyrzhapov@bolt.eu","Buin-Dylgyrzhap Dylgyrzhapov","\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160382|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160382|smart-card]","2026-01-12T11:36:46.455Z"],["3802919","SUPX-2316","SUPX","artem.kudlaienko@bolt.eu","Artem Kudlaienko","Once solved, review alerting threshold for *WARNING :: customer-support-cron :: Interaction type invalidated*\nTriggered with value *202.05 >= 200* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C061Q2ULEU8/p1768216969035829|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C061Q2ULEU8/p1768216969035829|smart-link] \n\nI’ve updated it to higher value but eventually the change should be reverted","2026-01-12T11:37:03.803Z"],["3802922","BDB-1510","BDB","taaniel.malleus@bolt.eu","Taaniel Malleus","Can we swap the sub and main headline? Makes the discount bigger and more visible.\n\n\n!thaiwok_1080x1920.jpg|width=780,alt=\"thaiwok_1080x1920.jpg\"!","2026-01-12T11:38:24.762Z"],["3802923","PFI-832322","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe user has a negative balance of 48.53 PLN. \nThe balance debt was created because the users payment failed with an error code card.declined. \n\nSince we could not capture anything from the payment method then it’s not possible to refund to the Original payment method. \n\nUnfortunately, I’m not able to advise why the Bolt Balance refund was failing. I suggest to check it with the technical support team instead. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T11:38:30.062Z"],["3802925","GEORM-464","GEORM","kenneth.tenny@bolt.eu","Kenneth Tenny","Should we move this to later and create a task another Debug task for making the Prelive Driver app testing easier?","2026-01-12T11:38:56.959Z"],["3802927","CSXRD-138","CSXRD","aleksandra.menio@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Menio","Done as part of this ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2479/CSEX-280|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2479/CSEX-280|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T11:39:16.140Z"],["3802928","LSS-55531","LSS","miroslava.gorejova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Gorejova","Hi [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d]  - I will have a look on it next days","2026-01-12T11:39:33.752Z"],["3802931","WFM-9936","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-12T11:40:32.260Z"],["3802935","LSS-61404","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:46ca1bd4-650e-4217-b42f-78a9deb502a3] please find reviewed NDA \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qzvvd65REC3GQJSns7J2MUQBypTgqg3_/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qzvvd65REC3GQJSns7J2MUQBypTgqg3_/edit|smart-link] \n\nI accepted some comments from the supplier. \n\nPlease share document with supplier. \n\nIf all agreed please  send the agreement to [+ahto.kink@bolt.eu+|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu] and cc [+signing@bolt.eu+|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] (we will not be able to find the request without putting this email in cc)","2026-01-12T11:40:58.900Z"],["3802936","LSS-60589","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:f4038db4-c597-4af7-9604-402e9f17edd5], please could you share the signed agreement with TP? In order to move forward with the analysis we have reviewed the word agreement that you have shared.\n\n\n\n+*Situation Overview*+\n\n*Scenario 1 – €11,000 Payment to Incorrect Account*\n\n* TP failed to verify that the bank account (RIB) belonged to the driver requesting a Bolt account. The driver is partially responsible for providing the wrong document.\n* As a result, the €11,000 was directed to a third party in error.\n* These were funds from passengers to drivers, with Bolt acting only as an intermediary. Thus, Bolt only suffered a limited direct financial loss because of the 11K EUR, we only reimbursed the driver of the amounts owed by Bolt approx. 200 EUR.\n* The remaining amount is to be claimed by Bolt from the bank.\n\n*Scenario 2 – €13,000 Sent to Wrong Account and Repaid*\n\n* TP again failed to correctly input/verify account details. This was entirely the fault of the TP agent.\n* This led Bolt to send €13,000 to the wrong recipient. To ensure the rightful driver was paid, Bolt had to reissue another €13,000 from its own funds.\n* We are now pursuing recovery from the mistaken beneficiary via an instalment plan.\n* This error represents a direct financial loss to Bolt.\n\n\n+*Legal Position (available options)*+\n\n* *Breach of Contract*: TP was responsible under the SOW for verifying RIBs as part of its back-office services. Failure to do so is a breach of its obligations under Schedule 2.\n* *Liability for Losses* (Schedule 6): TP is contractually required to fully compensate Bolt for any loss resulting from its breach. This applies to the €13K in Scenario 2.\n* *Contractual Penalties*: Bolt may claim a penalty of up to €50,000 per breach if the claim is made within 60 days of discovering the breach.\n* *Scenario 1* does not trigger a damages claim, but still represents a *performance failure* relevant for service credits, contractual escalation, or governance review.\n\n\n+*Legal Recommendation*+\n\nThe decision on how to proceed is yours, but here below are some suggestions as to how to approach this:\n\n* if the business wants to maintain a good relationship with TP: enter into a governance meeting schedule with a service improvement plan + retainment of service credits for failed targets;\n* if the business wants to ascertain a stronger position: request a contractual penalty from TP → NB. 60 days from discovery breach;\n* if the business is no longer satisfied with the services provided and would like to terminate: document all breaches and follow termination procedure.\n\n\nPlease review the feedback and let us know your thoughts on this - what is your position regarding TP, are there any additional incidents that have not been flagged above, have you already engaged in any conversations with them regarding the fault on their part, is Bolt also in fault in these instances?\n\nHappy to discuss this further following your shared insights. \n\nThank you ! \n","2026-01-12T11:41:06.827Z"],["3802937","DSR-3669","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T11:41:07.031Z"],["3802938","FX-3585","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768218056990979]*{color}:\nIt seems that after redeploying the service from the develop branch, the memory consumption issue no longer occurs. I will close the task until new alerts appear.\n[link|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/k8s_views_node_ns/kubernetes-node-namespace-view?orgId=1&amp;var-datasource=PA11421A75E8A2F15&amp;var-cluster=All&amp;var-namespace=fleet&amp;var-resolution=$__auto_interval_resolution&amp;var-deployment=fleet-car-data&amp;from=now-3d&amp;to=now&amp;refresh=1m]\n\nLinked files:\n* [image.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A7Z5CL867/image.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-12T11:41:11.744Z"],["3802939","PFI-832023","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for CZK 109.90 on Dec 12, 2025, 22:06:25 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 15265675346003959339080  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 12th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_JZT6TNGG7L52KZQ9_QRRX5TM2CN996JX3.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:41:16.833Z"],["3802940","BEE-3602","BEE","michal.bielecki@bolt.eu","Michał Bielecki","[~accountid:5ff4436491bb2e0108d1548d] said to skip this one for now so i’ll unassign myself","2026-01-12T11:41:19.218Z"],["3802941","FX-3585","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768218087959319]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3585 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T11:41:43.453Z"],["3802942","WFM-9926","WFM","mwenesi.constantine@bolt-outsource.eu","Mwenesi Constantine","Hello [~accountid:712020:ddf1e045-1184-4210-9e73-da3ce949a13b] ,\n\nWhat about 11 REG_Canada_Driver Registrations?","2026-01-12T11:41:53.181Z"],["3802944","WFM-9930","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Outsource CS - Business (ID: 270179) role access requested \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601632|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601632]","2026-01-12T11:42:16.869Z"],["3802945","LSS-61227","LSS","taras.stomin@bolt.eu","Taras Stomin","Hi, I marked them here as a Business approvers, but then after Anna’s message I thought it goes to you, sorry, kinda new and not really familiar with all the processes. Dear [~accountid:712020:f591bec1-eb45-451b-8e04-31edceeaabd0] and [~accountid:5b4c96fbda498c2c21cb8544] can we please here you feedback?","2026-01-12T11:42:21.177Z"],["3802946","PFI-832022","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for EUR 3.85 on Dec 24, 2025, 12:59:46 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 15265675358002195114062  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 24th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_DML5925P7R2LGCQ9_NH9K9696BLDSK7R9.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:42:30.056Z"],["3802948","PFI-832021","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 400.00 THB on 27/12/2025, 09:36:40UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 27th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:43:08.611Z"],["3802951","PFI-832017","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for EUR 7.30 on Dec 22, 2025, 15:23:15 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 74987505356003360796084  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 22nd of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_Q47SDVZF5LR42XW3_M3CK63H8834RSBP9.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:43:54.287Z"],["3802952","LSS-52184","LSS","liis.valdsalu@bolt.eu","Liis Valdsalu","[~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] Hey! Could we move forward with the contracting?","2026-01-12T11:44:08.517Z"],["3802954","PAW-14126","PAW","mihai.casandra@bolt.eu","Mihai Casandra","Product team found a solution, nothing to investigate anymore.","2026-01-12T11:45:23.821Z"],["3802955","RS-1875","RS","sorina.mihai@bolt.eu","Sorina Mihai","Hey!\n\nSo can I confirm to the MP that we are working on it and will come back when we have something ready?\n\nThanks!\n\nSorina ","2026-01-12T11:45:31.195Z"],["3802958","LSS-29559","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hello, status update: \n\n* asked the external law firm (SKJB) for preparing a claim to the court.","2026-01-12T11:46:30.149Z"],["3802965","PIF-3270","PIF","kristo.koert@bolt.eu","Kristo Koert","This is a bug that should be easy enough to reproduce and somwhat reasonable to fix or at-least detect for explicit error. This is a devx problem, where users hit an edge case and would likely need to spend considerable time to figure out what the actual problem is from a messy error.\n\nHard to say how often this is encountered, but likely not super often as the Partial<Record<T>> pattern is neither super niche nor also super common.","2026-01-12T11:46:51.352Z"],["3802966","PFI-832397","PFI","anna.betina@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Betina","[^Payouts draft(2025) - Sheet1 (3).csv]","2026-01-12T11:46:54.641Z"],["3802967","LSS-59165","LSS","keoagile.malakalaka@bolt.eu","Keoagile Malakalaka","Good day everyone, we have not been able to track down the original ticket, and without it we can't prove for sure that the agent did not receive a signed consent form giving him authority to share any data. As we have very little to go by, do you think it would be wise to reach out to the insurer and ask them for the original thread where they interacted with us, so that we can receive some information to help this investigation? [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ","2026-01-12T11:47:25.752Z"],["3802968","LSS-60907","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed agreement attached.\n\n[^Amendment no. 1 to the cooperation agreement_Bolt Rides PL Sp. z o.o._3M Drivers Sp. z o.o._3M CARS&PARTS SP. z o.o._Kordian Sommer_01.12.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T11:47:33.198Z"],["3802969","RDS-1407","RDS","josef.kurchishvili@bolt.eu","Josef Kurchishvili","Just for context: I remember doing some analysis on B2B and I saw that these matches have a much higher acceptance rate for drivers but also a higher cancellation rate by riders (for the same ETA bucket)","2026-01-12T11:47:48.231Z"],["3802971","LSS-61401","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:625fb49cacc90500688166a5] - Kindly grant access to the document. Thanks!","2026-01-12T11:48:10.240Z"],["3802972","HS-28811","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Waiting for termination document","2026-01-12T11:48:19.539Z"],["3802974","PFI-827614","PFI","sofija.danilevica@bolt.eu","Sofija Daņileviča","Hey! Here is the report [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/47059|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/47059]\nPlease let me know if it is sufficient.","2026-01-12T11:49:42.018Z"],["3802976","LSS-60674","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:5cf40694-0837-4f72-b92a-c4936529065f], for adding comments. Both documents are now ready for sharing with the partner:\n\n* General Terms: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dJIwxQM3MZBaDbAZaMLLTjoDJGAUA31x/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dJIwxQM3MZBaDbAZaMLLTjoDJGAUA31x/edit|smart-link] \n* Special Terms: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ttJWp85IXqke23Ex1Vp9pALCLnDMO6Kg/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ttJWp85IXqke23Ex1Vp9pALCLnDMO6Kg/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T11:50:02.684Z"],["3802978","PFI-832394","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:16feeee2-7721-43a0-8e2d-529b2d00b3e8],\n\nYou are most likely right (with about 99.90% certainty) that this is fraud.\n\nWhat I can see from the order, is that this is most likely a destination change abuse case, however, we still need to let the order go through for a moment.\nWhat I would recommend as next steps:\n1) Let the payment through with the initial actual price, which was 1070€ as you have mentioned, however, leave a comment “*Destination changes not logged. Will try to charge, if it fails will refund.*”.\n2) Wait for roughly 5 minutes for the payment things to do their things. If after 5 minutes by clicking on the card payment you see that the payment failed, then fully refund the entire order (Driver at fault) with this sentence: “*PR. Payment failed, unable to capture full amount, refunded.*”\n3) I will be closing the ticket, however, after the payment fails, please *tag* me within the ticket confirming that they Payment failed, after that I will go and Fraud-block the user so that all their payment methods and devices get blocked and that no further users can be created.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:50:12.780Z"],["3802979","CSDT-951","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Enriching stops after backfill ","2026-01-12T11:50:30.396Z"],["3802980","SAI-1399","SAI","oleg.alieksieienko@bolt.eu","Oleg Alieksieienko","Let's continue here. During the implementation of SelfServe, we developed with Payments external API to be called when needed. Now, when we need to display Payemnts SelfServe with detailed information about a specific order, the question is: how often do you need this information? T\n\nThe Self Serve was intentionally designed to serve scenarios where a user asks something about pre-authorization. Initially, we thought of showing SelfServe directly from the chat, instead of a typical chat response.\n\nDo you think the data will be used frequently, or is it mainly for pre-authorization issues?","2026-01-12T11:50:30.899Z"],["3802981","MLC-3776","MLC","lorrayne.oliveira@bolt.eu","Lorrayne Corais","* Push notifications and Subject lines done :done: \n* Waiting for the new email templates \n\n[Storytelling content block tracker|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1_KCw7yKyw94lnrMloZ77llXJfF7fBhpv9ohYaSKiTAY/edit?gid=0#gid=0] ⬅️ ","2026-01-12T11:50:39.013Z"],["3802984","PIF-2338","PIF","alexandru.somai@bolt.eu","Alexandru Șomai","This functionality is already present. The request is partially approved, then applied if only some roles are approved and others are rejected from the request.","2026-01-12T11:50:55.251Z"],["3802986","LSS-61353","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Apologies, [~accountid:712020:a975e2d9-679b-4d8a-a063-b831aafacd02]! Access granted","2026-01-12T11:51:21.768Z"],["3802990","WD-22539","WD","stefanus.sunarja@bolt.eu","Stefan Sunarja","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 13.46.09.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T11:51:55.494Z"],["3802997","FDBT-4782","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-12T11:52:27.212Z"],["3803000","MM-917","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements are provided. The issue lacks sufficient information for a developer to start.|\n|Clarity|🔴|The summary is vague and there are no details or sections to clarify the scope or intent.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting information are present.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is provided in the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Clarify the scope and intent of the \"Filter configuration Action\".\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-12T11:52:56.592Z"],["3803010","ML-3701","ML","bogdan.dobrica@bolt.eu","Bogdan Dobrică","Resurfacing this one too.\nNot sure why [Granian|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNFKZGTC6/p1767104296346079?thread_ts=1767090768.181619&cid=CNFKZGTC6] does not work :slightly_smiling_face:","2026-01-12T11:53:50.472Z"],["3803011","ML-3701","ML",null,"Slack","[Bogdan Dobrică|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/638713e39341d1f136084f22] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNFKZGTC6/p1768214757250329?thread_ts=1767090768.181619&cid=CNFKZGTC6|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNFKZGTC6/p1768214757250329?thread_ts=1767090768.181619&cid=CNFKZGTC6|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-12T11:53:51.317Z"],["3803016","HS-28715","HS","maria.krygier@bolt.eu","Maria Krygier","Hello [~accountid:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db], Thank you for the explanation. One more question, If i get eligible for the additional 6 days of Vacation in July, do I get all 6 days, or less because it happens in the middle of the year?\n","2026-01-12T11:54:39.622Z"],["3803019","FX-3604","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768218865409079]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@chantel.rowe>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3604] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T11:55:08.077Z"],["3803020","LSS-61401","LSS","kristel.lokk@bolt.eu","Kristel Lõkk","[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] Please add a signature to this file instead (access shared with you)\n[https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JlrMLGEaX84FXp7hJG2gozUNENINkA9F/view?usp=drive_link|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JlrMLGEaX84FXp7hJG2gozUNENINkA9F/view?usp=drive_link|smart-link] \n\n(The file linked in the ticket is already signed, my apologies)","2026-01-12T11:55:17.307Z"],["3803021","BDB-1510","BDB","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","[~accountid:60a8d3053fae6f00681b708e] yes, it works 🙂 ","2026-01-12T11:55:23.371Z"],["3803027","DSR-3671","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T11:56:25.223Z"],["3803028","LSS-61352","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Thank you and happy New Year to you too, [~accountid:712020:a975e2d9-679b-4d8a-a063-b831aafacd02]!\nThe document looks good and we can proceed with signing. Can you please share the email address and name of a person signing the agreement from partner’s side?","2026-01-12T11:56:26.646Z"],["3803030","TS-4652","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","Current plan:\n\n* [~accountid:5f64663c91091700760d3051] is organizing meetings with Galina & Isabel on Rider Campaigns this week (W3, 12-16.01)\n* I am doing introduction & high-level tech support calls with all newjoiners W3, 12-16.01\n* [~accountid:622b24e0db58c100687e214a] will organize Supply Campaigns training calls next week (W4, 19-23.01)\n* This way week over week we will go through all the technical domain-specific trainings with both Galina & Isabel.","2026-01-12T11:56:28.136Z"],["3803031","PFI-832028","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:83a000cd-5967-452e-8bb6-d8947c29e435],\n\nThe card that they are trying to use does not match the country, therefore, the scheduled trips do not work for them. This is intended.\nPlease advise them to use another payment method, or let them know that scheduled booking is currently unavailable for them at this time.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:56:35.315Z"],["3803032","TS-4653","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","Current plan:\n\n* [~accountid:5f64663c91091700760d3051] is organizing meetings with Galina & Isabel on Rider Campaigns this week (W3, 12-16.01)\n* I am doing introduction & high-level tech support calls with all newjoiners W3, 12-16.01\n* [~accountid:622b24e0db58c100687e214a] will organize Supply Campaigns training calls next week (W4, 19-23.01)\n* This way week over week we will go through all the technical domain-specific trainings with both Galina & Isabel.","2026-01-12T11:56:38.487Z"],["3803036","FX-3604","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768219018767049]*{color}:\nUpdate: there were 2 suspensions for this company, one for the bank statement, one for expired ID. I cleared ONE of them and the notification that suspension had been lifted related to that, even though there was still another suspension... this is confusing, that alert shouldn't show that your'e 'cleared' if there's still another fleet suspension active\n{quote}","2026-01-12T11:57:11.317Z"],["3803041","PFI-832395","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:ce514ac3-7ca9-4bbc-978d-90297ad242e1],\n\nThe device UID suspensions have been lifted.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:58:07.618Z"],["3803042","LSS-61407","LSS","jasmina.hegerova@bolt.eu","Jasmina Hegerova","!lmdcvtc.jpg|width=740,height=1600,alt=\"lmdcvtc.jpg\"!\n\n","2026-01-12T11:58:12.211Z"],["3803043","PFI-832016","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for  450.39 UAH on  2025-12-23 14:36:02.\n\nPlease note that in the customers bank statement the original payment for 450.39 UAH is not displayed. \nIt could be possible the users bank has removed the fully returned payment from their bank statement. \nHere is the proof of refund which you can share with the customer. \n\n[^pay_info_reverse_2129889069.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-12T11:58:21.201Z"],["3803044","FDBT-4783","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-12T11:58:21.738Z"],["3803046","PFI-831219","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nso you need to create new Base fee calculator for a city?\n\nor you need to change a Company commission?","2026-01-12T11:59:02.401Z"],["3803049","WFM-9951","WFM","khritina.batova@bolt-outsource.eu","Khritina Batova","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 125934.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T12:00:02.638Z"],["3803051","PFI-831387","PFI","sasha.maletskaya@bolt.eu","Aliaksandra Maletskaya","FO has closed bank account 04.10.2024\nproof is attached\n\n!IMG_20260107_122227_855.jpg.jpg|width=3456,height=4608,alt=\"IMG_20260107_122227_855.jpg.jpg\"!\n\n","2026-01-12T12:00:09.567Z"],["3803052","PASD-169","PASD","stella.soosaar@bolt.eu","Stella Soosaar","Hey, got everything covered already, so this ticket can be closed and I’ll keep the relevant POCs in mind for future requests. Thanks George! 🙂 ","2026-01-12T12:00:13.076Z"],["3803053","PIF-3258","PIF","kristo.koert@bolt.eu","Kristo Koert","A devx betterment that would reduce confusion for people - neither a critical devx problem but also not a trivial one. Expectation is that some will already be familiar with the nuance, other will look up other such patterns and figure it out and last group will struggle and be confused. More junior and unfamiliar new devs are most impacted by it.\n\nMain upside to making the betterment - implementing should be easy. \n\nMain downside - causing wide ranging changes in bolt-server that need PR/merge ceremony.","2026-01-12T12:00:22.182Z"],["3803054","PFI-831336","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Created new Base Fee calcualtor.","2026-01-12T12:00:24.100Z"],["3803062","LSS-61407","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T12:01:52.132Z"],["3803067","BB-2162","BB","ilya.goryachev@bolt.eu","Ilya Goryachev","For the sake history: as discussed with [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574], the query is incorrect since it selects all the invoice rows 22 without respect to the country of the invoice row.","2026-01-12T12:02:20.164Z"],["3803069","L10N-27337","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27328](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27328)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T12:02:23.504Z"],["3803070","L10N-27335","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ens