pic here: [L10N-27328](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27328)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T12:02:39.992Z"],["3803083","L10N-27354","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27328](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27328)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T12:02:40.107Z"],["3803084","L10N-27362","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27328](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27328)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T12:02:46.542Z"],["3803090","DSR-3085","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048], I’ve compiled the data [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oN-gH7KejSrVV4tfWRF8AFG1REQsFo1PwpC5DjN-l0w/edit?tab=t.0], and below I’ve prepared the response to be sent. Could you review it to let us know if it’s good to go?\n\n*TEMPLATE TO BE SENT*\n\nDear Adam Hansson,\nThank you for your data subject request, which was received by us on *December 13, 2025*.\nAfter conducting a diligent search for records relating to your access request, we have confirmed that we do process the personal data requested. Data protection law entitles individuals to a copy of their personal data within the search scope – that is personal data, which identifies them, or enables them to be identified from it as a living individual person.\nAs you may be aware, the right of access under data protection law does not provide an individual with an absolute right of full access to any and all documents containing their personal data. For example, that right should not adversely affect the rights of others, including our trade secrets or intellectual property and, in particular, the copyright protecting the software. Furthermore, we must point out that if, after careful analysis, we conclude that our rights or the rights of others prevail, we will not be able to provide you with access to certain documentation where an exemption applies.\nWe will share copies of the personal data we hold about *you* to which you are entitled. This includes: \n* On what basis is linked the ride to the scooter, timestamps, logs.\n*Please refer to the information below regarding the basis*:\n_To enable micromobility rental service, a ride is linked to a specific scooter when the user unlocks a scooter through the app. At that moment, the scooter’s unique identifier is recorded and associated with the user’s account and a newly created ride session. All subsequent ride data (duration, distance, cost) is linked to that scooter via this identifier._\nFor information on how we process relevant personal data, we refer you to our Privacy Policy at *EDIT (choose):* [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy|smart-link]  */* [https://gethopp.com/en/privacy|https://gethopp.com/en/privacy|smart-link] , which includes further information about:\n* The categories of personal data we process;\n* The purposes for which we process personal data;\n* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom the personal data has been or will be disclosed;\n* The criteria we use to determine how long to retain personal data;\n* The sources of personal data received from other parties;\n* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making/profiling of personal data; and\n* Details of any transfer of your personal data to third countries or international organisations and the safeguards used for any such transfers.\nYour rights\nIn addition to your right to access any personal data we hold about you, you have the right to request us to rectify, erase your personal data, restrict the processing of your personal data or object to such processing. Any such requests that are received will be considered in conjunction with the applicable provisions of relevant data protection laws.\nIf you are dissatisfied with this response to your request or in relation to any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve them. You also have the right to complain directly to your data protection/supervisory authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek a judicial remedy.\nIf you have any additional questions, please contact our Customer Support Team by replying to this message.\nBolt","2026-01-12T12:03:39.167Z"],["3803091","PFI-832407","PFI","jasmina.vaclavkova@bolt.eu","Jasmina Vaclavkova","[^Malta Futsal manual adjustment - Sheet1 (1).csv]\n\n[^Mediahut manual adjustment - Sheet1 (1).csv]\n\n[^Pink October manual adjustment - Sheet1 (1).csv]\n\n[^Primary Healthcare.numbers]","2026-01-12T12:03:57.821Z"],["3803092","PFI-832407","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T12:04:00.117Z"],["3803095","LSS-61041","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team,\n\nAs a brief update:\n\nWe have submitted our creditor claim, which the bankruptcy administrator has confirmed as received.\n\nTur Taxi AS has informed us that the company was compulsorily dissolved by the Oslo District Court solely due to the lack of a registered auditor. According to both Tur Taxi AS and the administrator, the company has no debts, liabilities, enforcement cases, or disputes, and an approved auditor has now been registered.\n\nReinstatement requires either settlement of all creditor claims or written consent from creditors. As the company currently lacks sufficient liquidity, it is seeking creditor consent instead. All other creditors have already provided their consent — Bolt is the only remaining one.\n\nThe administrator has confirmed that granting consent does not prejudice Bolt’s position:\n\n* if reinstatement does not occur, Bolt retains its claim in the bankruptcy estate;\n* if reinstatement does occur, Bolt’s claim must be serviced by the company.\n\nThe plan is for the company to continue operations immediately upon reinstatement.\n\n*Accordingly, we need to decide promptly whether Bolt will provide its written consent to the company’s reinstatement. If approved, I will notify both the administrator and Tur Taxi AS by email.*\n\n\nCould you please confirm who within the team has the authority to make this decision? \nThanks! \n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:d3fd53e6-f124-4770-a577-b09d6688566f] [~accountid:6073f7ad9361560068adbda1] [~accountid:712020:228a835c-834d-4ca5-b7c2-ebedb4eb0356] [~accountid:712020:552b5d62-f64b-4147-b52a-d5178d160c21] ","2026-01-12T12:04:20.294Z"],["3803097","SREDESK-7404","SREDESK","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","For the future - if you need to flush multiple SQS - you can create one ticket with all of SQS mentioned in \"Additional details\"","2026-01-12T12:04:30.098Z"],["3803098","RNTL-30289","RNTL","vinicius.ambrosi@bolt.eu","Vinicius Ambrosi","High level items:\n\n# FF for new icons + new icons (BE)\n# Scooter default icon switch (no need for FF) in both BE and FE\n# FF in client for icon size (FE)\n\nEstimates:\n\n# Backend: 2D\n# Client: 2D\n\nOld Estimates:\n\n# Backend: 1D\n# Client: nothing.\n\nConsiderations:\n\n# We’ll keep icon sizing on client side only for simplicity right now - can be re-evaluated in the future","2026-01-12T12:04:33.245Z"],["3803099","RDS-1246","RDS","katharina.skolimowski@bolt.eu","Katharina Skolimowski","Question regarding desktop-mobile. How much do we see adding functions used on mobile? Asking how prominent to keep it in mobile - as we have shortage of (the top bar) space and need to figure that out.\n[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] [~accountid:712020:e854dae7-fb7f-4a9a-99f9-77c95efd3abc] ","2026-01-12T12:04:35.055Z"],["3803101","CNT-341","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","[~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] Thanks for the update! Photos will be taken on January 15, and as soon as I have them, I’ll share them with you.","2026-01-12T12:04:45.637Z"],["3803103","HS-28512","HS","sweta.sahu@bolt.eu","Sweta Sahu","Hello [~accountid:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d] ,\n\n\n\nSo do we consider that there are no changes and hence form 145 has not been filled?\n\nKind Regards\n\nSweta","2026-01-12T12:05:30.278Z"],["3803104","SREDESK-7404","SREDESK","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Queue flushed.\n\n\n\nState before: \n\n!image-20260112-120523.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260112-120523.png\"!","2026-01-12T12:05:47.538Z"],["3803105","CNT-339","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","[~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] This is awesome, can’t wait to share it! We’ll share it on LinkedIn and in the #lifeatbolt internal channel once it’s ready.","2026-01-12T12:05:55.522Z"],["3803106","CNT-339","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","[~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] would you be able to let James know to delete his doc, so there isn’t an old version left lying around anywhere? Thanks! ","2026-01-12T12:06:45.877Z"],["3803109","WFM-9941","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Hello [~accountid:642a97a99f314a0a30143c18], \r\n\r\nAgents added to the queue. \r\nHave a great day! ","2026-01-12T12:07:27.221Z"],["3803111","SREDESK-7405","SREDESK","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, state before (had only 9 messages):\n\n!image-20260112-120726.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260112-120726.png\"!","2026-01-12T12:08:00.147Z"],["3803114","WFM-9940","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Hey [~accountid:642a97a99f314a0a30143c18], \r\n\r\nThis was also done. \r\nHave a good one!","2026-01-12T12:08:12.642Z"],["3803119","SREDESK-7403","SREDESK","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Pending for CostCenter/codeowner clarification.","2026-01-12T12:08:44.552Z"],["3803128","LSS-56824","LSS","karolina.jedrzejczak@bolt.eu","Karolina Jędrzejczak","Hey Team,\n\nPoA for Bolt Rides (and Bolt Poland) needs to be signed by Mahmoud - they are checking it very carefully with KRS. \nI just came back from post office and they accepted only document signed with profil zaufany. They rejected document signed with SpotDraft.  \nDoes Mahmoud have profil zaufany? \n\n[^Pelnomocnictwo-pocztowe BOLT POLAND.pdf]\n[^Pelnomocnictwo-pocztowe BOLT RIDES (1).pdf]\n\n\nAlso please make sure that his name is not only on the signature but also in lines with ‘DANE MOCODAWCY’\n\nAttached please find updated PoA for Bolt Rides and Bolt Poland and confirmation of receiving PoA. \n\n[^Postal PoA Bolt Services.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T12:09:28.957Z"],["3803131","LSS-61123","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340840|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340840|smart-link]  ","2026-01-12T12:09:36.878Z"],["3803136","LSS-61401","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","[~accountid:625fb49cacc90500688166a5] - Would it be possible to amend Bolt Market EE OÜ to Bolt Store EE OÜ at the top of the document where the initial agreement has been mentioned so the document would be correct? ","2026-01-12T12:09:53.772Z"],["3803137","PIF-3276","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* The draft explains the change of removing the 'keys' command support to enhance Redis infrastructure reliability. Key missing information includes links to documentation or guides for further reading on the implementation details and impacts. Placeholders are used for these references to ensure completeness once the information is available.","2026-01-12T12:10:13.115Z"],["3803145","LSS-59896","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5eda5ad54ec4270ba37d2e87] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bolt Drive Cooperation Pilot Agreement_Bolt Operations OÜ_Drive on Holidays (Movida)_12.01.2026.pdf] ","2026-01-12T12:11:31.518Z"],["3803147","FIS-4185","FIS","ievgen.godun@bolt.eu","Eugen Godun","Blocked because of [https://fonoasupport.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/requests/27331|https://fonoasupport.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/requests/27331]","2026-01-12T12:11:54.196Z"],["3803149","BDB-1521","BDB","liisi.tamra@bolt.eu","Liisi Tamra","Hey! Based on learnings from the Oslo campaign, where QR codes performed better than manual promo code entry, I suggest using them to keep the copy as concise as possible. \n\n\nWALL POSTER\n_I also suggest keeping the same creative idea as in Oslo and using reflective material for the poster._\n\n*If you think this is a mirror,* \n*it’s time to head home.*\nScan the code and get your first Bolt ride $20 off.\n+ QR code\n\n\n\nTABLE TALKER\n_Maybe we could play with the idea of drunk texting here?_\n\n*Whenn yuor txts loook liek thiss...*\n*ride home with Bolt.*\nGet your first ride $20 off.\n+QR code\n\n\nCOASTER\n*Get home safe!*\n+ QR code\n\n\n[~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] lmk what you think :)","2026-01-12T12:12:00.057Z"],["3803151","FIS-4186","FIS","ievgen.godun@bolt.eu","Eugen Godun","Blocked because of [https://fonoasupport.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/requests/27331|https://fonoasupport.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/requests/27331]","2026-01-12T12:12:07.536Z"],["3803155","PFI-832384","PFI","saima.tubaite@bolt.eu","Saima Tūbaitė","Hi. The Fleet Owner does not receive payouts since the beginning of December and they have to pay money to the drivers, can we send the payout this week?","2026-01-12T12:12:57.252Z"],["3803157","PAW-14787","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-12T12:13:04.306Z"],["3803159","SFLEET-196","SFLEET","charles.franca@bolt.eu","Charles França","According to Bohdan, reports that show data results over time need to have filter Active Snapshot = True.","2026-01-12T12:13:26.059Z"],["3803162","LSS-58530","LSS","elena.skoutaridou@bolt.eu","Elena Skoutaridou","Hey do you have any updates on this? [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] ","2026-01-12T12:13:38.480Z"],["3803163","WFM-9709","WFM","joao.grossi@bolt.eu","Jo Grossi","Things seem to be working. Thanks a lot [~accountid:61268a40129802006ae93f05] and team! \n\n","2026-01-12T12:13:46.080Z"],["3803164","SFLEET-196","SFLEET","charles.franca@bolt.eu","Charles França","[~accountid:712020:a1e1cc21-901c-43ed-b15e-7737d865bb5c] to take screenshots of reports and add them to the task.","2026-01-12T12:13:52.432Z"],["3803165","MLC-2749","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","[~accountid:712020:d30129ff-7d6f-4bbd-82d3-3c1cbd5e1d77] Updated","2026-01-12T12:14:05.249Z"],["3803168","LSS-61085","LSS","maksym.goncharuk@bolt.eu","Maksym Goncharuk","Hi, [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] We have added counterparty to the Workday, now it most be available.","2026-01-12T12:14:09.548Z"],["3803169","SCM-813","SCM","zuzanna.antoniewska@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Izabela Antoniewska","Put on hold, as we were able to minimise cost due to approval proces and good explanation points. I dont see bigger value of deep diving more for now. ","2026-01-12T12:14:18.537Z"],["3803170","PIF-2266","PIF","kristo.koert@bolt.eu","Kristo Koert","The way things currently work, it seems like a bit of a foot gun. Developers need to spend mental bandwith and manually manage the database connection limits. Mistakes can cause outages and confusing errors that take time to investigate (think increased latencies not straight obvious errors).\n\nRISK: Over-automation in this case can also have tradeoffs if the implementation is over-opaque as to the details. This is compared to a PR with hardcoded values that gets reviewed and sanity checked in review. Depends on the specifics of the implementation, but expectation is still that this would be low risk and upside would be a significant reduction in toil.","2026-01-12T12:14:42.590Z"],["3803172","LSS-61386","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:8bcb68bd-f8da-4da1-8320-2536f6bb0c0c] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bolt_NR acct CRA auth for signature (cc8d0150-2625-4924-8065-744e565e36ff).pdf] ","2026-01-12T12:14:50.718Z"],["3803173","CSXSF-138","CSXSF","teele.raudik@bolt.eu","Teele Raudik","*Update:* \n\n* Mock SOP ready to review with SIS + Training (meeting tomorrow) \n* Will action all feedback after sync \n* Then, discuss with Tecla next steps to push for pilot ","2026-01-12T12:15:03.012Z"],["3803178","TAXP-790","TAXP","tiiu.albin@bolt.eu","Tiiu Albin","[~accountid:62ea2a695111209f4fde8265] thats great, thanks so much for the update! ","2026-01-12T12:16:15.371Z"],["3803180","LSS-58530","LSS","elena.skoutaridou@bolt.eu","Elena Skoutaridou","I would appreciate it if you could share the digital POA as soon as possible, as I need to submit it to the Electricity Authority of Cyprus for our deposit refund.","2026-01-12T12:16:39.883Z"],["3803181","PFI-832408","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T12:16:44.451Z"],["3803182","PFI-832409","PFI","nadiya.yasee-ngo@bolt-outsource.eu","Nadiya Yasee-Ngo","!image-20260112-121406.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260112-121420.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T12:16:47.708Z"],["3803184","PASD-169","PASD","george.matu@bolt.eu","George Matu","Thank you for your understanding and maybe we will be able to help you next time.","2026-01-12T12:17:08.941Z"],["3803185","L10N-27232","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.641Z"],["3803186","L10N-27236","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.668Z"],["3803187","L10N-27234","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.704Z"],["3803188","L10N-27243","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.758Z"],["3803189","L10N-27241","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.824Z"],["3803190","L10N-27231","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.843Z"],["3803191","L10N-27240","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.853Z"],["3803192","L10N-27245","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.880Z"],["3803193","L10N-27246","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.887Z"],["3803194","L10N-27233","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.888Z"],["3803195","L10N-27237","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.900Z"],["3803196","L10N-27244","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.943Z"],["3803197","L10N-27235","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.976Z"],["3803198","L10N-27247","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:12.992Z"],["3803199","L10N-27249","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:13.007Z"],["3803200","L10N-27248","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:13.066Z"],["3803201","L10N-27242","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:13.113Z"],["3803202","L10N-27220","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:20.740Z"],["3803203","L10N-27228","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:20.752Z"],["3803204","L10N-27238","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:20.747Z"],["3803205","L10N-27230","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:20.850Z"],["3803206","L10N-27222","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:20.844Z"],["3803207","L10N-27239","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:20.989Z"],["3803208","L10N-27227","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:21.040Z"],["3803209","L10N-27229","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:21.184Z"],["3803210","L10N-27226","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:21.318Z"],["3803211","L10N-27224","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:22.899Z"],["3803212","L10N-27223","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:23.095Z"],["3803214","L10N-27219","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:26.483Z"],["3803215","L10N-27217","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:26.870Z"],["3803216","L10N-27221","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:26.890Z"],["3803217","L10N-27218","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:26.912Z"],["3803218","L10N-27215","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:26.959Z"],["3803219","L10N-27225","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:26.986Z"],["3803220","L10N-27216","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:27.197Z"],["3803221","L10N-27214","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:17:27.256Z"],["3803222","LSS-61357","LSS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey,\n\nApologies for the slight delay but here’s what Workiva wrote to us and the amended documents are attached for your review. \n\n_Please find two documents attached for your review._ \n\n[^Bolt Operations OU Amendment Contract 052924-22741 Price Guarantee 20260109 V0.pdf]\n[^SO FOR Modification order_ Bolt Operations OU - Carbon - 122325-62712 20260109 V0 (1).pdf]\n\n_Once we get your green light, I can share via Cogna to your e-signature._\n\n_As agreed, you will notice_\n\n* _2 year term with first segment being at a reduced price for both Carbon and Sustainability_\n* _2 year price lock_\n\n_Please let me know if you have any questions or concerns._\n\nSigning ticket is also ready and on hold til your review. [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61358|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61358|smart-link] \n\nThank you! 🙏 ","2026-01-12T12:17:28.593Z"],["3803231","DRX-28074","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Please check new order pushes appearing","2026-01-12T12:18:25.454Z"],["3803232","LSS-61356","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] ! The document has been signed.\n\nMay you please send the executed document to [*contracts@bolt.eu*|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] with the ticket number.\n\nMany thanks!","2026-01-12T12:18:31.018Z"],["3803235","PIF-3276","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is well-defined and addresses a clear problem with the use of the 'keys' command in Redis. To slightly improve, the acceptance criteria could include specific metrics or tests to ensure the correct implementation, such as verifying no blocking operations are occurring post-implementation or confirming system reliability improvements. Including a clear monitoring or testing strategy will enhance specific acceptance criteria. Clarifying the exact transition strategy or schedule might also increase clarity.","2026-01-12T12:19:08.594Z"],["3803237","PFI-832414","PFI","ibrahim.alhadi@bolt.eu","Ibrahim Alhadi","!Promo 2.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Promo.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T12:19:13.739Z"],["3803240","PFI-832415","PFI","nadiya.yasee-ngo@bolt-outsource.eu","Nadiya Yasee-Ngo","!image-20260112-121904.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260112-121910.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T12:19:35.741Z"],["3803244","PFI-831543","PFI","wallace.araujo@bolt-outsource.eu","Wallace Jhonatan Mendonca De Araujo","Hey, Ketlin. Hope you are doing okay.\n\nThis Courier Fleet Owner wants to know why in December they have received such a higher discount based on fee that they are deducted from Bolt as partner. \n\nThe invoice range is of the December 15th to 21th.\n\nBeing honest I think it’s higher due to the demand that we faced last month, it was a great month to ask for deliveries. However, if they claims something and OPS ask us to escalate for you, I think maybe there’s an issue with the fee.\n\nWould you please tell me if it’s really elevated in the case of percentual of the tax/fee (as an increase from Bolt) or if it's higher than the others weekly reports due to demand? \n\nWeird because Courier OPS have the same access for us and still brought the matter for FD hallways. Waiting for your answer. \n\n","2026-01-12T12:20:50.128Z"],["3803245","CCM-22268","CCM","ademola.oloja@bolt-outsource.eu","Ademola Oloja"," I have access to Delivery Admin","2026-01-12T12:20:54.705Z"],["3803246","PFI-832416","PFI","nadiya.yasee-ngo@bolt-outsource.eu","Nadiya Yasee-Ngo","!image-20260112-122108.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260112-122114.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T12:21:47.079Z"],["3803247","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Adding additional instance for switch:\n* [https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15346|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15346]","2026-01-12T12:21:48.256Z"],["3803250","WFM-9943","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-12T12:22:12.828Z"],["3803252","LSS-54833","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:2f68ebec-bff7-4acf-a855-0eeaf1c88737], I have reviewed their comments and suggestions and added a few from my side. Can you please have a look at them? Thank you!","2026-01-12T12:22:37.122Z"],["3803254","RNTL-30342","RNTL","vinicius.ambrosi@bolt.eu","Vinicius Ambrosi","Things to consider from backend:\n\n# FF micromobility_initial_zoom - very straight forward \n## If this value diverges from homepage, there’s movement anyway\n## Anything other than 16 will have movement\n# FF mm_clustering_ignore_rules - clustering (ofc)\n# city area {{zoom_range_id}} - when to render city area or not\n\nScope:\n\n# Zooming out when no vehicle around until it finds one - 1W\n\n\n\nPausing for now until Kaisa discusses with Aleksei.","2026-01-12T12:22:50.907Z"],["3803258","LOC-3503","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","Report HERE: [https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/17SB-CFGKU_Y7o-zPDjTEOhAkW4AHvX-WLjjPRWAFNz0/edit?slide=id.g38c09f379d6_0_632#slide=id.g38c09f379d6_0_632|https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/17SB-CFGKU_Y7o-zPDjTEOhAkW4AHvX-WLjjPRWAFNz0/edit?slide=id.g38c09f379d6_0_632#slide=id.g38c09f379d6_0_632|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T12:23:27.081Z"],["3803263","PFI-832418","PFI","nadiya.yasee-ngo@bolt-outsource.eu","Nadiya Yasee-Ngo","!image-20260112-122331.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260112-122337.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T12:24:11.724Z"],["3803264","LSS-54833","LSS","roisin.kirk@bolt.eu","Roisin Kirk","Thank you I think I have responded to the ones I’m tagged in.  Appreciate your work on this.  Let me know if I’ve missed any comments","2026-01-12T12:24:13.416Z"],["3803265","PFI-820892","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","I’ve changed Bolt Alesund fleet company to 10% commission starting from 13.01.2026. \n\nI now see that there is a [company based fleet created on 06.01.2026 |https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/262906?tab=profile]→ does that also need changing? Please confirm all fleet ids that need changing. ","2026-01-12T12:24:15.331Z"],["3803273","LSS-61411","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nSudipto Das has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-12T12:25:25.888Z"],["3803275","PFI-831543","PFI","wallace.araujo@bolt-outsource.eu","Wallace Jhonatan Mendonca De Araujo","Sorry, I have a typo. It’s January 15th to 21th. \n\nI’ll keep the demand way of thinking as well. ","2026-01-12T12:25:33.832Z"],["3803277","LSS-61386","LSS","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","Thank you!","2026-01-12T12:25:43.558Z"],["3803280","PFI-832421","PFI","nadiya.yasee-ngo@bolt-outsource.eu","Nadiya Yasee-Ngo","!image-20260112-122540.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260112-122546.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T12:26:08.554Z"],["3803283","PFI-820892","PFI","lasse.norgaard@bolt.eu","Lasse Duang Nørgaard","Thank you! Yes, please change that fleet.","2026-01-12T12:26:21.123Z"],["3803284","FPD-1420","FPD","anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu","Nastya Serebryannikova","I had discussions with [~accountid:712020:abc9fd59-ced8-4834-8627-722844558f0d] and [~accountid:6274fd88d7fd480068da636a] and we agreed that the current state of the validation should be enough for now and is sufficient for rolling the spreadsheet out. We need to see how the users would interact with the spreadsheet and and whether it would be used at all; based on this information, we will evaluate whether it’s necessary to enforce additional validation to prevent the users from entering incomplete or incorrect data. With this, I’m closing the ticket and marking it as done. ","2026-01-12T12:26:28.033Z"],["3803287","LSS-61405","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340859|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340859|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T12:26:56.455Z"],["3803289","WFM-9952","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Agent’s profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/21556?tab=settings|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/21556?tab=settings]\nID: 21556\n\nCurrent roles: OPS Outsource (Compliance) (ID: 240206) • OPS Outsource (Private) (ID: 57) • Beehive Rides OPS Agent (ID: 66)","2026-01-12T12:27:00.818Z"],["3803291","LSS-60959","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:114d9986-23af-448c-97ee-3686f141b0a3] – happy new year! I’ve been redirected back to you re issues with restoring the access. [~accountid:712020:7318e6cb-1341-4810-9653-b6398a38985e] mentioned she’ll pick it up separately with you on the issue that the driver is being redirected to a new [+driver lead account+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/driver-registration/driverRegistrations/edit/25015780?tab=details&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=America%2FToronto] that was created on 12/25 instead of their existing Driver account where access was restored. \n\n\n\nFrom Privacy side, we just need to confirm that access to the Driver account was restored and fill out internal documentation and then I can close the ticket.","2026-01-12T12:27:18.388Z"],["3803293","SREDESK-7398","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi Sofija,\n\nCan you please elaborate which engineering team referred you to this service desk form to ask for S3 access?\n\nAt the moment, only {{tax_report_generator_job_role}} and {{dap-group-billing-analyst}} system roles have permission to such directories and I don’t see any engineer with such access.\n\nPlease ask the related engineering team to plan adding this feature to the admin panel or follow the guide to get temporary S3 access.\n\nAWS comes with its own complexity and such features should be added to the Admin panel.","2026-01-12T12:28:12.501Z"],["3803294","MLC-1564","MLC","shubham.sureka@bolt.eu","Shubham Sureka","[~accountid:6336b241a84c7f79c387c386] I believe we can now close this task?","2026-01-12T12:28:20.497Z"],["3803298","CRC-2339","CRC","emre.cakmak@bolt.eu","Emre Can Çakmak","[update] Billing changes are ready. Invoices validated by Tax.","2026-01-12T12:28:59.101Z"],["3803299","WFM-9951","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, OS Restricted sites manager role in Assembled granted","2026-01-12T12:29:15.706Z"],["3803300","MLC-3821","MLC","shubham.sureka@bolt.eu","Shubham Sureka","[~accountid:712020:95d982df-1e72-4ba8-87c6-567f41fd157f] Please add the updates with more information here.","2026-01-12T12:29:17.139Z"],["3803301","FPD-1419","FPD","anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu","Nastya Serebryannikova","The PR was merged, the script can be found here:\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/blob/master/incentives/financial-planning/special_events/load_special_events.py|https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/blob/master/incentives/financial-planning/special_events/load_special_events.py|smart-link] \n\nThe databricks job that triggers this script is here and is run daily at 9 PM:\n\n[https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/33439583715162/runs?o=2472566184436351|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/33439583715162/runs?o=2472566184436351]","2026-01-12T12:29:37.719Z"],["3803302","CRC-1581","CRC","emre.cakmak@bolt.eu","Emre Can Çakmak","[update] Local team testing is in progress in order to validate fiscalization.","2026-01-12T12:29:59.366Z"],["3803304","RDS-1246","RDS","katharina.skolimowski@bolt.eu","Katharina Skolimowski","[~accountid:557058:666f23d7-c932-426d-a8de-4951fd310358] Are we planning to add “Create ride” to the scope as well? [~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] ","2026-01-12T12:30:16.682Z"],["3803307","LSS-61321","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340864|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340864|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T12:30:38.290Z"],["3803308","GRWA-1480","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","* PRs: [+dbt+|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15278], [+airflow+|https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9682]\n* Testing the new update [+here+|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/537853161560777/runs/1109499315701161?o=3598988355446810]\n\nThe pipeline is running smoothly now.","2026-01-12T12:30:49.406Z"],["3803314","MLC-1564","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","[~accountid:712020:d30129ff-7d6f-4bbd-82d3-3c1cbd5e1d77] Yes!","2026-01-12T12:31:46.846Z"],["3803315","L10N-27248","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:32:14.023Z"],["3803316","L10N-27246","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:32:14.117Z"],["3803317","L10N-27240","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:32:14.237Z"],["3803318","L10N-27238","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:32:14.242Z"],["3803319","L10N-27249","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:32:14.252Z"],["3803320","L10N-27241","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:32:14.270Z"],["3803321","L10N-27245","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:32:14.302Z"],["3803322","L10N-27247","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:32:14.315Z"],["3803323","L10N-27244","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:32:14.343Z"],["3803324","L10N-27236","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T12:32:14.356Z"],["3803325","L10N-2