g!","2026-01-12T12:32:28.833Z"],["3803358","L10N-27375","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27365](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27365)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T12:32:29.513Z"],["3803359","L10N-27376","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27365](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27365)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T12:32:30.698Z"],["3803362","MLC-3821","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","Content checked by project and ops team, sent for editorial review (due date 13.01), in progress. Will send to translations after. \nWe need customer attributes rather than events, Tudor will help. ","2026-01-12T12:32:36.737Z"],["3803363","RISK2-2991","RISK2","galina.matunova@bolt.eu","Galina Matunova","this needs to be confirmed by Legal, but the issue might get resolved soon ","2026-01-12T12:33:04.912Z"],["3803364","WFM-9949","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello [~accountid:64181e3d1273131f2ae1b51d],\n\nPlease reply using this template format so we can assist with the request:\n\n*Company:* [Insert company name]\n*Market:* [Insert market/region]\n*Function:* [Insert CS/OPS]\n*Access Duration:* [e.g., Specific Time Range / Permanent]\n*Task Description:* Describe what the admin access/role is needed for, add relevant admin and KB links(CS)]\n*Bolt Email(s) of Agent(s):* List all agent's Bolt emails either here or attach a file. NO screenshots ","2026-01-12T12:33:09.251Z"],["3803367","DLVR-341","DLVR","victor.garces@bolt.eu","Víctor Garcés","Update 12 Jan 2026\n\n[Product]: We have faced a problem where some of the merchants have churned from using DineOut because they couldn’t find a way how they could conveniently reconcile discounts in their POS systems without having to cancel pre-bills and generate the new ones (or having to get special admin access to be able to edit pre-bill, which most managers don’t want to provide). This has urged us to consider exploring alternative flows (i.e. claim-redeem voucher flow) back in November, whereby restaurants would not have to worry about editing pre-bills. This [research|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WyKGxoe8vk-Sr959SzvW0z7JLEZ4yjRBgr7F02GCkOs] has been finalized by Legal and Tax teams at the end of the year. While we don’t rule out a possibility that in near future we may switch to that alternative flow, today we still have reasons to believe our current flow could long-term work out as long as we find solutions to problems that are causing merchant churn risks among other things. *One of such solutions that we are considering to execute in coming weeks is to switch some restaurants to run cashback-based rewards, as opposed to discounts-based rewards.* The idea here is to have Bolt pre-fund cashback reward to customers’ Bolt Balance and then recharge the cost as marketing service (with VAT in localised countries or reverse charge in non-localised) to restaurants. Such approach wouldn’t require restaurants to apply any discounts to the POS and would thus make both initial staff training, as well as ongoing DineOut operations more seamless. We haven’t done that before in Bolt Food but we can draw a parallel with how we launched Bolt Plus, whereby on weekly basis we would add manual invoice rows to restaurants for the recharged cashback. +I have already received+ [+confirmation+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ooWnz7Y4po-S4H-87ZkPXv06N_vJyxDikQgdOW93urA/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.xtfrstd1mcay] +from Tax team that recharging cashback is feasible and most tax-compliant setup; however, I am still missing input if anything should be done about our T&Cs for us to be able to go ahead with execution as early as this month.+\n\nProduct Tax, Legal and VAT to discuss the above to move forward with the topic. Stakeholders tagged in Slack thread for continuation. ","2026-01-12T12:33:28.248Z"],["3803370","WFM-9948","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello [~accountid:64181e3d1273131f2ae1b51d],\n\nPlease reply using the template below:\n\n*Company:* [Insert company name]\n*Market:* [Insert market/region]\n*Function:* [Insert CS/OPS]\n*Access Duration:* [e.g., Specific Time Range / Permanent]\n*Task Description:* Describe what the admin access is needed for, add relevant admin and KB links(CS)]\n*Bolt Email(s) of Agent(s):* List all agent's Bolt emails either here or attach a file. NO screenshots ","2026-01-12T12:33:58.174Z"],["3803374","LSS-61285","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340866|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/340866|smart-link]  ","2026-01-12T12:34:27.229Z"],["3803376","WFM-9947","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello [~accountid:64181e3d1273131f2ae1b51d],\n\nPlease reply using the template below:\n\n*Company:* [Insert company name]\n*Market:* [Insert market/region]\n*Function:* [Insert CS/OPS]\n*Access Duration:* [e.g., Specific Time Range / Permanent]\n*Task Description:* Describe what the admin access is needed for, add relevant admin and KB links(CS)]\n*Bolt Email(s) of Agent(s):* List all agent's Bolt emails either here or attach a file. NO screenshots ","2026-01-12T12:34:45.303Z"],["3803380","WEB-9826","WEB","elina.heno@bolt.eu","Elina Liina Heno","The documentation of the properties of the input field is [here|https://www.figma.com/design/g0TPpE9SyhDZcsxVwl7L96/WTK-3.0-%E2%80%A2-SILK?node-id=4075-25274&t=A5FmOrwo38N18glt-1]\n\nThe link to the prototype is [here|https://cash-lab-51034202.figma.site]","2026-01-12T12:35:01.926Z"],["3803381","RISK2-2995","RISK2","galina.matunova@bolt.eu","Galina Matunova","need a sync with [~accountid:712020:95b78488-64d1-4339-8cfa-92c573553913] , a roadmap needs to be created; otherwise, local OPS are not using the document correctly","2026-01-12T12:35:12.659Z"],["3803382","RDS-1406","RDS","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","[~accountid:5ccc34a5326cf40e4549d40d] maybe you can take a look how many tickets we get with this request and what improvements (e.g. tooling, or policy) CS would need to tackle them better?","2026-01-12T12:35:14.114Z"],["3803384","WFM-9946","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello [~accountid:64181e3d1273131f2ae1b51d],\n\nPlease reply using the template below:\n\n*Company:* [Insert company name]\n*Market:* [Insert market/region]\n*Function:* [Insert CS/OPS]\n*Access Duration:* [e.g., Specific Time Range / Permanent]\n*Task Description:* Describe what the admin access is needed for, add relevant admin and KB links(CS)]\n*Bolt Email(s) of Agent(s):* List all agent's Bolt emails either here or attach a file. NO screenshots","2026-01-12T12:35:20.967Z"],["3803385","LSS-60959","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] tagging you for visibility → no action required. We have a phishing wave in Canada.\n\n\n\n*Usual approach:*\n\n\n\n# Investigate BH ticket and narrative → someone disguising as Bolt employee tricks Driver to share their OTP by which they gain access to their account and they kick the original owner out\n# Tag tickets with Canada_Driver_Phishing for easier record keeping\n# Ensure that CS restored access to the Driver and that no other changes were made (if changes were made, e.g. payout details changed, etc. ensure CS helps the Driver to rectify)\n# Internal Documentation: we fill out [Cognito Data Breach Risk assessment|https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyo%C3%BC/personaldatabreachriskassessment/1-all-entries] and [WF in ODPO channel|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0678KJ49UH]","2026-01-12T12:35:42.259Z"],["3803386","WFM-9945","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello [~accountid:64181e3d1273131f2ae1b51d],\n\nPlease reply using the template below:\n\n*Company:* [Insert company name]\n*Market:* [Insert market/region]\n*Function:* [Insert CS/OPS]\n*Access Duration:* [e.g., Specific Time Range / Permanent]\n*Task Description:* Describe what the admin access is needed for, add relevant admin and KB links(CS)]\n*Bolt Email(s) of Agent(s):* List all agent's Bolt emails either here or attach a file. NO screenshots","2026-01-12T12:35:44.314Z"],["3803387","WFM-9944","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello [~accountid:64181e3d1273131f2ae1b51d],\n\nPlease reply using the template below:\n\n*Company:* [Insert company name]\n*Market:* [Insert market/region]\n*Function:* [Insert CS/OPS]\n*Access Duration:* [e.g., Specific Time Range / Permanent]\n*Task Description:* Describe what the admin access is needed for, add relevant admin and KB links(CS)]\n*Bolt Email(s) of Agent(s):* List all agent's Bolt emails either here or attach a file. NO screenshots","2026-01-12T12:36:03.693Z"],["3803389","DSR-3673","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T12:36:17.888Z"],["3803391","MLC-1378","MLC","robert.pirnuta@bolt.eu","Robert-Mihai Pîrnuță","*Update*: FI has been launched on Monday, {{2026-01-12}}","2026-01-12T12:36:35.595Z"],["3803392","PIF-2840","PIF","alexandru.niculae@bolt.eu","Alexandru Niculae","Clarification: using {{CURRENT_TIMESTAMP}} for the places where date is set to Date.now() in JS; just pointing out that it is worth checking weather the current abstraction might be also used for setting specific times instead of the current time, in which case those must continue to be supported too\n\nScores:\nTime criticality: 5 (in one Q)\nRisk reduction: 3 (impacts more than 2 teams, but in really a security fix)\nBusiness Value: 2 (devs will use it -or benefit from it- from time to time)\nJob size: 2 (1-2 days)\nOpportunity: 3 (Workflows SDK is tier 4)","2026-01-12T12:36:49.839Z"],["3803393","LSS-55496","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","In regard to deductions from Connected Accounts: \n\nIn our Rides - [Hopp Drivers T&Cs for CA|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VdDcsBNs-h-LYkOd9hYoYMAfpqDrox8V751UfZpf1Vs/edit?usp=sharing] we have identified and suggested to remove the following: \n\n* Clause 9.6. \n* Clause 10.3.3.\n* Clause 10.4.\n* Clause 15.3\n\nThe right from Platforms (Bolt/Hopp) to deduct funds from Connected Accounts (Airwallex wallet) was already removed by Airwallex from the Connected Account Agreement (see here). \n\nAfter making this change to the Drivers T&Cs, it is to be determined if we need to amend the MSA with Airwallex in this sense. This is to be confirmed by them. \n\ncc [~accountid:61addb80b0b630006a695081] [~accountid:712020:f5c52198-9bb5-40b8-865d-70e96f6ccf5a] [~accountid:712020:f07ce685-1b60-4571-98ae-08c611861c25] [~accountid:6285ef56bd640f0068aeb51b] ","2026-01-12T12:36:56.897Z"],["3803394","PRODSEC-658","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","Hey hey, please complete task asap or move to [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRODSEC-694|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRODSEC-694|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T12:37:00.282Z"],["3803397","LOC-4714","LOC","miranisa.ollennu@bolt.eu","Miranisa Wallace-Ollennu","SOW  Document - [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H2o6J_ugrM_ej8slXCJAbC_NrClvFeaxRTB1xmAGgM8/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.m7xwqcjrlx6p|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H2o6J_ugrM_ej8slXCJAbC_NrClvFeaxRTB1xmAGgM8/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.m7xwqcjrlx6p|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T12:37:24.928Z"],["3803398","LSS-61363","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hello, [~accountid:712020:fa964ec4-f58a-4774-ae52-ae37590db000] ! Thanks for DM responses to my question on this matter. As I said, we have no grounds to compensate him in the amount of PLN 100 (approx. EUR 25). So for now, let’s propose him promocode. For any other compensation grounds like a transfer of money we must have more evidences that he would really have suffered that time due to driver’s cancelation (even justified). What he wrote in the letter, seems to be insufficient for such amount he proposed. ","2026-01-12T12:37:32.055Z"],["3803399","BP-13403","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Tested on Prelive for all 4 scenarios:\n\n*AC:1* (/) \n\n*To or From* \nWhen the policy type is “To or From permitted locations”\nThen the ride is allowed if *either the first pickup or the last drop-off* is in the permitted locations list\nAnd intermediate stops do not need to be validated\n\n*AC:2* (/) \n\n*Only From*\n\nOnly the *first pickup* must be in the allowed list\n\n*AC:3*  (/) \n\n *Only To*\n\nOnly the *last drop-off* must be in the allowed list\n\n*AC:4*  (/) \n\n*Between*\n\nAll stops must be in the allowed locations list (Same as current behaviour)","2026-01-12T12:37:37.350Z"],["3803400","PTWS-2125","PTWS","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","Main issue is that some of the data is from OneModel (unsure if it has a public API, need to talk to Kristo about this) and that there are actual screenshots in the report, which I am not sure Make or n8n can attach. This can possibly be resolved by creating charts/tables via the Google Docs API.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.32.46.png|width=806,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.32.46.png\"!","2026-01-12T12:37:43.242Z"],["3803402","SREDESK-7383","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi Kyrylo,\n\nI granted your permission via [*this PR*|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15347].","2026-01-12T12:37:45.826Z"],["3803403","PRODSEC-586","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","Hey hey, please complete task asap or move to [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRODSEC-694|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRODSEC-694|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T12:37:47.693Z"],["3803404","LSS-60730","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","Please can you send me a copy of the fully signed Transcom agreement?\n\nPlease can we upload all signed contracts to Spotdraft?\n\nCogs MSA and SOW should be ready for signature today, I will update here when ready. \n\nThanks","2026-01-12T12:38:11.335Z"],["3803406","LSS-61367","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Hi [~accountid:5dde532fcdc2d20d05377446] No problem. I will close this ticket. Thanks ","2026-01-12T12:38:18.540Z"],["3803408","PRODSEC-593","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","Hey hey, please complete task asap or move to [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRODSEC-694|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRODSEC-694|smart-link] . If this is no longer an important task, please reject.","2026-01-12T12:38:26.562Z"],["3803411","WFM-9949","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Agent’s profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/21820?tab=settings|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/21820?tab=settings]\nID: 21820","2026-01-12T12:38:50.600Z"],["3803412","PRODSEC-502","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","Task is currently not needed.","2026-01-12T12:39:02.119Z"],["3803413","LSS-61049","LSS","jan.uhlir@bolt.eu","Jan Uhlíř","Thanks! I’ve replied in the Slack group chat for visibility.\n\n","2026-01-12T12:39:18.281Z"],["3803414","WFM-9948","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Agent’s profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/21838?tab=settings|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/21838?tab=settings]\nID: 21838","2026-01-12T12:39:39.599Z"],["3803417","RISK2-806","RISK2","galina.matunova@bolt.eu","Galina Matunova","[~accountid:6328384efedc6169aed38521] is the POC","2026-01-12T12:40:02.126Z"],["3803418","WFM-9947","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Agent’s profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/18713?tab=settings|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/18713?tab=settings]\nID: 18713","2026-01-12T12:40:11.853Z"],["3803419","WFM-9946","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Agent’s profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/17866?tab=settings|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/17866?tab=settings]\nID: 17866","2026-01-12T12:40:50.037Z"],["3803420","LSS-61363","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Background: the client was +not+ charged with the ride price by Bolt as the ride has been cancelled by the driver (unjustifiably). ","2026-01-12T12:40:54.609Z"],["3803421","PFI-832424","PFI","kornwika.pattana@bolt-outsource.eu","Kornwika Pattana","!1768189420598.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_20260112_191532.jpg.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260112-123750.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T12:41:03.205Z"],["3803422","WFM-9945","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Agent’s profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/232725?tab=settings|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/232725?tab=settings]\nID: 232725","2026-01-12T12:41:25.894Z"],["3803423","WEB-9087","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:712020:e8f2de02-6346-4839-a1e5-fc656f320d5e] \n\nCould this ticket be closed, or is there anything else still expected from our side?","2026-01-12T12:41:35.747Z"],["3803424","LSS-54833","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Thanks a lot [~accountid:712020:2f68ebec-bff7-4acf-a855-0eeaf1c88737]!\n\n* I have reviewed IWG’s comments and suggestions, included mine and accepted theirs, where applicable.\n* One minor thing - can you please check my comment on section 3.4 before sending it to IWG? Not sure we are fine with disclosing our product capabilities.\n\nOtherwise, from my perspective, [the agreement in its current state|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dYx_XAB3R-JLuLXygvqfp1zAw7y2fhLh/edit] may be sent for IWG’s review. Let me know if you have any additional questions.","2026-01-12T12:41:38.294Z"],["3803425","PAW-18454","PAW","alexandru.niculae@bolt.eu","Alexandru Niculae","Clarification: the risk of a bad actor altering live services without any approval is serious and it must be mitigated\nScores:\nTime criticality: 8 (in one month)\nRisk reduction: 8 (improves the security in more than two services)\nBusiness value: 1 (rare journey)\nJob size: 3 (up to a week, because i remember there were opposing view of how this has to be implemented to those opinions should be reconciled)\nOpportunity: 5 (Service Runtime is tier 3)\n","2026-01-12T12:41:49.447Z"],["3803427","WEB-9052","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf3033a882e2be49d95a] \n\nCould this ticket be closed, or is there anything else still expected from our side?","2026-01-12T12:41:52.220Z"],["3803428","WFM-9944","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Agent’s profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/19433?tab=settings|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/19433?tab=settings]\nID: 19433","2026-01-12T12:42:05.147Z"],["3803429","WEB-9088","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:620102dfeaf9e200707370ef] \n\nCould this ticket be closed, or is there anything else still expected from our side?","2026-01-12T12:42:05.625Z"],["3803430","LSS-61159","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a], I see that the issue was resolved in the main ticket. Please loop me in once the team will make a decision to proceed with the supplier after the trial.","2026-01-12T12:42:12.153Z"],["3803431","WDFT-3417","WDFT","wenjing.zhang@bolt.eu","Grace Wenjing Zhang","Adding a new update also in the ticket:\n\n* [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] will merge 2 logics into one chart to track nonrecoverable cost sources - use “tax country” for regular cost and “supplier ID” for intercompany cost due to different system setups. Then add this view into dashboard.\n* [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] will collect all reports related to dashboard and add them under “Bolt Tax“ in WD\n\nCC: [~accountid:62bd9335018dea0d40751f4b] ","2026-01-12T12:42:16.494Z"],["3803433","WEB-9100","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:712020:dde115d4-4c0b-4866-a241-b3e21f211df3] \n\nCould this ticket be closed, or is there anything else still expected from our side?","2026-01-12T12:42:38.076Z"],["3803434","WEB-9101","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:712020:dde115d4-4c0b-4866-a241-b3e21f211df3] \n\nCould this ticket be closed, or is there anything else still expected from our side?","2026-01-12T12:42:46.558Z"],["3803441","PFI-832015","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team is unfortunately not able to assist with pricing, discount or promo code related questions. \nPricing is decided by the vertical and the customer payments team does not have any impact on it. \nCould you please raise a ticket with the verticals technical support team instead. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2]\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-12T12:43:58.471Z"],["3803442","PTWS-2113","PTWS","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","Created a new Google Sheet containing managers who are enrolled in the final module of the Manager Onboarding learning plan on Docebo, which contains enrollment date and completion date, as well as email. Populated the sheet via a Make automation that runs an API call to Docebo to get enrollments on the course, as well as their status (completed, enrolled, in progress). This will run daily to add people who have been enrolled as of the day the automations runs on (i.e new managers are added to the course during the day on the 13th of Jan and the automation runs on the 13th Jan at 8 PM and adds them to the tracking sheet). Next, there will be another automation that runs weekly which will check that the completion date is later than the current date - 1 week and remove people who are caught in this filter from the #manager-onboarding channel.\n\nOnly issue is that the people tech bot cannot add/kick people from channels currently, due to missing permissions. Need to check in with IT about this.\n\nedit: figured it out, the issue wasn’t that the bot was in the channel, but the user the bot was trying to remove had already been removed, but slack returns a generic error “not_in_channel” when this happens, which seems to refer to the bot, not to the user itself.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.39.52.png|width=899,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.39.52.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.38.32.png|width=884,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.38.32.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.38.45.png|width=884,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.38.45.png\"!","2026-01-12T12:44:14.590Z"],["3803444","FPD-1133","FPD","anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu","Nastya Serebryannikova","The feature is ready for being rolled out to the users.\n\n# [Special Events Spreadsheet|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1b_DtmqObaoRhlNDV4iK5p8u3MNPjzAIpRd18bYPFXuc/edit?usp=sharing] - the spreadsheet that the users should use for adding / editing the special events for the respective city / country\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/TwGQsgE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/TwGQsgE|smart-link] - the instruction for the users on how to use the spreadsheet\n# [Databricks job|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/33439583715162/runs?o=2472566184436351] that reads the events from the spreadsheet daily and stores them in spark under {{dev_incentives.special_events}}\n# the latest list of special events can be queried as follows:\n{noformat}SELECT *\nFROM dev_incentives.special_events\nWHERE ingestion_timestamp = (\n    SELECT MAX(ingestion_timestamp)\n    FROM dev_incentives.special_events\n);{noformat}\n# [script|https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/blob/master/incentives/financial-planning/special_events/create_special_events_spreadsheet.py] that was used for the initial population of the special events spreadsheet (not meant to be reused unless we lose all the data somehow)","2026-01-12T12:44:22.994Z"],["3803445","PFI-830905","PFI","wisdom.salaou@bolt-outsource.eu","Wisdom Delphine Salaou","Hello , is there any update for this case please","2026-01-12T12:44:38.561Z"],["3803448","HS-28715","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hi, you will be eligible to 6 days extra, it does not matter when you gain eligibility 🙂 ","2026-01-12T12:45:53.872Z"],["3803449","BP-12847","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","\"Remember this device\" feature [BP-12847|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-12847] in :thread:","2026-01-12T12:45:58.430Z"],["3803450","BP-12847","BP",null,"Slack","[Kristyna Mertova|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02AS5W6K52/p1768221804615399?thread_ts=1768221804.615399&cid=C02AS5W6K52|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02AS5W6K52/p1768221804615399?thread_ts=1768221804.615399&cid=C02AS5W6K52|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-12T12:45:59.355Z"],["3803452","BP-12847","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[@uladzislau.tsyrkunou|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:0559a7fa-2c87-497d-957a-02b7de3945e1] It feels as a small feature to have spec channel, so let's keep talking here for other's visibility. If we see that there is more discussion needed, let's move to a channel.","2026-01-12T12:46:00.724Z"],["3803453","BDB-1510","BDB","taaniel.malleus@bolt.eu","Taaniel Malleus","Cool, files here [https://www.figma.com/design/6dZXVE5nxhKXto9NJRe6HG/Bolt-Food---Bolt-Market-Ad-hoc?node-id=2879-1106|https://www.figma.com/design/6dZXVE5nxhKXto9NJRe6HG/Bolt-Food---Bolt-Market-Ad-hoc?node-id=2879-1106|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T12:46:04.737Z"],["3803454","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Nazrin Nasibova [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768221953662999]*{color}:\nHelloo,\n&gt; 2. Ensure these compensation types are clearly labelled as *non-revenue* and *out of scope / VAT 0%*.\nSince compensation_tax is 0% VAT in DK, all types of adjustment invoices will also reflect 0% VAT. However, if compensation VAT were, e.g, 20%, we do not currently have a tax rate separation by subtype logic and that would become an issue.\nOne more thing caught my attention: why are almost all companies named Bolt Rides DK ApS? While reviewing compensation and commission invoices, the flow appears to be → .\nIs this something that has been agreed upon? <@U090E7WNXUG> <@U04FV4Z0GQ4>\n\nLinked files:\n* [Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.43.58.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A7QEEDP9V/screenshot_2026-01-12_at_14.43.58.png]\n\n* [Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.44.04.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A7ZGDN54K/screenshot_2026-01-12_at_14.44.04.png]\n\n* [Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.44.28.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A7QEFGDRV/screenshot_2026-01-12_at_14.44.28.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-12T12:46:09.197Z"],["3803455","PAW-14790","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160389\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 12:46:11 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T12:46:11.863Z"],["3803456","LSS-61412","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T12:46:18.050Z"],["3803457","LSS-61357","LSS","alex.bucse@bolt.eu","Alex Bucșe","[~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257]  just a quick mention once we get the “go” from [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] . We usually accept supplier e-signature solution so I think Conga should also be fine, but remember that this should be signed by Ahto/authorised signatory. (they said “your” e-signature so I just mentioning that they do send it to you, as I have seen in the past cases of people signing contracts they were not authorised to sign) Mentioning just in case!\n\nAlternatively we can just sign ourselves using Spotdraft/DocuSign and send it over to them for their countersignature. (in case legal/legal ops have an issue with Cogna, their e-signature tool)","2026-01-12T12:46:25.995Z"],["3803459","PIF-3224","PIF","alexandru.niculae@bolt.eu","Alexandru Niculae","Clarification: e2e tests failures should be treated as serious as other tests so it’s worth making them visible and if they are flaky they must be fixed rather than hidden\n\nScores:\nTime criticality: 3 (in two Q)\nRisk reduction: 5 (reduces risk in more than 2 teams)\nBusiness value: 5 (devs will use regularly)\nJob size: 5 (1-2 weeks)\nOpportunity: 3 (admin panel is tier 4)\n","2026-01-12T12:46:56.113Z"],["3803460","BP-12847","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","Note\nAgreed to require 2FA and override \"remember this device\" if we or admin log the user out.\n\n{quote}I checked the code and according to it user is logged out very rarely, we perform refresh token cleanup every *180 days of inactivity,* when for an access token (which is being updated through the refresh token) the expiry time is *5 minutes*.\n\nBut there are nuances:\nThe user can be logged out by the administrator, the user can log out themselves, or if the user clears their browser cache (\n• VPN changes\n• Browser settings clearing cookies/storage on exit\n• Privacy extensions (Privacy Badger, uBlock Origin, etc.)\n• Incognito/Private browsing mode\n• Browser updates forcing cache clear\n• Multiple browser profiles switching\n)\nIn this case, they will have to log in again.{quote}","2026-01-12T12:47:12.894Z"],["3803461","BP-12847","BP","uladzislau.tsyrkunou@bolt.eu","Uladzislau Tsyrkunou","Good call, I'll create a tech document as well, we can discuss implementation aspects there as well.","2026-01-12T12:47:28.798Z"],["3803462","MKP-9422","MKP","andre.tamm@bolt.eu","Andre Tamm","Updated Confluence as well - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/1622645185/Cancellation+Fee+Summary|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/1622645185/Cancellation+Fee+Summary|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T12:47:36.604Z"],["3803464","LSS-61413","LSS","mitch.aniebonam@bolt.eu","Mitch Aniebonam","[^DOC180624-18062024125733 (1).pdf] _(7.67 MB)_","2026-01-12T12:48:19.509Z"],["3803466","CCM-22268","CCM","ademola.oloja@bolt-outsource.eu","Ademola Oloja","I would like this to be enabled for me under Instructor as I am a Trainer.\n\n","2026-01-12T12:49:10.470Z"],["3803468","CCM-22268","CCM","ademola.oloja@bolt-outsource.eu","Ademola Oloja","[~accountid:5eda5ad37d0c0f0ab21f155b] I would like this to be enabled for me under Instructor as I am a Trainer.\n\n","2026-01-12T12:49:36.344Z"],["3803469","RDS-1246","RDS","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:712020:505aebee-5cf4-438e-8909-a5524bd7a634] see here, you can play around - over 50% of these actions are undertaken on mobile, so i think yes [https://eu.mixpanel.com/s/4ebCzZ|https://eu.mixpanel.com/s/4ebCzZ|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T12:50:27.350Z"],["3803470","LSS-61410","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] ! I have granted you an access","2026-01-12T12:50:28.532Z"],["3803471","PRODSEC-679","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","[~accountid:6352ad6b76b91b62562cbb6c] please update your permissions to recognise [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRODSEC-694|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRODSEC-694|smart-link]  as the new epic for bugcrowd reports","2026-01-12T12:50:36.735Z"],["3803477","HS-28790","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hi [~accountid:712020:0858bdaa-9175-4f05-87d3-9b97ce90e1d0] , do you have any additional work certificates you have perhaps not provided? I can see your diploma, but with that only, you will reach eligibility in three months. Once reached, +6 days of annual leave will be added to your base balance.","2026-01-12T12:51:02.499Z"],["3803478","RDS-1246","RDS","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:712020:505aebee-5cf4-438e-8909-a5524bd7a634] Sorry what do you mean? it’s in scope, jus tbroken down by instant and scheduled where these are enabled. ","2026-01-12T12:51:07.562Z"],["3803479","SREDESK-7398","SREDESK","sofija.danilevica@bolt.eu","Sofija Daņileviča","[~accountid:712020:782f9535-5dfc-41e5-8bdf-057eef89f6ef] , but I am a Billing Analyst. Can’t I be added to {{dap-group-billing-analyst}} to have access to these directories? ","2026-01-12T12:51:10.792Z"],["3803483","HS-28861","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Waiting for JD.","2026-01-12T12:52:34.783Z"],["3803486","PIF-3277","PIF",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the User Story!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-12T12:52:56.200Z"],["3803488","LSS-61414","LSS","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","[^UMOWA_UGC_{linda}.pdf] _(333 kB)_\n\n[^UMOWA_UGC_{magdalena}.pdf] _(231 kB)_","2026-01-12T12:52:58.144Z"],["3803489","DBRE-7645","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* {{dev-partner-payments-support}} \n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C012KU8GJBW/p1768222343176039|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C012KU8GJBW/p1768222343176039|smart-link] ✅\n* {{dev-billing-financial-platform-support}}\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03FY31JC7L/p1768222439086109|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03FY31JC7L/p1768222439086109] ✅\n* {{dev-billing-rentals-support}}\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03K4AJEBQT/p1768222521755019|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03K4AJEBQT/p1768222521755019|smart-link] ✅\n* {{dev-billing-tax-tech-support}}\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01T8CPH2HY/p1768222652920659|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01T8CPH2HY/p1768222652920659] ✅\n* {{dev-billing-business-support}}\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01K5CYD5T5/p1768222724389719|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01K5CYD5T5/p1768222724389719] ⚠️ ( conditional yes )\n* {{dev-payments-support}}\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1768222766191119|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1768222766191119] ✅\n* {{dev-billing-rides-support}}\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1768222821467399|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1768222821467399] ✅\n* {{dev-billing-delivery-support}}\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02BZ67SKFG/p1768222879249419|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02BZ67SKFG/p1768222879249419|smart-link] ✅","2026-01-12T12:53:01.405Z"],["3803490","SREDESK-7398","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Which engineering team referred you to this service desk form to ask for S3 access?","2026-01-12T12:53:19.778Z"],["3803491","LSS-54833","LSS","roisin.kirk@bolt.eu","Roisin Kirk","Thanks so much - I have commented on 3.4.  Let me know when it’s ok to download and send to IWG.  Thanks for your help [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] ","2026-01-12T12:53:24.585Z"],["3803494","WEBSD-1468","WEBSD","zoe.johnson@bolt.eu","Zoë Johnson","[^Website changes  (1).pdf]","2026-01-12T12:54:21.686Z"],["3803501","LSS-61318","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:5d0c7ac70f1d390c4db46fed] [~accountid:712020:28f7389c-dc34-43f9-b4fc-4a3718af00ff] ! \nEE has used an outdated long-term vehicle agreement template. I have made a copy of the latest version for LT and added some additional clauses. Please review [this template |https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kTIKklb-zmf7GT5YM_Yxtpaf7UIqiimc/edit]for EE and address my questions directly in the document. \n\nOnce we finalise the EE template, *only this template should be used*, meaning that for any new clients a copy should be made and adjusted as needed. The template itself must not be amended by the business without Legal involvement.\n\n*Termination clause:*\nEarly termination rules are set out in clauses 8.2 and 8.3, in line with LV and LT. Please review and confirm whether this approach works for EE. The amounts of fees charged to clients are to be set by the business, not Legal. If you would like to apply different early termination rules in EE, please let me know what exactly to change.\n\n*Damages section:*\nIt is unclear what exactly you would like to update here. The Bolt Drive T&Cs form part of this Agreement; therefore, client liability, scope of liability, and the damage recovery process for long-term vehicle rental are the same as for short-term rental, as set out in the Bolt Drive T&Cs.\n\n*Branding clause:*\nA branding clause has been added as clause 8.3. Please review.","2026-01-12T12:55:51.699Z"],["3803505","LSS-61352","LSS","corneliu.radu@bolt.eu","Corneliu-Ștefan Radu","Sure here are the information : email : [torjoclarisa@gmail.com|mailto:torjoclarisa@gmail.com] Name: Larisa Torjoc","2026-01-12T12:56:32.342Z"],["3803506","LSS-56328","LSS","alex.bucse@bolt.eu","Alex Bucșe","Hey [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] - as discussed in Slack and as confirmed by [~accountid:712020:8bcb68bd-f8da-4da1-8320-2536f6bb0c0c] , please tell Leyton that the latest form of the agreement can be signed. (they need to update the English version too)\n\nOnce they send the final version, I have looped in Legal Ops here [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] to help with Ahto/counterparty signature. [mmueller@leyton.com|mailto:mmueller@leyton.com] is their signatory, Malte MÜLLER. \n\nI will share the signature ready version here (after Leyton cleans it up and adds the English part as well), but just giving the heads-up for Legal Ops. \n\n","2026-01-12T12:56:32.429Z"],["3803507","CCM-22266","CCM","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","Hi Theeranart!\n\nI have assigned the following courses to the two listed learners:\n\n* Ride-Hailing Onboarding\n* Ride-Hailing Safety Up-Skill Course (High & Significant)\n\nFor future training assignment requests, could you please refer to the exact course titles? This will help avoid any confusion.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T12:56:48.230Z"],["3803512","LSS-61288","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:dbef963c-e707-4042-8024-5afb4c08aa16] we are in the process of reviewing the document and will provide feedback once the review is complete. \n\nPlease advise whether Huawei has signed Special Terms?  \n\nPlease confirm that this is a standard Bolt Business relationship? ","2026-01-12T12:57:24.231Z"],["3803513","HS-28804","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hi [~accountid:712020:62e64c49-827e-411a-bd3f-c88209a0d39b] , your Workday balance has been updated to 26 days of annual leave a year. Thanks for flagging this, all the best!","2026-01-12T12:57:26.615Z"],["3803515","RNTL-30295","RNTL","vinicius.ambrosi@bolt.eu","Vinicius Ambrosi","Estimates remain the same - 3D BE only.","2026-01-12T12:57:40.184Z"],["3803516","FRAUD-5737","FRAUD","ivan.honchar@bolt.eu","Ivan Honchar","*Quickfix solution*\n\nBusiness Invoicing team claims that it intentionally was implemented in such way.\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01K5CYD5T5/p1768217044057089?thread_ts=1768212615.164549&cid=C01K5CYD5T5|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01K5CYD5T5/p1768217044057089?thread_ts=1768212615.164549&cid=C01K5CYD5T5]\n\nLuckily, we have order id and city id in our input from different source. So, we can change what is sent to metadata","2026-01-12T12:57:49.399Z"],["3803518","DSR-2322","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Hey [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] Are there any updates? 🙃","2026-01-12T12:57:57.254Z"],["3803523","PRODSEC-588","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","Whats the update/plan with this epic?","2026-01-12T12:58:41.222Z"],["3803524","DSR-2249","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Any updates? 🙂","2026-01-12T12:58:46.593Z"],["3803528","WDFT-3553","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:712020:b1a3aa39-56a5-492b-9453-5372da990388] !\n\nUnfortunately, I can not set up the rule in the way that revaluation results are posted to acc 8110. But I can add unique worktag to the rule, so you can filter revaluation results from all posting of 8112, at least it will hep to identify the revaluation related to these particular accounts. And then you can make manual journal to move the revaluation results to acc 8110. In future we can try to automate such manual journals. will this work for now?  If yes then what worktag should I use ? \n\n\n\n[~accountid:712020:11b028d0-a65b-4db4-93f7-938b14e353e9] [~accountid:6131df23b1894f00718e9faa]  adding you here for visibility. ","2026-01-12T12:59:30.595Z"],["3803531","RDS-1246","RDS","katharina.skolimowski@bolt.eu","Katharina Skolimowski","Ah yes now I see, sorry","2026-01-12T13:00:23.780Z"],["3803532","RNTL-24295","RNTL","marek.kikas@bolt.eu","Marek Kikas","Used to track UI tests. Closing. Will create new one if tests are going to fail","2026-01-12T13:00:25.012Z"],["3803535","PRODSEC-696","PRODSEC","allar.lauk@bolt.eu","Allar Lauk","[ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-348910?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6ImExNjY3ZjFkNWY0MDExNmNmMWQ2ZmIzZmJlNWM1ZTUzNGRjYjJlYTgzZWU1NmQyZmExNDE3ZGI5ZjVlNzMyMjkiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiMjkzNTUiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IklJUy0zNDg5MTAifSwiZXhwIjoxNzcwMzg5MDIyLCJpYXQiOjE3Njc5Njk4MjJ9.Y6u7kKNS6kuPTxZhOwfWROYyHEhNQs4xQDCqk5omX_A] created ","2026-01-12T13:01:03.865Z"],["3803537","PFI-832350","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-12T13:01:12.724Z"],["3803538","PFI-832337","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-12T13:01:13.766Z"],["3803539","DRX-28143","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Aleksandr Leontev, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-12T13:01:17.295Z"],["3803540","PFI-832438","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have investigated the issue and I found the payment method adding attempt fails with an error message 05: Do Not Honor. \n\nThe user is not able to add this card. Could you please ask them to try a different payment method. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T13:01:36.740Z"],["3803541","LSS-61415","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T13:01:52.619Z"],["3803542","LSS-61416","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T13:01:52.668Z"],["3803543","OKAI-179","OKAI","norman.tamm@bolt.eu","Norman Tamm","h1. Okai error collections 09.01.26-12.01.26\n\nAs of 12.01.26 14:26 we have *22241 operational OKAI* vehicles. In 3 days *859* vehicles triggered error collections with log-only mode enabled.\n\n*3.9% of operational OKAI fleet triggered collections.*\n\n[data in sheets|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1lkgK6OWYRIySXbAGfrp4O2HIX0CEB58NrGtI7HxiWJg/edit?usp=sharing]\n\n!Each error triggered count 09.01.26 - 12.01.26-20260112-123825.png|width=363,alt=\"Each error triggered count 09.01.26 - 12.01.26-20260112-123825.png\"!\n\n!Error collections count per city 09.01.26 - 12.01.26.png|width=356,alt=\"Error collections count per city 09.01.26 - 12.01.26.png\"!\n\nh2. Conclusion\n\nData was collected form 09.01.26 - 12.01.26.\n\n3.9% of operational OKAI fleet triggered collections (859 vehicles).\n\nThe highest number of collections was in Berlin, which is expected because there are 8036 operational OKAI vehicles there (Total 376 error collections).\n\nE49 was the error that triggered the most (290 times).","2026-01-12T13:02:12.104Z"],["3803544","WFM-9950","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Access provided, please let us know if you need anything else and have a nice day!☀️ ","2026-01-12T13:02:17.213Z"],["3803546","WD-14199","WD","kristiina.vaik@bolt.eu","Kristiina Vaik","Thank you [~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] \n\nCould you please also activate this task *Fix Unbalanced Journal from Supplier Invoice* in SB?\n\nSince we want to post this correction into the 2025 financial year and it is related to a purchase invoice, it is important that the suppliers for December 2025 are open. This raises the question of whether the Changzhou Bolt Technology Co., LTD customer also needs to be open as this fix is related with their invoice. We want to avoid creating any postings for them as a result of this correction.\n\nFor this reason, the idea was to test this first in SB 🙂 .","2026-01-12T13:02:26.685Z"],["3803547","DRX-25662","DRX","vishalkumar.singh@bolt.eu","Vishal Singh","[~accountid:5b7beae9dfe5ae2b3e4c548b] \n\nHi\nCan you please reach out to [#dev-rides-compliance-support|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70] ?\nThey are managing the documents search view in admin-panel","2026-01-12T13:02:46.298Z"],["3803548","PRODSEC-559","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","[~accountid:642aa1eb7e859baa54f54b06] [~accountid:712020:db2447cd-56f2-448b-a492-d023fd63690e] is this meant to be an Epic for 2026?? This was created since October 2025. Why not do the following?\n\n* Reject this epic and create a new one\n* Change this issue to task type and place under Pavel’s onboarding Epic in 2025 and create proper 2026 Epic for this","2026-01-12T13:03:03.345Z"],["3803549","WDFT-3553","WDFT","toomas.parts@bolt.eu","Toomas-Hendrik Parts","[~accountid:712020:b1a3aa39-56a5-492b-9453-5372da990388] Could you specify why do you need a separate account to identify FX impact from IC balances?\nFor consolidation purposes, it is important that this journal entry posted on 8110 or alternative account (8112 as Iryna suggested) DOES NOT have an Intercompany Affiliate tag as we cannot eliminate FX impact from IC balances on consolidation level.","2026-01-12T13:03:29.786Z"],["3803550","HS-28512","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","The deadline to request completion of the form was 10.01.2026. No requests were received, so there are no changes.","2026-01-12T13:03:49.918Z"],["3803551","WFM-9942","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Access provided, please let us know if you need anything else and have a nice day!☀️","2026-01-12T13:03:58.765Z"],["3803552","MKP-9685","MKP","alexandr.kuldin@bolt.eu","Alexandr Kuldin","I need to check if this field is still stored.","2026-01-12T13:04:14.702Z"],["3803554","PFI-832199","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe payment had gotten stuck in authorized state. \nThe customer payments team has confirmed with United Payment and released the authorization. \nPayment state in Admin has been corrected. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T13:04:29.212Z"],["3803557","WFM-9930","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Access provided, please let us know if you need anything else and have a nice day!☀️","2026-01-12T13:04:52.484Z"],["3803558","SCM-1074","SCM","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","Latest info from supplier is that we can not modify the current mould and if we want to improve the part then new mould have to be opened - in that case I would like to add BOLT logo or something to avoid that they can sell it to other customers or they should cover the cost of the mould.\n\n\n\nsupplier is preparing quotations and mould ETA - hopefully we can get the information {{2026-01-14}} ","2026-01-12T13:04:55.820Z"],["3803560","PFI-831895","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hi [~accountid:712020:694f79bb-3dfb-4daf-ace8-514947b16f2a]  \n\nTo be more compliant with tax rules, we do not reissue the rider invoices.\n\nPlease ask the user to make sure that their Personal Profile and/or Work profile have correct information. And make sure they pick the right Billing profile before the ride. \n\nIt is as essential as picking the right payment method before the ride.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,\n\nArtem Lishchuk  ","2026-01-12T13:05:22.184Z"],["3803561","BP-9869","BP","abhishek.gupta@bolt.eu","Abhishek Gupta","[~accountid:5b306883ed67e12dd27645e1] Let me confirm with the team. It somehow got lost in backlog. Will get back soon","2026-01-12T13:05:25.184Z"],["3803563","LSS-55496","LSS","kristjan.okas@bolt.eu","Kristjan Okas","Hey!\n\nThank you for the feedback; QQ: 15.3. - shall we remove the whole regulation or only the last sentence of the regulation? ","2026-01-12T13:05:40.023Z"],["3803565","LSS-61416","LSS","sofia.carto@bolt.eu","Sofia Cartó","[~accountid:712020:ab95f96b-73f1-4bb8-a5fd-5178ef3f1339] [~accountid:712020:d77c5e6c-f92f-4d79-955d-9f88e6d0a883] can we get the information about this driver’s trips since registering (19/02/2025)? \n\nIs there an issue with this [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ?\n\nI would say we get the list of trips he did, and then decide what to share and how then (maybe a list os trips with dat and time of of trips is enough and we don’t share more specific information about those trips) [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] WDYT?\n\n","2026-01-12T13:05:48.818Z"],["3803566","PFI-832408","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-12T13:05:56.138Z"],["3803568","PFI-832364","PFI","monica.kartsev@bolt.eu","Monica Kartsev","Hi team, adding additional details. The driver has shared more information regarding the rides and the rider(s). There is video evidence along with the names and phone numbers of all involved parties, where the rider confirms they created a Bolt Business account and used certain promo codes that allowed them to “not pay?”.\n\nAll of the rides were completed successfully, and the driver is not at fault(I think). Please advise on the next steps. It would be fair to compensate the driver for these completed trips.\nThnak you!\n\n","2026-01-12T13:06:27.182Z"],["3803569","LSS-61353","LSS","corneliu.radu@bolt.eu","Corneliu-Ștefan Radu","Hello [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] ! I corrected all the points, it looks cleaner now. 😆 ","2026-01-12T13:06:28.391Z"],["3803570","LSS-61357","LSS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","hey [~accountid:712020:985a985c-b403-41bd-b116-abbf44b22175] - not to fret, “I” sign a lot of agreements 😆  i.e. get Legal Ops to sign on Ahto’s behalf 🤓 \n\nWe signed the original agreement via Cogna so we’ll aim to proceed with the same for the revised one, too. 🙏 ","2026-01-12T13:06:33.713Z"],["3803572","PFI-831415","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hey, please, specify what does it mean “receiving information about his trips“","2026-01-12T13:06:42.317Z"],["3803573","LSS-61353","LSS","corneliu.radu@bolt.eu","Corneliu-Ștefan Radu","Information about the receiver :  Email [due.fratelli@yahoo.ro|mailto:due.fratelli@yahoo.ro] Name: Mihai Torjoc:  ","2026-01-12T13:07:43.599Z"],["3803574","LSS-61417","LSS","jurgen.kaevats@bolt.eu","Jürgen Kaevats","[^Authorised Signatory List - Bolt Holdings.pdf] _(70 kB)_\n\n[^Bolt Holdings - CLAOGB2LGOL v2.doc] _(43 kB)_\n\n[^GSAM BV Mosaic - Bolt Holdings.pdf] _(225 kB)_","2026-01-12T13:07:47.966Z"],["3803575","RDS-1246","RDS","katharina.skolimowski@bolt.eu","Katharina Skolimowski","To confirm:\nFor example for adding Shifts and Instant / Scheduled rides -  we open the adding modals wherever the user is at the moment, let them finish the flow and on submitting, direct them to the specific pages? Same as we actually do for vehicles and drivers, they end the flow in Applications tab. ","2026-01-12T13:08:07.369Z"],["3803577","PFI-830557","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nthe change to commission of companies will apply tomorrow.","2026-01-12T13:08:31.206Z"],["3803581","PFI-832440","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^Comprobante - Diferencia Gs. 196.284.pdf (2).pdf]","2026-01-12T13:09:38.186Z"],["3803582","PFI-832348","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, specify which values differ. Please, note that we don’t have access to the Bolt Business Portal, please, provide visual reference, if that’s required.","2026-01-12T13:09:55.003Z"],["3803583","LSS-61418","LSS","alejandro.sanz@bolt.eu","Alejandro Sanz","[^Bolt Poland - IC loans notice and acknowledgement - 12.01.2026.docx] _(2.37 MB)_","2026-01-12T13:09:59.247Z"],["3803585","PFI-832441","PFI","augustas.strimaitis@bolt-outsource.eu","Augustas Strimaitis","!Skärmavbild 2026-01-12 kl. 13.26.13.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T13:10:16.220Z"],["3803586","DSR-3673","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Email with response sent [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/721789476]","2026-01-12T13:10:18.760Z"],["3803589","PFI-832002","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm that this was likely not a payments related issue. \nThe payment failed due to insufficient funds and after 2 seconds and was rejected. \n\nThis seems like technical issue that should be escalated to the rides tech support team instead. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T13:10:59.556Z"],["3803590","RCE-84","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Daniel José [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768223450178049]*{color}:\n&gt; • Is there some regulation which is enforceable for us? Please can you share that, esp why waybill and not trip receipts are required?\n<@U04RDTQ5AJC> yes, it’s regulated by law: [https://www.boe.es/buscar/doc.php?id=BOE-A-2008-1094].\n\nFleets need to keep a record of waybills.\n\n&gt; • Why do we as Ops need to download the waybills? Is the liability not with Fleets who need to be able to do this?\nWe produce the waybills on the fleet’s behalf, so we either have to 1) Provide it in the Fleet Owner Portal so they can download it (ideal solution, this is what Uber does) or 2) Provide it to them on request\n\n&gt; • On Problem\n&gt;     ◦ How is this impacting onboarding of Fleets, by design that Fleet will have 0 trips, so the problem is unclear here for me\n&gt;     ◦ What are the CS Costs associated here? Please can you share weekly/monthly vols\nIssue is not on-boarding, is trading off between 1) Not providing the waybills on time risking the fleet partner getting a fine (can be €1,001 per each waybill not provided) leading to a) Fleet not working with us anymore or b) Us compensating the fine or 2) Drawing CS resources from other tasks to cover the worklaod.\n\nOn that basis, what exactly are you looking for in the business case? We can provide you:\n\n• Number of inspections fleets had in 2025\n• A rough estimate of how many  waybills we weren’t able to provide in time, and potential cost to us\n• % of time drawn from CS\nDoes that work? <@U06T0J3AHEK>\n\nLinked messages:\nBOE-A-2008-1094 Orden FOM/36/2008, de 9 de enero, por la que se desarrolla la sección segunda del capítulo IV del título V, en materia de arrendamiento de vehículos con conductor, del Reglamento de la Ley de Ordenación de los Transportes Terrestres, aprobado por Real Decreto 1211/1990, de 28 de septiembre.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T13:11:04.062Z"],["3803593","LSS-61401","LSS","kristel.lokk@bolt.eu","Kristel Lõkk","Thank you for pointing that out, updated doc here: [https://drive.google.com/file/d/1apK4ArBx1eZNV4YWVlSvDOPgazb2CSi7/view?usp=drive_link|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1apK4ArBx1eZNV4YWVlSvDOPgazb2CSi7/view?usp=drive_link|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T13:11:35.964Z"],["3803596","PFI-832443","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T13:11:48.508Z"],["3803597","PFI-831999","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 54.00 ZAR on 22/12/2025, 09:27:10UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 22nd of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-12T13:11:55.713Z"],["3803599","DSR-3085","DSR","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] \n\nDear Adam Hansson,\n\nThank you for your data subject request, which was received by us on *December 13, 2025*.\n\nTo enable micromobility rental service, a ride is linked to a specific scooter when the user unlocks a scooter through the app. At that moment, the scooter’s unique identifier is recorded and associated with the user’s account and a newly created ride session. All subsequent ride data is linked to that scooter via this identifier.\n\nPlease find the requested data for your ride attached:\n\n* Scooter UUID\n* Scooter internal ID\n* Order ID\n* Ride start timestamp\n* Ride end timestamp\n\nAs you may be aware, the right of access under data protection law does not provide an individual with an absolute right of full access to any and all documents containing their personal data. For example, that right should not adversely affect the rights of others, including our trade secrets or intellectual property and, in particular, the copyright protecting the software. Furthermore, we must point out that if, after careful analysis, we conclude that our rights or the rights of others prevail, we will not be able to provide you with access to certain documentation where an exemption applies.\n\nFor information on how we process relevant personal data, we refer you to our Privacy Policy at [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy|smart-link], which includes further information about:\n\n* The categories of personal data we process;\n* The purposes for which we process personal data;\n* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom the personal data has been or will be disclosed;\n* The criteria we use to determine how long to retain personal data;\n* The sources of personal data received from other parties;\n* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making/profiling of personal data; and\n* Details of any transfer of your personal data to third countries or international organisations and the safeguards used for any such transfers.\n\nYour rights\n\nIn addition to your right to access any personal data we hold about you, you have the right to request us to rectify, erase your personal data, restrict the processing of your personal data or object to such processing. Any such requests that are received will be considered in conjunction with the applicable provisions of relevant data protection laws.\n\nIf you are dissatisfied with this response to your request or in relation to any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve them. You also have the right to complain directly to your data protection/supervisory authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek a judicial remedy.\n\nIf you have any additional questions, please contact our Customer Support Team by replying to this message.\n\nBolt","2026-01-12T13:12:09.480Z"],["3803601","IOTTEAM-234","IOTTEAM","enari.saar@bolt.eu","Enari Saar","The uploading to artifactory works via github workflow. Tested in AIOT release workflow. Need to update dragon/eb1 as well. Then this should be done.","2026-01-12T13:12:33.147Z"],["3803604","WD-22541","WD","thalita.biancalana@bolt.eu","Thalita Biancalana","!Error.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T13:12:51.851Z"],["3803605","DLSP-1996","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","released","2026-01-12T13:12:57.476Z"],["3803608","DRAG101-405","DRAG101","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] FYI, too ⬆️ \n\nFor D3, no problem. However is there something we can adjust in the FW for old Dragon to match the original 365W nominal output power so we do not have to replace the labels when upgrading to 500w motors?","2026-01-12T13:13:28.936Z"],["3803610","LSS-59015","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41]. Could you please provide the following reply? Thank you!\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zdJbMHDCPSnIc_AmfZRDgqhOoyviqNtaD1u0LEkyDro/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zdJbMHDCPSnIc_AmfZRDgqhOoyviqNtaD1u0LEkyDro/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]","2026-01-12T13:14:02.246Z"],["3803612","HS-28804","HS","magdalena.jesiotr@bolt.eu","Magdalena Jesiotr","Thank you so much! ","2026-01-12T13:16:48.339Z"],["3803613","WDFT-3553","WDFT","joel.suldre@bolt.eu","Joel Süldre","These requested FX revaluation rules does not have anything do to with IC. [~accountid:712020:11b028d0-a65b-4db4-93f7-938b14e353e9]  lets sync separately if needed\n\n[~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] please use Trade Receivables Admin spend category if possible. Otherwise do nothing. I think we can find the revaluation journals and book the manual correction to 8110","2026-01-12T13:16:50.841Z"],["3803614","WFM-9949","WFM","bolajoko.kufoniyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Bolajoko Kufoniyi","Hi [~accountid:712020:74b4c3fb-6caf-4d5d-b7f8-c2ea38318e58] \n\nHere is the details you requested for: \n*Company:* Teleperformance Nigeria \n*Market:* Nigeria\n*Function:* CS Team Lead\n*Access Duration:* Permanent\n*Task Description:* Update training/coaching sessions on assembled \n*Bolt Email(s) of Agent(s):* [kaosara.rasheed@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:kaosara.rasheed@bolt-outsource.eu]\n[roseline.makinwa@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:roseline.makinwa@bolt-outsource.eu]\n[umenwanne.isika@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:umenwanne.isika@bolt-outsource.eu]\n[banji.balogun@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:banji.balogun@bolt-outsource.eu]\n[henrieta.ijeh@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:henrieta.ijeh@bolt-outsource.eu]\n","2026-01-12T13:16:55.956Z"],["3803615","L10N-27231","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.094Z"],["3803616","L10N-27248","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.268Z"],["3803617","L10N-27243","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.293Z"],["3803618","L10N-27249","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.338Z"],["3803619","L10N-27242","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.349Z"],["3803620","L10N-27230","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.381Z"],["3803621","L10N-27241","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.476Z"],["3803622","L10N-27237","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.499Z"],["3803623","L10N-27225","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.535Z"],["3803624","L10N-27246","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.541Z"],["3803625","L10N-27244","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.597Z"],["3803626","L10N-27245","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T13:17:15.603Z"],["3803627","L10N-27235","L10N",null,"Automation for Ji