questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27377](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27377)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T13:17:48.293Z"],["3803666","PFI-832448","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T13:18:21.667Z"],["3803667","WEB-9052","WEB","tom.gander@bolt.eu","Tom Gander","It can be closed now. ","2026-01-12T13:18:27.942Z"],["3803668","BB-2162","BB","ilya.goryachev@bolt.eu","Ilya Goryachev","I ran the following query to find affected records:\n\n{noformat}WITH target_aggregated_records AS (\n    SELECT ar.id\n    FROM ng_public_spark.business_invoicing_aggregated_record ar\n    INNER JOIN ng_public_spark.business_invoicing_business_company bc\n        ON ar.business_company_id = bc.id\n    WHERE bc.country = 'ee'\n      AND ar.period_end_ts >= DATE '2025-07-30'\n)\nSELECT r.*\nFROM ng_public_spark.business_invoicing_record r\nINNER JOIN target_aggregated_records tar ON r.aggregated_record_id = tar.id\nLEFT JOIN ng_public_spark.business_invoicing_claim c on c.id = r.claim_id\nWHERE r.type = 'business_order'\n  AND r.vat_percentage = 22\n  AND r.is_active = true\n  AND c.country = 'ee' -- we don't want to accidentaly change other countries 22% VAT\nORDER BY r.id; {noformat}\n\nI’ll wait for [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] to run her query to confirm my findings","2026-01-12T13:18:29.392Z"],["3803669","PIF-2255","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft succinctly conveys the newly added feature's purpose and benefit, staying within word limits and using simple language for clarity. It highlights the main advantage of the feature—speeding up role assignment—which directly impacts user efficiency. The draft acknowledges missing specific URLs or guides by incorporating placeholders where necessary.","2026-01-12T13:18:53.333Z"],["3803670","PIF-2254","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft is appropriate because it succinctly communicates the enhancement made to the critical error handling in ApiGen, ensuring that users are immediately aware of compilation issues and can address them promptly. Key information such as where the changes can be viewed (link to component admin panel) and additional guidance (guide, ADR) are not provided, hence placeholders are used.","2026-01-12T13:19:01.458Z"],["3803671","PIF-2224","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft communicates the introduction of a shared S3 storage solution for specific services, emphasizing the benefits of centralized data access and maintaining security for sensitive data. Missing information includes the specific location where stakeholders can check the feature implementation and a guide or ADR for further details.","2026-01-12T13:19:09.904Z"],["3803672","WFM-9949","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","IDs: 17866, 19433, 21820, 21838, 232725\n\nSince it is assembled related I will leave it to the WFM team.\n\nDuplicated tickets: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/WFM/queues/custom/2078/WFM-9948|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/WFM/queues/custom/2078/WFM-9948|smart-link] \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/WFM/queues/custom/2078/WFM-9946|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/WFM/queues/custom/2078/WFM-9946|smart-link] \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/WFM/queues/custom/2078/WFM-9945|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/WFM/queues/custom/2078/WFM-9945|smart-link] \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/WFM/queues/custom/2078/WFM-9944|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/WFM/queues/custom/2078/WFM-9944|smart-link] \n","2026-01-12T13:19:17.800Z"],["3803673","PIF-2223","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED, ADR_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft succinctly communicates the new feature addition for RnA users to cancel obsolete requests, which is beneficial in preventing resource blocking and reducing admin intervention. Appropriate placeholders are used where specific links to the guide and ADR are needed.","2026-01-12T13:19:19.166Z"],["3803676","PIF-2214","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED, ADR_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft summarizes the delivered feature, its implementation, and its benefits. A placeholder for additional documentation helps stakeholders find more detailed info. Missing links to the component admin panel and guide/ADR are replaced with placeholders.","2026-01-12T13:19:28.197Z"],["3803679","LSS-55531","LSS","miroslava.gorejova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Gorejova","HI [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] , I went through the whole deal in our CRM Salesforce etc.. and I found already a signed contract by both sides correctly - attaching it below.\n\nI presume you can close the ticket as the client has everything set up in our system correctly to be able to start to ride - so once again thank you for your help guys 🙂 \n\nBest \n\nMiroslava\n\n[^2025_241 NAKIT Bolt Business_Zvláštní podmínky _ podepsaná.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T13:19:40.858Z"],["3803680","LSS-61419","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","[^Agreement + Doc A (2).pdf] _(300 kB)_","2026-01-12T13:19:42.043Z"],["3803682","MARTECH3-1471","MARTECH3","prakhar.saini@bolt.eu","Prakhar Saini","For creative experiments ran in Q4, requested the ads team to rename the campaigns to “Creative Experiment Extra” and added it to the [exclusion list|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/martech/seeds/input_ads_bm_dict_is_excluded.csv] so that the spends do not show up in our tables.   ","2026-01-12T13:20:00.960Z"],["3803684","CSDA-281","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hey hey! Sorry for the delayed reply, and thank you for sharing the details and tagging me in the thread 🙌\n\nWe may not be able to build the report in Looker right away, but I will prep the query to get the data and have it shared with you on a constant basis meanwhile. What exactly would you like to check? And would you need to have an aggregated report or a report with Beehive case links and case attributes?","2026-01-12T13:20:19.372Z"],["3803685","PAW-14867","PAW",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the User Story!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-12T13:20:21.928Z"],["3803687","PFI-832397","PFI","anna.betina@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Betina","[^Payouts draft(2025) - Sheet1 (4).csv]\n\nI apologize for the mistake, this is not correct Dnipro Fleet 01 own Kamianske\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/183618?tab=profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/183618?tab=profile]\nIt should have been Cherkasy Fleet 00_04 park 7777777 [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/189073?tab=profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/189073?tab=profile]","2026-01-12T13:20:26.555Z"],["3803688","CSDA-281","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","{code:sql}select support_case_id, event_type, event_data, get_json_object(event_data, '$.ended_by.user_type') as ended_by_user_type, get_json_object(event_data, '$.close_call') as close_call\nfrom ng_customer_support_spark.support_case_event\nwhere event_type = 'voice_call_ended' and get_json_object(event_data, '$.callee_joined') = 'false' and created >= date('2026-01-01')\norder by 5 desc\nlimit 100{code}","2026-01-12T13:20:38.135Z"],["3803689","PFI-831992","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can see the user has successfully added 3 payment methods: 51697160 * 2084, 55421220 * 2271 and 53546210 * 9091. \n\nThe card adding attempts between 21st to 28th of December were failing because Bolt does not allow card adding in Montenegro. \n\nOnce the user arrived to a country where Bolt operates (Thailand) They were able to add the payment method. \n\nPlease let me know if the user is still having issues with their payment methods. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T13:20:39.623Z"],["3803690","WFM-9949","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello [~accountid:64181e3d1273131f2ae1b51d],\n\nI see that you created a separated ticket for each of the agents.\n\nI will close them as a duplicate and we will move forward with the request from this ticket.\n\nBest regards! ","2026-01-12T13:20:45.224Z"],["3803691","PFI-832337","PFI","klaudia.dzialak@bolt-outsource.eu","Klaudia Dzialak",".","2026-01-12T13:21:02.675Z"],["3803692","CSDA-281","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A0T3NATF1/p1767602096506829|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A0T3NATF1/p1767602096506829|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T13:21:08.514Z"],["3803693","WD-22540","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:712020:4031005b-be5e-413a-b7da-919304795012] !\n\nIf you filter you journal by currency USD , you will see that operational journal has two lines in relation to USD balance (second and last on the screen shot) , the sum effect is 0,02 . When you applier new revaluation rule system credited result from revaluation you did using old rules and debited result from new revaluation rule. In the end there is no effect on your balance. \n\n!image-20260112-132130.png|width=1053,alt=\"image-20260112-132130.png\"!","2026-01-12T13:21:20.661Z"],["3803695","LSS-57150","LSS","roman.igaz@bolt.eu","Roman Igaz","Hey [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] , table completed: 3 payments (€3006.00 each). Could you please arrange the signing of the agreement? Please find the email address of Eliáš Mitra: [mitraelias143@gmail.com|mailto:mitraelias143@gmail.com]. ","2026-01-12T13:22:22.658Z"],["3803696","LSS-61288","LSS","stephanie.oreoluwa@bolt.eu","Stephanie Oreoluwa","Huawei is a new account we are trying to onboard on Bolt Business. This Service Level Agreement is from them. We can only share our addendum after this SLA has been executed by both parties.","2026-01-12T13:22:50.723Z"],["3803697","LSS-60764","LSS","tanel.molok@bolt.eu","Tanel Molok","Hi Lucca,\n\nSeems good to me, feel free to publish if you haven’t done so already.\n\nTanel","2026-01-12T13:22:54.687Z"],["3803698","PFI-820892","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Fleet 262906 commission changed to 10% starting from 13.01, other settings remained the same. Please let me know if you have any other questions. ","2026-01-12T13:23:03.976Z"],["3803699","PAW-14867","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-alerting, pint-product-observability-and-incident-response-platform, pint-capability-observability\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-12T13:23:04.731Z"],["3803700","MARTECH3-1483","MARTECH3","prakhar.saini@bolt.eu","Prakhar Saini","Submitted the APR. ","2026-01-12T13:23:06.211Z"],["3803701","PFI-832449","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T13:23:08.000Z"],["3803702","PIF-3277","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-12T13:23:10.539Z"],["3803705","MARTECH3-1493","MARTECH3","mohd.goh@bolt.eu","Ameer Goh","Set the country-level online targets with Central Ops. See here: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1W_Gwbt6H5M0N6RFgABGdadOq13cYD0LKBFIG1RKYJxM/edit?gid=52716429#gid=52716429|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1W_Gwbt6H5M0N6RFgABGdadOq13cYD0LKBFIG1RKYJxM/edit?gid=52716429#gid=52716429|smart-link]. Note, while target has been set at monthly level, we’ll only report at the quarterly level.\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:93174aec-bd45-4d3a-9b14-935b5b7868f4] ","2026-01-12T13:24:04.607Z"],["3803708","CCM-22269","CCM","ademola.oloja@bolt-outsource.eu","Ademola Oloja","[^New Training Request form.xlsx]","2026-01-12T13:24:44.802Z"],["3803709","WFM-9948","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello,\n\nClosing this ticket as a duplicate.\n\nThe case will be handled here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WFM-9949|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WFM-9949] ","2026-01-12T13:24:48.909Z"],["3803710","LSS-60455","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] as Anna has still not received access to Jira, I’ve had a sit down with her regarding this agreement and she will draft the changes and share with the business over Slack. I’ve assigned the ticket to me in the meantime and informed the business accordingly. ","2026-01-12T13:25:25.109Z"],["3803711","LSS-55496","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:61addb80b0b630006a695081] only the text highlighted in green should be removed from 15.3. Thank you! \n\n ","2026-01-12T13:25:46.270Z"],["3803715","LSS-61100","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Thanks a lot [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] – we can keep the terms as in one for People team – i.e. agree to their standard DPA. The risk is low, since we only share employee email addresses and there won’t be any access to Admin systems, only screenshots for training purposes.","2026-01-12T13:26:29.234Z"],["3803716","LSS-59952","LSS","sofia.carto@bolt.eu","Sofia Cartó","Ok, so we need [~accountid:712020:d77c5e6c-f92f-4d79-955d-9f88e6d0a883] help again on this one, right? Please? 🙂 ","2026-01-12T13:26:29.603Z"],["3803717","PIF-2255","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 9\n• Problem Definition: 9\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is generally well-structured and addresses a meaningful user need. However, the acceptance criteria could be more specific. For example, specify if there are any edge cases or exceptions, such as handling situations where permission1 is already partially assigned to some roles. It may also be beneficial to define any UI/UX requirements or constraints that should be considered when implementing the feature. Additionally, ensure the linkage in the 'Notes' section facilitates quick reference, and verify access to the specified Slack channel for all relevant stakeholders.","2026-01-12T13:26:46.173Z"],["3803718","PC-4093","PC","devanshi.bansal@bolt.eu","Devanshi Bansal","We cant move to dynamic config as on payment side we don't have info whether the payment is from employee or not. Since the config is to be enabled for all employees, we cant support it using dynamic config.\nHence closing this ticket for now.","2026-01-12T13:26:51.507Z"],["3803719","PIF-2254","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 6\n• Relevance: 8\n• Problem Definition: 7\n• Accept: 6\n• Suggested improvements: 1. **Clarity**: The user story needs to improve in terms of defining key conditions and behaviors more clearly. Specifically, it should provide more detail on what it means for the 'generation to fail' and how failure will be communicated or handled. Consider describing the process or response of the system when this critical error is encountered. 2. **Relevance**: While the story is relevant in improving code reliability, it could strengthen the tie to platform objectives by detailing how frequent or impactful this problem is, for example, by providing statistics on how often the non-critical error surfaces. 3. **Acceptance Criteria**: The criteria lack specific guidance on measurable success, such as what constitutes failure of generation or how it is detected. Include specific actions to test the solution, like a test case with input leading to a failed compilation. 4. **Problem Definition**: While the problem is present, it can benefit from a clearer current-state versus desired-state description. For example, outline specific scenarios illustrating when the error has caused issues and what the ripple effects were, thus providing a stronger narrative and justifying the need for change. 5. Consider adding benchmarks for success (such as error suppression rates or incident reduction) as part of the acceptance criteria.","2026-01-12T13:26:54.723Z"],["3803720","WFM-9946","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello,\n\nClosing this ticket as a duplicate.\n\nThe case will be handled here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WFM-9949|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WFM-9949] ","2026-01-12T13:26:56.143Z"],["3803721","RDS-1118","RDS","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:5f5b4e09df83ab007d8c9a83] drafted the spec for this one - let’s review, and if you agree we’ll bring this up into Q1 and get started asap on it. ","2026-01-12T13:26:56.775Z"],["3803722","PIF-2224","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is strong in overall clarity, relevance, and problem definition. However, it could benefit from more detailed acceptance criteria. Consider specifying how success will be measured (e.g., latency improvements, data integrity, or security benchmarks). It would also be useful to define how limited access to this S3 storage is configured and monitored. Including these elements would make the criteria more specific and measurable, ensuring that the implementation meets all the necessary requirements.","2026-01-12T13:26:59.183Z"],["3803724","MARTECH3-1315","MARTECH3","prakhar.saini@bolt.eu","Prakhar Saini","*Update 12/01*\n\n* Automated the process of creating callouts at country level.\n* Worked on updating the numbers and the callouts in the [+review doc+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bGrgB-gub7kR-Inho9R4H3ez5nHVyb5UrNUa3cd5mxM/edit?tab=t.0].\n\n*Next Steps:*\n\n* Update measured spend numbers based on the new definition.\n* Make adjustments to the doc if necessary.","2026-01-12T13:27:01.972Z"],["3803725","TAXP-2138","TAXP","tanel.molok@bolt.eu","Tanel Molok","Thanks, seems good to me the way it is.","2026-01-12T13:27:25.477Z"],["3803726","PFI-832451","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 10.20.04 AM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T13:27:33.929Z"],["3803727","WFM-9945","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello,\n\nClosing this ticket as a duplicate.\n\nThe case will be handled here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WFM-9949|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WFM-9949] ","2026-01-12T13:27:34.833Z"],["3803728","LSS-54833","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:2f68ebec-bff7-4acf-a855-0eeaf1c88737]! All aligned, checked your comment! I am happy for the agreement to be sent 🙂  ","2026-01-12T13:27:54.990Z"],["3803730","WFM-9944","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello,\n\nClosing this ticket as a duplicate.\n\nThe case will be handled here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WFM-9949|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WFM-9949] ","2026-01-12T13:28:43.113Z"],["3803731","WD-22534","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Case got solved by customer credit adjustment posting","2026-01-12T13:28:43.456Z"],["3803733","DRAG-636","DRAG","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","As we agreed we will use D3 motors from now on for every Dragon scooter. This means that we must also pass the D1.08 + UL controller + 500W motor combination test with D3 motor.\n\n[~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] [~accountid:5eb363355862510b794e3507] can you please organize more D3 motors to HQ so we can prepare the test samples? We would need minimum 4pcs. (1x EMC, 2x motor power measurement, 1x technical inspection).","2026-01-12T13:29:01.848Z"],["3803735","MKP-9583","MKP","alexandr.kuldin@bolt.eu","Alexandr Kuldin","*Checking the effect of the timeout change*\n\nLast 7d on {{2026-01-12}} (after [this pipeline|https://unicorn-builder.platform.boltint.net/builder-ui/pipelines/327312] on Jan 5 for which t he last stage started at 17:20) only 15 {{Failed to get matching exclusions, using empty exclusions}} occurred ([absolute|https://kibana-logs.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/r/s/LKGhG] time logs).\n\nSo at least some changes are needed to guarantee that this will not happen again.\n\n[^Failed to get matching exclusions, using empty exclusions 7d 2026-01-12.csv]\n\n","2026-01-12T13:29:26.468Z"],["3803736","PFI-832452","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T13:29:47.816Z"],["3803739","GRWA-1484","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","This is done, the Rider AB Scorecard V4 is filtered with GMV UC Cuped bootstrap is not null now.","2026-01-12T13:30:59.392Z"],["3803740","LSS-61068","LSS","tanel.molok@bolt.eu","Tanel Molok","Hi, first and foremost - we should not, under any circumstances, actively push the drivers to register specifically for the Flat Rate Scheme. \n\nIn my opinion - section 3.8 of the guidance that you shared does not prevent private hire drivers using Bolt from joining the flat rate scheme. Iva, let us know if you disagree.","2026-01-12T13:31:11.930Z"],["3803743","LSS-61420","LSS","iryna.yatsyna@bolt.eu","Iryna Yatsyna","[^Act delivery.docx] _(20 kB)_\n\n[^NETTING ACT 31-12-2025.docx] _(20 kB)_","2026-01-12T13:32:13.761Z"],["3803744","PFI-832457","PFI","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.31.49.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T13:32:21.200Z"],["3803745","PFI-832458","PFI","mireya.bareiro@bolt-outsource.eu","Mireya Ojeda Bareiro","!Screenshot_20260112_102411_Bolt Driver.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T13:32:36.880Z"],["3803746","WD-14199","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:61c07bf9a54af90069a42e2f] i contacted Workday support to activate this task again in Sandbox","2026-01-12T13:32:37.745Z"],["3803749","LSS-61147","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:618b80b7785cb2006aff7ccd],  I reviewed the DPA and MSA:\n\nThe current Attio MSA limits Attio’s total liability for *all claims* - including those arising from *data protection breaches* - to the *fees paid in the 12 months prior to the incident*. Additionally, the agreement *excludes key categories of losses* (e.g., data loss, reputational harm) that are precisely the types of damages Bolt would incur in a security incident or privacy breach.\n\nTo mitigate this risk, we recommend the following changes:\n\n# *Carve-out Attio’s liability* for breaches of the DPA and applicable data protection laws from the general liability cap.\n# Alternatively, apply a *separate “super cap”* (e.g., 2x fees paid in 12 months) to data protection liabilities.\n# Allow recovery of *excluded loss categories* (e.g., data loss, reputational damage) where they result from a data protection breach.","2026-01-12T13:32:46.349Z"],["3803752","WFM-9926","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","queues added too","2026-01-12T13:32:57.407Z"],["3803753","CSDT-953","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Done here: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1BlnjfKHxXCU53N6U2rT59sjiE5HDflayrbBUjBbKt2Q/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1BlnjfKHxXCU53N6U2rT59sjiE5HDflayrbBUjBbKt2Q/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] \n\nComms: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C069Y8DNN7L/p1768216089788539|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C069Y8DNN7L/p1768216089788539]","2026-01-12T13:33:18.411Z"],["3803754","GRWA-1489","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","[+PR+|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15243] to extend the cuped bootstrapping calculation to D-5 before the campaign ends.","2026-01-12T13:33:25.336Z"],["3803756","PFI-832459","PFI","zuzanna.kaluzna@bolt-outsource.eu","Zuzanna Kaluzna","!Zrzut ekranu 2026-01-12 143317.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T13:33:37.442Z"],["3803757","WEBSD-1392","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95] 👋 \n\nI hope you are doing great!\n\nRegarding the recent updates, our current standard is to use HTML instead of PDFs to ensure the best result for SEO etc... Since [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd]  was covering/helping  while I was away, she used PDFs to make sure your request was handled quickly. I’m ok to leave it as-is for this time , but if the PDF format doesn't work please let me know.\n\n🙌 \n","2026-01-12T13:33:37.968Z"],["3803759","LSS-54833","LSS","roisin.kirk@bolt.eu","Roisin Kirk","Great thank you!","2026-01-12T13:33:55.942Z"],["3803761","GRWA-1485","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","[PR|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15286] to remove the balance_treatment_control function in the ETL.","2026-01-12T13:34:05.457Z"],["3803765","PFI-832460","PFI","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 14.34.29.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T13:34:43.375Z"],["3803767","BZNS-403","BZNS","daria.zaichykova@bolt.eu","Daria Zaichykova","FYI [~accountid:712020:05cbf403-315b-4845-a56c-6718f4ea6dbe] new hardcoded rules are in the development [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13394|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13394|smart-link] \nWe are waiting for the Company ID from [~accountid:712020:0290cf40-9f2e-408a-bbba-2c095cf95633] ","2026-01-12T13:36:20.044Z"],["3803768","LSS-28796","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:60d82cdd8a72bd006c366e1d] copied from Slack with Edik and Risto, ome good news - the law firm has received information from the Swedish Enforcement Authority confirming that funds have been received. In order for the reimbursement to be processed, they now require our bank account details.Could you please confirm which account the funds should be transferred to? My understanding is that Bolt Services AB has been the entity used for this matter previously so not sure if relating bank account details should be used, or rather another one.\n\nThank you![^DOC260108-20260108095501.pdf] ","2026-01-12T13:36:25.372Z"],["3803770","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Maret Ansperi-Mälberg [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768224988592269]*{color}:\nHmm, <@U090E7WNXUG> do you know why the haulier's name is replaced by \"Bolt Rides DK\"? The CVR number in the first invoice belongs to DANVIO NORDIC APS for example, a transport service provider\n{quote}","2026-01-12T13:36:44.121Z"],["3803771","PC-4911","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI meeting Notes:\n\n* Rollout of SF is planned via processout so we will not spend time on adding data into SF direct integration\n* Need to check with processout for PSPs including SF who are missing this ARN data in the events.","2026-01-12T13:36:48.855Z"],["3803773","PRODSEC-554","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","[~accountid:712020:db71f745-396f-4a86-8bfc-37f01498b899] [~accountid:712020:db2447cd-56f2-448b-a492-d023fd63690e]  Please move under appropriate 2026 Epic unless this task can be completed by 19th January.","2026-01-12T13:37:26.068Z"],["3803774","HS-28820","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hi Matthew!\n\nI did receive his offboarding task today and completed it.\n\n\nKind regards,\nKadri","2026-01-12T13:37:39.575Z"],["3803776","SREDESK-7406","SREDESK","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Created 3 weeks ago:\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-sns-sqs/pull/3885|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-sns-sqs/pull/3885|smart-card]","2026-01-12T13:37:55.998Z"],["3803777","LSS-61308","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] , please see attached\n\n[^orgchart.pdf] ","2026-01-12T13:38:22.137Z"],["3803779","PFI-832461","PFI","ruslana.korniiko@bolt-outsource.eu","Ruslana Korniiko","!IMG_1112.png|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_1118.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T13:38:55.100Z"],["3803780","FRAUD-5737","FRAUD","ivan.honchar@bolt.eu","Ivan Honchar","*Scope*\n\nThe bug is also visible in {{drive_capture_authorized_amount}} and {{micromobility_capture_authorized_amount}}\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/drive_capture_authorized_amount/5761408|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/drive_capture_authorized_amount/5761408]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/micromobility_capture_authorized_amount/17699744|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/micromobility_capture_authorized_amount/17699744]","2026-01-12T13:39:11.196Z"],["3803781","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768225139456069]*{color}:\nHi team, see [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1763119148093779] - this change by the team is currently being undone, ETA end of this week\n\nLinked messages:\n[November 14th, 2025 3:19 AM] ernests.rudzitis: Hi team! We have interesting case. Denmark team wanted to show specific company name for riders in the app, we changed all to Bolt Rides DK in order to satisfy this need, but now this name is shown in the FOP and beehive tickets and they cannot see proper company name of the fleet. Local team is asking if there are any ways to also show company name in the FOP rather than their generic name so that they are more identifiable internally\n{quote}","2026-01-12T13:39:12.094Z"],["3803783","LSS-61421","LSS","ramil.maharramov@bolt.eu","Ramil Maharramov","Thanks Bayram. The transfer will be applicable up to 70 cars that the investor can save. The new fleet will take the responsibility for the 3 remaining years for the marketing service in exchange to the co-invest support. ","2026-01-12T13:39:38.610Z"],["3803784","PC-4924","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI Meeting Notes:\n\n* Need product prioritization for this task.","2026-01-12T13:39:41.094Z"],["3803785","SREDESK-7406","SREDESK","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","First done, state before:\n\n!image-20260112-133918.png|width=1102,alt=\"image-20260112-133918.png\"!","2026-01-12T13:39:41.783Z"],["3803786","WDFT-3553","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Revaluation rules are created , the results will be recorded to 8112 without spend Trade Receivables Admin (not possible)\n\nthe rules are gathered into reevaluation group +*EE003 - 1203, 1204, 1206, 1208, 2106, 2107, 2108, 2109*+\n\n\n\n!image-20260112-133946.png|width=1235,alt=\"image-20260112-133946.png\"!","2026-01-12T13:39:50.961Z"],["3803788","SUPX-2316","SUPX","artem.kudlaienko@bolt.eu","Artem Kudlaienko","Suggesting extra 5 min before case is closed to give time for ssat expiration cron:\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160405|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160405|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T13:39:55.982Z"],["3803789","LSS-61308","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","Hey, Taxify BV was liquidated 17.12.2025, why is it here 100% ?","2026-01-12T13:40:10.427Z"],["3803790","SREDESK-7406","SREDESK","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Second done, state before:\n\n!image-20260112-134011.png|width=1102,alt=\"image-20260112-134011.png\"!","2026-01-12T13:40:15.829Z"],["3803792","SREDESK-7406","SREDESK","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","All done.","2026-01-12T13:40:42.942Z"],["3803797","MKP-9685","MKP","alexandr.kuldin@bolt.eu","Alexandr Kuldin","live:\n\n{noformat}select count(*) from order_rating t where t.admin_user_id is not null{noformat}\n\n{{0}}\n\nDatabricks:\n\n{noformat}select count(*) from ng_public_spark.user_driver_matching_exclusions_order_rating r where r.admin_user_id is not null{noformat}\n\n{{2257599}}\n\nOk. [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MKP-9632|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MKP-9632|smart-link] has been done for sure, so this field can be deleted 👍.\n\nIssue: we cannot distinguish deleted/moved rows in Databricks, because deleted rows are there, and the {{_deleted_from_source}} column is not configured to contain the proper boolean value.","2026-01-12T13:41:49.223Z"],["3803798","PIF-2260","PIF","uladzimir.danko@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Danko","[~accountid:712020:6a8c08e1-ab41-4fd9-afb9-e47c10d0b16b] I think the main problem is to create a unified dashboard that makes sense for all services. If we had this dashboard, everyone could use it, even without a direct link in the builder. \n\nIf you have some ideas, you can create a dashboard. Additionally, we could allow the provision of links to custom dashboards for packages. So, if a package doesn’t have a custom dashboard, then a default one can be used. ","2026-01-12T13:42:00.183Z"],["3803799","WD-22543","WD","ingrid.valgejarv@bolt.eu","Ingrid Valgejärv","Hey [~accountid:712020:176612de-64ab-442f-84ee-ed63bbac2b50], please move this ticket to People Tech team. Thank you!","2026-01-12T13:42:00.812Z"],["3803801","PRODSEC-577","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Reopened because still need to upload how to guide","2026-01-12T13:42:03.749Z"],["3803802","FX-3384","FX","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:61b0e47fef18ca0071ec305a] following up on this point?","2026-01-12T13:42:12.912Z"],["3803805","LSS-61413","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:642b0757551f476a04685f2d] thank you for raising, do you perhaps have access to the ticket where the initial contract was provided? Or the contract in a Google formate? Thanks!","2026-01-12T13:42:48.084Z"],["3803807","PFI-832394","PFI","monika.civrag@bolt.eu","Monika Čivrag","Hi [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] 🙂 \n\nThank you for the explanation on how to proceed. Just informing you that the payment failed so please proceed with blocking the user.\n\nNot sure if you can reply to the ticket once it is closed, but I just want to check what can I communicate to the driver, since in this case, he is charged with commission.","2026-01-12T13:43:10.608Z"],["3803809","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768225364475649]*{color}:\n<@U03P58BK5FY> does that mean we can proceed with Paula's suggestion or what are your thoughts here? [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768212832061739?thread_ts=1767619422.518249&amp;cid=C02FP2YL06L]\n\nLinked messages:\n[January 12th, 2026 2:13 AM] paula.espeja: Hi <@pema.matos> as mentioned, ideally, these movements should not be reflected on an invoice at all as they are out of scope of VAT. However, as a temporary solution is needed, the steps could be:\n1. If technically possible, use *dedicated compensation types presented on a separate compensation invoice/document*, rather than the regular monthly invoice.\n2. Ensure these compensation types are clearly labelled as *non-revenue* and *out of scope / VAT 0%*.\n3. Confirm that these amounts do *not flow into VAT reporting* or impact revenue figures.\n4. Limit the use strictly to *deposit paybacks / offboarding-related cases* as a temporary solution.\n5. Document this as an *exceptional workaround*, pending a proper product fix.\nIf using a separate compensation invoice is not possible and the amounts need to be included in the monthly invoice temporarily, then at a minimum they should be *clearly identified as out of scope and no VAT should be charged.*\n{quote}","2026-01-12T13:43:29.688Z"],["3803810","PFI-832350","PFI","andrea.caceres@bolt-outsource.eu","Andrea Luján Chávez Cáceres","Hi team, the problem in this case would be the final fare for the trip. The trip was made, but the system automatically performed a price review, marking the trip as not having taken place. For this reason, the final fare is marked as €0.00. Can you please help me with this?","2026-01-12T13:43:31.821Z"],["3803815","MKP-9653","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","Duplicate","2026-01-12T13:43:54.566Z"],["3803817","MKP-9653","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MKP-9733|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MKP-9733|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T13:44:01.074Z"],["3803819","LSS-60076","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hello [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nPlease find attached Certinal Order with redlines and comments from their legal.\n\nKindly provide your feedback and if we are good to proceed.\n\nThanks\n\n[^Jan 09_Certinal Order Form_Bolt.docx]\n\n","2026-01-12T13:44:32.988Z"],["3803820","PFI-813099","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi,\nWe need to refund back 10 PLN to the customer’s payment method and 6.34 PLN to their Bolt balance.","2026-01-12T13:44:57.334Z"],["3803821","LSS-61369","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hi, [~accountid:712020:fde8e40a-0c43-479b-a07d-dd05334dd10a] ! Can you please tell what exactly the link from Facebook covers? “*This content isn't available right now”*","2026-01-12T13:45:09.179Z"],["3803822","PFI-829900","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! I’d recommend to keep the communication less detailed. We’ve communicated with tax about this as well regarding risks. I recommend a response something similar to this: \n\n“At the moment, we’re not able to amend or reissue the invoices. Please note that drivers are expected to report VAT based on their actual tax status when submitting their tax returns.\n\nIf the tax authority reviews these invoices and asks for clarification or correction from Bolt, please let us know and we’ll review the situation further.”\n\nSo the same is for your side - if there’s issues from tax authority side, let us know and we’ll handle it further 🙂 ","2026-01-12T13:45:09.814Z"],["3803823","PAW-14801","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @suhovanton\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160404\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 13:45:20 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T13:45:21.024Z"],["3803825","PAW-14793","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @daysleeperx\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/autocode/pull/48\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 13:45:34 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T13:45:34.315Z"],["3803826","LSS-61308","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","The chart was uploaded automatically, I’ll try to look into it and understand.\nThank you for your patience.","2026-01-12T13:45:43.241Z"],["3803828","LSS-61416","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:712020:011a9eb3-77af-4c62-bb26-e6c10e6097ec]! Like we just discussed, we can start gathering the information, but the Police needs to send us the request in an oficial format (ofício).","2026-01-12T13:45:57.625Z"],["3803829","XP-3033","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","First point is clear - if we are adjusting for pre-test baseline then we should apply at same entity level as the baseline, which here should be [user] + [city]. As a side note, I think having [user] exploded by [city] has led to a lot of confusion and complexity, including incorrect variance estimation (assumes independence between units). \n\nI would be a fan of the following:\n\n* removing all non-targeted cities from data\n* assigning all activity of a user to their city of enrollment\n\nThis would leave only [user] level and fix the CUPED adjustment issue. The issue would be that we lose the ability to slice activity cleanly by city. However, this would be for a small share of users, and hopefully tests are run across neighboring cities which users are likely to move between.","2026-01-12T13:45:59.843Z"],["3803830","LSS-54291","LSS","viktor.skalivskyi@bolt.eu","Viktor Skalivskyi","Colleagues, thanks for your help! \n\n[~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] , [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7]  - I have included all your comments and suggestions in the document and will give it to the partner.\n\nNow they have to finally review everything and give it to me.","2026-01-12T13:46:01.850Z"],["3803831","CCM-22270","CCM","ilia.moroz@bolt-outsource.eu","Ilia Moroz","[^TalentLMS import sheet (1).xlsx]","2026-01-12T13:46:04.022Z"],["3803832","CSDT-951","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Backfill initiated, task considered to be done","2026-01-12T13:46:09.376Z"],["3803834","HS-28859","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Waiting information on the cancellation of NC.","2026-01-12T13:46:20.249Z"],["3803835","PIF-2223","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 10\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: ","2026-01-12T13:46:29.929Z"],["3803836","PIF-2214","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is well-structured and clearly connects to the business problem of offloading file upload responsibilities to a centralized service. However, the acceptance criteria could be more measurable and specific. For instance, in Scenario B, 'file is found malicious / infected by the antivirus' could specify the antivirus detection method or signature that would trigger blocking access. Similarly, for Scenarios C and D, defining thresholds for 'huge content' and 'abnormally large dimensions' would make the criteria more actionable and testable. Providing these specifics will ensure clear testing and validation processes.","2026-01-12T13:46:35.943Z"],["3803837","HWMISC-743","HWMISC","rasad.nadzafov@bolt.eu","Räšad Nadžafov","Tracking file updated (region-country-city level views) for Winter Repairs ('Global'). Progress review ongoing in regional calls based on tracking file data.","2026-01-12T13:46:46.530Z"],["3803838","SREDO-199","SREDO","tarmo.randel@bolt.eu","Tarmo Randel","rolling process within 14 days interval is good for stateless, with some additional points:\n\n* how emergency cases are solved (critical vulnerability actively exploited)\n* how exceptions are handled\n* how / where audit trail\n* how process integrity is checked\n\nMight be some other details as well but this is I leave for [~accountid:712020:44e59489-5db2-4488-8537-588bccee709b] to support you writing this down and making living process. We prefer you create process document yourself as you own the assets and process. Infosec needs to validate that process is working now-and-then (usually  audits, being it by in-house internal audit or other format).\n\nAivo will help with any questions and loop me in when necessary.","2026-01-12T13:46:49.561Z"],["3803839","LSS-61421","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T13:46:52.378Z"],["3803840","MARTECH3-1508","MARTECH3","sabrina.craffitasari@bolt.eu","Sabrina Lutfia Craffitasari","*Update Jan 12, 2026:*\n\n* Doc is accessible here [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7339410313/In+Review+2025-12+Eater+Reactivation+Discovery|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7339410313/In+Review+2025-12+Eater+Reactivation+Discovery|smart-link] \n* Some adjustments were required to align the method with Rider existing research, including calculation window and conversion window logic.","2026-01-12T13:46:52.672Z"],["3803841","WEB-9101","WEB","elizaveta.miroshnik@bolt.eu","Elizaveta Miroshnik","[~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] Yes, it could be closed 🙌 ","2026-01-12T13:47:00.911Z"],["3803843","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768225613579829]*{color}:\n<@U04FV4Z0GQ4> A potential temporary solution for handling deposit refunds would be to continue using the Viggo Console. However, this would require extending the use of a legacy tool and would only address one of the three outstanding issues—namely the refund of the equipment deposit. The remaining two challenges would still be unresolved: (1) transfer of the existing balance and (2) charging new FOs deposit for equipment.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T13:47:07.909Z"],["3803844","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768225624023879]*{color}:\nLet me know your toughts\n{quote}","2026-01-12T13:47:16.118Z"],["3803845","LSS-61413","LSS","mitch.aniebonam@bolt.eu","Mitch Aniebonam","Hey [~accountid:712020:7f47c2af-14e1-4206-a795-ac87cb906276] ! Yes the old ticket Mikael created is here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-32630|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-32630|smart-link] \n\nI added you as a participant. ","2026-01-12T13:47:22.001Z"],["3803846","FX-3365","FX","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:712020:3081727f-5ce0-4ec9-9ebc-e80faceb3d21] hey just to check, was this done? \n\n_Update default sort to be Request date, latest to oldest_\n\nWhen I’m landing on the page, I don’t see the kind of ‘sort’ indicator on the header, i.e \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 15.47.10.png|width=655,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 15.47.10.png\"!","2026-01-12T13:47:29.528Z"],["3803847","WEB-9100","WEB","elizaveta.miroshnik@bolt.eu","Elizaveta Miroshnik","[~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] Nothing else is explected, could be closed 🙌 ","2026-01-12T13:47:30.882Z"],["3803850","PFI-832459","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:0b5f2f39-ed53-492d-86d3-da6b3cc9d6f7],\n\nSeems like the user still has a *Hard block* on their profile, meaning that this has not been submitted to the Safety Team for review or that the process is incomplete.\n\nFraud Team does not remove *Hard-Blocks* from the profiles, we only help in removing the *device UID blocks* once the investigation has been finalized and the rest of the blocks have been removed.\nFor visual reference, please see the block mentioned:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 15.47.42.png|width=257,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 15.47.42.png\"!\n\nPlease let us know once the profile has been finalized.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you,\nMarten","2026-01-12T13:47:53.844Z"],["3803851","PC-3864","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI Meeting notes:\n- Rejecting it for now, as multiple tables contain multiple columns and need to find what benefits we will get from this exercise.","2026-01-12T13:48:03.669Z"],["3803854","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768225692491869]*{color}:\nJust keep in mind that we get these type of messages daily, and it will only increase:\n\nLinked files:\n* [image.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A90K9L8KA/image.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-12T13:48:25.311Z"],["3803856","PFI-832467","PFI","janek.vassin@bolt.eu","Janek Vassin","!image-20260112-134815.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T13:48:47.386Z"],["3803857","PFI-832467","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T13:48:49.596Z"],["3803859","DLSP-1982","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","released","2026-01-12T13:49:13.181Z"],["3803860","DLSP-2005","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","released","2026-01-12T13:49:19.774Z"],["3803863","SREDO-199","SREDO","tarmo.randel@bolt.eu","Tarmo Randel","for stateful systems twice a year would mean that there has to be ton of compensating controls in place. I suggest to figure out how to perform updates at least monthly, otherwise stricter access and management controls must be created.","2026-01-12T13:50:16.887Z"],["3803864","PFI-832470","PFI","folashade.akinsola@bolt.eu","Folashade Dolapo Akinsola","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 09.39.57.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T13:50:34.494Z"],["3803865","PFI-832470","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T13:50:36.838Z"],["3803870","LSS-61422","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","[^oneNDA_commercial_discussions.docx] _(3.11 MB)_","2026-01-12T13:51:20.593Z"],["3803871","WD-22535","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:6155b83199b4b8006a66bfd8], i just got information that person responsible was on holiday and got back today. The report was promised to be approved today.","2026-01-12T13:51:56.364Z"],["3803872","PC-3862","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI Meeting Notes:\n\n* Agreed on the approach (also mentioned in the task) to have versions at the end.\n* Closing this task for now, for all new APIs team needs to follow the new approach, will add them into [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4564385793/Customer+Payments+Coding+Standards|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4564385793/Customer+Payments+Coding+Standards|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T13:52:05.710Z"],["3803875","PFI-832394","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:16feeee2-7721-43a0-8e2d-529b2d00b3e8],\n\nThe rider will be blocked.\n\nPlease compensate the commission fee for the driver so that it would zero out everything.\nThere will be no gain or cost for this specific order.\nThe drivers should be aware of destination changes, and in this case it was not done, therefore the fault lays with them.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-12T13:52:23.205Z"],["3803877","RISK2-2634","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","fields shared with LogicGate here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09RH0NTS8J/p1767795950457459|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09RH0NTS8J/p1767795950457459|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T13:52:58.113Z"],["3803883","RISK2-2894","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","We agreed on the [https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/1HBlCkA3SY4p5Ypa_X5PKEx8dhwyrjVBO2MVSd6yWPXU/edit|https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/1HBlCkA3SY4p5Ypa_X5PKEx8dhwyrjVBO2MVSd6yWPXU/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T13:53:43.859Z"],["3803884","PFI-832394","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Additionally, forgot to mention, but if the rider can not change destinations, then it means that something is up with the rider, therefore the driver should not agree to driving somewhere else. They should only either 1) Drive to the initially requested destination or 2) Cancel the journey.","2026-01-12T13:53:45.882Z"],["3803886","DBRE-8688","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","{noformat}mysql> USE `taxify_category_stats`;\nDatabase changed\nmysql> show create table _category_stats_old_del\\G\n*************************** 1. row ***************************\n       Table: _category_stats_old_del\nCreate Table: CREATE TABLE `_category_stats_old_del` (\n  `id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `created` timestamp NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `last_update` timestamp NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `activated` timestamp NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `deactivated` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,\n  `driver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `vehicle_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `source` enum('driver_state','driver_location','fleet_system','driver_dispatch_pref','category_config') NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(10) unsigned NOT NULL,\n  `category_group` varchar(45) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `category_group_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `driver_id_finished` (`driver_id`,`deactivated`),\n  KEY `activated_idx` (`activated`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=40273072838 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4\n1 row in set (0.00 sec)\n\nmysql> RENAME TABLE `_category_stats_old_del` TO `_category_stats_old_20250112083252_del`;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected (0.00 sec){noformat}","2026-01-12T13:54:08.801Z"],["3803888","HS-28867","HS","yousef.moungad@bolt.eu","Yousef Moungad","[^FS4 Bolt.pdf]","2026-01-12T13:54:21.573Z"],["3803889","PFI-817652","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello [~accountid:61ae4180ebce470067c8cdc8] ,\n\nThe option to top up is what has been disabled. If the customers have already existing top ups on their account, it will be automatically deducted when they are making their next orders unless the top up amount is too small to cover for the full trip order amount. I will reach out to the Knowledge Management team to update the articles about the Top Up options in Switzerland, Netherlands and Italy.","2026-01-12T13:54:22.651Z"],["3803890","LSS-61423","LSS","elizabeth.aarma@bolt.eu","Elizabeth Aarma","[^VOLIKIRI.docx] _(101 kB)_","2026-01-12T13:54:31.536Z"],["3803891","PC-3178","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI Meeting notes:\n\n* Closing it for now, considering the priority of this change occurrence and required efforts to change to another approach (e.g. dynamic config).","2026-01-12T13:54:36.613Z"],["3803892","LSS-61423","LSS","elizabeth.aarma@bolt.eu","Elizabeth Aarma","[^Lepingutaotluse vorm (Tamrex Ohutuse OÜ).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T13:54:40.849Z"],["3803894","PFI-830875","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! These orders were done with the users work profile, not business profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-billing-profile/profiles?filter={\"filter\"%3A{\"user_id\"%3A54396095}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-billing-profile/profiles?filter=%7B%22filter%22%3A%7B%22user_id%22%3A54396095%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-12T13:55:45.733Z"],["3803898","PFI-832471","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T13:56:18.144Z"],["3803900","FRAUDOPS-1058","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","Okay, I’ve concluded that there currently is not easy pattern to follow that would help us with the Fraud scenarios. I am closing this case with the note that there may be future opportunities here.\n\n[https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3355551972186862?o=3598988355446810|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3355551972186862?o=3598988355446810]","2026-01-12T13:56:22.534Z"],["3803907","RISK2-3132","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","last sync with UK Compliance team [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09BE0AFYF4/p1767960880918669], notes here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BP2E4kURIAfe4xDgTP8BmzKMDhjw4IBcbs1c8-1NPrc/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BP2E4kURIAfe4xDgTP8BmzKMDhjw4IBcbs1c8-1NPrc/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T13:57:35.453Z"],["3803908","FRAUD-5676","FRAUD","liisi.laasik@bolt.eu","Liisi Dovbnja","Merged branch: [https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/pull/4558|https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/pull/4558|smart-link]. Waiting for data to magically appear in Databricks","2026-01-12T13:57:35.789Z"],["3803911","GRWA-1490","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","* dbt: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15288|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15288|smart-link] \n* airflow: [https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9687|https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9687|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T13:57:45.892Z"],["3803912","PAW-14570","PAW","mateusz.olszewski@bolt.eu","Mateusz Olszewski","Change already developed: [https://github.com/bolteu/alter-golang/pull/149|https://github.com/bolteu/alter-golang/pull/149|smart-link] . Closing the clarification.","2026-01-12T13:57:55.176Z"],["3803915","WFM-9949","WFM","bolajoko.kufoniyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Bolajoko Kufoniyi","Noted, thank you [~accountid:712020:74b4c3fb-6caf-4d5d-b7f8-c2ea38318e58] ","2026-01-12T13:58:15.309Z"],["3803916","PC-3935","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI meeting notes:\n\n* Need to publish a guideline for the team to add such feature supported logs, so they are clear and understandable. Prefixing with “feature-*” will help later cleanup of such logs without any extra investigations.\n* We have done some cleanup of such logs in the past months for PSP services and instrument services. [~accountid:61de8e0e7c6f980070b38d2b] \n* Closing it for now. ","2026-01-12T13:58:23.204Z"],["3803918","PFI-741241","PFI","clara.machado@bolt.eu","Clara Oliveira Machado","Hi team, \n\nI am having the same trouble. [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-832348|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-832348|smart-link] \n\nThanks","2026-01-12T13:59:21.572Z"],["3803929","LSS-58896","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:5b7bea33409ab057771e428c] I have reviewed the final draft and am comfortable. This version is approved for signature. ","2026-01-12T14:00:12.870Z"],["3803932","WD-22559","WD","bianca.medrea@bolt.eu","Bianca Medrea","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 15.47.54.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 15.48.05.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T14:01:32.019Z"],["3803934","PFI-826667","PFI","mark.bauer@bolt-outsource.eu","Mark Bauer","Apologies if the issue’s unclear - the coureir made a payment to the wrong account. Would it be possible to transfer that money to the correct account, so that the courier wouldn’t have to pay again?","2026-01-12T14:01:44.852Z"],["3803935","WD-22544","WD","ingrid.valgejarv@bolt.eu","Ingrid Valgejärv","Hey [~accountid:712020:176612de-64ab-442f-84ee-ed63bbac2b50], please move this ticket to People Tech team. Thank you!","2026-01-12T14:01:45.025Z"],["3803936","PRV-858","PRV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Updated KB here: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/70724?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/70724?country=global&language=en]\n\n\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02A2CYJSJ0/p1768226389929279|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02A2CYJSJ0/p1768226389929279|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T14:01:47.179Z"],["3803937","FRAUDOPS-1114","FRAUDOPS","andreas.latt@bolt.eu","Andreas Peeter Lätt","Tried finding more recent examples from same gateway, because they are faster to debug (I have some intermediate tables saved for last 120 days), but couldn't manually find more similar issues on checking like 10 orders","2026-01-12T14:01:52.358Z"],["3803941","LSS-61308","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] This is the latest version. I’ve checked with my colleagues, and we’re currently trying to understand why the entity was still shown.\n\n[^orgchart (1).pdf] ","2026-01-12T14:02:26.588Z"],["3803942","HS-28749","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountid:619e65173618cd006f8b68c9], we haven’t heard from you in a while. \n\nIf you’d like to keep this request open or have any additional information, please leave a comment, and we’ll get back to you as soon as possible.\n\nIf we don’t hear from you soon, we’ll proceed with closing the ticket, but feel free to reopen it anytime if needed.","2026-01-12T14:02:31.302Z"],["3803943","HS-28252","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountid:63