updated.","2026-01-12T14:02:43.681Z"],["3803972","L10N-27184","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:02:43.806Z"],["3803973","L10N-27178","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:02:44.052Z"],["3803974","L10N-27185","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:02:44.106Z"],["3803975","L10N-27183","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:02:44.464Z"],["3803976","L10N-27179","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:02:45.877Z"],["3803977","L10N-27180","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:02:47.434Z"],["3803978","L10N-27177","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:02:47.799Z"],["3803979","L10N-27181","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:02:47.842Z"],["3803980","L10N-27182","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:02:48.233Z"],["3803983","PFI-832394","PFI","monika.civrag@bolt.eu","Monika Čivrag","Thank you so much for the help. Have a nice day 🌞 ","2026-01-12T14:03:36.169Z"],["3803984","EBIKE1-366","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","Trying to make the validation this week {{2026-01-12}} - {{2026-01-16}} ","2026-01-12T14:03:41.993Z"],["3803986","PFI-814169","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","The refund of 10 PLN has now been successfully completed and should reflect on the customer’s account within 10 working days according to their bank internal processes.","2026-01-12T14:03:52.100Z"],["3803987","HS-28857","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:af987dc6-5d01-4b78-85a4-1365b29ddf64],\n\nI have sent the new form to [~accountid:712020:b16fc504-b70f-420b-9b1a-a29502f04664]. Once i have the new form, I will share it with payroll and close this ticket. \n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin  ","2026-01-12T14:03:52.365Z"],["3803988","RDS-1406","RDS","mariia.drohanova@bolt.eu","Mariia Drohanova","hey, I’ll take a look later this week. But I am afraid the volumes will be very low compared to everything else :smiling_face_with_tear: ","2026-01-12T14:04:03.489Z"],["3803989","LSS-61352","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:a975e2d9-679b-4d8a-a063-b831aafacd02]! The addendum has been sent for signing. You can track the process here: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341799|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341799|smart-link] \n\nI believe you should have received an invitation to set up an account with Spotdraft today or you should shortly receive one.","2026-01-12T14:04:16.289Z"],["3803990","LSS-61424","LSS","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","[^Bolt_Cybernetica SOW- Bolt chauffeur app pentesting.pdf] _(129 kB)_","2026-01-12T14:04:17.695Z"],["3803993","EBIKE1-367","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","Waiting for feedback from [~accountid:5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] . Hoping to release this to Genfo this week.","2026-01-12T14:04:28.623Z"],["3803994","WEBSD-1444","WEBSD","jan.huk@bolt.eu","Jan Huk","Please can you help with processing this?","2026-01-12T14:04:31.571Z"],["3803996","GS-251","GS","suzana.ene@bolt.eu","Suzana-Elisabeta-Georgiana Ene","Task on routing side was created: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/GRN-83|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/GRN-83]","2026-01-12T14:04:59.575Z"],["3803997","DLSP-1972","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","released","2026-01-12T14:05:01.811Z"],["3803998","LSS-61424","LSS","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","Correction, the date of testing is not later than 31th of January 2026!","2026-01-12T14:05:17.709Z"],["3804001","DRAG-636","DRAG","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] Can You please make ticket for 8 D3 motors with tires? 4 for homologation and 4 for in house development. I sent You my old ticket details in WeSlack.","2026-01-12T14:05:47.996Z"],["3804003","TS-4656","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","Proposed date: 29.01, 13:00-15:00, will confirm","2026-01-12T14:06:24.216Z"],["3804005","PFI-832348","PFI","clara.machado@bolt.eu","Clara Oliveira Machado","Hi [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] \n\nThanks. \n\nPlease consider values bellow: \n\n\n\n*Invoices Values:*\n\nKyle Poole Portugal NIF: 502857145 \n\n* Delivery fee 2.08€ \n* Service Fee 1.37€\n\nCecile McLorin Salvant Portugal NIF: 502857145 \n\n* Delivery fee 2.79€ \n* Service Fee 1.37€\n\nYasushi Nakamura Portugal NIF: 502857145 \n\n* Delivery Fee 2.59€ \n* Service Fee 1.37€ \n\n\n\n*Report Values*\n\nKyle Poole Portugal NIF: 502857145 \n\n* Delivery fee 4.25€\n* Service Fee 2.89€\n\nCecile McLorin Salvant Portugal NIF: 502857145 \n\n* Delivery fee 3.12€\n* Service Fee 2.72€\n\nYasushi Nakamura Portugal NIF: 502857145 \n\n* Delivery Fee 2.86€ \n* Service Fee 1.62€ \n\n\n\nLet me know of you need additional info.\n\n\n\nBest, \n\nClara.","2026-01-12T14:06:48.383Z"],["3804006","DLSP-2008","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","it has been implemented in another task","2026-01-12T14:07:26.414Z"],["3804012","PIF-3277","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED, ADR_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* The draft provides a brief explanation of the new feature to enforce the use of the local backend for debugging purposes. The information from the Jira ticket indicates why this feature is valuable, particularly for developers using Visual Studio Code. However, additional documentation or an ADR reference about this implementation might be needed for further technical details.","2026-01-12T14:08:33.269Z"],["3804014","GUM-36","GUM","octavian.moraru@bolt.eu","Octavian Moraru","Tested the following flows in prelive:\n\n✅ Order is accepted while driver is inside the geofence (within 500 meters of the pick-up location) → the “pick-up issue” option is present\n\n✅ Order is accepted while driver is outside of the geofence → the “pick-up issue” option is not present and is added once the driver enters the geofence; if the driver exits the geofence, the “pick-up issue” option remains in the list\n\n✅ Order is accepted while driver is outside of the geofence, riders updates the pick-up location → the “pick-up issue” option is added once the driver enters the _new_ pick-up’s geofence.","2026-01-12T14:08:36.670Z"],["3804015","PIF-2213","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft succinctly explains the new feature's addition, the problem it addresses, and its importance in chaos testing by isolating high-frequency callers to better identify vulnerable services. The placeholders are needed for the specific component admin panel view and additional resources which aren't available from the given information.","2026-01-12T14:08:41.991Z"],["3804018","LSS-50765","LSS","ariana.saplana@bolt.eu","Ariana Saplana","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742], thank you so much for this. It will be super helpful for upcoming campaigns! It looks very good as it is, I don’t have any questions, so you can close the ticket now. I’ll reach out to you again if I have any concerns but for now it looks perfect to me!","2026-01-12T14:09:14.982Z"],["3804019","HS-28781","HS","loredana.panait@bolt.eu","Loredana Panait","Hi [~accountid:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d] , \n\nThank you for the confirmation. \n\nBut the active ees were asked to fil int he new form, correct? Meaning is mandatory for them to do it now anyway, and again later if anything will change.\n\nAppreciate the feedback, \nLore","2026-01-12T14:09:34.515Z"],["3804020","DSR-3651","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Data shared with user","2026-01-12T14:09:38.906Z"],["3804022","DO-5780","DO","michal.konarski@bolt.eu","Michał Konarski","Owner assigned.","2026-01-12T14:09:41.453Z"],["3804023","LSS-61302","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:712020:52c03b81-3e44-455b-a71d-0e9088f7c7ad] the T&Cs according to this master agreement (sec. 8.6.) won’t apply. Please delate point 1.2. of the special terms as this provision will not apply in case of credit card payments only. Otherwise the contract can be forwarded to the client. \n\nPlease let me know in case you require further assistance. Thank you ","2026-01-12T14:09:59.100Z"],["3804028","LSS-61088","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Finalized to be shared with Partner. Still with Partner. No update.","2026-01-12T14:11:00.522Z"],["3804029","DRAG101-405","DRAG101","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] I will look into this but worst case we have to measure the power in Velotech before certification - right now Genfo measurements are 50W off compared to Velotech measurement (370W for Genfo and 420W for Velotech).\nI think that Genfo used the actual battery compared to velotech, which used power supply. I will check with Genfo what can be done.\nIt would be beneficial to know the following:\n  1. D3 measurement results\n\n# Allowed power deviation tolerance.\n\nBased on this we can have make a decision how to proceed with this. ","2026-01-12T14:11:37.876Z"],["3804032","SCM-1116","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","As of 12.01:\n1. Barcelona has accumulated 16 broken EB1 IOTs.\n2. Kaarel will finish the list of repair parts by 13.01.\n","2026-01-12T14:11:45.284Z"],["3804035","PAW-14794","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @not-much-io\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160393\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 14:12:17 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T14:12:17.742Z"],["3804037","PIF-3277","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 9\n• Problem Definition: 9\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: The story is mostly clear but could benefit from additional details in the acceptance criteria. Specifically, it would be helpful to specify how the dedicated query parameter should be formatted and any verification steps to confirm the correct backend is being used. For relevance, while the task improves the developer experience, it could slightly better highlight impacts on efficiency or other platform objectives. Acceptance criteria should also define what 'using local backend' specifically entails, considering scenarios of potential conflicts or unexpected behaviors.","2026-01-12T14:12:21.990Z"],["3804038","PIF-2213","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 9\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is mostly clear; however, the concept of 'targeting service' and 'chaos test' could be defined briefly for additional clarity. Additionally, the acceptance criteria could be more specific regarding how the exclusion of high-frequency callers should be implemented. It would be beneficial to include success metrics or thresholds to determine what defines a successful test outside of the RPM specification.","2026-01-12T14:12:26.239Z"],["3804043","CCM-22268","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Thank you for clarifying. 🙂 \n\nI added you now to more Food courses and all as isntructor, including the ones you had before. The most importnat ones are onbaording and up-skill and some local courses, like Cashback and Dine-in.\n\nThe rest of the trainings are practically the same units from the onboarding, just put as a separate course, such as Admin etc.\n\nLet me know if something else is needed. 🙌 \n\n\nBest,\nIrena","2026-01-12T14:13:12.583Z"],["3804046","HWMISC-771","HWMISC","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","I asked for an update from Mr. Ilves. He says that the flat braid wires they tried using did not work, because they needed too much heat to solder and as the length of the wire is so short, you can not solder one end at once.\n\nHe also said that have been repaired with the solder wick method coming back with broken nickel again are never due to a failed repair but it has actually failed at a different spot.\n\n\n\nBased on this I would say that the solution with solder wick works and until we have not found a better and more reliable method we can continue using it and update the SOP according to Ilvestments method.","2026-01-12T14:13:41.510Z"],["3804047","PFI-831591","PFI","sophie.chavaregi@bolt-outsource.eu","Sophie Chavaregi","New agent here; the ticket raised is “ UK National Living Wage adjustment review\" D has filed an appeal for the email they received as attached \n\n!Screenshot_2025-12-22-19-51-47-229_com.google.android.gm.jpg|width=720,height=1600,alt=\"Screenshot_2025-12-22-19-51-47-229_com.google.android.gm.jpg\"!\n\n","2026-01-12T14:15:02.654Z"],["3804052","BR-4095","BR","triinu.tasa@bolt.eu","Triinu Tasa","‘ma' needs to be added to dynamic config setting {{ride_hailing_partnerAggregated_hideInterestInfoCountryList}} in billing-document","2026-01-12T14:15:58.563Z"],["3804054","LSS-61353","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:a975e2d9-679b-4d8a-a063-b831aafacd02]! The addendum has been sent out for signing. You can track the progress here: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341807|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341807|smart-link] .\n\nLet me know if you have any questions 🙂 ","2026-01-12T14:16:40.730Z"],["3804056","HWMISC-776","HWMISC","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","LD suggested that as the raw material price is fluctuating at the moment, they can not give us a reliable quotation and that we should wait until the price of aluminum has stabilized before agreeing on a price. \n\n\n\n[~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e] what would you suggest in this kind of situation? Should we wait until after CNY to fix the price? We are not in a hurry really because we have so many of those brakes already in stock as I explained below.","2026-01-12T14:16:50.381Z"],["3804057","LSS-61427","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T14:16:55.732Z"],["3804059","DO-5784","DO","michal.konarski@bolt.eu","Michał Konarski","Closed on reporter request.","2026-01-12T14:17:11.992Z"],["3804061","L10N-27416","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27414](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27414)\n\nThanks for collabo