T14:17:17.795Z"],["3804067","L10N-27426","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27414](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27414)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T14:17:18.751Z"],["3804068","L10N-27427","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27414](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27414)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-12T14:17:19.208Z"],["3804070","CCM-22269","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey Ademola 👋 \n\nIt has been resolved in your previous ticket.\n\nLet me know if something else will be needed. 🌷 \n\nBest,\n\nIrena","2026-01-12T14:17:48.823Z"],["3804071","PFI-831543","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Mentioning it juuuust in case, sometimes people tend to miss this part: the invoices are from fleet to Bolt, meaning *Bolt pays the fleet*. This is any bonuses and adjustments that are not part of the individual order invoices from fleet to eater.\n\nSo likely it means that either couriers completed more deliveries, the delivery prices were higher, Bolt offered more bonuses etc. Most likely it’s a combination of all of these aspects 🙂 ","2026-01-12T14:17:50.195Z"],["3804072","XP-3033","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","Second point - it is not clear to me that CUPED is diverging from the metric definition. The metric definition is applied to the table aggregation level (e.g. sum all orders per user), and then in the CUPED query we have the following per CTE: \n\n* {{temp_cuped_[test/pretest]_variables}} the average value per metric per user (summed across period, then averaged over cities) ✅  \n* {{temp_cuped_theta_computation}} sample averages of metric are calculated over test and pretest periods, as per CUPED formula ✅ \n\nIm sum, I don’t think there is an issue here with the {{AVG}} that is different from the first issue, i.e. we should not apply _over different levels of granularity._","2026-01-12T14:17:54.280Z"],["3804074","TS-4656","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","Booked 29.01, 13:00-14:00, created the event and invited everyone.\n\nShould start creating slides - will use the previous year’s as the template.","2026-01-12T14:18:28.586Z"],["3804076","LSS-55531","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Thank You! Seems as this has indeed been solved then. I will close the ticket 💛 ","2026-01-12T14:18:36.442Z"],["3804079","IDC-1482","IDC","sergei.mironenko@bolt.eu","Sergei Mironenko","Marina to update the description.","2026-01-12T14:19:11.494Z"],["3804081","PFI-831415","PFI","dominika.wozniak@bolt-outsource.eu","Dominika Woźniak","The user is complaining that even after removing a user (Julia Opolska) from their Bolt business admin panel, invoices for that user's rides still appear on the company account, despite those rides being paid privately by the user. She questions whether deleting a user in Bolt automatically removes their connection to the company.","2026-01-12T14:19:37.861Z"],["3804084","SCM-572","SCM","omar.masum@bolt.eu","Omar Faruk Masum","[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] Hi, as discussed last overview meeting. This ticket we need to restart from beginning, as per last FAE meeting they want to go through majority of Dragon (D1) parts to make compatible with Dragon (D2) spare parts and adjust in WD.\n\nCurrently they finished adjustment and mark majority D1 parts in WD “restricted from purchasing” and updated the D1 and D2 purchase item group information. Now we need to collect again all “Inactive”, ““restricted from purchasing” and “non-rotating” spare parts complete list for FAE review to take their expect opinion about these parts future usability and take disposition recommendation ","2026-01-12T14:20:31.080Z"],["3804085","LSS-61096","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nJust to check, are we good to proceed with Articulate?\n\nWe now want to have 9 licences.\n\nThanks\n\n[^Articulate Renewal - ART-1241128 (2).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T14:20:35.340Z"],["3804092","RNTL-28048","RNTL","maksym.petrenko@bolt.eu","Maks Petrenko","Ticket is closed as a duplicate - 'cause it can only be tested, once BE implementation is done. ","2026-01-12T14:22:02.314Z"],["3804095","LSS-59665","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Agreement on provision of services_Bolt Operations OÜ_Astronex LLC_25.11.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T14:22:30.677Z"],["3804098","PRODSEC-559","PRODSEC","andres.jogi@bolt.eu","Andres Jõgi","[~accountid:5fca4b937cc1030069d2bae5] \n\nThis was initially meant as a follow-up epic to build something to allow for fancier integration (e.g. service we could call from Elastic of TheHive) for enrichment. However seeing internal-sec plans with TheHive are in state of change, I see no reason to expand on it for now. \n\nLet’s stick to current plan (under onboarding epic) and existing Q1 roadmap, no need to add separate epic.","2026-01-12T14:23:15.042Z"],["3804101","LSS-61428","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","[^AA South Africa - Notice of Termination of Contract .pdf] _(89 kB)_","2026-01-12T14:23:24.998Z"],["3804104","RNTL-30279","RNTL","robin.sulg@bolt.eu","Robin Sulg","Issue is that the persistence of intereference events saved only one. \nBecause in Oslo we have 3 models, then some events were not persisted leading to data regression","2026-01-12T14:23:39.543Z"],["3804106","CBFP-1011","CBFP","uladzislau.klimiankou@bolt.eu","Vlad Klimenkov","Inserted tasks to regen artefacts. [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160105|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160105|smart-link] \n\nWill be processed within ~40h","2026-01-12T14:24:54.324Z"],["3804107","CRC-1987","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Business Case revisited and linked","2026-01-12T14:25:30.809Z"],["3804109","CRC-1988","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Business Case revisited and linked","2026-01-12T14:25:38.486Z"],["3804111","CRC-1989","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Business Case revisited and linked","2026-01-12T14:25:45.788Z"],["3804112","PAW-14809","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-alex-somai\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160423\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 14:25:48 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T14:25:48.784Z"],["3804113","CRC-1990","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Business Case revisited and linked","2026-01-12T14:25:51.921Z"],["3804114","WD-22512","WD","demetri.manias@bolt.eu","Demetri Manias","Hi Oana,\n\nI get the same error message.\n\nThanks for your help,\nDemetri","2026-01-12T14:25:58.174Z"],["3804115","LSS-61401","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey!  Thank You! Please find the signed document attached from our side.\n\n[^Annex 2 - Rental premise handover act (üleandmise akt)_Bolt Store EE OÜ_OÜ Toompuiestee Büroohoone_06.12.24.asice]\n\nOnce getting this countersigned please send it to [contracts@bolt.eu|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] with a ticket number for archiving purposes and attach the document here for our own records.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T14:25:58.856Z"],["3804116","PAW-14807","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-alex-somai\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/pull/3077\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 14:26:00 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T14:26:00.955Z"],["3804117","WD-22546","WD","aneta.kopka@bolt.eu","Aneta Kopka","[^FC132860BLEE.pdf]","2026-01-12T14:26:04.043Z"],["3804118","PFI-831306","PFI","vieira.andre@bolt-outsource.eu","Andre Vieira","The block has been removed, please lift device block","2026-01-12T14:26:07.935Z"],["3804119","DAEN-1196","DAEN","liilia.tagel@bolt.eu","Liilia Tagel","{{gmv.view}} will be deprecated fully along with {{city_kpi_full}} explore, where it’s still currently used. ","2026-01-12T14:26:17.644Z"],["3804120","LSS-59751","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] \n\nWe received feedback from Pipedrive\n\n* *AI Model Training / Third-Party Use:* Our Terms (Section 3.11) explicitly state that we do not permit third parties to use Client Data to train their AI models. The only exception is if you were to specifically opt into a \"Beta Service.\" Standard service usage does not involve any AI training on your data.\n* *Data Use After Termination:* Our DPA (Section 5.11) ensures your data is not held indefinitely. Upon termination, we delete or return data per your instructions. By default, closed accounts are deleted within 180 days and server backups are retained for 90 days.\n* *Data Protection & Resilience:* To ensure no loss or corruption, we use AES-256 encryption at rest and TLS in transit. We maintain off-site backups and are independently audited for *ISO 27001, ISO 27701, and SOC 2 Type II*.\n* *EU Data Residency:* For EU-based clients, data is hosted within the EEA (Frankfurt and Dublin). Our DPA incorporates EU Standard Contractual Clauses, and Pipedrive Inc. is registered under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework. (Note: Once the account is provisioned, our support team can confirm your specific data centre location).\n* *Improvements & Anonymisation:* Any data used for Pipedrive’s internal service improvements is strictly limited to anonymised or aggregated forms, ensuring no Personal Data is exposed during our operational analysis.","2026-01-12T14:26:36.446Z"],["3804121","SRED-982","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Speed comparison:\n\n{noformat}# SSH\nPLAY RECAP **********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************\nr9.redis.boltint.net       : ok=39   changed=0    unreachable=0    failed=0    skipped=18   rescued=0    ignored=0   \n\n\nreal    0m34.930s\nuser    0m4.000s\nsys     0m3.677s\n\n# SSM\nPLAY RECAP **********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************\nr9.redis.boltint.net       : ok=39   changed=0    unreachable=0    failed=0    skipped=18   rescued=0    ignored=0   \n\n\nreal    3m7.282s\nuser    0m18.603s\nsys     0m8.471s{noformat}\n\nSo it takes longer, but in general we’re not running it so often. But it provides nice features, like audit and we don’t need to support ssm-agent anymore.\n\nHope that it will be improved [https://github.com/ansible-collections/amazon.aws/issues/2636|https://github.com/ansible-collections/amazon.aws/issues/2636|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T14:27:04.779Z"],["3804122","WFM-9938","WFM","floriana.rotella@bolt-outsource.eu","Floriana Rotella","Solved for both! Thank you!","2026-01-12T14:27:19.704Z"],["3804123","CSDT-949","CSDT","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","{{2026-01-12}} \n\nasked to delete old dashboards created by Asia and Snezana - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CF65PRL0N/p1768224440398559|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CF65PRL0N/p1768224440398559|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T14:27:20.406Z"],["3804124","GRN-99","GRN","karl.nurmeots@bolt.eu","Karl Nurmeots","ADR [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7340327028/2026-01+cold-traffic+speeds+as+rates+in+live+traffic|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7340327028/2026-01+cold-traffic+speeds+as+rates+in+live+traffic|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T14:27:25.353Z"],["3804126","LSS-61429","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^260112_BOL_PoA - Sophie Kotyzová case.docx.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T14:27:59.325Z"],["3804129","WD-17663","WD","anett.suurkask@bolt.eu","Anett Suurkask","Hey, we need to continue same number logic under BG002, could you please set it up in a way that first invoice number in BG0002 would be +0000000024+? \n\nalso it needs to be looked how it was made with Delivery vertical invoice numbers.. i think they started with 1000000000 under BG001.. and same way they should continue their logic as well in BG002. ","2026-01-12T14:29:36.166Z"],["3804130","HS-27878","HS","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Hey [~accountid:712020:dc0e5673-b376-43a7-acc2-defd031fd9cf] \n\nThe police has contacted us again regarding this case and sent us the Decision on declaring the temporary residence permit invalid. \nBeehive link [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/722125837]\nIs there any response required or we can close the Beehive ticket? \n\n\n\n[^Santiago Ariel Cobanera arvamused ja vastuv... (1).pdf.pdf]\n[^15.3-3.41685-2 12.01.2026 Väljaminev kiri.asice.asice]\n\n","2026-01-12T14:29:41.790Z"],["3804132","HS-28762","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:58704fb5-3b31-40a0-896f-1d862e6e1fd9],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-12T14:30:03.119Z"],["3804133","HS-28766","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:dc4824f4-a6bc-41f2-af89-59d155dc0cc8],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-12T14:30:07.641Z"],["3804135","FDBT-4770","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_delivery fails on 2026-01-11 07:00:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task pl_and_ledger_task failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details. This caused all downstream tasks to get skipped.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 402131561854334, 'task_key': 'pl_and_ledger_task'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_delivery/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-0