Hector, these should be under road tax renewal. Thank you. Also, left the same comment in the document\n\n!image-20260112-143157.png|width=314,height=802,alt=\"image-20260112-143157.png\"!\n\n!image-20260112-143211.png|width=272,height=396,alt=\"image-20260112-143211.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-12T14:33:22.879Z"],["3804180","L10N-27194","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:21.789Z"],["3804181","L10N-27190","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.021Z"],["3804182","L10N-27184","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.109Z"],["3804183","L10N-27177","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.167Z"],["3804184","L10N-27189","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.204Z"],["3804185","L10N-27182","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.275Z"],["3804186","L10N-27180","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.293Z"],["3804187","L10N-27185","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.297Z"],["3804188","L10N-27188","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.312Z"],["3804189","L10N-27183","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.426Z"],["3804190","L10N-27181","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.537Z"],["3804191","L10N-27178","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.639Z"],["3804192","L10N-27179","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T14:33:22.892Z"],["3804195","RDS-1286","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:c2b6ad0f-ebef-4615-8ab7-22b2786cdf4c] Wow! Thanks.","2026-01-12T14:34:51.069Z"],["3804196","LSS-61419","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Document has been sent out for signing to both parties!","2026-01-12T14:35:14.725Z"],["3804197","LSS-61419","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341826|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341826]","2026-01-12T14:35:18.267Z"],["3804198","HS-27878","HS","ingrid.valgejarv@bolt.eu","Ingrid Valgejärv","Hey!\n\nThank you for reaching out! I checked with our Global Mobility team and they said we can ignore this email. This person no longer works at Bolt.\n\nKind regards\nIngrid","2026-01-12T14:35:20.820Z"],["3804200","PFI-832487","PFI","carlo.mizzon@bolt.eu","Carlo Mizzon","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 16.35.22.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T14:35:42.512Z"],["3804206","PFI-832126","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there,\n\nPlease try:\n\n* Open the [Client page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] in Admin \n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open  {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ - The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see another _error_ → let us know.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the tab (or under {{Partner Invoices}})\n\nBest regards\n\nNikolay Roll ","2026-01-12T14:36:40.994Z"],["3804208","PFI-832461","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Checking with Fondy. \n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768228496888009|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768228496888009]","2026-01-12T14:37:13.580Z"],["3804209","PFI-831927","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi,\n\nbilling ops does not deal with refunds - CS does refunds.","2026-01-12T14:37:28.230Z"],["3804211","PFI-832461","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThank you for escalating! \nThe customer payments team will check with Fondy why the payments were rejected. \nWill let you know once we have any updates. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T14:37:55.093Z"],["3804213","DMC-353","DMC","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","[~accountid:60950a25539c14006ae92e40] Have you watched the video? Doing the same as the agent and not getting the data prefilled?","2026-01-12T14:38:13.306Z"],["3804214","LSS-56022","LSS","ramone.edwards@bolt.eu","Ramone Edwards","Hey [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] \n\n\n\n\n\n# +*Driver’s earnings (gross and net of income tax and NI)*+\n\n*We need to provide an actual, itemised breakdown rather than a general explanation of where the driver can view this themselves. Please can you provide some form of documentary output (e.g. a report or export) showing:*\n\n* *Gross earnings;*\n* *Deductions (including income tax and NI); and*\n* *Net earnings,*\n*for the relevant period(s).*\n\nWould a CSV file, detailing the drivers' in-app earnings and subsequent payouts, be suitable? It won’t show Deductions. \n\n\n\n\n\n[^BalanceHistory.csv]\n\n[^BalanceHistory (3).csv]\n[^BalanceHistory (2).csv]\n[^BalanceHistory (1).csv]\n\n\n\n----\n\n\n\n# +*Periods of absence from driving and reasons*+\n\n*You’ve confirmed that any absence was due to document blocks, which is helpful, but we need this to be more specific. Please can you confirm, for each instance:*\n\n* *The exact dates the driver was unable to drive (from / to); and*\n* *The specific document(s) that were missing or not uploaded on each occasion.*\n\nAll periods of inactivity were caused by temporary account blocks, related to expired, missing, or incorrectly uploaded documents, or automated regulatory restrictions (e.g. maximum online time). The account was never terminated.\n\nBelow is a breakdown of each instance, including the exact dates and specific reasons/documents involved.\n\nh3. Document-Related Blocks\n\n# 21 Dec 2023 – 9 Dec 2024\n#* Reason: Expired Private Hire Driver Licence\n#* Document: Private Hire Driver Licence (uk_private_hire_driver_licence)\n# 21 Dec 2023 – 21 Dec 2023\n#* Reason: Expired document (undefined system document type)\n#* Document: Document type ID 2772 (system-defined)\n# 15 Feb 2024 – 3 Feb 2024\n#* Reason: Expired Certificate of Compliance\n#* Document: MOT / Certificate of Compliance (mot_document)\n# 15 Feb 2024 – 10 Feb 2024\n#* Reason: Expired Private Hire Vehicle Licence\n#* Document: Private Hire Vehicle Licence (uk_private_hire_vehicle_licence)\n# 15 Feb 2025 – 17 Feb 2025\n#* Reason: Expired Private Hire Vehicle Licence\n#* Document: Private Hire Vehicle Licence (uk_private_hire_vehicle_licence)\n# 15 Feb 2025 – 16 Feb 2025\n#* Reason: Expired Certificate of Compliance\n#* Document: MOT / Certificate of Compliance (mot_document)\n# 20 Oct 2025 – 22 Oct 2024\n#* Reason: Expired Private Hire Insurance Certificate\n#* Document: Private Hire Insurance Certificate (uk_vehicle_insurance)\n# 20 Oct 2025 – 1 Aug 2025\n#* Reason: Expired Private Hire Insurance Certificate\n#* Document: Private Hire Insurance Certificate (uk_vehicle_insurance)\n# 21 Dec 2026 – 10 Mar 2025\n#* Reason: Expired document (undefined system document type)\n#* Document: Document type ID 2772 (system-defined)\n\nh3. Incorrect or Pending Document Uploads\n\n# 17 Feb 2025 – 18 Feb 2025\n#* Reason: Incorrect document uploaded\n#* Document: Private Hire Vehicle Licence\n#* Details: The uploaded document did not meet requirements. The driver was instructed to upload a clear colour photo of the valid PHV licence via the Driver Portal.\n# 9 Dec 2024 – 9 Dec 2024\n#* Reason: Pending document review\n#* Document: Driver documentation under review\n# 22 Oct 2024 – 22 Oct 2024\n#* Reason: Pending document review\n#* Document: Insurance documentation under review\n# 10 Feb 2024 – 10 Feb 2024\n#* Reason: Pending document review\n#* Document: Vehicle / compliance documentation\n# 3 Feb 2024 – 3 Feb 2024\n#* Reason: Pending document review\n#* Document: Compliance documentation\n# 21 Dec 2023 – 22 Dec 2023\n#* Reason: Pending document review\n#* Document: Driver documentation\n\n\n\nh3. Automated Online Time Restrictions \n\nThe following were automatic safety restrictions applied when the driver exceeded the maximum permitted online time. These are not suspensions and were lifted automatically after rest periods:\n\n* 27 Nov 2023\n* 3 Jan 2024\n* 12 Jan 2024\n* 13 Jan 2024\n* 19 Jan 2024\n* 8 Dec 2024\n\nEach instance occurred after approximately 11 hours 50 minutes online, exceeding the 12-hour limit.\n\n\n\n\n\n----\n\n\n\n\n\n*Thank you for confirming that the account has not been terminated. Please can you also confirm whether the account has ever been suspended at any point, and if so:*\n\n* The effective date(s) of any suspension;\n* The reason(s) for the suspension; and\n* When the suspension was lifted.\n\nThere has been *no safety suspension* on the driver’s account, only documents or online time restrictions. All blocks were lifted automatically once documentation was approved or regulatory conditions were met.\n\n\n\nHappy to sign the certificate! ","2026-01-12T14:38:22.550Z"],["3804215","WD-22538","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hi [~accountid:61f7dc37f5f5b80070c6540e] Activity is reactivated in PRD and SBX. Please let us know when we can inactivate it again.","2026-01-12T14:38:31.783Z"],["3804217","LSS-61221","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:2104a9ba-c467-45fa-a185-561039c3b4d4] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^NOVEMBER 2025 SERVICE ACCEPTANCE-BOLT RIDES-BOLT TANZANIA (49a1438e-02e8-4bc9-9bb1-85bdc9a629dc).pdf] \n\n[^DECEMBER 2025 SERVICE ACCEPTANCE-BOLT RIDES-BOLT TANZANIA (5e676654-ba32-4eaf-8b71-7104dcc6cd3f).pdf] ","2026-01-12T14:38:56.994Z"],["3804218","LSS-61419","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you very much, [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] !","2026-01-12T14:39:31.289Z"],["3804219","GUM-36","GUM","octavian.moraru@bolt.eu","Octavian Moraru","In LIVE (without enabling the geofence_enabled dynamic config), I noticed [this|https://kibana-logs.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/r/s/yEIvZ] log message, coming from [here|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/1e50d9eca95e26d80c1db957455df60cb1126f82/src/rides/driver/driver_map_reports/main/service/DriverGeofenceDataService.ts#L117]. This sometimes seems to happen when we handle an {{OrderStopQueueChangeType.PICKUP_CHANGE}}  event.\n\nHad a look at a few orders to understand what’s going on. In all cases this happens if the Rider changes their pick-up _before_ the Driver accepts (or after they have explicitly rejected); the {{OrderStopQueueChangeType.PICKUP_CHANGE}}event contains the previously assigned driver’s id. Guessing that this is expected behaviour for this case 🤷‍♂️ \n\nExample: [Log|https://kibana-logs.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/discover#/doc/4dd94040-4b00-11ed-a2c4-23a64d9ee89b/.ds-logs-nodejs-2026.01.12-016005?id=iaV4spsBfPSWSvvlnKPv], [Order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1627942778/136], [Order Try|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1627942778/136?orderTryId=2172095814]\n\n* Driver 7968568 rejected the order at 13:49:32 UTC\n* The Rider changed the pick-up location at 13:49:59 UTC\n* We processed the OrderStopQueue message at 13:50:00 UTC\n* At that point, Driver 7968568 had already rejected the offer, but no other Driver was assigned to the order\n\nAs far as I can tell, this shouldn’t cause any issues for us: a Driver will eventually accept an order, so we will handle an {{ OrderStopEventType.ACCEPTED}} event by creating a geofence for them.","2026-01-12T14:39:34.951Z"],["3804220","LSS-61424","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:5fca4b937cc1030069d2bae5] - Kindly clarify if anything needs to be changed in the document? Is the date in the comment just for clarification or do we need to make any contextual changes?","2026-01-12T14:39:51.439Z"],["3804221","PFI-831922","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there,\n\nPlease try:\n\n* Open the [Client page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] in Admin \n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open  {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ - The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see another _error_ → let us know.\n* if you see _to_execute →_ it means that the invoice still needs to be generated. You either look at the invoice for the current month (which does not have an invoice yet because month is still going). If you see that to_execute is for the invoice for multiple months → it means that in the past months it was not generated and will be generated in the end of the month.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the tab (or under {{Partner Invoices}})\n\nBest regards\n\nNikolay Roll ","2026-01-12T14:40:03.635Z"],["3804222","WD-22538","WD","merle.laaneots@bolt.eu","Merle Laaneots","FYI, found another temporary solution for YE close, please skip this (or close ticket) for now. Thanks, Merle","2026-01-12T14:40:06.641Z"],["3804224","MKP-4319","MKP","abdelhalim.machehalek@bolt.eu","Abdelhalim Machehalek","[~accountid:5b306883ed67e12dd27645e1] Yes, this will be taken into account as part of the initiative led by [~accountid:712020:fa6e0288-22fa-4792-afb4-b8d9a989084e] to improve pricing presentation.\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1N8sw6uoGv60S8W7Xyrb0FsUEIpBOh0lJZ0tzN_PRoFg/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1N8sw6uoGv60S8W7Xyrb0FsUEIpBOh0lJZ0tzN_PRoFg/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T14:40:29.714Z"],["3804225","PFI-831845","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there,\n\nPlease try:\n\n* Open the [Client page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] in Admin \n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open  {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ - The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see another _error_ → let us know.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the tab (or under {{Partner Invoices}})\n\nBest regards\n\nNikolay Roll ","2026-01-12T14:40:38.233Z"],["3804226","DSR-3675","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-12T14:41:06.753Z"],["3804227","HS-28664","HS","telvi.tonsiver@bolt.eu","Telvi Tonsiver","Hi! \n\n[~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] Attendance is counted equally between shortened and regular workday.","2026-01-12T14:41:12.854Z"],["3804228","LSS-60730","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:e7c4988a-ccaf-44c1-8546-2d01d1217937]\n\nPlease find signed MSA with Transcom [^MSA_Bolt Operations OÜ_Transcom WW Vilnius UAB_22.12.2025 (1).pdf] \n\nAlso shared in Slack ","2026-01-12T14:41:16.513Z"],["3804229","PFI-832487","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team has issued a refund to the customer. \nPlease note we had to issue two separate refunds. \n5 EUR refund from here [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3534190983|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3534190983]\n0.86 EUR refund from here [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3605630303|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3605630303]\n\nThe users balance unfortunately cannot be edited and they would keep the 5.86 EUR Bolt balance. \n\nCheers, \nMarten ","2026-01-12T14:41:16.633Z"],["3804230","RIDE-127","RIDE","ricardo.gallego@bolt.eu","Ricardo Gallego Gómez","[~accountid:624d3e6c7a3f9e006ab63c88] [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] was this linked to a specific tender? ","2026-01-12T14:41:39.364Z"],["3804231","INT-580","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","what’s the status of this one? [~accountid:712020:233144b7-8984-4e6b-922e-2ed0d6700d5f] ","2026-01-12T14:41:39.981Z"],["3804235","INT-739","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","was this done? [~accountid:712020:233144b7-8984-4e6b-922e-2ed0d6700d5f] ","2026-01-12T14:42:11.868Z"],["3804236","PFI-831423","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi, \n\nwhat bonus are we talking about?\n\nI am checking Balance history tool: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/balanceHistory?balanceHistoryFilterSearch={\"external_id\"%3A8186696%2C\"type\"%3A\"Driver\"%2C\"month\"%3A{\"year\"%3A2026%2C\"month\"%3A1}%2C\"viewType\"%3A\"weekly\"%2C\"week\"%3A{\"start\"%3A1766959200000%2C\"end\"%3A1767563999999}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/balanceHistory?balanceHistoryFilterSearch=%7B%22external_id%22%3A8186696%2C%22type%22%3A%22Driver%22%2C%22month%22%3A%7B%22year%22%3A2026%2C%22month%22%3A1%7D%2C%22viewType%22%3A%22weekly%22%2C%22week%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1766959200000%2C%22end%22%3A1767563999999%7D%7D]\n\nI do not see any records for bonuses - could you give more context?","2026-01-12T14:42:23.962Z"],["3804238","LSS-50276","LSS","ana.cordoba@bolt.eu","Ana de Córdoba","Hey team, they tell me Iciar should have signed the DSA, could you check it? Thanks a lot ","2026-01-12T14:42:41.038Z"],["3804239","LSS-60600","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hi [~accountid:712020:b75759f0-ea50-4319-bfe5-48b28f4cab21] [~accountid:5de0e6d708d48c0d13acbb53] \nThe Preliminary Privacy Risk Assessment has been completed and submitted :done: \n\nLink: [https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyoü/preliminaryprivacyriskassessmentforuse/1-all-entries/30|https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyo%C3%BC/preliminaryprivacyriskassessmentforuse/1-all-entries/30]\n\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a]  for visibility.","2026-01-12T14:43:04.110Z"],["3804241","WD-22545","WD","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","[~accountid:712020:b91275f1-415a-4b3c-8490-974f09f14a0d] Please help. Thank you","2026-01-12T14:43:09.568Z"],["3804242","PRODSEC-588","PRODSEC","andres.jogi@bolt.eu","Andres Jõgi","[~accountid:5fca4b937cc1030069d2bae5] To reject it for now, external people cannot create dependencies in our board, unless we create a dedicated form for them (might be a decent idea)\n\n\nor we migrate these requests to ISS ticket type?","2026-01-12T14:43:42.641Z"],["3804245","DLSP-1995","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","released","2026-01-12T14:45:12.565Z"],["3804246","PRODSEC-658","PRODSEC","andres.jogi@bolt.eu","Andres Jõgi","[~accountid:5fca4b937cc1030069d2bae5] Moved to new year","2026-01-12T14:45:21.410Z"],["3804247","LSS-58158","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341831|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341831|smart-link]  ","2026-01-12T14:45:29.181Z"],["3804248","PFI-831378","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nBilling team does not work with refunds.\n\nplease check KB to find the next steps.","2026-01-12T14:45:31.068Z"],["3804251","PFI-831038","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nthe Bot’s reply was incorrect.\n\nPlease reach out to CS Privacy Compliance team - they can extract invoices for the user.","2026-01-12T14:46:53.736Z"],["3804253","PFI-832497","PFI","fisola.kaejaiye@bolt-outsource.eu","Fisola Kaejaiye","!receipttttttttttttt.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T14:47:26.095Z"],["3804254","HWMISC-803","HWMISC","rasad.nadzafov@bolt.eu","Räšad Nadžafov","Postponed/on-hold due to priorities related to Winter repair. ETA updated to 23.01","2026-01-12T14:47:36.796Z"],["3804256","INT-739","INT","mateja.sela@bolt.eu","Mateja Sela","[~accountid:712020:bba87790-3d07-4531-9af3-f5df86d0d56a] It wasn’t picked up, for now, we can ignore this. I am not sure if we have a special tag to just park it for a long time. We have more important stuff to do.","2026-01-12T14:47:54.336Z"],["3804257","LSS-61112","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5c09426d957a4e56aa49222f] ! Please remove the highlights and fill the name of the Client","2026-01-12T14:48:15.735Z"],["3804260","PFI-830883","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey\n\nthis is not the link that was provided in the guide before please follow the guide:\n\n\n👋 Hey there,\n\nPlease try:\n\n* Open the [Client page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] in Admin \n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open  {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ - The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see another _error_ → let us know.\n* if you see _to_execute →_ it means that the invoice still needs to be generated. You either look at the invoice for the current month (which does not have an invoice yet because month is still going). If you see that to_execute is for the invoice for multiple months → it means that in the past months it was not generated and will be generated in the end of the month.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the tab (or under {{Partner Invoices}})\n\nBest regards\n\nNikolay Roll ","2026-01-12T14:48:34.142Z"],["3804261","CPRI-156","CPRI","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","asked for justification over slack","2026-01-12T14:49:27.675Z"],["3804266","PFI-830695","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nthese pages are maanged by Campaign team - please reach out to them\n\nsaying so because we do not know the REASONING behind WHY things happen the way they happen.\n\nbut we can see WHAT happened. 😄\n\nSo, please reach out to campaign team.","2026-01-12T14:50:55.568Z"],["3804270","DBRE-7638","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","Handled in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8433|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8433|smart-link] and [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8690|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8690|smart-link].","2026-01-12T14:52:46.096Z"],["3804273","INT-739","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","[~accountid:712020:233144b7-8984-4e6b-922e-2ed0d6700d5f] okay thanks! ","2026-01-12T14:53:16.686Z"],["3804274","PTWS-2123","PTWS","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","All reports were updated except for Calculated Fields and custom Discovery Boards as per request of Steve :done: \n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 16.51.01.png|width=654,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 16.51.01.png\"!","2026-01-12T14:53:22.325Z"],["3804276","PFI-832486","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe payment had gotten stuck due to connectivity issues. \nCustomer payments team has released the authorization and corrected the payment state. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-12T14:53:31.450Z"],["3804277","SUPX-2288","SUPX","pranav.dineshkumar@bolt.eu","Pranav Dinesh Kumar","Let's discuss this on a call or during grooming","2026-01-12T14:53:48.177Z"],["3804278","INT-739","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","[~accountid:712020:233144b7-8984-4e6b-922e-2ed0d6700d5f] but did we update the enrollments expiry dates manually? ","2026-01-12T14:53:49.680Z"],["3804279","PFI-823402","PFI","mihai.raucea@bolt.eu","Mihai Răucea","Hi [~accountid:557058:b2aaf2b9-4465-40fe-b31b-1711dbe61946] - agree, let’s report the CN with the details that are on the profile currently.","2026-01-12T14:54:09.034Z"],["3804280","LOC-4618","LOC","sandra.bergstrom@bolt.eu","Sandra Bergström","I would like to opt in, pending legal approval.","2026-01-12T14:54:12.896Z"],["3804281","LOC-4617","LOC","sandra.bergstrom@bolt.eu","Sandra Bergström","I would like to opt in, pending legal approval.","2026-01-12T14:54:22.853Z"],["3804283","WD-22545","WD","victor.stratan@bolt.eu","Victor Stratan","[~accountid:63e354dd8978d7a4353ce08d] following our previous discussions, statements for Swedbank get manually imported to WD 2 times per month. This is due to Swedbank not being integrated with TC. This issue should get solved in Q2 2026. Please refer to the post below for it.\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02NN7CANGJ/p1762149619979349?thread_ts=1760683387.333189&cid=C02NN7CANGJ|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02NN7CANGJ/p1762149619979349?thread_ts=1760683387.333189&cid=C02NN7CANGJ|smart-link]\n\n[~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] please find the statement below\n\n[^file-20260112-165400.txt]\n\n","2026-01-12T14:54:25.786Z"],["3804284","IDC-1555","IDC","artem.borisov@bolt.eu","Artem Borisov","Confirmed by the Fraud Specialist that everything works: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C063CK8C540/p1768228710020819?thread_ts=1765203709.780469&cid=C063CK8C540|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C063CK8C540/p1768228710020819?thread_ts=1765203709.780469&cid=C063CK8C540|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T14:54:37.848Z"],["3804285","LSS-60104","LSS","darius.poursiami@bolt.eu","Darius Poursiami","In that case, I think we can close the ticket. There are no signs that the fleet partner is willing to sign this agreement at the moment.","2026-01-12T14:55:57.937Z"],["3804287","LSS-61141","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341839|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T14:56:10.219Z"],["3804288","CPRI-154","CPRI","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","decided to share a databricks query instead and followup in the thread.\n[~accountid:633401e297148a8301fcc8fe] please share the query in the thread","2026-01-12T14:56:14.821Z"],["3804290","LSS-50276","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey [~accountid:712020:feba077c-0585-4e5b-8e4d-2cdc0e19ecf8] - DSA still shows me as not signed by Iciar.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 16.56.42.png|width=529,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 16.56.42.png\"!","2026-01-12T14:57:04.051Z"],["3804292","PFI-832499","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","\n\n[^Bolt xxx4045.pdf] _(352 kB)_\n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T14:57:25.344Z"],["3804295","PFI-829216","PFI","timofey.shapovalov@bolt-outsource.eu","Timofey Shapovalov","Any news regarding this issue?","2026-01-12T14:58:03.606Z"],["3804296","LSS-60403","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] please could you share your views on this? \n\nTranslation of the elements listed in the screenshot:\n\n* The list of driver accounts and associated vehicles, specifying the dates on which they were added or deleted.\n* {color:#ff5630}Invoices issued by Bolt Operations OU, in the name and on behalf of each EVTC number, for the period from 1 to 30 September 2025.{color}\n* Identification of the bank account (RIB/IBAN) into which Bolt operations OÜ pays the carrier's remuneration after collection from the customer.\n\n\nIn light of the feedback you have shared previously, I would think that this is disproportionate. What do you think?\n\nThank you ! \n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] ","2026-01-12T14:58:04.709Z"],["3804306","WFM-9956","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","* -CS - Safety role: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601640|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601640]-\n* -Queues-\n* -Assembled skill, site, Alvaria ID, team-","2026-01-12T14:58:23.731Z"],["3804307","CPRI-148","CPRI","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","was already taken care of my delivery team","2026-01-12T14:58:33.441Z"],["3804308","WFM-9956","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","All done, [~accountid:712020:8f5d63c5-8fe5-4ac9-8a6e-fd90ce9c04d7]. \r\n\r\nHave a great day!","2026-01-12T14:58:35.985Z"],["3804309","SREDESK-7403","SREDESK","gleb.timofeev@bolt.eu","Gleb Timofeev","Lets change the cost center to the {{ENG-EATER}} [confirmation|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07J6BR8A8G/p1768228897143099?thread_ts=1768212050.704329&cid=C07J6BR8A8G]\n\n","2026-01-12T14:58:37.108Z"],["3804312","LSS-61420","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^ACT of collected payments_Bolt Operations OÜ_LLC Bolt Operations Ukraine_31.12.25.pdf]\n[^Act 12 of collected payments_Bolt Operations OÜ_LLC Bolt Operations Ukraine_31.12.25.pdf]\n\nOnce getting these countersigned please send them to [contracts@bolt.eu|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] with a ticket number for archiving purposes and attach the documents here for our own records.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T14:59:38.727Z"],["3804313","PFI-832500","PFI","fisola.kaejaiye@bolt-outsource.eu","Fisola Kaejaiye","!RECEIPT NUMBER 2.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T14:59:48.061Z"],["3804317","LSS-61429","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed PoA attached.\n\n[^PoA - Sophie Kotyzová case_Bolt Services CZ s.r.o._JUDr. Matěj Krupa_12.01.26.pdf]\n\nOnce getting this countersigned please send it to [contracts@bolt.eu|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] with a ticket number for archiving purposes and attach the document here for our own records.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T15:00:42.316Z"],["3804322","LSS-61430","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T15:01:18.285Z"],["3804323","LSS-61405","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Response to Demand for Compensation_Bolt Operations OÜ_Kanyi Kiruchi & Co Advocates_12.01.2026.pdf] ","2026-01-12T15:01:22.311Z"],["3804327","DLSP-1952","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","the development was done in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLSP-1952|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLSP-1952|smart-link]  to decrease overhead","2026-01-12T15:02:23.261Z"],["3804329","SREDESK-7402","SREDESK","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","CostCenter should be {{ENG-EATER}}\n\nAnd codeowner {{eater-selection}}","2026-01-12T15:02:37.477Z"],["3804330","LSS-61411","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:62722e092db308007024a425] please support with Rides specific ticket ","2026-01-12T15:03:07.213Z"],["3804331","CRC-2291","CRC","ott.jalakas@bolt.eu","Ott Jalakas","[update] Migrated all daily models to {{fact_billing_core_balance_%}}","2026-01-12T15:03:10.440Z"],["3804335","LSS-60104","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","[~accountid:712020:6f563341-b27c-4653-b7d4-c67e881cc931] - I will keep the link active in SpotDraft for now so they can still sign, but other than that if You want this agreement to have a flexible date then the document needs to be changed and sent out again as it currently states the effective date as of 15.12.25.\n\nI will close the ticket for now","2026-01-12T15:03:59.558Z"],["3804337","HS-28840","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","Confirmation of Employment sent for signing by Kristin","2026-01-12T15:04:40.423Z"],["3804338","LSS-61181","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341850?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341850?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link]  ","2026-01-12T15:04:58.439Z"],["3804340","LSS-61414","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed documents attached.\n\n[^Influencer agreement_Bolt Poland Sp. z o.o._MagCreates Magdalena Wieczorek_09.01.26.pdf]\n[^Influencer agreement_Bolt Poland Sp. z o.o._Linda Filipkowska_09.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T15:05:09.137Z"],["3804341","LSS-61431","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nIvan Falco has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-12T15:05:34.271Z"],["3804346","LSS-60202","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Response sent [^Response to Demand for Compensation_Bolt Operations OÜ_Kanyi Kiruchi & Co Advocates_12.01.2026.pdf] ","2026-01-12T15:06:51.936Z"],["3804348","LSS-61253","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:071fb04b-7e5e-4774-81f6-fd12e7bf404c] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^SKM_C55826010720030 (a3cf5027-1c57-4ea3-9985-44b975c10e3e).pdf] ","2026-01-12T15:07:27.233Z"],["3804352","LSS-58484","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:5b0fdc5182e05b22cc7d4cf3] following up on the below please. ","2026-01-12T15:08:02.110Z"],["3804353","PIF-55","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 8\n• Relevance: 9\n• Problem Definition: 8\n• Accept: 8\n• Suggested improvements: The user story provides a reasonable overview, but could use more precise details. To enhance clarity, specify the process by which the local secrets will be set and accessed. This will aid developers in understanding the implementation's start point. Explain the current challenges with the existing system in more depth and how local secrets would align with security policies. The acceptance criteria need specific and measurable outcomes, such as confirming no secrets get pushed or metrics on time saved during testing. By incorporating these, the story would become clearer and more actionable for developers.","2026-01-12T15:08:31.137Z"],["3804354","PFI-832505","PFI","amenah.samad@bolt-outsource.eu","Amenah Samad","!IMG_6392.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T15:08:58.846Z"],["3804355","LSS-58186","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","[~accountid:5bdc750bd575d83fa35aaf70] closing the ticket - please follow standard channels should a data request be received. ","2026-01-12T15:09:17.993Z"],["3804356","PC-4039","PC","andrei.dunko@bolt.eu","Andrei Dunko","Rejected after discussion [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:09:49.092Z"],["3804357","LSS-61333","LSS","anna.surga@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Surga","Hey,\n\nYes, we have. However, we would like to sign another contract for cars that have been part of a different project over the last two years (Vehicle Financing Partnership with Santander).","2026-01-12T15:09:56.700Z"],["3804359","PC-4221","PC","andrei.dunko@bolt.eu","Andrei Dunko","Rejected after discussion [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:10:14.250Z"],["3804361","SUPX-2288","SUPX","iryna.mitsko@bolt.eu","Iryna Mitsko","Would you mind keeping me in the loop on how the discussion goes?\nAlso, feel free to reach out if any additional information is needed.","2026-01-12T15:10:18.905Z"],["3804362","PC-4231","PC","andrei.dunko@bolt.eu","Andrei Dunko","Rejected after discussion [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:10:31.757Z"],["3804363","PC-4258","PC","andrei.dunko@bolt.eu","Andrei Dunko","Rejected after discussion [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:10:49.100Z"],["3804364","LSS-61361","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached! I have asked Ahto to send the document to them via email as well. I have asked to add You in bcc for visibility.\n\n[^Service agreement_Nicchiano Sp. z o.o._ASB Poland Sp. z o.o._ASB Tax Sp. z o.o._02.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T15:11:09.276Z"],["3804366","LSS-58896","LSS","baaba.hammond@bolt.eu","Baaba Hammond","thanks - will revert","2026-01-12T15:11:45.958Z"],["3804368","LSS-61319","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Branding Contract - Bolt Club_Bolt Operations OÜ_Ka-Ra GmbH Personenbeförderung mit Mietwagen_15.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T15:12:12.633Z"],["3804370","PAW-14743","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-review-and-approval-system, pint-product-identity-and-communication-management, pint-capability-itgc\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-12T15:12:20.240Z"],["3804371","XP-3033","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","[~accountid:6268ef8e429789006946b1ac] We could at least compare different approaches to fixing on CUPED effectiveness","2026-01-12T15:12:27.449Z"],["3804373","PC-3488","PC","andrei.dunko@bolt.eu","Andrei Dunko","Moved to platform improvements from [Silverflow epic|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PC-2514] after discussion [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:12:31.338Z"],["3804375","WD-22485","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:637f26822acfad92d7b13ddb] , i did test run in Sandbox and i got errors on 71 expense reports that could not be canceled. Before performing process in Production could you please overview yellow lines in the file?[^Old ER reports to be cancelled (bdbb11f9-19f6-4b7d-9e3d-a3a9f9ad4782).xlsx] ","2026-01-12T15:12:38.005Z"],["3804376","PC-4079","PC","andrei.dunko@bolt.eu","Andrei Dunko","Moved to platform improvements from [Silverflow epic|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PC-2514] after discussion [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:12:47.408Z"],["3804378","INSUR-171","INSUR","alessandro@bolt.eu","Alessandro Milici","I’m reaching out to share that together with the Web Team, we are planning a centralised *Insurance Web Hub* on the Bolt website. This will serve as the single source of truth for all insurance-related information (coverage details, claim processes, etc.), replacing the scattered info currently found in FAQs, onboarding pages, and old blog posts.\n\n*How it will work:*\n\n* *Structure:* The hub will be organised strictly *by country and by vertical* to ensure users receive the exact information relevant to them.\n* *Content Migration:* I will review the information on our existing pages and migrate the relevant details into this new format, working closely with the content team.\n\nI’m handling most of the transition, but I wanted to keep you informed before we proceed with these changes, and possibly have one person within the local teams available to review it. ","2026-01-12T15:12:53.722Z"],["3804379","PC-4224","PC","andrei.dunko@bolt.eu","Andrei Dunko","Moved to platform improvements from [Silverflow epic|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PC-2514] after discussion [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GPAPKPCMQ/p1766414269878499|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:12:59.987Z"],["3804382","FX-3607","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768230795280779]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@chantel.rowe>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3607] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T15:13:32.192Z"],["3804383","LSS-50276","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Then have now signed the DSA! Please find it attached.\n\n[^DSA_Bolt Operations OÜ_IBERDROLA CLIENTES, S.A.U._04.12.25 (715f2160-8980-4b22-aff1-c3f9c087cb84).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T15:13:33.388Z"],["3804384","PC-3488","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-2514 has been resolved","2026-01-12T15:13:33.461Z"],["3804385","PC-2487","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-2514 has been resolved","2026-01-12T15:13:33.485Z"],["3804386","PC-4079","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-2514 has been resolved","2026-01-12T15:13:33.508Z"],["3804387","PC-4224","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-2514 has been resolved","2026-01-12T15:13:33.536Z"],["3804388","XP-3033","XP","danil.kazakov@bolt.eu","Danil Kazakov","[~accountid:6268ef8e429789006946b1ac] \n\n{quote}The metric definition is applied to the table aggregation level (e.g. sum all orders per user), and then in the CUPED query we have the following per CTE:{quote}\n\nJust to clarify: CUPED is applied first, and then metric definition.\nI’m not sure I’m following your point. In summary, the overall target metric is {{Sum GMV per User}}, while CUPED is optimized on {{Avg GMV per City per User}}. It would be identical in a case of all users having the same number of cities.","2026-01-12T15:13:48.529Z"],["3804390","DPM-2211","DPM","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","[~accountid:712020:ddfe83d1-e2c1-4238-8459-1dfffb836745] Done. Please check if any of the tickets I moved are actually done and should be closed.","2026-01-12T15:13:57.608Z"],["3804392","LSS-61286","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:58704fb5-3b31-40a0-896f-1d862e6e1fd9] !\n\nPlease see the PoAs attached\n\n# Tadych[^PoA_Bolt Services France_Karolina Tadych_04.09.2023 (1).pdf] \n# Mouyeket [^PoA_Bolt Services France SARL_Julien Mouyeket_13.01.23.pdf] ","2026-01-12T15:14:18.454Z"],["3804394","LSS-52854","LSS","matiss.panga@bolt.eu","Matīss Panga","Hello [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774], just now received answer from SPRK regarding Bolt’s updated T&C, bellow share their message - \n\n\n”Sabiedrisko pakalpojumu regulēšanas komisija ( turpmāk – Regulators) 2025. gada 16. decembrī saņēma Jūsu e-pasta vēstuli ar lūgumu sniegt savus ieteikumus un papildinājumus attiecībā uz dokumentu \"Platformas lietošanas noteikumi Kopbraukšanas pakalpojumu sniedzējiem: Pakalpojumu sniedzēji (Latvija)\", kas papildināti ar sūtījumu piegādes pakalpojumu kategorijā \"Bolt Send\" (turpmāk – Noteikumi).\n\nRegulators ir iepazinies ar Noteikumiem un secina, ka sadarbības partneri, saskaņā ar Noteikumu 5.27.apakšpunktu pasta sūtījumu piegādi veiks savā vārdā. Kā jau iepriekš sanāksmēs pārrunāts, pēc būtības pasta pakalpojumu lietotājam sniegs Bolt, kas noteiks gan tarifus, gan attiecībā pret lietotāju uzņemsies atbildību par sūtījumiem, savukārt sūtījumu piegāde tiks nodrošināta ar sadarbības partneru starpniecību, līdz ar to Noteikumos jāatspoguļo, ka faktiski sadarbības partneri sūtījumu piegādi veiks Bolt vārdā. Tādējādi nepieciešams skaidri nodalīt pušu atbildību, pienākumus un tiesisko statusu attiecībās ar lietotājiem.\n\nŅemot vērā minēto, Regulators aicina atbilstoši precizēt Noteikumus. Vienlaikus Regulators augsti novērtētu iespēju, pirms pakalpojuma “Bolt Send” ieviešanas iepazīties arī ar lietotājiem paredzētajiem pakalpojuma lietošanas noteikumiem kuriem jāatbilst Vispārējas atļaujas noteikumu 12.punktam, kuros skaidri un nepārprotami būtu ietverta šāda informācija:\n\n* pasta sūtījumu savākšanas un piegādes kvalitātes prasības;\n* kompensācijas piemērošanas kārtība sūtītājam, ja komersants nav nodrošinājis pasta sūtījumu savākšanas un piegādes kvalitātes prasības;\n* informācija par pasta komersanta materiālo atbildību un materiālās atbildības apmēriem;\n* informācija par sūdzības iesniegšanas un izskatīšanas kārtību, tostarp informācija par lietotāja tiesībām, ja lietotājs nav apmierināts ar pasta komersanta sniegto atbildi un sūdzība attiecas uz regulējamu pasta pakalpojuma veidu.”\n\n\n\nPlease share your comments on this 🙏\n\n","2026-01-12T15:14:26.081Z"],["3804397","INT-521","INT","marina.pai@bolt.eu","Marina Pai","archiving, since this should be on Analytics Jira. FYI [~accountid:61027991627b560068c6ec21] , please make sure it’s on your roadmap.","2026-01-12T15:15:21.120Z"],["3804398","INSUR-171","INSUR","alessandro@bolt.eu","Alessandro Milici","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Z3ogAVqt5RWxwlflr7qakpHpddmfa4JRBVMCDVENG60/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Z3ogAVqt5RWxwlflr7qakpHpddmfa4JRBVMCDVENG60/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:15:21.447Z"],["3804402","LSS-61252","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","Good day, i need to change contract for signing as 1 car got in accident during weekend. Changes made, new contract for signing. \n\nSorry for inconvenience\n\n[^EE20260109-001 Resa motors - Bolt Drive EE.docx (1).pdf]\n\n. ","2026-01-12T15:15:56.400Z"],["3804403","INT-319","INT","marina.pai@bolt.eu","Marina Pai","archiving, to be tracked on analytics JIRA. FYI [~accountid:61027991627b560068c6ec21] ","2026-01-12T15:16:13.684Z"],["3804404","LSS-61431","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T15:16:19.535Z"],["3804405","INT-317","INT","marina.pai@bolt.eu","Marina Pai","archiving, to be tracked on analytics JIRA. FYI [~accountid:61027991627b560068c6ec21] ","2026-01-12T15:16:21.718Z"],["3804406","INT-318","INT","marina.pai@bolt.eu","Marina Pai","archiving, to be tracked on analytics JIRA. FYI [~accountid:61027991627b560068c6ec21] ","2026-01-12T15:16:28.171Z"],["3804407","LSS-28796","LSS","brita.lubi@bolt.eu","Brita Lubi","Hi!\n\nThat is indeed some really good news! What is the reimbursement amount? Currently based on our SE001 balance sheet we are expecting to receive 179906 SEK - will we be receiving the full amount?\n\nIf yes, it should be as easy as transferring the amount to our SE1 entity and I will settle it against the deposit we have open.\n\nCompany: Bolt Services AB\nBank IBAN: SE9890400000090401415076\nSwift: CITISESX\n\n\n\nBest wishes\n\nBrita","2026-01-12T15:16:58.625Z"],["3804409","LSS-61160","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:61a62637d2e64c00715cbd9f] looks good, the draft is aligned with the template. You may share with the Partner for their consideration. ","2026-01-12T15:17:42.239Z"],["3804410","RNTL-30230","RNTL","mikhail.akopov@bolt.eu","Mikhail Akopov","Probably will be resolved once [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RNTL-30371|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RNTL-30371|smart-link]  is done","2026-01-12T15:17:44.150Z"],["3804414","BP-13421","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Assigned due to: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160379|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160379|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:18:39.840Z"],["3804415","PC-3351","PC","andrei.dunko@bolt.eu","Andrei Dunko","This was done in scope of firefighting ticket [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PC-4910|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PC-4910|smart-link] \nSee PR [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/158758|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/158758|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:18:40.273Z"],["3804416","PC-4756","PC","ilya.goryachev@bolt.eu","Ilya Goryachev","[~accountid:712020:76180c2c-9e2c-4717-8560-56ba59fe9cd8] Hi! Could you provide any ETA? We really want to remove the big chunk of code on our side; your change will definitely help with this 🙂","2026-01-12T15:19:00.446Z"],["3804417","XP-3033","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","{quote}It would be identical in a case of all users having the same number of cities.{quote}\n\nyes, so then, if we have just user level data in the table aggregation, we no longer have an issue of the {{AVG}} term in the CUPED query - is this correct?","2026-01-12T15:19:01.902Z"],["3804418","HS-28877","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Offer letter is missing - already in the hires-in-progress channel.","2026-01-12T15:19:15.514Z"],["3804420","LSS-60866","LSS","morenike.lanreologun@bolt.eu","Morenike Lanre-Ologun","Thank you [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] ! Please see attached the updated TOE based on your comments. The 'detailed time entries' proposed in Clause 3 does not apply since the fee is not time-based. \n\nPlease confirm if all looks good with this version. Thank you.\n\n[^ToE_2026_Bolt (dc5b9b57-051b-46de-9986-e62440c4bb1e).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T15:19:31.657Z"],["3804421","LEG-1133","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:bc3e1151-2459-4765-92b8-897f743d8296], I think you are referring to the FSN Code of Conduct we discussed quite some time ago. We can’t supplement it with any sections, unfortunately - it’s their unilateral document. If we don’t accept it, we can’t have a cooperation with them. We can discuss it on a call if it’s still not signed but I believe it is. ","2026-01-12T15:20:05.295Z"],["3804423","XP-3033","XP","danil.kazakov@bolt.eu","Danil Kazakov","[~accountid:6268ef8e429789006946b1ac] Yes, in that case Average over a single value would result in the same value.","2026-01-12T15:20:15.396Z"],["3804424","PFI-832511","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^transferencia-26010540927.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-12T15:20:20.454Z"],["3804427","GRWA-1497","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","Fleet has been added in the enrollment looks - [thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0682D79LQG/p1768230980006299?thread_ts=1762948773.578879&cid=C0682D79LQG]","2026-01-12T15:21:12.963Z"],["3804428","LSS-54244","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c] please allow me loop you in this ticket. \n\nElisabetta and I have been reviewing the T&Cs for the Family Accounts in France: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1x6c3J8sPhRE4HYnjO7hdcJG4IlvGSVTfH-BIGL7m2vI/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.xedyvn2gv1o2|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1x6c3J8sPhRE4HYnjO7hdcJG4IlvGSVTfH-BIGL7m2vI/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.xedyvn2gv1o2|smart-link] \n\nWe have some questions regarding the operational functioning of the feature: \n\n* When a member is added to a family account, do they get a confirmation of this by email?\n* In this confirmation email, are the members aware that the owner of the account can see the ride history of all the members of the Family Account?\n* Can the member remove themselves from the account? \n* Can a member have an individual account and an attachment to a family account?\n\n\n\nThank you in advance for your insights in this, or feel free to redirect if I should be asking someone else ! \n","2026-01-12T15:21:21.669Z"],["3804431","BRE-1229","BRE","uladzislau.klimiankou@bolt.eu","Vlad Klimenkov","RH: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07LQ8TDSSE/p1768214427314599|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07LQ8TDSSE/p1768214427314599|smart-link] \nCarsharing: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A1WGQ8JBE/p1767957842184519|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A1WGQ8JBE/p1767957842184519|smart-link]  (waiting for Ops reply)\n","2026-01-12T15:22:41.165Z"],["3804433","BB-2276","BB","uladzislau.klimiankou@bolt.eu","Vlad Klimenkov","Thread: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09LEB128QP/p1768229988942739|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09LEB128QP/p1768229988942739|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:23:13.378Z"],["3804436","PAW-14786","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160382\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 15:24:08 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T15:24:08.872Z"],["3804438","BP-13422","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","SRE request: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7407|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7407|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:24:20.763Z"],["3804440","RLONE-614","RLONE","noel.schutters@bolt.eu","Noël Schutters","Done - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08V772PRE3/p1760895416713529|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08V772PRE3/p1760895416713529|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:24:38.646Z"],["3804443","GRWA-1487","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","Added p5 and p95 in the [Campaigns tracking|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/196fkMEDScNxMBv4FTZy-u9LLmarN41lXpv8RfgDXn64/edit?gid=1482776815#gid=1482776815] in column AS and AT","2026-01-12T15:24:52.171Z"],["3804444","GRWA-1487","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 17.23.08.png|width=863,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 17.23.08.png\"!","2026-01-12T15:25:07.801Z"],["3804445","XP-3033","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","cool, lets discuss solution options tomorrow","2026-01-12T15:25:10.629Z"],["3804446","WD-22545","WD","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","Hello [~accountid:63e354dd8978d7a4353ce08d] \n\nThe file has been loaded to WD. ","2026-01-12T15:25:11.092Z"],["3804451","WD-22520","WD","alexandru.cerveanu@bolt.eu","Alex Cerveanu","Hi Andrea,\n\nBalances have been updated as per your request.\n\nWith Regards,\n\nAlex","2026-01-12T15:27:35.306Z"],["3804459","LSS-60808","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] not sure what Mapbox is trying to reach with this amendment. \n\n*Key points* \n\n* While cost and term improve, the *discount limitation* introduces a  restriction:\n\nOnly _Map Loads for Web (GL JS)_ get 75% off — *everything else (mobile SDKs, APIs, search, etc.) reverts to full price*.\n\n* Bolt must renew by June 2026 to avoid service interruption. Agreement’s length  changes to 8 months instead of 12 months \n* Total fee reduced from *$36,960 → $24,640*\n\nFee change also affects our liability limit under website terms. Since  amended Order reduces both price and duration, the monetary cap for Mapbox’s liability is now lower — $24,640 instead of $36,960.\n\nIf all these changes are acceptable we can move with signing. ","2026-01-12T15:29:51.959Z"],["3804462","WEBSD-1469","WEBSD","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","[^PDF Copy of Greek _ English Platform Terms for Ride-Hailing Services- Service Providers (Cyprus) .docx.pdf]\n\n[^Word. Greek _ English Platform Terms for Ride-Hailing Services- Service Providers (Cyprus) .docx]","2026-01-12T15:31:00.635Z"],["3804463","PFI-831927","PFI","georgios.bamos@bolt.eu","Georgios Thomas Bamos","Due to the rider having a discount, we are unable to provide a refund over 8.50€. It’s also confirmed that the driver charged 22€ in cash. If billing ops can’t provide a manual compensation, do you know where this can be escalated?","2026-01-12T15:31:02.628Z"],["3804464","HS-28252","HS","dmitriy.rassadkin@bolt.eu","Dmytro Rassadkin","Hey[~accountid:712020:e1427b30-bc75-43cd-9e45-85c863998272], can you please take a look at this request? Servicedesk starts sending me email that if I don’t reply - it’ll be automatically closed 😅 ","2026-01-12T15:31:07.939Z"],["3804465","LSS-61432","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T15:31:24.621Z"],["3804468","WFM-9957","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-12T15:33:06.505Z"],["3804469","L10N-27400","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated, please revisit.","2026-01-12T15:33:07.748Z"],["3804470","L10N-27408","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:08.910Z"],["3804472","L10N-27405","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:09.304Z"],["3804473","L10N-27413","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:09.335Z"],["3804474","L10N-27403","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:09.437Z"],["3804475","L10N-27404","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:09.413Z"],["3804476","L10N-27396","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:09.475Z"],["3804477","L10N-27411","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:09.487Z"],["3804478","L10N-27402","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","Th