9","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:15.278Z"],["3804496","L10N-27388","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:15.283Z"],["3804497","L10N-27393","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:15.302Z"],["3804498","L10N-27383","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:15.300Z"],["3804499","L10N-27391","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:15.363Z"],["3804500","L10N-27378","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:15.347Z"],["3804501","L10N-27381","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:15.365Z"],["3804502","L10N-27380","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:15.426Z"],["3804503","L10N-27392","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:15.568Z"],["3804504","L10N-27385","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-12T15:33:15.628Z"],["3804508","RDS-1395","RDS","rishi.kar@bolt.eu","Rishi Raj Kar","[~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] updated description and added Clara to feature channel. Let me know if you need something more","2026-01-12T15:33:56.291Z"],["3804509","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi,\n\nWhat’s the state of the [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7392|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7392|smart-link] ?\n\nIt’s waiting for your response.\n\nIf it is working, please update so we can close the ticket.\n\nThe previous ticket was applied via the following PRs. You can create similar PRs or I can create them:\n\n* [https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15309/changes|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15309/changes] \n* [https://github.com/bolteu/s3-configless/pull/422/changes|https://github.com/bolteu/s3-configless/pull/422/changes] ","2026-01-12T15:35:03.326Z"],["3804514","LSS-61315","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi, please find attached \n\n# Extract from the business register (not older than 6 months) (1 copy)\n# Notification from the Croatian Bureau of Statistics on classification according to NKD and the registration number\n\n[^00Asx-nVFG6-MSO2l-xGWsk-TxIPq-OUoNf-gw8Mm-zwoBL-0FnXk.pdf]\n[^250409_Obavijest Razvrstavanje_NKD (2).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T15:36:26.992Z"],["3804515","PC-4848","PC","andrei.dunko@bolt.eu","Andrei Dunko","[~accountid:712020:76180c2c-9e2c-4717-8560-56ba59fe9cd8] deploying [this PR|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159246] this week. After that we should continue with getting rid of the big query building in that table class. I can pick it up next firefighting if it waits","2026-01-12T15:36:41.777Z"],["3804516","PFI-831423","PFI","hana.maresova@bolt-outsource.eu","Hana Maresova","Hello,\n\nIt was bonus campaign that was happening on new years eve from 31.12- 18:00 until 01.01- 5:59, driver said he was active during the bonus but did not receive it. the bonus was suppose to be the commission for the app compensation. ","2026-01-12T15:37:02.284Z"],["3804517","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:63abfbf7159df2c252e762e5] If we make a 40x60cm rear carrier for EB1 then it will look like the picture below.\n\nThere are 3 issues with this concept. \n\n* The middle of the seat and the rear of the seat are far from the rear axle. The mass on the seat will lift the front side of the bike. It will not be convenient to put kid(s) on the seat while the e-bike on the kickstand. \n* Also, due to extra mass further from the rear axle, the riding experience worsens—less grip between the front tyre and road. Small bumps on the road or steep inclines can be hazardous. \n* We need to support the rear side of the seat with extra parts. Extra mass and fatigue will break the current fixation points. \n\nInstead of E-bike, can we use Cruiser for this purpose? Why:\n\n* We can use a longer seat (about 65cm) and utilise the space more efficiently.\n* A frame around the rear seat can still be used to secure kids or items that are carried. \n\n||*E-bike with rear carrier*||*Cruiser with rear carrier*||\n|!image-20260112-151225.png|width=472,alt=\"image-20260112-151225.png\"!|!image-20260112-153453.png|width=492,alt=\"image-20260112-153453.png\"!|\n|Middle of the seat and the axle distance  - 200mm\nThe rear seat and the axle distance is 300mm|The rear seat and the axle distance is less than 200mm|\n\n|!image-20260113-160849.png|width=340,alt=\"image-20260113-160849.png\"!|!image-20260113-160922.png|width=340,alt=\"image-20260113-160922.png\"!|\n|!image-20260113-161129.png|width=340,alt=\"image-20260113-161129.png\"!|!image-20260113-161212.png|width=340,alt=\"image-20260113-161212.png\"!|","2026-01-12T15:37:18.220Z"],["3804518","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Hi [~accountid:712020:782f9535-5dfc-41e5-8bdf-057eef89f6ef],\n\nI will remind the team to update the status tomorrow. As for this ticket - please create the relevant PRs.","2026-01-12T15:37:34.313Z"],["3804519","BDB-1494","BDB","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79]  kind reminder thank you!","2026-01-12T15:37:35.500Z"],["3804521","PFI-832514","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^comprobante.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T15:37:51.185Z"],["3804522","LSS-61335","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341858?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341858?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link]  ","2026-01-12T15:38:19.560Z"],["3804524","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","I will wait for the confirmation from your side.\n\nWe have self-service for this exact reason.\n\nThe PRs can be created by you and applied via Atlantis.\n\nIf any PR requires our review, we will review it.\n\nPlease avoid creating parallel tickets.\n\nIf the previous implementation doesn’t work, then we have to redo two tickets!","2026-01-12T15:39:43.249Z"],["3804525","LSS-61252","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, document has been swapped. Please let the partner know. Thanks!","2026-01-12T15:40:14.542Z"],["3804526","LSS-61252","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/339808|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/339808|smart-link] ","2026-01-12T15:40:21.408Z"],["3804528","LSS-61315","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:c4b40874-5082-43e8-bf03-940002fefe16] ,Unfortunately, we can’t sign a document that indicates it was scanned using CamScanner.\nCould you please scan it in the office or use another method so it appears as a standard document? In its current form, even Ahto’s wet-ink signature would not be sufficient.","2026-01-12T15:41:16.369Z"],["3804531","MKP-4319","MKP","aleksei.sivkov@bolt.eu","Alex Sivkov","[~accountid:712020:5290f272-66ef-467e-a008-8904b3bc928d] should we \n\n# Keep the ticket\n# Assign Pricing component\n# Keep as is?","2026-01-12T15:42:42.204Z"],["3804532","LSS-59952","LSS","afonso.azevedo@bolt.eu","Afonso Varão de Azevedo","Hey [~accountid:712020:011a9eb3-77af-4c62-bb26-e6c10e6097ec] \n\nHere are all documents for 82-ZT-16:\n\n*DUA*\n\n!8522044_Documento Único Automóvel_Contrato de Aluguer ()_164177078.jpg|width=350,height=240,alt=\"8522044_Documento Único Automóvel_Contrato de Aluguer ()_164177078.jpg\"!\n\n!8522044_certificado_matricula_verso_164176951.jpg|width=262,height=178,alt=\"8522044_certificado_matricula_verso_164176951.jpg\"!\n\n\n\n*Condições Particulares*\n\n\n[^8886221_Apólice de Seguro Automóvel (Condições Particulares)_174217590.pdf]\n\n*Carta Verde*\n\n!8886221_Apólice de Seguro Automóvel (Carta Verde) - Car_174185095.jpeg|width=390,height=640,alt=\"8886221_Apólice de Seguro Automóvel (Carta Verde) - Car_174185095.jpeg\"!\n\n*Inspeção*\n\n!8522044_inspecao_164176570.jpeg|width=1152,height=2048,alt=\"8522044_inspecao_164176570.jpeg\"!\n\n \n*Fleet Documents (*CORAIS & TEMPLOS - UNIPESSOAL LDA)\n\n*Licença Operador*\n\n\n!1413269_licenca_operador_163699090.jpeg|width=1152,height=2048,alt=\"1413269_licenca_operador_163699090.jpeg\"!\n\n*FO ID*\n\n!1413269_pt_fleet_id_back_163699264.jpg|width=1152,height=2048,alt=\"1413269_pt_fleet_id_back_163699264.jpg\"!\n\n*Certidão Permanente*\n\n\n!198791_certidao_permanente_comercial_179229902.jpeg|width=390,height=585,alt=\"198791_certidao_permanente_comercial_179229902.jpeg\"!\n\n*Seguro Acidentes* \n\n[^1413269_seguro_acidentes_163699491.pdf]\n\n*Seguro Responsabilidade*\n\n\n[^1413269_seguro_responsabilidade_163699560.pdf]\n\n*IBAN*\n\n[^1413269_pt_bank_details_163699595.pdf]\n\n\n\n\n[~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] There is no driver associate to the vehicle and there was no rides on the 25/11/2025\n\n\n\n\n\n","2026-01-12T15:42:52.217Z"],["3804533","LSS-61315","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","The agreement that needs to be signed is attached. \n\nWaiting for [~accountid:712020:c4b40874-5082-43e8-bf03-940002fefe16] 's new scan - once he sends it it needs to be signed by Ahto Kink, wet ink signature\n\nAdditionally, we need Ahto Kink’s passport scan ","2026-01-12T15:42:52.748Z"],["3804541","LSS-61207","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:daffdd55-b79f-408e-9859-186aadb103a8], please find here attached the LOI reviewed: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wQbFlqKtZwdOscq0VmVi-5vEPM-Ux7r9/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wQbFlqKtZwdOscq0VmVi-5vEPM-Ux7r9/edit|smart-link] \n\nSome elements are still highlighted in yellow (I assume these need to be filled out by you) and the expiry of the validity of the letter has been set by you to Friday 16th January. Is this still aligned with your timeline?\n\nAmendments have been made to replicate the previously signed LOI for Vincennes; as such, these should not be problematic for JLL. Signed LOI for Vincennes attached here for reference. In parallel, can you confirm that the partially signed Bail Commercial has never been signed?\n\n[^Bail Financière Melanie - Bolt (1).pdf] [^Bolt Services France SARL - Letter of Intent, signed.pdf] \n\n\n\nThank you !","2026-01-12T15:44:11.462Z"],["3804543","FIS-4202","FIS","iurii.shikanov@bolt.eu","Yurii Shykanov","Prepared 2025 Tax report, validated, and notified about missing data.\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/G01K5756FMK/p1768232570074729?thread_ts=1767791932.830939&cid=G01K5756FMK|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/G01K5756FMK/p1768232570074729?thread_ts=1767791932.830939&cid=G01K5756FMK]","2026-01-12T15:44:35.230Z"],["3804544","PFI-832515","PFI","george.ghiveciu@bolt.eu","George-Mihai Ghiveciu","[^PaymentProof2600213045461000 (1).pdf]","2026-01-12T15:44:49.112Z"],["3804545","RDS-1411","RDS","seidon.pereira@bolt.eu","Seidon Alexis Pereira","Seidon needs to check how previous implementation was and what happens when the user is also eligible for an actual promo","2026-01-12T15:44:52.000Z"],["3804547","LSS-61370","LSS","pedro.ferreira@bolt.eu","Pedro da Silva Ferreira","Hello,\n\nYes, I can confirm that *both accounts are currently blocked*.\n\nBy stating that _“he proceeded to use Bolt Business fraudulently”_, I mean that we started to identify *unusual and inconsistent usage patterns*, namely ride requests with *extravagant and recurrent pricing levels* that the client was *unable to clearly justify from a legitimate business use-case perspective*. The explanations provided were vague and which raised some red flags.\n\nPlease find *attached the two Special Terms / contractual addenda* that were signed for your reference.\n\nThanks\n\n[^Customer Special Terms - Bolt Business (3).pdf]\n[^Customer Special Terms - Bolt Business (4).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T15:45:05.121Z"],["3804549","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Hi [~accountid:712020:782f9535-5dfc-41e5-8bdf-057eef89f6ef],\n\nI would like to note that this is not a parallel ticket - this is for the *reseller* service and the *reseller-rides-report* bucket, while the other ticket handles the businessportal service and the bolt-business-portal bucket.\n\nAs far as I know, there have been no issues with the previous implementation. If there will be any issues here, I will let you know as soon as possible.\n\nI would appreciate the PRs being handled from your side, just like they were in the other ticket, so please do that if possible. Thank you in advance.\n\nBest regards,\nEdvards","2026-01-12T15:45:24.875Z"],["3804550","LOC-4369","LOC","ariana.saplana@bolt.eu","Ariana Saplana","[~accountid:712020:620ea7c5-429f-4501-a245-4d283f9eb036] Hi, the calendar has been updated!","2026-01-12T15:45:44.971Z"],["3804551","PFI-832516","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Report can be found in Google Drive folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Tv1K2FOxzRg_OjifW99b19A-5sRLyKx8\n\nPlease check the \"reconciliation\" tab for statistics.","2026-01-12T15:46:01.866Z"],["3804553","FDBT-4770","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-12T15:46:25.274Z"],["3804554","PC-4344","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","TODO:\n\n[1] is it relevant? In a sense - we don't need SNS/SQS there just SQS would be ok (one subscriber only)\n[2] if it is relevant switch it to plain SQS","2026-01-12T15:46:44.700Z"],["3804555","WEBSD-1447","WEBSD","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","# The images do not match the topic of the certificates. \n# Those external people, for example for tenders or  who we direct to our Sustainability webpage to access the PDFs will scroll past the images and not think the PDFs are hidden under the images.\n# The ‘Read more’ is not really true because there isn’t anything to read, there are just the certificates available. \n# The current section where they are is not linked to the PDFs, the technical logic doesn’t flow.  \n\nWe can use some other visual feature but it has to be clear that there are hyperlinks to those three certificates. \n\nThank you!🙏 ","2026-01-12T15:47:05.646Z"],["3804556","BDB-1494","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:628e5c9d8026a10068b1e457] The design team didn’t manage to сheck if printing files are 100% good to go. Would tomorrow morning be fine for you as well? Thank you! ","2026-01-12T15:47:24.778Z"],["3804557","CCM-22270","CCM","miroslava.solarova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Solárová","Hello Ilia,\n\nThe agents have been enrolled in the requested onboarding course.\n\nHave a lovely rest of your day! \n\nMirka 🙂 ","2026-01-12T15:48:48.114Z"],["3804561","PFI-832524","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Report can be found in Google Drive folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Tv1K2FOxzRg_OjifW99b19A-5sRLyKx8\n\nPlease check the \"reconciliation\" tab for statistics.","2026-01-12T15:50:45.757Z"],["3804562","LSS-61327","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:63314e9e9b32cfef93265252] please find attached the requested statement draft. \n\n[^IZJAVA O NEPOSTOJANJU POVEZANOSTI S TRGOVAČKIM DRUŠTVIMA KOJA IMAJU POREZNI DUG.docx]\n\n","2026-01-12T15:50:53.784Z"],["3804564","PAW-14791","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @xenJ\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160271\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 15:52:18 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T15:52:18.743Z"],["3804565","LSS-61370","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:712020:50554e69-c5e6-483a-a43b-b48bec17d7bb]. Thank you for the clarification. Just 2 more follow up questions:\n\n* Were there any issues regarding payments? Meaning, did these clients not pay their monthly invoices, or do we have any pending amounts to settle?\n* Did we communicate to the clients that their accounts had been blocked? If yes, did they present any complaint or asked for further clarifications or justification?","2026-01-12T15:52:18.974Z"],["3804567","FX-3609","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768233156735299]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3609] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T15:52:48.285Z"],["3804568","CRC-2329","CRC","dmitriy.filippov@bolt.eu","Dmitriy Filippov","[update] Performed dry-run, shared results with stakeholders → waiting for the feedback from stakeholders","2026-01-12T15:52:48.413Z"],["3804569","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","guglielmo.fontanarava@bolt.eu","Guglielmo Fontana-Rava Andreae","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] Can you explain more how you imagine the Cruiser solution. Does it mean that we will only have one very long seat?","2026-01-12T15:53:05.570Z"],["3804570","PFI-831489","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","Hello [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] This is the user’s phone number who is experiencing issues with their payment method. Attached are their [Admin profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/61460783/overview] and [order history|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A50%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22user_id%22%3A61460783%2C%22start_timestamp%22%3A1765554241%7D%7D]. The user mentioned that the issue started on January 9th, and the last order made using the Business payment method was on January 8th. I hope this helps! Thank you!\n\n","2026-01-12T15:53:09.338Z"],["3804571","PFI-832526","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Report can be found in Google Drive folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Tv1K2FOxzRg_OjifW99b19A-5sRLyKx8\n\nPlease check the \"reconciliation\" tab for statistics.","2026-01-12T15:53:17.209Z"],["3804572","FPD-1522","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","Zürich + [difference|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Lm52OYtsrF2YGwjUgI5vFJTSeNI_EE896uy053_nELk/edit?gid=148072228#gid=148072228] in the partner_churns_pct 31% in accuracy reporting while  in the [model File|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1mhBSaSDQw_2V9VDUe78661klJ9s3aEbShobOBSfeDHA/edit?gid=933025258#gid=933025258] we have 26.5%\nfor partner_churns_pct number coincide after adjustment","2026-01-12T15:53:33.847Z"],["3804577","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:63abfbf7159df2c252e762e5] Yes, one very long seat about 65cm. And if needed, a frame around the rear half of the seat for protection. ","2026-01-12T15:56:33.058Z"],["3804578","LSS-60495","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","* Should we list you as the “Principal Director”?\n** {color:#4c9aff}yes{color}\n* Besides you and Nick, are there any other individuals who are senior persons responsible for the company’s operations?\n** {color:#4c9aff}Kimberly Hurd{color}\n\n[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] can you please help us with answering below questions?\n\n* Do you know Markus’s date of birth?\n* Are Markus’s shares held in bearer form? [~accountid:712020:66939b2f-e5c1-42e2-8cbe-244458fd12f9] \n* For question 4d, should we confirm that Markus exercises ultimate control over the management of the company?\n** {color:#4c9aff}Yes{color}","2026-01-12T15:57:09.212Z"],["3804579","CRC-2336","CRC","dmitriy.filippov@bolt.eu","Dmitriy Filippov","[update] Performed dry-run: Deutsche Bank generated and uploaded statements to sftp → Treasury Core Adapter downloaded them → parsed to DB. Results are shared with stakeholders → waiting for the feedback from stakeholders to proceed.","2026-01-12T15:57:37.873Z"],["3804581","LSS-61037","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:5acb064d56d6c72b45183935]! \n\nThank you for your comments and apologies for the slower reply. The JV creation is a relatively new idea for us; therefore, Legal will only start this year to assess what is allowed, what is not, how we can best benefit from JVs, and what the key requirements for JV structures are in the Baltics.\n\nSince the Baltics are now part of the CEE region, in the coming weeks we will have a call with Legal counsels in Poland and Romania to understand their approach. After that, I will be able to comment in more detail. For now, the more information you can share about the expected deal, the better - in particular, which fleet the JV would be established with, the purpose of the JV (e.g. purchase of new vehicles and renting them to drivers), how decision-making and day-to-day operations would be divided, profit-sharing, and any other operational or corporate aspects.\n\nRegarding your questions:\n\n*1. What constitutes “dominant” in LT?*\n\nDominance is not determined solely by a fixed market share threshold, but by the ability to behave independently of competitors and customers. Uber’s 15–20% market does not automatically exclude our dominance, especially where:\n\n* Bolt has the largest share, strong brand recognition, and scale advantages;\n* there are network effects (drivers/fleets multi-home but may depend economically on one platform);\n* Bolt can materially influence market conditions (pricing, access to demand, fleet economics).\n\n For risk assessment purposes, we should assume Bolt is at least dominant or close to dominance in rides in LT.\n\n*2. Where could the competition risk come from?*\n\n* competitors (e.g. Uber) filing a complaint alleging foreclosure or exclusivity;\n* fleets or drivers claiming restrictive conditions (especially if economics later deteriorate);\n* competition authorities acting on their own initiative, particularly if the JV becomes visible.\n\n*3. JV limited only to co-financed vehicles*\n\nIf the JV holds only Bolt-co-financed vehicles, and the fleet’s remaining vehicles are free to operate across platforms, such a restriction could generally be justified by economic considerations.\n\n*4. Non-time-limited exclusivity*\n\nA non-time-limited exclusivity, even in a JV, is harder to defend under competition law than a time-limited one, as it may look more like behavioural control rather than investment protection. It would be difficult to argue that unlimited exclusivity is objectively necessary to secure ROI.\n\nEven if  1–4% of market volume is small, unlimited exclusivity still appears risky. A more defensible starting would be, for example, 36 months, with a possibility to extend only if ROI is objectively not ensured.\n\nInstead of a blanket, non-time-limited exclusivity, there are several alternatives to protect Bolt’s investment while reducing competition law risk:\n\n* *Early exit fees / repayment of outstanding financing -* If the fleet starts using the vehicles outside Bolt before Bolt has recovered its investment, the fleet could be required to: (i) repay the outstanding co-financing amount, and/or (ii) pay an early exit fee reflecting Bolt’s unrecovered investment or expected return.\n\n* *Buy-out options for Bolt’s stake or financed assets - i*nstead of exclusivity, the agreement could grant Bolt: (i) a right to require the fleet to buy out Bolt’s stake, or (ii) a right for Bolt to sell or transfer the co-financed vehicles at a pre-agreed valuation if the fleet wishes to exit.\n\n* *Step-down exclusivity*, for example: (i) full exclusivity during the first phase (when investment risk is highest); (ii) partial exclusivity or minimum-use commitments in the middle phase; (iii) no exclusivity once the investment is amortised.\n\nThese are just initial ideas - first, I need to better understand how similar deals are structured in other CEE countries.","2026-01-12T15:58:32.123Z"],["3804582","CRC-2259","CRC","linnet.puskar@bolt.eu","Linnet Puskar","[update] 2025 year end closing is done. Results:\nCollection clearing account balance reduced from 83 mln EUR (Aug 2025) → 2.8 mln EUR\nPayout clearing balance 221 mln EUR --> 1.1 mln EUR","2026-01-12T15:58:40.945Z"],["3804586","LSS-60495","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! \n\n* DoB for Markus: 17.12.1993","2026-01-12T16:01:01.695Z"],["3804587","ITI-1049","ITI","marko.toomla@bolt.eu","Marko Toomla","This task is currently postponed since we do not have a proper system for linking devices.\nSuggested a quick set-up with the Jira asset computer field or a new field with limited visibility.","2026-01-12T16:02:25.466Z"],["3804591","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","guglielmo.fontanarava@bolt.eu","Guglielmo Fontana-Rava Andreae","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] I think the idea is good. Lets discuss this on Wednesday during Development meeting.","2026-01-12T16:04:23.967Z"],["3804592","UXROPS-113","UXROPS","akram.yacob@bolt.eu","Akram Yacob","more details [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ah8XR_7oJM9iui0qy60KHJLNonXSagWbkHQonPviyX0/edit?tab=t.89m71ay8nk5s#heading=h.pu8f9vbyme01] (in the comment threads)","2026-01-12T16:04:43.227Z"],["3804595","LSS-61370","LSS","pedro.ferreira@bolt.eu","Pedro da Silva Ferreira","Hello,\n\nWhile the invoice due date (January 18th) has not yet been reached, I would like to flag that, based on the overall context and prior interactions with the client, there is a *material risk that the payment may not be settled as indicated*.\n\nThis assessment is not based on a missed payment to date, but rather on the broader pattern of behavior observed, including role misrepresentation, inconsistent explanations regarding usage, and the overall handling of the situation once concerns were raised.\n\nFor this reason, and from a risk mitigation perspective, I wanted to proactively highlight this concern to Legal and remain aligned on any preventive or follow-up actions that may be appropriate should the payment not occur as stated.\n\nI will continue to monitor the situation closely and will update you accordingly.\n\nBest regards","2026-01-12T16:04:50.071Z"],["3804599","LSS-60939","LSS","alejandro.sanz@bolt.eu","Alejandro Sanz","[^Bolt Drive Sublease Master Agreement amendment_Bolt Technology (3) (d32b005e-9856-4297-9c8a-3fffc2b604a4).docx]\n\n[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432]  , agree with the suggestion. Please use the attached version for signature collection purposes. I included additional changes based in background received in the lasts days. Please note that Bolt Solutions DE GmbH has also to sign the agreement (by Vincent Pickering on its behalf). Thank you!","2026-01-12T16:05:48.026Z"],["3804600","PAW-14808","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was closed\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160428\nStatus: closed\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 16:06:01 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T16:06:01.874Z"],["3804608","MKP-4319","MKP","abdelhalim.machehalek@bolt.eu","Abdelhalim Machehalek","[~accountid:5b306883ed67e12dd27645e1] Task already assigned to me => Assign pricing component ","2026-01-12T16:07:30.035Z"],["3804610","LSS-61252","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Motor vehicle sale agreement_Bolt Services EE OÜ_RESA Motors, UAB_09.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T16:07:39.835Z"],["3804611","LSS-61361","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","thank you Kirsika!","2026-01-12T16:07:40.228Z"],["3804615","LSS-61370","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Understood. Could you please clarify what is the amount of the invoice?\n\nAlso, regarding my other question - Did we communicate to the clients that their accounts had been blocked? If yes, did they present any complaint or asked for further clarifications or justification?","2026-01-12T16:09:52.947Z"],["3804619","PAW-14813","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-12T16:12:07.295Z"],["3804624","LSS-57632","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:5e4cfe3b393ea90c94b40eb0] we have responded to Bastion’s comments and attended to some amendments in line with their requests here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iSUg8z6o0ag_oKrMf6PVAamAzWN0YAeNcxiGjJv5aGo/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iSUg8z6o0ag_oKrMf6PVAamAzWN0YAeNcxiGjJv5aGo/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\n{color:#0747a6}*Please provide feedback to the comment at clause 3.1. as, based on your answer, we may need to include an additional amendment.* {color}","2026-01-12T16:13:23.761Z"],["3804627","WD-22551","WD","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 18.13.54.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T16:14:09.421Z"],["3804628","LSS-61361","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 18.14.07.png|width=529,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 18.14.07.png\"!","2026-01-12T16:14:18.865Z"],["3804629","LSS-61435","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^Copy of EE20260112-001 Exleasingcars - Bolt Drive EE.docx.pdf] _(404 kB)_","2026-01-12T16:14:19.297Z"],["3804631","DBRE-8547","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","Jan 13: more tests (1h); still blocked by [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5547|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5547].\n\n* As it’s not clear when (if at all) 5547 will be approved, closing this one as “Done”. There is nothing more to test – upgrade works with 5547 and doesn’t work without.\n\nJan 12: more tests (3h); blocked by [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5547|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5547].","2026-01-12T16:14:23.698Z"],["3804633","PFI-832530","PFI","jasmina.vaclavkova@bolt.eu","Jasmina Vaclavkova","[^MT6525-8245.pdf]\n\n[^MT6525-9104.pdf]\n\n[^MT6526-597.pdf]","2026-01-12T16:15:28.937Z"],["3804634","PFI-832530","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T16:15:31.279Z"],["3804638","LSS-61370","LSS","pedro.ferreira@bolt.eu","Pedro da Silva Ferreira","Hello,\n\nRegarding the invoice amounts it is around 12k, please note that these figures are indicative and subject to final confirmation once the billing cycle is closed.\n\nRegarding client communication, *yes, the clients were informed that their accounts had been blocked*.\n\nFollowing this communication:\n\n* The client associated with *Emotion Sports* questioned the decision and stated that the situation did not make sense from his perspective.\n* He did *not file a formal complaint*, but expressed disagreement with the reasoning provided and argued that the block occurred before the agreed payment date of January 18th.\n* He subsequently shared screenshots from his Uber Business dashboard, indicating amounts he claimed to have already paid on that platform.\n\nNo formal legal complaint or written dispute was submitted. The interaction remained at an informal clarification level, with the client denying wrongdoing and questioning the timing of the block.","2026-01-12T16:17:34.661Z"],["3804643","LSS-61124","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nWe have received the approval to proceed.\n\nCould you kindly support us with the signature?\n\nThank you.\n\n","2026-01-12T16:20:50.853Z"],["3804645","LSS-60202","LSS","steven.ochieng@bolt.eu","Steven Ochieng","The response has been shared here: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/722165051|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/722165051]","2026-01-12T16:21:22.376Z"],["3804649","WFM-9859","WFM","ottomar.meoste@bolt.eu","Ottomar Meoste","Hello Artur! \n\nOne of the role approvers seems to be on vacation and no one else has picked their tasks up. I will forward this to the higher ups and ask someone on there to approve it. Will get back to you tomorrow at the latest. ","2026-01-12T16:23:55.207Z"],["3804650","PAW-14814","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @suhovanton\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/16983\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 16:24:12 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T16:24:12.646Z"],["3804654","PFI-831543","PFI","davi.santos@bolt-outsource.eu","Davi Julião Da Silva Santos","Hello, Ketlin!\n\nThanks for the answer. In this case, I can tell this to the fleet? Or is there something else I need to tell him?\n\nI’ll be waiting for your follow up.","2026-01-12T16:26:10.247Z"],["3804657","LSS-60808","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nThis is their reasoning:\n\n{quote}\"It has been brought to my attention that we cannot book the previous order for Maps SDK for Mobile.\n\nThe justification here is that we have an actual technical limitation where we cannot have two different term dates, with different pricing, for the same Mapbox Account ID. \n\nThe proposal is that Bolt sign a simple Amendment stating that these additional SPP funds are co-terming with the Order you currently have for \"boltuser\", which ends on 6/30/2026.\n\nRevenue operations has drafted an Amendment for this, please see attached. \n\nThe other option is we rip and replace both contracts and replace with a fresh 12 month term, all credits will be applied and stated in the order form.\n\nApologies for the inconvenience.\"{quote}\n\nThanks","2026-01-12T16:28:30.102Z"],["3804660","LSS-61436","LSS","sorina.mihai@bolt.eu","Sorina Mihai","[^Agreement-ahto.kink_bolt.eu-signed (8).pdf] _(495 kB)_\n\n[^Anexa 6_Nota de comanda 5 ctr. cadru cu OMEGA Trust - Opinie de audit IT.docx] _(27 kB)_\n\n[^Act aditional nr. 1_Modificare date financiare.docx] _(25 kB)_","2026-01-12T16:30:14.433Z"],["3804661","PFI-832538","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 1.24.44 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T16:31:10.158Z"],["3804662","LSS-61436","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T16:31:43.823Z"],["3804663","LSS-56798","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:cc9fc6f2-33e3-41d1-a4e5-1587e9f47322] \n\nThank you for the update!\n\nLet me summarize my understanding and flag a few points where I still see open questions:\n\n# *Structure / entities*\nFrom what you describe, it sounds like the market model may involve:\n#* One entity acting purely as a technology and services provider (intermediation only, no merchant of record role). A new Bolt entity to be created?\n#* A separate entity acting as the seller towards the end customer and therefore collecting the payments (i.e. acting as Merchant of Record, (MoR)).\n# *Payment collection and licensing*\nCan you please confirm if you are suggesting Bolt to create a second entity which role would be collecting the money? If so, my key point is that in such a case, Bolt would need to hold the relevant PHV/transport-related license in Greece. If so, I am struggling to see how this materially changes our current setup, as the entity collecting the payment would still appear to be closely linked to the regulated activity.\n# *Bolt’s role as MoR vs. non-MoR*\nMy initial suggestion when we discussed a few weeks ago was slightly different that the one you described, namely:\n#* Bolt remaining as it is today from a platform perspective, but *without* collecting the money (i.e. not acting as MoR); and\n#* A *non-Bolt third party* acting as MoR, issuing invoices to customers and handling payment flows in the backend.\n# In that scenario:\n#* The simplest option operationally would be to leverage our existing platform while staying out of the transaction flow.\n#* If the third party is the MoR, it seems reasonable that Bolt would not need a license, *subject to confirmation by external counsel*.\n#* Assuming this is similar to what Uber is doing, we would need to assess whether this setup is feasible from a *Product and backend perspective.*\nTo recap, at this stage, when you describe *Bolt collecting payments on behalf of the third party,* this feels very close to our current operating model. If that is the case, I am concerned that the licensing requirement for Bolt would remain unchanged.\n\nHappy to discuss this further on a call and align on the most legally robust and operationally feasible approach.\n\nAdding [~accountid:609bd1fadafdf0006806ed70] and [~accountid:712020:dc012e17-7e04-4ad8-8750-81fc7f7c6047] in case they have any insights from a PP perspective.\n\nThanks again,\nElisabetta","2026-01-12T16:31:44.957Z"],["3804666","LSS-61437","LSS","paula.espeja@bolt.eu","Paula Espeja","[^Formulario Nº 90_BOLT_VAT_Diciembre 2025 13.01.2026.pdf]\n[^Formulario Nº 90_BOLT_INR_Diciembre 2026 13.01.2026.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-12T16:33:53.808Z"],["3804668","WD-22552","WD","lucas.santossilva@bolt.eu","Lucas Oliveira dos Santos Silva","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 08.39.04.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T16:34:05.935Z"],["3804669","LSS-61438","LSS","laura.newton@bolt.eu","Laura Newton","[^Rental agreement - phone booth_Bolt Ope...Limited_Pod Rent Ltd._24.03.25 (1).pdf] _(1.49 MB)_","2026-01-12T16:34:38.414Z"],["3804672","LSS-61370","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 16.28.58.png|width=753,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 16.28.58.png\"!\n\n[^SIRCOM_1241787_1298989929729.tif.pdf]\n\nBased in preliminary research, both contracts appear to have been signed by people who are not listed as managers of these companies, as per the commercial registry","2026-01-12T16:35:53.986Z"],["3804673","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9], Maël has shared the context regarding the passenger’s reclamation and the facts of the ride. \n\n\nI see two areas where Bolt has faulted:\n\n# From a consumer perspective, the price shown was not tranparent; and\n# CS should have refunded the 22.50€ directly to the payment method instead of offering promo codes, as this was money owed to the passenger. \n\n\nWith this in mind, I would however, push back on the request of 100€ because it is a request that is not founded on a loss incurred by the passenger and is purely a commercial gesture. \n\nTo address this case, I would offer a refund of the difference, so 22.50€ on top of the 25€ already received in the form of promo codes. \n\nAre you aligned with this approach? \n\nThank you !\n\n","2026-01-12T16:35:52.869Z"],["3804675","WD-22550","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","!image-20260112-163556.png|width=657,alt=\"image-20260112-163556.png\"!\n\n!image-20260112-163611.png|width=657,alt=\"image-20260112-163611.png\"!\n\n\n","2026-01-12T16:36:24.272Z"],["3804677","WD-22550","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:712020:2261816b-1a2b-4b75-b1dc-d5fce431ad15] , I have made updates, can you please review? 🙂 ","2026-01-12T16:36:42.734Z"],["3804679","PFI-812948","PFI","victor.garces@bolt.eu","Víctor Garcés","Hi [~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] , many thanks for the follow-up. Reviewed it and agree with what you proposed. Just to understand, those are already existing subtypes for which we should change the “VAT Liable?” status to “Yes”? And at a later stage we will create more granular ones?\n\nAdditionally, do you still plan to send any comms to local ops teams to align on the use of these subtypes going forward? When that happens, would you please keep me in the loop? I need to report that to my leads.\n\n ","2026-01-12T16:37:14.188Z"],["3804682","LSS-58367","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] ,\n\nYes, everything is clear now. Thank you very much for the explanation.\n\nI have asked for the document to be updated accordingly.\n\nThank you once again.\n\n","2026-01-12T16:38:39.556Z"],["3804684","FX-3611","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768235977844849]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@chantel.rowe>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3611] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T16:39:50.862Z"],["3804686","PFI-832545","PFI","daria.kubiak@bolt-outsource.eu","Daria Kubiak","[^5c4ba9e1-deda-45b2-af7c-1fd941ae33be.pdf]","2026-01-12T16:40:06.508Z"],["3804687","PFI-832545","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T16:40:08.617Z"],["3804689","LSS-60974","LSS","oleg.shimchik@bolt.eu","Aleh Shymchyk","Hi [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] \n\n[^Warp Product & Services Agreement .pdf]\n[^Warp - Data Processing Addendum (Aug. 2025).docx.pdf]\n\nHere are the files","2026-01-12T16:40:46.998Z"],["3804690","FX-3612","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768236036454599]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@chantel.rowe>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3612] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T16:40:49.023Z"],["3804691","FX-3613","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768236069165439]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@chantel.rowe>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3613] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-12T16:41:23.280Z"],["3804693","RDS-1403","RDS","rishi.kar@bolt.eu","Rishi Raj Kar","[~accountid:5b7d01f0b57ed25933f642e0] I would like to accept this dependency. Lets discuss","2026-01-12T16:42:10.503Z"],["3804696","LSS-61394","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:7eb363dc-ca9f-4746-abde-3581e042a507] ,\n\ncan you please provide more context on your request?\n\nit is not clear what type of bonus are you referring to, what type of fraud you are talking about.\n\nThanks for any additional context you may provide.\n\nElisabetta","2026-01-12T16:45:43.494Z"],["3804699","HS-28790","HS","anna.tiurina@bolt.eu","Anna Tiurina","Hi [~accountid:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db] and thank you for your reply!\n\nIn Ukraine, employment history is confirmed through an employment record book rather than work certificates. This document requires localization, and unfortunately, I was not aware that it could be submitted to qualify for 26 days of annual leave. As a result, I did not receive the additional 6 days of leave last year.\n\nWould it be possible to carry over the 6 days from the previous year, provided that I submit the relevant documentation confirming my work experience?","2026-01-12T16:46:54.755Z"],["3804700","WD-22551","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi Kadi, \nI’m a little bit confused on how I can support you here. You are able to download the invoice information yourself by running the report “Bolt Invoices - ESG Analysis (Utilities)”.\nGoing to the bottom of the results, there will be a row “Total”. Click on the blue number in the last column.\n\n!image-20260112-164611.png|width=719,alt=\"image-20260112-164611.png\"!\n\nA table will pop-up based on which all of the information you should require should be presented to you. \n\nLet’s know please if this resolves your issues, additionally we also have “Bolt Invoices - ESG Analysis (Utilities)_V2” report which is a similar raw_data format. Let me know if it suits your needs still or you need some extra information.\n\n\n","2026-01-12T16:48:30.220Z"],["3804703","LSS-61228","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ,\n\nyes if you are proposing as money owed to the passenger and not as promo code, I’m OK with your suggested approach.\n\nThank you!\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-12T16:49:48.587Z"],["3804704","BB-2162","BB","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","adding my recent query: \n\ngot 48 docs\n\n{code:sql}SELECT\n    etl.invoice_id,\n    -- etl.order_id,\n    -- etl.order_reference_id,\n    etl.business_company_country,\n    etl.document_source,\n    etl.to_agent_id,\n    etl.to_agent_name,\n    etlr.invoice_row_vat_percentage,\n    etl.sum,\n    etl.vat_sum,\n    etl.sum_with_vat,\n    etl.invoice_pdf_link,\n    etl.invoice_public_id,\n    etl.document_direction,\n    SUM(etlr.invoice_row_sum)          AS row_sum,\n    SUM(etlr.invoice_row_vat_sum)      AS row_vat_sum,\n    SUM(etlr.invoice_row_sum_with_vat) AS row_sum_with_vat\nFROM ng_commerce_billing_spark.etl_billing_invoicing_business_row etlr\nLEFT JOIN ng_commerce_billing_spark.etl_billing_invoicing_business etl\n  ON etl.invoice_id = etlr.invoice_id\n  AND etl.created_date >= DATE('2025-08-01')\nLEFT JOIN ng_public_spark.billing_document_invoice_document_row bdidr \n  ON bdidr.id = etlr.invoice_row_id\nWHERE etlr.created_date >= DATE('2025-08-01')\n  -- AND etl.invoice_period_end_date_local >= DATE('2025-09-01')\n  AND etlr.invoice_row_vat_percentage = 22\n  AND etl.to_agent_id NOT IN (\n    1043,2243,2459,3180,5479,18325,21147,21774,54966,66127,74501,75232,78358,78469,\n    82074,95957,100080,106470,116499,122013,122520,123501,139474,148210,163790,\n    206858,210113,228133,229228,230693,232358,233784,234954,249903,253044,255685,\n    257228,260352,264523,270180,275422,279191,283314,286615,288800,296802,299038,\n    303827,309522,333581,333962,337200,342538,345909,347307,354568,362751,372608,\n    375401,399256,399780,755406,757967,758643,760920,768674,769578\n  )\n  AND etl.business_company_country = 'ee'\n  AND etl.business_company_country IS NOT NULL\n  AND get_json_object(bdidr.payload_json, \"$.country\") = 'ee'\n  AND (etl.document_direction IS NULL OR LOWER(etl.document_direction) != 'credit')\nGROUP BY\n    etl.invoice_id,\n    etl.business_company_country,\n    etl.document_source,\n    etl.to_agent_id,\n    etl.to_agent_name,\n    etlr.invoice_row_vat_percentage,\n    etl.sum,\n    etl.vat_sum,\n    etl.sum_with_vat,\n    etl.invoice_pdf_link,\n    etl.invoice_public_id,\n    etl.document_direction;\n{code}","2026-01-12T16:50:56.085Z"],["3804706","LSS-57342","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*CALL W/ ZELLIS (12.01)*+\n\n* All DP issues settled expect for Clause 10 (Subprocessors) and Clause 13 (Indemnity / Liability Cap) ✅ \n* Main discussion points / resolutions were as follows:\n** *Zellis providing full copies of subprocessor contracts* :Google_Doc: \n*** +Rationale+: Zellis were hesitant to provide full copies of contracts, due to confidentiality. I proposed redacted copies; they rejcted this on the grounds that it would involve disproportionate operational effort on their side.\n*** +Proposal 1+: We agreed that Zellis could provide extracts of agreements containing what was “_necessary to demonstrate compliance with applicable laws_”\n**** +Thoughts+: This is something we can accept, as it gets to the core point of checking A28/security/international transfer mechanisms ✅ Zellis are currently drafting this and will share wording in the next version :loading: \n*** +Proposal 2+: Zellis also wants to {color:#ff5630}*limit the circumstances in which Bolt can request copies*{color} (i.e., when we actually need them).\n**** +Thoughts+: This is not ideal ⚠️ but may be something we need to concede on - let’s see what they have to say in amendments. I may need to advise the business on the risks here :loading: \n** *Zellis notifying Bolt about new subprocessors* 🔊 \n*** +Rationale+: Zellis has stated that they have strict internal compliance processes when onboarding subprocessors. As part of its own onboarding, Bolt can provide [privacy@bolt.eu|mailto:privacy@bolt.eu] email via Customer Portal, and opt-in to receive email notifications about new subprocessors. The emails are sent automatically, and effectively just say that a new subprocessor has been added, together with a link to the subprocessor list ([LINK|http://solutions.zellis.com/subprocessorlist]). I explained that this was not enough.\n**** NB. This list contains the following info about subprocessors: Name, address, processing country and sentence on the nature of processing. Does +*not*+ contain detailed purposes, categories of personal data, categories of data subjects, information ons security measures, nor information on international transfer mechanisms.\n**** Nevertheless, not all of these SPs apply to Bolt anyway (which _slightly_ lowers the risk profile).\n*** +Position+: Ultimately, {color:#ff5630}*Zellis is not willing to change its alerts / notification practices*{color} here. What Zellis proposed was that Bolt can request additional information on request, and if it does so, then Zellis will extend the 30-day review timeframe. \n**** +Thoughts+: IMO this is not ideal - to properly review each subprocessor we would always need to request more information, which creates undue process burden on the Bolt side⚠️  However, if the choice is between this concession and nothing, this would still be better. As such, IMO we should let Zellis propose this, and then I can advise the business on the risks :loading: \n** *Bolt objecting to new subprocessors / terminating those services* 🛑 \n*** +Rationale+: Zellis does not want Bolt to have the right to terminate; instead, Zellis wants _Bolt_ to suggest alternatives. Equally, Zellis wants to limit the scenarios in which Bolt can object to new subprocessors - I explained that A28(2) does not limit objection scenarios, but Zellis did not seem amenable to this argument.\n*** +Proposal+: Zellis are going to provide revisions re the {color:#ff5630}*only specific*{color} {color:#ff5630}*scenarios in which Bolt can object*{color}. IMO, having this (but still with the right to terminate) is better than being able to object on any grounds but with no right to terminate, as otherwise there is not real consequence to an objection from Bolt. We will wait to see Zellis’s suggestions, and then I will advise the business on the risks :loading: \n** *Pro-Bolt indemnity* 🛡️ \n*** +Rationale+: Zellis does not typically see pro-controller indemnities in DPAs (I countered that actually this is standard practice from our side). From their POV, if a processor breaches DP laws, the controller can recover via contractual damages (I reiterated why indemnities are preferred).\n*** +Proposal+: {color:#ff5630}*Zellis does not want any pro-Bolt DP indemnity*{color}. Instead, they are willing to increase the liability cap.\n**** +Thoughts+: This significantly shifts the risk onto us, and so I am not thrilled on this ⚠️ Let’s see what Zellis proposes, but I definitely need to escalate this to Gab and advise the business on the risks :loading: \n** *Limitations on Zellis liability* 💰 \n*** +Rationale+: Zellis cannot obtain Exec approval for a higher cap.\n*** +Proposal+: Zellis is proposing a £1m - £1.5m *_total_* super-cap (i.e., not per claim or aggregate of loss).\n**** +Thoughts+: Given that we are sharing financial data of all UK drivers, this is not ideal - a bad data breach could screw us ⚠️ I definitely need to escalate this to Gab and advise the business on the risks :loading: \n*** NB. I floated including specified deemed direct losses. Zellis stated this could result in further negotiation, but given the potential concessions here already, it would be preduct to include these ⚠️ As such, let’s wait to see Zellis’s comments, then include these :loading: \n* Aim is to have the contract signed by Friday 23 January 🕓 \n\n+*NEXT STEPS*+\n\n* Wait for Zellis suggestions re revised DPA.\n* Escalate points of contention to Gab for approval, given departure from our standard position.\n* We will also need Ed Riley’s / the business' approval for various points (particularly the indemnity / limitation of liability issue. Joe and Paddy would then need to also approve.\n** I have teed the business up for this, so that they are warned ([link|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C090BLAAVH8/p1768238535670529?thread_ts=1768209853.594659&cid=C090BLAAVH8]).","2026-01-12T16:52:42.798Z"],["3804710","MTE-1257","MTE","anton.hmelnitski@bolt.eu","Anton Hmelnitski","Is the default {{English, American}}? [~accountid:712020:0b749a8a-fe6a-4f53-837a-a79e10d19db5] ","2026-01-12T16:58:18.006Z"],["3804713","PFI-832545","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-12T17:01:09.488Z"],["3804714","PFI-832443","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-12T17:01:10.314Z"],["3804715","RDS-1074","RDS","vivaksha.singh@bolt.eu","Vivaksha Singh","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] Yes, we are currently calculating the rider cancellation/drop w.r.t increase in ETAs.","2026-01-12T17:01:18.188Z"],["3804716","RDS-1363","RDS","vivaksha.singh@bolt.eu","Vivaksha Singh","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] Let’s discuss in our next 1:1, post that I can modify this. ","2026-01-12T17:03:27.797Z"],["3804717","PFI-816808","PFI","jergus.janosik@bolt-outsource.eu","Jerguš Jánošík","Hello, any news ?\n\n","2026-01-12T17:03:56.496Z"],["3804718","PFI-832404","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hi Klaudia, those are bailiff payouts. They seem to be correct. The payouts are duplicated cause there was two files to be made, from 2 different weeks. One payout is from one file and the other one from another. Unfortunately I do not have more details once I just process what is there.\r\n\r\nI gave you access to the ticket. If we overpaid the authorities, they should be able to refund the difference to the partner directly. ","2026-01-12T17:04:59.269Z"],["3804719","LSS-60142","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hi [~accountid:712020:57b36b99-7144-476f-a96e-ee6e8296217c], thanks for sharing the information. \n\nIn my view, signing only acceptance–handover acts does not resolve the question of the content, duration, and scope of this cooperation. The main risks of proceeding without at least a minimal agreement are:\n\n* *Unclear legal basis* – the cooperation may be reinterpreted as a binding commitment, in-kind support, or another form of obligation.\n* *Expectation management* – the quantity, value, and duration of vouchers remain unclear and may be perceived as guaranteed.\n* *Weak position in case of disputes* – handover acts evidence transfer, but not liability allocation, usage rules, termination rights, or limits.\n* *Voucher use and liability* – there would be no clear agreement on how vouchers may be used, where responsibilities lie, and who handles and bears the risk of consumer complaints, etc.\n* *GDPR uncertainty* – it is unclear whether, how, and what information may be shared from a data protection perspective.\n* *No clean exit* – it would be difficult to clearly suspend or terminate participation if misuse or reputational risks arise.\n\nHow exactly has it been agreed with the municipality which vouchers will be provided, for how long, and with what total value, if only acceptance–handover acts are signed? Is this intended as a one-off action, with no additional vouchers to be transferred later?\n\nThanks! 🙏 ","2026-01-12T17:06:32.051Z"],["3804722","LSS-61443","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","[^HEERA LOGISTICS COOPERATION AGREEMENT CO-INVEST.docx (1).pdf] _(499 kB)_","2026-01-12T17:07:22.011Z"],["3804723","LSS-61443","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","Kindly ignore the KPI’s section as we’ll not be amending them. ","2026-01-12T17:08:16.123Z"],["3804730","LSS-61448","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","[^Cooperation agreement rides_Bolt Operations_Taufic Taya Transport & Logistics Limited_Solis Technologies Limited_03.10.2024 (2).pdf] _(458 kB)_","2026-01-12T17:14:17.426Z"],["3804731","PFI-832556","PFI","mercy.mulungye@bolt-outsource.eu","Mercy Mulungye","!Messenger_creation_0B8F182B-6003-4422-AB78-88D2A32F8D4B.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T17:14:31.151Z"],["3804734","PFI-832557","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T17:16:16.312Z"],["3804735","LSS-61448","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T17:16:19.449Z"],["3804736","LSS-61443","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-12T17:16:19.454Z"],["3804741","WEBSD-1470","WEBSD","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","[^PDF. Términos de la Plataforma para Servicios de Transporte bajo Demanda_ Proveedores de Servicios (Paraguay).docx.pdf]\n\n[^Word. Términos de la Plataforma para Servicios de Transporte bajo Demanda_ Proveedores de Servicios (Paraguay).docx]","2026-01-12T17:21:04.880Z"],["3804742","WFM-9959","WFM","shivam.pal@bolt-outsource.eu","Shivam Pal","priority - Permanent  ","2026-01-12T17:21:26.266Z"],["3804744","LSS-61394","LSS","christos.hadjistylianou@bolt.eu","Christos Hadjistylianou","Hey [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] \n\nThe campaign id is :489337, Description “Complete 30 trips in the next 30 days and get a 200 EUR bonus. You must be online for at least 120 hours to be eligible for the bonus.” \n\nThe driver initially received the 200€ bonus but the amount was retrieved after some rides were marked fraud. Additional 98€ were retrieved for fraud_adjustment. \n\nThe fraud I see is CASH_OUT_CAMPAIGNS, DRIVER_HAS_ACTIVE_BONUS_MARK_ORDER, Deduct cash campaign bonus, Mark order as fraud\n\n ","2026-01-12T17:24:31.388Z"],["3804746","LSS-61440","LSS","sofia.vasilakopoulou@bolt.eu","Sofia Vasilakopoulou","Pls cancel the ticket, I created a new one since this was probably the wrong place. Thanks!","2026-01-12T17:26:39.853Z"],["3804751","PFI-814171","PFI","christian.barrios@bolt.eu","Christian Junior Barrios Brassel","HI team!\n\nDo we have any updates regarding this case?\n\nThanks in advance!\n\n","2026-01-12T17:46:05.125Z"],["3804752","LSS-60246","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Hi [~accountid:5f802f9595fe8e0069b2c28c] - I have discussed with the team and my thoughts are below re Portugal:\n\n* Noted re the position in the Beehive article - thanks for flagging. Upon investigation, advice on this topic appears to be a global issue, and so would better be dealt with as a cross-border coordinated effort by our teams. As such, we (Privacy Team) are currently discussing this with CSPC and will work to align on and update the Beehive articles.\n* In terms of what this means for you in practical terms, in Portugal please feel free to continue to follow the current guidance for now, but note that this will soon change (we will likely change the instructions to be that we should pass the claims / rider details on to the fleet owner, rather than the other way around -  we are currently aligning on this with CSPC). For the case on this ticket (Spain), we can follow the steps outlined in my 23 December comment.\n\nI hope that this helps. Is anything further needed from the Privacy Team on this, or can I close the ticket? 🙂","2026-01-12T17:46:57.360Z"],["3804755","PFI-832567","PFI","suvi.tupola@bolt-outsource.eu","Suvi Tupola","!Screenshot_20260112_121930_Nordea Mobile.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot_20260112_133408_Bolt Driver.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T17:51:10.374Z"],["3804756","BP-12847","BP","anton.lyubarskiy@bolt.eu","Anton Lyubarskiy","{quote}the user can be logged out by an administrator {quote}\n\nAFAIK, we don't have it for the BP admins at the moment","2026-01-12T17:52:54.621Z"],["3804757","PFI-832569","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 2.47.06 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T17:53:24.266Z"],["3804758","LSS-60119","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:240e5e60-baab-4e72-a388-591f4f4ec6a2] \n\n* Please find my initial review of the agreement as it currently stands[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XX1_U_KwIh-dfuQqRSUiwFd3XfDJDchA/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XX1_U_KwIh-dfuQqRSUiwFd3XfDJDchA/edit|smart-link] \n* I note that the commercials and service levels are still being finalised. Once those core components are closer to being agreed, I’ll conduct a further review to ensure alignment and avoid rework. \n* Regarding the  [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gLIQlfQZ0v0BVL3JCLZsFonTZt6TCVuR/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gLIQlfQZ0v0BVL3JCLZsFonTZt6TCVuR/edit|smart-link] being included as an annexure - please provide a quick summary of what this covers and what the benefit would be? Is it up to date and aligned with the current arrangement? \n* {color:#ff5630}Yes please have CASI sign our NDA. {color}","2026-01-12T17:53:32.935Z"],["3804759","PFI-832545","PFI","daria.kubiak@bolt-outsource.eu","Daria Kubiak","Hi, user information is correct, they report that the VAT percentage is incorrect. It is supposed to be 8%, but it is 4% on the invoice. ","2026-01-12T17:53:54.122Z"],["3804760","LSS-61058","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] - we are currently considering the issue of multiple overlapping privacy notices / controller lists in different languages. Our current position is that we rely on the global controller list for the most up-to-date information, rather than updating every single document every time there is an update. Nevertheless, on this occasion, I have also updated the Belgian document ✅  This will likely go through / be published tomorrow - let me know if the public doc does not update. Otherwise, I will consider this ticket to be closed 🙂 ","2026-01-12T17:55:06.983Z"],["3804761","LSS-60617","LSS","anouar.miled@bolt.eu","Anouar Miled","[^2025-10_MV_Bolt_Müglitztal_15.01.2026.pdf]\n\nHi [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] ,\n\nThe following points have been updated in the contract. Kindly let me know if you approve so we can proceed with submitting it for signature:\n\n# *Index Clause – Outdated Reference (§ 6):*\nThe clause under “§ 6 Änderung des Mietzinses” has been amended as per your suggestion.\n# *Power Capacity – Missing Contractual Guarantee:*\nUnder “§ 20 Sonstige Vereinbarungen,” pt. 4 has been added/updated as follows:\n_“_Der Vermieter gewährleistet, dass dem Mieter ab Mietbeginn für dessen Geschäftsbetrieb eine Stromkapazität von mindestens 60 kW zur Verfügung steht._.”_\n\nRegarding the *6-month notice period for the break option (§ 2.3)*, we set a deadline date in our calendar to ensure the notice deadline is not missed and to make an earlier decision.\n\n[~accountid:5fc514a09592df00761a5d3d] Startdate changed to 15.01.2026","2026-01-12T17:55:14.980Z"],["3804762","LSS-61366","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","*NOTE*: Based on discussion with Gab, our previous position re sharing with competitors is to push for lobbying. If sharing competitor data with Bolt concerns limited drivers that we can trust, then could be reasonable (maybe not share _personal_ data)? Otherwise, we may not want to do it, as raises concerns re ‘spying’.","2026-01-12T17:57:52.847Z"],["3804763","PFI-832570","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T17:58:09.567Z"],["3804764","PFI-832571","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 2.55.04 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T17:59:21.320Z"],["3804770","PFI-832443","PFI","ondrej.knoll@bolt-outsource.eu","Ondrej Knoll","Hi,\nI understand that there might not be anything that you can do with the invoice, but I escaled this issue more about the driver profile.\n\nWe would like to know, if there is something wrong with the drivers account, since the invoice does not have any DPH counted in it.\n\n","2026-01-12T18:02:38.755Z"],["3804772","BP-12847","BP","uladzislau.tsyrkunou@bolt.eu","Uladzislau Tsyrkunou","[@anton.lyubarskiy|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5de0e6d42fd6260cf27c9663] thank you for highlighting it,\n\n{{src/business/core/business/main/portal/Bootstrap.ts > /internal/businessPortalAuth/revokeRefreshToken}} confused me a little.","2026-01-12T18:07:18.590Z"],["3804773","PFI-832578","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^ComprobanteTransferenciasTercerosOtrosBancos_17656_251213_224814.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-12T18:07:44.585Z"],["3804774","PFI-832579","PFI","christian.barrios@bolt.eu","Christian Junior Barrios Brassel","[^Comprobante-BOLT 6 DE ENRO.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-12T18:11:47.049Z"],["3804775","LSS-56160","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (12.01)*+\n\n* ENG have not yet confirmed whether the account was compromised. They have just flagged a “_suspected_” login session. \n* It seems likely that the original account owner is the one who messaged he to complain, given that the device ID has a login session from the day after the account was created.\n* It is still unclear what is meant by a “passkey” login. However, this was used by the ‘legit’ device, and so it seems unlikely that this would cause ongoing compromise.\n\n+*NEXT STEPS*+\n\n* It is still unclear if compromise took place here (and if so, how). I have re-asked here: [LINK|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06R63EQ6CS/p1768241739562079?thread_ts=1767354727.192229&cid=C06R63EQ6CS].\n** If compromise is confirmed, only then will I escalate to ODPO.\n* Nevertheless, if compromise did take place, it seems likely that this is no longer ongoing. In any case, this will not be reportable.","2026-01-12T18:15:46.300Z"],["3804776","LSS-55755","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team,\n[~accountid:712020:d3fd53e6-f124-4770-a577-b09d6688566f] thank you for the updates. \n\nSince the primary agreement was negotiated a few months ago and the changes to this annex were made without any track changes, I had to review the content of the annex again, left my comments and suggestions, please review.\n\n\nI cannot see whether these clauses had already been approved by colleagues previously, and as the agreement was negotiated some time ago, I have therefore involved Privacy and Tax/accounting colleagues in few places to confirm that the terms are appropriate. I believe their confirmations will not take long 🙏 \n\nThanks! ","2026-01-12T18:20:04.466Z"],["3804777","LSS-61366","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Hi [~accountid:61110fca627b56006860d802] - thanks for escalating this. In order to provide my thoughts, I need a bit more context behind what we are planning to do here. As such, please could you provide your thoughts on the following:\n\n# What _precisely_ would these “_weekly statements_” contain? I see you have listed some examples of personal data - is this the full list, and would it apply only to that driver?\n# Do we know if Uber’s driver T&Cs contain any obvious terms that prevent drivers from sharing these statements with a company like Bolt (such that this activity would pose a risk to the drivers sharing the info)?\n# What are you envisioning in terms of the “process”? Would this involve Bolt asking a very small number of Uber drivers for the documents, or a large number? Would Bolt want to do this quietly, or would we be open about it publicly? Just so I can understand how you imagine this will play out.\n# Why exactly do we need these weekly statements? What is the end goal?\n# Is the 2 February a hard deadline here? What is the pressing need for this on the business side?","2026-01-12T18:22:21.358Z"],["3804778","LSS-60031","LSS","ban.beidas@bolt.eu","Ban Beidas","[^Bolt Offers Partnership Agreement (Tessler) (1).docx]\n\nHi legal ops team! Could you please process this agreement for signing? Thanks!","2026-01-12T18:23:06.011Z"],["3804779","LSS-61264","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks all - taking a look from the privacy side. While I consider, can I just check - do we even have such footage? If we do not, then this makes our options considerably more limited, so it would be helpful to understand this as a preliminary point - please let me know! 🙂 ","2026-01-12T18:23:40.183Z"],["3804786","PFI-832592","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T18:59:47.429Z"],["3804788","LSS-46087","LSS","karoli.kesner@bolt.eu","Karoli Kesner","Hi [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] for the lawyers confirmation process in 2025 DE audit, could you please confirm which law firms the local entity cooperated with during the FY25? Last year it was Oppenländer; Orka Law; DLA Piper and lighthouse legal - has the list changed? Thank you and best wishes, Karoli","2026-01-12T19:07:10.258Z"],["3804789","LSS-61459","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","Campaigns need to be valid only in the time frame of the campaign and/or up to the max budget:\n\n* *Germany: €100k*\n* *France: €150k*\n\n","2026-01-12T19:08:01.973Z"],["3804791","PFI-831769","PFI","monika.znotinaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Monika Znotinaite","Hey! any update?","2026-01-12T19:15:55.640Z"],["3804792","PLUS-13","PLUS","simo.pahk@bolt.eu","Simo Pähk","07.01.26 meeting w/ Prateek & Reinis:\n\n# *Idea: extend grace period to 72h, but continue trying to charge every 24h* (+2mw+, requires syncing with billing)\n## Requires new condition property for managing the number of grace periods (e.g. grace_period=24h, grace_period_extensions=2)\n## Need to update all existing subscriptions affected via cron, because above-mentioned properties are fixed during subscription creation\n### Alternative: induce migration to same condition (might not work with current implementation, will only take effect after migration)\n### Alternative: use global dynamic config on billing side\n## We can act in response to every failed payment during period (automatic every 24h, also each time user unsuccessfully changes payment method)\n### We can send a new push\n### Emails are handled on billing side: if we want to supply custom content, need to add this to billing service, OR move responsibility to our side (like with pushes)\n# *Idea: remove benefits after 24h, but keep subscription in grace period* (+1.5mw+, requires updating LCM/campaign rules to account for new state, also requires 1. to be done)\n## If we reacted to failed payments during grace period, we could detect if 24h passed and unenroll user (and re-enroll after successful payment)\n## Probably need a new status (GRACE_PERIOD_WITHOUT_BENEFITS), which we can handle as GRACE_PERIOD in most contexts, but use for specific copy in webview\n# Question: does grace period shift next payment timestamp?\n## No, billing fixes payment timestamp at first failed payment, and adds billing period to it after success\n# Question: is new payment method charged immediately if user changes it in grace period?\n## Yes, and it does not affect grace period at all (next payment timestamp, scheduled tasks etc)\n# Question: can/should we differentiate different payment failures?\n## We have error_code for each failed payment, so we can react accordingly\n# *Idea: allow user to pause during grace period* (+2mw++, probably requires help from billing)\n## Currently explicitly disallowed on billing (and our) side\n## Not trivial, needs changes to state machine: how to switch between grace period/freeze/unfreeze, when to retry payment, how to re-calculate grace period end and charge retry timestamps\n# Question: can we detect email/push opening?\n## Yes for email, no for push\n## Emails are handled by billing, and they don’t track comms ID, so that needs to be changed and propagated to our side too\n# What real estate is there for displaying payment errors? (+1-2d+ for configurable in-apps given designs, +1mw+ for custom banners in webview or native apps)\n## Rider in-apps configurable in admin: banners (shown above bottom sheet in home & active order screen), modals (fullscreen, pops up on e.g. app opening), vertical banners (connected to stories, displayed under What’s new on home screen)\n## Rider app: [system notifications project|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/7174154?issueViewSection=comments&selectedIssue=RDS-618] planned for this Q\n## Other places in rider app under our control: side menu notification (just red dot on Subscription menu item), profile icon (currently plus logo for subscribers), sticky banner above ride category selection screen, upcoming (scheduled) ride banner, finished ride banner, finished rental ride banner, sticky banner in rental map screen, small badges on verticals in home screen, cancellation upsell modal\n## Eater in-apps configurable in admin: hero banner (shown on top of screen, e.g. home screen), grouped banner (carousel in different places, e.g. home screen), dynamic banner (floating modal that pops up on app open), promotional bottom sheet (some new things, similar to dynamic banners I guess)\n## Other places in eater app under our control: icon behind “Hello, X” under Account menu, subscription menu item (icon + text) under “Other”\n## Other places in eater app that could be tweaked by us: mini banners (shown in multiple places, e.g. provider screen or checkout)\n# *Question: how easy is it to customize push/email?* (+2d+, given copies)\n## Pushes are fully under our control, so just need a copy\n## Emails are configured via global templates, so either need to introduce new types (not recommended), or use templating logic to change some sentences here and there\n\n\n\n!IMG_8333.jpeg|width=1170,height=2532!\n\n!IMG_8334.png|width=1170,height=2532!\n\n!IMG_8335.jpeg|width=1170,height=2532!\n\n!IMG_8336.jpeg|width=1170,height=2532!\n\n!IMG_8338.jpeg|width=1170,height=2532!\n\n!IMG_8339.jpeg|width=1170,height=1628!\n\n!IMG_8340.jpeg|width=1170,height=2291!\n\n!IMG_8342.jpeg|width=1170,height=2532!\n\n!IMG_8343.jpeg|width=1168,height=1980!\n\n!IMG_8348.jpeg|width=1170,height=2532!\n\n!IMG_8349.jpeg|width=1170,height=2532!\n\n!IMG_8350.png|width=1170,height=2532!\n\n!IMG_8351.jpeg|width=490,alt=\"IMG_8351.jpeg\"!","2026-01-12T19:17:01.760Z"],["3804793","PFI-832605","PFI","eniola.oyedele@bolt-outsource.eu","Eniola Oyedele","!image-20260112-191457.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T19:18:14.637Z"],["3804796","WFM-9960","WFM","aurelija.jovani@bolt-outsource.eu","Aurelija Jovani","!assembled error.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T19:23:00.755Z"],["3804798","PFI-831689","PFI","ketevan.komladze@bolt.eu","Ketevan Komladze","hi, any updates?","2026-01-12T19:27:02.829Z"],["3804800","PFI-822092","PFI","denis.lauko@bolt-outsource.eu","Denis Lauko","Any updates???","2026-01-12T19:34:07.141Z"],["3804807","PAW-14657","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-juri-gavshin\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/pull/3072\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 19:48:45 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T19:48:45.413Z"],["3804817","PFI-831200","PFI","obehi.iruebafa@bolt-outsource.eu","Obehi Iruebafa","Hello team,\nThe payment is yet to reflect.","2026-01-12T20:29:04.191Z"],["3804823","PFI-832630","PFI","kehinde.lanlokun@bolt-outsource.eu","Kehinde Lanlokun","[^Beehive 14.html]","2026-01-12T20:51:19.143Z"],["3804824","LSS-61362","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:d3a24a53-8607-48c6-9240-bd0580c5293f] and [~accountid:712020:714baa0e-ddd0-4776-8064-c5a5d3ae37aa] please find below the Legal assessment:\n\nh4. Is the lunch permitted in principle?\n\nYes.\nClause 5.1 of the Policy permits reasonable and appropriate hospitality for maintaining or improving business relationships. A business lunch with an existing supplier for retrospective thanks and forward-looking discussions falls within this category.\n\nh4. Bribery / corruption risk\n\nBased on the facts provided, the lunch:\n\n* is not intended to influence impartiality or induce improper performance (Policy 5.3.1);\n* is open and transparent, with a receipt (Policy 5.3.5 and Section 7);\n* involves private individuals, not public officials;\n* is not linked to a specific procurement decision, tender, or award.\n\nNo red flags listed in Annex 2 are triggered on the current information.\n\nh4. Spend threshold and approvals\n\n* Under Policy 5.2, prior written approval from the Legal team is required if the value exceeds €100 (or equivalent) per gift or benefit.\n* As the spend is not yet confirmed, this approval may still be required once the expected cost is known.\n\nh4. Record-keeping\n\nThe intention to obtain and retain a receipt aligns with Section 7 (Record-Keeping). The business purpose should also be recorded when submitting the expense.\n\nh3. Conditions for compliance\n\nThe lunch will be compliant with the Policy provided that:\n\n# Spend is reasonable and proportionate for a standard business lunch.\n# If the value exceeds €100 per person (or equivalent), written Legal approval is obtained in advance, in line with Policy 5.2.\n# The receipt is retained and the expense is recorded with a clear business purpose.\n# The lunch is not used to influence any improper decision or create an expectation of preferential treatment.\n\nh3.  ","2026-01-12T21:00:26.768Z"],["3804825","PFI-832592","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\nIf you need a _report_, please refer to FleetX (DriverX). If your request concerns an _invoice_, follow these steps:\n\nPlease try:\n* Open the *Client page in Admin*: [link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D].\n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ - The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see another _error_ → provide us a link.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the {{Partner Invoices}}) tab\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-12T21:01:14.864Z"],["3804826","LSS-61460","LSS","joshua.okeleke@bolt.eu","Josh Okeleke","[^FinmidxBolt Partnership Agreement.pdf] _(297 kB)_\n\n!Finmid Data being shared.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T21:06:42.233Z"],["3804827","PFI-832635","PFI","emils.baranovskis@bolt-outsource.eu","Emils Baranovskis","!gmail_images20260111_161854.png.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T21:13:53.869Z"],["3804828","PFI-832635","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T21:13:56.405Z"],["3804837","PAW-14789","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17092\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-12 21:36:44 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-12T21:36:45.016Z"],["3804838","PFI-832647","PFI","jutamas.poldok@bolt-outsource.eu","Jutamas Poldok","!image-20260112-214957.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T21:50:06.869Z"],["3804839","LSS-61082","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Hi [~accountid:712020:714baa0e-ddd0-4776-8064-c5a5d3ae37aa] \n\nThanks for uploading the reference from Clockwise.  However, it mentions BSUK rather than Bolt Operations UK Ltd in the second paragraph.  Please could you ask them to amend it to BOUK? Thanks","2026-01-12T21:51:07.500Z"],["3804842","PFI-832648","PFI","sharon.ochieng@bolt-outsource.eu","Sharon Ochieng","!image.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-12T22:06:33.355Z"],["3804843","PFI-832651","PFI","dominika.kusz@bolt-outsource.eu","Dominika Kusz","[^1768247553487_.pdf (1).pdf]","2026-01-12T22:18:30.965Z"],["3804844","PFI-832651","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-12T22:18:33.109Z"],["3804845","CAMLE-9387","CAMLE","evgeniy.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Evgeniy Kuznetsov","Gave a demo to GAs. No plan to launch the feature in the near future","2026-01-12T22:20:34.280Z"],["3804846","PTWS-2074","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","[~accountid:712020:a5535fc2-4c96-407b-864b-f673b781e58e] reminder to document real time updates you’re making in Bolt 3 to be able to review and update the progress. \nI added Ethnicity drop down values to Estonia as these didn’t have any value attached","2026-01-12T22:21:57.120Z"],["3804849","LSS-57150","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^Scheduled payment agreement_Eliáš Mitra.docx.pdf]\n\nHi Team, please proceed with signing the attached document with Ahto’s Dokobit signature.\n\nHere are the other party’s details: Eliáš Mitra, [+mitraelias143@gmail.com+|mailto:mitraelias143@gmail.com].\n\nThank you!","2026-01-12T22:51:56.068Z"],["3804852","PTWS-2073","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","* [~accountid:712020:a5535fc2-4c96-407b-864b-f673b781e58e] Germany, Poland & Portugal: missing Race/Ethnicity on the Personal Info summary page in Employee Self service","2026-01-12T22:59:37.002Z"],["3804853","PTWS-2076","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","* -Configured active consent for Estonia, Romania and Germany-\n\nSteps followed: *Maintain Active Consent by Country* > added *Custom Consent Statement* > added *Personal Information Data To Be Processed* and also *Active Consent Processing Purposes*\n\n!image-20260112-230150.png|width=654,alt=\"image-20260112-230150.png\"!\n\n!image-20260112-230214.png|width=637,alt=\"image-20260112-230214.png\"!\n\n\n\n!image-20260112-230240.png|width=637,alt=\"image-20260112-230240.png\"!","2026-01-12T23:03:06.869Z"],["3804854","LSS-61050","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:712020:979961a6-5216-4ee0-aa85-a7302993f5e6] The attached NDA is mutual, as is ours. In this situation, I would not recommend signing two mutual NDAs, as this could create overlapping or potentially conflicting obligations.\n\nThe best approach would be to review the attached NDA and proceed with a single agreement only. Please let me know if this would work for you.","2026-01-12T23:04:05.928Z"],["3804856","LSS-61101","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^aneks czynsz 2026 bolt (edfacd3f-bb9b-4377-8f00-18e875eff923).docx]\n\nHi Team, please proceed with signing the attached document with Ahto’s Dokobit signature, thank you!","2026-01-12T23:08:59.517Z"],["3804857","PTWS-2076","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","||*Country*||*Active consent setup*||\n|Azerbaijan| |\n|Belgium| |\n|Bulgaria| |\n|Canada| |\n|China| |\n|Croatia| |\n|Cyprus| |\n|Czech Republic| |\n|Denmark| |\n|Estonia -|Yes|\n|Finland| |\n|France| |\n|Germany|Yes|\n|Ghana| |\n|Greece| |\n|Ireland| |\n|Italy| |\n|Kenya| |\n|Latvia| |\n|Lithuania| |\n|Malaysia| |\n|Malta| |\n|Netherlands| |\n|New Zealand| |\n|Nigeria| |\n|Norway| |\n|Paraguay| |\n|Poland -| |\n|Portugal| |\n|Romania -|Yes|\n|Slovakia| |\n|Slovenia| |\n|South Africa| |\n|Spain| |\n|Sweden| |\n|Switzerland| |\n|Tanzania| |\n|Thailand| |\n|Uganda| |\n|Ukraine| |\n|United Kingdom -| |","2026-01-12T23:12:43.607Z"],["3804858","LSS-61258","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:5bb399378eb5ad7760adb25e] I have amended section 3 so it reflects our standard PoA wording. Please let me know if it’s fine with you and I will proceed with signing. Thank you! ","2026-01-12T23:15:31.196Z"],["3804860","PFI-823181","PFI","pattranit.issariyasunthornkul@bolt-outsource.eu","Pattranit Issariyasunthornkul","Is there any update","2026-01-12T23:54:08.575Z"],["3804864","PFI-832667","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T00:10:52.796Z"],["3804865","RCE-346","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768263539649049]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@test_ci_notifier>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-346] `Create daily test stability report for 2026/01/12` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T00:19:12.484Z"],["3804866","FX-3615","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768263540222839]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@test_ci_notifier>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3615] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T00:19:13.530Z"],["3804867","PFI-832669","PFI","nattnaphak.dararak@bolt-outsource.eu","Nattnaphak Dararak","!image-20260113-003743.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260113-004707.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T00:48:04.468Z"],["3804868","C2-450","C2","yong.lin@bolt.eu","Yong Lin","[~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] I will check on {{2026-01-15}}. We had 2 suppliers for Cobra. FAX and Linan, need to check if Linan lever can fit on FAX bracket","2026-01-13T00:50:12.218Z"],["3804869","PFI-832668","PFI","sanita.tesa@bolt-outsource.eu","Sanita Teša","Also cannot open Payout link [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"start\"%3A1768168800%2C\"show_empty_rejection_code\"%3Afalse%2C\"show_total\"%3Afalse%2C\"id\"%3A591883%2C\"external_client_id\"%3A591883}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1768168800%2C%22show_empty_rejection_code%22%3Afalse%2C%22show_total%22%3Afalse%2C%22id%22%3A591883%2C%22external_client_id%22%3A591883%7D%7D]\n\n","2026-01-13T00:58:39.205Z"],["3804870","PFI-832635","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-13T01:01:18.619Z"],["3804871","PFI-832671","PFI","chonnikan.kaewmanee@bolt-outsource.eu","Chonnikan Kaewmanee","!image-20260113-011821.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260113-011832.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T01:20:11.184Z"],["3804872","PFI-832666","PFI","anna.savsajeva@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Šavšajeva","Issue is also present with Wise Bank, [Driver|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/6746108?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]/[Payout|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233223888]/[Beehive ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/722161508]","2026-01-13T01:22:14.579Z"],["3804875","DRAG101-463","DRAG101","susan.shao@bolt.eu","Cancan Shao","[~accountid:712020:e77ef51b-4584-479b-bc00-b172e7475d2e] Yes, the lead time is 3 weeks. I negotiated the MOQ yesterday, we can order less than 5K for the pilot run period. When do you think we might place the order? Before Chinese New Year or after that? The factory will be on holiday during 2/11-2/24. Some of their supplier may start the holiday even earlier, so we need to place the order as early as possible if we need to produce before CNY. ","2026-01-13T01:24:11.477Z"],["3804876","PFI-832663","PFI","sanita.tesa@bolt-outsource.eu","Sanita Teša","Also the same issue is here [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233140379?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233140379?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-13T01:24:18.535Z"],["3804878","HWMISC-776","HWMISC","susan.shao@bolt.eu","Cancan Shao","[~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] Prices for front and rear brakes based on current raw materials for reference are as following: \n\n* Front barke: 11.5 RMB/pcs\n* Rear brake:  16.2 RMB/pcs\n\nSince currently the raw material of aluminum is going up, normally it’s around 20~21RMB/kg last year, but now it’s more than 24RMB/kg,  they will update the prices once aluminum price drops to the normal level. ","2026-01-13T01:58:23.112Z"],["3804879","DRAG101-471","DRAG101","xinlong.tan@bolt.eu","Xinlong Tan","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] What’s the decision ? can we ship the 3 scooters by economic air ? ","2026-01-13T02:03:59.489Z"],["3804880","PFI-829465","PFI","aydan.kazimova@bolt-outsource.eu","Aydan Kazimova","Hello, I have no access to that. Can you provide it so we can send him?","2026-01-13T02:06:49.754Z"],["3804881","LSS-58646","LSS","lisha.ye@bolt.eu","Lisha Ye","Hey [~accountid:6017bc19dc29b4006a7f1025] is there any update? Yun Hu had already left Bolt, we need to do it asap.","2026-01-13T02:13:05.124Z"],["3804882","PFI-832678","PFI","edgars.belavskis@bolt-outsource.eu","Edgars Belavskis","!gmail_images20260111_161854.png.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T02:15:31.224Z"],["3804883","PFI-832678","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T02:15:33.303Z"],["3804884","LSS-50863","LSS","lisha.ye@bolt.eu","Lisha Ye","Hey [~accountid:61cc1c959ee70a00680edd89] is there any update? I have shared the meeting notes for you. [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S3xQZVHKse2_d0sijXs8830S-2vMM6YkP5XJOeiJDIo/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S3xQZVHKse2_d0sijXs8830S-2vMM6YkP5XJOeiJDIo/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] And this is the list what we could sold.\n\n!企业微信截图_d775e45d-0a22-40b8-844b-1ccd79bdc0e2.png|width=1346,height=549,alt=\"企业微信截图_d775e45d-0a22-40b8-844b-1ccd79bdc0e2.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-13T02:43:35.475Z"],["3804885","PFI-832681","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T02:50:37.641Z"],["3804886","SCM-526","SCM","zixi.chen@bolt.eu","Zixi Chen","Management wants to do the test before shipment, so we will [postpone|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02CCLN6QNR/p1767797323301219?thread_ts=1767584180.633839&cid=C02CCLN6QNR] the payment until we've done proper QC {{2026-02-05}} \n\n!image-20260113-025852.png|width=369,alt=\"image-20260113-025852.png\"!","2026-01-13T03:00:25.384Z"],["3804887","FDBT-4731","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_bank_payments fails on 2026-01-12 02:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _exec