6-01-13T03:12:06.130Z"],["3804888","FDBT-4761","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-13T03:22:41.068Z"],["3804889","WFM-9888","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Thank you, role applied!","2026-01-13T03:22:49.973Z"],["3804890","EBIKE1-350","EBIKE1","xiangxue.hu@bolt.eu","Xiangxue Hu","The checking jig will be finished by this week","2026-01-13T03:34:44.371Z"],["3804891","FDBT-4766","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-13T03:39:40.034Z"],["3804892","PFI-830803","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","Hi Team, any update on this one?. Thank you.","2026-01-13T04:01:22.714Z"],["3804894","DRAG101-426","DRAG101","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:5e4a421e691b8a0c95c2cdec] is there still active work ongoing on this task? If yes, then the due date should be updated.","2026-01-13T04:19:11.472Z"],["3804895","DRAG101-426","DRAG101","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","for visibility, posting here also the costs regarding bolts reworking:\n\n{quote}We decided to remove the glue on bolt FB_M5x35_V1& FB_ M4x45_V1 by soaking in sulfuric acid, but  after the glue was removed, it was found that all the bolts had been corroded and softened, and could not be used any more. \n\n* rework cost 20,000 RMB for removing the glue on the bolts;\n* scrap cost 3.68×20880=76,838.4RMB;{quote}","2026-01-13T04:23:09.660Z"],["3804897","DRAG101-471","DRAG101","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:5eb377ea021ae30ba83274e4] yes, let’s ship with economic air","2026-01-13T04:33:25.344Z"],["3804898","DRAG101-426","DRAG101","yong.lin@bolt.eu","Yong Lin","[~accountid:5e4a421e691b8a0c95c2cdec] \n\nPush/Pull test with Coeur cap: the front fork is broken after 500K cycles\n\nHandlebar tube fatigue test with Coeur cap, PASSED","2026-01-13T04:36:13.344Z"],["3804899","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] how would pedaling with the long seat work?","2026-01-13T04:39:52.218Z"],["3804901","PFI-832690","PFI","mathew.aluko@bolt-outsource.eu","Mathew Aluko","!Screenshot_20260112_090904_Bolt Driver.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T04:53:22.641Z"],["3804910","FDBT-4784","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-13T05:00:49.429Z"],["3804911","PFI-832678","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-13T05:01:20.458Z"],["3804915","HWMISC-768","HWMISC","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:712020:ca91afc6-5fa8-4501-b9e4-b54a8671e143] do we now have this file?","2026-01-13T05:21:51.376Z"],["3804921","FDBT-4706","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_data_integration_workiva_workday_report_for_cash_flow_parent fails on 2026-01-12 05:15:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 771, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 424, in wrapper\n    return func(self, *args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/operators/aws/ecr_docker_operator.py\", line 139, in execute\n    self.runtime_strategy.wait_until_done(self.container_id)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/docker/batch/aws_batch_container_runtime_strategy.py\", line 215, in wait_until_done\n    raise AirflowException(f\"Batch job status is {current_job.status}, failing downstream task\")\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Batch job status is FAILED, failing downstream task\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_data_integration_workiva_workday_report_for_cash_flow_parent/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-12T05%3A15%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=workiva_workday_report_for_cash_flow_parent_post_generate_files_task&base_date=2026-01-12T05%3A15%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-13T05:35:53.126Z"],["3804922","DSR-3079","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Good morning [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] , the driver is currently not accepting our response. One reason is he seemed to have missed the main folder, since the telemetry folder had to be broken down in several sub folders. I asked him to review the main folder. See latest response below:\n\n\n*Full response*\n\nHello, I am following up regarding the suspension of my driver account and the response you provided following my GDPR request. After reviewing the documents and the telemetry files provided, I would like to emphasize the following objective points: The transmitted telemetry files (GPS data in CSV format) contain exclusively information about routes, coordinates, and vehicle speed. These data DO NOT contain personal identification elements (selfie, biometric data, device ID, IP, authentication logs, etc.) and CANNOT support a conclusion regarding an alleged identity fraud.\nFrom the analysis of this data NO anomaly, discontinuity, or manipulation emerges that could justify a sanction or account suspension. In the GDPR response provided the following were not supplied: relevant logs, technical reports, clear explanations regarding the criteria used, evidence of a human review of the decision. Under these circumstances, the suspension decision appears to be based on an unclear automated assessment, without concrete evidence communicated and without the possibility of a real appeal, although the impact on my activity is significant. In view of the above, I respectfully request of you:\nan explicit clarification of the specific technical reasons that led to the suspension; confirmation of whether the decision was or was not reviewed by a human person; re-examination of my case on the basis that the provided data do not indicate any irregularity. I specify that this request is made in good faith and with the desire to clarify the situation amicably and transparently. Thank you and I await a detailed response. Sincerely, David Alexa","2026-01-13T05:35:56.527Z"],["3804924","PFI-832693","PFI","ivaniuk.habriella@bolt-outsource.eu","Ivaniuk Habriella","!Screenshot_20260113_073315_Bolt Food.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T05:41:57.459Z"],["3804925","LSS-61463","LSS","victor.stratan@bolt.eu","Victor Stratan","[^Bolt Services UK Limited - BizSpace DD.pdf] _(139 kB)_","2026-01-13T05:43:11.253Z"],["3804926","CSDA-294","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review ad-hoc requests once a day. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-13T05:43:44.980Z"],["3804927","CSDA-294","CSDA","delilah.omutanyi@bolt.eu","Delilah Eshiomunda Omutanyi","We need the data to help understand and improve quality issues for Bolt Send\n\n*Priority*\n\nHigh","2026-01-13T05:43:45.878Z"],["3804928","PFI-832678","PFI","jelena.griciva@bolt-outsource.eu","Jelena Griciva","invalid Request Type","2026-01-13T05:45:01.619Z"],["3804929","PFI-832678","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T05:45:05.508Z"],["3804932","PFI-832698","PFI","jelena.griciva@bolt-outsource.eu","Jelena Griciva","!gmail_images20260111_161854.png.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T05:54:24.770Z"],["3804933","PFI-832635","PFI","jelena.griciva@bolt-outsource.eu","Jelena Griciva","invalid Request Type ","2026-01-13T05:54:44.689Z"],["3804935","PFI-832635","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T05:54:48.105Z"],["3804937","DSR-3641","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Tool successfull - Data send out","2026-01-13T05:55:08.396Z"],["3804980","PFI-831489","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:43ac4a3a-cc65-4a9a-8cd3-9e1f27a93024],\n\nThis user has 12 Business profiles active on their profile. This is not legitimate. Especially considering that this user themselves has no other payment on their profile either.\n\nThe reason that they are currently not able to perform further trips, is that this user is related to a bad business account.\n\n*Please do note that all the information brought out above is strictly internal information and should not be passed down to the user by any means*.\n\nMain issue seems to be stimming from the fact that the business(es) are in debt. Due to this highly irregular activity we will not be making an exception for them nor whitelisting them.\n\nPlease do note, that you may only mention debt to them for the businesses that they *own,* if they do not own the business, then you’re not allowed to share information about it.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-13T06:03:22.847Z"],["3804981","PFI-831306","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi,\n\nDevice UID suspensions have been lifted.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-13T06:04:58.606Z"],["3804982","DSR-3643","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Hi [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] , since the comms plug in does not contain the requested information can you confirm that the manually prepared data [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1_cVIKZQU6jT_U_kctBc3ynq23-7Slkwy] is good to go ? 🙏 ","2026-01-13T06:06:16.155Z"],["3804985","PAW-14817","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-13T06:14:14.629Z"],["3804987","PAW-14538","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-13T06:15:07.793Z"],["3804988","LSS-60293","LSS","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","Morning [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] \nThe attorney came back with following:\nGood afternoon\n\nI have received the answer.\n\nSincerely, attorney Yevgeniy Bogdanov","2026-01-13T06:15:49.842Z"],["3804990","PFI-812948","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi [~accountid:712020:634c40ac-eff2-4487-aaa9-f38b92a7bf83]! Thank you! No, these are new subtypes that I’ll be creating → let’s consider this as the starting point for having more granular adjustment subtypes. \n\n\n\nAnd yes, I’ll communicate with the teams accordingly and keep you in the loop 🙂 \n\n\n\n[~accountid:712020:b1a3aa39-56a5-492b-9453-5372da990388] Should be all good to approve now based on our sync 🙂 ","2026-01-13T06:20:51.115Z"],["3804991","DSR-3677","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T06:21:06.899Z"],["3804992","LSS-61394","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:7eb363dc-ca9f-4746-abde-3581e042a507] \n\nThanks for reaching out.\n\nIn this case, we are not required to share detailed fraud findings, internal flags, or specific trips. Under our Terms (including point 4.9) and the DSA, we are only required to provide a *high-level reasoned explanation*, not the underlying detection logic.\n\n*What you can share with the driver:*\n\n* Confirm that the bonus was reversed following post-payment checks.\n* State that the checks identified irregular activity related to campaign participation.\n* Explain that, for *security and fraud-prevention reasons*, no further details can be disclosed.\n* Clarify that the action is *limited to the bonus/adjustment only.*\n* Inform the driver that, *where fraud is confirmed, Bolt may also suspend or restrict the driver’s access to the platform*, in line with the Terms.\n* Offer the *right to appeal/request a review*.\n\n*DSA appeal :* Drivers can submit an appeal under the DSA via Bolt’s complaints and appeal mechanism here:\n[https://bolt.eu/en/legal/dsa/|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/dsa/]\n\nLet me know if you have any further questions.\n\nThank you.\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-13T06:21:22.536Z"],["3804993","HS-28875","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Assigning this ticket to you, because your name is on the Smartsheet 😊 ","2026-01-13T06:21:30.386Z"],["3804995","PFI-832701","PFI","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","!9f964a43-3b5c-4630-9593-7248015414eb.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!cfc07b49-1181-425d-aeac-e37c82bf0364.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!e6b8c3c4-d8ee-4519-8b55-ffe372af88e5.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!ed5c09dc-997a-4880-9514-77ef040f1bdb.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T06:24:18.648Z"],["3804996","PFI-831543","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Yep! This should be a part of their T&C-s as well 🙂 ","2026-01-13T06:24:29.441Z"],["3804997","PAR-3839","PAR","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","[@ahmed.farghaly|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63fc5f040a4a47fb8d20cf92] Hi, client doesn't exist, but why we assign VA to the client which doesn't exist?:meow_thinking:","2026-01-13T06:25:04.736Z"],["3804998","PFI-832701","PFI","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Latest beehive conversation [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/718149291]","2026-01-13T06:25:10.900Z"],["3805002","LSS-61415","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ,\n\ncan you start looking at this when possible and we can maybe have a quick discussion with Xavier on Thuirday should he know more on this topic?\n\nThank you!\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-13T06:30:11.590Z"],["3805003","DSR-3679","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T06:31:05.791Z"],["3805004","WD-22485","WD","janeli.niinemaa@bolt.eu","Janeli Niinemaa","Hey, I checked a few and I think it is because there are some validations that are not met. There are a few different scenarios, but some variation of a critical error is the reason for the ones I checked. Any idea how to solve these issues? For some of them, the employee is already a prior worker. And even if they are not, it does not seem reasonable to ask them to do something now. \n\n!image-20260113-062929.png|width=1352,height=339,alt=\"image-20260113-062929.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-13T06:31:22.385Z"],["3805005","HS-28877","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Waiting for the offer letter.","2026-01-13T06:32:22.968Z"],["3805007","PFI-828779","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:18802c62-447e-4e77-9160-e18cb3f844a8],\n\nWe have not heard back from you in a while and do not see any changes on the profile, therefore, we assume that no assistance is required and the decision to keep user suspended remains.\n\nIf there is still a request for a device UID unblocking, then please complete the process first and then submit a new ticket.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-13T06:35:12.712Z"],["3805009","PFI-832480","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:f9063bf4-7d66-4270-b524-edfd2889c4fe],\n\nThe driver does not have any device UIDs blocked.\n\nLift of the regular hard-block and removal of the scheduled suspension belongs with the Safety team.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-13T06:38:39.629Z"],["3805013","PFI-832531","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:f9063bf4-7d66-4270-b524-edfd2889c4fe],\n\nThe driver does not have a device UID suspended.\n\nRegular Hard-blocks and Scheduled blocks should only be removed by the Safety team.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-13T06:40:04.704Z"],["3805015","DSR-3681","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T06:41:05.958Z"],["3805017","LSS-61464","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^Copy of LT20260113-001 United Motors - Bolt Drive LT.docx.pdf] _(421 kB)_\n\n[^Uittreksel KVK  United Motors B.V.pdf] _(117 kB)_\n\n[^VAT declaration Tax office.pdf] _(609 kB)_","2026-01-13T06:42:37.405Z"],["3805018","LSS-60240","LSS","natakun.punnahataivej@bolt.eu","Natakun Punnahataivej","[~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd]  The heading in Thai was corrected. Please help proceed next. Thank you!","2026-01-13T06:42:49.849Z"],["3805020","PFI-832564","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:dc8e54ad-0402-41f9-ba6e-9f25f8b451bf],\n\nI looked over the orders, and it seems that this issue has occurred mainly due to their GPS issues, creating false-positives in the system.\nYou may manually compensate the driver for the loss of their earnings.\n\nAdditionally, please tell to the driver, that they should either upgrade their device, or upgrade their internet provider, or if they are using a 3rd party application at the same time, then they should stop using it immediately. \nIf these issues keep happening for them, then we will not be able to help them out the next time.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-13T06:45:08.332Z"],["3805023","PFI-832707","PFI","lerato.kekana@bolt.eu","Lerato Mahlako Kekana","[^DOC-20260112-WA0103.PDF]","2026-01-13T06:47:12.095Z"],["3805025","PFI-832687","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:92e1ef86-c3f2-44dc-9919-605e500b8161],\n\nSeems like the user still has a *Hard block* on their profile, meaning that this has not been submitted to the Safety Team for review or that the process is incomplete.\n\nFraud Team does not remove *Hard-Blocks* from the profiles, we only help in removing the *device UID blocks* once the investigation has been finalized and the rest of the blocks have been removed.\nKindly look at the picture below of the suspension (Is blocked) that must be lifted by the Safety team before we can provide assistance from our side:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 08.47.13.png|width=394,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 08.47.13.png\"!\n\nPlease let us know once the profile has been finalized.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you,\nMarten","2026-01-13T06:47:43.735Z"],["3805026","PRODSEC-588","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","[~accountid:642aa1eb7e859baa54f54b06] ii think ISS is a better entrypoint for this.","2026-01-13T06:48:04.690Z"],["3805029","LSS-58367","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Thank you [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] \n\nIs there anything else I can support you with or can this ticket be closed?","2026-01-13T06:49:03.287Z"],["3805030","PFI-832349","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! One option would be for you to just download the invoices manually from here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-courier/fleets/18043?tab=invoices&filter={\"start_date_ts\"%3A1767218400%2C\"end_date_ts\"%3A1768255200%2C\"external_id\"%3A18043%2C\"namespace\"%3Anull%2C\"types\"%3A[\"delivery_fleet\"]%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"limit\"%3A25}&tz=Europe%2FLisbon|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-courier/fleets/18043?tab=invoices&filter=%7B%22start_date_ts%22%3A1767218400%2C%22end_date_ts%22%3A1768255200%2C%22external_id%22%3A18043%2C%22namespace%22%3Anull%2C%22types%22%3A%5B%22delivery_fleet%22%5D%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22limit%22%3A25%7D&tz=Europe%2FLisbon]\n\n\n\nBut the other option is to use this tool described here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6217073146/Bulk+invoice+download+User+Manual+for+CS+Privacy+Tax+etc.|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6217073146/Bulk+invoice+download+User+Manual+for+CS+Privacy+Tax+etc.|smart-link] \n\n\n\nLet me know if you have any questions 🙂 ","2026-01-13T06:50:34.746Z"],["3805032","DSR-3683","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T06:51:06.572Z"],["3805033","PRODSEC-681","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","what Epic does this go under? please assign to a parent [~accountid:712020:db2447cd-56f2-448b-a492-d023fd63690e] \nPlease do the same for linked tasks as well.","2026-01-13T06:51:06.636Z"],["3805036","LSS-61429","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Thank you [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] !","2026-01-13T06:53:38.459Z"],["3805038","LSS-61352","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hey, [~accountid:712020:a975e2d9-679b-4d8a-a063-b831aafacd02]! The addendum has been signed, please see it attached. Feel free to share it with the Partner.\n\n[^2026.01 Bolt Services RO Sesto Com Bolt Food Addendum (signed).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T06:53:57.265Z"],["3805040","WD-21965","WD","dagmar.olesk@bolt.eu","Dagmar Olesk","Hey! Reminding myself to you again 🙈 \nDo you have any update? 🙂 ","2026-01-13T06:57:10.009Z"],["3805045","PFI-832693","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:291ca72f-3929-4484-9fab-a29203ceb5ea],\n\nThis user spammed the everliving hell out of our systems, therefore they got velocity blocked for a while.\n\nAdditionally, this user attempted to use a promo code that they are no longer eligible for.\nYou may advise the user to try again in 24h (14th of January) and without a promo code. If they ask about the promo code, then simply let them know that they are no longer eligible for it.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-13T07:00:00.688Z"],["3805048","PFI-829544","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Ondrej Knoll,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T07:00:16.116Z"],["3805049","PFI-830460","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Angelika Kaleta,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T07:00:16.220Z"],["3805050","PFI-827514","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Barbara Bertalan,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T07:00:16.221Z"],["3805051","PFI-826494","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Yawovi Mawunyo Jean-Baptiste Segbe,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T07:00:16.222Z"],["3805052","PFI-830592","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Jelena Griciva,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T07:00:16.235Z"],["3805053","PFI-803207","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Anna Zaritska,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T07:00:16.398Z"],["3805054","PFI-826496","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Yawovi Mawunyo Jean-Baptiste Segbe,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T07:00:16.447Z"],["3805055","LSS-59990","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear João Nunes,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-13T07:00:25.586Z"],["3805071","PFI-832714","PFI","onyekachi.nwokocha@bolt-outsource.eu","Onyekachi Nwokocha","[^DOC-20260112-WA0103.PDF]","2026-01-13T07:02:17.259Z"],["3805074","LSS-61424","LSS","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","Hi! Nothing needs to be changed in the document. I am just correcting my statement in the description of this request that the start date of the test was last year (9th October). ","2026-01-13T07:03:30.121Z"],["3805075","WFM-9920","WFM","murad.abdullayev@bolt.eu","Murad Mir Abdullayev","Hello!\nWe have a lot of cases with drivers who were blocked by Anneli Tammesson due to missing documents. In Baku, we send blocked drivers to the office for OPS team to handle it, but unfortunately in a lot of regions there are not front offices to do so. I need this access to unblock drivers in regions where there is no front office.","2026-01-13T07:05:25.115Z"],["3805076","DSR-3685","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T07:06:09.932Z"],["3805078","PFI-832457","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-13T07:06:52.971Z"],["3805079","PFI-832460","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-13T07:06:55.656Z"],["3805080","PFI-832527","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-13T07:06:58.265Z"],["3805082","PFI-832601","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-13T07:07:00.937Z"],["3805085","HS-28874","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Hi Ala!\n\nIt is possible to change Your name and for that You would need to updated Your preferred name in Workday. You can find instructions for it here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BILP/pages/4839145484/Update+Personal+Information|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BILP/pages/4839145484/Update+Personal+Information|smart-link] .\n\nPlease let me know if You have any questions.\n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin","2026-01-13T07:08:08.505Z"],["3805086","HS-28877","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","I added the offer to the hire task :heart_hands: ","2026-01-13T07:08:26.792Z"],["3805089","PFI-829702","PFI","oluwaseun.adeyanju@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwaseun Adeyanju","HI *Narmin*, can we have an update about the payment? ","2026-01-13T07:10:41.201Z"],["3805093","PFI-832716","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Asking for a double approval \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768288316176?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768288316176?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-13T07:12:07.775Z"],["3805095","PFI-832202","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This early cashout payout has been successfully processed (state: finished on 2026-01-12). Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; funds should reflect shortly depending on their bank’s processing times. If the partner still cannot see the funds, ask them to contact their bank with the proof for tracing.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:12:49.783Z"],["3805097","PFI-832239","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still in pending status; the last update on 6 Jan shows it was accepted for processing but it has been pending longer than usual. This delay is likely due to a compliance review or technical issues on the provider’s side, and the Partner Payments team is actively monitoring and responding to any checks. Please inform the partner that no action is needed from their side and the funds will be credited once processing completes; if they receive the money before the app updates, the status will refresh on the next business day.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:13:30.892Z"],["3805099","PFI-832267","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected, and the bank/payment provider did not return a specific reason for the failure. Please inform the partner that it will be reprocessed automatically in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try to request it again. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase—feedback is welcome.","2026-01-13T07:13:57.589Z"],["3805100","PFI-832279","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This early cashout has been successfully processed (state: finished on 2026-01-13). Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the courier; if they still don’t see the funds, advise them to contact their bank with this proof for tracing. If you have any other questions, please feel free to reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:14:16.236Z"],["3805101","PFI-832301","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout shows as successfully processed on 2026-01-12. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still cannot see the funds, advise them to contact their bank to trace the transfer. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase—feel free to share any feedback.","2026-01-13T07:14:52.023Z"],["3805102","PFI-832315","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected because the amount exceeded the payment provider’s maximum per-transfer limit. Please inform the partner it will be automatically reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try to request it again (optionally for a smaller amount). P.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-13T07:15:52.185Z"],["3805105","PFI-832316","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. Our logs show this payout has been successfully processed on our side. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner so their bank can trace the incoming transfer if the funds are still not visible. If you have any other questions, please feel free to reply to this ticket. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:16:20.414Z"],["3805106","HS-28875","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Waiting on info about the termination date as it’s different that in the invol which is already signed.","2026-01-13T07:16:23.707Z"],["3805107","PFI-832338","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout is still in pending state, last updated on 08 Dec 2025; the file was accepted by the bank but has not been completed yet. The delay is likely due to an ongoing compliance review or technical issues on the provider’s side, and we are monitoring it and responding to any checks as soon as they come in. Please inform the partner that no action is required on their side right now; we will update the ticket as soon as it moves forward. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-13T07:16:59.440Z"],["3805108","PFI-832701","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe users fine payments have been failing with an error message 05 : Do not honor. This is a generic issuer (customers bank) decline. \n\nThe user can contact their bank to confirm why the transaction is declined and remove any temporary blocks if there are any. \nThe user could also try a different payment method. \n\nUnfortunately, I don’t have access to the tickets that you have provided, but I’ve seen that in many cases the rentals ops team has been able to issue an invoice for the fine payment. That would allow the user to pay off their fine with a bank transfer instead. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T07:17:11.256Z"],["3805109","PFI-832353","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the payment provider, and no specific reason was returned in our system logs. Please inform the partner that it will be reprocessed automatically during the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try requesting it again now. No further action is required from your side at this time.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:17:31.082Z"],["3805110","PFI-832383","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The last payout attempt was rejected, and the payment provider did not share an exact reason. Please inform the partner that it will be reprocessed automatically in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try requesting the cashout again now. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:17:57.170Z"],["3805113","PFI-832384","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the bank because the beneficiary account details are invalid or do not match the bank’s records. Please ask the partner to review and update their payout details (correct account/IBAN, beneficiary name exactly as on the bank account, and ensure the account is active); once corrected, the payout will be reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle, or they can re-request Early Cashout after updating. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:18:17.128Z"],["3805114","PFI-832386","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed with value date 2025-08-04. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still cannot locate the funds, ask them to contact their beneficiary bank using this proof to trace the transfer. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket. P.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-13T07:18:38.716Z"],["3805116","PFI-832691","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 98.08 ZAR on 29/12/2025, 15:20:11UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 29th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T07:19:12.052Z"],["3805118","PFI-832403","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the bank, and the provider returned a generic error without a clear description, so the exact reason was not provided. Please ask the driver to verify and, if needed, correct their payout details (exact account holder name as on the bank account, IBAN/account number, bank/branch information, and that the account is active and can receive transfers). Once the details are correct, the payout will be reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; for Early Cashout they can try submitting a new request. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-13T07:19:39.686Z"],["3805119","DSR-3643","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] – yes, it’s good to go!","2026-01-13T07:19:40.348Z"],["3805120","PFI-832439","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout is currently pending but has been accepted for processing by the bank; since the last update was today, it should reach the partner’s account within 1–2 business days. If it’s still not received after 2 business days, please ask the partner to check with their bank while we continue monitoring. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-13T07:20:07.805Z"],["3805121","PFI-832502","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed on 2026-01-12. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if the account was closed and funds were not credited, ask them to contact their bank to trace or confirm a return. If the bank returns the transfer, it will be handled automatically on our side in the next regular payout cycle. Please note the Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase.","2026-01-13T07:20:41.224Z"],["3805123","PFI-832546","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the bank/payment provider, but they did not share an exact reason. It will be retried automatically in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, please ask the partner to submit a new cashout request. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-13T07:21:05.120Z"],["3805124","PFI-832563","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still pending with payment validation in progress; the last update was on 5 Jan, so this has been pending longer than usual and may be due to a compliance review or a technical delay at the payment provider. Please inform the partner that we are actively monitoring these cases and responding to any compliance requests promptly, and the funds will be processed and arrive once the validation completes. If you have any other questions, please feel free to reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:21:40.300Z"],["3805126","PFI-832567","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed on 2026-01-12; if needed, please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner. The reported 3€ shortfall is a payout amount calculation matter, so please create a Service Desk ticket for the Billing team to investigate. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase.","2026-01-13T07:21:57.641Z"],["3805128","PFI-832568","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout was rejected and returned by the beneficiary bank; no detailed reason was provided beyond the return. Please ask the partner to verify and, if needed, correct their bank/card details with their bank (e.g., closed/blocked account, name/ID mismatch, card not enabled for transfers), and they may also contact their bank to understand the rejection. The amount will be reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; since this was an Early Cashout, the partner can also try to cash out again after confirming their details.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:22:24.685Z"],["3805129","PFI-832677","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nChecked the payment and I can see that everything is fine now. \nThe payment was pending because Bolt was looking to reuse the payment for a new order. \n\nThe booking was reused for this order. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2341222059/9?orderTryId=3010481479|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2341222059/9?orderTryId=3010481479]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-balance/trxHistory/user/12847487/booking/3790818319|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-balance/trxHistory/user/12847487/booking/3790818319]\n\nI can also confirm the pre-authorization has been released from Bolt’s end. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T07:22:42.499Z"],["3805130","PFI-832648","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the bank because the beneficiary account name or the account number does not match what the bank expects. Please ask the partner to double‑check and correct the exact account holder name (spelling/order) and the account number/IBAN in their payout details; once corrected, the payout will be reprocessed in the next regular cycle (for Early Cashout, they can try again after fixing the details). If you have any other questions, please feel free to reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:22:50.644Z"],["3805132","PFI-832654","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still pending; the last log on 2026-01-05 shows it’s under the payment provider’s validation/compliance checks, which explains the delay beyond the usual 2–3 business days. We are monitoring it and responding to any compliance requests so it can be released as soon as possible—please inform the partner that no action is needed from their side and the status will update once processed. If the complaint concerns only a portion of the amount being missing, please open a separate Billing ticket for amount calculation. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:23:24.095Z"],["3805135","PFI-832663","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed on 2026-01-12. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still cannot see the funds, advise them to contact their bank with the proof to trace the credit. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-13T07:23:40.704Z"],["3805139","PFI-832666","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout is in finished status and was successfully processed on 2026-01-12. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if the funds are still not visible, ask them to contact their bank with the proof to trace the transfer. In some cases, the beneficiary bank reflects incoming transfers only by the next business day. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-13T07:24:00.862Z"],["3805141","PFI-832247","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still in pending status (last update on 2026-01-05), which is longer than usual and likely due to ongoing compliance checks or technical issues on the provider’s side. Please inform the partner that we are monitoring this payout and will proceed as soon as the provider releases it—no action is needed from their side at the moment. The status will update automatically once it’s processed.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:24:20.205Z"],["3805143","PFI-832489","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the payment provider, and they did not share a specific reason. Please inform the partner that it will be reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try requesting it again. To reduce the chance of another failure, ask the partner to double-check that their beneficiary details (name, IBAN/account number, bank) are correct and up to date. If you have any other questions, please feel free to reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-13T07:24:33.181Z"],["3805146","PFI-832658","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is currently in pending status and was just created today, so it’s still processing and should appear on the beneficiary’s bank account within 1–2 business days. No action is required from your side right now; if it still hasn’t arrived after this timeframe, please reply to this ticket for further checks. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-13T07:24:53.406Z"],["3805150","CCM-22271","CCM","victoria.petrov@bolt.eu","Victoria Petrov","[^Copy of New TalentLMS Training Request Form.xlsx]","2026-01-13T07:25:16.673Z"],["3805173","SCM-978","SCM","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:5eb363355862510b794e3507] The issues caused by fixing the controller on the controller bracket, then connecting the connectors in the diagonal. Also, the temperature is low and cables are rather stiffer, which might worsen the situation. \n\nNow, they connect outside the frame then fix it on the controller bracket. After they switch to this, there are only 7 cases. \n\nOne suggestion from the supplier is to switch the connectors on the controller to female ones. So that we don’t break controllers, if needed, we can switch the cables if it is damaged. \n\nAnother option is to make the walls around the connectors higher so that other side of the connector can be aligned a bit better. \n\nFYI. [~accountid:624b3bdf8678e900705d9004] ","2026-01-13T07:28:00.118Z"],["3805174","RDS-1406","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:5ccc34a5326cf40e4549d40d] this would be completely unsurprising to me. And to be clear, this I don’t think this is a burning priority — just a nice quality improvement that would close feature gaps with comp.[~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] let’s build it in 2029 😅","2026-01-13T07:28:00.435Z"],["3805177","WEBSD-1471","WEBSD","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","[^Campaign Terms and Conditions - Dream Ride Online Campaign.pdf]","2026-01-13T07:28:09.052Z"],["3805181","PFI-832665","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nHere is the payment for 3.10 AZN. It failed because the user did not have sufficient funds on their card. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4025087253|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4025087253]\n\nPlease note since the authorization failed the order was not generated hence why you are seeing an error. \nI can confirm that it was related to a ride hailing order and the user was present when it was created. Unfortunately, I would not be able to see any further details about this. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T07:28:35.725Z"],["3805183","WDFT-3510","WDFT","kristiine.murd@bolt.eu","Kristiine Murd","[~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] please mark this entity as Region 3 entity","2026-01-13T07:28:38.243Z"],["3805185","PFI-832718","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:838d72ea-8423-46b8-a2f6-baeedd2bed2f],\n\nFor us to make decisions regarding this, then we would need more information and examples, especially examples.\nProvide us with at least 3-5 examples cases of this happening, and then we can take a look at the thresholds and happenings and if there is room for adjustments.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you,\nMarten","2026-01-13T07:28:52.569Z"],["3805188","WDFT-3535","WDFT","kristiine.murd@bolt.eu","Kristiine Murd","Please add this entity in ‘Region 3’","2026-01-13T07:29:09.891Z"],["3805192","LSS-60240","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Thank you [~accountid:712020:4f73f350-0bf3-4887-9902-fd54848247b3] !\n\nI’ve forwarded this to the web team for uploading. I cc’d you in the ticket, so that you would also have the visibility of the process.\n\nPlease let me know in case of any further questions.","2026-01-13T07:29:39.967Z"],["3805201","HS-28464","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:4888de6c-ac03-4e7d-85c8-91ac19352650],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-13T07:30:17.832Z"],["3805202","HS-28256","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-13T07:30:18.145Z"],["3805203","HS-28461","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:4888de6c-ac03-4e7d-85c8-91ac19352650],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-13T07:30:18.156Z"],["3805204","HS-28463","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:4888de6c-ac03-4e7d-85c8-91ac19352650],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-13T07:30:18.216Z"],["3805205","HS-28498","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:a335a5ec-2969-45be-8f2f-6561cf7e7d62],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-13T07:30:18.232Z"],["3805206","HS-28353","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:9d22087b-9bd3-42c9-944c-2112fcfa004e],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-13T07:30:18.290Z"],["3805207","HS-28370","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:4888de6c-ac03-4e7d-85c8-91ac19352650],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-13T07:30:18.477Z"],["3805208","HS-28494","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-13T07:30:18.503Z"],["3805209","HS-28358","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:4888de6c-ac03-4e7d-85c8-91ac19352650],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-13T07:30:18.729Z"],["3805210","HS-28501","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:9d22087b-9bd3-42c9-944c-2112fcfa004e],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-13T07:30:19.237Z"],["3805211","HS-28377","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:4888de6c-ac03-4e7d-85c8-91ac19352650],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-13T07:30:19.355Z"],["3805213","DSR-3085","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Thank you [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048]. I’ve already provided the data to the user.","2026-01-13T07:30:36.195Z"],["3805216","PFI-832316","PFI","daniele.fondjeutagouang@bolt.eu","Daniele Fondjeu Tagouang","Hi, the account information does not match, with the only difference being in the last two digits of the account number. The account details were updated on our end on [23 Nov 2025 at 08:45:57.|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8265096?tab=changeLogs&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_time%22%3A1762027200%7D%7D] Please advise.","2026-01-13T07:30:48.904Z"],["3805218","PFI-810851","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hello! I check his balance page and indeed seems the amount paid is right. \t\r\n69.76 EUR. You can raise a ticket to Billing team stating the difference on balance by what partner sees x what we see and they will be able to explain you better.","2026-01-13T07:31:02.191Z"],["3805227","HS-28664","HS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Thank you for the answer, but what is the logic behind it?\n\nIs there more context to this?\n\nI would really appreciate more details about this topic 🙂","2026-01-13T07:32:24.627Z"],["3805229","PFI-832414","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:c13b916c-640b-40f4-81ae-0f9d3a6a1ce7],\n\nThis question would be better suited for the Campaigns team.\n\nPerhaps it would be possible to reach out to them via Slack in #campaigns-support.\nThe Fraud team does not have region locks so to speak.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-13T07:32:37.215Z"],["3805234","DBRE-7638","DBRE","andrei.fedorov@bolt.eu","Andrei Fedorov","It’s not really handled, but rather set to default.\n\nT*hose values are conservative for local NVMe*. On *d-type EC2 instance-store NVMe, *1500 / 2000 is usually too low* and can cause InnoDB to fall behind on flushing even though the disk has plenty of headroom.\n\nBelow is the *proper way to think about and set* {{innodb_io_capacity}} */* {{innodb_io_capacity_max}} *for your setup (MySQL 5.7, Linux, local NVMe).*\n\n----\n\nh2. What these variables actually control (important distinction)\n\n* {{innodb_io_capacity}}\nThe _target_ rate (IOPS) InnoDB tries to use for background work:\n** flushing dirty pages\n** merging change buffer\n** read-ahead activity\n* {{innodb_io_capacity_max}}\nA _burst ceiling_ InnoDB may use when it is under pressure (checkpoint age high, many dirty pages, etc.).\n\nThey do *not* cap foreground query I/O — only background maintenance.\n\n----\n\nh2. Why the defaults are usually wrong for NVMe\n\nThe defaults were chosen for *rotational disks* era systems.\n\nOn local NVMe:\n\n* the disk can sustain *tens of thousands of IOPS*\n* InnoDB with {{1500}} IOPS may:\n** let dirty pages accumulate\n** delay checkpointing\n** cause sudden flush storms later (bad p99 latency)\n\nThis is one of the _most common_ causes of “InnoDB flushing lag” on fast disks.\n\n----\n\nh2. How to set them correctly (practical, safe method)\n\nh3. Step 1: Determine _safe_ write IOPS\n\nFrom PMM *Disk Details*:\n\n* Look at *avg write IOPS* and *avg await latency* under peak load\n* Find a write IOPS level where:\n** latency stays low and stable\n** disk util is well below saturation\n\nFor _d-type NVMe this is often_ *20k–50k+ IOPS*, but don’t guess — measure.\n\n----\n\nh3. Step 2: Pick values (good starting points)\n\nFor your environment, *these are sane starting values*:\n\n{noformat}innodb_io_capacity      = 10000\ninnodb_io_capacity_max  = 20000\n{noformat}\n\nWhy:\n\n* {{io_capacity}} ≈ 30–50% of sustainable write IOPS\n* {{io_capacity_max}} ≈ 2× {{io_capacity}}\n\nThis gives InnoDB enough room to keep up *without aggressive bursts*.\n\n----\n\nh2. How to validate in PMM\n\nAfter changing (these are *dynamic*, no restart):\n\nWatch these panels:\n\n* *InnoDB Dirty Pages %*\n* *InnoDB Checkpoint Age*\n* *InnoDB Pending IO*\n* *Disk write latency (await)*\n\n*Good signs:*\n\n* Dirty pages stop climbing during load\n* Checkpoint age stabilizes\n* Pending writes drop faster\n* Disk latency remains flat\n\n*Bad signs (too high):*\n\n* write latency spikes\n* OS shows high queue depth with rising await\n\nIf bad → reduce {{io_capacity_max}}, not the base value first.\n\n----\n\nh2. Important interaction with io_threads\n\nThis is key:\n\n{quote}On Linux + NVMe, {{innodb_io_capacity}} *almost always matters more than* {{innodb_write_io_threads}}.{quote}\n\nIf flushing falls behind:\n\n* raise {{innodb_io_capacity}}\n* _then_ consider write I/O threads *only if pending writes persist*\n\n----\n\nh2. TL;DR recommendation for your setup\n\n* Keep\n{{innodb_read_io_threads = 4–8}}\n{{innodb_write_io_threads = 4–8}}\n* Suggested to change *now (make sure those values align with the actual disk capacity, this is just an example)*:\n{noformat}innodb_io_capacity     = 10000\ninnodb_io_capacity_max = 20000\n{noformat}\n* Validate in PMM over a real peak","2026-01-13T07:33:08.875Z"],["3805242","PFI-828655","PFI","sabina.onomiruren@bolt-outsource.eu","Sabina Onomiruren","Hello team,\n\nAny update on this?","2026-01-13T07:34:05.875Z"],["3805246","LSS-60589","LSS","himanshu.narvekar@bolt.eu","Himanshu Narvekar","For scenario 1- I presume we need to wait for what the bank says, and if they will help us recover the money from the incorrect account where we transferred the money to. I am not sure what remedies are available to us if this fails - [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742]. I suppose we can’t claim these monies from TP?\n\nFor Scenario 2 - [~accountid:712020:f4038db4-c597-4af7-9604-402e9f17edd5] was this in France, or was this from some other market? When did this incident occur? If we are working on a repayment plan from the wrong party, then I don’t think we can claim this from TP. If repayment is not made, then surely we need to make a claim on TP. \n\n","2026-01-13T07:34:37.450Z"],["3805249","LSS-61058","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you very much [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] for the manual change ! \n\nWe have received complaints from our previous landlord because they were still receiving a lot of mail and parcels since we moved more than a year ago. Apparently, individuals would get the address from this page. \n\nI can’t see the update on the page yet, but I suppose it takes a bit of time to go live. You can close this ticket thank you !","2026-01-13T07:35:03.941Z"],["3805251","DBRE-7638","DBRE","andrei.fedorov@bolt.eu","Andrei Fedorov","Few more comments (some of those settings are already in place):\nRaising {{innodb_io_capacity}} is usually safe by itself, but a few *neighboring InnoDB knobs* can become the next limiter (or can help you avoid side-effects like flush bursts or extra CPU).\n\nHere’s what’s most commonly worth checking on *MySQL 5.7 + Linux + local NVMe*:\n\nh2. 1) Keep {{innodb_io_capacity_max}} in sync\n\nIf {{innodb_io_capacity}} goes up but {{innodb_io_capacity_max}} stays low, InnoDB can’t “catch up” when it’s behind.\n\n* Rule of thumb: {{innodb_io_capacity_max}} ≈ *2×* {{innodb_io_capacity}} (sometimes 3× if you want more burst).\n\nh2. 2) Disable “neighbor flushing” on SSD/NVMe\n\nOn spinning disks, InnoDB tried to flush adjacent pages together. On NVMe this is usually wasted work and can increase write amplification.\n\n* Set: {{innodb_flush_neighbors = 0}}\n\nh2. 3) Dirty page targets (controls flush pressure and burstiness)\n\nThese influence _when_ InnoDB starts pushing harder.\n\n* {{innodb_max_dirty_pages_pct}} (upper bound for dirty pages)\n* {{innodb_max_dirty_pages_pct_lwm}} (low-water mark where it starts being more proactive)\n\nIf you raise {{io_capacity}} and still see dirty pages drifting up and then sudden aggressive flushing, consider:\n\n* lowering {{innodb_max_dirty_pages_pct}} a bit, and/or\n* setting a sensible {{..._lwm}} so flushing ramps earlier and smoother.\n\nh2. 4) Page cleaner parallelism (can cap flushing throughput)\n\nIf flushing can’t keep up even with higher {{io_capacity}}, {{innodb_page_cleaners}} may be too low for your buffer pool size / write rate.\n\n* In 5.7 it defaults to a small number (often 4).\n* If you have a *large buffer pool* and heavy writes, try increasing (e.g., *4 → 8*), and watch CPU + “pending writes”.\n\nh2. 5) Redo log size (often the real reason you see flush pain)\n\nIf redo logs are small, MySQL checkpoints frequently and flushing gets spiky regardless of {{io_capacity}}.\n\nCheck:\n\n* {{innodb_log_file_size}}\n* {{innodb_log_files_in_group}}\n\nLarger redo logs often smooth write workloads and reduce emergency flushing. (Changing log file size requires careful procedure + restart.)\n\nh2. 6) {{innodb_lru_scan_depth}} (CPU cost of background scanning)\n\nHigher flushing capacity can increase background scanning work. If you see CPU jump after raising {{io_capacity}}, {{innodb_lru_scan_depth}} may be too high.\n\n* If CPU becomes an issue, reduce gradually (don’t slam it down).\n\nh2. 7) If you _still_ see backlog: only then look at I/O threads\n\nAfter {{io_capacity}} / page cleaners / dirty page behavior are sane:\n\n* {{innodb_write_io_threads}} (and sometimes {{innodb_read_io_threads}}) can be nudged up (e.g., 4→8).\nOn Linux with native AIO, this is often less impactful than the items above.\n\n----\n\nh3. A practical “raise io_capacity” checklist\n\nAfter you raise it, watch in PMM:\n\n* Dirty pages %\n* Checkpoint age / log checkpointing\n* Pending writes / pending fsync\n* Disk write latency (await) and queue depth\n* mysqld CPU (system + user)","2026-01-13T07:36:29.219Z"],["3805252","PFI-832666","PFI","tan.do@bolt-outsource.eu","Tan Dung Do","Could you please provide the transaction number for this payout? I need it to share with the driver.","2026-01-13T07:36:32.697Z"],["3805253","DRAG101-426","DRAG101","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","Waiting for new front forks to continue testing - ETA {{2026-01-20}} (new front fork)\n\nTesting can continue in February after the D3 production is finished because of our resources","2026-01-13T07:36:42.367Z"],["3805255","DBRE-7638","DBRE","andrei.fedorov@bolt.eu","Andrei Fedorov","[~accountid:712020:0c5038f7-7f89-46d8-b2ea-9f10c0c3bcc6] please consider these notes for your future activities\ncc: [~accountid:712020:0ef8f6fe-4761-4ff2-a1b7-74961ff962b3] ","2026-01-13T07:36:59.886Z"],["3805256","LSS-61394","LSS","alexia.matsangou@bolt.eu","Alexia Matsangou","Thank you very much!","2026-01-13T07:37:18.440Z"],["3805257","WFM-9962","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey [~accountid:712020:d104a676-2567-4f06-9d5a-6d6965edaeb9] ,\n\nThank you for reaching out.\n\nThe RTM Dashboard view access will be granted to [~accountid:712020:93c5213c-e7c3-4813-b854-77e885560eb1] with *Outsource CS - Team Lead (ID: 240201) role,* however, I wanted to ask if you need only 1 additional role, or all roles mirroring your roles?\n \n Can you share necessary links, KB articles to confirm that this is needed?\nLooking forward to your response,\n\nKamran\n","2026-01-13T07:37:28.767Z"],["3805259","LSS-61356","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","[~accountid:712020:176612de-64ab-442f-84ee-ed63bbac2b50] please send signed document to [+*contracts@bolt.eu*+|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] with the ticket number when it will be signed by both parties. Thanks!","2026-01-13T07:37:49.094Z"],["3805263","WFM-9961","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","This is unclear. Can you be more specific with the queues to assign and if they’re primary/secondary?","2026-01-13T07:39:03.558Z"],["3805266","FC-912","FC","katti.raudberg@bolt.eu","Katti Raudberg","Provided by Taras","2026-01-13T07:39:56.573Z"],["3805274","PFI-832727","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","!messageImage_1767947135429.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T07:41:41.453Z"],["3805275","PFI-832727","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T07:41:43.723Z"],["3805276","LSS-61356","LSS","aire.vaigu@bolt.eu","Aire Vaigu","Contract sent, thank you for your help! ","2026-01-13T07:42:17.728Z"],["3805277","PFI-832664","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI’m a bit confused about which payment are you referring to. The payment the user is asking about belongs to a different user. \n\n[Profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/9582140] that has been linked. \n[Profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/130797511] that made the payment. \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for EUR 3.50 on Dec 17, 2025, 15:22:35 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 15265675351002860922218 to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 17th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n\n[^Refund_Letter_NJ3STFFQ6KWGX9Q9_PWK2NSKKS4HC6JX3.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten\n\n\n","2026-01-13T07:43:18.549Z"],["3805278","PFI-832646","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T07:43:43.024Z"],["3805279","HS-28493","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Confirming entity","2026-01-13T07:43:48.095Z"],["3805280","LSS-59845","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nPlease find the redlines from Sentry attached.\n\nThey have also shared the following comment:\n\n{quote}I saw a comment in the MSA regarding SLA''s. What's good to know here is that:\n\n* *Slack + dedicated engineer* is centred around active engagement between Bolt devs and the Sentry team, and having a dedicated space to drop ad-hoc questions / requests for Bolt only.\n* *SLAs on the other hand are contractual guarantees*. And those are tied to Premium Customer Success (PCSS) which is a paid support SKU starting at $15,000/year.{quote}\n\nThanks!\n\n[^Bolt-Sentry MSA 2026 01 09 (Sentry Redlines).docx]\n\n","2026-01-13T07:44:29.747Z"],["3805284","HWMISC-776","HWMISC","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e] Thank you for pushing to get the prices!\n\n\nThe front brake is 2x cheaper than what we have purchased from OKAI before. and it is the already upgraded version.\n\nRear is also ~2.5RMB cheaper than we buy today (from YM I believe. In WD the supplier is marked as LongYue).","2026-01-13T07:45:34.660Z"],["3805285","LSS-61465","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T07:46:07.206Z"],["3805289","DSR-3653","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Tier 2 explained the situation to the driver. Everything is compensated to him, except for December yet, but he was informed on the comp amount.\n\nCurrently, we are waiting for Local OPS to open the old driver’s account so he could check for his old data.\n\nKeeping an eye on it, but might not need any support from the CSPC side afterall.\n\n*Full Tier 2 response:*\n\nHey team! This guarantee is for independant drivers in France :\n* Each hour should be paid 30€ at least (compensated by the end of the month based on the average revenue and hour worked -calculations are seen on this [sheet|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1eLvn1eJ8EIKQXSTbMthRv4xWaKufBSoQrqAbaB4UySI/edit?gid=560827052#gid=560827052], but it is not updated since november)\n* Each kilometer should be paid 1€, this is calculated directly on the order\n* Each order should be minimum 9€\nThis is based on this [agreement|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Accord-revenu-minimal-horaire-et-euro-kilometrique-19-Decembre-2023.pdf].\nDriver is now under a fleet, but was independant until the 06/01/2026 under id [5760201|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/5760201?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn].\nSearching this ID in the above sheet shows a result of 0€ compensation in november for example, as RPH was 32.78€ (so above 30€ per hour). Same goes for October, and in September for example RPH was 27.99€, so we compensated 29.4€ as shown in the last column. It's been paid [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records/26874495472] on the 31/10.\nWe do not have the data for December, this whole process is managed by Local Ops.\nDo you have an efficient way to compile the data the driver is asking for?\n* time spent during orders\n* time spent driving to pick up points\nFrom January to December 2025, separated by month.\nIf not, please send back and I'll try to prepare the data I can see from the sheet and send back for approval. Thanks!","2026-01-13T07:47:29.460Z"],["3805291","PFI-832734","PFI","tuukka.tammela@bolt.eu","Tuukka Tammela","!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 9.47.44.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T07:47:55.599Z"],["3805292","WDFT-3535","WDFT","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hi [~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044] , company is under Region 3, Polish entities\n\n!image-20260113-074759.png|width=779,alt=\"image-20260113-074759.png\"!","2026-01-13T07:48:07.003Z"],["3805293","CCM-22272","CCM","ilia.moroz@bolt-outsource.eu","Ilia Moroz","[^TalentLMS import sheet (3).xlsx]","2026-01-13T07:48:18.442Z"],["3805297","LSS-61124","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] please support with signing ","2026-01-13T07:49:07.343Z"],["3805298","LSS-61288","LSS","stephanie.oreoluwa@bolt.eu","Stephanie Oreoluwa","[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] Please confirm that contract is good to proceed? Please treat as urgent.","2026-01-13T07:49:38.648Z"],["3805299","LSS-52184","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:5f896ba356eec000768527be] can you please ask the counterparty to send us updated documents with  incorporated changes that has been agreed as per this ticket + InfoSec requested wording as per Viktoriia comment so we have current versions of the documents we can review and sign, if everything will be good?\n\nThanks!","2026-01-13T07:49:48.200Z"],["3805301","PFI-832736","PFI","oluwaferanmi.arogundade@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwaferanmi Arogundade","!JPEG_1767939537516_5586329705473875887.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T07:51:22.018Z"],["3805302","RS-1943","RS","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","[^ERTZAINTZA( BASQUE AUTONOMOUS POLICE) REQUEST- 589A2503890-BOLT .pdf (2).pdf] _(234 kB)_","2026-01-13T07:51:37.329Z"],["3805306","CCM-22273","CCM","alina.matviyuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Alina Matviyuk","[^training request.xlsx]","2026-01-13T07:52:25.433Z"],["3805308","WFM-9964","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","[req|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571686] raised ","2026-01-13T07:53:24.588Z"],["3805313","CCM-22273","CCM","alina.matviyuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Alina Matviyuk","Sorry, I added the wrong email :smiling_face_with_tear: . Here is the correct one.\n\n\n\n|[yurii.kotsaba@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:yurii.kotsaba@bolt-outsource.eu]|\n|[rostyslav.kukhar@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:rostyslav.kukhar@bolt-outsource.eu]|\n|[alina.kalinicheva@bolt.eu|mailto:alina.kalinicheva@bolt.eu]|\n|[mykyta.kasatkin@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:mykyta.kasatkin@bolt-outsource.eu]|\n|[kateryna.khryptiievska@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:kateryna.khryptiievska@bolt-outsource.eu]|\n\n","2026-01-13T07:54:45.528Z"],["3805314","DRX-27635","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.126.0 (1505) Firebase build on Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\n(/) The “Earnings island price visibility toggled” event is created when the driver blurs the earnings amount (value = false)\n(/) The “Earnings island price visibility toggled” event is created when the driver unblurs the earnings amount (value = true)\n(/) The “Earnings island expanded” event is created when the driver taps on the Earnings FAB\n\n(/) The “Earnings island collapsed” event is created when the driver closes the Earnings Island modal (when taping on the Earnings Island modal or outside the modal, duration value is added in milliseconds)\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.56.45.png|width=659,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-08 at 11.56.45.png\"!\n\n\n","2026-01-13T07:55:36.356Z"],["3805317","DSR-3687","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T07:56:06.194Z"],["3805321","G3IOT-701","G3IOT","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Quectel has sent DFOTA files. Need to prepare NA test setup. Contacted [~accountid:712020:d004c27c-42e6-4c71-83ea-39daf55c5a95] for help","2026-01-13T07:56:47.914Z"],["3805323","DRX-27946","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27635 has been resolved","2026-01-13T07:57:24.785Z"],["3805324","PFI-830835","PFI","kosisochukwu.ochuaka@bolt-outsource.eu","Kosisochukwu Ochuaka","Hello Team, Please, is there an update on the double payment","2026-01-13T07:57:46.508Z"],["3805329","LSS-61140","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:cf457436-e17c-4575-8d48-f2b9135ccc82], have you received any updates from the ARPE? \n\nYou have confirmed end of last week, that you have been able to negotiate an extension to Wednesday 14th - are we ready to sign and send the pseudonymised data? \n\nThank you","2026-01-13T07:58:45.669Z"],["3805331","LSS-60007","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:61f3e7cd632452006b8c120b] did you still need support on this ticket or can we close it? \n\nThank you !","2026-01-13T07:59:20.079Z"],["3805332","DO-5786","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Hey [~accountid:62a9856f188d08006fe1ffa6] 👋 \n\nYou should already have the access in [https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/sql/editor?o=3598988355446810|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/sql/editor?o=3598988355446810].\n\nI suppose you chose the wrong workspace/ misconfig the all-purpose cluster. If you misconfigure the all-purpose cluster, please follow this guide [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/6021087382/Data+Platform+Authorisation#Databricks|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/6021087382/Data+Platform+Authorisation#Databricks|smart-link]  \n","2026-01-13T07:59:41.406Z"],["3805333","LSS-60866","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Thank you [~accountid:712020:139dd7b4-1222-4d14-851c-785d158c5519] , all good. \n\nPlease provide name and email of the counterparty signatory and I will forward this for signing.","2026-01-13T07:59:44.915Z"],["3805335","LSS-61467","LSS","luke.grima@bolt.eu","Luke Grima","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac], good morning!\n\nIs this something we can discuss during our call later today, please? 🙏 ","2026-01-13T07:59:59.906Z"],["3805338","LSS-61109","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] please could you confirm if it is possible to send a reminder or set up recurring reminders to get the partner to sign? \n\nThank you !","2026-01-13T08:00:51.697Z"],["3805340","CRC-2328","CRC","sander.randorg@bolt.eu","Sander Randorg","[update] Now have cross-department agreement that we are not blocked by EMI for at least the next 1-2 months, pushing ahead with the milestone in its original form. Discussions regarding financial events, object design, invoicing logic etc happening this week. Aiming to deliver by end of Q1.","2026-01-13T08:01:33.122Z"],["3805341","LSS-61404","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","HI [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a], \n\nPlease find attached new feedback from the supplier [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S1QIiehiuJYhSeVCJJQfYYGhdsu3sOx1/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S1QIiehiuJYhSeVCJJQfYYGhdsu3sOx1/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:01:57.520Z"],["3805342","DSR-3643","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","File sent to the user","2026-01-13T08:02:15.815Z"],["3805343","HS-28848","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Contract went for a review. ","2026-01-13T08:02:16.903Z"],["3805344","LSS-60142","LSS","karolis.simkus@bolt.eu","Karolis Šimkus","[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] - it’s one off action. We give them promo codes - and they distribute them for newly registered people in Vilnius.\n\nThe promo codes we are giving:\n\n* Bolt Drive - 7 euros off from your first ride.\n* Ride-Hailing - 50% off (5 euros cap) for your first 2 rides.\n* Scooters - 30% off (2 euros cap) for your two rides.\n\nCodes are valid 90 days after the usage.\n\nYou can activate them until the end of the September.\n\nMunicipality will distribute them for every newly registered person in Vilnius during the campaign period (±9.5k people) together with all of the other campaign partners listed in this landing page - [https://vilnius.lt/tapkvilnieciu|https://vilnius.lt/tapkvilnieciu|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:02:52.330Z"],["3805345","DSR-3689","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T08:02:53.116Z"],["3805346","LSS-61467","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T08:02:53.831Z"],["3805347","HS-28877","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Task sent to Global Mobility.","2026-01-13T08:02:54.836Z"],["3805349","FX-3616","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768291377428519]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3616] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T08:03:33.494Z"],["3805353","LSS-61440","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, will cancel the ticket. Thanks!","2026-01-13T08:04:19.953Z"],["3805354","LSS-61438","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] forwarding this to you as it is related to phone booth rental for the UK office.","2026-01-13T08:04:23.726Z"],["3805358","LSS-61419","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached!\n\n[^Agreement + Doc A - E-Scooter Fines_Bolt Support Services MT Ltd_Local Enforcement System Agency (LESA)_12.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T08:05:21.142Z"],["3805360","PFI-832633","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 22.05 ZAR on 06/12/2025, 15:50:27UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 6th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T08:05:25.147Z"],["3805361","LSS-59165","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:5dbbe92cb87a410db33f7faa], yes, please do that so we can consider all information available.","2026-01-13T08:05:31.306Z"],["3805365","LSS-61221","LSS","mercynorah.nyiti@bolt.eu","Mercynorah Nyiti","Hello [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] the documents are not stamped with Bolt OU stamp, please assist to stamp them. ","2026-01-13T08:07:01.429Z"],["3805366","LSS-61109","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] - The system has an automated re-send function so it sends the contract once a day automatically.","2026-01-13T08:07:10.848Z"],["3805367","LSS-59845","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] [~accountid:5d7b698997d8980d8ead4b01] \n\nGreat news, Sentry accepted all our offers [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1g6sKwHOpR0dBmeEIDvEu5k8ZEEIsMARm/edit#heading=h.3znysh7|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1g6sKwHOpR0dBmeEIDvEu5k8ZEEIsMARm/edit#heading=h.3znysh7|smart-link] \n\nLast step: We added infosec code as annex which Sentry already accepted but they will add some changes. \n\n[~accountid:5d7b698997d8980d8ead4b01] [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] I asked if we can limit data processing to EU only and Sentry replied that it can be configured during first use of the software. \n\n[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] please share doc with Sentry ","2026-01-13T08:07:12.130Z"],["3805368","LSS-61109","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/339563?blocked=true&returnTo=%2Fcontracts%2Fv2%3FCONTRACTSV3_SEARCH%3DeyJxdWVyeSI6W3siZmllbGROYW1lIjoicXVlcnkiLCJ2YWx1ZSI6IkxhIHNvY2nDqXTDqSBQYXJpcyBGbGVldCBEcml2ZSBMdXgiLCJvcGVyYXRvciI6ImVxIn1dfQ%253D%253D%26clusterId%3DEU%26workspaceId%3D31839&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/339563?blocked=true&returnTo=%2Fcontracts%2Fv2%3FCONTRACTSV3_SEARCH%3DeyJxdWVyeSI6W3siZmllbGROYW1lIjoicXVlcnkiLCJ2YWx1ZSI6IkxhIHNvY2nDqXTDqSBQYXJpcyBGbGVldCBEcml2ZSBMdXgiLCJvcGVyYXRvciI6ImVxIn1dfQ%253D%253D%26clusterId%3DEU%26workspaceId%3D31839&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:07:19.359Z"],["3805369","SUPX-2316","SUPX","artem.kudlaienko@bolt.eu","Artem Kudlaienko","!image-20260113-080703.png|width=785,alt=\"image-20260113-080703.png\"!\n\nIssue mitigated, alert thresholds restored","2026-01-13T08:07:35.393Z"],["3805372","BDB-1521","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] \nPlease let me know if copy works for you and I’ll create the visuals. \nThank you!","2026-01-13T08:07:51.036Z"],["3805373","CRC-2105","CRC","sander.randorg@bolt.eu","Sander Randorg","[update] Still in the long-tail end of reconciling data, FDWH doing checks and may have identified an issue with cross border service fees and region assignments. Depending on the severity to decide this week if we accept the new data and close the MS or we go in for the fixx.","2026-01-13T08:08:02.834Z"],["3805374","DRX-27797","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.126.0 (1505) Firebase build on Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\n||*Screenshot*||FF must be enabled: \"prod_is_earnings_island_enabled\": true||\n|!Screenshot_20260113-095913.png|width=147,alt=\"Screenshot_20260113-095913.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 10.06.47.png|width=312,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 10.06.47.png\"!|","2026-01-13T08:08:12.966Z"],["3805377","LSS-61292","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Hi [~accountid:60feb11575ad960069b6163f] have you had time to check over the open parts from the comments. First round comments you already answered, but some are still open - e.g. pricing related. \n\nLiisa","2026-01-13T08:08:55.281Z"],["3805378","CRC-1901","CRC","romet.varts@bolt.eu","Romet Varts","[update] Test for last update","2026-01-13T08:08:55.546Z"],["3805379","PFI-832606","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T08:09:27.367Z"],["3805380","PFI-832470","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, two different Business Accounts are attached; one - Rosetti; other - Konga Pay. Please, specify what is the question/problem from Billing perspective and I can help; Please, note that we don’t have local market context.","2026-01-13T08:09:32.956Z"],["3805381","PFI-832471","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, what is the reason the ticket to the Business Billing SD is created?","2026-01-13T08:10:36.689Z"],["3805382","WD-22517","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:60ab52d6411c2200681a75e4]  the files are loaded now. Please review. \n\n!image-20260112-212726.png|width=853,alt=\"image-20260112-212726.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-13T08:11:06.200Z"],["3805384","LSS-61404","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:46ca1bd4-650e-4217-b42f-78a9deb502a3] NDA is ready to be signed \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S1QIiehiuJYhSeVCJJQfYYGhdsu3sOx1/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S1QIiehiuJYhSeVCJJQfYYGhdsu3sOx1/edit|smart-link] \n\nIf all agreed please ask them to send the agreement to [+ahto.kink@bolt.eu+|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu] and cc [+signing@bolt.eu+|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] (we will not be able to find the request without putting this email in cc)\n\nOr we can initiate signing, for this we need email, full name, title of signing person ","2026-01-13T08:11:43.354Z"],["3805386","LSS-57150","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] - As this is for Slovakia then I have sent it out for signing via SpotDraft instead.","2026-01-13T08:11:52.471Z"],["3805387","FDBT-4785","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_delivery fails on 2026-01-12 07:00:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/l