4417115279|smart-link] \n* PR that originally was supposed to solve this issue: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/143466|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/143466|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:14:33.250Z"],["3805417","DBRE-8688","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Done","2026-01-13T08:14:36.237Z"],["3805418","LSS-60808","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] can we also ask for confirmation from business to proceed with signing ? ","2026-01-13T08:14:46.965Z"],["3805419","DLSP-2006","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","released","2026-01-13T08:14:50.622Z"],["3805420","HS-28006","HS","evgenia.moronova@bolt.eu","Evgenia Moronova","Hi ladies,\n\nPlease find attached Confirmation of Income and ELDP  for SK December leaver Tomáš Gally E011895 (12.12.2025).\n\nBest Regards,\n\nEvgenia\n\n[^E011895 Gally Tomáš ELDP.pdf]\n[^E011895 Gally Tomáš PoZP.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T08:14:52.813Z"],["3805421","DLSP-1952","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","released","2026-01-13T08:14:58.894Z"],["3805424","CMO-12994","CMO","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","Summary draft\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/14DmUBgD96aXQfuGammK9asplytl_T-JHgKWFsW-2rb0/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/14DmUBgD96aXQfuGammK9asplytl_T-JHgKWFsW-2rb0/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] \n\nsupporting visuals \n\n\n\n[https://www.figma.com/design/r4QkcTOZsbBUAhkBqPnFYM/Personal-space--Taisiia?node-id=262-18&t=JcdUW4z4hRlNelPI-0|https://www.figma.com/design/r4QkcTOZsbBUAhkBqPnFYM/Personal-space--Taisiia?node-id=262-18&t=JcdUW4z4hRlNelPI-0|smart-card]","2026-01-13T08:16:15.281Z"],["3805425","LSS-61435","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Dokobit: [https://app.dokobit.com/signing/fdb3b093183119eccb66c97bc3c346be1b71e5d0|https://app.dokobit.com/signing/fdb3b093183119eccb66c97bc3c346be1b71e5d0]","2026-01-13T08:16:18.709Z"],["3805427","LSS-61468","LSS","elena-roxana.iordachel@bolt.eu","Elena-Roxana Iordăchel","[^5000-K14165-26 Andre Hörberg.pdf]\n[^Begäran BOLT.pdf.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T08:16:33.183Z"],["3805428","LSS-60708","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^2024 - short-form NDA template_revised.docx]\n\nHi [~accountid:712020:1a447c27-5947-4ed5-b674-3b465dfa89ac]please find attached a revised version of the NDA. The changes reflect adjustments made to align the NDA with a mutual version and our standard provisions. Please let me know if you have any questions.","2026-01-13T08:16:36.590Z"],["3805432","RDXENG-4527","RDXENG","daniel.tjulinov@bolt.eu","Daniel Tjulinov","was fixed here [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159533|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159533|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:17:21.201Z"],["3805434","LSS-57150","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Sure [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] thank you! ","2026-01-13T08:18:07.469Z"],["3805435","DMC-353","DMC","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e]  What I meant is that I was not able to reproduce it with quick effort, meaning that probably there are some specific preconditions for it which will require further investigation for reproduction.","2026-01-13T08:18:14.424Z"],["3805438","PFI-832585","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nWe are not able to provide a letter of authorization release. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten","2026-01-13T08:18:52.095Z"],["3805439","PFI-832502","PFI","illia.drobzhev@bolt-outsource.eu","Illia   Drobzhev","The bank has indicated that the funds have been returned to you.","2026-01-13T08:18:53.153Z"],["3805440","WD-22547","WD","marja.laanep@bolt.eu","Marja Laanep","Done:)","2026-01-13T08:19:07.326Z"],["3805442","PRF-1771","PRF","carelin.magi@bolt.eu","Carelin Mägi","There is an account for Saudi Arabia in Snap already","2026-01-13T08:19:24.158Z"],["3805443","CRC-2075","CRC","daniil.musienko@bolt.eu","Daniil Musienko","[update]\n\nProgress: We completed implementation and internal testing. On 12.01, we enabled the feature for some BINs for external users.\n\nNext: Monitor results. 15.01 - enable for all Cartes Bancaires BINs","2026-01-13T08:19:31.668Z"],["3805444","DSR-3687","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] \n\n\n\nFrom what I see the User contacted us in-app asking to remove their email from the account but to keep the account intact. Moreover, their email address is verified.\n\n\n\nCan you please instruct Tier 2 to confirm with the User what does the User want? Please ask them to explain that the User needs to have some email address linked to their account, ask whether they want to only change the email address or delete their account? \n\n\n\nInstruct Tier 2 to proceed accordingly based on User’s response.\n\n\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] ","2026-01-13T08:19:32.267Z"],["3805445","LSS-61050","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:712020:979961a6-5216-4ee0-aa85-a7302993f5e6] The attached NDA is mutual, as is ours. In this situation, I would not recommend signing two mutual NDAs, as this could create overlapping or potentially conflicting obligations.\n\nThe best approach would be to use our template NDA as this would avoid excessive work. If this is impossible I would recommend to review the attached NDA and proceed with a single agreement only. Please let me know how should we proceed. ","2026-01-13T08:20:22.027Z"],["3805446","RLONE-506","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Can you get back here [~accountid:712020:5d844768-bae2-474d-8de8-69336d3a4dea] ?","2026-01-13T08:20:28.963Z"],["3805447","CRC-2172","CRC","kenechukwu.nwankwo@bolt.eu","Kenechukwu Nwankwo","[update] Reporting Integration is Live.  Flows still under close monitoring during the Hypercare period with review of failed invoices and  BAU Ops setups.\n\n*Open issues to be resolved*\n\n* We are missing onboarding & certificates for one of the Bolt entities on the provider side. Coordinating with the local team to have this sorted as this is handled on their side today.\n* Finance doesn’t have an appointed access point to receive e-invoices so invoices to the Bolt entities issued from the billing platform will not go through. We are exploring having the commerce provider support this use case as a stop gap until Finance team closes out with their provider.\n* Solidifying Buyer Identity ( WP and Business companies).","2026-01-13T08:20:51.259Z"],["3805448","CRC-2171","CRC","kenechukwu.nwankwo@bolt.eu","Kenechukwu Nwankwo","[update] Reporting Integration is Live.  Flows still under close monitoring during the Hypercare period with review of failed invoices and  BAU Ops setups.","2026-01-13T08:21:02.874Z"],["3805449","LSS-59845","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nI have shared it with Sentry\n\nThanks!","2026-01-13T08:21:06.491Z"],["3805450","ITI-1165","ITI","leila.toomet@bolt.eu","Leila Toomet","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/145ZYirpJLLCvK7Zk7IZ40b7ghpt3bybLVBwRf5EG0no/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/145ZYirpJLLCvK7Zk7IZ40b7ghpt3bybLVBwRf5EG0no/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:21:06.603Z"],["3805451","CRC-2107","CRC","sander.randorg@bolt.eu","Sander Randorg","[update] Changed gears on the RH commission invoice reconciliation gap metric, as we hit multiple walls, decided to zoom in on the 5 top markets (generating 33% of GMV). Worked out a prioritization framework for choosing which are the important markets to govern first — GMV*(Sensitivity+Set-up Complexity)","2026-01-13T08:21:16.929Z"],["3805452","RLONE-435","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Dev has delayed the rollout and new ETA is this week, read more [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C089BFQABB4/p1761138404548099].","2026-01-13T08:21:58.802Z"],["3805453","CSDT-950","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","* create semantic of dim_support_case_tier_history ✅ \n* create a measure in dim_support_case_tier_history semantic model that counts tier changes after escalation ✅ \n* Create simple metrics for measures above ✅ \n* add count above to mart_support_case_metrics as a derived dimension ✅ \n* Re-generate mart ✅ \n* Merge & backfill \n* create a metric that uses the derived dimension to get the count of escalated solved & closed cases without tier change post escalation as well as the rate metrics","2026-01-13T08:22:01.958Z"],["3805455","CRC-1689","CRC","kristiina.taube@bolt.eu","Kristiina Taube","\n\n[update - change in metrics due to input data adjustment] Live countries validated: 87% (2% WoW), #46 (1 WoW) of #53 (0 WoW) (results).\nLive/planned WIP: #0 ( 0 WoW).","2026-01-13T08:22:36.446Z"],["3805456","LSS-61109","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thanks for your confirmation [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] !","2026-01-13T08:22:50.747Z"],["3805458","RLONE-506","RLONE","laura.decampos@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Pereira De Campos","[~accountid:712020:78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a] If your are offboarding then check if they are in the whatsapp group and remove them, we discussed this when the group was created, the same goes for onboarding you just add them instead of removing them. ","2026-01-13T08:23:01.955Z"],["3805459","DRX-27840","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.126.0 (1505) Firebase build on Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\n||*Fleet Driver*||*Fleet Owner*||*Private Driver*||\n|!Screenshot_20260113-100201.png|width=202,alt=\"Screenshot_20260113-100201.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260113-102045.png|width=202,alt=\"Screenshot_20260113-102045.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260113-101821.png|width=202,alt=\"Screenshot_20260113-101821.png\"!|","2026-01-13T08:23:17.461Z"],["3805460","CRC-2319","CRC","kenechukwu.nwankwo@bolt.eu","Kenechukwu Nwankwo","[update] No big updates as focus has been on getting urgent mandates out.\n\n* *Fiscal Devices/ Cash Register* — Migrating fleets to new vendor app to kickoff in Q1. We can only switch to the new vendor API when fleet migration is done.\n* *E-invoicing (KSEF)* — We’ll be changing vendors to Fonoa  since Sovos doesn’t seem to be responsive. Initial technical review done and missing some unhappy paths. We’ll check in Jan for updates on these.","2026-01-13T08:23:19.078Z"],["3805461","RLONE-576","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Was supposed to be fixed last week, but Chantel did not mange the timeline and has confirmed a new ETA for this week, read more [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1767621348393349?thread_ts=1763119148.093779&cid=C02FP2YL06L,]. ","2026-01-13T08:23:34.758Z"],["3805463","LSS-61470","LSS","annika.helimets@bolt.eu","Annika Helimets","[^Bolt teenusleping taksofirmaga Sõidame OÜ.asice.asice]\n\n","2026-01-13T08:23:36.638Z"],["3805464","CRC-2346","CRC","kenechukwu.nwankwo@bolt.eu","Kenechukwu Nwankwo","[update] Reporting Integration upgrades are Live with close monitoring during the Hypercare period.","2026-01-13T08:23:36.649Z"],["3805465","HS-28790","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hey, yes, if you could provide me with the Ukrainian work book which shows you reached eligibility last year, then I will add you 6 days retrospectively to 2025 as well!:)","2026-01-13T08:23:42.401Z"],["3805467","CRC-1858","CRC","kenechukwu.nwankwo@bolt.eu","Kenechukwu Nwankwo","[update]\n\nETA1:  *SII: E-reporting for big companies – 1st Jan 2026*\n\nETA 2: *Verifactu: certification of billing software – 1st July 2025* \n\n* *Tech Integration – SII:* Reporting Integration is Live with close monitoring in hypercare period. Some issues to be resolved;\n** Reporting for Business invoices from December 25 generated this year (Resolved)\n** Reporting transactions with Non ES customers\n** Reporting Purchases by the ES Bolt Ops Entity\n* *Tech Integration – Verifactu:* Commercial contracts shared and awaiting signing.  To be picked up in Q1.","2026-01-13T08:24:08.030Z"],["3805468","RLONE-512","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Please follow this [link|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1m3zW-Xl44osENYPKHdn3bbDYiq8EMZCOamr-ACpg-cw/edit?gid=1402701839#gid=1402701839] to to get exact stats in regards to the progress.","2026-01-13T08:24:37.259Z"],["3805469","LSS-60768","LSS","wiktoria.lis@bolt.eu","Wiktoria Lis","[~accountid:712020:b1700666-82b2-4a86-82f7-550a84f716c8] did we receive signed version from Kamil? he confirmed he signed the document","2026-01-13T08:24:48.219Z"],["3805471","LSS-61442","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341980|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341980|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:25:19.835Z"],["3805472","PFI-830803","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello,\n\nAll invoices are available in the Admin. For the Monthly Statements/Invoices/SF Invoices, please, find those in the Invoices tab in the Business Invoicing Admin Panel. For the Ride Invoices, it’s possible to find Order links, when filtering via Claims in the Balance Entries Tab.\n\nIf there’s Invoice for the Ride/Monthly Invoice missing from there, please, provide links and I’d be happy to help","2026-01-13T08:25:21.074Z"],["3805474","WD-22428","WD","janeli.niinemaa@bolt.eu","Janeli Niinemaa","Hey, would really appreciate help with this ticket as it would ensure timely payments to the employees 🙏 ","2026-01-13T08:25:50.199Z"],["3805478","PFI-829210","PFI","mary.adjakonor@bolt-outsource.eu","Mary Adjakonor","Hello [~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24] \n\nThank you for the update.\n\nHave a good day.\n\nMary","2026-01-13T08:26:19.649Z"],["3805479","PFI-829900","PFI","juozas.masteika@bolt.eu","Juozas Masteika","[~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] Thank you very much for the answer 🙏  We can close the ticket 🙂 ","2026-01-13T08:26:42.127Z"],["3805482","LSS-60199","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hi [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] ,\n\nThank you very much.\n\nWe will add reminders to our calendars regarding the renewal / termination dates.\n\nMay I kindly ask for your help in getting the Order Form signed?\n\nThank you.\n\n[^Articulate Amendment Quote for Bolt.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T08:27:39.184Z"],["3805484","LSS-61471","LSS","getter.tammeri@bolt.eu","Getter Tammeri","[^M. Zimmermann - Letter of Confirmation (Good Leaver).pdf] _(102 kB)_","2026-01-13T08:28:04.107Z"],["3805487","PFI-827514","PFI","barbara.bertalan@bolt.eu","Barbara Bertalan","Hi,\n\nI am still waiting for a response as the FAQs did not answer my question.\n\nThanks,\n\nBarbara","2026-01-13T08:28:57.539Z"],["3805488","PFI-831415","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Where does the Customer sees their Rides? I opened their rides.csv for the December and I wasn’t able to see rides done by Julia Opolska. \n\nPlease, specify in details the issue, where does the customer see, any visual proof, if possible, etc. Please, note that we don’t have the ability to communicate with Customers and hence not having needed information results in longer resolutions. Thank you","2026-01-13T08:29:01.630Z"],["3805489","HS-28888","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Task sent to Global Mobility.","2026-01-13T08:29:02.164Z"],["3805491","LSS-61449","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341982|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341982|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:29:35.871Z"],["3805493","PFI-832750","PFI","sabina.onomiruren@bolt-outsource.eu","Sabina Onomiruren","!image-20260113-082930.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T08:29:44.786Z"],["3805494","LSS-61472","LSS","svenkristjan.bormann@bolt.eu","Sven-Kristjan Bormann","[^Scan Pass Joshua.pdf.pdf] _(599 kB)_\n\n[^Geburtsurkunde Joshua.pdf.pdf] _(394 kB)_","2026-01-13T08:29:45.808Z"],["3805495","LSS-61472","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nSven-Kristjan Bormann has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-13T08:29:47.143Z"],["3805497","CCM-22273","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey Alina 👋 \n\nThey have all been assigned to the Food Delivery Up-skill course. 🙂 \n\nAll the best,\nIrena","2026-01-13T08:30:18.203Z"],["3805503","RCE-275","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768293124317459]*{color}:\nHi! The changes to waybills in France are now live. Notable changes:\n• Added \"Heure de réservation\" showing the time when the ride was requested by the rider. For scheduled rides this is when it was originally scheduled.\n• Added \"Durée de la prise en charge\" that displays the time driver spend going to pick up the rider, shown as duration.\n    ◦ For on-going orders this is *elapsed* time, not the expected time.\n    ◦ It will be shorter than time between booking time and pickup time even for normal orders (by the time it took for the driver to accept the order).\n• Added \"SIREN\" for drivers with company invoicing based on TIN in company profile. The field was not added for drivers with individual invoicing.\n• Added \"Numéro d'identification de l'émetteur\" for drivers with individual invoicing based on invoice issues reg. code in driver profile.\nAttached are examples for drivers with individual and company invoicing respectively. The second example is for a scheduled ride.\n\nLinked files:\n* [Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 09.51.38.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A8RNECNUR/screenshot_2026-01-13_at_09.51.38.png]\n\n* [Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 09.57.54.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A97478VNC/screenshot_2026-01-13_at_09.57.54.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-13T08:32:20.660Z"],["3805505","HS-28664","HS","telvi.tonsiver@bolt.eu","Telvi Tonsiver","The rationale is that these are work days (short or not) and only national holidays and personal days off/sick leaves, etc are considered as no work days (where the actual whole day is off).\n\nAlso in WD, we only record public holidays properly, we do not record shortened work days. ","2026-01-13T08:32:40.255Z"],["3805508","LSS-61450","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341983|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341983|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:33:14.104Z"],["3805511","LSS-60768","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:712020:7ebf1982-dd36-43fb-a386-42b4b1ee6b59] - yes! please find the signed doc attached. have a great day! 🙂\n\n[^Notification and consent_Bolt Poland sp. z.o.o_Eter Poland Sp. z.o.o._23.12.25.pdf] ","2026-01-13T08:34:04.079Z"],["3805515","WFM-9963","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541695|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541695]","2026-01-13T08:35:17.224Z"],["3805519","DSR-3691","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T08:36:07.921Z"],["3805520","DSR-3693","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T08:36:07.996Z"],["3805521","WFM-9964","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","hi [~accountid:712020:647d9435-b4ad-4729-aebd-e4f4f0044a62] ,\nRoles were adjusted to a Marcus's profile, please check if all is working as intended.","2026-01-13T08:36:12.442Z"],["3805522","LSS-61454","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341985|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/341985|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:36:39.784Z"],["3805527","WFM-9963","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey WFM team, 02 MM_Global_English country access were provided to [franco.david@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:franco.david@bolt-outsource.eu].","2026-01-13T08:37:38.684Z"],["3805528","LSS-61466","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:f7dcb856-08aa-436d-bc9b-34ba3f9585a5] - Please attach the document or link. Thanks","2026-01-13T08:37:42.333Z"],["3805531","HS-28876","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:f34c9a00-e304-45e0-9f86-2fd25df12ec1], the letter is sent for signing. Once it’s done you will receive it on your e-mail. Closing this ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-13T08:38:17.846Z"],["3805532","DSR-3637","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] Just a reminder that the deadline for this is today 🙂 ","2026-01-13T08:38:23.033Z"],["3805535","CNT-339","CNT","aleksandra.onutsina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Onutšina","[~accountid:610a6c97ec92ab0070d4d852] I’ll let him know","2026-01-13T08:39:06.006Z"],["3805536","PFI-830803","PFI","pakrampar.silrapasangchai@bolt.eu","Pakrampar Silrapasangchai","HI [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] ,\n\nThere is no receipt provided for [4166.04 thb|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/74596440?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Asia%2FBangkok].\n\n[^PYMTADV_f8b4d6f2545b4de4a00f0522e5a48cc4_251219172349116.PDF.PDF]\n\n!Screenshot 2569-01-13 at 15.35.34.png|width=1037,height=676,alt=\"Screenshot 2569-01-13 at 15.35.34.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-13T08:39:13.238Z"],["3805538","RS-1875","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:60f2a71843c956007065f2ad] ,\n\nYes! We are currently working to present data similar to what they have provided. Thanks for your support!","2026-01-13T08:39:15.881Z"],["3805542","PFI-817417","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Tech Support] App related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/104\n- [Customer Payments] Payment related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/313\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/314\n[Billing] - Invoice and Balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/315\n[Billing/ Tax Tech]- Invoices not reported (Fiscalized): https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n[Billing/Configuration Changes]- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T08:39:26.054Z"],["3805544","HS-28889","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-13T08:39:31.569Z"],["3805546","PFI-832753","PFI","ivaniuk.habriella@bolt-outsource.eu","Ivaniuk Habriella","!IMG_4949.png|thumbnail!\n\n!ScreenRecording_01-08-2026 10-18-39_1.mp4|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T08:40:33.383Z"],["3805547","WFM-9958","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","Play mode was adjusted, WFM team please assist on creating a queue 🙌 \nAgent’s [profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/652786?tab=settings] ","2026-01-13T08:40:53.133Z"],["3805549","LSS-60550","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Hey [~accountid:712020:a9500cde-28bc-4a8e-95d6-7818a2252cf8] has there been any feedback from Banca Transilvania on the draft?\n\nLiisa","2026-01-13T08:41:59.869Z"],["3805550","WFM-9959","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","[agent’s|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/502501?tab=settings] profile","2026-01-13T08:42:06.797Z"],["3805551","LSS-59211","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Hi [~accountid:712020:a9500cde-28bc-4a8e-95d6-7818a2252cf8] [~accountid:712020:853cbe25-4d18-40c3-8211-69c3936bf72f] \n\nHas there been any feedback from Luminor?\n\nLiisa","2026-01-13T08:42:29.607Z"],["3805552","DSR-3637","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC, thanks for escalating. I agree with [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] - this case should have been escalated to Privacy on 13 December. Please prioritise this case so that we can send out an answer ASAP. \n\nThe user is requesting: \n\n* Concerning the ride itself:\n** _1. All Internal Notes and Log Entries: Any and all records, notes, email chains, and customer support chat transcripts (including internal logs) relating to my complaint about the driver, the missing wedding cake, and the demand for a $\\text{£}60$ payment_.\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"taskList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"taskItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"emoji\",\"attrs\":{\"shortName\":\":arrow_right:\",\"id\":\"27a1\",\"text\":\"➡️\"}},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" CSPC: Please source and extract \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"all \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"relevant tickets concerning this issue. This includes the CS chat, and if there’s any, the chat between the driver and the user.\"}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"181229eb-cf14-4f1a-8983-8944b3d501e7\",\"state\":\"DONE\"}},{\"type\":\"taskItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"emoji\",\"attrs\":{\"shortName\":\":arrow_right:\",\"id\":\"27a1\",\"text\":\"➡️\"}},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" Estelle: I will review internal notes\"}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"a8ab95c4-8e8b-4e96-93b3-6316e8488e5b\",\"state\":\"DONE\"}}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"3445768a-e064-4c71-9fa7-de1aa592291d\"}}\n{adf}\n** _2. Records of Payment: Any record or note of the $\\text{£}60$ payment I had to make, and any subsequent communication or notes regarding this payment, potential refunds, or resolution_.\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"taskList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"taskItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"emoji\",\"attrs\":{\"shortName\":\":arrow_right:\",\"id\":\"27a1\",\"text\":\"➡️\"}},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" CSPC: Please source the data relevant to payments: the invoice for the ride, the payment methods saved to the user’s profile, and any log of a refund offered\"}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"26f98e3a-0dcc-46b3-99a7-9e04fb4f0ffa\",\"state\":\"DONE\"}}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"87c25f91-85a7-44f5-90ec-c8eaaa7a0269\"}}\n{adf}\n** _3. Data about the Driver: Any personal data about the driver that was processed as part of the investigation and is considered my personal data (e.g., the driver's ID number, name, or vehicle registration number, if shared with me or TFL/Police)_\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"taskList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"taskItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"emoji\",\"attrs\":{\"shortName\":\":arrow_right:\",\"id\":\"27a1\",\"text\":\"➡️\"}},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" The driver’s personal data is not considered the rider’s personal data. We will not be providing this.\"}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"19cda734-53c5-4ffa-ae71-03bfa139e584\",\"state\":\"TODO\"}}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"12e01118-e1c0-4a4b-90f2-4e75243a488f\"}}\n{adf}\n* Concerning Bolt’s disclosure to Police/TfL:\n** _1. Data Shared with the Police: A copy of all my personal data (e.g., my name, contact details, account of the incident) that was passed to the police._ \n_I also request the Crime Reference Number or Incident Log Number and the name of the police unit or contact that the report was submitted to._ \n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"taskList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"taskItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"emoji\",\"attrs\":{\"shortName\":\":arrow_right:\",\"id\":\"27a1\",\"text\":\"➡️\"}},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" CSPC: please double-check this - was there a police report made concerning this case? Do we have a copy of this? \"}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"80bae521-e8d3-4602-9157-1ef791ed3c76\",\"state\":\"TODO\"}}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"24199a04-ffa7-4193-9c86-dfdcc09baf82\"}}\n{adf}\n** _2. Data Shared with TfL (Transport for London): A copy of all my personal data that was passed to TfL, including the date of disclosure and details of the information shared._ \n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"taskList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"taskItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"emoji\",\"attrs\":{\"shortName\":\":arrow_right:\",\"id\":\"27a1\",\"text\":\"➡️\"}},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" CSPC: please double-check this - was there a TfL report made concerning this case? Do we have a copy of this?\"}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"c3fc2fd8-3982-4be2-9f7e-30b605f77245\",\"state\":\"TODO\"}}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"24199a04-ffa7-4193-9c86-dfdcc09baf82\"}}\n{adf}\n** _3. Legal Basis for Disclosure: For all data shared with the police and TfL, please state the specific legal basis under UK GDPR that you relied upon for that disclosure (e.g., performance of a public task, legitimate interest, or legal obligation)._ \n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"taskList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"taskItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"emoji\",\"attrs\":{\"shortName\":\":arrow_right:\",\"id\":\"27a1\",\"text\":\"➡️\"}},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" Estelle: include reference and answer to this in answer letter.\"}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"edb34045-15f0-44c2-97f7-d7d5a1bc38bf\",\"state\":\"TODO\"}}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"b82617ae-d1df-4a5b-9af3-0c8290f93529\"}}\n{adf}\n* Supplementary Information:\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"taskList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"taskItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"emoji\",\"attrs\":{\"shortName\":\":arrow_right:\",\"id\":\"27a1\",\"text\":\"➡️\"}},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" Estelle: all queries relate to information available in the PN. Usual reference to it should be sufficient. \"}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"343e0f2f-004f-45f2-9c24-1617373048aa\",\"state\":\"TODO\"}}],\"attrs\":{\"localId\":\"728645e5-5134-4015-9f29-9785793a7c4e\"}}\n{adf}","2026-01-13T08:42:34.709Z"],["3805558","PFI-830803","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, consider that invoices are issued for the provided services and not for the Payments done. Each Ride decreases the Balance, and Payments simply Top Up the Balance of the Company. \n\nPlease, refer to the Ride Invoices or SF Invoices as the confirmation of the services provided. If there’s some other document needed (i.e. proof of payment confirmation, etc), please, raise it with Partner Payments Team.","2026-01-13T08:43:01.281Z"],["3805560","PFI-832754","PFI","agne.majauskaiteshah@bolt-outsource.eu","Agnė Majauskaiteshah","!Screenshot 2026-01-13 104221.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T08:43:05.853Z"],["3805562","PFI-830803","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Partner Payments] Business made payment, but didn't reflect: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306\n- [Customer Payments] Business had issues with their credit card: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/303\n\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/304\n\n[Billing] - Business invoicing and balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305\n\n[Billing/Tax Tech]- Business invoice has not been reported (Fiscalized) : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T08:43:06.646Z"],["3805564","LSS-60630","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:5de3bf86-6cba-4bd9-b71a-087b2b4da2eb] \n\nThank you for following up - apologies for the delayed response, as I was on leave.\n\nI will have a look at the assessment and will provide responses where I can. I will complete this by EoW.","2026-01-13T08:43:25.409Z"],["3805566","PFI-832565","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 55.00 ZAR on 17/12/2025, 10:29:58UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 17th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T08:43:58.539Z"],["3805568","DRX-26216","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","Tested and verified on DI.127.0 (194761070) using iPhone 11, iOS 26.2\n\n* verified registration flow\n* Error screen on forgot password flow when internet is disabled\n** error screen resolves when internet is enabled\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-13-2026 10-37-22 AM_1.MP4]\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-13-2026 10-42-02 AM_1.MP4]\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-13-2026 10-39-40 AM_1.MP4]","2026-01-13T08:44:24.807Z"],["3805571","WFM-9959","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","[req|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601643] raised for the access to all countries - *approved* & queue added. WFM team please assist on adjusting it in the Assembled, if applicable  🙌 ","2026-01-13T08:44:36.773Z"],["3805572","FDBT-4787","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_finance_model_ledger_aggr_vs_ledger_test fails on 2026-01-12 01:00:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task test failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 250166655882489, 'task_key': 'test'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_finance_model_ledger_aggr_vs_ledger_test/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-12T01%3A00%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=finance_model_ledger_aggr_vs_ledger_test.finance_model_ledger_aggr_vs_ledger_test&base_date=2026-01-12T01%3A00%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-13T08:44:37.156Z"],["3805573","DRX-26235","DRX","oliver.meus@bolt.eu","Oliver Meus","This task added following banner to every screen that is implemented using NavigationActivity. Please test these screens to verify that the banner works and nothing else is broken. This list is couple of months old so probably doesn’t include everything now, but if most of these are working well, it is unlikely to have issues on others anyway.\n\n* Transactions history\n** main list view\n** transaction details view\n* Earnings\n** main landing screen\n* Permission onboarding\n* Full screen driver preferences {{dev_is_full_screen_driver_preferences_enabled=true}}\n** Main preferences view\n** Vehicle list\n** Vehicle categories\n** Pricing methods\n** Auto accept filters (I was able to trigger with deeplink)\n* Lead became driver screen\n* Terminal connection screen (boltdriverapp://posTerminal/connect)\n* Driver profile screens (I was able to trigger most of them with deeplinks but not sure where they would appear in the app)\n** Add driver profile list\n** Driver profile list\n** Activate driver profile\n** Driver profile explanatory screen\n* Offers screen:\n** Feedback usage (appears after like/dislike)\n** Feedback reasons screen\n\n!image-20260113-083826.png|width=1080,alt=\"image-20260113-083826.png\"!","2026-01-13T08:44:51.288Z"],["3805574","DSR-3623","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","* ⛔ Got a response from the verification support Slack:\n** _The faces are not matching. We wouldn't advise unblocking, as we consider this a potential fraud/impersonation attempt._\n* ⌛ PDE tool started [+_here_+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/personal-data-export/exports/1237288?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]\n* ✅ RESPONSE doc adjusted","2026-01-13T08:45:02.088Z"],["3805575","PFI-805526","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Hello \n\n  \n\nSending chargeback report \n\n  \n\nSincerely \n\n *{color:#767171} {color}* \n\n *{color:#767171} *Nino Kabulashvili*{color}*\n{color:#767171} E-Commerce Partners Relationship Senior Manager{color} {color:#767171}| Payments Business |{color}{color:#767171}{color} {color:#767171}Bank of Georgia\n Bank of Georgia: Tbilisi, 29A Gagarini Str., 0160 | E-mail:{color} [{color:#767171} {color}{color:#767171}NKabulashvili@bog.ge{color}{color:#767171}{color}|mailto:NKabulashvili@bog.ge]{color:#767171}\n Phone: (+995 32) 2444 444 (ext. 7492) | Mobile: (+995 555) 444405{color}{color:#767171}{color}{color:#767171}{color}{color:#1F497D}{color}{color:blue}{color}  \n\n  \n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://bankofgeorgia.ge/retail]>{color:blue}{color}!image002.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[https://www.facebook.com/119630781428450]>{color:blue}{color}!image003.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://instagram.com/bankofgeorgia]>{color:blue}{color}!image004.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://www.youtube.com/bankofgeorgiatv]>{color:blue}{color}!image005.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://www.linkedin.com/company/bank-of-georgia]>{color:#1F497D}{color}\n\n[^Wolt 1-11 Jan.xlsx] _(11 kB)_","2026-01-13T08:45:03.172Z"],["3805577","LSS-60119","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] \n\n1. Thanks\n2. Sure - [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] kindly add your comments (If any) so we send them once to G4S. \n\n# SOP - It covers the Standard Operating Procedures that CASI and BOLT will follow. Kindly review it too. \n# Okay\n\n","2026-01-13T08:45:13.879Z"],["3805579","WFM-9963","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","*Outsource CS - Micromobility* role access for [franco.david@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:franco.david@bolt-outsource.eu] : [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571688|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571688]","2026-01-13T08:45:26.192Z"],["3805583","LSS-58772","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Hi [~accountid:712020:853cbe25-4d18-40c3-8211-69c3936bf72f] [~accountid:712020:a9500cde-28bc-4a8e-95d6-7818a2252cf8] please make sure Luminor signed NDA as well. At the end of last year they didn’t have any significant comments to add to the NDA only two small open points - Luminor’s signee and effective date of NDA. Then we could sign the document. \n\nLiisa","2026-01-13T08:46:26.077Z"],["3805584","PFA-560","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","*[NULL Unassignment Reason Deep Dive]*\nHello Greg,\n\n*Update*\nWant to make an update regarding unassignment reason:\n\n* 99.1% are identifiable *(on top of all automation attempts)*\n* 0.57% are caused by bug something like\n** SOLUTION_DOES_NOT_MATCH_TO_CONTEXT\n** ACTION_NOT_ELIGIBLE\n** PUBLIC_TEXT_MESSAGING_NOT_ALLOWED\n* 0.33% are still unidentified\n** quick deep dive some of cases are associated to the customers that rejection monetary solution from the alfred\n\nIf you have time, kindly review it the attachment below\n\n*Action Item / Think to be asked*\n\n* want to reconfirm my understanding -so the ideal state is unassignment_reason is only identifiable when there is an automation_attempt (especialy from Alfred). is it correct?\n*  just curious why there is some cases where the {{automation_attempt}} is FALSE but the {{unassignment_reason}} is unidentified (detail is attached, just curious)\n* in parallel I will move to enable it in our Routines Dashboards\n\n[+Attachment+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yQ-0P5lsLMIJ3TJeKEVuVh0UK7oSdWA5N9E_Wz_vCdU/edit?gid=273539380#gid=273539380]","2026-01-13T08:46:26.608Z"],["3805587","LSS-60487","LSS","laura.decampos@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Pereira De Campos","Hi Emelie,\n\nThank you for advice and clarifying 🙂 ","2026-01-13T08:47:50.022Z"],["3805590","LSS-58103","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","[~accountid:712020:3aab0dff-7ae2-461e-b7c7-c61be1f47a3c] could you please share signed version of API terms as well as Special terms with Araz under this ticket for archiving purposes. \n\ncc: [~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] \n\nLiisa","2026-01-13T08:48:07.339Z"],["3805591","PFI-832758","PFI","oluwatosin.akinbolasere@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwatosin Akinbolasere","!image-20260113-084756.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T08:48:11.616Z"],["3805592","LSS-52184","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:5f896ba356eec000768527be] - the privacy team requires the updated document from the counterparty, including the DPA.\n\nAccording to my latest update, the only pending item is the approval from Infosec regarding the suggestions from City Legal. Otherwise, everything appears to be in order.","2026-01-13T08:48:21.145Z"],["3805594","HS-28651","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hi [~accountid:60069928e2a1350069629f4b] \n\nHer contract is ready with the start date of 16.03.2026.\n\nI close this task but could you please Slack me when her visa docs are fine and I can send the contract for signing.\n\n\n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-13T08:49:35.973Z"],["3805596","LSS-52335","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update (22.01):*\n\n# Infosec review completed; Infosec requests additional contractual safeguarding wording to be added to the Order Form; details are in the main ticket.\n# Awaiting for the final version of the DPA to review & confirm alignment on the remaining points.","2026-01-13T08:49:44.383Z"],["3805597","LEG-382","LEG","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] I think we can close this ticket since latest ticket I have for Araz in AZ (linked to this ticket above) should be signed and I don’t see that stakeholders would have carried this ticket over to Q1 2026. If needed we can always reopen it. \n\nPS! Regarding Araz, then most probably same group other brands will be added in Q1 and Q2. If needed then I can support with those myself and if needed we can divide the workload if I see that they want to launch several partners from the group same time. Separate MVRA ticket for AZ key accounts was created for Q1 2026. \n\nLiisa","2026-01-13T08:49:49.264Z"],["3805600","LSS-60282","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi team [~accountid:712020:7f47c2af-14e1-4206-a795-ac87cb906276] [~accountid:712020:67606a59-d726-4e53-8ba7-862b9e82da34] , sharing the EN version of document: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ircdMfzg3kk5zpfAozDEjKGtGzrjE05I0DdwcbA6CIE/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.equlr1c8x1j5|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ircdMfzg3kk5zpfAozDEjKGtGzrjE05I0DdwcbA6CIE/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.equlr1c8x1j5]","2026-01-13T08:50:07.075Z"],["3805603","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","Improvement Idea: *Bluetooth unlock fallback for scooters in no-signal areas*\n\nWe regularly have scooters parked underground (parking garages / ground floor of large buildings) where they lose IoT connectivity. When that happens they appear unavailable to rent, and we end up paying for a rebalance just to recover them.\n\nCompetitors like Ryde/Voi handle this by allowing the app to find and unlock the scooter via Bluetooth even when the scooter has no signal (the app prompts the user to enable BT, then unlocks).\n\nI think we should build the same: if a scooter is offline/unavailable due to connectivity, allow a Bluetooth-based unlock flow so a nearby user can still start a ride.\n\nThis is not the greatest driver of unavailability in Oslo, but we still see ~15–30 cases daily, and some of these underground locations are city regulated parking spots (e.g., the hospital), meaning we simply cant remove them.\n\n*Impact estimate/month:* *~€2-3k* 3PL rebalance cost + *~€3–5k GMV* lost from *~2–3k rides*.\n\nWould be interesting to see if this is also an issue in other markets, *@user-U03EM10HA3C*,*@user-U01HXMFV927* and *@user-U02UN3MB36V*  do you experience this in your cities?","2026-01-13T08:50:46.328Z"],["3805604","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT",null,"Slack","[Klemet-Gustav Tamm|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNZ5V326L/p1767868914348229?thread_ts=1767868914.348229&cid=CNZ5V326L|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNZ5V326L/p1767868914348229?thread_ts=1767868914.348229&cid=CNZ5V326L|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-13T08:50:47.162Z"],["3805605","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","pavel.k@bolt.eu","Pavel Karagjaur","FYI we have this in Bolt Drive. Not sure if helpful :smile:","2026-01-13T08:50:48.417Z"],["3805606","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT",null,"Slack","[@aare.palm|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] not sure if there is a separate firmware team for Drive and MM but do you think we could \"simply\" copy this feature from cars to scooters? Assuming the IOT in both our cars and scooters are somewhat similar?","2026-01-13T08:50:49.961Z"],["3805607","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","aare.palm@bolt.eu","Aare Palm","The feature cannot be copied from Drive. Micromobility needs a new development.","2026-01-13T08:50:50.956Z"],["3805609","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","aleksei.kovalev@bolt.eu","Aleksei Kovalev","we have this feature in a charger app for micromobility, so our chargers can find and collect this scooter. for our riders i believe we also planned something similar, i hope [@vadim.gerassimov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/60e01bce7fcd82007303f981] could help here :pray::skin-tone-2:","2026-01-13T08:50:53.817Z"],["3805610","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","vadim.gerassimov@bolt.eu","Vadim Gerassimov","[@aleksei.kovalev|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/61d554b649f195006941c5bd] it’s for finding via iBeacon, but not unlocking when there is no mobile network connectivity","2026-01-13T08:50:54.771Z"],["3805611","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","katharina.muhlen@bolt.eu","Katharina Mühlen","[@kasper.virkesdal|https://taxify.slack.com/team/U02LVR3AY6B] you are referring to allowing users to unlock these vehicles, right and not drivers?","2026-01-13T08:50:55.727Z"],["3805612","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT",null,"Slack","[@katharina.muhlen|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:b453d711-e8b8-450d-9d06-5538889f1d87] Yes, customers unlocking scooters with no signal","2026-01-13T08:50:57.286Z"],["3805613","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","katharina.muhlen@bolt.eu","Katharina Mühlen","ok","2026-01-13T08:50:58.094Z"],["3805614","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","hannalore.taal@bolt.eu","Hannalore Taal","Thanks, [@kasper.virkesdal|https://taxify.slack.com/team/U02LVR3AY6B] that's a good idea, but not sure if/how feasible it is technically, requires evaluation from [@vadim.gerassimov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/60e01bce7fcd82007303f981], [@aare.palm|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] I believe. Once we have this preliminary technical feasibility analysis done, can evaluate where does this position to in relation to the other priorities.\n\nHowever, we have been thinking about a use-case to enable users to start the ride with Bluetooth (e.g. holding the throttle), so maybe this could be one case to address as part of this functionality?","2026-01-13T08:50:59.100Z"],["3805615","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","vadim.gerassimov@bolt.eu","Vadim Gerassimov","{quote}However, we have been thinking about a use-case to enable users to start the ride with Bluetooth (e.g. holding the throttle), so maybe this could be one case to address as part of this functionality?{quote}\n\nThrottle + iBeacon can be a solution here assuming that mobile phone has network connectivity","2026-01-13T08:50:59.735Z"],["3805616","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","vadim.gerassimov@bolt.eu","Vadim Gerassimov","However, no, without connectibity to the iot we are not able to send an unlock command","2026-01-13T08:51:00.634Z"],["3805617","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT",null,"Slack","In 99% of cases I still have phone signal when unlocking either a Ryde or Voi scooter, so I doubt there is a need for a \"no phone signal + no scooter signal solution\"","2026-01-13T08:51:02.309Z"],["3805619","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] how much effort do you estimate the firmware development from our side would take?","2026-01-13T08:51:22.986Z"],["3805620","LSS-61362","LSS","venice.sagyaman@bolt.eu","Venice Sagyaman","Hey [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] Thank you for the detailed assessment and confirmation!\n\nWe anticipate that the value of the lunch will most likely exceed the €100 per person threshold. In line with Policy 5.2, we would therefore like to request written Legal approval in advance.\n\nWe will ensure the spend remains reasonable and proportionate, retain the receipt, and clearly document the business purpose when submitting the expense.\n\nPlease let us know if you need any further information from us.\n\nThank you for your support.","2026-01-13T08:51:37.764Z"],["3805623","SUPX-2265","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Hey :wave::skin-tone-2:\n\nTook a bit longer than expected, but change has been merged. Testing on prelive currently, so far seems all is good :+1::skin-tone-2:","2026-01-13T08:51:51.130Z"],["3805624","BDB-1533","BDB","taaniel.malleus@bolt.eu","Taaniel Malleus","Bags in [Bolt Food brand guides |https://www.figma.com/design/ul1vRACzd39OcFvvPshute/Bolt-Food-Brand-Guidelines--internal-?node-id=0-1&t=uTp481PMHZGNzSQC-1]\nBag [print files|https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/vaod9y8lr8ia5kmlmb8ge/AHxCJljklZ6v91TuhLWfzw8?rlkey=jg7gs0e74sd516kyn103a2wcv&dl=0]","2026-01-13T08:52:07.938Z"],["3805626","PAW-14520","PAW","mihai.casandra@bolt.eu","Mihai Casandra","Issue will be fixed by PINT in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PIF-3278|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PIF-3278|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:52:34.612Z"],["3805627","DSR-3577","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Hey [~accountid:712020:da839b78-87fc-4471-947b-3aae59c6030b] Since Eliise Saarelaan has left the company asking your advice on this ticket 🙂 \n\nUK Workplace Experience Manager is raising a request to obtain restricted, role-based access to UK only employee personal data.\n\nCould you please advise if this request has been escalated correctly, who should handle this request and is there any assistance needed from CSPC side? ","2026-01-13T08:52:36.672Z"],["3805628","LSS-61469","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! I couldn’t find any board or shareholder meeting documents starting from September. I did find 3 management board decisions regarding options if these are be relevant. Attaching them here just in case.\n\n[^Resolutions of the Management Board (Option Acceleration)_Bolt Technology OÜ_Geert-Jan Kistemaker_30.09.2025.pdf]\n[^Management Board Decision_Bolt Technology OÜ_Gaurav Bhattacharya_06.11.2025.pdf]\n[^Management Board Decision_Bolt Technology OÜ_Karel Jaama_06.11.2025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T08:52:43.898Z"],["3805629","SAI-1401","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","{quote}*= 4*{quote}\n\n:redalert: *ERROR :: cs-rides-refund :: [Logs] NJSC errors last 2 min* Triggered with value *4.57* ","2026-01-13T08:52:51.631Z"],["3805630","SAI-1401","SAI",null,"Slack","[Grzegorz Brotoń|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:f79c0085-d2cb-444c-a121-d9c86bb2bfca] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C060Y4GTY6R/p1768292072046729?thread_ts=1768292072.046729&cid=C060Y4GTY6R|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C060Y4GTY6R/p1768292072046729?thread_ts=1768292072.046729&cid=C060Y4GTY6R|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-13T08:52:52.538Z"],["3805631","SAI-1401","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Might require investigation, should not happen that often\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7XF52S07/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7XF52S07/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-13T08:52:53.040Z"],["3805632","SAI-1401","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","1 week:\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A97833VLG/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A97833VLG/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-13T08:53:18.630Z"],["3805633","SAI-1401","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7XFE05NK/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A7XFE05NK/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-13T08:53:34.118Z"],["3805635","DBRE-7638","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","[~accountid:712020:0ef8f6fe-4761-4ff2-a1b7-74961ff962b3] Since Innodb IO setting-related tasks are well handled by [~accountid:712020:0c5038f7-7f89-46d8-b2ea-9f10c0c3bcc6] and [~accountid:5e7dbc6d1e65980c42bb9755] , it's unnecessary for me to have ownership of this ticket. Would you consider changing the Assignee to one of them?","2026-01-13T08:53:45.869Z"],["3805637","LSS-61471","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:5d5149bc92705e0c1c5e519a] – Is only scan sufficient or is delivery needed as well? If delivery is needed please provide name of the recipient, address and phone number.","2026-01-13T08:54:13.981Z"],["3805639","WFM-9962","WFM","surendran.sathananthan@bolt-outsource.eu","Surendran Sathananthan","All the role would be ideal","2026-01-13T08:54:49.256Z"],["3805640","LSS-61466","LSS","maarifa.pashayeva@bolt.eu","Maarifa Pashayeva","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lNf2g7CrUYPNPELpus9toaAiMdNtSiL_/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lNf2g7CrUYPNPELpus9toaAiMdNtSiL_/edit|smart-link]  ","2026-01-13T08:54:57.942Z"],["3805641","PAR-3839","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","This is another issue ( you can create a ticket ) , but the good thing that we didn't allocate this payment\n\n{quote}client doesn't exist, but why we assign VA to the client which doesn't exist?{quote}","2026-01-13T08:55:01.124Z"],["3805643","LSS-61466","LSS","maarifa.pashayeva@bolt.eu","Maarifa Pashayeva","Added ","2026-01-13T08:55:04.409Z"],["3805646","LSS-60617","LSS","balthasar.scheder@bolt.eu","Balthasar Scheder","Thx Anouar for the updated version. All remaining commercial risks are approved from. my end. @Dawit - I will initiate signature collection. Many thanks.","2026-01-13T08:55:21.754Z"],["3805648","PFI-832555","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThank you for escalating! This is very interesting how the user received the negative balance. \n\nThere was a transaction cash adjustment on the users previous order on 30 Jul 2024, 16:40:05 (UTC+03:00)\nWhen the adjustment was created it gave the user a temporary bolt balance. \n\nUser created a new order a few minutes later 30 Jul 2024, 18:43:39 (UTC+03:00) when they had the temporary balance. Since the system thought the user has positive balance it was used to pay for the order. \n\nOnce the adjustment settled on 31 Jul 2024, 16:39:24 (UTC+03:00) the user received the negative balance. \n\n!image-20260113-085248.png|width=1387,height=547!\n\nPlease ask the user to top up their balance or cover their debt with their next order. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T08:55:40.613Z"],["3805650","HS-28252","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","Hey\nSince the effective date has already passed I'm also unable to cancel it myself so I’m waiting for support from the People Technology team. \n\nBest\nAlice, People Ops ","2026-01-13T08:56:02.623Z"],["3805651","CSDT-918","CSDT","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","*1-1 with Andrei Dubonossov — Senior Customer Experience Manager (Rides)*\n13.01.2026\n\n*Topics covered:*\n\n* Current MBR process and opportunities for automation\n(significant manual and unnecessary work today)\n* Use of AI summaries to speed up MBR review and preparation of core insights\n* Main focus areas of CS Experience:\n** Internal processes within Bolt\n** Knowledge base and enablement inside Customer Support\n* AI routines:\n** Technical troubleshooting (TS) steps\n** Human-readable workflows for CS agents\n** Integration of AI-made steps to workflow of CS agents\n* 2026 initiative to improve customer self-service and reduce CS contact volume\n\n*Key requests from CS Experience to Data team:*\n\n# Centralized MBR data in one place (already in progress)\n# Data automation for external partners (will be covered in probation project)\n# Core dashboards for the Safety team (main needs to be decided and reviewed in Q1-Q2 2026)\n\n*Key takeaways:*\n\n* Strong need for automation and consolidation of MBR reporting\n* AI-driven summaries already provide tangible time savings\n* Clear opportunity for CS Data to support self-service and Safety initiatives\n* Alignment between CS Experience priorities and ongoing data platform improvements\n\n*Follow-ups / Notes:*\n\n* Track progress of centralized MBR reporting\n* Consider Safety dashboards as a potential future initiative\n* Keep self-service and automation goals in mind when designing data products","2026-01-13T08:56:05.968Z"],["3805653","LSS-58830","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","Hi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] please see feedback below from EOS:\n\nThe contractual partner will also be *EOS KSI Inkasso Deutschland GmbH,* who will then transfer the cases through our Cross Border platform to relevant local entities (EOS companies or partners depending on country).\n\nI hope this helps. ","2026-01-13T08:56:33.280Z"],["3805654","DGD-173","DGD","friedrich.vogt@bolt.eu","Friedrich Vogt","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Y5d26uljDZVWYWCehp1zdGF-chIwwmgn07XjWnX4yzY/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.mencigfo8uq8|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Y5d26uljDZVWYWCehp1zdGF-chIwwmgn07XjWnX4yzY/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.mencigfo8uq8|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T08:56:40.237Z"],["3805656","PFI-830460","PFI","angelika.kaleta@bolt.eu","Angelika Kaleta","Hey!\n\nStill waiting for an answer for the billing. Client expect us to provide single invoice, billing model was changed automatically without prior notice to us + we have legal obligations due to our agreements signed with them. Please respond. Thx!","2026-01-13T08:56:46.057Z"],["3805657","HS-28880","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:412d25be-980a-4f21-8e1a-c152e40d03ef], the confirmation letter has been sent for signing. Once completed, you will receive it by email. Closing this ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-13T08:56:53.141Z"],["3805658","PAW-15268","PAW","cristian.lupu@bolt.eu","Cristian Lupu","I gave this a JobSize of 2 since IMO the simplest solution is catching the {{User is not active}} error and forcing a logout (clear local storage / cookies)\n\nUncertain if this is just a symptom of a much larger issue with authentication within builder.","2026-01-13T08:57:01.736Z"],["3805659","DLVR-319","DLVR","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] why don’t we have dedicated sub-ticket for regional/local legal counsel for Q1 added here? Is it bc they haven’t added their hours?\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] \n\nLiisa","2026-01-13T08:57:05.855Z"],["3805661","PFI-829646","PFI","natalia.fronczuk@bolt.eu","Natalia Frończuk","Hi Team, I have received a few more complaints that the payouts they received are not matching their Earnings breakdown screens.\n\nDriver 1:\n\n* Name: [Jake Zerafa|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8365561?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FMalta]\n* Payout period: 29 Dec - 4 Jan\n* Payout received: 228 EUR\n* Link to payout: [232469122|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/232469122?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FMalta]\n\n!Jake Zerafa.png|width=1080,height=2400,alt=\"Jake Zerafa.png\"!\n\n\n\nFleet 1:\n\n* Name: [Valletta Fleet Noah’s Fleet Ltd.|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/111817?tab=profile]\n* Payout period: 15 Dec - 21 Jan\n* Earnings screen: 433.34 EUR\n* Payout received: 423.74 EUR\n* Link to payout: [230478898|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/230478898?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FMalta]\n\n[^Valletta Fleet Noah's Fleet Ltd..pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T08:57:25.870Z"],["3805662","DGD-174","DGD","friedrich.vogt@bolt.eu","Friedrich Vogt","Experiment design [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Y5d26uljDZVWYWCehp1zdGF-chIwwmgn07XjWnX4yzY/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.pfu9kyrfsl0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Y5d26uljDZVWYWCehp1zdGF-chIwwmgn07XjWnX4yzY/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.pfu9kyrfsl0|smart-link] \n\nNotebook [https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2313199745469119?o=2472566184436351#command/7292602953557020|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2313199745469119?o=2472566184436351#command/7292602953557020]","2026-01-13T08:57:26.690Z"],["3805663","RLONE-525","RLONE","laura.decampos@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Pereira De Campos","[~accountid:712020:bc7bca9c-4d13-42b6-9684-04014a47f7aa] perfect,\nfeel free to share feedback \n[https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScBsZQXkW8q1hqRAipP1JD40suRacqwehYcHqY2NmARGUS4Ow/viewform|https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScBsZQXkW8q1hqRAipP1JD40suRacqwehYcHqY2NmARGUS4Ow/viewform]","2026-01-13T08:57:27.968Z"],["3805665","DSR-3637","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}\nInternal note for Privacy - case overview and timeline:\n\n* On 13 December 2025, Rider opened a [case|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/703514801] with CS to report an issue with their ride. In that report, he already clearly requested various personal data related to the ride. The case was escalated to CSPC, but unfortunately CSPC replied “Not privacy related yet - kindly treat as a usual complaint for now.”\nAs a result, CS carried on with the case without addressing the user’s request for a copy of their personal data related to the trip. \n* On 15 and 16 December 2025, further requests for a copy of this data were left unanswered.\n* On 17 December 2025, the rider was [contacted|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/706792159] by CS and was offered:\n** A refund (rider accepted);\n** Information that the the matter was reported to the Metropolitan Police under reference SP-205540-25-0101-00 and that Transport for London was also notified.\n* On 8 January 2026, the user [submitted|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/720115630] the webform and requested a copy of their personal data linked to the ride and case at hand (the request is the same as the one submitted on 15 December 2025). \n* On 9 January evening, the case was escalated to CSPC and then to Privacy. The Privacy POC was OOO on the following Monday (12 Jan 2025) and thus only found out about the case on 13 Jan 2026. \n* On 13 January 2026, Privacy becomes aware of the case and starts sourcing relevant data with CSPC.\n{panel}","2026-01-13T08:57:32.721Z"],["3805666","PFI-832753","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:291ca72f-3929-4484-9fab-a29203ceb5ea],\n\nThis user is attempting to use the Bolt Food service with a discount, a discount that they are not eligible for.\nThe user needs to remove the aforementioned discount and then try again.\nKindly note that since I can see that they have absolutely spammed the confirm option, then they might be currently stuck behind a velocity check.\n\nPlease advise them to try again *without* discount applied in the next 1-2 hours.\nIf they argue about wanting to use the discount, then simply let them know that they are not eligible for it. Do not provide the user with additional promotional codes/discounts.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-13T08:57:49.957Z"],["3805668","PFI-832547","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 125.00 ZAR on 27/12/2025, 17:23:13UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 27th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T08:58:21.947Z"],["3805670","SCM-1074","SCM","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","The quotation for the reinforced handle (inner radius change + extra material on the handle outer sides:\n\n* Add 1.5 mm + 1 yuan\n* Add 1 mm + 0.8 yuan\n* Add 0.5 mm + 0.5 yuan\n\n\n\nNew mould cost:\n\n* Die casting mold fee: 48,000 yuan.\n* ETA - 30 days","2026-01-13T08:58:44.510Z"],["3805671","MM-919","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description, requirements, or acceptance criteria provided.|\n|Clarity|🟡|Summary is clear, but lack of detail makes intent ambiguous.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting sources.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-13T08:59:06.605Z"],["3805674","PFI-832716","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nChecked with United Payment and I can confirm the payment failed due to connectivity issues. \nThe payment has been released to the customer and the payment state has been updated in Admin. \n\nThis failed payment created a negative bolt balance for the user which has been already topped up. \n\nCheers, \nMarten\n","2026-01-13T08:59:56.457Z"],["3805677","DAEN-1301","DAEN","silja.mardla@bolt.eu","Silja Märdla","*@user-U06CT6YQKT6* 2 issues remain:\n1. I am unable to retrieve data before a specific point. For [this|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/45614?toggle=dat,vis] requested data set, I am unable to pull {{Surge}}data before February 2022. For the other [request|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/45783?toggle=dat,fil], I can't pull {{Orders}} before Dec 2021.\n2. We need a solid reason to provide the commission for the variance in the first submission, and this new submission","2026-01-13T09:00:45.001Z"],["3805678","DAEN-1301","DAEN",null,"Slack","[Silja Märdla|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63dd0f6fa5d0c826306adb04] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09BSV4UVD3/p1768293221857439?thread_ts=1765447789.215149&cid=C09BSV4UVD3|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09BSV4UVD3/p1768293221857439?thread_ts=1765447789.215149&cid=C09BSV4UVD3|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-13T09:00:46.143Z"],["3805679","LSS-61478","LSS","balthasar.scheder@bolt.eu","Balthasar Scheder","[^2025-10_MV_Bolt_Müglitztal_15.01.2026.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T09:00:56.129Z"],["3805680","PFI-832528","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe refund has been issued to the customers OPM instead of the Bolt Balance. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3985947347|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3985947347]\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T09:01:06.381Z"],["3805681","PFI-832681","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-13T09:01:16.629Z"],["3805682","PFI-832525","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T09:01:30.725Z"],["3805685","LSS-59845","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Question from Sentry:\n\n{quote}Just curious, all the previous comments made by your legal team are no longer visible. Does that mean our suggested comments were all accepted?{quote}\n\nAm I correct in understanding that we have accepted their comments?\n\nThanks!","2026-01-13T09:02:13.011Z"],["3805686","LSS-61477","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T09:02:35.301Z"],["3805687","DSR-3695","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T09:02:40.200Z"],["3805688","PRF-1230","PRF","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","Hi [~accountid:5d639884388d780dac23dfe7] do you have any english copies ready for launch markets?","2026-01-13T09:02:44.144Z"],["3805689","PFI-832267","PFI","alexia.matsangou@bolt.eu","Alexia Matsangou","Hello!\n\nThank you very much for your reply, I will inform the driver and will get back to you if any questions rise. ","2026-01-13T09:02:51.022Z"],["3805690","DSR-3557","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] – this is more of a consumer claim than privacy claim. \n\nPlease ask Tier 2 to escalate the Consumer claim relating to transparency of T&Cs.\n\n{quote}Dear *[DATA SUBJECT]*,\n\nThank you for your data subject request, which was received by us on *[DATE]*. In your request you asked us to provide the following:\n\n# Confirmation of how your personal data is stored and used, and whether it can be deleted.\n# Whether your identity data would have been requested if you had known you were not eligible to rent a particular vehicle.\n# An explanation of why the conditions to rent a specific vehicle were only presented after identity verification, and a request for compensation.\n\n*Identity verification and use of your personal data*\n\nBolt Drive requires identity verification in order to allow access to car sharing services. This process is necessary to confirm a user’s eligibility to drive a vehicle, including legal and safety requirements. Identity verification is therefore a mandatory step before a rental can be completed.\n\nYour identity data is used only for purposes related to providing Bolt Drive services, complying with legal obligations, and preventing fraud. For more information about how your personal data is stored and used, please refer to our Privacy Notice at: [https://bolt.eu/et-ee/privacy/privacy-for-bolt-drive/?category=boltDrive|https://bolt.eu/et-ee/privacy/privacy-for-bolt-drive/?category=boltDrive|smart-link].\n\n*Deletion of your personal data*\n\nYou have the right to request deletion of your personal data. You may request deletion of your entire Bolt account, or you may request deletion of specific data only. If you wish to delete only the identity verification photos, we can do so upon your request. Please note that deletion of certain data may result in you no longer being able to use Bolt Drive services.\n\n*Transparency of rental conditions and compensation request*\n\nYour concerns regarding the availability of vehicle specific conditions and the timing of this information relate to consumer and contractual matters. These issues fall outside the scope of a data subject rights request under the applicable data protection law.\n\nWe will forward your feedback to our Customer Support Team, who may escalate the matter to the relevant Legal department for review. From a data protection perspective, there are no grounds for compensation, as no damage has occurred in connection with the processing of your personal data.\n\nFor information on how we process relevant personal data, we refer you to our Privacy Notice at [https://bolt.eu/et-ee/privacy/privacy-for-bolt-drive/?category=boltDrive|https://bolt.eu/et-ee/privacy/privacy-for-bolt-drive/?category=boltDrive|smart-link], which includes further information about the categories of personal data we process, the purposes of processing, data retention, recipients, and your rights.\n\n*Your rights*\n\nIn addition to your right to access any personal data we hold about you, you have the right to request us to rectify or erase your personal data, restrict the processing of your personal data, or object to such processing. Any such requests will be assessed in line with applicable data protection laws.\n\nIf you are dissatisfied with this response or have further questions, please contact our Customer Support Team by replying to this email.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nBolt{quote}\n\n\n\nIf User requests deletion of their verification photos, please action the request by messaging verification team via email [verification-support@bolt.eu|mailto:verification-support@bolt.eu] in the following format:\n\n\n\n{quote}Hi team! \n\nCan you please help me with deleting this user's (hyperlink) verification photos? It was a part of their deletion request under GDPR and we're obliged to delete it.\n\nThank you very much in advance!{quote}\n\n\n\nThey’ll schedule the deletion – please inform the user that the deletion may take 30 days.","2026-01-13T09:03:03.867Z"],["3805692","LSS-61479","LSS","svenkristjan.bormann@bolt.eu","Sven-Kristjan Bormann","[^micromobility-invoice-187254769-0.pdf] _(28 kB)_\n\n[^AN-1264.pdf] _(77 kB)_\n\n[^Schadenersatzforderung_Bolt_Felix_Mueller_2026-01-12.pdf] _(1.55 MB)_","2026-01-13T09:03:28.958Z"],["3805693","LSS-61479","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nSven-Kristjan Bormann has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-13T09:03:29.623Z"],["3805697","PRF-1230","PRF","carelin.magi@bolt.eu","Carelin Mägi","[~accountid:628e5c9d8026a10068b1e457] Hey you can find all the copies and creatives from this [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1E6sB_ICMa1f7sm0gcGdXgiBVMTl5R04SA1tnGhYaTl8/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1E6sB_ICMa1f7sm0gcGdXgiBVMTl5R04SA1tnGhYaTl8/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T09:04:13.004Z"],["3805699","PFI-832767","PFI","stephen.nyabuto@bolt.eu","Stephen Nyabuto","!IMG_0916.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T09:04:32.136Z"],["3805705","LSS-61471","LSS","getter.tammeri@bolt.eu","Getter Tammeri","[~accountid:60918c062c2f6c0068da0d43] directing this question to you 🙏 ","2026-01-13T09:05:10.202Z"],["3805707","PFI-820795","PFI","evghenii.leanca@bolt.eu","Evghenii Leanca","Hi, any news when changes will apply? Thx a lot ","2026-01-13T09:05:50.706Z"],["3805710","IDC-2279","IDC","marina.gaponova@bolt.eu","Maryna Gaponova","As mentioned in [response|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C063CK8C540/p1768295151426199?thread_ts=1755779214.988149&cid=C063CK8C540]\n\nThere were 3 campaigns for provider {{24319}} to which enrollment was active during request time. Campaign ids:\n[564363|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-campaign/eater/targetedCampaigns/edit/564363], [549636|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-campaign/eater/targetedCampaigns/edit/549636], [540606|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-campaign/eater/targetedCampaigns/edit/540606] with 15% off discount.\nFor all 3 of them\n\n* Enrollment state = '{{active}}' (provider is still enrolled)\n* Campaign state = '{{aborted}}' (campaign itself was stopped, manually stopped, after it was approved)\n\nThe Admin Panel likely filters out enrollments to aborted campaigns, which is why it shows \"no enrollment\" even though the enrollment record exists.","2026-01-13T09:06:40.884Z"],["3805711","G3IOT-690","G3IOT","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] let’s also consider breathing for the availability light consumption optimization","2026-01-13T09:07:01.754Z"],["3805714","HWMISC-787","HWMISC","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] do you see a possibility for doing some initiatives also for Cobra during Q1 or rather something to be tackled in Q2?","2026-01-13T09:07:54.098Z"],["3805715","LSS-48761","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","13.01.2026: Slacked [~accountid:712020:a8e993c7-e089-4c7f-96d3-8d2e1ee4caa6] to agree syncing time with him on this topic. ","2026-01-13T09:08:01.706Z"],["3805716","RDS-1146","RDS","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] agree, also, the reference is also US-centric. Which is why we have been de-prioritising it in the backlog so far and focusing on other items first.","2026-01-13T09:08:25.197Z"],["3805718","PFI-817572","PFI","evghenii.leanca@bolt.eu","Evghenii Leanca","Hi, any updates on when the changes will apply? It’s been a month already, thanks!","2026-01-13T09:08:43.177Z"],["3805719","MM-921","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|The issue lacks detailed requirements, acceptance criteria, and edge cases. Only a brief summary is provided.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The summary is somewhat understandable but lacks context and detail for someone unfamiliar with the background.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to supporting documentation or references are included.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is provided on the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add detailed requirements, acceptance criteria, and edge cases.\n* Provide links to relevant documentation or specs.\n* Add a time estimate to the issue.","2026-01-13T09:09:00.361Z"],["3805722","PAW-20172","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* The draft announcement concisely describes the new feature to validate the branch HEAD after branch protection, preventing builds with outdated commits. This is essential for ensuring integrity during deployments. Missing information includes links to the component or panel where users can see or manage this feature and additional guides or documentation for implementation details.","2026-01-13T09:09:16.459Z"],["3805723","LSS-58469","LSS","rita.agnilleri@bolt.eu","Rita Agnilleri","Hi Elisabetta, \n\nplease close this ticket, the claim was already managed here  [LSS-59670|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-59670]\n\nThanks\n","2026-01-13T09:09:18.461Z"],["3805724","MM-922","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|The issue lacks detailed requirements, acceptance criteria, and edge cases. Only a brief summary is provided.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The summary is understandable but vague; more context and specifics are needed for clarity.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to supporting documentation or references are present.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time or effort estimate is provided on the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add detailed requirements, acceptance criteria, and edge cases.\n* Provide links to relevant documentation or specs.\n* Include a time or story point estimate.","2026-01-13T09:09:22.006Z"],["3805725","PIF-2210","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft provides a concise explanation of the newly added feature related to security requirements for auth responses by verifying the presence of the Cache-control: no-store header. This feature is crucial for maintaining the security integrity of our services and aligns with information security standards. The draft does not contain real links due to the absence of specific documentation or guide details.","2026-01-13T09:09:24.396Z"],["3805727","LSS-61102","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","13.01.2026: Together with regional counsel we will have a sync with stakeholders on 15.01.2026. \n\nContext:\n[+https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C05698E5UVA/p1766486278131249+|https://www.google.com/url?q=https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C05698E5UVA/p1766486278131249&sa=D&source=calendar&ust=1768724653795291&usg=AOvVaw3nRI2WEiWWMM4tgpa-IKbj]\nShort context:\n[+@pawel.orfin+|https://www.google.com/url?q=https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/UJBEX0CKC&sa=D&source=calendar&ust=1768724653795291&usg=AOvVaw28mYziqfCgSHE3jonzfHT_] raised an issue with Carrefour regarding the presentation of omnibus prices, which they claim is not compliant with regulations. The legal team reviewed the issue and provided recommendations on the necessary changes.\n\nMeeting notes: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lPJhhtwVkvqAsbZFtleko41KhG01f6qbE1Zs8YRkk_U/edit?usp=meetingnotes|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lPJhhtwVkvqAsbZFtleko41KhG01f6qbE1Zs8YRkk_U/edit?usp=meetingnotes|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T09:09:32.434Z"],["3805728","PIF-2209","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* The draft VI succinctly communicates the delivery of a feature allowing domain-based request validation. It covers the functionality for processing requests based on black/white lists, emphasizing its importance for security. Missing details include where to configure these lists and a guide for usage.","2026-01-13T09:09:33.332Z"],["3805729","PIF-2208","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft announcement focuses on the delivery of a read-only filesystem for containers to enhance security and minimize tampering risks. It addresses both service ownership and Infosec requirements. However, specific details on where the feature can be checked and comprehensive guides or ADR documents are not included in the Jira ticket and would require placeholders.","2026-01-13T09:09:43.063Z"],["3805730","LSS-55158","LSS","miroslava.gorejova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Gorejova","Hi [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] , I am coming back to you directly as I can see Julia is deactivated in the system.\n\nHere below the Client is sending couple of points they don’t agree with in “our version of their Frame contract which would be applicable for us” - if you can have a look.\n\nthank you\n\nMiroslava\n\n[^FRAME-Contract-Ramcova-smlouva-o-preprave-osob-en-US(2).docx]\n\n","2026-01-13T09:10:04.738Z"],["3805733","IDC-1488","IDC","marina.gaponova@bolt.eu","Maryna Gaponova","Waiting for response in [thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C093W0QFX1S/p1765370758365009]","2026-01-13T09:10:30.287Z"],["3805734","IDC-1497","IDC","marina.gaponova@bolt.eu","Maryna Gaponova","Is blocked by response in [thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C093W0QFX1S/p1765370758365009]","2026-01-13T09:11:08.167Z"],["3805736","WD-22540","WD","angelina.korol@bolt.eu","Angelina Korol","[~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] thank you very much for the explanation! The second entry didn’t have the supplier worktag — that’s why I saw a difference when checking the Trade Payables balances.\n\nIs it technically possible for the revaluation rule to add the worktag to both entries (for future revaluations)? I’m thinking whether I should periodically clean up these balances (worktag adjustment), or if this can be automated.\n\n!image-20260113-091106.png|width=1838,height=75,alt=\"image-20260113-091106.png\"!\n\n!image-20260113-090441.png|width=1784,height=59,alt=\"image-20260113-090441.png\"!\n\n\n\n!image-20260113-090356.png|width=1781,height=62,alt=\"image-20260113-090356.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-13T09:11:16.761Z"],["3805737","RS-1937","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey [~accountid:63d0ecd1d73cd1e44e22078f] ,\n\nAs promised on the Slack [thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08NXQK5WBH/p1767622856061459], coming back to you with an answer now that the new week is upon us. \n\nResearched Sustainability awards for projects and companies that have a global reach. Had to throw aside quite a lot of ones which were associated with an awarding organisation only with a one country reach. \n\nThe edie award is given out by an online publication operated from the UK but with a global reach of 100,000 sustainability professionals. The awards are given out by a jury but a number of them are, of course, from the organisations who also feature as supporters of the edie platform so it is not impossible that some lobbying and favouritism could be involved to receive an award. \n\nA more household name, Reuters, is also giving out a Sustainability award. There are a lot of [categories|https://events.reutersevents.com/sustainable-business/sustainability-awards/categories] and we surely could fit into one or few of them with a submission. \n\nI also thought about this from the perspective of potentially seeking an Estonia-based award but still advertising it globally with the reasoning that the Group is, indeed, registered in Estonia but our operations are global. Estonia-based awards, however, seemed to feature and favour innovation projects and start-ups. I wasn’t able to find something suitable for our field and size. \n\nWith the awards we can either submit for a MM specific category or company wide. Thinking about it from the corporate level only, one recognition to strive for could be the [Carbon Disclosure Project|https://www.cdp.net/en/data/scores]’s (CDP) ‘A list’. Pursuing validation of our carbon emission data by CDP has been on the cards before but  due to time constraints and prioritising Science Based Targets initiative’s verification, it was put on hold. Still, it is a possible way to stand out even more if we  sought their approval and to the level of recognition of being on the A list. \n\nOn the topic of standing out, are you aware that we are pursuing EPD(s) (Environmental Product Declaration) for some MM products? EPDs are a step up from LCA with much more rigour and the certificate would be publicly available on a database. We are waiting for the [standard|https://www.environdec.com/pcr-library/pcr_1031ae1a-861b-4662-9882-08dc8bad37af] to be released, currently pushed to later in 2026. \n\nAlso, I hope you have spotted in one of the Slack channels that Sustainability team is taking on publishing our first Sustainability report this year based on 2025 data, taking inspiration from [Voi|https://www.voi.com/blog/sustainability-report-2024] and[ TIER-Dott|https://ridedott.com/tier-dotts-2024-sustainability-report/]. This has long been asked for to be on the same level as competition with our tender submissions. \n\nLet us know your thoughts and suggestions based on my input above. We can take these for internal discussion with our leadership if the feeling remains that we ought to pursue something extra to stand out to win more business.  \n\nThank you,\n\nKadi ","2026-01-13T09:11:55.562Z"],["3805740","HWMISC-768","HWMISC","rasad.nadzafov@bolt.eu","Räšad Nadžafov","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] Yes, file is created, West region info is already synced in. Working with North to set up similar workflow as is already used in DE. File link added to ticket description (and [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1STOin8oIo6__KMD74M7am0LQIVMWT4KiICyOGMm-xQk/edit?usp=sharing])\nWill close the task once North/ROW numbers are integrated automatically (ETA updated to 15.11)","2026-01-13T09:13:03.924Z"],["3805741","FDBT-4787","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-13T09:13:13.362Z"],["3805745","PFI-832498","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T09:13:49.596Z"],["3805746","PFI-812940","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Apologies for delay, invoice reissued","2026-01-13T09:13:49.674Z"],["3805748","LSS-58369","LSS","mihaela.vatamanu@bolt.eu","Mihaela Vatamanu","hi [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] , sorry for the long time to get back here! the broker got back with their feedback. they are ok with almost everything, they just offered arguments for keeping one of the clauses 4.2., you will find their comments attached. thanks! \n\n[^251120 Bolt - VN SOW (Aon Contract) (DP Schedule Update 12.11.2025) (2).docx]\n\n","2026-01-13T09:14:06.276Z"],["3805750","LSS-61463","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^DD_Bolt Services UK Limited - BizSpace_12.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T09:14:13.955Z"],["3805751","PAW-14500","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-13T09:14:15.263Z"],["3805752","BEE-3637","BEE","adam.kudybinski@bolt.eu","Adam Kudybiński","[~accountid:5d807af94f9cf00d60213212] please come back to the requester and check if updating priority for these cases is going to work for them","2026-01-13T09:14:57.663Z"],["3805753","WFM-9960","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey [~accountid:712020:3a3742eb-3298-4df7-a8af-c0fd7279bf95] ,\n\nThank you for reaching out!\n\nCan you please, resend the attachment screenshot that you sent? It is too blurry, we can’t make out any details. \nLooking forward,","2026-01-13T09:15:23.895Z"],["3805754","LSS-61471","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Please find the signed document attached. Will close the ticket in the meantime, but please do let me know if we need to ship out the document as well. Thanks!\n\n[^Letter of confirmation_Bolt Technology OÜ_Markus Zimmermann_13.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T09:15:25.178Z"],["3805755","WEB-9593","WEB","samuel.oyekeye@bolt.eu","Samuel Oluseyi Oyekeye","Hi [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] \nI see the page design on figma includes buttons to the speakUp channel and app. Can we get the app link and if the channel refers to something other than the reporting page can we get a link to that as well?","2026-01-13T09:16:51.151Z"],["3805758","PAW-20172","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 9\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is generally well-written with clear intentions and problem definition. However, to improve acceptance criteria quality: \n1. Specify the success metrics by detailing what will happen if the build is stopped, such as notifications or logs. \n2. Provide performance benchmarks to understand the expected behavior after the fix is implemented, like the maximum delay allowed for branch updates before stopping the build.","2026-01-13T09:17:35.617Z"],["3805759","PIF-2210","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 8\n• Relevance: 9\n• Problem Definition: 8\n• Accept: 8\n• Suggested improvements: 1. Clarify the context: Include more background such as why the Cache-Control: no-store header is specifically important for security in auth responses and what risks it mitigates. This can enhance the understanding of the necessity of the change. \n2. Acceptance Criteria: Expand the acceptance criteria to include the exact parameters for the automated test such as thresholds, performance benchmarks, and how report success is defined. \n3. Define metrics: Outline specific, measurable success metrics for what constitutes a successful implementation of the 'no-store' header verification.\n4. Clarify endpoint scope: Specify any critical endpoints that should be prioritized or any known exceptions to the requirement.","2026-01-13T09:17:41.446Z"],["3805760","PIF-2209","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 10\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: ","2026-01-13T09:17:44.717Z"],["3805763","LSS-60509","LSS","mihaela.vatamanu@bolt.eu","Mihaela Vatamanu","hi [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] , Happy New Year! we found out that the initial employee representative was simply nominated and Tisco confirmed they are ok with this approach. we were able to nominate Sukvasa Wongprasertsri as the new employee representative. thank you! ","2026-01-13T09:18:07.311Z"],["3805765","PFI-832770","PFI","milana.biesiedina@bolt-outsource.eu","Milana Biesiedina","[^account-statement_2025-12-29_2026-01-13_ru_ead5f7 (1).pdf]","2026-01-13T09:18:29.276Z"],["3805767","PFI-832771","PFI","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","[^20260112_Rahalise_nõude_arestimisest-BOLT_OPERATIONS_OÜ_(OÜ__EUROTRADE_GROUP_).pdf]","2026-01-13T09:18:41.843Z"],["3805768","LSS-59467","LSS","andres.jogi@bolt.eu","Andres Jõgi","Hey [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] \n\nWhat is the expected timeline for ODPO decision?","2026-01-13T09:18:45.207Z"],["3805769","CSDA-282","CSDA","jelena.voitenko@bolt.eu","Jelena Voitenko","Hey-hey, getting back on this:\n\n*Samuel Tetteh*  [11:32|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D03N18USUF4/p1767691973731819]\n\nYes, the Supplier has access to the reports feature in sprout.\nThey are able to see what we have customised per market and they have access to also customise their own report to see what they need to see.\nThey have full access to all the reporting features, FRT, AHT, Incoming (Opened), Closed (resolved).\n\nThey have full access to all the features in the reports to be able to fetch what they need.\n\n\n\nHowever, as I mentioned, Sprout reports are not the same as our reports, thus not very useful for us","2026-01-13T09:19:07.081Z"],["3805770","LSS-58896","LSS","baaba.hammond@bolt.eu","Baaba Hammond","Huawei has come back and added some clause .\n   *Taxes*\n\nEach Party shall bear the taxes payable by each Party in accordance with the applicable law and agreed Incoterms (if any).\n\n \n\n*Withholding tax:* If Huawei needs to withhold and pay corresponding taxes according to applicable laws and regulations, Huawei will fulfil the withholding obligation and pay the net amount after the withholding tax is deducted to the supplier. In this case, Huawei can provide the withholding certificate issued by the relevant authority to the supplier upon request.\nIf the tax type and tax rate are adjusted, the two parties shall negotiate friendly according to the principle of fair tax burden.\n\nSupplier shall issue a VAT invoice indicating tax-inclusive amount to Huawei. The basic elements of said invoice must be complete, including but not limited to, the supplier’s and recipient’s name, address and GST numbers, invoice date, currency, VAT amount, etc. VAT shall be listed separately.\n\nHuawei reserves the right to return the invoices that do not meet the preceding requirements to supplier and supplier shall re-issue and provide qualified invoices. supplier shall bear all liabilities and losses caused by the unqualified invoice issued by supplier. If Huawei suffers losses due to non-compliant invoices issued by supplier and supplier shall indemnify the above losses.\n\nKindly find attached\n\n\n[^Bolt Business GH_Special Terms - Huawei Online Car Hire (3).docx]\n\n\n","2026-01-13T09:19:19.911Z"],["3805772","DSR-3585","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Incident reported here: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/701952624|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/701952624]\n\n* Forwarded to Allianz under _S-1090760_ ","2026-01-13T09:19:56.664Z"],["3805773","MM-907","MM","maksym.hayduk@bolt.eu","Maksym Haiduk","Research complexity and filter “event” only, if its too complex then hard code it.","2026-01-13T09:20:11.687Z"],["3805774","LSS-59845","LSS","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","I have configured our Sentry instance to be in the EU region only. Proof below\n\n!image-20260113-091954.png|width=1541,height=342,alt=\"image-20260113-091954.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-13T09:20:16.344Z"],["3805775","GRACQ-422","GRACQ","dzmitry.ulezla@bolt.eu","Dzmitry Ulezla","For create - {{delivery-provider-pos/adminPanel/providerIntegration/create}}\nFor update - {{delivery-provider-pos/adminPanel/providerIntegration/update}}","2026-01-13T09:20:22.249Z"],["3805777","DSR-3577","DSR","joyanne.njau@bolt.eu","Joyanne Njau","Hello [~accountid:603cb85ec58c720071175949] Let me have a look and get back to you on this. ","2026-01-13T09:20:30.073Z"],["3805778","SAI-1201","SAI","przemyslaw.wiczolek@bolt.eu","Przemysław Wiczołek","Done along with [SAI-1307|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SAI-1313?search_id=2e76e8e7-5374-42ee-a058-4992a2d2889d]","2026-01-13T09:20:55.488Z"],["3805780","DSR-3157","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Safety Incident Specialist response:\n_Hey, so this is a second report for the High severity case, even if it's not confirmed, there should be a Review Termination and in the case of this D, I will go with Termination, because person has a lot of different safety cases, rating reports etc. BUT - we have not sent out the termination email to the D_","2026-01-13T09:21:03.343Z"],["3805782","WD-22557","WD","brita.lubi@bolt.eu","Brita Lubi","Please make sure to provide access to both Workday and Workday Sandbox.","2026-01-13T09:22:36.826Z"],["3805783","WD-22485","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:641ae2031273131f2ae2333a], in order to proceed with mass maintenance, we need to add security to *Cancel Expense Report (Web Service)*. I suggest to assign *Bolt Expense Management Specialist* so that team would also be able to perform mass cancellation in future. If you think it is okay could you please approve? \n\n!image-20260113-092230.png|width=799,alt=\"image-20260113-092230.png\"!","2026-01-13T09:22:39.676Z"],["3805784","LEG-1133","LEG","michael.roberts@bolt.eu","Michael Roberts","Hey @Ana Abenza. As mentioned on Slack, I have added comments in the doc. 👌 \n\nRe: mystery shopper surveys, my understanding is that this involves Bolt testing service standards directly, but let me know if you had something else in mind.\n\nIs the intention to link the results to KPIs, either as standalone KPIs or as additional criteria? Either way, this would show Bolt directly monitoring driver service standards, so this is higher risk than rider rating based KPIs, but we can include such a KPI for fleets (e.g. if you think it is business critical / worthwhile set against it being riskier). If we did include it, then I think cautious fleets could view this as giving Bolt giving itself a unilateral ability to withhold incentives, for example by marking drivers as performing poorly.\n\nAn alternative that may ‘work’ is to run mystery shopper surveys without linking them to KPIs. If standards are poor and fleets receive negative feedback from Bolt, they remain incentivised to improve given the risk of Bolt cancelling or not renewing the arrangement, so you could have some impact with mystery shoppers without ‘express KPIs’. I appreciate that tying it directly to KPIs might be a more effective control (if fleets agree to it).\n\nLet me know your preference and I’ll deal with it in the document  👍 ","2026-01-13T09:23:02.874Z"],["3805786","LSS-60882","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","Hi [~accountid:5e0f07ab9a4b780d990e9fb9]! In my view, it is justified that we claim the fine from the user. However, since we expect him to challenge the decision, it may be more cost-efficient not to direct it to the debt collector. I’m also not sure how much the initial information about the lack of fine may influence the outcome.\n\nI consulted Matej on the above, I will let you know about the recommended steps once I hear back from him. Thank you! ","2026-01-13T09:23:27.011Z"],["3805788","FPD-1522","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","!image-20260113-091906.png|width=625,alt=\"image-20260113-091906.png\"!","2026-01-13T09:23:44.555Z"],["3805789","PFI-832767","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nWe could not find the 500 GHS payment made by the customer. \nThe 500 GHS payment was not sent to Bolt. It had the Reference: SportyBet LTD Collections. \nIt is unclear why the user thinks the funds are with Bolt. \n\nCellulant is a mobile money payments service provider and is used by Bolt and by SportyBet LTD. \n\nWe would suggest the customer to reach out to SportyBet to confirm 500 GHS has been added to their account. \nAlternatively they should reach out to their mobile money service provider to understand who was the recipient of their 500 GHS payment. \n\nHope this helps! \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T09:23:47.504Z"],["3805791","FPD-1522","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","We checked yesterday evening with @andrei.kuchev Zürich and Tallinn and they had different root causes for discrepancies\n\nfor Tallinn difference in s2o_conversion_rate -  in the generation of the S2O \n\n!image-20260113-092344.png|width=773,alt=\"image-20260113-092344.png\"!","2026-01-13T09:23:55.047Z"],["3805794","LSS-61478","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342008|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342008|smart-link], review ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-60617|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-60617|smart-link]  ","2026-01-13T09:24:19.045Z"],["3805797","PAW-14826","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-juri-gavshin\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160503\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 09:24:34 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T09:24:34.535Z"],["3805799","WD-22485","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[^Cancel_Expense_Report_v41.1.xlsx]\n\nPlease find EIB with data for latest list of expense reports that needs to be cancelled","2026-01-13T09:24:56.997Z"],["3805800","WD-22559","WD","bianca.medrea@bolt.eu","Bianca Medrea","Hey team, [~accountid:712020:aa053ee2-e95f-465c-b26b-662401a1de60] and [~accountid:712020:a975e2d9-679b-4d8a-a063-b831aafacd02] should also report to me directly; could you please speed this process up? I need to submit some bonuses in the system today, so it’s crucial to have them visible in Workday.","2026-01-13T09:24:57.499Z"],["3805802","WFM-9960","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey WFM team, agent [Aurelija Jovani|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-user/users/edit/382630?tab=details] has access to all the markets that she requested: Lithuania, Latvia, Estonia, Croatia, Sweden, Norway, Finland, Netherlands, Denmark, as well as *Outsource CS - Workforce Management.* \n\nCan you please check and give her requested access on Assembled, if necessary? ","2026-01-13T09:25:30.112Z"],["3805804","LSS-61481","LSS","louis.humbert@bolt.eu","Louis Humbert","!adhoc_dnd_all_components-preview copie.png|thumbnail!\n\n!adhoc_dnd_all_components-preview.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T09:26:09.654Z"],["3805805","PFI-829733","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, apologies for delay, all invoices now are properly fiscalized.","2026-01-13T09:26:33.479Z"],["3805807","PFI-832770","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for UAH 135.00 on Dec 29, 2025, 11:38:36 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 74987505363002333400213  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 29th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_Z7SD9DDTQWXDDSQ9_C4JGGN3FM6TS3NQ9.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T09:26:35.500Z"],["3805809","PAW-13138","PAW","mihai.casandra@bolt.eu","Mihai Casandra","Decided with SRE to be cautious and run a proper experiment to confirm the cost cutting for the new objects: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09S61106QJ/p1768229075403009|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09S61106QJ/p1768229075403009|smart-link] \nWill delay the rollout of mandatory opt-out intelligent tier storage configuration to legacy buckets until we have confirmation. ETA: 5-6 weeks.","2026-01-13T09:26:38.396Z"],["3805811","DLVR-319","DLVR","vincenzo.rinella@bolt.eu","Vincenzo Aglieri Rinella","[~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2] Cause the automations are still running 🙂 and I will give announcement in the slack channel when everything is done. We just approved the plan yesterday :)","2026-01-13T09:27:35.862Z"],["3805812","PFI-832775","PFI","blessing.otih@bolt-outsource.eu","Blessing Otih","!image-20260113-092459.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T09:27:36.862Z"],["3805813","PFI-832479","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nPlease note that pre-authorizations cannot be refunded as they never leave the customers account. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T09:27:40.847Z"],["3805814","PFI-812866","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, seems like one-off bug, I reissued the corresponding invoice.","2026-01-13T09:28:24.764Z"],["3805817","PFI-832442","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe payment status is refunded as of 12/01/2026, 13:18:33UTC. \nThe users funds have been returned. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T09:29:02.138Z"],["3805821","HS-28749","HS","patryk.wojtowicz@bolt.eu","Patryk Wojtowicz","Hi, I am collecting documents, I will attach them as soon as possible.","2026-01-13T09:29:37.952Z"],["3805824","LSS-60630","LSS","oluwatosin.ogunsanwo@bolt.eu","Oluwatosin Ogunsanwo","Hello [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] \nThanks for the update! Looking forward to receiving it.","2026-01-13T09:29:57.502Z"],["3805828","LSS-61288","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:dbef963c-e707-4042-8024-5afb4c08aa16] I acknowledge this is urgent and it is under review. We are currently working through it alongside other priority items. Legal will confirm once it’s approved—please don’t proceed until then.","2026-01-13T09:30:51.092Z"],["3805829","LSS-61481","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T09:31:08.220Z"],["3805830","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:dbc22d70-1983-4414-80b3-27f087787ae4] please could you confirm whether the rider has a card linked to her account? Would it be technically possible to issue a refund of 22.50€ to her credit card directly even though the payment method used was cash? \n\nThank you ! ","2026-01-13T09:31:14.269Z"],["3805834","PTWS-2073","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Also can you make all consent data not go through process approvals?","2026-01-13T09:32:20.708Z"],["3805835","LSS-61472","LSS","svenkristjan.bormann@bolt.eu","Sven-Kristjan Bormann","Case should be similar to [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57286|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57286|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T09:32:28.475Z"],["3805837","FIN2-942","FIN2","vincenzo.rinella@bolt.eu","Vincenzo Aglieri Rinella","[~accountid:638476d83e79f12e572272f3] should this ticket be yours?","2026-01-13T09:32:51.046Z"],["3805838","PFI-831984","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe users negative balance of 11.18 PLN is coming from this payment instead. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4024093884|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4024093884]\n\nWe were not able to capture the full amount from the user and charged their Bolt balance instead. \n\nPlease note that BLIK is an Alternative payment method and does not support dual messaging like authorization + capture. There is just capture. \n\nSince we are able to capture only at the start of the ride user will receive a negative balance if the ride price exceeds the initially estimated price. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T09:33:02.587Z"],["3805839","LSS-60293","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] - let’s wait a few days and see if they send any follow-ups. If not, then we can close the ticket 🙂 ","2026-01-13T09:33:10.684Z"],["3805841","LSS-59325","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:712020:0d5c2446-e91c-4d85-8707-d65ea96725bc] Apologies for missing this earlier. I will review and revert as soon as I humanly can. ","2026-01-13T09:33:31.415Z"],["3805842","PIF-2208","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 10\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: ","2026-01-13T09:33:37.510Z"],["3805843","PFI-831981","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T09:33:39.037Z"],["3805844","MM-918","MM","maksym.hayduk@bolt.eu","Maksym Haiduk","solved, not an issue its cost-calculator response just to know the metadata info","2026-01-13T09:33:49.995Z"],["3805846","PFI-831956","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T09:34:07.240Z"],["3805847","WD-21745","WD","ingrid.valgejarv@bolt.eu","Ingrid Valgejärv","Hey Steve! I wanted to check in - how is it going with automating this task? Thank you!\n\nKind regards\n\nIngrid","2026-01-13T09:34:09.612Z"],["3805849","LSS-61058","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks for the helpful context [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] - understood. The Belgian page should now have been published (there is indeed a delay sometimes between inputting the edits and the edits being uploaded). I hope this suffices 🙂 ","2026-01-13T09:34:36.153Z"],["3805850","PFI-831921","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 199.00 ZAR on 26/12/2025, 09:10:12UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 25th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T09:35:06.533Z"],["3805851","WEBSD-1469","WEBSD","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Thank you [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] ! Useful to see this for the future 🙂 ","2026-01-13T09:35:43.159Z"],["3805852","LSS-61258","LSS","sylwia.wiktorowska@bolt.eu","Sylwia Wiktorowska","Hi Giulia. I have only one concern regarding *“This Power of Attorney is granted without the right to delegate authority.”* From time to time, we need to delegate authority to our mechanic to retrieve a scooter in cities where we don’t have anyone from our OPS team. This would be very problematic for us. Is it possible to remove it?","2026-01-13T09:35:48.010Z"],["3805855","LSS-58530","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432],\n\nCould you please help us obtain *Ahto’s signature* on the attached PoA? We’ll also need a *witness signature on the second page*—this can be you or anyone from your team.\n\nOnce signed, could you please share a scanned copy with me in this ticket and then send the hard copy to [~accountid:712020:9123a82b-d263-4c1d-b16e-3f2a995b6f62] , at the address she will provide?\n\nMany thanks in advance!🙏 \n\n[^Elena's PoA (2).docx]\n\n","2026-01-13T09:35:58.657Z"],["3805856","DSR-3675","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Invoices sent out (/) ","2026-01-13T09:36:02.513Z"],["3805857","LSS-61466","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","[~accountid:712020:f7dcb856-08aa-436d-bc9b-34ba3f9585a5] - Please grant access to the document as well.","2026-01-13T09:36:08.590Z"],["3805859","BRE-1229","BRE","alexander.blinov@bolt.eu","Alexander Blinov","Delivery should be properly migrated, most probably they will not be able to do this in time. However, if I remember correctly, Delivery is out of scope for fiscalization. Better clarify with [~accountid:712020:8b906c76-e5e5-4982-a2e9-3b1fc964a2e7] or [~accountid:712020:fb07882f-e7b7-4ccc-a944-5b44db14f802]","2026-01-13T09:36:33.040Z"],["3805860","PFI-831843","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T09:36:48.896Z"],["3805861","PFI-831821","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T09:37:06.606Z"],["3805865","PFI-831794","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 11.47 ZAR on 21/12/2025, 09:36:28UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 21st of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T09:38:15.336Z"],["3805866","LSS-61280","LSS","marcis.bakis@bolt.eu","Mārcis Baķis","Hey, [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] and [~accountid:712020:ef6a9562-f9aa-4bb5-a4d5-2b18cc77085b] [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1syTMmBr9xzeFC4tnrwYmBtmLe26i3_i6CJ94h4wH-cc/edit?tab=t.0] is the draft, please review. 🙏","2026-01-13T09:38:20.288Z"],["3805867","PFI-831792","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 35.00 ZAR on 16/12/2025, 20:01:27UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 16th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T09:38:46.414Z"],["3805869","LSS-61112","LSS","jelena.glavas@bolt.eu","Jelena Glavaš","[^Nalog_Order_HR_ENG_17.12.25.pdf]\n\nhello team, contract was already signed \n\n[^Nalog_Order_HR_ENG_Bolt services (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T09:39:01.966Z"],["3805870","CNT-431","CNT","aleksandr.komolov@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Komolov","Hey [~accountid:6163ec849cdb930072d02e8e] I’ve updated our file according comments, in the [doc|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_eJq9XiyP5Vm5qnNy7ZeJVP4RSOkD1cgVM02M5XrzE4/edit?tab=t.0]. Text is slightly updated by me, but feel free to correct and improve it.\n\nAlso, new semantics were added to the file with [draft|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WHqq4dPScFLzlaWq-59FUcoXQSurbbpH0MPRTwQL9Wo/edit?tab=t.0]. Pay attention that the home page is usually a quite broad page, and normally it shouldn’t be too keyword-heavy, but there are some broad keywords we can definitely focus on. \n\nAnother useful addition is the inclusion of LSI keywords. I’ve added a brief explanation in the same file on how to use them, but to summarise: they serve as guidance on what we can include on the page to ensure relevance to our target keywords, rather than being mandatory terms that must be used.\n\nAnd one last thing that is not 100% clear is the new value props for Bolt Business. The only document I’ve found is this: [https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1gl07qhJwcUbdjfdVlAyz8w5SSsorX9kepRRQoM3_KwU/edit?slide=id.g39eec8b2f67_0_2553#slide=id.g39eec8b2f67_0_2553|https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1gl07qhJwcUbdjfdVlAyz8w5SSsorX9kepRRQoM3_KwU/edit?slide=id.g39eec8b2f67_0_2553#slide=id.g39eec8b2f67_0_2553|smart-link] \n\nBut maybe there are more of them. I’ve already asked Nick, as soon as he replies to me I will update the ticket with relevant information.","2026-01-13T09:39:13.211Z"],["3805871","LSS-60495","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","Hi, [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] no, Markus holds the shares through his company Mordor Management OÜ.","2026-01-13T09:39:20.350Z"],["3805872","LSS-48561","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:115f7041-7822-4d70-9ec6-a6159271466a] ,\n\nHaving in consideration the time elapsed, I will now close this ticket. Let us know is something else comes up and we will happily reopen it. Thank you!","2026-01-13T09:39:30.527Z"],["3805873","PFI-831790","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T09:39:36.572Z"],["3805874","LSS-61484","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","[^192533-E569136-04E---Demande-recevable.pdf] _(85 kB)_","2026-01-13T09:39:45.020Z"],["3805875","LSS-58369","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:f50af85a-3d8b-4b5c-b19d-ad552b86d158] - thanks. I will review and send a final draft back by Friday.","2026-01-13T09:40:06.803Z"],["3805876","PFI-831703","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Hello,\nFinal payout processed. \nPlease check if the payout was processed and if you encounter some errors on it, please do let us know.","2026-01-13T09:40:15.733Z"],["3805877","PFI-832786","PFI","sophia.ayison@bolt.eu","Sophia Naa Oboshie Ayison","!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 9.40.09 AM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T09:40:22.554Z"],["3805878","PAW-14820","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @daysleeperx\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160490\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 09:40:32 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T09:40:32.997Z"],["3805879","PAW-14819","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @daysleeperx\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17109\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 09:40:39 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T09:40:40.137Z"],["3805880","SREC-370","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Done in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREC-366|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREC-366|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T09:40:40.291Z"],["3805881","LSS-61256","LSS","lilijana.zaiceva@bolt.eu","Lilijana Zaiceva","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] , do we have an idea when the document will be signed? As usually we provide them within 1-2 working days.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-13T09:41:39.136Z"],["3805882","LSS-59015","LSS","gabriel.souza@bolt.eu","Gabriel Gonçalo","Hello [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] . Response sent. (/) \n\nThank you! ","2026-01-13T09:41:48.054Z"],["3805883","LSS-56824","LSS","karolina.jedrzejczak@bolt.eu","Karolina Jędrzejczak","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] Hey Aleksandra, can we re-open this ticket pls? Hope it’s the last time 🙂 Please take a look at my yesterday’s update. Thank you! ","2026-01-13T09:42:30.193Z"],["3805885","LSS-61258","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[~accountid:5bb399378eb5ad7760adb25e] noted, I have removed this part, thank you! ","2026-01-13T09:43:11.244Z"],["3805886","RLONE-509","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PRODWIKI/pages/4322492840/Scheduled+Rides|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PRODWIKI/pages/4322492840/Scheduled+Rides|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T09:43:36.796Z"],["3805887","FX-3617","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Meruzhan Kerobyan [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768297425573549]*{color}:\n\n\nLinked files:\n* [Screen Recording 2026-01-13 at 11.40.19.mov|https://files.slack.com/files-tmb/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A89RLH49K-ba5fbdce2f/screen_recording_2026-01-13_at_11.40.19.mp4]\n{quote}","2026-01-13T09:43:58.628Z"],["3805888","FX-3617","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768297431330289]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@meruzhan.kerobyan>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3617] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T09:44:04.689Z"],["3805891","RNTL-29728","RNTL","aytan.gurbanova@bolt.eu","Aytan Gurbanova","We don’t show banner on iOS [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RNTL-30237|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RNTL-30237|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T09:44:28.569Z"],["3805893","LSS-59165","LSS","arno.booyzen@bolt.eu","Arno Booyzen","[Outgoing ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/722389535] has been created to [claims@prime.co.za|mailto:claims@prime.co.za].","2026-01-13T09:45:20.420Z"],["3805895","DELIVERY-191","DELIVERY","varvara.kazakova@bolt.eu","Varvara Kazakova","26W3: UI/UX ready, animation is being polished by [~accountid:712020:f4c80226-e776-499a-9333-119bafdd4f4d] \nAdding more more excitement to progress bar was created as separate task for [~accountid:712020:f4c80226-e776-499a-9333-119bafdd4f4d] ","2026-01-13T09:45:32.861Z"],["3805896","LSS-58566","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:632a94a1-c879-41ac-8205-40429df7b583] !\nDo you have any additional questions and/or comments re this topic?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-13T09:45:32.960Z"],["3805898","DSR-3697","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T09:46:06.063Z"],["3805899","LSS-61484","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T09:46:07.940Z"],["3805901","LSS-59609","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:cb7d1436-9800-43db-821c-db7028a6ff03] !\nIs this ticket still relevant?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-13T09:46:16.280Z"],["3805902","PFI-829733","PFI","catarina.silva@bolt.eu","Catarina Caneira da Silva","Thank you [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] \nDo we know why this happened?\nThank you!","2026-01-13T09:46:25.913Z"],["3805903","PFI-831769","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nUnfortunately, the customer payments team doesn’t have any overview of the rental fine payments. \nI could not find any records of the fine payment failing. \n\nThe user is not able to switch the payment method to their own card. It has to be paid with the business method. \n\nMaybe you could check with the rental OPS team who would be able to issue an invoice for the user to pay off the fine with a different method? \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T09:46:40.192Z"],["3805904","LSS-59990","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:cb7d1436-9800-43db-821c-db7028a6ff03] !\nIs this ticket still relevant?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-13T09:46:49.067Z"],["3805905","DELIVERY-1114","DELIVERY","varvara.kazakova@bolt.eu","Varvara Kazakova","26W3: In progress. Planned: Design Critique, Product discussion\n","2026-01-13T09:46:53.672Z"],["3805906","LSS-60119","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Dear [~accountid:712020:240e5e60-baab-4e72-a388-591f4f4ec6a2] - thank you for following up.\n\nI’ve updated the agreement to include a new clause (no. 25) on data protection and added a clarifying comment for B4S.\n\nThis is based on Bolt’s light touch clauses on data protection and offers a simpler solution to advance this matter, as personal data transfer is limited—only name and phone number are shared by Bolt. This copies the approach taken in the Rescue Kenya Contract.\n\n*Detailed Summary of Key Improvements – For Audit Trail:*\n\n✅ *Independent Responsible Party Relationship* – It is now expressly stated that *G4S* and *Bolt (the Customer)* act as *independent responsible parties* under the *SA* *Protection of Personal Information Act, 2013 (POPIA)*.\n✅ *Limited Data Sharing by Bolt* – Bolt only provides the *name and contact phone number* of the individual in danger when the SOS button is triggered, strictly for the purpose of enabling *G4S* to coordinate the emergency response via the Emergency Response Platform.\n✅ *G4S’s Independent Processing* – Any *additional or special personal information* (including medical/health data) is provided *voluntarily and directly by the individual* to *G4S (or its third-party providers)* and is processed *independently by G4S*, which bears full compliance responsibility under POPIA.\n✅ *No Access to Medical Data by Bolt* – Bolt does *not require and will not have access* to personal medical or sensitive information by default, and such data will not be shared by G4S unless strictly required by law and handled in accordance with POPIA safeguards.\n✅ *Cooperation Obligations* – The clause includes express operational cooperation requirements, including:\n* Mutual notice and cooperation in the event of a *personal information breach*;\n* Coordination on *data subject rights requests*, with referral to the appropriate responsible party;\n* Assistance with *regulatory inquiries, audits, or investigations* by the Information Regulator;\n* Cooperation on *risk assessments*, where applicable;\n* Obligation for each party to maintain *records and audit trails* demonstrating POPIA compliance.\n✅ *G4S’s Responsibility for Sub-providers* – It is confirmed that *G4S remains responsible* for ensuring that any third-party emergency or security providers it engages comply with applicable *data protection and confidentiality obligations* under POPIA.\n✅ *Data Retention Period* – The clause includes an explicit *retention limitation* for personal information received from Bolt:\n* Data must be *deleted or anonymised within 30 days* of incident closure, unless longer retention is required by law or for legitimate regulatory, legal, or insurance purposes.\n✅ *Security Measures and Lawful Basis* – Both parties warrant that they:\n* Implement and maintain *appropriate technical and organisational security measures*; and\n* Process personal information only on the basis of a *valid lawful ground* under POPIA.\n✅ *Indemnity Clause* – A new provision requires each party to *indemnify and hold the other harmless* for any non-compliance, breach, or unlawful processing of personal information. The clause expressly states that this *indemnity prevails over any conflicting limitation of liability or indemnity provisions* elsewhere in the Agreement.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions. I will close the privacy sub-ticket if there are none, but it can be reopened if needed.","2026-01-13T09:47:03.208Z"],["3805907","SAI-1402","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Hi Team :wave:,\n\nWhile investigating a [refund issue|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07LQ8TDSSE/p1767949824639979?thread_ts=1767865037.281719&cid=C07LQ8TDSSE], I learned that the Alfred bot has started issuing automated refunds for micromobility rides (bookings). For regular orders, these automated refunds work as expected. However, we also have special type of order (booking) called *Bundled*, where multiple micromobility rides are grouped together and charged as a single payment.\n\nFor these Bundled bookings, the Alfred bot will need to perform a [few extra steps or checks|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C078D7V8DC6/p1739464505917969?thread_ts=1737465983.851699&cid=C078D7V8DC6] before issuing any refunds. To handle this we see two possible approaches:\n1. Enhance the automated refund flow to include the required additional steps for bundled bookings.\n2. Route all bundled micromobility bookings to CS agents for manual handling.\nPlease let me know which approach would work best for your team, and I’ll share further details accordingly.","2026-01-13T09:47:07.614Z"],["3805908","SAI-1402","SAI",null,"Slack","[Grzegorz Brotoń|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:f79c0085-d2cb-444c-a121-d9c86bb2bfca] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768216034078469?thread_ts=1768216034.078469&cid=C064FCFAT0S|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768216034078469?thread_ts=1768216034.078469&cid=C064FCFAT0S|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-13T09:47:08.606Z"],["3805909","SAI-1402","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Hey, so it is clear now, so we have to check if the payment is part of the bundle.\n\nFirst let's confirm if we have a reliable way to determine if the order is part of bundle payment. We do it in the following way:\nWe call {{commerce-gateway/internal/getPayment}} and we check if {{bundle}} is present:\n\n{noformat}    export interface PaymentResponseV5 {\n        ...\n        bundle?: BundleInformationWithPayments;\n        ...\n    }{noformat}\n\nIf it is we assume the order was part of the bundle payment.\n\nI see that in order to issue a refund first, we would have to cancel the bundle. Could you explain what that means in terms of the bundle and associated orders?\n\nI think we will just not allow for refunds which are part of the bundle payments for now, and later on we will figure out the proper solution. But before we do that, please help me clarifying above concerns. Thank you! :pepelove-2:","2026-01-13T09:47:08.972Z"],["3805910","SAI-1402","SAI","rushang.chauhan@bolt.eu","Rushang Chauhan","{quote} If it is we assume the order was part of the bundle payment.{quote}\n\nYes.\n\n{quote}see that in order to issue a refund first, we would have to cancel the bundle…..{quote}\n\nIt’s not about canceling the bundle, but about charging (closing) it. With bundled payments, the user is not charged immediately. We wait until either the bundle expiry time or the bundle limit is reached, at which point the bundle is charged (closed).\n\nGiven the current implementation, issuing a refund for an order within a bundle requires the bundle to be charged (closed) first. This is a known limitation of the bundled payments flow.\n\n{quote}I think we will just not allow for refunds which are part of the bundle payments for now, and later on we will figure out the proper solution.{quote}\n\nAgreed. Let’s proceed with blocking automated refunds for bundled payments for now and revisit a proper solution in a later phase. :thanku:","2026-01-13T09:47:09.748Z"],["3805911","SAI-1402","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","cool, let me do it then","2026-01-13T09:47:10.364Z"],["3805912","DBRE-7645","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Mid-report on the result\n\n{noformat}taxify_payouts                            | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_partner_payments_city24            | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_payout_client_account              | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_invoicing_payment                  | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_partner_payments_instant_payout    | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_partner_payments_yigim             | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_partner_payments_payout_generation | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_billing_adjustment                 | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_billing_payout                     | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_rental_car_billing                 | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_subscription_invoicing             | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_billing_user_tax_filing            | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_invoicing_tax_report               | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_business_invoicing                 | Conditionally OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_balance_user_order                 | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_billing_payment                    | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_invoicing_document                 | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_corporate                          | deprecated schema\ntaxify_invoicing_router                   | deprecated schema\ntaxify_invoicing2_audit                   | deprecated schema{noformat}\n\n* About Conditionally OK to disable nightly sync on taxify_business_invoicing.\ntaxify_business_invoicing(337G) in Invoicing cluster nightly sync has a dependency on taxify_business(1.9G) in Central cluster.\nBoth teams agree in disabling nightly sync; however, there are conditions:\n     (a) The sync stops at the same. \nor (b) taxify_business sync stops first, and taxify_business_invoicing sync stops later.\n\nPossible solutions are:\n     (a-1) Stop nightly sync for Central and Invoicing at the same time.\nor (b-2) Enable selective nightly sync for 49 schemas(7700G) in Central cluster and stop Invoicing cluster nightly sync.\nor (c-3) Enable selective nightly sync for taxify_business_invoicing(337G) in invoicing.\nor (d-4) Migrate taxify_business(1.9G) in Central cluster to TiDB and stop Invoicing cluster nightly sync.\n\nThe following solutions are unrealistic because:\n     (a-1) There are 50 schemas in Central cluster, and it will be very hard to negotiate with each team to make the stop sync.\n     (b-2) and (c-3) Enable selective nightly sync will likely have a big issue with large data size. Also, selective nightly sync needs all the infrastructure as it is and adding software complexity, so this solution is out of scope for this ticket.\n\nTherefore, the following solution is the only option:\n     (d-4) It is the realistic option. Also, the team mentioned that they have a plan to migrate the schema; however, it has not been scheduled anytime soon.\n\n* About the schema, which doesn’t have the DB owner team information.\ntaxify_invoicing_router : [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/INFRA-3350|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/INFRA-3350|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T09:47:20.807Z"],["3805913","SAI-1403","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Hey, so it is clear now, so we have to check if the payment is part of the bundle.\n\nFirst let's confirm if we have a reliable way to determine if the order is part of bundle payment. We do it in the following way:\nWe call {{commerce-gateway/internal/getPayment}} and we check if {{bundle}} is present:\n\n{noformat}    export interface PaymentResponseV5 {\n        ...\n        bundle?: BundleInformationWithPayments;\n        ...\n    }{noformat}\n\nIf it is we assume the order was part of the bundle payment.\n\nI see that in order to issue a refund first, we would have to cancel the bundle. Could you explain what that means in terms of the bundle and associated orders?\n\nI think we will just not allow for refunds which are part of the bundle payments for now, and later on we will figure out the proper solution. But before we do that, please help me clarifying above concerns. Thank you! :pepelove-2:","2026-01-13T09:47:37.528Z"],["3805914","SAI-1403","SAI",null,"Slack","[Grzegorz Brotoń|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:f79c0085-d2cb-444c-a121-d9c86bb2bfca] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768295161249279?thread_ts=1768216034.078469&cid=C064FCFAT0S|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768295161249279?thread_ts=1768216034.078469&cid=C064FCFAT0S|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-13T09:47:38.472Z"],["3805915","BEE-3602","BEE","adam.kudybinski@bolt.eu","Adam Kudybiński","Before proceeding, let’s evaluate the business value behind this change. Andri pointed out he had a task to hide some tiers, because agents were doing weird things and there’s a risk of immediate unassignment if the task is created in a restricted queue.","2026-01-13T09:47:38.696Z"],["3805917","SAI-1403","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SAI-1402|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SAI-1402|smart-link]  was a quick fix, we need proper implementation","2026-01-13T09:48:19.866Z"],["3805920","LSS-60929","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] , [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Annex no. 1 to intra-group loan agreement.docx (1) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-13T09:48:48.142Z"],["3805921","RLONE-511","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","It is allocated to a driver and not car.","2026-01-13T09:48:59.259Z"],["3805922","LSS-60122","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","Hi All, \n\n!image-20260113-094807.png|width=730,height=159,alt=\"image-20260113-094807.png\"!\n\nAttaching approval confirmation from management. \n\nAs soon as I have confirmation or feedback from the Landlord on the above topic, then I will let you know [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] ","2026-01-13T09:49:05.624Z"],["3805923","LSS-60735","LSS","alex.bucse@bolt.eu","Alex Bucșe","[~accountid:712020:66939b2f-e5c1-42e2-8cbe-244458fd12f9] [~accountid:712020:b0c68d76-b9b0-4476-8967-e1963bc1a6d2] as most of the conversations/discussions were directly on Slack, feel free to mark this as complete when convenient. Also just to confirm Joe approved this (also in Slack) For future reference, all discussions/approvals are stored in the [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C09L57LSKPZ|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C09L57LSKPZ|smart-link] #project-diamond-procurement channel. \n\nOr alternatively you can use this ticket to get Legal Ops to sign the EL prior to closing it. [~accountid:712020:66939b2f-e5c1-42e2-8cbe-244458fd12f9] ","2026-01-13T09:49:06.688Z"],["3805924","LSS-61258","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^PoA_odbiór_hulajnóg_kwalifikowany_2026.pdf]\n\nHi Team, please proceed with signing the attached PoA with Ahto’s wet-ink signature.\n\nPlease note that the PoA should be printed and signed in 8 copies, on a single sheet of paper, double-sided.\n\nOnce signed, please attach the scans here and send the original versions to the Warsaw office (Prosta 67) to Sylwia Wiktorowska, +48 508579795\n\nThank you!","2026-01-13T09:49:18.321Z"],["3805925","SREDESK-7408","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi Tekla,\n\nA change to your Okta user is needed.\n\nI contacted IT.\n\nAfter that, your user will have the Zero Trust permission required for CMS.\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-349203|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-349203|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T09:49:30.509Z"],["3805927","LSS-61157","LSS","mikk.vachtmeister@bolt.eu","Mikk Vachtmeister","No","2026-01-13T09:50:01.005Z"],["3805928","CORA-387","CORA","riin@bolt.eu","Riin Kotsalainen","[~accountid:712020:0d04167f-dce4-443a-8156-8acc576e7815] \nCan you also please provide us same overview for companies that are status: active and have done rides in 2025\n\nData points:\n\n|Company Name|\n|Registration Number|\n|Tax Identification Number|\n|Liable for VAT|\n|VAT code|\n|EC VAT code/GST|\n|Address|\n|Phone Number|\n|Email Address|\n|Payout details (separate fields on company page listed below)|\n|Account recipient\nIBAN\nBank\nSWIFT\nBank address\nBranch code|","2026-01-13T09:50:02.167Z"],["3805929","PFI-813668","PFI","nantawat.boonchu@bolt-outsource.eu","Nantawat Boonchu","Dear payment team,\n\nKindly follow up on updating driver commission on 8 Dec 25.\n\nThank you in advance.","2026-01-13T09:50:03.565Z"],["3805930","LSS-61228","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ! The rider has indeed one card linked to his account, but he never made any payment with it.\n\nWe do not have any way to send money to a card if there was no previous transaction, as our way to do so is a refund.\n\nWhat we could advise is to ask the rider if he can pay his next rides by card, so we would be able to refund 22.50€ after they’re done.\n\nI do not have any other way to refund in mind, we can enroll in a 15€ campaign on Beehive or provide additionnal promo code expiring in 2027, but the rider would be unhappy with it.\n\nLast resort would be a bank transfer, in that case we need to make a ticket to Commerce, it has been done with cases involving Europe’s center for consumer rights.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-13T09:50:12.247Z"],["3805931","LSS-60929","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Thank you [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] !","2026-01-13T09:50:42.382Z"],["3805932","DISC-3752","DISC","diana.brata@bolt.eu","Diana Brata","[~accountid:712020:82be5457-bc4f-4060-a784-a0e5cfa9744d], [~accountid:619f70219615eb006fe5a142] I just want to share a possible consequence of this change: if a brand has multiple providers, because of this and deduplication across categories, this can result in displaying only the 1, the closest provider for that brand, while currently multiple could be displayed.","2026-01-13T09:51:03.606Z"],["3805933","PAW-14829","PAW","mihai.casandra@bolt.eu","Mihai Casandra","Will exclude bucket {{bolt-fraud-archive}} from the experiment because it is only read by component {{./src/platform/commerce/fraud_logs_storage}}. Couldn’t find any node.js backend component that writes to it, the feature will have no effect in this case.","2026-01-13T09:51:05.059Z"],["3805934","HS-28894","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-13T09:51:25.994Z"],["3805938","PAW-14811","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/autocode/pull/52\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 09:52:36 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T09:52:37.049Z"],["3805939","LSS-50863","LSS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Hi [~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] , just confirming we will review the notes and the draft agreement in the ticket during this and the next week and get back to you.","2026-01-13T09:52:47.977Z"],["3805940","LSS-56824","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:590a0677-fdbb-4c13-9916-d32af1588d3e] ! \n\nThere is also wet-ink version, signed by Mahmoud is coming. DHL: [^1ZG8R4200418618140.pdf] .\n\nI have reached out to Mahmoud regarding profil zaufany.","2026-01-13T09:52:49.442Z"],["3805941","LSS-61128","LSS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","Hey Giulia, \n\nhas this been already signed by any chance? 🙏 \n\nThanks, \nEwa","2026-01-13T09:52:51.943Z"],["3805942","PFI-829733","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","The agent was missing one field, which caused our system to believe that “invoice is out of scope” → i.e. in suspended state. A bug occurred, and it was fixed now. Based on the error code, seems like its one such case. ","2026-01-13T09:53:18.392Z"],["3805943","BP-13420","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Tested on Prelive for all 4 scenarios:\n\n*AC:1* (/)\n\n*To or From* \nWhen the policy type is “To or From permitted locations”\nThen the ride is allowed if *either the first pickup or the last drop-off* is in the permitted locations list\nAnd intermediate stops do not need to be validated\n\nTests:\n\n# Start from allowed pickup location → Add multiple stops that are not allowed locations → Ride can be taken → Start ride → Then add another stop that is not on allowed location list → Ride allowed (/) \n# Start from location not on allowed list → Have multiple location not from allowed list → Ride can’t be taken (/) \n# Start from location not on allowed list → Have destination from allowed location list → Ride can be taken → Start ride → Then add new destination that is not on allowed location list → Ride can’t be taken (/) \n# Start from location not on allowed list → Have destination from allowed location list → Ride can be taken → Start ride → Then add new destination from allowed location list → Ride can be taken (/) \n\n*AC:2* (/)\n\n*Only From*\n\nOnly the *first pickup* must be in the allowed list\n\nTests:\n\n# Start from allowed pickup location → Destination on allowed location list or not allowed → Ride can be taken (/) \n# Start from not allowed pickup location → Destination on allowed location list or not allowed → Ride cannot be taken (/) \n# Start from allowed pickup location → Destination on allowed location list or not allowed → Ride can be taken → Add new destination and/or stops (allowed or not list both scenarios) → Destination/Stop successfully added and ride can be continued (/) \n\n*AC:3*  (/)\n\n *Only To*\n\nOnly the *last drop-off* must be in the allowed list\n\nTests:\n\n# Start from allowed/not allowed pickup location → Destination on allowed location list → Ride can be taken (/) \n# Start from allowed/not allowed pickup location → Destination is not on allowed location list → Ride cannot be taken (/) \n# Start from allowed/not allowed pickup location → Destination on allowed location list → Ride can be taken → Add new destination that is on allowed locations list → new destination successfully added and ride can be continued (/) \n# Start from allowed/not allowed pickup location → Destination on allowed location list → Ride can be taken → Add new destination that is Not on allowed locations list → new destination is not added and error is shown when trying to confirm new route (/) \n# Start from allowed/not allowed pickup location → Destination on allowed location list → Ride can be taken → Add new destination that is on allowed locations list → new destination successfully added and ride can be continued → User adds a stop in between initial and new destinations → Adding of stop is allowed and route can be confirmed → Try  to remove new destination from route → Route confirmation doesn’t go trough and  an error is shown (/) \n\n*AC:4*  (/)\n\n*Between*\n\nAll stops must be in the allowed locations list (Same as current behaviour)\n\nTests:\n\n# Start from allowed → Destination on allowed location list → Ride can be taken (/) \n# Start from allowed pickup location → Destination not on allowed location list → Ride cannot be taken (/) \n# Start from not allowed pickup location → Destination on allowed location list → Ride cannot be taken (/) \n# Start from not allowed pickup location → Destination not on allowed location list → Ride cannot be taken (/) \n# Start from allowed → Destination/Stops on allowed location list → Start ride → Add stop or destination that is on allowed list → Route confirmation works and user allowed to continue ride (/) \n# Start from allowed → Destination/Stops on allowed location list → Start ride → Add stop or destination that is Not on allowed list → Route confirmation doesn’t go trough and  an error is shown (/) ","2026-01-13T09:53:20.029Z"],["3805944","GRWA-1499","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","Date filtering has been enabled in all tiles and dashboard is working fine with different granularities.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.53.14.png|width=789,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.53.14.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.52.05.png|width=789,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.52.05.png\"!","2026-01-13T09:53:22.088Z"],["3805946","PFI-831766","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nThe order payment method was card, and the initial attempt failed due to insufficient funds. Following this, Bolt continued retrying the payment in line with our retry logic. The payment was successfully captured on 9 December for the amount of EUR 60.40.\n\nThe payment was not captured on 28 October. This date corresponds to the first retry attempt, which also failed due to insufficient funds.\n\nPlease note that customers are not expected to pay in cash when a card payment fails.\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T09:53:36.535Z"],["3805947","CCM-22272","CCM","miroslava.solarova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Solárová","Hello Ilia,\n\nAnna has been enrolled in the requested onboarding course. \n\nHave a lovely rest of your day! \n\nMirka 🙂 ","2026-01-13T09:54:10.598Z"],["3805950","HWMISC-836","HWMISC","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","h3. Hypothesis of the issue\n\nDragon battery does not allow charging when battery temperature is <3 degrees and allows it again at >5 degrees only. This is likely the window where there is perception that there is no regen. Voi & Ryde likely have better optimised temperatures (around 0 degrees). Dragon has this set as legacy safety feature, as there was a situation with Cobra fires and we wanted to be cautious around some of the safety features to opt more for safety.\n\n[~accountid:712020:7636318d-11ba-448e-8ae7-b935370c0640] did some ride tests in Oslo during 2024, and at sub-zero temperatures neither Ryde nor Voi regenerated during braking in sub-zero temperatures, Ryde scooters just started beeping informing the user to brake downhill as a safety measure. Both operators still use Li-ION batteries which we do, so cell chemistry wise we are all limited the same way. Janeli googled, NB batteries charge when >0 degrees.\n\nIn conclusion, this creates a perception that we don’t regen and they do, just during temperatures around 0 degrees C.\n\nh3. What to do to validate\n\n* Test Voi & Ryde scooters in sub-zero temperatures and try regen braking downhill to see if they regen or the feedback from LOPS is false. Agreed it makes most sense to do it ourselves for most control.\n\nh3. How to bring Dragons to the level of other providers\n\n* Test BMS FW where the allowed charging temperatures are adjusted. Check NB battery datasheet for how they have solved it and cooperate with TWS on the impact. Test the FW.\n\nh3. Input for future developments\n\nHow to facilitate regen braking in sub-zero temperatures for new battery/scooter developments? (brainstorm)\n\n* Let’s place a resistive load which we can use to discharge to in sub-zero temperatures when BMS can’t charge the corepack. Instead we would heat up the battery with the generated heat. As an added benefit, when we reach the temperatures when battery can be charged, we can continue with regenerative charging as well. Can be done either inside the battery or inside the frame. The coil can have multiple uses in different scenarios (pre-heating for charging etc.). Could double as floorboard heating.\n** Challenges:\n*** ECU feature development from Genfo\n*** Heat differences causing slippery floorboard\n**** Could be mitigated by some different floorboard grip material.\n* We could use hand-warming grips which for short rides could utilize the braking power to heat this. Combined with armguards (or wind deflectors) it can be a great tender feature and UX improvement.\n* Possibly throttle heating (avoid sticking throttles as in Tallinn..)\n* Seat warmer for EB1 can also be used as a heat transfering source\n* *Slightly off topic but still relevant:* EB1 higher speed coasting could regen slightly to offset some battery drop as mechanic cadence effort is low to maintain the speed. ","2026-01-13T09:55:17.115Z"],["3805952","MM-921","MM","maksym.hayduk@bolt.eu","Maksym Haiduk","Align with [~accountid:6305dd7403058426d64af3df] on this one","2026-01-13T09:56:08.181Z"],["3805953","DSR-3699","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T09:56:09.509Z"],["3805955","LSS-56824","LSS","karolina.jedrzejczak@bolt.eu","Karolina Jędrzejczak","Hey, they do not accept wet-ink version - the presence of the person granting the power of attorney is required at the post office in such cases. \n\nPlease make sure that he will sign POC’s for Bolt Rides and Bolt Poland with profil zaufany - both files in yesterday’s message. \n\nThank you so much! ","2026-01-13T09:56:44.083Z"],["3805956","MKP-9751","MKP","iaroslav.melnichuk@bolt.eu","Iaroslav Melnichuk","[~accountid:5d8df26bf2f0670dcb6dacbb] [~accountid:6401e59e9ce2cd2c240e8ddc] please describe configuration decision in desc or comments","2026-01-13T09:57:07.652Z"],["3805957","CCM-22271","CCM","miroslava.solarova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Solárová","Hello Victoria,\n\nThe request form you sent does not include an email address. Could you please add it? Additionally, which vertical onboarding should be assigned?\n\nOnce I have this information, I can proceed with the next steps.\n\nLet me know 🙂. ","2026-01-13T09:57:19.247Z"],["3805958","LSS-60487","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:5d844768-bae2-474d-8de8-69336d3a4dea] no worries! Do you need any further assistance here for now or can I close the ticket? Thanks!","2026-01-13T09:57:29.325Z"],["3805959","PFI-832740","PFI","sandra.davidsson@bolt.eu","Sandra Davidsson","Hey again! 🙂 Can you also mark 762, 541 payments as paid invoices? I checked now, but they still seems to look as unpaid in our system? ","2026-01-13T09:57:44.819Z"],["3805960","PFI-829733","PFI","catarina.silva@bolt.eu","Catarina Caneira da Silva","Thank you!","2026-01-13T09:58:07.451Z"],["3805961","PFI-829733","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T09:58:11.001Z"],["3805962","LSS-60199","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] , sure, please provide counterparty signatory name and email.","2026-01-13T09:58:15.107Z"],["3805964","RLONE-510","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","It seem to be sent as soon as the customer makes the SR booking, and if no driver accepts it or it is canceled 40 min before, the trip is sent as a on demand trip, but still reading to get a 100% confirmation.","2026-01-13T09:58:34.210Z"],["3805965","HS-28802","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-13T09:58:53.676Z"],["3805966","WEB-9087","WEB","vishal.kapoor@bolt.eu","Vishal Kapoor","[~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] No changes were done as part of this one. This ticket never made it to the board, looks like replica of something [~accountid:64009ca94307e46ad144aee7]  did?\n\nCan be closed","2026-01-13T09:59:31.253Z"],["3805968","LSS-60487","LSS","laura.decampos@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Pereira De Campos","No need for further assistance 🙂 ","2026-01-13T09:59:55.718Z"],["3805969","LSS-61483","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^Bolt Services PL_Zenoriah_Request for the landlord consent for sublease_(ENG-PL).docx (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T10:00:00.646Z"],["3805970","PFI-832794","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T10:00:03.196Z"],["3805971","LEG-721","LEG","emilie.chesse@bolt.eu","Emilie Chesse","[~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] do you think we could close this ticket, or is it still needed? Thanks!","2026-01-13T10:00:16.453Z"],["3805974","LSS-61128","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] any updates re signing? Thank you! ","2026-01-13T10:01:05.357Z"],["3805975","PFI-831984","PFI","milena.sukiennik@bolt-outsource.eu","Milena Sukiennik","Hello, But this trip didn't take place, so we should make the balance 0","2026-01-13T10:01:53.643Z"],["3805977","SREDESK-7409","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","\n\n* Schema has been created on prelive and LIVE:\n{noformat}root@ti-prelive-dba.sqldb:(none)>CREATE DATABASE taxify_iam;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.520s\n\nroot@ti-user-dba.sqldb:(none)>CREATE DATABASE taxify_iam;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.516s{noformat}","2026-01-13T10:02:14.098Z"],["3805979","FDBT-4786","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-13T10:02:24.558Z"],["3805980","SREDESK-7410","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","\n\n* Schema has been created on prelive and LIVE:\n{noformat}root@ti-prelive-dba.sqldb:(none)>CREATE DATABASE taxify_iam_gateway;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.519s\n\nroot@ti-user-dba.sqldb:(none)>CREATE DATABASE taxify_iam_gateway;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.516s{noformat}","2026-01-13T10:02:28.085Z"],["3805982","SUPX-2265","SUPX","raido@bolt.eu","Raido Kuli",":wave: How would you describe the upgrade experience with AI?","2026-01-13T10:03:22.660Z"],["3805984","LSS-56824","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:590a0677-fdbb-4c13-9916-d32af1588d3e] , here are the signed documents via profil zaufany (Mahmoud’s signature).\n\nSorry for previous misunderstanding!\n\n[^Pelnomocnictwo-pocztowe BOLT RIDES (1) (1).pdf]\n[^Pelnomocnictwo-pocztowe BOLT POLAND (ebdb6b98-0e0d-4cbb-bd0b-4e12d9e93abd).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T10:03:54.224Z"],["3805985","RLONE-506","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","[~accountid:712020:5d844768-bae2-474d-8de8-69336d3a4dea] I think this might need some more thinking, as I don’t onboard new FOs, is this something you are currently doing [~accountid:712020:0f7ea54d-49d1-4ea3-812e-c82192605f82] ?\n\nDid you create a document regarding the above, or is it a verbal agreement?","2026-01-13T10:03:55.262Z"],["3805986","SUPX-2265","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","pretty quick, there were some problems, but they were mainly due to old dependencies that we had. But all were pretty straight forward to resolve :+1::skin-tone-2:","2026-01-13T10:04:39.191Z"],["3805987","LSS-61128","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Ewa Ożańska PEL Bolt Poland (1).pdf] ","2026-01-13T10:05:34.759Z"],["3805988","PFI-823249","PFI","patrycja.kowalczyk@bolt.eu","Patrycja Kowalczyk","[~accountid:62026399c4e2c9006ae5fb59] Could you help, please?","2026-01-13T10:05:34.233Z"],["3805989","PFI-831475","PFI","yuliia.nenasheva@bolt.eu","Yuliia Nenasheva","Hello, team! Is there any update?","2026-01-13T10:05:41.521Z"],["3805990","DRX-27665","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","Tested and verified on DI.127.0 (194761070) using iPhone 11, iOS 26.2\n\n* verified match destination is only disabled / turned off when (x) button is tapped\n\n\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-13-2026 12-03-02 PM_1.MP4]","2026-01-13T10:05:51.451Z"],["3805991","DRX-27610","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27665 has been resolved","2026-01-13T10:05:57.322Z"],["3805992","INT-768","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","Jan 13: Note from [~accountid:6282158fc217e200698b7a4a] for Poland --\n\nuntil 2025: Bolt Poland → 2026: may need legal entity check. Delivery is provided by Bolt Ops.","2026-01-13T10:07:35.552Z"],["3805995","DRX-27736","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","Tested on DA.126.0 (1505) Firebase build on Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\n❌ When {{prod_is_new_online_button_enabled}} is set to {{true}} and the Earnings FAB, TTD, and Working Time block are all displayed on the home screen, the Earnings FAB overlaps the TTD in landscape mode.\n❌ When {{prod_is_new_online_button_enabled}} is set to {{false}} and the TTD and Working Time block are both displayed on the home screen, the TTD banner overlaps the Go Offline button in landscape mode.\n\n*prod_is_new_online_button_enabled: true*\n\n|❌ *Earnings FAB + TTD + Working time block*|✅  *Earnings FAB + TTD*|✅  *TTD + Working time block*|✅ *TTD*|\n|!share_2637219260700382182.png|width=202,alt=\"share_2637219260700382182.png\"!|!share_6117194325613746253.png|width=202,alt=\"share_6117194325613746253.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260113-115002-1.png|width=148,alt=\"Screenshot_20260113-115002-1.png\"!|!share_1930397271257754257 (1).png|width=148,alt=\"share_1930397271257754257 (1).png\"!|\n|!share_4880168471881068151.png|width=148,alt=\"share_4880168471881068151.png\"!|!share_8973319630087124593.png|width=148,alt=\"share_8973319630087124593.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260113-115010.png|width=148,alt=\"Screenshot_20260113-115010.png\"!|!share_6142112671095933375.png|width=148,alt=\"share_6142112671095933375.png\"!|\n\n\n*prod_is_new_online_button_enabled: false*\n\n||✅ *TTD*||❌ *TTD + Working time block*||\n|!Screenshot_20260113-113622.png|width=202,alt=\"Screenshot_20260113-113622.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260113-114812.png|width=202,alt=\"Screenshot_20260113-114812.png\"!|\n|!Screenshot_20260113-113644.png|width=202,alt=\"Screenshot_20260113-113644.png\"!|!Screenshot_20260113-114820.png|width=202,alt=\"Screenshot_20260113-114820.png\"!|","2026-01-13T10:08:20.958Z"],["3805996","RLONE-506","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","I will create a task to establish a clear Bolt offboarding playbook. Additional context will be added to the [Jira task|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/RLONE/boards/6805?assignee=712020%3A78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a&issueType=10000%2C10100%2C10101&label=Denmark%2CDK_Ad-Hoc%2CDK_Driver-engagement%2CDK_Expedite%2CDK_Fleet%2CDK_Marketplace%2CDK_Planning%26Analysis%2CDK_Riders%2CDK_Driver-Growth&selectedIssue=RLONE-810].","2026-01-13T10:08:35.884Z"],["3805999","HS-28252","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","Should be all done. \n\nBest\nAlice, People Ops ","2026-01-13T10:08:44.532Z"],["3806000","DBRE-7645","DBRE","andrei.fedorov@bolt.eu","Andrei Fedorov","[~accountid:5c2c61f8d254b55db84ca612] {{taxify_corporate}},{{taxify_invoicing_router}},{{taxify_invoicing2_audit}} (and others) were discussed in the original thread:\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CH2AKR18A/p1715757845118349|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CH2AKR18A/p1715757845118349|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T10:08:46.296Z"],["3806002","LSS-60581","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Summary of updates:*\n\n# Updated the agreement to include a new clause (no. 25) on data protection and added a clarifying comment for B4S.\n# This is based on *Bolt’s light touch clauses on data protection and not a DSA,* as personal data transfer is very limited—only name and phone number are shared by Bolt.\n# *No Access to Medical Data by Bolt* – Bolt does *not require and will not have access* to personal medical or sensitive information, and such data will not be shared by G4S unless strictly required by law and handled in accordance with POPIA safeguards. *In this case, the parties will sign a separate Data Sharing Agreement.*\n\nCC [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ⤴️ \n\n*Detailed Summary of Key Improvements – For Audit Trail:*\n\n✅ *Independent Responsible Party Relationship* – It is now expressly stated that *G4S* and *Bolt (the Customer)* act as *independent responsible parties* under the *SA* *POPIA*.\n✅ *Limited Data Sharing by Bolt* – Bolt only provides the *name and contact phone number* of the individual in danger when the SOS button is triggered, strictly for the purpose of enabling *G4S* to coordinate the emergency response via the Emergency Response Platform.\n✅ *G4S’s Independent Processing* – Any *additional or special personal information* (including medical/health data) is provided *voluntarily and directly by the individual* to *G4S (or its third-party providers)* and is processed *independently by G4S*, which bears full compliance responsibility under POPIA.\n✅ *No Access to Medical Data by Bolt* – Bolt does *not require and will not have access* to personal medical or sensitive information, and such data will not be shared by G4S unless strictly required by law and handled in accordance with POPIA safeguards. *In this case, the parties will sign a separate Data Sharing Agreement.*\n✅ *Cooperation Obligations* – The clause includes express operational cooperation requirements, including:\n* Mutual notice and cooperation in the event of a *personal information breach*;\n* Coordination on *data subject rights requests*, with referral to the appropriate responsible party;\n* Assistance with *regulatory inquiries, audits, or investigations* by the Information Regulator;\n* Cooperation on *risk assessments*;\n* Obligation for each party to maintain *records and audit trails* demonstrating POPIA compliance.\n✅ *G4S’s Responsibility for Sub-providers* – *G4S remains responsible* for ensuring that any third-party emergency or security providers it engages comply with applicable *data protection and confidentiality obligations* under POPIA.\n✅ *Data Retention Period* – The clause includes an explicit *retention limitation* for personal information received from Bolt:\n* Personal data must be *deleted or anonymised within 30 days* of incident closure, unless longer retention is required by law.\n✅ *Security Measures and Lawful Basis* – Both parties warrant that they:\n* Implement and maintain *appropriate technical and organisational security measures*; and\n* Process personal information only on the basis of a *valid lawful ground* under POPIA.\n✅ *Indemnity Clause* – A new provision requires each party to *indemnify and hold the other harmless* for any non-compliance, breach, or unlawful processing of personal information. The clause expressly states that this *indemnity prevails over any conflicting limitation of liability or indemnity provisions* elsewhere in the Agreement.\n\n*Status*: waiting for confirmation from business that no further support is needed.","2026-01-13T10:09:38.342Z"],["3806004","ADS-224","ADS","dane.david@bolt.eu","Dane David","-This seems to be already supported in the backend.-","2026-01-13T10:10:03.617Z"],["3806005","FIN2-943","FIN2","vincenzo.rinella@bolt.eu","Vincenzo Aglieri Rinella","[~accountid:63d0ecc7f386bda5dcab9d72] is this ticket yours?","2026-01-13T10:10:11.241Z"],["3806007","LSS-56824","LSS","karolina.jedrzejczak@bolt.eu","Karolina Jędrzejczak","Amazing, thank you very much for your help! ","2026-01-13T10:10:42.899Z"],["3806009","SREDESK-7408","SREDESK","tekla.chikhradze@bolt.eu","Tekla Chikhradze","Thank you, Amin!","2026-01-13T10:10:55.517Z"],["3806010","MLC-3771","MLC","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","*W3:* Finalising the response options with the Product & Hardware teams. Reached out to the Research team for their input on the current questions. ","2026-01-13T10:10:57.692Z"],["3806014","RLONE-506","RLONE","laura.decampos@bolt.eu","Laura Cristina Pereira De Campos","[~accountid:712020:78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a]  this was presented and updated during weekly updates in addition I tagged you and Ole in [this task|https://taxify.atlassian.net/issues?assignee=712020%3Aa64346d5-231a-4365-8d2d-9befbf6aa068&filter=-9&jql=statusCategory%20%3D%20Done%20AND%20assignee%20%3D%20712020%3A5d844768-bae2-474d-8de8-69336d3a4dea%0AORDER%20BY%20updated%20DESC&selectedIssue=RLONE-338] for visibility \n\nMy only task was to create never maintain it, which was briefed several times back in October and afterwards.","2026-01-13T10:11:40.118Z"],["3806015","WEB-9593","WEB","samuel.oyekeye@bolt.eu","Samuel Oluseyi Oyekeye","[~accountid:63874527f6c85b343c0b7f4b] Can you provide metadata for this page?","2026-01-13T10:11:51.296Z"],["3806016","DMB-1702","DMB","raj.parekh@bolt.eu","Raj Parekh","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7383515695/2026+Jan+-+Offline+hours+in+scheduled+orders|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7383515695/2026+Jan+-+Offline+hours+in+scheduled+orders]","2026-01-13T10:11:53.352Z"],["3806018","LSS-61050","LSS","dieulinh.tran@bolt.eu","Diệu Linh Tran","The supplier has indicated that they are willing to execute only their NDA. The reason cited is a clause related to contractual penalties included in our standard NDA.\n\nPlease advise on the appropriate course of action:\n\n* whether we should amend our standard NDA to address the supplier’s concern, or\n* whether it is acceptable to proceed with executing the supplier’s NDA only.\n\nYour guidance will allow us to move forward with discussions with the supplier while ensuring appropriate legal coverage.\n\n","2026-01-13T10:12:33.124Z"],["3806023","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768299185327059]*{color}:\nHi <@U03P58BK5FY> and <@U04FV4Z0GQ4> what are your thoughts regarding the above?\n{quote}","2026-01-13T10:13:18.392Z"],["3806025","FIN2-943","FIN2","laura.nurmela@bolt.eu","Laura Nurmela","[~accountid:712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] You can allocate to me, yes","2026-01-13T10:14:28.310Z"],["3806029","PRF-1783","PRF","beste.dulger@bolt.eu","Beste Dülger","Also have a TikTok Ad Account.","2026-01-13T10:15:17.439Z"],["3806032","DELIVERY-430","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W3*:* We fixed an issue discovered in December, we will enable the feature for the employees this week","2026-01-13T10:15:31.846Z"],["3806033","LSS-61488","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T10:16:06.960Z"],["3806036","DELIVERY-542","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W03: Feature was stopped during the code freeze. We enabled to employees last week and this week we are enabling it to a bigger audience","2026-01-13T10:16:36.811Z"],["3806037","LSS-59572","LSS","alistair.blaza@bolt.eu","Alistair Blaza","Hi team,\n\nJust following up on Mo’s earlier comment. Are we able to sign in this way?\n\nThanks,","2026-01-13T10:17:08.793Z"],["3806039","DELIVERY-999","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W3: Technical scope-out almost finished. We will start working on it from next week.","2026-01-13T10:17:40.158Z"],["3806040","PRV-1085","PRV","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","Questions reviewed by Samantha: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/14F9-3EohthnFGE9zr9RvkZCr969kzUO0z1xVF5qE2S4/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.aax1ti54tnhp|https://docs.google.com/document/d/14F9-3EohthnFGE9zr9RvkZCr969kzUO0z1xVF5qE2S4/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.aax1ti54tnhp|smart-link]  ","2026-01-13T10:17:40.897Z"],["3806043","L10N-27432","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27431](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27431)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T10:18:14.833Z"],["3806044","L10N-27435","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27431](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27431)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T10:18:17.157Z"],["3806045","L10N-27437","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27431](https://taxify.atlassian.