or Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27431](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27431)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T10:18:27.086Z"],["3806057","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Nazrin Nasibova [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768299516545549]*{color}:\nBalance movement and deposit compensation subtypes are non-invoicable and therefore cannot be used in this case.\nIs there any alternative compensation subtype available ? If not, you may request a new one by raising a ticket.  \n{quote}","2026-01-13T10:18:50.465Z"],["3806058","PFI-832797","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T10:18:52.462Z"],["3806059","DELIVERY-1540","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W3: We are starting the development this week. We aim to release it to the users in app version 104 (next release)","2026-01-13T10:19:12.397Z"],["3806060","LSS-61254","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:60fa95ef411fae0070ad24fe] \n\nBased on a review of the *Vendor Personal Data Consent Form*, completing this form *does not present a material data protection or breach risk for Bolt*, provided it is completed *only by the relevant Bolt account manager / designated representative* and not on behalf of Bolt as a corporate entity.\n\nThis form relates to Bolt’s *representative* *individual-level personal data*, not user data.","2026-01-13T10:19:20.864Z"],["3806067","LSS-61254","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Please let me know if you have any further questions. I will prepare to close the ticket. For signature support, please raise a separate Administrative support ticket.","2026-01-13T10:19:53.284Z"],["3806069","PRV-851","PRV","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (13.01)*+\n\n* Business has started to roll kiosks out in hospitals, in addition to airports. The highest GMV venues remain a priority ([link|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C097B56T3QR/p1768298929649589?thread_ts=1768219669.074219&cid=C097B56T3QR]).\n** Rolling out in hospitals is not necessarily an issue from a privacy law POV. Although the location concerns health, ordering a trip from a hospital does not involve SCD. We can argue that there is no clear nexus to infer anything about the data subject’s health. As such, no operational changes required, and purposes/legal bases remain the same.\n** The only area this affects is the risk profile of any data breaches - if data is breached, then the data is more sensitive. However, this does not require any changes to the system or user flow for now.\n** Ultimately, this would only require additional review if the name of the hospital location was particularly suggestive (e.g., a cancer clinic), although even this is a stretch (e.g., I could be visiting someone else). As such, *no operational changes are required for now for hospitals - it just slightly raises the risk profile*.\n*** *UPDATE (21.04)*: I confirmed the same to Merve here: [LINK|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C040NCWV75H/p1776789546607199?thread_ts=1776763082.613689&cid=C040NCWV75H].\n* We have launched in airports in EE and LV. Next up is AZ, TH and MT ([Link|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C097B56T3QR/p1768288762521569?thread_ts=1768219669.074219&cid=C097B56T3QR]).","2026-01-13T10:20:04.966Z"],["3806071","HS-28803","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-13T10:20:12.613Z"],["3806074","WEB-9593","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi[~accountid:712020:2bb94136-b4e4-463e-a0f6-8be773ff520f] \n\nSpeakUP app links: \n\n[https://apps.apple.com/us/app/speakup-doing-right-made-easy/id1573760238|https://apps.apple.com/us/app/speakup-doing-right-made-easy/id1573760238|smart-link] \n\n[https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.peopleintouch.speakup&hl=en|https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.peopleintouch.speakup&hl=en|smart-link]  \n\n[~accountid:62b2cf3033a882e2be49d95a] could you please support with a onelink here 🙏 \n\nChannel (same as “Report”): [https://bolt.speakup.report/en-GB/bolt/home|https://bolt.speakup.report/en-GB/bolt/home|smart-link]  ","2026-01-13T10:21:09.017Z"],["3806076","PFI-823249","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello [~accountid:712020:6fa15e67-72d3-46af-bdee-4c985e3ae441], could you please check with the finance team regarding the refund that was requested by bank transfer via their Service Desk?","2026-01-13T10:21:19.723Z"],["3806081","PFI-832795","PFI","ugne.guigaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Ugnė Guigaitė","Driver is also requesting a proof of payout","2026-01-13T10:22:21.058Z"],["3806083","WFM-9914","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! Please check and let me know if all good now, Driver Document Renewal via BH - Agent role was added for agents; Play more was removed for you. ","2026-01-13T10:22:35.308Z"],["3806085","LSS-61489","LSS","nicoleta.pandelea@bolt.eu","Nicoleta-Steluta Pandelea","[^Bolt x David Ioan_Agreement_January2025 (1).pdf] _(264 kB)_","2026-01-13T10:22:50.186Z"],["3806087","DRX-24780","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","Tested and verified on DA.126.0 (1505) - debug build using OPPO Reno 13, Android 15\n\n* Error modal is now displayed when “delete account” label is tapped while internet is disabled\n\n\n\n!mobizen_20260113_121619.mp4|width=418,alt=\"mobizen_20260113_121619.mp4\"!","2026-01-13T10:23:08.685Z"],["3806088","DELIVERY-1065","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W3:  {{M2: Optimistic price calculation on the \"View Basket\" button}} was not merged in 102 because of slower progress (we realised more things need to be implemented after design and code review)","2026-01-13T10:23:10.930Z"],["3806089","DSR-3637","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Invoice and credit note added\nRider and driver CS case added, redacted \nNo chat/call log between driver and rider found. ([comms history|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-channels/commsHistory?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A%2225%22%2C%22offset%22%3A%220%22%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22order_id%22%3A604114451%2C%22city_id%22%3A25%2C%22order_system%22%3A%22taxi%22%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FLondon] is stored for 30 days in the)\nPolice repot was made 17/12/25 ref nr SP-205540-25-0101-00, from a previous case I know that we do not have a copy of the report that was submitted because they fill it out online. [Confluence page|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SCCML/pages/3898183153/London+Police+Reporting+Met+Police] about the report.\nTFL report - Sent DM to UK case manager Vivien :loading: \n","2026-01-13T10:23:13.301Z"],["3806090","DRX-24746","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-24780 has been resolved","2026-01-13T10:23:17.138Z"],["3806091","LSS-60169","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:5f5b9372dd6835007546bdbd], please could you take a look at my comment from 17th December and investigate further? We’ve been chased on this one so it would be great if we could provide an update soon 🙂 ","2026-01-13T10:23:30.979Z"],["3806092","PAW-14835","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-alex-somai\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17113\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 10:23:37 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T10:23:37.976Z"],["3806093","DELIVERY-1515","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W3: Project finished","2026-01-13T10:23:47.836Z"],["3806094","PFI-832799","PFI","anna.zhou@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Zhou","[^report_13-01-2026_12-09-24.pdf]","2026-01-13T10:24:27.931Z"],["3806095","LSS-61264","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*BACKGROUND*+\n\n* On 19 December 2025, BCGL sent us a letter (unclear on which day we received) requesting camera footage.\n** BCGL represent Maya Elamrousy (Malta rider). Client booked a Bolt ride on 14 December 2025. Something happened during the ride which traumatised the client (another passenger acted inappropriately towards her).\n*** NB. BCGL claims to have attached a screenshot, but I cannot see one.\n** BCGL has asked that we “_elevate the camera footage, and any other possible evidence which sheds light on what happened, and to ensure that all evidence is preserved and not deleted_”.\n** BCGL has requested “urgent cooperation” (unfortunately, this ticket was only escalated on 8 January 2026).\n* CS has apparently already contacted the driver and confirm whether the vehicle was equipped with a camera (Beehive link has not been provided).\n** CS wants to know (if the footage exists) whether we can share it. CS also wants us to draft the response.\n* Based on my own investigation I do not have any information with which to identify the driver or the rider on our side. CS will need to provide this.\n\n+*THOUGHTS*+\n\n* This is a mixture of a DSAR submitted on behalf of a data subject as well as a general third-party request. This was escalated late.\n** Re the former, the deadline is 19 Jan (Monday), but the lawyer has not provided proof of authority to act. As such, we would need to request this before providing it.\n* If the driver does not have a camera, then we do not have any footage to provide.\n** In which case, we can offer any other data we can find (e.g., trip information, any redacted internal comments, etc.) as an olive branch.\n* If the driver does have a camera, then the driver is the controller of this data. As such, it is up to the driver whether to share it; we cannot enforce it.\n** The driver may no longer have it - this is up to them. We will then need to update BCGL accordingly.\n\n+*NEXT STEPS*+\n\n* QUESTIONS:\n** When did we receive the letter?\n** Where is the rider’s profile - Have we found this? If not, do we need to request contact details from BCGL?\n** Did BCGL attach a screenshot to their letter? If so, where is it?\n** Can you provide the Beehive thread with the driver so that I can take a look?\n** Have we confirmed whether the recording actually exists?\n** Presumably the lawyer did not provide any proof of authority to act.\n* Get CS to write back to BCGL informing them that we have received their request, and asking them for proof of authority to act  request personal data.\n* Depending on what we hear from the driver, we can either: (a) provide the footage; (b) provide limited data about the trip; or (c) flag that we do not have anything to provide.","2026-01-13T10:24:47.179Z"],["3806096","CMO-12988","CMO","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","13.01 - initial format, not language specific check done from my side\nTLs are still checking ","2026-01-13T10:25:00.964Z"],["3806099","CAMLE-9438","CAMLE","samuel.castaneda@bolt.eu","Samuel Castaneda","Trying Baca on this one:\n[https://jenkins.boltint.net/blue/organizations/jenkins/PL%2Fautocode-baca-autocode/detail/autocode-baca-autocode/161/pipeline|https://jenkins.boltint.net/blue/organizations/jenkins/PL%2Fautocode-baca-autocode/detail/autocode-baca-autocode/161/pipeline]","2026-01-13T10:25:10.755Z"],["3806100","XVER-313","XVER","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","phase 2 is UI changes and billing logic update and may not need MVRA input, but to be discussed cc [~accountid:712020:6f095333-c438-429c-9660-a9de5d845fe7] ","2026-01-13T10:25:11.665Z"],["3806103","CSDT-956","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15302|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15302]","2026-01-13T10:26:33.015Z"],["3806105","DELIVERY-45","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W3: Technical scope-out started. We are aiming to have the feature in app version 106 for employees and 107 for global release. Actual work will start in week 4-5 of 2026","2026-01-13T10:26:58.911Z"],["3806106","GEORM-398","GEORM","vlad.foamete@bolt.eu","Vlad Foamete","It’s hard to get a baseline for what’s the right color value but for start we might want to look into Google API to see if can make a comparison. ","2026-01-13T10:27:04.056Z"],["3806107","CSDT-956","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","* create semantic of dim_support_case_tier_history ✅\n* create measures in dim_support_case_tier_history semantic model that counts tier changes after escalation with certain tiers ✅\n* Create simple metrics for measures above ✅\n* add counts above to mart_support_case_metrics as a derived dimension ✅ \n* Re-generate mart ✅ \n* Merge nad backfill\n* create a metric that uses the derived dimension to get the count of escalated solved & closed cases without tier change post escalation\n* Use refinements to create dimensions for counts of tier changes → needed for deep diving and dashboards","2026-01-13T10:27:13.682Z"],["3806108","CSDT-956","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15302|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15302|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T10:27:19.663Z"],["3806109","PFI-798762","PFI","illia.drobzhev@bolt-outsource.eu","Illia   Drobzhev","Hello, team.\n\nAre there any updates regarding this request?","2026-01-13T10:27:20.945Z"],["3806111","RS-1938","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hi [~accountid:712020:996ce528-b0dc-49e2-89b8-a8b37096b3ab],\n\nThank you for your patience and as promised, here is my reply to your request. \n\nSustainability-related claims have been checked, edited and commented on. Please refer to the slides you referred to in the [deck|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eSEKjWFUEO3FoyGpvZ6wCjDHC5gG8CKE9yArEhxW67s/edit?usp=sharing]:\n\n* ✅ Customer needs\n* ✅ Our advantages\n* ✅ Product: Sustainability\n\nTo understand your scope a bit better, do I understand correctly that you are building a sales deck that will include Sustainability slides and these might look a little something like we’ve had in the past, see [here|https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/10TzBmfwBINXwppHMVdKV9jxS-W51u9fZJaYXcjcxrcQ/edit?usp=sharing]? If so, then I would be happy to reuse some of the slides from this old deck, update them and slot them into the new presentation you are creating. \n\nPlease let me know how we will proceed from here and what are your timelines.\n\nThank you for your patience again,\n\nKadi","2026-01-13T10:27:28.846Z"],["3806114","CRC-1987","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Business Case revisited and linked","2026-01-13T10:28:17.822Z"],["3806115","CRC-1988","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Business Case revisited and linked","2026-01-13T10:28:29.915Z"],["3806116","LSS-60908","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Dear [~accountid:712020:3b4c18b5-d699-45e9-b875-1c6e35fcf7f1],\n\nThank you for sharing this. From the Beehive thread, I see the customer received instructions to change their password but has not responded since.\n\nWe will assess the activity internally and inform you if further action is needed.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nPlease ensure that any future suspicious activity in the account is addressed according to this procedure: https:/beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/70724?country=global&language=en\n{panel}","2026-01-13T10:28:30.408Z"],["3806118","CRC-1989","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Business Case revisited and linked","2026-01-13T10:28:36.028Z"],["3806119","LSS-61489","LSS","nicoleta.pandelea@bolt.eu","Nicoleta-Steluta Pandelea","We also need Ahto's signature on this document.\n\n[^RO, Bolt x Influencers Contract, Robert Ștefănescu VDAY feb 2025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T10:28:36.868Z"],["3806120","LSS-60169","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* correspondence between myself and JF Law Ltd.\n\n[^Bolt Mail - Request for Information Ms Cheriess McCalla - Alleged Incident on 16 April 2025.pdf]\n[^Bolt Mail - RE_Request for Information Ms Cheriess McCalla - Alleged Incident on 16 April 2025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T10:28:49.801Z"],["3806121","CRC-1990","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Business Case revisited and linked","2026-01-13T10:28:43.022Z"],["3806122","BDB-1521","BDB","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","Hi [~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c] \n\nMy preference would be to keep this as is for a couple of reasons.\n\n1) We’re leading with a “get home safe” message because this is what we’ve discussed with the venues, I’m not actually certain that they’ll accept the ads if we’re light-heartedly promoting being drunk and this campaign is already faced delays because of the holiday period. \n\n# We need to add promo codes to track the campaign, the discount in the code is slightly better than the current sign up offer available. Ideally we’d have the ability to insert a promo code directly into a QR code but at the moment that is not a possibility.  ","2026-01-13T10:29:04.475Z"],["3806123","WFM-9962","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541702|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541702]","2026-01-13T10:29:07.688Z"],["3806125","RS-1938","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Forgot to add - please also rummage through the Sustainability Confluence pages referred to here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BFB/pages/7173866243/Bolt+Business+Deal+Desk|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BFB/pages/7173866243/Bolt+Business+Deal+Desk|smart-link]  \n\nIf anything catches your eye that you know BB clients are interested in, please let me know and I will tailor the content for your purpose. \n\nKadi 🙏 ","2026-01-13T10:29:33.315Z"],["3806126","LSS-60908","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Internal - to complete Cognito Form","2026-01-13T10:29:43.396Z"],["3806127","SUPX-2265","SUPX","raido@bolt.eu","Raido Kuli","If you think about the amount of changes and details it covered, if you had to do it manually - how much time do you think it would have took? Like subjective gut feeling opinion as it widely depends on how familiar one is with the code space and all those tools in general.","2026-01-13T10:30:07.692Z"],["3806131","MKP-9751","MKP","albert.tumanov@bolt.eu","Albert Tumanov","[~accountid:712020:d88f5976-1e33-47f5-acb2-a9c422493f69] [~accountid:6401e59e9ce2cd2c240e8ddc] the proposed targeting config [added to the Design Doc|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7298154538/2025+Q4+Prioritize+certain+drivers+for+orders+towards+airport#Implementation-Details]","2026-01-13T10:30:51.350Z"],["3806132","PFI-802926","PFI","guru.prasath@bolt.eu","Guru .","[~accountid:627b6b92f29dcb0068f8d1e0] could you confirm if we are planning to add logo for Hopp plus invoicces?","2026-01-13T10:31:19.797Z"],["3806134","LSS-61431","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:622b6eb2302c6b006af70509], thank you for raising this ticket with the Legal team. Confirming that I will be picking this one up and will get back to you shortly.","2026-01-13T10:31:30.441Z"],["3806135","FRAUD-5281","FRAUD","martin.lovisuda@bolt.eu","Martin Lõvisüda","We decided to increase the timeout from 2.5 → 5 seconds, to hopefully resolve most of the slow loading issues.","2026-01-13T10:31:44.736Z"],["3806136","PFA-568","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","Dashboard Referred: [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/25805?Case+Created+Date+(UTC)+Date=12+week+ago+for+12+week&User+Persona=&Issue+Key=&Dynamic+Timeframe+Picker=month&Case+State=-draft%2C-duplicate&Is+Partner+market+(Yes+%2F+No)=No|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/25805?Case+Created+Date+%28UTC%29+Date=12+week+ago+for+12+week&User+Persona=&Issue+Key=&Dynamic+Timeframe+Picker=month&Case+State=-draft%2C-duplicate&Is+Partner+market+%28Yes+%2F+No%29=No]","2026-01-13T10:33:01.668Z"],["3806138","LSS-61050","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[~accountid:712020:979961a6-5216-4ee0-aa85-a7302993f5e6] our standard NDA template doesn’t include penalty clauses – here you can find this template: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/3434252224/NDA+Non-Disclosure+Agreement+SpotDraft+Self+Service#%F0%9F%94%B9-NDA-TEMPLATE-LINK-%F0%9F%94%B9|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/3434252224/NDA+Non-Disclosure+Agreement+SpotDraft+Self+Service#%F0%9F%94%B9-NDA-TEMPLATE-LINK-%F0%9F%94%B9|smart-link]  [on the same page there is a localized one for Poland if needed] Please let me know if in such a case the supplier would be willing to proceed with this template. In any case, it is always better for us to proceed with our template and make eventual amendments. Thank you! ","2026-01-13T10:33:38.285Z"],["3806143","PIF-2324","PIF","mateusz.olszewski@bolt.eu","Mateusz Olszewski","This feature was already implemented. Alter automation PR generation now runs on PR open. [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/.github/workflows/alter-automation-skeema.yml|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/.github/workflows/alter-automation-skeema.yml|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T10:34:47.482Z"],["3806144","SUPX-2265","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Uff, good question. I’d say atleast a couple of hours (maybe even more) to ensure all deps, etc work as expected and finding correct versions to use.","2026-01-13T10:34:50.684Z"],["3806148","HWMISC-776","HWMISC","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","I asked Oslo to send 4pcs of Dragon front brakes with bushing to Tallinn to check if there is a way we could rework the existing stock of brakes to accept the LingDong bushing system \n\n\nI will put the task to “ON HOLD” until they arrive. ETA to be confirmed :loading:  \n","2026-01-13T10:35:59.795Z"],["3806149","LSS-58768","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Great, thank you for confirming [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] . Will wait for the feedback from Coachhub re/ the commented DSA which I shared in late Dec.","2026-01-13T10:36:27.006Z"],["3806150","BEE-3626","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko",":wave: and another update on this one - it was just released :xp-done:\n\none comment around it just to avoid any confusion - in the current implementation that \"Metric value\" displayed basically shows \"contribution\" to the total \"count of high-reopen cases\", which for each individual case is guaranteed to be 1 (as we are just counting total number of cases matching that \"reopened too many times\" criteria)\n\n:warning: i.e. it _should not_ be confused with actual number of \"reopens\" which was considered when \"choosing\" particular case for inclusion into that metric\n\nI think it might kind of make sense to include that \"reopen count\" somewhere in UI as well, but within current capabilities of underlying framework it would increase complexity and delivery time quite much - that's why feature released in such form, which I hope should still be useful :pray: - but of course if you have different opinions on it or there are any other comments/questions/concerns around this metric - please let us know, thanks! :bowing:\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8H4UHV9S/screenshot_2026-01-13_at_11.24.38.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8H4UHV9S/screenshot_2026-01-13_at_11.24.38.png|smart-link]","2026-01-13T10:36:37.049Z"],["3806155","MKP-8186","MKP","daniil.popov@bolt.eu","Daniil Popov","The {{order_search_filter}} table contains filters for a specific order. Previously, we stored the search category id here as well. But once we introduced the “any car” category, the search category may vary between order tries of the same order. Thus, the operating model must be stored on a per-order-try level, not order level.","2026-01-13T10:37:19.557Z"],["3806156","CCM-22271","CCM","victoria.petrov@bolt.eu","Victoria Petrov","[mihaela.kawinska@bolt.eu|mailto:mihaela.kawinska@bolt.eu]","2026-01-13T10:37:34.914Z"],["3806157","PFI-832793","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:1a432dac-5ac7-4448-8541-db565c574fba],\n\nWith the driver account they have not performed activities that would lead to loss of GMV.\nRider account was used intentionally to cause loss to us. The user will not be unblocked and the decision will not be changed.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-13T10:37:41.705Z"],["3806158","LSS-61486","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Assigning to [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] for tomorrow’s Incident handling session – we’ll go over it together. Scooter riders are the same as Riders for the demo purposes 🙂 \n\n\n\nCS KB was updated in the meantime – we’ll check what was followed as well.\n\n\n\nFYI [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ","2026-01-13T10:37:46.192Z"],["3806160","PFI-832028","PFI","akram.abubaker@bolt.eu","Akram Abubaker","\n\nHello [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] \nCan you please clarify what is meant by “card does not match the country”? The rider is using a *CAPITAL ONE NATIONAL ASSOCIATION* card while physically located in the UAE, and the card is functioning normally without any issues.","2026-01-13T10:38:34.243Z"],["3806161","LSS-60738","LSS","lilijana.zaiceva@bolt.eu","Lilijana Zaiceva","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432], is there an update on the ticket?\n\nThanks","2026-01-13T10:38:40.763Z"],["3806162","LSS-61368","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5], thank you for raising this ticket with the Legal team. I can confirm that the addendum amends the client name from “BOLT” to “Bolt Operations UK Limited” only - no other commercial or legal terms are changed.\n\nThis means the Slough unmanned office may be used *solely in connection with the Bolt Flex Private Hire Operator licence*. There is *no reference to Bolt Services UK Limited* in the addendum. Therefore, please can I check that you are happy with this set-up?\n\nOnce you confirm, I can arrange signing 🙂 ","2026-01-13T10:39:34.465Z"],["3806163","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you for your sharing the available options[~accountid:712020:dbc22d70-1983-4414-80b3-27f087787ae4] - the refund should not be conditioned on another ride to be paid by the passenger, or take the form of a promo code which is also only applicable to a further ride. The passenger should receive the refund of 22.50€ outright.\n\nI will create a ticket to Commerce in order to enable a bank transfer to the passenger’s account. Could you share payment link (would this be a link confirming it was cash?) and the driver profile link? \n\nThank you !","2026-01-13T10:39:40.678Z"],["3806164","LSS-61428","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342056|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342056|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T10:39:58.583Z"],["3806165","WD-22557","WD","birgit.puksa@bolt.eu","Birgit Puksa","Please aslo grant access to [~accountid:712020:07f1e332-abd8-45eb-a3b9-0dd3708ef2d7] \n\n\n\nBR,\n\nBirgit","2026-01-13T10:41:18.446Z"],["3806166","WFM-9962","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey, [~accountid:712020:d104a676-2567-4f06-9d5a-6d6965edaeb9] \n\n Access request was raised, and now it’s pending approval. It may take couple of minutes for changes to take effect.\n\nKindly raise another request if you need further accesses based on agent [~accountid:712020:93c5213c-e7c3-4813-b854-77e885560eb1] 's role requirements.\n\nHave a nice day.","2026-01-13T10:41:36.980Z"],["3806167","PFI-829610","PFI","sofija.danilevica@bolt.eu","Sofija Daņileviča","TEST","2026-01-13T10:41:41.274Z"],["3806168","PFI-829610","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T10:41:44.805Z"],["3806170","LSS-60946","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] - yes, please kindly proceed with informing the user of the nature of the unrecognised login.","2026-01-13T10:42:13.448Z"],["3806171","LSS-58899","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] - can you please take this forward with [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - shouldn’t be much required to complete.","2026-01-13T10:42:14.593Z"],["3806172","LSS-55403","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9], Marc has reviewed the memo and made two comments. Could we review and discuss this further to align ? \n\nComments: \n\n* *Category pricing*: I think that as we are not looking at this from a distinct category perspective but from a standard category with add ons, I think that adding a price per service (i.e. 5€ for pet, 1€ for child seat etc) would be possible. To be dicussed and verified with Ops.\n* *Service animals*: I agree with Marc that we should align locally on how we manage services for riders with an assitance animal - The pet category is mandatory for pets in order to avoid any cleaning issues or allergies for other passengers, how does this transpose for service animals? The global guidance (from [Flank|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08PM0Q9BUM/p1768301465554989?thread_ts=1768301415.585219&cid=C08PM0Q9BUM]) is the following: \n** Yes, we do have global guidance on how we manage rides for passengers with assistance animals.\nHere's a summary of our approach:\n*** Refusing an assistance animal is illegal, unless the driver has a health exemption. Refusing an emotional support or regular animal is at the driver's discretion.\n*** Neither we nor our drivers should ask passengers to prove that their animal is an assistance animal.\n*** If a driver claims exemption due to health issues, they should be asked to provide documentation.\n*** Passengers with assistance animals can book trips using any category (e.g., Bolt, XL); they do not need to select the Pet category.\n*** Globally, if a driver refuses an assistance animal, we consider issuing a warning to the driver.\n\nThank you ! ","2026-01-13T10:42:42.667Z"],["3806173","RS-1941","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey [~accountid:712020:996ce528-b0dc-49e2-89b8-a8b37096b3ab],\n\nHere’s the update on our input: \n\n# ✅ Sustainability 1-pager\n# ✅ B4B Overview 1-pager\n# ✅  B4B Overview slide deck - see also [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/RS/queues/custom/668/RS-1938|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/RS/queues/custom/668/RS-1938|smart-link] \n\nWhere I have made a comment in one of them, but not repeated in the others, it still stands and please apply it across all three deliverables. \n\nWith this, both this ticket and the slide deck specific ticket  are now back with you within the timeframe you requested.\n\nWe await your reply on next steps and timelines.\n\nThank you,\n\nKadi ","2026-01-13T10:42:44.307Z"],["3806174","LSS-57900","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] - picked this up in my queue from Aleks and would appreciate your support in pushing it forward/closing it out. Thanks.","2026-01-13T10:42:52.490Z"],["3806175","HS-28298","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Amendment signed by both parties. ","2026-01-13T10:43:12.591Z"],["3806177","LSS-56393","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] - another ticket I’d appreciate your support driving forward as I need to focus my energy on more strategic priorities at the moment. Thank you.","2026-01-13T10:43:39.973Z"],["3806178","LSS-61480","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi Susan! \n\nThanks for raising the ticket.\n\nBefore we get to task related questions - for future requests, it would be really helpful if Jira tickets included as much relevant information as possible (for example: background/context, objective of the request, impacted suppliers or contracts, timelines, and any commercial implications), with the required fields filled in and any relevant participants/approvers added at the time of creation. This helps us understand the request more quickly and move things forward efficiently.\n\nWhile this request is assumed not to result in additional cost for us, please also note for future reference that any matters involving spend or commercial impact are subject to the Transaction Approval and Signatory Policy: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BILP/pages/1525121359/Transaction+Approval+and+Signatory+Policy|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BILP/pages/1525121359/Transaction+Approval+and+Signatory+Policy|smart-link]  \n\nI’m happy to help if there are any questions, and you may also want to consult with your team as needed to check how they usually approach legal ticket creation 🙂 \n\n*Regarding the task:*\n\nTo help us take this forward, could you please clarify the following:\n\n# *Which suppliers are in scope* (e.g. all current suppliers or a defined subset)? Please list if possible, as we will need to check the main agreements.  \n# *Is the annex intended to be standard or customised per supplier*?\n# *How are the commercial mechanics expected to work* (e.g. fixed percentage of free spare parts, tiered approach linked to MOQ)?\n# *Are there any logistics or operational requirements to be reflected* (e.g. delivery timing, bundling with main orders, reporting or tracking requirements)?\n# *What is the expected timeline* (e.g. target date for finalising negotiations or implementing the annex)?\n\nThank you and let me know if you have any questions. \nVeera \n\n","2026-01-13T10:44:09.609Z"],["3806179","LSS-61490","LSS","brendanasomah.stahl@bolt.eu","Brendan Asomah Stahl","[^MTS 2 - Bolt Cooperation Agreement - Germany.docx.pdf] _(485 kB)_","2026-01-13T10:44:27.589Z"],["3806181","LSS-61368","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Hi [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f], yes it’s fine for the agreement to state Bolt Operations UK. Thanks.","2026-01-13T10:44:42.907Z"],["3806183","PFI-832676","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","U128 is indication of outbound bank not active, we have resent their available balance here https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233602754 ","2026-01-13T10:45:15.667Z"],["3806184","LSS-60753","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hey [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] 🙂 \n\nHere’s your 2nd People PPRA — for Greenhouse Real Talent.\n\nCan you prepare a draft in line with the context in the Parent Ticket, and share in this Ticket for my review?\n\nThank you.","2026-01-13T10:45:25.370Z"],["3806185","PFI-831984","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:712020:62769622-0528-4eb3-a492-063568681855] \n\nHere is the finisher order. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2337766377/307?orderTryId=3004627899|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2337766377/307?orderTryId=3004627899]\n\nThe CS teams own the refunding process. \nIf you think the user should be refunded then you can issue a BB refund for the customer to eliminate the negative balance. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T10:45:45.418Z"],["3806188","PFI-832819","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-13T10:46:04.917Z"],["3806189","PFI-830486","PFI","judith.hutschemaekers@bolt.eu","Judith Hutschemaekers","money was paid out","2026-01-13T10:46:09.600Z"],["3806190","LSS-61368","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Thank you [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5]!\n\n*Legal Ops:* please can you arrange for the attached to be signed by *Alex Wong* on behalf of *Bolt Operations UK Limited* - thank you in advance! 🙏 \n\n[^Name Change Addendum - BOLT (cce04e79-4b62-4428-984f-136394df90e9).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T10:46:16.613Z"],["3806192","LSS-61492","LSS","risto.kukk@bolt.eu","Risto Kukk","[^ADDENDUM BOLT (T) LIMITED  ADDITIONAL SPACE 3 2026 (1).pdf] _(97 kB)_","2026-01-13T10:46:43.843Z"],["3806194","RLONE-813","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1feK8N2wgo_5mCIjDumkXkBP2CKX8N3sWk5FVeH7jGFM/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1feK8N2wgo_5mCIjDumkXkBP2CKX8N3sWk5FVeH7jGFM/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T10:46:59.816Z"],["3806195","LSS-61228","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","I totally agree the available options are not ideal in this case. \nHere are the infos you could need for the ticket  [+Order+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1494055239/18?orderTryId=2824714159] - [+Rider+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/293952193] - [+Beehive case+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/710550573]\nWe do not have any payment link for cash rides, but the order page shows it was cash.\n\nI added you in a [similar case|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-808950] for inspiration 😉 ","2026-01-13T10:47:04.727Z"],["3806197","LSS-60939","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:614ae82ed747e80075f8baa5] ! I am on it, thank you!","2026-01-13T10:47:19.058Z"],["3806198","PFI-832028","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:83a000cd-5967-452e-8bb6-d8947c29e435],\n\nWe have had incidents involving this scheme that has caused us financial losses, therefore we have strictened the rule for *scheduled booking* - this means that normal orders will go through as per usual.\nThe card is still foreign, and not AE card.\nPlease see the picture attached below.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 12.45.39.png|width=205,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 12.45.39.png\"!\n\nThese types of cards will not be able to place scheduled bookings.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-13T10:47:37.166Z"],["3806200","PFI-832715","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","This error is indication of recipient bank not active, payment can be resent. This driver has chosen cashout today to receive their funds. ","2026-01-13T10:48:37.278Z"],["3806202","CAMLE-9438","CAMLE","samuel.castaneda@bolt.eu","Samuel Castaneda","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160535|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160535|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T10:49:31.084Z"],["3806203","INT-686","INT","olga.vyrostko@bolt.eu","Olga Vyrostko","[~accountid:62a9857bd0132d0068809cdd] Will accumulate from subtasks","2026-01-13T10:49:33.957Z"],["3806204","UI-827","UI","elina.eltmaa@bolt.eu","Elina Eltmaa","Created variations of Tab, using examples of Eater and Rides apps \n\n# Unselected tab font weight to {{Compact Regular}}\n# Unselected tab font weight to {{Compact Regular}}; added {{24 px}} padding to the sides of the tab\n# Unselected tab font weight to {{Compact Regular}}; added {{24 px}} padding to the sides of the tab; added {{12 px}} padding inside the TabItem\n# Unselected tab font weight to {{Compact Regular}}; added {{24 px}} padding to the sides of the tab; added {{12 px}} padding inside the TabItem and changed the underline from {{3 px to 2 px}}","2026-01-13T10:49:47.638Z"],["3806206","SUPX-2265","SUPX","raido@bolt.eu","Raido Kuli","If there was anything specific that should have been done out of the box related to ESLint, Prettier, tsconfig etc. please let me know, we can adjust the prompts :)","2026-01-13T10:50:06.794Z"],["3806207","LSS-60855","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:619628e6b0b630006a6d2919] please see below the revised version but keeping our proposal for not specifying the exact dates. Please let me know if anything else is needed here.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PFfrqXbbxKWdmuxDMSaqDylB5ove_7CP/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PFfrqXbbxKWdmuxDMSaqDylB5ove_7CP/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T10:50:07.433Z"],["3806208","BDB-1494","BDB","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Hi [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] yes ok but we cannot delay any further than today please! thank you!","2026-01-13T10:50:08.179Z"],["3806209","INT-686","INT","olga.vyrostko@bolt.eu","Olga Vyrostko","*26W3*: Main development and e2e testing is finished. Small new tasks are added as a result of e2e testing, would be taken and finished this week. ","2026-01-13T10:50:24.753Z"],["3806210","CSDA-281","CSDA","polina.fateeva@bolt.eu","Polina Fateeva","It would be amazing is to be able to filter call-backs triggered by an abandoned call. Meaning, to be able to export all “abandoned call” callback links for analysis, etc. but also check the overall volume of them (successful/unsuccessful).\n\nThe only other thing that would be curious to see long-term is the response time (e.g. how soon after the first call being abandoned the callback request was made) - unsure if it is possible with the existing views, but please let me know! \n\nThanks so much!","2026-01-13T10:50:59.088Z"],["3806211","DSR-3701","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T10:51:06.655Z"],["3806213","LSS-60557","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","Hey [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] Everything is fine. They accepted corrected versions 🙂 \n\nWe can proceed with signatures 😄 ","2026-01-13T10:51:27.023Z"],["3806216","LSS-58530","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] ! Alright, will perform ASAP. I am on it.","2026-01-13T10:51:52.102Z"],["3806217","WFM-9899","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! Role was added; Wish you a great day!","2026-01-13T10:52:01.872Z"],["3806218","LSS-61256","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bolt Inbank confirmation (Nataliya Rodevich) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-13T10:52:34.848Z"],["3806220","PFI-832831","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T10:53:19.612Z"],["3806221","PFI-832726","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Available balance has been resent","2026-01-13T10:53:28.468Z"],["3806222","GUM-37","GUM","octavian.moraru@bolt.eu","Octavian Moraru","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09NS2H0C48/p1768301589309579|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09NS2H0C48/p1768301589309579]","2026-01-13T10:53:37.406Z"],["3806223","PFI-832724","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Available balance has been resent","2026-01-13T10:53:41.664Z"],["3806224","WFM-9920","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! Totally understand but we need a process for this, Can you share the KB link for this? 🙏 ","2026-01-13T10:53:46.584Z"],["3806225","PFI-832705","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Available balance has been resent","2026-01-13T10:53:53.337Z"],["3806226","PFI-832830","PFI","valdas.jocas@bolt-outsource.eu","Valdas Jocas","[~accountid:5e7c8e7379f5ad0c3411d7e0] ","2026-01-13T10:54:00.627Z"],["3806230","BEE-3626","BEE",null,"Slack","Hey Stas, thanks a lot for the update and for calling this out so clearly :pray:\n This makes total sense and we’re fully aligned with the current implementation.\nWe’ll make sure to clearly communicate to TLs/Managers that the metric value represents the count of high-reopen cases (each contributing “1”), and not the actual reopen number per case, to avoid any confusion on the Ops side.\nCompletely understand the trade-off around showing the actual reopen count in the UI even in its current form this is already very valuable and actionable for queue monitoring, coaching, and early intervention. The teams are genuinely excited about this addition.\nThanks again to you and the team for pushing this through so quickly :raised_hands:\n If any feedback comes up from usage, we’ll consolidate and share it with you.","2026-01-13T10:54:57.792Z"],["3806234","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you [~accountid:712020:dbc22d70-1983-4414-80b3-27f087787ae4] this is very helpful !\n\nI have raised a ticket to Commerce here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-832832?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-832832?created=true|smart-link] \n\nI will wait for their confirmation on whether we can issue the refund by bank transfer before drafting the letter of response to the passenger. ","2026-01-13T10:55:27.338Z"],["3806237","PFI-832467","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hey,\n\n*the 1st report Monthly report* was issued accidentally - we only use it in Spain atm. So, it should be ignored for now.\n\n*the commission invoice and app:*\n\nIn Estonia we have commission netting.\n\n_Through commission netting, your campaigns/bonuses/compensations are reflected as a discount from your commission, instead of each having their individual invoices. Simply, your commission is reduced in the amount of your campaigns/bonuses/compensations - ensuring a more clear invoicing process, and less invoicing noise._\n\n_For example, previously you would see a commission of 416.91€ and separate bonus lines of 11€ on your invoice, which totaled up to 361.92€. Now, you would only see a single row of commission in the amount of 361.92€, meaning the calculation is already done in the background._\n\n\n\nExample for some [Driver|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/3318350?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]:\n\nTaking November 2025 example from [Balance history|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/balanceHistory?balanceHistoryFilterSearch=%7B%22external_id%22%3A3318350%2C%22type%22%3A%22Driver%22%2C%22month%22%3A%7B%22month%22%3A11%2C%22year%22%3A2025%7D%2C%22viewType%22%3A%22monthly%22%2C%22week%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1762725600000%2C%22end%22%3A1763330399999%7D%7D]. \n\nCommission that driver had to pay is\n\n{quote}*Commission = expense_cash_commission* + *expense_commission* (48.50 EUR + 190.83 EUR) = €239.33 EUR{quote}\n\nthis commission is ±20% of the amount driver had in Ride fees\n\n{quote}Fees = *earning_in_app_ride_fee* + *earning_cash_ride_fee* (947.70 EUR + 242.50 EUR) = €1,190.20 EUR\n\nCommission % = commission / fees = €239.33 EUR / 1,190.20 EUR = 0.20 = 20%{quote}\n\nthe [invoice|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5649895597?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] was issued for 132.94 euro, which is less than 239.33 because we do *commission netting* in Estonia.\n\n{quote}*What is Commission Netting?*\n\n*Commission netting* is a process used to simplify how drivers are invoiced for commissions, especially when there are bonuses, campaigns, or compensations involved.\n\n*Without Netting:*\n\nNormally, a driver would receive separate invoices:\n\nOne for the commission they owe (e.g., 20% of ride fees)\n\nSeparate invoices for any bonuses, campaigns, or compensations they receive\n\n*With Netting (as done in Estonia):*\n\nInstead of issuing multiple invoices, the system *reduces the commission amount* by the total value of any bonuses, campaigns, or compensations the driver earned.\n\nThe driver receives a *single, lower commission invoice* that already accounts for these discounts.{quote}\n\nYou can see discounts earned via cash and app rides in *earning_cash_discount_netted* and *earning_in_app_discount_netted.*\n\nSo we can calculate the final netted commission like this:\n\n{quote}Netted Commission = Commission - *earning_cash_discount_netted - earning_in_app_discount_netted* = €239.33 - 26.70 EUR - 79.70 EUR = €132.93{quote}\n\n132.93 is the same amount you can see on Monthly invoice (take invoice from November from [+here+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients/128179276?tab=partner_invoices&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn])\n\n✨ That’s how you can calculate Commission Netting in Balance history.\n\nNikolay Roll   ","2026-01-13T10:56:07.472Z"],["3806238","SCM-998","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","Pricing comparison done. Pricing negotiation will be taken up as the situation with Schenker terminal fire develops.\n[Slack Channel|https://join.slack.com/share/enQtMTAyODU3NDc3NDc3NzgtNTU3YWFhOThkZDEwZDc4ZDA2ZDczOTRlZmI0N2U2Y2Y4ZmFkM2ZmNGZjZDljNDcyNDI4YmRkMWU1YzBmZDdhNw]\n","2026-01-13T10:56:10.026Z"],["3806241","SCM-998","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","Similar operations pricing difference calculation done in October2025.\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1MW-8mfUAP-MjpnN_X5hx51U2AUtZC1yNYUMkyw3CQvY/edit?gid=368370543#gid=368370543|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1MW-8mfUAP-MjpnN_X5hx51U2AUtZC1yNYUMkyw3CQvY/edit?gid=368370543#gid=368370543|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T10:56:58.700Z"],["3806242","LSS-61492","LSS","kerubo.ombati@bolt.eu","Kerubo Ombati","[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] Existing DEC Agreement  and addendum for additional space[^ADDENDUM to lease agreement_Bolt (T) LIMITED_ VINTAGE INTERNATIONAL LIMITED_17.07.2025) (2).pdf]  [^Office space agreement_Bolt (T) Limited_Vintage International Limited_01.03.25 (1) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-13T10:57:01.292Z"],["3806243","PFI-832364","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Billing does not handle fraud, please reach out to Fraud team to help determine why it was marked like that and whether it’s correct. ","2026-01-13T10:58:04.335Z"],["3806245","PFI-832833","PFI","anzhela.shahbazyan@bolt-outsource.eu","Anzhela Shahbazyan","!Screenshot 2026-01-13 2.51.46 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T10:58:08.855Z"],["3806247","PFI-832364","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T10:58:11.735Z"],["3806250","CAMLE-9411","CAMLE","marina.gaponova@bolt.eu","Maryna Gaponova","[~accountid:63d0ecc2f386bda5dcab9d6e] to check with [~accountid:712020:66bb9418-0d92-46e7-811e-6ba68a304999] ","2026-01-13T10:58:41.351Z"],["3806251","PFI-832830","PFI","valdas.jocas@bolt-outsource.eu","Valdas Jocas","Wrong escalation","2026-01-13T10:58:53.393Z"],["3806253","SREDESK-7411","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","\n\n* Schema has been created on prelive and LIVE:\n\n{noformat}root@ti-prelive-dba.sqldb:(none)>CREATE DATABASE taxify_fraud_core;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.522s\n\n\nroot@ti-fraud-dba.sqldb:(none)>CREATE DATABASE taxify_fraud_core;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 1.011s{noformat}","2026-01-13T10:59:15.348Z"],["3806254","LSS-61259","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","* [https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyo%C3%BC/personaldatabreachriskassessment/1-all-entries/280|https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyo%C3%BC/personaldatabreachriskassessment/1-all-entries/280]\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0678KJ49UH/p1767887650004089|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0678KJ49UH/p1767887650004089|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T10:59:16.551Z"],["3806258","WD-22552","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","Hi, you should be able now to enter it, please reopen the ticket if not,\n\nKind regards,\n\nOli","2026-01-13T11:00:10.568Z"],["3806262","PFI-832835","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T11:00:53.264Z"],["3806265","LSS-61228","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Perfect, keeping myself available to send the response when the refund will be made. 🙏 ","2026-01-13T11:01:10.747Z"],["3806266","HS-28867","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:0b9924ff-04d9-493a-9bc0-d3ae48359ea8], thank you! The form will be sent to signing and forwarded to Payroll. I will close this ticket.","2026-01-13T11:01:17.704Z"],["3806270","LSS-58680","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Thanks [~accountid:63dcee0028cddcc70772479d] 🙏  closing ticket (/) ","2026-01-13T11:01:40.733Z"],["3806271","DELIVERY-562","DELIVERY","varvara.kazakova@bolt.eu","Varvara Kazakova","26W3: Design ready, handed to engineers","2026-01-13T11:02:09.798Z"],["3806272","LSS-57290","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:5e3d86bd22a6390c9c0ebc42] hey, below is the link to the revised main text of the agreement. Please check my comments and confirm so we can finalize it. \n\nWe will also separately receive and revise the annexes with the specific commercial terms - will keep you updated.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oN7YZ5A7qceet-UNzGScwB255tP6iNIN/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oN7YZ5A7qceet-UNzGScwB255tP6iNIN/edit|smart-link] \n\ncc [~accountid:712020:b1bcb605-06fc-4bbd-b599-897a42958257] ","2026-01-13T11:02:27.465Z"],["3806273","LSS-58338","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:6012aaf8a41ea5006a613a63] - did you receive any more messages from the lawyer? If not, I will close this ticket 🙏 ","2026-01-13T11:02:32.907Z"],["3806275","DRX-27860","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","Tested and verified on DI.127.0 (194761070) using iPhone 11, iOS 26.3\n\n* password screen is no longer skipped to OTP verification screen\n\n{color:#36b37e}*FIXED*{color}\n\n[^Issue fixed.MP4]\n\n\n\n\n\nISSUE\n\n[^Password screen skipped.MP4]","2026-01-13T11:03:21.598Z"],["3806276","LSS-60738","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8] ! I am on it. Currently waiting for Ramūnas' signature.\n\nThank you","2026-01-13T11:03:28.794Z"],["3806278","SUPX-2265","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","I don’t think there was anything. We had some other adjustments we needed to do, but they are most likely specific to only us. Here is the PR itself if you want to take a look - [https://github.com/bolteu/support-webview/pull/1138/files|https://github.com/bolteu/support-webview/pull/1138/files]","2026-01-13T11:04:16.640Z"],["3806279","PAW-14779","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160358\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 11:04:42 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T11:04:43.058Z"],["3806281","LSS-58338","LSS","innaaime.kalju@bolt.eu","Inna Aime Kalju","hi, no updates from their side, i think you can close the case for now\n\n","2026-01-13T11:05:09.889Z"],["3806282","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","[^Bilag A. Kravsspecifikation taxaudbud.xlsx] _(65 kB)_","2026-01-13T11:05:10.963Z"],["3806283","LSS-61493","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nMalene Støjberg-Olsen has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-13T11:05:12.610Z"],["3806285","DO-5779","DO","volha.anishchanka@bolt.eu","Volha Anishchanka","Guide [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/7149092932/Looker+MCP#Installation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/7149092932/Looker+MCP#Installation|smart-link] + I’ll send you credentials via [pass.bolt.eu|http://pass.bolt.eu] ","2026-01-13T11:05:26.779Z"],["3806286","LSS-58338","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Great, thanks a lot! ","2026-01-13T11:05:29.798Z"],["3806289","PIF-2207","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft effectively communicates the new features of receiving alerts and logging failed authentication attempts, explaining their significance for security and auditing. However, it lacks specific links to where the feature can be accessed or a guide for using it, which are crucial for the platform team to fully understand and utilize the new functionality.","2026-01-13T11:06:16.963Z"],["3806290","PFI-832467","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hey [~accountid:62380b3ba2f6400069e990d0] ,\n\ncan you please ask the driver where they got this report.\n\nseems like an urgent bug.\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-13 at 13.06.20@2x-20260113-110623.png|width=895,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-13 at 13.06.20@2x-20260113-110623.png\"!","2026-01-13T11:06:43.424Z"],["3806291","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","# Ad-hoc solution to fix the phone holder to the bracket\n## Wuerth *Ethyl-2-cyanoacrylate* super glue secures it. Tests are below in the table.\n### LY will not do extra work this year since:\n#### The pre-assembly is complete.\n#### Many employees are heading home to celebrate NY.\n# To create a customized clip for a long-term solution with additional features, an injection mold needs to be opened at *15000 RMB.*\n\n!image-20260113-090631.png|width=207,alt=\"image-20260113-090631.png\"!\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"ddadd115-b54a-40a6-af39-03d2757f8aea\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":5},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"orderedList\",\"attrs\":{\"order\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Wuerth \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Ethyl-2-cyanoacrylate\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" glue\"}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":301,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"ff0f43fa551078d91565f3bbf3883c76-20260113-110311.jpg\",\"alt\":\"ff0f43fa551078d91565f3bbf3883c76-20260113-110311.jpg\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":221,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"55104adad9996fa5f120422770627b34-20260113-110408.jpg\",\"alt\":\"55104adad9996fa5f120422770627b34-20260113-110408.jpg\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"078f217edf9845121aad6e153bec7524.mp4\",\"alt\":\"078f217edf9845121aad6e153bec7524.mp4\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":960,\"width\":544}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"3a2a8dc5809cb649400110150332ffe1.mp4\",\"alt\":\"3a2a8dc5809cb649400110150332ffe1.mp4\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":960,\"width\":544}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"67ed84cb610ac6d820de8a5002b9fbdf.mp4\",\"alt\":\"67ed84cb610ac6d820de8a5002b9fbdf.mp4\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":960,\"width\":544}}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-13T11:06:46.600Z"],["3806295","LSS-58470","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:b33fa9fc-2e0e-4ab0-a8b3-85f9683a7c93] closing the ticket until we have a confirmation on the project, thank you!","2026-01-13T11:06:57.495Z"],["3806296","PFI-831433","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Escalated to engineering for review! ","2026-01-13T11:07:00.979Z"],["3806297","PFI-831433","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02BZ67SKFG/p1768293232384289|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02BZ67SKFG/p1768293232384289]","2026-01-13T11:07:14.915Z"],["3806298","WD-22544","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","Hi,\n\nSorry I dont understand what you want to do? \n\nif you want to recruit for the headcount P002058, please “start job req” you will be able to change the job profile and anything related to the headcount. \n\nLEt me know,\n\noli","2026-01-13T11:07:16.860Z"],["3806300","PFI-831433","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team!  🍔\n\n- Provider/Courier payment didn't reflect in their balance: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/503\n- Provider/Courier didn't receive payout: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/319\n- Eater had issues with the payment: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/316\n- Early cashout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/556\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/317\n- App and backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/76\n- Balance and Invoices issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/318\n- Invoice Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T11:07:20.769Z"],["3806302","PFI-814507","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! We’re already looking into this with engineering. Rest assured, if we discover that something is indeed off, it will be compensated accordingly. ","2026-01-13T11:08:13.227Z"],["3806304","WD-22543","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","Hi,\n\nWe change job profile, which are linked to comp range,\n\n[~accountid:712020:09fb9e39-8738-4af0-b134-11592f52c14c] please advise which job profile they shouldbe?","2026-01-13T11:08:44.177Z"],["3806305","LSS-60472","LSS","alexia.lia@bolt.eu","Alexia Lia","Hey! [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] \n\nShall we keep discussing on this one? As the other one has steered off from the topic at hand I believe. \n\nNo I have not contacted Transport Malta as of yet, however TM should not be a blocker, this is a diversification of our normal service offering. ","2026-01-13T11:08:52.601Z"],["3806306","EBIKE1-421","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] Long seat option is for Cruiser only. ","2026-01-13T11:08:53.278Z"],["3806308","LSS-55403","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ,\n\nto speed up, would you kindly set up a quick call on Thursday so that we can discuss in person?Maybe we can do the same for all other open tickets (if needed?) WDYT?\n\nThanks a lot\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-13T11:09:13.431Z"],["3806310","PFI-832666","PFI","jelena.griciva@bolt-outsource.eu","Jelena Griciva","We still need assistance. All the payments that were marked as finished, are not getting rejected. ","2026-01-13T11:09:20.633Z"],["3806311","CSDA-258","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hey hey!\n\nFinally came back to this request, and we have everything needed in Looker already ✨. Here are a few ways to get the data you need:\n\n# Use the {{fact_rides_order}} explore. Here is the query: [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/cross_domain/fact_rides_order?qid=q6XKL3UWGEX4u1WJbk4ozq&toggle=fil|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/cross_domain/fact_rides_order?qid=q6XKL3UWGEX4u1WJbk4ozq&toggle=fil]. You should have access to this explore; let me know if you don't 🙏 The only potential disadvantage of this option is the lack of refund details (i.e., refund target, admin agent ID).\n# Use the {{CS Case - Explorer}}. Here is the query: [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/customer_support/support_case_explorer?qid=FuzlX8XQPsBwCm3DD3MY1m&origin_space=9376&toggle=fil|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/customer_support/support_case_explorer?qid=FuzlX8XQPsBwCm3DD3MY1m&origin_space=9376&toggle=fil]. You may need to extend the date range in filters tho, as refunds can be initiated the week after case creation week.\n# Use a merged query. Here is the query: [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/merge?mid=Cv3iAPg5bSDm5O9pRztZp3&toggle=mrp,vis,vse|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/merge?mid=Cv3iAPg5bSDm5O9pRztZp3&toggle=mrp,vis,vse]. This option is more complex, and you will need to exclude cases refunded before the last complete week during your analysis manually.\n\nI would recommend the first option if you only need order details; it is easy and very efficient (time- and cost-wise). You can save it as a Look in your personal Looker folder and set up a scheduled job to receive those reports via email or Slack automatically.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any further questions or comments 🙌","2026-01-13T11:09:41.898Z"],["3806313","DSR-3637","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[^Police Report Notification  - 298076 - Mohammed Akbar Adelzade.pdf] The only information sent to TFL about this case was a police report notification. No official report with investigation notes was sent to them.\n[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] Let me know if I missed anything and need to add it \n","2026-01-13T11:09:50.339Z"],["3806315","HS-28847","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Waiting for JD","2026-01-13T11:10:08.157Z"],["3806319","WD-22542","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","Thanks for raising this — you’re absolutely right, and we understand the limitation this creates for cross-team visibility.\n\nImproving absence visibility beyond direct manager/team relationships is on the roadmap. Unfortunately, due to current Workday constraints, we’re limited in what we can change today, and we’re not able to share a timeline yet.\n\nThanks for flagging this and for your patience as we work through it.","2026-01-13T11:10:49.910Z"],["3806320","PFI-832832","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Checking with Karan","2026-01-13T11:10:49.975Z"],["3806321","LSS-61494","LSS","brian.sun@bolt.eu","Brian Sun","[^[Accessible Fleet] Bolt - Fleet Partnership Agreement Taiwan - (CN trans)_FINAL.docx (2).pdf] _(611 kB)_","2026-01-13T11:11:25.439Z"],["3806322","WD-22541","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","you can now add you german iban\n\nOli","2026-01-13T11:11:36.936Z"],["3806323","LSS-61388","LSS","paolo.catani@bolt.eu","Paolo Catani","This is an investor audit request. Please complete as soon as you can.\nThank you!","2026-01-13T11:11:40.362Z"],["3806324","INT-769","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","26W3: MVRA and marketing work in progress, prod needs to finalise value prop","2026-01-13T11:11:43.006Z"],["3806326","INT-768","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","26W3: MVRA and marketing work in progress, prod needs to finalise value prop","2026-01-13T11:11:51.152Z"],["3806327","WD-22170","WD","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi! Are there any updates about this topic? 🙏 ","2026-01-13T11:12:09.984Z"],["3806328","INT-811","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","26W3: after discussing MVRA stakeholders, added the April launch to list, in order to kick off prep work in Q1","2026-01-13T11:12:25.406Z"],["3806329","INT-812","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","26W3: after discussing MVRA stakeholders, added the April launch to list, in order to kick off prep work in Q1","2026-01-13T11:12:32.281Z"],["3806330","DRX-27780","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","Tested on DA.126.0 (1505) Firebase build on Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\n❌ The last digits are hidden when the amount on the Earnings FAB increases with additional digits after completing a ride.\n\n!screen-20260113-122141.mp4|width=320,alt=\"screen-20260113-122141.mp4\"!","2026-01-13T11:12:43.226Z"],["3806331","FX-3618","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768302756937869]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@chantel.rowe>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3618] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T11:12:49.295Z"],["3806332","WD-22170","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Hi Kristi! we have this logged as a sprint item, i will work on it this week and should be good to test and deploy next week.","2026-01-13T11:13:05.839Z"],["3806333","LSS-59633","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:b33fa9fc-2e0e-4ab0-a8b3-85f9683a7c93] hey, please check the last comment in clause 11 of Annex 1 to the agreement, after that I will send you the finalized revised version.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fxfzd8W0TsdmNrqrtPJIdVxdPkWNtS-E/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fxfzd8W0TsdmNrqrtPJIdVxdPkWNtS-E/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T11:13:17.649Z"],["3806334","PFI-832666","PFI","jelena.griciva@bolt-outsource.eu","Jelena Griciva","Correction: all the payments that were marked as finished, are *now** getting rejected.\n\n","2026-01-13T11:13:27.964Z"],["3806335","ITI-1166","ITI","leila.toomet@bolt.eu","Leila Toomet","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1NmtskRG7TbewF2L_1lTW7XzhXcp_smCesbzZy3HwRLY/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1NmtskRG7TbewF2L_1lTW7XzhXcp_smCesbzZy3HwRLY/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T11:13:49.994Z"],["3806336","HS-28847","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Sent the doc to PP","2026-01-13T11:13:54.308Z"],["3806337","LSS-61264","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Hi [~accountid:712020:cb7d1436-9800-43db-821c-db7028a6ff03] - I have now had a proper chance to review this in full, and I have some thoughts on how to approach this. However, before providing my thoughts, I need further visibiluty on the following - can you please confirm?\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n# On what date did we actually receive the letter? Did it come with any attachments?\n# Please provide links to both: (a) the rider’s profile; and (b) the thread with the driver in which we have asked for the footage.\n{panel}\n\nAlso, while we wait for a response from the driver (and on the assumption that there were no attachments to the letter - please confirm if this is the case, as it impacts whether we should send the below), please could you email the below to BCGL ([ruthe@bcgladvocates.com|mailto:ruthe@bcgladvocates.com]) to let them know that we have received their request and require a little more information from their side? +*Please send this ASAP this week*+, given that BCGL originally submitted their request on 19 December. \n\n{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}\nDear Ms. Ellul,\n\nWe write further to your letter dated 19 December 2025, in which you requested (on behalf of Ms Maya Elamrousy) evidence of an incident that took place during a Bolt trip on 14 December 2025.  Please note that we are currently investigating whether the trip was recorded by any driver-owned dashcam and we will get back to you as soon as possible.\n\nIn the meantime, to help us ensure the security of the personal data that we hold about your client, we need to verify your legal authority to submit this request on behalf of Ms Maya Elamrousy. We would accept either a written consent signed by the data subject, or a certified copy of a power of attorney. Please be aware that we are unable to fully respond to your request until we receive this information, and any applicable deadlines will be paused until we have received it.\n\nPlease provide the additional information by responding to this email. We appreciate your cooperation in this matter and look forward to receiving the requested information from you.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nBolt\n{panel}","2026-01-13T11:14:04.655Z"],["3806339","WD-22170","WD","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Perfect, thank you!","2026-01-13T11:15:05.446Z"],["3806341","LSS-58530","LSS","elena.skoutaridou@bolt.eu","Elena Skoutaridou","office address: Griva Digenis Ave 81–83, 5th Floor, Nicosia 1090, Cyprus [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] FYI","2026-01-13T11:16:09.819Z"],["3806342","PIF-2207","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 10\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: ","2026-01-13T11:16:11.233Z"],["3806343","LSS-55755","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] [~accountid:712020:d3fd53e6-f124-4770-a577-b09d6688566f] just responded in the ticket regarding DSA. [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-55755?focusedCommentId=3626620|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-55755?focusedCommentId=3626620|smart-link]  → as I understand from Kirsika’s comment, the DSA was signed already, can we keep it or do we need to re-negotiate and if so - why?","2026-01-13T11:16:13.879Z"],["3806346","PFI-831591","PFI","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","hey Daphne. \n\nthis is a duplicated escalation. issue was already raised on [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-826271|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-826271|smart-link] where we replied on 29/12/25. \n\nhere’s our response:\n\n{quote}The driver had one order removed from his top-up calculation that affected the sum that he received by 5.95 GBP. It was this order here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/604972705/759?orderTryId=1484195745|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/604972705/759?orderTryId=1484195745]\n\nYou can share the order details with the driver. The driver himself told us that the ride didn’t happen, but it was a trip started by him that stayed active for 27min. You can educate the driver to be more cautious to start trips, and if the passenger doesn’t show, he can collect a cancellation fee to pay for his time.\n\nIn terms of his appeal, we won’t be adjusting his top-up compensation further. Our decision is final.{quote}\n\npls make sure to leave links to SD in the Beehive ticket and a profile note when a driver appeals, and we respond to it. to prevent duplicates like it happened here. ","2026-01-13T11:17:07.093Z"],["3806347","WD-22563","WD","peggy.dano@bolt.eu","Peggy Stefany Dano","[^2026 Bolt Iceland Primary Payroll Report Schedule.xlsx]","2026-01-13T11:17:09.263Z"],["3806348","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi Edvards,\n\nI prepared the PR.\n\nWhen you have time, can you [please review it|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15360]?\n\nBy the way, from the AWS console we can check the {{last used}} time for the access keys.\n\nSo after switching from IAM credentials to IAM roles, please ping us to delete these IAM credentials. 🙏 \n\n!image-20260113-111427.png|width=1083,alt=\"image-20260113-111427.png\"!\n\n!image-20260113-111439.png|width=1067,alt=\"image-20260113-111439.png\"!\n\n!image-20260113-111454.png|width=1067,alt=\"image-20260113-111454.png\"!\n\n!image-20260113-111504.png|width=1067,alt=\"image-20260113-111504.png\"!","2026-01-13T11:17:13.158Z"],["3806350","HS-28838","HS","salman.babazade@bolt.eu","Salman Babazade Jr.","!IMG_5424.jpeg|width=440,height=284,alt=\"IMG_5424.jpeg\"!\n\n","2026-01-13T11:17:32.627Z"],["3806351","LSS-61495","LSS","therese.ilves@bolt.eu","Therese Ilves","[^Partnership agreement_Bolt Operations OÜ_AUTODOC SE_20.05.25.pdf]\n[^2. Addendum to the Partnership Agreement_Bolt Operations OÜ_AUTODOC SE_21.10.25.pdf]\n[^3. Addendum to the Partnership Agreement_Bolt Operations OÜ_AUTODOC SE_21.10.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T11:17:43.533Z"],["3806353","L10N-27442","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.714Z"],["3806354","L10N-27449","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.793Z"],["3806355","L10N-27450","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.805Z"],["3806356","L10N-27438","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.826Z"],["3806357","L10N-27444","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.866Z"],["3806358","L10N-27443","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.874Z"],["3806359","L10N-27451","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.882Z"],["3806360","L10N-27455","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.938Z"],["3806361","L10N-27454","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.951Z"],["3806362","L10N-27456","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.968Z"],["3806363","L10N-27439","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.967Z"],["3806364","L10N-27440","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.970Z"],["3806365","L10N-27441","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:07.970Z"],["3806366","L10N-27453","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:08.005Z"],["3806367","L10N-27445","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:08.003Z"],["3806368","L10N-27452","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:08.011Z"],["3806369","L10N-27457","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:08.088Z"],["3806370","L10N-27448","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:08.078Z"],["3806371","L10N-27446","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:08.119Z"],["3806372","L10N-27447","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:08.154Z"],["3806373","L10N-27436","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:13.081Z"],["3806374","L10N-27437","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:13.307Z"],["3806375","L10N-27434","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:13.448Z"],["3806376","L10N-27435","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:13.624Z"],["3806377","L10N-27432","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:13.811Z"],["3806378","L10N-27433","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T11:18:14.085Z"],["3806380","LSS-31377","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* email and letter received from Gary Matthews Solicitors re mediation offer.\n\n{color:#ff5630}*Deadline to respond - Monday 19 January.*{color}\n\n[^Ltr to 3PS re Mediation.pdf]\n[^Bolt Mail - OUR CLIENT_ Peter Mooney, YOUR CLIENT_ Bolt Itx Limited.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T11:19:11.302Z"],["3806383","WD-22517","WD","peggy.dano@bolt.eu","Peggy Stefany Dano","Hi Yuvraj, \n\nThank you so much for your help. \n\nKind regards, \n\nPeggy","2026-01-13T11:19:43.102Z"],["3806385","RDS-267","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","IMO it should be P0 or P1: they are redundant but also the content in both is different. For example Payment can be find only in Hamburger Menu. \n\nCleaning this up, will make whole app navigation less complex and more intuitive.","2026-01-13T11:20:16.333Z"],["3806387","PFI-832681","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey [~accountid:63bff28d49a31f95b8740233] ,\n\nthis is a wrong queue:\n\nplease create a ticket here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T11:20:26.763Z"],["3806389","HS-28838","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Visa letter is ready and has been sent to your regional People Partner Fidan, you will receive it from her once she has signed it! ","2026-01-13T11:21:52.558Z"],["3806390","RCE-347","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768303312627539]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@katlin.parl>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-347] `Improve document download process for multiple boroughs` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T11:22:04.210Z"],["3806391","FDBT-4731","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-13T11:22:17.765Z"],["3806392","LSS-60707","LSS","oldrich.plechacek@bolt.eu","Oldřich Plecháček","Thank you for the reply. As for your points:\n\n# Termination period - If there wasn’t a legal issue with shortening the period to 7 days, I would still prefer going with it to cover potential last minute changes, even though we would still strive to inform the drivers more in advance. If it isn’t possible, then let’s go with 14/15 days. {color:#36b37e}*LEGAL: If it is doable for fleets to terminate the agreement within 7 days (especially unwrapping their vehicles - PLEASE CONFIRM), we can change the period for 7 days instead of 15 days.* {color}\n# Incentive period - the standard procedure and practical timelines are as follows:\n\n a) A new car applies for branding via a form\n\nb) If their application is approved, they can set an appointment with a wrapping company\n\nc) Once the car is branded, the driver uploads a photo of it in their driver documents - this is the *manual review/verification* stage.\n\nd) The incentive for said car starts the following Monday 00:00 after the photo was uploaded. There is a deadline for uploads at Friday noon. Any later submissions are considered the same as next week’s uploads.\n\ne) On the first day of the incentive a new verification process is triggered for the car, in order for the driver to be able to perform *automated verifications* going forward. This means the driver needs to upload new pictures of the car directly through the app (not uploading a document in their document set as before). The driver has 7 days to perform the in-app verification.\n\nIf they fail, they lose the branding bonus (it will have effectively lasted only 7 days) and they need to go back to step c)\n\nIf they succeed, the incentive period is automatically prolonged for 30 days since the day of the successful verification. 7 days before this period ends, the in-app verification process is triggered again. This would then go on indefinitely as long as the driver successfully verifies and we don’t deactivate the bonus on the car manually.\n\nPlease let me know if you this needs any further clarification.\n\n{color:#36b37e}*LEGAL: Seems to be clear to me now. Thanks! I will rephrase and update the T&C regarding your clarification*{color}\n\n# The requirements are easily available on the website/blog. {color:#36b37e}*LEGAL:*{color} {color:#36b37e}*Fine*{color}\n# Re-affixing services cost - Sorry for the phrasing. We actually never inform the drivers about the costs. {color:#36b37e}*LEGAL:*{color} {color:#36b37e}*Fine*{color}\n\n____________\n\n\n\nAdditionally:\n\n# The T&Cs state “The version of the terms that will apply to You for an Incentive Period will remain the version of these terms that were in force on the first day of the Incentive Period.”\n\nSo following the T&Cs future update, the old version would still apply for ~3 months  due to the original incentive periods?\n\n{color:#36b37e}*LEGAL:*{color} {color:#36b37e}*Yes – as the clauses are currently drafted, following a T&C update, the old version would continue to apply for until the end of that Incentive Period.* {color}\n\n{color:#36b37e}*If greater flexibility is required, the clause would need to be amended to:*{color}\n\n* {color:#36b37e}*carve out exceptions (e.g. for incentive mechanics), or*{color}\n* {color:#36b37e}*allow certain changes to apply during an ongoing Incentive Period with appropriate notice.*{color}\n\n{color:#36b37e}*Please let me know.* {color}\n\n# Are we legally limited in the timeframes of changing the actual requirements for reaching the bonus (referring to part 2.6 of the T&Cs)? I mean the requirements of finished rides etc, which are listed on the blog and not explicitly in the T&Cs. Should we include a T&C provision to explicitly allow us maximum flexibility? We will need to change the requirements in the beginning of February. \n\n{color:#36b37e}*LEGAL: Changes to bonus requirements are not clearly covered by this clause. But as long as a given bonus requirement is not covered by the whole T&C (but only by blog or website content), there is no legal red flag to change it now. Please keep a reasonable, non-retroactive and proportional timeframe to the type of change. Anyway, I will amend this clause for the future so that it explicitly covers Bolt’s right to change the bonus requirements specified in sources other than T&C (meaning blogs, website etc) within the time proportional to the type and impact of the change.*  {color}\n\n# The published CZ version of the T&Cs is outdated and different from the EN version for the Czech market. Can you please update it so it matches the more comprehensive EN version? Does the translation process go solely through Legal, or is any local OPS input necessary here? {color:#36b37e}*LEGAL: For translation checks (translated through Deepl before), we can rely on local OPS speaking Czech*{color}","2026-01-13T11:22:38.927Z"],["3806393","PFI-832797","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi,\n\nplease use KB for receipt: https:/beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/115003655854?country=global&language=en\n\nor please use KB for invoices: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399]","2026-01-13T11:22:56.853Z"],["3806394","HS-28899","HS","ingrid.valgejarv@bolt.eu","Ingrid Valgejärv","task with global mobility","2026-01-13T11:23:11.292Z"],["3806395","PFI-807439","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment has been received here [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/68760458|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/68760458]\nShould we allocate these funds to a specific client (no client ID has been provided in the ticket) or return the payment back to sender?","2026-01-13T11:23:17.170Z"],["3806396","EBIKE1-322","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] Is this still relevant?","2026-01-13T11:23:22.391Z"],["3806397","PTWS-2073","PTWS","alexandru.cerveanu@bolt.eu","Alex Cerveanu","For each country, it is necessary to access *Maintain Race/Ethnicity Details* and configure the following fields:\n\n* *Race/Ethnicity Details Category*\n* *Race/Ethnicity Details Value*\n\nIn order to establish the *Links to Race/Ethnicity*, it is also required to access *Maintain Ethnicities* and, for the corresponding country, configure:\n\n* *Race/Ethnicity*\n* *Maps to*\n\nAfter this is done I will look on how to skip process approvals. :loading: ","2026-01-13T11:23:39.009Z"],["3806399","PFI-807481","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Hello,\nFinal payout processed. \nPlease check if the payout was processed and if you encounter some errors on it, please do let us know.","2026-01-13T11:24:26.434Z"],["3806400","WD-22539","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","you can now add your german iban","2026-01-13T11:24:31.140Z"],["3806402","PFI-807555","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Hey, no need to escalate payouts that have been rejected with the reason too_big_payout. \nOur team monitors such rejections. We then split the payout and resend the funds on the same day usually. \n\n","2026-01-13T11:25:29.646Z"],["3806404","DRX-28156","DRX","abhishek.shyam@bolt.eu","Abhishek Shyam","Updated CODEOWNERS file to change code ownership from {{@bolteu/driver-loyalty}} to {{@bolteu/driver-progression}}.\n\n*Changes made:*\n\n* Replaced all 20 occurrences of {{@bolteu/driver-loyalty}} with {{@bolteu/driver-progression}}\n\n*Affected paths:*\n\n* {{/tooling_scripts/code_complexity/}}\n* {{common/driver/home_screen/}}\n* {{common/inMemoryDataStore/translation/TranslationDriverBoltClub/}}\n* {{common/inMemoryDataStore/translation/TranslationDriverHelpSection/}}\n* {{common/inMemoryDataStore/translation/TranslationDriverInAppTraining/}}\n* {{common/inMemoryDataStore/translation/TranslationDriverLoyalty/}}\n* {{common/inMemoryDataStore/translation/TranslationDriverProfileMobile/}}\n* {{common/inMemoryDataStore/translation/TranslationDriverSidebar/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/circlek/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/driver_bolt_club/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/driver_in_app_training/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/driver_loyalty/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/driver_help_section/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/driver_sidebar/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/driver_profile_mobile/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/driver_online_incentives/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/in_app_notification_center/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/driver_home_screen/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/driver_preferences/}}\n* {{src/rides/driver/driver_home_screen_banner/}}","2026-01-13T11:25:47.235Z"],["3806406","LSS-59990","LSS","joao.nunes@bolt.eu","João Nunes","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ,\nNo, this is sorted, thank you ","2026-01-13T11:26:20.781Z"],["3806407","PFI-807714","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Driver has no balance","2026-01-13T11:26:35.936Z"],["3806408","PFI-832845","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-13T11:26:55.112Z"],["3806410","LSS-61494","LSS","magdalena.kowara@bolt.eu","Magdalena Kowara","Hi [~accountid:712020:9fd45c83-380e-410c-83d8-9f700c4718bd]does this version include a new VAT clause included in the annex to the previous agreements? [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09CJJJJ1U4/p1767164095714939|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09CJJJJ1U4/p1767164095714939|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T11:27:16.102Z"],["3806412","LSS-61496","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","[^Central Bedfordshire - Licence Agreement 2026.pdf] _(203 kB)_\n\n[^BOLT SERVICES LICENCE AGREEMENT .pdf] _(2.24 MB)_","2026-01-13T11:28:00.285Z"],["3806413","PFI-807957","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T11:28:13.383Z"],["3806417","PFI-832846","PFI","paul.mwangi@bolt-outsource.eu","Paul Mwangi","[^plata f 179607.pdf]\n\n[^plata f 221545.pdf]\n\n[^plata f 407263.pdf]","2026-01-13T11:29:10.705Z"],["3806418","LSS-61404","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a], supplier has asked us to start the signing process. Could you please support with adjusting the status of the ticket accordingly? \n\nDetails of the signatory: \nDaniel Patterson, SVP Global Operations, [daniel.patterson@trulioo.com|mailto:daniel.patterson@trulioo.com]\n\ncc to be added: [alex.trocjuks@trulioo.com|mailto:alex.trocjuks@trulioo.com]\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-13T11:29:27.629Z"],["3806419","SCM-1059","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","Following-up on prioritizing Dashboard update with [~accountid:5d773c785a4d810d2c4de81c] and [~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] \n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A7YAYRG23/p1768303610457939|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A7YAYRG23/p1768303610457939|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T11:29:33.489Z"],["3806420","PFI-832833","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nthe ride was charged from the company balance as it was a business ride - so the company will see this ride as part of their monthly report.","2026-01-13T11:29:52.215Z"],["3806421","PFI-832449","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! It doesn’t seem like there were any orders done neither under work nor business profile for the user, hence no invoice. ","2026-01-13T11:30:00.991Z"],["3806423","WD-22537","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","Hi [~accountid:6086bb10bb0b0500704a737d] \n\nHave you cecked time off result by period,\n\nSee screenshot please advise where you disagree, \n\nKind regards,\n\nOli\n\n!Capture d’écran 2026-01-13 à 12.29.03.png|width=595,alt=\"Capture d’écran 2026-01-13 à 12.29.03.png\"!","2026-01-13T11:30:22.861Z"],["3806425","LSS-61496","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T11:31:08.800Z"],["3806428","LSS-59609","LSS","joao.nunes@bolt.eu","João Nunes","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ,\nSorry for not answering this one.\nThis was sorted as well.\nThank you \n\n","2026-01-13T11:31:56.633Z"],["3806429","BB-2276","BB","uladzislau.klimiankou@bolt.eu","Vlad Klimenkov","one more to clarify: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09LEB128QP/p1768303734502829|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09LEB128QP/p1768303734502829]","2026-01-13T11:32:01.354Z"],["3806430","BRE-1204","BRE","mariia.bukhanska@bolt.eu","Mariia Bukhanska"," Rejection comment: small changes like links, hints and refactor could be done later  ","2026-01-13T11:32:01.526Z"],["3806431","BB-2162","BB","ilya.goryachev@bolt.eu","Ilya Goryachev","Reissue is done, [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] please find [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1nmTd1JqzkaNYopc4eCECKFugcU3cYv74q6jF_ssUnYU/edit?usp=sharing] the business companies list with their balances to adjust 🙂","2026-01-13T11:33:13.309Z"],["3806432","BDB-1521","BDB","liisi.tamra@bolt.eu","Liisi Tamra","[~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] ok, gotcha! Thanks for clarifying what’s been agreed with the venues. In that case, I’d just suggest tweaking the headlines a bit and adding more CTA-led subheadlines:\n\nPOSTER\n*Move smart after last call.*\n*Get home safe with Bolt*\nDownload the Bolt app and use code NZHOMESAFE for $20 off your first ride.\n\n\n\nTABLE TALKER\n*Out late? Ride safe.*\n*Bolt makes getting home easy.*\nDownload the Bolt app and use code NZHOMESAFE for $20 off your first ride.","2026-01-13T11:33:50.631Z"],["3806433","PFI-807439","PFI","jelena.griciva@bolt-outsource.eu","Jelena Griciva","Hi! The Fleet Owner asked to return the money. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-13T11:33:56.963Z"],["3806434","RLONE-813","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Budget forecast blueprint [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1feK8N2wgo_5mCIjDumkXkBP2CKX8N3sWk5FVeH7jGFM/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.qw1y4o70gwlg]. ","2026-01-13T11:33:58.239Z"],["3806435","LSS-59845","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] yes, all previous comments were accepted ","2026-01-13T11:33:58.761Z"],["3806436","PFI-832850","PFI","laura.ernestova@bolt.eu","Laura Ernestová","[^2025-12-01 -- 2025-12-08 Curry Garden Indicka Restaurace Weekly Report.pdf]\n\n[^2025-12-08 -- 2025-12-15 Curry Garden Indicka Restaurace Weekly Report.pdf]\n\n[^2025-12-15 -- 2025-12-22 Curry Garden Indicka Restaurace Weekly Report.pdf]\n\n[^2025-12-22 -- 2025-12-29 Curry Garden Indicka Restaurace Weekly Report.pdf]\n\n[^2025-12-29 -- 2026-01-05 Curry Garden Indicka Restaurace Weekly Report.pdf]\n\n!Snímek obrazovky 2026-01-13 v 12.33.41.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T11:34:10.644Z"],["3806437","PFI-832850","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-13T11:34:12.727Z"],["3806439","DSR-3557","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","I have sent the response to the user and escalated back to Tier 2 with instructions.","2026-01-13T11:34:41.581Z"],["3806440","DRX-27817","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DI.127.0 (194761070) Firebase build on iPhone 14 Pro, OS:18\n\n||*Dark theme*||*Light theme*||*Scheduled rides*||\n|!IMG_4374.PNG|width=164,alt=\"IMG_4374.PNG\"!|!IMG_4379.PNG|width=164,alt=\"IMG_4379.PNG\"!|!IMG_4380.PNG|width=164,alt=\"IMG_4380.PNG\"!|\n|!IMG_4376.PNG|width=164,alt=\"IMG_4376.PNG\"!|!IMG_4377.PNG|width=164,alt=\"IMG_4377.PNG\"!|!IMG_4381.PNG|width=164,alt=\"IMG_4381.PNG\"!|","2026-01-13T11:34:58.312Z"],["3806441","DMC-238","DMC","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","26W02 report\n\n* The Global roll out Epic was closed, although the decision was made to roll out gradually, country-by-country, instead of an actually Global Release.\n* A few of the uncompleted tasks from the previous Epic made it into the current one.\n\n26W03 plans\n\n* Understand the current state of PIM AI Translations, and try to enable in Live\n* Work on Highest Priority tasks, since they are blocking Ops team from creating menus in PIM (bad experience, based on feedback)","2026-01-13T11:35:06.307Z"],["3806443","RDS-1403","RDS","rishi.kar@bolt.eu","Rishi Raj Kar","[~accountid:712020:47e6816d-876b-4d46-8a97-5225889a64c8] [~accountid:60717fb33e6ea000688f67b4] lets make a plan for this please 🙏 ","2026-01-13T11:35:58.657Z"],["3806446","LSS-56022","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df],\n\nHope you’re well - please could you support us with this ticket? We are already past the initial deadline to respond to the court order, so I’d really appreciate if you could get back to me asap on this please 🙏 \n\nRamone has now shared the data we are proposing to disclose in response to the court order. Could you please take a look at his most recent comment and confirm whether, from a privacy perspective, we are able to share this information as-is?\n\nIn particular, it would be helpful to know:\n\n* Whether any redactions should be applied (e.g. in relation to suspension data), in line with Thomas’s advice from 31 December; and\n* Whether we need to involve any other legal team before sharing the CSV files, detailing the drivers' in-app earnings and subsequent payouts?\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-13T11:36:53.276Z"],["3806450","WFM-9969","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","Agent’s IDs:\nandrii.kozhemiako - 233254\nanastasiia.syrovatko - 19983\nandrii.latyk - 16729","2026-01-13T11:37:46.724Z"],["3806451","WD-22415","WD","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","Hello [~accountid:712020:80f31809-0e9d-4c0f-8939-db5dd3d77922] [~accountid:63934c5900cb2fc3f98c7e44] \n\nCan you confirm what’s the plan regarding: Armenia, Cyprus, Uzbekistan, Kazakhstan, Malaysia, Uganda and Thailand? We haven’t received the schedule yet - are these onboarded in Papaya? ","2026-01-13T11:38:03.463Z"],["3806453","WD-21965","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:6131df23b1894f00718e9faa] , sorry I was catching up after the sabbatical. To answer your message:\n”What I meant was:\n\nIf I book 19 journals in a row which are above 100k and the 20th is below 100k, based on the logic you described above, will this 20th journal which is below 100k journal need an approval or not?\n\nThe idea is that this 20th journal is 1st journal which is under 100k and shouldn’t go to the approval flow.”\n\nBased on the proposed logic, the 20th invoice which is below 100k will go for approval. It will not be a first invoice as you expected. \n\nYour proposed flow to count invoices below <100k EUR and then initiate approval flow on the 20th invoice counted, I’m not entirely sure it’s possible to do in Workday. But if that’s a hard requirement from your side, I’ll work on exploring how to do it. \n\nI apologise for the delay on this ticket. ","2026-01-13T11:38:13.002Z"],["3806454","CCM-22274","CCM","andreea.tureac@bolt-outsource.eu","Andreea Tureac","[^Training Request MD 13.01.xlsx]","2026-01-13T11:38:32.544Z"],["3806455","PFI-809177","PFI","kitija.akmane@bolt.eu","Kitija Akmane","Hello [~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24] \nI don’t have access to the provided ticket. Can you add me, please?  \n\n","2026-01-13T11:38:36.188Z"],["3806456","TAX2-624","TAX2","alejandro.sanz@bolt.eu","Alejandro Sanz","According to the [Percurso Deal Sheet|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kPW8zSHzTbTAY29wl_OoMH5VMho-IPgtMybWIztkhB0/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.94r3tis2fqpp], Bolt will provide financing to an SPV (as per the attached structure) that will be 0% owned by Bolt. The financing will be through a bond issued by the SPV.\n\n!image-20260113-113436.png|width=752,alt=\"image-20260113-113436.png\"!\n\nConsidering the 0% Bolt ownership on the SPV and the fact that, as far as the Transfer Pricing team knows, there is no IC bonding within the Bolt Group, this project does not have any Transfer Pricing/Inter-company impact for Bolt. In any case, we recommend using Bolt Holdings OÜ (subject to alignment with other Teams as Legal, Finance and Treasury) as the entity acquiring the bond from the SPV.\n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:dcaeeaea-b979-4efa-93e7-594a518b6eb5] , [~accountid:62615f256cb53d006a6a3fe1] , [~accountid:62567ec6a872710069210b83] , [~accountid:712020:c9e0b423-51d9-40ce-a9ef-b4c651b92973] ","2026-01-13T11:38:37.482Z"],["3806457","RDS-1118","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] Yep, agree this is a good thing to solve. On prio, I cant say - up to you.","2026-01-13T11:38:42.351Z"],["3806460","WFM-9967","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","issue key added: rider_lost_item","2026-01-13T11:39:22.755Z"],["3806461","WFM-9967","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","Hi [~accountid:5f06c5841a26ad0014019484] issue key has been added to the queue criteria. ","2026-01-13T11:39:57.581Z"],["3806462","GRWA-1502","GRWA","taron.davtyan@bolt.eu","Taron Davtyan","Data is collected in [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1sKA21srCnsh0u-NZ2C8nFvCqiiWqySZTKlXvsAasU-I/edit?gid=223512576#gid=223512576|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1sKA21srCnsh0u-NZ2C8nFvCqiiWqySZTKlXvsAasU-I/edit?gid=223512576#gid=223512576|smart-link] \n\nShared with Helder and Kripal in slack","2026-01-13T11:40:13.653Z"],["3806464","RDS-1276","RDS","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:712020:505aebee-5cf4-438e-8909-a5524bd7a634] Good questions (and also great stereotypes 😆 ) - from my understanding, the default is that scheduled rides are handled automatically by our matching engines, UNLESS the fleet picks it up and assigns a driver themselves - they do this from a list of drivers eligible for scheduled rides. \n\nPer Joel, this is happening (last 30 days) 16,500 times:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 21.47.26.png|width=1198,height=286,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 21.47.26.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 21.47.43.png|width=371,height=407,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 21.47.43.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 21.47.48.png|width=405,height=530,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-12 at 21.47.48.png\"!","2026-01-13T11:40:16.840Z"],["3806465","PFI-832852","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T11:40:28.436Z"],["3806466","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768304455152069]*{color}:\nWe have the generic <@U03P58BK5FY> but what are your thoughts? Should we create a new temporary one for the cases above?\n{quote}","2026-01-13T11:41:09.295Z"],["3806468","WFM-9959","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-13T11:41:38.725Z"],["3806469","FIN2-945","FIN2","vincenzo.rinella@bolt.eu","Vincenzo Aglieri Rinella","[~accountid:712020:11b028d0-a65b-4db4-93f7-938b14e353e9] is this EPIC for you?","2026-01-13T11:41:47.794Z"],["3806470","LSS-56022","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* Slack message sent to Ramone, clarifying figures for the automated online time restrictions.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.41.04 AM.png|width=960,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.41.04 AM.png\"!","2026-01-13T11:42:01.096Z"],["3806473","WFM-9966","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey WFM team, all of the agents [adjo.hodji@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:adjo.hodji@bolt-outsource.eu], [akou.donyo@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:akou.donyo@bolt-outsource.eu], [yannick.weka@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:yannick.weka@bolt-outsource.eu], [essowedeou.ana@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:essowedeou.ana@bolt-outsource.eu] have their *CS - Safety* role assigned, and country accesses : France, Belgium, Malta, Cyprus, Greece. ","2026-01-13T11:43:00.421Z"],["3806483","WFM-9968","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","Hi [~accountid:712020:52653792-3c71-4c24-814c-4fa6697f1bbd] , could you specify if this queue has to be assigned as Primary or Secondary for the agents?","2026-01-13T11:43:33.503Z"],["3806484","WFM-9966","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Can you please add the necessary Safety queues? ","2026-01-13T11:43:36.382Z"],["3806485","SRED-1062","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Nodes stats:\n\n{noformat}$ for nodepool in $(k get nodepool|cut -f 1 -d ' '); do echo \"\\n---\\n$nodepool\"; k get nodeclaim -owide|grep $nodepool|wc -l; sleep 1; done\n---\neng-billing\n       6\n\n---\neng-business\n       4\n\n---\neng-city-solutions (needs switch)\n       8\n\n---\neng-commerce\n       6\n\n---\neng-comms\n       6\n\n---\neng-data-platform\n       2\n\n---\neng-delivery-pricing\n       2\n\n---\neng-drive (needs switch)\n      14\n\n---\neng-driver (switched already)\n       8\n\n---\neng-eater (switched already)\n       8\n\n---\neng-fleet (needs switch)\n      10\n\n---\neng-fraud\n       2\n\n---\neng-geo (switched already)\n      26\n\n---\neng-geo-n\n       2\n\n---\neng-groceries (needs switch)\n       9\n\n---\neng-identity-trust (switched already)\n       5\n\n---\neng-incentives (switched already)\n      15\n\n---\neng-logistics (needs switch)\n      15\n\n---\neng-micromobility (needs switch)\n      16\n\n---\neng-micromobility-n\n       2\n\n---\neng-payments\n       2\n\n---\neng-pint (switched already)\n       4\n\n---\neng-provider (needs switch)\n      10\n\n---\neng-rentals\n       2\n\n---\neng-rider (switched already)\n       4\n\n---\neng-rides-marketplace\n       2\n\n---\neng-safety (needs switch)\n       8\n\n---\neng-shared\n       4\n\n---\neng-tools-workflows (needs switch)\n      10\n\n---\neng-wave\n       2{noformat}","2026-01-13T11:43:52.546Z"],["3806486","SUPX-2317","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","{quote}*= 1*{quote}\n\n:warning: *WARNING :: customer-support-cron :: Cases escalated to agent by cron* Triggered with value *1.33* ","2026-01-13T11:43:56.484Z"],["3806487","SUPX-2317","SUPX",null,"Slack","[Christian Kalme|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ae966399abb77267ba68b16] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C061Q2ULEU8/p1768304128321309?thread_ts=1768304128.321309&cid=C061Q2ULEU8|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C061Q2ULEU8/p1768304128321309?thread_ts=1768304128.321309&cid=C061Q2ULEU8|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-13T11:43:57.433Z"],["3806488","SUPX-2317","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Seems there is some issue with escalations for payment flows. Currently seen this with 5 cases\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722697491|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722697491]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722522580|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722522580]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/721906210|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/721906210]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722435553|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722435553]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/721904787|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/721904787]\n\nPayment flow unlinked, but case is not escalated","2026-01-13T11:43:57.864Z"],["3806489","PFI-807439","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","\nWe will prepare for the funds to be returned.","2026-01-13T11:44:10.718Z"],["3806495","LSS-57632","LSS","nafiu.raheem@bolt.eu","Nafiu Raheem","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1], thank you for this. Comment has been provided. Please review","2026-01-13T11:45:35.842Z"],["3806496","WFM-9971","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey [~accountid:712020:b2d15fe0-4ac2-48c5-9e25-34268c88fe65] ,\n\n*Kindly adhere to the correct template, so that we can clarify your request further.* \n\n*Company:* [Insert company name]\n*Market:* [Insert market/region]\n*Function:* [Insert CS/OPS]\n*Access Duration:* [e.g., Specific Time Range / Permanent]\n*Task Description:* Describe what the admin access is needed for, add relevant admin and KB links(CS)]\n*Bolt Email(s) of Agent(s):* List all agent's Bolt emails either here or attach a file. NO screenshots","2026-01-13T11:45:42.290Z"],["3806497","LSS-61266","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] \n\nWe have completed an initial review - please see our version with comments here [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LxwXKq2JbDsY58t42OwTe48_idAJFEFB/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LxwXKq2JbDsY58t42OwTe48_idAJFEFB/edit|smart-link]  Items which require your input are marked as “For Bolt”. \nHowever, before finalising legal review, we’d like to align on a few points to ensure this is the appropriate agreement and structure for the intended cooperation: \n\n# *Nature of the agreement (priority item)*\nAs currently drafted (see *Clause 3*), our obligations read more like those under a corporate fleet agreement, which seems to assume that Bolt would promote Hyundai internally to employees for vehicle purchase and company-car use. Also, the agreement is structured primarily around the marketing fee, and we did not see references to other forms of support or discount arrangements. \nPlease let us know whether this reflects the intended setup, as this point is key for us in assessing whether the agreement is fit for purpose.\n\nSubject to alignment on point 1:\n\n# *Completion of annexes*\n\nFor Bolt, the following annexes are currently left empty. Please complete the following (2,5,7) and review from a commercial standpoint (3) :\n\n* Annex 2 (List of Affiliates)\n* Annex 3 (Marketing Fees)\n* Annex 5 (Trademark)\n* Annex 7 (Territory)\n\n# *Trademark approval*\nAs noted by Thiago in relation to Clause 4, if the use of Bolt’s trademark is required, obtain the necessary approval from the Brand team.\n\nThank you and let me know if you have any questions. \n\nVeera ","2026-01-13T11:45:45.050Z"],["3806501","PFI-810564","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","A driver can request an Early Cashout if they \n\n* Completed at least 25 trips during the last two months.\n* If there is not any other pending cashout/payout in the balance\n* If the above is met, it might be that some fraud rule is blocking the early cashout option. → Check the fraud score or create a ticket to Commerce Fraud\n* If the above reasons did not solve the problem, it might be a technical issue. → For this please create a ticket for Tech Support","2026-01-13T11:46:32.095Z"],["3806505","PFI-832855","PFI","nara.aiamlaoo@bolt-outsource.eu","Nara Aiamlaoo","!image-20260113-114557.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260113-114610.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260113-114624.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T11:47:11.423Z"],["3806506","PFI-826388","PFI","yuliia.nenasheva@bolt.eu","Yuliia Nenasheva","Payouts all done.","2026-01-13T11:47:13.658Z"],["3806507","RS-1782","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Following the tender Slack channel (https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C08GHN0R5QT) it would appear Sustainability input was not required for the submission. Should the need arise, we welcome the Licensing team to raise another ticket. ","2026-01-13T11:47:16.857Z"],["3806512","PRODSEC-576","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Added schedule in databricks notebook each 6h","2026-01-13T11:47:28.928Z"],["3806513","PRODSEC-577","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/GgCOuAE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/GgCOuAE|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T11:47:40.304Z"],["3806514","LSS-59572","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432],\n\nCould you please help us obtain *Ahto’s wet-ink signatures* on the attached NDA? Please note that *Ahto should sign every page*, not just the final page.\n\nMany thanks!\n\n[^NDA - ENG - BK 2021 - BK recibe info (3).docx]\n\n","2026-01-13T11:47:44.982Z"],["3806515","PFI-832825","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Fondy portal is currently down :( Checking with Fondy. \n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768303282988979|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768303282988979]","2026-01-13T11:48:06.100Z"],["3806516","PFI-809849","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","payout was bounced back thus rejected and added to partner balance !\r\n\r\n","2026-01-13T11:48:08.029Z"],["3806517","WFM-9970","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Request approved","2026-01-13T11:48:08.103Z"],["3806520","WFM-9970","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","[request|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541704]","2026-01-13T11:48:20.128Z"],["3806521","PFI-832557","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! We have reported this issue to engineers already and they’re looking into this → will keep you updated if we receive any updates. ","2026-01-13T11:48:46.808Z"],["3806523","PFI-832557","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1767597721342579|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1767597721342579|smart-card]","2026-01-13T11:49:01.540Z"],["3806525","PFI-832557","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! \n\nLooks like this issue needs input from our developers. The issue has been flagged to them & they are investigating. We will keep you posted with any updates! \n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T11:49:15.210Z"],["3806526","PFI-812948","PFI","victor.garces@bolt.eu","Víctor Garcés","Perfect, and understood. Please keep us posted as per the above discussion! and many thanks Ketlin.","2026-01-13T11:49:19.574Z"],["3806527","PFI-832857","PFI","jakub.pekar@bolt-outsource.eu","Jakub Pekar","[^20251208_Ing. David Žďárský_Oznámenie o oprave chýb.pdf.pdf]\n\n!image-20260113-114800.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260113-114822.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T11:49:19.587Z"],["3806528","PFI-832857","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T11:49:29.723Z"],["3806529","FC-915","FC","mirjam.arrak@bolt.eu","Mirjam Arrak","As all AV CC-s have related worktags set up starting Dec 2025 that only permit Autonomous Driving BL with AV CCs, we shouldn’t have any costs where BL = All in those AV CCs.","2026-01-13T11:49:30.717Z"],["3806530","RPA-298","RPA","afolashakin.ajayi@bolt.eu","Afolashakin Ajayi","From our discussion today [~accountid:712020:cffcb775-5358-4c94-bc0f-1e597facd7da] \n\n* Questions:\n** How can we set up the experiment to be able to track this?\n** How can we separate scouts from drivers?\n** Any other analytics event tracking we need ahead of the experiment?\n* Answers from [+Georg Gorbatovski+|mailto:georg.gorbatovski@bolt.eu]:\n** We randomize based on referrer, track the campaign tiers completed per referee\n** Main metrics to track:\n*** Most beneficial for us to have more referrals i.e. number of referrals with x amount of finished rides with treatment vs control\n*** Avg referees per partner\n*** Number of finished rides per referee\n*** Numbers of tiers completed per referee\n*** 7D activation rate (control vs treatment)\n** Enrolment criteria: Check with engineering if it is possible to have enrollment criteria as follows: Enroll to control or treatment only AFTER they have at least one referral during the experiment window.\n** Sample size: Need to potentially run a pre-analysis\n*** Need access to the base table to be able to run analysis on the number of referrals per driver\n*** Engineering POC: [+Mariia Nazarenko+|mailto:mariia.nazarenko@bolt.eu] \n* Other things to do:\n** Announcement story: For awareness of the referrals tracking and to get more referrals\n*** [+Afolashakin Ajayi+|mailto:afolashakin.ajayi@bolt.eu] to speak with [+Alex David+|mailto:constantin.david@bolt.eu] \n** Create JIRA task for experiment setup\n*** [+Afolashakin Ajayi+|mailto:afolashakin.ajayi@bolt.eu] to create the ticket","2026-01-13T11:49:53.963Z"],["3806531","DSR-3295","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Update from SD ticket - device is unblocked now","2026-01-13T11:50:17.293Z"],["3806532","PFA-503","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","Carried over - will be negotiated with Hena","2026-01-13T11:50:32.540Z"],["3806533","UXA-2190","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","I’ve tried if i can external IP from the request, but it’s not possible. We need to pass it explicitly from the clients to the oidc-provider.","2026-01-13T11:50:41.646Z"],["3806534","LSS-60589","LSS","ana.rosa@bolt.eu","Ana Rosa","Hey [~accountid:712020:54af1c3b-f46c-435b-b870-e013cd29eada]  - the ticket was raised pertaining just one order (the 11k one), which happened in October, in France. We confirm that so far, we haven’t been able to reach out to the erroneous paid party and start any repayment plan, so maybe [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] can help us and clarify the scenario 2 option?","2026-01-13T11:50:43.044Z"],["3806544","WD-22558","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hi expense item *Sports* added for South Africa","2026-01-13T11:52:12.029Z"],["3806545","SOBB-1019","SOBB","luca.cardoso@bolt.eu","Luca Cardoso de Gouvea","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1TBYwtL2mBXh_a-tHrRfl8J7trA5JCYjl3s18ZO5Kzv0/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1TBYwtL2mBXh_a-tHrRfl8J7trA5JCYjl3s18ZO5Kzv0/edit?usp=sharing]","2026-01-13T11:52:13.366Z"],["3806547","WD-22551","WD","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey [~accountid:5e5cecb04befbd0c96cab72a] \n\nI need the actual PDFs downloaded in bulk, I am currently only able to figure out how to download the invoices one by one. \n\nIf I am mistaken, please slack msg me and show me in a call as to how I can self-serve the bulk download.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-13T11:52:24.134Z"],["3806549","PFI-811020","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Hey, as the payments were sent to collection account we received and allocated all the payment to this fleet balance.\n106,55 EUR on 11.08 [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/63946208|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/63946208]\n\n321,65 EUR on 02.09 [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/65700350|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/65700350]\n\n419,82 EUR on 10.10 [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/68985942|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/68985942]\n\nAll these payments would have then been account for their [next regular payouts |https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22show_empty_rejection_code%22%3Afalse%2C%22show_total%22%3Afalse%2C%22external_client_id%22%3A184898%7D%7D]and all funds would have been returned back to the fleet in this case as part of their payouts and would have been reflected on their reports. \n","2026-01-13T11:52:32.238Z"],["3806552","ITI-1155","ITI","marko.toomla@bolt.eu","Marko Toomla","Made some minor changes since the Approval Engine Trigger was edited by automation every 15 minutes. Changed the field type to numbers and now count the number of approvals, which may reduce the edit action.","2026-01-13T11:53:10.357Z"],["3806558","DELIVERY-1403","DELIVERY","cristian.uricec@bolt.eu","Cristian-Dumitru Uricec","26W3: We continued working on it, we started implementation of the new services.","2026-01-13T11:53:50.254Z"],["3806560","DELIVERY-107","DELIVERY","cristian.uricec@bolt.eu","Cristian-Dumitru Uricec","26W3: A/B test started.","2026-01-13T11:54:11.796Z"],["3806562","DELIVERY-1077","DELIVERY","cristian.uricec@bolt.eu","Cristian-Dumitru Uricec","26W3: Development finished. QA will start testing.","2026-01-13T11:55:02.081Z"],["3806563","PFI-832857","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hi,\n\nif there is some data that needs to be fixed about driver’s profile becauase they were incorrectly onboarded - please reach out to local ops so they could properly onboard the driver.","2026-01-13T11:55:04.649Z"],["3806565","PFI-832860","PFI","paulina.grigaliunaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Paulina Grigaliūnaitė","[^Mokejimas_RMO24799213 (3).pdf]","2026-01-13T11:55:25.341Z"],["3806566","PFI-832860","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T11:55:27.840Z"],["3806572","DELIVERY-1009","DELIVERY","cristian.uricec@bolt.eu","Cristian-Dumitru Uricec","26W3: We started the experimentation phase where we want to understand what would be the best vector DB for our needs. Currently researching RedisDB and ES.","2026-01-13T11:56:43.143Z"],["3806574","LSS-61152","LSS","karolina.tadych@bolt.eu","Karolina Tadych","Any update on this please \n\n","2026-01-13T11:56:45.545Z"],["3806575","SRED-1062","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","{{eng-city-solutions}} *before*:\n\n{noformat}8 nodes (   10944Mi/15153800Ki) 74.0% memory ██████████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░ $0.356/hour | $260.172/month\n1,950 pods (0 pending 1,950 running 1,950 bound)\n\nip-172-28-119-31.eu-central-1.compute.internal  memory ███████████████████████████████████  99% (13 pods) c6g.large/$0.0776  On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-160-124.eu-central-1.compute.internal memory █████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  61% (8 pods)  c6g.medium/$0.0388 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-190-46.eu-central-1.compute.internal  memory ██████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  51% (8 pods)  c6g.medium/$0.0388 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-122-216.eu-central-1.compute.internal memory █████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  61% (8 pods)  c6g.medium/$0.0388 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-158-158.eu-central-1.compute.internal memory █████████████████████████████████░░  95% (7 pods)  c6g.medium/$0.0388 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-187-45.eu-central-1.compute.internal  memory ██████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░  62% (8 pods)  m6g.medium/$0.0460 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-145-12.eu-central-1.compute.internal  memory ██████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  51% (8 pods)  c6g.medium/$0.0388 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-142-155.eu-central-1.compute.internal memory █████████████████████████████████░░  95% (8 pods)  c6g.medium/$0.0388 On-Demand - Ready -{noformat}\n\nAfter:\n\n{noformat}4 nodes (   10144Mi/12836928Ki) 80.9% memory ████████████████████████████████░░░░░░░░ $0.310/hour | $226.592/month\n1,781 pods (0 pending 1,781 running 1,781 bound)\n\nip-172-28-163-58.eu-central-1.compute.internal  memory ███████████████████████████████████  99% (13 pods) c6g.large/$0.0776 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-112-206.eu-central-1.compute.internal memory ███████████████████████████████████  99% (14 pods) c6g.large/$0.0776 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-187-23.eu-central-1.compute.internal  memory ██████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░  63% (11 pods) c6g.large/$0.0776 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-120-204.eu-central-1.compute.internal memory ██████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░  63% (10 pods) c6g.large/$0.0776 On-Demand - Ready -{noformat}","2026-01-13T11:57:21.491Z"],["3806579","PFI-808686","PFI","kitija.akmane@bolt.eu","Kitija Akmane","Hello [~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24] \n\nWhat is the specific ETA for this issue to be resolved? The user has been charged 66,20 EUR more without any reason. I also need to know why this has happened so the information can be provided to the user. They have spent over 700 EUR for this ride and they deserve to know the reason for something that looks like fraud from our side.","2026-01-13T11:58:11.930Z"],["3806581","PFI-832860","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-13T11:58:34.668Z"],["3806582","PFI-832794","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-13T11:58:35.384Z"],["3806583","SRED-1062","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","{{eng-drive}} *before*:\n\n{noformat}14 nodes (   33584Mi/50093268Ki) 68.7% memory ███████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░ $0.652/hour | $475.668/month\n1,950 pods (0 pending 1,950 running 1,950 bound)\n\nip-172-28-115-233.eu-central-1.compute.internal memory ██████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░  74% (8 pods) m6g.medium/$0.0460 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-135-77.eu-central-1.compute.internal  memory ███████████████████████████░░░░░░░░  78% (8 pods) m6g.medium/$0.0460 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-190-96.eu-central-1.compute.internal  memory ██████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░  74% (8 pods) m6g.medium/$0.0460 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-190-221.eu-central-1.compute.internal memory ██████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░  74% (8 pods) m6g.medium/$0.0460 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-127-58.eu-central-1.compute.internal  memory ████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  46% (8 pods) r6g.medium/$0.0608 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-149-204.eu-central-1.compute.internal memory ██████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░  74% (8 pods) m6g.medium/$0.0460 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-181-20.eu-central-1.compute.internal  memory ███████████████████████████░░░░░░░░  78% (8 pods) m6g.medium/$0.0460 On-Demand - Ready -\nip-172-28-147-248.eu-central-1.compute.internal memory ████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░  69% (7 pods) m6g.medium/$0.0460 On-D