sa Kamarik","Closing ticket as funds would have been already paid with the next regular payout cycle. ","2026-01-13T12:06:06.823Z"],["3806626","BDB-1521","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] ok, let’s do it his way! \nBut could you please change the copy in the media plan?\nThank you","2026-01-13T12:06:21.200Z"],["3806627","PFI-832814","PFI","ugne.guigaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Ugnė Guigaitė","Resolved","2026-01-13T12:06:22.671Z"],["3806630","PFI-808686","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:5d831b1d30926d0c33b2795f] \n\nUnfortunately, I’m not able to advise on this. \n[~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] Do you have an ETA when the issue would be fixed? ","2026-01-13T12:06:59.818Z"],["3806631","PFI-832864","PFI","volodymyr.gonchar@bolt.eu","Volodymyr Gonchar","[^Bolt Club_Ukraine_Sep 2025.pdf]","2026-01-13T12:07:08.293Z"],["3806632","PFI-832864","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T12:07:10.279Z"],["3806634","HS-28901","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-13T12:07:23.742Z"],["3806635","WFM-9966","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","Hi WFM team, the following adjustments were applied, please double-check form your side if needed and leaving for changes in Assembled 🙌 \n[adjo.hodji|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/232458?tab=settings] - has only mentioned queues as primary and [+01 RH_Greece_T1+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/queues/edit/960009?tab=manage_agents] as a fallback\n[akou.donyo|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/232772?tab=settings] - has only mentioned queues as primary and [+01 RH_Cyprus_T1+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/queues/edit/180016?tab=manage_agents] & 01 RH_Greece_T1 assigned as a fallback \n[yannick.weka|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/562467?tab=queues] - has all mentioned queues as as primary, none of fallback or secondary \n\n[essowedeou.ana|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/382364?tab=queues] - has all mentioned queues as promary, 01 RH_France_T1 & 01 RH_France_T1_Low/Moderate changes to 2nd prio\n","2026-01-13T12:07:37.623Z"],["3806636","PFI-808116","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Driver has cleared balance via cashout","2026-01-13T12:08:05.461Z"],["3806641","LSS-61404","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ! May you please give me an access to the doc.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-13T12:09:45.055Z"],["3806642","PFI-808167","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Hey, please return the funds using the the same account details where you received this payment from and using the Payment ID as reference, just as you see on the payment reference you received. Our system should they pick this up as a return, but do share the payment link for reference to check if it worked or we need to manually mark it. ","2026-01-13T12:10:31.400Z"],["3806645","PFI-808176","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T12:11:12.382Z"],["3806646","WFM-9965","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","Hi team, all agents apart from Silvester Peter have access all to countries and cities, however Silvester Peter has access to Canada. Also, all agents have RH role","2026-01-13T12:11:35.139Z"],["3806647","DO-5787","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Unused github action removed\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-pypi-internal/pull/27|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-pypi-internal/pull/27|smart-card]\n\n ","2026-01-13T12:11:42.115Z"],["3806648","LSS-59572","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] !\n\n[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] would gladly assist.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-13T12:11:53.394Z"],["3806649","LSS-61404","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432], access is shared with you. \n\nThank you! ","2026-01-13T12:12:00.812Z"],["3806650","LSS-61459","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:a9500cde-28bc-4a8e-95d6-7818a2252cf8] \n\nit’s Rides only, correct ?\n\nI will share template that we had with banks and other financial institution. ","2026-01-13T12:12:02.732Z"],["3806652","LSS-55755","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd], thanks for picking this up! \nYes, we have signed the DSA previously with the main agreement, but I wanted your confirmation with the wording used in this new Annex 1 of the Appendix 1.","2026-01-13T12:12:22.214Z"],["3806653","WD-22415","WD","mo.salama@bolt.eu","Mo Salama","Hi Dominika,\n\nArmenia & Uganda ==> not active in Payroll\n\nCyprus, Uzbekistan, Kazakhstan, Malaysia & Thailand ==> transitioned to Papaya\n\nSincerely,\n\nMo","2026-01-13T12:12:25.219Z"],["3806659","LSS-61124","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Order Form_Bolt Operations OÜ_Qminder Limited_05.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T12:13:16.359Z"],["3806660","PFI-829951","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","კოლეგებო, სალამი.  \n\n  \n\nარ მიგვიღია უკუკავშირი. \n\n  \n\nროგორ მოვიქცეთ მოვხსნათ ბლოკი?  \n\n   \n\nSincerely, \n\n________________________________________ \n\nთეკლე გოი/ Tekle goi \n\nCard Manager \n\nCustomer Support Department \n\nTel: +(995 32) 2 27 27 27 \n\n[{color:#0563C1}www.tbcbank.ge{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge] \n\n  \n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!{color:#0093D3}{color}","2026-01-13T12:13:23.190Z"],["3806667","DO-5788","DO","kristo.sarnets@bolt.eu","Kristo Sarnets","Yup, works now.\n\nThanks a lot 🙂 ","2026-01-13T12:14:25.729Z"],["3806668","DRAG101-405","DRAG101","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] With the old controller there is no way for the scooter itself to determine which motor is installed, right? \n\nI gave it some thought and I think we can not do as I described above, because if we lower the output power to match the 365W with the new motor,  it will also reduce the output power with the old 350W motor even further, which will make the scooters sluggish and we are already getting feedback that our scooter is slow..","2026-01-13T12:14:42.110Z"],["3806671","FIN2-945","FIN2","toomas.parts@bolt.eu","Toomas-Hendrik Parts","[~accountid:712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] Sorry, what does ‘EPIC’ mean in this context? Our teams responsibility is to analyse to cooperation agreement with the Partner to make sure we do not exercise control (in accounting terms) over them.","2026-01-13T12:15:26.354Z"],["3806677","PFI-832856","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nWhat an interesting case! \n\nThe payment failed can caused a negative balance of 3.23 HRK. \nI can see there has been a conversion 3.23 HRK to 0.43 EUR on 01/01/2023, 15:54. \n\nConversions on balances is not a feature that Bolt is able to offer to customers. \n\nThe conversion happened because Croatia adopted EUR currency on 1st of Jan 2023. All of the balances in HRK were converted to EUR. \n\nI could not find any evidence of the customer creating a top up. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T12:17:20.891Z"],["3806679","BDB-1461","BDB","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","Hey [~accountid:5d289a7c3e09b40c262cfaa9]! Do we already have a logo for Hopp Plus that we can use for setting up LCM automations for the launch?","2026-01-13T12:17:27.798Z"],["3806680","SCM-800","SCM","federico.levi@bolt.eu","Federico Levi","*Update and project end*:\ndue to original google sheets capability, the Relocation dashboard has moved to a new file:\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1h981z4ZzkKkFBh_V1qGSSB0ypcQ3kP2eTf_xRkW722c/edit?gid=276065013#gid=276065013|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1h981z4ZzkKkFBh_V1qGSSB0ypcQ3kP2eTf_xRkW722c/edit?gid=276065013#gid=276065013|smart-link] \n\n❗  Please note: these calculations will suggest relocation options, but won’t tie us to follow blindly the below “settings”❗ \n\n[*Relocation settings*|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1h981z4ZzkKkFBh_V1qGSSB0ypcQ3kP2eTf_xRkW722c/edit?gid=659794121#gid=659794121]:\n\n* Country mapping\nwe used a map to identify (and exclude) the countries which we will connect with relocation options.\nWhat we want to avoid is to suggest relocation options that would impact on the Logistics costs (example, we’ll exclude transportations from Estonia to Portugal due to distance; we will exclude transportations between countries where customs costs will apply [exception for CH and NO, where the Dragon fleet might require active stock relocations]\n* Spare parts criticality (critical vs non-critical)\nWe have identified two groups of critical spare parts: the business critical ones, agreed with management, and those for which the CWH stock can’t support the entire network with a 3 months buffer stock\n* Cities priorities\nBased on RpV and GMV, we have ranked all our cities and grouped them in 4 tiers. For the Relocation, if a city has overstock of an item and two cities need that item, the higher tier city will be prioritised\n\n*QTYs to relocate*:\n\nIn the [original dashboard|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1cM2tNxN__5oAXlO0PnQvwzpN1_hLMKUUvqWlTl0_WyU/edit?gid=895481172#gid=895481172&range=BB5:BE5], we have calculated two groups of data:\n\n* How much to relocate: knowing the expected consumption of the next months, we have identified per each city and each item what’s the quantity of stock which is “overstocked”. We will consider relocatable the overstock by more than 4 months worth of expected consumption.\n_4 months explained_: we aim to provide a 3 months buffer stock to the cities, and we add an extra month of consumption to the calculations to avoid relocating parts from A to B and then resupplying parts from CWH to A.\n* How much to receive: knowing the expected consumption of the next months, we have identifyied per each city and each item what’s the quantity of stock which keeps the warehouse not “understock” (less than a month worth of expected consumption\n\n\n\nThe Relocation dashboard takes all the above bullets in consideration and suggests relocation options.\n\n*Extra features*:\n\n* _fully automated by AppScript_ 🚀  - the calculation refreshes with the click of a button, which allows proper planning rather than a live update of data based on spare parts consumption\n* _internal relocation weekly report created_ 🗓️  - LOPS will be more incline to internally relocate spare parts. We plan to test and continuously provide local teams with this report on Mondays.","2026-01-13T12:17:28.817Z"],["3806681","PFI-819935","PFI","anna.zaritska@bolt.eu","Anna Zaritska","Hi colleagues! Could we please sync on the next steps for this case?\nAre there any remaining blockers?\n\n","2026-01-13T12:17:43.313Z"],["3806682","HS-28830","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Employee cancelled.","2026-01-13T12:17:49.617Z"],["3806683","LSS-61315","LSS","ivan.halapa@bolt.eu","Ivan Halapa","[^20260113121407_001.pdf]\n\nHi [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf], Scanned document attached.","2026-01-13T12:18:10.811Z"],["3806685","L10N-27491","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27488](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27488)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T12:18:14.826Z"],["3806686","L10N-27490","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27488](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27488)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T12:18:15.589Z"],["3806687","L10N-27498","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27488](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27488)\n\nThanks for 