ic here: [L10N-27458](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27458)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T12:18:35.724Z"],["3806699","PFI-808184","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Please contact Billing team to move the balance from one client to the other. \nIf this is related to one specific payment, we can reallocate the funds, but if now one specific payment, the balances need adjustment. ","2026-01-13T12:18:42.812Z"],["3806701","WD-22557","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:712020:c6829626-18d0-4d73-9974-74d1569b4bdf] , can you please confirm that I can remove you from the roles of these three companies? \n\nAdditionally, do I need to grant access for Birgit and Karmen also for Account Certifications?\nCC [~accountid:623de186b75ca8007057c6f9] [~accountid:712020:07f1e332-abd8-45eb-a3b9-0dd3708ef2d7] ","2026-01-13T12:19:04.391Z"],["3806702","PFI-832794","PFI","tomasz.mendziuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Tomasz Mendziuk","still need help ","2026-01-13T12:19:22.142Z"],["3806707","PFI-832470","PFI","folashade.akinsola@bolt.eu","Folashade Dolapo Akinsola","The issue was raised by Kongapay, who observed that when their invoices are downloaded, the name displayed is *ROSETTI PIVOT LIMITED* instead of *Kongapay*. The client has expressed concern, as they have no affiliation with ROSETTI PIVOT LIMITED, and the account manager has confirmed that no changes were made to their business profile.\n\nKindly assist in clarifying why this is occurring and how it can be corrected, as the client is keen to understand how this happened. An invoice downloaded today is attached for reference, showing ROSETTI PIVOT LIMITED instead of Kongapay. Thank you.\n\n[^NG6526-533.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T12:21:49.760Z"],["3806708","CSDA-291","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hey hey! Thank you for raising a request to our team 🙌 \n\nUnfortunately, it is not possible to build such a report in Looker at the moment. I will leave this request to be in the backlog for now.\n\nAs for the data points - do you need them now for any reason, or can it wait untill February/March when the new Looker report will be built?","2026-01-13T12:21:50.190Z"],["3806711","LSS-60076","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] \n\n* As expected, Certinal didn’t accept termination for convenience \n* FYI SLA for monthly avaliability 99,5 % \n* We got termination right in case of montly availability breach. If Supplier fails to maintain an average monthly Certinal uptime availability of at least 99.5% for three (3) consecutive calendar months, or for any four (4) calendar months in any rolling twelve (12) month period during the agreed term, the Licensee shall have the right to terminate this Agreement or relevant Order without any liability or obligation to pay fees for future years. \n\nWe are ready to move with signing [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yO5HZLl_x7XSc3bhZKpACDQlmyHd-pKb/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yO5HZLl_x7XSc3bhZKpACDQlmyHd-pKb/edit|smart-link] \n\nDo we have signing details from Certinal ?","2026-01-13T12:22:29.483Z"],["3806713","PFI-832870","PFI","timofey.shapovalov@bolt-outsource.eu","Timofey Shapovalov","!IMG_3124.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T12:23:05.549Z"],["3806715","BB-2162","BB","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Thank youu [~accountid:62fc9aa82e3849d137774ba7] \n\nBalance fix has been completed →  [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-adjustment/adjustmentApproval/details/33997|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-adjustment/adjustmentApproval/details/33997]","2026-01-13T12:23:31.145Z"],["3806716","LSS-60753","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Thank you [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] \nWill be done EOD 👌 ","2026-01-13T12:23:31.178Z"],["3806719","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Can you please review and approve [this PR|https://github.com/bolteu/s3-configless/pull/432]?\nIt has to be reviewed by Bolt Business.\nThanks.","2026-01-13T12:24:44.738Z"],["3806722","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Reviewed both PRs related to this ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-13T12:25:45.544Z"],["3806726","GRWA-1500","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","Negative spend is expected behavior in incentives data. Here’s why:\nDrivers are initially paid the full incentive amount when a campaign runs.\nLater, the Incentives team may review performance and find that some drivers did not meet the campaign requirements (e.g., incomplete tasks, low activity, missing criteria).\nWhen this happens, the previously paid amount is deducted from the driver, which appears in the data as a negative spend.\n\n# This is why some days show negative values it reflects adjustments or clawbacks rather than new negative incentives.\n\nWhy we shouldn’t filter out negative values\nFiltering out negative numbers would distort the true spend. Example:\n\n* 01/01: +100 EUR incentive paid\n* 02/01: –10 EUR adjustment (driver didn’t qualify)\n\nIf we remove the –10 EUR:\nDashboard shows 100 EUR spend\n\n* Actual spend is 90 EUR\n\nSo the negative values are important to accurately represent real net incentive spend.","2026-01-13T12:26:58.797Z"],["3806729","LSS-61357","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] [~accountid:712020:985a985c-b403-41bd-b116-abbf44b22175] I took a look at the orders, please move forward with signing ","2026-01-13T12:27:32.168Z"],["3806731","PFI-830609","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo, \n\nRegarding the start date, should I set it for next week, or do you have any preference?","2026-01-13T12:27:40.099Z"],["3806733","LSS-61424","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Dokobit: [https://app.dokobit.com/signing/16da3be42222b887f349a8941e9974af2702c6ce|https://app.dokobit.com/signing/16da3be42222b887f349a8941e9974af2702c6ce]","2026-01-13T12:27:50.131Z"],["3806737","LSS-60149","LSS","edik.davtian@bolt.eu","Edik Davtian","upd: request was shared with the partner - so it is on my side","2026-01-13T12:28:24.799Z"],["3806738","PFI-808167","PFI","karl.kastein@bolt.eu","Karl Johan Kastein","[^payment.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T12:28:36.504Z"],["3806739","PFI-832470","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","The name is still set to ROSETTI PIVOT LIMITED.\n\n!image-20260113-122605.png|width=657,alt=\"image-20260113-122605.png\"!\n\nBased on the Audit Log, the change was done by employees internally: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/audit-log/audit-logs/view/5127874416|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/audit-log/audit-logs/view/5127874416]","2026-01-13T12:28:45.282Z"],["3806742","FX-3616","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768307360137889]*{color}:\nI checked it locally, nothing can break in the test.\nTest passed last checks - [https://jenkins.boltint.net/job/Bolt/job/bolt-server/job/develop/136548/testReport/jun[…]arch_Company_Application___Correct_sorting_is_used/history/|https://jenkins.boltint.net/job/Bolt/job/bolt-server/job/develop/136548/testReport/junit/%5Bcomp%5D/src_rides_vehicle_vehicle_marketplace_test_comp_application_fop-search-company-application-comp/Vehicle_Marketplace___Fleet_Owner_Portal___Search_Company_Application___Correct_sorting_is_used/history/]\n{quote}","2026-01-13T12:29:34.676Z"],["3806745","FX-3616","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768307385770589]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3616 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T12:30:06.702Z"],["3806746","PFI-829951","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","შეასრულეთ.{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}  \n\n  \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n   \n\n პატივისცემით \n\n +Best Regards+ \n\n  \n\n{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#595959} -{color} {color:#595959}მირა წოწორია / Miranda{color} {color:#595959}Mira{color} {color:#595959} tsotsoria{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Customer Journey Expert{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Payments Development Tribe{color}{color:#595959}{color} \n\n[{color:#595959}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#595959}{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge/]{color:#595959}{color}{color:#595959}{color}\n !image001.png|thumbnail!{color:#595959}{color}","2026-01-13T12:30:07.569Z"],["3806748","PFI-832872","PFI","oluwaferanmi.arogundade@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwaferanmi Arogundade","!Screenshot_20251219_170834_com_hihonor_hnoffice_PDFPhoneActivity0.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T12:30:15.452Z"],["3806749","PFI-830336","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo, done. will go live on 01.02 → [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/174977?tab=profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/174977?tab=profile]","2026-01-13T12:30:22.217Z"],["3806750","LSS-60738","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Amendment To Appendix A – Service Fees (edited).docx (3).adoc] ","2026-01-13T12:31:00.130Z"],["3806751","LOC-4690","LOC","laura.suveika@bolt.eu","Laura Suveika","The LV General Manager for Rides, Kristine, said that this is not an appropriate time for this type of campaign. Considering that there was recently negative PR and the general sentiment was more about riders needing to be more polite, I agree with her view. Please opt out LV.","2026-01-13T12:31:03.121Z"],["3806754","PFI-808167","PFI","karl.kastein@bolt.eu","Karl Johan Kastein","Hey, I transferred the money back, see the payment doc attached. Thanks.","2026-01-13T12:31:16.339Z"],["3806755","PFI-812866","PFI","kiril.pahhomov@bolt-outsource.eu","Kiril Pahhomov","Will the user keep receiving the invoices with a correct name now?","2026-01-13T12:31:19.468Z"],["3806756","DSR-3705","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T12:31:24.411Z"],["3806757","PFI-832836","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:63baf8b7-d00b-423e-815e-9c22e82927d0],\n\nSeems like this has mainly occurred due to the fact that these orders were extremely short distance, while the campaigns were also applied *and* it was the same rider, due to all of these overlapping, then yes, our rules stepped in as this is rather unnatural.\nHowever, nothing really indicates straightly onto fraud, and since we are not 100% certain, then please manually compensate the driver for the loss of their earnings, it seems that after their bonuses the incident has not repeat itself.\nAdditionally, if such cases seem to repeat in the given city more often, then please gather up all the drivers that have been affected and then submit a new ticket, in that case we would have a reason to look over our rules and perhaps make an exception for the given city, however, we will not be doing so for 1 driver.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-13T12:31:25.315Z"],["3806758","PFI-832865","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe user had three payments for the amount of 255.29 GHS on 31st of December. \n\nThe first two attempts failed with an error message Payment expired. This means the customer did not authorize the payment and it was rejected. \nI have checked with Cellulant and the customer has not been charged for those. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3995370458|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3995370458]\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3995469731|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3995469731]\n\nThe third payment was successful.\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3995404233|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3995404233]\n\nSince Bolt did not receive any funds for the failed payments then I would suggest the user to reach out to their mobile money service provider to check if the money has gotten stuck with them. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T12:31:29.216Z"],["3806761","LSS-61499","LSS","tomasz.symonowicz@bolt.eu","Tomasz Symonowicz","[^Szczególne warunki Bolt Business PL 16.12_zwer..pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T12:32:43.467Z"],["3806763","PFI-832864","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nWhat you refer to is commission netting and it is supported in Ukraine - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/3978592615/Commission+Netting+Rollout+List|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/3978592615/Commission+Netting+Rollout+List|smart-link] \n\nIt works so that if we pay some sort of bonus - it gets deducted from the commission that driver pays to us → we owe smaller VAT.\n\nIt is automatic that bonuses get deducted.\n\n*Does it help?*\n\n\n\nI also attach FAQ about Commission netting that we share with CS teams - might be useful.\n\n\nHey,\n\nIn Ukraine we have commission netting.\n\n_Through commission netting, your campaigns/bonuses/compensations are reflected as a discount from your commission, instead of each having their individual invoices. Simply, your commission is reduced in the amount of your campaigns/bonuses/compensations - ensuring a more clear invoicing process, and less invoicing noise._\n\n_For example, previously you would see a commission of 416.91€ and separate bonus lines of 11€ on your invoice, which totaled up to 361.92€. Now, you would only see a single row of commission in the amount of 361.92€, meaning the calculation is already done in the background._\n\n\n\nExample for some [Driver|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/3318350?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]:\n\nTaking November 2025 example from [Balance history|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/balanceHistory?balanceHistoryFilterSearch=%7B%22external_id%22%3A3318350%2C%22type%22%3A%22Driver%22%2C%22month%22%3A%7B%22month%22%3A11%2C%22year%22%3A2025%7D%2C%22viewType%22%3A%22monthly%22%2C%22week%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1762725600000%2C%22end%22%3A1763330399999%7D%7D]. \n\nCommission that driver had to pay is\n\n{quote}*Commission = expense_cash_commission* + *expense_commission* (48.50 EUR + 190.83 EUR) = €239.33 EUR{quote}\n\nthis commission is ±20% of the amount driver had in Ride fees\n\n{quote}Fees = *earning_in_app_ride_fee* + *earning_cash_ride_fee* (947.70 EUR + 242.50 EUR) = €1,190.20 EUR\n\nCommission % = commission / fees = €239.33 EUR / 1,190.20 EUR = 0.20 = 20%{quote}\n\nthe [invoice|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5649895597?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] was issued for 132.94 euro, which is less than 239.33 because we do *commission netting* in Estonia.\n\n{quote}*What is Commission Netting?*\n\n*Commission netting* is a process used to simplify how drivers are invoiced for commissions, especially when there are bonuses, campaigns, or compensations involved.\n\n*Without Netting:*\n\nNormally, a driver would receive separate invoices:\n\nOne for the commission they owe (e.g., 20% of ride fees)\n\nSeparate invoices for any bonuses, campaigns, or compensations they receive\n\n*With Netting (as done in Estonia):*\n\nInstead of issuing multiple invoices, the system *reduces the commission amount* by the total value of any bonuses, campaigns, or compensations the driver earned.\n\nThe driver receives a *single, lower commission invoice* that already accounts for these discounts.{quote}\n\nYou can see discounts earned via cash and app rides in *earning_cash_discount_netted* and *earning_in_app_discount_netted.*\n\nSo we can calculate the final netted commission like this:\n\n{quote}Netted Commission = Commission - *earning_cash_discount_netted - earning_in_app_discount_netted* = €239.33 - 26.70 EUR - 79.70 EUR = €132.93{quote}\n\n132.93 is the same amount you can see on Monthly invoice (take invoice from November from [+here+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients/128179276?tab=partner_invoices&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn])\n\n✨ That’s how you can calculate Commission Netting in Balance history.\n\nNikolay Roll   ","2026-01-13T12:32:47.960Z"],["3806764","PFI-832847","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi [@julia.markuszewska|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U08E8KJNS83],\n\nWill be copy-paste’ng the same answer as I provided in the Slack channel.\n\nThis is a rather suspicious user/business.\nThe user requesting it in a hurry has not done a single order with us, seems to be a shadow account created in 2021.\nAdditionally, the business owner failed all the verification attempts, that's why the card adding failed.\nThey tried to add 2x different US origin cards and 2x different cards origining from Oman. All 4 different cards with the user failed the verifications. \nI can also see that one of the error codes was 327 which is a temporary error response from payment service provider based on their own anti fraud measures.\nPlease advise them to reach out to their bank as anti fraud response is not from our side and might be card related, however, most likely they will not be reaching out as this looks highly suspicious. Thank you.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-13T12:33:10.464Z"],["3806766","PFI-832795","PFI","ugne.guigaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Ugnė Guigaitė","Another payout rejected: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233606493?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233606493?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-13T12:33:16.216Z"],["3806767","PFI-829364","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Hi completed, will go live on 01.02-> [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/186180?tab=profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/186180?tab=profile]","2026-01-13T12:33:56.493Z"],["3806768","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Perfect.\n\nDid these changes have any impact on the Reseller service?\n\nIn [this PR|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15360], I refactored the IAM permission to make it similar to {{bolt-business-portal}} .\nI applied the changes.\nIf you notice any issues with the Reseller service, please let me know to revert the changes.\nIf you notice any errors like permission denied or a specific error about S3, please share them with me.\nThanks. 🙏 ","2026-01-13T12:33:57.281Z"],["3806769","PFI-825367","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi [~accountid:63ca4493d7f68827e6b6763b]  \n\n*I reissued the invoice several times → But invoice still comes out with incorrect data?*\n\nIf you reissue an invoice several times and it gets fiscalised with a VAT code at least once (ie you get an invoice with a QR) → whatever newly reissued (with a different VAT code) invoices will not get fiscalised.\n\nTherefore invoices get stuck with incorrect (old fiscalised) data.\n\n*What is the solution?*\n\nWe investigate with the provider if there is a workaround for it. However, it is not a high priority change as of now.\n\n*What to do now?*\n\nFrom now on please make sure that you reissue invoices to the correct Data (correct VAT code).\n\nBest regards,\n\nNikolay Roll ","2026-01-13T12:34:02.620Z"],["3806770","LSS-61500","LSS","anton.schoeps@bolt.eu","Anton Schöps","[^DEHA2016 GmbH - Kickback - DE_Rides_BoltClub_Berlin (1).pdf] _(132 kB)_","2026-01-13T12:34:04.030Z"],["3806771","PFI-832854","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 550 KES on 19 Dec 2025 18:32:08\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their momo statement as proof. It should be dated from 19th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^payout_TLJFN1I10M.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T12:34:05.920Z"],["3806773","LSS-61258","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] - Would it possible for You to share access for me to the word version instead? Maybe we can fit this on two pages instead of 3 as they need this double sided.","2026-01-13T12:34:11.478Z"],["3806775","LSS-59601","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9], I have drafted an initial MSA to provide a framework for this partnership: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OC5-sbaRX1TymT0WcJ6TsJbIxaAAxh1J/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OC5-sbaRX1TymT0WcJ6TsJbIxaAAxh1J/edit|smart-link] \n\n\n\nDo you think that this format is acceptable? Can I tag Dimitrios in the document to review and add details where needed?\n\nThank you !","2026-01-13T12:35:14.968Z"],["3806776","PFI-832449","PFI","gabriel.zarza@bolt-outsource.eu","Gabriel Duarte Zarza","Thanks team!","2026-01-13T12:35:15.385Z"],["3806777","PFI-830609","PFI","agil.heydarli@bolt.eu","Agil Heydarli","Hi Nazrin, \n\n\n\nThe sooner the better 🙂 ","2026-01-13T12:35:21.123Z"],["3806778","WD-22539","WD","stefanus.sunarja@bolt.eu","Stefan Sunarja","Fantastic - it works now. Thanks, Olivier!","2026-01-13T12:35:28.658Z"],["3806780","LOC-4616","LOC","teun.esveld@bolt.eu","Teun Esveld","Opt-in for NL and BE in March.","2026-01-13T12:35:57.018Z"],["3806781","PFI-832818","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Fondy portal is down. Checking with fondy. \n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768303282988979|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768303282988979]","2026-01-13T12:36:09.859Z"],["3806782","DSR-3645","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Comms file sent to user","2026-01-13T12:36:26.835Z"],["3806783","PFI-832812","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T12:36:31.797Z"],["3806785","PFI-832801","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 205.00 on 23/12/2025, 04:28:10UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 21st of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T12:37:10.623Z"],["3806789","PFI-830703","PFI","wisdom.salaou@bolt-outsource.eu","Wisdom Delphine Salaou","The manager finally received the payout.","2026-01-13T12:37:53.880Z"],["3806791","DBRE-7645","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Final report on the result\n\n{noformat}taxify_payouts                            | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_partner_payments_city24            | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_payout_client_account              | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_invoicing_payment                  | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_partner_payments_instant_payout    | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_partner_payments_yigim             | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_partner_payments_payout_generation | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_billing_adjustment                 | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_billing_payout                     | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_rental_car_billing                 | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_subscription_invoicing             | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_billing_user_tax_filing            | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_invoicing_tax_report               | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_business_invoicing                 | Conditionally OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_balance_user_order                 | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_billing_payment                    | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_invoicing_document                 | OK to disable nightly sync\ntaxify_corporate                          | deprecated schema\ntaxify_invoicing_router                   | deprecated schema\ntaxify_invoicing2_audit                   | deprecated schema{noformat}\n\n* About Conditionally OK to disable nightly sync on taxify_business_invoicing.\ntaxify_business_invoicing(337G) in Invoicing cluster nightly sync has a dependency on taxify_business(1.9G) in Central cluster.\nBoth teams agree in disabling nightly sync; however, there are conditions:\n     (a) The sync stops at the same. \nor (b) taxify_business sync stops first, and taxify_business_invoicing sync stops later.\nPossible solutions are:\n     (a-1) Stop nightly sync for Central and Invoicing at the same time.\nor (b-2) Enable selective nightly sync for 49 schemas(7700G) in Central cluster and stop Invoicing cluster nightly sync.\nor (c-3) Enable selective nightly sync for taxify_business_invoicing(337G) in invoicing.\nor (d-4) Migrate taxify_business(1.9G) in Central cluster to TiDB and stop Invoicing cluster nightly sync.\nThe following solutions are unrealistic because:\n     (a-1) There are 50 schemas in Central cluster, and it will be very hard to negotiate with each team to make the stop sync.\n     (b-2) and (c-3) Enable selective nightly sync will likely have a big issue with large data size. Also, selective nightly sync needs all the infrastructure as it is and adding software complexity, so this solution is out of scope for this ticket.\nTherefore, the following solution is the only option:\n     (d-4) It is the realistic option. Also, the team mentioned that they have a plan to migrate the schema; however, it has not been scheduled anytime soon.\n* Conclusion\nSince (d-4) is the only realistic option for disabling Invoicing cluster nightly sync, we need an official TiDB migration request from the related team. I will close this ticket for now, and we can re-open this ticket or create a new ticket to disable nightly sync, remove unneeded Invoicing prelive infra after the successful TiDB migration of taxify_business.\n\n","2026-01-13T12:38:37.505Z"],["3806793","LSS-61368","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342177|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342177|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T12:39:23.472Z"],["3806794","DBRE-7645","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Done","2026-01-13T12:39:25.091Z"],["3806796","CCM-22275","CCM","cheila.aniceto@bolt.eu","Cheila Aniceto","!image-20260113-123953.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T12:40:00.598Z"],["3806797","LSS-61358","LSS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hello, \n\nLegal review is complete. \n\nPlease refer to the ticket for confirmation. \n\nAs the first iteration of the agreement was initiated and signed via Cogna, for continuity, let’s apply the same logic. \n\nPlease accept signing request upon receipt from Workiva. \n\nThanks,\n\nKadi 🙏 ","2026-01-13T12:40:10.249Z"],["3806804","DSR-3707","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T12:41:06.937Z"],["3806806","PFI-829951","PFI","support@flitt.com","support@flitt.com","გამარჯობა,\n\nრით შეგვიძლია დაგეხმაროთ?\nპატივისცემით,\n\nNino Pachulia\n\n{color:#1d1c1d}Support Specialist{color}\n\n\n\n{color:#222222}+995 325 00 01 02{color}\n\n[npachulia@flitt.com|mailto:npachulia@flitt.com] | [LinkedIn|https://www.linkedin.com/in/nino-pachulia/] | [www.flitt.com|https://flitt.com/]{color:#202124}{color}{color:#202124}{color}\n\n\n\n\n!https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdesUJg1p54UqXLenrFQFanpvXuj_umTqEFnw1W5JR9LBf8O3m6bGImWLGpg2ulKBMgaF3p6b25v6bmXHIHIZutpHE-jvRov39TlA4JBIsOA1TnvQv9Hi1Pl6DSaGos3E_cDDVNa_WgN0NWjc5AHd9dzQAW?key=gAVmix1twk-tFXoz-xQXqA!{color:#202124}{color}\n\n\n---- on Tue, 13 Jan 2026 16:30:42 +0400  *\"pfi\"<pfi@taxify.atlassian.net>*  wrote ---- \n\n\n{quote}\n\n\n\n{color:#333333}{color}{color:#999999} —-—-—-—{color} {color:#333333}\n{color}{color:#999999} Reply above this line.{color} {color:#333333}\n\n\nchargeback_reports commented:\n\nშეასრულეთ.\n\nპატივისცემით\n\n +Best Regards+\n\n{color}{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#333333}{color}{color:#595959} -{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#595959}მირა წოწორია / Miranda{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#595959}Mira{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#595959} tsotsoria{color}{color:#333333}\n\n{color}{color:#595959}Customer Journey Expert{color}{color:#333333}\n\n{color}{color:#595959}Payments Development Tribe{color}{color:#333333}{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#333333}{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge/]{color:#333333}{color}\n {color:#333333}{color} !1767942492548013_292097426.png|thumbnail!{color:#333333}  <[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/request/2972373/attachment/1103910]>{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:#3572b0}View request{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-829951?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6IjJkOGQxMmYwNGQ0ODVkNGYyMGVhMTA3ZjFjNjI2NjEzYWFjMTA5YmY0YmQwZmYzZTRhMzQzYjlkM2NmNWY2ZTciLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiNTM4MDYiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IlBGSS04Mjk5NTEifSwiZXhwIjoxNzcwNzI2NjQxLCJpYXQiOjE3NjgzMDc0NDF9.7ZxzHh_xYXZf2O8gS32eZf8fjLDZphJb9taLEoLRwmQ&sda_source=notification-email]{color:#3572b0}{color}{color:#333333} ·{color} [{color:#333333}{color}{color:#3572b0}Turn off this request's notifications{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-829951/unsubscribe?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..kHrB3NA5SQIOvGoK2lz8AM4x08HeqQaCmXVpGJK5fOs]{color:#3572b0}{color}{color:#333333}\n\n{color}{color:#707070}This is shared with chargeback_reports and{color} [{color:#707070}support@flitt.com{color}|mailto:support@flitt.com]{color:#707070}.{color}{color:#333333}{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:#707070}Powered by Jira Service Management{color}|https://www.atlassian.com/software/jira/service-desk/powered-by?utm_medium=jira-in-product&utm_source=jira_service_desk_email_footer&utm_content=taxify]{color:#707070}{color}{color:#333333}\n Sent on January 13, 2026 2:30:41 PM EET{color} \n!http://use1-track.atlassian.com/CI0/0100019bb756436c-d12538be-5387-4ee0-a808-e09aacd26bfb-000000/F3geOumjX7Ru2eLKrSd6yQPDTkae-FSWTFu8LzOGZHk=440!{color:#333333}{color} {quote}","2026-01-13T12:42:20.792Z"],["3806807","PFI-812866","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Yes, they should be correct in future. If the issue occurs again, let’s revisit this case/create a new one.","2026-01-13T12:42:23.258Z"],["3806808","WEB-9593","WEB","roberts.calijs@bolt.eu","Robert Chaliy","[~accountid:712020:2bb94136-b4e4-463e-a0f6-8be773ff520f] *Whistleblower meta tags*\n\n* *Meta title:* Report a concern | Speak up with Bolt’s Whistleblower Program\n* *Meta description:* Raise concerns safely and confidentially through Bolt’s whistleblower program, supported by the independent platform SpeakUp®.","2026-01-13T12:42:27.618Z"],["3806810","PFI-824866","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","The driver is not vat liable - therefore the vat % is 0%.\n\neven if rider is vat liable → driver’s not liability means that VAT is 0%.","2026-01-13T12:43:09.099Z"],["3806826","PFI-832799","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nYes you are right. The amount of 169 UAH should have been released to the customer. \n\nI have checked with our payment service provider and I can confirm the last action was the void authorization. The funds have been released. \nHere is the payment timeline for reference, please do not share it with the customer. \n\n\n!image-20260113-124217.png|width=895,height=713!\n\nWe have noticed that in some cases banks can misinterpret the void authorization message as a charge and incorrectly display it to the customer. \n\nCustomer payments team suggests the user would reach out to their bank and would clarify why this transaction is displayed as a debit instead of credit. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T12:43:36.129Z"],["3806827","LSS-60609","LSS","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","Hi! Sharing the reply I received from Keeleamet below:\n\n_Thank you for your response._\n\n_The change in our practice is due to a large number of complaints received by Keeleamet, which indicates that this is a problem that requires a solution. As a job advertisement contains important information as a whole, it is likely that providing only a summary would not be sufficient._\n\n_Keeleamet is aware of the development of a translation tool, and if this tool makes it possible to resolve the issue, we have no objections to its implementation._\n\n_Kind regards,_\n_Epp Käen_\n_Senior Inspector_\n_Keeleamet_","2026-01-13T12:43:38.068Z"],["3806828","LSS-61501","LSS","angelina.korol@bolt.eu","Angelina Korol","[^Acts-20260113T124026Z-1-001.zip] _(117 kB)_\n\n[^Invoices-20260113T124028Z-1-001.zip] _(104 kB)_","2026-01-13T12:44:07.473Z"],["3806829","WEB-9593","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Discussed this with Tom, and we can’t use onelink for the third-party app. [~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] , would it be possible to adjust the design so we have separate App Store and Play Store links?","2026-01-13T12:44:12.243Z"],["3806831","DSR-3157","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] I have finalised the response letter. Please double check the prepared data.\nSafety mentioned they have not yet sent the termination email. Does this affect our response ?","2026-01-13T12:44:28.569Z"],["3806832","LSS-61501","LSS","angelina.korol@bolt.eu","Angelina Korol","[^Invoices-20260113T124028Z-1-001 (24ef3593-6302-43b5-a804-535864db6480).zip]\n[^Acts-20260113T124026Z-1-001 (870859cf-30c0-41b5-b688-9029b4bed46c).zip]\n\n","2026-01-13T12:44:37.819Z"],["3806833","LSS-61467","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:289d7ba0-a9c0-4cbb-82d4-a9ed8c05aeab] !\nThank you for raising this ticket!\n\nI can already tell you that, from my high-level research, this is something that appears to be high risk in Malta.\n\nUnder S.L. 499.68, the restrictions are broader than “street hailing” and include prohibitions around standing/plying for hire, selling LPT services on the road, and soliciting passengers. \n\nWith an on-ground agent at the airport who (i) collects cash, (ii) determines eligibility / whether the shuttle is full, and (iii) issues fiscal receipts, this can be perceived as a curbside sale / on-street organization of transport, even if the user first taps “Bolt Shuttle” in the app. That’s also likely to attract attention/complaints from airport taxi stakeholders and the wider LPTV operator community.\n\nSo, from a Malta regulatory perspective, we believe this would likely expose Bolt to material compliance risk, including the risk of being seen as intermediating / facilitating a breach of the applicable passenger transport rules (particularly given the “on-the-ground” cash collection and decision-making on eligibility / capacity).\n\nWhile making the service free during the test may reduce the most obvious trigger (cash collection / receipt issuance), it does not eliminate the underlying risk and, again, would still be highly likely to attract negative attention, not only from airport taxi operators, but also from the LPTV community / operators, given the appearance of “on-street” organization of rides at the airport.\n\nIn addition, this specific operational flow does not appear to be covered by our current Malta T&Cs (as it introduces ground agents handling rider interaction and payment/receipt processes outside the app flow).\n\nBut let’s discuss during our call today!\n\nThank you!\n\n\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:011a9eb3-77af-4c62-bb26-e6c10e6097ec] ","2026-01-13T12:44:38.014Z"],["3806834","DPM-2320","DPM","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] when it comes to filters, do we also consider text search as a filter option we wanna persist? or only those values in Filter Drawer/Panel?\n[update] This was discussed offline, and we do want to maintain search text as well","2026-01-13T12:44:40.235Z"],["3806835","PFI-832852","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hey [~accountid:712020:33a1a5e8-52cb-4605-9ef3-0b89d57fe7b8] [~accountid:557058:b2aaf2b9-4465-40fe-b31b-1711dbe61946]!\n\nCan you, please, provide your input about the upcoming KSeF regulations in Poland and the timelines we fall under.","2026-01-13T12:44:43.659Z"],["3806836","PFI-831763","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T12:44:58.545Z"],["3806838","LSS-61489","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342188|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342188|smart-link]  & [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342187|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342187|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T12:45:13.400Z"],["3806840","LSS-61357","LSS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Thank you! \n\nSent Workiva an email to initiate the signing process and posted an update on the signature collection Jira ticket. ","2026-01-13T12:45:54.779Z"],["3806842","PAW-14841","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @BoltCristianLupu\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160554\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 12:46:09 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T12:46:09.460Z"],["3806843","DMC-559","DMC","fedor.novikov@bolt.eu","Fedor Novikov","The issue was in invalid campaign setup","2026-01-13T12:46:30.465Z"],["3806845","MTE-1257","MTE","raman.nikitsenka@bolt.eu","Raman Nikitsenka","[~accountid:5d6e089134b3d20d9777ef90] in Crowdin default language for source files is configured in our current project as {{{id: \"en\", locale: \"en-US\", name: \"English\"}}} We will keep it consistent with Crowdin, so yes, American one","2026-01-13T12:46:56.057Z"],["3806847","LSS-61500","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] - Has this been ran through by You? I believe we haven’t received any of these before","2026-01-13T12:47:05.361Z"],["3806848","LSS-59990","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:cb7d1436-9800-43db-821c-db7028a6ff03] . I will close it then 🙂 ","2026-01-13T12:47:22.891Z"],["3806849","LSS-55755","LSS","federico.michelini@bolt.eu","Federico Michelini","Thanks [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] ! All comments in the Annex should be solved now. Can you also confirm that the Amendment is good? will you accept Stella’s suggestions and send for signatures?","2026-01-13T12:47:26.609Z"],["3806851","PFI-832881","PFI","mercynorah.nyiti@bolt.eu","Mercynorah Nyiti","[^Bolt Swift Transfer-Advice-HZ1JC670KI38AAB6-131225_142518 (1).pdf]\n\n[^receipt (2) (3).pdf]","2026-01-13T12:47:53.449Z"],["3806852","LSS-59609","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:cb7d1436-9800-43db-821c-db7028a6ff03] . I will close it then 🙂 ","2026-01-13T12:47:55.662Z"],["3806859","RISK2-3185","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","[Reviewed ERM Matrix on-call 09.01.|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1m_R3ozky9DaIkCemNVMbM91XhAiKMPR7/edit?gid=1529975088#gid=1529975088]. Added in InfoSec access\n\nCompliance permissions still to be reviewed","2026-01-13T12:49:25.516Z"],["3806861","LSS-61488","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-19693?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6ImQ5OGRhY2ZlOWM4ZTIxNjE2Y2UwY2RiMjAxZWM1ZGVkMGMxYjcxYzkwZmRiMmI4NDc1ZTQ4NDFhMWUzYWU3NzkiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiNDQxNjkiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IkxTUy0xOTY5MyJ9LCJleHAiOjE3NzA3MTc5MTMsImlhdCI6MTc2ODI5ODcxM30.tb-Qr6tBnNKAwhoY_6Jn5oyvR_TYKoQC2xspbJV64qE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-19693?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6ImQ5OGRhY2ZlOWM4ZTIxNjE2Y2UwY2RiMjAxZWM1ZGVkMGMxYjcxYzkwZmRiMmI4NDc1ZTQ4NDFhMWUzYWU3NzkiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiNDQxNjkiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IkxTUy0xOTY5MyJ9LCJleHAiOjE3NzA3MTc5MTMsImlhdCI6MTc2ODI5ODcxM30.tb-Qr6tBnNKAwhoY_6Jn5oyvR_TYKoQC2xspbJV64qE|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T12:49:48.441Z"],["3806863","CSDT-871","CSDT","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","{{2026-01-08}} sync with Chirag\n\n{quote}submissions driver reg - # of submissions, # of registrations, tat\nsubmissions vehicle reg - # of submissions, # of registrations, tat\nsubmissions fleet reg - not available now, but will be\ndocument processing - # of documents, tat\naudit vehicle reg - ???\naudit driver reg - ???\nbeehive tasks driver reg - # of tasks, aht\nbeehive tasks doc renewals - # of tasks, aht{quote}\n\nChecking in with Shahzad re audit data - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D08SDL878PJ/p1768308573559659|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D08SDL878PJ/p1768308573559659|smart-link] \n\nFollowing up with Chirag - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09P5LZV7DM/p1768311784076359|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09P5LZV7DM/p1768311784076359|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T12:50:53.680Z"],["3806865","PFI-832879","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:70879987-57f8-46a2-8d57-28ca896f822a],\n\nBasically, to put it simply, then the user spammed the everliving hell out of the confirmation button, it kept failing, however, they kept on doing it until our velocity checks kicked in.\n\nPlease advise the user to try again in 1-2h, then everything should work as per usual.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-13T12:51:43.388Z"],["3806868","PFI-832879","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Forgot to mention, but please make sure to mention that the user starts off with card payment first.\nIf the cash payment does not work, then it means it is currently not available and that they should use another method.","2026-01-13T12:52:35.530Z"],["3806869","FX-3615","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768308742118869]*{color}:\nI checked it locally, nothing can break in the test.\nTest passed last checks - [https://jenkins.boltint.net/job/Bolt/job/bolt-server/job/develop/136548/testReport/jun[…]arch_Company_Application___Correct_sorting_is_used/history/|https://jenkins.boltint.net/job/Bolt/job/bolt-server/job/develop/136548/testReport/junit/%5Bcomp%5D/src_rides_vehicle_vehicle_marketplace_test_comp_application_fop-search-company-application-comp/Vehicle_Marketplace___Fleet_Owner_Portal___Search_Company_Application___Correct_sorting_is_used/history/]\n{quote}","2026-01-13T12:52:35.832Z"],["3806871","PFI-820795","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nhere is the new setup:\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-13 at 14.51.23@2x-20260113-125126.png|width=638,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-13 at 14.51.23@2x-20260113-125126.png\"!\n\nwill start tomorrow","2026-01-13T12:52:59.741Z"],["3806872","FX-3615","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768308768294909]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3615 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T12:53:03.482Z"],["3806874","PFI-832832","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nUnfortunately, it is not possible for us to issue refunds via bank transfer. We do not have an account or process in place to support this, nor is there an established workaround. Any refund must have a clear funding source, and issuing refunds via bank transfer would raise AML concerns.\n\nThere have been a few exceptional cases in the past where the accounting team facilitated such refunds manually. If refunding the amount to the customer’s Bolt balance is not an option, you may reach out to Accounting to check whether they can support this request as an exception.\n\nBest regards,\n\nMarten","2026-01-13T12:53:42.900Z"],["3806875","LSS-61503","LSS","leonora.lukoviczki@bolt.eu","Leonóra Lukoviczki","[^PoA_Leonora Lukoviczki_01.09.2025.pdf] _(2.45 MB)_","2026-01-13T12:54:08.867Z"],["3806878","DSR-3687","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","I have escalated the case back to Tier 2 with instructions. ","2026-01-13T12:54:28.358Z"],["3806879","LSS-61503","LSS","leonora.lukoviczki@bolt.eu","Leonóra Lukoviczki","[^PoA_Leonora Lukoviczki_01.09.2025 (48705a51-1b92-4b73-b3f4-300cfb519779).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T12:54:45.117Z"],["3806880","LSS-61501","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","[~accountid:712020:4031005b-be5e-413a-b7da-919304795012]  - We don’t have stamp for AZ in Estonia, this needs to be handled by the local team.","2026-01-13T12:55:18.631Z"],["3806881","PFI-831762","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team is unfortunately not able to assist with pricing, discount or promo code related questions. \nPricing is decided by the vertical and the customer payments team does not have any impact on it. \nCould you please raise a ticket with the verticals technical support team instead. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2]\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T12:55:25.804Z"],["3806882","PFI-832883","PFI","matej.makan@bolt.eu","Matej Makáň","!IMG_0675.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Snímka obrazovky 2026-01-09 o 12.51.57.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T12:55:34.448Z"],["3806883","C2-456","C2","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","Discussions - [https://docs.google.com/document/d/19uxDjGHfAWhppK7-tn6cCTy15dbC4EB-s534YwIOQK4/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/19uxDjGHfAWhppK7-tn6cCTy15dbC4EB-s534YwIOQK4/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T12:55:43.787Z"],["3806886","PFI-832882","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T12:56:40.961Z"],["3806889","LSS-48620","LSS","emilie.chesse@bolt.eu","Emilie Chesse","Hi [~accountid:61cc1c959ee70a00680edd89] \n\nI understand the concern, but from our side, maintaining a dual-language (EN + local) version in one document is significantly more practical. It allows us to *manage a single version for updates and publication, which reduces maintenance time and the risk of misalignment* between versions.\n\nSince we're working with multilingual internal stakeholders, the side-by-side format is also more convenient for  review - ensuring clarity, traceability, and consistency in both languages. Managing separate documents increases the likelihood of inconsistencies.\n\nAs for the T&Cs page structure, I understand it's currently split by language, but we could upload the same bilingual version under both sections. That would still offer a clearer experience for end users, and from a consumer law perspective, having a single, accessible version per product and per country seems preferable.\n\nOtherwise, we could consider publishing only in the local language (which is done in some countries), but IMO that introduces access issues - both for international teams and, more importantly, for users like tourists (e.g., visiting Lisbon) who need to understand which terms apply to them. \n\nCan you please look into fixing the display issues (or tell us who to contact to raise this) to allow us to go ahead with a dual-column format where possible. \n\nLet me know your thoughts - and thanks again for looking into it!\n\nNB: I've also seen some formatting issues on some current T&Cs that aren't in dual-language format, so it seems to be a wider problem - but hopefully one that can be fixed 🙏 ","2026-01-13T12:56:50.823Z"],["3806891","PFI-830609","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Thank you, changes will go live tomorrow","2026-01-13T12:57:01.799Z"],["3806893","SUPX-2317","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","*Krzysztof Szlachetka* [Jan 13, 2026 2:48 PM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768308504508939] in Slack channel [#dev-support-automation-support|https://slack.com/app_redirect?channel=C064FCFAT0S]\n\n{quote}Hey :wave:\n{quote}\n\nFollowing re-enablement of the payment issue flow, we see a number of alerts about cases getting escalated to an agent by cron.\n\nExamples:\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722697491|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722697491]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722522580|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722522580]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/721906210|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/721906210]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722435553|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/722435553]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/721904787|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/721904787]\n\nNow: this happens in the following scenario:\n• user goes through the flow and navigates to chat\n• a prompt for more information is added asking the user to provide more info about what is that they're looking for (at that time case remains assigned to system bot and pending)\n• upon user responding and providing more info, case gets re-opened and escalated to an agent\nThing is, the escalation is supposed to be performed by {{SupportAutomationsSolutionRunner}} and not the {{escalate_to_agent_cron}}.\nBased on the solution agreed with *@user-U0465FUPDL3* , what's supposed to happen is:\n1. We have the {{SupportCasePromptCommentSubmitted}} event which sets {{isActivePrompt}} to {{true}} on the snapshot\n2. Then upon client adding comment,  {{maybeResetSystemBotAssignee}} kicks in which resets system bot assignment\n3. That should cause {{SupportAutomationsSolutionRunner}} to pick it up and escalate due to {{attempt_automatic_solution}} being {{false}}\n#1 and #2 are happening but #3 isn't.\n\nAn example of a support case where everything worked as expected:\n\n[https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/360450442|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/customer-support/casedata/360450442]\n(it's prelive but I can find one in live if needed)\n\nCould you please check why is the {{SupportAutomationSolutionRunner}} not picking it up? :prayge:","2026-01-13T12:57:10.008Z"],["3806894","TAX2-561","TAX2","victor.garces@bolt.eu","Víctor Garcés","+Update 13 Jan 2025 - On B2G central model alignment+\n\nBilling confirmed that the intended setup should be feasible for B2G model, noting that active driver switching would take about two weeks of effort and that reusing supply would be necessary for efficiency, as confirmed by other functions.\n\nTax confirmed that the proposed setup should work for centralised and for localised models. VAT treatment needs a country-by-country check (clarify VAT status of Gov institution/Client), but this should not be a blocker.\n\nLegal will create another slide with co-payment option flow, to be further reviewed.","2026-01-13T12:57:14.425Z"],["3806895","PFI-831746","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nPlease note there is no refund. \nThe authorized amount was 60.49 AZN and the capture amount 41.84 AZN. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T12:57:24.787Z"],["3806896","LSS-61258","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^PoA_odbiór_hulajnóg_kwalifikowany_2026 (5f563588-2cf2-4e68-90a8-11f651af2a7d).pdf]\n\nRight, sorry! here it is on 2 pages, thank you [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] ","2026-01-13T12:57:29.049Z"],["3806898","PFI-831714","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team is unfortunately not able to assist with pricing, discount or promo code related questions. \nPricing is decided by the vertical and the customer payments team does not have any impact on it. \nCould you please raise a ticket with the verticals technical support team instead. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2]\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T12:57:59.013Z"],["3806906","WEB-9593","WEB","conor.mclaughlin@bolt.eu","Conor McLaughlin","[~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] [~accountid:62b2cf3033a882e2be49d95a] [~accountid:712020:2bb94136-b4e4-463e-a0f6-8be773ff520f] \n\nI added this as inline links and removed the single button. I hope that helps resolve your issue?\n\n!image-20260113-125800.png|width=248,alt=\"image-20260113-125800.png\"!","2026-01-13T12:58:47.512Z"],["3806907","PFI-832886","PFI","parvin.alirrzayeva@bolt-outsource.eu","Parvin Alirrzayeva","!Screenshot_20260113_131611_az_kapitalbank_mbanking_r8lambda1gQbndCOH6SF0uVz57ONY5S.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T12:58:49.311Z"],["3806908","PFI-832886","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T12:58:51.353Z"],["3806911","PFI-831713","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 25.54 ZAR on 20/12/2025, 16:23:08UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 20th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T12:59:15.219Z"],["3806915","MP-3473","MP","taxifyqa@bolt.eu","QA Testing","PR comment for QA:\nTo be tested with the feature","2026-01-13T12:59:44.805Z"],["3806916","LSS-61189","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9], please allow me to share a recommended approach to respond to this ticket. \n\n*The question is : how and who should file a complaint to the police?* \n\nIn my experience, there were two instances where police reports were filed: \n\n* By Simon when we wanted to inform the police that a driver had threatened to set himself on fire in front of the hub;\n* By Anne-Cécile when a Bolt agent was acting fraudulently in favour of fleet owners.\n\n\nIn this instance, where we need to file a report against a rider, I would create an account on France Connect for Bolt (or check with Safety whether we already have on) and file a complaint via the online form: [https://www.masecurite.interieur.gouv.fr/fr/fiches-pratiques/depot-plainte-personne-morale|https://www.masecurite.interieur.gouv.fr/fr/fiches-pratiques/depot-plainte-personne-morale|smart-link] \n\nIn order to complete the form we would need the screenshots and the details of the rider and confirmation on which date they were blocked from their account. \n\nWhat do you think?","2026-01-13T12:59:55.745Z"],["3806918","HS-28905","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Caleb! There’s no separate sign up link for Vitality, but I forwarded your information to them and asked for you to be added to the health insurance. Once I receive the confirmation from them, I’ll share the Vitality Membership number with which you can log into the Member Zone.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-13T13:00:24.386Z"],["3806919","LSS-61501","LSS","angelina.korol@bolt.eu","Angelina Korol","[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] please advise how should I proceed, should I ask the local team to provide scanned documents and then attach them in this ticket?","2026-01-13T13:00:32.553Z"],["3806920","PFI-832886","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-13T13:00:41.164Z"],["3806923","PFI-832857","PFI","jakub.pekar@bolt-outsource.eu","Jakub Pekar","Hi, Local OPS informed us to create an SD","2026-01-13T13:01:16.357Z"],["3806925","PAW-14843","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-13T13:01:42.040Z"],["3806931","LSS-57420","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you [~accountid:612f31d89976c300693ebaf7] !\nYour thoughts are very helpful. I will respond to [~accountid:6320602ec7601c8e4abeda47] accordingly 🙂 ","2026-01-13T13:03:04.706Z"],["3806933","CNT-348","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","[~accountid:610a6c97ec92ab0070d4d852] please grant me access to the updated generic candidate pack.","2026-01-13T13:03:12.385Z"],["3806934","L10N-27515","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27512](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27512)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T13:03:13.642Z"],["3806935","L10N-27520","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27512](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27512)\n\nThanks for collaborat