948","CEBF-1759","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Task is completed. User can now easily winning the opp by just following the error message.\n\n!2026-01-13_14-16-50.mp4|width=621,alt=\"2026-01-13_14-16-50.mp4\"!","2026-01-13T13:04:01.136Z"],["3806952","SREP-1069","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","* Re-provisined correct secret \n* Reinstall everything \n* added ch test db: \n\nSQL LAB works again: \n\n!image-20260113-130432.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260113-130432.png\"!","2026-01-13T13:04:39.933Z"],["3806956","PFI-832832","PFI","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:cfea02e5-8522-43c8-9f69-236d8bece552] I hope that you are well. Please allow me to loop you in this ticket. \n\nWe need to refund a passenger of 22.50€ for a price difference that was not correctly displayed at the moment the passenger ordered the ride. \n\nThe issue is that the passenger paid for the ride in cash, therefore we cannot refund the amount via the payment method. \n\nIt would not be compliant to compensate via promo codes or by Bolt Balance because this is money that should be directly reimbursed to the passenger. Please can you share some guidance on our available options, and if it would be possible to send the refund via bank transfer to the bank details available on his account - or we can ask him to confirm his bank details?\n\nThank you !","2026-01-13T13:05:40.577Z"],["3806957","LSS-61105","LSS","vivien.antoniou@bolt.eu","Vivien Antoniou","hi [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] this was the latest communication from the driver\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 13.04.45.png|width=632,height=362,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 13.04.45.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-13T13:05:43.832Z"],["3806960","WEB-9593","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","[~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] perfect, thanks!","2026-01-13T13:05:48.878Z"],["3806961","FIN2-945","FIN2","vincenzo.rinella@bolt.eu","Vincenzo Aglieri Rinella","[~accountid:712020:11b028d0-a65b-4db4-93f7-938b14e353e9] this ticket","2026-01-13T13:06:00.721Z"],["3806962","FX-3619","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768309555209379]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@gricelda.fuentes>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3619] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T13:06:07.464Z"],["3806964","CRC-1901","CRC","hasan.tanvir@bolt.eu","Hasan Mohammed Tanvir","[update] no update on this because of other priorities. Agreed with DAP that I will get back on it 2026 Q1. ","2026-01-13T13:06:32.681Z"],["3806965","LSS-60557","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hi, [~accountid:712020:5edd7b8a-e535-468c-85fd-63f0b6de01b2] ! thank you for the follow-up. Could you please confirm with them the address should we send the agreement to for signing (*_Eryk Połeć, ul. Ciechanowska 15, 03- 107 Warszawa_*)? ","2026-01-13T13:06:45.895Z"],["3806968","LSS-57420","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:6320602ec7601c8e4abeda47] !\n\nA quick follow-up on this, adding to my previous answer:\n\nOn the “where is this already live?” point: I can’t confirm a comprehensive list from Legal side, so it’s best to check with Central Ops to understand whether acceptance-rate gating is already being used elsewhere and in what form.\n\nFrom a legal risk perspective, as I already wrote in my first response, there is a level of risk that can’t be ignored. Changing how we use acceptance rate (e.g., using it for blocking / gating category access) can be seen as “work to access work” and can be sensitive in EU / higher-risk markets. Even if it may not dramatically shift our risk profile given we already use driver score gating in Malta, it keeps us firmly in an “obviously at risk” zone.\n\nGiven that, I’d recommend you also flag this to Tom Tuxworth (Public Policy), so he can advise whether this change should be escalated to the Reclassification Committee (especially for EU markets / where reclass risk is already elevated).\n\nThanks!","2026-01-13T13:07:21.876Z"],["3806971","HS-28781","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:63934c5900cb2fc3f98c7e44] , yes, the new form has been sent to all employees. Additionally it is set to be sent to all new employees and to current employees whenever there are changes to their data.","2026-01-13T13:08:16.266Z"],["3806972","RNTL-29746","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","[~accountid:712020:e77ef51b-4584-479b-bc00-b172e7475d2e] let’s start testing it out. \n\n\n\nWould this kind of explore work for you? \n\n[https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/rental/vehicle_batteries_by_states_count_by_days?qid=AfKtRcjyw9oXK07AXkQEb5&toggle=fil,vis|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/rental/vehicle_batteries_by_states_count_by_days?qid=AfKtRcjyw9oXK07AXkQEb5&toggle=fil,vis]","2026-01-13T13:08:35.182Z"],["3806975","PFI-830112","PFI","mia.hartova@bolt.eu","Mia Hartová","Hello,\nany news?","2026-01-13T13:09:07.247Z"],["3806978","BRE-1229","BRE","kenechukwu.nwankwo@bolt.eu","Kenechukwu Nwankwo","[~accountid:5e343c77a7f27d0e6c6d6698] Yes delivery is out of scope for Poland E-invoicing","2026-01-13T13:09:56.845Z"],["3806980","HS-28818","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:dc4824f4-a6bc-41f2-af89-59d155dc0cc8],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-13T13:10:15.641Z"],["3806981","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Currently getting this error on prelive:\n\n{noformat}{\n  \"err\": \"AccessDenied: User: arn:aws:sts::799029546920:assumed-role/prelive-eu-central-1-reseller/aws-sdk-js-session-1768309078929 is not authorized to perform: s3:PutObject on resource: \\\"arn:aws:s3:::reseller-rides-reports/PRELIVE/reports/1078/2026-01-09-2026-01-13.csv\\\" because no resource-based policy allows the s3:PutObject action\",\n  \"file_path\": \"reports/1078/2026-01-09-2026-01-13.csv\",\n  \"root_bucket\": \"reseller-rides-reports\",\n  \"root_path\": \"PRELIVE/\"\n}{noformat}\n\n","2026-01-13T13:10:29.813Z"],["3806989","LSS-57359","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","comms were sent to the User. closing the ticket.","2026-01-13T13:10:55.490Z"],["3806990","WEB-9598","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] \n\nA few more comments from the stakeholder that need to be updated in the design (from the [file|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1_rHIKmOGVqaFq63mWE0ykEtCZtdywvRJ52kbdPb75j0/edit?usp=sharing]): \n\n# *You invite*\nInvite a referral to learn about Bolt for Business by sharing your unique link -or sending an email.-.\n# Learn about Bolt *for* Business\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.09.16.png|width=680,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.09.16.png\"!\n# “.” missing from the second bullet in design\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.09.39.png|width=655,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.09.39.png\"!\n# FAQs: remove \"Do referrals expire\" section\n\nThanks a lot!","2026-01-13T13:11:21.046Z"],["3806993","FRAUD-4986","FRAUD","jaroslav.judin@bolt.eu","Jaroslav Judin","instead there was added {{frictionless}} parameter in the events which resolves to the needed result in fraud-data query.\nimplemented in [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/113495|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/113495|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T13:11:57.413Z"],["3806997","LSS-60557","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","+*The signing procedure:*+\n\n* wet ink of the parties ([~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] signature is needed on behalf of Bolt Services PL sp. z .o.o.).\n* please make *two copies* of each annex and put the signature of Ahto Kink on each of them. Then, send back two copies of each annex *to the address of Eryk Połeć (TBC)* so that he can sign these copies and *ask him to send us back one copy* of each signed annex to the Bolt Warsaw Office (*_ul. Prosta 67, 00-838 Warsaw_*). ","2026-01-13T13:12:26.355Z"],["3806998","PFI-832893","PFI","glory.ogbuewu@bolt-outsource.eu","Glory Ogbuewu","!commission 1.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T13:12:31.240Z"],["3807000","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","On LIVE:\n\n\n{noformat}{\n  \"err\": \"AccessDenied: User: arn:aws:sts::307626443147:assumed-role/live-eu-central-1-reseller/aws-sdk-js-session-1768309888169 is not authorized to perform: s3:PutObject on resource: \\\"arn:aws:s3:::reseller-rides-reports/LIVE/reports/1078/2026-01-05-2026-01-13.csv\\\" because no resource-based policy allows the s3:PutObject action\",\n  \"file_path\": \"reports/1078/2026-01-05-2026-01-13.csv\",\n  \"root_bucket\": \"reseller-rides-reports\",\n  \"root_path\": \"LIVE/\"\n}{noformat}\n\n","2026-01-13T13:12:54.149Z"],["3807003","LSS-61437","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:1eca79ab-231a-45b5-b53f-3471723b5176] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Formulario Nº 90_BOLT_VAT_Diciembre 2025 13.01.2026 (1).pdf] \n\n[^Formulario Nº 90_BOLT_INR_Diciembre 2026 13.01.2026 (1).pdf] ","2026-01-13T13:13:05.395Z"],["3807004","PFI-832889","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:a96f9985-acf7-4e03-93e8-aab94e95513b],\n\nSeems to be a false-positive.\nPlease kindly manually compensate the driver for the loss of their earnings due to this.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-13T13:13:20.185Z"],["3807005","PFI-808167","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Thank you!\nI will check again tomorrow if the payment has been received as a return for the payment here [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/223787401|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/223787401] \nOnce funds returned, it will be included in the client next regular payout. ","2026-01-13T13:13:53.053Z"],["3807006","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Checking.","2026-01-13T13:14:15.513Z"],["3807009","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","What’s the impact of this error?\nCan I take some time to investigate it or should I revert the changes right away?","2026-01-13T13:14:39.794Z"],["3807011","PFI-832471","PFI","mikaela.leinonen@bolt-outsource.eu","Mikaela Victoria Leinonen","Business administrator reports that the payments does not match the company automatically and does not reset the spending limit after they have paid, even when reference number is included in payment. She informs us that this takes a long time (4 days in this incident), and has happened every month since they signed up for Bolt Business and would like a solution to the issue so she does not have to manually contact us to reset the spending limit, can you assist please?\n\nEscalating after instructions from T2.\n\nIf I have opened a ticket with the wrong department, could you kindly point me in the right direction? I had some troubles figuring out where in Business Commerce to ask. Thank you in advance.","2026-01-13T13:15:23.368Z"],["3807012","LSS-58059","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:0b1b647b-217c-4a05-99f8-56f5705c6307] any updates on this matter?","2026-01-13T13:15:30.077Z"],["3807018","LSS-60915","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:5ee36bc8e31f620aba841240] please find attached the translated version of the document. I will request the signing. \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XjUOVgntCHPqlpMLW__2L3b8rNpKJSQA/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XjUOVgntCHPqlpMLW__2L3b8rNpKJSQA/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T13:16:23.629Z"],["3807019","LSS-60149","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Thanks [~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] for the update, co for now I am closing the ticket, able to be reopened in the case arise again.","2026-01-13T13:16:31.375Z"],["3807022","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","It directly impacts the generation of reports in ride booker, which is rather critical. I would advise to revert the changes right away unless we can have PutObject work just as quickly.","2026-01-13T13:17:04.043Z"],["3807023","LSS-60984","LSS","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","Hello team,\n\nThe authority has responded again, emphasizing the urgent need to resolve this case as quickly as possible due to the risk to the person's life.\n\n\n\n*Authority's message (translated from Portuguese):*\n\n{quote}_Good morning._\n\n_Given the date of the initial request and considering this is a domestic violence case with circumstances that may endanger the victim's life and physical integrity, we are resubmitting this communication and requesting a response marked as VERY URGENT._{quote}\n\n","2026-01-13T13:17:04.763Z"],["3807024","PAW-14839","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @udankobolt\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160541\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 13:17:08 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T13:17:08.731Z"],["3807026","PFI-832471","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hey, thank you! Sure, please, proceed the ticket here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T13:17:42.022Z"],["3807028","FX-3618","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768310262927759]*{color}:\nAs far as I can see, if we don't pass the status, only active drivers for the driver performance table or those who were active during the selected period will be returned.\n\nApparently, driver profiles in all statuses are returned for the search.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T13:17:56.729Z"],["3807029","LSS-61501","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Either that way or we can sign and You can forward the signed documents to them for stamping only. Usually +*Malaka Nasirova*+ has assisted with the stamps but she is on a vacation currently.","2026-01-13T13:18:05.561Z"],["3807030","L10N-27548","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27512](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27512)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T13:18:20.923Z"],["3807032","PFI-832883","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:61096e48b704b40068fefc4c],\n\nThis sort of behaviour is more for the local-OPS team to decide if they are okay with it.\n\nFrom the Fraud team’s perspective, they are not causing us to take financial losses, we are actually getting positive GMV.\nWould recommend discussing it over within the OPS team and making a decision.\nWe have seen these in the past as well, and we always recommend for the local-ops team to make a decision.\nIn Bolt’s context the Fraud team deals with payment issues such as credit cards, and in this scenario we are still receiving positive commissions.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-13T13:19:22.980Z"],["3807033","ROPSC-483","ROPSC","riin@bolt.eu","Riin Kotsalainen","Data collected and shared with local team and Partner team - [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1HVrbz9cnUriTqN52EjQSA7-Ecg_CMQSBHEQf6gcLItI/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1HVrbz9cnUriTqN52EjQSA7-Ecg_CMQSBHEQf6gcLItI/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T13:19:32.048Z"],["3807034","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","How about now?\nI reverted the changes.","2026-01-13T13:19:36.950Z"],["3807035","PFI-831710","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThis does not seem to be like a payments related issue, rather an app issue. \nI checked the #beehive-agent-support Slack channel and noticed that some other agents were reported similar app behavior on the 10th of January. \n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C021M19NET1/p1768058555187399|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C021M19NET1/p1768058555187399]\n\nMy understanding is the incident has been solved. If the user requires any further assistance then I would suggest reaching out to the app technical support team for assistance. \n\nCheers, \nMarten ","2026-01-13T13:19:37.133Z"],["3807038","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Checking, will update in two mins","2026-01-13T13:20:16.891Z"],["3807041","DSR-3709","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T13:21:26.122Z"],["3807042","LSS-61469","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] - I have got two documents from [~accountid:712020:66939b2f-e5c1-42e2-8cbe-244458fd12f9]. Attaching these here. One is out of scope but I believe wasn’t share before.\n\n[^MB resolution - conversion 29.12.2025 (1).asice]  \n\n[^Voting record  - shareholders - 14.02.2025 - signed.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T13:21:32.186Z"],["3807046","GRWA-1487","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","Simplified the 3 columns to 1 column.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 13.37.42.png|width=736,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 13.37.42.png\"!","2026-01-13T13:21:52.833Z"],["3807047","PFI-827394","PFI","chiamaka.madujibeya@bolt-outsource.eu","Chiamaka Madujibeya","We are still waiting on the review. No respond yet","2026-01-13T13:21:55.250Z"],["3807048","LSS-61501","LSS","angelina.korol@bolt.eu","Angelina Korol","I will investigate who can stamp instead of Malaka. If Ahto Kink can sign tomorrow - please proceed with this part at first. If not - i will ask local team to start with their part to save time.\n\n\n\n","2026-01-13T13:21:57.214Z"],["3807049","LSS-59755","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:63314e9e9b32cfef93265252] , please find attached the external opinion. \n\n[^Bolt Services HR d.o.o. 30_12_2025 - 30_12_2025 (1).pdf]\n\nSummary: \n\n* A company can have *only one principal business activity (NKD)*.\n* Poslovne vožnje d.o.o. currently has *passenger transport agency services* as its principal activity and *cannot have two principal activities at the same time*.\n* To change the principal activity, the *standard process* is:\n*# add new business activities in the Commercial Court,\n*# request a change of principal activity from the Croatian Bureau of Statistics (CBS),\n*# register the new principal activity in the Commercial Court\n→ this usually takes *~1 month*.\n* Normally, CBS requires *financial data*, but in this case they have *informally indicated flexibility*:\n** the change *may be approved without financial data*, if justified by the need to join the Transport Association.\n** they also *may allow a simplified approach* without first adding new activities — *not guaranteed*.\n* *Licence risk:*\n** there is a *low but non-zero risk* to the agency licence,\n** the licensing authority has *informally confirmed* that the licence should remain valid as long as agency activity stays registered (even if not principal),\n** we recommend getting this *confirmed in writing* before proceeding.\n\nPlease let me know how would you like to proceed.","2026-01-13T13:22:22.916Z"],["3807051","GRWA-1486","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","Added the inefficient spend to GMV % in column AL\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.21.11.png|width=874,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.21.11.png\"!","2026-01-13T13:22:30.179Z"],["3807052","LSS-60646","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:5382507a-151c-4326-b1f8-6a2d888c30bb] , getting back with an overview of this / some recommendations from a privacy POV.\n\n# First question we need to answer to understand whether this is even allowed in the first place is: *do our T&C prohibit such behaviour*. I understand that this is indeed the case but adding [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] to confirm.\n# Second, it’s important to ensure that while taking action against drivers for engaging in prohibited behaviour, we are following the *Suspension and Termination Framework*: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PLBK/pages/6091145449/Driver+Suspension+Termination+Framework|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PLBK/pages/6091145449/Driver+Suspension+Termination+Framework|smart-link]  (it depends on whether we’re suspending the *driver or the vehicle*, so check it out). If there’s any questions, I suggest consulting [~accountid:624d3e6b699649006aea9c98] \n## [~accountid:624d3e6b699649006aea9c98] could you perhaps take a look and advise if this looks consistent with the global framework?\n# Regarding transparency - we cannot surprise the drivers with blocks, and should also follow the global framework when informing drivers about suspensions.\n# Now, *regarding the data collection itself:* the most important thing is that we collect data in a way that aligns with our accountability requirements, and that allows us to have proof of violation of T&Cs. I do not believe that an employee spotting the car, without having pictures for proof, is a good enough reason to suspend a vehicle, and in case of a dispute, this does not seem like a defendable position. That said, my advice would be to create a process/define how we collect such information and why. I’d say that rider complaints are valid proof, as well as pictures, if they’re taken by authorized employees with reasonable suspicion (read: we should not be taking pictures of random Uber cars) and documented properly. \n# *Driver requests for copy of data:* as we saw in the regulator’s inquiry, we must ensure that we follow our global processes and honour driver data access requests as per this process. These requests should be escalated as per [this guidance |https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951?country=global&language=en], so we can ensure that the response is provided within the statutory timeline of 30 days, that the request is fully complied with, and that we don’t breach GDPR while handling the request. \n# *Data retention and storage:* is there a possibility for us to store this data in Admin rather than google sheets? The latter creates issues because it’s harder to control proper data retention (i.e. deletion after a set period of time), proper access rights management. We can’t keep this data forever, so we need to set a retention period for it. The question is - how long do you need it for; is retaining until the driver profile is deleted doable and enforceable? ","2026-01-13T13:23:17.772Z"],["3807053","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Works now after reverting, thank you.","2026-01-13T13:23:35.347Z"],["3807056","LSS-61474","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hi, [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] ! Please find the generated reports for Bolt Ops and Bolt Tech from September 1st 2025 until January 13th 2026.\n\n[^SpotDraft Contract Report Jan-13-2026.xlsx]\n\n","2026-01-13T13:25:04.803Z"],["3807057","FX-3619","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768310726374119]*{color}:\nHey!\nPlease ask in the <#C0576CT9MQD|> channel first.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T13:25:40.713Z"],["3807059","PFI-826495","PFI","tomasz.mendziuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Tomasz Mendziuk","help","2026-01-13T13:26:18.697Z"],["3807060","LSS-61362","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:d3a24a53-8607-48c6-9240-bd0580c5293f] Approved.","2026-01-13T13:26:25.307Z"],["3807061","PFI-826495","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T13:26:34.245Z"],["3807063","HS-28908","HS","slawomir.klimkiewicz@bolt.eu","Sławomir Klimkiewicz","!AnyScanner_01_12_2026-02.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T13:26:59.453Z"],["3807065","WEB-9593","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:712020:2bb94136-b4e4-463e-a0f6-8be773ff520f] \n\nOne more comment: we’re currently missing the T&C links at the end of the page. I’ve created a ticket here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/WEBSD/queues/custom/2293/WEBSD-1475|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/WEBSD/queues/custom/2293/WEBSD-1475|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T13:27:21.377Z"],["3807067","LSS-55755","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[~accountid:712020:d3fd53e6-f124-4770-a577-b09d6688566f] thanks! \nI think that we are all good with Annex, I can send it for signatures. \nHowever, with the Amendment, I would like to clarify few points:\n\n* *_Appendix 1, Clause 1.a.i.1_* previously provided for specific discounts; after the amendment, the clause no longer specifies any concrete discounts, only that they are determined at the partner’s discretion. Are we really comfortable with such wording, given that it is completely unclear what concrete benefit the partner is actually committing to provide to drivers?\n\n* *_Appendix 1, Clause 3.b_* — if we accept their proposal for the contract amendments, we waive the specific territory in which this agreement applies. Do we plan to expand the territorial scope of the agreement? What is the rationale behind this amendment to the clause?\n\nThanks! ","2026-01-13T13:27:40.344Z"],["3807068","PFI-832668","PFI","arina.gudramovica@bolt-outsource.eu","Arina Gudramoviča","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-root/partners/edit/11720065?tab=partner_profile&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-root/partners/edit/11720065?tab=partner_profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] This C also did not receive his payout. [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/722453910|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/722453910] ","2026-01-13T13:27:46.332Z"],["3807069","LSS-61407","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9], \n\n*Issue*: LMDVTC (Serenity) is using contact data collected from drivers via their own appointment booking tool (for sticker applications) to solicit those drivers to join their fleet.\n\n*Assessment*: [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1BpvEX1JzcLc__4rwaYYC7vJcSi4DTvDV|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1BpvEX1JzcLc__4rwaYYC7vJcSi4DTvDV|smart-link] \n\n* Contractually, all use of driver data is limited to the Branded Car Program scope (per MSA + SOW + DSA).\n* The DSA restricts data use to “facilitation of services” under the agreement – recruiting drivers is outside that scope.\n* Their conduct likely breaches:\n** GDPR purpose limitation (Art. 5)\n** DSA (Appendix 2 - Agreed Purpose clause)\n** MSA good faith obligations (4.1.8)\n** SOW exclusivity clause (Section 8)\n\nThe fact that they use their own website does not change the legal limits on how that data can be used.\n\n\n\n*Proposed Response*:\n\n# In a first instance, *clarify with LMDVTC* in writing that any driver data obtained under the Branded Car Program cannot be reused for fleet recruitment or unrelated marketing.\n# As an escalation solution, *send cease-and-desist letter* to LMDVTC citing:\n## Breach of data use restrictions under DSA;\n## Conflict of interest + breach of exclusivity;\n## Request immediate stop to driver outreach + deletion of misused data.\n\n\n\nOn a separate note, it would be worth noting and raising the point that we should be moving appointment bookings to a Bolt-controlled tool/form going forward.\n\n\n\nWhat do you think? Thank you ! \n\n ","2026-01-13T13:27:56.729Z"],["3807070","LSS-48620","LSS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Hi [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1] , thanks for the additional info and for sharing your view. \n\nI believe that at the end of the day Regional Legal should indeed decide what works best in their particular markets, given the local requirements and needs. Therefore, no objections from my side to proceed as you proposed. I just thought important to share the potential issues this approach may create.\n\nYour solution to duplicate the document in the EN and PT sections should work, although it might still lead to higher maintenance time and risk of inconsistencies among versions. For example, if we forget to update one of the files or delete outdated version in future updates.\n\nAs for the display issues, this is being looked into along with a broader Legal webpage ownership review but there’s no easy fix at the moment. Unfortunately, it seems the only way right now is for the webpage team to upload the version and then together with the responsible legal counsel check if it’s properly displayed in web and mobile, and if not adjust it until it is.\n\nFinal remark from me is that this dual-column approach is not replicable in all markets and this is one of the reasons we have not adopted it as the standard at Bolt. As you know, there are some markets where we need to support 3, 4 or more languages, in which case dual-column simply doesn’t work.\n\nThanks again for your comments. Do let me know if I can be of further help.\n\nBest,\n\nThiago","2026-01-13T13:28:03.356Z"],["3807071","RS-1928","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","[~accountid:6001a723d364960139286c95] thank you for clarifying! No response from the authority. Closing the ticket","2026-01-13T13:28:04.741Z"],["3807073","LSS-61381","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","Hi [~accountid:61b1d141b0b630006a9698e1] please confirm:\n\n# Deniss Osman needs to be added to all PoAs?\n# All PoAs shall be extended till 01.07.2027?\n# I can see only one PoA for Swedbank AS in the attached documents. Does it mean that we need to draft the new one for Swedbank Liising AS? If yes, please let me know whether all the details will be the same (contact details, terms etc) or any changes are needed?","2026-01-13T13:28:08.063Z"],["3807074","PFI-820777","PFI","innaaime.kalju@bolt.eu","Inna Aime Kalju","i dont know, how to search for payouts under the link, which you provided\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"start\"%3A1768255200%2C\"show_empty_rejection_code\"%3Afalse%2C\"show_total\"%3Afalse}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1768255200%2C%22show_empty_rejection_code%22%3Afalse%2C%22show_total%22%3Afalse%7D%7D]\ni need help","2026-01-13T13:28:15.271Z"],["3807075","DPM-2317","DPM","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","Need to to researched to estimate","2026-01-13T13:28:44.813Z"],["3807076","CSDA-296","CSDA","iuliia.vlasenko@bolt.eu","Iuliia Vlasenko","Context here is that it gives the team quick summary of whether we have particular providers which are attracting most tickets, so we need to deal with them with relevant priority.\n\n","2026-01-13T13:28:59.402Z"],["3807078","PFI-832901","PFI","kodjo.aglonou@bolt-outsource.eu","Kodjo Josias Merveil Aglonou","!IMG_5528.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T13:29:08.341Z"],["3807079","RS-1932","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Closing the ticket since we don’t have enough information to locate the order","2026-01-13T13:29:12.573Z"],["3807080","LSS-61235","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342231|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342231|smart-link]  ","2026-01-13T13:29:30.834Z"],["3807081","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Found the issue.\n\nIn {{bolt-business-portal}}, directories are live and prelive.\n\nIn {{reseller-rides-reports}}, directories are LIVE and PRELIVE.\n\n\n\n!image-20260113-133002.png|width=1067,alt=\"image-20260113-133002.png\"!\n\n!image-20260113-132950.png|width=1083,alt=\"image-20260113-132950.png\"!","2026-01-13T13:30:26.564Z"],["3807084","FX-3609","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768311082361979]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3609 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T13:31:37.883Z"],["3807085","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","That explains it.\n\nLet’s try to apply changes again tomorrow morning or in the afternoon. What time works for you?","2026-01-13T13:31:42.711Z"],["3807086","DSR-3711","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-13T13:31:53.143Z"],["3807087","LSS-61508","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T13:32:04.460Z"],["3807090","LSS-57226","LSS","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","*Feedback received from the bank:*\n\n{quote}_Hi, Cesar._\n\n_The contract draft provided to you has been prepared by the Legal Department and constitutes an official template. It is important that you record your feedback and comments directly on the document shared with you.Kindly add your notes using the attached form and submit it accordingly._\n\n_Thank you._{quote}\n\n*Shared file attached:*\n\n[^İnteqrasiya və əməkdaşlıq Müq_eng-az (014a1a5c-107b-4e1e-aafd-3357f2a3a0af).docx]\n\n","2026-01-13T13:33:21.131Z"],["3807092","PFI-827943","PFI","bhuvaneswari.sanmugam@bolt-outsource.eu","Bhuvaneswari Sanmugam","Hi Team, any update\n\n","2026-01-13T13:33:57.611Z"],["3807095","PFI-832904","PFI","oluwatosin.akinbolasere@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwatosin Akinbolasere","!image-20260113-133224.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260113-133235.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T13:34:09.103Z"],["3807096","CNT-348","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","[~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] just make a copy of it, no need to change the original file atm. ","2026-01-13T13:34:12.716Z"],["3807097","DPM-2321","DPM","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","This task is already included in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPM-2289|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPM-2289|smart-link]. I will close this duplicated ticket.","2026-01-13T13:34:22.109Z"],["3807098","DMC-327","DMC","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","Requires some investigation, noting what errors are currently exist and what is missing. There’s some feedback when errors are very generic, or arrives late. ","2026-01-13T13:34:25.537Z"],["3807102","LSS-61481","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9], for context, Louis discussed this matter with me before I asked him to raise a ticket.\n\nIn the code des transports, the only limitation is 7 years for thermal cars; there are no limitations for electric or hybrid cars.\n\nI also spoke with Xavier, who confirmed that we have no legal grounds to limit cars older than 20 years. If this is a commercial decision or an internal privacy, we should verify the risks of this, but as it stands, there is no legal or regulatory support for this position.\n\nSince the code des transports does not address this, I will check the code de la consommation to ensure we don’t have any legal standing. However, we may need to advise Louis to remove the 20-year limitation and unblock drivers affected by this issue.","2026-01-13T13:35:01.655Z"],["3807103","GRN-39","GRN","irina.nedelcu@bolt.eu","Irina Nedelcu","Implement usage of CT speed as rate: [https://github.com/bolteu/tools/pull/840|https://github.com/bolteu/tools/pull/840|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T13:35:10.781Z"],["3807104","LSS-61509","LSS","heleri.alliksoo@bolt.eu","Heleri Alliksoo","[^4590060756.pdf] _(40 kB)_","2026-01-13T13:35:22.789Z"],["3807106","RIDE-594","RIDE","vincenzo.rinella@bolt.eu","Vincenzo Aglieri Rinella","[~accountid:63d0ecc7f386bda5dcab9d72] I see you decreased the hours for finance to 0, can we close your epic?","2026-01-13T13:35:41.604Z"],["3807107","WFM-9966","WFM","mohamed.moustapha@bolt.eu","Mohamed-Said Moustapha","Hello Team \n\nPlease do not forget to set other queues ( [01 RH_France_T1_Low/Moderate|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/queues/edit/870044?tab=manage_agents]\n\n[01 RH_France_T1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/queues/edit/150022?tab=manage_agents]   ) in secondary. \n\nThanks \n\n","2026-01-13T13:35:50.438Z"],["3807108","DMC-327","DMC","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","we could start with the 5 examples described here","2026-01-13T13:35:54.700Z"],["3807112","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Can you please test prelive again?\n\nI applied the new changes only on prelive now.\n\nLive still has the old config.","2026-01-13T13:36:44.270Z"],["3807116","FPD-1522","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","!image-20260113-132229.png|width=717,alt=\"image-20260113-132229.png\"!\n\nTallinn and Riga have very common pattern of discrepancies in metrics -  we have issues with almost all the metrics but {{online hours per active partner }}\n\n{{online hours per active partner}} is stable across the models for all the markets with discrepancies in Finished Orders.\n\nBarcelona -  has issues with {{active riders}}, {{rider churn}} and {{rider activation}} metrics.\n\nIn Kosice we have issues with s2O conversion rate and online hours, where discrepancies persist up to partner churn and partner activations.\n\nIn Phuket we have issues with {{search sessions}} and {{Online hours}} - with discrepancies going down to partner churn and partner activations.\nIn Stockholm we have issues starting from {{online hours }}and they go down to {{partner_churn}} and {{partner_activations}}, as well as {{active_partners}}. Very similar to what we have in Kosice","2026-01-13T13:37:06.933Z"],["3807118","PFI-811574","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hi team, apologies for delay on this. I believe the March and Feb have been creditted and reissued (if my memory serves correctly in scope of other ticket to our team). Are there any other changes still needed?","2026-01-13T13:37:53.121Z"],["3807123","PFI-832906","PFI","ugne.guigaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Ugnė Guigaitė","[^Mokejimas_RMO24799213.pdf]","2026-01-13T13:39:06.716Z"],["3807125","LSS-61328","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342244?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342244?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T13:39:16.169Z"],["3807126","CSDA-296","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review ad-hoc requests once a day. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-13T13:40:04.306Z"],["3807127","WFM-9718","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey [~accountid:712020:647d9435-b4ad-4729-aebd-e4f4f0044a62] , I checked and agent [edma.nogueira@bolt.eu|mailto:edma.nogueira@bolt.eu] has everything that they need, is there any reason why ticket reopened? \n\nThank you,\n\nSCC team","2026-01-13T13:40:09.275Z"],["3807128","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","I will take a look in the morning; can’t check at the moment as there is another pipeline I need to finish for reseller, after which another colleague has another deployment as well.","2026-01-13T13:40:24.906Z"],["3807129","HS-28730","HS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","Heyo, our receptionist sent the document now. \nThanks! ","2026-01-13T13:40:26.526Z"],["3807130","BEE-3650","BEE","piotr.musiol@bolt.eu","Piotr Musioł","Hey team, were there any changes on the outgoing call process, as agent has [reported|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C021M19NET1/p1768306953292839] an issue of not being able to select issue when wrapping up a call, in order to do so she has to close the wrap up to select the necessary issues.","2026-01-13T13:40:40.310Z"],["3807131","WFM-9971","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","OPS request, TL will handle the ticket.\nCC: [~accountid:61268a40129802006ae93f05] ","2026-01-13T13:40:40.416Z"],["3807132","BEE-3650","BEE",null,"Slack","[Piotr Musioł|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6017bc27a41ea5006a86f73b] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C032D4ZGZR6/p1768310958491279?thread_ts=1768310958.491279&cid=C032D4ZGZR6|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C032D4ZGZR6/p1768310958491279?thread_ts=1768310958.491279&cid=C032D4ZGZR6|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-13T13:40:41.201Z"],["3807133","BEE-3650","BEE","piotr.musiol@bolt.eu","Piotr Musioł","ok, I can see that, I'll fix that soon!","2026-01-13T13:40:41.737Z"],["3807135","PFI-807434","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T13:41:03.483Z"],["3807136","WFM-9718","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","[~accountid:5f802f9595fe8e0069b2c28c] could you please explain to [~accountid:6294d703e76a9c00705d0785] the issue you mentioned in the DM?\n\n\n\nThanks!","2026-01-13T13:41:16.090Z"],["3807137","PFI-831689","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nSorry for a delayed response. \nI think I have located the payment. I’m 99% sure it’s this payment. \nThe payment date: 10 Jan 2026, 13:16:18 (UTC+04:00)\nUser app interface: JSC LIBERTY BANK\nCard scheme: Visa\nAmount/currency: 6.5 GEL\nWeren’t able to locate the payment with the card number because ApplePay payments are tokenized and using a different PAN. \nVertical: Ride hailing\n\nCould you please provide the user the first name Ბოლქვაძე and the last 4 digits of the phone number 0399 to see if the users know each other? \n\nProfile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/241233709|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/241233709]\nPayment: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4023513253|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4023513253]\n\n\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-13T13:41:16.615Z"],["3807139","LSS-61501","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! We have signed the documents and stamped then from our side. Attaching the complete scans so local team could print them more easily.\n\n[^Invoices.pdf]\n[^Acts.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T13:41:35.263Z"],["3807141","DMC-380","DMC","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","[~accountid:712020:a5a9bde0-6d51-468a-85a6-ee3e42b31f73] will go ahead and split this task into smaller subtasks and will further estimate them","2026-01-13T13:41:34.858Z"],["3807142","RS-1942","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] , this looks suspicious. Please ask for the formal request/court order, including case reference and official stamp or signature. It’s most likely not real authority","2026-01-13T13:41:35.138Z"],["3807144","LSS-59633","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:b33fa9fc-2e0e-4ab0-a8b3-85f9683a7c93] thank you for your help - please send the below draft to the landlord. \n\nPlease also share the following comments with them:\n\n# _Автомайданчик в Договорі визначений як частина Паркінгу. Проте, як ми бачимо з наданих графічних матеріалів, Автомайданчик розміщений за межами будівлі ТРЦ. Просимо надати документальне підтвердження того, що Автомайданчик частиною Паркінгу (будівлі). В іншому випадку, потенційна угода може трактуватись як суборенда частини земельної ділянки. Це може мати суттєве значення для структурування даної угоди._\n# _Просимо уточнити необхідність отримання та використання перепусток Суборендарем у контексті використання Автомайданчику, що перебуває за межами внутрішнього Паркінгу та не має потребувати окремих перепусток. У випадку підтвердження відсутності необхідності отримання та використання перепусток, просимо внести відповідні зміни до договору._\n# _Оскільки ТЗ, які перебуватимуть на території Автомайданчика, не є власністю або не перебувають в керуванні Суборендаря, із договору видалені відповідні гарантії щодо стану ТЗ та дій водіїв ТЗ, оскільки Суборендар не має на них прямого впливу._\n\n[^13.01.2026_Договір_суборенди_ТУ_Сервісез_Укр.docx]\n\n","2026-01-13T13:41:45.911Z"],["3807146","LSS-61135","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Comms shared – closing.","2026-01-13T13:41:53.656Z"],["3807150","PFI-831248","PFI","faith.osunde@bolt-outsource.eu","Faith Osunde","Hello Team,\n\nPlease assist in reviewing this payment. The client mentioned that they have checked with their bank, and they confirmed that the payment was processed.","2026-01-13T13:42:09.422Z"],["3807151","PFI-831681","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team is unfortunately not able to assist with pricing, discount or promo code related questions. \nPricing is decided by the vertical and the customer payments team does not have any impact on it. \nCould you please raise a ticket with the verticals technical support team instead. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2]\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-13T13:42:21.528Z"],["3807152","LSS-60372","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Advise provided. Closing.","2026-01-13T13:42:36.106Z"],["3807153","LSS-60031","LSS","mariam.maghalashvili@bolt.eu","Mariam Maghalashvili","Hi there, it seems the contract didn’t get through. Could you please resend it?","2026-01-13T13:42:44.026Z"],["3807155","LSS-59572","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey, please find the signed NDA attached in wet ink.\n\n[^NDA_Bolt Operations OÜ_Bankinter S.A._13.01.26.pdf]\n\nOnce getting this countersigned please send it to [contracts@bolt.eu|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] with a ticket number for archiving purposes and attach the document here for our own records.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-13T13:43:03.994Z"],["3807156","PFI-807792","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Client has no available balance","2026-01-13T13:43:21.472Z"],["3807158","WFM-9718","WFM","nisley.ciacareli@bolt.eu","Nisley Ciacareli","HI team!\n@edma.nogueira still doesn't have access to the Beehive and she needs to complete her training 🙂\nCan you help me please?","2026-01-13T13:43:45.359Z"],["3807161","L10N-27553","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27549](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27549)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T13:44:01.637Z"],["3807162","L10N-27559","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one p