ing on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27549](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27549)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T13:44:15.247Z"],["3807173","L10N-27579","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27549](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27549)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T13:44:18.144Z"],["3807174","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Got it.\n\nPlease let me know when you manage to test it.\n\nThen I will apply the same for Live.\n\nCurrently, they are a bit inconsistent.\n\nPrelive has the new changes applied.\n\nLive has the previous changes.\n\nThe sooner we manage to test prelive and apply the changes on live, the better. 😄 \n\nThanks a lot. 💚 ","2026-01-13T13:44:21.985Z"],["3807175","LSS-61258","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed PoA attached. 8 copies have been prepared and will be sent for delivery as soon as possible.\n\n[^PoA_Bolt Services PL Sp. z o.o._kowalewska_Ners_Wiktorowska_Sochacki_Nowak_Znaczko_Madry_Chudy_13.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T13:44:23.637Z"],["3807182","PAW-14842","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160568\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 13:45:21 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T13:45:21.325Z"],["3807183","LSS-60199","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] ,\n\nMay we sign it on our side and share it with them to help speed up the process?\n\nThank you","2026-01-13T13:45:39.294Z"],["3807185","LSS-61407","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ,\n\nwhy you propose two steps and not a cease and desist letter as first step? I think we can move directly with a formal notice based on what is stated on the contract. WDYT?\n\nthanks,\n\nEli ","2026-01-13T13:45:44.991Z"],["3807186","LSS-61430","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9], \n\n# *Legal risk of compensating drivers (€50 – cash vs gift card)*\n\nCompensating drivers €50 for a one-off, voluntary roundtable is legally permissible, but it carries *some reclassification risk* because it combines several classic indicators assessed by French courts (fixed duration, inability to drive during the session, compensation linked to attendance). This *risk remains low and manageable* if the payment is framed as a _fixed, one-off participation compensation_, unrelated to the provision of transport services and with no repetition or performance element. From a risk and compliance perspective, *cash or a cash-equivalent payout* is preferable to a gift card: gift cards may be viewed as a “benefit in kind”, whereas a small cash compensation is easier to defend as a neutral indemnity or commercial gesture.\n\n# *Whether (and how) to communicate on the compensation*\n\nWhile it is legally allowed to mention the €50 amount upfront, it is *safer not to disclose the amount in the initial invitation*. Stating a precise amount in writing, tied to a fixed time slot, can make the compensation look like _remuneration for time worked_, which is one of the cumulative criteria used in reclassification claims. It also creates clear written evidence (e.g. “€50 for 2 hours”) that could later be reused out of context by a driver, a union, or an inspector to argue the existence of an organised, paid activity. By contrast, referring initially to a “participation compensation” and disclosing the amount only after registration better supports the narrative of a voluntary, non-professional gesture and reduces evidentiary risk. If Ops requires full transparency, mentioning the €50 is still acceptable, but the wording must be tightly controlled and avoid any employment-style language. \n\nDo you agree with this approach?\n\nThank you !","2026-01-13T13:45:54.032Z"],["3807188","LSS-61337","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342249|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342249|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T13:46:06.070Z"],["3807190","CNT-348","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","Shared [some examples|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1DSmbvSY7zS08P__4EofLqySzQXtzkA5S9mAcccibN0w/edit?usp=sharing] with Catalina, Joanna and Petra, deadline for their review: next Friday, the 23rd","2026-01-13T13:46:16.818Z"],["3807194","LSS-61407","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thanks for reviewing [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] given our relationship with LMDVTC and N. Vedovato, starting with a commercial negotiation seems less aggressive than a formal legal complaint. ","2026-01-13T13:47:46.892Z"],["3807196","WFM-9718","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hey [~accountid:712020:5633e692-7475-4dcb-9d5a-d755c99e48c3],\n\nCould you please check this ticket for Nisley? 🙏 Thank you ","2026-01-13T13:48:29.957Z"],["3807198","ITI-1162","ITI","marko.toomla@bolt.eu","Marko Toomla","!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.48.11.png|width=760,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.48.11.png\"!","2026-01-13T13:48:46.154Z"],["3807200","LSS-60199","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi Legal Ops, please organize Ahto signature on the attached document. Thanks! [^Articulate Amendment Quote for Bolt (36227017-965f-4c8f-a7c1-393bced36820).pdf] ","2026-01-13T13:49:21.939Z"],["3807204","LSS-59633","LSS","maryna.romaniuk@bolt.eu","Maryna Romaniuk","Thank you very much [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7]!\nWill share this with the partner and get back to you once there is a feedback from the partner’s Legal team.","2026-01-13T13:51:42.355Z"],["3807205","RS-1943","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hi [~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] ,\n\nThis is a verified domain. You can find it in the market info sheet:green-check: data can be disclosed.","2026-01-13T13:52:06.395Z"],["3807208","LSS-60076","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nI have requested the signing details.\n\nThank you","2026-01-13T13:52:50.949Z"],["3807209","LSS-60621","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:70d80a66-553d-4db2-b50f-6bdb7d3bd7a1],\n\nI’ve updated the [agreement|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GXwY1ASbBtSE3VU5i_jYy4GyMod6-x2l/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=106326439712206242177&rtpof=true&sd=true] and revised clause 12 on data protection. I also added a comment for GS. I clearly indicated that Bolt will have separate agreements with corporate clients (business customers) ordering rides through the GS System.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nPlease review the clause. If it accurately reflects the collaboration and relationship between Bolt, GS, and our business customers, consider this completed from my side.\n{panel}","2026-01-13T13:53:02.574Z"],["3807220","LSS-61388","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342252?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342252?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link]  ","2026-01-13T13:53:25.616Z"],["3807221","LSS-58363","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] can you please take a look? Thanks!","2026-01-13T13:53:26.064Z"],["3807222","RNTL-29225","RNTL","arnaud.lafeuillade@bolt.eu","Arnaud Lafeuillade","Admin Panel wasn’t synced with BE markers","2026-01-13T13:53:36.489Z"],["3807224","WEB-9892","WEB","roberts.calijs@bolt.eu","Robert Chaliy","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tT3w6tdnTU6NuSW1S63oeLWne-VMersPJn8Rhr_C1Fc/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tT3w6tdnTU6NuSW1S63oeLWne-VMersPJn8Rhr_C1Fc/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-13T13:53:53.704Z"],["3807232","WEB-9891","WEB","roberts.calijs@bolt.eu","Robert Chaliy","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tT3w6tdnTU6NuSW1S63oeLWne-VMersPJn8Rhr_C1Fc/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tT3w6tdnTU6NuSW1S63oeLWne-VMersPJn8Rhr_C1Fc/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-13T13:54:37.576Z"],["3807233","RNTL-30028","RNTL","karolina.epifantseva@bolt.eu","Karolina Epifantseva","For the context:\nin iOS bottom sheet reopens with animation each time user select different station (see screencast)\nin Android bottom sheet remains in place and height gets adjusted if needed\nits not a priority, but for consistency we could refactor iOS to have same behavior\nI suggest keep in backlog for now","2026-01-13T13:54:43.302Z"],["3807234","FPD-1524","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","Rides Finance team weight the MAPE for rides by Adjusted planned finished orders in a market\n\n!image-20260113-135409.png|width=1124,alt=\"image-20260113-135409.png\"!","2026-01-13T13:54:51.797Z"],["3807235","DMC-353","DMC","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] will confirm with other agents if they have similar expirience","2026-01-13T13:54:52.192Z"],["3807236","CNT-348","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","[~accountid:610a6c97ec92ab0070d4d852] To be clear, the task is to create one generic pack for the whole engineering?","2026-01-13T13:55:29.098Z"],["3807237","LSS-61192","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - I hope you are well.  Client has signed NDA.  They are asking about the contract?  Could we have feedback for them by tomorrow?\n\n[^NDA.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T13:55:45.981Z"],["3807238","PFI-832461","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nWe have checked with our payment service providers and unfortunately, there are no good news. \n\nThe payment fails with an error message “Country not allowed by bank-acquirer”. This is happening because foreign cards are not allowed to be processed without 3DS authentication. \n\nThe customer payments team is unable to route the foreign cards for delivery through another payment service provider that would accept foreign cards without 3DS. \n\nWe are able to investigate with the fraud team to force 3DS for foreign cards. \n\nWill let you know once we have further updates. \n\nCheers, \nMarten\n\n","2026-01-13T13:56:02.143Z"],["3807240","CMO-12996","CMO","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Decks checked and feedback written. Also reached out to TLs/STLs to check the decks.","2026-01-13T13:56:59.279Z"],["3807242","LSS-60609","LSS","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","And a reply from [CV.ee|http://CV.ee] 👇\n\n_Hi,_\n\n_We had a meeting with the Language Inspectorate yesterday, and overall, the solution we proposed was considered suitable._\n\n_I understand that since we proactively offered solutions, they will also respond to any future complaints by stating that technical solutions are in progress. The Language Inspectorate’s approach has been quite positive and considerate of both sides. They are mainly reacting to complaints from private individuals, which are currently more frequent due to the difficult situation in the job market and increased frustration among job seekers._\n\n_I hope we can close and resolve this topic in the first half of the first quarter. Since your job ads are text-based, the first-round solution should work well for you._\n\n_The proposed solution itself addresses the issue for text-based job ads, for example:_\n[https://cv.lv/en/vacancy/1493838/oro-pay-ltd/onboarding-and-compliance-officer|https://cv.lv/en/vacancy/1493838/oro-pay-ltd/onboarding-and-compliance-officer|smart-link] \n\n\n\n!translate.png|width=1354,height=1238,alt=\"translate.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-13T13:57:22.018Z"],["3807246","PFI-832879","PFI","nutsa.guraspashvili@bolt.eu","Nutsa Guraspashvili","Thanks a lot for the response. \n\n","2026-01-13T13:57:46.619Z"],["3807248","LSS-56363","LSS","mykhailo.boiko@bolt.eu","Mykhailo Boiko","Hey [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] \n1. Any updates here regarding the amendment to the contract?\n2. Can the partner send us an invoice that should be paid? (We have a couple of TOP Accounts that we should pay for their integration).","2026-01-13T13:58:04.090Z"],["3807249","ITI-1162","ITI","marko.toomla@bolt.eu","Marko Toomla","h3. 💡 Workaround:\n\n# Navigate to your Google Workspace Admin dashboard\n# Search \"API controls\" with the search bar on the top and select the option nested under \"Security\"\n# Click \"Manage App Access\" on the right side of the page\n# Click \"View list\" under the Configured Apps card\n# Filter by “App name” and look for *Atlassian*\n\nYou should be able to see an app with ID [+727132345682-9186ghgimhvpp8un6vjb8m9att2a26eu.apps.googleusercontent.com+|http://727132345682-9186ghgimhvpp8un6vjb8m9att2a26eu.apps.googleusercontent.com/]. From there, click *Change Access,* and then mark it as *Trusted* for all users.","2026-01-13T13:58:05.546Z"],["3807250","LSS-60857","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Asked our Flank AI and haven’t vetted the information yet but providing for visibility and can be used as basis: \n\n_In cases of suspected unauthorized account use and fraudulent activity, such as the one described, we should take the following steps:_\n\n# *_Investigate the suspected unauthorized use and fraudulent activity._* _Our anti-fraud system is designed to detect and investigate such activities._\n# *_Temporarily suspend the Bolt service for the rider_* _until their identity verification is completed. This is in line with our Passenger Terms and Conditions for Sweden, which state that if Bolt cannot verify a rider's identity, the service may be suspended until verification is complete._\n# *_Request the rider to verify their identity._* _This is crucial to prevent and address unauthorized uses of Bolt accounts._\n# *_Involve the Privacy team_* _for guidance on handling the personal data breach and potential fraud. The Privacy Legal Team advises on the implementation of product features when personal data is used and assesses potential/confirmed personal data breaches. You can submit a ticket via the_ [_Privacy Team's Service Desk_|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/157]_._\n\n*_Further reading (internal):_*\n\n* [_Global Privacy Notice for Passengers_|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders/]\n* [_Allmänna villkor för passagerare (gäller från och med 01.02.2024)_|https://bolt.eu/sv-se/legal/tnc-rides/?category=rides]\n* [_Privacy & Data Protection_|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/5363925214/Privacy+Data+Protection]","2026-01-13T13:58:20.216Z"],["3807251","PFI-832920","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T13:58:53.650Z"],["3807252","LSS-61430","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ,\n\nthis sounds reasonable, but do you know if Valentin has any screenshot/ emails/slack from last year and conversation he had with Micheala or Emilie? \n\nI think it could be useful to look also at the approach taken by them last year.\n\nWould you mind asking him first to double check this and share with us any content he might have?\n\nthanks \n\nElisabetta","2026-01-13T13:59:05.139Z"],["3807253","CNT-348","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","[~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] Yes, like this: [https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AIFQ3oPCO3_cJZFRpB9U42ZO9UrVUDE-/view?usp=share_link|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AIFQ3oPCO3_cJZFRpB9U42ZO9UrVUDE-/view?usp=share_link|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T13:59:35.441Z"],["3807255","MTE-1311","MTE","sergei.drondin@bolt.eu","Sergei Drondin","[~accountid:6321aad6cf721d09b0166767] I enabled phone and email for the required Eater events, we can enable {{Google Ads Offline Conversions Delivery}} Rudderstack destination now.","2026-01-13T13:59:42.649Z"],["3807258","BEE-3650","BEE",null,"Slack","[@piotr.musiol|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6017bc27a41ea5006a86f73b] one more thing that agent has mentioned on the canceled call, i see that Andri [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C032D4ZGZR6/p1767948264632919?thread_ts=1767946626.373169&cid=C032D4ZGZR6] mentioned on a similar report that you guys are aware in the issue, but will be there a solution in the future? :eyes:","2026-01-13T14:00:32.493Z"],["3807259","WFM-9954","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541710|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541710] ","2026-01-13T14:00:34.325Z"],["3807261","MM-923","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🟡|Some requirements and open questions are listed, but acceptance criteria, edge cases, and detailed requirements are missing.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The description is understandable but could be clearer; open questions and options are not resolved.|\n|Auditability|🟡|No links to supporting documentation or specs; only an image is attached.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate provided in the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add acceptance criteria and clarify requirements.\n* Resolve open questions or document how they will be answered.\n* Link to any relevant specs or documentation.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-13T14:00:48.199Z"],["3807263","BEE-3650","BEE","piotr.musiol@bolt.eu","Piotr Musioł","yes, we are aware of that, but currently cannot fix it easily :disappointed:","2026-01-13T14:00:54.392Z"],["3807265","BEE-3650","BEE",null,"Slack","i see, thanks for the check anyway :jake_dance:","2026-01-13T14:01:25.028Z"],["3807266","LSS-61407","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","sure, agree with you, but what you suggest to negotiate? I think we should make very clear (in a nice way maybe) that we are not happy. Or when you say ‘negotiate’ you suggest asking for a compensation due to the wrong use of data?\n\nthanks\n\nEli ","2026-01-13T14:01:25.027Z"],["3807268","WFM-9954","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571703|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571703]","2026-01-13T14:01:37.295Z"],["3807269","DO-5790","DO","michal.konarski@bolt.eu","Michał Konarski","Access was already granted before.","2026-01-13T14:01:38.322Z"],["3807272","WFM-9859","WFM","ottomar.meoste@bolt.eu","Ottomar Meoste","Roles approved on our end, should be good to go! ","2026-01-13T14:01:48.063Z"],["3807276","PAI-897","PAI","hanshendrik.karro@bolt.eu","Hans-Hendrik Karro","For UA we’ve calculated the DS results and it’s overdue BUT unless it’s blocking Product, I’d recommend we update it together with other markets in Feb.","2026-01-13T14:02:33.697Z"],["3807277","LSS-58369","LSS","mihaela.vatamanu@bolt.eu","Mihaela Vatamanu","thank you very much!","2026-01-13T14:03:05.576Z"],["3807278","PFI-832921","PFI","eunice.mukey@bolt.eu","Eunice Mukey","!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 1.57.39 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T14:03:20.182Z"],["3807279","LSS-61430","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you for raising this ticket [~accountid:712020:255e9251-2a80-4b03-82b7-1ebc3abacf51] ! \n\nWas there a legal ticket raised for this last year to advise on this before? If not, do you have any Slack conversations or screenshots to understand the rationale of the approach taken last year?\n\nThank you ","2026-01-13T14:03:40.933Z"],["3807283","LSS-59808","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","\n\nMain ticket solved.","2026-01-13T14:04:07.193Z"],["3807285","LSS-60076","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\n*Sudhir Kaveti*\n\n*VP – Global Sales | Certinal*\n\n*Mobile: +91 9704750535 | Email:* [*sudhir.kaveti@zycus.com*|mailto:sudhir.kaveti@zycus.com]\n\nThank you!","2026-01-13T14:04:28.875Z"],["3807286","LSS-60135","LSS","marta.klekocinska@bolt.eu","Marta Klekocińska","The contract is signed between us and verification points, not fleets. Could you please help us with the creation of an annex?","2026-01-13T14:04:40.000Z"],["3807292","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] during upfitting? How does it impact maintainability?","2026-01-13T14:07:14.951Z"],["3807296","LSS-60557","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","[~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] \n\nYes, the address is correct as u provided. I confirmed it with them a moment ago 🙂 ","2026-01-13T14:07:59.804Z"],["3807297","WFM-9955","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541711|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541711] Hana.Belanova","2026-01-13T14:08:04.898Z"],["3807299","PFI-832924","PFI","jana.jilkova@bolt-outsource.eu","Jana Jilkova","And what can we tell the rider ? unusual activity ?\n\n","2026-01-13T14:08:37.505Z"],["3807300","WFM-9955","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! I can’t find nina.barbacka account, please give me the email that ends with [bolt-outsource.eu|http://bolt-outsource.eu] ","2026-01-13T14:08:41.242Z"],["3807301","MTE-1311","MTE","maarja.maarjakoiv@bolt.eu","Maarja Maarjakõiv","Thank you, noted :)\n\n_This comment was left via Slack._","2026-01-13T14:09:09.719Z"],["3807302","LSS-61481","LSS","xavier.bendavid@bolt.eu","Xavier Bendavid","Hi everyone ! Thank you for sharing. You are right : the current French regulations only stipulate an age limit for combustion engine vehicles. We therefore have no legal argument to protect us here. If Bolt's standards include an age limit for electric or hybrid vehicles, I assume that this will be included in the T&Cs. We must also ensure that this rule does not lead to our drivers being reclassified as employees by forcing them to change vehicles. \n\n\n\n","2026-01-13T14:09:23.915Z"],["3807303","FX-3618","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768313351668349]*{color}:\n<@U02DHFUNR4J> asked me to raise this, he's looking into\n• provided examples where deactivated ones DO show in table without filter, and \n• Even if I filter on deactivated, this marko guy still does not show up in results, so need to investigate\n{quote}","2026-01-13T14:09:24.406Z"],["3807304","BPPA-72","BPPA","hanshendrik.karro@bolt.eu","Hans-Hendrik Karro","Sharing a caveat: we discovered in the process that currently we’re double counting trial to paid conversion, but we shouldn't factor it twice (noted [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1idGaSJZ0andirYezRjmEeluQM4SFUA8YEwfwMrOj9HQ/edit?disco=AAAByeQ6BLw]).","2026-01-13T14:09:28.437Z"],["3807308","LSS-60655","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey team! \n[~accountid:712020:07746941-2eee-430d-a2cf-f3aa307d9a17] thank you for the initial draft! 💪 \n\nHere’s the updated response:\nDear Albert,\n\nThank you for your patience and for raising your questions. We would like to provide a clear and structured explanation as to why certain service categories are currently not visible in your account and the basis on which this occurs.\n\nOn the Bolt platform, each ride-hailing service category has specific requirements that apply equally to all drivers. Higher-tier categories, such as _Comfort_ or services that include a child seat, are subject to stricter quality criteria, including a minimum driver rating. If a driver temporarily no longer meets the requirements applicable to a particular category, access to that category is automatically restricted until the requirements are met again. This process does not constitute a disciplinary measure or an individual decision; rather, it is a predefined and automated element of how the platform operates.\n\nWe note that these principles are clearly defined and communicated in advance in the Bolt Platform Terms applicable to Ride-Hailing Services (the _Terms_). In particular, Clause 3.4.5 of the Terms provides that “the right to use the Bolt platform in order to view and, where applicable, make use of opportunities to provide Ride-Hailing Services is granted to the Driver only in respect of any Category, and only for as long as the Driver meets the applicable Category requirements, if any.”\n\nFurthermore, Clause 5.21 of the Terms expressly states that “the Categories available to a Driver will depend on factors specific to each Category and market,” and that “the Driver’s right to use a Category ceases if the Driver no longer meets the requirements of that Category.” This means that access to specific categories is neither permanent nor unconditional, but depends directly on whether the driver meets the applicable criteria at a given time.\n\nIn your case, the decrease in your rating was due to low ratings left by passengers after trips. Passengers are entitled to leave a star rating without providing an additional comment; therefore, if no reason was specified, neither you nor Bolt are able to see it. The rating reflects the passenger’s overall experience, which is assessed subjectively, even in situations where certain factors, such as traffic conditions, are outside the driver’s control.\n\nA driver’s rating is calculated using a rolling average based on the most recent 50 trips. As you complete new trips and receive positive ratings, older ratings gradually lose their impact on the overall average. Accordingly, once your rating again reaches the minimum threshold applicable to a given category, access to that category will be restored automatically, without the need for an additional request or a separate decision.\n\nThis category access system is consistent with the requirements of Regulation (EU) 2019/1150 (the P2B Regulation), which obliges platform operators to ensure fair, transparent, and predictable relationships with business users and consumers. The category requirements, the conditions for their application, and the consequences of not meeting them are set in advance, publicly available, and applied equally to all drivers. In addition, under Article 3(1) of the Law of the Republic of Lithuania on Consumer Protection, consumers have the right to receive safe and appropriate-quality services, and the driver rating system is one of the tools used to help ensure these expectations are met.\n\nWe hope that this explanation clearly clarifies the reasons for the situation and the operating principles of the platform. Should you have any further questions, we will be happy to assist.\n\nKind regards,\n*The Bolt Team*\n\n[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] please have a look and confirm, thanks! 🙏  ","2026-01-13T14:10:27.823Z"],["3807309","WFM-9955","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","also to add them queues: 11 REG_Poland_Fleet_Driver Registrations and 11 REG_Poland_Driver_Onboarding Registrations","2026-01-13T14:10:41.326Z"],["3807311","WD-22563","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:60ab52d6411c2200681a75e4] , thanks for writing. Nope, no one shared the schedule for Iceland. \n\nI will setup the following now:\n\n!image-20260113-141125.png|width=391,alt=\"image-20260113-141125.png\"!","2026-01-13T14:11:36.217Z"],["3807312","LSS-60076","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi Legal Ops \n\nPlease support with signing of the agreement [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yO5HZLl_x7XSc3bhZKpACDQlmyHd-pKb/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yO5HZLl_x7XSc3bhZKpACDQlmyHd-pKb/edit|smart-link] \n\nPlease send this out today ","2026-01-13T14:12:07.359Z"],["3807314","RDXENG-4562","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","*Tested and OK* (/) \n\n||*Device name*||Google Pixel 8a||\n|OS Version|16|\n|Client build|CA.193.0 (develop)|\n|Comment|physical|\n\n!Screenshot_20260113-160826-20260113-140826.png|width=284,alt=\"Screenshot_20260113-160826-20260113-140826.png\"!","2026-01-13T14:12:24.819Z"],["3807315","WEB-9593","WEB","samuel.oyekeye@bolt.eu","Samuel Oluseyi Oyekeye","[~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] noted, thanks.","2026-01-13T14:12:40.242Z"],["3807318","WFM-9955","WFM","marta.klekocinska@bolt.eu","Marta Klekocińska","Bolt needs to create an email with this domain. It’s not on Cognizant’s tasks.","2026-01-13T14:13:32.909Z"],["3807321","WFM-9718","WFM","ottomar.meoste@bolt.eu","Ottomar Meoste","Hello [~accountid:5f802f9595fe8e0069b2c28c]!\n\nBased on what I can see, the agent has all of the necessary roles and queues added, so I can’t determine any apparent reasons for why she can’t access Beehive. Is there an error she is getting or anything else that could give further hints on what the issue might be? \n\nAre her certificates in order? \n\nLet me know and I’ll check up on it asap! Thanks!","2026-01-13T14:14:18.648Z"],["3807322","PFI-832933","PFI","christian.barrios@bolt.eu","Christian Junior Barrios Brassel","[^BOLT.pdf]","2026-01-13T14:14:40.688Z"],["3807325","LSS-61493","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] thank you so much for helping with this. The excel file below needs to be downloaded for everything to show and it’s in DK but should be possible to copy/paste the text into DeepL or similar. ","2026-01-13T14:15:08.246Z"],["3807326","PFI-832471","PFI","mikaela.leinonen@bolt-outsource.eu","Mikaela Victoria Leinonen","Thank you so much! ","2026-01-13T14:15:16.351Z"],["3807329","PFI-832471","PFI","mikaela.leinonen@bolt-outsource.eu","Mikaela Victoria Leinonen","Wrong department","2026-01-13T14:15:42.743Z"],["3807331","PFI-832471","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T14:15:47.353Z"],["3807333","PFI-832531","PFI","vieira.andre@bolt-outsource.eu","Andre Vieira","[~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] the instructions from SIS is that when a partner profile is blocked an SD ticket needs to be created to lift the block of the partner profile. This has been the procedure for the last year without any issues or reports of it being incorrect. What changed? We are the safety team handling the safety tickets and suspensions.","2026-01-13T14:16:00.805Z"],["3807335","WEBSD-1313","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:4305a8c1-0495-4265-b6e0-ae34aff86b22]  👋 \n\nI think everything should be there already.\n\nI added images and made changes in the text accordingly .","2026-01-13T14:16:52.998Z"],["3807336","LSS-61080","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d15dd8c0d64020c403ae98c] thank you for raising this ticket. \n\nPlease could you provide some additional information to help us manage this request:\n\n* Please could you add me and Elisabetta as participants to the insurance ticket as we cannot access it?\n* Could you confirm if the driver has contacted CS to share his version of the situation?\n* Can you share screenshots of the exchange between this rider and the CS?\n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] ","2026-01-13T14:16:54.513Z"],["3807337","WD-22563","WD","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","Hi Yuvi, \n\n\n\nThey shared this schedule here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22415?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiM2RlMWE2MWMzMmQ0NDhlYmIwYmZjODMzNWYyY2ExMGUiLCJwIjoiaiJ9|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22415?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiM2RlMWE2MWMzMmQ0NDhlYmIwYmZjODMzNWYyY2ExMGUiLCJwIjoiaiJ9|smart-link] \n\nCan we please make sure all of the countries mentioned in the file were scheduled on prod? Thanks","2026-01-13T14:17:21.776Z"],["3807338","LSS-61370","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Summary of meeting with [~accountid:712020:50554e69-c5e6-483a-a43b-b48bec17d7bb], to align on next steps\n\n+*Context*+\n\nThe BB team follows a due diligence process before onboarding clients. They have access to an online data base, where they can verify the corporate and financial information of companies, including who are their legal representatives and conduct a risk evaluation of the client, which allows to make decisions regarding credit limits.\n\nThe BB team followed the process for these companies (Moldistar and Emotion Sports), and no concerning information was found. The team is also able to verify if the credit card added to the account is subject to any fraud risk.\n\nBoth these clients were then onboarded, and their accounts had a monthly credit limit, with fixed term for payment. The credit card added to the account did not raise any fraud risk.\n\nHowever, the BB team proceeded to signature of the Special Terms, and the person who signed was not any of the listed as legal representatives of these companies.\n\nThe “fraudulent activity” that raised concerns in the BB team was the consumption associated with these client’s accounts. Both accounts had, everyday, rides in the amount of +/- 200€, which, according to the team, is not within normal usage of the BB account and raises fraud suspicion.\n\nFollowing this, BB team communicated to their POC that the accounts had been blocked due to fraud, without major response or pushback.\n\n+*Concerns*+\n\nThe BB team contacted both companies (Moldistar and Emotion Sports) through their publicly available contacts online, and both companies confirmed that they did not sign up for a Bolt Business account, nor do they know the POC who set up the BB accounts and signed the Special Terms.\n\nThe Legal Team also verified, through the publicly available information of the commercial registry, that the individuals that signed the Special Terms are not registered as legal representatives of such companies (if they have PoA, such circumstance is unknown to Bolt).\n\nAt this point, it seems possible that the individuals who signed the Special Terms misappropriated the corporate information of these companies to create business accounts.\n\nThe *first concern is the payment of pending amounts*. The deadline for payment of the consumption of these accounts is 18 January for Emotion Sports and 1 February for Moldistar. Since both accounts were blocked before the deadline for payment, there is the risk that the payment may not be settled.\n\nThe *second concern is the potencial legal consequences of the misappropriation of these companies information and signature of contract by individuals other than their legal representatives*, without proven powers to act in that capacity, with the corresponding issuing of invoices.\n\nThe +misrepresented companies could pursue action against Bolt+ and, adding to this, +in case of non payment of the invoices, the misrepresentation also compromises the recoverability of the debt+.\n\n+*Course of Action*+\n\nIt was agreed that, at the time being, the inicial step is to +verify if the pending invoices are paid on their due date+.\nAfter this, depending on wether the payments are made and +if there is any reaction from the misappropriated companies, further action will be decided+.","2026-01-13T14:17:24.573Z"],["3807341","RDXENG-4584","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","*Tested and unable to reproduce* (/) \n\n||*Device name*||Google Pixel 8a||\n|OS Version|16|\n|Client build|CA.193.0 (develop)|\n|Comment|physical|\n\n!expected.mp4|width=320,alt=\"expected.mp4\"!","2026-01-13T14:18:03.967Z"],["3807343","WFM-9952","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","roles requested, awaiting approval","2026-01-13T14:18:11.876Z"],["3807344","LSS-61512","LSS","bruna.miguel@bolt.eu","Bruna Miguel","[^Contract Sigmaelle.pdf] _(1.25 MB)_\n\n[^Sigmaelle Contract - Termination Document 2026 H&S.docx] _(27 kB)_","2026-01-13T14:18:14.284Z"],["3807345","WFM-9975","WFM","ottomar.meoste@bolt.eu","Ottomar Meoste","CS related roles requested [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571704]","2026-01-13T14:18:51.299Z"],["3807346","WFM-9890","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","OS restricted sites manager, won’t be in Assembled","2026-01-13T14:19:08.968Z"],["3807347","WFM-9972","WFM","ottomar.meoste@bolt.eu","Ottomar Meoste","marked as CS, but role description is OPS based I think","2026-01-13T14:19:34.912Z"],["3807349","WFM-9890","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-13T14:19:44.345Z"],["3807350","PFI-832945","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T14:19:44.508Z"],["3807351","WD-22563","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:60ab52d6411c2200681a75e4] my applogies, I see this schedule is already created and was shared. \n\n\n\nI read it as ireland instead of Iceland. There should be no action on us atm. 🙂 ","2026-01-13T14:20:07.817Z"],["3807354","LSS-61369","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","FYI: Uploaded by Indrek (thank you) \n\n!image-20260113-142005.png|width=630,alt=\"image-20260113-142005.png\"!","2026-01-13T14:20:22.619Z"],["3807355","WFM-9973","WFM","ottomar.meoste@bolt.eu","Ottomar Meoste","request [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571705]","2026-01-13T14:20:30.760Z"],["3807356","DSR-3621","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NE2bTutH3-AoF32jUpCL8zRjXZCkpMgu9KstbuUo6qw/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NE2bTutH3-AoF32jUpCL8zRjXZCkpMgu9KstbuUo6qw/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T14:20:42.239Z"],["3807357","WFM-9973","WFM","ottomar.meoste@bolt.eu","Ottomar Meoste","Hello!\n\n\n\nRoles have been approved and applied. Let us know if there’s anything else!\n\n\n\nKind regards","2026-01-13T14:20:43.610Z"],["3807358","WFM-9969","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","roles requested, awaiting approval","2026-01-13T14:21:02.057Z"],["3807359","WFM-9969","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571706|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571706]","2026-01-13T14:21:06.671Z"],["3807366","PFI-796383","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Hi [~accountid:634e4f09c97f5473af6dcdf9] ! Sorry for the delay in getting back to you. Engineering ticket is solved, you (and the customer from the app) should be able to download the invoice now 🙂 \n\nPlease let us know if you still run into issues with this.","2026-01-13T14:22:24.294Z"],["3807370","WFM-9923","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, access for business granted. Into what queues agents should be assigned for?","2026-01-13T14:23:35.644Z"],["3807372","LSS-61078","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# Privacy updated the [+agreement+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GXwY1ASbBtSE3VU5i_jYy4GyMod6-x2l/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=106326439712206242177&rtpof=true&sd=true] and revised clause 12 on data protection; also added a comment for GS.\n# It was clearly indicated that Bolt will have separate agreements with corporate clients (business customers) ordering rides through the GS System.\n\nStatus: business to review the clause and confirm accuracy. If it accurately reflects the collaboration and relationship between Bolt, GS, and our business customers, consider this completed from privacy side.","2026-01-13T14:24:17.572Z"],["3807374","LSS-61513","LSS","irene.cobian@bolt.eu","Irene Cobian Martin","[^ACH_20form_20Sept_202019.pdf] _(624 kB)_","2026-01-13T14:24:46.955Z"],["3807377","HS-28911","HS","darius.poursiami@bolt.eu","Darius Poursiami","[^PKO BP - Zaświadczenie umowa o pracę_zał.4a_30.06.2025.pdf]\n\n[^mBank - Zaświadczenie o zatrudnieniu - umowa o pracę_01.12.2025.pdf]","2026-01-13T14:25:41.932Z"],["3807378","CMS-477","CMS","burak.ozdemir@bolt.eu","Burak Özdemir","*TypeError*\n\n[Events (total)|https://bolt-eu.sentry.io/issues/86715119/events/?environment=live&project=4510578420023376&query=is%3Aunresolved&referrer=issue-stream]\n\nUsers (90d)\n\nLevel: Error\n\nCannot read properties of null (reading 'url')\n\n[https://bolt-eu.sentry.io/issues/86715119/?environment=live&project=4510578420023376&query=is%3Aunresolved&referrer=issue-stream|https://bolt-eu.sentry.io/issues/86715119/?environment=live&project=4510578420023376&query=is%3Aunresolved&referrer=issue-stream|smart-link] \n\n[~accountid:624407b28678e900705a1a54] , image is required, but it can be removed from media library, that’s the issue.","2026-01-13T14:26:19.456Z"],["3807379","PIF-2266","PIF","kristo.koert@bolt.eu","Kristo Koert","RnD: There was a previous attempt at introducing a per-service DB connections limit: [+ADR+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/6794314264/2025-09-08+Per-service+DB+connections+limiting], [+Design Doc+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/YYAXlQE], and there was a decision _not_ to go forward with it, but rather push for introducing the limit on the infra-side. If the limit is enforced on the infra side, then we need to understand how the service runtime could read it to adjust the local limits accordingly. The history can be seen in [feature-db-connections-limit|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C09EGDL1DT3].\n\nAlso it isn’t totally clear that limits should be evenly distributed in all cases.\n\n","2026-01-13T14:26:47.777Z"],["3807380","LSS-61080","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9], \n\nAnticipating Emilie’s response, I would say that our position is that the contract is formed between the driver and the rider - the responsability falls on the driver. The articles within the code civil that the rider cites: [Article 1240|https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/codes/article_lc/LEGIARTI000032041571] and [Article 1242|https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/codes/article_lc/LEGIARTI000051786000], these apply to the individual who has committed the damage or to individuals responsible for another (i.e. parents → enfants mineurs, artisans → apprentis).\n\nLet’s wait for her response to get further information of the situation, but if you agree I can start drafting a letter of response in this way.\n\nThank you !","2026-01-13T14:26:54.540Z"],["3807381","SREDESK-7345","SREDESK","yehor.naumenko@bolt.eu","Yehor Naumenko","set to 10 days now.\nwill set to 3 tomorrow.","2026-01-13T14:27:04.236Z"],["3807382","LSS-60915","LSS","karlo.masnjak@bolt.eu","Karlo Masnjak","[~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] Thank you, I will wait to have signed documents as well, and I will send it to the provider. ","2026-01-13T14:27:21.308Z"],["3807383","LSS-57939","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Internal comments: The question raised is not something we looked into in light of the expansion questionnaire and Commerce has informed the below. I believe, if there are unclarities to transport regulation, then we could and should consult external counsel. I’ve previously received the following from Commerce: \n\n_The question/request:\"We would like legal clarification regarding whether a driving office (kørselskontor) in Denmark is legally required to collect passenger payments directly under the Danish Taxi Act (Taxiloven)._\n_During an internal discussion about POS systems, it was mentioned that since we operate as a driving office, we might be obligated to collect the payments ourselves. However, based on our review of Taxiloven §20, the law only specifies that a driving office must record payment details for each trip, not necessarily collect the payments._\n\n_Could you please confirm:_\n_Whether a driving office is legally required to collect passenger payments directly; and_\n_If not, whether there are any compliance or licensing implications if payments are collected directly by Fleet Owners meaning that FOs have their own POS and the money going directly to the FOs business account for street hailing.\"As I understand the first question is about what is actually required/allowed under the Danish Taxi Act (Taxilovel) - this seems to be a question around local transportation regulations. Please correct me if this is not the case, but in case there is sth potentially required under local transportation laws, this would be covered by local legal advisors for Rides? If needed, I can give my opinion, but I'm not really that well versed in understanding transportation regulation.What could potentially be relevant for FinReg is, if there is in fact a requirement in the Taxi Act that the driving office (btw - is this the same as \"taxi dispatcher\"?) must actually collect payments from riders ( and it cannot be the fleet company directly), then FinReg must look into whether this requirement is aligned with the commercial agent exemption requirements. I understand that we are speaking in the_ *_context of street hailing_*_, right? In case of street hailing, I assume that the order will not be made through the Bolt platform, so in this case it is also logical that the actual transportation provider (driver, fleet) should also be collecting the payments from customers directly.Let me know, if you want to discuss this in call._ ","2026-01-13T14:27:29.039Z"],["3807386","WFM-9953","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","roles requested, awaiting approvals","2026-01-13T14:27:48.023Z"],["3807387","PFI-832954","PFI","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.21.51.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T14:27:54.023Z"],["3807388","WD-22415","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:623ace37b75ca80070562c04] , I see that the Canada period is not updated yet:[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22415?focusedCommentId=3796216|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22415?focusedCommentId=3796216|smart-link] . Please advice. 🙂 \n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-13T14:28:00.916Z"],["3807391","DO-5792","DO","volha.anishchanka@bolt.eu","Volha Anishchanka","Hey! Can you ask Tanel to add “Approve“ comment here?","2026-01-13T14:28:35.560Z"],["3807392","LSS-60545","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:62c696a740923988ba0ae796],\n\nJust a quick update on this matter. We have finalized the review of the addendum to Prosegur’s contract and we have sent it to our external partner for signature. Once we receive it, we will get back to you. ","2026-01-13T14:28:42.850Z"],["3807395","HS-28825","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-13T14:30:05.927Z"],["3807396","CSDA-286","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hey hey!\n\nHere is the draft of the report - [QA - Agent Reviews (WIP)|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/29526?Country%20Name=&Safety%20Related%20(Yes%20%2F%20No)=&Vertical=&Scorecard%20Name=Case-level%20QA,Case-level%20qa&Dynamic%20Timeframe%20Picker=Month&Review%20Created%20UTC%20Date=3%20month%20ago%20for%203%20month&Bolt%20Business%20Flag%20(Yes%20%2F%20No)=&Reviewer%20Agent%20Team%20Lead=&User%20Persona=&Reviewer%20Agent%20Organization=Bolt&Reviewer%20Agent%20Name=&Reviewer%20Agent%20Email=]. Please have a look and let me know if smth is off or not working.\n\nLooking forward to your reply 🙌 ","2026-01-13T14:30:09.779Z"],["3807398","PFI-832957","PFI","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.22.16.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.25.13.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T14:30:20.579Z"],["3807399","DO-5789","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Granted!","2026-01-13T14:30:20.801Z"],["3807400","PFI-792392","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Hi [~accountid:712020:8dbed75f-ea0e-49a3-936f-217237e71175] ! This specific invoice that you have linked here is definitely reported (investigating why the PDF is not updated in billing document, but you can find the reported PDF in [Fiscalization → Invoices|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-fiscalization/fiscalization/invoices?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22create_time_from_timestamp%22%3A1765663200%2C%22create_time_to_timestamp%22%3A1768314213.045%2C%22uuid%22%3A%222175069-RO1125-72%22%7D%7D]). With quite a delay but reported. Please follow the troubleshooting and escalation guide [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6803423312/Romania+E-invoicing+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6803423312/Romania+E-invoicing+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|smart-link] , highly likely the issue was with either the supplier or customer billing details that has been fixed and if reported via correct channels, these kinds of issues get solved more efficienly 🙂 ","2026-01-13T14:30:48.524Z"],["3807401","DO-5791","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Granted!","2026-01-13T14:30:51.612Z"],["3807402","LSS-61488","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:5f0c30effe23000022252e68] ,\n\nThanks for raising this and sharing your initial analysis.\n\nWe agree with your assessment that the proposed Bolt Send model - where delivery is limited to light vehicles and avoids key postal processing stages - falls outside the scope of both postal services regulation (DL 150/91) and goods transport licensing under DL 257/2007 (for vehicles under 2500kg).\n\nHowever, in order to properly assess this initiative, we have a few +*preliminary questions:*+\n\nCan you please clarify s\n\n* If the idea is to have Bolt Send with TVDE vehicles and with couriers simultaneously? \n* Whether couriers would be employed by existing fleets, or contracted directly;\n* Whether couriers would be using personal or company-owned vehicles;\n\n* The vehicle types couriers would use (car, bike, e-moped, etc.);\n* The registration and vetting process on the platform;\n* The expected contractual structure (e.g. courier-fleet-Bolt, courier-Bolt direct);\n* Whether any changes to insurance or delivery protocols (e.g. ID checks, return logistics) are planned.\n* Will the clients have the possibility to choose if they want the delivery to be performed by a TVDE operator (by car) or by a courier? \n\nThank you!","2026-01-13T14:32:04.194Z"],["3807404","LSS-59480","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:dc5a9fc0-ec62-423d-a2f8-435f02007669],\n\nFollowing up on this, have you received reply from the landlord confirming receipt of the notice?\n\nThanks! ","2026-01-13T14:32:11.005Z"],["3807405","PFI-832960","PFI","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.22.29.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.25.13.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T14:32:12.111Z"],["3807408","LSS-47933","LSS","igne.martutaityte@bolt.eu","Ignė Martutaitytė","You can keep me as a reporting person any time 😄 \n\nFrom my side:\n1. Sales agreemnt is ~ fine\n\nOn the repurchase:\n\n# As we receive higher RVs than Swedbank accepts, we no longer use the construct reviewed here. However, we usually use something similar to [Moller templates|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1akAaLWl5ZrnOWp0R6GB8lAj4KIwFpiss/edit] (i.e., we sign two buyback prices: the lower one between Swedbank and the buyback provider, and the higher one between us and the buyback provider, allowing us to sell the car for the higher price and retain the difference). Could we add those clauses into the agreement?\n# What is our main goal of this review? For me, there are several points:\n## Decrease the reliance on the decisions from the bank side (as a rule, they are risk-averse; they don’t want to go to the court with the buyback providers, we can’t take them to the court or even threaten them with it) and cover the risk we have on the repurchase price due to the parental guarantee. So the question is how to localize any conflicts and make the bilateral. \n### I see we are changing the structure; that dealers need to claim the damages from us rather than paying less to the bank. Which is good; but maybe I’d also check how it’s worded in Luminor (not to make it too agressive to avoid the pushback from the dealers. Basically, not going straight to disputes but start with the clear structure of who pays to whom for what. And the fact that buyback provider cannot reduce the buyback goes more of a disclaimer.)\n### We talk about assigning the claim. We know that such a construct works in EE; but not really in LV (and LT is unclear). Here we are still depending on the bank (technically, we provide the parental guarantee to the bank so Swedbank has a way to claim the full repurchase prices from us without assigning any claims; thus we have an open risk). I’d rather structure it the way: the essence of the buyback is that dealer has to buy the car on preagreed price; technical condition and date. And both parties have the right to claim the buyback (us or the bank; and it shouldn’t matter which party sells the car). What we have to be mindfull though is that if bank claims the buyback; usually it gives ~30 days to pay; then let’s assume they claim the guarantee and we need to claim the buyback>>> it might take a few months after the official buyback date (but worst case we can expect which dealers will be probalmeatic after the first return.\n## Making sure we can meet the requirements on the repairs/maintenance & etc>>> to avoid ecesive requirements (like original parts) but ensure that dealers can still swallow it. I wouldn’t relay on this fully as a lot of dealers will want to change the conditions (they need certain guarantees that the quality of repairs and maintenance is actually fine)\n## Get rid of any conditions impossible to meet (short periods for 3rd party evaluations) or any conditions leaving us in the deadlock (e.g. allowing dealer to unilaterally reduce the repurchase price) which seems to be covered in this agreement.\n\n","2026-01-13T14:33:13.465Z"],["3807409","LSS-47933","LSS","igne.martutaityte@bolt.eu","Ignė Martutaitytė","And obv. [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] please review from your side as well","2026-01-13T14:33:30.975Z"],["3807410","PFI-832963","PFI","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.22.40.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 15.25.13.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T14:33:47.375Z"],["3807412","LSS-61494","LSS","brian.sun@bolt.eu","Brian Sun","[^[Accessible Fleet] Bolt - Fleet Partnership Agreement Taiwan - (CN trans)_FINAL.docx (4).pdf]\n\nHey [~accountid:62d7b457807cf6f78ca9d117] , \n\nThanks for the reminder, here is the updated version of the agreement where the new clause in included in section 3.6. Please kindly proceed with this version instead, thanks! \n\n","2026-01-13T14:34:20.521Z"],["3807413","PFI-832964","PFI","chiamaka.mmeka@bolt-outsource.eu","Chiamaka Mmeka","!{8BFA43D4-81A3-4D97-9759-806DBE9535FC}-20260113-143117.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T14:34:37.026Z"],["3807414","LSS-58800","LSS","maria.paraschiv@bolt.eu","Maria-Speranta Paraschiv","[~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95], please find here the NDA with comments from IDrive:\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1U3mMoSHIAqIIBIf6DwTsaxmn1jsmYhGM/edit?rtpof=true&sd=true&tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1U3mMoSHIAqIIBIf6DwTsaxmn1jsmYhGM/edit?rtpof=true&sd=true&tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T14:34:41.537Z"],["3807415","WFM-9718","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","pls ask for a screenshot of the error ","2026-01-13T14:34:46.562Z"],["3807416","SREDESK-7412","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","\n\n* Schema has been created on prelive and LIVE:\n\n{noformat}root@ti-prelive-dba.sqldb:(none)>CREATE DATABASE taxify_bolt_brand_visualisations_gateway;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.521s\n\nroot@internal-dba.sqldb:(none)>CREATE DATABASE taxify_bolt_brand_visualisations_gateway;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 1.016s{noformat}","2026-01-13T14:35:09.409Z"],["3807418","WFM-9974","WFM","valeria.tiilikainen@bolt.eu","Valeria Tiilikainen","solved via DM in Slack","2026-01-13T14:35:30.632Z"],["3807419","BD-1978","BD","ave.tarend@bolt.eu","Ave Tarend","The issue is solved. Ketlin contacted local ops to fix the address","2026-01-13T14:35:47.199Z"],["3807421","LSS-58216","LSS","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","Feedback provided to Solidgate with this state\n\n[^MSA_Solidgate_Bolt_Acceptance Bonus_Integration (Bolt DSA Update 05.01.2025) (d72228b3-0b1b-414f-8a47-9fdf1a088dec).docx]\n\n","2026-01-13T14:36:01.334Z"],["3807422","PFI-831433","PFI","fabricia.silva@bolt.eu","Fabrícia Silva Alcântara","Hi, \nCan you please provide a feedback here?","2026-01-13T14:36:13.958Z"],["3807423","PFI-831433","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-13T14:36:17.654Z"],["3807425","LSS-60403","LSS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b] ,\n\nCan you please help me understand what the EVTC number means? Seems like they are interested in invoices for specific EVTC numbers. ","2026-01-13T14:37:26.191Z"],["3807426","PFI-831313","PFI","yurii.bondarchuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Yurii Bondarchuk","Hi! Driver’s still waiting. What’s the progress?","2026-01-13T14:37:32.995Z"],["3807428","GRWA-1503","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","The Weekly KPIs [dashboard|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/18724?City+Name+%28All+%2F+City+Name%29=All&Year=2024%2C2025&Country+Name=Germany] was fixed.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 16.40.55.png|width=751,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 16.40.55.png\"!","2026-01-13T14:41:07.698Z"],["3807430","RNTL-29429","RNTL","karolina.epifantseva@bolt.eu","Karolina Epifantseva","@[~accountid:5cefa522f34cf30f24aaef42]  Currently refueling diesel cars is not working (see screenshot)","2026-01-13T14:41:37.457Z"],["3807431","BD-1976","BD","ave.tarend@bolt.eu","Ave Tarend","Turned out that the issue was in unchanged in memory datastore which belongs to dev-logistics-efficiency-support.\n\nThe currency in city settings for that in memory data store was changed on {{2026-01-08}}\n\nOps is now able to transfer the balances from old couriers to new.","2026-01-13T14:41:44.949Z"],["3807432","PFI-831313","PFI","yurii.bondarchuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Yurii Bondarchuk","The driver is from Zaporizhia. He can't get early cashouts due to provider issues in this city.","2026-01-13T14:42:13.416Z"],["3807433","DSR-3705","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Order history sent to user","2026-01-13T14:43:21.562Z"],["3807434","PFI-830796","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment imported https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/77005066 ","2026-01-13T14:43:39.481Z"],["3807436","L10N-27591","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27587](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27587)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T14:43:50.652Z"],["3807437","L10N-27589","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27587](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27587)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T14:43:51.046Z"],["3807438","L10N-27595","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27587](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27587)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T14:43:51.676Z"],["3807439","L10N-27593","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27587](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27587)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T14:43:52.219Z"],["3807440","L10N-27596","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27587](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27587)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T14:43:52.860Z"],["3807441","L10N-27594","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above 