to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27587](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27587)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T14:43:53.995Z"],["3807445","PFI-832531","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi [~accountid:5e0f07ad5361330daaeab025],\n\nAdded you to the ticket in order for you to see the general issue that we talked about and that is still on-going.\n\nThe procedure has always been, that the Fraud team only assists with removing *Device UID* suspensions.\nThe Fraud team does NOT remove Hard-Blocks nor Scheduled blocks that have been *placed by the Safety team.* We do not take the responsibility of removing these.\nI remember you raising this argument before and I explained the situation to you back then as well.\n\nIs the Safety team not able to remove the regular (driver) Hard-blocks that have been placed?\nI already know that the Safety team can remove rider hard-blocks, therefore I find it hard to believe that you can not remove these.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you both,\nMarten","2026-01-13T14:44:07.107Z"],["3807446","LSS-61338","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342292|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342292|smart-link]  ","2026-01-13T14:44:08.204Z"],["3807448","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] \nAdjusted the designs. If all good, I’ll provide printing files. Also, we need DOOH in motion. When all approved, I’ll hand it over to a motion designer. \n\nPreviews are here:\n[https://www.figma.com/design/gUQE4YwqN5X2mPCleXqJe0/Airport-and-Venues-Ad-hoc?node-id=529-2438&t=sXCefD9kPd5piIYx-1|https://www.figma.com/design/gUQE4YwqN5X2mPCleXqJe0/Airport-and-Venues-Ad-hoc?node-id=529-2438&t=sXCefD9kPd5piIYx-1|smart-link] \n\nPlease also provide one more category for 16mx4xm designs, it would be much better design-wise.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-13T14:44:26.918Z"],["3807449","ITI-1162","ITI","marko.toomla@bolt.eu","Marko Toomla","Problem solved","2026-01-13T14:44:32.206Z"],["3807450","DRX-27934","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","❌ The break button overlaps the TTD banner\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 16.41.46.jpeg|width=200,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 16.41.46.jpeg\"!","2026-01-13T14:44:37.109Z"],["3807453","WFM-9718","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey [~accountid:5f802f9595fe8e0069b2c28c] ,\n\nDropping my additional suggestion here as well, can you have Edma Nogueira to send us error screenshot?\nIt might help us to locate the issue quicker.","2026-01-13T14:45:32.586Z"],["3807455","LSS-60989","LSS","petr.kratky@bolt.eu","Petr Krátký","Hello, could you please share what is the current status?\n\nThank you","2026-01-13T14:46:05.069Z"],["3807456","LSS-61515","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T14:46:07.306Z"],["3807461","SAI-1402","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","FYI We disabled refunds for MM for bundle order payments. In the future we will implement proper solution.","2026-01-13T14:47:01.133Z"],["3807464","BDB-1494","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:628e5c9d8026a10068b1e457] Hey, here you are: [https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/26w5o137lzdi8c45ixph4/AIQEZbv1qRoFepJJKEmX_1Y?rlkey=li8wf96iqr4zu27n0sall5yjp&dl=0|https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/26w5o137lzdi8c45ixph4/AIQEZbv1qRoFepJJKEmX_1Y?rlkey=li8wf96iqr4zu27n0sall5yjp&dl=0|smart-link] \nPlease let me know if everything works for you, thank you!","2026-01-13T14:47:33.486Z"],["3807465","HS-28913","HS","mykhailo.brynchak@bolt.eu","Mykhailo Brynchak","!Screen Recording 2026-01-12 at 10.45.15.mov|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T14:47:40.210Z"],["3807470","GRWA-1504","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","Added 3 additional tiles to have the {{all year summary}} vs {{year to date summary}}, for yearly, monthly, and weekly + city.\n\nHere is the [dash|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/25235?Country=Germany&Period+Year=2024%2C2025&City=&Month+Filter+%28YTD+Monthly+tile+only%29=&Week+of+Year+Filter+%28YTD+Weekly+tile+only%29=&City+Group+Tier=]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 16.34.59.png|width=1140,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 16.34.59.png\"!\n\n\n","2026-01-13T14:48:52.223Z"],["3807471","GEORM-18","GEORM","ilya.rybin@bolt.eu","Ilya Rybin","closing this because it did not work out","2026-01-13T14:49:03.761Z"],["3807472","PFI-832924","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:7837f0a4-cc9c-48c7-9fe9-71cece7a1020],\n\nThis user has created a lot of duplicate/similar users that are also attached to the same device.\nDue to this they are no longer eligible for the aforementioned campaign. Most likely the user is simply trying to abuse our system and trying to phish for additional discounts.\n\nIf possible, please try to give as little information to the user as possible, since we do not want them to know what they got caught with, otherwise they may try attempting something new.\nKeeping it the usual “unusual activity” is generally the best.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-13T14:49:15.631Z"],["3807473","RDS-613","RDS","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","True. Was P1 when I handed it over, what happened here? Maybe you can give a status update [~accountid:627b6b8f19b1290068296d3b] [~accountid:712020:2791559d-8cee-435c-95ba-4a8c95b36b65] pls","2026-01-13T14:49:21.841Z"],["3807476","LSS-60076","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342300|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342300|smart-link]  ","2026-01-13T14:49:40.294Z"],["3807478","LSS-61080","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742]! I just added you and [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] to the insurance ticket.\n\nThe driver has not been contacted and did not get in touch neither.\n\nIt looks like something that could be covered by driver’s RC Pro.\n\n----\n\nHere is the summary of the [Beehive case|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/716924132]\n\n*Customer*\n\n{quote}Le chauffeur a ouvert le coffre, ma valise est tombée et la coque s’est fissurée. La valise est inutilisable. Valeur : 349 €. Je demande une indemnisation.{quote}\n\n!IMG_9803 (902471f5-61f6-4ffc-b65c-b9de8ea1d349).jpeg|width=3024,height=4032,alt=\"IMG_9803.jpeg\"!\n\n[^Facture valise (4446ba39-5e01-46d7-8e37-69c7b054767e).pdf]\n\n*Support*\n_Case handled by alfred_\n\n{quote}Je vous renvoie à un spécialiste en charge des cas de sécurité qui vous répondra sous peu. Rassurez-vous, une personne en chair et en os est présente pour vous aider ! 🤝\n\nIl examinera votre cas et vous appellera si nécessaire.{quote}\n\n_Case sent to Safety Team_\n\n{quote}Bonjour Stephen! C'est Weal de l'équipe Bolt. Nous sommes en train d'examiner la situation et moi ou l'un des membres de mon équipe reviendra vers vous.{quote}\n\n\n\n{quote}Je suis vraiment désolé pour le comportement inapproprié du chauffeur pendant votre course précédente. Merci beaucoup d’avoir pris le temps de nous en informer — c’est grâce à vos retours que nous pouvons améliorer notre service.\n\nRassurez-vous, l’équipe concernée a été informée et des mesures seront prises pour éviter que cela ne se reproduise.{quote}\n\n\n\n{quote}Pour une meilleure assistance, je vous invite à me donner plus de détails sur les circonstances dans lesquelles le chauffeur a ouvert le coffre et me confirmer s'il l'a fait exprès.{quote}\n\n*Customer*\n\n{quote}Bonjour, Il a placé lui-même les bagages dans le coffre lors du chargement, puis arrivée à l’aéroport, au moment de tout sortir il a ouvert son coffre et la valise est tombée. Ce n’était pas fait exprès non.{quote}\n\n*Support*\n\n{quote}Je vous remercie pour votre retour et les informations fournies. Par ailleurs, je suis navré de ne pas pouvoir vous rembourser des frais de la valise.{quote}\n\n\n\n{quote}Passez une excellente journée, surtout prenez soin de vous.{quote}\n\n*Customer*\n\n{quote}Vos chauffeurs peuvent endommager les effets personnels de votre clientèle en toute impunité ?{quote}\n\n\n\n{quote}Votre réponse est juridiquement insuffisante.\n\nLe chauffeur a manipulé lui-même mon bagage, ce qui engage sa responsabilité civile pour le dommage causé. Le caractère non intentionnel est juridiquement sans effet.\n\nEn l’absence de base légale valable justifiant votre refus, votre position constitue un refus d’indemnisation non motivé, contraire aux obligations prévues par le Code civil (articles 1240 et 1242).\n\nSans régularisation rapide de la situation, je transmettrai ce dossier complet (photos, facture, échanges) aux autorités compétentes (SignalConso / DGCCRF) et engagerai les démarches nécessaires pour obtenir réparation.{quote}\n\n\n\n{quote}Je relance{quote}\n\n\n\n{quote}?{quote}\n\n_Esclated to tier 2 as rider reached out on social media_\n_”_[_Social Media request_|https://app.sproutsocial.com/case/CASE-626381/view/activity] _: The rider report that the driver damage his property, and he is unhappy about the customer support. Please assist.”_\n\n*Support*\n\n{quote}Bonjour Stephen, je suis Emilie et je vais prendre le relais.{quote}\n\n_Created SD to insurance_\n\n{quote}Votre dossier a été transmis à notre service d'assurance pour une analyse approfondie. Nous reviendrons vers vous dès que nous aurons reçu leur retour concernant l'indemnisation. Nous vous remercions de votre patience.{quote}\n\n*Customer*\n\n{quote}Bonjour Emilie Merci d’avoir repris le dossier. Pouvez-vous me dire d’ici combien de temps dois-je m’attendre à une réponse ?{quote}\n\n*Support*\n\n{quote}Bonjour Stephen, ma collègue a transmis votre dossier et nous espérons pouvoir vous donner une réponse dans la semaine. Bonne journée à vous.{quote}\n\n","2026-01-13T14:49:58.982Z"],["3807479","WEB-8719","WEB","mykhailo.kudla@bolt.eu","Mykhailo Kudla","Hi, team, do we have any ETAs for this project to go live?","2026-01-13T14:50:02.623Z"],["3807484","LSS-60989","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:5ece16662490cf0c09d78cae] !\n\nI have send 71 contract for signature out of total number. Some contracts have already been executed. Should I send them all together or send you the ones that ready?","2026-01-13T14:51:40.389Z"],["3807486","WDFT-3486","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1srmGr8LDLORAqRi2RDMUi-AgjCn3omQu/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=107772986506248968601&rtpof=true&sd=true|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1srmGr8LDLORAqRi2RDMUi-AgjCn3omQu/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=107772986506248968601&rtpof=true&sd=true|smart-card]","2026-01-13T14:52:26.161Z"],["3807491","SREDESK-7413","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi Mahmoud,\n\nI granted your access via [this PR|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15369].","2026-01-13T14:53:58.006Z"],["3807495","LSS-61335","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:9cfda827-f644-48a1-9da8-aff3fd427bf9] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Fleet Agreement_Elvira Sampaio Unipessoal Lda (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T14:54:47.146Z"],["3807496","PFI-832531","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Additionally, please keep in mind that the Driver related blocks are owned by the Compliance team. Even the ones that the Fraud team has, is via the service of Compliance (Central OPS)","2026-01-13T14:54:53.481Z"],["3807497","LSS-61369","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","{color:#006644}+*Legal analysis and recommendation to be concerned:*+{color}\n\n* A fabricated crash image can be framed as an *unlawful interference with Bolt’s good reputation*, especially where it implies safety issues, misconduct, or systemic risk.\n* I understand that the whole picture has been AI generated and the case presented in the picture has never happened due to Bolt fleet cars.\n* 👉  {color:#36b37e}*demanding letter:* {color}In this case I would suggest to prepare a demanding letter to the Taxi Association to stop publishing and delete the post from the social media immediately. If the post has been going viral and spreading across media we also can demand them to publish a correction and public apology on their social website. This letter could include also objections against breaching of IP rights (forgery of a Bolt mark), if any - tbc with [~accountid:6172754ef485cd006863a3a8] [{color:#ff5630}*TBC by* {color}[~accountid:712020:fde8e40a-0c43-479b-a07d-dd05334dd10a] ] *Please  let me know if you want to proceed with this so that we could draft such a letter.*\n* 👉 {color:#36b37e}*PR aspect:*{color} If the post has been going viral and spreading across media, especially made lots of negative comments appear in the social media, *please* [~accountid:712020:fde8e40a-0c43-479b-a07d-dd05334dd10a]  *r*{color:#ff5630}*each out to PR team*{color} [~accountid:712020:475fe025-bbd5-4b05-8b72-81e652464744] *what next steps you should take, regardless of the legal steps.*\n\nBest,\n\nJola\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] ","2026-01-13T14:55:07.921Z"],["3807498","LSS-60989","LSS","petr.kratky@bolt.eu","Petr Krátký","I think that collect some of the signatures will be difficult, so it would be better to send it once they are ready.","2026-01-13T14:55:08.554Z"],["3807499","LSS-61181","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:9cfda827-f644-48a1-9da8-aff3fd427bf9] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Fleet Agreement_Portu-Bangla (1).pdf] ","2026-01-13T14:56:32.927Z"],["3807500","RDS-1133","RDS","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] as the discrepancy was present in control and treatment, it alone cannot explain the results. hence for sure some kind of UI reason. after we made ETAs visually smaller again the issue ceased. \n\nNext Step to properly understand what’s driving it\n\n# finalize [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDS-1161|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDS-1161|smart-link] (which solves ETA discrepancies)\n# then re-test ETA UI small vs large\n## if cancellation issues re-emerges → best guess hypothesis: riders simply dislike the ETA and making them bigger, makes them wanna cancel → re-arrange sizes in LA UI\n## if cancellation issues don’t re-emerge → issue was discrepancy (/) → rollout intended design","2026-01-13T14:56:38.612Z"],["3807501","FPD-1524","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","Figures out with Andrea that RF is using different formula for comparison forecast vs actualy","2026-01-13T14:56:59.192Z"],["3807503","PFI-832470","PFI","samuel.ojo@bolt.eu","Samuel Ojo"," [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] , I do not have access to view the employee who made this change. Could you please confirm which employee carried it out? Additionally, can this change be reverted to the business name, as this is causing an issue for our business client.\ncc [~accountid:712020:325e1882-ed1b-40c9-9f18-3c2345e5578a] ","2026-01-13T14:57:25.593Z"],["3807504","LSS-60989","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[^DP Eco-Consult s.r.o. SLAs contract, 2026.pdf]\n[^Dávid Lischka SLAs contract, 2026.pdf]\n[^BRZIPARI s.r.o. SLAs contract, 2026.pdf]\n[^Artworks s.r.o. SLAs contract, 2026.pdf]\n\nthose are currently ready","2026-01-13T14:57:42.273Z"],["3807506","LSS-60989","LSS","petr.kratky@bolt.eu","Petr Krátký","Thank you! Do we send any reminders?","2026-01-13T14:58:20.419Z"],["3807507","LSS-61517","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nElisabeth Gunnarsson has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-13T14:58:32.644Z"],["3807509","FX-3620","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768316302662279]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@chantel.rowe>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3620] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T14:58:46.002Z"],["3807511","LSS-59952","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello team!\n\nCould we provide the following reply? Thank you\n\n_Exmo. Senhor Comandante da Esquadra de Trânsito em Suplência da Amadora - Comando Metropolitano de Lisboa_\n\n_No seguimento do pedido de informação, relativamente ao veículo de matrícula 82-ZT-16, que mereceu a nossa melhor atenção, remetem-se os elementos solicitados em anexo._\n\n_Quanto aos elementos “3 - Contrato de comodato, e qual a empresa Operadora TVDE, nos períodos abaixo identificados” e “5 - Identificação do condutor associado ao veículo/empresa”, esclarece-se o seguinte:_\n\n_O veículo encontra-se associado ao Operador TVDE “Corais & Templos - Unipessoal Lda.”, com a licença n.º 213128/2025._\n\n_Não obstante o veículo se encontrar registado na Plataforma Bolt, associado ao referido Operador, o veículo não realizou quaisquer viagens no período compreendido entre 31-03-2025 e 10-12-2025, motivo pelo qual não existe qualquer condutor associado ao veículo nem contrato de comodato._\n\n_Encontramo-nos disponíveis para qualquer esclarecimento adicional necessário._\n\n_Atentamente,_\n\n[^DOCS FINAL.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T14:58:54.044Z"],["3807515","LSS-60169","LSS","domagoj.klemen@bolt.eu","Domagoj Klemen","Hey Sasha, honest apologies for the late.\n\nI have reviewed the trips the user had on the Bolt platform, and they haven’t had any on the 16th of April. \n\nI have managed to find out that the user has finished 1 trip with a driver who drove a car with the given registration (LY69 EXA, on the 17th of April), but there are no reports of any incidents, either from the driver or the rider. \n\n\n\nI’m at your disposal if you have additional questions.\n\n\n\nHave a nice day!","2026-01-13T14:59:35.914Z"],["3807516","LSS-60989","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Yes, I resend reminders every week","2026-01-13T14:59:47.764Z"],["3807517","LSS-60557","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","many thanks [~accountid:712020:5edd7b8a-e535-468c-85fd-63f0b6de01b2] ! you can let them also know that we are proceeding with signing procedure and they will get 2 copies to be signed sent from HQ office in Tallinn, EE  and *ask him to send us back one copy* of each signed annex to the Bolt Warsaw Office (*_ul. Prosta 67, 00-838 Warsaw_*).\n\n📝 Then, Legal OPS: please send the signed annexes to the address as follows: *_Eryk Połeć, ul. Ciechanowska 15, (Ciechanowska 15 Street), 03- 107 Warszawa (Warsaw, Poland)_*.","2026-01-13T14:59:49.144Z"],["3807522","WFM-9955","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","oki, got it! Then please raise a ticket to IT Bolt to create an account for the agent and then come back to us to give the agent the roles and queues needed 🙏 \n\n \nPlease keep in mind for Hana.Belanova I requested the roles (pending approval, will be approved soon) and added her 2 queues (the same ones valeriia.sliesarieva have) : \n\n 11 REG_Poland_Fleet_Driver Registrations \n\n 11 REG_Poland_Driver_Onboarding Registrations","2026-01-13T15:01:05.419Z"],["3807523","LSS-61516","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T15:01:33.685Z"],["3807524","LSS-61517","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T15:01:34.673Z"],["3807525","WFM-9952","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","[+Rides - UK Compliance Agent (210558)+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-user/roles/edit/210558] role rejected by its owner\n\npending: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571710|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571710]","2026-01-13T15:01:37.261Z"],["3807526","LSS-61381","LSS","igne.martutaityte@bolt.eu","Ignė Martutaitytė","# Yes please, and I’m adding [~accountid:5fedbf6f8332a1010eb155b7] for the sake of the visibility.\n#  Yes.\n# Can we include both swedbanks into a single POA? (last year Swedbank changed the entity they are doing the leases, thus we have the cars leased in 2 different Swedbank entities, and thus we need the POA for both but besides this, POA is identical).\n\n","2026-01-13T15:01:41.360Z"],["3807528","WFM-9972","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","CS - Rides - OPS is CS role, you can give ","2026-01-13T15:01:51.800Z"],["3807529","CMO-12978","CMO","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Passed Global Safety Induction course","2026-01-13T15:01:58.995Z"],["3807532","LSS-61369","LSS","helena.vaht@bolt.eu","Helena Vaht","Hi! I think the correct point of contact regarding this case should be [~accountid:5bb7726959e46d7be31aad4c] .","2026-01-13T15:02:17.309Z"],["3807534","CSDA-295","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review ad-hoc requests once a day. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-13T15:02:44.425Z"],["3807535","WFM-9954","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! Roles were applied ","2026-01-13T15:03:04.585Z"],["3807537","FX-3621","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768316572711329]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@chantel.rowe>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3621] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T15:03:17.214Z"],["3807538","BEE-3650","BEE","piotr.musiol@bolt.eu","Piotr Musioł","hey, the issue with the call wrap-up should be fixed :smile:\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A99MZK4DN/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A99MZK4DN/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-13T15:03:52.203Z"],["3807539","LSS-61459","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","Yes, rides only. ","2026-01-13T15:04:00.047Z"],["3807541","XVER-233","XVER","vincenzo.rinella@bolt.eu","Vincenzo Aglieri Rinella","[~accountid:605ee3012f7d900070c2e492] Andre is deactivated and Liis is off. Can you reassign this initiative accordingly? Thank you","2026-01-13T15:04:38.512Z"],["3807545","WFM-9971","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571711|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571711] ","2026-01-13T15:07:39.709Z"],["3807547","LSS-59134","LSS","margarita.karamysheva@bolt.eu","Margarita Karamysheva","Hi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] Apologies for the delays!\n\n# This feature is currently considered for Odysse only and applies exclusively to M&G orders.\n# At this stage, the feature is not available in the UK, as Odysse is currently the only active fleet. We also do not yet have any dedicated materials available for drivers. My understanding is that, given the fleet fully employs all drivers in the case of Odysse, it would be the fleet’s responsibility to communicate any potential developments of this nature to their drivers. Please let me know if that’s correct?\n# To the best of my knowledge, there is no separate notification sent to drivers when the fleet owner manually allocates an order. However, I will confirm this with the relevant team and follow up accordingly.\n\nThank you!\n\n","2026-01-13T15:08:00.378Z"],["3807549","RDS-267","RDS","andreas.palm@bolt.eu","Andreas Palm","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] Was prioritized lower due to other projects (co-badge cards and business individual payment method) beforehand which were both P0. Also afaik the priorities are team specific, and there are no higher priorities anymore now that co-badged is launched and BIP is 99% ready. Updated to P1","2026-01-13T15:08:15.595Z"],["3807551","DLVR-305","DLVR","anna.aalberg@bolt.eu","Anna-Lota Aalberg","Legal & Privacy are complete. Following a meeting with Billing & Controlling, we decided to *put the initiative on hold* until we can define a stronger product & ops-led approach. Targeting *Q3 2026*, we’ll restart discussions to agree on any required developments and initiate a new MVRA stream. In the meantime, Billing will focus on strengthening the core capabilities needed to support courier debt collection, so the eventual solution is sustainable and business-positive rather than a manual, ad-hoc process involving several stakeholders.\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] [~accountid:712020:b1a3aa39-56a5-492b-9453-5372da990388] [~accountid:712020:28f1a8fb-1d02-4f0c-b69a-61a5b33fc8de] [~accountid:5a670f010c10ac2e28964251] [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03] [~accountid:63b29b637cde7bff9d796748] [~accountid:6285ef56bd640f0068aeb51b] ","2026-01-13T15:09:23.192Z"],["3807554","PRIV-486","PRIV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Closing. Project on hold by business.","2026-01-13T15:10:44.465Z"],["3807556","PAW-14521","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-review-and-approval-system, pint-product-identity-and-communication-management, pint-capability-itgc\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-13T15:11:39.752Z"],["3807557","CCM-22271","CCM","miroslava.solarova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Solárová","Thank you for confirming, Victoria. I have spoken with Mihaela on Slack, and we agreed on the following courses:\n\n* CEE | Ride-Hailing Onboarding\n* Privacy Training: Data Requests\n* Handling cases related to employment\n* Privacy: Requests to unsubscribe from emails\n* Ride-Hailing Safety Up-Skill Course (High and Significant)\n* Micromobility Up-Skill Course\n* Micromobility Safety Up-Skill Course\n\nHave a lovely rest of your day!\n\nMirka 🙂","2026-01-13T15:11:41.108Z"],["3807559","XVER-303","XVER","vincenzo.rinella@bolt.eu","Vincenzo Aglieri Rinella","[~accountid:62a9857bd0132d0068809cdd] no hour assigned","2026-01-13T15:11:54.006Z"],["3807561","PFI-832978","PFI","tomas.matijoska@bolt-outsource.eu","Tomas Matijoška","[^payment-1.pdf]","2026-01-13T15:12:46.583Z"],["3807562","PFI-832564","PFI","grigoria.papageorgiou@bolt.eu","Grigoria Papageorgiou","[~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] Driver is also reporting a missing 90 EUR. Is this something you can look into, or point me towards the correct escalation?","2026-01-13T15:13:30.755Z"],["3807563","SCM-1116","SCM","kaarel.vandler@bolt.eu","Kaarel Vandler","Work in progress\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1bemO9iJfEklS9VzF1kaAwpjG_ShgGxT376bKGAXtB70/edit?pli=1&gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1bemO9iJfEklS9VzF1kaAwpjG_ShgGxT376bKGAXtB70/edit?pli=1&gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T15:13:30.790Z"],["3807564","DCOR-132","DCOR","anna.aalberg@bolt.eu","Anna-Lota Aalberg","Legal & Privacy are complete. Following a meeting with Billing & Controlling, we decided to *put the initiative on hold* until we can define a stronger product & ops-led approach. Targeting *Q3 2026*, we’ll restart discussions to agree on any required developments and initiate a new MVRA stream. In the meantime, Billing will focus on strengthening the core capabilities needed to support courier debt collection, so the eventual solution is sustainable and business-positive rather than a manual, ad-hoc process involving several stakeholders.","2026-01-13T15:14:24.756Z"],["3807565","CCM-22274","CCM","miroslava.solarova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Solárová","Hello Andreea,\n\nThe agents have been enrolled in the requested onboarding course. \n\nHave a lovely rest of your day! \n\nMirka 🙂 ","2026-01-13T15:14:26.024Z"],["3807566","TAXP-790","TAXP","tung.lok@bolt.eu","Zip Lok","Hi [~accountid:61b9ad7c2900b00071da0b68], Pillar 2 declaration is submitted and approved today.  EY will share the submission copy shortly.  I will save the correspondences here: [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1mpQ2MdCET0fO-_IA6XoHHiUYaZdJomDK?usp=share_link|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1mpQ2MdCET0fO-_IA6XoHHiUYaZdJomDK?usp=share_link|smart-link].  Thank you.","2026-01-13T15:14:35.177Z"],["3807567","MTE-1257","MTE","raman.nikitsenka@bolt.eu","Raman Nikitsenka",">This needs a specific language list. At the moment the provided language list is the following (in the future some adjustments may happen):\n\n[~accountid:712020:0b749a8a-fe6a-4f53-837a-a79e10d19db5] as discussed in [the thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09B98XMHHR/p1768307121089389], let’s try to stabilize the language list as mush as possible from the beginning, because later before implementing [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MTE-1335|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MTE-1335|smart-link] , it won’t be possible to add new ones","2026-01-13T15:15:56.995Z"],["3807568","RDS-991","RDS","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","[~accountid:712020:13244152-55c1-46c5-a6f1-86ca2de2c01c] maybe worth archiving and creating more specific tickets instead. This was very much a placeholder for discovery, back when we knew, that we know nothing 😄 Of course let me know if you have questions on the content in the doc above! Here for handover/onboarding. ","2026-01-13T15:16:09.119Z"],["3807569","PFI-832980","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T15:16:32.885Z"],["3807570","LSS-61489","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed agreements attached.\n\n[^Social media influencer agreement - Robert Ștefănescu_Bolt Services RO S.R.L._LYONESS MEDIA SERVICES S.R.L._07.02.25.pdf]\n[^Social media influencer agreement - David Ioan_Bolt Services RO S.R.L._NIT MEDIA S.R.L._15.01.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T15:17:36.603Z"],["3807572","RS-1942","RS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Thank you, I asked for those things (using the template from KB).","2026-01-13T15:19:46.820Z"],["3807573","LSS-61516","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey, [~accountid:603cb85ec58c720071175949], thank you for the ticket.\nUnfortunately, the link does not work for me. \nCould you please provide official claim made by driver and also all communication related to this matter between Bolt and the driver? \nThanks! ","2026-01-13T15:20:00.470Z"],["3807574","PFI-832983","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T15:20:14.993Z"],["3807577","LSS-60199","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342325?blocked=true&returnTo=%2Fcontracts%2Fv2&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342325?blocked=true&returnTo=%2Fcontracts%2Fv2&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T15:21:33.567Z"],["3807578","PFI-829664","PFI","diogo.pedrollo@bolt-outsource.eu","Diogo Klinghor Pedrollo","Hey [~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56], we checked and the eaters can’t download the delivery invoice via app following the instructions above. \n\n","2026-01-13T15:21:41.847Z"],["3807579","LSS-61085","LSS","maksym.goncharuk@bolt.eu","Maksym Goncharuk","Hi [~accountid:62a3287576c0360069f59b72] do we need to take any other actions to assist you with the ticket?\n\n","2026-01-13T15:21:58.961Z"],["3807580","LSS-60557","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Kindly also share phone number for delivery to *_Eryk Połeć_* since we are using DHL for delivery. Thank You!","2026-01-13T15:23:42.462Z"],["3807582","LSS-61343","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342327|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342327|smart-link]  ","2026-01-13T15:24:31.633Z"],["3807583","HS-28916","HS","rubendaniel.carvalhomagalhaes@bolt.eu","Ruben Magalhaes","[^casa 5.pdf]","2026-01-13T15:24:38.492Z"],["3807584","PFI-832470","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, update the account to the correct value; I believe Local Team has permissions to do so.","2026-01-13T15:25:34.527Z"],["3807585","DISC-3726","DISC","bertalan.vad@bolt.eu","Bertalan Vad","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/food-delivery-eater-app/pull/8741|https://github.com/bolteu/food-delivery-eater-app/pull/8741]","2026-01-13T15:27:25.984Z"],["3807586","WEB-9593","WEB","samuel.oyekeye@bolt.eu","Samuel Oluseyi Oyekeye","[~accountid:63874527f6c85b343c0b7f4b] the title has 61 characters and of course our validation is set to 60 max 😄 just a little tweak will do","2026-01-13T15:28:00.390Z"],["3807587","PFI-832924","PFI","jana.jilkova@bolt-outsource.eu","Jana Jilkova","Hello [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] , \n\nThank you so much for the quick response, and for the advice. \n\nI am wishing you a pleasant rest of the day,\nJana. ","2026-01-13T15:28:08.903Z"],["3807589","LSS-60556","LSS","jiri.maixner@bolt.eu","Jiří Maixner","[~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] reason of sale is just we dont want this car in fleet anymore - it was “special” one and we decided to sell it and yes it was sold to andrea cos she wanted\n\n- approved by [~accountid:712020:4a020e03-91ec-4656-9308-5b9b6428f675] \n\n","2026-01-13T15:28:28.869Z"],["3807592","LSS-61296","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (13.01)*+\n\n* Response to the complainant: [LINK|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jPCcOZhTCJdoKWdRrOAmbiMubTYxgm_WEotBmtePeQA/edit?tab=t.0]\n* Response to AKI: [LINK|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IfIn7WtwWZvyt-Y-6TdcXyIrw5hAGJCfH3F3CiH6hQA/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-13T15:29:16.423Z"],["3807593","LSS-61519","LSS","liam.james@bolt.eu","Liam James","[^MSA_Uppforandekod_Leverantorer_Engelska_2025.pdf] _(5.99 MB)_","2026-01-13T15:30:01.204Z"],["3807595","LSS-61519","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T15:31:12.378Z"],["3807596","WFM-9953","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","*Driver Auto-processing fallbacks via BH - Agen* role rejected\n\npending request: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571712|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571712]","2026-01-13T15:31:14.586Z"],["3807597","PC-4933","PC","pavel.melnikau@bolt.eu","Pavel Melnikau","For now the error code was mapped to permanent error and new task created to analyze if it’s reasonable to introduce new code for abandoned payments [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PC-4934|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PC-4934|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T15:31:17.532Z"],["3807598","PFI-832267","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hi! They cannot cashout because the payouts are disabled. I don't see the reasons why, but if everything is fine and no restrictions in your side, you can enable the payouts back by going to the partner profile, billing section, payout disabled: NO.","2026-01-13T15:31:19.052Z"],["3807599","LSS-61496","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5], thank you for raising this ticket with the Legal team. Confirming that I will pick this one up and get back to you soon.","2026-01-13T15:31:20.268Z"],["3807600","IDC-1497","IDC","marina.gaponova@bolt.eu","Maryna Gaponova","As discussed in [thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C093W0QFX1S/p1768309815512749?thread_ts=1765370758.365009&cid=C093W0QFX1S]\n\nEvery entry in {{food_discount_indices}} will point to that specific entry in the {{ProviderDiscountDescription}},without additional changes in merge/properties logic. So no need in this merge task anymore","2026-01-13T15:31:31.150Z"],["3807601","LSS-60989","LSS","petr.kratky@bolt.eu","Petr Krátký","amazing! Thank you","2026-01-13T15:31:39.631Z"],["3807602","LEG-1356","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03]! This one seems to be purely Delivery related, so assigning this to you but let me know if I got this wrong. ","2026-01-13T15:32:10.329Z"],["3807603","LSS-61519","LSS","liam.james@bolt.eu","Liam James","[^ESG Questionnaire - Bolt Technology OÜ 2024-05-22.docx]\n\n","2026-01-13T15:32:32.267Z"],["3807605","LEG-1357","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03]! Seems to be purely Delivery-related, hence, assigning this one to you. ","2026-01-13T15:32:50.848Z"],["3807606","SREC-372","SREC","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","*group-S073WHTJAH1* I noticed in AWS Inspector that *2 VPN* instances and *PKI* ec2 have *critical security vulnerabilities* detected, PTAL\nP.S. Inspector is in security account, [link|https://eu-central-1.console.aws.amazon.com/inspector/v2/home?region=eu-central-1#/findings/instance].","2026-01-13T15:33:00.220Z"],["3807607","SREC-372","SREC",null,"Slack","[Amin Khoshnood|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:782f9535-5dfc-41e5-8bdf-057eef89f6ef] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GDK93KKT8/p1768304458217429?thread_ts=1768304458.217429&cid=GDK93KKT8|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GDK93KKT8/p1768304458217429?thread_ts=1768304458.217429&cid=GDK93KKT8|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-13T15:33:01.504Z"],["3807609","SREC-372","SREC","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Considering vulnerability is in kernel, probably reboot will help.\n\n{noformat}CVE-2024-47685 - linux-image-aws{noformat}","2026-01-13T15:33:01.890Z"],["3807610","LEG-1352","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03]! Seems to be purely Delivery-related, hence, assigning this one to you. ","2026-01-13T15:33:08.799Z"],["3807611","LEG-1355","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03]! Seems to be purely Delivery-related, hence, assigning this one to you. ","2026-01-13T15:33:24.675Z"],["3807612","LSS-61417","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:1d5cdb11-f6a1-4354-9cfb-27fd32cf4daa] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^11 Complete_with_Docusign_Authorised_Signatory_ copy.pdf]\n\n [^Complete_with_Docusign_Authorised_Signatory_.pdf] \n\n\n\n[^Bolt Holdings - CLAOGB2LGOL v2.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T15:33:38.336Z"],["3807613","LSS-61520","LSS","angelika.kaleta@bolt.eu","Angelika Kaleta","[^PDF - podpis.pdf] _(153 kB)_","2026-01-13T15:33:45.993Z"],["3807614","LEG-1351","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03]! Seems to be purely Delivery-related, hence, assigning this one to you. ","2026-01-13T15:33:53.559Z"],["3807615","LEG-1353","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03]! Seems to be purely Delivery-related, hence, assigning this one to you. ","2026-01-13T15:34:11.604Z"],["3807616","LSS-60557","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","[~accountid:712020:5edd7b8a-e535-468c-85fd-63f0b6de01b2] could you ask them for phone number, please?","2026-01-13T15:35:10.466Z"],["3807617","XVER-310","XVER","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:62a9857bd0132d0068809cdd]! Can you please confirm this project is related to the Delivery vertical only? If this is the case, I will need to dedicate another team member to handle this. ","2026-01-13T15:35:49.142Z"],["3807620","LEG-1354","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03]! Seems to be purely Delivery-related, hence, assigning this one to you. ","2026-01-13T15:36:38.893Z"],["3807622","FRAUDOPS-1014","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","Some conclusions on the markings: [https://github.com/bolteu/databricks-profiling-queries/blob/main/order_fraud/get_order_fraud_driver_bad_payment.sql|https://github.com/bolteu/databricks-profiling-queries/blob/main/order_fraud/get_order_fraud_driver_bad_payment.sql] \n\n||Rule||Primary Signal||Volume / Ratio Condition||Supporting Signals||\n|Rule 1|Bad order concentration|≥ 40% bad orders|None|\n|Rule 2|High loss share|≥ 60% bad amount|Avg distance ≤ 1000|\n|Rule 3|High loss + repetition|≥ 50% bad amount OR ≥ 40% + >3 orders|Distance ≤ 500 OR card age ≤ 7|\n|Rule 4|New cards + short trips|≥ 20% bad orders OR ≥ 20% bad amount|Distance ≤ 500 AND card age ≤ 7|\n|Rule 5|Consistent moderate abuse|≥ 25% bad orders AND ≥ 25% bad amount|Distance ≤ 1000 OR card age ≤ 7|\n|Rule 6|Foreign card dominance|≥ 69% foreign bad orders and ≥ 3 orders|Distance ≤ 1000 OR card age ≤ 7|\n\nh1. Break-down of the profiling\n\nCore conditions & filters for *ORDER BEING MARKED*\n\n* etl.order_type = 'rides'\n* etl.order_state = 'finished'\n* etl.payment_method_group = 'in-app'\n* etl.created >= DATEADD(day, -30, CURRENT_DATE)\n* ot.state = 'finished' \n* ot.retry_to_try IS NULL\n* *etl.is_payment_problem* OR *etl.is_initial_chargeback* OR *etl.is_current_failed_payment*\n\n----\n\nIncluded drivers are based on filters. Not all drivers are included. Past *30 days* of orders are inspected. \n\n*There is an odd sub-condition:* \n\n{noformat}(bad_payment_count >= 2 AND bad_payment_ratio >= 0.40) \nOR bad_payment_count >= 4{noformat}\n\n{color:#bf2600}*AND*  {color}\n\n{noformat}bad_payment_amount >= 10{noformat}\n\n{color:#bf2600}*AND* {color}:red_arrow: 🚩 \n\n{noformat}(\n  (\n    bad_payment_ratio >= 0.10\n    OR \n    bad_payment_amount_ratio >= 0.20\n  )\n  OR\n  (\n    bad_payment_ratio >= 0.20\n    OR \n    foreign_bad_payment_ratio >= 0.50\n  )\n){noformat}\n\n{color:#bf2600}*AND*{color} *one of more of the RULE conditions:* \n\nRule 1: \n\n{noformat} bad_payment_ratio >= 0.40{noformat}\n\nRule 2: \n\n{noformat}  bad_payment_amount_ratio >= 0.60\nAND \n  avg_bad_payment_distance <= 1000{noformat}\n\nRule 3:\n\n{noformat}    (\n      bad_payment_amount_ratio >= 0.50\n      OR\n      (\n        bad_payment_amount_ratio >= 0.40\n        AND \n        bad_payment_count > 3\n      )\n    )\nAND\n    (\n      avg_bad_payment_distance <= 500\n      OR \n      avg_bad_payment_card_age <= 7\n    ){noformat}\n\nRule 4: \n\n{noformat}  avg_bad_payment_distance <= 500\n  AND \n  avg_bad_payment_card_age <= 7\n  AND\n    (\n      bad_payment_ratio >= 0.20\n      OR \n      bad_payment_amount_ratio >= 0.20\n    ){noformat}\n\nRule 5: \n\n{noformat}  bad_payment_ratio >= 0.25\n  AND \n  bad_payment_amount_ratio >= 0.25\n  AND\n    (\n      avg_bad_payment_distance <= 1000\n      OR \n      avg_bad_payment_card_age <= 7\n    ){noformat}\n\nRule 6: \n\n{noformat}  foreign_bad_payment_ratio >= 0.69\n  AND \n  foreign_bad_payment_count >= 3\n  AND\n    (\n      avg_bad_payment_distance <= 1000\n      OR \n      avg_bad_payment_card_age <= 7\n    ){noformat}\n\n*Rules*\n\n{noformat}\n(\n                                (COUNT(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN k.order_id ELSE NULL END) * 1.00 /\n                                NULLIF(COUNT(k.order_id), 0)      >= 0.4)\n                                --RULE_1\n                                OR (SUM(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN k.amount_eur ELSE NULL END) * 1.00 /\n                                NULLIF(SUM(k.amount_eur), 0)     >= 0.6 AND AVG(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN CAST(k.distance AS double) ELSE NULL END)     <= 1000)\n                                --RULE_2\n                                OR (\n                                    (\n                                        SUM(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN k.amount_eur ELSE NULL END) * 1.00 /\n                                NULLIF(SUM(k.amount_eur), 0)     >= 0.5\n                                        OR (SUM(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN k.amount_eur ELSE NULL END) * 1.00 /\n                                NULLIF(SUM(k.amount_eur), 0)     >= 0.4 AND COUNT(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN k.order_id ELSE NULL END) > 3)\n                                    )\n                                    AND (AVG(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN CAST(k.distance AS double) ELSE NULL END)     <= 500 OR AVG(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN CAST(k.card_age AS bigint) ELSE NULL END)   <= 7)\n                                )\n                                --RULE_3\n                                OR (\n                                    AVG(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN CAST(k.distance AS double) ELSE NULL END)     <= 500\n                                    AND AVG(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN CAST(k.card_age AS bigint) ELSE NULL END)   <= 7\n                                    AND (COUNT(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN k.order_id ELSE NULL END) * 1.00 /\n                                NULLIF(COUNT(k.order_id), 0)      >= 0.2 OR SUM(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN k.amount_eur ELSE NULL END) * 1.00 /\n                                NULLIF(SUM(k.amount_eur), 0)     >= 0.2)\n                                )\n                                --RULE_4\n                                OR (\n                                    COUNT(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN k.order_id ELSE NULL END) * 1.00 /\n                                NULLIF(COUNT(k.order_id), 0)      >= 0.25\n                                    AND SUM(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN k.amount_eur ELSE NULL END) * 1.00 /\n                                NULLIF(SUM(k.amount_eur), 0)     >= 0.25\n                                    AND (AVG(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN CAST(k.distance AS double) ELSE NULL END)     <= 1000 OR AVG(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN CAST(k.card_age AS bigint) ELSE NULL END)   <= 7)\n                                )\n                                --RULE_5\n                                OR (\n                                    COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN foreign_card = 1 AND k.bad_payment_order = 1\n                                THEN k.order_id ELSE NULL END) * 1.00 /\n                                NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN k.order_id ELSE NULL END), 0) >= 0.69\n                                    AND COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN foreign_card = 1 AND k.bad_payment_order = 1\n                                THEN k.order_id ELSE NULL END) >= 3\n                                    AND (AVG(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN CAST(k.distance AS double) ELSE NULL END)     <= 1000 OR AVG(CASE WHEN k.bad_payment_order = 1 THEN CAST(k.card_age AS bigint) ELSE NULL END)   <= 7))\n                                )\n                                --RULE 6{noformat}\n\nIn conclusion, included are partner with activities in the following: \n\n* AVG distance of bad payment rides\n* AVG card age of bad payment rides\n* RATIO SUM of earnings from bad payment rides\n* RATIO COUNT of bad payment rides\n* RATIO COUNT of foreign-card bad payment rides\n* COUNT of bad payment rides\n* SUM of bad payment rides","2026-01-13T15:37:43.828Z"],["3807624","WFM-9952","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","Rides - UK Compliance Agent (210558) role rejected by its owner. the rest added","2026-01-13T15:38:08.681Z"],["3807627","WD-22540","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:712020:4031005b-be5e-413a-b7da-919304795012] !\n\nIn fact new rule has Supplier worktag and the old one did not have any \n\nNew rule\n\n!image-20260113-153636.png|width=1423,alt=\"image-20260113-153636.png\"!\n\nOld rule \n\n!image-20260113-153658.png|width=1404,alt=\"image-20260113-153658.png\"!\n\nSo when you filtered by worktag you saw posting made by new rule. As I mentioned earlier , when you applier new rule WD made reverse posting (without wortag) of revaluation result made by old rule and add new  posting with worktag. \n\nYou can check revaluation posting you did in Nov 2025 (when old rule was used). The posting does not have any Supplier worktag [https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/10498$16787/rel-task/2997$6675.htmld|https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/10498$16787/rel-task/2997$6675.htmld]\n\n!image-20260113-153927.png|width=1404,alt=\"image-20260113-153927.png\"!","2026-01-13T15:40:22.844Z"],["3807628","LSS-61514","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi Aleksei, many thanks for the ticket!\nWhile we review the Google Maps ToS & policies and any applicable agreements we have between ourselves and Google in this regard, could you let me know if you’re aware of any:\n\n#  Specific Google Maps agreement or addendum signed that affects logo visibility? \n#  warnings, feedback, or review comments from Google related to attribution or logo usage in this flow or elsewhere?\n# Also, has this pattern ever been flagged or reviewed before (internally)? \n\nThank you in advance!\n\nVeera","2026-01-13T15:42:08.374Z"],["3807629","LSS-61315","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^20260113121407_001 (1aa5839c-848d-46a5-b2b1-e2e86253c06d).pdf] \n\nThere is a passport copy:\n\n[^Ahto Passport 10.09.25 (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T15:42:09.813Z"],["3807631","LSS-61241","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41] and [~accountid:5b7bea09d08e47445d6fd01e]. Thank you for the clarifications. I just have one further question.\n\nIn one of the emails below it is mentioned the occurence of an accident with injuries/structural damages.\n\nCould you please inform if there was ever any communication with the driver regarding this specific incident, or any other of the safety issues that were verified? Thank you","2026-01-13T15:43:57.878Z"],["3807632","L10N-27581","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:06.863Z"],["3807633","L10N-27573","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:06.884Z"],["3807634","L10N-27570","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:06.898Z"],["3807635","L10N-27571","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:06.931Z"],["3807636","L10N-27567","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:06.934Z"],["3807637","L10N-27577","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.014Z"],["3807638","L10N-27583","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.102Z"],["3807639","L10N-27580","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.109Z"],["3807640","L10N-27566","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.102Z"],["3807641","L10N-27575","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.102Z"],["3807642","L10N-27578","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.140Z"],["3807643","L10N-27576","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.153Z"],["3807644","L10N-27582","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.177Z"],["3807645","L10N-27579","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.172Z"],["3807646","L10N-27568","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.214Z"],["3807647","L10N-27569","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.237Z"],["3807648","L10N-27572","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.253Z"],["3807649","L10N-27584","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:07.291Z"],["3807650","L10N-27585","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:09.282Z"],["3807651","L10N-27574","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:09.339Z"],["3807652","L10N-27565","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:10.499Z"],["3807653","L10N-27562","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:10.798Z"],["3807654","L10N-27564","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:11.938Z"],["3807655","L10N-27563","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.018Z"],["3807656","L10N-27553","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.069Z"],["3807657","L10N-27554","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.080Z"],["3807659","L10N-27556","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.167Z"],["3807660","L10N-27560","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.262Z"],["3807661","L10N-27555","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.222Z"],["3807662","L10N-27561","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.273Z"],["3807663","L10N-27552","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.332Z"],["3807664","L10N-27557","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.457Z"],["3807665","L10N-27551","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.516Z"],["3807666","L10N-27558","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.536Z"],["3807667","L10N-27559","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.664Z"],["3807668","L10N-27550","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T15:44:12.721Z"],["3807669","PFI-832990","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T15:45:46.369Z"],["3807673","RDS-607","RDS","vivekkumar.singh@bolt.eu","Vivek Kumar Singh","Hi [~accountid:712020:13244152-55c1-46c5-a6f1-86ca2de2c01c] I have listed out the updated requirements for the topic in this ticket [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/INT-457|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/INT-457|smart-link]  - but happy to discuss it in a call.","2026-01-13T15:46:52.311Z"],["3807674","LSS-60556","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","[~accountid:712020:cc83342e-0406-4e66-8201-8b0cd5b64c98] thank you. If the car was “special”, why it was bought in the first place? Would you consider the price to correspond to the market prices for this type of car?","2026-01-13T15:47:17.469Z"],["3807676","EBIKE1-392","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Protruding sheet metal tips enhance usability, compared to the off-the-shelf product, allowing users to better support the kickstand when folding it down.\n\nThis feature is useful since half of the stand remains hidden when folded on the Cruiser.\n\nThe maximum width of the stand for the e-bike is 250mm to prevent it from hitting users' heels while pdaling.\n\n30mm tire clearance has been taken over from Okai EB100.\n\nFor the next:\n\n# Install the kickstand to the e-bike and ride it to ensure the tips of the legs do not touch the heels.\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"7d53cfc8-248c-4aba-9f19-7a52ad571276\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"3D scan of LY`s off-the-shelf kickstand\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"3D model based on the 3D scan\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":5},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Kustomised kickstand spec\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Tire clearance:\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Around 30mm\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Leg angle: 13deg\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Kickstand H: 245mm\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Legs W: 250mm\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":4},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":226,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260113-143343.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260113-143343.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":640,\"width\":640}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":221,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260113-154719.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260113-154719.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":649,\"width\":649}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":221,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260113-154003.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260113-154003.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":684,\"width\":684}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":221,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260113-154141.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260113-154141.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":693,\"width\":693}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":140,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"1ea2bfae1d6de8096847036b13ed6fbd-20260113-154913.jpg\",\"alt\":\"1ea2bfae1d6de8096847036b13ed6fbd-20260113-154913.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":118,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"9bc0361926595268043977fbc13189ae-20260113-154920.jpg\",\"alt\":\"9bc0361926595268043977fbc13189ae-20260113-154920.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":118,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"9bc0361926595268043977fbc13189ae-20260113-154959.jpg\",\"alt\":\"9bc0361926595268043977fbc13189ae-20260113-154959.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":101,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"4dde4b98510190e8fcd8af1d37de2a25-20260113-155011.jpg\",\"alt\":\"4dde4b98510190e8fcd8af1d37de2a25-20260113-155011.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-13T15:47:36.870Z"],["3807678","UXROPS-112","UXROPS","alisa.kamnerov@bolt.eu","Alisa Kamnerov","About \"be a courier\" from [@marcell.antolik|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/UJGPALA1G]\n\n* I'm planning to pick up be a courier in the beginning of Q2, once we have the most pressing launched done from Q1\n* In the meantime, in Feb/March, I'll do some preliminary work with Legal and Billing teams to ensure we have a clear process and green light from both","2026-01-13T15:48:18.778Z"],["3807680","LSS-61509","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:637f4716de5cdaba3a67c532] ! \n\nHere is the contract: [^Bolt UGC Alina contract.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-13T15:49:16.068Z"],["3807685","LSS-61500","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:1d600e3f-d3ca-4f4e-b8af-f6c7510bb923] have changes been applied to the template? ","2026-01-13T15:50:16.209Z"],["3807686","LSS-61231","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","+Update from Partner (provided by Asher) - 13.01.2026+:\n\n\n\n!image.png|width=1332,alt=\"image.png\"!","2026-01-13T15:50:38.802Z"],["3807687","LSS-57542","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached. \n\n[^(External) LOI_Stella_Sweden.docx (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T15:51:13.860Z"],["3807688","LSS-61500","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] thanks! Let me check, I dont think so ","2026-01-13T15:51:13.407Z"],["3807690","LSS-61104","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:289d7ba0-a9c0-4cbb-82d4-a9ed8c05aeab] and [~accountid:712020:1e9398f2-efcd-4dcd-8ece-28e6f8578e37] ,\n\nFollowing our meeting, WDYT about the following response?\n\n\n\n_“Dear Mr Spiteri,_\n\n_Thank you for your email and for sharing the supporting materials._\n\n_Bolt takes passenger safety and service standards seriously._ \n\n_Having reviewed our internal support records for the complainant, we confirm that the two mentioned complaints were not escalated and handled in line with our internal protocols at the time. We apologize to the complainant for this shortcoming and for the inconvenience caused._\n\n_We also have taken corrective steps internally to ensure this does not repeat, including:_\n\n* _reinforcing the correct escalation path for safety/behavior complaints;_\n* _reminding the responsible support teams of the required handling standards and documentation of outcomes;_\n* _implementing additional internal checks to ensure similar complaints are promptly identified and routed for appropriate action._\n\n_We trust the above addresses your concerns regarding our handling of the matter. Please let us know if you require any additional information from our side._\n\n_Kind regards,”_","2026-01-13T15:52:06.895Z"],["3807691","FRAUDOPS-1014","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","So to shortly state: \n\nin order for the order to be marked, the *driver has to qualify* based on their past month volume -> then all orders satisfying base conditions are marked 🔴 \n\n✔ *Driver qualification is based on past-month (rolling 30-day) volume*\n\n* Counts, ratios, amounts, distances, card age, and foreign-card share\n* All computed over the same 30-day window\n\n✔ *Qualification happens first, then orders are marked*\n\n* The driver either qualifies or not\n* Order marking depends on that result\n\n✔ *Qualification can be triggered by activity anywhere in the 30-day window*\n\n* Including activity that occurred _after_ the order being marked\n\n!IMG_9095.heic|width=409,alt=\"IMG_9095.heic\"!","2026-01-13T15:52:19.608Z"],["3807693","PAW-14846","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @daysleeperx\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160603\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 15:52:40 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T15:52:40.642Z"],["3807694","LSS-61231","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:262f6569-8615-451c-9647-ce9929ef2eb6], \n\nPlease find attached the final agreement in pdf format ready for signature. \n\nIf the partner prefers to sign the agreement through their e-signature system, this could be accepted (even though it is non standard and it will be slower on our side). \n\nThe signatory details for Bolt: \n- Ahto Kink, [ahto.kink@bolt.eu|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu]\n- in cc. [signing@bolt.eu|mailto:signing@bolt.eu]\n\n\n\nPlease let me know if the partner needs anything else to issue the NDA for signature, and kindly confirm when the partner sends the agreement so that I can inform the legal ops team.\n\n[^Bolt NDA (Non-disclosure agreement)_VFIN.pdf]  ","2026-01-13T15:53:14.320Z"],["3807695","LSS-58451","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:c428e4fe-c7e8-428c-98b9-afce638acb45] no all good, we can collect signatures here if you please provide the latest Agreement and email and name of the counterparty!","2026-01-13T15:53:38.575Z"],["3807697","HS-28837","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Visa letter has been sent to signing","2026-01-13T15:54:12.105Z"],["3807698","DMB-1705","DMB","rachit.dua@bolt.eu","Rachit Dua","There’s a new error which popped up since new analytics package. Since dev-dependencies/peer-dependencies have changed in the package, we need to update our dependencies as well.","2026-01-13T15:54:17.176Z"],["3807699","DRAG101-427","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","DC has initiated a remake of the QR code screw hole.\n\nThe mold has been changed, and new parts have been produced.\n\n[~accountid:60b9e4f58cf91900699878ec] conducted the QR fitment test in China.\n\n[~accountid:5e46575fc8ec310c955b0d4a] conducted re-test in Estonia.\n\n[~accountid:5e46575fc8ec310c955b0d4a] updated the 3D and 2D drawings to reflect the modifications made by DC.\n\nUpdated 3D and 2D have been added to the BOM.\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"d2190f39-ada8-4a6f-993b-24523a69a8d3\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Old\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"New\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"New, the one initiated by DC, results in tilted screw\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":110,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260113-135535.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260113-135535.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":324,\"width\":324}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":195,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260113-135026.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260113-135026.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":376,\"width\":376}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":195,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"d00cb5421c9145013b421d7f761438c1-20260113-135108.jpg\",\"alt\":\"d00cb5421c9145013b421d7f761438c1-20260113-135108.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":195,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"b1de1bb94fe38090924d6a8e3677ebc2-20260113-135127.jpg\",\"alt\":\"b1de1bb94fe38090924d6a8e3677ebc2-20260113-135127.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":142,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"b8950999b567505ad82b6e1c29bb8f0c-20260113-135135.jpg\",\"alt\":\"b8950999b567505ad82b6e1c29bb8f0c-20260113-135135.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-13T15:54:50.334Z"],["3807701","TAXP-2279","TAXP","tung.lok@bolt.eu","Zip Lok","Hi [~accountid:712020:3c92a0f8-cf5a-446c-a2f4-4f4460994d1b], no significant updates on my countries but I’d like to include also Philippines and Vietnam in “New in 2025” as there are intracompany transactions and support payments transaction.  Both are non-operational countries.  Do you agree?","2026-01-13T15:55:29.319Z"],["3807702","LSS-60177","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","Hi [~accountid:6169660ebfa2c1006b56c18f] could you provide mw with the contract please? Also what service are they providing for us?\n","2026-01-13T15:56:13.024Z"],["3807703","LSS-60177","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu"," [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] could you advise on the next steps, once we received this information by Marc, thanks!","2026-01-13T15:56:22.909Z"],["3807704","RCE-348","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768319777946379]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@oliver.hilsky>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-348] `Generate api for fleet-documents service` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-13T15:56:32.805Z"],["3807706","PC-4919","PC","rushang.chauhan@bolt.eu","Rushang Chauhan","I reviewed the [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0754PSUQ9X|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0754PSUQ9X|smart-link]  and found fewer than 15 alerts related to the new country-based circuit breaker over an 11-day period (17th to 27th December).\n\nSince this implementation hasn’t resulted in a spike in alerts or shown any consistent pattern, I recommend keeping the current configuration as is and continuing to observe it for some time before making any changes to the circuit breaker.\n\n\n\nCC: [~accountid:61de8e0e7c6f980070b38d2b] [~accountid:62a98578979e6e0069055c5a] ","2026-01-13T15:57:54.293Z"],["3807709","LSS-57645","LSS","manuel.sanz@bolt.eu","Manuel Gil Sanz","Hi [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] ,\n\nDid we finally sign the contract? Can you please share with me so I can pass it to the airport?\n\nThanks!","2026-01-13T15:58:41.833Z"],["3807710","LSS-59767","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:5de3bf86-6cba-4bd9-b71a-087b2b4da2eb] is any of that data in the sheet valuable for us? If yes, we should include it in the scope within the NDA!","2026-01-13T15:59:01.973Z"],["3807712","PFI-833004","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-13T15:59:53.015Z"],["3807713","LSS-60177","LSS","marc.naether@bolt.eu","Marc Naether","[~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] there has been some progress since, it could be that the issue is already resolved (at least Gaiyo claims that the sums have actually been paid).\n[~accountid:63dba2fb1b13d42998e22e00] could you maybe give an update here on where this stands, and if we need to take this further legally, or if it is solved by now?","2026-01-13T16:00:11.211Z"],["3807714","LSS-60177","LSS","marc.naether@bolt.eu","Marc Naether","Gaiyo is a MaaS app","2026-01-13T16:00:31.913Z"],["3807715","LSS-61241","LSS","joao.ramos@bolt.eu","João Nuno Ferreira Ramos","He was warned via email several times, as you can see in the attachment. \n\nAdding to this, he replied to one of the emails, starting an interaction with CS : \n\n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/573150089|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/573150089]\n\nPlus, he was warned several times about his behaviour and interacted with in other occasions: \n\n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/556115084|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/556115084]\n\n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/530835569|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/530835569]\n\n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/557971316|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/557971316]","2026-01-13T16:00:33.223Z"],["3807718","LSS-60617","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","Outstanding commercial risks approved by [~accountid:5fc514a09592df00761a5d3d] \n\n@ Legal ops please collect wet ink signatures by Ahto Kink, thank you!","2026-01-13T16:02:25.435Z"],["3807719","LSS-57645","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] - Did we finally sign this contract? Many thanks!","2026-01-13T16:02:33.610Z"],["3807720","LSS-60557","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","+48 790 342 243 ","2026-01-13T16:02:41.988Z"],["3807723","LSS-46087","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:6411c587f1b529dfa98c0e66] I confirm that these are the only law firms I am aware of, thanks!","2026-01-13T16:03:42.796Z"],["3807724","TAXP-2279","TAXP","stefan.chirila@bolt.eu","Stefan Chirila","Hi [~accountid:62ea2a695111209f4fde8265]— yes, I agree. Even if these are non-operational, the intracompany transactions/support payments mean there is economic activity in those jurisdictions, so it makes sense to include them under “New in 2025.","2026-01-13T16:05:17.247Z"],["3807725","LSS-58451","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","@ Legal ops, it would be great if you could collect *wet ink sigantures* by Ahto once Anour uploads the latest Agreement, thank you!\n\n[~accountid:712020:c428e4fe-c7e8-428c-98b9-afce638acb45] please provide the address of the landlord to send them the physical Agreement once signed, thanks!","2026-01-13T16:05:52.337Z"],["3807730","PTWS-2124","PTWS","alexandru.cerveanu@bolt.eu","Alex Cerveanu","Added the new list of Contingent workers type to sandbox via Maintain Contingent Worker Types (to access this task you will need Job and Position Configurator role). The existing roles have not been yet removed: 3PL Mechanics, B2B Contractors, Consultant, Employer of Record, Vendor.\nAlso, as 3PL Mechanics, B2B Contractors have a separate access linked to them, the suggestion is to leave them as they are currently.","2026-01-13T16:07:30.405Z"],["3807733","PIF-2190","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* The draft effectively conveys the main feature update and its purpose, while highlighting the security benefits of implementing an allow list. It follows the requirement to use placeholders for missing links to the component view and guides, ensuring clarity on what needs to be detailed further. Additional information like specific locations or technical references is not available in the ticket and hence appropriately indicated as missing.","2026-01-13T16:08:30.391Z"],["3807735","PIF-2175","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft is appropriate because it succinctly communicates the new feature's availability and its purpose, ensuring all internal stakeholders understand the value it brings to monitoring the Presto client. Information about where to access the dashboard and additional guidance materials is missing, necessitating placeholders.","2026-01-13T16:08:38.304Z"],["3807736","PIF-2174","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft is appropriate as it succinctly communicates the key outcome of adding alerting common rules for the Presto client integration. It highlights the benefit of ensuring prompt notifications about malfunctions, which is critical for developers relying on this integration. However, specifics like where to view this feature and related guides or documentation are missing, so placeholders are used.","2026-01-13T16:08:48.575Z"],["3807737","PIF-2162","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED, ADR_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft effectively communicates the essence of the newly added feature which synchronizes team channels from live to prelive in the Directory. This is important as it reduces redundancy, aligns with chaos testing needs, and potentially simplifies ongoing management. However, specific links to where the feature can be accessed (component admin panel) or further details (guide or ADR) are missing, hence placeholders have been used.","2026-01-13T16:08:58.305Z"],["3807738","PIF-2190","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is well-defined, but the clarity and acceptance criteria could be enhanced with a bit more specificity. Specifically, improving clarity on how an 'opt-in' feature is expected to function operationally and further specifying what would distinguish a successful implementation (e.g., types of misuse prevented, specific modules, or services prioritized) could solidify its clarity and measurable outcomes.","2026-01-13T16:09:16.437Z"],["3807739","PIF-2175","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 8\n• Relevance: 9\n• Problem Definition: 7\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: To improve clarity and problem definition, specify what specific Presto client metrics will be monitored and why they are important. This would help in understanding the business problem and how the dashboard will be beneficial. To enhance acceptance criteria, include specific success metrics or benchmarks that would define the dashboard as effectively tracking the desired metrics, such as reducing the time taken to identify issues or improving system performance analysis.","2026-01-13T16:09:21.338Z"],["3807740","PIF-2174","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 7\n• Relevance: 9\n• Problem Definition: 7\n• Accept: 8\n• Suggested improvements: The user story could benefit from more detail in several areas. The clarity and problem definition lack specifics about what constitutes a 'malfunction' or 'production problems' for the Presto client, which could vary widely in interpretation. It's important to detail the types of issues that require alerts and how they will be identified. The acceptance criteria are quite vague, lacking precision on the conditions under which alerts should trigger, the types of alerts, and their thresholds. For improvement, define these scenarios more explicitly and provide concrete success metrics or benchmarks that could be used to verify the implementation's effectiveness and completeness.","2026-01-13T16:09:28.123Z"],["3807741","GCAP-271","GCAP","hana.rotinsulu@bolt.eu","Hana Rotinsulu","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1aqrN0NDYyEk7hfzZIPEda2ny1zQVSnZh9igTzozzUA0/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1aqrN0NDYyEk7hfzZIPEda2ny1zQVSnZh9igTzozzUA0/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T16:10:23.174Z"],["3807743","LSS-61234","LSS","jack.cook@bolt.eu","Jack Cook","Hi [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] no worries - [~accountid:5c987f2c0cf73c3215ff6aa7] would you or someone in your team be able to assist? These are essentially super detailed AI questions from the EY Infosec team. Thanks! ","2026-01-13T16:11:17.214Z"],["3807744","LSS-61165","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hi, FYI, Safety just came back with the case, Cognito tool is now closed, and they said the insurance claim has been filled and sent to the insurance company. I do not have access to the claim. Lawyer has not been provided any answer since 05.01 as followed : \n\n{quote}Bonjour Maître Colombine,\n\nVeuillez faire preuve de patience, je viens de transmettre ce rapport à l’équipe concernée pour qu’elle vous apporte davantage d’aide.\n\nAmanda, Bolt{quote}\n\n","2026-01-13T16:11:52.315Z"],["3807745","LSS-61165","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d15dd8c0d64020c403ae98c] thank you for raising this ticket ! \n\nPlease could you share some additional info:\n\n* Could you share the email or letter received from the lawyer? \n* Has a ticket for the insurance team been raised before contacting Legal?\n* Is the insurance claim an internal or external process you are referring to? Has Safety completed the claim? \n\nThank you !","2026-01-13T16:13:00.039Z"],["3807749","L10N-27600","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27599](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27599)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T16:13:54.751Z"],["3807750","L10N-27604","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the