laborating!","2026-01-13T16:14:04.814Z"],["3807758","L10N-27624","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27599](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27599)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T16:14:06.247Z"],["3807759","L10N-27625","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27599](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27599)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T16:14:06.768Z"],["3807760","L10N-27628","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27599](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27599)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T16:14:08.020Z"],["3807761","L10N-27635","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27599](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27599)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-13T16:14:10.053Z"],["3807763","DAEN-1268","DAEN","abraham.verhoef@bolt.eu","Bram Verhoef","{code:sql}\nWITH dim_fact_models AS (\n    SELECT\n        m.unique_id           AS model_unique_id\n        , m.name              AS model_name\n        , m.package_name      AS project_name\n        , m.database_name\n        , m.schema_name\n        , m.tags\n        , m.package_name\n    FROM dbt_meta_spark.dbt_models m\n    WHERE(\n        LOWER(m.name) LIKE '%dim%'   -- approx. python regex (dim|fact)\n         OR LOWER(m.name) LIKE '%fact%'\n      )\n    --Note: this filtering should be based on criticality tiers.\n)\n\n\n, tests_scoped AS (\n    SELECT\n        t.unique_id\n        , t.parent_model_unique_id\n        , t.test_column_name\n        , t.test_original_name\n        , t.package_name\n    FROM dbt_meta_spark.dbt_tests t\n)\n\n, model_tests AS (\n    SELECT\n        t.parent_model_unique_id AS model_unique_id\n        , COUNT(*)                  AS test_count\n    FROM tests_scoped t\n    WHERE t.test_column_name IS NULL\n    GROUP BY 1\n)\n\n, column_tests AS (\n    SELECT\n        t.parent_model_unique_id AS model_unique_id\n        , t.test_column_name       AS column_name\n        , COUNT(*)                 AS test_count\n    FROM tests_scoped t\n    WHERE t.test_column_name IS NOT NULL\n    GROUP BY 1,2\n)\n\n, dim_fact_columns AS (\n    SELECT\n        c.parent_unique_id AS model_unique_id,\n        c.name             AS column_name,\n        c.data_type,\n        c.description\n    FROM dbt_meta_spark.dbt_columns c\n    JOIN dim_fact_models m\n      ON m.model_unique_id = c.parent_unique_id\n)\n\nmodel_column_stats AS (\n    SELECT\n        m.model_unique_id\n        , m.model_name\n        , m.project_name\n        , COUNT(DISTINCT c.column_name) AS total_columns\n        , COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN ct.column_name IS NOT NULL THEN c.column_name END) AS tested_columns\n        , CASE\n            WHEN COUNT(DISTINCT c.column_name) = 0 THEN 0.0\n            ELSE\n                COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN ct.column_name IS NOT NULL THEN c.column_name END)\n                / CAST(COUNT(DISTINCT c.column_name) AS DOUBLE)\n        END AS coverage\n    FROM dim_fact_models m\n    LEFT JOIN dim_fact_columns c\n      ON c.model_unique_id = m.model_unique_id\n    LEFT JOIN column_tests ct\n      ON ct.model_unique_id = c.model_unique_id\n     AND ct.column_name      = c.column_name\n    GROUP BY ALL\n)\n\n, models_with_any_column_tests AS (\n    SELECT DISTINCT model_unique_id\n    FROM column_tests\n)\n\n, models_with_any_tests AS (\n    SELECT model_unique_id FROM model_tests\n    UNION\n    SELECT model_unique_id FROM models_with_any_column_tests\n)\n\nproject_level_agg AS (\n    SELECT\n        m.project_name\n        , COUNT(DISTINCT m.model_unique_id) AS total_models\n        , COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN aw.model_unique_id IS NOT NULL THEN m.model_unique_id END) AS models_with_any_test\n        , SUM(ms.total_columns) AS total_columns\n        , SUM(ms.tested_columns) AS total_tested_columns\n    FROM dim_fact_models m\n    LEFT JOIN models_with_any_tests aw\n      ON aw.model_unique_id = m.model_unique_id\n    LEFT JOIN model_column_stats ms\n      ON ms.model_unique_id = m.model_unique_id\n    GROUP BY 1\n)\n\nSELECT\n    project_name\n    , total_models\n    , models_with_any_test\n    , total_tested_columns\n    , total_columns\n    , CASE WHEN total_models = 0 THEN 0.0 ELSE models_with_any_test / CAST(total_models AS DOUBLE) END AS model_coverage\n    , CASE WHEN total_columns = 0 THEN 0.0 ELSE total_tested_columns / CAST(total_columns AS DOUBLE) END AS column_coverage\nFROM project_level_agg{code}","2026-01-13T16:14:43.304Z"],["3807764","DPX-3557","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","QA Notes:\n\n\n\n[~accountid:60950a25539c14006ae92e40]  I applied distribute_feature label to the PR [https://github.com/bolteu/food-delivery-provider-app/pull/3537|https://github.com/bolteu/food-delivery-provider-app/pull/3537]","2026-01-13T16:16:52.703Z"],["3807765","LSS-61165","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thanks [~accountid:712020:dbc22d70-1983-4414-80b3-27f087787ae4] - I drafted my comment before seeing the update you shared. \n\nPlease could you send the lawyer’s emails or letters + the confirmationo of the form filed by Safety?\n\nThank you !","2026-01-13T16:18:32.245Z"],["3807772","PFI-614842","PFI","tuuli.poldma@bolt.eu","Tuuli Põldma","Hi [~accountid:557058:b2aaf2b9-4465-40fe-b31b-1711dbe61946] [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f]  , any feedback? Or you are not the correct contact? Should I make a separate ticket?","2026-01-13T16:20:54.795Z"],["3807774","LSS-56022","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* working draft response letter to court order. Awaiting confirming from Estelle and Ramone (expected tomorrow) and then will be able to finalise and arrange signing of the certificate by Ramone.\n\n[^DRAFT Response Letter to Thorntons Court Order - Bolt Services UK Limited.docx.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T16:21:47.281Z"],["3807776","PIF-2162","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 9\n• Problem Definition: 9\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: Overall, the user story is well-crafted with clear objectives and acceptance criteria. However, slight improvements can be made: 1. Clarity: Specify more about how frequently the data synchronization occurs (e.g., daily) or if it is triggered by a specific event. 2. Relevance: Although the story is relevant, a brief statement on how frequently this syncing issue occurs or its impact on users would underline its importance. 3. Acceptance Criteria: Consider adding measurable outcomes or success metrics. For example, state what 'eventually synced' means in technical terms and outline the steps to verify successful sync. 4. Problem Definition: Provide specific examples of manual efforts required now and the anticipated reduction in workload following implementation to strengthen the rationale further.","2026-01-13T16:22:29.399Z"],["3807781","PAW-14847","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @not-much-io\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160599\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 16:24:41 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T16:24:41.638Z"],["3807782","PTWS-2114","PTWS","alexandru.cerveanu@bolt.eu","Alex Cerveanu","# Access *Create Compensation Rounding Rule* task.\n# Select the *Rounding Option*\n# Rounding Option: *Round up*\n# *Round to Nearest 1*\n# Added the rounding rule to compensation plans (12 month salary plan, ITA 14 Month Salary Plan, Annual Review, Frontliners Annual Review) as of {{2026-01-01}}\n# to add the rule search for compensation plans report, salary plan->edit->add the new rule","2026-01-13T16:27:11.178Z"],["3807783","BIZ-308","BIZ","teresa.rodrigues@bolt.eu","Teresa Cipriano Rodrigues","[~accountid:63dba2fb1b13d42998e22e00] i think i need hours from you here","2026-01-13T16:27:22.006Z"],["3807784","MM-925","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🟡|The issue describes the task and links to a Google Doc, but lacks in-issue acceptance criteria, requirements, and edge cases.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The summary is understandable, but the description could be clearer and more detailed within the issue itself.|\n|Auditability|🟢|The issue links to an external Google Doc for further details.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is provided in the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add acceptance criteria and requirements directly in the issue.\n* Provide a time estimate.\n* Summarize key points from the linked Google Doc in the issue description.","2026-01-13T16:27:30.000Z"],["3807787","LSS-61165","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hey again! This is the summary of the case :\n\n*Lawyer -* 01.12.25, 12:58\n\n{quote}Madame, Monsieur,\n\nJ’ai l’honneur d’intervenir en qualité de conseil de Ekrem KAVAK, propriétaire du véhicule BMW 730D immatriculé 1 NRG 708, endommagé le 24 décembre 2024 à la suite d’un accident impliquant une trottinette électrique exploitée par votre société BOLT, conduite par M. David HUYS, utilisateur dûment identifié au moment des faits.\n\nUn constat amiable d’accident a été dressé le jour même, dont copie est annexée à la présente.\n\nSelon les informations recueillies, BOLT est couverte par une assurance en responsabilité civile pour les dommages causés par les utilisateurs de ses trottinettes. C’est dans ce cadre que j’introduis la présente réclamation pour indemnisation.\n\nL’expertise du véhicule effectuée conclut à un montant de réparation s’élevant à 2 522,62 € hors TVA, soit 3 052,37 € TVA comprise.\n\nÀ ce montant s’ajoutent :\n\nFrais administratifs forfaitaires : 100,00 €, Indemnité pour chômage du véhicule : 30,00 € (1,5 jour à raison de 20 €/jour).\n\nSoit un total dû de : 3 182,37 € (TVA comprise).\n\nPar la présente, je vous mets formellement en demeure de verser la somme totale de 3 182,37 € sur le compte tiers BE48 6301 8503 4027 ouvert à mon nom pour le 10 décembre 2025 au plus tard.\n\nÀ défaut de règlement dans le délai précité, j’ai reçu instruction d’introduire sans autre avertissement une procédure judiciaire en recouvrement des montants dus, augmentés des intérêts légaux et des frais de procédure.\n\nJe vous rappelle que la présente lettre constitue un recouvrement amiable et ne vaut ni saisie, ni assignation.\n\nJe vous prie d’agréer, Madame, Monsieur, l’expression de mes salutations distinguées\n\nColombine Escarmelle{quote}\n\n[^BOLT_assurance_responsabilite_generale.pdf (5e7f17b3-9eb7-4cc0-8425-a6c1edf0dc7c).pdf]\n[^Constat_Kavak.pdf (9cbcb960-ffe0-40ee-bc48-153aef90a3b0).pdf]\n[^FactureBolt100563995.pdf.pdf]\n[^25R41532_00010_Rapport_expertise_rparation.pdf (24607ebf-e9d9-49f6-b34f-80afed730a83).pdf]\n\n*Support -* 01.12.25, 13:07\n\n{quote}Bonjour Colombine,\n\nJe suis Robert de l'équipe sécurité Bolt\n\nJe vous remercie de nous avoir fait part de l'accident de votre client. Vous avez bien fait de nous en informer. Pour une meilleure assistance, je vais effectuer des vérifications et je vous ferai un retour très vite.\n\nMerci pour votre compréhension.\n\nRobert, l'équipe sécurité Bolt{quote}\n\n13:28\n\n{quote}Bonjour Colombine,\n\nC’est Weyinmi du support Bolt. Merci de nous avoir contactés !\n\nPeux-tu nous envoyer une photo du numéro UUID de la trottinette (situé sous le code QR) ? Si le code QR est endommagé, indique le numéro VIN (gravé sur le cadre de la trottinette).\n\nPeux-tu aussi nous préciser l’heure et le lieu de l’incident ainsi que ton numéro de téléphone pour que nous puissions te contacter ?\n\nBien à toi,\n\nWeyinmi{quote}\n\n*Lawyer -* 01.12.25, 13:49\n\n{quote}Madame, Monsieur,\n\nVoici la facture.\n\nLe constat est clair en ce qui concerne l’heure et le lieu.\n\nSentiments distingués.\n\nColombine Escarmelle{quote}\n\n[^FactureBolt100563995.pdf (12f4ea89-ad25-4b0e-86d4-85fe0fdf1ed5).pdf]\n\n*Support -* 01.12.25, 20:24\n\n{quote}J’ai transmis votre dossier à l’équipe concernée pour une enquête plus approfondie. Merci pour votre patience.\n\nCordialement,\n\nWeyinmi{quote}\n\n03.12.25, 16:17\n\n{quote}Bonjour Colombine,\n\nMerci de patienter, j’ai transmis votre signalement à l’équipe concernée pour qu’ils puissent vous aider davantage.\n\nAmanda, Bolt{quote}\n\n08.12.25, 21:42\n\n{quote}Bonjour Colombine,\n\nC'est l'équipe Sécurité de Bolt. J'ai consulté vos messages précédents et je vais poursuivre là où nous en étions restés.\n\nComme nous n'avons pas encore reçu de réponse de votre part, je vais clôturer ce dossier. N'oubliez pas que votre sécurité est notre priorité. N'hésitez pas à nous contacter si vous avez d'autres questions ou préoccupations.\n\nCordialement,\n\nEsther, équipe Sécurité Bolt{quote}\n\n*Lawyer -* 09.12.25, 09:57\n\n{quote}Merci de ne pas m’appeler par mon prénom : je suis avocate et non cliente !!!\n\nColombine Escarmelle{quote}\n\n*Support -* 09.12.25, 10:25\n\n{quote}Bonjour Maître Colombine,\n\nNous comprenons que vous cherchez une indemnisation pour votre client. Chez Bolt, la sécurité est notre priorité et nous avons mis en place plusieurs mesures pour prévenir les blessures, les dommages et les pertes.\n\nIl est important de comprendre que nous ne pouvons pas contrôler toutes les actions de nos utilisateurs ou de tiers lorsqu'ils utilisent nos véhicules électriques, comme un mauvais stationnement, une mauvaise manipulation ou même du vandalisme. Malheureusement, tous les incidents ne peuvent pas être évités.\n\nAprès examen de votre réclamation et des éléments disponibles, nous constatons que la responsabilité directe de Bolt pour les dommages allégués n'a pas été établie. Par conséquent, nous ne pouvons pas nous porter responsables et nous ne sommes pas en mesure d'accéder à votre demande d'indemnisation. Nous vous recommandons de contacter la compagnie d'assurance tiers pour demander une prise en charge des dommages. Bien que nous ne puissions pas aller plus loin dans cette demande spécifique, nous nous excusons pour la gêne occasionnée et espérons que vous comprendrez notre position sur ce dossier.\n\nCordialement,\n\nAmanda, équipe Sécurité Bolt{quote}\n\n*Lawyer -* 05.01.26, 13:41\n\n{quote}Madame,\n\nJ’introduis donc une procédure devant le tribunal, ce qui entraînera inévitablement des frais supplémentaires qui seront mis à votre charge.\n\nSentiments distingués.\n\nColombine Escarmelle{quote}\n\n*Support -* 05.01.26\n\n{quote}Bonjour Maître Colombine,\n\nVeuillez faire preuve de patience, je viens de transmettre ce rapport à l’équipe concernée pour qu’elle vous apporte davantage d’aide.\n\nAmanda, Bolt{quote}\n\n_Here, case is escalated from safety to tier 2, this ticket is opened and the safety workflow is followed again by safety internally. Insurance claim allegedly sent by safety on 06.01.26, 15:32._\n\nYou can access the cognito tool [here|https://www.cognitoforms.com/Taxify1/GlobalEventAssessmentTool2#TXZAb1KzVObFVRJWk7BLxFCybMqiaUU6gyCz-2gQl-k$*] with code S-1085021.\n\nSadly I do not have any info about the form sent by safety, I will query more information about their workflow with the insurance company to understand if we can provide any proof the issue is looked into on the insurance’s side.","2026-01-13T16:28:28.484Z"],["3807788","LSS-60176","LSS","emilie.chesse@bolt.eu","Emilie Chesse","that’s perfect, thanks for your draft assessment [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ! Pls feel free to share with [~accountid:6320602ec7601c8e4abeda47] .\n\nAdding here for records the assessment conducted by Central Legal: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/17RG7YW9p1VTkhsqUy73HmVhnhvRtCY5o/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/17RG7YW9p1VTkhsqUy73HmVhnhvRtCY5o/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T16:29:47.871Z"],["3807789","PFI-819356","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hi Ana, I can see that all of those transactions were properly credited to the IBAN FR7614518292670014644524030. Unfortunately we are not able to recall the funds. The best option would be the partner getting in touch with the IBAN owner to claim back the funds. ","2026-01-13T16:29:55.108Z"],["3807792","MM-926","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🟡|Basic steps are listed, but lacks detailed requirements, edge cases, and acceptance criteria. Most info is in an external doc.|\n|Clarity|🟡|Steps are understandable, but context and details are minimal. Relies on external doc for clarity.|\n|Auditability|🟢|Links to a Google Doc with more information. Source is referenced.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate provided in the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a time estimate to the issue.\n* Summarize key requirements and acceptance criteria from the linked doc directly in the issue for completeness and clarity.","2026-01-13T16:30:07.515Z"],["3807793","MM-927","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|The issue lacks a description, requirements, edge cases, and acceptance criteria.|\n|Clarity|🔴|The summary is brief and lacks context or explanation, making it hard to understand the scope.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting information are provided.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is present on the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Clarify the summary and scope.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-13T16:30:23.977Z"],["3807795","DAEN-1316","DAEN","kevin.sutanto@bolt.eu","Kevin Sutanto","Exploration notebook\n\n[https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2086094145167691?o=3598988355446810#command/7109144182605032|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2086094145167691?o=3598988355446810#command/7109144182605032]","2026-01-13T16:32:34.475Z"],["3807797","LSS-60176","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:6320602ec7601c8e4abeda47] ,\n\nThis feature was assessed by Central Legal and has been classified has *medium risk.*\n\nIn regards to Malta, the short answer is: yes, this type of feature _can_ be deployed in Malta, but the way it’s configured and communicated matters a lot. The biggest risks are (i) fairness/transparency to business users (fleets/drivers) and (ii) worker-status / “control” optics if non-users are materially disadvantaged.\n\nFrom a regulatory perspective, I have analyzed *S.L. 499.68* and did not find anything in the regulation that prohibits a platform from using dispatch logic that accounts for driver settings/preferences. In fact, Transport Malta can require intermediary booking platforms to take measures about how booking requests are communicated (e.g., around restricted zones near taxi stands/bus stops), which implicitly recognizes that platforms do control dispatch/matching mechanics.\n\nFrom a *P2B Regulation perspective,* we believe the risk is also medium. Fleets (and sometimes drivers) are “business users” of an online intermediation service. If Smart Accept gives preferential access to work, that might be seen as ranking/prioritisation.\n\nFrom a *Reclassification POV*, we are aligned with Central Legal and view this feature as medium risk.\n\nThe main legal risk here isn’t the existence of an opt-in productivity feature; it’s when:\n\n* opting out materially reduces earnings/opportunity, or\n* the feature becomes mandatory, or\n* comms sound like performance management (“you must enable to get orders”, etc.).\n\nHaving in consideration what you described in the ticket, and because fleets/drivers have already noticed, the immediate risk is, in our perspective, fairness perception and complaints (which can also escalate into P2B-type issues).\n\nPlease let us know if you need any additional information and or if you have any question.\n\nThank you!\n\n\n\ncc: [~accountid:62722e092db308007024a425] [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2]  [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1]","2026-01-13T16:33:47.118Z"],["3807798","PFI-833010","PFI","viktor.kravchenko@bolt-outsource.eu","Viktor Kravchenko","!IMG_7624.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T16:34:40.768Z"],["3807799","MM-928","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Emoji Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🟡|Some requirements and a doc link are provided, but acceptance criteria and edge cases are missing from the issue body.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The description is somewhat clear but relies on external documentation and uses some jargon without explanation.|\n|Auditability|🟢|Relevant documentation is linked in the issue description.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is provided in the issue.|\n\n*Suggestions:*\n\n* Add acceptance criteria and edge cases directly in the issue.\n* Provide a time estimate.\n* Summarize key requirements from the linked doc in the issue for clarity.","2026-01-13T16:34:54.940Z"],["3807800","DAEN-1310","DAEN","kevin.sutanto@bolt.eu","Kevin Sutanto","Requirements have been gathered here\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1BlnjfKHxXCU53N6U2rT59sjiE5HDflayrbBUjBbKt2Q/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1BlnjfKHxXCU53N6U2rT59sjiE5HDflayrbBUjBbKt2Q/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T16:35:23.403Z"],["3807803","PFI-833012","PFI","oluwabunmi.vivian@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwabunmi Vivian","[^Bosun 9300.pdf]","2026-01-13T16:38:02.608Z"],["3807804","LSS-60146","LSS","jake.murphy@bolt.eu","Jake Murphy","Hey did we get anywhere with reviewing [Salescloser.ai|http://Salescloser.ai]?\nThey’re about to sign our NDA next week and keen to progress to mobilising our pilot in non-GDPR markets for Feb\n\nThey have offered a session with their technical / privacy teams if needed to cover off any questions.","2026-01-13T16:42:35.431Z"],["3807807","WFM-9976","WFM","mihaela.pahontu@bolt-outsource.eu","Mihaela Pahontu","Please use it also as reactive disruption- message sent to user: eater.","2026-01-13T16:47:33.217Z"],["3807809","TAXP-790","TAXP","tiiu.albin@bolt.eu","Tiiu Albin","[~accountid:62ea2a695111209f4fde8265] That’s excellent, thanks a mill! ","2026-01-13T16:49:09.648Z"],["3807811","LSS-31377","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:628b3e951a437e0070414307], do you know if any physical reports were made by either our or the claimant’s engineers following the inspection of the e-bike on Wednesday 17 December? We have received the attached letter from the claimant’s solicitors, and before I assess our options, it would be good to see any engineer reports.\n\n[^Ltr to 3PS re Mediation (2f5a8801-3e46-4e5e-ade5-af6ff45151b8).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T16:53:18.885Z"],["3807813","LSS-61515","LSS","maria.montoya@bolt.eu","Maria Paula Montoya","Please disregard my previous comment - this is the right one: \n\nDrivers spend approximately 15% of their GMV on fuel, making it a critical lever for driver retention and engagement within the Bolt Rewards loyalty program, which aims to reduce churn among high-performing drivers and re-engage less active drivers by maximizing net earnings.\n\nWhile Bolt currently partners with WEX for fuel discounts, adoption remains extremely limited (~60 active drivers). A recent driver survey confirms that the main barriers are low awareness and unclear redemption processes, rather than a lack of interest in fuel discounts. These frictions prevent Bolt from fully capturing the value of one of its most impactful reward categories.\n\nTo address this, I propose piloting an alternative fuel partnership that removes the upfront deposit requirement. Under this setup, Bolt would contract directly with the partner, simplifying access for drivers and reducing entry barriers. The pilot would target Platinum and Diamond non-EV drivers, representing approximately 1,600 high-performing drivers and €8.6M in monthly GMV.\n\nBy lowering barriers and simplifying access to fuel benefits, the pilot is expected to drive higher adoption and improve driver engagement, with a positive impact on GMV through increased retention and activity.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/12qkyvT5ykjqhsxmle8leb3rFwD-97nsSILUQ9iDQ5X4/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/12qkyvT5ykjqhsxmle8leb3rFwD-97nsSILUQ9iDQ5X4/edit?usp=sharing]","2026-01-13T16:54:42.753Z"],["3807815","LSS-60361","LSS","ben.strey@bolt.eu","Ben Strey","[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] the buyer said he did not receive an E-Mail can you please send it again? ","2026-01-13T16:55:19.337Z"],["3807816","LSS-57342","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (13.01)*+\n\n* Zellis has responded via email with its comments (stakeholders are yet to escalate a centralised editable GDoc - I have created my own [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XpJ_Vvu9Kw74m78bXeLJUbQwkcxRD0On/edit] in the interim).\n* (Unsurprisingly) Only remaining points of contention are the Subprocessor and Indemnity/Liability issues. Zellis’s proposals are summarised below.\n** NB. These seem to be the man outstanding points in the agreement and stakeholders are keen to push this over the line. As such, it is unlikely we have a window  for much further discussion unless: (a) material new issues are identified; or (b) we see anything to suggest that Zellis will budge on their previously-held positions.\n\n||*Issue*||*Previous wording*||*Zellis proposal*||*Thoughts / response*||\n|*Subprocessors (Contracts)*\n(Clause 10.2 of the DPA)|Bolt can request copies of subprocessor contracts, although Zellis can redact commercially sensitive info.|Zellis has amended the Clause to say the following:\n* On Bolt’s reasonable written request, Zellis will provide “_extracts_” of relevant provisions sufficient to demonstrate compliance with DP laws.\n* Bolt can only request these extracts in the case of: (a) a regulatory inquiry; (b) a personal data breach; or (c) where Bolt has reasonable grounds to suspect that the subprocessor is non-compliant (provided the info is not already available to Bolt).\n* Extracts can be redacted as necessary to avoid Zellis breaching confidentiality obligations, and Zellis is not required to disclose commercial terms.|IMO we can accept this ✅  \nAlthough this limits the circumstances in which we can request contractual terms of subprocessors, it covers the key scenarios. It seems very unlikely that Zellis will budge any further on this.\n+Next Steps+: Flag to Gab for completeness, but recommend acceptance.|\n|*Subprocessors (Notification)*\n(Clause 10.3 of the DPA)|Each time Zellis appoints a new subprocessor, Bolt should be provided with enough information to make an informed decision about approval, including specified datapoints.|Zellis has made the following changes:\n* Zellis will only provide information about the subprocessor (beyond what is in the subprocessor list) to Bolt on written request.\n* If, within 30 days of appointment, Bolt requests additional information, the deadline will be extended to 45 days (or such longer notice as the parties may agree in good faith).|IMO we can accept this ✅  \nAlthough this requires Bolt to be more proactive in getting certain information about subprocessors from Zellis, it still gives us a viable mechanism to do so. It seems very unlikely that Zellis will budge any further on this.\n+Next Steps+: Flag to Gab for completeness, but recommend acceptance.|\n|*Subprocessors (Objection)*\n(Clauses 10.3(a) & 10.5 of the DPA)|If Bolt objects to a subprocessor within the 30-day period,|Zellis has made the following changes:\n* Bolt’s objections must be specifically tied to “_data protection_”.\n* If Bolt objects, then Bolt (not Zellis) can nominate an alternative subprocessor, at which point Zellis can charge for the necessary changes.\n* If the parties  cannot agree on the additional charges or amendments to the services, then (subject to the below) Bolt can terminate the affected services without liability upon written notice.\n* Bolt can only terminate subprocessor services where Bolt’s objection is based on: (a) the subprocessor posing a material risk to the overall services or to the confidentiality of customer data; (b) the subprocessor is subject to sanctions / adverse findings / material reputational concerns; or (c) the subprocessor “_introduces regulatory non-compliance_” affecting Bolt. Also, Bolt and Zellis must have tried to resolve the concerns first.\n* Bolt must have paid for “_all Services performed up to the termination date_”. It is not clear if this applies to the SP services, or all services under the agreement.|We can largely accept this ✅ subject to these qualifiers 💡 \n* Objections should be tied to 10.5(a) - i.e., SP data protection compliance, material reputational concern, or anything materially impacting Bolt’s own DP compliance.\n* We clarify that the payment obligation applies to the “affected” Services only.\nOtherwise, I doubt that we will get any better than this. Although this introduces additional hurdles, it still provides Bolt with a mechanism to not get locked into an arrangement that it cannot accept. \n+Next Steps+: Flag to Gab for completeness, but recommend acceptance / tweaks.|\n|*Indemnity*\n(Clause 13 of the DPA)|We included our standard pro-Bolt indemnity.|Zellis has removed this wholesale, and instead demands that we rely on recovery via damages claims.|This is not ideal ⚠️ given that:\n* Damages claims are subject to remoteness and mitigations, and are more time-consuming.\n* It will be much harder to recover costs if Zellis suffers a _personal data breach_ that causes liability issues for Bolt.\n* Clause 10.3 excludes liability for “indirect” losses (accepted by Legal). Again - this makes it harder for us to recover.\nZellis have dragged their heels on this and are unwilling to be convinced that this should be included. As such, if we demand this again, it seems very unlikely that Zellis will include it. I also floated the idea of including ‘Deemed Direct Losses’, but: (a) Zellis expressed they would likely be unwilling to accept this; and (b) given that the liability limitations clause is not DP-specific, this would reopen clauses already agreed by Legal.\n+Next steps+: Flag to Gab and the business as a risk for approval.|\n|*Liability Cap*\n(Clause 10.4 of the Agreement)|We proposed a £1m cap for DP violations / personal data breaches of £1m per _claim / aggregate of loss_.|Zellis has proposed a _total_ £1.5m super-cap: “_the Supplier’s total aggregate liability, whether in contract, tort (including negligence), indemnity, or otherwise, arising from a breach of its obligations under the Data Protection Schedule shall be limited to an amount equal to the greater of (i) one million and five hundred thousand pounds (£1,500,000) and (ii) three hundred per cent (300%) of the Charges paid to the Supplier during the 12-month period immediately preceding the event giving rise to the first claim_”.|This is not ideal ⚠️  given that:\n* In light of the fact that we are sharing employment / financial / identity information of all UK drivers with Zellis, I have identified the risk profile as *medium*. I would ordinarily push for 2-3m per claim / aggregate of loss.\n* Zellis have also removed the pro-Bolt indemnity, and so this is yet another hurdle to recovering what we need if things go wrong. \nZellis have dragged their heels on this and have previously claimed they will be unable to secure Exec approval of a higher sum. As such, it seems unlikely that we will be able to negotiate a higher sum.\n+Next steps+: Flag to Gab and the business as a risk for approval.|","2026-01-13T16:58:58.785Z"],["3807818","LSS-61416","LSS","sofia.carto@bolt.eu","Sofia Cartó","[~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] \n\nwe received the following communication (pdf attached) \n\n\nExma, Direção da BOLD Portugal,\n\n \n\nNo âmbito de um processo de inquérito que corre termos neste Núcleo de Deontologia e Disciplina da Polícia de Segurança Pública, e para efeitos de apuramento de factualidade relevante no exercício das respetivas competências legais, encarrega-me o Exmo. Comandante Distrital – Superintendente Mário Nuno campos de Oliveira – de solicitar a V. Exa. a seguinte informação:\n\n– Se Alfredo Rebelo Pereira, com certificado n.º 944113/2025, exerceu atividade enquanto motorista de transporte individual e remunerado de passageiros em veículos descaracterizados (TVDE) através da plataforma eletrónica BOLT, durante o ano de 2025;\n\n– Em caso afirmativo, solicita-se a listagem dos serviços de transporte TVDE prestados no referido período, ou, em alternativa, a indicação do número total de serviços efetuados, com referência temporal.\n\nA presente solicitação é formulada exclusivamente para fins instrutórios, no estrito respeito pelos princípios da legalidade, necessidade e proporcionalidade, agradecendo-se a colaboração dessa entidade na prestação da informação solicitada.\n\n\n\n\n\nCom os melhores cumprimentos,\n\nPDF","2026-01-13T16:59:36.847Z"],["3807819","LSS-61416","LSS","sofia.carto@bolt.eu","Sofia Cartó","[https://drive.google.com/file/d/1A3UZUKcDPVzSZxstky0e2N5Pz72V_I2O/view?usp=drive_link|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1A3UZUKcDPVzSZxstky0e2N5Pz72V_I2O/view?usp=drive_link|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T16:59:45.593Z"],["3807820","WFM-9978","WFM","shivam.pal@bolt-outsource.eu","Shivam Pal","Request - 2\n\nAgent ID’s - 412411,442432,442434,472419,442431,472418\n\nAssigned queues as permanently as secondary  - 01 RH_Canada_T1_Calls\n\nReason - agent will be handling RH Canada calls","2026-01-13T17:00:24.384Z"],["3807821","LSS-61241","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41]. Could you please provide the following response? Thank you!\n\n_Exma. Senhora Dr.ª Crystal Lynn Meneses,_\n\n_Ilustre Mandatária,_\n\n_Acusamos a receção da sua comunicação, acompanhada de Procuração, relativa ao bloqueio da conta do S/ Constituinte, Sr. Lakhvinder Singh, a qual mereceu a nossa melhor atenção._\n\n_Informamos que a decisão de bloqueio da conta teve por base o reporte e ocorrência de sucessivas situações de segurança, designadamente excesso de velocidade e utilização de dispositivos móveis durante a condução, em desrespeito pela legislação aplicável._\n\n_Mais se informa que, contrariamente ao invocado, os motivos inerentes ao bloqueio foram comunicados tanto ao respetivo Gestor de Frota, como ao S/ Constituinte, tendo-lhe sido dada oportunidade de pronúncia, tendo o mesmo estabelecido diversos contactos com a Bolt relativamente a esta questão e sido prestados os necessários esclarecimentos._\n\n_Informa-se ainda que o S/Constituinte já anteriormente havia sido alvo de suspensão de acesso á sua conta, tendo sido posteriormente restabelecido o acesso. Não obstante, o S/ Constituinte voltou a reincidir em comportamentos da mesma natureza._\n\n_Tais condutas configuram violação dos Termos e Condições aplicáveis e das regras legais em vigor, não sendo compatíveis com a manutenção do acesso à Plataforma Bolt._\n\n_Face ao exposto, informamos que será mantido o bloqueio do acesso à Plataforma Bolt. _\n_Com os melhores cumprimentos,_ ","2026-01-13T17:01:23.543Z"],["3807822","MM-929","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🟡|The issue describes the system and alert logic, but lacks explicit acceptance criteria and edge cases for the new adaptation.|\n|Clarity|🟢|The description is well-structured, uses clear language, and explains the current system and requirements.|\n|Auditability|🟢|Key source files, alert logic, and related components are referenced in the description.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is provided in the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add explicit acceptance criteria and edge cases for the adaptation.\n* Provide a time estimate to meet readiness requirements.","2026-01-13T17:01:48.372Z"],["3807825","LSS-60169","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hey [~accountid:5f5b9372dd6835007546bdbd], no worries and thank you for picking it up!\n\nBased on your findings, I have drafted the attached letter which I will send to JF Law Ltd now.\n\nThanks again! 🙂 \n\n[^Letter to JF Law Ltd - Bolt Services UK Limited - 13 January 2026.docx.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T17:06:36.340Z"],["3807826","FRAUDOPS-1014","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","h2. *MARKED ORDERS VS ACTUAL UNCOVERED*\n\nLooking at the uncovered comparison from all marked bad pay orders:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 19.00.45.png|width=852,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 19.00.45.png\"!\n\nOnly failed payment scenarios where there was an initial failed pay or current failed pay. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 18.57.37.png|width=852,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 18.57.37.png\"!\n\n\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nSo this tells us that we are constantly over-evaluating or giving weight to failed payment rides by approx 50% due to looking at total order values regardless of the actual uncovered amounts.\n{panel}\n\nBreaking it down then we can see that the biggest group of orders we mark for failed pay have actually low % coverage of the ride user price.\n\n E.g. anything including and under 30% make up *20K eur of issue for the trips valued 157K eur.*  In this range we also do the most of our markings markings.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 19.03.35.png|width=852,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 19.03.35.png\"!","2026-01-13T17:07:25.642Z"],["3807828","LSS-60169","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* copy of email and letter sent to JF Law Ltd today.\n\n[^Letter to JF Law Ltd - Bolt Services UK Limited - 13 January 2026.docx (77a3d70a-0a2b-4d70-b087-6f5d9604ae20).pdf]\n[^Bolt Mail - RERequest for Information Ms Cheriess McCalla - Alleged Incident on 16 April 2025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T17:08:43.461Z"],["3807829","LSS-31377","LSS","john.buckley@bolt.eu","John Buckley","Hi [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] on the inspection day the other parties engineer took photos and notes. We havent had any engineers reports completed.\n\n","2026-01-13T17:09:22.075Z"],["3807831","LSS-59848","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] please allow me to follow up on the request below. Could you confirm if the driver got an email when he was blocked? Thank you ! 🙏 ","2026-01-13T17:10:45.725Z"],["3807833","PFI-813839","PFI","iveta.griskeviciute@bolt-outsource.eu","Iveta Griškevičiūtė","Still waiting for help","2026-01-13T17:11:59.960Z"],["3807834","LSS-60541","LSS","sandra.figari@bolt.eu","Sandra Figari","Hi [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f]  I’m aware it would be more practical to keep the document in english, however our partners are likely to feel comfortable reviewing the document in spanish. \n\nThe content of the letter looks great to me so I have no comments or suggestions. \n\nPlease let me know if having the bilingual document this week looks feasible. \n\nThank you!\n\n","2026-01-13T17:12:07.739Z"],["3807835","LSS-59694","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] please allow me to follow up on this ticket. Are you able to confirm whether we are fully compliant in light of the association’s push back? Thank you !","2026-01-13T17:12:26.846Z"],["3807836","LSS-60304","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41]. Could you confirm if the response has been sent? Thank you!","2026-01-13T17:15:56.141Z"],["3807837","LSS-31377","LSS","john.buckley@bolt.eu","John Buckley","Their enginner detailed the fail safe measures on the bike that keeps the wheel in place and suggested to our 3PL that their must have been a strong impact.","2026-01-13T17:15:58.086Z"],["3807838","LSS-61524","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-13T17:16:07.277Z"],["3807840","LSS-61525","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nJoão Nuno Ferreira Ramos has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-13T17:19:29.487Z"],["3807841","LSS-60304","LSS","andrezza.demarchi@bolt.eu","Andrezza Perfetto Demarchi","Hey [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] \nYess, I reached out to the user - we are now just waiting to see if she will accept the offer.","2026-01-13T17:20:44.505Z"],["3807842","LSS-61525","LSS","joao.ramos@bolt.eu","João Nuno Ferreira Ramos","h3. Joaquina Maria Guimaraes Rodrigues\n\n<[jguirodrigues@psp.pt|mailto:jguirodrigues@psp.pt]>\n\n\n\nto [documentacao@bolt.eu|mailto:documentacao@bolt.eu], [sofia.carto@bolt.eu|mailto:sofia.carto@bolt.eu], Mario Nuno Campos De Oliveira, CD FARO - Núcleo Deontologia Disciplina\n\n[http://Ex.ma|http://Ex.ma|smart-link]  Direção da BOLD Portugal,\n\n \n\nNo âmbito de um processo de inquérito que corre termos neste Núcleo de Deontologia e Disciplina da Polícia de Segurança Pública, e para efeitos de apuramento de factualidade relevante no exercício das respetivas competências legais, encarrega-me o Exmo. Comandante Distrital – Superintendente Mário Nuno campos de Oliveira – de solicitar a V. Exa. a seguinte informação:\n\n– Se Alfredo Rebelo Pereira, com certificado n.º 944113/2025, exerceu atividade enquanto motorista de transporte individual e remunerado de passageiros em veículos descaracterizados (TVDE) através da plataforma eletrónica BOLT, durante o ano de 2025;\n\n– Em caso afirmativo, solicita-se a listagem dos serviços de transporte TVDE prestados no referido período, ou, em alternativa, a indicação do número total de serviços efetuados, com referência temporal.\n\nA presente solicitação é formulada exclusivamente para fins instrutórios, no estrito respeito pelos princípios da legalidade, necessidade e proporcionalidade, agradecendo-se a colaboração dessa entidade na prestação da informação solicitada.\n\n\n\n\n\nCom os melhores cumprimentos,\n\n \n\n_“Presente pela Proximidade, Próxima na Segurança!” – Estratégia PSP 2025-2027_\n\n\nSorry.","2026-01-13T17:20:51.511Z"],["3807843","PFI-833024","PFI","liam.james@bolt.eu","Liam James","[^UoW - Payment Import - 12_01 - UK Payment Import.csv]","2026-01-13T17:21:06.055Z"],["3807844","LSS-58451","LSS","anouar.miled@bolt.eu","Anouar Miled","Tobias Henschke\nHT Unternehmensgruppe\nVerlängerte Freiimfelder Straße 3\n06112 Halle","2026-01-13T17:21:15.297Z"],["3807845","LSS-61526","LSS","dennis.hennemann@bolt.eu","Dennis Hennemann","[^MWG Drive GmbH - Bolt Cooperation Agreement - Germany.pdf] _(494 kB)_","2026-01-13T17:23:03.937Z"],["3807847","LSS-61525","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Duplication of ticket [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61416|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61416|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T17:24:55.897Z"],["3807848","LSS-61082","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* email correspondence with Voi legal team, arranging call to sync on next steps.\n\n[^Bolt Mail - Voi Liverpool Warehouse.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T17:25:19.044Z"],["3807850","WD-22525","WD","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Idy1kExE42Pn8YL5PlojvsCyBBhIAhpI8-u-2YoI5XY/edit?gid=73181483#gid=73181483|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Idy1kExE42Pn8YL5PlojvsCyBBhIAhpI8-u-2YoI5XY/edit?gid=73181483#gid=73181483|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T17:27:33.544Z"],["3807853","FIN2-942","FIN2","subarna.sharna@bolt.eu","Subarna Islam Sharna","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] no. My colleagues and I (accounting) do not deal with partner market entities during agreement negotiations and launch planning","2026-01-13T17:32:51.883Z"],["3807854","PFI-813099","PFI","nikodem.johnson@bolt-outsource.eu","Nikodem Johnson","I dont think we can escalate these refunds on our end, as ride has already been refunded for this ride [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/689114130|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/689114130]\n\nany suggestions?","2026-01-13T17:34:31.177Z"],["3807856","PFI-813099","PFI","nikodem.johnson@bolt-outsource.eu","Nikodem Johnson","[~accountid:62026399c4e2c9006ae5fb59] ","2026-01-13T17:34:52.782Z"],["3807859","LSS-61416","LSS","joao.ramos@bolt.eu","João Nuno Ferreira Ramos","Hey! \n\nThe driver is registered on our platform and has finalised 2713  rides with us in 2025. \n\n","2026-01-13T17:37:07.938Z"],["3807860","L10N-27582","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:02.333Z"],["3807861","L10N-27578","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:02.338Z"],["3807862","L10N-27576","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:02.353Z"],["3807863","L10N-27579","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:02.353Z"],["3807864","L10N-27577","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:02.445Z"],["3807865","L10N-27580","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:02.494Z"],["3807866","L10N-27581","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:02.555Z"],["3807867","L10N-27585","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:02.595Z"],["3807868","L10N-27584","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:02.897Z"],["3807869","L10N-27566","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:02.961Z"],["3807870","L10N-27573","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:03.210Z"],["3807871","L10N-27570","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:03.270Z"],["3807872","L10N-27575","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:03.311Z"],["3807873","L10N-27574","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:03.345Z"],["3807874","L10N-27571","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:03.418Z"],["3807875","L10N-27562","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:03.568Z"],["3807876","L10N-27569","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:03.618Z"],["3807877","L10N-27572","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:03.720Z"],["3807878","L10N-27558","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:03.971Z"],["3807879","L10N-27557","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:06.510Z"],["3807880","L10N-27552","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:07.140Z"],["3807881","L10N-27568","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:07.209Z"],["3807882","L10N-27567","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:07.221Z"],["3807883","L10N-27556","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:07.269Z"],["3807884","L10N-27565","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:07.285Z"],["3807885","L10N-27564","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:07.274Z"],["3807886","L10N-27559","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:07.633Z"],["3807887","L10N-27550","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:08.233Z"],["3807888","L10N-27563","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:08.296Z"],["3807889","L10N-27560","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:08.321Z"],["3807890","L10N-27561","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:08.345Z"],["3807891","L10N-27551","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:08.453Z"],["3807892","L10N-27554","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:08.526Z"],["3807893","L10N-27555","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:08.546Z"],["3807894","L10N-27553","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:08.569Z"],["3807895","L10N-27583","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-13T17:44:13.876Z"],["3807896","WFM-9960","WFM","emilija.kisieliute@bolt-outsource.eu","Emilija Kisieliūtė","!Screenshot 2026-01-13 194544.png|width=807,height=250,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 194544.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-13T17:46:03.584Z"],["3807898","LSS-54100","LSS","oleg.shimchik@bolt.eu","Aleh Shymchyk","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] PTAL","2026-01-13T17:48:08.291Z"],["3807900","LSS-61496","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5] I can confirm that the only changes are to the Bolt entity and start date - no other commercial or legal terms are changed.\n\nAs mentioned previously, this means that the office may be used solely in connection with the Bolt Flex Private Hire Operator licence because there is no reference to Bolt Services UK Limited in the agreement.\n\nSince this is now being signed on behalf of Bolt Operations UK Limited, the contact name will need to be changed from Ahto Kink to Alex Wong.\n\nPlease provide an updated document and we can arrange signing - thanks 🙂 ","2026-01-13T17:50:49.829Z"],["3807901","CSXRD-353","CSXRD","david.tomes@bolt.eu","David Tomeš","ETA: W3/W4","2026-01-13T17:51:16.216Z"],["3807905","LSS-57342","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Hey [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] - As discussed on Monday, I would be grateful if you could review / approve of specific clauses in this DPA ([+*link*+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XpJ_Vvu9Kw74m78bXeLJUbQwkcxRD0On/edit]), given that we would be substantially deviating from our standard position. Relevant details are below:\n\n* *Background*: We are contracting with a pension administrator (Zellis) as part of a project for auto-enrolling all UK drivers into a pension scheme (unless they object). The specific details of data processing are listed in Appendix 1 of the agreement, including the categories of data. Zellis will be acitng as processor. Zellis have insisted on using their DPA.\n* *Status*: We have had a lot of back-and-forth with Zellis (during which I have pushed our usual positions), and we seem to have reached the point where it is unlikely that Zellis will change anything unless we present them with a particularly compelling argument. The business wants to get the agreement signed by 23 January (although ideally they are pushing for sooner).\n* *Clauses to review / approve*: Clause 10 of the Agreement (Limitation of Liability) and Clause 10.2-10.5 of the DP Schedule (Subprocessors).\n** Zellis’s proposals and my thoughts are summarised in my previous comment on this ticket (see the table). The most important issue is the indemnity / liability point - Zellis have pushed for: (a) no pro-Bolt indemnity for DP violations / data breaches; (b) exclusion of liability for indirect losses; and (c) a £1.5m super-cap _in total_ (not per claim) for DP violations. This obviously shifts a lot of the commercial risk onto Bolt, hence why I feel approval is needed ⚠️ \n\nLet me know if you have any questions 🙂 ","2026-01-13T17:58:51.587Z"],["3807907","LSS-61082","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* email received from Brabners dated 6 January re assignment of the existing lease and funds on account. I plan to respond once we align with Voi’s legal team on next steps (potentially tomorrow). \n\n[^Bolt Mail - Unit 9 Phoenix Park [IMAN-WSLIVE.FID4687096].pdf]\n\n","2026-01-13T18:00:28.292Z"],["3807912","LSS-57395","LSS","weyinmi.aghadiuno@bolt.eu","Weyinmi Aghadiuno","HI [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] Happy New Year. I hope you are well. Please do you have a copy of the signed MoU. I have been trying to locate it. Thank you","2026-01-13T18:07:51.022Z"],["3807913","LSS-61488","LSS","carolina.patricio@bolt.eu","Carolina Patrício","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac],\nThanks for the quick response.\n\nPlease find our answers below for clarification:\n\n*If the idea is to have Bolt Send with TVDE vehicles and with couriers simultaneously?* \n\n* No. The idea is to keep two separate categories:\n** Parcel delivery from A to B by a TVDE driver (current setup), exclusive to TVDE drivers.\n** A new door-to-door delivery category, exclusive to couriers.\nSupply would not be mixed under this setup.\n\n*Whether couriers would be employed by existing fleets, or contracted directly;*\n\n* The same arrangement currently in place for Bolt Food fleets. Only couriers belonging to fleets that are validated and active on the Bolt Food platform would be considered for this category.\n\n*Whether couriers would be using personal or company-owned vehicles:*\n\n* Same arrangement as Bolt Food.\n\n*Vehicle types couriers would use (car, bike, e-moped, etc.):*\n\n* Bike and e-moped.\n\n*The registration and vetting process on the platform;*\n\n# Fleet creates a company profile on the rides platform\n# Fleet registers couriers and uploads the relevant documentation\n# Fleet registers vehicles and uploads the relevant documentation\n# Bolt validates the documentation and creates the account, granting the courier access exclusively to the new Bolt Send category\n\n*Expected contractual structure (e.g. courier–fleet–Bolt, courier–Bolt direct):*\n\n* Courier → Fleet → Bolt\n\n*Changes to insurance or delivery protocols (e.g. ID checks, return logistics):*\n\n* Return logistics are already defined in the current Bolt Send category and should apply as-is.\n\n*Whether clients can choose between TVDE delivery (car) and courier delivery:*\n\n* Yes. Clients will be able to choose, as these will be set up as separate categories.\n\nAdditionally, please let us know if there are any *specific guidelines or requirements regarding documentation* that we should be aware of.\n\nLet me know if you need any additional details.\n\nBest regards,\nCarolina","2026-01-13T18:13:56.618Z"],["3807915","TAXP-2348","TAXP","pedro.yaguezbovio@bolt.eu","Pedro Yaguez Bovio","Local Filed was prepared and submitted. Further information in FY2024 TP Doc tracker.","2026-01-13T18:16:26.424Z"],["3807916","LSS-56393","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:376f7d25-47fd-46e7-ba19-ca9cb0fe977e] [~accountid:5dbbe92cb87a410db33f7faa]\n\nThe privacy team has resumed the assessment of this incident. *Could you confirm ASAP whether the refund to the driver has been completed?*\n\nIf not, to mitigate the risks of the incident, we strongly recommend issuing a refund immediately. Please let us know if you have any questions or need further support from the privacy team re/ this.\n\n----\n\nAdditionally, we are considering collecting statistics from CS on similar incidents in SA where drivers are robbed, and their accounts are accessed by intruders who change payout details. [~accountid:5dbbe92cb87a410db33f7faa], we would appreciate your support with this.","2026-01-13T18:17:49.768Z"],["3807917","LSS-57395","LSS","weyinmi.aghadiuno@bolt.eu","Weyinmi Aghadiuno","[~accountid:63b59fb7d3aeefa40543d2e5] Please can you help with raising another ticket for this MoU to be signed again. I can’t locate a copy","2026-01-13T18:19:28.428Z"],["3807918","LSS-56393","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Internal [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] - I will support this🙂. The ODPO team [deemed|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0678KJ49UH/p1763645358682049] this incident reportable in SA due to the financial loss incurred by the driver.\n\nI am confirming with CS whether the refund was issued to mitigate this risk and avoid reporting it to the regulator. As for additional safeguards, I believe the issue of payout security will be addressed centrally with the partner payments team. I’ve [followed up|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C063R9GEDHC/p1768329599091829?thread_ts=1764154780.385589&cid=C063R9GEDHC] with them to move this central discussion forward.","2026-01-13T18:24:36.747Z"],["3807919","PAW-14844","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @sergey-seleznev\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160433\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-13 18:24:59 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-13T18:24:59.874Z"],["3807920","LSS-61403","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Hi [~accountid:6052892160d39e006f72f166] - will take a look. Just to confirm, is the partenr visit on 16 January? Just so I can understand what the deadline is and how to prioritise this 🙂 ","2026-01-13T18:27:05.512Z"],["3807922","LSS-61460","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:49ec724a-806f-42f1-86dc-bf9f93671a23] - taking a look. As a preliminary question - is 16 January a hard deadline, or a nice to have? Just so that I can prioritise this against other urgent matters 🙂 ","2026-01-13T18:28:00.631Z"],["3807923","LSS-56987","LSS","yasir.mazumder@bolt.eu","Yasir Kabir Mazumder","[^FLO-Mutual NDA- Bolt Services Canada CA Inc. - Executed (1).pdf]\n\nHi Legal team,\nAttached is the final completed the NDA from Flo EV. Sharing for record keeping.\n\nThank you,\n\nYasir","2026-01-13T18:29:55.053Z"],["3807926","LSS-58830","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:240e5e60-baab-4e72-a388-591f4f4ec6a2] - Just to be clear on this, I am more interested in the _dataflows_ (i.e., which entity / entities from the Bolt side are sending the data, and which EOS entities are receiving them directly from Bolt), rather than the contractual parties.\n\nAre you saying that under the agreement, data will be transferred exclusively between Bolt Ops Ou and EOS KSI Inkasso Deutschland GmbH (the latter of which will then send the data onwards to other EOS entities)? Or would it instead be the case that Bolt Ops OU could be sending the data directly to local EOS entities (i.e., bypassing EOS KSI Inkasso Deutschland GmbH)? This is the core question I have been getting at since November.\n\nIf it is the former (i.e., direct data exchange is only between Bolt Ops OU and EOS KSI Inkasso Deutschland GmbH), then I have not further comments from the privacy side on the Special Terms that I provided on 15 December ([LINK|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1u3PfoKaCL2k1cg6eMe3btFlR97ammFpZ/edit]), unless EOS have since proposed changes to these terms (in which case, let me know). If it is the latter, then I will consider whether any further edits are needed from my side 🙂 ","2026-01-13T18:40:33.453Z"],["3807927","LSS-58645","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:608009c6f74b3f006a326795] 👋 \n\nCan you kindly clarify if this is still relevant and you still require support from legal and privacy teams?\n\nDue to lack of activity, we are preparing to close this ticket.","2026-01-13T18:42:33.408Z"],["3807928","LSS-58960","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","*UPDATE*: Only outstanding point is to confirm whether: (a) data exchange is only between Bolt Ops OU and EOS GmBH (in which case, no further comments); or (b) Bolt is sending data directly to local EOS entities in various countries (in which case, should be fine anyway - both direct restricted transfers and onward restricted transfer are covered, we just need to know for accountability purposes).\n\n* We are also waiting for any DSA edits / proposals from EOS.","2026-01-13T18:42:42.699Z"],["3807929","LSS-58899","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Thanks [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] . Seems there was no activity in the main ticket since Nov. I’ve followed up with the business to confirm if the request is still relevant.\n\nCC [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] ","2026-01-13T18:43:19.115Z"],["3807930","BDB-1521","BDB","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] - done - FYI I kept the original poster headlines but otherwise added [~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c] ‘s changes. \n\nAs mentioned as soon as I can I’ll specify if we can have unique promo codes added to these assets or not, I’ll hopefully have more to share on this tomorrow.","2026-01-13T18:50:44.783Z"],["3807931","LSS-57900","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Noted [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] \n\n# From the Beehive thread, I see that the issue was successfully deescalated by the CS following the KB procedure back in Oct. 2025.\n# Re/ the investigation of the unauthorised access, I’ve requested access to the IT ticket that Alex linked to check the status.","2026-01-13T18:53:15.432Z"],["3807933","PFI-833042","PFI","frank.ezeakacha@bolt-outsource.eu","Frank Ezeakacha","[^DOC-20260113-WA0000..pdf]","2026-01-13T18:59:28.125Z"],["3807934","TAXP-1511","TAXP","pedro.yaguezbovio@bolt.eu","Pedro Yaguez Bovio","The presentation should only take place in the first applicable FY, further CbCR Notification are only required if any information changes so no submission was made","2026-01-13T18:59:41.318Z"],["3807936","PFI-833045","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T19:14:13.613Z"],["3807937","LSS-60753","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hey [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] \nPlease find the draft PPRA [here|https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyo%C3%BC/preliminaryprivacyriskassessmentforuse/1-all-entries/31]","2026-01-13T19:17:03.547Z"],["3807938","DMC-725","DMC","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","Confident original estimate of 2d","2026-01-13T19:18:40.677Z"],["3807940","DMC-342","DMC","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","Confident original estimate of 1w","2026-01-13T19:20:36.295Z"],["3807941","DMC-342","DMC","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","This task has a dependency on [DPM-2332|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPM-2332]","2026-01-13T19:21:05.810Z"],["3807942","DMC-724","DMC","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","Confident original estimate of 3h","2026-01-13T19:22:44.381Z"],["3807943","PFI-822383","PFI","roberts.jakubovskis@bolt-outsource.eu","Roberts Jakubovskis","So this question is resolved?","2026-01-13T19:24:34.135Z"],["3807944","DMC-346","DMC","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","Confident original estimate of 4h","2026-01-13T19:26:16.549Z"],["3807945","HS-27194","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Contract now signed by both parties. ","2026-01-13T19:28:06.499Z"],["3807946","DMC-726","DMC","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","Confident original estimate of 2h","2026-01-13T19:28:21.550Z"],["3807947","DMC-344","DMC","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","Confident original estimate of 1w","2026-01-13T19:29:36.676Z"],["3807948","DMC-343","DMC","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","Uncertain original estimate of 1w","2026-01-13T19:32:05.361Z"],["3807949","LSS-61082","LSS","laura.newton@bolt.eu","Laura Newton","Hi [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5], see updated version here. \n\n[^Updated Bolt Operations UK Limited - Reference Letter 07.01.2026.pdf]\n\nKind regards, \n\nLaura\n","2026-01-13T19:32:06.657Z"],["3807950","PFI-826753","PFI","joanna.stefaniak@bolt-outsource.eu","Joanna Stefaniak","we still need help","2026-01-13T19:41:39.069Z"],["3807951","LSS-61394","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","do you need further support or I can close this ticket?\n\nthank you [~accountid:712020:7eb363dc-ca9f-4746-abde-3581e042a507] !\n\nElisabetta","2026-01-13T20:11:48.283Z"],["3807952","RDS-1246","RDS","katharina.skolimowski@bolt.eu","Katharina Skolimowski","Linked the early phase ideation file here. Feel free to add comments and specially answers to purple notes 🙂 ","2026-01-13T20:17:43.627Z"],["3807954","DBRE-8691","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","[Alertmanager] TiKV_server_report_failure_msg_total","2026-01-13T20:23:33.667Z"],["3807955","DBRE-8691","DBRE",null,"Slack","[Leandro Morgado|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f5b4e070e396800690aa153] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03055EHHPS/p1768335159385939|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03055EHHPS/p1768335159385939|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-13T20:23:35.031Z"],["3807956","DRAG101-463","DRAG101","tom.evans@bolt.eu","Tom Evans","Hi [~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e] , \n\nHere is the feedback from the SW team: \n\n“I have been doing some testing with the NFC tags and so far we have 2 problems:\n\n# *Incompatible with iOS devices.* The tags are using chips manufactured by *Shanghai Fudan Microelectronics Co. Ltd.*. While they claim to be compatible with iOS devices, they are clones of standard NXP chips and the scan logs explicitly show they are *'NOT ISO/IEC 14443-2 (Type A) compatible'*. This standard defines the physical layer of the communication stack. It specifies signal power, frequency, modulation etc. And since iOS has stricter requirements when it comes to signal strength and integrity it might explain why they aren't working on iPhones.\n# *Poor read range.* The physical tag size appears too small for our use case. While Android devices can read the tag, they practically have to be touching the enclosure to get a successful scan. This will likely be even tougher for users with smartphone cases.” \n\n\n\nHere are the logs from the testing of the device: [^taginfo_scan_collection260112144054.txt] \n\nLine 304 says: \"NOT ISO/IEC 14443-2 (Type A) compatible\"\n\nThere are other differences as well.\n\nFor instance working tag says:\nLine 99: * TAG: Tech [android.nfc.tech.NfcA, android.nfc.tech.MifareClassic, android.nfc.tech.Ndef]Not working one:\nLine 308: * TAG: Tech [android.nfc.tech.NfcA, android.nfc.tech.Ndef]\n\n\n\nPlease can you clarify this with the supplier? Are they definitely compatible with IOS? We need to understand quickly to know whether we can go forward with this supplier or need to find a new one. Thanks! ","2026-01-13T20:24:46.080Z"],["3807957","DBRE-8691","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","* TiKV restarted\n[https://ti-incentives.grafana.db.boltint.net/d/eDbRZpnWk/ti-incentives-overview?orgId=1&from=1768333977782&to=1768335226850&theme=dark|https://ti-incentives.grafana.db.boltint.net/d/eDbRZpnWk/ti-incentives-overview?orgId=1&from=1768333977782&to=1768335226850&theme=dark]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 20.25.19.png|width=1113,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 20.25.19.png\"!\n* Attaching timestamp and logs below\n{noformat}{\"level\":\"FATAL\",\"caller\":\"lib.rs:479\",\"message\":\"assertion `left == right` failed\\n  left: TimeStamp(463558332737127155)\\n right: TimeStamp(463558332750233629)\",\"time\":\"2026/01/13 20:05:05.116 +00:00\",\"thread_id\":44,\"backtrace\":\"   0: tikv_util::set_panic_hook::{{closure}}\\n             at /workspace/source/tikv/components/tikv_util/src/lib.rs:478:18\\n   1: <alloc::boxed::Box<F,A> as core::ops::function::Fn<Args>>::call\\n             at /root/.rustup/toolchains/nightly-2023-12-28-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/lib/rustlib/src/rust/library/alloc/src/boxed.rs:2029:9\\n      std::panicking::rust_panic_with_hook\\n             at /root/.rustup/toolchains/nightly-2023-12-28-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/lib/rustlib/src/rust/library/std/src/panicking.rs:783:13\\n   2: std::panicking::begin_panic_handler::{{closure}}\\n             at /root/.rustup/toolchains/nightly-2023-12-28-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/lib/rustlib/src/rust/library/std/src/panicking.rs:657:13\\n   3: std::sys_common::backtrace::__rust_end_short_backtrace\\n             at /root/.rustup/toolchains/nightly-2023-12-28-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/lib/rustlib/src/rust/library/std/src/sys_common/backtrace.rs:171:18\\n   4: rust_begin_unwind\\n             at /root/.rustup/toolchains/nightly-2023-12-28-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/lib/rustlib/src/rust/library/std/src/panicking.rs:645:5\\n   5: c