email addresses listed below:\n\n\n* [+Charles.oyakhilome@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:Charles.oyakhilome@bolt-outsource.eu]\n* [eze.akunne@Bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:eze.akunne@Bolt-outsource.eu]\n* [bayode.adeola@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:bayode.adeola@bolt-outsource.eu]\n* [anthony.ndubuisi@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:anthony.ndubuisi@bolt-outsource.eu]\n* [michael.oparah@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:michael.oparah@bolt-outsource.eu]\n* [endurance.abubakar@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:endurance.abubakar@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n","2026-01-13T21:27:56.482Z"],["3807969","WFM-9980","WFM","samuel.koku@bolt-outsource.eu","Samuel Koku","We recently had the Queues removed and we have no idea why.","2026-01-13T21:30:03.744Z"],["3807970","DBRE-8691","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0459EFQ8HJ/p1768339842889929|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0459EFQ8HJ/p1768339842889929|smart-link] ","2026-01-13T21:31:53.642Z"],["3807971","DBRE-8691","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Looks like fix is in 8.5.4 [https://docs.pingcap.com/tidb/dev/release-8.5.4/|https://docs.pingcap.com/tidb/dev/release-8.5.4/|smart-link] \n\n{quote}* Fix the issue that assertion errors in TiKV might cause TiCDC to panic [#18498|https://github.com/tikv/tikv/issues/18498] @[tharanga|https://github.com/tharanga]{quote}\n\n\n[https://github.com/tikv/tikv/issues/18498|https://github.com/tikv/tikv/issues/18498|smart-link] \n\nThere are plans to upgrade to 8.5.4 or 8.5.5 soon.","2026-01-13T21:37:27.138Z"],["3807973","PFI-833073","PFI","oluchi.onochie@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluchi Onochie","!Screenshot_20260112_085802_capitec_acuity_mobile_prod_MainActivity.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-13T21:38:00.063Z"],["3807974","PFI-833074","PFI","adeoluwa.odunuga@bolt-outsource.eu","Adeoluwa Odunuga","[^Support case_ 721604363 - Customer Support - Beehive (dfb5a8cd-b10b-47dd-bbae-b2c61ac70281).html]\n\n[^Support case_ 721604363 - Customer Support - Beehive.html]","2026-01-13T21:45:14.811Z"],["3807978","FPD-1524","FPD","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","we checked and the data points are exactly the same. The difference is that in the sheets RF calculates the mape as {{abs(actual - predicted)/predicted}}, while we calculate it as {{abs(predicted - actual)/actual}} - which is the most correct definition of MAPE","2026-01-13T22:02:03.199Z"],["3807980","PFI-830203","PFI","neirune.kupstaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Neirūnė Kupstaitė","I wanted to add that courier did contact their bank and they informed courier to get back to us ","2026-01-13T22:26:16.041Z"],["3807983","INT-668","INT","alexander.tsyba@bolt.eu","Alexander Tsyba","[~accountid:63f5cbeb1223974bc04b700e] I had a thought about slight clarification in requirements - perhaps we should not apply budget control at all if merchant just joined Bolt Food (within first 30 days), otherwise averages over last 4 weeks may be really low.","2026-01-13T23:03:37.332Z"],["3807985","PAW-14321","PAW","cristian.lupu@bolt.eu","Cristian Lupu","Positional argument is best left as is for now.\n\nDesync between development branches and builder agent could cause invalid parsing.\n\nCan be revisited after builder forces a commit to be present in the source branch before continuing!","2026-01-13T23:40:44.785Z"],["3807986","PAW-14307","PAW","cristian.lupu@bolt.eu","Cristian Lupu","Closing for now, medium effort with low result.","2026-01-13T23:44:19.412Z"],["3807987","PRV-1045","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Current status:\n\n# Reviewing Ellex’s input - [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nNukeond3mJ5mfK1nt7EZyffgmQijLP8/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=106326439712206242177&rtpof=true&sd=true|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nNukeond3mJ5mfK1nt7EZyffgmQijLP8/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=106326439712206242177&rtpof=true&sd=true|smart-link] ;\n# Further iteration will be required to clarify certain provisions.\n\nNext steps:\n\n# [Kostiantyn Ponomarov|mailto:kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu] clean up the content to be sent to Ellex. DDL: 1/16/2026 .\n# Likely will require one last round of feedback and improvements based on Ellex feedback.\n\nFinal version internally eady by 1/27/2026.","2026-01-13T23:46:52.336Z"],["3807988","PRV-1066","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Current status:*\n\n# Aligned with Ellex that PayCo Personal Data Retention Procedure will be integrated as an annex to Bolt’s existing Personal Data Retention Policy. \n# The [Ellex’s draft|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sEwqEyFxgHZ8VDrtQdR36EshQ9sgws6m/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=106326439712206242177&rtpof=true&sd=true] was significantly updated by Ellex, shortened and refined to remove duplication with Bolt Group Policies, retaining only the provisions required by the applicable regulatory regime.\n# Next steps:\n## To review Ellex’s input in detail. A further iteration will be required to clarify certain provisions.\n## The template will be split into separate appendices:\n### Data Classification - owned by Infosec and addressed under a separate Data Classification document.\n### Data Retention - owned by Privacy and addressed as ","2026-01-13T23:50:16.155Z"],["3807989","PFI-833085","PFI","cesar.meza@bolt-outsource.eu","Cesar Maria Verza Meza","[^invoice.pdf]","2026-01-13T23:53:26.063Z"],["3807990","PFI-833085","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-13T23:53:28.252Z"],["3807992","PRV-1067","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Status & next steps:*\n\n# Samantha has raised an issue that there may be a conflict of interest of her being both the DPO and SB member.\n# *Action item:* Kostiantyn Ponomarov to confirm with Samantha Sayers who will be the DPO, DDL end of this week Fri, 1/16/2026\n## If it not Samantha, that other person will also need to go through the fit & proper process (Samantha will do the SB fit & proper anyways).","2026-01-14T00:03:51.798Z"],["3807993","PRV-1068","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Status & next steps:*\n\n# TBC","2026-01-14T00:06:39.992Z"],["3807994","PRV-1069","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","TBC","2026-01-14T00:08:59.590Z"],["3807995","PRV-1070","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","In the privacy work stream, to be addressed under:\n\n* *Personal Data Protection Policy*\n* *Data Classification & Retention Policy*\n\nStatus: TBC","2026-01-14T00:12:30.958Z"],["3807996","PRV-1071","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","TBC - primarily to be addressed under Personal Data Protection Procedure.","2026-01-14T00:18:17.792Z"],["3807997","PRV-1072","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Status: [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e]  to talk to Jaanus and review the existing procedure to ensure there are no conflicts with other data protection procedures.\n\nETA for update next week - 20st of January.","2026-01-14T00:21:44.463Z"],["3807998","PRV-1073","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Scope includes:*\n\n* Lawful basis mapping for all processing activities\n* Explicit consent handling (PSD2-specific)\n* PayCo privacy notices\n* Data Subject Rights procedures\n* DPIAs for high-risk processing\n* Transfer Risk Assessments and SCC/BCR coverage\n* RoPA updates and retention schedules\n\nNext steps: TBC following license submission.","2026-01-14T00:27:16.219Z"],["3807999","PRV-1074","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","TBC","2026-01-14T00:34:41.867Z"],["3808000","FX-3624","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768351689543419]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@test_ci_notifier>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3624] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-14T00:48:23.610Z"],["3808001","RCE-349","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768351918336419]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@test_ci_notifier>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-349] `Disable tests team report as of 2026/01/14` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-14T00:52:11.405Z"],["3808002","FX-3625","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768351920278989]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@test_ci_notifier>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3625] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-14T00:52:13.176Z"],["3808003","PFI-833085","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-14T01:00:51.106Z"],["3808004","PFI-833089","PFI","pimthada.atirojtirakorn@bolt-outsource.eu","Pimthada Atirojtirakorn","!image-20260114-013133.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260114-013140.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T01:33:59.860Z"],["3808005","LSS-61527","LSS","lisha.ye@bolt.eu","Lisha Ye","[^Bolt Operations NDA-Computer Components Ltd.docx] _(50 kB)_","2026-01-14T01:36:35.754Z"],["3808006","PFI-833085","PFI","sergio.acosta@bolt-outsource.eu","Sergio David Ramirez Acosta","I understand, but I should mention that the problem is that the trip amount is incorrect on the invoice; the rider's information is correct.","2026-01-14T01:37:06.087Z"],["3808007","PFI-829428","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","Hi Team, could you help recheck again regarding the payment proof in the previous reply. Thank you.","2026-01-14T02:18:51.061Z"],["3808008","PFI-828490","PFI","ricardo.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu","Ricardo Fernandes","Hello, still need help with this.","2026-01-14T03:01:26.603Z"],["3808009","PFI-833093","PFI","ampikar.ouantai@bolt.eu","Ampikar Ouantai","[^TH6525-3605.pdf]","2026-01-14T03:28:16.849Z"],["3808010","PFI-833093","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-14T03:28:19.515Z"],["3808013","FDBT-4790","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-14T03:32:00.922Z"],["3808016","PFI-833093","PFI","ampikar.ouantai@bolt.eu","Ampikar Ouantai","Hi Team,\n\nSorry for the inconvenience, I mistakenly set the title automatically.\n\nThe correctly subject is the client would like to have an English statement version. \n\nThank you.\nAmpikar","2026-01-14T03:40:10.429Z"],["3808021","PFI-833096","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","\n\n[^M2309128.TXT] _(0.4 kB)_","2026-01-14T04:01:02.876Z"],["3808025","WFM-9968","WFM","farhan.morris@bolt.eu","Farhan Morris","Any update [~accountid:712020:824016bc-1a7a-4038-a3aa-448d64c000d1] ","2026-01-14T04:39:03.144Z"],["3808026","WFM-9976","WFM","ulyana.auchynnikavaa@bolt.eu","Ula Auchynnikava","Hey [~accountid:712020:207c95ff-c39e-492c-9c31-f804f0b6bb8a], proactive comms were set up for eater and provider, reactive comms have been up since 11.01.2026 and will remain active until 18.01.2026","2026-01-14T04:39:54.010Z"],["3808028","PFI-832687","PFI","lidia.wozniak@bolt-outsource.eu","Lidia Wozniak","Hello,\nThank you for the information. The passenger profile block has been removed as per your instructions. \nIs it now possible to remove device UID block from this user?","2026-01-14T04:40:39.300Z"],["3808031","LSS-61528","LSS","george.xenokratis@bolt.eu","George Xenokratis","[^BOLT Operations NDA (Mutual) (1).pdf] _(165 kB)_\n\n[^Xerox Scan 2026-01-12 03.54.55 PM.pdf] _(148 kB)_","2026-01-14T04:48:06.015Z"],["3808037","FDBT-4789","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-14T05:01:42.212Z"],["3808041","DSR-3713","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-14T05:26:21.398Z"],["3808044","FDBT-4706","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_data_integration_workiva_workday_report_for_cash_flow_parent fails on 2026-01-13 05:15:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 771, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 424, in wrapper\n    return func(self, *args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/operators/aws/ecr_docker_operator.py\", line 139, in execute\n    self.runtime_strategy.wait_until_done(self.container_id)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/docker/batch/aws_batch_container_runtime_strategy.py\", line 215, in wait_until_done\n    raise AirflowException(f\"Batch job status is {current_job.status}, failing downstream task\")\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Batch job status is FAILED, failing downstream task\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_data_integration_workiva_workday_report_for_cash_flow_parent/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-13T05%3A15%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=workiva_workday_report_for_cash_flow_parent_post_generate_files_task&base_date=2026-01-13T05%3A15%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-14T05:29:11.764Z"],["3808045","LSS-61516","LSS","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Hey [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] , please see the conversation below:\n\n\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n*From Latvian, Lettish*\n\n*Show original*\n\nHello, Timur! How can we help?\n\nBolt\n\n10.01.26, 23:00\n\nTK\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nGive me back the money I'm owed for the passenger not showing up\n\nTimur Kushenko\n\n10.01.26, 23:01\n\n10.01.26, 23:01:Bolt changed support case status from \"Draft\" to \"Open\"\n\n10.01.26, 23:01:Bolt initialized support case tier with \"Tier 1\"\n\n10.01.26, 23:01:\n\nBolt added following issue:\n\n+I didn't receive a cancellation fee+\n\n10.01.26, 23:01:Support case was assigned to Alfred\n\nTK\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nHow long will this continue? You are cheating your drivers out of money\n\nTimur Kushenko\n\n10.01.26, 23:01\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/de9172e31c4a6983.png|alt=\"alfredAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nI understand that it is very unpleasant when a passenger does not show up, and you wait and expect a cancellation fee.\n\nUnfortunately, I cannot see a specific order linked to this request, so I cannot process this particular request. Please create a new support ticket and be sure to select the order for which you want to receive the cancellation fee. Then we will be able to check everything and resolve the payment issue.\n\nIf there are several such rides, submit a separate request for each of them.\n\nAlfred\n\n10.01.26, 23:01\n\n10.01.26, 23:01:Alfred changed support case status from \"Open\" to \"Solved\"\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nDid we resolve your issue?\n\nBolt\n\n10.01.26, 23:01\n\nTK\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nNo, I still have questions\n\nTimur Kushenko\n\n10.01.26, 23:01\n\n10.01.26, 23:01:Bolt changed support case status from \"Solved\" to \"Open\"\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nI'm very sorry. Please tell me what else I can help you with?\n\nBolt\n\n10.01.26, 23:01\n\n10.01.26, 23:01:Bolt changed support case status from \"Open\" to \"Pending\"\n\nTK\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nTranslate the request to the staff\n\nTimur Kushenko\n\n10.01.26, 23:02\n\n10.01.26, 23:02:Bolt changed support case status from \"Pending\" to \"Open\"\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/de9172e31c4a6983.png|alt=\"alfredAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nI understand that the situation is unpleasant, and thank you for writing again.\n\nAt the moment, I still don't have a specific order linked to this request that I can associate with a cancellation payment. Without a selected trip, I unfortunately cannot check whether you are entitled to a cancellation payment or credit it.\n\nPlease create a new support request and be sure to select the order for which the rider did not show up and for which you want to receive the cancellation fee. If there are several such orders — submit a request for each of them separately.\n\nAs soon as there is a request with a linked order, we will be able to check everything in detail and, if the conditions are met, credit you the cancellation payment.\n\nAlfred\n\n10.01.26, 23:02\n\n10.01.26, 23:02:Alfred changed support case status from \"Open\" to \"Solved\"\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nDid we resolve your issue?\n\nBolt\n\n10.01.26, 23:02\n\nTK\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nNo, I still have questions\n\nTimur Kushenko\n\n10.01.26, 23:02\n\n10.01.26, 23:02:Bolt changed support case status from \"Solved\" to \"Open\"\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nI'm very sorry. Please advise how else I can help you?\n\nBolt\n\n10.01.26, 23:02\n\n10.01.26, 23:02:Bolt changed support case status from \"Open\" to \"Pending\"\n\nTK\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nYou will never be able to help me with anything, you dumb machine. Forward the request to support.\n\nTimur Kushenko\n\n10.01.26, 23:03\n\n10.01.26, 23:03:Bolt changed support case status from \"Pending\" to \"Open\"\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/de9172e31c4a6983.png|alt=\"alfredAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nI understand that you are angry — waiting for a booking and then not receiving the cancellation fee is indeed very upsetting.\n\nAt the moment, I still don't have a linked booking in this request. Without a specific trip, I unfortunately cannot check whether you are entitled to a cancellation fee or credit it.\n\nPlease create a new support request and be sure to select the booking for which the passenger didn't show up and for which you want to receive the cancellation fee. A separate request is needed for each such booking.\n\nAs soon as there is a request with the selected booking, we will be able to check the conditions and, if everything is met, credit the cancellation fee to you.\n\nAlfred\n\n10.01.26, 23:03\n\n10.01.26, 23:03:Alfred changed support case status from \"Open\" to \"Solved\"\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nDid we resolve your issue?\n\nBolt\n\n10.01.26, 23:03\n\nTK\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nNo, I still have questions\n\nTimur Kushenko\n\n10.01.26, 23:03\n\n10.01.26, 23:03:Bolt changed support case status from \"Solved\" to \"Open\"\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nI'm very sorry. Please tell me what else I can help you with?\n\nBolt\n\n10.01.26, 23:03\n\n10.01.26, 23:03:Bolt changed support case status from \"Open\" to \"Pending\"\n\nTK\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nThe agent will find the booking themselves, I don't know which booking the passenger requested a refund for. Translate to a real person\n\nTimur Kushenko\n\n10.01.26, 23:04\n\n10.01.26, 23:04:Bolt changed support case status from \"Pending\" to \"Open\"\n\n10.01.26, 23:04:Support case was unassigned\n\n10.01.26, 23:04:First reply SLO set to 3 hours\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nThe request has been forwarded to another colleague who will be able to help you more effectively 🤝\n\nOur colleague will contact you shortly. You may close this window: the chat is available in the “Support” section.\n\nBolt\n\n10.01.26, 23:04\n\n11.01.26, 12:08:Support case was assigned to Alina Stepovikova\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\nrider [case|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/720948473]\n\nAlina Stepovikova\n\n11.01.26, 12:09 · Internal Note\n\n11.01.26, 12:09:Alina Stepovikova edited+case data+\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nHello Timur! I’m Mira from the Bolt team.👋\n\nAlina Stepovikova\n\n11.01.26, 12:10\n\n11.01.26, 12:10:First reply SLO missed\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nI will process a refund of the cancellation fee and the amount will be credited to your balance within 14 working days.\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nAll the best!\n\nAlina Stepovikova\n\n11.01.26, 12:10\n\n11.01.26, 12:10:Alina Stepovikova changed support case status from \"Open\" to \"Solved\"\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*Компенсация в размере 3.15€ на ваш баланс*Rejected\n\nAlina Stepovikova\n\n11.01.26, 17:19\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nHave we resolved your issue?\n\nBolt\n\n11.01.26, 12:10\n\nTK\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nNo, I still have questions\n\nTimur Kushenko\n\n11.01.26, 17:19\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nI am very sorry. Please tell me how else I can help you?\n\nBolt\n\n11.01.26, 17:19\n\n11.01.26, 17:19:Bolt changed support case status from \"Solved\" to \"Pending\"\n\nTK\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nI do not accept the compensation; I still have claims against the Bolt platform. Since my trust in the platform has been undermined by Bolt’s systematic attempts to deceive me, I demand:\n\n# An explanation of why such a situation occurs and how to avoid it in the future.\n# A detailed report of all cancellations I have made during my 4 years of work with the Bolt platform and of all cases where customers received a refund of compensation.\n# The address for legal correspondence in Latvia and Estonia to send a pre-trial claim. Within the next week, my lawyers and I will prepare a complaint against the Bolt platform to the appropriate authorities.\n\nTimur Kushenko\n\n11.01.26, 17:26\n\n11.01.26, 17:26:Bolt changed support case status from \"Pending\" to \"Open\"\n\n11.01.26, 17:26:Follow-up reply SLO set to 6 hours\n\n11.01.26, 17:26:Support case was unassigned because it went active and the agent was offline\n\n12.01.26, 02:51:Support case was assigned to Anna Šavšajeva (displayed as \"Anna 💚\")\n\n12.01.26, 02:54:\n\nAnna Šavšajeva added following issue:\n\n+I want to request my personal data+\n\n+I want to request my Bolt account balance statement+\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nHello Timur, I’m Anna. From this moment I will handle your request. Thank you for waiting for a response; at the moment we have encountered a large number of requests and were unable to reply to you earlier.\n\nAnna Šavšajeva (displayed as \"Anna 💚\")\n\n12.01.26, 02:54\n\n12.01.26, 02:54:Follow-up reply SLO missed\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nThank you for your request for access to data dated *12.01.2026* and for choosing to exercise your data subject rights under the data protection law.\n\nBolt is committed to providing the highest level of data protection for our customers, employees, and independent partners, and to ensuring timely and comprehensive responses to incoming requests.\n\nWe estimate that we will be able to provide a response to your request within one month from the date of receipt, no later than *12.02.2026*. However, we would like to inform you that, in certain cases, the data protection law allows for an extension of the response period by an additional two months due to the complexity of the request. If it becomes necessary to extend the response time, we will notify you in advance within the next month.\n\nIf we are unable to fulfill your request, the response will include the justification for such a decision.\n\nIf you have any questions about the status of your data access request, please contact support by replying to this message.\n\nAnna Šavšajeva (displayed as \"Anna 💚\")\n\n12.01.26, 02:57\n\n!https://beehive.bolt.eu/modules/customer_support/0.1253.0/4787e2fa23602c16.svg|alt=\"boltAvatarIcon\"!\n\n*From English, American*\n\n*Show original*\n\n*To the Dearest Tier 2:* Hi! Driver requests a report of all their deductions and explanation to each of them for the last4 years. They also are asking for address for legal correspondence in Latvia and Estonia for sending a pre-trial claim, as they want to sue Bolt\n\n*Links:* [Driver|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/3769599?tab=profile]\n\nAnna Šavšajeva\n\n12.01.26, 02:59 · Internal Note\n\n12.01.26, 02:59:Anna Šavšajeva edited+case data+\n\n12.01.26, 02:59:Anna Šavšajeva changed support case tier from \"Tier 1\" to \"Tier 2\"\n\n12.01.26, 02:59:Support case was unassigned because the agent lost access to the case\n\n12.01.26, 02:59:Follow-up reply SLO set to 6 hours\n\nTK\n\n*From Russian*\n\n*Show original*\n\nI did not receive an answer from you to the question of why this situation is occurring?\n{panel}\n\n","2026-01-14T05:32:28.042Z"],["3808049","DSR-3715","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-14T05:41:06.412Z"],["3808052","DSR-2608","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Good monring [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] , the driver send one more follow up as follows. I believe we have fulfilled our part?\n\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nHello,\n\nFollowing your last message informing me that the suspension of my Bolt partner account could not be lifted, I inform you that I have, at this stage, filed a complaint with the CNIL.\n\nThis action follows the lack of a proposed solution despite my repeated exchanges, and concerns exclusively the aspects related to the processing of my personal data and the procedure that led to the definitive suspension of my account.\n\nI remain of course available for any discussion or reconsideration of the situation that may take place within this framework.\n\nKind regards,\n\nYoucef-Amin Alem\n\nBolt partner driver\n{panel}","2026-01-14T05:46:30.172Z"],["3808053","DSR-2997","DSR","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","Solving - No reply from user","2026-01-14T05:49:20.312Z"],["3808057","BDB-1461","BDB","alexsandra.kruusberg@bolt.eu","Alexsandra Kruusberg","Hey [~accountid:5fb225a6f2df6c00762b994d] ! Let me check with the team today and if not I will create one so you could start using it. We would need to have one for OOH anyways 🙂 \n\nwill give you an update here by EOD\n\nAlex ","2026-01-14T05:56:17.222Z"],["3808058","DSR-3015","DSR","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","Solving - No reply from user","2026-01-14T05:57:40.178Z"],["3808075","WFM-9920","WFM","murad.abdullayev@bolt.eu","Murad Mir Abdullayev","Unfortunately, there are no KB articles related to blocks caused by Anneli Tammesson.\nHowever, similar cases continue to come in.\nCould you please suggest a solution?\nThank you.","2026-01-14T06:01:30.497Z"],["3808076","MARTECH3-1509","MARTECH3","anton.bugaev@bolt.eu","Anton Bugaev","Some improvements for next time:\n\n* priors should be incorporated based on experiments (i.e. there should be “market-level“ incrementality)\n* Instead of scipy_a,loc,scale, better run the model two times:\n** other without cost and market-level parameters\n** one with cost and market-level parameters, calculating all the uncertainty inside one script.\n** models will need to be reproducible with rng\n* *main question:* improve sensitivity for quasi-experiments","2026-01-14T06:02:11.825Z"],["3808078","PFI-833112","PFI","valeriia.kuchynska@bolt-outsource.eu","Valeriia Kuchynska","!IMG_2740.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T06:04:36.429Z"],["3808079","PFI-830336","PFI","lawrancetshepo.motsepe@bolt.eu","Lawrance Tshepo Motsepe","Thank you, I will inform the customer.","2026-01-14T06:07:19.347Z"],["3808080","PIF-3272","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Automated transition to Ready:*\n\nThis ticket has been automatically moved from Clarification to Ready based on:\n- Presence of a WSJF Score\n- WSJF Score set more than the required delay period ago\n\nAny linked clarification tickets have been closed.\n\n*Note:* If this ticket needs a Value Increment, please run vi_generator.py or add it manually.","2026-01-14T06:07:55.811Z"],["3808081","PAW-15476","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Automated transition to Ready:*\n\nThis ticket has been automatically moved from Clarification to Ready based on:\n- Presence of a WSJF Score\n- WSJF Score set more than the required delay period ago\n\nAny linked clarification tickets have been closed.\n\n*Note:* If this ticket needs a Value Increment, please ru