en Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Auto-set WSJF Opportunity Enablement*\n- Component: `pint-component-builder`\n- Tier: 1\n- Opportunity Enablement: 13\n\nReason: Opportunity Enablement is derived from component tier.","2026-01-14T06:11:47.500Z"],["3808138","PIF-2107","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Auto-set WSJF Opportunity Enablement*\n- Component: `pint-component-alerting`\n- Tier: 2\n- Opportunity Enablement: 8\n\nReason: Opportunity Enablement is derived from component tier.","2026-01-14T06:11:49.469Z"],["3808139","PIF-2100","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Auto-set WSJF Opportunity Enablement*\n- Component: `pint-component-njsc-db`\n- Tier: 3\n- Opportunity Enablement: 5\n\nReason: Opportunity Enablement is derived from component tier.","2026-01-14T06:11:51.304Z"],["3808140","PIF-2098","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Auto-set WSJF Opportunity Enablement*\n- Component: `pint-component-alerting`\n- Tier: 2\n- Opportunity Enablement: 8\n\nReason: Opportunity Enablement is derived from component tier.","2026-01-14T06:11:53.254Z"],["3808141","PIF-2083","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Auto-set WSJF Opportunity Enablement*\n- Component: `pint-component-alerting`\n- Tier: 2\n- Opportunity Enablement: 8\n\nReason: Opportunity Enablement is derived from component tier.","2026-01-14T06:11:55.140Z"],["3808142","PFI-832752","PFI","ugne.guigaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Ugnė Guigaitė","Re-sent payout","2026-01-14T06:13:19.409Z"],["3808144","LSS-56393","LSS","keoagile.malakalaka@bolt.eu","Keoagile Malakalaka","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] , conversations about process and refunds have begun regarding these incidents with [~accountid:5b161c006256d01ad54eb09a] and [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] I am happy to align and support where needed when it comes to privacy. \n\n[~accountid:712020:376f7d25-47fd-46e7-ba19-ca9cb0fe977e] , please investigate and provide feedback as soon as possible. Thank you. ","2026-01-14T06:17:34.225Z"],["3808145","PIF-2150","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 9\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is overall well-defined and connects with the platform team objectives. To improve clarity, more specific examples or scenarios could be included regarding how the change will be operationally different from current practices, along with potential edge cases or exceptions that need to be handled. Additionally, providing more specific, measurable criteria for 'clear distinction' could enhance the acceptance criteria quality.","2026-01-14T06:17:37.725Z"],["3808146","PIF-2154","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 9\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: The user story can be improved by clearly defining the success metrics and performance benchmarks. Specify how successful synchronization will be measured (e.g., percentage of successful updates, error rates) and detail any specific performance requirements. Additionally, include more information on how the synchronization process will be monitored and any notifications or logging needed in case of failures.","2026-01-14T06:17:42.547Z"],["3808147","PIF-2121","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 9\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is generally well-defined, but the acceptance criteria could benefit from more specificity. Consider outlining exactly how the notification should be delivered to the user (e.g., console log message, system alert, etc.). Additionally, defining success metrics, such as how quickly the notification should trigger or clarifying what 'notified' means in a measurable context, would strengthen the acceptance criteria. Including performance benchmarks could also help in more precisely guiding implementation and testing.","2026-01-14T06:17:47.164Z"],["3808148","DSR-3081","DSR","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","Solving - No reply from user","2026-01-14T06:19:38.430Z"],["3808154","DSR-3101","DSR","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","Solving - No reply from user","2026-01-14T06:29:04.044Z"],["3808156","PIF-2113","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: The story is well-structured with a clear summary and description, effectively explaining the problem and context. To enhance clarity, it would be helpful to elaborate further on what the 'Builder's API' entails and explicitly define key fields in the 'machine-readable format' for the deployment configs within the acceptance criteria. Additionally, consider specifying performance benchmarks or success metrics that quantify the efficiency of retrieving deployment configurations through the API.","2026-01-14T06:33:44.049Z"],["3808157","PIF-2107","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 9\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: To improve clarity and acceptance criteria quality, the story should specify which 'important parameters' are expected to be included in the dashboard for it to be informative. Additionally, clarify what constitutes 'not functioning normally' to ensure measurable outcomes.","2026-01-14T06:33:47.415Z"],["3808158","PIF-2100","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 9\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is generally well-crafted with clear motivation and objectives. However, to improve clarity and acceptance criteria, it could benefit from specifying the types of AWS failures to simulate (for instance, network timeouts, service unavailability, or throttling). Additionally, incorporate more precise conditions on what constitutes successful error handling of these AWS-related failures in the services being tested. Clarifying these aspects would improve the implementation readiness and testability.","2026-01-14T06:33:51.552Z"],["3808159","LSS-61529","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^LT20250114-001 Fleetcom - Bolt Drive LT.docx.pdf] _(348 kB)_","2026-01-14T06:35:20.991Z"],["3808161","LSS-52369","LSS","kristiina.klemm@bolt.eu","Kristiina Klemm","Hi All! [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf]  [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] [~accountid:712020:8a510079-f35e-41ce-8bd4-2649e41767cb] [~accountid:712020:985a985c-b403-41bd-b116-abbf44b22175] We have received Zellis cleaned up version of the redlined draft, please revert with your comments [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oeReVShoHGyRsUya4_KUIxTcPjxAvsSA/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=111055727617137734027&rtpof=true&sd=true].\n\nThanks a lot!\n\n\n\nOriginal email from Zellis:\n\nAs agreed, we have updated the document to reflect the points discussed and have also addressed the remaining key items:\n\n \n\n·         Clause 5.2 (suspension)\n\n·         Clause 10 (limitation of liability)\n\n·         DPA Paragraph 10 (subprocessing)\n\n \n\nThese updates include the uplift to the data protection liability super-cap, which we have secured approval for, subject to agreement on the other outstanding terms.\n\n \n\nTo ensure clarity, we have prepared a clean Word version to resolve prior formatting issues and attached a redline showing changes against the version shared by Bolt yesterday.\n\n \n\nWe would appreciate confirmation that the other terms are agreed in principle, as this will assist us in finalising the business case internally for the proposed break clause, which would be incorporated into the Customer Agreement.\n\n \n\nPlease let us know if you have any questions or require further clarification.","2026-01-14T06:36:46.705Z"],["3808165","LSS-61494","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Dear Legal Ops,\n\nPlease collect via SpotDraft to the attached agreement.\n\nBolt - Ahto\nCounterparty - 林垂穎：Mick9319@gmail.com\n\nShould you have any further questions, please don’t hesitate to reach out.\n\nThank you in advance!\n\n[^[Accessible Fleet] Bolt - Fleet Partnership Agreement Taiwan - (CN trans)_FINAL.docx (4) (95393669-0dad-471e-8c08-687972cf3f54).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T06:43:20.002Z"],["3808168","WFM-9923","WFM","nontando.cele@bolt.eu","Nontando Cele","Hi Marcin,\n\n05 Business South Africa\n\nWe have also been having issues where we filter for business and not see these tickets so I’m not absolutely certain if there is something else to look out for. In the case that the ticket is not in this queue but has business persona and needs our attention. FOr clarity, all these agents are inhouse Tier 2.\n\nPlease let me know.\n\nThank you","2026-01-14T06:45:45.824Z"],["3808169","PIF-2150","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED, ADR_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft emphasizes the enhancement in notification delivery for prelive chaos testing, aligning with both the testing admin and maintainer perspectives. It highlights the contextual need to separate live and prelive notifications and provides clarity to stakeholders. Missing links to component admin panel views, guides, or ADRs are noted with placeholders.","2026-01-14T06:46:01.949Z"],["3808170","PIF-2154","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED, ADR_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft succinctly outlines the new feature and its benefits, making it clear to stakeholders what has been achieved and its impact. The placeholders indicate where additional technical and user documentation might be required to provide further details.","2026-01-14T06:46:08.942Z"],["3808171","PIF-2121","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft is appropriate as it clearly outlines the new feature that notifies backend developers of port conflicts when starting Docker instances, which prevents unnecessary debugging. The exact location in the product where the feature can be checked and supplementary documentation are missing, hence placeholders are used.","2026-01-14T06:46:16.519Z"],["3808172","PIF-2113","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft provides a brief and clear overview of the new feature: a read-only API for accessing deployment configurations in a machine-readable format, highlighting its purpose in preparing for peak loads. The draft is concise, as requested, and highlights the importance of the API feature for engineers. It also notes the potential value of a future enhancement to edit configurations. However, it lacks specific links to the component admin panel view and relevant guides or documentation.","2026-01-14T06:46:24.861Z"],["3808173","PIF-2107","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* The draft clearly communicates the new feature of the dedicated dashboard for app-log monitoring and its importance for visualizing service parameters. It specifies the improved capabilities while noting missing links and guides required for further guidance.","2026-01-14T06:46:32.778Z"],["3808174","PIF-2100","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED, ADR_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft summarizes the introduction of a chaos testing feature for AWS services, highlighting its practical use and potential benefits. Missing information includes where stakeholders can view this feature and where they can find a guide or ADR for its implementation.","2026-01-14T06:46:40.335Z"],["3808175","PIF-2098","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft addresses the need to improve our alerting system regarding Crowdin downtime by implementing a feature that triggers alerts when Crowdin is down. The draft clearly states what has been added and its potential benefits, but requires additional links to relevant guides or technical references.","2026-01-14T06:46:47.175Z"],["3808177","PIF-2083","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft illustrates the new alerting feature that enables proactive monitoring of Persistent Volumes (PV) in Kubernetes by sending disk space alerts directly to the team's support channel. This feature improves operational efficiency by allowing teams to prevent potential outages related to disk space issues. Essential information such as the exact location to view the feature and further reading documentation is missing.","2026-01-14T06:46:55.519Z"],["3808178","CCM-22275","CCM","nigel.janssen@bolt.eu","Nigel Janssen","[~accountid:5acbd98f2bb3112b34c4adeb] Will you take this one?","2026-01-14T06:46:55.834Z"],["3808182","PIF-2098","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 7\n• Relevance: 9\n• Problem Definition: 7\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: The story should provide more context about the specific impact on the translation process when Crowdin is down. Define the current behavior when the service is down and why this needs improvement. The acceptance criteria would benefit from more detail, such as specific error thresholds, what constitutes 'Crowdin being down,' and the expected alert generation process. Consider elaborating on how the current request rate affects the system and user experience.","2026-01-14T06:51:46.301Z"],["3808183","PIF-2083","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 9\n• Accept: 9\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is generally clear but could benefit from additional detail in the acceptance criteria. Specifically, it would be helpful to define what 'almost full' means in a measurable way, perhaps as a percentage of disk usage. This would ensure that all stakeholders have a precise understanding of when alerts are triggered. Additionally, specifying the frequency of the stats population from NJSC would clarify the data refresh rate. These improvements would make the story even more actionable and eliminate any lingering ambiguity about thresholds and scheduling.","2026-01-14T06:51:50.627Z"],["3808184","MICRO-334","MICRO","hannalore.taal@bolt.eu","Hannalore Taal","Thread in Slack: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNZ5V326L/p1767868914348229?thread_ts=1767868914.348229&cid=CNZ5V326L|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNZ5V326L/p1767868914348229?thread_ts=1767868914.348229&cid=CNZ5V326L|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T06:52:01.042Z"],["3808185","PFI-830850","PFI","shaila.sultana@bolt.eu","Shaila Sultana","Hi, [~accountid:712020:1a99e337-a650-4a85-a8ed-f0825a04e850] Can you please have a look and suggest us?","2026-01-14T06:53:15.589Z"],["3808187","DSR-3719","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-14T06:56:21.846Z"],["3808188","LSS-58896","LSS","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] , \n\nThe tax clauses (both withholding and vat) looks okay and that should be the standard process. There is withholding tax on service fees and the client should always pay net of this tax and provide a certificate as evidence of tax payment. From a VAT perspective, Bolt should issue an invoice showing service fee, VAT at the appropriate rate and then amount inclusive of VAT. Please proceed","2026-01-14T06:56:28.692Z"],["3808191","LSS-61531","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^LT20260114-002 United Motors - Bolt Drive LT.docx.pdf] _(365 kB)_","2026-01-14T06:56:43.696Z"],["3808194","LSS-58433","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Ben Strey,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-14T07:00:38.571Z"],["3808195","LSS-58443","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Lucca Carney,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-14T07:00:39.736Z"],["3808196","PFI-830972","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Sheraton Donbosco,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T07:00:54.377Z"],["3808197","PFI-828388","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Polina Racheeva,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T07:00:54.500Z"],["3808198","PFI-826032","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Nikola Osadca,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T07:00:56.236Z"],["3808199","PFI-828109","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Julija Gorskova,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T07:00:56.711Z"],["3808200","PFI-828083","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Ivy Nanyendo,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T07:00:56.842Z"],["3808201","PFI-827507","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 George-Mihai Ghiveciu,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T07:00:57.199Z"],["3808202","PFI-827957","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Orkhan İsayev,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T07:00:57.335Z"],["3808203","PFI-828386","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Huseyn Huseynli̇,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T07:00:57.379Z"],["3808204","PFI-813243","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Nadeem Amar,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 2