5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T07:01:09.116Z"],["3808219","PFI-820416","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Murad Mir Abdullayev,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T07:01:10.262Z"],["3808222","LSS-57542","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432], thank you very much! \n[~accountid:712020:d3fd53e6-f124-4770-a577-b09d6688566f] please find the signed document version below.\n\nThanks everyone!","2026-01-14T07:05:11.135Z"],["3808223","PRODSEC-588","PRODSEC","andres.jogi@bolt.eu","Andres Jõgi","[~accountid:5fca4b937cc1030069d2bae5] agreed, will create a follow-up task to investigate ISS project and to potentially add dependency request ticket type there.\n\nAlthough there is reasoning to have all requested dependencies visible company wide (or at least ENG wide) to avoid duplication and to allow endorsement of requests with larger number of beneficiaries.","2026-01-14T07:05:44.701Z"],["3808224","DSR-3721","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-14T07:06:21.456Z"],["3808225","PFI-832668","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-14T07:06:35.066Z"],["3808226","PIF-2209","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Automated transition to Ready:*\n\nThis ticket has been automatically moved from Clarification to Ready based on:\n- Presence of a WSJF Score\n- WSJF Score set more than the required delay period ago\n\nAny linked clarification tickets have been closed.\n\n*Note:* If this ticket needs a Value Increment, please run vi_generator.py or add it manually.","2026-01-14T07:08:10.901Z"],["3808227","PIF-2208","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Automated transition to Ready:*\n\nThis ticket has been automatically moved from Clarification to Ready based on:\n- Presence of a WSJF Score\n- WSJF Score set more than the required delay period ago\n\nAny linked clarification tickets have been closed.\n\n*Note:* If this ticket needs a Value Increment, please run vi_generator.py or add it manually.","2026-01-14T07:08:17.820Z"],["3808228","PIF-2207","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Automated transition to Ready:*\n\nThis ticket has been automatically moved from Clarification to Ready based on:\n- Presence of a WSJF Score\n- WSJF Score set more than the required delay period ago\n\nAny linked clarification tickets have been closed.\n\n*Note:* If this ticket needs a Value Increment, please run vi_generator.py or add it manually.","2026-01-14T07:08:24.733Z"],["3808229","PIF-2154","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Automated transition to Ready:*\n\nThis ticket has been automatically moved from Clarification to Ready based on:\n- Presence of a WSJF Score\n- WSJF Score set more than the required delay period ago\n\nAny linked clarification tickets have been closed.\n\n*Note:* If this ticket needs a Value Increment, please run vi_generator.py or add it manually.","2026-01-14T07:08:30.215Z"],["3808230","PIF-2082","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft captures the new feature's function and its practical benefit to developers, emphasizing stricter validation rules for robustness. Essential information like the component's location and user guide links is missing, which users might need to fully understand and implement this feature.","2026-01-14T07:09:07.983Z"],["3808231","PIF-2067","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* This draft succinctly demonstrates the key value delivered by the feature. It explains the new capability to receive notifications for failed archive jobs, highlighting the benefit of quicker response times, which is critical for maintaining operational efficiency. The placeholders indicate missing links to the component's location and any guiding documentation.","2026-01-14T07:09:15.713Z"],["3808232","CSDT-936","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","# Build metrics (tasks related above)\n# Add refinements for dimensions counts \n# Looker sync","2026-01-14T07:09:17.802Z"],["3808233","PIF-2064","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: LINK_NEEDED, GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* The draft is appropriate as it provides a concise explanation of the new feature and its benefits. It explains the issue resolved by sharded circuit breakers, allowing for improved reliability when interacting with sharded services. However, detailed information about where this feature can be checked or additional resources like a user guide and architectural decision record are missing, hence placeholders are used.","2026-01-14T07:09:24.225Z"],["3808234","PIF-2047","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED, ADR_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* The draft provides a succinct summary of the new ability for Workflow SDK users to initialize cron jobs during the Bootstrap phase, enabling cron helpers to be generated for comp-test. This is relevant for users needing automation in their workflow processes. The draft correctly does not include specific URLs, but placeholders are used to signal where further information should be provided, such as detailed component views or technical guides.","2026-01-14T07:09:33.315Z"],["3808235","PIF-2082","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Auto-set WSJF Opportunity Enablement*\n- Component: `pint-component-api-generator`\n- Tier: 2\n- Opportunity Enablement: 8\n\nReason: Opportunity Enablement is derived from component tier.","2026-01-14T07:09:34.797Z"],["3808236","PIF-2067","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Auto-set WSJF Opportunity Enablement*\n- Component: `pint-component-data-archiving`\n- Tier: 1\n- Opportunity Enablement: 13\n\nReason: Opportunity Enablement is derived from component tier.","2026-01-14T07:09:37.428Z"],["3808237","PIF-2064","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Auto-set WSJF Opportunity Enablement*\n- Component: `pint-component-njsc-core`\n- Tier: 3\n- Opportunity Enablement: 5\n\nReason: Opportunity Enablement is derived from component tier.","2026-01-14T07:09:39.553Z"],["3808238","LSS-58578","LSS","toomas.parts@bolt.eu","Toomas-Hendrik Parts","Hello\n\nWhat is the status of this request? We need to send the memo/letter to the auditors this week!","2026-01-14T07:11:11.921Z"],["3808239","CSDA-284","CSDA","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Hey, Jose! Since there was no further reply on the ticket, I will close it. In case of any additional questions, please feel free to reach out! ","2026-01-14T07:11:29.345Z"],["3808241","PFI-832686","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still in pending state and has been pending longer than usual; this can happen due to an ongoing compliance review or technical issues on the payment provider’s side. Please inform the partner that we are actively monitoring such cases and respond to any provider requests as soon as they come in—no action is needed from their side right now, and the payout will be processed automatically once cleared. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase—feedback is welcome.","2026-01-14T07:12:22.579Z"],["3808242","PFI-833130","PFI","pimchanok.pipattanakij@bolt-outsource.eu","Pimchanok Pipattanakij","!image-20260114-071141.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260114-071159.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260114-071225.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T07:12:33.137Z"],["3808243","PFI-832698","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was successfully processed (value date 2026-01-05); please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner—if they still don’t see the funds, ask them to check with their bank using the proof. If the issue is about an incorrect/partial amount, please create a ticket for the Billing team, as payout amounts are calculated by Billing.  \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-14T07:12:41.909Z"],["3808244","PFI-832709","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the payment provider; no exact reason was provided, and it will be automatically reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle. If this was an Early Cashout, please ask the partner to try requesting it again. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-14T07:13:15.043Z"],["3808246","PFI-832748","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The latest payout attempt (logged on 2026-01-13) is in rejected status; the bank did not provide a specific reason. Please inform the partner that it will be automatically reprocessed in the next regular weekly cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can request it again. Ask the partner to double-check their beneficiary bank details (IBAN/account name) and that the account is active; they may also contact their bank to ensure incoming transfers aren’t blocked. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-14T07:14:06.414Z"],["3808247","LSS-61041","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Update:\nBolt team discussed this on Slack and agreed to grant consent for Tur Taxi to be reinstated.\nFor now, no actions are required from Bolt’s side.","2026-01-14T07:14:18.612Z"],["3808249","PFI-832752","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. Despite the “VALUE DATE 2026-01-12” note, the latest status shows the payout was rejected by the bank and, unfortunately, no exact rejection reason was provided. Please inform the partner that it will be reprocessed automatically in the next regular payout cycle. If the issue persists after the next cycle, please reply to this ticket so we can review again.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-14T07:14:52.314Z"],["3808250","PFI-832754","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the bank/payment provider; unfortunately, no specific rejection reason was provided in the return message. Please inform the partner that the payout will be retried automatically in the next regular payout cycle (if this was an Early Cashout, they can submit a new Cashout request). If the partner needs funds urgently, they may also check with their beneficiary bank for any potential holds or issues on incoming transfers.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-14T07:15:17.938Z"],["3808252","PFI-832785","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The last payout is still in pending status since 2026-01-07, which is longer than usual; this typically indicates a compliance review or a temporary technical delay on the payment provider’s side. No action is needed from the partner right now—our team is monitoring pending payouts and will ensure it gets released; once processed, it will reflect on the partner’s bank account. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-14T07:15:48.937Z"],["3808253","DSR-3723","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-14T07:16:07.851Z"],["3808254","PFI-832795","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the bank, and they did not provide an exact reason. There is no proof of payment available because the transfer did not go through. Please inform the partner that the payout will be reprocessed automatically in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try to cash out again.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-14T07:16:15.960Z"],["3808255","MM-930","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🟡|The issue describes the task and links a Slack message, but lacks explicit acceptance criteria and details on edge cases or requirements.|\n|Clarity|🟢|The language is clear and the objective is understandable, with a direct summary and actionable description.|\n|Auditability|🟡|There is a Slack message linked, but no additional documentation or references to templates or specs.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is provided in the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add acceptance criteria and specify which templates are in scope.\n* Provide a time estimate.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or template lists for better auditability.","2026-01-14T07:16:37.144Z"],["3808256","PFI-832806","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been pending since 5 Jan and is currently under payment validation (a standard compliance review at the provider). Because it has been pending longer than usual, please inform the partner that a provider-side review or technical delay is likely; no action is needed from their side and we are monitoring and responding to any checks to get it cleared. We will update the status as soon as it progresses.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-14T07:16:42.658Z"],["3808258","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14], thank for raising this.\nCould you please clarify the deadline? Is it Friday (16 January), or Monday (19 January)? \nThanks.","2026-01-14T07:17:04.555Z"],["3808259","PFI-832808","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the bank, so no funds were sent; unfortunately, the provider did not share a specific rejection reason. It will be automatically reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, the partner can try to request it again. If the partner asks when it was sent, please clarify it wasn’t delivered to their bank due to the rejection.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-14T07:17:24.846Z"],["3808260","PFI-832811","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout shows as rejected by the bank, and unfortunately no exact rejection reason was provided. It will be automatically reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, the partner can try requesting it again. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-14T07:17:44.471Z"],["3808262","PFI-832834","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout was rejected because the bank couldn’t route the transfer: the account number and/or bank code in the payout details are invalid. Please ask the courier to correct their bank details (IBAN/account number and bank code) and then request the Early Cashout again; once updated, the next regular payout will also process normally. If they can’t edit the details right now due to a temporary lock/blackout, please ask them to try again after the lock lifts.\n\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-14T07:18:18.093Z"],["3808263","PIF-2082","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 10\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: ","2026-01-14T07:18:33.883Z"],["3808264","PIF-2067","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 10\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: ","2026-01-14T07:18:36.795Z"],["3808265","PFI-832851","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the bank, and no clear rejection reason was provided in the response. Please ask the partner to verify and, if needed, correct their beneficiary bank details (account name match, IBAN/account number, bank code) so the next attempt can succeed; the payout will be reprocessed during the next regular payout cycle. If this was an Early Cashout, the partner can try requesting it again after confirming the details.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-14T07:18:39.445Z"],["3808266","PIF-2064","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 9\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: The user story effectively communicates the business problem of ensuring that errors in one shard do not affect the operations of other shards, maintaining the resilience and availability of the service. However, the acceptance criteria could be more detailed. Consider specifying the conditions under which the CB for shard1 opens (e.g., specific error rates or error types) and the expected response time of the system when switching to another shard.","2026-01-14T07:18:41.839Z"],["3808267","HS-28905","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi again! I can confirm that you have been added to the Vitality health insurance. Your Vitality membership number is 1286138431 which you can use to log into the Member Zone.\n\nIf you want more information about Vitality then you can head to [Confluence|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/ZAKxXw] or reach out to Niall Tierney.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina ","2026-01-14T07:18:43.485Z"],["3808268","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","Hi [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] thank you for looking into this. Sorry about the confusion. Deadline is friday this week as we will have to run through it with our partners in 4x27. ","2026-01-14T07:18:57.227Z"],["3808269","PFI-832890","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the bank, and they did not provide a clear reason (only a generic UPI error code). Please ask the partner to verify and, if needed, correct their payout details (UPI ID, account number, IFSC) and ensure the account is active and able to receive UPI transfers. The payout will be reprocessed during the next regular payout cycle; for Early Cashout, they can try requesting it again after fixing the details. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase; feedback is welcome.","2026-01-14T07:19:05.746Z"],["3808270","PFI-825637","PFI","bhuvaneswari.sanmugam@bolt-outsource.eu","Bhuvaneswari Sanmugam","Any update on this since the status is still pending?","2026-01-14T07:19:10.849Z"],["3808272","PFI-821256","PFI","milosz.jasinski@bolt-outsource.eu","Milosz Jasinski","Hi, any upd?","2026-01-14T07:19:39.925Z"],["3808273","PFI-832891","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The Early Cashout was rejected by the receiving bank (the payment instruction was not accepted), most likely due to an issue with the beneficiary details such as account number/format, bank selection, or the account holder name not matching bank records. Please ask the partner to review and correct their payout details in the app and then submit a new Early Cashout request. If they believe the details are already correct, they can try again, but ensuring the exact legal name and correct account format usually resolves it. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase; please share any feedback.","2026-01-14T07:19:42.459Z"],["3808275","PFI-832901","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed with value date 2026-01-07 (state: finished). Please download the proof of payout (if available) and send it to the partner; if they still do not see the funds, ask them to contact their bank to trace the transfer. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-14T07:20:04.909Z"],["3808276","LSS-60808","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nDouble-checked with the business and all is good to proceed. MapBox will send the signing request via DocuSign to Ahto, with [*signing@bolt.eu*|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] included in CC.\n\nThank you.","2026-01-14T07:20:17.039Z"],["3808277","PFI-832916","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed with value date 2026-01-12. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if funds are still not visible, ask them to contact their beneficiary bank for a trace using the proof. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase—feedback is welcome.","2026-01-14T07:20:22.475Z"],["3808278","PFI-833027","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still pending and has not moved since 2026-01-05, which is longer than usual. It may be delayed due to an ongoing compliance review or technical issues on the payment provider’s side; the Partner Payments team monitors such cases and responds to any requests promptly. Please inform the partner that processing is in progress and the funds will be credited once the provider completes its checks; no action is needed from their side at this time. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-14T07:20:55.739Z"],["3808279","HS-28925","HS","darwin.natapradja@bolt.eu","Darwin Natapradja","[^Employer Attestation Certificate.docx]","2026-01-14T07:21:15.577Z"],["3808281","PFI-833079","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The early cashout requested on 2026-01-05 is still pending with “Payment validation is in-progress.” As it has been pending longer than usual, this likely relates to a compliance/technical review on the provider’s side; we are monitoring it and will proceed as soon as validation completes. Please inform the partner that no action is needed from their side for now, and the payout will be processed and reflected on their bank account once cleared.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-14T07:21:23.572Z"],["3808282","PFI-827157","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Yes - Bolt can’t issue invoices on behalf of restaurants, so the user needs to request them from restaurants separately. ","2026-01-14T07:21:35.868Z"],["3808283","MM-931","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements provided; not enough info for a developer to start.|\n|Clarity|🔴|No content or structure; summary alone is insufficient for understanding scope.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting sources included.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate or original estimate provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-14T07:21:46.392Z"],["3808284","PFI-817572","PFI","evghenii.leanca@bolt.eu","Evghenii Leanca","Hi, any updates on when the changes will apply? It’s been a month already, thanks!","2026-01-14T07:21:50.429Z"],["3808285","PFI-829664","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! In this case, please reach out to the privacy team via BH who can help with downloading the delivery (not food) invoices ","2026-01-14T07:22:57.687Z"],["3808286","CCM-22275","CCM","margarita.hobo@bolt.eu","Margarita Hobo","Thank you [~accountid:5bd98a0abd2c4c2de48b7c7d]! Will do! ","2026-01-14T07:23:20.865Z"],["3808287","CCM-22276","CCM","theeranart.seatia@bolt-outsource.eu","Theeranart Seatia","[^Request training material.txt]","2026-01-14T07:24:33.512Z"],["3808289","PFI-832833","PFI","anzhela.shahbazyan@bolt-outsource.eu","Anzhela Shahbazyan","Hey, thank you for the feedback.","2026-01-14T07:25:44.953Z"],["3808291","BSKT-4346","BSKT","isham.faizal@bolt.eu","Isham Faizal","Rejected in favor of creating some kind of \"Cuisine Page\" for SEO purposes to list the restaurants in a city that provides the cuisine. More details here [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/6965264611/Q4+2025+-+SEO+Implementation+Plan#Content-Improvements|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/6965264611/Q4+2025+-+SEO+Implementation+Plan#Content-Improvements|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T07:26:45.127Z"],["3808294","WFM-9978","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","[~accountid:712020:86fe5543-2da3-4e6f-a318-f35fcc13371b]\r\n\r\nQueues added.","2026-01-14T07:28:10.284Z"],["3808295","LSS-61532","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:63e3ef2dbf837c6893db58e3] Please give me access to the document 🙂 ","2026-01-14T07:29:10.999Z"],["3808296","WDFT-3538","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Local GAAP book is added for PL006\n\nPL006 is added to asset book rules related to Polish Companies \n\n!image-20260114-072944.png|width=1442,alt=\"image-20260114-072944.png\"!","2026-01-14T07:29:49.173Z"],["3808297","LSS-61532","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-14T07:31:07.814Z"],["3808298","PIF-2047","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 7\n• Relevance: 8\n• Problem Definition: 6\n• Accept: 7\n• Suggested improvements: To improve clarity, clarify who 'Apigen' is and what it specifically generates for cron runs. Make the connection between initialization in the Bootstrap and the expected outcomes more explicit. The relevance could be enhanced by addressing why this separation of concerns (moving cron initialization out of the SDK) impacts platform objectives. Acceptance criteria could be bolstered with more specific, measurable conditions, such as how success is determined (e.g., by verifying cron jobs are triggered correctly or compile tests pass). The problem definition should explain why initializing crons in the SDK was problematic and why the proposed solution addresses these issues effectively.","2026-01-14T07:33:34.994Z"],["3808304","HS-28925","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Darwin! Would it be okay if I provided the employment letter with your child’s information on our own template, rather than the one the school has provided?","2026-01-14T07:35:37.097Z"],["3808307","LSS-61536","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","[^Schedule 2_Bolt Technology_Xconnect Services_19.05.2025.pdf] _(853 kB)_\n\n[^Service Agreement_Bolt Technology_XConnect Services_26.03.2025 (1).pdf] _(770 kB)_","2026-01-14T07:38:05.890Z"],["3808308","LSS-61536","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nPolina Novikova has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-14T07:38:07.526Z"],["3808310","LSS-61537","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^CI Myriam Muzzolini.pdf] _(124 kB)_\n\n[^CONF_NACE_FR.pdf] _(315 kB)_\n\n[^Extrait_RCS GARAGE MUZZOLINI.pdf] _(386 kB)_\n\n[^TVA Intracommunautaire.pdf] _(1.44 MB)_\n\n[^EE20260114-001 Used NExt - Bolt Drive EE.docx.pdf] _(342 kB)_","2026-01-14T07:38:59.174Z"],["3808313","WDFT-3545","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","PL006 is added into following rules\n\n* Group – Cash II\n* Group – IC II\n* Group – Other II\n* Group – Provisions II\n* IFRS – Cash II\n* IFRS – IC II\n* IFRS  – Other II\n* IFRS  – Provisions II\n* Statutory – Cash\n* Statutory – IC\n* Statutory  – Other\n* Statutory  – Provisions","2026-01-14T07:40:17.734Z"],["3808314","HS-28913","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:5fedbf726420890141c7ea53],\n\nThank you for raising this! I wil lshare the video with the Pergamin Helpdesk. I hope they will find a quick solution for this.\n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-14T07:40:25.279Z"],["3808317","LSS-61534","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hey [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] - please look into this one, use the guidance provided by [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] and let me know if you want to discuss any aspect of it via Slack. \n\nFrom an Admin point of view, please don’t forget to complete *Vertical*, *Function Selection*, and *Country* fields.\n\nThank you.","2026-01-14T07:41:38.389Z"],["3808318","WFM-9972","WFM","ottomar.meoste@bolt.eu","Ottomar Meoste","requested [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541721]","2026-01-14T07:42:22.396Z"],["3808319","WFM-9972","WFM","ottomar.meoste@bolt.eu","Ottomar Meoste","Hello!\n\n\n\nAccess has been requested, will update you once it’s been approved as well.","2026-01-14T07:42:34.277Z"],["3808320","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","[~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390]\n\nThere’s a better fix for the issue that does not significantly impact maintenance compared to the solution previously shown.\n\nThe solution below does not require glue to be added between the bracket and phone holder.\n\nThey can be separated easily if needed. The clip in the middle and phone holder have to be thrown away since they are merged with glue.\n\n[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] \n\n!image-20260114-073837.png|width=567,alt=\"image-20260114-073837.png\"!","2026-01-14T07:42:43.542Z"],["3808321","RDS-1413","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","Two more things to consider:\n\n* *Feature*: allowing users to rebook multi-stop rides from their ride history. Right now, the experience is inconsistent, and rebooking doesn’t always include the full ride with stops ([discussion|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CKYJD8AC8/p1767883157947309]). This might be handled as part of [#feature-activity-tab-v2|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0A1DRRNVA9] though, I’m not sure.\n* *UX*: The interaction design of adding a stop is broken. I showed this to designers a couple months ago, and the unanimous consensus was that it is very bad. But there were too many issues for devs to fix on duty, so I just recorded them here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/6301152?selectedIssue=RDS-1220|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/6301152?selectedIssue=RDS-1220|smart-link] (the video in that ticket has audio with explanations)\n\nFew other notes:\n\n* About #1, here’s an existing ticket I had in the backlog — maybe can link/merge/delete: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/6301152?selectedIssue=RDS-1189|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/6301152?selectedIssue=RDS-1189|smart-link] \n* About #3, agree with you, and I actually think this headline should have ETA information rather than generic “driving to stop” or “driving to destination” info. If we could add ETA info there, it would improve the experience not only for multi-stop rides but for all standard rides as well. For multi-stop rides, the copy could be:\n** First stop in 4 min\n** Next stop in 8 min\n** Next stop in 5 min\n** [etc]\n** Dropoff in 3 min","2026-01-14T07:42:46.851Z"],["3808322","LO-270","LO","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1bHWWQXr_zC_JIoxSULJ-3kXAmGSyY_sO/edit?gid=1674244241#gid=1674244241|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1bHWWQXr_zC_JIoxSULJ-3kXAmGSyY_sO/edit?gid=1674244241#gid=1674244241|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T07:44:21.103Z"],["3808328","RF-146","RF","afua.tutuwaa@bolt.eu","Afua Tutuwaa-Ampofo","Started  conversation with Dria and Sean to incorporate initiatives in CBTs and country summary tabs","2026-01-14T07:46:17.599Z"],["3808331","PFI-796383","PFI","angela.gray@bolt.eu","Angela Gray","Hello [~accountid:557058:b2aaf2b9-4465-40fe-b31b-1711dbe61946]  , He is still not able to download this invoice, and it will not allow us to manually produce one, too. He needs this for TAX  purposes, so it's important to have the invoices. Thanks ","2026-01-14T07:46:56.679Z"],["3808333","PFI-833121","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Hey, not sure if we can give accurate information on this. \nLooking at the Invoices issued to them, I see it states Momsregistreringsnr.: SE502082296001\nThis is then our Tax identifier in Sweden, at the same time the legal entity used is Estonian, so it could be EE.\nI would ask from the tax team perhaps about this to be 100% sure. [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/TAX/pages/6240534921/Global+Tax+Field+Team|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/TAX/pages/6240534921/Global+Tax+Field+Team|smart-link]  \n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 09.40.09.png|width=278,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 09.40.09.png\"!","2026-01-14T07:48:45.502Z"],["3808334","WDFT-3548","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Bank accounts : DUMMY for prepayments Zenoriah sp. z o.o. and Dummy for Netting Zenoriah sp. z o.o. are created ","2026-01-14T07:49:09.778Z"],["3808337","LSS-61538","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^CI Myriam Muzzolini.pdf] _(124 kB)_\n\n[^CONF_NACE_FR.pdf] _(315 kB)_\n\n[^Extrait_RCS GARAGE MUZZOLINI.pdf] _(386 kB)_\n\n[^LV20260114-001 Used NExt - Bolt Drive LV.docx.pdf] _(335 kB)_\n\n[^TVA Intracommunautaire.pdf] _(1.44 MB)_","2026-01-14T07:50:27.452Z"],["3808338","LSS-59751","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a], thanks for sharing. Did they address our concerns re liability caps? Will we sign their standard terms or a separate MSA?","2026-01-14T07:51:04.388Z"],["3808339","DSR-3725","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-14T07:51:06.460Z"],["3808340","WDFT-3551","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Supplier Group PL006 Suppliers Is Created ","2026-01-14T07:51:13.414Z"],["3808341","CSDA-258","CSDA","polina.fateeva@bolt.eu","Polina Fateeva","Hello [~accountid:5bdc567ddabb7e15b08738ec], amazing - thanks so much! \n\nThe merged view is super helpful, in our case we look to verify whether the refund occurred, and if it was done correctly - this gives that context right away which is perfect. About the first view - don’t have access unfortunately,  please let me know what’s the best way to get this permission 🙏 ","2026-01-14T07:51:17.683Z"],["3808343","WD-21965","WD","dagmar.olesk@bolt.eu","Dagmar Olesk","Thanks Marko! \n\nIt would be a requirement, yes. \n\nOtherwise we may end up in a situation where every 20th journal is above 100k and is approved anyways. \nThis way we won’t be compliant with the requirement that every x journal below 100k is reviewed and approved.","2026-01-14T07:51:59.658Z"],["3808345","LSS-55755","LSS","federico.michelini@bolt.eu","Federico Michelini","hey [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] , as per our Slack discussion:\n\n\n\n* *Appendix 1, Clause 1.a.i.1:* yes we are ok with the wording as commented in the appendix due to fluctuating energy prices we need to leave flexibility\n* *Appendix 1, Clause 3.b:* the reason for deleting was to not limit to Oslo in case of their expansion outside the city, but if it is better to keep some geographical scope even just as “Norway” we can do that -> please let me know\n\nThanks!\n\n","2026-01-14T07:52:40.330Z"],["3808347","PFI-833143","PFI","oluwatosin.akinbolasere@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwatosin Akinbolasere","[^BOLT SERVICES - REMIT.pdf.pdf]\n\n!image-20260114-075057.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T07:52:48.137Z"],["3808348","LSS-57542","LSS","federico.michelini@bolt.eu","Federico Michelini","Thanks all!","2026-01-14T07:53:27.268Z"],["3808350","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Rundeck started at 2026-01-14 09:55\n* [https://r.db.boltint.net/execution/show/139328#nodes|https://r.db.boltint.net/execution/show/139328#nodes] 🚫\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09T8620KLK/p1768377245578169|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09T8620KLK/p1768377245578169|smart-link] \n* [https://r.db.boltint.net/execution/show/139331#nodes|https://r.db.boltint.net/execution/show/139331#nodes]\n\n\n!image-20260114-075350.png|width=970,alt=\"image-20260114-075350.png\"!","2026-01-14T07:53:53.493Z"],["3808351","PFI-828879","PFI","elizabeth.wambugu@bolt-outsource.eu","Elizabeth Wambugu","update please?\n\n","2026-01-14T07:54:02.977Z"],["3808352","LSS-56393","LSS","lawrancetshepo.motsepe@bolt.eu","Lawrance Tshepo Motsepe","The driver has not been compensated yet, so I have added them to the *ZA_Ops_Compensation_Sheet* for processing.","2026-01-14T07:54:48.815Z"],["3808353","MM-907","MM","kristjan.praks@bolt.eu","Kristjan Praks","Duplicate issue: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MM-824|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MM-824|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T07:55:20.412Z"],["3808355","LSS-61096","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nWe need to have some additional licences asap.\n\nIt is $90.36 until 24th of January, sharing here for visibility.\n\nMay you please add legal ops to get this and the renewal Order Form signed?\n\nThanks!\n\n[^Articulate Amendment - ART-1241128 (2).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T07:55:24.071Z"],["3808372","WDFT-3549","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Bolt Accountant role is assigned to Yana Matos and @Kristiine Murd","2026-01-14T07:59:55.806Z"],["3808373","LSS-59845","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:c94f2cba-c25e-4b00-8ef4-2cad9045ee22] ,\n\nPlease see a few edits to the attached Infosec exhibit form for Sentry.\n\nLet us know your feedback.\n\nThank you.\n\n[^Bolt-Sentry MSA 2026 01 13 (Sentry Redlines) (1).docx]\n\n","2026-01-14T07:59:59.418Z"],["3808375","LSS-50776","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hey [~accountid:6215e9ed2d1a9d0069952697]  — this is fine, provided (i) the consent wording we recommended is used, and (ii) you’re comfortable that the survey tool and the storage location for responses are appropriately secure.\n\nA reminder that you remain independently responsible for the respondent data end-to-end. I recommend you test the survey configuration to confirm there is no field or free-text option that would allow engineers to include an email address (or any other directly identifying information).","2026-01-14T08:00:39.016Z"],["3808379","CSDT-954","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Link to board: [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/boards/1760|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/boards/1760]\nShared for review with the team: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C067TB84C1G/p1768377795136589|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C067TB84C1G/p1768377795136589]","2026-01-14T08:01:35.254Z"],["3808380","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Ad hoc solution to prevent the phone holder from rotating.\n\nAdd *Ethyl-2-cyanoacrylate* (Wuerth super glue) between the clip and the top of the phone holder. Clean any glue residue after application.\n\nThis method preserves maintenance, unlike the previous version where glue was applied between the holder and plastic bracket. All components can be separated, except for the clip and phone holder, which are fixed with glue.[~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390] \n\n|!image-20260114-073837 (2b08c9fe-34aa-4aac-ad02-fcbc2a2481fe).png|width=468,alt=\"image-20260114-073837.png\"!|!1207bd5f6e31a1e403e717b80d52fe34-20260114-084144.jpg|width=292,alt=\"1207bd5f6e31a1e403e717b80d52fe34-20260114-084144.jpg\"!|!4b70fa0e07826a92614fe3a0c5c1b260.mp4|width=446,alt=\"4b70fa0e07826a92614fe3a0c5c1b260.mp4\"!|","2026-01-14T08:01:48.565Z"],["3808384","PFI-833145","PFI","obozna.oleksandrivna@bolt.eu","Kateryna Obozna","[^7Угода_щодо_виконання_доручення Заповнена_signed (5).pdf]","2026-01-14T08:02:11.264Z"],["3808385","PFI-833146","PFI","kosisochukwu.ochuaka@bolt-outsource.eu","Kosisochukwu Ochuaka","!image-20260114-080152.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T08:02:17.124Z"],["3808386","MM-932","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements are provided; only a summary exists.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The summary is understandable but lacks detail and context.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting information are present.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate or original estimate is provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-14T08:02:22.819Z"],["3808390","RIDE-594","RIDE","laura.nurmela@bolt.eu","Laura Nurmela","[~accountid:712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] Yes, since the scope of the project is legal evaluation for now, then currently finance doesn’t need to be involved. If the project moves to implementation, then we’d need to create a new epic. ","2026-01-14T08:03:07.804Z"],["3808401","BR-4056","BR","arsen.ali@bolt.eu","Arsen Ali","tax-engine autoscaling is configured.","2026-01-14T08:05:09.492Z"],["3808404","PIF-2047","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Automated transition to Ready:*\n\nThis ticket has been automatically moved from Clarification to Ready based on:\n- Presence of a WSJF Score\n- WSJF Score set more than the required delay period ago\n\nAny linked clarification tickets have been closed.\n\n*Note:* If this ticket needs a Value Increment, please run vi_generator.py or add it manually.","2026-01-14T08:06:29.652Z"],["3808406","PFI-833147","PFI","elmar.agabeyov@bolt.eu","Elmar Agabeyov","[^Manual payout's W3.csv]","2026-01-14T08:06:36.910Z"],["3808407","PIF-2041","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Auto-set WSJF Opportunity Enablement*\n- Component: `pint-component-admin-panel`\n- Tier: 4\n- Opportunity Enablement: 3\n\nReason: Opportunity Enablement is derived from component tier.","2026-01-14T08:07:10.095Z"],["3808409","EBIKE1-322","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] Maybe not but also we haven’t got any feedback from the street. Let’s observe the situation in Barcelona and see the situation.","2026-01-14T08:08:01.487Z"],["3808412","DBRE-8599","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Upscale ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8409|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8409|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T08:08:12.587Z"],["3808413","PIF-2041","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* The draft concisely explains the new feature addition, highlighting its significance in improving user experience by optimizing screen space and enhancing form usability. The absence of direct URLs is mitigated by using placeholders to indicate where more detailed information should be provided. Missing links include where stakeholders can find the updated Admin Panel view and additional documentation or guides.","2026-01-14T08:08:14.763Z"],["3808415","LSS-61329","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","h3. Jira ticket summary — Greenhouse Talent Matching (Real Talent) disclaimer\n\n{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}\n* Jorick asked whether the existing Recruitment Privacy Notice wording was sufficient, or whether an explicit disclaimer was needed for Greenhouse’s AI-powered Talent Matching (Real Talent) pilot.\n* Alon advised that a candidate-facing disclaimer is required for transparency; relying on the Privacy Notice alone is not sufficient.\n* Due to limited placement options, Jorick and Alon aligned on using the Greenhouse job post “AI Disclaimer” with a “Learn more” expandable section (instead of a separate Bolt website page).\n* *Latest status:* Alon provided the final disclaimer and “Learn more” wording and has already reviewed/approved the text. Jorick to implement the copy in Greenhouse (including inserting the recruitment contact email) and track under Jira LSS-61329.\n{panel}","2026-01-14T08:08:29.791Z"],["3808417","PFI-832864","PFI","volodymyr.gonchar@bolt.eu","Volodymyr Gonchar","Hey Nikolay!\n\nThank you for response. We know that it is automatic that bonuses get deducted. But, as far as I know, it works when bonuses are set up in Admin.\n\nIn our case we calculate bonus for fleet manually and then it is manually compensated.\nWe are interested whether it is possible to net VAT in this case, so our VAT liability will be smaller due to the deduction of this bonus.","2026-01-14T08:10:19.766Z"],["3808418","PFI-832831","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-14T08:10:39.094Z"],["3808419","PFI-832531","PFI","maaike.boogaers@bolt.eu","Maaike Boogaers","Hi,\n\nPlease do not unblock the driver, as the correct driver was blocked.\n\n[~accountid:712020:f9063bf4-7d66-4270-b524-edfd2889c4fe], please let me know via Slack why you believe the driver was incorrectly blocked. Any unblocking requests should always be reviewed and approved by me or Ops first.\n\nWe can remove these unblocking requests accordingly.","2026-01-14T08:11:05.702Z"],["3808420","PFI-832835","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Closing this ticket, seems like duplication of the [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-832831|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-832831|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T08:11:26.972Z"],["3808421","FDBT-4785","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_delivery fails on 2026-01-13 07:00:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs