Kutta","Hey [~accountid:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb] do you know why he had to pay? eLMED is one of Medicovers partners. Does using partner facilities mean that employees always have to pay on the spot..?","2026-01-14T08:12:26.536Z"],["3808424","LSS-57342","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] , reviewed the clauses of the agreement and DP schedule and confirm that we’re fine to proceed :done:  ","2026-01-14T08:12:27.496Z"],["3808425","PFI-830768","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment imported and allocated to C balance https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/77072339","2026-01-14T08:12:38.185Z"],["3808426","LSS-57332","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:5d81df0e9581710c30328f3a] - is support on this still required?","2026-01-14T08:13:04.190Z"],["3808428","CSDT-950","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Enable measure in the mart_support_case_metrics semantic: \n\n* count_cases_with_tier_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n* count_cases_without_tier_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n\nEnable measure in fact_support_case semantic\n\n* count_incoming_escalated_support_cases_utc ✅ \n\nEnable simple metrics: \n\n* count_cases_with_tier_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n* count_cases_without_tier_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n* count_incoming_escalated_support_cases_utc ✅ \n\nEnable derived rate metric\n\n* first_tier_resolution_rate_post_escalation_utc\n** count_cases_without_tier_transfer_post_escalation_utc / count_incoming_escalated_support_cases_utc ✅ ","2026-01-14T08:13:16.501Z"],["3808434","BDB-1534","BDB",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Henno Luts 👋. This is a reminder, that the task is due today or it's resolved but hasn't been moved to \"Done\" status yet.\n\n- If the task is resolved, move it to the \"Done\" status. Or if the task is canceled, move it to \"Canceled\" status\n\n- If the task can't be resolved in the initial timeframe, then make sure that the Project Manager(Team Lead, in case PM is not available), and Customer are notified. And change the new due date accordingly.","2026-01-14T08:15:27.407Z"],["3808436","SREC-371","SREC","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CN6SFK4SW/p1768314334854879|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CN6SFK4SW/p1768314334854879|smart-link] \n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15371|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15371|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T08:15:36.235Z"],["3808438","PFI-832530","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-14T08:16:19.669Z"],["3808440","CCM-22275","CCM","margarita.hobo@bolt.eu","Margarita Hobo","Discussed it with Cheila in DMs, added both Cheila and Goncalo to Bolt Lux up-skill LP","2026-01-14T08:16:52.946Z"],["3808442","PFI-833093","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, unfortunately, it’s not possible to change the language of the documents.","2026-01-14T08:17:03.973Z"],["3808443","PIF-2041","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 9\n• Relevance: 10\n• Problem Definition: 10\n• Accept: 10\n• Suggested improvements: The user story is very well-documented, providing a clear understanding of the business problem and a logical motivation behind the change. However, the acceptance criteria could benefit from being slightly more detailed, such as specifying any exceptions or edge cases in field types if necessary. Although mostly clear, clarifying any potential platform or compatibility constraints could be beneficial as well. Overall, the story is comprehensive and well-prepared for the engineering clarification process.","2026-01-14T08:17:16.388Z"],["3808444","PFI-831414","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, provide an invoice link","2026-01-14T08:17:30.765Z"],["3808446","WFM-9978","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","[~accountid:712020:86fe5543-2da3-4e6f-a318-f35fcc13371b]\r\n\r\nPlease be informed, that the queues are updated.\r\nHave a nice day!","2026-01-14T08:18:05.483Z"],["3808450","WFM-9923","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","[req|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601663] for RH role raised ","2026-01-14T08:18:38.612Z"],["3808451","LSS-53527","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey team 🙂 Getting back regarding this. Can we please first close the topic of driver comms before we move to riders? [~accountid:62a057bc122dfd0069061724] do we need a call to align on the remaining outstanding points?\n\nThis is what we defined as next steps for drivers:\n\n* For transactional comms we flagged as “marketing” based on common sense, but LCM does not want to categorise as marketing: our suggestion is for LCM to rephrase these comms to make them genuinely transactional in tone and substance. See this [+sheet+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1GvLkl71wIXMp9Nh0L6vF7rqkwQ6jJdOQIKNskzIvdWY/edit?gid=1413809671#gid=1413809671], Column K.\n* We will review and confirm the updated drafts. It’s too much effort and too operationally heavy for us to rewrite these ourselves, so we cannot resolve this on our side.","2026-01-14T08:18:44.194Z"],["3808452","LSS-59480","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","Hi there Angela, I hope that you're well! \n\nNo, I have not received any reply via email at all. Is a reply needed for verification? Surely the notice has been sent and we have proof thereof so we are covered?\n\n\nThanks","2026-01-14T08:18:44.234Z"],["3808453","PFI-832308","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","When has the discrepancy occured, I don’t see any months with SF = 159.02\n\n!image-20260114-081834.png|width=657,alt=\"image-20260114-081834.png\"!","2026-01-14T08:19:02.897Z"],["3808455","PFI-831405","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","reissued","2026-01-14T08:19:37.863Z"],["3808456","PFI-833156","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-14T08:19:50.096Z"],["3808457","CCM-22276","CCM","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","Hi Theeranart!\n\nI have assigned the two listed courses to the learner.\n\nBest, Taisiia","2026-01-14T08:19:52.087Z"],["3808458","LSS-60920","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:f2997f1b-74b8-443e-a7cc-28b3ace90931], \n\nFollowing our call last week, do you still need support before sending these comms? As discussed, the contact email should be changed to a generic email to avoid sharing an individual’s email address in a broad communication. \n\nPlease let me know if you need any further legal support or if I can close this ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-14T08:20:25.447Z"],["3808459","PFI-831379","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, verify whether emails has been sent via: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/sent/?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"start_date\"%3A1767774020.831%2C\"end_date\"%3A1768378820.831%2C\"type\"%3A\"all\"%2C\"status\"%3A\"all\"}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/sent/?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_date%22%3A1767774020.831%2C%22end_date%22%3A1768378820.831%2C%22type%22%3A%22all%22%2C%22status%22%3A%22all%22%7D%7D]\n\nAdmin page","2026-01-14T08:20:31.017Z"],["3808461","PFI-831398","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-14T08:21:05.102Z"],["3808463","SREP-1098","SREP","igor.ignatev@bolt.eu","Igor Ignatev","!image-20260114-082131.png|width=654,alt=\"image-20260114-082131.png\"!","2026-01-14T08:21:36.842Z"],["3808464","PFI-832448","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-14T08:21:45.259Z"],["3808465","LSS-61539","LSS","triin.soonkoster@bolt.eu","Triin Soon-Köster","[^Bolt_Letter of contract termination.pages] _(692 kB)_","2026-01-14T08:21:48.851Z"],["3808466","LSS-59401","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:5b7beabdb96a5b58cd3e06ef] - is any further support required here or can I close this ticket?","2026-01-14T08:22:23.577Z"],["3808467","WD-22550","WD","anett.suurkask@bolt.eu","Anett Suurkask","Hey [~accountid:62b1977ddcafd965c5ddc33e] did you made updates only in production? I tested customer invoice creation in sandbox, but this was not working.. please see invoice attached and i’m also attaching last invoice from BG001 for comparison. \n\n[^0000000010 2026-01-14.pdf]\n[^Bolt Operations OÜ Adjustment_ 0000000023 2026-01-12 (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T08:22:57.473Z"],["3808473","LSS-57332","LSS","elmar.agabeyov@bolt.eu","Elmar Agabeyov","Hey [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] .There’s only one thing left for us to do - prepare the Terms & Conditions. If you’ll also be involved in this process, then yes, we’ll need support. If not, thank you very much for your help!","2026-01-14T08:26:07.219Z"],["3808476","BDB-1482","BDB","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] , we need to make improvements in backlight design and mockup. They now shared some additional templates with me. Can you please support [^mockups.pdf] [^backlight.pdf] ?","2026-01-14T08:27:03.579Z"],["3808477","LSS-60664","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:f2997f1b-74b8-443e-a7cc-28b3ace90931], \n\nI cleaned the following document to leave only visible the comments and the outstanding questions: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/15qTFZ8RKr7xIcB6JVNZxDkamW0Cnb6FG5A38jFeCHxY/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/15qTFZ8RKr7xIcB6JVNZxDkamW0Cnb6FG5A38jFeCHxY/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nPlease could you review and confirm?\n\nThank you ! ","2026-01-14T08:27:04.083Z"],["3808480","WFM-9968","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","hi [~accountid:712020:52653792-3c71-4c24-814c-4fa6697f1bbd] & [~accountid:712020:45bb0bab-840a-4442-9766-624581cf64c1], the agents are already assigned to the mentioned queue as primary, which is named 11 REG_UAE_Driver Registrations. \nAre they experiencing any issues accessing tickets?\n","2026-01-14T08:27:59.319Z"],["3808481","BEE-3637","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Hi [@mari-liis.pork|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5b7beb0cc4e4892a5b7889d6], we've discussed this topic with the team and we'd like to clarify if instead of creating dedicated queues, perhaps we can adjust the priorities/SLOs of the voicemail cases? Because the essential problem is that voicemail cases are not being addressed in time, right?","2026-01-14T08:28:24.651Z"],["3808483","WEBSD-1313","WEBSD","daryl.teoh@bolt.eu","Daryl Teoh","Thanks Hector, 2 more changes require your help. The first image in the ms and zh are still in english 🙏 \n\n!image-20260114-082922.png|width=1325,height=908,alt=\"image-20260114-082922.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-14T08:29:40.154Z"],["3808484","HS-28908","HS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","Cześć Sławek, \n\nczy mógłbyś dać nam kontekst, dlaczego musiałeś zapłacić za badania medycyny pracy? Korzystamy z Medicover i to pracodawca płaci za te badania. Dlaczego zdecydowałeś się umówić badania poza placówkami, z którymi współpracujemy? \n\nZ góry dzięki za kontekst, \nEwa","2026-01-14T08:29:56.061Z"],["3808487","WEBSD-1373","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:acac9ebc-221a-4fd9-a729-81559cb66520]  👋 \n\nWe received this ticket. Are you aware of it?\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WEBSD-1473|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WEBSD-1473|smart-link] \n\nPlease let me know your comments.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-14T08:31:08.999Z"],["3808489","PFI-802926","PFI","emre.cakmak@bolt.eu","Emre Can Çakmak","Today, we don’t display the logo for Hopp in other verticals. I guess it makes sense to keep it consistent with other verticals, and hide it for subscription invoices too. Afaik, there is no legal constraint on that.","2026-01-14T08:31:56.428Z"],["3808490","LSS-61500","LSS","anton.schoeps@bolt.eu","Anton Schöps","Hey [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] this is based on Thale’s draft Contract! ","2026-01-14T08:32:18.867Z"],["3808491","WEBSD-1373","WEBSD","fatmakhanim.mammadova@bolt.eu","Fatya Mammadova","yes, we can close this ticket, ticked you sent is valid\n\n","2026-01-14T08:32:32.616Z"],["3808492","DPLC-614","DPLC","michal.konarski@bolt.eu","Michał Konarski","Blocked until I get back from vacation on {{2026-01-26}}. No need to force it now, it’s not a blocker for anything else.","2026-01-14T08:32:38.762Z"],["3808497","WEB-9836","WEB","mohammad.rahil@bolt.eu","Shaikh Mohd Rahil","hey [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] ! could u point to where this exists? i think all references were removed.","2026-01-14T08:34:07.200Z"],["3808498","WEB-9614","WEB","mohammad.rahil@bolt.eu","Shaikh Mohd Rahil","hey [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] , is this time sensitive now that its mid jan?","2026-01-14T08:34:31.646Z"],["3808499","LSS-61422","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e]  , which Bolt entity will be entering this NDA?\n\nI have reviewed the proposed NDA against our standard NDA template and two points I would like to highlight and request to change:\n\n# Definition of Affiliates - The current definition extends to funds and entities that are merely managed or advised by a party (clause 1 (b) (ii)). For confidentiality purposes we need to limit disclosure to group companies under ownership or control. Please request to delete clause 1 (b) (ii) or provide explanation why this is needed in our situation.\n# Retention / destruction of Confidential Information - The draft allows retention in line with general record-retention policies, which for us is too open-ended. We’re happy for each party to retain copies only where strictly required by law or regulatory obligations. Proposal to adjust clause 3(d) so that the Receiver may retain copies of Confidential Information +only to the extent required by applicable law or mandatory regulatory obligations+, with any retained copies remaining subject to the NDA.\n\nPlease share this with the counterparty for their review. Thanks!","2026-01-14T08:35:44.368Z"],["3808500","PFI-833120","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Trying to capture the payment in Fondy. Waiting for the payment to be captured. \n\n","2026-01-14T08:35:50.266Z"],["3808501","WD-22546","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Tax Authority name is: Agencia de Recaudación y Control Aduanero (ARCA)","2026-01-14T08:36:58.761Z"],["3808502","HS-28926","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Aqida! Your employment confirmation letter will be forwarded to you via BoxSign to your personal email.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-14T08:37:08.339Z"],["3808505","LSS-60361","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:6423e317b05b4e3e7dabadb6] - Link re-sent, please ask them to also check spam just in case. Invitation is from SpotDraft","2026-01-14T08:38:02.156Z"],["3808507","WFM-9971","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hey! I added a role for them, please let me know if now they can access","2026-01-14T08:38:16.579Z"],["3808508","PFI-833011","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-14T08:38:52.788Z"],["3808509","WFM-9923","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hi [~accountid:5d831b1c519d370d960d8ba8] . roles was granted and I assigned agents for T2 and Business queues. Please check if everything is working now. If still something is not working please attach screenshot with error If possible","2026-01-14T08:39:08.469Z"],["3808510","LSS-57888","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Hi [~accountid:557058:67e15ba9-0972-4bf7-9e81-826e62fc001b] [~accountid:5f8d84bfddb0df006e611144] \n\nI know that for now you plan to add usual delivery ratings for DineOut providers. However, I want to confirm over whether you want legal team to proceed with the discovery of adding Google reviews under DineOut or even under delivery providers?  Below you can see the info shared with Google POC and their latest answer from December 8th. \n\nIf you are interested then please let me know and we will contact Google again on this topic. \n\nLiisa","2026-01-14T08:39:35.659Z"],["3808511","LSS-58433","LSS","ben.strey@bolt.eu","Ben Strey","Ticket can be closed ","2026-01-14T08:40:14.586Z"],["3808512","LSS-59742","LSS","r.lonander@bolt.eu","Robin Lönander","Hi!\n\nOur consultant has been waiting for over 1,5 month for the contract by now. We need to have it ready to be signed by EOW. \nCan anyone please check up on this so that we can have a contract asap?\n\nRegards, \nRobin","2026-01-14T08:40:15.021Z"],["3808513","DLSP-1999","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","Rejected, because we decided to backfill all 3 months ","2026-01-14T08:40:32.704Z"],["3808514","PFI-813839","PFI","monika.paskeviciute@bolt.eu","Monika Paškevičiūtė","Escalated via Slack to commerce. ","2026-01-14T08:40:42.463Z"],["3808515","SREDESK-7345","SREDESK","yehor.naumenko@bolt.eu","Yehor Naumenko","I’ve just set it to 3 days.\nClosing the ticket.","2026-01-14T08:41:17.660Z"],["3808516","PFI-833166","PFI","hans-kristjan.volmerson@bolt-outsource.eu","Hans-Kristjan Volmerson","[^Miko Marten Mägi 1072926162.pdf]","2026-01-14T08:41:18.370Z"],["3808517","WFM-9920","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! I can suggest that you to reach out to the Experience team/Process ([https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2479/group/3831/create/5974|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2479/group/3831/create/5974|smart-link] ) , as they are they are the ones in chanre of procedures and agree on a process for AZ. After this, ideally it should be added in KB, but this can take more time ,so you can share with te the ticket or the process agreed and I will be able to offer this permission. ","2026-01-14T08:41:21.850Z"],["3808518","HS-28458","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Updated contract sent out.","2026-01-14T08:41:28.622Z"],["3808519","LSS-61500","LSS","anton.schoeps@bolt.eu","Anton Schöps","[^DEHA2016 GmbH - Kickback - DE_Rides_BoltClub_Berlin (2).pdf]\n\nChecked again - all based on thales draft","2026-01-14T08:41:41.492Z"],["3808520","LSS-60920","LSS","maria.montoya@bolt.eu","Maria Paula Montoya","All clear, I will request the modifications. Thank you! ","2026-01-14T08:42:17.286Z"],["3808524","HS-28927","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Kateriin! The contract can be downloaded from [here|https://bolt.box.com/s/vbb5vymhies5j9qlhxgqpw49rm82j2na].\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-14T08:43:34.478Z"],["3808525","DRX-28173","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Sumit Lakra, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-14T08:43:47.535Z"],["3808526","PFI-833168","PFI","anas.birouti@bolt.eu","Anas Birouti","[^EA_20251208_Bolt_Invoice Guests Logistics100_Airwallex.pdf]","2026-01-14T08:43:52.250Z"],["3808528","PFI-826509","PFI","dmytro.lysenko@bolt-outsource.eu","Dmytro Lysenko","Hey team! Please proceed with this request\n\n","2026-01-14T08:44:12.072Z"],["3808529","PAW-14860","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160635\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-14 08:44:14 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-14T08:44:15.087Z"],["3808532","RCE-348","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768380256571509]*{color}:\nNot anymore on develop, no. :disappointed: Did not see this issue before.\n{quote}","2026-01-14T08:44:31.261Z"],["3808533","LSS-61540","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDominika Kozub has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-14T08:44:43.559Z"],["3808534","EBIKE1-419","EBIKE1","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","LOPS ended up replacing the IOT, main splitter cable & ECU. They reported that refitting and inserting battery did not work and waiting did not help. Asked LOPS to send the replaced components back to HQ so we can test the components ourselves.","2026-01-14T08:45:13.660Z"],["3808537","RCE-348","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768380343893509]*{color}:\nBut the cause does seem fairly clear - `MissingData` used for location is falsy, triggering this error.\n{quote}","2026-01-14T08:45:58.205Z"],["3808539","DRX-28174","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Sumit Lakra, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-14T08:46:12.428Z"],["3808540","PFI-833151","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 40 TWD on 15/12/2025, 22:22:01UTC\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 7658373211946979804096 to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 15th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n\n[^Proof of Refund 16-12-2025.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-14T08:46:15.131Z"],["3808541","RCE-348","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Oliver Hilsky [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768380373176049]*{color}:\nIt works now. Not sure what exactly fixed it, I just reset and regenerated everything\n{quote}","2026-01-14T08:46:26.211Z"],["3808546","SAI-1406","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","hey guys :wave::skin-tone-3:\n\n:flag-sa:Is there any chance that AI could read the content below the {{Rejected by external authority}} and pass the next steps to the support case issuer based on a [comms playbook |https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1B8USQCN7d7YXMjzrn1bqjJSwv21_Oo4-oVAn45cDQA8/edit?gid=1809309095#gid=1809309095]we have created?\n\n[Ticket example|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/720372795]\n\n[*Context*|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11jmVhGkf4K0etbdg0KJpnPE95Kbzai-9G12m61ugLtc/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.uwslsok6sh4p]\n\nWhile the root cause is poor driver documents maintenance and that our suspension banner is too general, we wanted to explore whether AI could forward the user to a right direction.","2026-01-14T08:47:25.574Z"],["3808547","WEBSD-1313","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:4305a8c1-0495-4265-b6e0-ae34aff86b22]  👋 \n\nIndeed the images were in English so I changed them already.\n\nPlease let me know if any comments.\n\nregards,","2026-01-14T08:47:25.662Z"],["3808548","SAI-1406","SAI",null,"Slack","[Grzegorz Brotoń|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:f79c0085-d2cb-444c-a121-d9c86bb2bfca] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768231777059739?thread_ts=1768231777.059739&cid=C064FCFAT0S|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768231777059739?thread_ts=1768231777.059739&cid=C064FCFAT0S|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-14T08:47:26.518Z"],["3808549","SAI-1406","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Hey hey, we might do it. When we introduce routine for that issue key, we will try to include it.","2026-01-14T08:47:26.929Z"],["3808550","RCE-348","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Jakovlev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768380437344829]*{color}:\nVery curious. But at least you are not blocked any more by this.\n{quote}","2026-01-14T08:47:29.720Z"],["3808554","RCE-348","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Oliver Hilsky [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768380466004289]*{color}:\nYes, strange. Thank you for your help though\n{quote}","2026-01-14T08:47:57.461Z"],["3808555","LSS-61255","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","HI All, \n\nAdding here the Google docs version as well, so we can review and add comments to the same file\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kMp6CDkEGsEervXTpJ4WHqaQc_6v1VtT/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kMp6CDkEGsEervXTpJ4WHqaQc_6v1VtT/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T08:48:28.064Z"],["3808559","DRX-28175","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Sumit Lakra, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-14T08:48:55.003Z"],["3808562","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* CS cluster: [https://eu-central-1.console.aws.amazon.com/ec2/home?region=eu-central-1#Instances:instanceState=running;tag:Cluster=CS;v=3;$case=tags:true\\,client:false;$regex=tags:false\\,client:false|https://eu-central-1.console.aws.amazon.com/ec2/home?region=eu-central-1#Instances:instanceState=running;tag:Cluster=CS;v=3;$case=tags:true%5C,client:false;$regex=tags:false%5C,client:false]\n* Configuration drift: [https://monitor.boltint.net/d/aespm5sw1a03kb/configuration-drift?orgId=1&refresh=1m|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/aespm5sw1a03kb/configuration-drift?orgId=1&refresh=1m]","2026-01-14T08:49:24.329Z"],["3808565","PFI-833141","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe payment were indeed created by user [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/193637551|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/193637551]\n\nThe payments can be found from here [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments?userId=193637551&tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"userType\"%3A\"user\"%2C\"from\"%3A1752451200.723%2C\"to\"%3A1768435199.723%2C\"userId\"%3A193637551}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments?userId=193637551&tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22userType%22%3A%22user%22%2C%22from%22%3A1752451200.723%2C%22to%22%3A1768435199.723%2C%22userId%22%3A193637551%7D%7D]\n\nThe payment method 49201700*7894 2026-01 has been added under two profiles. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/methods?mask=49201700*7894%202026-01&tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22mask%22%3A%2249201700*7894%202026-01%22%7D%7D|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/methods?mask=49201700*7894%202026-01&tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22mask%22%3A%2249201700*7894%202026-01%22%7D%7D]\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-14T08:50:00.167Z"],["3808566","DBRE-8599","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* order-zaf cluster: [https://eu-central-1.console.aws.amazon.com/ec2/home?region=eu-central-1#Instances:instanceState=running;tag:Cluster=ORDER-ZAF;v=3;$case=tags:true\\,client:false;$regex=tags:false\\,client:false|https://eu-central-1.console.aws.amazon.com/ec2/home?region=eu-central-1#Instances:instanceState=running;tag:Cluster=ORDER-ZAF;v=3;$case=tags:true%5C,client:false;$regex=tags:false%5C,client:false]\n\n!image-20260114-085027.png|width=942,alt=\"image-20260114-085027.png\"!","2026-01-14T08:50:04.526Z"],["3808568","HS-28908","HS","slawomir.klimkiewicz@bolt.eu","Sławomir Klimkiewicz","Hej Ewa \n\nBadania były wykonywane w firmie współpracującej z Medicoverem (Elmed), umówiłem się na nie poprzez infolinię, po wykonaniu badań zostałem poinformowany o tym że rachunek nie został uregulowany i trzeba to zrobić na miejscu.\n\n\nśr., 14 sty 2026, 09:30 użytkownik Ewa Ożańska <[jira@taxify.atlassian.net|mailto:jira@taxify.atlassian.net]> napisał:\n\n{quote}{color:#333333}{color}{color:#999999}{color} \n \n {color:#333333}{color}{quote}","2026-01-14T08:50:28.149Z"],["3808571","DLSP-1985","DLSP","emanuel.peroni@bolt.eu","Emanuel Peroni","courier status and city naming when all items are chosen. _It will be City (All) and courier status (all) you can also see it_ [+_here_+|https://www.figma.com/design/Kj8TTVRtrmjeXy4eXlCVWn/Fleet-Portal?node-id=3182-450105&t=Oog06F4ANyKFb9ZY-4]","2026-01-14T08:51:06.617Z"],["3808573","FX-3582","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dzmitry Andryienka [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768380665318819]*{color}:\nHey <@UCVT712UR> did you have a chance to reach customer on this matter?\n{quote}","2026-01-14T08:51:19.819Z"],["3808574","PFI-833171","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Tried to initiate the capture through the Fondy portal. \n\nCapture is processing. Will check again later. \n","2026-01-14T08:51:23.977Z"],["3808575","DELIVERY-1472","DELIVERY","yehor.burdaiev@bolt.eu","Yehor Burdaiev","26W03: Design critiqued, addressing feedback ","2026-01-14T08:51:58.201Z"],["3808576","HWMISC-836","HWMISC","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390] very thorough description and good ideas. Thanks for taking it up!","2026-01-14T08:52:07.134Z"],["3808578","DBRE-8599","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Downscale to i3en.6xlarge\n* [https://instances.vantage.sh/aws/ec2/i3en.6xlarge?currency=USD|https://instances.vantage.sh/aws/ec2/i3en.6xlarge?currency=USD|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T08:52:27.125Z"],["3808580","LSS-28796","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:c6829626-18d0-4d73-9974-74d1569b4bdf] thank you! I don’t know if this will be the full reimbursement or just parts of it, but I’ve asked our external counsel to confirm, will let you know!","2026-01-14T08:52:46.135Z"],["3808584","LSS-60183","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:642aa1eb7e859baa54f54b06], could you please share the summary of the investigation? namely:\n\n* when the vulnerability was introduced (and fixed, if not on Jan 7);\n* were there any other types of docs accessible other than driver’s license;\n* confirm if the vulnerability could not be exploited by parties outside Bolt.","2026-01-14T08:54:46.011Z"],["3808585","LSS-61382","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:712020:ef6a9562-f9aa-4bb5-a4d5-2b18cc77085b] [~accountid:712020:0c099dc2-02ab-4a79-8eef-b7123d25380d] , lūdzu skatīt [argumentus|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vmYMMZUsD0PdOSZm425IdFddxuBBeVGtee3Jth22hEQ/edit?tab=t.0], kurus varat izmantot, lai aizstāvētu mūsu pozīciju, ka EUR 5 atcelšanas maksa ir pamatoti iekasēta. \nNākamreiz, lūdzu, atrunājiet šādus gadījumus (kad kaut kas neiet pēc plāna) ļoti skaidri ar klientu un iekļaujiet šo info cenu piedāvājumā. Paldies! 🙂 ","2026-01-14T08:54:50.948Z"],["3808588","DRX-28177","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Sumit Lakra, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-14T08:55:13.453Z"],["3808589","LSS-61422","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] ,\n\nBolt Operations OÜ.\n\nI will share your comments with Revolut People.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-14T08:55:28.491Z"],["3808590","BDB-1521","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] so all approved by [~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c], right?","2026-01-14T08:55:31.092Z"],["3808592","PFI-832564","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi [~accountid:712020:7eb363dc-ca9f-4746-abde-3581e042a507],\n\nDriver payout related issues are handled in #commerce-support-partner-payments.\nvia SD they should also have a Billing section, I would recommend reaching out there.\n\nMarten","2026-01-14T08:55:57.368Z"],["3808595","DRX-28178","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Sumit Lakra, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-14T08:56:26.057Z"],["3808596","EBIKE1-322","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","I close this task as it seems that the parameters for the gear fixation pins from Genfo tests are OK and the motor that broke was prototype motor with the pin made with other method than the ones in the mass production. During the Tallinn on field tests we did not have any motor failures.\n\nIf the problem persists during the Barcelona testing, we shall reassess this issue and then we probably have to ask Genfo to take action by making changes to the motor mechanical design.","2026-01-14T08:56:30.710Z"],["3808599","CEBF-1829","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Bug is fixed\n\n!2026-01-14_10-56-24.mp4|width=649,alt=\"2026-01-14_10-56-24.mp4\"!","2026-01-14T08:57:22.972Z"],["3808600","CSDT-956","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Enable measure in the mart_support_case_metrics semantic:\n\n* count_cases_with_tier_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n* count_cases_with_global_to_tier_1_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n* count_cases_with_tier_1_to_tier_2_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n* count_cases_with_tier_1_to_local_ops_pam_bqs_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n\nEnable measure in fact_support_case semantic\n\n* count_incoming_escalated_support_cases_utc ✅ \n* count_incoming_escalated_tier_1_support_cases_utc ✅ \n* count_incoming_escalated_global_support_cases_utc ✅ \n\nEnable simple metrics:\n\n* count_cases_with_tier_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n* count_cases_with_global_to_tier_1_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n* count_cases_with_tier_1_to_tier_2_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n* count_cases_with_tier_1_to_local_ops_pam_bqs_transfer_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n* count_incoming_escalated_support_cases_utc ✅ \n* count_incoming_escalated_tier_1_support_cases_utc ✅ \n* count_incoming_escalated_global_support_cases_utc ✅ \n\nEnable derived rate metrics:\n\n* tier_transfer_rate_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n** count_cases_with_tier_transfer_post_escalation_utc / count_incoming_escalated_support_cases_utc\n* tier_transfer_rate_global_to_tier_1_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n** count_cases_with_global_to_tier_1_transfer_post_escalation_utc / count_incoming_escalated_global_support_cases_utc\n* tier_transfer_rate_tier_1_to_tier_2_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n** count_cases_with_tier_1_to_tier_2_transfer_post_escalation_utc / count_incoming_escalated_tier_1_support_cases_utc\n* tier_transfer_rate_tier_1_to_local_ops_pam_bqs_post_escalation_utc ✅ \n** count_cases_with_tier_1_to_local_ops_pam_bqs_transfer_post_escalation_utc / count_incoming_escalated_tier_1_support_cases_utc","2026-01-14T08:57:32.409Z"],["3808601","EBIKE1-322","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] As we did not discover any problems here in Tallinn, I will close this task and if the problem persists in Barcelona or England, let’s have a look into this problem again. I wrote the conclusion as a new comment.","2026-01-14T08:57:38.001Z"],["3808602","PFI-833180","PFI","arina.gudramovica@bolt-outsource.eu","Arina Gudramoviča","!Screenshot_20260114_104932_Bolt Courier.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot_20260114_104941_Bolt Courier.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T08:57:49.709Z"],["3808604","DELIVERY-1772","DELIVERY","yehor.burdaiev@bolt.eu","Yehor Burdaiev","26W03: Aligning on requirements and started explorations","2026-01-14T08:59:27.272Z"],["3808607","DBRE-8599","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Terraform-main: [https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15374|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15374|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T09:00:43.549Z"],["3808608","PFI-833156","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Adjustments, Compensations*\n* If driver was compensated a while ago in some CS ticket - and this compensation is still not added to driver's balance -> please raise it with Local operations.\n\n*Why?* \nWhen Compensation is created in CS ticket -> it gets added to a csv file. Then local ops take it once a month and submit it into Manual Adjustment tool. They might submit it late, or submitting csv file gets delayed.\n\n\n*Campaign Bonus*\n* If driver did not recevei a bonus for a campaign -> please raise it with campaign team.\n\n*Why?*\nBilling team does not handle campaign setups. So we do not know when, why, how drivers should receive bonuses.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-14T09:00:49.008Z"],["3808611","LSS-61436","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","hi [~accountid:60f2a71843c956007065f2ad] , I have reviewed [Appendix no. 6|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1o85dkVFILOKvT76JV-X-7cJnit6mPdnB/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=105918918024913866295&rtpof=true&sd=true] to the Agreement. As you will observe, I have made a few alteration to it, mainly aiming at aligning its clauses to the Agreement, but also inserted a few comments for the attention of the Provider, to either explain modifications made, or to request clarifications. Provider should be fine with all alterations I have made.\nBest,\n\nAlex","2026-01-14T09:01:28.586Z"],["3808612","PFI-831414","PFI","felicia.oprea@bolt-outsource.eu","Felicia Ștefania Oprea","Hello, \n\nHere is the link for the invoice: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/792106?tab=invoices&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/792106?tab=invoices&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]\n\n","2026-01-14T09:01:47.766Z"],["3808613","SREDESK-7415","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","Hey [~accountid:5fca4ca93b4f5900680dbef2] , \n\nCould you please clarify what kind of access you need? Are you able to access that URL through OKTA? If not, you should contact IT to request that monitor-grafana be added to your OKTA app list.","2026-01-14T09:01:55.789Z"],["3808614","LSS-61543","LSS","victor.stratan@bolt.eu","Victor Stratan","[^Citi KZ - AML PoA.pdf] _(75 kB)_","2026-01-14T09:02:07.223Z"],["3808615","LSS-61542","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-14T09:02:24.377Z"],["3808616","DSR-3727","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-14T09:02:25.691Z"],["3808618","RLONE-589","RLONE","niklas.svegeboe@bolt.eu","Niklas Svegeboe","# *Review process for gathering NPS and update Looker*\n## *Test the NPS flow ourselves*","2026-01-14T09:02:52.832Z"],["3808620","LSS-61450","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Agreement on mandatory protective equipment_Bolt Operations OÜ_FFCS ltd_13.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T09:03:02.972Z"],["3808621","MLC-3291","MLC","yulia.nikitina@bolt.eu","Yulia Nikitina","*W3:* \n\n* app inbox task is [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MTE-1142]","2026-01-14T09:03:41.874Z"],["3808623","LSS-59855","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1] ! I will add what you suggested - to which I agree with - and will reply. ","2026-01-14T09:04:03.270Z"],["3808626","WD-22557","WD","birgit.puksa@bolt.eu","Birgit Puksa","Hello Marko,\n\nI think for now we need to keep also access for [@brita.lubi|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U07H8PV6CF3]. We are still in handover period.  For certifications only I need access.\n\nBR,\n\nBirgit","2026-01-14T09:04:32.868Z"],["3808627","PFI-833139","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Checking with Fondy \n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768381328902959?thread_ts=1768303282.988979&cid=C042VFGJRA5|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768381328902959?thread_ts=1768303282.988979&cid=C042VFGJRA5]","2026-01-14T09:04:38.047Z"],["3808629","MLC-1440","MLC","gabriel.oprea@bolt.eu","Gabriel-Constantin Oprea","h1. Q1 planning review \n\nh2. Progress last Q \n\nLast quarter, we designed and implemented the new automated communications successfully in 15 countries.\n\nh2. Scope for Q1 \n\nThis will carry over for support and on-demand scaling. Effort should not be considerable as things stand but would still take it into account in case things change and we need to scale aggressively.","2026-01-14T09:04:46.659Z"],["3808631","LSS-60361","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Motor vehicle sale agreement_Bolt Services DE GmbH_Cartrade2B GmbH_10.12.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T09:05:07.077Z"],["3808633","BEE-3637","BEE","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Hi [@andri.jasinski|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d807af94f9cf00d60213212]- the main issue is yes that the cases don't make it to our Local OPS in time - they would like to directly recieve these cases, but it's impossible as they're together with the Tier 1. Adjusting the SLO though should already help improve the situation if developing the queues takes more effort :ok_hand: \n\nWould it also be possible to adjust the SLO per market? As for Poland we still receive thousands of empty voicemails every month, which should not be prioritised over actual customer queries","2026-01-14T09:05:11.340Z"],["3808634","PFI-833138","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Checking with Fondy \n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768381328902959?thread_ts=1768303282.988979&cid=C042VFGJRA5|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768381328902959?thread_ts=1768303282.988979&cid=C042VFGJRA5]","2026-01-14T09:05:16.871Z"],["3808636","LSS-61544","LSS","evelin.press@bolt.eu","Evelin Press","[^DECEMBER25_INTRA_FORM_SALES.PDF] _(642 kB)_","2026-01-14T09:06:06.916Z"],["3808640","PFI-833181","PFI","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","[^DOC-20251230-WA0014. (1).pdf]","2026-01-14T09:08:07.005Z"],["3808641","LSS-60199","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Articulate Amendment Quote_Bolt Operations OÜ_Articulate_13.01.26.pdf]\n\nOnce getting this countersigned please send it to [contracts@bolt.eu|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] with a ticket number for archiving purposes and attach the document here for our own records.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-14T09:08:28.113Z"],["3808642","TAXP-791","TAXP","tiiu.albin@bolt.eu","Tiiu Albin","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TAXP-737?focusedCommentId=3777439|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TAXP-737?focusedCommentId=3777439|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T09:08:28.844Z"],["3808643","LSS-54100","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:63e354e3010d35637974a02c] apologies for the delay, we’re checking your request. \n\nI will try to provide the review of the website terms today","2026-01-14T09:08:32.544Z"],["3808644","PIF-2289","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Automated transition to Ready:*\n\nThis ticket has been automatically moved from Clarification to Ready based on:\n- Presence of a WSJF Score\n- WSJF Score set more than the required delay period ago\n\nAny linked clarification tickets have been closed.\n\n*Note:* If this ticket needs a Value Increment, please run vi_generator.py or add it manually.","2026-01-14T09:08:35.407Z"],["3808645","BDB-1482","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey[~accountid:6358f0a501c2ff842c182ef2]  \n\nI have couple of questions regarding this edit:\n\n# This is completely another format. The asset in the media plan is horisontal, but the one you’ve sent is vertical. Also, you’ve sent two files. Could you please clarify which one is correct?\n# And do you have an example of how it looks like in real life? \n# Any deadlines?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-14T09:08:41.257Z"],["3808647","BDB-1521","BDB","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79]- I’ve just kept one of the lines which was validated by the Content Team.\n\n\n“*Move smart after last call.*” sounds a little clunky as a native English speaker (smartly would be better) but I don’t think this works. ","2026-01-14T09:08:48.170Z"],["3808648","PIF-2176","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Auto-set WSJF Opportunity Enablement*\n- Component: `pint-component-finops`\n- Tier: 1\n- Opportunity Enablement: 13\n\nReason: Opportunity Enablement is derived from component tier.","2026-01-14T09:09:17.024Z"],["3808649","LSS-59742","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:712020:ca818823-efac-45fe-ba7d-a6686a5e08b5], thanks for reaching out! \nI’ll do my best to review this agreement this week.\nThank you for your patience!","2026-01-14T09:09:25.281Z"],["3808650","LSS-59855","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:1e9398f2-efcd-4dcd-8ece-28e6f8578e37] !\n\nFirst of all, sorry for the delay in the response.\n\nA couple of clarifications, because I don’t want my earlier message to be read as “benchmarking is fine, no incremental risk”:\n\nIn our view, KPI-gating is not risk-free.\n\nUsing KPIs as eligibility criteria for higher-value categories can increase reclassification risk (it looks like platform-controlled, performance-based access to earning opportunities). We believe it can still be manageable in Malta, but it’s not “no additional regulatory risk” - it’s a business decision with legal trade-offs.\n\nThe main de-risking principles remain:\n\n* Basic categories must remain unaffected (no impact on core access to work).\n* KPIs should be objective, transparent, and visible to drivers in-app.\n* The KPI should be necessary/justified by what the rider is paying extra for (reliability/quality/safety).\n\n\nOn AR, DS, OH, FR - risk differs:\n\n* *Finished rides (FR / completed trips)*: generally the lowest-risk and easiest to justify (experience/reliability proxy).\n* *Driver Score (DS):* medium risk, but can be acceptable if it’s based on objective components and is transparent.\n* *Acceptance Rate (AR):* high(er) risk because it directly touches “control of work allocation” optics.\n* *Online Hours (OH):* highest risk of the list (most “employment-like”). I’d recommend not using OH as an eligibility gate in Malta unless there’s a very strong, defensible rationale.\n\nSo: yes, AR/DS/FR can be used for HVC enrollment; OH is the one I’d push back on most.\n\nAnswering your question re selecting AR as the criterion: yes, apply it only to HVC eligibility (not standard), and ideally with safeguards:\n\n* a reasonable measurement window (e.g., rolling 30 days),\n* clear visibility of AR to the driver,\n* warnings / chance to improve rather than surprise removal,\n* and an appeal/review path.\n\nConcerning Driver Rating, you’re right that invisible metrics shouldn’t be used for eligibility.\n\nBut even once Driver Rating is visible, it’s not zero risk, since it’s still a behavioral/performance metric and can be argued as a control lever. Also:\n\n* ratings can be subjective and noisy,\n* and if the driver can’t understand/improve it (no transparency), it becomes more problematic.\n\nIf you want to use rating, the safer path is:\n\n* rating must be clearly visible, with how it’s calculated explained at a high level,\n* use it as a soft criterion (e.g., minimum average rating over X trips) rather than a harsh gate,\n* pair it with objective metrics like FR and cancellations.\n\n \n\n*Legal recommendation for Malta:*\n\nIf you want the “least risky” set for HVC enrollment in Malta, we would recommend:\n\n* *FR / completed rides* + *low cancellation* (if available) + possibly *DS*\nand avoid *OH*, and use *AR* only if there’s a strong premium-category justification.\n\n\nHappy to review any concrete proposal you’re considering, and also the comms or in-app display text to make sure the rationale and transparency safeguards are framed appropriately.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-14T09:09:30.656Z"],["3808651","PIF-2176","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *AI-Generated Value Increment (Draft):*\n\nA draft Value Increment has been generated and added to the ticket. Please review and update as needed before delivery.\n\n*Note:* The following placeholders need to be filled in: GUIDE_NEEDED\n\n*Reasoning:* The draft is appropriate as it outlines the integration of durable workflows for crons, explaining its purpose and benefit. However, it lacks specific locations and guides for stakeholders to review or understand the feature in detail.","2026-01-14T09:09:34.585Z"],["3808653","SREDESK-7395","SREDESK","yusuf.daniju@bolt.eu","Yusuf Daniju","Hello SRE, is there something I need to do to get this approved?\n\n\nThank you!","2026-01-14T09:10:01.972Z"],["3808654","BDB-1521","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] Let’s please make sure it’s also aligned with [~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c] 🙏 ","2026-01-14T09:10:22.812Z"],["3808655","LSS-61255","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","Thanks [~accountid:712020:46ca1bd4-650e-4217-b42f-78a9deb502a3] !","2026-01-14T09:10:32.823Z"],["3808658","MLC-2448","MLC","gabriel.oprea@bolt.eu","Gabriel-Constantin Oprea","h1. Q1 planning review\n\nh2. Progress last Q\n\nLast quarter, we worked with the content team to create new content and designs for 7 selected automations with the most volume of sends. We managed to implement 2 out of 7: the recurring email for leads and the recurring email for online drivers with 0 times, respectively. Implementation has been slowed down by issues with the new designs, specifically related to the footer.\n\nh2. Scope for Q1\n\nThis will carry over to implement the content that was created for:\n\n* Enrolled in campaign\n* Bonus start\n* Enrolled in bundle campaigns\n\nApart from these, we also have content for:\n\n* No earnings made journey\n* No app installed journey\n\nWe did not decide if we keep these journeys in their current form going forward, but we can still make use of the content in other forms.","2026-01-14T09:11:00.618Z"],["3808659","PFI-832819","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Reissued the invoices: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"created_from\"%3A1768341600%2C\"created_to\"%3A1768428000%2C\"to_agent_id\"%3A156970%2C\"to_agent_type\"%3A\"delivery_provider\"}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22created_from%22%3A1768341600%2C%22created_to%22%3A1768428000%2C%22to_agent_id%22%3A156970%2C%22to_agent_type%22%3A%22delivery_provider%22%7D%7D]","2026-01-14T09:11:06.479Z"],["3808660","WEBSD-1478","WEBSD","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^[CZ] Global Template_ Customer Terms (Rides) [CONFIDENTIAL AND SUBJECT TO LEGAL PRIVILEGE]_FINAL.docx.pdf]","2026-01-14T09:11:06.508Z"],["3808661","PFI-831414","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","reissued","2026-01-14T09:11:46.832Z"],["3808664","PFI-833112","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe user currently has 61.94 UAH on their Bolt balance. \nThe refund was successful. \n\n\n!image-20260114-091139.png|width=1369,height=520!\n\n\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-balance/trxHistory?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"target_account_id\"%3A82208548}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-balance/trxHistory?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22target_account_id%22%3A82208548%7D%7D]\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-14T09:12:02.705Z"],["3808666","BDB-1482","BDB","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] thank you.\n1. It should be horizontal for the backlight (I believe it is about bleeds)\n2. Attached\n3. We need to deliver it eod if we want to have installation next week :(\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 10.10.50.png|width=487,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 10.10.50.png\"!","2026-01-14T09:12:09.596Z"],["3808668","LSS-33312","LSS","kristiina.taube@bolt.eu","Kristiina Taube","Hi [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] \n\nI see that as of 5.01.2026 the Rides T&Cs for Service Providers has been updated according to the latest global template. This eliminates majority of the compliance gaps in the Service Provider side T&Cs. So the issues raised in this ticket are partially resolved. Thank you!\n\nIn addition:\n\n# Issue with the definition of ‘Bolt’ [the entity who is authorised to act as the commercial agent] still remains. The issue is not so much that there are separate sections (i) and (ii), but rather that in the section (i) as platform provider we  still refer to also other Bolt Group companies.  *Why is this general reference necessary in item (i) of the definition?* --> _“ ‘Bolt’ (‘we’ / ‘us’ / ‘our’) means: (i) the owner of the Bolt application and the operator of the Bolt digital platform, namely Bolt Operations OÜ, a private limited company established and registered in accordance with the laws of the Republic of Estonia, with registration number 14532901, having its registered office at Vana-Lõuna tn 15, Tallinn 10134, Republic of Estonia;_ *_as well as the companies within the Bolt Group (local subsidiaries, representatives, affiliates, agents, etc.);_* \n# Passenger side T&Cs - when do you expect to update them? \n\nCould you also clarify, is there currently a separate set of T&Cs for “drivers” (who are not providers of transport services, but use the app)?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-14T09:12:31.700Z"],["3808669","BEE-3637","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Great, thank you for the info :ok_hand::skin-tone-2: Do you know if agents set any ATI (issue key) on voicemail cases specific to voicemail?\n\n [@jana.mariakova|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ee36bc3283ae50ab5999c9e] do you have suggestions towards what should be FRT and follow-up RT for voice mail cases?\n\n{quote}Would it also be possible to adjust the SLO per market? As for Poland we still receive thousands of empty voicemails every month, which should not be prioritised over actual customer queries{quote}\n\nAFAIK not at this moment, however, we can take a look into this. Can you share a bit more details about \"empty\" voicemails? Does it mean calls with no speaking or spamming?","2026-01-14T09:13:05.547Z"],["3808670","PFI-833183","PFI","pareena.klinkaewpa@bolt-outsource.eu","Pareena Klinkaewpa","!image-20260114-090544.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260114-091027.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260114-091036.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T09:13:07.394Z"],["3808673","LSS-59597","LSS","ann.koljalg@bolt.eu","Ann Kõljalg","Hi [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] \n\nThanks! Could you let us know when you expect to complete the review, so we can share it with the landlord?\n\nI just want to highlight again that this is becoming urgent - we’re hiring more people and are already out of available desks.\n\nI’m cc’ing my manager [~accountid:5cf7cf76840f290e75625425]  here as well for visibility.","2026-01-14T09:13:50.677Z"],["3808676","PAW-14068","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-14T09:14:29.140Z"],["3808677","MLC-3744","MLC","mariaadelina.stana@bolt.eu","Maria Adelina Stana","Update 14/01:\nThe communications have been established and prepared for seven cities; however, the team is currently awaiting the central office to finalize the calculation agreements before proceeding with the go-live.","2026-01-14T09:14:32.182Z"],["3808681","BEE-3637","BEE","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","It's an issue with the Polish provider on Sinch side, [context|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C032D4ZGZR6/p1741341957414479?thread_ts=1733737070.862989&cid=C032D4ZGZR6].\n\nThe issue key would depend on the voicemail itself - if its a badly parked scooter report it would be related to it, otherwise something else.","2026-01-14T09:15:37.508Z"],["3808684","LSS-57888","LSS","jevgeni@bolt.eu","Jevgeni Beloussov","Hey [~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2]. Yes, we want to stick to showing Delivery ratings. We don’t want to add Google reviews under DineOut profiles and I am not the person to ask of our plans to add Google reviews under Delivery providers (I haven’t heard of any such initiatives).","2026-01-14T09:16:17.573Z"],["3808685","LSS-59480","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:dc5a9fc0-ec62-423d-a2f8-435f02007669],\n\nThank you for the update. According to the contract, sending notice is sufficiently valid for the purposes of termination.\n\nThe only pending matter from your side would be to *ensure that the amount that Bolt paid as deposit is reimbursed by the contractor*. \n\nI will proceed to close this ticket, but please reach out to us if you have any further questions regarding this matter.\n\nBest,\n\nAngela ","2026-01-14T09:16:23.836Z"],["3808689","PFI-833185","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","[^2025-11-30_2025-12-31_rides (1).csv]\n\n[^LV1526-67.pdf]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.16.42.png|thumbnail!\n\n[^Taxi report December 2025.xlsx (1).xlsx]","2026-01-14T09:17:18.298Z"],["3808691","PFI-833185","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-14T09:17:20.725Z"],["3808692","PFI-833186","PFI","innaaime.kalju@bolt.eu","Inna Aime Kalju","[^251221-1700-087037 (1).pdf]","2026-01-14T09:17:32.861Z"],["3808694","PIF-2176","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Clarity: 4\n• Relevance: 5\n• Problem Definition: 3\n• Accept: 0\n• Suggested improvements: The story lacks a clear explanation of the business problem and why durable workflows are needed for the crons. There is no context provided about the current limitations or pain points with the existing cron setup. It is unclear how integrating durable workflows will impact system efficiency, user experience, or platform scalability. The acceptance criteria are missing, and there are no success metrics or performance benchmarks indicated. To improve, the story should clearly state the problem being addressed, the motivation for using durable workflows, and specific outcomes that will be achieved. Acceptance criteria should be defined with measurable and testable conditions, including success metrics.","2026-01-14T09:17:40.109Z"],["3808695","LSS-61468","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","[~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c], I believe this should have been escalated to you as a LER (? ) - could you please review and advise whether a ticket with your team should be submitted?","2026-01-14T09:18:41.429Z"],["3808697","BEE-3637","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","{quote}The issue key would depend on the voicemail itself - if its a badly parked scooter report it would be related to it, otherwise something else.{quote}\n\ndo you have example of a good voicemail ticket where problem was clear and correct issue key was applied?","2026-01-14T09:19:08.279Z"],["3808700","PFI-833187","PFI","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 10.15.16.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 10.19.07.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T09:19:25.475Z"],["3808702","LSS-61545","LSS","ewoma.jerryogeme@bolt.eu","Ewoma Jerry-Ogeme","[^MoU  CGM & BOLT - After Privacy Review v.2.docx] _(214 kB)_","2026-01-14T09:20:01.847Z"],["3808708","RCE-350","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768382451211909]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@yurii.cherabai>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-350] `Review pull request for bolt-server repository` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-14T09:21:04.445Z"],["3808711","SREDESK-7415","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","He needs editor access on Grafana, granted access.","2026-01-14T09:21:28.433Z"],["3808712","UXA-2190","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","Follow up task to add client_ip parameter: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/UXA-2208|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/UXA-2208|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T09:22:08.295Z"],["3808713","PFI-833190","PFI","hans-kristjan.volmerson@bolt-outsource.eu","Hans-Kristjan Volmerson","!537ccf5e-b245-456a-8ce2-c1e09a854d39 (1).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T09:22:17.876Z"],["3808714","PFI-833190","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-14T09:22:20.031Z"],["3808715","MLC-3892","MLC","mariaadelina.stana@bolt.eu","Maria Adelina Stana","Status Update: Denamrk email has been sent on Dec 15th with follow-up on Dec 22nd\n\n Next on: the following markets on Jan 16 and 2nd follow up comms on Jan 30.\n\nRomania, Croatia, Czech Republic, Slovakia, Estonia, France, Germany, Norway, Portugal, Spain, Sweden.","2026-01-14T09:22:27.999Z"],["3808716","PFI-833108","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThank you for providing the bank statement! \n\nThe bank statement main body does not include the original payment or the refund. \n\nThe refund has been listed under the scheduled payments. \nCapture amount 72 ZAR - refund 18 ZAR = 54 ZAR. \n\nUnfortunately, this is how CAPITEC BANK displays the refunds to the customer. \nWe would suggest the user to reach out to their bank to confirm the refund for 18 ZAR has been issued and it’s listed under “Scheduled payments”\n\n\n!image-20260114-091941.png|width=980,height=186!\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-14T09:22:34.995Z"],["3808717","LSS-61546","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1swy4ghdi5jjfaTkLFVYZNIfRlytiwRPw/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1swy4ghdi5jjfaTkLFVYZNIfRlytiwRPw/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T09:22:39.613Z"],["3808718","PFI-830929","PFI","hans-kristjan.volmerson@bolt-outsource.eu","Hans-Kristjan Volmerson","Made ticket to Billing, thank you.","2026-01-14T09:22:58.192Z"],["3808719","EBIKE1-30","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","putting this to backlog as the only sub task here is in the backlog.","2026-01-14T09:22:59.552Z"],["3808721","DELIVERY-1467","DELIVERY","tomas.jundo@bolt.eu","Tomaš Jundo","26W02: Ready for dev. Need a  grooming with engineers","2026-01-14T09:23:11.272Z"],["3808722","HS-28802","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hey, could you please attach your passport copy to this email as well, as we usually include that to the visa letter too. \n\nDoes a digital signature work for you? ","2026-01-14T09:23:13.658Z"],["3808723","LSS-60984","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41] thank you, did they attach any documents?","2026-01-14T09:23:15.891Z"],["3808724","PFI-833144","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:9e2f1406-ae3b-4949-af4d-db71447ee529],\n\nThere is a high chance that this was indeed a self-order, however, we can not confirm it with 100% certainty. Since there is room for error, then I would suggest proceeding as per usual and closing the PR normally.\nThe patterns will be automatically picked up by our Fraud Engine, and if the driver attempts something more in the future, then the actions will be caught, however, please for now proceed  normally and do not consider this as fraud.\n\nThe “Other Fraud” mentioned, is essentially a simple check due to the over-average cost. The Driver will still be paying us commission, therefore, we are not losing on this action.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-14T09:23:41.938Z"],["3808725","MLC-3396","MLC","mariaadelina.stana@bolt.eu","Maria Adelina Stana","Status update: Setting up comms for the go-live phase.\n\nExpected launch date: first week of February ","2026-01-14T09:23:47.084Z"],["3808728","LSS-61539","LSS","triin.soonkoster@bolt.eu","Triin Soon-Köster","Update: Please close the ticket. We discussed with the provider and decided to wait out the policy to simplify the process for all parties. ","2026-01-14T09:24:16.276Z"],["3808730","BEE-3637","BEE",null,"Slack","Hey, hey,\nRegarding the FRT and RT, I believe this is on the operations and experience team.\nTagging also [@iuliia.vlasenko|https://taxify.slack.com/team/ULN50021L] & [@elizabeth.kivi|https://taxify.slack.com/team/U01DGQASF7E] for Estonia. If any other country from the regions needs to be discussed please let me know and I add more people to this thread.","2026-01-14T09:24:30.062Z"],["3808731","PAW-14858","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @tomekt-bolt\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/pull/3079\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-14 09:24:58 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-14T09:24:58.527Z"],["3808732","LSS-61264","LSS","joao.nunes@bolt.eu","João Nunes","Hi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] \nHere is the information requested.\n- We received the letter on 08/01/2025\n- The [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2296991322/324?orderTryId=2934197040] and [driver|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/7354595?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FMalta], and the initial thread where we asked for footage [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/704369368].\n- Second message [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/719766734]\nAlso, we didn't receive any attachments","2026-01-14T09:25:36.955Z"],["3808733","WFM-9979","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-14T09:25:55.041Z"],["3808735","LSS-61241","LSS","andrezza.demarchi@bolt.eu","Andrezza Perfetto Demarchi","Response sent accordingly ","2026-01-14T09:26:17.179Z"],["3808737","PFI-822451","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo, done. will go live on 01.02","2026-01-14T09:26:23.376Z"],["3808739","PFI-822451","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T09:26:42.977Z"],["3808740","MLC-1744","MLC","gabriel.oprea@bolt.eu","Gabriel-Constantin Oprea","h1. Q1 planning review\n\nh2. Progress last Q\n\nLast quarter, we assessed stakeholders' feedback and plans for the activation stage, along with relevant data that will comprise the basis of what we’re looking to implement going forward in Q1. This quarter, we should decide on the final form of the activation stage and proceed to make changes in the form of optimized existing automations or new automations created.\n\nh2. Scope for Q1\n\nNot fully clear at this moment in time, but the effort could be considerable. The objective at the end of Q1 would be to have the bulk of the work done, with the aim of having a full activation stage revamped in terms of targeting, content, and designs based on the objectives presented on the Confluence page.","2026-01-14T09:27:09.828Z"],["3808741","DO-5787","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Terraform removed\n[https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15362|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15362]","2026-01-14T09:27:44.129Z"],["3808742","WFM-9982","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-14T09:27:50.512Z"],["3808744","PFI-833107","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:63e39f98724a5c79c7bb5d91] \n\nThanks for providing the bank statement. \n\nThe original payment or the refunds shows up in the bank statement main body. \nHowever, it’s listed at the bottom of the statement under Pending Card Transactions. \n\nPlease instruct the user to check with their bank to understand why the funds are still pending. \n\n!image-20260114-092737.png|width=976,height=206!\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-14T09:27:59.378Z"],["3808746","PFI-833163","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:c3203dc1-e02d-4575-a380-8484a28c8b42],\n\nEverything seems to be correct, therefore, we’re dealing with a false-positive in this case.\n\nPlease manually compensate the driver for the loss of their earnings.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-14T09:28:24.224Z"],["3808747","LSS-59597","LSS","mikael.uusivuori@bolt.eu","Mikael Uusivuori","adding [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774]  for visibility as well","2026-01-14T09:28:24.597Z"],["3808749","LSS-28796","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi again [~accountid:712020:c6829626-18d0-4d73-9974-74d1569b4bdf] the Swedish Enforcement Authority has not informed how much the reimbursement will cover, can we still proceed with the details provided below? Thank you!","2026-01-14T09:28:26.978Z"],["3808750","PFI-830438","PFI","vadim.kozjakov@bolt.eu","Vadim Kozjakov","hey [~accountid:712020:fc661671-1d51-4372-9578-b46465bd51ac]what do you think regarding the message above?","2026-01-14T09:28:45.289Z"],["3808751","PFI-817572","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nboth will apply starting tomorrow.\n\nalso 0s can’t be applied to credit limits. The credit limit will be following:\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-14 at 11.27.36-20260114-092738.png|width=644,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-14 at 11.27.36-20260114-092738.png\"!","2026-01-14T09:28:47.004Z"],["3808752","PFI-833193","PFI","oleksandra.pidhorna@bolt-outsource.eu","Oleksandra Pidhorna","!IMG_5347.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T09:28:55.549Z"],["3808753","DRX-28183","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Sumit Lakra, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-14T09:29:02.200Z"],["3808757","LSS-61547","LSS","kerubo.ombati@bolt.eu","Kerubo Ombati","[^Bolt Outside Counsel Billing Policy 2026x.pdf] _(359 kB)_","2026-01-14T09:30:51.539Z"],["3808759","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Translated document (DeepL): [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1lEHQB3bjkpmrtaQsPOsQqJcidjZxtzzG/edit?gid=420706529#gid=420706529|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1lEHQB3bjkpmrtaQsPOsQqJcidjZxtzzG/edit?gid=420706529#gid=420706529|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T09:31:35.559Z"],["3808760","LEG-1353","LEG","maria.ingvoldstad@bolt.eu","Maria Ingvoldstad","[~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2] Hi - It’s in the parent ticket I believe? cc [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03] ","2026-01-14T09:31:42.972Z"],["3808761","PFI-819008","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo, done. will go live on 15.01","2026-01-14T09:32:01.414Z"],["3808762","LSS-61539","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! will close the ticket! Regarding the question about authorized signatories then all directors have been marked here: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1cmDN9QgyyO4DQsLY8uDMpo1GkfRQqleVSVxQ3WM4xL4/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1cmDN9QgyyO4DQsLY8uDMpo1GkfRQqleVSVxQ3WM4xL4/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T09:32:04.882Z"],["3808763","CNT-377","CNT","aleksandra.onutsina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Onutšina","[~accountid:712020:f172cd28-e81b-4011-8942-5ec6b2912f37] , please check the first draft of the assets here: [https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=5422-44775&p=f&t=ig8RMYnEqDM0Zzvn-0|https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=5422-44775&p=f&t=ig8RMYnEqDM0Zzvn-0|smart-link] \n\nPS We’ll be gathering all the LCM assets for Bolt Plus under that same link and the toolkit is underway.","2026-01-14T09:32:13.588Z"],["3808764","LSS-61244","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","hi [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] , I have reviewed the [PoA|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Lh3GtMoggrAeAOXNqacbSYTdeSHmLV6y8ouXWYmUtW0/edit?usp=sharing] attached and made slight amendments to it. However, I do have a concern on whether the PoA should bear an apostille as well (which I think is needed) in view of its possible future use in front of the Romanian authorities:\n”t_o  represent  the  Company  in concluding transactions, as well as in and performing acts related to the Company's daily economic activities i_+*_n front of all state and municipal institutions_*+ _as well as in front of all local trade organisations and in front of private legal persons and natural persons in Romania,_ […]”_._\n\nIs there a different procedure to be followed for obtaining an apostille?\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex","2026-01-14T09:33:05.074Z"],["3808769","LSS-60866","LSS","morenike.lanreologun@bolt.eu","Morenike Lanre-Ologun","Thanks [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] please see below. Thank you:\n\nAnne Babu\n\nFounding Partner \n\n[ababu@abadvocates.co.ke|mailto:ababu@abadvocates.co.ke] ","2026-01-14T09:34:08.782Z"],["3808770","PFI-812086","PFI","pareena.klinkaewpa@bolt-outsource.eu","Pareena Klinkaewpa","Dear payment team,\nCould you please provide an update regarding the commission issue?","2026-01-14T09:35:02.988Z"],["3808771","RNTL-30276","RNTL","aytan.gurbanova@bolt.eu","Aytan Gurbanova","works now, rejecting ticket","2026-01-14T09:36:03.791Z"],["3808773","FX-3630","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768383370269359]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3630] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-14T09:36:22.245Z"],["3808775","PFI-832845","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! From our side, we can’t reissue or reinitiate the refund, especially considering that we do have two successful refund records from our side. Once applied here: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/697179349|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/697179349] and second time applied here for the same case: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/693400369|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/693400369]\n\nFrom my side it seems to be a customer payments issue, but would like to get to the bottom of this. Can you please reach out in #commerce-support-customer-payments and you can tag me there so they can look into this and I can provide the necessary input from billing side where needed? \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.28.50.png|width=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.28.50.png\"!","2026-01-14T09:36:32.677Z"],["3808776","WD-22554","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:712020:0b06ed83-51bc-4df8-b60e-7afb530afe5e] is this access for Workday?","2026-01-14T09:36:35.917Z"],["3808778","HS-28906","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","waiting for mutual agreement doc","2026-01-14T09:37:13.449Z"],["3808779","FX-3630","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Halavan [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768383420777089]*{color}:\nFinal step - increase sorting limit . That should cover companies of all possible size (currently max is ~14k drivers)\n{quote}","2026-01-14T09:37:15.484Z"],["3808780","LSS-60617","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Closing this one as we have a separate signature collection ticket here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61478|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61478|smart-link]. Signatures to be collected electronically as agreed on in another ticket. ","2026-01-14T09:37:22.723Z"],["3808782","PFI-829905","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","{color:#172B4D}Добрый день, коллеги! По РРН 528101694278 528601093297 528601870966 528801745518 уведомляем об удержании суммы, так как документы не были предоставлены в срок. Прошу не проводить возвраты на своей стороне.{color} \n----\n \n{color:#172B4D}{color}{adf}{\"type\":\"expand\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"  \"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"With respect,\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#172b4d\"}}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"  \"},{\"type\":\"hardBreak\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Ramazanov Bektemir Erikuly\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#172b4d\"}}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"  \"},{\"type\":\"hardBreak\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Dispute Resolution Specialist\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#172b4d\"}}]}]}],\"attrs\":{\"title\":\"Signature\"}}{adf}","2026-01-14T09:37:47.307Z"],["3808787","BP-13224","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Tested on feature preview branch [https://ridebooker.prelive.bolt.eu/feature-BP-13219-support-dialog/#/today|https://ridebooker.prelive.bolt.eu/feature-BP-13219-support-dialog/#/today] (using “Business Team Test” reseller)\n\nEmail prefilled with “Open Email”\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 15.55.39.png|width=617,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 15.55.39.png\"!\n\nIssues found during testing:\n\n# *[fixed]* Button overflows the window size in certain languages (Greek and Ukrainian)\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.34.46.png|width=605,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.34.46.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.37.04.png|width=605,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.37.04.png\"!\npost fix:\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.50.26.png|width=593,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.50.26.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.51.17.png|width=593,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.51.17.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.51.30.png|width=593,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.51.30.png\"!\n# *[fixed]* Tooltip missing for Copy button on desktop view (Design criteria “Add [+Tooltip+|https://www.figma.com/design/llcJcgCsRkj5TSlfqSq2W1/Business-UI-Kit?node-id=13856-22913&t=RjsJgYs6uJtj9BrE-4] for desktop hover state for the copy icon button”)\npost fix:\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.51.53.png|width=593,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.51.53.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.51.42.png|width=593,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.51.42.png\"!\n# *[fixed]* “Feedback” needs to be removed (based on design criteria “Remove Feedback from sidebar”)\n# *[fixed]* Spacing and placement of button does not align with design in mobile view\npost fix:\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.53.14.png|width=593,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.53.14.png\"!\n(design)\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.47.53.png|width=321,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.47.53.png\"!\n(currently mobile view - old version)\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.47.40.png|width=593,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.47.40.png\"!\n# *[to be fixed in a separate ticket* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13476|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13476|smart-link] *]*Toast for copy buttons not visible in mobile view currently\n(design)\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.51.17.png|width=232,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.51.17.png\"!\n(current mobile view)\n!Screen Recording 2026-01-14 at 11.53.04.mov|width=605,alt=\"Screen Recording 2026-01-14 at 11.53.04.mov\"!","2026-01-14T09:39:07.433Z"],["3808788","C2-457","C2","janeli.takk@bolt.eu","Janeli Takk","List of batteries sent to repair from Bielefeld \n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/15kLm_VwnjrKB4pAszJUoFn8AT30SIO869JUJl1jjUw4/edit?usp=drive_link|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/15kLm_VwnjrKB4pAszJUoFn8AT30SIO869JUJl1jjUw4/edit?usp=drive_link|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T09:39:06.938Z"],["3808790","BEE-3637","BEE","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","[@andri.jasinski|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d807af94f9cf00d60213212]\n• I want to report a Bolt scooter parking on private property - [*BH*|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/658950560]\n• I want to report disruptive or poor parking - [BH|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/658148188] \nThe issue keys would have to always be added manually - BH doesn't attach anything pre-emptively\n\nWhen it comes to FRT, it should just be above other, regular cases (apart from Safety), so the FRT itself doesn't matter as much as long as our Local OPS receives the case ASAP & it's above others (they have to have the scooter moved within 3 hours of the report made)","2026-01-14T09:39:32.548Z"],["3808791","LSS-58081","LSS","lynda.wamuthiani@bolt.eu","Lynda Wamuthiani","[~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c]  could you please share with me a copy of the standard agreement we have with companies for me to share with Lynx for their upfront review? \n\nThanks. ","2026-01-14T09:39:47.507Z"],["3808795","PFI-833106","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nThe payment the customer is looking for is here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3970470149|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3970470149]\n\nAuthorized amount 27.86 EUR. \nCaptured amount 2.30 EUR. \n\n24.36 EUR seems to be related to an action called void authorization. We have noticed that some bank incorrectly interpret the void authorization message as a debit instead of a credit action. \nWe would suggest the user to confirm with their bank the funds were returned to their account not withdrawn. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-14T09:40:37.464Z"],["3808797","ROPSC-347","ROPSC","riin@bolt.eu","Riin Kotsalainen","Reminder post 14.01 \n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C045B2ATEN4/p1768383400782669?thread_ts=1767961550.750969&cid=C045B2ATEN4|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C045B2ATEN4/p1768383400782669?thread_ts=1767961550.750969&cid=C045B2ATEN4|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T09:40:47.689Z"],["3808798","LSS-60866","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi Lega Ops, please organize signing of the attached document:\n\nCounterparty signatory: Anne Babu, [+ababu@abadvocates.co.ke+|mailto:ababu@abadvocates.co.ke] \n\nBolt: Ahto\n\nThanks! [^ToE_2026_Bolt (1).pdf] ","2026-01-14T09:40:54.028Z"],["3808799","PFI-833193","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team is unfortunately not able to assist with pricing, discount or promo code related questions. \nPricing is decided by the vertical and the customer payments team does not have any impact on it. \nCould you please raise a ticket with the verticals technical support team instead. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2]\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-14T09:40:59.493Z"],["3808800","BEE-3637","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","OK, so we have at least a baseline of 3 hours","2026-01-14T09:41:07.960Z"],["3808801","PFI-833199","PFI","blessing.otih@bolt-outsource.eu","Blessing Otih","!image-20260114-093606.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T09:41:11.230Z"],["3808803","PAW-14861","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @tomekt-bolt\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160638\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-14 09:41:30 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-14T09:41:36.335Z"],["3808805","BEE-3637","BEE","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Yes, but in those 3 hours we have to 1. receive the case 2. send to Local OPS 3. they have to already move it - so the FRT itself has to give Local OPS enough room to 1. identify the scooters location 2. move it","2026-01-14T09:42:04.431Z"],["3808806","FX-3630","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768383726958839]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3630 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-14T09:42:20.333Z"],["3808807","HS-28148","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hey\r\nHave you gotten the document yet?","2026-01-14T09:42:31.374Z"],["3808816","PFI-833200","PFI","chatrawee.saenwerm@bolt-outsource.eu","Chatrawee Saenwerm","!image-20260114-094244.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260114-094251.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T09:43:38.675Z"],["3808819","BEE-3637","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Who's a decision maker when it comes to FRT numbers?","2026-01-14T09:44:02.319Z"],["3808821","PFI-833102","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Checking with Fondy. \n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768303282988979|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C042VFGJRA5/p1768303282988979]","2026-01-14T09:44:22.187Z"],["3808822","LSS-58518","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","*PT model under the discussions currently:*\n\n* *Pharmas are independent sellers & have provider profiles:* Each pharmacy signs its own contract with Bolt (onboarding form as an annex to master agreement) and joins Bolt Food individually, but benefits from the commercial terms pre-negotiated between Bolt and Addo Pharm.\n* *Payments:* Payments for orders are done directly to pharmas, not to Addo Pharma. So usual flow.\n* *Agency fees:* Bolt pays to Addo Pharma only one time signing bonus.  Pharmas pay agency fees to Bolt as usual.\n* *Addo Pharm supports onboarding and integration*, provides pharmacy data (pricing, stock, location), and ensures pharmacies comply with legal requirements for OTC sales.\n* *Bolt applies the agreed commercial terms* to all Associated Pharmacies, provides technical support, and operates the delivery service through its platform.\n* *Addo Pharm has onboarding and performance commitments*, including maintaining a minimum number of active pharmacies.\n* *Pharmacies remain independent sellers*, responsible for product compliance, preparation, stock accuracy and safety obligations, while Bolt handles delivery and client complaint workflows.\n\nDraft of the initial agreement (WIP): [^AGREEMENT Bolt food Vs ADDO PHARM.pdf]\n\nIf we should implement “PT” model for UA then differences, things to consider would be:\n\n* *Selling under LIKI24 storefront:* Pharmas wouldn’t have separate profiles. Sellers would be marked under the product description. \n** How this affects invoicing? Who assembles the orders - pharmas themselves? If yes then how to solve a situation where person orders different OTCs from different pharmas - separate invoices on all order bags? how couriers will collect those - should there be any geo restriction on? If yes, then this should implemented on the Liki store. \n** ","2026-01-14T09:44:39.303Z"],["3808823","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey [~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14], thank you for the clarification.\n\nI have reviewed the file you shared and would like to ask a few questions:\n\n* Could you please clarify the value of this tender?\n\n* We also note that, in the document shared, none of the sections appear to be completed. Are the responsible teams currently in the process of filling it in?\n* Am I correct in understanding that, from a Legal perspective, we are expected to complete only the “Legal requirements” section of this document?\n* Additionally, do we have access to PwC’s Code of Conduct so that we can review and assess it?\n* Finally, were any additional materials or documents provided together with the tender (for example, a draft of the final agreement or similar)?\n\nThank you 🙏 ","2026-01-14T09:44:43.782Z"],["3808825","XP-2738","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","ADDITIONAL TASK: restrict all non-timeslice tests to start/end on the hour","2026-01-14T09:45:15.445Z"],["3808826","PFI-833080","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 53.00 ZAR on 14/12/2025, 10:04:08UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 13th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-14T09:45:16.698Z"],["3808830","LSS-61534","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hi [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] - tagging you for a sense check.\n\nI’ve reviewed the Admin data (recent rides, login sessions, authentication methods) together with the Beehive conversation to understand both user intent and the access pattern.\n\n◾  *From an Admin perspective:*\n• The disputed activity occurred via valid credentials from devices that have been historically associated with the account.\n• Login location and IP patterns are consistent (Johannesburg, South Africa).\n• There is no indication of unauthorised access to Bolt systems, third-party compromise, or a wider pattern affecting other users.\n\n◾ *From a CS / user-intent perspective:*\n• The user contacted support in-app requesting removal of unfamiliar devices and securing their account.\n• CS performed “log out all devices” and provided standard security guidance.\n• The user confirmed resolution and no further suspicious activity has been reported.\n\n❗*One point I wanted to flag:* a passkey was added on 13 Jan 2026 during the incident window. As passkeys can enable persistent access, could you please confirm whether the “log out all devices” action also invalidates/removes newly added passkeys, or whether CS should explicitly remove it as an additional precaution?\n\nBased on current facts, I’m classifying this as an account-level security incident rather than a notifiable personal data breach, pending confirmation on the passkey handling.\n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ","2026-01-14T09:45:49.589Z"],["3808831","PFI-833201","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-14T09:45:57.102Z"],["3808832","PFI-833201","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:712020:cd367b4f-9ca2-4acd-bd4a-af6de2c8976a, 61f3e7cd632452006b8c120b] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T09:45:58.538Z"],["3808834","DSR-3729","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-14T09:46:05.569Z"],["3808836","LSS-61502","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] , can you please also arrange signing of the first agreement - Ugovor o certificiranju \n\n[^Ugovor o certificiranju (1) (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T09:46:15.811Z"],["3808838","BEE-3637","BEE","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Do you mean the attached SLO here? As the FRT will most likely differ from it..\n\nI'd say:\n\n• First response SLO - 10 min (based on other SLO's already set)\n• First response follow-up SLO - 30 min (we will not be receiving any follow-ups from the customer as it's not a regular ticket)","2026-01-14T09:46:32.908Z"],["3808839","LSS-61315","LSS","jelena.glavas@bolt.eu","Jelena Glavaš","Adding proof of payment to have all documents at one place. Still pending signed contract \n\n[^ProofOfPayment (96).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T09:46:37.007Z"],["3808841","WD-22554","WD","yana.matos@bolt.eu","Yana Matos","Hi Magnus,\n\nThis is for Citibank online banking access (with restrictions for\naccountants) to view bank statements etc. The access should be granted\nthrough Treasury or Legal, I believe.\n\nYana","2026-01-14T09:46:38.097Z"],["3808843","PFI-833069","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 76.00 ZAR on 21/12/2025, 11:17:08UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 21st of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-14T09:46:56.165Z"],["3808845","MLC-3821","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","Content approved by PM and ops team, Phase 1 ready to send to translations.","2026-01-14T09:47:22.157Z"],["3808850","LSS-61383","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:93a83d4d-5005-4a53-ad96-dc0c8205bf70], thanks a lot for the ticket! [~accountid:62615f256cb53d006a6a3fe1] looping you in from Tax side, so that we are aligned on this topic from both Legal and Tax side (I understand you have already had a chat with [~accountid:712020:93a83d4d-5005-4a53-ad96-dc0c8205bf70] on this). ","2026-01-14T09:48:06.841Z"],["3808852","HS-28802","HS","tudor.maxim@bolt.eu","Tudor Maxim","Sure, here’s a photo of the passport, I don’t have a copy.\nI believe digital signature works.\n\n!IMG_8410.jpg|width=3024,height=4032,alt=\"IMG_8410.jpg\"!\n\n","2026-01-14T09:48:25.519Z"],["3808859","LSS-59597","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hello [~accountid:5cf7cf76840f290e75625425][~accountid:712020:e81c1984-54f1-46ce-bc81-864b3748de94] ! \n\n* To ensure an efficient legal review, could you please highlight the *key commercial terms* agreed with the landlord, such as rent and other fees, lease term, termination rights, and any service charges, so we can understand where to concentrate our review efforts. \n* Please also flag *any specific arrangements* that should be reflected in the lease agreement.\n* Is there a plan to carry out *any fit-out or renovation* *works* to adapt the premises to Bolt’s operational needs?\n\nLease agreements are usually reviewed jointly by Legal, the Business team, and the responsible Workplace manager who is in charge of coordinating technical requirements, fit-out works, or premises adjustments that need to be contractually reflected. [~accountid:5cf7cf76840f290e75625425] are you directly in charge of this for Finland, or somebody else from your team? 🙂 \n","2026-01-14T09:50:16.877Z"],["3808861","PTWS-2115","PTWS","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","The Google Sheet was updated and reorganised, and the date columns were reformatted so the automation can correctly pick them up. The mappings within the automation were also adjusted to align with the updated column structure.\n\nAfter these changes, the automation was tested multiple times together with Mo and successfully passed all tests. :done: ","2026-01-14T09:50:41.280Z"],["3808866","PFI-830438","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\n{quote}Subjects are obligated to pay VAT on our commission{quote}\n\nno commission occured during that period - so nothing to pay VAT on as I understand.\n\nin such case FO should consult with their accountant.","2026-01-14T09:51:19.254Z"],["3808868","PFI-833050","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Payment pending. Should be resolved after 24 hours. Will check again in the afternoon. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4032252550|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4032252550]","2026-01-14T09:51:30.594Z"],["3808869","PAW-14870","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-14T09:51:37.164Z"],["3808871","DPX-3557","DPX","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","[~accountid:60f2a71a2f97d5006920d5de]  Looks like the fix unfortunately still allows for previously reproduced case:\n[https://kibana-logs.prelive.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/discover#/doc/07282ab0-48a5-11ed-998d-03ff1d825bc9/.ds-logs-nodejs-2026.01.14-002265?id=WNjpu5sBTeoT-qHBmd3k|https://kibana-logs.prelive.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/discover#/doc/07282ab0-48a5-11ed-998d-03ff1d825bc9/.ds-logs-nodejs-2026.01.14-002265?id=WNjpu5sBTeoT-qHBmd3k]","2026-01-14T09:51:49.961Z"],["3808873","L10N-27637","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27636](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27636)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T09:52:11.490Z"],["3808874","L10N-27638","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27636](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27636)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T09:52:13.046Z"],["3808876","L10N-27645","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27636](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27636)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T09:52:16.234Z"],["3808877","L10N-27642","L10N",null