ions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27636](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27636)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T09:52:19.696Z"],["3808881","L10N-27651","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27636](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27636)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T09:52:21.060Z"],["3808882","L10N-27649","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27636](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27636)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T09:52:21.055Z"],["3808883","L10N-27656","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27636](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27636)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T09:52:22.311Z"],["3808884","L10N-27655","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27636](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27636)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T09:52:22.961Z"],["3808887","LSS-61512","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:49595943-fb9f-4151-8a74-b00c57b18f30] ,\n\nI’ve reviewed the letter and that’s OK for me. Let me know if you need anything else.\n\nThank you!\n\nElisabetta \n","2026-01-14T09:52:55.785Z"],["3808888","PAW-14868","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-juri-gavshin\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160616\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-14 09:53:09 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-14T09:53:09.556Z"],["3808889","CAMLE-9813","CAMLE","mykhailo.pohoda@bolt.eu","Mykhailo Pohoda","Most likely flow is:\n• user searches for a ride\n• price prediction is generated without code with key that doesn't have a code\n• user types in a code, gets enrolled\n• but app still sends key without a code (just didn't fetch updated list of campaigns or something)\n• so price prediction without discount is being used\nMost likely we cannot affect app behaviour there, so perhaps easiest way to improve is to invalidate existing price predictions in that case.","2026-01-14T09:53:23.113Z"],["3808890","CAMLE-9813","CAMLE",null,"Slack","[Mykhailo Pohoda|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5e21ae91ac570b0caa8672c1] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C062940V5JB/p1768383693293839?thread_ts=1768382462.484839&cid=C062940V5JB|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C062940V5JB/p1768383693293839?thread_ts=1768382462.484839&cid=C062940V5JB|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-14T09:53:24.244Z"],["3808891","PAW-14862","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160638\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-14 09:53:26 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-14T09:53:26.516Z"],["3808895","LSS-61546","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1swy4ghdi5jjfaTkLFVYZNIfRlytiwRPw/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1swy4ghdi5jjfaTkLFVYZNIfRlytiwRPw/edit|smart-link]  \n\n[~accountid:712020:46ca1bd4-650e-4217-b42f-78a9deb502a3] please find the reviewed NDA \n\nIf all agreed please  ask them to send the agreement to [+ahto.kink@bolt.eu+|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu] and cc [+signing@bolt.eu+|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] (we will not be able to find the request without putting this email in cc)","2026-01-14T09:54:08.780Z"],["3808896","WDFT-3529","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044] !\n\nI got you point, and in fact, you are right, in Statutory reporting assets in PL002 should be recognized at NBV as acquisition cost.\n\nThen and Group/IFRS books we need to adjust the cost and Accumulated depreciation accounts. \n\n[~accountid:639b20bdf78d12c0f471a5e4] [~accountid:6285ef56bd640f0068aeb51b] adding tyou here for visibility , plus what to check with you what is current practice re correcting assets that were transferred intracompany.\n\nSo Kristiine will have to do intracompany transfer of Computers from PL003 to PL002 , which mean that in PL002 these computers will have acquisition cost as their NBV at PL003 at the moment of transfer. So on group level the same assets are “losing” the part of Acquisition cost (in amount equal to their accumulated depreciation at the moment of transfer) and Accumulated depreciation. How do you correct such cases now ? Make manual journal in Group book in acquiring company? If yes, what book code you use for such journals? ","2026-01-14T09:54:13.384Z"],["3808897","LSS-57939","LSS","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Hi [~accountid:712020:7f47c2af-14e1-4206-a795-ac87cb906276],\n\nCould you please get back to me here once you have the time.\n\nGreetings,\n\nPema","2026-01-14T09:54:23.915Z"],["3808898","DRAG101-463","DRAG101","susan.shao@bolt.eu","Cancan Shao","[~accountid:712020:e77ef51b-4584-479b-bc00-b172e7475d2e] The supplier will make new samples for us, but the lead time is 1 week, should we wait for that or look for some other options in the meantime? It seems we only have GUYUAN for labels in our supplier pool right now, but maybe I can look for someone else for more options. ","2026-01-14T09:54:32.550Z"],["3808899","PFI-832850","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Helloo! It’s because there were cash orders (meaning orders where the courier paid in cash at the restaurant for some orders). In December they didn’t have a big order volume and for example during the week 01.12-07.12, they only had one order and that was a cash order, so the  restaurant has the earnings for this order in cash, and we need to deduct the fees from that amount. Usually this doesn’t make the balance go negative if there are other in-app orders, but in this case it did.  \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.53.07.png|width=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.53.07.png\"!","2026-01-14T09:54:41.844Z"],["3808900","LSS-61539","LSS","triin.soonkoster@bolt.eu","Triin Soon-Köster","Thank you! Will highlight it in favorites bar to not lose it. 🙂 ","2026-01-14T09:55:11.761Z"],["3808902","PFI-833085","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nthere are 2 invoices for this ride - pls find here:\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"order_id\"%3A1506459691%2C\"city_id\"%3A150%2C\"system_type\"%3A\"ride_hailing\"%2C\"created_from\"%3A1768265740}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22order_id%22%3A1506459691%2C%22city_id%22%3A150%2C%22system_type%22%3A%22ride_hailing%22%2C%22created_from%22%3A1768265740%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-14T09:55:18.105Z"],["3808903","LSS-61170","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","@ Legal Ops, could you please collect Ahto’s signtaure? Thanks a lot!","2026-01-14T09:55:23.698Z"],["3808904","UXA-2098","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","The problem occurs only for cross-app (2 cases for sms) - for all rider and food apps. Backend is called twice with /profile/crossApp/login. Most duplicate calls happen within seconds, but there are cases of over 2 days distance as well.  All cases (except 3) have different root_hash, suggesting those are separate calls.\n\nThe [backend logic|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/master/src/platform/user/user/main/service/IdentityService.ts#L240] is that when the existing login session is detected based on user_id/phone_uuid, existing session is reused.\n\n!image-20260114-092540.png|width=844,alt=\"image-20260114-092540.png\"!\n\n!image-20260114-092555.png|width=757,alt=\"image-20260114-092555.png\"!\n\n!image-20260114-094202.png|width=361,alt=\"image-20260114-094202.png\"!\n\n\n\n!image-20260114-094227.png|width=361,alt=\"image-20260114-094227.png\"!\n\n!image-20260114-094719.png|width=564,alt=\"image-20260114-094719.png\"!","2026-01-14T09:55:38.834Z"],["3808906","PFI-820777","PFI","innaaime.kalju@bolt.eu","Inna Aime Kalju","[~accountid:712020:03b9dd47-a13b-4694-b2eb-fcd7e49b9c60] i need help","2026-01-14T09:55:59.277Z"],["3808907","DSR-3731","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-14T09:56:06.376Z"],["3808909","PIF-3280","PIF",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the bug!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-14T09:56:40.858Z"],["3808910","LSS-59597","LSS","ann.koljalg@bolt.eu","Ann Kõljalg","Thank you for the quick response [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] .\n\nAll agreed commercial terms are reflected in the lease agreement. Any items we would like to negotiate further are already highlighted in my comments, and the link to those comments is shared above for reference.\n\nRegarding fit-out / renovation works, all current requirements are also listed in the lease agreement. We’ve already had initial discussions with the landlord about the build-out; however, they cannot start any construction works or place orders before the lease is signed.\n\nFrom the Real Estate side, I will be leading the project. [~accountid:634e7fb1fe5ff3752357b3c9]  will support on-site coordination, and as the location is close to Tallinn, I’ll also be doing site visits myself to review the progress of the build-out and ensure alignment.\n\nPlease let me know if there’s anything specific you’d like us to clarify further.","2026-01-14T09:56:49.197Z"],["3808913","LSS-61550","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd], I believe that this relates to your vertical, please reassign the ticket accordingly ","2026-01-14T09:57:10.779Z"],["3808915","PIF-3280","PIF","mateusz.olszewski@bolt.eu","Mateusz Olszewski","Related support ticket - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAW-14682|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAW-14682|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T09:57:21.871Z"],["3808916","MLC-3884","MLC","meeli.tuoppi@bolt.eu","Meeli Tuoppi","*Update:*\n\n* Created emails with the web tool builder based on Figma design file.\n\n*Next steps:*\n\n* Upload images to the web tool library.\n* Upload to Braze.","2026-01-14T09:57:25.094Z"],["3808917","LSS-61255","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:dc5a9fc0-ec62-423d-a2f8-435f02007669] Do I understand correctly that we are moving from the 14th to the 16th within the same building?\n\nAre all commercials checked and approved by you?","2026-01-14T09:57:25.719Z"],["3808919","LSS-61038","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* further follow-up email sent to the claimant. I plan to reject the claim in full via the Government portal by Friday morning.\n\n[^Bolt Mail -   Request for Further Information Regarding Court Claim (Claim No. 763MC252).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T09:58:37.054Z"],["3808923","LSS-58081","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","[~accountid:624d3e6b699649006aea9c98] This [agreement|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1g-PX4a3du1HlWbH3OZBC-XepMHRHYN2k/edit] (also shared in the ticket above) is the standard partnership agreement. I believe this is already shared with Lynx and as per [~accountid:5d1b218591943f0d2ac52db0] 's comment below (date: 19th Nov 2025) they have already reviewed the contract and are okay with the terms. ","2026-01-14T09:59:14.185Z"],["3808925","LOC-4780","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","[~accountid:5ca4a9b9307b0637cbbd81fb]  Find here with your QBR to work on with the team ahead of the Q4.25 QBR. Please do mind the deadline for Data input in 26th {{2026-01-26}}.\n\ncc: [~accountid:625e805e9506d6006fd8ba83]  [~accountid:624abfc1f813eb00692c3c5a] ","2026-01-14T09:59:47.969Z"],["3808926","CNT-348","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","[~accountid:610a6c97ec92ab0070d4d852] Ok, I now got access to it ","2026-01-14T09:59:57.220Z"],["3808927","LSS-60647","LSS","yuliya.shulayeva@bolt.eu","Yuliya Shulayeva","Hi [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] ,\n\nThank you for your reply. \n\nThe client is still coming back and insisting that we pay them. \n\n[~accountid:712020:54af1c3b-f46c-435b-b870-e013cd29eada] would like to get clarity on these:\n\nCan we get 100% confirmation from the legal team that:\n\n# We are not in the wrong here\n# If the user makes a formal GDPR complaint, then we have a defensible position and have no liabilities coming back to us?\n# The user has provided counter arguments on why he thinks we are in breach, so can we get this validated from the legal team one more time? Especially the replies that have come in after Susanna’s final reply\n\nThe last reply from the client:\n\nHello Susanna,\n\nThank you for your response.\n\nI must express my disappointment with your decision to close this matter without addressing the clear GDPR violations and the procedural failures I have repeatedly highlighted. Your refusal to engage further, despite the serious concerns raised, demonstrates a lack of commitment to data protection obligations.\n\nLazarus Davidsson\n\n\n\nThe courier’s use of a private number for customer contact is a direct breach of the safeguards Bolt claims to have implemented.\n\nYour own admission that Bolt cannot fully control how couriers handle personal data contradicts your legal obligations under GDPR.\n\nThe failure to ensure compliance with these safeguards constitutes a clear violation of Articles 5, 24, and 32 GDPR.\n\nYour dismissal of these points without offering any meaningful resolution leaves me with no choice but to escalate this matter.\n\nPlease do not be dismissive or ignore this issue as the first person I spoke with, John, did. That approach was unhelpful and only exacerbated the situation.\n\nHowever, I am willing to consider this matter resolved if Bolt agrees to compensate me with €500 in Bolt credit. I believe this is a reasonable offer that reflects the seriousness of the breach and the inconvenience caused.\n\nLD\n\nI hereby inform you that, unless I receive a substantive response addressing my concerns and a reasonable offer of compensation within 14 days, I will proceed with filing a formal complaint with the relevant data protection authority.\n\nI urge you to reconsider your position carefully. Failing to do so may lead to regulatory scrutiny that could have significant consequences for Bolt.\n\nPlease confirm receipt of this message and that it will be retained as part of your GDPR compliance records. And also the message i wrote to the CEO on linkedin.","2026-01-14T10:00:12.686Z"],["3808928","RDS-613","RDS","andreas.palm@bolt.eu","Andreas Palm","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] We've currently fixed the way loading data is collected and most likely the misconfigured setup caused wrong numbers and therefore a untrue picture of the loading health. As of now we’re collecting the new data to see what's the realistic situation and then deciding further.","2026-01-14T10:00:22.458Z"],["3808931","LOC-4763","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","[~accountid:712020:646a712a-8a6c-463c-961f-5109f9d647a0]  Find here with your QBR to work on  ahead of the Q4.25 QBR. Please do mind the deadline for Data input in 26th {{2026-01-26}}.","2026-01-14T10:00:59.936Z"],["3808933","LSS-57645","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:61b6f8b2599f18006a270ae2] [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Adenda_-_AMCV25-000217_TOBERAS.docx.pdf] [^AMCV25-000118_Bolt_Toberas_14Oct25-09Ene26_Exhib (03cdce26-8c16-424a-b232-b26880414007).pdf] [^AMCV25-000118_Bolt_Toberas_14Oct25-09Ene26_Total (a7a1eaf9-1f1e-4a3f-94a2-387f13a52e9b).pdf] [^AMCV25-000191_Bolt_Dig_15Oct-31Dic_2025_Exhib (8caa4a92-0d96-47da-abb9-5e9b9e1ea833).pdf] [^AMCV25-000191_Bolt_Dig_15Oct-31Dic_2025_Total (c2ed6d89-cca0-447a-a684-0a0bdf532997).pdf] [^AMCV25-000217_Bolt_Toberas_10Ene26-09Ene27_Aena.pdf] [^AMCV25-000218_Bolt_Dig_01Ene-31Dic_2026_Exhib.pdf] [^AMCV25-000218_Bolt_Dig_01Ene-31Dic_2026_Total.pdf] ","2026-01-14T10:01:11.410Z"],["3808934","LSS-61545","LSS","ewoma.jerryogeme@bolt.eu","Ewoma Jerry-Ogeme","Hello,\nPlease this is the email address of the counterparty [countysec@mombasa.go.ke|mailto:countysec@mombasa.go.ke]\n\ncc [chiefofstaff@mombasa.go.ke|mailto:chiefofstaff@mombasa.go.ke]","2026-01-14T10:01:11.026Z"],["3808938","PFI-833207","PFI","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","[^PE-80_2025.pdf]","2026-01-14T10:01:44.313Z"],["3808944","RCE-350","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768384948591099]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-350 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-14T10:02:59.465Z"],["3808945","WDFT-3529","WDFT","katti.raudberg@bolt.eu","Katti Raudberg","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] / [~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044] \n\nThe corrections were booked via manual journals. \n\nIn the seller’s side: Book Code Group Assets \nIn the purchaser’s side: Book Code Consolidation Adjustments\nI will share the detailed journals as an example with Kristiine in Slack\n","2026-01-14T10:03:07.869Z"],["3808947","LSS-59597","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team! \n[~accountid:712020:e81c1984-54f1-46ce-bc81-864b3748de94] thank you for the update! \nI’ll review the agreement today, thanks. ","2026-01-14T10:03:12.236Z"],["3808949","PFI-833186","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, refer to the Customer Payments Team.","2026-01-14T10:03:38.387Z"],["3808951","PFI-833186","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Tech Support] App related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/104\n- [Customer Payments] Payment related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/313\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/314\n[Billing] - Invoice and Balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/315\n[Billing/ Tax Tech]- Invoices not reported (Fiscalized): https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n[Billing/Configuration Changes]- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T10:03:44.342Z"],["3808952","LSS-58896","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","[~accountid:61447d4ac2fda2006a972cbb] thank you for your review. \n\nAccording we can agree to the amendment and proceed [~accountid:5b7bea33409ab057771e428c] ","2026-01-14T10:03:54.606Z"],["3808954","PFI-833191","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, we don’t issue WP invoices for the passes","2026-01-14T10:04:19.505Z"],["3808957","PFI-833208","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-14T10:04:33.440Z"],["3808959","BDB-1494","BDB","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] thank you so much for completing these! I have sent them to the airport accordingly. Kindly keep the ticket open just in case any queries pop up.","2026-01-14T10:04:49.427Z"],["3808960","HS-28148","HS","maciej.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Maciej Bednarczyk","Hi Miina, sorry, I'm adding this task to my calendar. \n\nI will deliver it this evening - sorry for the delay.  \n\n","2026-01-14T10:04:53.400Z"],["3808962","LSS-61502","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^111 Ugovor o certificiranju (1) (1) copy.pdf] ","2026-01-14T10:05:32.090Z"],["3808964","RLONE-820","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Local Operations to test and validate TMS in-app rides functionality.\n\n*Owner:*\nPema Couto Matos\n\n*Sprint / Week:*\nW3\n\n*Acceptance Criteria / Notes:*\n\n* Initial feedback from drivers is positive\n* Data validation pending with support from Shreya\n* Confirm results via data before final sign-off","2026-01-14T10:05:46.434Z"],["3808969","GRWA-1415","GRWA","marina.khanukaeva@bolt.eu","Marina Khanukaeva","Campaign Setup Challenges\n\n* *Branding campaigns*: High volume leads to errors\n** Single analyst managing 20-30 cities across 4-6 countries\n** City-by-city setup for tier 1/2 markets increases complexity\n** Date/time mistakes common when cloning campaigns\n* *Complex tiered campaigns*: Zagreb example shows difficulty\n** Multiple tiers per day require extensive copying\n** Peak hour changes force complete recreation\n** Admin campaigns not sorted by date, making validation hard\n* *CSV validation needed for setup accuracy*\n** Reward amounts vs ASP (typically max 30%, warning at 40%)\n** Time interval consistency checks\n** Cohort overlap detection\n** Period overlap prevention\n\nCost Calculator Issues\n\n* *Data science model unreliable and limited*\n** Doesn’t support per-ride bonus types\n** Requires historical data that often unavailable\n** Error rates significant (Zagreb: predicted 4%, actual 13%)\n* *Custom approaches proving more accurate*\n** Arda’s calculator: 10% variance vs actual costs\n** Uses historical hit rates for market/time/cohort combinations\n** Supports fixed fee, per-ride, commission kickback types\n** Launch markets need separate training (weekly vs 4-week average)\n* *Need for shared Growth team calculator if DS improvements don’t come*\n\nCampaign Design & Analytics Gaps\n\n* *Hit rate estimation challenges*\n** Hard to predict bonus achievement rates with AR/RPH thresholds\n** Current process: iterate weekly from 2% to 6% hit rates\n** Need driver distribution visibility for given conditions\n* *Dashboard fragmentation for supply design*\n** Currently using 3 separate dashboards (Driver AV, Partner, Growth)\n** Unified view would significantly improve efficiency\n* *Supply recommendations underutilized*\n** 8-week average too long for market changes\n** Seasonality not properly accounted for\n** 1-2 week periods more reliable for most markets\n\nTechnical Limitations\n\n* *Polygon support incomplete*\n** Can’t update coordinates in templates\n** Cost calculator doesn’t support polygons\n** Format requirements complex and error-prone\n** Regional setups within cities becoming more common\n* *Launch market cost estimation poor*\n** Weekly growth of 10-20% makes 4-week averages irrelevant\n** Need separate model training for launch vs established markets\n\nNext Steps\n\n* Arda to share cost calculator comparison data with DS model\n* Marina and Andrea to arrange shadowing sessions for setup process\n* Team to compile pinpoint details with examples in shared spreadsheet\n* Consider custom Growth calculator if DS improvements not prioritized\n* Explore unified dashboard solution for campaign design","2026-01-14T10:06:47.217Z"],["3808971","BR-4097","BR",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-14T10:07:24.506Z"],["3808972","L10N-27661","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27636](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27636)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T10:07:25.103Z"],["3808973","LSS-58451","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] , am I right, that the latest version of the contract is not here yet?\n\nThanks!","2026-01-14T10:07:26.163Z"],["3808975","LOC-4799","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c]  Find here with your QBR to work on with the team ahead of the Q4.25 QBR. Please do mind the deadline for Data input is {{2026-01-26}}\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:76c1fb97-5fec-4f3e-b4ac-4d5a4977f048]  ","2026-01-14T10:08:01.283Z"],["3808978","PFI-833211","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-14T10:08:48.053Z"],["3808979","PFI-833211","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:712020:140cd5da-13da-4a76-91d2-dc8a151f6472] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T10:08:49.611Z"],["3808983","LOC-4800","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","[~accountid:5c38a44ad254b55db84d200a]  Find here with your QBR to work on  ahead of the Q4.25 QBR. Please do mind the deadline for Data input in {{2026-01-26}}\n\ncc: [~accountid:625e805e9506d6006fd8ba83]  FYI for Driver community","2026-01-14T10:09:39.373Z"],["3808985","RCE-350","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768385386622999]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-350 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-14T10:09:59.708Z"],["3808986","HS-28934","HS","justyna.stahlberg@bolt.eu","Justyna Stahlberg","!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 11.09.44.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T10:10:12.960Z"],["3808987","HS-28848","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Contract signed by both parties. ","2026-01-14T10:10:17.202Z"],["3808988","WDFT-3529","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","[~accountid:639b20bdf78d12c0f471a5e4] \n\nWe need to do journal on seller side if we sell with the price lower then NBV.  in Kristiine case the computers will be transferred at NBV (no loss on disposal), so we need do correction only in the purchaser, right? ","2026-01-14T10:10:30.583Z"],["3808990","WAVE-229","WAVE","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","So far I have done\n\n* reach out to [~accountid:5ae966399abb77267ba68b16]  and explain Sentry context\n* Create Jenkins key for source maps uploads to Sentry SaaS","2026-01-14T10:11:17.935Z"],["3808992","PIF-3280","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-product-data-management, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-14T10:11:36.367Z"],["3808995","WDFT-3529","WDFT","katti.raudberg@bolt.eu","Katti Raudberg","[~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] In this case, yes - the correction is only needed in the purchaser side","2026-01-14T10:12:21.950Z"],["3808997","WD-22550","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:712020:2261816b-1a2b-4b75-b1dc-d5fce431ad15] , the sandbox is updated too now. Please feel free to test there. 🙂 Let me know incase of any issues. I try to help asap. 😉","2026-01-14T10:12:49.261Z"],["3809000","PFI-832850","PFI","laura.ernestova@bolt.eu","Laura Ernestová","Thank you Ketlin! I thought it might be cause by this, but never experienced the balance to go negative, and I thought there’s an algorithm that should prevent it from happening.\n\n","2026-01-14T10:13:03.151Z"],["3809001","LOC-4801","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango"," [~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] Find here with your QBR to work on with the team ahead of the Q4.25 QBR. Please do mind the deadline for Data input in {{2026-01-26}}\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:76c1fb97-5fec-4f3e-b4ac-4d5a4977f048] FYI for driver community","2026-01-14T10:13:07.900Z"],["3809002","RLONE-820","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Thread in Slack: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08HP71C4ET/p1765879324632069|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08HP71C4ET/p1765879324632069|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T10:13:34.085Z"],["3809008","WD-22554","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:712020:0b06ed83-51bc-4df8-b60e-7afb530afe5e] please submit your request from here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/34|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/34|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T10:14:29.107Z"],["3809009","WD-21831","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","!image-20260114-101437.png|width=764,alt=\"image-20260114-101437.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\ncc: [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] ","2026-01-14T10:14:49.433Z"],["3809010","SREDESK-7395","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","[~accountid:712020:692d366e-16c2-448b-aa6a-c8a95d47e6ef] , we apologize for the inconvenience. We are currently addressing the issue.","2026-01-14T10:15:12.636Z"],["3809012","XP-3046","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","De-activating CUPED for non-timeslice tests and announcing issue until solution released","2026-01-14T10:16:01.370Z"],["3809013","LSS-60915","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342681|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342681|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T10:16:10.328Z"],["3809016","LSS-61398","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","hi [~accountid:61e144f79ee70a0068ec7efd] thanks for reaching out! I am afraid that the ticket raised is not a legal team issue, but rather a tax team issue. In order to ease your job, please see below:\n- dedicated Confluence page for such type of requests: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/TAX/pages/1850245987/TAX+VAT+registration+numbers|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/TAX/pages/1850245987/TAX+VAT+registration+numbers|smart-link] ;\n- in case the above is not useful, please reach out to dedicated tax team through: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/21|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/21|smart-link] .\n\nAlso, in order to avoid further misunderstanding in the future, please reach out directly to Flank, as this type of request can easily be fixed and solved by using dedicated tool.\n\nHope I’ve helped,\n\nAlex","2026-01-14T10:16:45.417Z"],["3809019","PFI-833220","PFI","innaaime.kalju@bolt.eu","Inna Aime Kalju","[^251221-1700-087037 (1).pdf]","2026-01-14T10:18:18.671Z"],["3809021","LSS-61554","LSS","karolina.jedrzejczak@bolt.eu","Karolina Jędrzejczak","[^PoA Jedrzejczak (1).pdf] _(1.78 MB)_","2026-01-14T10:19:02.252Z"],["3809023","LSS-60984","LSS","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","[~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd], they did not attach new documents, unfortunately. ","2026-01-14T10:19:11.137Z"],["3809027","HS-28902","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hi, the document has been sent to your People Partner for signing. Once signed, a copy will reach your personal email. Let me know in case of any questions!\n\nFeel better soon!","2026-01-14T10:20:44.404Z"],["3809033","LSS-60711","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:0c90413b-741f-4463-8f2a-012d18e770c7] all good, confirming we can proceed to have the Lease Agreement signed. \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/159/create/742|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/159/create/742|smart-link] \n\nI note the landlord signed in wet ink - before logging the ticket for signature, please confirm whether they require a wet ink signature or if Bolt sign via its standard digital method. Risto can be witness. \n\nAs this has been finalised I will proceed to close the ticket. Please re-open if further legal assistance is required. ","2026-01-14T10:22:15.903Z"],["3809034","ML-1444","ML","nadezhda.kiriushkina@bolt.eu","Nadya Kiriushkina","We have an alert from PINT now on old tokens in backend. No alert on Github, tho. Not sure about Airflow-main. I think we have an alert","2026-01-14T10:22:28.995Z"],["3809035","PFI-833221","PFI","liam.james@bolt.eu","Liam James","[^_Searcys - Payment Import - 14_01 - UK Payment Import.csv]","2026-01-14T10:22:51.837Z"],["3809036","LSS-61555","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nMatīss Panga has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-14T10:23:01.690Z"],["3809039","LSS-61416","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:712020:011a9eb3-77af-4c62-bb26-e6c10e6097ec]. Considering that the Police is requesting this information only for disciplinary purposes and they mention that an indication of completed rides is enough, alternatively to sending a list of all the rides, I propose we respond in the following terms: \n\n_Núcleo de Deontologia e Disciplina da Polícia de Segurança Publica de Faro_\n\n_Exmo. Comandante Distrital – Superintendente Mário Nuno campos de Oliveira,_\n\n_No seguimento do pedido de informação recebido, que mereceu a nossa melhor atenção, vem a Bolt prestar os seguintes esclarecimentos:_\n\n* _Alfredo Rebelo Pereira, com o certificado de motorista de TVDE n.º 944113/2025, exerceu a atividade de motorista de TVDE a partir da plataforma electrónica Bolt durante o ano de 2025, tendo executado, no período temporal referido, 2713 viagens._\n\n_Encontramo-nos ao dispor para qualquer esclarecimento adicional necessário._\n\n_Atentamente,_","2026-01-14T10:23:53.484Z"],["3809040","LSS-61388","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:0dcccdab-40ef-4e81-988a-67af3ae07691] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^E03 - D1 Private Confirmation - Bolt_V1 (1).pdf] ","2026-01-14T10:23:59.718Z"],["3809041","PAW-14865","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160657\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-14 10:23:58 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-14T10:23:58.811Z"],["3809042","LSS-61555","LSS","matiss.panga@bolt.eu","Matīss Panga","[^TEMPLATE_ENG_driver partnership collaboration agreement Bolt_Ignitis_v1_19.12.2025.docx]\n[^ENG-LV_BOLT Mutual NDA - Bolt x Ignitis_v1_19.12.2025.docx]\n\n","2026-01-14T10:24:02.316Z"],["3809045","SREDESK-7416","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","[~accountid:5e21ae91ac570b0caa8672c1] It’s not showing{{v2-bulk-import}} user/group. Do you mean {{v2-campaign-bulk-import}} ?\n\n\n{noformat}root@ti-incentives-dba.sqldb:(none)>SELECT * FROM information_schema.resource_groups WHERE NAME like '%archiver%' OR NAME LIKE '%bulk-import%';\n+-------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------+\n| NAME                    | RU_PER_SEC | PRIORITY | BURSTABLE | QUERY_LIMIT | BACKGROUND |\n|-------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------|\n| archiver                | 5000       | MEDIUM   | YES       | <null>      | <null>     |\n| v2-campaign-bulk-import | 5000       | MEDIUM   | YES       | <null>      | <null>     |\n+-------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------+{noformat}","2026-01-14T10:24:18.722Z"],["3809047","LSS-61388","LSS","paolo.catani@bolt.eu","Paolo Catani","Thank you!","2026-01-14T10:24:45.763Z"],["3809049","LSS-61554","LSS","victoria.maliuk@bolt.eu","Victoria Maliuk","approved ","2026-01-14T10:24:58.993Z"],["3809050","MVRT-1026","MVRT","aleksandra.onutsina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Onutšina","Hi, [~accountid:60a8d3053fae6f00681b708e] [~accountid:5d289a7c3e09b40c262cfaa9] here’s an incoming request from Delivery, I’ll tag Taaniel again once the copy is figured out.","2026-01-14T10:24:59.776Z"],["3809051","FX-3626","FX","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:712020:0fffdf32-b581-494a-8d8a-f431b780b28e] should we just open it? i.e just send you to the page as if you clicked the button? ","2026-01-14T10:25:02.823Z"],["3809053","PFI-833222","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-14T10:25:26.925Z"],["3809058","PRV-976","PRV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Latest update from Edik: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-51110?focusedCommentId=3779581|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-51110?focusedCommentId=3779581|smart-link] \n\n# Verification is enabled for all tobacco products via Veritas on country level\n# Courier would verify at delivery","2026-01-14T10:26:30.184Z"],["3809060","RIDE-247","RIDE","subarna.sharna@bolt.eu","Subarna Islam Sharna","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] the hours assigned from accounting (6 hours) are carried forwarded from last Q4. No additional hours are estimated. Please adjust as necessary, if it’s creating duplicated impact. Thanks!","2026-01-14T10:26:41.667Z"],["3809061","PFI-831450","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Thanks for attaching the process doc - that was helpful! I’ve created a ticket to engineering 🙂 Since we didn’t notice the ticket before, can you please also let us know in #commerce-support-billing for future tickets so we can make sure we don’t miss this 🙏\n\n\n\nEither way, will keep you updated regarding the engineering ticket! ","2026-01-14T10:26:45.118Z"],["3809062","PFI-831450","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! \n\nLooks like this issue needs input from our developers. The issue has been flagged to them & they are investigating. We will keep you posted with any updates! \n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-14T10:26:55.256Z"],["3809064","LSS-59601","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ,\n\nthanks for drafting this contract! I’ve drafted some suggestions to clause 4 and 5 of the SOW, I let you review and let me know if fine for you too. Those should be checked with Dimitrios as well.\n\nThe rest looks fine to me!\n\nThanks a lot\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-14T10:27:44.039Z"],["3809066","BP-13439","BP","uladzislau.tsyrkunou@bolt.eu","Uladzislau Tsyrkunou","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101098?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101098?created=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T10:27:57.724Z"],["3809067","LOC-4806","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","Hey [~accountid:628b4f089c617b006a6c6efb]  Kindly assist to input Rider LCM data for Q4, 2025 for the AF markets ahead of our scheduled QBR ( {{2026-02-06}} ). thank you.\nCC: [~accountid:6270f0bd807e0000691b79bb] ","2026-01-14T10:28:20.109Z"],["3809069","RIDE-250","RIDE","subarna.sharna@bolt.eu","Subarna Islam Sharna","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] the hours assigned from accounting (15 hours) are carried forwarded from last Q4. No additional hours are estimated. Please adjust as necessary, if it’s creating duplicated impact. Thanks!","2026-01-14T10:28:33.856Z"],["3809070","PFI-833225","PFI","liam.james@bolt.eu","Liam James","[^_Searcys - Payment Import - 14_01 (2) - UK Payment Import.csv]","2026-01-14T10:28:37.817Z"],["3809072","LOC-4807","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","Hey [~accountid:712020:d98a1599-2e3b-4bac-bd9d-3c7377960838]   Kindly assist to input Driver LCM data for Q4, 2025 for the AF markets ahead of our scheduled QBR ( {{2026-02-06}} ). thank you.\nCC: [~accountid:62a057bc122dfd0069061724]","2026-01-14T10:29:02.240Z"],["3809075","HS-28935","HS","peter.smith@bolt.eu","Peter Smith","!Peter Smith EofW 1 of 2.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!Peter Smith EofW 2 of 2.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-14T10:30:14.980Z"],["3809076","LSS-61555","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-14T10:31:08.001Z"],["3809077","FIN2-969","FIN2","subarna.sharna@bolt.eu","Subarna Islam Sharna","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] the hours assigned from accounting (2 hours) are carried forwarded from last Q4. No additional hours are estimated. Please adjust as necessary, if it’s creating duplicated impact. Thanks!","2026-01-14T10:31:20.825Z"],["3809081","GUM-36","GUM","octavian.moraru@bolt.eu","Octavian Moraru","Enabled geofencing logic in LIVE, no performance issues, see this thread for details [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09HMSQ4W22/p1768232949629319|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09HMSQ4W22/p1768232949629319|smart-link] \n\nOne thing we need to fix though: it seems that we are removing the same geofence multiple times. The flow is:\n\n* driver accepts → we create a geofence\n* driver enters or is inside the geofence → we [remove|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/2fa2d4f87e1c79355f65de5ec833e8a9c4d8f891/src/rides/driver/driver_map_reports/main/service/GeofenceEventHandler.ts#L53] the geofence\n* order transitions to a different state → we [remove|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/df6b37f81c6f5e20fae69f709aa43e1826fafcb9/src/rides/driver/driver_map_reports/main/service/OrderStopQueueEventHandler.ts#L147] the geofence again\n\nWhile this doesn’t cause any functional issues, it does make {{route-prediction}} log an [error|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/8a0f43a6d90b5948c92ce0c319fbdebe0194d71b/src/platform/geo/route_prediction/main/state/GeofencingStorer.ts#L305].\n\nPossible fixes:\n\n# Only remove the geofence once the order transitions to a different state. The downside is that we will needlessly increment the order version in cases where the driver enters the geofence multiple times.\n# Store a {{geofence_removed}} flag in the cache and check it before any removal attempt.\n\nWill create a separate ticket to address this.","2026-01-14T10:32:06.365Z"],["3809082","PFI-832850","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Well, kinda, but system just prevents us from payout out more than the available balance. In this case there’s technically nothing “wrong” → the provider received earnings for the order, but since it’s in cash we can’t automatically deduct the fees in there are no other orders, so yep, unfortunately can cause it to go negative. ","2026-01-14T10:32:20.797Z"],["3809084","LSS-57632","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Thanks [~accountid:5e4cfe3b393ea90c94b40eb0] [draft|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iSUg8z6o0ag_oKrMf6PVAamAzWN0YAeNcxiGjJv5aGo/edit?tab=t.0] updated accordingly.\n\nBelow are 2 versions to download and share with parter, one with track changes and other is a clean, final draft as we trust that all amendments will now be accepted. \n\nNote that you may just need to update the dates in Annex 1 - Period of Campaign.  \n\n[^2026.01 Bolt Rewards NG_Partnership Agreement - Bastion Health (final draft) (clean).docx]\n[^2026.01 Bolt Rewards NG_Partnership Agreement - Bastion Health (review 12.01.2026).docx]\n\n","2026-01-14T10:33:20.934Z"],["3809087","ADS-215","ADS","daniel.kamkha@bolt.eu","Daniel Kamkha","Crowdin Food: [https://bolt.crowdin.com/u/projects/24|https://bolt.crowdin.com/u/projects/24|smart-link] \n\nTranslation file in Admin: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/backend-platform/translations/files/edit/210409|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/backend-platform/translations/files/edit/210409]","2026-01-14T10:34:59.060Z"],["3809091","PFI-832977","PFI","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hi team, the bank details were not updated correctly, sorry. Could you please initiate another payment? Thanks!","2026-01-14T10:37:32.347Z"],["3809102","LSS-53508","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey [~accountid:5c010fa68ce9b546efc49454] - We have signed the documents that arrived to HQ. Date was not added. Please find the scan attached. I believe it’s the best if we send them back to Polish office and You can organise delivery from there. Shipment tracking code will be posted once recieved.\n\n[^Donation contract annex - Gdańsk_Bolt Services PL sp. z o.o._Gamina Miasta Gdanska_2025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T10:39:23.795Z"],["3809105","MM-933","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements are provided; only a summary exists.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The summary is understandable but lacks detail and context.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting information are present.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate or original estimate is provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description with requirements and acceptance criteria.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate for the issue.","2026-01-14T10:39:29.804Z"],["3809106","PFI-833220","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:6012aaf8a41ea5006a613a63] \n\nThere are 10 other accounts associated with this profile. These can be reviewed here:\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/userRelations/288109283|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/userRelations/288109283]\n\nAll associated accounts have been flagged by the Fraud team. For any questions related to these accounts, the Fraud team should be consulted, as they are the subject-matter experts. If further clarification is required, please let me know and I will include Fraud Ops in this ticket.\n\nI was unable to find any records of refunds. The payments currently show a CHARGEBACK status. When a chargeback occurs, the funds are returned directly to the original account holder, which may be interpreted as a refund.\n\nNo refunds have been issued to the user’s Bolt balance.\n\nPlease note that funds cannot be forwarded to another user. Any refund can only be processed back to the original payment source. Bolt balances cannot be transferred to other users or converted into other currencies.\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-14T10:39:36.390Z"],["3809107","SREDESK-7416","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Resource groups have been changed.\nPlease note that existing connections will use the old definition, only new connections get the updated resource group. It might take some time until all connections are recycled and new groups are effective.\n\n{noformat}root@ti-incentives-dba.sqldb:(none)>ALTER RESOURCE GROUP `archiver` RU_PER_SEC = 5000 BURSTABLE = FALSE;\nYou're about to run a destructive command.\nDo you want to proceed? (y/n): y\nYour call!\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.514s\nroot@ti-incentives-dba.sqldb:(none)>ALTER RESOURCE GROUP `v2-campaign-bulk-import` RU_PER_SEC = 5000 BURSTABLE = FALSE;\nYou're about to run a destructive command.\nDo you want to proceed? (y/n): y\nYour call!\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 1.014s\nroot@ti-incentives-dba.sqldb:(none)>SELECT * FROM information_schema.resource_groups WHERE NAME like '%archiver%' OR NAME LIKE '%bulk%';\n+-------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------+\n| NAME                    | RU_PER_SEC | PRIORITY | BURSTABLE | QUERY_LIMIT | BACKGROUND |\n|-------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------|\n| archiver                | 5000       | MEDIUM   | NO        | <null>      | <null>     |\n| v2-campaign-bulk-import | 5000       | MEDIUM   | NO        | <null>      | <null>     |\n+-------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------+\n2 rows in set\nTime: 0.006s{noformat}","2026-01-14T10:40:10.777Z"],["3809110","LSS-61477","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:61b9ef0e9e8a370068af893c] ,\n\nThanks for the visibility. No red flag from my side at this stage.\n\nCan you confirm that the time limitation for car branding (max 12 months, ideally capped at 6 months with possible renewal) is respected  for Branded Cars in general and also for this pilot?\n\nThanks\n\nElisabetta \n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] FYI","2026-01-14T10:41:02.096Z"],["3809113","WD-22557","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] , can you please assign the certifications for SE001, SE002 and FI002 to [~accountid:623de186b75ca8007057c6f9] as requested here. \n\nI already provided access (Bolt Accountant) to these entities to Birgit and Karmen in WD and SBX as requested.","2026-01-14T10:42:28.426Z"],["3809114","WFM-9968","WFM","ahmed.othman@bolt.eu","Ahmed Othman","Thanks [~accountid:712020:824016bc-1a7a-4038-a3aa-448d64c000d1] , all is fine now, the queue is assigned to the list.\n\n\n","2026-01-14T10:42:35.299Z"],["3809116","LSS-61353","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hello, [~accountid:712020:a975e2d9-679b-4d8a-a063-b831aafacd02]! The addendum has been signed, please find it attached. Please feel free to share it with the partner.\n\n[^2026.01 Bolt Support Services RO Mino Serv Bolt Food Addendum (signed).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T10:42:45.679Z"],["3809117","PFI-833198","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:a86e3f5d-8ff8-4fd2-bac0-2e4712e56a68],\n\nThis is a fraudulent business.\nThe very same user is related to this [business|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessCompanies/806179?tab=business_company] that has already been deactivated for fraudulent activities.\nFrom [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/users/412063496?tab=instruments] it is visible that the user has made multiple attempts with the same method.\nThey do not have a single regular orders.\n\nAdditionally, this business has only conducted trip with this one specific driver, therefore, we can assume that the driver collaborated with the aforementioned user.\n\nThe driver will not be blocked, as they have still generated good GMV to us.\nThe rider and business account will be blocked for fraudulent activities.\n\nYou may manually compensate the commission fees to the driver, however, nothing else.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-14T10:42:47.441Z"],["3809118","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","Hi Beatrice, thank you for loooking into this. I am filling out the form with our partners form 4x27. I will invite you to all the documents received from PWC. For this purpose I will only need help with the legal perspective, which has been translated to you. \n\nKind regards, \nMalene\n\n","2026-01-14T10:42:52.682Z"],["3809119","PFI-833181","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment matched to client https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75707331","2026-01-14T10:43:04.802Z"],["3809120","LSS-61483","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi! would it be possible to have this signed by tomorrow? Thank you!","2026-01-14T10:43:04.957Z"],["3809121","LSS-53508","LSS","weronika.ners@bolt.eu","Weronika Ners","Thank you very much! Yes, please send them back to the PL office, I’ll take care of it then 🙂 ","2026-01-14T10:43:38.995Z"],["3809124","PFI-833041","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for EUR 3.50 on Dec 17, 2025, 15:22:35 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 15265675351002860922218 to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 17th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n\n[^Refund_Letter_NJ3STFFQ6KWGX9Q9_PWK2NSKKS4HC6JX3 (1).pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-14T10:44:11.616Z"],["3809125","PFI-833228","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-14T10:44:12.612Z"],["3809127","LOC-4818","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","Hey [~accountid:603364eaac6e4e0069c2ef37] Kindly assist to input Driver performance data for Q4, 2025 for the AF markets ahead of our scheduled QBR ( 6th Feb 26). thank you.\ncc: [~accountid:5c61221fdb49e4016460f3c1] \n\n","2026-01-14T10:44:22.994Z"],["3809130","LOC-4817","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","Hey [~accountid:6230b0de1c09d2007013be85] Kindly assist to input Driver performance data for Q4, 2025 for the AF markets ahead of our scheduled QBR ( 6th Feb 26). thank you.\ncc: [~accountid:5fb227c70d2f61006ff6cce2] \n","2026-01-14T10:45:00.133Z"],["3809132","PFI-833187","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment allocated to client https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/76905544","2026-01-14T10:45:31.215Z"],["3809133","FRAUDOPS-562","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","~75-80% of all orders with destination changes are on the {{new_route}} config. with [FRAUD-5602|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FRAUD-5602], all of our reject decisions will turn into adjustments, which I expect to overturn a lot of these rejections into passes. therefore, doesn’t make too much sense to look for marginal optimizations here, as the whole flow will already be optimized to have lower friction. \n\nadditionally, instead of straight-up rejecting every request based on current rule triggers, I’ll edit rules to not target orders with multiple predictions where we know the price increase is marginal vs the currently authorized amount. ","2026-01-14T10:45:47.867Z"],["3809134","LOC-4816","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","CC: [~accountid:637dde50fde064eda2edd049] ","2026-01-14T10:46:02.162Z"],["3809135","DSR-3733","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-14T10:46:06.776Z"],["3809136","PRODSEC-705","PRODSEC","aghadadash.guliyev@bolt.eu","Dadash Guliyev","This task creates S3, where all the SBOM/SCA related scan results will be stored in the format of:\n\n{noformat}s3://prodsec-scan-data/raw/\n  scanner=trivy/\n    scan_type=vuln/\n      target_type=image/\n        scan_date=YYYY-MM-DD/\n          run_id=<uuid>/\n            metadata.json  <-- Each Run Creates Metadata\n            targets.jsonl  <-- List Of The Targets For Scan\n            logs.txt\n            target_hash=<sha>/\n              output.json\n            target_hash=<sha2>/\n              output.json\n              target.json\n    scan_type=sbom/\n      ......\n  scanner=trufflehog/\n    target_type=github/\n      ........{noformat}\n\nExample:\n{{s3://prodsec-scan-data/raw/scanner=trivy/scan_type=vuln/target_type=image/scan_date=2026-01-01/run_id=GUID4/target_hash=sha}}\n\n\n\nStore {{metadata.json}} and logs under\n{{s3://prodsec-scan-data/raw/scanner=trivy/scan_type=vuln/target_type=image/scan_date=2026-01-01/run_id=GUID4}}\n\n\n\nPotential Metadata:\n\n{noformat}{\n  \"run_id\": \"GUID4\",\n  \"scan_date\": \"2026-01-01\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-01-01T01:00:12Z\",\n  \"finished_at\": \"2026-01-01T01:23:45Z\",\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n\n  \"scanner\": \"trivy\",\n  \"scanner_version\": \"0.50.0\",\n  \"scan_type\": \"vuln\",\n  \"target_type\": \"image\",\n\n  \"source\": \"jfrog\",\n  \"scope_type\": \"jfrog_repo\",\n  \"scope_value\": \"docker-backend-local\",\n\n  \"config_version\": \"2026-01-01.1\",\n  \"pipeline_version\": \"scanner-job@1.0.0\",\n\n  \"targets_total\": 42,\n  \"targets_succeeded\": 41,\n  \"targets_failed\": 1,\n\n  \"s3_prefix\": \"s3://prodsec-scan-data/raw/scanner=trivy/scan_type=vuln/target_type=image/scan_date=2026-01-01/run_id=GUID4/\",\n\n  \"notes\": \"Nightly Trivy vulnerability scan for JFrog docker-backend-local live-* images\"\n}{noformat}\n\n\n\ntargets.jsonl (contains details about all targets):\n\n{noformat}{\n  \"run_id\":\"GUID4\",\n  \"target_hash\":\"a1b2c3\",\n  \"target_type\":\"image\",\n  \"target_id\":\"registry.live.boltint.net/docker-backend-local/taxify-server/live-businessportal:20260112-1126-6f39cf1d3fe7-arm64\",\n  \"registry\":\"registry.live.boltint.net\",\n  \"repo\":\"docker-backend-local\",\n  \"image\":\"taxify-server/live-businessportal\",\n  \"tag\":\"20260112-1126-6f39cf1d3fe7-arm64\",\n  \"digest\":null,\n  \"platform\":\"linux/arm64\",\n  \"status\":\"success\",\n  \"output_s3\":\"s3://prodsec-scan-data/raw/.../run_id=GUID4/target_hash=a1b2c3/output.json\"\n}\n{\n  \"run_id\":\"GUID4\",\n  \"target_...........\n  ......................\n}{noformat}\n\n\n\n\n\nExample query for Databricks from s3:\n\n{noformat}CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS prodsec;\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS prodsec.scan_raw\nUSING DELTA\nLOCATION 's3://prodsec-scan-data/raw/';\n\nSELECT *\nFROM prosec.scan_raw\nWHERE scanner = 'trivy'\n  AND scan_type = 'sbom'\n    AND scan_date >= '2026-01-01'{noformat}","2026-01-14T10:46:09.503Z"],["3809140","HS-28888","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Sent for signature.","2026-01-14T10:46:51.046Z"],["3809141","LSS-61557","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","[^Copie de Mise_en_demeure RAHIEL MOUHCIN.pdf] _(327 kB)_\n\n[^pre assignation tribunal de commerce M. MOUHCIN RAHIEL.pdf] _(320 kB)_","2026-01-14T10:46:53.062Z"],["3809142","LSS-61557","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDolinda Mbensa has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-14T10:46:54.661Z"],["3809143","LSS-61552","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:5b7beae4ed4f842a6ddb4712] - can you please resubmit this ticket to [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] via the Legal Service Desk?\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/1310/create/753|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/1310/create/753]","2026-01-14T10:46:58.282Z"],["3809144","HS-28877","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Sent for signature.","2026-01-14T10:47:12.634Z"],["3809147","LSS-51110","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] I’ll support Privacy changes in this quarter. Thanks for letting us know of the changes!\n\n\n\nDo I understand correctly that we’re going to both:\n\n# verify via our internal verification system at purchase in-app; and\n# instruct the Courier to also verify the age at Delivery","2026-01-14T10:47:44.759Z"],["3809149","LSS-58800","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","hi [~accountid:712020:ec09f884-709e-4d12-8b74-3045f0b19650] , please create different ticket for the NDA, as it will have a different path in terms of course of action. Sorry for the misunderstanding!\n\nBest,\n\nAlex","2026-01-14T10:48:18.048Z"],["3809150","LSS-61493","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14] , and thanks [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] for adding me.\n\nI’ve taken a look at the document, and I see only one requirement from a privacy POV: \n\n* _[tab Legal Requirements, row L10]_ *To sign a data processing agreement with PwC*, but the agreement is not in the file. In principle, I have no issues with that (and it’s aligned with the approach we’ve taken in Swedish tenders), but we’ll need to negotiate the agreement to ensure we get the most favourable clauses possible. For now, I can’t unfortunately comment on something I haven’t seen. \n** What we can say at this point is that we will conclude the agreement, but it will need to be reviewed.\n* One important thing to flag is that we are required to perform criminal background checks _[tab Legal Requirements, row L17]  -_ as I know (see [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-56083] for reference), we do not perform background checks in DK, and therefore we’ll need to start doing so for this specific tender. Let’s align in the near future on what the requirements are - as discussed in the past, there are major privacy law constraints for this so we need to implement such checks carefully.\n\nIf you’ll be having any alignment meetings or if there’s a channel - please add me 🙂 ","2026-01-14T10:48:25.296Z"],["3809153","LSS-61548","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Support provided in the main ticket.","2026-01-14T10:48:40.455Z"],["3809154","PFI-833010","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nPlease note that Bolt was having technical difficulties with Fondy, the local Ukrainian entity that processes the food delivery payments. To handle the payment service provider downtime we have routed the payment through our international entity. \n\nI have checked the payment and I can confirm the payment was done through Bolt international entity. \nThis can be considered as an international payment and there could be additional charges included from the users bank. \n\nWe would suggest the user to reach out to their bank to clarify what are the additional charges. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-14T10:49:06.014Z"],["3809156","LSS-61554","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","[~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] could you confirm if Bolt Rides is still active in these terms or Bolt Poland took it over?","2026-01-14T10:49:10.816Z"],["3809157","LSS-61244","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95]! Simple Spotdraft signature is fine for this one as there will be no dealings with state authorities. The POA uses our standard template for GM POAs, but not always all the rights are exercised, which is the case here.\n\nHey, [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432]! Can you please help to collect Ahto’s signature via Spotdraft for the attached POA?\n\n[^2025.12 Power of Attorney (Bogdan Clipici) (091d9f8b-e841-4106-9933-1fab99458fbe).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T10:50:08.272Z"],["3809160","LSS-61481","LSS","louis.humbert@bolt.eu","Louis Humbert","Ok thanks for the answer [~accountid:712020:cf457436-e17c-4575-8d48-f2b9135ccc82] , \n\nBut as we are already applying a car age criteria in our Premium categories, why couldn’t we apply a car age criteria to get access to Bolt ? We can explain that after 20 years, a car may have safety flaws and may be less effective in the event of an accident ?\n\nCould we explain that in order to offer the safest possible ride, we have set this age limit at 20?","2026-01-14T10:50:56.649Z"],["3809165","LSS-61096","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] \n\nI checked the T&C [https://www.articulate.com/360/terms-of-service/|https://www.articulate.com/360/terms-of-service/|smart-link] \n\nIn the [ticket of People team|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-60199?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6IjU4YjYwZjNlNzQwYWM2YjkzNGRlOTcxN2ZlMDRmOWQ4NTc4NjE3MTdiODgzZTZlZDljN2Q1ZmZjNTNmNzZjMDQiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiMzYzNTkiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IkxTUy02MDE5OSJ9LCJleHAiOjE3Njg1NTg5NTAsImlhdCI6MTc2NjEzOTc1MH0.T81dWa3_wqUcVgHua-6AtDgONXuT6Hl8ln8Q9HsAboQ] it’s stated that supplier does not accept any changes.  \n\n*Risks that Raivis highlighted for People team agreement* \n\nh4. 1. Unilateral Changes to Terms\n\n* Articulate may change terms at any time via web posting.\n* Our use of the platform after such change implies acceptance.\n* _Recommendation_: Monitor term updates or ask Articulate to notify us when changes are made, even if not contractually required.\n\nh4. 2. No Termination for Convenience\n\n* We are locked into the subscription term \n\nAdditionally: \n\n# *Unfavourable governing law for Bolt: New York, US*\n\n* Bolt prefers Estonian or English law as a compromise, US law expose us to high litigation costs. \n\n# *Automatic renewal* \n\n* Services shall *automatically renew* unless there is at least thirty (30) days before the end of the then-current Subscription Term.\n\n# *Low liability limit:* 12 months fees. \n\n* In our case this is 15 000 which is a very low limit is case of any damages. \n\n[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] I would advise to ask Articulate again if we can: \n\n* remove automatic renewal \n* have notifications about updates to T&C \n* change governing law to English law \n* have possibility to increase liability limit ","2026-01-14T10:51:25.098Z"],["3809166","WFM-9984","WFM","duke.aminga@bolt.eu","Duke Aminga","[Beehive|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/] see the sample link","2026-01-14T10:51:43.937Z"],["3809168","L10N-27667","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27663](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27663)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T10:52:14.062Z"],["3809169","L10N-27668","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27663](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27663)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T10:52:14.948Z"],["3809170","PFI-830438","PFI","vadim.kozjakov@bolt.eu","Vadim Kozjakov","That doesn't make sense, in December he had GMV around 16300 CZK (665€) so his commission is around 4000 CZK (163€)","2026-01-14T10:52:15.361Z"],["3809171","L10N-27672","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source o