ded under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27663](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27663)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T10:52:43.330Z"],["3809185","PFI-831450","PFI","agnes.furtos@bolt.eu","Ágnes Fürtös","Hi Ketlin!\nThank you for your support, yes I’ll create a post next time and I’ll add it to the process doc as well.\nThanks a lot!","2026-01-14T10:53:06.573Z"],["3809188","PFI-833222","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, generally we have separate Billing Model (Resale vs Intermediary) and Payments methods (Postpaid vs Credit Card). Based on the credit card requirement, only credit card is likely gonna apply.\n\n* Resale model: each Ride Invoiced is issued to the Bolt Entity and is resold in a single invoice to the Business Account monthly; It’s possible to enable that credit card is charged after each Ride.\n* Intermediary model: each Ride is invoiced to the Company entity directly from the Driver. Monthly SF Invoice is Issued and Statement.\n\nI believe, the latter is gonna work from invoicing perspective. I would confirm whether it’s possible/comfortable to ensure that correct credit card is used per ride in case of multiple cc needed → please, confirm it with the #commerce-support-customer-payments or with the Business Product Team, as we don’t have the access to the Business Portal.","2026-01-14T10:53:29.705Z"],["3809189","RDXENG-4652","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","Hey *@user-U01F8CDK7RD*!\n\n[TECH-150166|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TECH-150166]: CA.193.0 *PL*: Report by Pavel P stating:\n\n{quote}Different numerals{quote}\n\nConsistently reproducible in Tallinn with the {{Priority}} category, [there are no Search filters in PL for the category|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/system-data/categories/edit/14699], not sure if it has anything to do with this. :eyes:","2026-01-14T10:53:39.169Z"],["3809190","RDXENG-4652","RDXENG",null,"Slack","[Ankit Goyal|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6358f09ab0b6ef03564955ba] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1768293559325389?thread_ts=1768293559.325389&cid=CSFF3R571|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1768293559325389?thread_ts=1768293559.325389&cid=CSFF3R571|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-14T10:53:40.282Z"],["3809191","RDXENG-4652","RDXENG","anton.belka@bolt.eu","Anton Belka","[@germo.rikk|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d5ff31d5a68ef0ca6258fd8] Hi, could you please check on iOS? Look like BE issue","2026-01-14T10:53:41.041Z"],["3809192","RDXENG-4652","RDXENG","germo.rikk@bolt.eu","Germo Rikk","Yes, same on iOS - [@ankit.goyal|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6358f09ab0b6ef03564955ba] ptal :prayge:","2026-01-14T10:53:42.158Z"],["3809193","RDXENG-4652","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","Hey!\nDo you know who/when was the change for numericals in Arabic language done?","2026-01-14T10:53:42.859Z"],["3809194","RDXENG-4652","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","[@sergei.budkov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:7c45f6ec-c1df-48ed-b544-312d6b586eb1] Would you know?","2026-01-14T10:53:43.657Z"],["3809195","RDXENG-4652","RDXENG","sergei.budkov@bolt.eu","Sergei Budkov","No, haven't heard of any related to Arabic lng","2026-01-14T10:53:45.069Z"],["3809197","RDXENG-4652","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","I have posted the [request|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C05K8Q3TUG3/p1768306383649129] here.","2026-01-14T10:53:45.715Z"],["3809198","LSS-60550","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","Hi [~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2]!  \n\nAdding luminor comments here and my comments in red. Can you pleas ehelp us reflect this changes and let us know. \n\n\n* Could you please add the clause that during cooperation with Luminor in Lithuania (during the term of the agreement) Bolt shall cooperate exclusively with Luminor in relation to the services covered by the agreement. Bolt shall not enter cooperate with, provide services to any other bank or financial institution.  {color:#bf2600}Let’s add it only for Lithuania.{color}\n* Also, about the term in your sent agreement added that the cooperation term is 1 year, lets put 6 months as was agreed with you and business decision from our side is made, with possibility to prolong it. {color:#bf2600}Ok{color}\n* In agreement was added that Annex will be added online and might be changed at any time. I think this is a very flexible solution but also includes the risk for us. So, our proposal to keep annex’s in more conservative way with possibility to initiate changes after parties agreed/signed.\n* The clause 6.4: The Advertiser has 5 business days to dispute an invoice by email with stated reasons. Question: Can we expand it to 10 business days? {color:#bf2600}Ok{color}\n* Could we have as additional clause in Annex about report (it was informed by Ruska that we will get it on weekly basis) –more detailed description : what data will be delivered, on which day, will there be included apple wallet payments, how frequent, based on which data we will be billed? \n{color:#bf2600}Weekly reporting includes only:{color}\n{color:#bf2600}- Campaign Spend  {color}\n{color:#bf2600}- Number of Users engaged in the campaign {color}\n{color:#bf2600}- Volume of transactions{color}{color:#bf2600} {color}\n{color:#bf2600}Apple wallet payments don’t enter in the campign.{color}\n{color:#bf2600}On a monthly reporting we can include share of wallet{color}\n* Also add into Annex, what €20k contains: how many customers you are planning to engage (switch to Luminor) , as it was defined in presentation for the primary both countries budget of €37k+. This information is also needed in out internal business case calculation+, so could you please share via email as well?\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 04.52.08.png|width=1240,height=144,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 04.52.08.png\"!\n* In Annex No 2, c clause: let’s include that Business Luminor cards are excluded from the scope since our focus group is private customers. {color:#bf2600}OK{color}\n* In Annex No 2, k clause: *“*+Bolt Mobility Platform+:  Bolt will advertise the Campaign offers to every user that opens or uses Bolt Platform apps and apply the discount to existing and new users that order a service by using a Luminor's Card with valid BINs”. The advertise should be visible for other bank card users not to every user, as pre-discussed in our first discussions with Ruska.\n* About the clause of 5.1.2 : “_not make any disclosure or announcement (orally or in writing) to the public or to a third party, in relation to this Agreement or its subject matter without the prior written approval of Bolt (unless required by law which may be withdrawn by Bolt at any time if it is given. If the Advertiser wishes to make any announcement or share information about this Agreement or its cooperation with Bolt with any third party (including its own clients), the Advertiser must obtain Bolt’s prior written approval by email. Etc.._” We would like to add into our web the notification of partnership, or send letters to our customer data base – should we align each send out with you?\n\n","2026-01-14T10:53:47.555Z"],["3809199","LSS-57332","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Thanks [~accountid:5d81df0e9581710c30328f3a] - please ensure that the Data Sharing Agreement we provided is properly signed through our Legal Operations Team ([~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] can support with arranging that) and submitted in this ticket for record-purposes.","2026-01-14T10:54:02.490Z"],["3809200","DRAG101-453","DRAG101","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","All labels are confirmed and finished (/) \n\nStill waiting for DfT to do the the speed measurement, which is depending on weather. Last information was that they can not do it before 18th January  :loading: ","2026-01-14T10:54:59.777Z"],["3809201","RDS-1355","RDS","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","[~accountid:712020:9db8be0f-eb61-4ebc-bac7-a9563c14e4b0] designs added to ticket now ☝️ ","2026-01-14T10:55:06.142Z"],["3809202","LSS-61496","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Hey [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] , the contact name has now been changed\n\n[^WPL 2025 Residential Licence Template.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T10:55:11.769Z"],["3809203","WDFT-3543","WDFT","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","We operate under EE003 in Poland for Micromobility.","2026-01-14T10:55:34.636Z"],["3809205","EBIKE1-422","EBIKE1","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] Let’s please follow up on this","2026-01-14T10:55:47.514Z"],["3809206","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi Edvards,\n\nHow is it going on prelive?\n\nCan I apply the change on live?","2026-01-14T10:56:11.451Z"],["3809211","EBIKE1-318","EBIKE1","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","On hold until IOT FW is finished.","2026-01-14T10:58:45.737Z"],["3809212","SREDESK-7407","SREDESK","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Hi [~accountid:712020:782f9535-5dfc-41e5-8bdf-057eef89f6ef],\n\nI will check back here in about an hour - still have one more ticket to deploy first","2026-01-14T10:58:57.133Z"],["3809213","LSS-61559","LSS","sandra.loewe@bolt.eu","Sandra Löwe","[^Urban Drive Co-Invest + Kick-Back - Bolt Cooperation Agreement - Germany.docx - Google Docs.pdf] _(364 kB)_","2026-01-14T10:59:19.302Z"],["3809218","LSS-60557","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed documents attached from our side! Two copies of each document have been prepared and will be sent to *_Eryk Połeć_* for signing. Attaching here scans of the already signed documents just in case. After documents have been countersigned kindly send the documents for archiving to [contracts@bolt.eu|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] with a ticket number and attach the documents here for our records as well. Thank You! Shipment tracking code will be shared here as well once received.\n\n[^Annex to the cooperation agreement 25.11.21_Bolt Services PL Sp. z o.o._Erykiem Połeć_14.01.26.pdf]\n[^Annex to the cooperation agreement 16.09.21_Bolt Services PL Sp. z o.o._Erykiem Połeć_14.01.26.pdf]\n[^Annex to the cooperation agreement 23.11.21_Bolt Services PL Sp. z o.o._Erykiem Połeć_14.01.26.pdf]\n[^Annex to the cooperation agreement 14.10.21_Bolt Services PL Sp. z o.o._Erykiem Połeć_14.01.26.pdf]\n[^Annex to the cooperation agreement 26.11.21_Bolt Services PL Sp. z o.o._Erykiem Połeć_14.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T11:00:21.843Z"],["3809219","SRED-927","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Update started, gradually rolling out nodepools updates.","2026-01-14T11:00:21.744Z"],["3809220","BDB-1482","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:6358f0a501c2ff842c182ef2] yes, but the mockups you’ve sent are like this: \nand dimesions are 1500x2500, not 6200x2900, so it doesn’t match with the example you’ve sent.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 12.58.57.png|width=530,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 12.58.57.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 12.58.04.png|width=554,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-14 at 12.58.04.png\"!","2026-01-14T11:01:03.758Z"],["3809222","RS-1946","RS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","[^Doručenka.pdf.pdf]\n[^Žiadosť.pdf.pdf]\n[^Žiadosť.pdf en-US.pdf]\n[^Doručenka.pdf en-US.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T11:01:25.389Z"],["3809224","LSS-61557","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-14T11:01:37.142Z"],["3809225","LSS-61496","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Thank you [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5]!\n\n*Legal Ops:* please can you arrange for the attached to be signed by *Alex Wong* on behalf of *Bolt Operations UK Limited* - thank you in advance! 🙏\n\n[^WPL 2025 Residential Licence Template (36b23cad-4a60-42ed-9607-455fce508602).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-14T11:02:11.064Z"],["3809228","UXROPS-81","UXROPS","akram.yacob@bolt.eu","Akram Yacob","archiving this since its covered as part of building the participant management tool [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/UXROPS/ideas?selectedIssue=UXROPS-82|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/UXROPS/ideas?selectedIssue=UXROPS-82|smart-link] ","2026-01-14T11:02:29.362Z"],["3809229","DO-5795","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Webhook and connection created.(/) \nCode tested on staging environment. (/) \n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9698|https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9698]  ","2026-01-14T11:04:20.284Z"],["3809231","PAW-14812","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @udankobolt\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160455\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-14 11:05:29 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-14T11:05:29.389Z"],["3809232","LSS-61561","LSS","risto.kukk@bolt.eu","Risto Kukk","[^SBH - GHSTNBOFF102 - BOLT HOLDINGS OU.pdf] _(3.06 MB)_","2026-01-14T11:06:05.559Z"],["3809233","LSS-60647","LSS","yuliya.shulayeva@bolt.eu","Yuliya Shulayeva","If the user files a GDPR violation complaint, is our legal team 100% sure that we can\n\n# Defend it\n# We are not wrong\n# We won’t be liable for any fines\n\nWe need a Yes or No answer from legal on this.","2026-01-14T11:06:28.729Z"],["3809235","L10N-27699","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27663](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27663)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T11:07:19.992Z"],["3809236","L10N-27698","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27663](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27663)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-14T11:07:20.018Z"],["3809239","SREC-225","SREC","andrus.viik@bolt.eu","Andrus Viik","\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/pci-security/tree/main/_diagrams/v2|https://github.com/bolteu/pci-security/tree/main/_diagrams/v2|smart-card]","2026-01-14T11:07:56.760Z"],["3809241","PFI-833241","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","[^RO1526-2274.pdf]","2026-01-14T11:08:24.323Z"],["3809242","PFI-833241","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-14T11:08:26.522Z"],["3809243","PFI-808167","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment has been reversed back to client. \nThank you!","2026-01-14T11:08:43.904Z"],["3809245","LSS-61541","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:dc8e54ad-0402-41f9-ba6e-9f25f8b451bf],\n\nThank you for reaching out and for the context on this case. In order to have a clearer picture of what has happened, and how to provide accurate and timely response to the customer, I kindly ask you the following information:\n\n# *What’s the exact date in which Bolt received this communication from the customer?*\n# *When did the customer start the first complaints with Bolt?*\n# *Can we please have copy of the tickets (i.e. tech, customer support, others) to see the flow of communications, the information that was requested by the customer and the information Bolt provided?*   \n# *Has an investigation been opened on the inconsistencies of addresses that the customer is highlighting? Any results on it?*\n\nMany thanks! \n\nAngela","2026-01-14T11:09:16.386Z"],["3809249","LSS-57632","LSS","nafiu.raheem@bolt.eu","Nafiu Raheem","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1], thank you very much, as these two versions of the partnership agreement will be shared with the Bastion team\n\n\n\nThe Period of Campaign has been updated","2026-01-14T11:09:50.783Z"],["3809250","CSDA-275","CSDA","zaur.ayralov@bolt.eu","Zaur Ayralov","[~accountid:5d723b3830f82c0c36be5b56]  I will take it next week - will try to enhance as much as I can according to your requirements.\nHowever we can mark it as temporary solution , we need a solid identification for that as volume increase significantly. It would be ideal for us to collect these cases which were sent to api partner email under some tier or user persona to have clear reporting logic for them. \n","2026-01-14T11:10:25.404Z"],["3809252","EBIKE1-422","EBIKE1","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390] investigation still ongoing what exactly was wrong.\n\nSo far we know:\n\n* the hatch was physically open. The lock itself is working as it should.\n* Local team claims that the lock pops open with vibration. I gave them some items to check and report back.","2026-01-14T11:11:28.943Z"],["3809256","LSS-61520","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached. I believe Your scan had two copies of the same document so I only printe